AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6411969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a consequence of the high percentage of endogamous marriages among their inhabitants, in each isolate the majority of the current population are connected in a unique huge genealogy, and descend from a few number of founding lineages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000039> "A cohort of residents of the genetically isolated villages Campora, Gioi and Cardile in Cilento, southern Italy, providing genealogical and genomic data to investigate human genetic variation and the inherited determinants of complex traits and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6411969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data of the Cilento isolates have contributed to many Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) for several complex traits of clinical interest14–20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000039> "A cohort of residents of the genetically isolated villages Campora, Gioi and Cardile in Cilento, southern Italy, providing genealogical and genomic data to investigate human genetic variation and the inherited determinants of complex traits and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6411969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study describes the genetic architecture of the isolated populations of Cilento, through the analysis of exome sequence data of 245 representative individuals of these populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000039> "A cohort of residents of the genetically isolated villages Campora, Gioi and Cardile in Cilento, southern Italy, providing genealogical and genomic data to investigate human genetic variation and the inherited determinants of complex traits and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30858532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6411969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To try to fill this gap, we have performed a whole-exome sequencing study on individuals from the populations of three small villages (Campora, Gioi, and Cardile) located in an inland area of the “National Park of Cilento and Vallo di Diano”, in Southern Italy, included in the “Genetic Park of Cilento and Vallo di Diano Project”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000039> "A cohort of residents of the genetically isolated villages Campora, Gioi and Cardile in Cilento, southern Italy, providing genealogical and genomic data to investigate human genetic variation and the inherited determinants of complex traits and disease.")

