# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3095685/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To provide more definitive evidence for the role of FTO variation in BMI and Type 2 diabetes in South Asians, we used data from 1666 individuals recruited to the Karachi population-based Control of Blood Pressure and Risk Attenuation (COBRA) study and 2745 individuals of Punjabi ancestry ascertained as part of a Type 2 diabetes case–control study, the UK Asian Diabetes Study/Diabetes Genetics in Pakistan (UKADS/DGP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049> "A case-control collection of people of Punjabi ancestry, predominantly originating from Mirpur, Pakistan, with type 2 diabetes or normal glucose regulation, assembled to investigate genetic susceptibility to diabetes and related glycaemic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3176767/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Normal glucose tolerance in the DGP control group was defined as fasting whole blood glucose ≤5.6 mmol/l.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049> "A case-control collection of people of Punjabi ancestry, predominantly originating from Mirpur, Pakistan, with type 2 diabetes or normal glucose regulation, assembled to investigate genetic susceptibility to diabetes and related glycaemic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3176767/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the investigation (Table 1) were from two studies of South Asian individuals; the United Kingdom Asian Diabetes Study (UKADS; 857 participants with type 2 diabetes, 417 without) [2], [3] and the Diabetes Genetics in Pakistan study (DGP; 821 participants with type 2 diabetes, 1167 without) [3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049> "A case-control collection of people of Punjabi ancestry, predominantly originating from Mirpur, Pakistan, with type 2 diabetes or normal glucose regulation, assembled to investigate genetic susceptibility to diabetes and related glycaemic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21949744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3176767/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were all of Punjabi ancestry, confirmed over three generations, and originated predominantly from the District of Mirpur, Pakistan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000049> "A case-control collection of people of Punjabi ancestry, predominantly originating from Mirpur, Pakistan, with type 2 diabetes or normal glucose regulation, assembled to investigate genetic susceptibility to diabetes and related glycaemic traits.")

