AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24004118") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3951177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In previously reported studies, including the Dutch–Belgian Randomized Lung Cancer Screening Trial (NELSON), more than 20% of participants who underwent low-dose CT screening required a repeat CT, positron-emission tomographic imaging, or a biopsy procedure within 12 months after their first screening low-dose CT because of suspicious or intermediate lung nodules.1,3,29,30") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000058> "A randomised trial cohort of current and former smokers selected from the Dutch and Belgian general population to compare low-dose computed-tomography screening with no screening for reduction of lung-cancer mortality.")
