AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5913637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, the use of electronic record linkage, which automatically updates patient details and grants access to NHS data as far back as 1987, makes GoDARTS a longitudinal cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082> "A cohort of people with type 2 diabetes and non-diabetic controls in Tayside, Scotland, recruiting from 1998 and linking biological samples to longitudinal health records to investigate genetic and environmental determinants of diabetes onset, progression and treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5913637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1998, consenting patients within this electronic database were recruited to the Genetics of DARTS (GoDARTS) study and invited to provide a blood sample for DNA extraction, for research purposes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082> "A cohort of people with type 2 diabetes and non-diabetic controls in Tayside, Scotland, recruiting from 1998 and linking biological samples to longitudinal health records to investigate genetic and environmental determinants of diabetes onset, progression and treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5913637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This gives a current total GoDARTS cohort of 18 306 participants, 10 149 of whom have T2D ( ∼ 44.8% of the DARTS study, representing the diabetic population in Tayside) and 8157 of whom were healthy controls at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082> "A cohort of people with type 2 diabetes and non-diabetic controls in Tayside, Scotland, recruiting from 1998 and linking biological samples to longitudinal health records to investigate genetic and environmental determinants of diabetes onset, progression and treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5913637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This resource was intended to help identify the relative contribution of specific genetic and environmental factors that are associated with disease onset, progression and response to treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000082> "A cohort of people with type 2 diabetes and non-diabetic controls in Tayside, Scotland, recruiting from 1998 and linking biological samples to longitudinal health records to investigate genetic and environmental determinants of diabetes onset, progression and treatment response.")

