AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6124629/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described in the Cohorts Profile published in 2012,4 decades later, participants of both Surveys, mostly living in Edinburgh and the surrounding area (the Lothians) in older age, were invited to participate in the Lothian Birth Cohort (LBC) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000111> "A research programme comprising two cohorts, the Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 and 1936, whose members took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 and 1947 and were recruited in older age, mostly in Edinburgh and the Lothians, for repeated study of cognitive ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6124629/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given the unusual separation in time between the original intelligence test at age 11 and repeat testing in old age, a central contribution of the LBC studies has been to examine intelligence across most of the lifespan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000111> "A research programme comprising two cohorts, the Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 and 1936, whose members took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 and 1947 and were recruited in older age, mostly in Edinburgh and the Lothians, for repeated study of cognitive ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6124629/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LBC studies set out principally to examine the nature and determinants of non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age, and within in older age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000111> "A research programme comprising two cohorts, the Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 and 1936, whose members took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 and 1947 and were recruited in older age, mostly in Edinburgh and the Lothians, for repeated study of cognitive ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6124629/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 (LBC1921) and 1936 (LBC1936) were designed as follow-up studies to the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 (SMS1932) and 1947 (SMS1947), respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000111> "A research programme comprising two cohorts, the Lothian Birth Cohorts of 1921 and 1936, whose members took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Surveys of 1932 and 1947 and were recruited in older age, mostly in Edinburgh and the Lothians, for repeated study of cognitive ageing.")

