AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3181335") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients had a history of a first VT event documented by venography, Doppler ultrasound, angiography and/or ventilation/perfusion lung scan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000113> "A cohort of unrelated patients with documented venous thrombosis recruited at La Timone Hospital in Marseille, France, in 1994–2005, excluding recognised major thrombophilias, for investigation of genetic susceptibility to venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3181335") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MARTHA patients (n=1,592) are unrelated VT patients, mainly of French origin, consecutively recruited at the Thrombophilia center of La Timone hospital (Marseille, France) between January 1994 and October 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000113> "A cohort of unrelated patients with documented venous thrombosis recruited at La Timone Hospital in Marseille, France, in 1994–2005, excluding recognised major thrombophilias, for investigation of genetic susceptibility to venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3181335") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were all free of any chronic conditions and free of any well characterized genetic risk factors including anti-thrombin, protein C or protein S deficiency, homozygosity for FV Leiden or FII 20210A, and lupus anticoagulant.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000113> "A cohort of unrelated patients with documented venous thrombosis recruited at La Timone Hospital in Marseille, France, in 1994–2005, excluding recognised major thrombophilias, for investigation of genetic susceptibility to venous thrombosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000114> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000114>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37821706+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, using ancestry deconvolution and inference of identity-by-descent segments, we inferred ancestral population sizes across Mesoamerican regions over time, unravelling Indigenous, colonial and postcolonial demographic dynamics2-6.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000114> "A biobank of individuals from rural and urban localities across all 32 Mexican states, linking genome-wide genotypes to disease and complex-trait information to investigate population history and genetic and environmental contributions to health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37821706+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To fill this gap, the Mexican Biobank project genotyped 6,057 individuals from 898 rural and urban localities across all 32 states in Mexico at a resolution of 1.8 million genome-wide markers with linked complex trait and disease information creating a valuable nationwide genotype-phenotype database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000114> "A biobank of individuals from rural and urban localities across all 32 Mexican states, linking genome-wide genotypes to disease and complex-trait information to investigate population history and genetic and environmental contributions to health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37821706") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37821706+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We identified genetic and environmental factors associating with trait variation, such as the length of the genome in runs of homozygosity as a predictor for body mass index, triglycerides, glucose and height.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000114> "A biobank of individuals from rural and urban localities across all 32 Mexican states, linking genome-wide genotypes to disease and complex-trait information to investigate population history and genetic and environmental contributions to health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3356921/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among the African Americans in the present study, a subset of 180 cases and 200 controls from the MIRAGE Study and 221 cases and 186 controls from the GenerAAtions Study was included in another recent study24 that evaluated the association of AD with PICALM, CLU, and CR1 SNPs highlighted in the original studies reports.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115> "A cohort of families including siblings discordant for Alzheimer disease, with African-American and white family samples, assembled for genetic investigation through the Multi-Institutional Research on Alzheimer Genetic Epidemiology (MIRAGE) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3356921/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For comparison, we also examined 5 white AD GWAS data sets containing 3568 cases and 6205 controls, namely, the MIRAGE Study white families") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115> "A cohort of families including siblings discordant for Alzheimer disease, with African-American and white family samples, assembled for genetic investigation through the Multi-Institutional Research on Alzheimer Genetic Epidemiology (MIRAGE) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3356921/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One subject group includes participants of the Multi-Institutional Research on Alzheimer Genetic Epidemiology (MIRAGE) Study, which contains primarily discordant sibling pairs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115> "A cohort of families including siblings discordant for Alzheimer disease, with African-American and white family samples, assembled for genetic investigation through the Multi-Institutional Research on Alzheimer Genetic Epidemiology (MIRAGE) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159054") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22159054+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed a genome-wide set of 2.5 million imputed markers to evaluate the genetic basis of AD in an African American population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000115> "A cohort of families including siblings discordant for Alzheimer disease, with African-American and white family samples, assembled for genetic investigation through the Multi-Institutional Research on Alzheimer Genetic Epidemiology (MIRAGE) programme.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature08192/MediaObjects/41586_2009_BFnature08192_MOESM270_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Self‐reported European ancestry (EA) and African American (AA) unrelated adult cases with DSM‐IIIR (SGI study) or DSM‐IV (MGS1, MGS2 studies) schizophrenia (SZ) or schizoaffective disorder (SA) were collected under institutional review board‐approved protocols in three studies") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116> "A consortium of schizophrenia case-control collections from three National Institute of Mental Health repository studies, including people of European and African-American ancestry, combining genetic data to identify schizophrenia-susceptibility variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2775422/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To search for common schizophrenia susceptibility variants, we carried out a GWAS in cases from three methodologically similar National Institute of Mental Health repository-based studies, and screened controls from the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116> "A consortium of schizophrenia case-control collections from three National Institute of Mental Health repository studies, including people of European and African-American ancestry, combining genetic data to identify schizophrenia-susceptibility variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19571809+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We carried out a genome-wide association study of common SNPs in the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia (MGS) case-control sample, and then a meta-analysis of data from the MGS, International Schizophrenia Consortium and SGENE data sets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116> "A consortium of schizophrenia case-control collections from three National Institute of Mental Health repository studies, including people of European and African-American ancestry, combining genetic data to identify schizophrenia-susceptibility variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19571809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2775422/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because the frequencies of tag SNPs and disease susceptibility alleles can vary across populations, we carried out a primary analysis of the larger MGS European-ancestry sample (2,681 cases, 2,653 controls) and then additional analyses of the African American sample (1,286 cases, 973 controls) and of both of these samples combined, to test the hypothesis that there are alleles that influence susceptibility in both populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000116> "A consortium of schizophrenia case-control collections from three National Institute of Mental Health repository studies, including people of European and African-American ancestry, combining genetic data to identify schizophrenia-susceptibility variants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000117> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000117>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19520994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19520994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19520994+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up data were collected in 43 cohorts in 18 populations in 8 European countries surveyed for cardiovascular risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000117> "A project combining prospective population cohorts from European countries to examine cardiovascular risk factors and their associations with subsequent stroke and other cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19520994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19520994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19520994+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the framework of the MOnica Risk, Genetics, Archiving and Monograph (MORGAM) Project, the variations in impact of classical risk factors of stroke by population, sex, and age were analyzed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000117> "A project combining prospective population cohorts from European countries to examine cardiovascular risk factors and their associations with subsequent stroke and other cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19520994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22848412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3405046/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MORGAM project comprises >128,000 men and women from 57 European (mainly white Caucasian) cohorts which were harmonised and prospectively followed up for incident coronary heart disease events [15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000117> "A project combining prospective population cohorts from European countries to examine cardiovascular risk factors and their associations with subsequent stroke and other cardiovascular events.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000118> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000118>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2807705+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Its objective is to measure trends in cardiovascular mortality and morbidity and to assess the extent to which these trends are related to changes in risk factor levels and/or medical care, measured at the same time in defined communities in different countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000118> "A project combining standardised cardiovascular surveillance in populations aged 35–64 years across 26 countries in Europe, North America and the Western Pacific to relate changes in mortality and morbidity to risk factors and medical care.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2807705+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHO MONICA Project is a multicentre international collaborative project coordinated by the World Health Organization.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000118> "A project combining standardised cardiovascular surveillance in populations aged 35–64 years across 26 countries in Europe, North America and the Western Pacific to relate changes in mortality and morbidity to risk factors and medical care.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2807705") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2807705+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thirty-nine collaborating centres from 26 countries of Europe, North America, and the Western Pacific collaborate in this project, using a standardized protocol and covering a population of approximately 10 million men and women aged 35-64.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000118> "A project combining standardised cardiovascular surveillance in populations aged 35–64 years across 26 countries in Europe, North America and the Western Pacific to relate changes in mortality and morbidity to risk factors and medical care.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12397006+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Approximately 38% of the cohort will be White, 28% African-American, 23% Hispanic, and 11% Asian (of Chinese descent).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119> "A cohort of men and women aged 45–84 years from six United States centres, including White, African-American, Hispanic and Chinese-ancestry participants, established in 2000 to investigate the prevalence, determinants and progression of subclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12397006+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Multi-Ethnic Study of Atherosclerosis was initiated in July 2000 to investigate the prevalence, correlates, and progression of subclinical cardiovascular disease (CVD) in a population-based sample of 6,500 men and women aged 45-84 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119> "A cohort of men and women aged 45–84 years from six United States centres, including White, African-American, Hispanic and Chinese-ancestry participants, established in 2000 to investigate the prevalence, determinants and progression of subclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12397006") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12397006+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort will be selected from six US field centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000119> "A cohort of men and women aged 45–84 years from six United States centres, including White, African-American, Hispanic and Chinese-ancestry participants, established in 2000 to investigate the prevalence, determinants and progression of subclinical cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6927206/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case subjects had DSM-III-R diagnoses of schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder (probands had schizophrenia), which cosegregate in families (20) and are difficult to differentiate reliably (21).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120> "A project combining seven collections of families with multiple members affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, including European-ancestry and admixed families from research sites in Europe, Australia and the United States, to investigate common and rare genetic contributions to schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6927206/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample (Table 1) includes seven subsamples that were recruited for linkage studies (8–15) and subsequently combined (16–19), excluding families from the National Institute of Mental Health’s Schizophrenia Genetics Initiative because a previous GWAS studied the probands (2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120> "A project combining seven collections of families with multiple members affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, including European-ancestry and admixed families from research sites in Europe, Australia and the United States, to investigate common and rare genetic contributions to schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22885689+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The authors used a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of multiply affected families to investigate the association of schizophrenia to common single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) and rare copy number variants (CNVs).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120> "A project combining seven collections of families with multiple members affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, including European-ancestry and admixed families from research sites in Europe, Australia and the United States, to investigate common and rare genetic contributions to schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22885689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6927206/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on principal components analysis of 55,010 autosomal SNPs with low pairwise linkage disequilibrium (LD), families were divided into six ancestry groups (Table 1; see also Figure S1 in the data supplement that accompanies the online edition of this article): European, Mediterranean (primarily Sephardic Jewish), and four with varying degrees of African or South Indian admixture (Reunion Island).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000120> "A project combining seven collections of families with multiple members affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, including European-ancestry and admixed families from research sites in Europe, Australia and the United States, to investigate common and rare genetic contributions to schizophrenia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10695593+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As sufficient numbers of cancer cases are identified through surveillance of the cohort, dietary and other hypotheses will be tested in prospective analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121> "A cohort of adults aged 45–75 years from multiple ethnic groups in Hawaii and California, principally Los Angeles County, recruited during 1993–1996 and followed prospectively to investigate diet and other determinants of cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10695593+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1993 to 1996, participants entered the cohort by completing a 26-page, self-administered mail questionnaire that elicited a quantitative food frequency history, along with demographic and other information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121> "A cohort of adults aged 45–75 years from multiple ethnic groups in Hawaii and California, principally Los Angeles County, recruited during 1993–1996 and followed prospectively to investigate diet and other determinants of cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10695593+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The authors describe the design and implementation of a large multiethnic cohort established to study diet and cancer in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121> "A cohort of adults aged 45–75 years from multiple ethnic groups in Hawaii and California, principally Los Angeles County, recruited during 1993–1996 and followed prospectively to investigate diet and other determinants of cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10695593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10695593+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort consists of 215,251 adult men and women (age 45-75 years at baseline) living in Hawaii and in California (primarily Los Angeles County) with the following ethnic distribution: African-American (16.3%), Latino (22.0%), Japanese-American (26.4%), Native Hawaiian (6.5%), White (22.9%), and other ancestry (5.8%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000121> "A cohort of adults aged 45–75 years from multiple ethnic groups in Hawaii and California, principally Los Angeles County, recruited during 1993–1996 and followed prospectively to investigate diet and other determinants of cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2726929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between March 1999 and September 2004, consecutive patients aged <70 years with a first episode of deep venous thrombosis (leg or arm) or pulmonary embolism were included from the files of six participating anticoagulation clinics in the Netherlands (Amersfoort, Amsterdam, The Hague, Leiden, Rotterdam, and Utrecht).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122> "A case-control collection of patients younger than 70 with a first deep-vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism, recruited through six Dutch anticoagulation clinics in 1999–2004, with partner and population controls, for investigation of environmental and genetic thrombosis risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2726929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 2002 until September 2004, additional controls were recruited by random digit dialling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122> "A case-control collection of patients younger than 70 with a first deep-vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism, recruited through six Dutch anticoagulation clinics in 1999–2004, with partner and population controls, for investigation of environmental and genetic thrombosis risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2726929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Partners of patients <70 years old were invited to participate as controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122> "A case-control collection of patients younger than 70 with a first deep-vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism, recruited through six Dutch anticoagulation clinics in 1999–2004, with partner and population controls, for investigation of environmental and genetic thrombosis risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19679614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2726929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This analysis was performed using data from the MEGA study (multiple environmental and genetic assessment of risk factors for venous thrombosis-study), a large, population based, case-control study on risk factors for venous thrombosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000122> "A case-control collection of patients younger than 70 with a first deep-vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism, recruited through six Dutch anticoagulation clinics in 1999–2004, with partner and population controls, for investigation of environmental and genetic thrombosis risk factors.")

