# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000145> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000145>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3510312/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples of the Psoriasis/Arthritis Genetics Extension (PAGE) and the Genetic Analysis of Psoriasis Consortium (GAPC) datasets (Supplementary Table 1 and 2) were collected from subjects of European Caucasian descent at the participating institutions after obtaining informed consent in adherence with the Declaration of Helsinki Principles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000145> "A case-control collection of people of European ancestry with psoriasis and unaffected controls recruited at participating institutions for genetic analysis using the Immunochip.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3510312/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We combined three existing GWAS datasets (hereafter referred to as Kiel3, CASP4 and WTCCC25) with two independent European-descent case-control datasets genotyped on the Immunochip: the Psoriasis Association Genetics Extension (PAGE: 3,580 cases and 5,902 controls)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000145> "A case-control collection of people of European ancestry with psoriasis and unaffected controls recruited at participating institutions for genetic analysis using the Immunochip.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20955924+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Psychiatric GWAS Consortium was founded with the aim of conducting statistically rigorous and comprehensive GWAS meta-analyses for five major psychiatric disorders: ADHD, autism, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder, and schizophrenia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies that combines data on attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, autism, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder and schizophrenia through meta-analysis to investigate genetic susceptibility to psychiatric disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2991765/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the PGC, raw individual-level and de-identified phenotype and genotype data from each study were uploaded to a high performance computing cluster and processed through a robust and comprehensive quality control pipeline conforming to best-practice protocols in order to minimize chances of false positive results (e.g., due to population stratification).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies that combines data on attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, autism, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder and schizophrenia through meta-analysis to investigate genetic susceptibility to psychiatric disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20955924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2991765/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The initial iteration of the PGC had four scientific aims, which were designed to facilitate the over-arching scientific goal of attempting to identify secure associations of comprehensive assessment of common genetic variation with five critically important psychiatric diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000146> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies that combines data on attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, autism, bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder and schizophrenia through meta-analysis to investigate genetic susceptibility to psychiatric disorders.")

