AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4554719/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four lung cancer GWAS in the International Lung Cancer Consortium were used to identify variants associated with both lung cancer and first-degree family history of lung cancer: the Toronto study [Hung et al., 2008; McKay et al., 2008], the Central Europe study [Hung et al., 2008], the MD Anderson study [Amos et al., 2008], and the Germany study [Landi et al., 2009; Sauter et al., 2008].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000165> "A German lung cancer case-control genome-wide association sample, combining cases from the LUng Cancer in the Young (LUCY) study of 2000-2008 and a Heidelberg case-control study of 1997-2007 with population controls from the KORA surveys of 1990-1998, contributed to the International Lung Cancer Consortium as its Germany study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4554719/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HMGU Germany 2000–2008 (LUCY) Population CC 504 484 Illumina HumanHap550 1990–1998 (KORA) 1997–2007 (Heidelberg)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000165> "A German lung cancer case-control genome-wide association sample, combining cases from the LUng Cancer in the Young (LUCY) study of 2000-2008 and a Heidelberg case-control study of 1997-2007 with population controls from the KORA surveys of 1990-1998, contributed to the International Lung Cancer Consortium as its Germany study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.downstate.edu/research/centers-departments/henri-begleiter-neurodynamics-laboratory/_documents/2012-Hartz-IncreasedgeneticvulnerabilitytosmokingatCHRNA5inearly-onsetsmokers-Supplement.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LUCY (LUng Cancer in the Young) is an multicenter study with 31 recruiting hospitals in Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000165> "A German lung cancer case-control genome-wide association sample, combining cases from the LUng Cancer in the Young (LUCY) study of 2000-2008 and a Heidelberg case-control study of 1997-2007 with population controls from the KORA surveys of 1990-1998, contributed to the International Lung Cancer Consortium as its Germany study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.downstate.edu/research/centers-departments/henri-begleiter-neurodynamics-laboratory/_documents/2012-Hartz-IncreasedgeneticvulnerabilitytosmokingatCHRNA5inearly-onsetsmokers-Supplement.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "was made up of three independent German studies as detailed below: In total 506 incident lung cancer cases (LUCY-study: n=305, Heidelberg lung cancer case-control study: n=201) were compared to 480 popula-tion controls (KORA surveys KORA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000165> "A German lung cancer case-control genome-wide association sample, combining cases from the LUng Cancer in the Young (LUCY) study of 2000-2008 and a Heidelberg case-control study of 1997-2007 with population controls from the KORA surveys of 1990-1998, contributed to the International Lung Cancer Consortium as its Germany study.")

