AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22253318+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK's largest registry of adult twins, or TwinsUK Registry, started in 1992 and encompasses about 12000 volunteer twins from all over the United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000175> "A registry of volunteer adult twins from across the United Kingdom, established in 1992, with repeated clinical assessments, questionnaires and molecular data to investigate genetic and environmental contributions to ageing and complex disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22253318+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The most recent follow-up visit, known as Healthy Ageing Twin Study (HATS), involved 3125 female twins aged >40 years with at least one previous clinical assessment to enable inspection of longitudinal changes in ageing traits and their genetic and environmental components.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000175> "A registry of volunteer adult twins from across the United Kingdom, established in 1992, with repeated clinical assessments, questionnaires and molecular data to investigate genetic and environmental contributions to ageing and complex disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31526404") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31526404+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Such collection methods have resulted in very detailed longitudinal clinical, biochemical, behavioral, dietary and socioeconomic cohort characterization; it provides a multidisciplinary platform for the study of complex disease during the adult life course, including the process of healthy aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000175> "A registry of volunteer adult twins from across the United Kingdom, established in 1992, with repeated clinical assessments, questionnaires and molecular data to investigate genetic and environmental contributions to ageing and complex disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22253318") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31526404") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31526404+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The major strength of TwinsUK is the availability of several 'omic' technologies for a range of sample types from participants, which includes genomewide scans of single-nucleotide variants, next-generation sequencing, metabolomic profiles, microbiomics, exome sequencing, epigenetic markers, gene expression arrays, RNA sequencing and telomere length measures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000175> "A registry of volunteer adult twins from across the United Kingdom, established in 1992, with repeated clinical assessments, questionnaires and molecular data to investigate genetic and environmental contributions to ageing and complex disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4380465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 500,000 participants were assessed between 2006 and 2010 in 22 assessment centres throughout the UK") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176> "A cohort of adults aged 40–69 recruited across the United Kingdom in 2006–2010, with biological samples, extensive phenotyping and prospective health follow-up, established to investigate genetic and nongenetic determinants of diseases of middle and older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4380465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The age range for inclusion of 40–69 years represented a pragmatic compromise between participants being old enough for there to be sufficient incident health outcomes during the early years of follow-up and young enough for the initial assessment to occur before incipient disease had a material impact on exposures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176> "A cohort of adults aged 40–69 recruited across the United Kingdom in 2006–2010, with biological samples, extensive phenotyping and prospective health follow-up, established to investigate genetic and nongenetic determinants of diseases of middle and older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4380465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The assessment visit comprised electronic signed consent; a self-completed touch-screen questionnaire; brief computer-assisted interview; physical and functional measures; and collection of blood, urine, and saliva (Table 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176> "A cohort of adults aged 40–69 recruited across the United Kingdom in 2006–2010, with biological samples, extensive phenotyping and prospective health follow-up, established to investigate genetic and nongenetic determinants of diseases of middle and older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25826379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4380465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK (United Kingdom) Biobank is a very large, population-based prospective study, established to allow detailed investigations of the genetic and nongenetic determinants of the diseases of middle and old age [5,6].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000176> "A cohort of adults aged 40–69 recruited across the United Kingdom in 2006–2010, with biological samples, extensive phenotyping and prospective health follow-up, established to investigate genetic and nongenetic determinants of diseases of middle and older age.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals were confirmed to be neuropathologically normal by a consultant neuropathologist using histology performed on sections prepared from paraffin-embedded brain tissue blocks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177> "A consortium of brain-tissue collections from neuropathologically normal donors in Edinburgh, United Kingdom, and the United States, combining genotypes and expression measurements across brain regions to investigate genetic regulation of brain gene expression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Central nervous system (CNS) tissues originating from 134 control individuals was collected by the Medical Research Council (MRC) Sudden Death Brain and Tissue Bank, Edinburgh, UK (Millar et al. 2007), and the Sun Health Research Institute (SHRI) an affiliate of Sun Health Corporation, USA (Beach et al. 2008).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177> "A consortium of brain-tissue collections from neuropathologically normal donors in Edinburgh, United Kingdom, and the United States, combining genotypes and expression measurements across brain regions to investigate genetic regulation of brain gene expression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From each individual we analyzed up to 10 brain regions:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177> "A consortium of brain-tissue collections from neuropathologically normal donors in Edinburgh, United Kingdom, and the United States, combining genotypes and expression measurements across brain regions to investigate genetic regulation of brain gene expression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ukbec.wordpress.com/materials-methods/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The QTL analysis was run for each expression profile (either exon-level or gene-level) against every genetic marker (either SNP or indel) in MatrixEQTL (Shabalin, 2012).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000177> "A consortium of brain-tissue collections from neuropathologically normal donors in Edinburgh, United Kingdom, and the United States, combining genotypes and expression measurements across brain regions to investigate genetic regulation of brain gene expression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10737392+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All children known to be suffering from one or other type of the disease over periods of 4-5 years have been included, and control children matched for sex, age and area of residence have been selected at random from population registers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178> "A case-control collection of children with cancer and controls matched by sex, age and residence throughout England, Scotland and Wales during 1991–1998, assembled to investigate causes of childhood cancer using interviews, records, exposure measurements and biological samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10737392+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An investigation into the possible causes of childhood cancer has been carried out throughout England, Scotland and Wales over the period 1991-1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178> "A case-control collection of children with cancer and controls matched by sex, age and residence throughout England, Scotland and Wales during 1991–1998, assembled to investigate causes of childhood cancer using interviews, records, exposure measurements and biological samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10737392+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed accounts are given of the nature of the information obtained in sections describing the general methodology of the study, the measurement of exposure to ionizing and non-ionizing radiation, the classification of solid tumours and leukaemias, and the biological material available for genetic analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178> "A case-control collection of children with cancer and controls matched by sex, age and residence throughout England, Scotland and Wales during 1991–1998, assembled to investigate causes of childhood cancer using interviews, records, exposure measurements and biological samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10737392") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10737392+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information about both groups of children (with and without cancer) has been obtained from parental questionnaires, general practitioners' and hospital records, and from measurement of the extent of exposure to radon gas, terrestrial gamma radiation, and electric and magnetic fields.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000178> "A case-control collection of children with cancer and controls matched by sex, age and residence throughout England, Scotland and Wales during 1991–1998, assembled to investigate causes of childhood cancer using interviews, records, exposure measurements and biological samples.")

