AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11174331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11174331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11174331+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients are followed up at 6 months after hospital discharge to identify recurrent coronary events, use of various medications, and mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000192> "A registry of patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndromes at centres across multiple countries, followed prospectively during admission and after discharge to compare treatment practices, clinical characteristics and outcomes and improve care.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11174331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11174331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11174331+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of GRACE is to improve the quality of care for patients with ACS by describing differences in, and relationships between, patient characteristics, treatment practices, and in-hospital and postdischarge outcomes at hospitals around the world.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000192> "A registry of patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndromes at centres across multiple countries, followed prospectively during admission and after discharge to compare treatment practices, clinical characteristics and outcomes and improve care.")

