AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31953381") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6969170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this study we used three independent Dutch cohorts: (1) a general population cohort, LifeLines-DEEP, consisting of 1539 individuals; (2) 544 patients with IBD from the 1000 IBD cohort of the University Medical Center of Groningen (UMCG); and (3) an IBS case–control cohort with 313 participants from Maastricht University Medical Center + (MUMC + )37–39.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000293> "A collection of irritable bowel syndrome cases and controls from studies at Maastricht University Medical Centre, the Netherlands, whose gut microbiomes were characterised by metagenomic sequencing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001924") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Metagenomic sequencing of the human gut in Maastricht IBS studies, cases and controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000293> "A collection of irritable bowel syndrome cases and controls from studies at Maastricht University Medical Centre, the Netherlands, whose gut microbiomes were characterised by metagenomic sequencing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001924") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00763-1/MediaObjects/41588_2020_763_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At present, it includes 520 subjects with a clinical diagnosis of IBS according to the Rome III criteria (from primary-tertiary care) and 220 age- and gender-matched healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000293> "A collection of irritable bowel syndrome cases and controls from studies at Maastricht University Medical Centre, the Netherlands, whose gut microbiomes were characterised by metagenomic sequencing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000629") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19079050") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3758999") Annotation(rdfs:comment "building a global network for sharing data on the genomic epidemiology of malaria; collecting DNA and clinical data from individuals with different phenotypes of malaria; characterizing genetic variation in populations in malaria-endemic regions") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294> "An international network of investigators that assembles samples and data from malaria-endemic countries in Africa, Asia and Oceania to study the genomic epidemiology of malaria, including a low-coverage whole-genome sequence reference set of African ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000629") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19079050") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19079050+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network (MalariaGEN) is now working to overcome these obstacles, using a consortial approach that brings together researchers from 21 countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294> "An international network of investigators that assembles samples and data from malaria-endemic countries in Africa, Asia and Oceania to study the genomic epidemiology of malaria, including a low-coverage whole-genome sequence reference set of African ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000629") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6914791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, individuals were sampled from 12 study sites, including 10 in sub-Saharan Africa and the others in Vietnam and Papua New Guinea (PNG; Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294> "An international network of investigators that assembles samples and data from malaria-endemic countries in Africa, Asia and Oceania to study the genomic epidemiology of malaria, including a low-coverage whole-genome sequence reference set of African ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000629") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6914791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address this, we sequenced the genomes of 773 individuals from ten ethnic groups in east and west Africa (specifically from the Gambia, Burkina Faso, Cameroon and Tanzania), including 207 family trios (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000294> "An international network of investigators that assembles samples and data from malaria-endemic countries in Africa, Asia and Oceania to study the genomic epidemiology of malaria, including a low-coverage whole-genome sequence reference set of African ethnic groups.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000295> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000295>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001006518") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37101199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37101199+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we report an analysis of 492 breast cancer samples from the Malaysian Breast Cancer cohort where we examined the impact of TP53 somatic mutations in relation to PAM50 subtypes by comparing whole exome and transcriptome data from tumours with mutant and wild-type TP53.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000295> "A hospital-based cohort of breast cancer patients in Malaysia whose tumours, including triple-negative cancers, have been characterised by exome and RNA sequencing to develop classifiers such as a gene signature for homologous recombination deficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001006518") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38649964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11035138/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MyBrCa tumour cohort comprises of 934 female breast cancer patients of self-reported Malaysian nationality who were sequentially recruited from two Malaysian hospitals, Subang Jaya Medical Centre and Universiti Malaya Medical Centre.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000295> "A hospital-based cohort of breast cancer patients in Malaysia whose tumours, including triple-negative cancers, have been characterised by exome and RNA sequencing to develop classifiers such as a gene signature for homologous recombination deficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001006518") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001006518") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed a gene expression-based classifier for homologous recombination deficiency (HRD) in breast cancer patients using WES and RNA-seq data obtained from 94 TNBC samples from a Malaysian hospital-based cohort (MyBrCa).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000295> "A hospital-based cohort of breast cancer patients in Malaysia whose tumours, including triple-negative cancers, have been characterised by exome and RNA sequencing to develop classifiers such as a gene signature for homologous recombination deficiency.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000936") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8429286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8429286+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initially food intake, heredity, socio-economic factors, life-style pattern, occupational situation, previous and current diseases, symptoms and medications, will be determined.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296> "A population-based prospective cohort of about 30,000 residents of Malmö, Sweden, born 1923–1950 and recruited during 1991–1996 with dietary, lifestyle, clinical and genetic data to investigate diet, cancer and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000936") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9004064/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A random selection from the MDC were invited 1991–1994 for further clinical testing and collection of blood samples, the so-called cardiovascular subcohort (MDC-CC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296> "A population-based prospective cohort of about 30,000 residents of Malmö, Sweden, born 1923–1950 and recruited during 1991–1996 with dietary, lifestyle, clinical and genetic data to investigate diet, cancer and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000936") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9004064/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All residents in Malmö, Sweden born between 1923 and 1950 without exclusions were invited to an initial screening 1991–1996 and 30,446 participated [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296> "A population-based prospective cohort of about 30,000 residents of Malmö, Sweden, born 1923–1950 and recruited during 1991–1996 with dietary, lifestyle, clinical and genetic data to investigate diet, cancer and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000936") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9004064/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Malmö Diet and Cancer (MDC) cohort is a population-based cohort originally created to study if dietary habits were associated with cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000296> "A population-based prospective cohort of about 30,000 residents of Malmö, Sweden, born 1923–1950 and recruited during 1991–1996 with dietary, lifestyle, clinical and genetic data to investigate diet, cancer and cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26970340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5248602/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MeDALL has linked epidemiological, clinical and basic research using a stepwise, large‐scale and integrative approach: MeDALL data of precisely phenotyped children followed in 14 birth cohorts spread across Europe were combined with systems biology (omics, IgE measurement using microarrays) and environmental data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project that combines European birth cohorts, including INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA, to investigate the mechanisms of the development of allergy through harmonised phenotypes and epigenetic and other omic measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26970340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5248602/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MeDALL knowledge base integrates historical and newly collected data from around 44 000 participants on 398 clinical and phenotypic attributes (harmonized from 7495 individual cohort variables) and 160 different follow‐ups at 25 different time points between pregnancy and age 20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project that combines European birth cohorts, including INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA, to investigate the mechanisms of the development of allergy through harmonised phenotypes and epigenetic and other omic measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6071724/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work was supported by Mechanisms of the Development of Allergy (MeDALL), a collaborative project done within the European Union under the Health Cooperation Work Program of the seventh Framework program (grant no. 261357).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project that combines European birth cohorts, including INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA, to investigate the mechanisms of the development of allergy through harmonised phenotypes and epigenetic and other omic measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001002169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5217260/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected cord blood and peripheral blood samples from 632 children from four European birth cohorts: INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000297> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project that combines European birth cohorts, including INMA, EDEN, BAMSE and PIAMA, to investigate the mechanisms of the development of allergy through harmonised phenotypes and epigenetic and other omic measurements.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353151") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6336775/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Medical Genome Reference Bank (MGRB) has conducted WGS of 4000 healthy older adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298> "A whole-genome sequence resource of 4,000 healthy individuals aged 60 to 95 with no history of cancer, cardiovascular disease or dementia, recruited from two Australian community-based cohorts to serve as a reference population depleted of pathogenic alleles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353151") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30353151+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Aged and healthy populations are more likely to be selectively depleted of pathogenic alleles and therefore particularly suitable as a reference population for the major diseases of clinical and public health importance.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298> "A whole-genome sequence resource of 4,000 healthy individuals aged 60 to 95 with no history of cancer, cardiovascular disease or dementia, recruited from two Australian community-based cohorts to serve as a reference population depleted of pathogenic alleles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MGRB comprises 4,000 healthy, older individuals with no reported history of cancer, cardiovascular disease or dementia, recruited from two Australian community based cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298> "A whole-genome sequence resource of 4,000 healthy individuals aged 60 to 95 with no history of cancer, cardiovascular disease or dementia, recruited from two Australian community-based cohorts to serve as a reference population depleted of pathogenic alleles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001003511") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MGRB will measure genome wide genetic variation in 4,000 individuals, mostly of European decent, aged 60 to 95 years (mean age 75 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000298> "A whole-genome sequence resource of 4,000 healthy individuals aged 60 to 95 with no history of cancer, cardiovascular disease or dementia, recruited from two Australian community-based cohorts to serve as a reference population depleted of pathogenic alleles.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000299> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000299>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001004812") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36705549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9881451/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we describe the dataset generated by the MESOMICS project that collected more than 100 MPM tumors with extensive clinical, epidemiologic, and morphologic annotations and profiled their genome, transcriptome, and epigenome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000299> "A collection of malignant pleural mesothelioma samples from the French MESOMICS project, characterised by whole-genome sequencing, RNA sequencing and methylation arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001004812") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36705549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9881451/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the context of the MESOMICS project, we have performed the most comprehensive molecular characterization of MPM to date, with the underlying dataset made of the largest whole-genome sequencing series yet reported, together with transcriptome sequencing and methylation arrays for 120 MPM patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000299> "A collection of malignant pleural mesothelioma samples from the French MESOMICS project, characterised by whole-genome sequencing, RNA sequencing and methylation arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001004812") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36705549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9881451/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples used in this study belong to the French MESOBANK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000299> "A collection of malignant pleural mesothelioma samples from the French MESOMICS project, characterised by whole-genome sequencing, RNA sequencing and methylation arrays.")

