# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3554384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC)-Potsdam is part of the ongoing multicenter EPIC study and comprises 27,548 participants from the general population in the area of Potsdam in eastern Germany who were mainly 35–65 years of age at time of recruitment between 1994 and 1998 (17).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the start of the study in 1994, the women were 35 to 64 years old and the men were 40 to 64 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1994 and 1998, potential study participants were drawn from the population registers of Potsdam and the surrounding area using a random procedure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPIC was developed to examine the relationships between diet, nutritional status, lifestyle and environmental factors, as well as the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases lilke type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (EPIC)-Potsdam Study is a population-based prospective cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23043162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.dife.de/en/research/cooperations/epic-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There are two study centres in Germany: the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) supervises the EPIC-Heidelberg cohort and the DIfE is participating in the cohort with the EPIC-Potsdam Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000387> "A population-based prospective cohort of 27,548 adults from Potsdam and the surrounding area in eastern Germany, drawn at random from the population registers and recruited in 1994–1998, when the women were 35–64 and the men 40–64 years old; one of the two German centres of the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition (the other is EPIC-Heidelberg), run by the German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke to study diet, nutritional status and lifestyle in relation to the incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20609343+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(2) describe the positive and negative consequences of immigration and acculturation of Hispanics/Latinos to the mainstream United States life-styles, environment and health care opportunities") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20609343+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HCHS/SOL will recruit 16,000 men and women who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, 18 to 74 years of age, from a random sample of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami, and San Diego.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20609343+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hispanic Community Health Study (HCHS)/Study of Latinos (SOL) is a comprehensive multicenter community based cohort study of Hispanics/Latinos in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20609343+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study includes research in the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, kidney and liver function, diabetes, cognitive function, dental conditions, and hearing disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC11751521/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 16,415 participants of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban, and Central and South American background aged 18–74 years were recruited from four U.S. cities between 2008 and 2011: Bronx, NY; Chicago, IL; Miami, FL; and San Diego, CA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20609343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39644095") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC11751521/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Households were selected via two-stage sampling within census block groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000388> "A multicentre community-based cohort of 16,415 men and women aged 18–74 who self-identify as Hispanic or Latino, of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Dominican, Cuban and Central and South American background, recruited in 2008–2011 through two-stage random sampling of households in defined communities in the Bronx, Chicago, Miami and San Diego in the United States, to study the prevalence of and risk factors for heart, lung, blood and sleep disorders, diabetes, kidney and liver function and other chronic conditions, and the health effects of immigration and acculturation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18714779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2542953") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Residents of the Western Australian town of Busselton underwent investigation with a home sleep apnea monitoring device (MESAM IV).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3852572/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Busselton Shire has been the scene of repeated cross-sectional health surveys since 1966 although there have been only 2 major surveys since 1990 in 1994–95 and 2005–08.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3852572/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shire of Busselton is a coastal community in the South-West of Western Australia with a relatively stable population of predominantly European descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9170690/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the discovery cohort (n = 4492) were all participants of the 1994/95 survey of the long-running epidemiological study, the BHS, for whom genome-wide SNP data, extensive longitudinal phenotype data, and blood serum were available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9170690/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BHS is a community-based study in Western Australia that includes both related and unrelated individuals (predominantly of European ancestry) and has been described in more detail elsewhere46–48.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24099269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35668104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://bpmri.org.au/about-us.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study comprises a series of major cross‑sectional and longitudinal cohorts, including: Historic repeated whole community health surveys (1966-1990s) Respiratory, metabolic and sleep‑related studies (1990s-present)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000389> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of residents of the town and Shire of Busselton in south-western Western Australia, surveyed since 1966 and including related and unrelated individuals of predominantly European ancestry, whose 1994/95 follow-up provided blood samples for genetic studies of cardiovascular, respiratory and metabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish Infrastructure for Medical Population-Based Life-Course and Environmental Research (SIMPLER; https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en) includes data from two large, ongoing population-based studies: the Cohort of Swedish Men (COSM) and the Swedish Mammography Cohort (SMC)58.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current analysis is based on a subsample selected randomly from these studies who were invited for clinical examination with genotype and gut microbiome data: SIMPLER-Västmanland (SIMPLER-V) and SIMPLER-Uppsala (SIMPLER-U).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en/about-us") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish Research Council classified SIMPLER as a national infrastructure in 2014, and has provided financing since 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en/about-us") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of the infrastructure SIMPLER is to provide national and international researchers with data for research about dietary and lifestyle factors as well as genetics, and how they affect our health, particularly in the latter part in life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en/about-us") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two subgroups have also visited the research clinics in Uppsala and Västerås for biometric measurements and sampling, and they create the subcohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.simpler4health.se/w/sh/en/researchers") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts were established more than 30 years ago for women and over 20 years ago for men, and participants have been followed with repeated assessments of exposures over time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000390> "A Swedish research infrastructure combining two large ongoing population-based cohorts, the Cohort of Swedish Men and the Swedish Mammography Cohort, whose randomly selected subsamples from Västmanland and Uppsala were clinically examined with genotyping and biosampling for life-course studies of health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744991/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects are recruited and examinations performed at six Swedish university hospitals (Gothenburg, Linköping, Malmö/Lund, Stockholm, Umeå and Uppsala), each site recruiting 5000 individuals from the respective municipality areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26096600+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish CArdioPulmonarybioImage Study (SCAPIS) combines the use of new imaging technologies, advances in large-scale 'omics' and epidemiological analyses to extensively characterize a Swedish cohort of 30 000 men and women aged between 50 and 64 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26096600+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The information obtained will be used to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and optimize the ability to study disease mechanisms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11958696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2013 and 2018, 30,154 subjects aged 50–64 were randomly recruited from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11958696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish CArdioPulmonary bioImage Study (SCAPIS) is a prospective, population-based observational study with 30,154 individuals aged 50–64 years13,14.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26096600") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40164586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12931-026-03853-6") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish CArdioPulmonary bioImage Study (SCAPIS) (http://scapis.org/) is a major collaborative national project in Sweden to study mortality and morbidity from cardiovascular disease, pulmonary disease and related metabolic disorders [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000391> "A national multicentre population-based cohort of 30,154 Swedish men and women aged 50–64, randomly recruited in 2013–2018 from the national population register in six areas adjacent to six Swedish university hospitals and characterised with imaging, large-scale omics and epidemiological data to improve risk prediction of cardiopulmonary diseases and study their mechanisms.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7847466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children (G2) and grandchildren (G3) to index individuals in G1 are recruited, using official register information from the Swedish Tax Agency.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7847466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Malmö Offspring Study that started in 2013, we have so far been able to examine about 4700 subjects (18–71 years) representing children and grandchildren of index subjects from the first generation, examined in the Malmö Diet Cancer Study during 1991 to 1996.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7847466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Invitations are sent by mail and followed up by phone calls following full ethical approval of the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7847466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study participants of MOS consists of invited adult children and grandchildren to participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study—Cardiovascular Cohort (MDCS-CC, n = 6103), which is a random, deeply phenotyped subpopulation of the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study (MDCS) [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7847466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will provide extensive genotyping and phenotyping including cardiovascular and respiratory function, as well as markers of glucose metabolism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33222051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41688638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12987725/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection in MOS began in 2013 and included 4,721 participants by 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000392> "A family-based cohort of the adult children and grandchildren of participants in the Malmö Diet and Cancer Study–Cardiovascular Cohort in Malmö, Sweden, identified from Swedish Tax Agency registers and invited by mail, and examined from 2013 (4,721 participants aged 18–71 by 2020) with genotyping and cardiovascular, respiratory, metabolic, cognitive, dietary and gut and oral microbiota phenotyping, to study family traits of chronic disease across three generations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28119442+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Extensive genotyping and exome sequencing have been performed for essentially all METSIM participants, and >2,000 METSIM participants have been whole-genome sequenced.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28119442+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our ongoing follow-up study, we have, to date, reexamined 6,496 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28119442+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Metabolic Syndrome in Men (METSIM) study is a population-based study including 10,197 Finnish men examined in 2005-2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28119442+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The protocol includes a detailed phenotyping of the participants, an oral glucose tolerance test, fasting laboratory measurements including proton NMR measurements, mass spectometry metabolomics, adipose tissue biopsies from 1,400 participants, and a stool sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960770/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we do so, reporting genome-wide association study (GWAS) results for 1391 plasma metabolites (Metabolon platform) in 6136 participants in METSIM, a study of middle-aged and older men recruited from a single site in late-settlement northeast Finland3, who were part of our previous study2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28119442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35347128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960770/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "METSIM is a study of 10,197 Finnish men from Kuopio in the late-settlement region of northeast Finland designed to investigate factors associated with type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular diseases3 (Supplementary Table 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000393> "A population-based cohort of 10,197 middle-aged and older Finnish men from a single site in north-eastern Finland, examined in 2005–2010 with detailed metabolic phenotyping, oral glucose tolerance tests, metabolomics and extensive genotyping and sequencing, and followed up to study nongenetic and genetic risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34428338") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38550311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39020067") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33623009") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902658/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The QGP is a population-based study designed to perform whole genome sequencing of the Qatar Biobank (QBB) participants9 with the aim to gain insights into the population structure and the genetic architecture of clinically relevant phenotypes in the Middle Eastern Qatari population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394> "A national whole-genome sequencing programme of the Qatar Foundation that sequences volunteers from the Qatar Biobank and combines their genomes with the biobank's phenotype data to study the Qatari and wider Arab and Middle Eastern populations at the molecular level.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34428338") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38550311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39020067") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34428338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34428338+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Qatar Genome Program (QGP) generates whole-genome sequencing (WGS) data and combines it with phenotypic information to create a comprehensive database for studying the Qatari and wider Arab and Middle Eastern populations at the molecular level.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394> "A national whole-genome sequencing programme of the Qatar Foundation that sequences volunteers from the Qatar Biobank and combines their genomes with the biobank's phenotype data to study the Qatari and wider Arab and Middle Eastern populations at the molecular level.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34428338") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38550311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39020067") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38550311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10977610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One of Qatar’s significant achievements in the field of precision medicine and PGx is the launch of its own large-scale national genome project in 2015, the Qatar Genome Program (QGP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394> "A national whole-genome sequencing programme of the Qatar Foundation that sequences volunteers from the Qatar Biobank and combines their genomes with the biobank's phenotype data to study the Qatari and wider Arab and Middle Eastern populations at the molecular level.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34428338") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38550311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39020067") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39020067") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11576737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Qatar Biobank and Qatar Genome Program are both Research, Development, and Innovation entities within Qatar Foundation for Education, Science, and Community Development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000394> "A national whole-genome sequencing programme of the Qatar Foundation that sequences volunteers from the Qatar Biobank and combines their genomes with the biobank's phenotype data to study the Qatari and wider Arab and Middle Eastern populations at the molecular level.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2017–19, all adult residents of Trøndelag were invited to the HUNT4 survey.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> "A population-based cohort of the adult population of Trøndelag County, Norway, in which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag aged 20 or over have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984–86, extended to Sør-Trøndelag in 2017–19, collecting questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and biological samples on a broad range of health topics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the HUNT Study, all residents aged ≥20 years in the Nord-Trøndelag region, Norway, have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984-86.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> "A population-based cohort of the adult population of Trøndelag County, Norway, in which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag aged 20 or over have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984–86, extended to Sør-Trøndelag in 2017–19, collecting questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and biological samples on a broad range of health topics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It was previously called the Nord-Trøndelag Health Study, until the study in 2019 expanded to cover both regions of Trøndelag County, Nord-Trøndelag and Sør-Trøndelag.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> "A population-based cohort of the adult population of Trøndelag County, Norway, in which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag aged 20 or over have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984–86, extended to Sør-Trøndelag in 2017–19, collecting questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and biological samples on a broad range of health topics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Trøndelag Health Study (the HUNT Study) is a population-based cohort study of the adult population in Trøndelag County, Norway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> "A population-based cohort of the adult population of Trøndelag County, Norway, in which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag aged 20 or over have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984–86, extended to Sør-Trøndelag in 2017–19, collecting questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and biological samples on a broad range of health topics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35578897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908054/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study has been running in Nord-Trøndelag since 1984 and is designed to cover a broad range of health-related topics through repeated surveys with questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and storage of biological samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000395> "A population-based cohort of the adult population of Trøndelag County, Norway, in which all residents of Nord-Trøndelag aged 20 or over have been invited to repeated surveys since 1984–86, extended to Sør-Trøndelag in 2017–19, collecting questionnaires, interviews, clinical examinations, laboratory measurements and biological samples on a broad range of health topics.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7444276/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Any individual living in the United States with a professional diagnosis (by a physician, psychologist, or therapist) of ASD plus their parents and an unaffected sibling are eligible to participate in SPARK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7444276/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SPARK began nationwide recruitment with 21 clinical sites and a multi-pronged social media strategy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7444276/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI) has launched SPARKForAutism.org, a dynamic platform that is engaging thousands of individuals with autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and connecting them to researchers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7444276/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "collected a total of 25,919 saliva samples, and has begun WES and genome-wide genotyping") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7444276/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "online access to participants; ability to recontact and recruit for new research studies; genomic, environmental, and longitudinal behavioral and medical information on all participants; and support for participants through communication of meaningful genetic and other ASD-relevant information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29420931") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41606319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12979206/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we analysed DNA sequencing reads previously generated from whole-genome sequencing (WGS) of saliva samples from 12,519 participants in the Simons Foundation Powering Autism Research (SPARK) cohort25") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000396> "A US cohort, launched by the Simons Foundation Autism Research Initiative (SFARI), of individuals living in the United States with a professional diagnosis of autism spectrum disorder together with their parents and an unaffected sibling, recruited nationwide through 21 clinical sites and social media and taking part remotely online, with questionnaires and saliva samples for genetic analysis (exome sequencing and genome-wide genotyping, later also whole-genome sequencing), collecting genomic, environmental and longitudinal behavioural and medical data, returning genetic results to participants, and recontacting them and connecting them with researchers for new studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12819321+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CRIC will include a racially and ethnically diverse group of adults aged 21 to 74 yr with a broad spectrum of renal disease severity, half of whom have diagnosed diabetes mellitus.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12819321+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects will undergo extensive clinical evaluation at baseline and at annual clinic visits and via telephone at 6 mo intervals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12819321+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chronic Renal Insufficiency Cohort (CRIC) Study was established to examine risk factors for progression of CRI and CVD among CRI patients and develop models to identify high-risk subgroups, informing future treatment trials, and increasing application of preventive therapies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8855239/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chronic Renal Insufficiency Cohort (CRIC) Study is a multicenter observational cohort study that enrolled 5499 adults from 7 clinical centers across the US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13273469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, eligibility for phase 1 included adults aged 21 to 74 years with eGFR of 20 to 70 ml/min per 1.73 m2, whereas phase 3 required participants to have more preserved kidney function (eGFR: 45–70 ml/min per 1.73m2) and older age (45–79 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12819321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35175342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42318085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13273469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study consisted of a prospective cohort of participants enrolled in phase 1 (2003–2008) and phase 3 (2013–2015) of the CRIC study, a multicenter, prospective, observational cohort study of participants with CKD in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000397> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of 5,499 racially and ethnically diverse adults with chronic kidney disease, recruited at seven clinical centres in the United States in two phases, 2003–2008 (adults aged 21 to 74 with an estimated glomerular filtration rate of 20–70 mL/min/1.73 m²) and 2013–2015 (adults aged 45 to 79 with more preserved kidney function, eGFR 45–70), and followed with annual clinic visits, six-monthly telephone contacts and annual blood and urine collection to examine risk factors for the progression of chronic kidney disease and cardiovascular disease.")

