Study/Memory and Aging Project (ROSMAP1-2) and the Chicago Health and Aging Project
(CHAP) cohort studies at Rush University") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000400> "A pair of harmonized longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort studies of aging and Alzheimer's disease run at Rush University, the Religious Orders Study (from 1994, nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (from 1997, lay persons from northeastern Illinois), whose older participants enrol without dementia and agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6858142/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 56 862 participants enrolled (21% response rate) into the Mayo Clinic Biobank from Rochester, Minnesota (77%, n=43 836), Jacksonville, Florida (18%, n=10 368) and La Crosse, Wisconsin (5%, n=2658).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401> "A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6858142/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we provide examples of the types of studies that have successfully utilised the resource, including (1) investigations of the population itself, (2) provision of controls for case–control studies, (3) genotype-driven research, (4) EHR-based research and (5) prospective recruitment to other studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401> "A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6858142/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were all Mayo Clinic patients, 18 years of age or older and US residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401> "A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31699749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6858142/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mayo Clinic Biobank was established to provide a large group of patients from which comparison groups (ie, controls) could be selected for case–control studies, to create a prospective cohort with sufficient power for common outcomes and to support electronic health record (EHR) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000401> "A clinic-based prospective cohort of about 57,000 adult Mayo Clinic patients who are US residents, enrolled at Rochester, Minnesota, Jacksonville, Florida and La Crosse, Wisconsin, established to supply control groups for case-control studies, form a prospective cohort for common outcomes and support electronic health record and genotype-driven research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39753034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39972214") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00928473") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39753034") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11754075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population consisted of children and adolescents from the HOLBAEK Study (previously known as The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank),17 including an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile for sex and age (BMI standard deviation score [SDS] > 1.28) according to a Danish reference; and a population-based cohort, recruited from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand, Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402> "A Danish cohort of children and adolescents, formerly called The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank, run since 2009 from the Children's Obesity Clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk, that combines an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile, included continuously and followed longitudinally during multidisciplinary obesity treatment, with a population-based reference cohort recruited cross-sectionally from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand; by 2020 it held data on more than 5,250 obesity clinic and more than 4,200 population-based participants, with biosamples, genotyping and cardiometabolic phenotyping, as a platform for research on childhood obesity and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39753034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39972214") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00928473") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39972214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906355/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in this study were genotyped in three batches on the Infinium HumancoreExome12 (v.1.0) and HumancoreExome24 (v.1.1) Beadchips (Illumina).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402> "A Danish cohort of children and adolescents, formerly called The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank, run since 2009 from the Children's Obesity Clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk, that combines an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile, included continuously and followed longitudinally during multidisciplinary obesity treatment, with a population-based reference cohort recruited cross-sectionally from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand; by 2020 it held data on more than 5,250 obesity clinic and more than 4,200 population-based participants, with biosamples, genotyping and cardiometabolic phenotyping, as a platform for research on childhood obesity and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39753034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39972214") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00928473") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39972214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11906355/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were recruited from two groups: the Children’s Obesity Clinic, Centre of Obesity Management offering the multidisciplinary childhood obesity management program at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk69, and a population-based cohort from schools across 11 municipalities in Zealand, Denmark70, as part of a cross-sectional study conducted between January 2009 and April 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000402> "A Danish cohort of children and adolescents, formerly called The Danish Childhood Obesity Biobank, run since 2009 from the Children's Obesity Clinic at Copenhagen University Hospital Holbæk, that combines an obesity clinic cohort with a BMI above the 90th percentile, included continuously and followed longitudinally during multidisciplinary obesity treatment, with a population-based reference cohort recruited cross-sectionally from schools in 11 municipalities in Zealand; by 2020 it held data on more than 5,250 obesity clinic and more than 4,200 population-based participants, with biosamples, genotyping and cardiometabolic phenotyping, as a platform for research on childhood obesity and its complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9849126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FinnGen is a public–private partnership research project that combines imputed genotype data generated from newly collected and legacy samples from Finnish biobanks and digital health record data from Finnish health registries (https://www.finngen.fi/en) with the aim to provide new insights into disease genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9849126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population isolates such as those in Finland benefit genetic research because deleterious alleles are often concentrated on a small number of low-frequency variants (0.1% ≤ minor allele frequency < 5%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9849126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FinnGen study aims to construct a resource that combines the power of nationwide biobanks, structured national healthcare data and a unique, isolated population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FinnGen has collected and correlated genome and longitudinal health data of more than 500 000 Finns, which is almost 10% of the Finnish population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FinnGen study utilises samples collected by a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.finngen.fi/en") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is based on combining genome information with digital health care data from national health registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000403> "A public–private partnership research project in Finland that combines genotype data from newly collected and legacy samples of about 500,000 participants of a nationwide network of Finnish biobanks with digital health data from national health registers, to provide genetic insights into disease in an isolated population enriched for low-frequency variants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7610553") Annotation(rdfs:comment "9,802 of the participants (75%) had a rare disease or an extreme measurement of a quantitative trait, of whom 9,024 were probands and 778 were affected relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7610553") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each participant was assigned to one of 18 domains with pre- specified enrolment criteria (Supplementary Table 1): 7,388 to one of 15 rare disease domains, 50 to a control domain, 4,835 to a Genomics England Limited (GEL) domain and 764 to a domain comprising UK Biobank participants with extreme red blood cell indices (Supplementary Information, Supplementary Table 1, Extended Data Fig. 1b).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7610553") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were enrolled by one of three mechanisms between December 2012 and March 2017 under the overall coordination of the National Institute for Health Research BioResource (NBR) at the University of Cambridge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7610553") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed WGS of 13,037 individuals enrolled at 57 National Health Service (NHS) hospitals in the United Kingdom and 26 hospitals in other countries (Fig. 1a, Extended Data Fig. 1a, Supplementary Table 1), in three batches, to clinical standard (Fig. 1b).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32581362+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we used whole-genome sequencing (WGS) in a national health system to streamline diagnosis and to discover unknown aetiological variants in the coding and non-coding regions of the genome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32581362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32581362+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study demonstrates a synergy by using WGS for diagnosis and aetiological discovery in routine healthcare.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000404> "A cohort of patients with rare diseases or extreme measurements of quantitative traits, their affected relatives and controls, enrolled mainly at National Health Service hospitals in the United Kingdom between 2012 and 2017 under the coordination of the NIHR BioResource at the University of Cambridge, whose whole genomes were sequenced to provide genetic diagnoses and discover aetiological variants within routine healthcare.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One quarter of the sample also underwent amyloid PET brain imaging with Pittsburgh compound B (PiB PET) and MRI brain imaging, and a subgroup of 10% had ActiGraph activity monitoring and body composition scanning.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle (AIBL) flagship study of aging aimed to recruit 1000 individuals aged over 60 to assist with prospective research into Alzheimer's disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They will be reassessed at 18-month intervals in order to determine the predictive utility of various biomarkers, cognitive parameters and lifestyle factors as indicators of AD, and as predictors of future cognitive decline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19470201+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Volunteers underwent a screening interview, had comprehensive cognitive testing, gave 80 ml of blood, and completed health and lifestyle questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8293663/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AIBL is a two-site study: Melbourne, Victoria (60%) and Perth, Western Australia (40%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470201") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38770381") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8293663/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Imaging, Biomarkers and Lifestyle (AIBL) Study commenced in 2006 as a prospective study of 1,112 individuals (768 cognitively normal (CN), 133 with mild cognitive impairment (MCI), and 211 with Alzheimer’s disease dementia (AD)) as an ‘Inception cohort’ who underwent detailed ssessments every 18 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000405> "A longitudinal cohort of volunteers aged over 60 in Australia, including people with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment and healthy controls, recruited at centres in Perth and Melbourne and reassessed at 18-month intervals with cognitive testing, blood biomarkers, lifestyle questionnaires and amyloid PET and MRI imaging to study predictors of Alzheimer's disease and cognitive decline.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16490960+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PopGen currently pursues recruitment, sampling and processing activities in close collaboration with a multitude of clinical partners, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16490960+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Precise estimates of population-specific genotypic risks can be obtained efficiently through the complete ascertainment of patients in a geographically confined area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16490960+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PopGen project uses the most northern part of Germany as a target region for such a pursuit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25903422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4423213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institute of Epidemiology and Biobank PopGen, Christian Albrechts University, Kiel, Germany") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35348614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC9976967") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control population used in this study consisted of a cohort of 1081 individuals, part of the PopGen cohort, a population-based biobank in Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16490960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.popgen.de/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Neben Populations-Kontroll-Kohorten existieren bei der Biobank popgen Sammlungen zu verschiedenen Krankheiten bzw. wissenschaftlichen Fragestellungen, die in der Regel in enger Kooperation mit klinischen Kolleginnen und Kollegen aufgebaut wurden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000406> "A population-based biobank in the most northern part of Germany, run from Kiel University, that recruits patients through complete ascertainment in a geographically confined area together with population controls, covering cardiovascular, neuropsychiatric and environmental diseases, to estimate population-specific genotypic risks for complex diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000407> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000407>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6542096/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DN cohort recruited 2080 outpatient participants with T2D from the diabetes centre (Chinese N = 1309, Malay = 411, Asian Indian = 360) in a regional hospital between March 2004 and December 2015 with the primary aim to study the development and progression of DN and the secondary aim to study the major cardiovascular diseases (CVD) in T2D patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000407> "A cohort of outpatients with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay and Asian Indian ancestry recruited from the diabetes centre of a regional hospital in Singapore between 2004 and 2015 to study the development and progression of diabetic nephropathy and of major cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6542096/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The authors thank all the research team members from Clinical Research Unit and clinicians in Khoo Teck Puat Hospital, Singapore for their assistance with patient recruitment and data input for SMART2D and DN cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000407> "A cohort of outpatients with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay and Asian Indian ancestry recruited from the diabetes centre of a regional hospital in Singapore between 2004 and 2015 to study the development and progression of diabetic nephropathy and of major cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5865208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants for this study were recruited in the diabetes centres in Singapore as described previously in our Diabetic Nephropathy (DN) cohort9.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000407> "A cohort of outpatients with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay and Asian Indian ancestry recruited from the diabetes centre of a regional hospital in Singapore between 2004 and 2015 to study the development and progression of diabetic nephropathy and of major cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6542096/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, SMART2D is a prospective cohort with the objective to study risk factors for vascular complications in patients with T2D. 2057 outpatients with T2D (Chinese N = 1053, Malay N = 483, Asian Indians N = 443, others N = 78) were recruited consecutively from a secondary hospital and a primary care medical facility in Singapore between August 2011 and March 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10704954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It adopted a three-wave longitudinal design with intervals of 3 years between consecutive waves.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10704954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is a prospective cohort study that recruited T2DM patients from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in the northern region of Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10704954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The findings may also guide us on the use of the longitudinal parameters in future assessment of diabetic complications.MethodsThe Singapore Study of Macro-Angiopathy and microvascular Reactivity in Type 2 Diabetes (SMART2D) was started in 2011 to study the impact of T2DM on blood vessel function and diabetes-related complications including diabetic kidney disease, retinopathy, diabetic foot syndrome, cognitive dysfunction and mood disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10704954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients were first recruited between 2011 and 2014 (first wave).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38059349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38059349+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IntroductionThe Singapore Study of Macro-Angiopathy and microvascular Reactivity in Type 2 Diabetes (SMART2D) is a prospective cohort study which was started in 2011 to investigate the effect of risk factors on vascular function and diabetes-related complications in Asians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000408> "A prospective cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes of Chinese, Malay, Indian and other ancestry recruited in 2011–2014 from a public hospital and primary care polyclinics in northern Singapore and followed in three-yearly waves to study risk factors for vascular function and diabetes-related complications such as kidney disease, retinopathy and cognitive dysfunction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6659146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between 1993 and 1998, postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years at study entry were recruited through 40 clinical centers into either a randomized clinical trial (RCT) component (n = 68 132) or an observational study (OS) component (n = 93 676 women).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6659146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RCTs consisted of 4 trials including 1 dietary modification trial, 2 hormonal therapy trials, and 1 calcium and vitamin D trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31339542+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A nationwide prospective cohort study of 156 624 postmenopausal women enrolled in the Women's Health Initiative at 40 clinical centers in the United States between 1993 and 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Postmenopausal women ranging in age from 50 to 79 are enrolled at one of 40 WHI clinical centers nationwide into either a clinical trial (CT) that will include about 64,500 women or an observational study (OS) that will include about 100,000 women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Women's Health Initiative (WHI) is a large and complex clinical investigation of strategies for the prevention and control of some of the most common causes of morbidity and mortality among postmenopausal women, including cancer, cardiovascular disease, and osteoporotic fractures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339542") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women are screened for participation in one or both of the components--dietary modification (DM) or hormone replacement therapy (HRT)--of the CT, which will randomize 48,000 and 27,500 women, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000409> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–79 enrolled from 1993 at 40 clinical centres across the United States into a clinical trial of dietary modification, hormone therapy and calcium and vitamin D supplementation or into a parallel observational study, followed to study the prevention of cancer, cardiovascular disease and osteoporotic fractures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37731490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10507260/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Study of Health in Pomerania (SHIP) is a longitudinal population-based study which aims to determine the incidence and prevalence of common risk factors, subclinical disorders and clinical disease (30, 31).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11291685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts do not overlap, as participation in a previous cohort is an exclusion criterion for each subsequent cohort.During initial sampling, adults aged 20–79 were selected from registration data in a randomized, two-stage cluster method stratified by sex and age45.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11291685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first two cohorts are named SHIP-START and SHIP-TREND, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39085387+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohorts are sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39085387+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data was analyzed from 8134 individuals from the population-based Study of Health in Pomerania (SHIP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39085387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39085387+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population represents a cross-sectional analysis from the cohorts SHIP-START (recruited 1997-2001) and SHIP-TREND (recruited 2008-2012), sampled for baseline investigations (SHIP-START-0 and SHIP-TREND-0) at the age of 20-79 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000410> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 20–79 sampled from Western Pomerania, a rural region of north-eastern Germany, and recruited in 2008–2012 as the second, independent cohort of the Study of Health in Pomerania, examined at baseline and followed up to study health, disease and their risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837648/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is a consortium project consisting of six prospective cohort studies that would be categorized into population-based and gene-environment model studies (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> "A consortium of six Korean cohorts, population-based and gene–environment model studies initiated from 2001 with about 245,000 participants, investigating the genetic and environmental determinants of health, disease and ageing in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13585397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initiated in 2001, the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES) is a large-scale, population-based cohort study to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of health and disease in the Korean population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> "A consortium of six Korean cohorts, population-based and gene–environment model studies initiated from 2001 with about 245,000 participants, investigating the genetic and environmental determinants of health, disease and ageing in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13585397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 2001, >245 000 participants have been enrolled, with data collected on demographic characteristics, lifestyle behaviours, dietary habits, medical history, and environmental exposure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> "A consortium of six Korean cohorts, population-based and gene–environment model studies initiated from 2001 with about 245,000 participants, investigating the genetic and environmental determinants of health, disease and ageing in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13585397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES) has undergone a strategic transformation towards ageing research with its 245 000 participants, now in their sixties and seventies, providing an invaluable long-term resource for studying healthy ageing and longevity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> "A consortium of six Korean cohorts, population-based and gene–environment model studies initiated from 2001 with about 245,000 participants, investigating the genetic and environmental determinants of health, disease and ageing in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42753719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13585397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The consortium comprises six distinct cohorts, each investigating specific health aspects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000411> "A consortium of six Korean cohorts, population-based and gene–environment model studies initiated from 2001 with about 245,000 participants, investigating the genetic and environmental determinants of health, disease and ageing in the Korean population.")

