# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5755749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Such data will provide new knowledge on the early temporal course of AD pathophysiology and inform the design of secondary prevention clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5755749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer's Prevention (WRAP), established in 2001 [2], is a longitudinal observational cohort of participants who enrolled at midlife (mean age 54), and that is enriched with risk for late-onset AD due to parental history (PH) of AD dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5755749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This research was supported by the National Institutes of Health awards (R01 AG027161, R01 AG021155, R01 AG054047, R01 AG037639, P50 AG033514, UL1 TR000427, K23 AG045957, F30AG054115, T32 GM007507, and T32 GM008692) and grants from the Alzheimer's Association, Extendicare Foundation, and Northwestern Mutual Life Foundation to the University of Wisconsin–Madison") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29322089+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Serially assessed cognition, self-reported medical and lifestyle histories (e.g., diet, physical and cognitive activity, sleep, and mood), laboratory tests, genetics, and linked studies comprising molecular imaging, structural imaging, and cerebrospinal fluid data have yielded many important findings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29322089+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since late 2001, Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer's Prevention has enrolled 1561 people at a mean baseline age of 54 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://wrap.wisc.edu/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29322089") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29322089+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wisconsin Registry for Alzheimer's Prevention is a longitudinal observational cohort study enriched with persons with a parental history (PH) of probable Alzheimer's disease (AD) dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000413> "A longitudinal observational cohort of middle-aged adults enriched for persons with a parental history of probable Alzheimer disease dementia, enrolled since 2001 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, and followed with serial cognitive assessments, medical and lifestyle histories, laboratory tests, genetics and linked imaging and cerebrospinal fluid studies to study the early course of Alzheimer disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7803963/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(4) middle-aged adults with a positive parental history of AD; (5) middle-aged adults with a negative parental history of AD; and (6) middle-aged adults with indeterminate parental history of AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7803963/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the inclusion criteria for WADRC participants included an age ≥45, decisional capacity, and the ability to fast from food and drink for 12 h.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7803963/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WADRC, previously described92, is a longitudinal cohort study of memory, aging, and AD in middle and older-aged adults who were recruited into one of six subgroups: (1) mild late-onset AD; (2) mild cognitive impairment (MCI); (3) age-matched healthy older controls (age > 65);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A fasting blood drawA physical examA study partner who can come with you to study visits and answer questions about your memory and daily lifeBiomarker visits to help identify early markers for Alzheimer’ disease:MRI (magnetic resonance imaging) scan: a very detailed image of the brainLumbar puncture: collection of cerebrospinal fluid from the lower backPET (positron emission tomography) scan") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People who join the Clinical Core attend either annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner and undergo memory and thinking abilities evaluations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/clinical-core") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/structure-and-cores") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://adrc.wisc.edu/history-and-mission") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wisconsin ADRC was established in 2009 with funding from a National Institutes of Health/National Institute on Aging grant for Alzheimer’s Research Centers (P30-AG062715).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000414> "A longitudinal cohort, the Clinical Core study of the Wisconsin Alzheimer's Disease Research Center, a National Institute on Aging-funded centre established in 2009 at the University of Wisconsin–Madison, United States, in which adults aged 45 and over, recruited into subgroups with mild late-onset Alzheimer disease, mild cognitive impairment, healthy older controls, and middle-aged adults with a positive, negative or indeterminate parental history of Alzheimer disease, attend annual or every-other-year visits with a study partner for memory and thinking evaluations, blood draws and biomarker visits with MRI, lumbar puncture and PET, to study memory, ageing and Alzheimer disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the first recruitment phase referred to as baseline in the following, data were collected between 2011 and 2014 from 1811 adults (18–83 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up for the assessment of disease progression, as well as the onset of new diseases with changes in subject’s phenotype, diet or lifestyle factors is planned every 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Food Chain Plus (FoCus) cohort was launched in 2011 for population-based research related to metabolic inflammation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was set-up to represent a Northern German population of the Kiel region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To characterize this novel pathology in a comprehensive manner, data collection included multiple omics layers such as phenomics, microbiomics, metabolomics, genomics, and metagenomics as well as nutrition profiling, taste perception phenotyping and social network analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9630232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two-step recruitment included the randomised enrolment of participants via residents’ registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig–Holstein (UKSH).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000415> "A cohort of 1,811 adults aged 18–83 from the Kiel region of northern Germany, enrolled in 2011–2014 at random via residents' registration offices and via the Obesity Outpatient Centre of the University Medical Center Schleswig-Holstein, for population-based research on metabolic inflammation with multi-omics, nutrition and follow-up every five years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35393526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Investigators at the University of Maryland Baltimore have been studying the genetic determinants of cardiometabolic health in this population since 1993.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> "A research programme of the University of Maryland studying adults of the Old Order Amish founder population of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, of whom over 7,000 have taken part in one or more of its studies of the genetics of complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35393526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Old Order Amish (OOA) population of Lancaster County, PA immigrated to the Colonies from Central Europe in the early 1700’s.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> "A research programme of the University of Maryland studying adults of the Old Order Amish founder population of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, of whom over 7,000 have taken part in one or more of its studies of the genetics of complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35393526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To date, over 7000 Amish adults have participated in one or more of our studies as part of the Amish Complex Disease Research Program72.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> "A research programme of the University of Maryland studying adults of the Old Order Amish founder population of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, of whom over 7,000 have taken part in one or more of its studies of the genetics of complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5015947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects included in this report are members of the Amish community in Lancaster County, PA who are at least 18 yrs old and have previously participated in one or more Institutional Review Board (IRB)-approved studies conducted at the University of Maryland School of Medicine Amish Research Clinic (ARC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> "A research programme of the University of Maryland studying adults of the Old Order Amish founder population of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, of whom over 7,000 have taken part in one or more of its studies of the genetics of complex diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8989972/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5015947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To date, we have screened ∼6500 Amish adults for a variety of risk factors related to cardiovascular disease (Mitchell et al. 2008), diabetes (Hsueh et al. 2000), and osteoporosis (Streeten et al. 2006) as part of the Amish Complex Disease Research Program (ACDRP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000416> "A research programme of the University of Maryland studying adults of the Old Order Amish founder population of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, of whom over 7,000 have taken part in one or more of its studies of the genetics of complex diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18500243+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An \"opt-out\" model was implemented after significant review and revision.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33441150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our primary analysis was performed at VUMC which is a tertiary care center providing inpatient and outpatient care in Nashville, TN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BioVU is Vanderbilt’s biorepository of de-identified samples extracted from discarded blood collected during routine clinical testing and linked to de-identified medical records in the Synthetic Derivative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BioVU now accrues 500-1000 samples per week, totaling more than 300,000 DNA samples as of January 2023.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Planning for BioVU began in mid-2004 and the first samples were collected in February 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of BioVU is to provide a resource to Vanderbilt investigators for studies of genotype-phenotype associations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Vanderbilt clinic patients may sign the BioVU Consent Form if they wish to donate their excess blood samples, or not sign the form if they do not wish to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18500243") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://victr.vumc.org/biovu-description/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7807864/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000188.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An important potential enabling resource for Personalized Medicine is the combination of a DNA repository with Electronic Medical Record (EMR) systems sufficiently robust to provide excellence in clinical care and to serve as resources for analysis of disease susceptibility and therapeutic outcomes across patient populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000417> "A biobank of Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, which since February 2007 has banked DNA extracted from blood left over from routine clinical testing of its patients, originally under an opt-out model and now from patients who sign the BioVU consent form, with more than 300,000 samples by January 2023, each linked to a de-identified copy of the patient's electronic health record (the Synthetic Derivative), as a resource for genotype–phenotype studies and personalised medicine.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000418> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000418>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38371883") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It recruited predominantly European (EA), South Asian (SA) and African Caribbean (AC) participants living in West and North London; details have been previously described [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000418> "A tri-ethnic longitudinal cohort of people of European, South Asian and African Caribbean ethnicity living in West and North London, United Kingdom, set up in 1988 to examine ethnic differences in chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38371883") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SABRE was set up in 1988 as a tri-ethnic longitudinal cohort study to examine ethnic differences in chronic disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000418> "A tri-ethnic longitudinal cohort of people of European, South Asian and African Caribbean ethnicity living in West and North London, United Kingdom, set up in 1988 to examine ethnic differences in chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38371883") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10874717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of this study therefore was to investigate cross-sectional associations between carotid atherosclerosis and cognitive function and brain health in a UK multi-ethnic community-based sample including people of European, South Asian, and African-Caribbean ethnicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000418> "A tri-ethnic longitudinal cohort of people of European, South Asian and African Caribbean ethnicity living in West and North London, United Kingdom, set up in 1988 to examine ethnic differences in chronic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9205783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(2) gut-and-liver axis–healthy participants (GALA–HP), a cross-sectional cohort of healthy controls matched to GALA–ALD from the GALAXY Horizon2020 consortium (livergalaxy.eu) (n = 137);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9205783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the GALA–ALD cohort (n = 459) we recruited patients consecutively through standard referrals to three outpatient liver clinics, from two municipal alcohol rehabilitation centers and through a community call to screen for ALD in the Region of Southern Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9205783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we used MS-based proteomics to analyze paired liver tissue and plasma samples, and clinical outcomes, from a large cohort of patients with a history of alcohol misuse and with asymptomatic ALD representing early stages on the disease spectrum, and from healthy controls with age and gender matched to the ALD cohort, totaling 596 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41935631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Odense University Hospital recruited participants between 2013 and 2018, and obtained informed consent from all participants before inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41935631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted using plasma and fecal samples from the GALAXY cross-sectional cohort of individuals with a history of harmful drinking (men >36 g/day, women >24 g/day EtOH for at least 1 year) with an average of 19 years of excess alcohol use.[22], [23], [24] This cohort focuses on asymptomatic ALD across the early disease stages") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35654907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/668031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41935631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13233754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated BA homeostasis in a cross-sectional ALD cohort (n = 462), alongside matched healthy controls (n = 148), and validated key findings in two independent ALD cohorts (n = 34 and n = 52).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000419> "A cohort of the EU Horizon 2020 GALAXY (Gut-and-liver axis in alcoholic liver fibrosis) consortium, recruited between 2013 and 2018 by Odense University Hospital in the Region of Southern Denmark, of about 460 consecutively recruited patients with a history of harmful drinking (more than 36 g of alcohol a day for men and 24 g for women for at least a year) and early, asymptomatic alcohol-related liver disease (GALA-ALD), most with a liver biopsy, and some 140 to 150 healthy participants matched to them by age and sex (GALA-HP), to study the gut–liver axis and non-invasive markers of alcohol-related liver fibrosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26407342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4583245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Young Finns Study (YFS) is a large follow-up study of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood [29].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10726240/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 1980, the cohort has been regularly followed-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10726240/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline study was conducted in 1980 when 3596 randomly selected children and adolescents aged 3, 6, 9, 12, 15 and 18 years participated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10726240/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The prospective YFS has followed a population-based cohort from childhood to adulthood that were sampled from five cities with university hospitals in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Oulu, Tampere, and Turku) and their rural surrounds.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10726240/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, using data from a population-based sample of individuals followed from childhood to adulthood for up to 31 years in the Cardiovascular Risk in Young Finns Study (YFS), we investigated the association between number of siblings with markers of preclinical CVD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38115890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38115890+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample comprised 2776 participants (54 % female) from the Cardiovascular Risk in Young Finns Study who had CVD risk factor data measured in childhood in 1980 (aged 3-18 years) and markers of preclinical CVD measured in adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000420> "A population-based cohort of 3,596 randomly selected Finnish children and adolescents aged 3–18 years at baseline in 1980, followed into adulthood for over three decades to study how cardiovascular risk factors in childhood relate to preclinical markers of cardiovascular disease in adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6771941/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this population‐based study, genetic variants of CRC susceptibility were investigated for their relevance in CRC survival based on analyses of variants identified in genome‐wide association studies (GWASs).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> "A population-based case–control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, recruiting colorectal cancer cases and population controls since 1999, whose genotyped cases are followed for survival, used to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6771941/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Previously we have shown that SOCCS study is representative of British and Scottish populations and cases from SOCCS cluster tightly with population‐based controls from SOCCS and Generation Scotland.31, 32") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> "A population-based case–control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, recruiting colorectal cancer cases and population controls since 1999, whose genotyped cases are followed for survival, used to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6771941/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted the analysis in a well‐characterized population‐based study of 5,675 patients after CRC diagnosis in Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> "A population-based case–control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, recruiting colorectal cancer cases and population controls since 1999, whose genotyped cases are followed for survival, used to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6771941/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a population‐based case–control study (Study of Colorectal Cancer in Scotland, SOCCS; 1999‐current)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> "A population-based case–control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, recruiting colorectal cancer cases and population controls since 1999, whose genotyped cases are followed for survival, used to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31271446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5772647/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Scottish Colorectal Cancer Study (SOCCS) is a case-control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, UK, recruiting subjects prospectively on a population-wide basis between 1996 and 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000421> "A population-based case–control study of colorectal cancer in Scotland, recruiting colorectal cancer cases and population controls since 1999, whose genotyped cases are followed for survival, used to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer and its outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analyses of genome-wide genotyping, for >100,000 participants using custom-designed Axiom arrays, reveal extensive relatedness, recent consanguinity, and signatures reflecting large-scale population movements from recent Chinese history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 512,000 adults recruited in 2004–2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions of China, with baseline questionnaires and physical measurements, periodic resurveys, genome-wide genotyping of over 100,000 participants and electronic linkage to death, disease and health-insurance records, supporting studies of disease risk factors, genetics and drug targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed data from questionnaires and physical measurements were collected at baseline, with additional measurements at three resurveys involving ∼5% of surviving participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 512,000 adults recruited in 2004–2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions of China, with baseline questionnaires and physical measurements, periodic resurveys, genome-wide genotyping of over 100,000 participants and electronic linkage to death, disease and health-insurance records, supporting studies of disease risk factors, genetics and drug targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Systematic genome-wide association studies of incident disease, captured through electronic linkage to death and disease registries and to the national health insurance system, replicate established disease loci and identify 14 novel disease associations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 512,000 adults recruited in 2004–2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions of China, with baseline questionnaires and physical measurements, periodic resurveys, genome-wide genotyping of over 100,000 participants and electronic linkage to death, disease and health-insurance records, supporting studies of disease risk factors, genetics and drug targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The China Kadoorie Biobank (CKB) is a population-based prospective cohort of >512,000 adults recruited from 2004 to 2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions across China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 512,000 adults recruited in 2004–2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions of China, with baseline questionnaires and physical measurements, periodic resurveys, genome-wide genotyping of over 100,000 participants and electronic linkage to death, disease and health-insurance records, supporting studies of disease risk factors, genetics and drug targets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37601966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37601966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Together with studies of candidate drug targets and disease risk factors and contributions to international genetics consortia, these demonstrate the breadth, depth, and quality of the CKB data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000422> "A population-based prospective cohort of more than 512,000 adults recruited in 2004–2008 from 10 geographically diverse regions of China, with baseline questionnaires and physical measurements, periodic resurveys, genome-wide genotyping of over 100,000 participants and electronic linkage to death, disease and health-insurance records, supporting studies of disease risk factors, genetics and drug targets.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31217584") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6785182/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the United States, the All of Us Research Program embraces the reality that the success of precision medicine requires precision genomics, and therefore emphasizes the recruitment and active participation of underrepresented populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All of Us opened for enrollment in May 2018 and currently enrolls participants 18 years of age or older from a network of more than 340 recruitment sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Elements of the program protocol include health questionnaires, electronic health records (EHRs), physical measurements, the use of digital health technology, and the collection and analysis of biospecimens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "More than 80% of these participants are from groups that have been historically underrepresented in biomedical research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The All of Us Research Program plans to enroll a diverse group of at least 1 million persons in the United States in order to accelerate biomedical research and improve health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31412182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8291101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Precision Medicine Initiative (PMI) Working Group of the Advisory Committee (ACD) to the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Director generated the initial blueprint for the structure and goals for the All of Us (AoU) program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000423> "A national research cohort led by the National Institutes of Health that aims to enrol diverse adults in the United States, most from groups historically under-represented in biomedical research, through more than 340 recruitment sites, collecting health questionnaires, electronic health records, physical measurements, digital health data and biospecimens to advance precision medicine.")

