AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31217584") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-019-1310-4/MediaObjects/41586_2019_1310_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BioMeTM enrolled over 26,500 participants from September 58 2007 through August 2013, with 25% African American,36% Hispanic/Latino (primarily of Caribbean origin), 59 30% Caucasian, and 9% of Other ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9729131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mount Sinai BioMe Biobank, founded in 2007, is an ongoing electronic health record-linked biorepository that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System, comprising approximately 60,000 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9729131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mount Sinai Health System serves a diverse group of communities in the greater New York City area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9729131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Regeneron Genetics Center (Tarrytown, NY, USA) generated exome sequencing files from 31,591 BioMe participants, using the Illumina NovaSeq 6000 platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11992084/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Charles Bronfman Institute for Personalized Medicine’s BioMe BioBank Program located in New York City97; both studies had genetic data linked to electronic health records (EHR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36216889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC12488948/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PAGE includes individuals from the following ongoing population-based biobanks and cohorts: Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities (ARIC) Study, the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai BioMe biobank in New York City (BioMe)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000424> "An electronic health record-linked biobank founded in 2007 at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai that enrols participants non-selectively from the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, comprising about 60,000 ancestrally diverse participants with genotype and sequence data for genetic and clinical research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7373261/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We evaluated the role of smoking history in abdominal adipose deposition and, specifically, its role in muscle composition and quality using CT in more than 3,000 Coronary Artery Risk Development in Young Adults (CARDIA) participants aged 43 to 55.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> "A prospective cohort of young adults aged 18–30 years, balanced by sex and by Black and White race, recruited in 1985–1986 at four field centres in Birmingham, Alabama, Chicago, Illinois, Minneapolis, Minnesota and Oakland, California, and followed with repeated examinations into midlife to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32692748+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The longitudinal CARDIA study was initiated in 1985 with the recruitment of young adult participants (aged 18-30 years) equally balanced by female and male sex and black and white race at 4 field centers located in Birmingham, AL, Chicago, IL, Minneapolis, MN, and Oakland, CA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> "A prospective cohort of young adults aged 18–30 years, balanced by sex and by Black and White race, recruited in 1985–1986 at four field centres in Birmingham, Alabama, Chicago, Illinois, Minneapolis, Minnesota and Oakland, California, and followed with repeated examinations into midlife to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36853610+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the CARDIA study were aged 18 to 30 years when they completed the baseline graded exercise test protocol in 1985 to 1986 and have since undergone follow-up examinations biannually and every 2 to 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> "A prospective cohort of young adults aged 18–30 years, balanced by sex and by Black and White race, recruited in 1985–1986 at four field centres in Birmingham, Alabama, Chicago, Illinois, Minneapolis, Minnesota and Oakland, California, and followed with repeated examinations into midlife to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4821694/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CARDIA study is a prospective multicenter study designed to investigate the development of cardiovascular disease risk factors and subclinical and clinical disease in young (18–30 years) Black and White men and women from four geographic locations in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> "A prospective cohort of young adults aged 18–30 years, balanced by sex and by Black and White race, recruited in 1985–1986 at four field centres in Birmingham, Alabama, Chicago, Illinois, Minneapolis, Minnesota and Oakland, California, and followed with repeated examinations into midlife to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32692748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36853610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CARDIA study is a prospective, multi-center investigation of the natural history and etiology of cardiovascular disease in African Americans and whites 18-30 years of age at the time of initial examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000425> "A prospective cohort of young adults aged 18–30 years, balanced by sex and by Black and White race, recruited in 1985–1986 at four field centres in Birmingham, Alabama, Chicago, Illinois, Minneapolis, Minnesota and Oakland, California, and followed with repeated examinations into midlife to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors and disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12764833/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from the Singapore general population11,13,14.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12764833/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HELIOS Study is a prospective population-based cohort, comprising men and women aged 30 to 84 years, living in Singapore") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12764833/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HELIOS Study operates under the governance framework of the Nanyang Technological University, and with Institutional Review Board approval (Ref: 2016-11-030).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12764833/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 10,004 Asian men and women aged 30 to 84 years to the HELIOS Study between 2018 and 2022 (www.healthforlife.sg).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41469377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our unique HELIOS Asian Precision Medicine cohort study represents a state-of-the-art platform to enable biomedical researchers to understand the aetiology and pathogenesis of diverse disease outcomes in Asia, and to generate insights that have the potential to improve health outcomes for Asian populations globally.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.healthforlife.sg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41469377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address this gap, we have initiated the Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS) longitudinal cohort study, comprising comprehensive behavioural, phenotypic, and genomic measurements from 10,004 Asian men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000426> "A prospective population-based cohort of 10,004 men and women of Chinese, Indian or Malay background aged 30–84, recruited from the Singapore general population in 2018–2022 by Nanyang Technological University, with behavioural, phenotypic and multi-omic measurements and health-record linkage for precision-medicine research in Asian populations.")

