# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5465083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, 151,677 Icelanders have been genotyped using Illumina SNP chips and genotype probabilities for untyped relatives has been calculated based on Icelandic genealogy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5465083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is based on whole-genome sequence data from the whole blood of 15,220 Icelanders participating in various disease projects at deCODE genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5465083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We estimated the risk ratio among siblings (λS) of Icelandic patients with appendicitis (N = 8,160) to be 1.95 by cross-matching with the nationwide genealogy7 (Supplementary Table 2).In order to discover sequence variants associating with risk of appendicitis, we performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of appendicitis, combining data from Icelandic and Dutch populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Speech samples were obtained from 14,144 Icelandic participants as a part of the deCODE Health Study in Iceland, which involves comprehensive phenotyping of a general population sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These phenotypes were collected through the deCODE Health Study and other research projects at deCODE genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28596592") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6680338/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Germline DNA was isolated at the Radboudumc (HPC patients and referents) or at the deCODE Genetics facilities in Reykjavik, Iceland (SPC patients).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000428> "A population sample of Icelanders recruited through the disease-specific and general-population research projects of deCODE genetics in Reykjavik, Iceland, including the deCODE Health Study, whose chip genotypes and whole-genome sequences, combined with the nationwide Icelandic genealogy, are used for genome-wide association studies of diseases and other traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5073566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the patients and controls undergo blood sampling for -omics determinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5073566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are enrolled according to the following inclusion criteria: older than 18 years, no chronic pain (lasting longer than 12 weeks) in the past 12 months, written informed consent obtained and Caucasian ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5073566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients fulfilling the following conditions will be considered for enrolment: age 18 years and older; chronic pain (pain lasting longer than 12 weeks) between the costal margins and gluteal fold, with or without symptoms in one or both legs, written informed consent signed and Caucasian ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5073566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is part of the PainOMICS project that includes four different trials and was reviewed and funded by European Community in the Seventh Framework Programme (FP7)—THEME (HEALTH.2013.2.2.1-5—Understanding and controlling pain).The project includes six clinical centres from Italy, Croatia, Belgium, Australia and the USA, and four centres for scientific analyses from Croatia, France, Germany and UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5073566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is registered at Clinicaltrials.gov (NCT02037789).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5411039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we validated an SOP model that will be used in the multicentre (5 centres) retrospective “PainOmics” study, funded by the European Community in the 7th Framework Programme, which aims to develop new biomarkers for CLBP through three different -omics approaches: genomics, glycomics and activomics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244589/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PainOmics (Allegri et al., 2016) was the case-control study aimed at finding potential biomarkers for dorsalgia and therapeutic targets for its management.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27798002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28459826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02037789") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37293449") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244589/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample of 3400 participants including the residents of Italy, Belgium, England, and Croatia was composed in the years from 2014 to 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000429> "A retrospective, multicentre case–control study of adults of Caucasian ancestry with chronic low back pain and controls without chronic pain, run within the European Union FP7-funded PainOMICS project (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT02037789), which enrolled 3,400 participants between September 2014 and February 2016 at clinical centres in Italy, Belgium, the United Kingdom and Croatia (the registered protocol also listed sites in the United States and Australia), collecting clinical data and blood samples for genome-wide association, glycomics and activomics analyses of chronic low back pain.")
