# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4242463/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HELIC collections include blood for DNA extraction, lab-based haematological and biochemical measurements, and interview-based questionnaire data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4242463/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HELIC-Pomak collection comprises individuals from the Pomak villages located in the regional unit of Xanthi (estimated to be 25,000 in total).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4242463/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Under the auspices of the HELlenic Isolated Cohorts study (HELIC) we have collected samples from two isolated populations in Greece: the Pomak villages (HELIC-Pomak), a set of religiously-isolated mountainous villages in the North of Greece; and the Mylopotamos mountainous villages (HELIC-MANOLIS) on the island of Crete.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6950453/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They represent a Muslim minority in Greece with uncertain origins [13].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6950453/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We contacted the local Health Centre in Echinos and, with the cooperation of the local doctors and nurses, a total of 1702 volunteers were recruited between July 2010 and March 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25373335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31847144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34857772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8640022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use whole-genome sequencing (WGS) to capture the entire allele frequency spectrum in 2,893 samples from two Greek population-based cohorts, MANOLIS and Pomak.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000430> "A population-based cohort of adults from the Pomak villages of the regional unit of Xanthi, a set of religiously isolated mountainous villages of the Muslim Pomak minority in northern Greece, 1,702 of whom were recruited as volunteers through the local health centre in Echinos between July 2010 and March 2013 within the Hellenic Isolated Cohorts (HELIC) study, with interview-based questionnaires, anthropometric, haematological and biochemical measurements and blood samples for DNA that were genotyped and whole-genome sequenced, to study the genetics of cardiometabolic and other medically relevant complex traits in an isolated population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4574249") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided a saliva sample and broadly consented to the use of their DNA, mailed survey response data, and linked electronic health records in health research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4574249") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GERA cohort of 110,266 participants was formed by in- cluding samples from all racial and ethnic minority par- ticipants in the RPGEH enrolled through February 2011 (the conclusion of DNA extraction for the project), with the remainder of the cohort composed of samples from non-Hispanic white participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26092718+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kaiser Permanente (KP) Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), in collaboration with the University of California-San Francisco, undertook genome-wide genotyping of >100,000 subjects that constitute the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the GERA cohort were recruited from the adult membership of the KPNC health plan, a large integrated health care system that provides comprehensive medical services to four million members.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RPGEH was developed by the KPNC Division of Research as a resource that links together surveys, biospecimens and electronic health record data for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26092718") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33778338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cross-sectional study of TL included 84,996 non-Hispanic white adults in the GERA cohort who had a valid TL measurement that passed quality control checks and a successfully geocoded residential address.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000431> "A multi-ethnic cohort of over 100,000 adult members of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California health plan who consented to the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH), linking survey data, saliva-derived DNA with genome-wide genotypes and telomere length, and electronic health records for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common age-related diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper, we describe the generation of a new and large data set for eQTL analysis (350 healthy individuals) in nine cell types that are potentially relevant for IBD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> "A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected peripheral blood as well as intestinal biopsies (ileum, transverse colon, rectum) from 323 healthy Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège as part of a national screening campaign for colon cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> "A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We generated transcriptome data for six circulating immune cell types (CD4+ T lymphocytes, CD8+ T lymphocytes, CD19+ B lymphocytes, CD14+ monocytes, CD15+ granulocytes, platelets) as well as ileal, colonic, and rectal biopsies (IL, TR, RE), collected from 323 healthy Europeans (141 men, 182 women, average age 56 years, visiting the clinic as part of a national screening campaign for colon cancer) using Illumina HT12 arrays (CEDAR data set; Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> "A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use this “Correlated Expression and Disease Association Research” data set (CEDAR) to identify 23,650 significant cis-eQTL, which fall into 9720 regulatory modules of which at least ∼889 affect more than one gene in more than one tissue.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> "A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29930244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40593539") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12218978/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CEDAR | Correlated Expression & Disease Association Research | Population | 323 | Belgian |  | 29930244, 10.1038/s41467-018-04365-8") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000432> "A cohort of about 320 healthy adult Europeans visiting the Academic Hospital of the University of Liège, Belgium, as part of a national colon-cancer screening campaign, from whom peripheral blood and intestinal biopsies were collected to generate transcriptomes of circulating immune cell types and gut tissues for expression quantitative trait locus analysis of inflammatory bowel disease risk loci.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Common health conditions such as heart disease, stroke and depression are a common cause of chronic suffering and economic burden worldwide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 24 084 adult participants, including 5501 families, were recruited between 2006 and 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2006 and 2011, over 24 000 adult volunteer participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or participated by post, and consented to genetic studies, linkage to their medical records and to be recontacted for future research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, potential participants aged 35–65 years (study probands) were selected from lists of collaborating general medical practices in Scotland. They were invited to participate in the study and asked to identify at least one adult (18+ years old) first-degree relative to invite to the study. This included volunteers from the Glasgow and Tayside areas from 2006 to 2011 and was extended to include Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GS was founded as a multi-institutional, cross-disciplinary collaboration between the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and the National Health Service (NHS) Scotland, with key resources, expertise and input from the Medical Research Council Human Genetics Unit, the National eScience Centre and the Scottish School of Primary Care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Generation Scotland (GS) is a large family-based cohort study established as a longitudinal resource for research into the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of physical and mental health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29040551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38908846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11340249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 126 000 individuals were invited to participate, of whom 6665 responded and met the study criteria (response rate of 5.3%). An additional 17 419 family members were recruited via these probands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000433> "A family-based population cohort of 24,084 adults, including 5,501 families, recruited in Scotland between 2006 and 2011 by Generation Scotland, a collaboration of the Universities of Aberdeen, Dundee, Edinburgh and Glasgow and NHS Scotland. It comprises 6,665 probands aged 35–65, selected from lists of collaborating general practices in the Glasgow and Tayside areas (extended to Ayrshire, Arran and Grampian in 2010), and 17,419 of their adult relatives. Participants completed questionnaires, attended a clinic visit or took part by post, gave DNA for genome-wide genotyping and consented to record linkage and recontact, for the study of the genetic, lifestyle and environmental determinants of common diseases such as heart disease, stroke and depression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15121494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15121494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15121494+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy (GENOA) study enrolled sibships between 1997 and 1999, including 1329 hypertensive non-Hispanic blacks (1057 sibling pairs) from Jackson, Mississippi, 1133 hypertensive non-Hispanic whites (859 sibling pairs) from Rochester, Minnesota, and 752 hypertensive Hispanic whites (627 sibling pairs) from Starr County, Texas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434> "A community-based family study of hypertensive sibships, recruited from 1996 among non-Hispanic Black adults in Jackson, Mississippi, non-Hispanic white adults in Rochester, Minnesota and (initially) Hispanic adults in Starr County, Texas, to identify genes influencing blood pressure and hypertensive target-organ damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15121494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8764761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GENOA is a community-based study in Rochester, MN and Jackson, MS that was established to identify genes influencing blood pressure [33].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434> "A community-based family study of hypertensive sibships, recruited from 1996 among non-Hispanic Black adults in Jackson, Mississippi, non-Hispanic white adults in Rochester, Minnesota and (initially) Hispanic adults in Starr County, Texas, to identify genes influencing blood pressure and hypertensive target-organ damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15121494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8764761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first phase of GENOA (Phase I: 1996–2001), sibships with at least two adults with clinically diagnosed essential hypertension before age 60 were recruited, and all siblings in the sibship were invited to participate regardless of hypertension status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434> "A community-based family study of hypertensive sibships, recruited from 1996 among non-Hispanic Black adults in Jackson, Mississippi, non-Hispanic white adults in Rochester, Minnesota and (initially) Hispanic adults in Starr County, Texas, to identify genes influencing blood pressure and hypertensive target-organ damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15121494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35039093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37169753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10175543/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Epidemiology Network of Arteriopathy (GENOA) study is a community-based study of hypertensive sibships that was designed to investigate the genetics of hypertension and target organ damage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000434> "A community-based family study of hypertensive sibships, recruited from 1996 among non-Hispanic Black adults in Jackson, Mississippi, non-Hispanic white adults in Rochester, Minnesota and (initially) Hispanic adults in Starr County, Texas, to identify genes influencing blood pressure and hypertensive target-organ damage.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12095082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) [17] is a birth cohort of pregnant women and their offspring from the Finnish provinces of Oulu and Lapland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12095082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1986 (NFBC1986) [19] was initiated 20 years after the NFBC1966 in the same two northernmost provinces of Finland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12095082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from two general population birth cohort studies, Northern Finland Birth Cohorts 1966 and 1986 (NFBC1966 and NFBC1986).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the Northern Finland Birth Cohorts – Research program for health and well-being cohort members have been studied on a regular basis since the fetal period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Northern Finland Birth Cohorts comprise collections of data from large population studies that are administrated by the Infrastructure for Population Studies at the Medical Faculty, University of Oulu.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39820013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/university/faculties-and-units/faculty-medicine/northern-finland-birth-cohorts-and-arctic-biobank") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Northern Finland Birth Cohorts form a longitudinal research program which aims to promote health and well-being of the population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000435> "A longitudinal research programme of the University of Oulu comprising two general-population birth cohorts from the two northernmost provinces of Finland, Oulu and Lapland, the Northern Finland Birth Cohort 1966 (NFBC1966) and 1986 (NFBC1986), whose members have been followed since the fetal period to study health and well-being.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903657/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As of August 2021, a total of 151,406 volunteers have joined the biobank, among which 37,508 have completed the first round of follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903657/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At recruitment, participants provided a written informed consent and had their baseline data collected through questionnaires, physical examination, and blood and urine tests (Figure 1A; Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903657/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nearly all individuals are of Han Chinese descent (Figure 2A), reflective of the ancestry composition in Taiwan.2 We demonstrate the biobank characteristics using a TWB release containing 108,955 individuals with genome-wide genotype data available at the time of our analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36776991+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A linkage to Taiwan's National Health Insurance database of >25 years and other registries is underway to enrich the phenotypic spectrum and enable deep and longitudinal genetic investigations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36776991+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TWB provides one of the largest biobank resources for biomedical and public health research in East Asia that will contribute to our understanding of the genetic basis of health and disease in global populations through collaborative studies with other biobanks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36776991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36776991+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Taiwan Biobank (TWB) is an ongoing prospective study of >150,000 individuals aged 20-70 in Taiwan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000436> "An ongoing prospective population biobank of more than 150,000 predominantly Han Chinese volunteers aged 20-70 recruited across Taiwan, with questionnaire, physical-measurement, biomarker and genome-wide genetic data and linkage to national health insurance records, built as a resource for biomedical and public health research in East Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35130028+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected a prospective cohort of 7342 individuals (64% women, mean age 56 years) and estimated their 10-year risk for atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease both by a traditional risk score and a composite score combining the effect of a polygenic risk score and clinical risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37907536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, online advertising was used to recruit 1116 blood donors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37907536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Further 1369 individuals were recruited from customers of Helsinki and Turku offices of a private and occupational health care provider.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37907536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from the Kymenlaakso province in South-Eastern Finland by identifying 4857 individuals from the population register at random and inviting them by mail.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37907536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort includes 7292 participants (4642 women, 2624 men), who were recruited from Southern Finland during 2015–2017 at age of 45–66 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35130028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37907536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use data from the prospective GeneRISK cohort46 whose principal aim is to assess the impact of communication of genetic risk information of CVD to study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000437> "A prospective cohort of about 7,300 adults aged 45-66 recruited in southern Finland in 2015-2017 (from the Kymenlaakso population register, occupational health care customers in Helsinki and Turku, and blood donors) to assess the impact of communicating genetic risk information for cardiovascular disease to participants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3040595/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our baseline is representative of working-age African Americans and whites between 30–64 years old recruited as a fixed cohort of participants by household screenings from an area probability sample of twelve neighborhoods (contiguous census tracts) in Baltimore City and one dress rehearsal neighborhood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3040595/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With this background, we developed the Healthy Aging in Neighborhoods of Disparities across the Life Span (HANDLS) study to investigate whether race and SES influence health status and age-related health disparities separately or synergistically as co-factors of behavioral, psychosocial, and environmental conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20828101+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We designed a multidisciplinary, community-based, prospective longitudinal epidemiologic study among socioeconomically diverse African Americans and Whites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20828101+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 3722 participants from Baltimore, Md. with a mean age of 47.7 (range 30-64) years, 45% males; 2200 African Americans (59%) and 1522 whites (41%); 41% reported household incomes below the 125% poverty delimiter.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13274012/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Black and White participants aged 30–64 years old in Baltimore City were recruited in a four-way factorial cross of sex, age, race, and poverty status (defined by self-reported household incomes above/below 125% of the 2004 Federal Poverty Guidelines) between 2004 and 2009 [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20828101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42050538") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://handls.nih.gov/01Design.htm") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The area probability sample was designed to sample a wide range of socioeconomic and income circumstances in a 4-way factorial cross of age (seven five-year age bands between 30-64), sex, race, and socioeconomic status indexed by poverty status (below or above 125% of the Federal Poverty Guidelines for 2004).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000438> "A community-based prospective longitudinal cohort of 3,722 socioeconomically diverse African American and white adults aged 30-64, recruited between 2004 and 2009 by household screening from an area probability sample of 13 neighbourhoods of Baltimore, Maryland, in a factorial design by age, sex, race and poverty status, to examine how race and socioeconomic status influence the development of age-related health disparities.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33813036") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients (>18 years of age) were enrolled during their standard of care colonoscopy visit while non-IBD control subjects were undergoing colon cancer screening (Figure 1A).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were used for DNA extraction, and genotype data generated using the high-density Illumina Multi-Ethnic Global Array (MEGAEX) and Infinium ImmunoArray-24 v2 BeadChip arrays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with UC (n=484) or CD (n=464) and HCs (ages 18+, n=365) were recruited as part of a cross-sectional study, the Mount Sinai Crohn’s and Colitis Registry (MSCCR), between December 2013 and September 2016 from the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed fluorescence-activated cell sorting or CyTOF analysis on blood from 728 Crohn’s disease, 464 ulcerative colitis, and 334 non-IBD patients, with available demographics, endoscopic and clinical examinations and medication use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mount Sinai Crohn’s and Colitis registry (MSCCR is a prospective cross-sectional cohort consisting of ~1500 IBD patients and controls recruited during their endoscopy visit from December 2013–September 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8263768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873918/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9214725/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10014487/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Paired blood and biopsy RNA sequencing (RNA-Seq) data were generated at the time of clinical, histological and endoscopic assessments (Figure 1a).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000439> "A prospective cross-sectional cohort of about 1,500 adults with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls (people undergoing colon cancer screening), recruited between December 2013 and September 2016 during their endoscopy visits to the outpatient and endoscopy units of the Mount Sinai Hospital, with paired intestinal biopsies and blood samples, RNA sequencing, genotype data and clinical, endoscopic and histological assessments for molecular studies of inflammatory bowel disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6878352") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In line with the rationales mentioned earlier, NESDA was designed as a naturalistic, longitudinal cohort study including respondents from different health care settings (community, primary care and specialized mental health care) and in different stages of the devel- opmental history of disorders (normals, high familial risk, subthreshold disorders, first and recurrent epi- sodes).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18763692+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Its design is an eight-year longitudinal cohort study among 2981 participants aged 18 through 65 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33773360+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NESDA sample recruited initially 2329 persons with a remitted or current DSM-IV based depressive (major depressive disorder, dysthymia) and/or anxiety disorder (panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia, generalized anxiety disorder), 367 of their siblings and 652 healthy controls, yielding a total of 3348 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33773360+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety (NESDA, www.nesda.nl) is a longitudinal, multi-site, naturalistic, case-control cohort study set up to examine the etiology, course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2004 we recruited 2981 participants with and without symptoms from primary care practices and specialised mental health institutions in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18763692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33773360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nesda.nl/researchers/about-nesda/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 2014, we have also included 367 brothers and sisters of NESDA respondents and we are currently recruiting the offspring of participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000440> "A multi-site naturalistic longitudinal case-control cohort in the Netherlands of 2,981 adults aged 18-65, 2,329 with a current or remitted depressive and/or anxiety disorder and 652 healthy controls, recruited from 2004 in the general population, primary care and specialised mental health care in the regions of Amsterdam, Leiden and Groningen, extended from 2014 with 367 of their siblings to 3,348 participants and reassessed repeatedly over more than nine years, to study the aetiology, long-term course and consequences of depressive and anxiety disorders by integrating psychological, social, biological and genetic factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40044514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7218493/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health, Aging, and Body Composition (Health ABC) study11 was a prospective longitudinal observational study designed to assess the association of body composition with physical function and disability in older adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> "A prospective cohort of 3,075 community-dwelling Black and white adults aged 70-79, recruited from 1997 from white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible Black residents in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania and Memphis, Tennessee, and followed for about 17 years to study body composition, functional decline and disease in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40044514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7218493/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study enrolled 3075 well-functioning community-dwelling older adults aged 70 to 79 years at enrollment from a random sample of white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible black residents in designated zip code areas in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and Memphis, Tennessee, between March 1997 and July 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> "A prospective cohort of 3,075 community-dwelling Black and white adults aged 70-79, recruited from 1997 from white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible Black residents in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania and Memphis, Tennessee, and followed for about 17 years to study body composition, functional decline and disease in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40044514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health ABC Study began in 1997 and collected data for 17 years on a cohort of older Black and White adults living in Memphis and Pittsburgh.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> "A prospective cohort of 3,075 community-dwelling Black and white adults aged 70-79, recruited from 1997 from white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible Black residents in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania and Memphis, Tennessee, and followed for about 17 years to study body composition, functional decline and disease in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40044514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health, Aging and Body Composition Study (Health ABC) is an interdisciplinary study focused on risk factors for functional decline in older adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> "A prospective cohort of 3,075 community-dwelling Black and white adults aged 70-79, recruited from 1997 from white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible Black residents in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania and Memphis, Tennessee, and followed for about 17 years to study body composition, functional decline and disease in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32396194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40044514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://healthabc.nia.nih.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While the study is no longer recruiting participants, it can be used as a resource to investigate the relationship between body composition and age-related diseases and disability.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000441> "A prospective cohort of 3,075 community-dwelling Black and white adults aged 70-79, recruited from 1997 from white Medicare beneficiaries and all eligible Black residents in and around Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania and Memphis, Tennessee, and followed for about 17 years to study body composition, functional decline and disease in older age.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9932985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this article, we describe the Michigan Genomics Initiative (MGI), a single-health-system biobank recruited from adult patients receiving care at Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan’s health system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442> "A single-health-system biobank of more than 91,000 adult patients recruited mainly during surgical encounters at Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, linking genotypes to electronic health records for disease genetics research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36819667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we describe the Michigan Genomics Initiative (MGI), a single-health-system biobank currently consisting of >91,000 participants recruited primarily during surgical encounters at Michigan Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442> "A single-health-system biobank of more than 91,000 adult patients recruited mainly during surgical encounters at Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, linking genotypes to electronic health records for disease genetics research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36819667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Michigan Genomics Initiative: A biobank linking genotypes and electronic clinical records in Michigan Medicine patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442> "A single-health-system biobank of more than 91,000 adult patients recruited mainly during surgical encounters at Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, linking genotypes to electronic health records for disease genetics research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36819667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36819667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The surgical enrollment results in a biobank enriched for many diseases and ideally suited for a disease genetics cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000442> "A single-health-system biobank of more than 91,000 adult patients recruited mainly during surgical encounters at Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, linking genotypes to electronic health records for disease genetics research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42378311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Although this cohort was ascertained for children with autism spectrum disorder (ASD) and other neurodevelopmental disorders (DD), we gained novel insight into how maternal and fetal genetics shape levels of immune mediators in pregnancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> "A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42378311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our current IMPaCT (Immune and Metabolic Markers during Pregnancy and Child Development) study also oversamples pregnancies resulting in children with ASD and DD, and matches general population (GP) controls to these demographics [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> "A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All mothers had previously consented to participate in the Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health (RPGEH) pregnancy cohort (25), including donation of a blood sample during the first and second trimesters of pregnancy and permission to access their own and their child’s KPNC electronic health records (EHRs) for future studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> "A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population for the IMPaCT (Immune and Metabolic Markers during Pregnancy and Child Development) Study was selected from children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) from January 2011 to January 2016, who survived to age 2 years and whose mothers received health care during the 2 years prior to delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> "A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689278/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a case-control study among children born in California from 2011 to 2016 to investigate maternal immune-mediated and cardiometabolic conditions during pregnancy and risk of ASD (n = 311) and DDs (n = 1291) compared with children from the general population (n = 967).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000443> "A case-control study of mothers and children born at Kaiser Permanente Northern California from January 2011 to January 2016, oversampling children later diagnosed with autism spectrum disorder or other developmental delay alongside general-population controls, with maternal first- and second-trimester blood samples from the RPGEH pregnancy cohort, to study maternal immune and metabolic markers and child neurodevelopment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20031568") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20031568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20031568+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium was formed to facilitate genome-wide association studies meta-analyses and replication opportunities among multiple large population-based cohort studies, which collect data in a standardized fashion and represent the preferred method for estimating disease incidence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444> "A consortium of large prospective population-based cohort studies from the United States and Europe, founded with the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility-Reykjavik Study, the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Heart Study and the Rotterdam Study, formed to facilitate genome-wide association meta-analyses and replication across cohorts with similarly measured phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20031568") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20031568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20031568+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The design of the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium includes 5 prospective cohort studies from the United States and Europe: the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility-Reykjavik Study, the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Heart Study, and the Rotterdam Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000444> "A consortium of large prospective population-based cohort studies from the United States and Europe, founded with the Age, Gene/Environment Susceptibility-Reykjavik Study, the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Heart Study and the Rotterdam Study, formed to facilitate genome-wide association meta-analyses and replication across cohorts with similarly measured phenotypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27699078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27699078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5036950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We studied 1082 subjects belonging to the Helsinki Birth Cohort Study (born 1934-1944), undergoing two visits (2001-2004 and 2011-2014).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445> "A birth cohort of the 13,345 singletons born in one of the two maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland, between 1934 and 1944, followed up in later life to study how early life shapes adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27699078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our study comprising 1872 participants from the Helsinki Birth Cohort Study born in 1934–1944, we investigated the association of various forms of ELS and their accumulation with self-reported anxiety symptoms at the age of 65–77 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445> "A birth cohort of the 13,345 singletons born in one of the two maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland, between 1934 and 1944, followed up in later life to study how early life shapes adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27699078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study sample is a part of the Helsinki Birth Cohort Study (HBCS), comprising all 13345 individuals (52.3% male) born singleton in one of the two maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland, between 1934 and 1944.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445> "A birth cohort of the 13,345 singletons born in one of the two maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland, between 1934 and 1944, followed up in later life to study how early life shapes adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27699078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6416302/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/hbcs") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main aim of HBCS is to assess the importance of early life factor on later health outcomes taking into account adult lifestyle, socioeconomic factors and genetic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000445> "A birth cohort of the 13,345 singletons born in one of the two maternity hospitals in Helsinki, Finland, between 1934 and 1944, followed up in later life to study how early life shapes adult health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5233749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection in parents and their children included questionnaires, interviews, detailed physical and ultrasound examinations, behavioural observations, lung function, Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) and biological sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> "A population-based prospective cohort from fetal life onwards of 9,778 mothers with delivery dates from April 2002 to January 2006 in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, and their children, designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes of normal and abnormal growth, development and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5233749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women with an expected delivery date between April 2002 and January 2006 living in Rotterdam were eligible for participation in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> "A population-based prospective cohort from fetal life onwards of 9,778 mothers with delivery dates from April 2002 to January 2006 in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, and their children, designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes of normal and abnormal growth, development and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28070760+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 9778 mothers with a delivery date from April 2002 until January 2006 were enrolled in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> "A population-based prospective cohort from fetal life onwards of 9,778 mothers with delivery dates from April 2002 to January 2006 in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, and their children, designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes of normal and abnormal growth, development and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28070760+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Generation R Study is a population-based prospective cohort study from fetal life until adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> "A population-based prospective cohort from fetal life onwards of 9,778 mothers with delivery dates from April 2002 to January 2006 in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, and their children, designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes of normal and abnormal growth, development and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28070760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28070760+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes and causal pathways leading to normal and abnormal growth, development and health from fetal life, childhood and young adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000446> "A population-based prospective cohort from fetal life onwards of 9,778 mothers with delivery dates from April 2002 to January 2006 in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, and their children, designed to identify early environmental and genetic causes of normal and abnormal growth, development and health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/500fg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5787854/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In three studies within the Human Functional Genomics Project we assessed the effect of environmental and non-genetic host factors, of the genetic make-up of the host, and of the intestinal microbiome, on the cytokine responses in humans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> "A cohort of about 500 healthy adult volunteers of Western European ancestry recruited at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in 2013–2014 within the Human Functional Genomics Project, to study how genetic, environmental, host and microbiome factors shape individual cytokine and immune responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/500fg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5787854/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion of the volunteers took place between 8/2013 until 12/2014 in the Radboud University Medical Center, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> "A cohort of about 500 healthy adult volunteers of Western European ancestry recruited at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in 2013–2014 within the Human Functional Genomics Project, to study how genetic, environmental, host and microbiome factors shape individual cytokine and immune responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/500fg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5787854/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was approved by the Ethical Committee of Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen (NL42561.091.12, 2012/550).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> "A cohort of about 500 healthy adult volunteers of Western European ancestry recruited at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in 2013–2014 within the Human Functional Genomics Project, to study how genetic, environmental, host and microbiome factors shape individual cytokine and immune responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/500fg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5787854/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within HFGP, the first major study that intends to assess the variability of human cytokine responses is the 500 Functional Genomics (500FG) study, comprising of a group of approximately 500 healthy volunteers of Western-European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> "A cohort of about 500 healthy adult volunteers of Western European ancestry recruited at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in 2013–2014 within the Human Functional Genomics Project, to study how genetic, environmental, host and microbiome factors shape individual cytokine and immune responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27814508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/500fg/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38326779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 500FG cohort is a population-based cohort of healthy individuals of Western European ancestry consisting of 237 males and 296 females with age range of 18-75 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000447> "A cohort of about 500 healthy adult volunteers of Western European ancestry recruited at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, in 2013–2014 within the Human Functional Genomics Project, to study how genetic, environmental, host and microbiome factors shape individual cytokine and immune responses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4981567/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of a collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center DNA samples are also used for exome sequencing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4981567/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Geisinger Health System (GHS), an integrated health system located in north central and northeastern PA, possesses a unique combination of resources to accelerate clinical translational research 1–3.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26866580+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2007, Geisinger launched MyCode, a system-wide biobanking program to link samples and EHR data for broad research use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26866580+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MyCode samples have been used to generate molecular data, including high-density genotype and exome sequence data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26866580+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participation in MyCode is based on opt-in informed consent and allows recontact, which facilitates collection of data not in the EHR and, since 2013, the return of clinically actionable results to participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26866580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36192519") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9529959/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GHS MyCode study is a health system-based cohort of patients from Central and Eastern Pennsylvania (USA) recruited in 2007–2019") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000448> "A biobank cohort of patients of Geisinger Health System, an integrated health system in central and eastern Pennsylvania, United States, who since 2007 have given opt-in consent to link their samples to electronic health record data for broad research use, with genotype and exome sequence data generated in collaboration with the Regeneron Genetics Center.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8562028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were drawn from the customer base of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> "A cohort of customers of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company, who have been genotyped and have consented to take part in online research, answering web-based questionnaires under an IRB-approved protocol, whose genotype and self-reported data are used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8562028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided informed consent and participated in the research online, under a protocol approved by the external AAHRPP-accredited IRB, Ethical & Independent Review Services (www.eandireview.com).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> "A cohort of customers of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company, who have been genotyped and have consented to take part in online research, answering web-based questionnaires under an IRB-approved protocol, whose genotype and self-reported data are used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8562028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To test this hypothesis, we performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of problematic opioid use (POU) in 23andMe research participants of European ancestry (N = 132,113; 21% cases).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> "A cohort of customers of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company, who have been genotyped and have consented to take part in online research, answering web-based questionnaires under an IRB-approved protocol, whose genotype and self-reported data are used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3121750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Determination of case status was conducted through a set of online questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> "A cohort of customers of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company, who have been genotyped and have consented to take part in online research, answering web-based questionnaires under an IRB-approved protocol, whose genotype and self-reported data are used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34728798") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3121750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These two SNPs, both rare variants, were included as part of the custom set of variants used to genotype the 23andMe cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000449> "A cohort of customers of 23andMe, Inc., a direct-to-consumer genetics company, who have been genotyped and have consented to take part in online research, answering web-based questionnaires under an IRB-approved protocol, whose genotype and self-reported data are used for genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26197779+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our objective is to investigate prevalences, early onset markers, genetic predispositions, and the role of lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases, with primary focus on metabolic and vascular diseases, heart function, cognitive impairment, brain function, depression, sleep disorders and vigilance dysregulation, retinal and optic nerve degeneration, and allergies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> "A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26197779+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LIFE-Adult-Study is a population-based cohort study, which has recently completed the baseline examination of 10,000 randomly selected participants from Leipzig, a major city with 550,000 inhabitants in the east of Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> "A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26197779+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline examination was conducted from August 2011 to November 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> "A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26197779+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study covers a main age range from 40-79 years with particular deep phenotyping in elderly participants above the age of 60.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> "A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26197779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26197779+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is conducted by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000450> "A population-based cohort of 10,000 randomly selected adults, mainly aged 40–79, from the city of Leipzig in eastern Germany, examined in 2011–2014 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) with deep phenotyping to study the prevalence, early markers, genetic predispositions and lifestyle factors of major civilization diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30267427+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A questionnaire to assess pica, restless leg syndrome, iron supplementation, hormone use, and menstrual and pregnancy history was completed at enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30267427+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 13,403 racially/ethnically diverse (12% African American, 12% Asian, 8% Hispanic, 64% white, and 5% multiracial/other) donors of both sexes were enrolled and ranged from 18 to 90 years of age; 15% were high-intensity donors (nine or more donations in the prior 24 mo without low hemoglobin deferral).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30267427+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Red Blood Cell (RBC)-Omics study was initiated to build a large data set containing behavioral, genetic, and biochemical characteristics of blood donors with linkage to outcomes of the patients transfused with their donated RBCs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6361628/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment began in December 2013 and was conducted over a 22-month period ending in October 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6361628/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RBC-Omics cohort was recruited from four large blood centers across the United States: the American Red Cross (ARC, Farmington, CT), the Institute for Transfusion Medicine (ITxM, Pittsburgh, PA), BloodCenter of Wisconsin (BCW, Milwaukee, WI), and the Blood Centers of the Pacific (BCP, San Francisco, CA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267427") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36395887") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36395887+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The red blood cell (RBC)-Omics study, part of the larger NHLBI-funded Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study (REDS-III), aims to understand the genetic contribution to blood donor RBC characteristics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000451> "A cohort of 13,403 racially and ethnically diverse volunteer blood donors aged 18 or older, enrolled from December 2013 to October 2015 at four large blood centres across the United States (in Connecticut, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and California) by the NHLBI Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III), who completed a questionnaire and gave blood for blood counts, ferritin and DNA and a sample of their red cells for haemolysis testing at the end of storage, with donors of extreme haemolysis recalled for a second donation, to study the genetic and biological determinants of donor iron metabolism, pica, restless legs syndrome and red cell storage haemolysis, and to link donors to the outcomes of the patients transfused with their red cells.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000452> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000452>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27125947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2965351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 2101 cases and 3914 controls (of which 1453 were unique) formed the final genotyped COROGENE case-control sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000452> "A prospective cohort of consecutive Finnish patients referred for coronary angiography at Helsinki University Central Hospital in 2006–2008, assembled to study the genetic predisposition to coronary heart disease; its acute coronary syndrome cases, with controls sampled from FINRISK, form a genotyped case-control sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27125947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2965351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of these patients, 2118 (53%) had acute coronary syndrome and were selected as COROGENE cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000452> "A prospective cohort of consecutive Finnish patients referred for coronary angiography at Helsinki University Central Hospital in 2006–2008, assembled to study the genetic predisposition to coronary heart disease; its acute coronary syndrome cases, with controls sampled from FINRISK, form a genotyped case-control sample.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27125947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20971364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2965351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls for COROGENE cases were selected from the Helsinki-Vantaa region participants of FINRISK 1997, 2002, and 2007 by risk set sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000452> "A prospective cohort of consecutive Finnish patients referred for coronary angiography at Helsinki University Central Hospital in 2006–2008, assembled to study the genetic predisposition to coronary heart disease; its acute coronary syndrome cases, with controls sampled from FINRISK, form a genotyped case-control sample.")
