# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4149396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was a cross-sectional observational study of patients admitted to MMT for the treatment of opioid addiction at four clinical sites of the Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres (OATC), between June and December 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4827793/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study utilized patient data collected for the Genetics of Opioid Addiction (GENOA) Research Collaborative between the Population Genomics Program at McMaster University and the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (CATC, formerly known as the Ontario Addiction Treatment Centre and home to the largest network of methadone clinics in North America) and the Peter Boris Centre for Addiction Research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10370765/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected as part of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction (GENOA) pilot, GENOA and Pharmacogenetics of Opioid Substitution Treatment Response (POST) programs, prospective cohort studies designed to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes in patients diagnosed with OUD and receiving treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10370765/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants with genotyped data available (nGENOA PILOT = 182, nGENOA = 1314, nPOST = 3125) were recruited from 76 Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (CATC) sites across Ontario, Canada, from 2011–2012, 2013 to 2016 and 2018 to 2022 for the GENOA pilot, GENOA and POST, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As previously reported, participants were followed for a 12-month period through their electronic medical record which documented their weekly or biweekly Urine Drug Screens (UDS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25187714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27103815") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37494403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, participants (nGENOA = 1536, nPOST = 3319) were recruited from 76 CATC sites across Ontario, Canada (GENOA, 2013–2016, POST, 2018–present).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000467> "A prospective cohort of adults with opioid use disorder receiving treatment, mainly methadone maintenance treatment, at Canadian Addiction Treatment Centre (formerly Ontario Addiction Treatment Centres) clinics in Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University with the clinics in a pilot at four clinics in 2011–2012 and a main phase in 2013–2016 (about 1,500 participants, interviewed at entry, giving blood for DNA and followed through the urine drug screens in their medical records), to identify factors, including genetic risk factors, associated with opioid use and treatment outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8596997/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Photographs were taken at the same time plasma samples were collected from participants in the deCODE Health study (18) and scored for the presence and severity of osteoarthritis, resulting in an aggregate score.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8190123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DHS dataset is based on audiometric measures for 11,484 Icelanders, including 4140 ARHI cases (PTA > 25 dB HL) and 7344 controls, who are part of a comprehensive phenotyping of a general population sample enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high impact mutations25.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DXA body composition was measured in the deCODE Health Study using DEXA by Hologic (S/N200547).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Speech samples were obtained from 14,144 Icelandic participants as a part of the deCODE Health Study in Iceland, which involves comprehensive phenotyping of a general population sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These phenotypes were collected through the deCODE Health Study and other research projects at deCODE genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33982893") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34108613") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37294764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10256171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed 39.2 million high-quality sequence variants, detected through whole-genome sequencing of 63,460 Icelanders and imputed into 173,025 chip-typed Icelanders and their relatives (43, 44).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000468> "A general-population sample of Icelanders, enriched for carriers of rare and potentially high-impact mutations, comprehensively phenotyped by deCODE genetics in Iceland (e.g. audiometry, speech recordings, DXA body composition, plasma proteomics) and combined with the Icelandic genotype and sequence data for genetic association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment to the pilot was initiated on the 11th December 2012 and we report on data collected to 20th February 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> "A population-based prospective cohort of adult Qatari nationals and long-term residents (living in Qatar for at least 15 years), recruited by the Qatar Biobank from December 2012 with extensive lifestyle, clinical, imaging and biological-sample data and long-term follow-up, to study the causes, progression and burden of disease in the Qatari population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Qatar Biobank aims to collect extensive lifestyle, clinical, and biological information from up to 60,000 men and women Qatari nationals and long-term residents (individuals living in the country for ≥15 years) aged ≥18 years (approximately one-fifth of all Qatari citizens), to follow up these same individuals over the long term to record any subsequent disease, and hence to study the causes and progression of disease, and disease burden, in the Qatari population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> "A population-based prospective cohort of adult Qatari nationals and long-term residents (living in Qatar for at least 15 years), recruited by the Qatar Biobank from December 2012 with extensive lifestyle, clinical, imaging and biological-sample data and long-term follow-up, to study the causes, progression and burden of disease in the Qatari population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Qatar Biobank involves collection of extensive questionnaire information, clinical phenotyping and biological samples from Qatari nationals and long-term residents (≥15 years living in Qatar) aged 18 or more years, who comprise the eligible population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> "A population-based prospective cohort of adult Qatari nationals and long-term residents (living in Qatar for at least 15 years), recruited by the Qatar Biobank from December 2012 with extensive lifestyle, clinical, imaging and biological-sample data and long-term follow-up, to study the causes, progression and burden of disease in the Qatari population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Qatar Biobank was set up by the Qatar Foundation and the Supreme Council of Health in collaboration with Imperial College London, as the first Qatar national population based prospective cohort study, and includes the collection of biological samples, with long-term storage of data and samples for future research (biobank).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> "A population-based prospective cohort of adult Qatari nationals and long-term residents (living in Qatar for at least 15 years), recruited by the Qatar Biobank from December 2012 with extensive lifestyle, clinical, imaging and biological-sample data and long-term follow-up, to study the causes, progression and burden of disease in the Qatari population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26635005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4669623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These include data from questionnaires, extensive clinical measurements and imaging, and biological samples (blood, urine, and saliva), which are being stored long-term, with consent, for future (unspecified) research use including for genetic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000469> "A population-based prospective cohort of adult Qatari nationals and long-term residents (living in Qatar for at least 15 years), recruited by the Qatar Biobank from December 2012 with extensive lifestyle, clinical, imaging and biological-sample data and long-term follow-up, to study the causes, progression and burden of disease in the Qatari population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20736269") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2723948/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AGES-Reykjavik stems from the Reykjavik Study, a cohort established in 1967 to prospectively study cardiovascular disease in Iceland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> "A population-based cohort of men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, randomly selected from residents of the Reykjavik area, examined at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik from 1967 and followed since in Iceland by the Icelandic Heart Association, to study cardiovascular disease and its risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20736269") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17351290+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AGES-Reykjavik sample is drawn from an established population-based cohort, the Reykjavik Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> "A population-based cohort of men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, randomly selected from residents of the Reykjavik area, examined at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik from 1967 and followed since in Iceland by the Icelandic Heart Association, to study cardiovascular disease and its risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20736269") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17351290+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort of men and women born between 1907 and 1935 has been followed in Iceland since 1967 by the Icelandic Heart Association.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> "A population-based cohort of men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, randomly selected from residents of the Reykjavik area, examined at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik from 1967 and followed since in Iceland by the Icelandic Heart Association, to study cardiovascular disease and its risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20736269") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3133934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, residing in the Reykjavik area and a few adjacent communities on 1 December 1966, were randomly selected for participation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> "A population-based cohort of men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, randomly selected from residents of the Reykjavik area, examined at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik from 1967 and followed since in Iceland by the Icelandic Heart Association, to study cardiovascular disease and its risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17351290") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20736269") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19438929") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3133934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study cohort, which was divided into six groups of men and women, was investigated at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik during the period 1967–1996 (CRP was not measured in the sixth group n=478, and therefore this group was omitted from the analysis).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000470> "A population-based cohort of men born 1907–1934 and women born 1908–1935, randomly selected from residents of the Reykjavik area, examined at the Heart Preventive Clinic in Reykjavik from 1967 and followed since in Iceland by the Icelandic Heart Association, to study cardiovascular disease and its risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38326779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both cohorts are part of the Human Functional Genomics Project (wwww.humanfunctionalgenomics.org), aimed at identifying the genetic and non-genetic determinants of the immune response.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2000HIV This study consists of 1895 participants living with HIV.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5787854/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion of the volunteers took place between 8/2013 until 12/2014 in the Radboud University Medical Center, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both cohorts are part of the Human Functional Genomics Project (wwww.humanfunctionalgenomics.org), aimed at identifying the genetic and non-genetic determinants of the immune response.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 300-Obese (300-OB) cohort, one of the studies of the Human Functional Genomics Project, comprises a group of more than 300 individuals of Western-European ancestry with a body mass index (BMI) greater than or equal to greater than or equal to 27 kg/m2, aged between 55 and 80 years (12).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In three studies within the Human Functional Genomics Project we assessed the effect of environmental and non-genetic host factors, of the genetic make-up of the host, and of the intestinal microbiome, on the cytokine responses in humans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HFGP aims to understand the individual sources of variability in immune responses by studying human cytokine production capacity in response to a comprehensive panel of microbial and metabolic stimuli.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://humanfunctionalgenomics.org/projects/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10851559/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5787854/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within HFGP, the first major study that intends to assess the variability of human cytokine responses is the 500 Functional Genomics (500FG) study, comprising of a group of approximately 500 healthy volunteers of Western-European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000471> "A research programme based at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, that collects distinct cohorts of healthy volunteers and patients (among them 500FG, 200FG, 300BCG, 300OB, 300DM and 2000HIV) profiled with genetic, immunological and other omics data, to identify the genetic and non-genetic determinants of human immune and cytokine responses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, there will be numerous analyses of large \"core\" databases; the international programs have each constructed a donor and donation database while the domestic program has established a detailed research database that links data from blood donors and their donations, the components made from these donations, and data extracts from the electronic medical records of the recipients of these components.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Second, there are more than 25 focused research protocols involving transfusion recipients, blood donors, or both that either are in progress or are scheduled to begin within the next 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Recipient Epidemiology and Donor Evaluation Study-III (REDS-III) is a 7-year multicenter transfusion safety research initiative launched in 2011 by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The domestic component involves four blood centers, 12 hospitals, a data coordinating center, and a central laboratory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24188564+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The international component consists of distinct programs in Brazil, China, and South Africa, which involve US and in-country investigators.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24188564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10155195/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was conducted within the Brazil Sickle Cell Disease Cohort Study as part of the Recipient Epidemiology Donor Evaluation Study III (REDS-III).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000472> "A seven-year multicentre transfusion-medicine research programme launched in 2011 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, with a domestic component of four blood centres and 12 hospitals and international programmes in Brazil, China and South Africa, which built linked donor, donation and transfusion-recipient databases and ran more than 25 focused studies of blood donors and recipients, such as RBC-Omics and the Brazil sickle cell disease cohort.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All mothers had previously provided written consent to participate in the Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health (RPGEH) pregnancy cohort [61], including donation of a blood sample during the first and second trimesters of pregnancy and permission to access their own and their child’s KPNC electronic health records for future studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473> "A research resource developed by the Kaiser Permanente Northern California Division of Research from consenting members of the KPNC health plan, linking surveys, biospecimens and electronic health records and including the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and a pregnancy cohort, for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GERA cohort is part of the Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473> "A research resource developed by the Kaiser Permanente Northern California Division of Research from consenting members of the KPNC health plan, linking surveys, biospecimens and electronic health records and including the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and a pregnancy cohort, for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RPGEH was developed by the KPNC Division of Research as a resource that links together surveys, biospecimens and electronic health record data for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473> "A research resource developed by the Kaiser Permanente Northern California Division of Research from consenting members of the KPNC health plan, linking surveys, biospecimens and electronic health records and including the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and a pregnancy cohort, for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340790/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7939422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We thank the Kaiser Permanente Northern California members who have generously agreed to participate in the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000473> "A research resource developed by the Kaiser Permanente Northern California Division of Research from consenting members of the KPNC health plan, linking surveys, biospecimens and electronic health records and including the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and a pregnancy cohort, for research on the genetic and environmental determinants of common, age-related complex health conditions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11164120+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Affected sib-pairs (ASP) along with unaffected spouse controls are being enrolled and examined in West Africa, with two sites established in Ghana (Accra and Kumasi) and three in Nigeria (Enugu, Ibadan, and Lagos).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> "A genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes begun in 1997 as a collaboration of West African and US investigators, enrolling affected sib-pairs with type 2 diabetes and unaffected controls in Ghana and Nigeria and later participants in Eldoret, Kenya, to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in the West African ancestral populations of African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11164120+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this study is to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in West African ancestral populations of African-Americans, through an international collaboration between West African and US investigators.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> "A genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes begun in 1997 as a collaboration of West African and US investigators, enrolling affected sib-pairs with type 2 diabetes and unaffected controls in Ghana and Nigeria and later participants in Eldoret, Kenya, to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in the West African ancestral populations of African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11164120+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With full informed consent, 162 individuals from 78 families have been enrolled and examined since the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus (AADM) study began in June of 1997.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> "A genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes begun in 1997 as a collaboration of West African and US investigators, enrolling affected sib-pairs with type 2 diabetes and unaffected controls in Ghana and Nigeria and later participants in Eldoret, Kenya, to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in the West African ancestral populations of African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34620218") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected in three cities in Nigeria (Ibadan, Enugu, and Lagos), two cities in Ghana (Accra, and Kumasi), and in the city of Eldoret in Kenya.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> "A genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes begun in 1997 as a collaboration of West African and US investigators, enrolling affected sib-pairs with type 2 diabetes and unaffected controls in Ghana and Nigeria and later participants in Eldoret, Kenya, to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in the West African ancestral populations of African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11164120") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8499470/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7202134/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AADM is an ongoing genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes and related traits in Africans") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000474> "A genetic epidemiology study of type 2 diabetes begun in 1997 as a collaboration of West African and US investigators, enrolling affected sib-pairs with type 2 diabetes and unaffected controls in Ghana and Nigeria and later participants in Eldoret, Kenya, to map type 2 diabetes susceptibility genes in the West African ancestral populations of African Americans.")

