AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-022-01042-4/MediaObjects/41593_2022_1042_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-022-01042-4/MediaObjects/41593_2022_1042_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ALS Utrecht | WGS Illumina HiSeq2000 and HiSeqX | None | Called directly") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000506> "A case-control sample of 158 people of European ancestry, patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis and healthy controls, from University Medical Center Utrecht, the Netherlands, with longitudinal 3.0 T brain MRI and whole-genome sequencing, contributed to the ENIGMA Plasticity Working Group genome-wide meta-analysis of brain structure change.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-022-01042-4/MediaObjects/41593_2022_1042_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10040206/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our GWAS meta-analysis, we sought genetic loci associated with annual change rates in 8 global and 7 subcortical morphological brain measures in a coordinated two-phased analysis using data from 40 longitudinal cohorts (Extended Data Fig 1 and Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000506> "A case-control sample of 158 people of European ancestry, patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis and healthy controls, from University Medical Center Utrecht, the Netherlands, with longitudinal 3.0 T brain MRI and whole-genome sequencing, contributed to the ENIGMA Plasticity Working Group genome-wide meta-analysis of brain structure change.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-022-01042-4/MediaObjects/41593_2022_1042_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35383335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10040206/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ENIGMA-Plasticity working group is part of the ENIGMA World Aging Center, funded by NIA grants R56 AG058854- and R01 AG058854.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000506> "A case-control sample of 158 people of European ancestry, patients with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis and healthy controls, from University Medical Center Utrecht, the Netherlands, with longitudinal 3.0 T brain MRI and whole-genome sequencing, contributed to the ENIGMA Plasticity Working Group genome-wide meta-analysis of brain structure change.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3975119/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of this study the BIG subject-pool consisted of 2337 self-reported healthy individuals (1248 females) who had undergone anatomical (T1-weighted) MRI scans, usually as part of their involvement in diverse smaller-scale studies at the DCCN, and who had given their consent to participate in BIG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> "A pool of self-reported healthy volunteers, many of them university students, who took part in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, and consented to pooling of their anatomical MRI scans with DNA for imaging genetics; established in 2007 and now part of the Cognomics initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3975119/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brain Imaging Genetics (BIG) study was initiated in 2007 and comprises healthy volunteer subjects, including many university students, who participate in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging (DCCN), Nijmegen, The Netherlands") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> "A pool of self-reported healthy volunteers, many of them university students, who took part in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, and consented to pooling of their anatomical MRI scans with DNA for imaging genetics; established in 2007 and now part of the Cognomics initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3975119/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The proportion of left-handers in our sample was lower than in the general population, due to an exclusion of left-handers from some of the smaller studies that were pooled to create our BIG dataset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> "A pool of self-reported healthy volunteers, many of them university students, who took part in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, and consented to pooling of their anatomical MRI scans with DNA for imaging genetics; established in 2007 and now part of the Cognomics initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3975119/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This resource is now part of Cognomics (www.cognomics.nl), a joint initiative by researchers of the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging, the Human Genetics and Cognitive Neuroscience departments of the Radboud university medical centre and the Max Planck Institute for Psycholinguistics in Nijmegen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> "A pool of self-reported healthy volunteers, many of them university students, who took part in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, and consented to pooling of their anatomical MRI scans with DNA for imaging genetics; established in 2007 and now part of the Cognomics initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24734025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25013396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4076884/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To obtain DNA, saliva was collected using Oragene containers (DNA Genotek, Ottawa, ON, Canada).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000507> "A pool of self-reported healthy volunteers, many of them university students, who took part in diverse imaging studies at the Donders Centre for Cognitive Neuroimaging in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, and consented to pooling of their anatomical MRI scans with DNA for imaging genetics; established in 2007 and now part of the Cognomics initiative.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Brain scans were acquired using 1.5 Tesla Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), which provided volumetric measures and measures of cortical thickness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Buccal swabs were collected for DNA isolation for future candidate gene and genome-wide analysis studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection included psychometric IQ tests, a comprehensive neuropsychological testing protocol, and parental and self-ratings of behavioral and emotional problems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hormonal levels (cortisol, luteinizing hormone, follicle-stimulating hormone, testosterone, and estrogens) were assessed in urine and saliva.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In The Netherlands, we initiated a longitudinal study in which twins, their siblings and their parents are assessed at three year intervals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were recruited from The Netherlands Twin Register (NTR) and at baseline consisted of 112 families, with 9-year-old twins and an older sibling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000508> "A longitudinal study of Dutch twin families recruited from the Netherlands Twin Register, starting with 112 families of 9-year-old twins and an older sibling who were assessed at three-year intervals with IQ and neuropsychological tests, behavioural ratings, pubertal hormones, brain MRI and DNA collection, to study genetic and environmental influences on brain structure and cognition from childhood into adolescence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our ‘Cognitive Neurogenetics Project’ started in 2003 with the objective of assessing the influence of APOE and other candidate genes relevant for cognition on normal cognitive aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This resulted in a final dataset of 554,225 SNPs genotyped in a homogeneous Norwegian sample of 670 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Another unique property is the large-scale (sample size 300-700) use of experimental cognitive tasks focusing on attention and working memory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection for the Norwegian Cognitive NeuroGenetics sample (NCNG) was initiated in 2003") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2009, a genome-wide association (GWA) study was undertaken, and the NCNG proper was established to study the genetics of cognitive and brain function more comprehensively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22856377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22856377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prominent features of the NCNG are the adult life-span coverage of healthy participants with high-dimensional imaging, and cognitive data from a genetically homogenous sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000509> "A genetically homogeneous sample of healthy Norwegian adults spanning the adult life span, collected from 2003 to study cognitive ageing and genetic risk factors and genome-wide genotyped in 2009, with MRI and experimental cognitive data on attention and working memory, for studies of the genetics of cognitive and brain function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25012461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Collected data include a diagnostic interview, behavioural questionnaires, cognitive measures, structural and functional neuroimaging, and genome-wide genetic information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510> "A multi-site prospective cohort following up the Dutch families of the International Multicenter ADHD Genetics project together with newly recruited families, comprising 1,069 children from ADHD and control families and 848 parents assessed with diagnostic interviews, questionnaires, cognitive tests, structural and functional MRI and genome-wide genotyping, to study the course of ADHD into adolescence and adulthood and its genetic, environmental and neural underpinnings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25012461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Combined with newly recruited participants the NeuroIMAGE study comprehends an assessment of 1,069 children (751 from ADHD families; 318 from CON families) and 848 parents (582 from ADHD families; 266 from CON families).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510> "A multi-site prospective cohort following up the Dutch families of the International Multicenter ADHD Genetics project together with newly recruited families, comprising 1,069 children from ADHD and control families and 848 parents assessed with diagnostic interviews, questionnaires, cognitive tests, structural and functional MRI and genome-wide genotyping, to study the course of ADHD into adolescence and adulthood and its genetic, environmental and neural underpinnings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25012461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is a multi-site prospective cohort study designed to investigate the course of ADHD, its genetic and environmental determinants, its cognitive and neurobiological underpinnings, and its consequences in adolescence and adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510> "A multi-site prospective cohort following up the Dutch families of the International Multicenter ADHD Genetics project together with newly recruited families, comprising 1,069 children from ADHD and control families and 848 parents assessed with diagnostic interviews, questionnaires, cognitive tests, structural and functional MRI and genome-wide genotyping, to study the course of ADHD into adolescence and adulthood and its genetic, environmental and neural underpinnings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25012461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25012461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NeuroIMAGE study is a follow-up of the Dutch part of the International Multicenter ADHD Genetics (IMAGE) project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000510> "A multi-site prospective cohort following up the Dutch families of the International Multicenter ADHD Genetics project together with newly recruited families, comprising 1,069 children from ADHD and control families and 848 parents assessed with diagnostic interviews, questionnaires, cognitive tests, structural and functional MRI and genome-wide genotyping, to study the course of ADHD into adolescence and adulthood and its genetic, environmental and neural underpinnings.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14663300+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The article describes the study and baseline results.MethodsFrom a population of 61,301 individuals two random samples (high intensity intervention group (A), n = 11,708; low intensity intervention group (B), n = 1308) are screened to assess their absolute risk of IHD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14663300+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The total population is followed through central registers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3674994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Inter99 cohort is a randomized, non-pharmacological intervention study for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, conducted on 6,784 randomly ascertained participants aged 30 to 60 years at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Denmark [45] (ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT00289237).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4352560/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From the remaining 48,285 persons in the study population, a random sample of 5,264 persons equally distributed on sex and age was drawn and followed by questionnaires (group C – control group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4352560/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inter99 is a population-based randomized intervention study initiated in March 1999 and completed in April 2006 and conducted at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health, The Capital Region, Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14663300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23754956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25886540") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25886540+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was a population-based randomized controlled trial, Inter99 (1999-2006), Copenhagen, Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000511> "A population-based randomised non-pharmacological lifestyle intervention trial for the prevention of ischaemic heart disease, run in 1999–2006 at the Research Centre for Prevention and Health in Glostrup, Copenhagen, Denmark, on random samples of adults aged 30–60 drawn from a population of 61,301 and followed through questionnaires and central registers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5754466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was extracted from the neonatal dried blood spot samples obtained from the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and genotyped using the Illumina PsychChip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5754466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals diagnosed with schizophrenia, mood disorders, bipolar affective disorder, autism and attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder were identified through linkage between Danish population-based registers along with a random sample of the same population that supplied the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5754466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) consortium has established a large Danish population-based Case–Cohort sample (iPSYCH2012) aimed at unravelling the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5754466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The iPSYCH2012 sample is nested within the entire Danish population born between 1981 and 2005, including 1 472 762 persons.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The newly updated cohort, named iPSYCH2015, expands the study base with 56,233 samples, to a combined total of 141,265 samples. The cohort is nested within the Danish population born between 1981 and 2008 and is a Case-Cohort design including 50,615 population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28924187") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:PPR247289%20AND%20SRC:PPR&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also added two additional focus phenotypes, schizophrenia spectrum disorder (N=16,008) and post-partum disorder (N=3,421).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000512> "A Danish population-based case-cohort sample established by the Lundbeck Foundation Initiative for Integrative Psychiatric Research (iPSYCH) to study the genetic and environmental architecture of severe mental disorders, combining persons diagnosed with schizophrenia, autism, ADHD or affective disorder with a random sample of the population, genotyped from neonatal dried blood spots in the Danish Neonatal Screening Biobank and linked to national registers, whose first wave (iPSYCH2012) sampled individuals born in 1981-2005 and which was expanded as iPSYCH2015 to 141,265 samples, including 50,615 population controls, nested within the Danish population born in 1981-2008 and adding schizophrenia spectrum and post-partum disorder cases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8974329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LLFS successfully enrolled and extensively phenotyped 4,953 individuals from 539 two-generational families that demonstrated clustering for exception longevity in the upper generation (ie, with a sibship FLoSS > 7) from 3 US field sites (Boston University, Boston, MA; Columbia University, New York, NY; and University of Pittsburgh, Pittsburgh, PA) and one field site in Denmark") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513> "A longitudinal, multicentre, multinational family study of 4,953 members of 539 two-generation families selected for exceptional familial longevity, recruited in 2006-2009 through field centres in Boston, New York and Pittsburgh in the United States and in Denmark and re-examined in 2014-2017, to study the genetic and non-genetic determinants of exceptional longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8974329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original recruitment and examination for LLFS were conducted over a 3-year period, April 2006–May 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513> "A longitudinal, multicentre, multinational family study of 4,953 members of 539 two-generation families selected for exceptional familial longevity, recruited in 2006-2009 through field centres in Boston, New York and Pittsburgh in the United States and in Denmark and re-examined in 2014-2017, to study the genetic and non-genetic determinants of exceptional longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8974329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Visit 2 (2014–2017) repeated all Visit 1 protocols and added carotid ultrasonography of atherosclerotic plaque and wall thickness, additional cognitive testing, and perceived fatigability.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513> "A longitudinal, multicentre, multinational family study of 4,953 members of 539 two-generation families selected for exceptional familial longevity, recruited in 2006-2009 through field centres in Boston, New York and Pittsburgh in the United States and in Denmark and re-examined in 2014-2017, to study the genetic and non-genetic determinants of exceptional longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34739053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34739053+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NIA Long Life Family Study (LLFS) is a longitudinal, multicenter, multinational, population-based multigenerational family study of the genetic and nongenetic determinants of exceptional longevity and healthy aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000513> "A longitudinal, multicentre, multinational family study of 4,953 members of 539 two-generation families selected for exceptional familial longevity, recruited in 2006-2009 through field centres in Boston, New York and Pittsburgh in the United States and in Denmark and re-examined in 2014-2017, to study the genetic and non-genetic determinants of exceptional longevity and healthy ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20214461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both Non-Hispanic white and African-American subjects are included in the cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20214461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPDGene is a multicenter observational study designed to identify genetic factors associated with COPD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20214461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPDGene will enroll 10,000 smokers with and without COPD across the GOLD stages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20214461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, subtypes of COPD based on these phenotypes will be used in a comprehensive genome-wide study to identify COPD susceptibility genes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20214461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to the cross-sectional enrollment process, these subjects will be followed regularly for longitudinal studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20214461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37241208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10221198/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPDGene enrolled 10,198 former and current smokers aged 45–80 years with a history of ≥10 pack-year smoking with and without COPD from initiation in P1 from 21 clinical centers across the United States (Figure 1) [4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000514> "A multicentre observational cohort of about 10,000 non-Hispanic white and African American current and former smokers with and without COPD, aged 45-80, enrolled at 21 clinical centres across the United States and followed longitudinally with chest CT imaging and genome-wide genotyping to identify genetic factors and CT-defined subtypes of COPD.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exclusion criteria are any cardiovascular disease, diabetes, obstructive sleep apnoea syndrome, daily intake of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs and a body mass index >35 kg/m².") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up examinations are scheduled every 3-5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GAPP affords an excellent opportunity to assess genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors and their progression over time in young and healthy adults from the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since June 2010, 1,333 participants have been enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The genetic and phenotypic determinants of blood pressure and other cardiovascular risk factors (GAPP) study is a population-based prospective cohort study involving a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 years in the Principality of Liechtenstein.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23299990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23299990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "blood pressure measurement (clinic and 24-hour ambulatory monitoring), electrocardiography (12-lead and 24-hour Holter monitoring), bioimpedance analysis, blood, urinary and genetic sampling, spirometry and sleep pulse oximetry with nasal flow measurement.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000515> "A population-based prospective cohort of a representative sample of healthy adults aged 25-41 in the Principality of Liechtenstein, enrolled from June 2010 without cardiovascular disease, diabetes or severe obesity, with ambulatory blood pressure, Holter ECG, spirometry, sleep oximetry and blood, urine and genetic sampling, and followed up every 3-5 years to study genetic and phenotypic predictors of cardiovascular risk factors in young adults.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By linking genome-wide data to the existing epidemiologic databank of the parent WHS, which includes comprehensive dietary, behavioral, and traditional exposure data on each participant since cohort inception in 1992, the WGHS will also allow exploration of gene-environment and gene-gene interactions as they relate to incident disease states.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> "A prospective genome-wide association cohort of more than 25,000 initially healthy American female health professionals aged 45 or older from the Women's Health Study who gave a baseline blood sample, followed since 1992 for incident cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Rationale, design, and methodology of the Women's Genome Health Study: a genome-wide association study of more than 25,000 initially healthy american women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> "A prospective genome-wide association cohort of more than 25,000 initially healthy American female health professionals aged 45 or older from the Women's Health Study who gave a baseline blood sample, followed since 1992 for incident cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the Women's Genome Health Study (WGHS) is to create a comprehensive, fully searchable genome-wide database of >360 000 single nucleotide polymorphisms among at least 25 000 initially healthy American women participating in the ongoing NIH-funded Women's Health Study (WHS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> "A prospective genome-wide association cohort of more than 25,000 initially healthy American female health professionals aged 45 or older from the Women's Health Study who gave a baseline blood sample, followed since 1992 for incident cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These women have already been followed over a 12-year period for major incident health events including but not limited to myocardial infarction, stroke, cancer, diabetes, osteoporosis, venous-thromboembolism, cognitive decline, and common visual disorders such as age- related macular degeneration and cataracts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> "A prospective genome-wide association cohort of more than 25,000 initially healthy American female health professionals aged 45 or older from the Women's Health Study who gave a baseline blood sample, followed since 1992 for incident cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38052102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10767824/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Women’s Genome Health Study (WGHS) is a population-based, prospective cohort of initially healthy, female North American health care professionals at least 45 years old at baseline, representing participants in the Women’s Health Study (WHS) who provided a blood sample at baseline and consented for blood-based analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000516> "A prospective genome-wide association cohort of more than 25,000 initially healthy American female health professionals aged 45 or older from the Women's Health Study who gave a baseline blood sample, followed since 1992 for incident cardiovascular disease, cancer, diabetes and other outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2879985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Brownsville (Cameron County, Texas; 2006 population: 172,437 [14]) provides a unique environment to examine health disparities in Mexican Americans in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517> "A community-based cohort of Mexican Americans in Brownsville, Cameron County, Texas, on the United States-Mexico border, established in 2004 by the University of Texas School of Public Health Brownsville campus from households in randomly selected census tract blocks, to study the prevalence and determinants of obesity, diabetes and related chronic disease in this population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2879985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2004, we began to recruit a cohort, now numbering 2,000, drawn from randomly selected households on the basis of 2000 Census tract data (15), with the purpose of establishing a \"Framingham-like\" cohort in this population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517> "A community-based cohort of Mexican Americans in Brownsville, Cameron County, Texas, on the United States-Mexico border, established in 2004 by the University of Texas School of Public Health Brownsville campus from households in randomly selected census tract blocks, to study the prevalence and determinants of obesity, diabetes and related chronic disease in this population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20394692+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established a cohort on the United States-Mexico border to determine the prevalence of obesity and diabetes in this Mexican American population and to see whether minor economic advantages had any effect on health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517> "A community-based cohort of Mexican Americans in Brownsville, Cameron County, Texas, on the United States-Mexico border, established in 2004 by the University of Texas School of Public Health Brownsville campus from households in randomly selected census tract blocks, to study the prevalence and determinants of obesity, diabetes and related chronic disease in this population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20394692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cameron County Hispanic Cohort (CCHC) is a community-based cohort study initiated in 2004 of Mexican Americans in Brownsville, Texas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000517> "A community-based cohort of Mexican Americans in Brownsville, Cameron County, Texas, on the United States-Mexico border, established in 2004 by the University of Texas School of Public Health Brownsville campus from households in randomly selected census tract blocks, to study the prevalence and determinants of obesity, diabetes and related chronic disease in this population.")

