AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11385320/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case-control, family-based, and longitudinal AD genetic cohorts from the Alzheimer’s Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC) and Alzheimer’s Disease Sequencing Project (ADSP) (release 3) were available through public repositories with genetic data from SNV microarrays and whole-genome sequencing (eTable 1 and 2 in Supplement 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39250132+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was a meta-analysis of genetic association studies in case-control, family-based, population-based, and longitudinal AD-related cohorts from the US Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium, the Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project, the UK Biobank, the Finnish health registry, and the US Million Veterans Program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40676597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40676597+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We construct and analyze a multi-ancestry GWAS dataset in the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC) to test for novel shared and population-specific late-onset Alzheimer's disease (LOAD) susceptibility loci and evaluate underlying genetic architecture in 37,382 non-Hispanic White (NHW), 6728 African American, 8899 Hispanic (HIS), and 3232 East Asian individuals") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12635870/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We obtained GWAS and smoking history data for participants in 34 ADGC GWAS datasets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11385320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we implemented a cross‐sample phenotype harmonization procedure aiming to standardize pathology‐verified diagnoses where possible, share unique missing information across all duplicate entries of a given subject") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39250132") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41268768") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4154667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To test these hypotheses the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC) assembled a set of 4,914 samples with genome-wide genotyping data and neuropathologic data, and performed genome-wide association tests of AD and related diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000518> "A US consortium that assembles genome-wide genotype data and harmonized phenotypes from many case-control, family-based, population-based and longitudinal Alzheimer disease cohorts, in more than 30 GWAS datasets of several ancestries, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")

