AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25254375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27193062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37156940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25254375") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25254375+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Admixture in Latin America: geographic structure, phenotypic diversity and self-perception of ancestry based on 7,342 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519> "A sample of about 7,300 adult volunteers of mixed African, European and Native American ancestry, mostly university students and staff (and, in Chile, mainly soldiers), recruited by a consortium of Latin American and UK groups in México City, Medellín, Lima, Arica and Porto Alegre and characterised for physical appearance, facial photographs, self-perceived ancestry and genetic ancestry, with genome-wide genotyping of about 6,000 of them, to study admixture and the genetics of physical traits in Latin America.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25254375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27193062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37156940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27193062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27193062+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report a genome-wide association scan for facial features in ∼6,000 Latin Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000519> "A sample of about 7,300 adult volunteers of mixed African, European and Native American ancestry, mostly university students and staff (and, in Chile, mainly soldiers), recruited by a consortium of Latin American and UK groups in México City, Medellín, Lima, Arica and Porto Alegre and characterised for physical appearance, facial photographs, self-perceived ancestry and genetic ancestry, with genome-wide genotyping of about 6,000 of them, to study admixture and the genetics of physical traits in Latin America.")

