AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25194498+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By the end of 2012, the study had recruited 42,112 participants, of whom 35,199 (83.6%) had attended the health screening.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25194498+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2004, participants from each force who agreed to participate were enrolled either with an enrolment questionnaire or a comprehensive health screening performed locally.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25194498+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Airwave Health Monitoring Study was established to evaluate possible health risks associated with use of TETRA, a digital communication system used by police forces and other emergency services in Great Britain since 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25194498+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study has been broadened to investigate more generally the health of the work force.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25194498+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This includes questionnaire, 7-day food diaries, anthropometry, measurements of cardiovascular and cognitive function, blood chemistry, coagulation and haematology. Blood and urine samples are stored in vapour phase liquid nitrogen allowing long-term access for biochemical or genetic analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25194498") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41251127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963709/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Airwave Health Monitoring Study is an occupational cohort involving police forces across Great Britain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000521> "An occupational cohort of police officers and staff of police forces across Great Britain, enrolled from 2004, with health screening attended by most participants enrolled by the end of 2012 and including questionnaires, food diaries, physical and cognitive measurements and stored blood and urine, set up to evaluate possible health risks of the TETRA digital radio system and broadened to study the health of the police workforce.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18366642+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to assess the prevalence of cardiovascular risk factors (CVRFs) in the Caucasian population of Lausanne, Switzerland, we conducted a population-based study (Colaus Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18366642+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Single-center, cross-sectional study including a random sample of 6,188 extensively phenotyped Caucasian subjects (3,251 women and 2,937 men) aged 35 to 75 years living in Lausanne, and genotyped using the 500 K Affymetrix chip technology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18366642+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CoLaus study: a population-based study to investigate the epidemiology and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and metabolic syndrome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38388190+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based prospective study conducted in Lausanne, Switzerland, with a follow-up between 2003 and 2021.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38388190+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Total and CVD mortality as well as any CVD event were assessed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18366642") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38388190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/all/collections/COLAUS%20Study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Starting in 2004, over 4000 CoLaus participants underwent an extensive psychiatric phenotypization (PsyCoLaus).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000522> "A population-based cohort of a random sample of 6,188 Caucasian adults aged 35 to 75 living in Lausanne, Switzerland, extensively phenotyped and genotyped genome-wide at baseline to study the prevalence and genetic determinants of cardiovascular risk factors and the metabolic syndrome, and followed up prospectively (with its psychiatric arm PsyCoLaus) from 2003 for cardiovascular events and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34921685") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9545863/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The prospective Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study 18 (MCCS) recruited 41 513 Melbourne residents in 1990–1994.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At both waves, socio-demographic, lifestyle, and health data, as well as physical measurements and blood samples were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and their vital status were ascertained through the Victorian Cancer Registry and the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare, including the Australian Cancer Database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During 2003–2007, a face-to-face follow-up was carried out.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MCCS was initially carried out to study a wide range of research questions, primarily the link between lifestyle and the risk of cancer and other chronic diseases") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12490524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study (MCCS), a prospective study that recruited 41,513 middle-aged and older Australians (99 % aged between 40 and 69 years, 59 % females) of white European origin between 1990 and 1994 (baseline)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000523> "A prospective cohort of 41,513 middle-aged and older adults of white European origin, almost all aged 40–69, recruited in Melbourne, Australia, in 1990–1994 by Cancer Council Victoria and followed up face to face in 2003–2007 and by record linkage to cancer and death registries, collecting socio-demographic, lifestyle and health data to study risk factors for cancer and other chronic diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339762/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described in the original cohort profile,1 the overall objective of TRAILS is ‘to contribute to the understanding of the determinants of adolescents’ mental (ill-)health and social development during adolescence and young adulthood, as well as the mechanisms underlying the associations between determinants and outcomes’.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339762/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical cohort consists of individuals who have been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands any time before the age of 11.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339762/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The outcome measures encompass both mental and physical health conditions as well as various indicators of social functioning, and the determinants encompass a wide range of biological, psychological, and social markers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339762/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population cohort includes participants born between 1 October 1989 and 30 September 1991, who lived in the North of The Netherlands at the time of the baseline assessment in 2001/02.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25431468+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since the IJE published a cohort profile on the TRAILS in 2008, the participants have matured from adolescents into young adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25431468+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TRAILS consists of a population cohort (N=2230) and a clinical cohort (N=543), both of which were followed from about age 11 years onwards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000524> "A Dutch prospective cohort study, run in the North of the Netherlands, consisting of a population cohort of 2,230 children born between October 1989 and September 1991 and a clinical cohort of 543 children referred to child psychiatric outpatient care before age 11, followed from about age 11 into young adulthood with repeated assessments of mental health, social development and physical health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583712/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADDITION-PRO is a population-based, longitudinal cohort study of individuals at high risk for diabetes. 16,136 eligible individuals were identified at high risk following participation in a stepwise screening programme in Danish general practice between 2001 and 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of 2,082 Danish adults at different levels of diabetes risk, sampled from the 16,136 high-risk individuals identified by the 2001–2006 stepwise diabetes screening programme in Danish general practice of the Danish arm of ADDITION-Europe, examined in 2009–2011 with detailed cardiometabolic phenotyping and followed for cardiovascular disease and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583712/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All ADDITION-PRO participants are being followed for incident cardiovascular disease and death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of 2,082 Danish adults at different levels of diabetes risk, sampled from the 16,136 high-risk individuals identified by the 2001–2006 stepwise diabetes screening programme in Danish general practice of the Danish arm of ADDITION-Europe, examined in 2009–2011 with detailed cardiometabolic phenotyping and followed for cardiovascular disease and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583712/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals with impaired glucose regulation at screening, those who developed diabetes following screening, and a random sub-sample of those at lower levels of diabetes risk were invited to attend a follow-up health assessment in 2009–2011 (n = 4,188), of whom 2,082 (50%) attended.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of 2,082 Danish adults at different levels of diabetes risk, sampled from the 16,136 high-risk individuals identified by the 2001–2006 stepwise diabetes screening programme in Danish general practice of the Danish arm of ADDITION-Europe, examined in 2009–2011 with detailed cardiometabolic phenotyping and followed for cardiovascular disease and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583712/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate these issues, we invited individuals at different levels of diabetes risk identified from the stepwise screening programme of the Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe study [3] to take part in a longitudinal cohort study (ADDITION-PRO).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of 2,082 Danish adults at different levels of diabetes risk, sampled from the 16,136 high-risk individuals identified by the 2001–2006 stepwise diabetes screening programme in Danish general practice of the Danish arm of ADDITION-Europe, examined in 2009–2011 with detailed cardiometabolic phenotyping and followed for cardiovascular disease and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23241242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23241242+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The health assessment included detailed measurement of anthropometry, body composition, biochemistry, physical activity and cardiovascular risk factors including aortic stiffness and central blood pressure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of 2,082 Danish adults at different levels of diabetes risk, sampled from the 16,136 high-risk individuals identified by the 2001–2006 stepwise diabetes screening programme in Danish general practice of the Danish arm of ADDITION-Europe, examined in 2009–2011 with detailed cardiometabolic phenotyping and followed for cardiovascular disease and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413555/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples are genotyped by employing the 5' nuclease assay and fluorogenic allele-specific TaqMan MGB probes") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> "A clinical cohort of patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2008 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413555/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FINCAVAS compiles an extensive set of data on patient history, genetic variation, cardiovascular parameters, ECG markers as well as follow-up data on clinical events, hospitalisations and deaths.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> "A clinical cohort of patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2008 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413555/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to repeated measurement of heart rate and blood pressure, digital high-resolution ECG at 500 Hz is recorded continuously during the entire exercise test, including the resting and recovery phases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> "A clinical cohort of patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2008 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413555/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of the Finnish Cardiovascular Study (FINCAVAS) is to construct a risk profile – using genetic, haemodynamic and electrocardiographic (ECG) markers – of individuals at high risk of cardiovascular diseases, events and deaths.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> "A clinical cohort of patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2008 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16515696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6330693/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Finnish Cardiovascular Study (FINCAVAS), all consecutive patients referred for an exercise test at Tampere University Hospital and willing to participate were enrolled between October 2001 and December 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000526> "A clinical cohort of patients scheduled for an exercise stress test at Tampere University Hospital, Finland, recruited between October 2001 and December 2008 with continuous high-resolution ECG, haemodynamic measurements, genotyping and follow-up of clinical events and deaths, to construct risk profiles for cardiovascular disease, events and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33185675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33185675") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7666422/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health Professionals Follow-up Study is a prospective study of US male health professionals who enrolled in 1986 by completing a mailed questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527> "A prospective cohort of 51,529 US male health professionals aged 40 to 75 enrolled in 1986, whose demographics, health, diet and lifestyle are updated by questionnaire every two years (diet every four), with follow-up exceeding 90% of eligible person-time.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33185675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37165447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In each of the cohorts, detailed information on demographics, health, diet, and lifestyle factors was collected and updated every 2 years (every 4 years for diet).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527> "A prospective cohort of 51,529 US male health professionals aged 40 to 75 enrolled in 1986, whose demographics, health, diet and lifestyle are updated by questionnaire every two years (diet every four), with follow-up exceeding 90% of eligible person-time.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33185675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37165447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HPFS began in 1986 and enrolled 51,529 male health professionals, aged 40 to 75 years [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527> "A prospective cohort of 51,529 US male health professionals aged 40 to 75 enrolled in 1986, whose demographics, health, diet and lifestyle are updated by questionnaire every two years (diet every four), with follow-up exceeding 90% of eligible person-time.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33185675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37165447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10173489/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The follow-up rates in all 3 cohorts exceed 90% of eligible person-time [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000527> "A prospective cohort of 51,529 US male health professionals aged 40 to 75 enrolled in 1986, whose demographics, health, diet and lifestyle are updated by questionnaire every two years (diet every four), with follow-up exceeding 90% of eligible person-time.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30470734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000917") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30470734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6251918/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ARGO comprises osteoarthritis cases and healthy controls from Larisa, Greece.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528> "A Greek collection of more than 1,500 well-phenotyped patients with severe hip or knee osteoarthritis undergoing total joint replacement, recruited in hospitals of Athens (2015-2017) and Larissa together with healthy controls, set up to study the genetic architecture of osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30470734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000917") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "More than 1,500 patients with severe OA, undergoing hip and/or knee total joint replacement were recruited from the cities of Athens and Larissa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528> "A Greek collection of more than 1,500 well-phenotyped patients with severe hip or knee osteoarthritis undergoing total joint replacement, recruited in hospitals of Athens (2015-2017) and Larissa together with healthy controls, set up to study the genetic architecture of osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30470734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000917") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ARGO collection was conducted in three public hospitals (Attikon University General Hospital of Athens, Nea Ionia General Hospital Konstantopouleio, and KAT Hospital) and one private hospital (Lefkos Stavros General Hospital) in the city of Athens, Greece between February of 2015 and March 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528> "A Greek collection of more than 1,500 well-phenotyped patients with severe hip or knee osteoarthritis undergoing total joint replacement, recruited in hospitals of Athens (2015-2017) and Larissa together with healthy controls, set up to study the genetic architecture of osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30470734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001000917") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ARGO study, was set up to investigate the genetic architecture of hip and knee OA in a Greek population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000528> "A Greek collection of more than 1,500 well-phenotyped patients with severe hip or knee osteoarthritis undergoing total joint replacement, recruited in hospitals of Athens (2015-2017) and Larissa together with healthy controls, set up to study the genetic architecture of osteoarthritis.")

