AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9792260/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline participants were 10,030 Koreas aged 40 to 69 years who were from Ansan or Anseong of Gyeonggi-do (province), South Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000530> "A community-based prospective cohort of 10,030 men and women aged 40–69 from the urban city of Ansan and the rural town of Ansung (Anseong) in Gyeonggi Province, South Korea, recruited in 2001–2002 as the first cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and re-surveyed every two years, to study common chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12691764/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the baseline (2001–2002), 10,030 individuals aged 40–69 years were recruited, and the participants underwent repeated follow-up examinations every 2 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000530> "A community-based prospective cohort of 10,030 men and women aged 40–69 from the urban city of Ansan and the rural town of Ansung (Anseong) in Gyeonggi Province, South Korea, recruited in 2001–2002 as the first cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and re-surveyed every two years, to study common chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12691764/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we utilized data derived from the Ansan and Ansung cohort, part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES), a long-term community-based prospective cohort initiated in 2001–2002 [114].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000530> "A community-based prospective cohort of 10,030 men and women aged 40–69 from the urban city of Ansan and the rural town of Ansung (Anseong) in Gyeonggi Province, South Korea, recruited in 2001–2002 as the first cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and re-surveyed every two years, to study common chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12691764/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The well-characterized Ansan (urban) and Ansung (rural) sub-cohorts were included in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000530> "A community-based prospective cohort of 10,030 men and women aged 40–69 from the urban city of Ansan and the rural town of Ansung (Anseong) in Gyeonggi Province, South Korea, recruited in 2001–2002 as the first cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and re-surveyed every two years, to study common chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36573383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within KoGES, genotypes from 5,493 participants in the KoGES_Ansan/Ansung cohort were sequenced utilizing the Korea Biobank array and served as controls in our study who were recruited to examine the associations between chronic diseases and lifestyle or diet from two cities in Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000530> "A community-based prospective cohort of 10,030 men and women aged 40–69 from the urban city of Ansan and the rural town of Ansung (Anseong) in Gyeonggi Province, South Korea, recruited in 2001–2002 as the first cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study and re-surveyed every two years, to study common chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")

