# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31152163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6698888/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed 121 GWAS encompassing 765,348 individuals of European (n = 567,460), East Asian (n = 165,726), African-American (n = 13,842), South Asian (n = 13,359) and Hispanic (n = 4,961) ancestry (median age, 54 years; 50% female; Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31152163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6698888/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore conducted a trans-ancestry GWAS meta-analysis in the CKD Genetics (CKDGen) Consortium (n = 765,348) and replicated findings in the Million Veteran Program (MVP; n = 280,722)23, for a combined sample size of greater than 1 million participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34272381") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also provide summary statistics genome-wide for association with eGFRcrea, eGFRcys, and BUN as an important resource for even larger future GWAS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CKDGen Consortium is an international collaborative effort dedicated to the investigation of the genetic underpinnings of kidney function and disease (PMID: 31980069)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The datasets are hosted by the Genetic Epidemiology, Medical Center - University of Freiburg, Freiburg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This site provides genome-wide association study (GWAS) summary statistics and additional information from published projects of the CKDGen Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ckdgen.imbi.uni-freiburg.de/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8285412/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-69367-3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CKDGen is a consortium of multi-ancestry population-based studies50 set up to uncover genetic loci associated with kidney function and disease in individuals of different ancestries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000532> "An international collaborative consortium, co-directed by Anna Köttgen and Cristian Pattaro with its data hosted at the University of Freiburg, that meta-analyses genome-wide association results from many, mostly population-based, studies to investigate the genetic basis of kidney function and disease, releasing summary statistics for markers such as estimated glomerular filtration rate and blood urea nitrogen.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Great East Japan Earthquake (GEJE) and resulting tsunami of March 11, 2011 gave rise to devastating damage on the Pacific coast of the Tohoku region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533> "A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tohoku Medical Megabank Project (TMM), which is being conducted by Tohoku University Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (ToMMo) and Iwate Medical University Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (IMM), has been launched to realize creative reconstruction and to solve medical problems in the aftermath of this disaster.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533> "A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The integrated biobank of TMM consists of health and clinical information, biospecimens, and genome and omics data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533> "A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27374138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We started two prospective cohort studies in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures: a population-based adult cohort study, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study (TMM CommCohort Study), which will recruit 80 000 participants, and a birth and three-generation cohort study, the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000533> "A Japanese genome cohort project launched after the 2011 Great East Japan Earthquake and run by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Iwate Medical University, comprising two prospective cohorts in Miyagi and Iwate Prefectures, the TMM Community-Based Cohort Study of adults and the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study, with an integrated biobank of health information, biospecimens and genome and omics data.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2360390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case patients (n=290) included in this analysis are Caucasian and African American men diagnosed with histologically confirmed adenocarcinoma of the prostate before age 55 years and who participated in one of two population-based case–control studies of prostate cancer conducted in King County, Washington.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2360390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident cases in both studies were identified through the population-based Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, which also provided information on Gleason score, tumour stage, and serum prostate-specific antigen (PSA) level at diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5510189/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first study included men aged 40–64 years who were diagnosed between 1993 and 1996, while the second study focused on men aged 35–74 years who were diagnosed between 2002 and 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10592169/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both the HPFS/PHS and FH genetic studies are within the framework of the PRACTICAL (Prostate Cancer Association Group to Investigate Cancer-Associated Alterations in the Genome) Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10592169/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based controls without a history of prostate cancer (n = 1,133) were identified using random digit telephone dialing, recruited evenly throughout the ascertainment periods for cases, and frequency-matched to cases by 5-year age group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17700570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28145099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37555839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10592169/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study participants were part of the Physicians’ Health Study (PHS), Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS), and a Seattle-based Fred Hutchinson (FH) Cancer Center Prostate Cancer Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000534> "A prostate cancer study run at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center that comprises two population-based case-control studies in King County, Washington, whose cases, identified through the Seattle-Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, were men aged 40–64 diagnosed in 1993–1996 and men aged 35–74 diagnosed in 2002–2005, and whose controls without prostate cancer were found by random-digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age; its genotyped samples contribute to the PRACTICAL consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34996099") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FHCRC study cohort included 4270 recipients of European ancestry who had a first allogeneic HCT with marrow or growth factor-mobilized blood cells at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 through 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> "A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recipients suffered from a hematologic malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome and were treated in a highly structured clinical research environment with comprehensive monitoring and systematic data recording.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> "A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population represents a large cohort from the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and consists of 4,471 recipients and 4,628 donors containing 4,258 recipient-donor pairs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> "A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This retrospective cohort study was designed to identify single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) that are associated with complications after allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation (HCT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> "A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9043943/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001918.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used proportional hazards analyses to test for associations with acute and chronic GVHD, acute kidney injury, gram-negative bacteremia, invasive fungal disease, CMV infection and disease, recurrent malignancy, death not attributable to recurrent malignancy, and death after recurrent or progressive malignancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000535> "A retrospective cohort of patients with a haematological malignancy or myelodysplastic syndrome who had a first allogeneic haematopoietic cell transplant at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center and Seattle Cancer Care Alliance from 1990 to 2011, together with their donors, genotyped to find variants associated with graft-versus-host disease, recurrent malignancy and other complications after transplantation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39280063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we provide exome-array GWAS meta-analysis results for glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c, up to 144,060 participants), fasting glucose (FG, up to 129,665 participants), fasting insulin (FI, up to 104,140) and 2hr glucose post-oral glucose challenge (2hGlu, up to 57,878).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39280063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this MAGIC effort, individuals without diabetes of self-reported and genetically clustered European (85%), African American (6%), South Asian (5%), East Asian (2%) and Hispanic (2%) ancestry from up to 64 cohorts participated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39280063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAGIC (Meta-Analysis of Glucose and Insulin-related traits Consortium) was established to focus on the genetic analysis of glycemic traits in individuals without diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAGIC (the Meta-Analyses of Glucose and Insulin-related traits Consortium) represents a collaborative effort to combine data from multiple GWAS to identify additional loci that impact on glycemic and metabolic traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAGIC investigators have initially studied fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2h glucose and HBA1c, as well as performed meta-analysis of more sophisticated measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399760/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://magicinvestigators.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are releasing results from our meta-analyses and these can be accessed through the data downloads pages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000536> "A collaborative consortium that combines genome-wide association and exome-array data from many cohorts of individuals without diabetes in meta-analyses of glycaemic traits (fasting glucose, fasting insulin, 2-hour glucose and HbA1c) and measures of insulin secretion and sensitivity, to find loci influencing glycaemic and metabolic traits, and releases its summary results.")

