# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-09775-w/MediaObjects/41467_2019_9775_MOESM5_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DACHS | DACHS Study, excluding previously reported cases and controls (GECCO study) | German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) | Population-based incidence cases aged>30 at diagnosis in the Rhine-Neckar-Odenwald region (southwest Germany).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, patients with a first diagnosis of CRC aged 30 years or older were recruited in the 22 hospitals providing first-line therapy for CRC in the study region (approximately 2 million inhabitants).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruited patients were followed up with respect to therapy, the course of the disease, and survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population for this analysis included patients diagnosed with CRC and recruited in the DACHS study (Darmkrebs: Chancen der Verhütung durch Screening), an ongoing multi-center population-based case-control study with additional active follow-up of cases conducted in the Rhine-Neckar region in the South of Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9940696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Smoking history and other known or suspected CRC risk factors were ascertained in detail in personal interviews among 6264 CRC patients and 6866 controls (frequency matched for age, sex, and county of residence) who were recruited in 2003-2020 in the DACHS study (Darmkrebs: Chancen der Verhütung durch Screening [German]; Colorectal Cancer: Chances for Prevention Through Screening [English]), a population-based case-control study from Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5946295/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001315.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This German study was initiated as a large population-based case-control study in 2003 in the Rhine-Neckar-Odenwald region (southwest region of Germany) to assess the potential of endoscopic screening for reduction of colorectal cancer risk") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000556> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the Rhine-Neckar region of south-west Germany, led from the German Cancer Research Center in Heidelberg, which from 2003 recruited patients aged 30 or over with a first colorectal cancer diagnosis from the 22 hospitals treating the disease in the region, and actively follows the cases to study colorectal cancer risk, prevention by screening and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000557> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000557>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12826435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16754790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19304780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12826435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12826435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Medical Research Council BRItish Genetics of HyperTension (BRIGHT) study, we aim to identify these genetic factors by scanning the human genome for susceptibility genes for essential hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000557> "A UK resource of white European families with severe essential hypertension, collected by the Medical Research Council British Genetics of Hypertension (BRIGHT) study through the MRC General Practice Framework and other primary care practices, including affected sibling pairs and parent-offspring trios, with normotensive controls matched by age, sex and geography across the UK, for linkage and association studies of the genetics of hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12826435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16754790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19304780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12826435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12826435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We phenotyped 2010 affected sibling pairs drawn from 1599 severely hypertensive families, and completed a 10 centimorgan genome-wide scan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000557> "A UK resource of white European families with severe essential hypertension, collected by the Medical Research Council British Genetics of Hypertension (BRIGHT) study through the MRC General Practice Framework and other primary care practices, including affected sibling pairs and parent-offspring trios, with normotensive controls matched by age, sex and geography across the UK, for linkage and association studies of the genetics of hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12826435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16754790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19304780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16754790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16754790+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3 positive markers in the chromosome 5 region were also genotyped in 712 distinct parent-offspring trios with the same severe phenotype to replicate linkage and association.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000557> "A UK resource of white European families with severe essential hypertension, collected by the Medical Research Council British Genetics of Hypertension (BRIGHT) study through the MRC General Practice Framework and other primary care practices, including affected sibling pairs and parent-offspring trios, with normotensive controls matched by age, sex and geography across the UK, for linkage and association studies of the genetics of hypertension.")
