AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8744710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shimane CoHRE study conducted by Shimane University in Japan worked in collaboration with Okinoshima town in the Shimane prefecture to identify potential factors of healthy aging among rural residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000591> "An ongoing community cohort run by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) of Shimane University, built on health examinations of community-dwelling people, largely older adults in rural towns, in Shimane Prefecture, Japan, in collaboration with local municipalities, to identify factors in healthy ageing and chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8744710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cross-sectional study used data from older adults who participated in the Shimane CoHRE study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000591> "An ongoing community cohort run by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) of Shimane University, built on health examinations of community-dwelling people, largely older adults in rural towns, in Shimane Prefecture, Japan, in collaboration with local municipalities, to identify factors in healthy ageing and chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9456574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This longitudinal study was a part of the Shimane Community-Based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) study that collected data from a health examination conducted from June to October of 2012 and 2019 in Shimane, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000591> "An ongoing community cohort run by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) of Shimane University, built on health examinations of community-dwelling people, largely older adults in rural towns, in Shimane Prefecture, Japan, in collaboration with local municipalities, to identify factors in healthy ageing and chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11106293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Shimane CoHRE Study is an ongoing health examination for the community-dwelling people in Shimane prefecture, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000591> "An ongoing community cohort run by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) of Shimane University, built on health examinations of community-dwelling people, largely older adults in rural towns, in Shimane Prefecture, Japan, in collaboration with local municipalities, to identify factors in healthy ageing and chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36079021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38769351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11106293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cross-sectional study is a part of the cohort study conducted by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education in Shimane University (Shimane CoHRE Study)19,20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000591> "An ongoing community cohort run by the Center for Community-based Healthcare Research and Education (CoHRE) of Shimane University, built on health examinations of community-dwelling people, largely older adults in rural towns, in Shimane Prefecture, Japan, in collaboration with local municipalities, to identify factors in healthy ageing and chronic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000592> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000592>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501403") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3380865") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our analyses are based on the Fangchenggang Area Male Health and Examination Survey (FAMHES), which was designed to investigate the effects of environmental and genetic factors and their interaction with the development of age-related chronic diseases [21–23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000592> "A population-based study of 4,303 non-institutionalized Chinese men aged 17–88 who attended routine physical examinations at the Medical Centre of Fangchenggang First People’s Hospital in Guangxi, China, from September to December 2009, surveyed and sampled to investigate environmental and genetic factors, and their interaction, in age-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501403") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3380865/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A comprehensive demographic and health survey was conducted among a consecutive series of 4303 men participating in the routine physical examination at the Medical Centre in Fangchenggang First People’s Hospital from September 2009 to December 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000592> "A population-based study of 4,303 non-institutionalized Chinese men aged 17–88 who attended routine physical examinations at the Medical Centre of Fangchenggang First People’s Hospital in Guangxi, China, from September to December 2009, surveyed and sampled to investigate environmental and genetic factors, and their interaction, in age-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501403") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22737230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3380865/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the FAMHES was a population-based study conducted among non-institutionalized Chinese men aging from 17 to 88 years old in Guangxi, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000592> "A population-based study of 4,303 non-institutionalized Chinese men aged 17–88 who attended routine physical examinations at the Medical Centre of Fangchenggang First People’s Hospital in Guangxi, China, from September to December 2009, surveyed and sampled to investigate environmental and genetic factors, and their interaction, in age-related chronic diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1051/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1051_MOESM5_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is aimed to study six different isolated villages situated in North-Eastern Italy (FVG).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1051/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1051_MOESM5_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Friuli Venezia Giulia Project was initiated in 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0205-x/MediaObjects/41588_2018_205_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "INGI-FVG | Italian Network on Genetic Isolates - Friuli Venezia Giulia Genetic Park | population based |  | Europeans from North-East Italy | 1610 | [PMID:23249956]") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The INGI-FVG cohort consisted of about 1700 subjects drawn from the project “Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All three populations belong to the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates (INGI), a project aimed at studying the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes (including eating habits) [41].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4997959/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In particular, our study used 370 individuals from INGI-CARL, a population coming from Carlantino, a small village located in Puglia (Southern Italy), and 843 defined as INGI-FVG, making reference to 6 villages situated in the Friuli Venezia Region in North-Eastern Italy for a total of 1207 samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7080768/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436946/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study examined 6 isolated villages in the North-East of Italy between 2008 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000593> "A population-based cohort of about 1,700 people from six isolated villages in the Friuli Venezia Giulia region of north-eastern Italy, examined between 2008 and 2010 in the Genetic Park of Friuli Venezia Giulia project; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates, which studies the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34354128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four clinical sites (Memorial Hospital of Rhode Island, The Ohio State University, University of Maryland and Johns Hopkins University, and the University of Pittsburgh) recruited participants between February 2004 and May 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34354128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three subcohorts are identified; Progression subcohort, Incidence subcohort, and Non-exposed control subcohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Bilateral standing postero-anterior fixed-flexion knee radiographs were acquired annually at baseline, 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months’ follow-up using a SynaFlexerTM frame (Synarc, San Francisco, CA, USA) [40, 41].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, 4796 men and women aged between 45 and 79 years were recruited at four clinical sites across the USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We utilized data from the Osteoarthritis Initiative (OAI), a publicly available, multicentre, observational cohort study of risk factors for knee OA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8342605/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8487312/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.niams.nih.gov/grants-funding/funded-research/osteoarthritis-initiative") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This Initiative is a public-private partnership between the NIH and private industry that seeks to develop a public-domain research resource to facilitate the scientific evaluation of biomarkers for osteoarthritis as potential surrogate endpoints for disease onset and progression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000594> "A multicentre prospective observational study of knee osteoarthritis, run as a public-private partnership between the NIH and industry, that recruited 4,796 men and women aged 45-79 at four US clinical sites in 2004-2006 into progression (symptomatic knee osteoarthritis), incidence (increased risk) and non-exposed reference subcohorts, and followed them with clinical examinations, knee radiographs at baseline and 12, 24, 36, 48, 72 and 96 months, and biospecimen collection, to identify risk factors and biomarkers for the onset and progression of knee osteoarthritis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4983010/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SELECT was coordinated by SWOG, a national consortium of institutions and investigators that conducts multidisciplinary clinical trials to improve the practice of medicine in preventing, detecting, and treating cancer, and to enhance the quality of life for cancer survivors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27519183+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial (SELECT) was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, prostate cancer prevention study funded by the National Cancer Institute and conducted by SWOG (Southwest Oncology Group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32009305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To gain a more complete understanding of AYA enrollment patterns in both the pediatric and adult cooperative group settings, the objective of this current study was to evaluate AYA enrollment onto SWOG trials during the same time interval at NCI‐designated Cancer Centers, CCOP sites, and other sites that participate in NCI‐funded clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To this end, we used clinical, genotyping, and pre-treatment candidate protein marker data obtained from patients with mCRC randomized to the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB, now part of the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology (Alliance)) and the Southwest Oncology Group, CALGB/SWOG 80405.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3139891/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PCPT was a Phase III double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, that tested whether finasteride could reduce the period prevalence of prostate cancer during a 7-year intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2014 the CCOP transitioned into the NCORP to expand the reach and impact of the program and align its goals with the NCI National Clinical Trials Network.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25028457") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11092225/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7064039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NCTN provides funding and clinical trial infrastructure support to over 3000 sites via membership in NCTN network groups, including the SWOG Cancer Research Network (SWOG; formerly the Southwest Oncology Group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000595> "A cancer clinical trials network, formerly the Southwest Oncology Group, that is one of the network groups of the US National Cancer Institute's National Clinical Trials Network and runs multicentre cancer treatment and cancer prevention trials in adults at its member sites; its trial cohorts include the CALGB/SWOG 80405 trial in metastatic colorectal cancer, the Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial and the Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12584178+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A study of 500 incident colorectal cancer cases and population controls, matched for age, sex and general practitioner, was conducted in the UK to investigate this hypothesis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12584178+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Usual meat intake and lifetime smoking habits were estimated using a detailed questionnaire administered by interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29425227") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An age and sex matched control with no history of previous cancer at the time of recruitment was identified for each case between 1997 and 2000 at all 3 sites, and following 2000, friends or spouse of cases from Leeds site with no history of cancer at the time of recruitment were collected for the study to complement GP recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29425227") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, cases between the age of 45 and 80 years with histologically confirmed incident CRC and diagnosed in the period of 1997–2000, were identified at all three sites while for 2000–2013 only from Leeds.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29425227") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From the UK-CCSG dataset, CRC cases and controls from all three study sites (Leeds, Dundee and York) were included in the analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29425227") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a meta-analysis using two large population-based case-control datasets, the UK-Leeds Colorectal Cancer Study Group and the NIH-Colon Cancer Family Registry, having a combined total of 3325 cases and 2262 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12584178") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5806861/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001415.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following local ethical approval, colorectal cancer cases were recruited from 1997 until 2012 in Leeds, UK through surgical clinics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000596> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in the United Kingdom that recruited histologically confirmed incident cases aged 45–80, diagnosed in 1997–2000 at hospitals in Dundee, Leeds and York and in 2000–2013 in Leeds only, with controls matched for age and sex from the cases' general practice lists (supplemented after 2000 by friends or spouses of Leeds cases), all interviewed about diet, smoking and other lifestyle factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2709952/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional eligibility requirements were: aged 40–80 years, residence in one of the 33 counties, able to give informed consent and complete an interview, had a driver’s license or identification card issued by the North Carolina Department of Motor Vehicles (if under the age of 65), and had no objections from the primary physician in regards to contacting the individual.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2709952/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NCCCS II included patients with a first diagnosis of histologically confirmed invasive adenocarcinoma of the sigmoid colon, rectosigmoid, or rectum (hereafter collectively referred to as rectal cancer) between May 2001 and September 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "African American cases were oversampled to yield a 1∶1 Caucasian:African American ratio, and controls were sampled to match the distribution by race, age, and gender of the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were identified between October 1, 1996 and September 1, 2000 using a rapid ascertainment system implemented in cooperation with the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls younger than 65 years from the same 33-county area were selected from the Department of Motor Vehicles Registry database, and controls 65 years and older were selected from Health Care Financing Administration database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19336553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19842051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4067325/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6013500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, NCCCS was a population-based case-control study with participants drawn from 33 counties in eastern and central North Carolina.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000597> "A population-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in African Americans and whites in 33 counties of central and eastern North Carolina, United States, in which cases aged 40–80 were identified by rapid ascertainment through the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry, African Americans were oversampled, and controls were drawn from motor vehicle and Health Care Financing Administration records. Phase I enrolled colon cancer cases from October 1996 to September 2000 and phase II (NCCCS-II) cases of sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer from May 2001 to September 2006, both collecting interview data on diet, medication use and other risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40401725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, ATBC was a randomized placebo‐controlled trial (NCT00342992 clinicaltrials.gov) examining α‐tocopherol and/or β‐carotene for primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male Finnish smokers, aged 50–69 years at recruitment between 1985 and 1988.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40401725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident primary PDAC (International Classification of Diseases‐O‐3: C25.0‐C25.3, C25.7‐C25.9) was ascertained via linkage to the Finnish Cancer Registry through December 2011 for ATBC") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://atbcstudy.cancer.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, in order to evaluate the long-term effects of the vitamins on cancer incidence, and overall and cause-specific mortality, they were followed after the trial ended using data from the national registries in Finland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369914/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 5-year cumulative lung cancer incidence was highest in ATBC (2·2%), a cohort of currently smoking males, and lowest in EPIC-Norway (0·3%), a cohort of females younger than 60 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male Finnish smokers (N = 29,133) ages 50–69 years were assigned to receive either alpha-tocopherol (dl-α-tocopheryl-acetate, 50 mg/day), beta-carotene (20 mg/day), both vitamins, or placebo for 5–8 years (a median of 6.1 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329778/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9992367/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/atbc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Secondary objectives are to evaluate the effects of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene on the incidence of other major cancers and to study overall and cause-specific mortality and incidence of other non-communicable diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000598> "A randomized, placebo-controlled trial of alpha-tocopherol and beta-carotene supplements for the primary prevention of lung and other cancers in 29,133 male smokers aged 50–69 in Finland, recruited in 1985–1988 and supplemented for five to eight years, whose participants have since been followed as a cohort for cancer and other outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32674402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7400834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, GOCS is a population-based ambispective cohort of 1195 children, born in 2002–2003, from six low-middle income counties from the southeast area of Santiago, Chile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8553699/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annual measurements were carried out at Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos (INTA), Santiago, Chile, by trained dietitians, and since 2010 visits took place every 6 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8553699/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Height was measured on roughly a 6-month basis from childhood to adolescence between 2006 and 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8553699/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population represents a middle-low socioeconomic level and all participants were singleton births occurring during 2002-2003, who had birth weights between 2500 and 4500 g, with no medical or mental conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8553699/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a longitudinal follow-up of 1195 individuals recruited in 2006 (aged 3.5 years old) at different childcare centers from the South East Area of Santiago, Chile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34047840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3545681/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study sample was drawn from children enrolled in the Growth and Obesity Chilean Cohort Study, which assesses the association of early growth and development of adiposity and metabolic risk (21, 22).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000599> "A longitudinal cohort of 1,195 children born in 2002-2003 and recruited in 2006 at about 3.5 years of age from childcare centres of the low-to-middle income South East Area of Santiago, Chile, measured annually (six-monthly from 2010) at the Instituto de Nutrición y Tecnología en Alimentos into adolescence to study growth, puberty and obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5837648") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline KoGES 10030 (2001–2002) KoGES_ Ansan and Ansung study 173357 (2004–2013) KoGES_HEXA study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> "A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5837648") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population-based cohorts in the KoGES, including the KoGES_Ansan and Ansung study, the KoGES_health exam- inee (HEXA) study and the KoGES_cardiovascular disease as- sociation study (CAVAS), consist of community-dwellers and participants recruited from the national health examinee regis- try, men and women,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> "A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837648/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first stage of recruitment was completed during an extended time period for the KoGES_HEXA and the KoGES_CAVAS studies (2004–2013 and 2004–2011, respectively), which probably led to variations in exposures between participants recruited at early and late stages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> "A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we conducted a GWAS analysis on patients with gout in Korea based on the Health Examinees study (HEXA) cohort and KARE cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study (KoGES).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> "A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38060535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39050255") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11266026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HEXA cohort was initiated in 2004 to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans, targeting men and women over 40 years of age who visited medical examination centers in urban areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000600> "A population-based cohort of about 173,000 Korean men and women aged 40 and over recruited in 2004–2013 from the national health examinee registry at health examination centres, mainly in urban areas, as the largest cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for major chronic diseases in Koreans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10689-006-9104-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to investigate the factors, especially genetic components, responsible for CRC we established the Newfoundland Colorectal Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10689-006-9104-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Newfoundland (population 517,000) has the highest incidence of colorectal cancer of all Canadian provinces.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10689-006-9104-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pathology-confirmed cases of colorectal cancer diagnosed under age 75 between 1997 and 2000 (OFCCR) or between 1999 and 2003 (NFCCR) were identified from the respective provincial tumour registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6973587/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Newly diagnosed cases identified between 1999 and 2003 were frequency-matched by 5-year age group and sex with controls selected from the residents of NL through random digit dialing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34309201") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we examined large sets of common genetic variants (˜ 4.7 million SNPs and 254 CNVs/INDELs) and their associations with disease‐specific survival and recurrence/metastasis‐free survival in a colorectal cancer patient cohort (n = 505 and 495, respectively) followed up to 19 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17039269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21033532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4393623/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8637572/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/ng2089") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Newfoundland Familial Colon Cancer Registry at the Memorial University of Newfoundland") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000601> "A population-based registry of colorectal cancer patients in the Canadian province of Newfoundland and Labrador, run from Memorial University of Newfoundland, that in 1999–2003 recruited patients diagnosed under the age of 75 to study the genetic and familial factors behind the province's high colorectal cancer incidence and has followed them for recurrence and survival for up to 19 years, with controls for a population-based case-control study frequency-matched to the cases by age group and sex and selected from the province's residents by random digit dialling.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11994816/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we first performed GWAS of common side effects from COVID-19 booster vaccination utilizing a corporate genome cohort in the Japanese population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> "A corporate genome cohort of employees of Toshiba Corporation, a Japanese electronics company, whose health-care database for precision-medicine research holds genomic, health check-up, questionnaire and prescription data of consenting employees (over 11,600 of whom had given genetic samples by 2024), used for genetic studies such as of side effects after COVID-19 booster vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11994816/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This database includes genomic, health checkup, questionnaire, and prescription data of their employees who have individually informed consented.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> "A corporate genome cohort of employees of Toshiba Corporation, a Japanese electronics company, whose health-care database for precision-medicine research holds genomic, health check-up, questionnaire and prescription data of consenting employees (over 11,600 of whom had given genetic samples by 2024), used for genetic studies such as of side effects after COVID-19 booster vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11994816/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Toshiba has established a health-care database focusing on “Research aimed at realizing precision medicine that can select optimal preventive and treatment methods”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> "A corporate genome cohort of employees of Toshiba Corporation, a Japanese electronics company, whose health-care database for precision-medicine research holds genomic, health check-up, questionnaire and prescription data of consenting employees (over 11,600 of whom had given genetic samples by 2024), used for genetic studies such as of side effects after COVID-19 booster vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12531883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted at Toshiba Corp, an electronics manufacturer in Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> "A corporate genome cohort of employees of Toshiba Corporation, a Japanese electronics company, whose health-care database for precision-medicine research holds genomic, health check-up, questionnaire and prescription data of consenting employees (over 11,600 of whom had given genetic samples by 2024), used for genetic studies such as of side effects after COVID-19 booster vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40222985") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41100086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12531883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited study participants from 11 605 employees who had already provided genetic samples to the company.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000602> "A corporate genome cohort of employees of Toshiba Corporation, a Japanese electronics company, whose health-care database for precision-medicine research holds genomic, health check-up, questionnaire and prescription data of consenting employees (over 11,600 of whom had given genetic samples by 2024), used for genetic studies such as of side effects after COVID-19 booster vaccination.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000603> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000603>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=bioproject&id=225655") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12928021/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=bioproject&id=225655") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This substudy contains genotypes generated using Illumina Omni Express on additional WHI European American (EA) participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000603> "A genome-wide association sub-study of the Women's Health Initiative hormone therapy trials (dbGaP WHIMS+) of European-ancestry trial participants genotyped on the Illumina HumanOmniExpress array, selected so that together with WHI GARNET they represent the WHI European American hormone trial population, comprising the participants of the WHI Memory Study (an ancillary trial of hormone therapy and cognition in women aged 65–80) who were not in GARNET and other hormone trial women, aged 65 or over or younger, who were in neither WHIMS nor GARNET.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=bioproject&id=225655") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12928021/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=bioproject&id=225655") Annotation(rdfs:comment "When these participants are combined with the GARNET participants, they form a population that is representative of the entire WHI EA HT population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000603> "A genome-wide association sub-study of the Women's Health Initiative hormone therapy trials (dbGaP WHIMS+) of European-ancestry trial participants genotyped on the Illumina HumanOmniExpress array, selected so that together with WHI GARNET they represent the WHI European American hormone trial population, comprising the participants of the WHI Memory Study (an ancillary trial of hormone therapy and cognition in women aged 65–80) who were not in GARNET and other hormone trial women, aged 65 or over or younger, who were in neither WHIMS nor GARNET.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=bioproject&id=225655") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12928021/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "3) women from the WHI-HT younger than age 65 at enrollment who were neither in WHIMS nor GARNET.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000603> "A genome-wide association sub-study of the Women's Health Initiative hormone therapy trials (dbGaP WHIMS+) of European-ancestry trial participants genotyped on the Illumina HumanOmniExpress array, selected so that together with WHI GARNET they represent the WHI European American hormone trial population, comprising the participants of the WHI Memory Study (an ancillary trial of hormone therapy and cognition in women aged 65–80) who were not in GARNET and other hormone trial women, aged 65 or over or younger, who were in neither WHIMS nor GARNET.")
