AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20732625") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21473745") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3082291/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participating families were recruited between April 2003 and April 2007 in 11 European specialist ADHD centres") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000607> "A European multi-site family sample of children aged 5 to 17 with DSM-IV combined-type ADHD, their siblings and parents, all of white European Caucasian descent, recruited in 2003-2007 at specialist ADHD clinics in eight countries for molecular genetic studies of ADHD, including candidate-gene, linkage and genome-wide association analyses; a second phase (IMAGE II) combined ADHD cases from the original project and from further clinics in Germany, the Netherlands and the UK with population controls for genome-wide association.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11799070+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Family Blood Pressure Program (FBPP) consists of 4 independently established multicenter networks of investigators who have complementary approaches to the genetics of blood pressure levels and hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11799070+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "standardized clinic and laboratory protocols for core variables to facilitate direct comparison of results among networks") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11799070+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "standardized clinic and laboratory protocols for core variables to facilitate direct comparison of results among networks, (2) coordination among laboratories to avoid unnecessary duplication of effort, (3) utilization of a single laboratory for genome-wide marker typing, and (4) a pooled data set containing phenotype and genotype information") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FBPP is comprised of 4 different networks: GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN, and SAPPHIRe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FBPP pooled database (version 3) of 13,592 participants from 4 different networks represents one of the largest compilations of ethnically diverse data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3405908/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1995 the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute established a collaboration of 4 multicenter networks, known as the Family Blood Pressure Program (FBPP), to investigate the genetic determinants of inter-individual BP variation in Asians, African Americans, Mexican Americans, and Caucasians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11799070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1201342/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01553-1/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1553_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The initial exam (1995-2000) enrolled 1583 non-Hispanic white participants from Rochester, Minnesota, and 1854 African American participants from Jackson, Mississippi.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000608> "An NHLBI-sponsored programme uniting four independently established multicentre family networks (GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN and SAPPHIRe) that recruited African American, Mexican American, Asian and non-Hispanic white participants, with standardised core protocols and a pooled phenotype and genotype data set of 13,592 individuals, to study the genetic determinants of blood pressure and hypertension.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17370032") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Women’s Health Study (WHS) was a randomized, double-blind, clinical trial of low-dose aspirin and vitamin E in the primary prevention of CVD and cancer among 39,876 apparently healthy women age ≥45 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609> "A randomized, double-blind trial of low-dose aspirin and vitamin E for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer among 39,876 apparently healthy US female health professionals aged 45 or older, begun in 1992 and followed as a prospective cohort for incident disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17370032") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study assessed awareness and determinants of cholesterol knowledge among 39,876 US female health professionals in the Women’s Health Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609> "A randomized, double-blind trial of low-dose aspirin and vitamin E for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer among 39,876 apparently healthy US female health professionals aged 45 or older, begun in 1992 and followed as a prospective cohort for incident disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By linking genome-wide data to the existing epidemiologic databank of the parent WHS, which includes comprehensive dietary, behavioral, and traditional exposure data on each participant since cohort inception in 1992, the WGHS will also allow exploration of gene-environment and gene-gene interactions as they relate to incident disease states.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609> "A randomized, double-blind trial of low-dose aspirin and vitamin E for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer among 39,876 apparently healthy US female health professionals aged 45 or older, begun in 1992 and followed as a prospective cohort for incident disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1852917/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18070814") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18070814+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, with continued follow-up of the WHS, the WGHS provides a unique scientific resource-a full-cohort, prospective, genome-wide association study among initially healthy American women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000609> "A randomized, double-blind trial of low-dose aspirin and vitamin E for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer among 39,876 apparently healthy US female health professionals aged 45 or older, begun in 1992 and followed as a prospective cohort for incident disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Box 19024 Mail Stop M4-B402 Seattle, WA 98109-1024") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, we are investigating the impact of germline genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors on the tumor genome, microbiome and immune response and the impact on survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO) is an international collaboration that focuses on the identification and characterization of genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer (CRC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GECCO coordinating center manages individual level genetic and epidemiological data of over 130,000 participants from 70 studies from North America, Australia, Asia, and Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The coordinating center for this international consortium is based at Fred Hutch.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001415.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trail (PLCO): PLCO enrolled 154,934 participants (men and women, aged between 55 and 74 years) at ten centers into a large, randomized, two-arm trial to determine the effectiveness of screening to reduce cancer mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.fredhutch.org/en/research/divisions/public-health-sciences-division/research/cancer-prevention/genetics-epidemiology-colorectal-cancer-consortium-gecco.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001415.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium (GECCO) is a collaborative effort comprised of a coordinating center and scientific researchers from well-characterized cohort and case-control studies conducted in North America and Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000610> "An international consortium coordinated at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Center in Seattle that pools individual-level genetic and epidemiological data from about 70 colorectal cancer case-control, cohort and trial studies in North America, Australia, Asia and Europe, over 130,000 participants, to identify genetic risk factors and gene-environment interactions for colorectal cancer and study their effects on tumours and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18708398+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We evaluated the most significant single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNP) in these loci using a worldwide consortium of 13 groups (PRACTICAL).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2776652/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were included from 13 studies comprising prostate cancer cases and controls: 6 from Europe, 5 from North America, and 2 from Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2776652/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To this end, we have established a new international consortium, PRACTICAL (Prostate cancer association group to investigate cancer associated alterations in the genome).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26387087") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed the relationship of the height and BMI genetic risk scores with prostate cancer risk, stage, and grade across all 22 eligible studies contributing to PRACTICAL using logistic regression to compute ORs, with robust standard errors to account for within-study clustering.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COSM Cohort of Swedish Men Stockholm Sweden Population-based cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected individual-level data for 10 404 participants from 14 PRACTICAL Consortium study groups across North America (five study groups), Europe (six study groups), Asia (one study group), and Australia (two study groups).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a case–control study based on 20,848 prostate cancers and 20,214 controls of European ancestry from 22 studies in the PRACTICAL consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18708398") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4596899/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8381233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5008293/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In association with the Prostate Cancer Association Group to Investigate Cancer Associated Alterations in the Genome (PRACTICAL) consortium for prostate cancer predisposition study, we investigated genetic predisposition to prostate cancer in men of Han Chinese ancestry using the custom Illumina single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) array (iCOGS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000611> "An international consortium of prostate cancer study groups, reported in 2008 as a worldwide consortium of 13 groups, that pools genotype and clinical data from prostate cancer case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia to investigate inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its clinical course.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29452397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6530395/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Essentially, the study participants were Singaporeans or permanent residents of three ethnic groups (ie, Chinese, Malay and Indian), aged ≥21 years and free from cancer, heart disease, stroke, renal failure, asthma and mental illness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612> "A population-based cohort of 14,530 Singapore citizens and permanent residents of Chinese, Malay and Indian ethnicity aged 21 years and older, recruited in 2004–2010 mainly from the Singapore Prospective Study Program and the Singapore Cardiovascular Cohort Study, with additional recruitment oversampling Malays and Indians, to study chronic disease in a multi-ethnic Asian population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29452397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6530395/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the recruitment of additional participants, the minority ethnic groups, Malays and Indians, were recruited following a convenience sampling methodology and purposively oversampled through public outreach at community events, mosques and temples as well as referrals from existing cohort members in addition to household visitation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612> "A population-based cohort of 14,530 Singapore citizens and permanent residents of Chinese, Malay and Indian ethnicity aged 21 years and older, recruited in 2004–2010 mainly from the Singapore Prospective Study Program and the Singapore Cardiovascular Cohort Study, with additional recruitment oversampling Malays and Indians, to study chronic disease in a multi-ethnic Asian population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29452397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6530395/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MEC participants were mainly recruited from the existing cohorts between 2004 and 2007, that is, Singapore Prospective Study Programme (SP2) and Singapore Cardiovascular Cohort Study (SCCS2),16 17 with additional participants recruited between 2007 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612> "A population-based cohort of 14,530 Singapore citizens and permanent residents of Chinese, Malay and Indian ethnicity aged 21 years and older, recruited in 2004–2010 mainly from the Singapore Prospective Study Program and the Singapore Cardiovascular Cohort Study, with additional recruitment oversampling Malays and Indians, to study chronic disease in a multi-ethnic Asian population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29452397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31110091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6530395/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Multi-Ethnic Cohort (MEC) Study is a population-based study in Singapore (n=14 530) with recruitment conducted between 2004 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000612> "A population-based cohort of 14,530 Singapore citizens and permanent residents of Chinese, Malay and Indian ethnicity aged 21 years and older, recruited in 2004–2010 mainly from the Singapore Prospective Study Program and the Singapore Cardiovascular Cohort Study, with additional recruitment oversampling Malays and Indians, to study chronic disease in a multi-ethnic Asian population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADDITION-Denmark consisted of two phases: (i) a stepwise screening programme; and (ii) a cluster-randomised, parallel-group trial comparing the effects of intensive multifactorial treatment with routine care among individuals with screen-detected type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613> "The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, between 2001 and 2006, a population-based stepwise screening programme was performed among people aged 40–69 years without known diabetes in 181 general practices in Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613> "The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe study7 was a trial of intensive treatment of people with screen-detected diabetes, which included training in motivational interviewing for GPs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613> "The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32071038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7330202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Training of GPs in intensive multifactorial treatment, with or without motivational interviewing, was not associated with a reduction in mortality or CVD among those with screen-detected diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000613> "The Danish arm of the ADDITION-Europe trial, in which people aged 40–69 without known diabetes registered with 181 general practices in Denmark were screened stepwise for diabetes in 2001–2006 and those with screen-detected type 2 diabetes, in practices cluster-randomised to routine care or intensive multifactorial treatment (with or without GP training in motivational interviewing), were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3136726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, ADDITION-Europe consisted of two phases: a screening phase and a pragmatic, cluster-randomised, parallel-group trial in Denmark, the Netherlands, and the UK (in Cambridge and Leicester).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614> "A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3136726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a pragmatic, cluster-randomised, parallel-group trial done in Denmark, the Netherlands, and the UK, 343 general practices were randomly assigned screening of registered patients aged 40–69 years without known diabetes followed by routine care of diabetes or screening followed by intensive treatment of multiple risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614> "A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3136726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Screening identified 3233 patients with type 2 diabetes, of whom 3057 agreed to take part (Denmark, n=1533; Cambridge, UK, n=867; Netherlands, n=498; and Leicester, UK, n=159).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614> "A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21705063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3136726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "When compared with routine care, an intervention to promote target-driven, intensive management of patients with type 2 diabetes detected by screening was associated with small increases in the prescription of drugs and improvements in cardiovascular risk factors, but was not associated with significant reductions in the incidence of cardiovascular events or death over 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000614> "A pragmatic cluster-randomised trial in 343 general practices in Denmark, the Netherlands and the UK, in which registered patients aged 40–69 without known diabetes were screened and the 3,057 with screen-detected type 2 diabetes received routine care or early intensive multifactorial treatment and were followed for cardiovascular events and death.")

