AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16466435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed anthropometric measurements were taken from both parents at 28 weeks' gestation, and from their children at birth, 12 weeks, 1 year and 2 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000616> "A prospective family study of both parents and their children from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16466435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Insulin and other biochemical analysis were measured in fasting parental samples and an umbilical cord blood sample taken at delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000616> "A prospective family study of both parents and their children from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16466435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Exeter Family Study of Childhood Health is a prospective study, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis, and to identify genetic polymorphisms that play a role in determining birthweight and early postnatal growth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000616> "A prospective family study of both parents and their children from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16466435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16466435+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 1017 families from a postcode-defined area in central Exeter.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000616> "A prospective family study of both parents and their children from a postcode-defined area of central Exeter, United Kingdom, with anthropometry and fasting biochemistry at 28 weeks of gestation, cord blood at delivery and child follow-up to age 2 years, set up to test the fetal insulin hypothesis and identify genetic variants influencing birthweight and early postnatal growth.")

