AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were collected on a subset of participants in 1996-1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NHS II was established in 1989 to study a population younger than the original NHS cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nurses’ Health Studies are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women (https://nurseshealthstudy.org/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12225639/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Started in 1989, NHSII recruited 116,429 female registered nurses ages 25–42 from 14 states with large numbers of registered nurses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12225639/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study participants were followed biennially by mailed questionnaires, with NHS participants responding to surveys in even years and NHSII participants responding in odd years, with response rates of ≥90% (Bao et al., 2016b; Morabia, 2016).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38677085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12225639/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population is comprised of participants from two nationwide prospective cohorts, the Nurses’ Health Study (NHS) and the Nurses’ Health Study II (NHSII), which have been described in detail elsewhere (Bao et al., 2016a; Morabia, 2016).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000619> "A prospective cohort of 116,429 female registered nurses aged 25–42 recruited in 1989 from 14 states of the United States, a younger population than the original Nurses' Health Study, followed by biennial mailed questionnaires and biospecimen collection to study risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8243879/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All EA and AA participants were genotyped with the Illumina OmniExpress and Illumina OmniExpressExome BeadChips (Illumina, San Diego, CA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620> "A sample of healthy controls of European American and African American ancestry recruited at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, National Institutes of Health, USA, who did not meet criteria for alcohol dependence or other major psychiatric disorders on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV and gave blood samples used for genome-wide DNA methylation analysis and genotyping on Illumina OmniExpress arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8243879/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants completed the Structured Clinical Interview for Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM)-IV-TR (SCID-IV) and were included if they did not meet criteria for alcohol dependence or other major psychiatric disorders and were considered healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620> "A sample of healthy controls of European American and African American ancestry recruited at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, National Institutes of Health, USA, who did not meet criteria for alcohol dependence or other major psychiatric disorders on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV and gave blood samples used for genome-wide DNA methylation analysis and genotyping on Illumina OmniExpress arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8243879/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants provided a blood sample which was used for genome-wide DNA methylation analysis and clinical marker collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620> "A sample of healthy controls of European American and African American ancestry recruited at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, National Institutes of Health, USA, who did not meet criteria for alcohol dependence or other major psychiatric disorders on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV and gave blood samples used for genome-wide DNA methylation analysis and genotyping on Illumina OmniExpress arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8243879/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample consisted of 119 European American (EA) and 82 African American (AA) healthy controls that were recruited at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism (NIAAA) at the National Institutes of Health (NIH), USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000620> "A sample of healthy controls of European American and African American ancestry recruited at the National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, National Institutes of Health, USA, who did not meet criteria for alcohol dependence or other major psychiatric disorders on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV and gave blood samples used for genome-wide DNA methylation analysis and genotyping on Illumina OmniExpress arrays.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41909911") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12973162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the SCCS enrolled ~85,000 English‐speaking individuals aged 40–79 years during years 2002–2009 in 12 states in the southeastern United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> "A prospective cohort of about 85,000 English-speaking adults aged 40–79, predominantly Black and low-income, enrolled in 2002–2009 in 12 states of the southeastern United States, designed to study racial disparities in cancer and other chronic disease outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41909911") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12973162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To accomplish this aim, we utilize data from the Southern Community Cohort Study (SCCS), a cohort with rich multilevel data designed to help address racial disparities in cancer outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> "A prospective cohort of about 85,000 English-speaking adults aged 40–79, predominantly Black and low-income, enrolled in 2002–2009 in 12 states of the southeastern United States, designed to study racial disparities in cancer and other chronic disease outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41909911") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosmedicine/article?id=10.1371/journal.pmed.1001830") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of approximately 85,000 SCCS participants, over two-thirds were African-American, and over half were poor, with an annual household income of less than US$15,000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> "A prospective cohort of about 85,000 English-speaking adults aged 40–79, predominantly Black and low-income, enrolled in 2002–2009 in 12 states of the southeastern United States, designed to study racial disparities in cancer and other chronic disease outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41909911") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosmedicine/article?id=10.1371/journal.pmed.1001830") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SCCS was funded by the National Cancer Institute and was initiated in 2001 with the goal of addressing unresolved questions about the causes of cancer and other chronic diseases, as well as reasons for health disparities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> "A prospective cohort of about 85,000 English-speaking adults aged 40–79, predominantly Black and low-income, enrolled in 2002–2009 in 12 states of the southeastern United States, designed to study racial disparities in cancer and other chronic disease outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41609390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41909911") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosmedicine/article?id=10.1371/journal.pmed.1001830") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We examined the associations of adherence to the DGA with total and cause-specific mortality in the Southern Community Cohort Study, a prospective study that recruited 84,735 American adults, aged 40–79 y, from 12 southeastern US states during 2002–2009, mostly through community health centers that serve low-income populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000621> "A prospective cohort of about 85,000 English-speaking adults aged 40–79, predominantly Black and low-income, enrolled in 2002–2009 in 12 states of the southeastern United States, designed to study racial disparities in cancer and other chronic disease outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12675286/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After providing informed consent, participants donated blood samples for genotyping and agreed to have their EMRs de-identified, encrypted and securely transmitted to the TPMI server.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12675286/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EMR access is both retrospective and prospective, allowing longitudinal studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12675286/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genetic profiling is done with population-optimized arrays of single-nucleotide polymorphisms for people of Han Chinese ancestry, which enable genome-wide association3,4, phenome-wide association5,6 and polygenic risk score7,8 studies to be performed to evaluate common disease risk and pharmacogenetic response.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41092961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41092961+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we present the Taiwan Precision Medicine Initiative (TPMI), established by Academia Sinica in collaboration with 16 major medical centres around Taiwan, which has recruited 565,390 participants who consent to provide DNA samples for genetic profiling and grant access to their electronic medical records (EMRs) for research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000622> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 565,000 participants recruited by Academia Sinica with 16 major medical centres across Taiwan, genotyped on arrays optimised for Han Chinese ancestry and linked to retrospective and prospective electronic medical records, for genome-wide, phenome-wide and polygenic risk studies of common disease and pharmacogenetic response.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort profile: the Baependi Heart Study-a family-based, highly admixed cohort study in a rural Brazilian town.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> "A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Having expanded beyond cardiovascular health outcomes, the phenotype datasets now include genetics, biochemistry, anthropometry, mental health, sleep and circadian rhythms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> "A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Probands were recruited in Baependi, a small rural town in the state of Minas Gerais, Brazil, following by first-degree and then increasingly more distant relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> "A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Baependi Heart Study was set up in 2005 to develop a longitudinal family-based cohort study that reflects on some of the genetic and lifestyle-related peculiarities of the Brazilian populations, in order to evaluate genetic and environmental influences on CVD risk factor traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> "A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27797990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27797990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first follow-up wave took place in 2010, and the second in 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000623> "A longitudinal family-based cohort of highly admixed residents of Baependi, a small rural town in Minas Gerais, Brazil, recruited from 2005 through probands and their relatives and followed up in 2010 and 2016 to study genetic and environmental influences on cardiovascular risk factors, sleep, circadian rhythms and mental health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-017-0239-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the same period a total of 1,053,000 biological samples have been collected from participants, including maternal, paternal and infant blood, cord blood, placenta, umbilical cord, and maternal and infant stool samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Guangzhou, China, recruited in early pregnancy at Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center from 2012, with biological samples from mothers, fathers and infants and planned follow-up of the children to age 18 years, to study social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28321694+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At 30 April 2016, a total of 75,422 questionnaires have been collected, while 14,696 live births have occurred with planned follow-up of cohort children until age 18 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Guangzhou, China, recruited in early pregnancy at Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center from 2012, with biological samples from mothers, fathers and infants and planned follow-up of the children to age 18 years, to study social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28321694+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women who reside in Guangzhou and who attend Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center (GWCMC) for antenatal care in early pregnancy (<20 weeks' gestation) are eligible for inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Guangzhou, China, recruited in early pregnancy at Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center from 2012, with biological samples from mothers, fathers and infants and planned follow-up of the children to age 18 years, to study social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28321694+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study recruitment commenced in February 2012, with an overall participation rate of 76.3%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Guangzhou, China, recruited in early pregnancy at Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center from 2012, with biological samples from mothers, fathers and infants and planned follow-up of the children to age 18 years, to study social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28321694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28321694+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Born in Guangzhou Cohort Study (BIGCS) is a large-scale prospective observational study investigating the role of social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development in an urban setting in southern China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000624> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Guangzhou, China, recruited in early pregnancy at Guangzhou Women and Children's Medical Center from 2012, with biological samples from mothers, fathers and infants and planned follow-up of the children to age 18 years, to study social, biological and environmental influences on pregnancy and child health and development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22993228") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3686263/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GARP study comprises white sibling pairs of Dutch origin affected by OA at multiple sites and is aimed at identifying determinants of OA susceptibility and progression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> "A cohort of about 190 white Dutch sibling pairs aged 40–70 with symptomatic osteoarthritis at multiple joint sites, recruited from rheumatology, orthopaedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, the Netherlands, by Leiden University Medical Center to identify determinants of osteoarthritis susceptibility and progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited from the rheumatologic, orthopedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> "A cohort of about 190 white Dutch sibling pairs aged 40–70 with symptomatic osteoarthritis at multiple joint sites, recruited from rheumatology, orthopaedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, the Netherlands, by Leiden University Medical Center to identify determinants of osteoarthritis susceptibility and progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is part of the Genetic ARthrosis and Progression (GARP) study, a cohort study aimed at identifying determinants of OA susceptibility and progression.[12] In this cohort, 192 Caucasian sib-pairs (384 patients), aged 40 to 70 years were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> "A cohort of about 190 white Dutch sibling pairs aged 40–70 with symptomatic osteoarthritis at multiple joint sites, recruited from rheumatology, orthopaedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, the Netherlands, by Leiden University Medical Center to identify determinants of osteoarthritis susceptibility and progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To be included, patient should have symptomatic OA at multiple joint sites in the hands or OA in two or more of the following joint sites: hand, spine (cervical or lumbar), knee, or hip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> "A cohort of about 190 white Dutch sibling pairs aged 40–70 with symptomatic osteoarthritis at multiple joint sites, recruited from rheumatology, orthopaedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, the Netherlands, by Leiden University Medical Center to identify determinants of osteoarthritis susceptibility and progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198737/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4660891/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics Osteoarthritis and Progression (GARP) study from The Netherlands was supported by Leiden University Medical Centre, the Dutch Arthritis Association, and Pfizer Inc., Groton, Connecticut.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000625> "A cohort of about 190 white Dutch sibling pairs aged 40–70 with symptomatic osteoarthritis at multiple joint sites, recruited from rheumatology, orthopaedic and general practice clinics around Leiden, the Netherlands, by Leiden University Medical Center to identify determinants of osteoarthritis susceptibility and progression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11171146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PHS I was initiated in 1982 and was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of 22,071 US male physicians aged 40–84 years aimed at evaluating the impact of aspirin and beta-carotene on cardiovascular disease (CVD) and cancer outcomes, respectively [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> "A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11171146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PHS II was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial that followed in 1996 and that included 7641 PHS I participants plus an additional 7000 US male physicians aged ≥50 years to determine the impact of beta-carotene, vitamin C, vitamin E, and a daily multivitamin on the prevention of CVD, cancer, and other aging-related outcomes [23,24,25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> "A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11171146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Physicians’ Health Study (PHS) cohort comprises two groups: PHS I and II [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> "A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11171146/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The morbidity and mortality outcomes for the PHS participants were determined through annual questionnaires and endpoint follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> "A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38893188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001081.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original trial ended, but the men are followed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000626> "A cohort of US male physicians enrolled in two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials, PHS I (begun in 1982 with physicians aged 40–84) and PHS II, testing low-dose aspirin, beta-carotene and vitamins for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease and cancer, and followed thereafter as a prospective cohort.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9644178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 2508 individuals were eligible to participate, gave written informed consent, and completed a questionnaire") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627> "A cohort of 2,508 healthy young adults of Irish ancestry aged 18–28, recruited at Trinity College Dublin, Ireland, in 2003–2004, with plasma and serum samples and genotypes used to study genetic influences on circulating metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9644178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were collected as part of the Trinity Student Study (TSS), in which a cohort of healthy young adults (aged 18–28 y) were recruited at Trinity College Dublin over a 1-y period (2003–2004), as described previously (36–38).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627> "A cohort of 2,508 healthy young adults of Irish ancestry aged 18–28, recruited at Trinity College Dublin, Ireland, in 2003–2004, with plasma and serum samples and genotypes used to study genetic influences on circulating metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9644178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This has previously allowed study of genetic associations with multiple metabolites in plasma and serum in the TSS cohort (33).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627> "A cohort of 2,508 healthy young adults of Irish ancestry aged 18–28, recruited at Trinity College Dublin, Ireland, in 2003–2004, with plasma and serum samples and genotypes used to study genetic influences on circulating metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36774100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3545809/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Although the TSS cohort was 100% ethnically Irish, the GABC cohort was of mixed ancestry, consistent with the University of Michigan student population from which participants were recruited (24).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000627> "A cohort of 2,508 healthy young adults of Irish ancestry aged 18–28, recruited at Trinity College Dublin, Ireland, in 2003–2004, with plasma and serum samples and genotypes used to study genetic influences on circulating metabolites.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6336846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants for the discovery GWAS in this study were recruited from five sites in the eastern United States, for studies of the genetics of drug or alcohol dependence - the Yale-Penn study10–13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628> "A sample of more than 11,000 African American and European American participants recruited through treatment centres and advertisements at sites including Yale University, the University of Pennsylvania, McLean Hospital and the Medical University of South Carolina for genetic studies of cocaine, opioid and alcohol dependence, genotyped in three waves (Yale-Penn 1–3).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6336846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided written informed consent and the study was approved by the institutional review board at each participating site (Yale Human Research Protection Program, University of Pennsylvania Institutional Review Board, University of Connecticut Human Subjects Protection Program, Medical University of South Carolina Institutional Review Board for Human Research, and the McLean Hospital Institutional Review Board).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628> "A sample of more than 11,000 African American and European American participants recruited through treatment centres and advertisements at sites including Yale University, the University of Pennsylvania, McLean Hospital and the Medical University of South Carolina for genetic studies of cocaine, opioid and alcohol dependence, genotyped in three waves (Yale-Penn 1–3).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described previously11, specimens from participants in the discovery sample were genotyped using one of three genome-wide SNP arrays: the Illumina HumanOmni1-Quad v1.0 microarray containing 988,306 autosomal SNPs (Yale-Penn 1), the Illumina Infinium Human Core Exome microarray containing 265,919 exonic SNPs and approximately 240,000 tagging SNPs (Yale-Penn 2), and the Illumina Multi-ethnic Global Array containing 1,779,819 markers representing five major populations (Yale-Penn 3).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628> "A sample of more than 11,000 African American and European American participants recruited through treatment centres and advertisements at sites including Yale University, the University of Pennsylvania, McLean Hospital and the Medical University of South Carolina for genetic studies of cocaine, opioid and alcohol dependence, genotyped in three waves (Yale-Penn 1–3).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30655502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery sample was derived from the Yale-Penn sample, a cohort of 11,439 participants (5758 AAs and 5681 EAs) recruited through treatment centers and advertisements for genetic studies of cocaine, opioid or alcohol dependence11.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000628> "A sample of more than 11,000 African American and European American participants recruited through treatment centres and advertisements at sites including Yale University, the University of Pennsylvania, McLean Hospital and the Medical University of South Carolina for genetic studies of cocaine, opioid and alcohol dependence, genotyped in three waves (Yale-Penn 1–3).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837648/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KoGES consortium was designed to investigate and assess genetic and environmental factors as correlates or determinants of the incidence of chronic diseases in Koreans, such as type 2 diabetes, hypertension, cardiovascular diseases and cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837648/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first stage of recruitment was completed during an extended time period for the KoGES_HEXA and the KoGES_CAVAS studies (2004–2013 and 2004–2011, respectively), which probably led to variations in exposures between participants recruited at early and late stages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837648/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population-based cohorts in the KoGES, including the KoGES_Ansan and Ansung study, the KoGES_health examinee (HEXA) study and the KoGES_cardiovascular disease association study (CAVAS), consist of community-dwellers and participants recruited from the national health examinee registry, men and women, aged ≥ 40 years at baseline (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837648/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The KoGES_cardiovascular disease association study (CAVAS) was initiated to investigate risk factors for CVD in addition to the major disease targets of the KoGES by setting up a community-based cohort in rural counties.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12096789/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CAVAS (2005–2012) enrolled 28,337 individuals aged ≥ 40 years from rural areas, while the HEXA study (2004–2013) enrolled 173,199 individuals aged ≥ 40 years from health examination centers in metropolitan and major cities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27085081") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42158258") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40405233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12096789/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up surveys were conducted for CAVAS participants in six of the 11 counties and for HEXA participants in 17 of 39 centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000629> "A population-based cohort of about 28,000 men and women aged 40 and over living in rural areas of South Korea, recruited in 2004–2011 as part of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study, with follow-up surveys in some counties, to study cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and their genetic and environmental risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3869031/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore in-depth community data are collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> "A household-based cohort of individuals, households and communities in provinces across China, surveyed repeatedly since 1989 with all household members studied and in-depth community data collected, to understand how social and economic change in China affects nutrition and health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3869031/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CHNS cohort includes new household formation and replacement communities and households; all household members are studied.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> "A household-based cohort of individuals, households and communities in provinces across China, surveyed repeatedly since 1989 with all household members studied and in-depth community data collected, to understand how social and economic change in China affects nutrition and health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3869031/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CHNS rounds have been completed in 1989, 1991, 1993, 1997, 2000, 2004, 2006, 2009, and 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> "A household-based cohort of individuals, households and communities in provinces across China, surveyed repeatedly since 1989 with all household members studied and in-depth community data collected, to understand how social and economic change in China affects nutrition and health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3869031/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CHNS was designed as a prospective household-based study that includes multiple ages and cohorts across nine diverse provinces and eight rounds of surveys between 1989 and 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> "A household-based cohort of individuals, households and communities in provinces across China, surveyed repeatedly since 1989 with all household members studied and in-depth community data collected, to understand how social and economic change in China affects nutrition and health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24341753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24341753+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The China Health and Nutrition Survey (CHNS) began in 1989 with the goal of creating a multilevel method of data collection from individuals and households and their communities to understand how the wide-ranging social and economic changes in China affect a wide array of nutrition and health-related outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000630> "A household-based cohort of individuals, households and communities in provinces across China, surveyed repeatedly since 1989 with all household members studied and in-depth community data collected, to understand how social and economic change in China affects nutrition and health outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32529242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 300-Obese (300-OB) cohort, one of the studies of the Human Functional Genomics Project, comprises a group of more than 300 individuals of Western-European ancestry with a body mass index (BMI) greater than or equal to greater than or equal to 27 kg/m2, aged between 55 and 80 years (12).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> "A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32529242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was designed to discover novel pathways contributing to CVD in overweight and obese individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> "A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32529242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to investigate the association of aldosterone concentrations with inflammation, metabolic disturbances, and atherosclerosis in overweight and obese individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> "A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36522747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "300OB is an obese cohort of 302 individuals aged 54–81 years old, who were enrolled in the study at the Radboud University Medical Center, Nijmegen, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> "A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320834/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36522747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9753387/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, all participants had a body mass index (BMI) ≥ 27 kg/m2 at screening (mean = 30.73, median = 29.89).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000631> "A cohort of about 300 overweight or obese adults (BMI of 27 kg/m2 or more) aged 54–81 of Western European ancestry, enrolled at Radboud University Medical Center in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, within the Human Functional Genomics Project to discover pathways, including inflammation and immune responses, that contribute to cardiovascular disease in overweight and obese people.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37458272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37458272+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Persons 65 to 85 years of age with a global Clinical Dementia Rating score of 0 (range, 0 to 3, with 0 indicating no cognitive impairment and 3 severe dementia), a score on the Mini-Mental State Examination of 25 or more (range, 0 to 30, with lower scores indicating poorer cognition), and elevated brain amyloid levels on 18F-florbetapir positron-emission tomography (PET) were enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632> "A phase 3 clinical prevention trial that screened cognitively unimpaired adults aged 65–85 with amyloid PET at 67 sites in Australia, Canada, Japan and the USA from 2014 to 2017 and tested, in those with elevated brain amyloid, whether the anti-amyloid antibody solanezumab slows cognitive decline in preclinical Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12825300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were screened for the A4 study from 67 sites across Australia, Canada, Japan and the USA between April 2014 to December 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632> "A phase 3 clinical prevention trial that screened cognitively unimpaired adults aged 65–85 with amyloid PET at 67 sites in Australia, Canada, Japan and the USA from 2014 to 2017 and tested, in those with elevated brain amyloid, whether the anti-amyloid antibody solanezumab slows cognitive decline in preclinical Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12825300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Anti-Amyloid Treatment in Asymptomatic AD (A4) study was a phase 3 clinical prevention trial (ClinicalTrials.gov Number: NCT02008357) to determine if solanezumab, a monoclonal antibody against monomeric forms of Aβ, could slow the progression of cognitive decline in people with preclinical AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632> "A phase 3 clinical prevention trial that screened cognitively unimpaired adults aged 65–85 with amyloid PET at 67 sites in Australia, Canada, Japan and the USA from 2014 to 2017 and tested, in those with elevated brain amyloid, whether the anti-amyloid antibody solanezumab slows cognitive decline in preclinical Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41569280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12825300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were 4486 pre-randomization participants who were screened for the A4 study and underwent amyloid PET scanning.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000632> "A phase 3 clinical prevention trial that screened cognitively unimpaired adults aged 65–85 with amyloid PET at 67 sites in Australia, Canada, Japan and the USA from 2014 to 2017 and tested, in those with elevated brain amyloid, whether the anti-amyloid antibody solanezumab slows cognitive decline in preclinical Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22506305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At age 15 (CATSS-15) and 18 (CATSS-18), twins and parents complete questionnaires that, in addition to assessments of somatic and mental health, include measures of personality development and psychosocial adaptation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> "An ongoing longitudinal study of all twins born in Sweden since July 1992, whose parents are interviewed about the children's somatic and mental health and social environment at age 9 or 12, with follow-up questionnaires at ages 15 and 18 and clinical assessments at 15 of screen-positive twin pairs and controls, to study the aetiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in later adjustment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22506305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 2004, parents of twins are interviewed regarding the children's somatic and mental health and social environment in connection with their 9th or 12th birthdays (CATSS-9/12).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> "An ongoing longitudinal study of all twins born in Sweden since July 1992, whose parents are interviewed about the children's somatic and mental health and social environment at age 9 or 12, with follow-up questionnaires at ages 15 and 18 and clinical assessments at 15 of screen-positive twin pairs and controls, to study the aetiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in later adjustment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22506305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CATSS study has the potential of answering important questions on the etiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in the development of later adjustment problems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> "An ongoing longitudinal study of all twins born in Sweden since July 1992, whose parents are interviewed about the children's somatic and mental health and social environment at age 9 or 12, with follow-up questionnaires at ages 15 and 18 and clinical assessments at 15 of screen-positive twin pairs and controls, to study the aetiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in later adjustment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22506305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Child and Adolescent Twin Study in Sweden (CATSS) is an ongoing longitudinal twin study targeting all twins born in Sweden since July 1, 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> "An ongoing longitudinal study of all twins born in Sweden since July 1992, whose parents are interviewed about the children's somatic and mental health and social environment at age 9 or 12, with follow-up questionnaires at ages 15 and 18 and clinical assessments at 15 of screen-positive twin pairs and controls, to study the aetiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in later adjustment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22506305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22506305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twin pairs in CATSS-9/12 with one or both twins screening positive for autism spectrum disorders, attention deficit/hyperactivity disorder, tic disorders, developmental coordination disorder, learning disorders, oppositional defiant disorder, conduct disorder, obsessive-compulsive disorder, and/or eating problems have been followed with in-depth questionnaires on family, social environment and personality, and subsequently by clinical assessments at age 15 together with randomly selected population controls") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000633> "An ongoing longitudinal study of all twins born in Sweden since July 1992, whose parents are interviewed about the children's somatic and mental health and social environment at age 9 or 12, with follow-up questionnaires at ages 15 and 18 and clinical assessments at 15 of screen-positive twin pairs and controls, to study the aetiology of childhood mental health problems and their role in later adjustment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Campaign Against Cancer and Heart Disease, is a prospective cohort designed to identify biomarkers and other factors associated with risk of cancer, heart disease, and other conditions12") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12575652/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We thank the participants of Clue I and Clue II and appreciate the continued efforts of the staff at the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center for Public Health Research and Prevention in the conduct of the Clue Cohort Studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer cases in the CLUE II cohort have been identified through linkage of the cohort participants with the Washington County Cancer Registry and, since 1992, with the Maryland Cancer Registry") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1989, a local campaign against cancer and heart disease named CLUE II was conducted in Washington County, Maryland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the baseline visit (1989 for CLUE II), brief medical histories, blood pressure readings, and blood samples were collected on 32,894 participants (25,076 of which were residents of Washington County).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Comparisons with published figures from the 1990 Census indicated that approximately 30 percent of adult residents had participated: 98.3% were White, reflecting the population of this county, and 59% were female, with the better-educated and the age group 45 to 70 years having higher participation rates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241297/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9970317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals included in this analysis were selected from participants in the CLUE II study, a prospective cohort study initiated in Washington County, Maryland, in 1989 [19, 20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000634> "A community-based prospective cohort of 32,894 mostly White adults in Washington County, Maryland, USA, who gave blood samples, blood pressure readings and brief medical histories during a 1989 campaign against cancer and heart disease run from the Johns Hopkins George W. Comstock Center, followed through cancer-registry linkage to study risk factors for cancer and heart disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26984683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, nuclear families (all of white European ancestry) with both parents (aged 40–60 years) and two adult (⩾18 years) offspring were identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and invited to participate through an invitation letter sent through the mother.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26984683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 2024 individuals from 520 nuclear families recruited in GRAPHIC, individuals who were receiving anti-hypertensive medications (n=135) were excluded from the current analysis to avoid any confounding caused by modulation of diurnal variation in BP by drugs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26984683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place between 2002 and 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3978/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3978_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Regulation of Arterial Pressure in Humans in the Community (GRAPHIC) Study is a family based population study comprising of 510 nuclear families (two parents aged 40-60 years at recruitment and two adult offspring aged 18-40 years) recruited through primary care in Leicestershire between 2003 and 200552 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3978/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3978_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the GRAPHIC study was to investigate the genetic basis of blood pressure variation and all subjects underwent 24-hour ambulatory BP measurements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24391740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5144126/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7242331/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRAPHIC Study comprises 2024 individuals from 520 nuclear families recruited from the general population in Leicestershire, UK between 2003-2005 for the purpose of investigating the genetic determinants of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000635> "A family cohort of about 2,000 white European adults from 520 nuclear families (both parents aged 40–60 and two adult offspring), identified through general practices in Leicestershire, UK, and recruited in 2002–2005 to study the genetic regulation of blood pressure and related cardiovascular traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000636> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000636>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MYHAT is an ongoing population‐based study that recruited 1982 individuals aged ≥ 65 from southwestern Pennsylvania by age‐stratified random sampling from electoral rolls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000636> "A population-based cohort of 1982 adults aged 65 and over from southwestern Pennsylvania, USA, recruited by age-stratified random sampling from electoral rolls and followed with longitudinal cognitive assessments to study cognitive decline and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included 3021 participants (1476 male and 1545 female) from three cohorts with longitudinal cognitive assessment: the Gingko Evaluation of Memory (GEM) study, the Monongahela‐Youghiogheny Healthy Aging Team (MYHAT), and the Monongahela Valley Independent Elders Survey (MoVIES).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000636> "A population-based cohort of 1982 adults aged 65 and over from southwestern Pennsylvania, USA, recruited by age-stratified random sampling from electoral rolls and followed with longitudinal cognitive assessments to study cognitive decline and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://adsp.niagads.org/data/contributing-cohorts/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MYHAT project seeks to describe the distribution of Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) and related entities, their associated features, their outcomes over time, and the predictors of these outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000636> "A population-based cohort of 1982 adults aged 65 and over from southwestern Pennsylvania, USA, recruited by age-stratified random sampling from electoral rolls and followed with longitudinal cognitive assessments to study cognitive decline and dementia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3173859") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These included all HapMap Phase I and II samples, along with further samples from the same four populations: individuals from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collected in Utah, USA, with ancestry from northern and western Europe (CEU); Han Chinese in Beijing, China (CHB); Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (JPT); and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe, originally collected by the Centre d'Etude du Polymorphisme Humain (CEPH), that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25569183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4287989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HapMap data set consisted of a publicly available RNAseq data set35 from transformed lymphoblastoid cell lines from 41 CEPH Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe (HapMap-CEU) samples available from the Gene Expression Omnibus repository ( http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo) under accession number GSE16921.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe, originally collected by the Centre d'Etude du Polymorphisme Humain (CEPH), that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2687076") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inference relies on the identification of stretches of haplotype shared between study samples and individuals in HapMap CEU reference panel.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe, originally collected by the Centre d'Etude du Polymorphisme Humain (CEPH), that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1880871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cell lines and DNA are available at the Coriell Institute for Medical Research (http://locus.umdnj.edu/nigms/products/hapmap.html).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe, originally collected by the Centre d'Etude du Polymorphisme Humain (CEPH), that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1880871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The specific samples examined are: (1) 90 individuals (30 parent–offspring trios) from the Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (abbreviation YRI); (2) 90 individuals (30 trios) in Utah, USA, from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collection (abbreviation CEU); (3) 45 Han Chinese in Beijing, China (abbreviation CHB); (4) 44 Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (abbreviation JPT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000637> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Utah residents with ancestry from northern and western Europe, originally collected by the Centre d'Etude du Polymorphisme Humain (CEPH), that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3173859") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These included all HapMap Phase I and II samples, along with further samples from the same four populations: individuals from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collected in Utah, USA, with ancestry from northern and western Europe (CEU); Han Chinese in Beijing, China (CHB); Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (JPT); and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Yoruba people in Ibadan, Nigeria, including parent–child trios, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1880871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cell lines and DNA are available at the Coriell Institute for Medical Research (http://locus.umdnj.edu/nigms/products/hapmap.html).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Yoruba people in Ibadan, Nigeria, including parent–child trios, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1880871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we report a public database of common variation in the human genome: more than one million single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) for which accurate and complete genotypes have been obtained in 269 DNA samples from four populations, including ten 500-kilobase regions in which essentially all information about common DNA variation has been extracted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Yoruba people in Ibadan, Nigeria, including parent–child trios, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1880871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The specific samples examined are: (1) 90 individuals (30 parent–offspring trios) from the Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (abbreviation YRI); (2) 90 individuals (30 trios) in Utah, USA, from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collection (abbreviation CEU); (3) 45 Han Chinese in Beijing, China (abbreviation CHB); (4) 44 Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (abbreviation JPT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Yoruba people in Ibadan, Nigeria, including parent–child trios, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3897378/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data setconsists of gene expression profiles generated using RNA extracted from lymphoblastoid cell lines derived from the 210 unrelated HapMap individuals from four sample groups (60 CEU, 45 CHB, 45 JPT and 60 Yoruba in Ibadan (YRI)).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000638> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Yoruba people in Ibadan, Nigeria, including parent–child trios, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15521375+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four hundred eleven infants of asthmatic mothers were enrolled at the age of 1 month.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15521375+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The children were born between August 2, 1998, and December 28, 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15521375+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the relationships among genetic, environmental, and lifestyle factors in the development of atopic diseases in high-risk children with the aim of developing evidence-based prevention strategies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11367328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COPSAC2000 is a single-centre clinical, prospective, mother–child cohort study of 411 individuals born to mothers with asthma who were recruited during pregnancy from the Danish National Birth Cohort (DNBC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11367328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The children were included at one month of age and visited the COPSAC research unit at scheduled visits every 6 months until age 7 and again at ages 12 and 18.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15521375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39214547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39214547+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This huge dataset on health and habits, exposures, metabolism, multiorgan assessments and biosamples from COPSAC2000 by age 18 provides a unique opportunity to explore risk factors and underlying mechanisms of atopic disease and other lifestyle-related, non-communicable diseases such as obesity and neuropsychiatric disorders, which are highly prevalent in the community and our cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000639> "A single-centre Danish prospective clinical birth cohort (COPSAC2000) of 411 children born in 1998–2001 to mothers with asthma, enrolled at 1 month of age and followed closely at the COPSAC clinical research unit in Copenhagen through childhood and to age 18 to study genetic, environmental and lifestyle risk factors for asthma, atopic dermatitis, allergy and other chronic inflammatory disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6308232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DemGene is a Norwegian network of clinical sites collecting cases from Memory Clinics based on standardized examination of cognitive, functional and behavioral measures and data on progression of most patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> "A Norwegian multi-centre network of clinical sites that pools Alzheimer's disease dementia and mild cognitive impairment cases from memory-clinic and other studies (among them NorCog, DemVest, the AHUS study, HUNT dementia studies, TrønderBrain and DDI), examined with standardized cognitive, functional and behavioural measures and followed for progression, together with cognitively normal and population controls, for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6308232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To increase the statistical power of our association analysis, the controls were combined with additional 4,475 population controls from Norwegian blood donor samples (Oslo University Hospital, Ullevål Hospital, between 18–60 years) and 723 controls from the Thematically Organized Psychosis Research (TOP) Study27 (between 25–65 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> "A Norwegian multi-centre network of clinical sites that pools Alzheimer's disease dementia and mild cognitive impairment cases from memory-clinic and other studies (among them NorCog, DemVest, the AHUS study, HUNT dementia studies, TrønderBrain and DDI), examined with standardized cognitive, functional and behavioural measures and followed for progression, together with cognitively normal and population controls, for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6308232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected genotype data from the Norwegian DemGene network consisting of 2,893 cases and 1,660 healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> "A Norwegian multi-centre network of clinical sites that pools Alzheimer's disease dementia and mild cognitive impairment cases from memory-clinic and other studies (among them NorCog, DemVest, the AHUS study, HUNT dementia studies, TrønderBrain and DDI), examined with standardized cognitive, functional and behavioural measures and followed for progression, together with cognitively normal and population controls, for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6308232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of AD cases and controls of European descent from the multi-center DemGene network across Norway and two independent European cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> "A Norwegian multi-centre network of clinical sites that pools Alzheimer's disease dementia and mild cognitive impairment cases from memory-clinic and other studies (among them NorCog, DemVest, the AHUS study, HUNT dementia studies, TrønderBrain and DDI), examined with standardized cognitive, functional and behavioural measures and followed for progression, together with cognitively normal and population controls, for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30591712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6308232/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We diagnosed 2,135 cases of AD dementia as well as 758 cases of Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) as a proxy of prodromal AD, from 7 studies (mean age = 73.2 ± 9.9): the Norwegian Register of persons with Cognitive Symptoms (NorCog), the Progression of Alzheimer’s Disease and Resource use (PADR), the Dementia Study of Western Norway (DemVest), the AHUS study, the Dementia Study in Rural Northern Norway (NordNorge), HUNT Dementia Study and the Nursing Home study, the TrønderBrain study, and the Dementia Disease Initiation study (DDI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000640> "A Norwegian multi-centre network of clinical sites that pools Alzheimer's disease dementia and mild cognitive impairment cases from memory-clinic and other studies (among them NorCog, DemVest, the AHUS study, HUNT dementia studies, TrønderBrain and DDI), examined with standardized cognitive, functional and behavioural measures and followed for progression, together with cognitively normal and population controls, for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease and dementia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Across 36 fine-mapping regions on Metabochip that contain T2D susceptibility loci (including 27 explicitly chosen by DIAGRAM), we compared the characteristics of previously reported lead SNPs (defined by GWAS and HapMap imputation) and those emerging from the Stage 2 Metabochip meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in people of European descent, whose successive case-control meta-analyses (DIAGRAMv2, DIAGRAMv3 and later) were used to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Combining Stage 1 and Stage 2 meta-analyses (Supplementary Fig. 2), we identified eight new T2D susceptibility loci at genome-wide significance (P < 5 × 10−8)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in people of European descent, whose successive case-control meta-analyses (DIAGRAMv2, DIAGRAMv3 and later) were used to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The T2D-nominated component of Metabochip comprises 21,774 variants, including 5,057 “replication” SNPs that capture the strongest, independent (CEU r2< 0.2) autosomal association signals from the GWAS meta-analysis conducted by the DIAbetes Genetics Replication and Meta-analysis (DIAGRAM) Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in people of European descent, whose successive case-control meta-analyses (DIAGRAMv2, DIAGRAMv3 and later) were used to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This genome-wide meta-analysis (“DIAGRAMv3”) includes data from 12,171 cases and 56,862 controls of European descent imputed up to 2.5 million autosomal SNPs, and augments the previously published “DIAGRAMv2” meta-analysis4 with four additional GWAS (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in people of European descent, whose successive case-control meta-analyses (DIAGRAMv2, DIAGRAMv3 and later) were used to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3442244/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC11228889/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GWAS summary statistics of T2D were obtained from the DIAbetes Genetics Replication And Meta-analysis (DIAGRAM) study, including 74,124 cases and 824,006 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000641> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in people of European descent, whose successive case-control meta-analyses (DIAGRAMv2, DIAGRAMv3 and later) were used to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes susceptibility loci.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29296818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5728332/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the parent study was designed to find common germ line genetic variation associated with survival after an URD-BMT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> "A study population of patients with acute myeloid leukaemia, myelodysplastic syndrome or acute lymphoblastic leukaemia who received an unrelated-donor blood or marrow transplant in 2000–2011, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, contributed by 151 US transplant centres to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research, assembled in two cohorts to find non-HLA genetic variants associated with one-year survival after transplant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8548922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional inclusion criteria were T-cell replete peripheral blood or marrow grafts, an available bio-repository sample from both recipient and donor, with no restrictions on conditioning regimen, age, sex or race/ethnicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> "A study population of patients with acute myeloid leukaemia, myelodysplastic syndrome or acute lymphoblastic leukaemia who received an unrelated-donor blood or marrow transplant in 2000–2011, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, contributed by 151 US transplant centres to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research, assembled in two cohorts to find non-HLA genetic variants associated with one-year survival after transplant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8548922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort 1 received a first URD-BMT (10/10 HLA-matched) between 2000 and 2008; Cohort 2 received a first URD-BMT (10/10 HLA-matched) between 2009 and 2011 or an 8/8 (but <10/10) HLA-matched first URD-BMT between 2000 and 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> "A study population of patients with acute myeloid leukaemia, myelodysplastic syndrome or acute lymphoblastic leukaemia who received an unrelated-donor blood or marrow transplant in 2000–2011, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, contributed by 151 US transplant centres to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research, assembled in two cohorts to find non-HLA genetic variants associated with one-year survival after transplant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8548922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DISCOVeRY-BMT study population was contributed by 151 centers in the United States to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research (CIBMTR) and consists of two cohorts of ALL, AML and MDS patients and their healthy ≥8/8 HLA-matched URDs described previously [5], [6], [7], [8], [9], [10], [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> "A study population of patients with acute myeloid leukaemia, myelodysplastic syndrome or acute lymphoblastic leukaemia who received an unrelated-donor blood or marrow transplant in 2000–2011, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, contributed by 151 US transplant centres to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research, assembled in two cohorts to find non-HLA genetic variants associated with one-year survival after transplant.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34746714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8548922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We hypothesized that non-HLA loci contributed significantly to 1-year overall survival (OS), disease related mortality (DRM) or transplant related mortality (TRM) after unrelated donor (URD)BMT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000642> "A study population of patients with acute myeloid leukaemia, myelodysplastic syndrome or acute lymphoblastic leukaemia who received an unrelated-donor blood or marrow transplant in 2000–2011, and their HLA-matched unrelated donors, contributed by 151 US transplant centres to the Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research, assembled in two cohorts to find non-HLA genetic variants associated with one-year survival after transplant.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19734903") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19734903+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify other risk loci, we conducted a large genome-wide association study of 2,032 individuals from France with Alzheimer's disease (cases) and 5,328 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643> "A French consortium whose genome-wide association dataset of 2,032 Alzheimer's disease cases and 5,328 controls from France was assembled to identify late-onset Alzheimer's disease risk loci, and which later formed one of the four founding datasets of the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2989531/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We identified 2708 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) with p-values<10−3, and in Stage 2 pooled results for these SNPs with the European AD Initiative (2032 cases, 5328 controls) to identify ten loci with p-values<10−5.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643> "A French consortium whose genome-wide association dataset of 2,032 Alzheimer's disease cases and 5,328 controls from France was assembled to identify late-onset Alzheimer's disease risk loci, and which later formed one of the four founding datasets of the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9421597/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Alzheimer's Disease Initiative (EADI) is composed of several case-control studies and 1 population-based cohort, 3C.27 The case-control studies are composed of AD cases and cognitively normal controls across France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643> "A French consortium whose genome-wide association dataset of 2,032 Alzheimer's disease cases and 5,328 controls from France was assembled to identify late-onset Alzheimer's disease risk loci, and which later formed one of the four founding datasets of the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-22491-8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage 1 of the IGAP comprises 21,982 AD cases and 41,944 cognitively normal controls from four consortia: the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC), the European Alzheimer’s Disease Initiative (EADI), the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology (CHARGE) Consortium, and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in AD/Defining Genetic, Polygenic, and Environmental Risk for Alzheimer’s Disease (GERAD/PERADES) Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000643> "A French consortium whose genome-wide association dataset of 2,032 Alzheimer's disease cases and 5,328 controls from France was assembled to identify late-onset Alzheimer's disease risk loci, and which later formed one of the four founding datasets of the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672363/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "European Community (EC; FP6 project EPICURE: LSHM‐CT2006‐037315)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672363/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From those participants, the following subjects were excluded for those analyses requiring individual‐level genotype data: Finnish ancestry (none had genetic generalized epilepsy [GGE]) and the subset of the EPICURE‐SP1 cohort that lacked informed consent for the current analyses, resulting in subject‐level genotype data being available for 11 446 people with epilepsy and 22 078 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Coordinated by FONDAZIONE IRCCS ISTITUTO NEUROLOGICO \"CARLO BESTA\" Italy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPICURE Grant agreement ID: 37315 Project closed Start date 1 January 2007 End date 30 June 2011") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPICURE intends to bring together expertise from different research areas both clinical and laboratory-based with the common goal of advancing European epilepsy research to bring about novel therapeutic benefits to patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34002374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/37315") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4189926/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPICURE cohort, in which 2p16.1 was originally proposed as a risk factor for genetic generalised epilepsy, was included in our meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000644> "A European consortium of clinical and laboratory epilepsy research groups, funded in 2007–2011 by the EU Sixth Framework Programme as the EPICURE project and coordinated by the Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta in Italy, whose collections of people with genetic generalized epilepsy (such as the EPICURE-SP1 cohort) contributed cases to genome-wide association studies of epilepsy.")

