AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2845877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, in Stage 1, we tested 529,205 autosomal SNPs for association in up to 11,789 subjects (3,941 AD cases, 7,848 controls of which 2,078 were elderly screened controls, see Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://data.dpuk.ukserp.ac.uk/CohortDirectory/Item?fingerPrintID=GERAD") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institution Name Cardiff University Department Name Medicine City Cardiff University") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "6,129 population con- trols were drawn from large existing cohorts with available GWAS data, including the 1958 British Birth Cohort (1958BC) (http://www.b58cgene.sgul.ac.uk), the KORA F4 Study and the Heinz Nixdorf Recall Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and elderly screened controls were recruited by the Medical Research Council (MRC) Genetic Resource for AD (Cardiff University; Institute of Psychiatry, London; Cambridge University; Trin- ity College Dublin), the Alzheimer’s Research Trust (ART) Collaboration (University of Nottingham; University of Manchester; University of Southampton; University of Bristol; Queen’s University Belfast; the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing (OPTIMA), Oxford University); Washington University, St Louis, United States;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Competence Network of Dementia (CND) and Department of Psychiatry, University of Bonn, Germany; the National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH) AD Genetics Initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2989531/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, two large GWAS, the UK-led Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer’s Disease 1 consortium (GERAD1),13 and the European Alzheimer Disease Initiative (EADI) Stage 1,14 reported 3 new genome-wide significant loci for AD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39633006") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-22491-8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage 1 of the IGAP comprises 21,982 AD cases and 41,944 cognitively normal controls from four consortia: the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC), the European Alzheimer’s Disease Initiative (EADI), the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology (CHARGE) Consortium, and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in AD/Defining Genetic, Polygenic, and Environmental Risk for Alzheimer’s Disease (GERAD/PERADES) Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000646> "A consortium led from Cardiff University that brought together Alzheimer's disease cases and screened elderly controls recruited by institutions in the United Kingdom, Germany and the United States, with population controls from existing British and German cohorts, into a genome-wide association dataset of Alzheimer's disease; one of the four datasets meta-analysed by the International Genomics of Alzheimer's Project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6612519") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genes for Good is an ongoing, large- scale study of health, genetic, and behavioral information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31204010+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As of March 2019, we engaged >80,000 individuals, sent spit kits to >32,000 individuals who met minimum participation requirements, and collected >27,000 spit kits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31204010+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Health history and daily tracking surveys are administered through a Facebook application, and participants who complete a minimum number of surveys are mailed a saliva sample kit (\"spit kit\") to collect DNA for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31204010+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants come from all 50 states and include a diversity of ancestral backgrounds.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31204010+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genes for Good study uses social media to engage a large, diverse participant pool in genetics research and education.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31204010") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34957435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8654685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genes for Good study (GFG, https://genesforgood.sph.umich.edu/) is a population-based cohort initiated by the University of Michigan in 2015, which includes participants across the US who provided a saliva sample for DNA genotyping") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000647> "A University of Michigan study that engages the public through a Facebook application for health-history and daily-tracking surveys and mails saliva kits for genotyping to participants who complete enough surveys, having engaged more than 80,000 people from all 50 US states by 2019 for genetic research on health and behaviour.")

