# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in both SAFHS and SAFDGS were followed in a mixed longitudinal fashion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAFDGS also began in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study [2] and recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in an earlier epidemiologic survey, the San Antonio Heart Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAFHS began in 1991 with 40- to 60-year-old low-income Mexican Americans, selected at random without regard to presence or absence of disease, who were almost exclusively from Mexican American census tracts in San Antonio, Texas [1].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These family data were obtained from two studies: the San Antonio Family Heart Study (SAFHS) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (SAFDGS), which are together referred to as the San Antonio Family Studies (SAFS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8901667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among Mexican Americans from San Antonio (Tex), we quantified the relative contributions of both genetic and environmental influences to a large panel of cardiovascular risk factors, including serum levels of lipids, lipoproteins, glucose, hormones, adiposity, and blood pressure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8901667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Members of 42 extended families were studied, including 1236 first-, second-, and third-degree relatives of randomly ascertained probands and their spouses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000649> "A family-based study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, made up of the San Antonio Family Heart Study (extended families of randomly selected low-income Mexican American probands) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (extended families of probands with type 2 diabetes from the San Antonio Heart Study), both begun in 1991 and followed with repeated examinations, to study the genetics of cardiovascular disease, type 2 diabetes and related traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12283397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SATSA dataset was drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry and includes same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden separated before the age of 11 years and reared apart.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> "A longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden and drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry, including pairs separated before age 11 and reared apart, with questionnaires and in-person testing from 1984 to 2014, to understand the factors that contribute to healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12283397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish Adoption/Twin Study of Aging (SATSA) includes extensive in-person testing of same-sex twins over a 30-year period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> "A longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden and drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry, including pairs separated before age 11 and reared apart, with questionnaires and in-person testing from 1984 to 2014, to understand the factors that contribute to healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://researchdata.se/en/catalogue/dataset/ext0044-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SATSA started with a survey in 1984 where a questionnaire was sent to all surviving individuals (n=2845).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> "A longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden and drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry, including pairs separated before age 11 and reared apart, with questionnaires and in-person testing from 1984 to 2014, to understand the factors that contribute to healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://researchdata.se/en/catalogue/dataset/ext0044-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of SATSA was to study the origins of individual differences in aging and the environmental and genetic factors that are involved.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> "A longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden and drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry, including pairs separated before age 11 and reared apart, with questionnaires and in-person testing from 1984 to 2014, to understand the factors that contribute to healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40188287") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://researchdata.se/en/catalogue/dataset/ext0044-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Time period(s) investigated: 1984 - 2014") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000650> "A longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in Sweden and drawn from the Swedish Twin Registry, including pairs separated before age 11 and reared apart, with questionnaires and in-person testing from 1984 to 2014, to understand the factors that contribute to healthy ageing and longevity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Investigators harmonize ischemic stroke phenotyping using the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke (CCS) system, with data entered by trained and certified adjudicators at participating GRCs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Institute of Neurologic Disorders and Stroke (NINDS) has established the Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN) with the goal of assembling the largest possible sample of individuals with ischemic stroke for genetic studies, where each individual has been uniformly and thoroughly characterized for stroke subtyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SiGN responded to a Request for Applications (RFA) issued by the NINDS that proposed establishing a genome-wide association study consortium focused on identifying genes or genomic regions that affect either the susceptibility to, or outcome of, ischemic stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NINDS Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN) includes ischemic stroke cases from 24 Genetic Research Centers (GRCs), 13 from the US and 11 from Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4912948/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SiGN study was a cooperative agreement with the United States National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke (NINDS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36672803") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858999/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SiGN is an international collaboration of 31 studies across North America, Europe, and Australia to identify genetic determinants of ischemic stroke [6].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000651> "A network, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that brought together ischaemic stroke case collections from genetic research centres in the United States, Europe and Australia, with stroke subtypes harmonised by the web-based Causative Classification of Stroke system, for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3954445/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants must be 40–80 years of age at baseline, have a smoking history of ≤ 1 pack-year (Stratum 1) or ≥ 20 pack-years (Strata 2–4) and meet lung function criteria as specified in Table 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3954445/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Primary Aim 1 is to identify homogeneous subgroups of COPD patients for targeted enrollment in future therapeutic clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3954445/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SPIROMICS is a prospective cohort study that will enroll 3,200 participants into four strata (Non-smokers, Smokers without airflow obstruction, Mild/Moderate COPD, and Severe COPD) as shown in Table 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3954445/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SPIROMICS will endeavor to identify intermediate outcome measures that predict long-term clinical endpoints of morbidity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3954445/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There are baseline (Visit 1) and three annual in-person follow-up visits (Visits 2–4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24029743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8077917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SPIROMICS study is a multicenter study that includes current and former smokers (≥ 20 pack years) with or without airflow obstruction and healthy participants who were non-smokers aged 40 to 80 years recruited from 12 clinical sites spread across the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000652> "A multicentre observational cohort of current and former smokers aged 40–80 with or without airflow obstruction, and never-smoking controls, recruited at clinical sites across the United States with baseline and annual follow-up visits, to find subgroups of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and biomarkers usable as intermediate outcomes in therapeutic trials.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomic DNA was separated from venous blood samples, and 100 ng DNA was genotyped using Korea Biobank Array Affymetrix Axiom 1.1 (Affymetrix, Santa Clara, CA), which was designed by the Korean National Institute of Health43.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VHSMC cohort is a hospital-based elderly cohort that includes many patients with various diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current study conducted a GWAS meta-analysis on sarcopenia phenotypes using Korean relatively aged cohorts, combining the Veterans Health Service Medical Center (VHSMC) and Korean Association Resource (KARE) cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The mean age of the VHSMC cohort was higher than that of the KARE cohort (69.10 ± 7.83 years vs 62.79 ± 8.33 years, P < 0.001, Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VHSMC (Veterans Health Service Medical Center) cohort: This study was conducted with bioresources from the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank, Republic of Korea (VBP-2020-03).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35241739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8894365/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Veterans Medical Research Institute, Veterans Health Service Medical Center, Jinhwangdo-ro 61-gil 53, Gangdong-gu, Seoul, 05368 South Korea") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000653> "A hospital-based cohort of older adults, many with various diseases, at the Veterans Health Service Medical Center in Seoul, South Korea, with samples held by the Veterans Medical Research Institute Biobank and genotyped on the Korea Biobank Array for genome-wide association studies of body composition and cardiometabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19659826+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this purpose, DNA from approximately 1100 patients with CAD, and 2000 healthy controls is being collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19659826+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, detailed clinical, laboratory, diagnostic, therapeutic, and outcome data are being collected from all participants applying predefined criteria and definitions in a standardized way.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19659826+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our aim is to identify genetic variants associated with an increased risk of CAD and possibly gene-environment interactions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19659826+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CADISP network will provide detailed and novel data on environmental risk factors and genetic susceptibility to CAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19659826+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We organized a multinational European network, Cervical Artery Dissection and Ischemic Stroke Patients (CADISP), which aims at increasing our knowledge of the pathophysiological mechanisms of this disease in a large group of patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19659826") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22150935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22150935+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-control study is based on the CADISP (Cervical Artery Dissection and Ischemic Stroke Patients) population comprising 983 consecutive CeAD patients (mean age: 44.1 ± 9.9 years) and 658 control patients with a non-CeAD ischemic stroke (IS) (44.5 ± 10.5 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000654> "A multinational European network of patients with cervical artery dissection, with ischaemic stroke patients of other causes and healthy controls, recruited with standardised clinical, laboratory, imaging, treatment and outcome data to identify genetic variants and environmental factors associated with cervical artery dissection.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26842272+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between January 2010 and June 2013, we invited pregnant women aged ≥ 18 years old who visited the blood sampling in pregnancy clinic in Sherbrooke for their first trimester clinical blood samples: 1034 women accepted to participate in our cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> "A prospective prebirth cohort of about 1,000 pregnant women aged 18 or over recruited in the first trimester at the pregnancy blood-sampling clinic in Sherbrooke, Canada, between 2010 and 2013, and their children, followed to study the biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation in pregnancy and its effects on fetal development and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26842272+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We initiated the Genetics of Glucose regulation in Gestation and Growth (Gen3G) prospective cohort to increase our understanding of biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation during pregnancy and their impact on fetal development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> "A prospective prebirth cohort of about 1,000 pregnant women aged 18 or over recruited in the first trimester at the pregnancy blood-sampling clinic in Sherbrooke, Canada, between 2010 and 2013, and their children, followed to study the biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation in pregnancy and its effects on fetal development and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11931902/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up visits 3 and 5 years after delivery aimed to investigate pregnancy-related risk factors such as maternal obesity and gestational hyperglycaemia in relation to the mother’s metabolic health after pregnancy, and with offspring health outcomes such as risk of obesity and neurodevelopmental problems in early childhood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> "A prospective prebirth cohort of about 1,000 pregnant women aged 18 or over recruited in the first trimester at the pregnancy blood-sampling clinic in Sherbrooke, Canada, between 2010 and 2013, and their children, followed to study the biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation in pregnancy and its effects on fetal development and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11931902/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Gen3G is a prospective pregnancy and birth cohort that recruited 1024 pregnant women in the first trimester of pregnancy in Sherbrooke, Canada, between January 2010 and June 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> "A prospective prebirth cohort of about 1,000 pregnant women aged 18 or over recruited in the first trimester at the pregnancy blood-sampling clinic in Sherbrooke, Canada, between 2010 and 2013, and their children, followed to study the biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation in pregnancy and its effects on fetal development and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26842272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40122564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11931902/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since then, both the mothers and their offspring were reassessed 3 and 5 years after delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000655> "A prospective prebirth cohort of about 1,000 pregnant women aged 18 or over recruited in the first trimester at the pregnancy blood-sampling clinic in Sherbrooke, Canada, between 2010 and 2013, and their children, followed to study the biological, environmental and genetic determinants of glucose regulation in pregnancy and its effects on fetal development and offspring health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12688622+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NACManchester Asthma and Allergy Study is a prospective study of the development of asthma and allergies in childhood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656> "A population-based birth cohort of children recruited in utero through the antenatal clinics of Wythenshawe and Stepping Hill Hospitals in South Manchester and Cheshire, England, with parents screened for atopy, and followed prospectively through childhood to study the genetic and environmental determinants of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12688622+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects (995 children at age 3 years) were recruited in utero by screening parents in the antenatal clinic using skin prick testing and a questionnaire regarding allergic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656> "A population-based birth cohort of children recruited in utero through the antenatal clinics of Wythenshawe and Stepping Hill Hospitals in South Manchester and Cheshire, England, with parents screened for atopy, and followed prospectively through childhood to study the genetic and environmental determinants of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9356009/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All pregnant women were screened for eligibility at antenatal visits (8th–10th week of pregnancy) between 1995 and 1997.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656> "A population-based birth cohort of children recruited in utero through the antenatal clinics of Wythenshawe and Stepping Hill Hospitals in South Manchester and Cheshire, England, with parents screened for atopy, and followed prospectively through childhood to study the genetic and environmental determinants of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12688622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35931775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9356009/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children have been followed prospectively, and attended review clinics at ages 1, 3, 5, 8 and 11 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000656> "A population-based birth cohort of children recruited in utero through the antenatal clinics of Wythenshawe and Stepping Hill Hospitals in South Manchester and Cheshire, England, with parents screened for atopy, and followed prospectively through childhood to study the genetic and environmental determinants of asthma and allergic disease.")
