AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6797314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At 6 weeks and 3, 15 and 51 months after diagnosis, participants fill out a general questionnaire, and questionnaires about their lifestyle habits and HRQOL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6797314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four-day diaryFrequency micturition, amount and type of fluid intake XXX Blood EDTA whole blood for DNA isolation X EDTA plasma, heparin plasma XX TissueFormalin-fixed paraffin-embedded tissue of the primary tumourX") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6797314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information about disease characteristics and therapy for the primary tumour and subsequent recurrences is collected from the medical records by the Netherlands Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6797314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UroLife study is a multicentre prospective cohort study among more than 1100 newly diagnosed patients with NMIBC recruited from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6797314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main aim of this study is to evaluate whether lifestyle habits are related to prognosis and HRQOL in patients with NMIBC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31619424") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11826114/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited in 22 participating hospitals in the Netherlands in two phases: from May 2014 to May 2017, patients with primary stage Ta, T1, and carcinoma in situ (CIS) were included; from May 2017 to April 2021 recruitment was restricted to patients with stage T1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000661> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with non-muscle-invasive bladder cancer, recruited in 2014–2021 from 22 hospitals in the Netherlands and followed with questionnaires, diaries, blood and tumour samples and cancer registry data to study how lifestyle habits relate to prognosis and health-related quality of life.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8177429") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was from the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium (CAPOC) (19), which was established in 2010, the members of which come from five research centers (Peking University Sixth Hospital, West China Hospital of Sichuan University, the Second Xiangya Hospital of Central South University, Beijing Anding Hospital affiliated to Capital Medical University, and Beijing HuiLongGuan Hospital).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8177429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both first-episode patients (FEP) and relapsed patients with schizophrenia were enrolled from the inpatient departments of the psychiatric hospitals affiliated with CAPOC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8177429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is a 6-week multicenter randomized open-label pharmacogenetic trial designed to identify predictors of antipsychotic drug efficacy and adverse reaction in patients with schizophrenia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12362978/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the CAPOC cohort were randomly assigned to 1 of 6 treatment groups: risperidone, olanzapine, quetiapine, aripiprazole, ziprasidone, or an FGA (haloperidol or perphenazine).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12362978/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients in both the discovery and validation cohorts were diagnosed with schizophrenia according to the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition, and were of Han Chinese ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34093281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37269009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40826483") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12362978/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery cohort consisted of 3067 patients (2016 participants were reserved after quality control) with schizophrenia in the acute phase and was derived from the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium (CAPOC) [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000662> "A six-week multicentre randomised open-label pharmacogenetic trial cohort of about 3,000 Han Chinese inpatients with schizophrenia in an acute phase, recruited through the Chinese Antipsychotics Pharmacogenomics Consortium of five research centres and their affiliated psychiatric hospitals in China, established in 2010, and randomly assigned to one of six antipsychotic treatments, to identify predictors of antipsychotic efficacy and adverse reactions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37108169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we used the data from three sub-cohorts for which we had bacterial and viral infections disease data—Korčula (N = 2833), Vis (N = 1039) and Split (N = 1012).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37108169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is based on the Croatian biobank 10,001 Dalmatians [78,79], the most comprehensive research resource for investigating genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37108169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While the first two are isolated island populations, the third originates from the second-largest city in Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CROATIA-Split study, Croatia, is a population-based, cross-sectional study in the Dalmatian City of Split that includes 1000 examinees aged 18-95.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of our study is identification of novel loci associated with the parathyroid function, by performing a GWAS meta-analysis of plasma PTH levels within two genetically isolated Croatian populations (Korcula and Vis) following by replication analysis in the urban population of Split.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was performed on samples from three Croatian populations: from the Dalmatian islands of Korcula and Vis and the mainland city of Split, within the large-scale project of “10,001 Dalmatians” (Rudan et al., 2009).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000663> "A population-based cohort of about 1,000 adults from the mainland city of Split, the second-largest city in Croatia, recruited within the 10,001 Dalmatians biobank project as an urban counterpart to the isolated island cohorts of Vis and Korčula, for studies of the genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35624665+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of the FlOPs level in 1216 adults from the case-control and family-based EGEA study (mean age 43 years old, 51% women, and 23% current smokers) to identify genetic variants associated with FlOPs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A third survey (EGEA3) consisting in a self-completed questionnaire has been initiated in 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EGEA is a unique 20-year cohort set up to investigate the genetic and environmental factors and their interactions in asthma and asthma-related phenotypes (bronchial hyperresponsiveness, atopy), and to clarify the phenotypic heterogeneity [1, 2].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were examined in seven centers from five French cities (followed by latitude and longitude coordinates): Grenoble (45.182359, 5.718384), Lyon (45.754269, 4.855957), Marseille (43.295532, 5.380554), Montpellier (43.602604, 3.878174) and Paris (48.883979, 2.373047).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Temporal coverage The start and end dates of the biological collection are 1991 to 1995 (EGEA1), and 2003 to 2007 (EGEA2, 11.4 years apart on average after EGEA1, range 5.3–14.9 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35624665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8590334") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.24") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first EGEA survey (EGEA1) included cases with asthma, recruited in five chest clinics, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, recruited in the early 90’s in 5 French cities (total: n = 2047).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000664> "A French case-control and family-based cohort of asthma cases recruited in chest clinics in Grenoble, Lyon, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, their first-degree relatives and population-based controls, enrolled in 1991–1995 and followed up in 2003–2007 and later, to study the genetic and environmental causes of asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and atopy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41803162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 9,940 individuals aged 50–75 years were recruited by their general practitioners (GPs) during routine health screenings between July 2000 and December 2002, and were followed up every two to three years thereafter.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41803162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide DNAm was assessed using the Infinium MethylationEPIC (850 K) BeadChip Kit (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA), according to the manufacturer’s instructions, by the Genomics and Proteomics Core Facility at the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), Heidelberg, Germany30,35,36.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41803162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Strengths include that it is based on a large population-based cohort study with extensive collection of biospecimen, life style and medical data, and comprehensive long-term prospective follow-up with respect to morbidity and mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41803162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population was drawn from the ESTHER cohort, an ongoing population-based cohort study conducted in Saarland, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2816642/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "German Cancer Research Centre ESTHER (Epidemiologische Studie zu Chancen der Verhütung, Früherkennung und optimierten Therapie chronischer Erkrankungen in der älteren Bevölkerung) Population-based biobank project 670 670") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12992613/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/esther") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The examination and improvement of prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older age, e.g. cardiovascular diseases, diabetes, or cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000665> "A population-based cohort of 9,940 adults aged 50–75 recruited by their general practitioners during routine health check-ups in Saarland, Germany, between 2000 and 2002 and followed every two to three years, run by the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg to study the prevention, early detection and treatment of chronic diseases in older people.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36066633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36066633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9547780/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the Gothenburg H70 Birth Cohort studies and clinical AD samples from Sweden, the QC and imputation procedures were described elsewhere [48].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666> "A collection of Alzheimer's disease cases and dementia-free controls from Sweden that combines cases diagnosed in memory clinics in different parts of Sweden or identified in two population-based studies in Gothenburg, the Prospective Population Study of Women and the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies (H70, H85 and 95+), with controls from those Gothenburg population studies, genotyped for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36066633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls originate from the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies and PPSW.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666> "A collection of Alzheimer's disease cases and dementia-free controls from Sweden that combines cases diagnosed in memory clinics in different parts of Sweden or identified in two population-based studies in Gothenburg, the Prospective Population Study of Women and the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies (H70, H85 and 95+), with controls from those Gothenburg population studies, genotyped for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36066633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13263136/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gothenburg H70 Birth Cohort Studies and Clinical AD from Sweden (Gothenburg) AD cases originate from Sweden and were either collected in memory clinics (in different parts of Sweden) or as a part of two population-based epidemiological studies in Gothenburg; the Prospective Population Study of Women (PPSW) and the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies (H70, H85 and 95+)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666> "A collection of Alzheimer's disease cases and dementia-free controls from Sweden that combines cases diagnosed in memory clinics in different parts of Sweden or identified in two population-based studies in Gothenburg, the Prospective Population Study of Women and the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies (H70, H85 and 95+), with controls from those Gothenburg population studies, genotyped for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36066633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-021-00921-z/MediaObjects/41588_2021_921_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gothenburg H70 Birth Cohort Studies and Clinical AD from Sweden (Gothenburg) dataset (712 cases, 2523 controls) was used as the independent test set because it was the dataset with the largest number of cases of the available genotype-level data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000666> "A collection of Alzheimer's disease cases and dementia-free controls from Sweden that combines cases diagnosed in memory clinics in different parts of Sweden or identified in two population-based studies in Gothenburg, the Prospective Population Study of Women and the Gothenburg Birth Cohort Studies (H70, H85 and 95+), with controls from those Gothenburg population studies, genotyped for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease and its biomarkers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based families were recruited from the Greater San Francisco Bay area, California, USA, by the Northern California Cancer Center; from the province of Ontario, Canada, by Cancer Care Ontario; and from the metropolitan areas of Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, by the University of Melbourne and the New South Wales Cancer Council.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15217505+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This resource is available to internal and external researchers for collaborative, interdisciplinary, and translational studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases aged 18–64 years diagnosed from 1995 to 2007 were ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility (diagnosis at the age of <35 years, bilateral breast cancer with the first diagnosis at the age of <50 years, a personal history of ovarian or childhood cancer and a family history of breast or ovarian cancer in first-degree relatives) were oversampled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population controls were identified through random-digit dialing and frequency-matched on 5-year age groups to cases diagnosed from 1995 to 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We initially performed a GWAS of Latina women from the San Francisco Bay Area including 977 cases and 722 controls, from the San Francisco Bay Area Breast Cancer Study (SFBCS), the Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry (NC-BCFR) and the Genetics of Asthma in Latino Americans (GALA1, controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Northern California Breast Cancer Family Registry (NC-BCFR) was initiated in 1995 and enrolled ~4000 women with incident breast cancer and family members") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000667> "The Northern California site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, which from 1995 enrolled about 4000 women with incident breast cancer, ascertained through the Greater Bay Area Cancer Registry in the San Francisco Bay Area with oversampling of cases with indicators of increased genetic susceptibility, together with their family members and random-digit-dialled population controls, to study the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Breast Cancer Family Registry was established in 1995, with six participating sites from the USA, Canada, and Australia ascertaining families either from cancer registries (identifying population-based families) or seen in clinical and community settings (identifying clinic-based families) (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668> "A breast cancer family registry established in 1995 with US National Cancer Institute support as a collaboration of six academic and research institutions in the USA, Canada and Australia, enrolling population-based families (through cancer registries) and clinic-based families with common questionnaires, biospecimen protocols and pathology review, to support studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15217505+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sites have developed core family history and epidemiology questionnaires, data dictionaries, and common protocols for biospecimen collection and processing and pathology review.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668> "A breast cancer family registry established in 1995 with US National Cancer Institute support as a collaboration of six academic and research institutions in the USA, Canada and Australia, enrolling population-based families (through cancer registries) and clinic-based families with common questionnaires, biospecimen protocols and pathology review, to support studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15217505+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This resource is available to internal and external researchers for collaborative, interdisciplinary, and translational studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668> "A breast cancer family registry established in 1995 with US National Cancer Institute support as a collaboration of six academic and research institutions in the USA, Canada and Australia, enrolling population-based families (through cancer registries) and clinic-based families with common questionnaires, biospecimen protocols and pathology review, to support studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15217505+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address urgent research questions and to expedite the translation of research results to the clinical setting, the National Cancer Institute (USA) supported in 1995 the establishment of a novel research infrastructure, the Breast Cancer Family Registry, a collaboration of six academic and research institutions and their medical affiliates in the USA, Canada, and Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000668> "A breast cancer family registry established in 1995 with US National Cancer Institute support as a collaboration of six academic and research institutions in the USA, Canada and Australia, enrolling population-based families (through cancer registries) and clinic-based families with common questionnaires, biospecimen protocols and pathology review, to support studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3040659/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Institute of Aging-Late Onset Alzheimer's Disease Family Study and the National Cell Repository for Alzheimer's Disease conducted a joint genome-wide association study (GWAS) of multiplex LOAD families (3,839 affected and unaffected individuals from 992 families plus additional unrelated neurologically evaluated normal subjects) using the 610 IlluminaQuad panel.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3270040/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NIA-LOAD Family Study recruited 992 multiplex LOAD families, with at least two living affected individuals, from throughout the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9250549/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy controls without a family history of AD in a first‐degree relative, who were 55 years of age or older were also recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9250549/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Institute on Aging Late‐Onset Alzheimer's Disease Family Based Study (NIA‐LOAD FBS) was established to study the genetic etiology of Alzheimer's disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9250549/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The criteria for study entry included two living affected siblings, 60 years of age or older, and a third living relative, similar in age, with or without dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21379329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9250549/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also included families with deceased affected siblings, as long as frozen brain tissue was available for affected members.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000669> "A family study that recruited multiplex late-onset Alzheimer's disease families, with two living affected siblings or deceased affected siblings whose frozen brain tissue was available, together with unrelated neurologically evaluated controls, from throughout the United States, for genetic studies of late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36658081") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36658081+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a GWAS on a composite measure of executive function that included measures of mental flexibility and reasoning using data from the Northern Manhattan Study, a racially and ethnically diverse cohort (N = 1077, 69% Hispanic, 17% non-Hispanic Black and 14% non-Hispanic White).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NOMAS is an ongoing population-based study designed to determine stroke incidence, risk factors and outcome in an urban multiethnic population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11757223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, the NOMAS cohort is followed over time and the cognitive status of individuals is regularly assessed for the generation of longitudinal data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11757223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NOMAS is a racially/ethnically diverse prospective cohort with 3298 stroke-free participants enrolled between 1993 and 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2003 until 2008, a total of 1290 NOMAS participants (including 199 household members) were recruited into a magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) sub‐study during annual follow‐up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13482911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NOMAS is a community‐based longitudinal cohort study of 3298 urban‐dwelling adults 40 years of age or older with a household telephone at the baseline visit. 12 Clinically stroke‐free participants living in Northern Manhattan at enrollment were recruited between 1993 and 2001 using random digit dialing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000670> "A community-based longitudinal cohort of 3,298 stroke-free, predominantly Hispanic, Black and White adults aged 40 or older living in northern Manhattan, New York City, recruited by random-digit dialling in 1993–2001 and followed for stroke, vascular risk factors, brain MRI markers and cognitive outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment of participants and the collection of the dental data for POFC started in 2006 and finished in 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The POFC study populations were recruited from multiple cleft centers in the USA, including Colorado, Iowa, Pennsylvania, Texas, and Puerto Rico, and internationally, from Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala, and Hungary for the purpose of studying orofacial clefts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort included 1,392 control individuals, including control probands, their parents and siblings, and 2,187 unaffected relatives of individuals with orofacial clefts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7937973/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The POFC project recruits individuals with clefts, their family members, and population-based controls for extensive phenotypic and genomic analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9086172/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sample recruitment was carried out in accordance with ethics approval procedures at the University of Pittsburgh, the coordinating center for the Pitt-OFC study, as well as the respective institutions that contributed samples to the Pitt-OFC study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9086172/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pitt-OFC resource is a rich collection of nsOFC families across multiple racial/ethnic groups, including simplex, multiplex, and extended pedigrees (~12,000 participants) with precise and detailed information on the types of nsOFC observed within multiple generations of the relatives of the probands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000671> "A multiethnic family-based collection of people with nonsyndromic orofacial clefts, their unaffected relatives and unaffected controls, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh through cleft centres in the United States and Puerto Rico and in Argentina, the Philippines, Colombia, Guatemala and Hungary to study the genetics of orofacial clefts and related dental traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "95% of participants reported being given a diagnosis of depression by a medical practitioner and 88% met the criteria for a lifetime depressive episode.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 20 689 participants were recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, 75% of whom were female.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants completed an online questionnaire that consisted of a compulsory module that assessed self-reported psychiatric history, clinical depression using the Composite Interview Diagnostic Interview Short Form and experiences of using commonly prescribed antidepressants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided extensive information on their experience with depression through a web-based questionnaire and the majority provided a saliva sample for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited to the AGDS (www.geneticsofdepression.org.au) using two separate approaches: (1) recruitment based on nationwide, pharmaceutical prescription history in the last 4.5 years and (2) a media publicity campaign throughout Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32461290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7259831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of establishing this cohort is to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and response to commonly prescribed antidepressants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000672> "A cohort of 20,689 adults in Australia, most of whom reported being diagnosed with depression, recruited through the Australian Department of Human Services and a media campaign, who completed online questionnaires on psychiatric history and antidepressant response, with saliva DNA provided by a subset, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for depression and antidepressant response.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000673> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000673>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5593097") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ARIES is a population-based resource of DNA methylation data accessible by the research community, established with the aim of improving our understanding of the determinants and consequences of epigenetic variation, in particular the role of DNA methylation in health and development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000673> "A sub-study of the Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and Children comprising 1,018 mother-offspring pairs with genome-wide DNA methylation profiled at birth, in childhood and in adolescence for the children and at two time points for the mothers, established as an openly accessible resource to study the determinants and consequences of epigenetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5593097") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ARIES is a sub-study of the Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and Children (ALSPAC). 1,2 A sub-set of 1018 mother-offspring pairs were included in ARIES and were selected based on availability of DNA samples at two time- for the mother (at an antenatal clinic and at a follow-up clinic when their offspring were mean age 15.5 years) and three time points for the offspring [at birth, childhood, (mean age 7.5 years) and adolescence at mean age 15.5 years].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000673> "A sub-study of the Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and Children comprising 1,018 mother-offspring pairs with genome-wide DNA methylation profiled at birth, in childhood and in adolescence for the children and at two time points for the mothers, established as an openly accessible resource to study the determinants and consequences of epigenetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25991711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5593097") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To this end, ARIES has profiled genome-wide DNA methylation on samples selected from approximately 1000 mother-child pairs at three time points in children and two time points in their mothers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000673> "A sub-study of the Avon Longitudinal Study of Parents and Children comprising 1,018 mother-offspring pairs with genome-wide DNA methylation profiled at birth, in childhood and in adolescence for the children and at two time points for the mothers, established as an openly accessible resource to study the determinants and consequences of epigenetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000674> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000674>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34741163") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34741163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8571093/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data used for the analyses pertinent to the Bellygenes initiative include both individual-level and aggregate data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000674> "An international collaborative initiative that pooled individual-level and aggregate genetic data on 12,852 people with irritable bowel syndrome and 139,981 controls from multiple studies for genome-wide association studies of irritable bowel syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34741163") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34741163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8571093/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We then meta-analyzed IBS GWAS data from UKB (40,548 cases) and Bellygenes initiative (12,852 cases and 139,981 controls; Supplementary Table 9), an international collaboration studying IBS genetics based on electronic medical records, specialist diagnoses form tertiary clinics and questionnaire data (including Rome III criteria) across multiple cohorts, having again demonstrated high genetic correlation between them (rg = 0.998, s.e.m. = 0.129).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000674> "An international collaborative initiative that pooled individual-level and aggregate genetic data on 12,852 people with irritable bowel syndrome and 139,981 controls from multiple studies for genome-wide association studies of irritable bowel syndrome.")

