AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25987846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2210776226000724-mmc1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2210776226000724-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GWAS results of multiple recurrence analysis in NBCS-1, NBCS-2, UroLife and Barcelona were meta-analysed with GWAS results for recurrence-free survival in the BCPP, GUB-1, GUB-2 and Sheffield cohorts") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000683> "A biobank set up in 2008 at Princess Margaret Hospital, Toronto, Canada, holding biospecimens, including blood for DNA extraction, from patients attending its Genito-Urinary Oncology clinics for the suspicion, diagnosis or treatment of prostate, kidney, bladder, testis or penile tumours, whose non-muscle invasive bladder cancer patients, in two batches (GUB-1 and GUB-2), were used in genetic studies of recurrence and progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25987846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2210776226000724-mmc1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S2210776226000724-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The biospecimens of the GUB, including blood samples for DNA extraction, were obtained from the patients attending clinics for the suspicion, diagnosis and/or treatment of a genito-urinary tumor (prostate, kidney, bladder, testis, penis) within the Genito-Urinary Oncology division of The Princess Margaret’s Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000683> "A biobank set up in 2008 at Princess Margaret Hospital, Toronto, Canada, holding biospecimens, including blood for DNA extraction, from patients attending its Genito-Urinary Oncology clinics for the suspicion, diagnosis or treatment of prostate, kidney, bladder, testis or penile tumours, whose non-muscle invasive bladder cancer patients, in two batches (GUB-1 and GUB-2), were used in genetic studies of recurrence and progression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After excluding subjects with a history of stroke or coronary heart disease, 901 control subjects were included in the genome-wide association study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were enrolled from the participants in the Hisayama Study, an ongoing population-based epidemiological study of cardiovascular disease in the town of Hisayama, Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the genome-wide association study, 1113 cases with ischemic stroke (370 large artery stroke, 137 cardioembolic stroke, 483 small vessel occlusion, 123 undetermined subtype) were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The individuals with ischemic stroke were recruited from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan (Kyushu University Hospital, Hakujyuji Hospital, Fukuoka Red Cross Hospital, Kyushu Medical Center, Imazu Red Cross Hospital, Fukuoka Higashi Medical Center, and Seiai Rehabilitation Hospital) in 2004 (The Fukuoka Stroke Registry [FSR]) .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9524349/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HISAYAMA_FSR |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | 1113 | 1113 | 137 | 483 | 370 | NA | 901 |  |  |  | Clinic-based case-control study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000684> "A case-control study of ischaemic stroke in Japan combining 1,113 patients with ischaemic stroke recruited in 2004 from seven hospitals in Fukuoka Prefecture (the Fukuoka Stroke Registry) with 901 controls free of stroke and coronary heart disease drawn from the population-based Hisayama Study, used in genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6463297/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Risk for late-onset Alzheimer’s disease (LOAD), the most prevalent dementia, is partially driven by genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685> "An international collaboration that first meta-analysed genome-wide association data on late-onset Alzheimer's disease in individuals of European ancestry from four consortia, the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium, the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium, the European Alzheimer's Disease Initiative and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer's Disease Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6463297/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "our group, the International Genomics of Alzheimer’s Project (IGAP) (composed of four consortia:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685> "An international collaboration that first meta-analysed genome-wide association data on late-onset Alzheimer's disease in individuals of European ancestry from four consortia, the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium, the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium, the European Alzheimer's Disease Initiative and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer's Disease Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3896259/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the stage 1 meta-analysis, we used data from four consortia: the Alzheimer’s Disease Genetic Consortium (ADGC), the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology (CHARGE) Consortium, the European Alzheimer’s Disease Initiative (EADI) and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer’s Disease (GERAD) Consortium (Table 1, Online Methods, Supplementary Table 1 and Supplementary Note).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685> "An international collaboration that first meta-analysed genome-wide association data on late-onset Alzheimer's disease in individuals of European ancestry from four consortia, the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium, the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium, the European Alzheimer's Disease Initiative and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer's Disease Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532500") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3896259/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a large, two-stage meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies (GWAS) in individuals of European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000685> "An international collaboration that first meta-analysed genome-wide association data on late-onset Alzheimer's disease in individuals of European ancestry from four consortia, the Alzheimer Disease Genetics Consortium, the Cohorts for Heart and Aging Research in Genomic Epidemiology Consortium, the European Alzheimer's Disease Initiative and the Genetic and Environmental Risk in Alzheimer's Disease Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000686> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000686>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family members of probands with documented coronary artery disease were recruited from the Los Angeles area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000686> "A family study of Mexican Americans in the Los Angeles area, United States, in which the families of probands with documented coronary artery disease were recruited to examine the genetic basis of coronary artery disease and insulin resistance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mexican-American Coronary Artery Disease (MACAD) Study was designed as a family study to examine the genetic basis of coronary artery disease and insulin resistance.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000686> "A family study of Mexican Americans in the Los Angeles area, United States, in which the families of probands with documented coronary artery disease were recruited to examine the genetic basis of coronary artery disease and insulin resistance.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24124113+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GUARDIAN is comprised of seven cohorts, consisting of 4,336 Mexican-American individuals in 1,346 pedigrees.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> "A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family members of probands with documented coronary artery disease were recruited from the Los Angeles area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> "A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four studies measured insulin sensitivity by FSIGT (IRAS, IRAS Family, BetaGene, TRIPOD) and three by euglycemic clamp (MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> "A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seven cohorts are included in the GWAS phase of the GUARDIAN study: five family-based studies (IRAS Family, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero; total 3925 individuals) and two non-family based studies (IRAS, TRIPOD; total 411 individuals).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> "A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3968231/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study described herein, Genetics UndeRlying Diabetes In hispANics, or GUARDIAN, was formed to eventually conduct a GWAS in seven Mexican-American cohorts of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance directly quantified by the euglycemic clamp and FSIGT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000687> "A consortium of seven Mexican-American cohorts in the United States (the IRAS Family Study, BetaGene, MACAD, HTN-IR, NIDDM-Athero, IRAS and TRIPOD; 4,336 individuals in 1,346 pedigrees) formed to conduct genome-wide association studies of insulin sensitivity and insulin clearance measured by euglycemic clamp or frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3490334/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery sample consisted of 15 cohorts of patients with ischaemic stroke who were of European ancestry from Europe, North America, and Australia, together with controls of matched ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688> "A collaboration that meta-analyses genome-wide association datasets from ischaemic stroke case-control cohorts of European ancestry (initially 15 cohorts with 12,389 cases and 62,004 controls) to validate previously reported associations and identify new genetic associations with ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3490334/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established the METASTROKE collaboration with the aim of validating associations from previous GWAS and identifying novel genetic associations through meta-analysis of GWAS datasets for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688> "A collaboration that meta-analyses genome-wide association datasets from ischaemic stroke case-control cohorts of European ancestry (initially 15 cohorts with 12,389 cases and 62,004 controls) to validate previously reported associations and identify new genetic associations with ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3490334/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We meta-analysed data from 15 ischaemic stroke cohorts with a total of 12 389 individuals with ischaemic stroke and 62 004 controls, all of European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000688> "A collaboration that meta-analyses genome-wide association datasets from ischaemic stroke case-control cohorts of European ancestry (initially 15 cohorts with 12,389 cases and 62,004 controls) to validate previously reported associations and identify new genetic associations with ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2062416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2062416+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A random sample of 1,350 persons aged 65 years and older in a rural community underwent cognitive screening as part of a survey to establish a population-based registry of dementing disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689> "A prospective cohort of 1681 adults aged 65 and over living in the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania, USA, recruited from voter registration lists in 1987–1989 and followed every other year for up to 12 years to study cognitive decline and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MoVIES participants were followed every alternate year up to a maximum of 12 years with a mean follow‐up of 11.43 years (SD = 2.15, range = 2–12 years, range of assessments/visits = 2–7).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689> "A prospective cohort of 1681 adults aged 65 and over living in the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania, USA, recruited from voter registration lists in 1987–1989 and followed every other year for up to 12 years to study cognitive decline and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880917/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MoVIES was a prospective study that recruited 1681 individuals aged ≥ 65 residing within the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania during 1987 through 1989 using a voter's registration list.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689> "A prospective cohort of 1681 adults aged 65 and over living in the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania, USA, recruited from voter registration lists in 1987–1989 and followed every other year for up to 12 years to study cognitive decline and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40042063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/movies") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Target number of participants: 1681 Countries: USA startYear: 1987 endYear: 2002") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000689> "A prospective cohort of 1681 adults aged 65 and over living in the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania, USA, recruited from voter registration lists in 1987–1989 and followed every other year for up to 12 years to study cognitive decline and dementia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4769149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the community-based subsample, we recruited 3702 singleton pregnant women within the same pregnancy weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4769149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the high-risk subsample, we recruited 973 singleton pregnant women with risk factors for preeclampsia and 110 singleton pregnant women without known risk factors as a comparison group at 12 0/7–13 6/7 gestational weeks as previously described [13,15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4769149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 4785 recruited mothers, we had data on birth outcomes from the birth register and the two-week interval self-report of positive affect, depressive symptoms, and state anxiety during pregnancy for 3376 mothers (70.6% of those recruited).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4769149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The recruitment took place between September 2005 and February 2010 when these women attended their first ultrasound scan in one of ten hospital maternity clinics participating in the PREDO.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12964119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study population came from 3 Finnish studies, the Prediction and Prevention of Pre-eclampsia and Intrauterine Growth Restriction (PREDO) study [26]") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26919119") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27639277") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12964119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PREDO study recruited between 12 and 14 gestational weeks (GWs) 1079 pregnant women with known risk factor status for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction from 10 hospitals [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000690> "A Finnish pregnancy cohort of 4,785 women recruited at their first ultrasound scan in ten hospital maternity clinics between 2005 and 2010, comprising a high-risk subsample with and without risk factors for preeclampsia and intrauterine growth restriction and a community-based subsample, followed with their children to study the prediction and prevention of pregnancy complications and prenatal influences on offspring development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control participants for this subset of young onset stroke were individuals enrolled in the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study (PROMIS), a case-control study of acute MI based in Pakistan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691> "A case-control study of stroke recruiting imaging-confirmed stroke cases and controls from seven centres in Pakistan, investigating genetic, biomarker and lifestyle determinants of stroke and its subtypes, and using controls from the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants from both these investigations are derived from similar catchment areas, hence providing an attractive opportunity for RACE to utilize PROMIS controls as common controls for genetic investigations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691> "A case-control study of stroke recruiting imaging-confirmed stroke cases and controls from seven centres in Pakistan, investigating genetic, biomarker and lifestyle determinants of stroke and its subtypes, and using controls from the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Risk Assessment of Cerebrovascular Events (RACE) is an on-going existing case-control study of stroke now involving over 5000 imaging confirmed cases of stroke and 5000 controls, recruited from seven centers in Pakistan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691> "A case-control study of stroke recruiting imaging-confirmed stroke cases and controls from seven centres in Pakistan, investigating genetic, biomarker and lifestyle determinants of stroke and its subtypes, and using controls from the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000456.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is aimed to investigate the genetic, biomarker and lifestyle determinants of stroke and its subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000691> "A case-control study of stroke recruiting imaging-confirmed stroke cases and controls from seven centres in Pakistan, investigating genetic, biomarker and lifestyle determinants of stroke and its subtypes, and using controls from the Pakistan Risk of Myocardial Infarction Study for genetic analyses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000692> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000692>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9554233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9241245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REGARDS was designed to investigate reasons underlying the higher rate of stroke mortality among Black compared to White individuals, as well as why residents of the Southeastern U.S. had worse death rates compared to other US regions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000692> "A prospective population-based cohort of 30,239 African American and European American adults aged 45 or older recruited from the 48 contiguous US states and the District of Columbia in 2003–2007, designed to measure stroke incidence and its risk factors and to explain geographic and racial differences in stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9554233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9554233/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 2003 to October 2007, 30,239 participants (42% AA, 55% women) were recruited from the 48 contiguous U.S. states and the District of Columbia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000692> "A prospective population-based cohort of 30,239 African American and European American adults aged 45 or older recruited from the 48 contiguous US states and the District of Columbia in 2003–2007, designed to measure stroke incidence and its risk factors and to explain geographic and racial differences in stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9554233/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9554233/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The REGARDS study is one of the largest ongoing prospective population-based studies in the U.S. and was designed to measure stroke incidence and associated risk factors in AA and European-Americans adults ≥45 years of age (8).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000692> "A prospective population-based cohort of 30,239 African American and European American adults aged 45 or older recruited from the 48 contiguous US states and the District of Columbia in 2003–2007, designed to measure stroke incidence and its risk factors and to explain geographic and racial differences in stroke.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3705339/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 35,533 eligible men from the US, Canada, and Puerto Rico were enrolled in a 3-year period, exceeding the goals for both number of participants and for length of the accrual period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 2 × 2 factorial trial of selenium and vitamin E, alone and in combination, for the prevention of prostate cancer, which enrolled 35,533 men from the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico at more than 400 clinical sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3705339/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Regardless, because SELECT was a very large trial it was necessary to be inclusive with regards to geography in order to accrue an adequate number of participants and the study was conducted through more than 400 clinical sites across the United States, Puerto Rico, and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 2 × 2 factorial trial of selenium and vitamin E, alone and in combination, for the prevention of prostate cancer, which enrolled 35,533 men from the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico at more than 400 clinical sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3705339/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Selenium and Vitamin E Cancer Prevention Trial (SELECT) was conducted to assess the efficacy of selenium and vitamin E alone, and in combination, on the incidence of prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 2 × 2 factorial trial of selenium and vitamin E, alone and in combination, for the prevention of prostate cancer, which enrolled 35,533 men from the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico at more than 400 clinical sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23552052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3705339/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 2 × 2 factorial design clinical trial found that neither selenium nor vitamin E reduced the incidence of prostate cancer after seven years and that vitamin E was associated with a 17% increased risk of prostate cancer compared to placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000693> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, 2 × 2 factorial trial of selenium and vitamin E, alone and in combination, for the prevention of prostate cancer, which enrolled 35,533 men from the United States, Canada and Puerto Rico at more than 400 clinical sites.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4225229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "5023 acute patients with stroke (aged 18–55 years) patients (96.5% Caucasians) were enrolled in the study between April 2007 and January 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4225229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Forty-seven centres from 15 European countries participate in sifap1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4225229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present investigation is a secondary analysis addressing stroke presenting symptoms with a special regard to signs included in the FAST scheme.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4225229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "sifap1 was originally designed to investigate the relation of juvenile stroke and Fabry disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4225229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the sifap1 study was designed as a multicenter multinational prospective observational study of young patients with stroke across Europe (table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25380809") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SIFAP study is a multicenter study carried out to determine the frequency of Fabry disease in an unselected group of young adult patients with acute cerebrovascular events defined as having had an acute ischemic stroke or transient ischemic attack less than three months before enrollment into the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000694> "A multicentre, multinational European prospective observational study of 5,023 patients aged 18–55 with acute stroke or transient ischaemic attack, enrolled at 47 centres in 15 European countries between 2007 and 2010, originally designed to investigate the relation between juvenile stroke and Fabry disease and also used to study stroke patterns in young adults.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2862965") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SpiroMeta consortium consists of 14 GWAS studies: ALSPAC, B58C-T1DGC, B58C- WTCCC, EPIC (obese and population-based substudies)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> "A consortium of cohort studies of European-ancestry individuals, initially 14 genome-wide association studies with 20,288 participants and later expanded, established to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of spirometric lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2862965") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included 14 studies of individuals of European ancestry, with sample sizes totaling 20,288 (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> "A consortium of cohort studies of European-ancestry individuals, initially 14 genome-wide association studies with 20,288 participants and later expanded, established to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of spirometric lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2862965") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested genome-wide association with forced expiratory volume in 1 s (FEV1) and the ratio of FEV1 to forced vital capacity (FVC) in the SpiroMeta consortium (n = 20,288 individuals of European ancestry).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> "A consortium of cohort studies of European-ancestry individuals, initially 14 genome-wide association studies with 20,288 participants and later expanded, established to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of spirometric lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2862965") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore established the SpiroMeta consortium to facilitate large-scale meta-analysis of GWAS of lung function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> "A consortium of cohort studies of European-ancestry individuals, initially 14 genome-wide association studies with 20,288 participants and later expanded, established to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of spirometric lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20010834") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30804560") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6397078/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, through additional analysis of the spirometry data in UK Biobank and substantial expansion of the SpiroMeta consortium, we have markedly increased samples sizes to almost seven times those included in previous studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000695> "A consortium of cohort studies of European-ancestry individuals, initially 14 genome-wide association studies with 20,288 participants and later expanded, established to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of spirometric lung function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data spanning almost 60 years allow researchers to link family background, adolescent characteristics, educational experiences, employment experiences, income, wealth, family formation and social and religious engagement to midlife and late-life physical health, mental health, psychological well-being, cognition, end of life planning and mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696> "A longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957, most born in 1939, and one of their randomly selected siblings, followed for almost 60 years to link family background, adolescent characteristics, education, work and family life to later-life physical and mental health, cognition and mortality, with saliva samples for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Further, recently collected saliva samples allow researchers to explore the inter-relationships among genes, behaviours and environment, including genetic determinants of behaviours (e.g. educational attainment); the interactions between genes and environment; and how these interactions predict behaviours.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696> "A longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957, most born in 1939, and one of their randomly selected siblings, followed for almost 60 years to link family background, adolescent characteristics, education, work and family life to later-life physical and mental health, cognition and mortality, with saliva samples for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Most panel members were born in 1939, and the sample is broadly representative of White, non-Hispanic American men and women who have completed at least a high school education.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696> "A longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957, most born in 1939, and one of their randomly selected siblings, followed for almost 60 years to link family background, adolescent characteristics, education, work and family life to later-life physical and mental health, cognition and mortality, with saliva samples for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585852") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937969/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wisconsin Longitudinal Study (WLS) is a longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957 and one of their randomly selected siblings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000696> "A longitudinal study of men and women who graduated from Wisconsin high schools in 1957, most born in 1939, and one of their randomly selected siblings, followed for almost 60 years to link family background, adolescent characteristics, education, work and family life to later-life physical and mental health, cognition and mortality, with saliva samples for genetic studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2785858/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we found that African-American and subjects of other ethnicities with low socioeconomic status, ascertained while receiving primary care at an urban, public hospital, were at high risk of exposure to traumatic events and the development of stress-related psychiatric illness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697> "A study of low-income, predominantly African American adults recruited from the primary care and obstetrics-gynaecology clinics of Grady Memorial Hospital, an urban public hospital in Atlanta, United States, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for trauma-related disorders such as posttraumatic stress disorder and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2785858/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initial interviews were performed with 1600 participants approached while in the waiting rooms of primary care or obstetrical-gynecological clinics of Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia from 2005 to 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697> "A study of low-income, predominantly African American adults recruited from the primary care and obstetrics-gynaecology clinics of Grady Memorial Hospital, an urban public hospital in Atlanta, United States, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for trauma-related disorders such as posttraumatic stress disorder and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2785858/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data from this study were collected to investigate the demographic and trauma exposure characteristics of a population of urban, low-income, predominantly African-American men and women and the relationship of these variables to post-traumatic stress and depressive symptomatology as well as the presence of PTSD and MDD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697> "A study of low-income, predominantly African American adults recruited from the primary care and obstetrics-gynaecology clinics of Grady Memorial Hospital, an urban public hospital in Atlanta, United States, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for trauma-related disorders such as posttraumatic stress disorder and depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19892208") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34187551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8243879/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Grady Trauma Project (GTP) investigates the influence of genetic and environmental factors on response to stressful events in a predominantly African-American, urban population of low socioeconomic status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000697> "A study of low-income, predominantly African American adults recruited from the primary care and obstetrics-gynaecology clinics of Grady Memorial Hospital, an urban public hospital in Atlanta, United States, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for trauma-related disorders such as posttraumatic stress disorder and depression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30134803") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The “10 001 Dalmatians” project was funded by grants from the Medical Research Council (UK)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> "A Croatian biobank project, based at the University of Split with UK Medical Research Council funding, that recruited adults from the isolated Dalmatian islands of Vis and Korčula and from the mainland city of Split into separate cohorts, to investigate genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30134803") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was performed on samples from three Croatian populations: from the Dalmatian islands of Korcula and Vis and the mainland city of Split, within the large-scale project of “10,001 Dalmatians” (Rudan et al., 2009).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> "A Croatian biobank project, based at the University of Split with UK Medical Research Council funding, that recruited adults from the isolated Dalmatian islands of Vis and Korčula and from the mainland city of Split into separate cohorts, to investigate genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36914875") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10011137/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three cohorts have been recruited as part of the CROATIA study: CROATIA-Vis13 , CROATIA-Korcula14 and CROATIA-Split15 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> "A Croatian biobank project, based at the University of Split with UK Medical Research Council funding, that recruited adults from the isolated Dalmatian islands of Vis and Korčula and from the mainland city of Split into separate cohorts, to investigate genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "No specific inclusion or exclusion criteria were established, except for age > 18 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> "A Croatian biobank project, based at the University of Split with UK Medical Research Council funding, that recruited adults from the isolated Dalmatian islands of Vis and Korčula and from the mainland city of Split into separate cohorts, to investigate genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6016867/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10138356/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is based on the Croatian biobank 10,001 Dalmatians [78,79], the most comprehensive research resource for investigating genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000698> "A Croatian biobank project, based at the University of Split with UK Medical Research Council funding, that recruited adults from the isolated Dalmatian islands of Vis and Korčula and from the mainland city of Split into separate cohorts, to investigate genetic, environmental and social determinants of health and disease in Croatia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described in the Cohorts Profile published in 2012,4 decades later, participants of both Surveys, mostly living in Edinburgh and the surrounding area (the Lothians) in older age, were invited to participate in the Lothian Birth Cohort (LBC) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2004 and 2007, 1091 members of SMS1947 were recruited to Wave 1 of the LBC1936 study, at a mean age of 70 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, the availability of five waves of consistently measured cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging, psychosocial, lifestyle and other data in the LBC1921 and four waves of such data in the LBC1936 mean that longitudinal analyses are possible, covering the age ranges 79-92 and 70-79, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LBC studies set out principally to examine the nature and determinants of non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age, and within in older age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The same MHT was administered to almost every child born in 1936 and attending school on 4 June 4 1947 for the SMS1947 (N = 70 805).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29546429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6124629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Waves of testing have been conducted at roughly 3-yearly intervals since inception: the LBC1921 have been followed up five times, from age 79 to age 92 years;8–11 and the LBC1936 have been followed up four times from age 70 to age 79 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000699> "A cohort of 1,091 people born in 1936 who took an intelligence test at age 11 in the Scottish Mental Survey of 1947, recruited in 2004–2007 at a mean age of 70, mostly living in Edinburgh and the Lothians, and retested about every 3 years with cognitive, biomedical, brain imaging and lifestyle assessments to study non-pathological cognitive ageing from childhood to older age.")

