AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18216052+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate End-points (ECLIPSE) is a 3-yr longitudinal study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000706> "A 3-year multinational observational cohort of 2,164 patients with moderate to very severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and smoking and non-smoking controls, recruited at 46 centres in 12 countries in North America, Europe and New Zealand, to define COPD subtypes and find clinical, imaging, biomarker and genetic predictors of disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2944278/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based upon these calculations, we studied 2164 patients with COPD (GOLD stage 2-4), 337 smoking controls and 245 non-smoking controls (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000706> "A 3-year multinational observational cohort of 2,164 patients with moderate to very severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and smoking and non-smoking controls, recruited at 46 centres in 12 countries in North America, Europe and New Zealand, to define COPD subtypes and find clinical, imaging, biomarker and genetic predictors of disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2944278/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate Endpoints (ECLIPSE) is a large observational study of COPD patients and controls conducted at 46 centres in 12 countries aimed at defining COPD phenotypes and identifying biomarkers and/or genetic parameters that help to predict disease progression [4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000706> "A 3-year multinational observational cohort of 2,164 patients with moderate to very severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and smoking and non-smoking controls, recruited at 46 centres in 12 countries in North America, Europe and New Zealand, to define COPD subtypes and find clinical, imaging, biomarker and genetic predictors of disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2944278/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In these individuals, we measured clinical parameters, nutritional status, spirometry, exercise tolerance, and amount of emphysema by computed tomography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000706> "A 3-year multinational observational cohort of 2,164 patients with moderate to very severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and smoking and non-smoking controls, recruited at 46 centres in 12 countries in North America, Europe and New Zealand, to define COPD subtypes and find clinical, imaging, biomarker and genetic predictors of disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18216052") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8777202/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Evaluation of COPD Longitudinally to Identify Predictive Surrogate Endpoints
(ECLIPSE) study was a longitudinal study of subjects with COPD, enrolled at multiple study centers in Europe,
the USA, Canada, and New Zealand, with a small number of controls with normal lung function4") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000706> "A 3-year multinational observational cohort of 2,164 patients with moderate to very severe chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and smoking and non-smoking controls, recruited at 46 centres in 12 countries in North America, Europe and New Zealand, to define COPD subtypes and find clinical, imaging, biomarker and genetic predictors of disease progression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35186809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35186809+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We describe how a set of early life factors used in a large, prospective community cohort from Australia are associated with language abilities across the preschool years, and determine if either an accumulation of risk factors or a clustering of risk factors provide a feasible approach to surveillance of language development in preschool children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707> "A population-based cohort of 1910 infants recruited at 8 months of age in Melbourne, Australia, in 2003–2004 and followed through childhood with parent reports and language assessments to study language development and its early-life predictors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ELVS | Population-based | Australia | European | [7] | 5, 7 or 11* | 5, 7 or 11* | WRAT-4 | 484 | 258 | 226 | Castles and Coltheart | 630 | 326 | 304 | WRAT-4 | 481 | 256 | 225 | CTOPP | 494 | 249 | 247 | CNRep | 476 | 237 | 239 | WAIS | 480 | 255 | 225") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707> "A population-based cohort of 1910 infants recruited at 8 months of age in Melbourne, Australia, in 2003–2004 and followed through childhood with parent reports and language assessments to study language development and its early-life predictors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41237490+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Early Language in Victoria Study (ELVS) recruited 1910 8-month-olds in Melbourne in 2003-2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707> "A population-based cohort of 1910 infants recruited at 8 months of age in Melbourne, Australia, in 2003–2004 and followed through childhood with parent reports and language assessments to study language development and its early-life predictors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41237490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41237490+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used ensemble method SuperLearner to estimate how accurately the parent-reported predictors and polygenic scores predict low 11-year language outcome (>1.5 standard deviations below the mean) in each cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000707> "A population-based cohort of 1910 infants recruited at 8 months of age in Melbourne, Australia, in 2003–2004 and followed through childhood with parent reports and language assessments to study language development and its early-life predictors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6040001/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINIplus consists of two study arms with specific aims: “German Infant Nutritional Intervention Study (GINI study)” and a non-interventional study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6040001/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINIplus is a prospective population-based birth cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6040001/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy, mature newborns with German parents and a birth weight of more than 2,500 g were recruited between September 1, 1995 and October 31, 1997 (Munich) or until June 30, 1998 (Wesel) in obstetric hospitals in Munich (10 hospitals) and Wesel (8 hospitals).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6040001/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 5,991 newborns recruited, 3,317 (55.4%) could be followed until the age of 10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6040001/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The interventional arm of the GINIplus study was a double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial (DBRCT) using hydrolyzed formula nutrition and carried out in children with a family history of allergy during the first 4 months of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30402607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30402607+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed the natural course of atopic diseases and the role of life-style, environmental, and genetic factors for disease onset, intermediate phenotypes, and genes involved in detoxification and oxidative stress.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000708> "A prospective population-based German birth cohort of 5,991 healthy term newborns recruited in obstetric hospitals in Munich and Wesel in 1995–1998, comprising a double-blind randomised trial of hydrolysed infant formula in children with a family history of allergy (the German Infant Nutritional Intervention study, GINI) and a non-interventional arm, about 55% of whom were followed for the first 10 years to study the natural course of atopic diseases and their determinants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrolled subjects were between 18 and 20 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> "A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GOOD study subjects (study inclusion criteria described under the cortical bone thickness GWA study) were contacted and invited to participate in a five-year follow-up exam [51].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> "A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gothenburg Osteoporosis and Obesity Determinants (GOOD) study was initiated to determine both environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass [39] [40].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> "A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were no other exclusion criteria, and 49% of the study candidates agreed to participate (n = 1068).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> "A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Young men were randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area in Sweden using national population registers, contacted by telephone, and invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000709> "A cohort of 1,068 young men aged 18–20, randomly identified in the greater Gothenburg area of Sweden from national population registers, initiated to determine environmental and genetic factors involved in the regulation of bone and fat mass, with a five-year follow-up examination.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3174168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two different cohorts were used, the Danish National Birth Cohort for women and a draft board examination cohort for men, both of which were constituted by young Danish adults with negligible admixture of other ethnicities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710> "A case-control sample of extremely overweight young Danish adults and equal numbers of randomly drawn population controls, selected from women of the Danish National Birth Cohort and men of a Danish draft-board examination cohort, for genome-wide association study of body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21935397+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From two large Danish cohorts we selected all extremely overweight young men and women (n = 2,633), and equal numbers of population-based controls (n = 2,740, drawn randomly from the same populations as the extremes, representing ∼212,000 individuals).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710> "A case-control sample of extremely overweight young Danish adults and equal numbers of randomly drawn population controls, selected from women of the Danish National Birth Cohort and men of a Danish draft-board examination cohort, for genome-wide association study of body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21935397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21935397+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to identify new loci associated with BMI and to ascertain whether using an extreme sampling design would identify the variants known to be associated with BMI in general populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000710> "A case-control sample of extremely overweight young Danish adults and equal numbers of randomly drawn population controls, selected from women of the Danish National Birth Cohort and men of a Danish draft-board examination cohort, for genome-wide association study of body mass index.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000711> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000711>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10405/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10405_MOESM207_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Most of the studies contributing to the ICBP-GWAS were general population samples, and were recruited for classical or genetic epidemiological purposes, as described below.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000711> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of systolic and diastolic blood pressure, whose 2011 multi-stage meta-analysis combined about 200,000 individuals of European descent to find blood pressure loci and relate them to hypertension and cardiovascular disease risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21909115+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genetic risk score based on 29 genome-wide significant variants was associated with hypertension, left ventricular wall thickness, stroke and coronary artery disease, but not kidney disease or kidney function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000711> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of systolic and diastolic blood pressure, whose 2011 multi-stage meta-analysis combined about 200,000 individuals of European descent to find blood pressure loci and relate them to hypertension and cardiovascular disease risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21909115+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This genome-wide association study of systolic and diastolic blood pressure, which used a multi-stage design in 200,000 individuals of European descent, identified sixteen novel loci: six of these loci contain genes previously known or suspected to regulate blood pressure (GUCY1A3-GUCY1B3, NPR3-C5orf23, ADM, FURIN-FES, GOSR2, GNAS-EDN3); the other ten provide new clues to blood pressure physiology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000711> "A consortium of genome-wide association studies of systolic and diastolic blood pressure, whose 2011 multi-stage meta-analysis combined about 200,000 individuals of European descent to find blood pressure loci and relate them to hypertension and cardiovascular disease risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24509779") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3655151/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Associations of SNPs within ANKK1 (rs2734849 and rs11604671) were replicated in the Iowa LI cohort with LI case-control status (OR = 1.4 [1.1–2.0]; p≤7.41×10−3) (Table 9).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> "A case-control sample of 219 children with language impairment and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa, United States, who completed a battery of language measures (including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test and nonword repetition) used to define case status, and reading, spelling and IQ assessments, used in genetic association studies of language impairment and of reading- and language-related skills.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24509779") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3655151/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects completed various language measures, including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test (PPVT) and NWR, which were used to derive a composite language score, which was dichotomized into case-control status at −1.14 standard deviations [40].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> "A case-control sample of 219 children with language impairment and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa, United States, who completed a battery of language measures (including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test and nonword repetition) used to define case status, and reading, spelling and IQ assessments, used in genetic association studies of language impairment and of reading- and language-related skills.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24509779") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3655151/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Iowa LI cohort is comprised of 219 LI cases and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> "A case-control sample of 219 children with language impairment and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa, United States, who completed a battery of language measures (including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test and nonword repetition) used to define case status, and reading, spelling and IQ assessments, used in genetic association studies of language impairment and of reading- and language-related skills.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24509779") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Iowa study, word and nonword reading was measured with the Woodcock Reading Mastery Tests-Revisited (WRMT-R) (55) using the Word Identification and Word Attack subtests, respectively. In these tests, participants are asked to read aloud isolated words or nonwords from a list with increased difficulty. Spelling was assessed using the Test of Written Spelling-2 (TWS2) (56),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> "A case-control sample of 219 children with language impairment and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa, United States, who completed a battery of language measures (including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test and nonword repetition) used to define case status, and reading, spelling and IQ assessments, used in genetic association studies of language impairment and of reading- and language-related skills.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23691092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24509779") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Performance IQ was measured with the WISC (37). The study was approved by the Institutional Review Board of the University of Iowa IRB-01 (#200511767). All subjects in the Iowa cohort were minors who assented to participation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000712> "A case-control sample of 219 children with language impairment and 209 sex- and age-matched, unrelated controls collected at the University of Iowa, United States, who completed a battery of language measures (including the Peabody Picture Vocabulary Test and nonword repetition) used to define case status, and reading, spelling and IQ assessments, used in genetic association studies of language impairment and of reading- and language-related skills.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 28 centers have participated in these cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As of December 2023, K-ROAD has recruited over 5,800 participants, including individuals across the Alzheimer’s clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment, and frontotemporal dementia spectra.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It consists of three prospective cohorts supported by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency, the Ministry of Health and Welfare, and the Samsung medical center intramural fund, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent clinical evaluations, neuroimaging, and biomarker analysis, with data collected on a range of clinical and genomic markers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Korea-Registries to Overcome Dementia and Accelerate Dementia Research (K-ROAD) aims to establish a large-scale, hospital-based dementia cohort to address this gap, with a focus on understanding disease progression, developing early diagnostics, and supporting treatment advancements specific to the Korean population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The three cohorts include the precision medicine platform for mild cognitive impairment based on multi-omics, imaging, evidence-based R&BD (PREMIER) consortium, the longitudinal/cohort study of patients with late onset dementia (LLOD) cohort, and the Samsung Medical Center (SMC) amyloid PET cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000713> "A hospital-based Korean dementia research programme made up of three prospective cohorts (the PREMIER consortium, the LLOD cohort and the Samsung Medical Center amyloid PET cohort) at 28 centres, which by December 2023 had recruited over 5,800 participants across the Alzheimer's clinical syndrome, subcortical vascular cognitive impairment and frontotemporal dementia spectra, with clinical, neuroimaging, biomarker and genomic data, to study disease progression and early diagnosis of dementia in the Korean population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3127556") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase 1, which has been completed, includes participants from 3 studies funded by the National Institutes of Health, which sought to identify genetic determinants of peripheral arterial disease (PAD), venous thromboembolism, and pan- creatic cancer, respectively, with a combined total sample size of 6307 unique participants (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714> "A genotype-phenotype resource assembled at Mayo Clinic from participants of multiple Mayo Clinic research studies who gave general research consent to share their high-throughput genotyping data, linked to electronic medical record data for phenotype extraction, to enable cost-effective genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21646302+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study to identify genetic variants associated with total bilirubin levels was conducted to test the genetic research capability of the MayoGC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714> "A genotype-phenotype resource assembled at Mayo Clinic from participants of multiple Mayo Clinic research studies who gave general research consent to share their high-throughput genotyping data, linked to electronic medical record data for phenotype extraction, to enable cost-effective genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21646302+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants include those who gave general research consent in the contributing studies to share high-throughput genotyping data with other investigators.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714> "A genotype-phenotype resource assembled at Mayo Clinic from participants of multiple Mayo Clinic research studies who gave general research consent to share their high-throughput genotyping data, linked to electronic medical record data for phenotype extraction, to enable cost-effective genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21646302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21646302+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To create a cohort for cost-effective genetic research, the Mayo Genome Consortia (MayoGC) has been assembled with participants from research studies across Mayo Clinic with high-throughput genetic data and electronic medical record (EMR) data for phenotype extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000714> "A genotype-phenotype resource assembled at Mayo Clinic from participants of multiple Mayo Clinic research studies who gave general research consent to share their high-throughput genotyping data, linked to electronic medical record data for phenotype extraction, to enable cost-effective genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35227251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, after signing informed consent, participants aged 30 to 75 years were randomly selected from the Malmö census register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715> "A population-based cohort of people aged 30–75 years born in Iraq or Sweden and resident in Malmö, Sweden, randomly selected from the Malmö census register, to study the impact of migration and ethnicity on type 2 diabetes and related metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35227251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from the MEDIM study has revealed that Iraqi migrants in Malmö are at twice the risk of T2D [9] and have younger age of disease onset compared with the Swedish born population, with high burden of diabetes family history, and poorer glycemic control and insulin sensitivity [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715> "A population-based cohort of people aged 30–75 years born in Iraq or Sweden and resident in Malmö, Sweden, randomly selected from the Malmö census register, to study the impact of migration and ethnicity on type 2 diabetes and related metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35227251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MEDIM cohort (the impact of Migration and Ethnicity on Diabetes in Malmö) is a population-based cohort comprised of people aged 30 to 75 years, born in either Iraq or Sweden, and resident in Malmö.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715> "A population-based cohort of people aged 30–75 years born in Iraq or Sweden and resident in Malmö, Sweden, randomly selected from the Malmö census register, to study the impact of migration and ethnicity on type 2 diabetes and related metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8886846/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37061557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10105731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People born in Iraq or Sweden, who were 30–75 years of age, were invited from 2010 to 2012 to participate in the population based MEDIM study including a health exam, fasting blood sampling, assessment of insulin secretion and action (through oral glucose tolerance test) and questionnaires assessing history of CVD, cancer and T2D.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000715> "A population-based cohort of people aged 30–75 years born in Iraq or Sweden and resident in Malmö, Sweden, randomly selected from the Malmö census register, to study the impact of migration and ethnicity on type 2 diabetes and related metabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38490347") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11193636") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CSMC-MIRIAD (any IBD) and RISK (CD only) had serology data available for evaluation (Table S2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38490347") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11193636") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cedars-Sinai has the right to receive future royalty payments from Prometheus Biosciences, Inc., a wholly-owned subsidiary of Merck which has access to the data and specimens in Cedars-Sinai’s MIRIAD Biobank (including a proportion of the data used in this study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38490347") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11193636") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These current analyses not only utilized the immune-focused Immunochip array, but also included an expanded CSMC study cohort in addition to NIDDK, SHARE and RISK cohorts, allowing for the investigation of IBD EIMs in the largest sample size to-date.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13046806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, to carry out an indirect assessment of imputation performance, where phenotype information is necessary, we rely exclusively on the MIRIAD dataset, as it is the only dataset with comprehensive clinical phenotype information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13046806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phenotype composition differs across cohorts: RISK contains only CD cases, PROTECT contains only UC, while MIRIAD includes CD, UC, and non-IBD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41748696") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13046806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts include IBD cohorts from the Cedars-Sinai IBD Biobank (MIRIAD, size = 9231),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000716> "A biobank of patients with Crohn's disease or ulcerative colitis and non-IBD controls recruited with informed consent at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, United States, holding clinical phenotype, serological and genetic data and specimens for inflammatory bowel disease research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4939239/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stage 1 analysis included 1737 cases and 3602 controls among African Americans drawn from eight studies of lung cancer (Supplementary Table 2a).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> "A collection of African American lung cancer cases and controls drawn from eight US lung cancer studies, among them the Southern Community Cohort Study, the NCI-MD Lung Cancer Case-Control Study, the MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study and the Northern California Lung Cancer Study, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4939239/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study aimed to conduct a GWAS in African Americans, who have higher rates of lung cancer despite smoking fewer cigarettes per day when compared with Caucasians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> "A collection of African American lung cancer cases and controls drawn from eight US lung cancer studies, among them the Southern Community Cohort Study, the NCI-MD Lung Cancer Case-Control Study, the MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study and the Northern California Lung Cancer Study, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4939239/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the association between smoking behavior and lung cancer, we performed linear regression analysis for CPD and pack years as the outcomes, adjusting for study, age, gender, coefficient for YRI, current smokers, and eigenvectors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> "A collection of African American lung cancer cases and controls drawn from eight US lung cancer studies, among them the Southern Community Cohort Study, the NCI-MD Lung Cancer Case-Control Study, the MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study and the Northern California Lung Cancer Study, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4939239/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped 1,024,001 SNPs in 1737 cases and 3602 controls in stage 1, followed by a replication phase of 20 SNPs (p<1.51×10−5) in an independent set of 866 cases and 796 controls in stage 2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> "A collection of African American lung cancer cases and controls drawn from eight US lung cancer studies, among them the Southern Community Cohort Study, the NCI-MD Lung Cancer Case-Control Study, the MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study and the Northern California Lung Cancer Study, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27393504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4939239/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from the following studies: MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study, The Multiethnic Cohort Study (MEC), NCI-MD Lung Cancer-Case Control Study, Northern California Lung Cancer Study, Project CHURCH (Creating a Higher Understanding of Cancer Research & Community Health), Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial (PLCO), Southern Community Cohort Study (SCCS)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000717> "A collection of African American lung cancer cases and controls drawn from eight US lung cancer studies, among them the Southern Community Cohort Study, the NCI-MD Lung Cancer Case-Control Study, the MD Anderson Lung Cancer Epidemiology Study and the Northern California Lung Cancer Study, genotyped for a genome-wide association study of lung cancer and smoking phenotypes in African Americans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000718> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000718>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9851382/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IBD cases recruited at each center had their diagnoses of CD, UC, and IBD-U confirmed by chart review, as per the IBDGC phenotyping manual (https://ibdgc.uchicago.edu/files/IBDGC_Phenotyping_Manual_2019-10.pdf).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000718> "A cohort of patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease recruited since 2003 by the genetic research centres of the NIDDK IBD Genetics Consortium in the United States and Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by chart review, for IBD gene discovery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9851382/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IBDGC cohort was established in 2003, when 6 genetic research centers (GRCs) in the United States and Canada began recruiting patients with confirmed CD, UC, or IBD-U, for IBD gene discovery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000718> "A cohort of patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease recruited since 2003 by the genetic research centres of the NIDDK IBD Genetics Consortium in the United States and Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by chart review, for IBD gene discovery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36686985") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9851382/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We observed that in our National Institutes of Diabetes, Digestion and Kidney Diseases IBDGC cohort (a cohort used in multiple studies to elucidate the genetics of IBD as well as other factors), features are similar to those of most cohorts44, 45, 46 with only a few exceptions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000718> "A cohort of patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease recruited since 2003 by the genetic research centres of the NIDDK IBD Genetics Consortium in the United States and Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by chart review, for IBD gene discovery.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048805/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ADGC is a collaborative network in the United States that includes the 29 NIA-funded ADCs and numerous AD genetics investigators who are working to identify genes responsible for AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719> "A case-control collection of autopsied Alzheimer disease cases and non-demented controls, drawn from longitudinal aging research cohorts at 10 NIA-funded Alzheimer's Disease Centers in the United States and assembled at Oregon Health & Science University for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer disease and its neuropathology within the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048805/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Oregon Health and Science University (OHSU) were recruited from aging research cohorts at 10 NIA-funded ADCs and do not overlap with other ADGC samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719> "A case-control collection of autopsied Alzheimer disease cases and non-demented controls, drawn from longitudinal aging research cohorts at 10 NIA-funded Alzheimer's Disease Centers in the United States and assembled at Oregon Health & Science University for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer disease and its neuropathology within the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048805/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts used included unrelated Caucasian cases and controls from the following sources: the NIA-funded ADCs, ADNI, UM/VU/MSSM, TGEN, and OHSU.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719> "A case-control collection of autopsied Alzheimer disease cases and non-demented controls, drawn from longitudinal aging research cohorts at 10 NIA-funded Alzheimer's Disease Centers in the United States and assembled at Oregon Health & Science University for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer disease and its neuropathology within the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20697030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2802/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2802_MOESM27_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The OHSU dataset includes 132 autopsy-confirmed AD cases and 153 deceased controls that were evaluated for dementia within 12 months prior to death (age at death >65 years), which are a subset of the 193 cases and 451 controls examined in our previous study [1] meeting more stringent QC criteria in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000719> "A case-control collection of autopsied Alzheimer disease cases and non-demented controls, drawn from longitudinal aging research cohorts at 10 NIA-funded Alzheimer's Disease Centers in the United States and assembled at Oregon Health & Science University for genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer disease and its neuropathology within the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33133009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7198638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy volunteers were recruited to the PAGES (Phenomics and Genomics Sample) sample from the Munich greater area and were of German descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720> "A sample collected at the University of Munich, Germany, of about 3,000 healthy volunteers of German descent from the Munich area, assessed with structured psychiatric interviews covering themselves and their first-degree relatives, together with about 1,000 patients with schizophrenia and about 300 people with other diagnoses, including Alzheimer's disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic, used as a case and control resource in genetic studies of psychiatric, neurological and neurodegenerative disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33133009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7198638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PAGES consists of approximately 3000 healthy individuals with a detailed medical, neurological, and psychiatric history of the participants themselves, and their first-degree relatives who were assessed using semi-structured and comprehensive interviews including the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV (SCID I, II) [18, 19] and the Family History Assessment Module [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720> "A sample collected at the University of Munich, Germany, of about 3,000 healthy volunteers of German descent from the Munich area, assessed with structured psychiatric interviews covering themselves and their first-degree relatives, together with about 1,000 patients with schizophrenia and about 300 people with other diagnoses, including Alzheimer's disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic, used as a case and control resource in genetic studies of psychiatric, neurological and neurodegenerative disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33133009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33133009") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7579408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples from 1,775 unrelated healthy subjects of European ancestry were taken from the Phenomics and Genomics Sample (PAGES), which is comprised of ~3,000 controls, 1,000 schizophrenia patients and 300 individuals with other diagnoses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720> "A sample collected at the University of Munich, Germany, of about 3,000 healthy volunteers of German descent from the Munich area, assessed with structured psychiatric interviews covering themselves and their first-degree relatives, together with about 1,000 patients with schizophrenia and about 300 people with other diagnoses, including Alzheimer's disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic, used as a case and control resource in genetic studies of psychiatric, neurological and neurodegenerative disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32157568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33133009") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9005347/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PAGES study: This study includes 301 subjects. AD patients were recruited at the memory clinic of the Department of Psychiatry, University of Munich, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000720> "A sample collected at the University of Munich, Germany, of about 3,000 healthy volunteers of German descent from the Munich area, assessed with structured psychiatric interviews covering themselves and their first-degree relatives, together with about 1,000 patients with schizophrenia and about 300 people with other diagnoses, including Alzheimer's disease patients from the psychiatric memory clinic, used as a case and control resource in genetic studies of psychiatric, neurological and neurodegenerative disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21134251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3019209/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An asthma questionnaire is completed and returned by post. At a routine clinic visit saliva is collected for DNA extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> "A study of children and adolescents aged 2–16 years with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited through 15 secondary-care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011, with questionnaire and DNA data to study genetic and environmental influences on asthma and its treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21134251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3019209/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we describe the methodology and experiences in establishing a database for childhood asthma designed to study gene-environment interactions (PAGES - Paediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> "A study of children and adolescents aged 2–16 years with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited through 15 secondary-care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011, with questionnaire and DNA data to study genetic and environmental influences on asthma and its treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25616159+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a meta-analysis of three cohort studies: Pharmacogenetics of Asthma Medication in Children: Medication with Anti-Inflammatory effects (n = 357, age: 4-12 years, the Netherlands), BREATHE (n = 820, age: 3-22 years, UK) and Paediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study (n = 391, age: 2-16 years, UK).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> "A study of children and adolescents aged 2–16 years with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited through 15 secondary-care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011, with questionnaire and DNA data to study genetic and environmental influences on asthma and its treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4461653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PAGES study recruited children and adolescents (age: 2-16 years) with physician-diagnosed asthma through 15 secondary care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> "A study of children and adolescents aged 2–16 years with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited through 15 secondary-care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011, with questionnaire and DNA data to study genetic and environmental influences on asthma and its treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25616159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8503671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pediatric Asthma Gene Environment Study (PAGES) is a cross sectional observational study designed to relate asthma outcomes to environmental and genetic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000721> "A study of children and adolescents aged 2–16 years with physician-diagnosed asthma recruited through 15 secondary-care asthma clinics across Scotland from 2008 to 2011, with questionnaire and DNA data to study genetic and environmental influences on asthma and its treatment response.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28259484+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A competing-risk model for disease complications was derived and validated in independent groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28259484+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We did a prospective inception cohort study of paediatric patients with newly diagnosed Crohn's disease at 28 sites in the USA and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5719489/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1813 patients were enrolled in our study (table 1). 402 did not have gut inflammation on endoscopy and were controls for microbial and gene expression studies. 204 patients were diagnosed with ulcerative colitis, and 111 with unspecified inflammatory bowel disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5719489/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotypes, antimicrobial serologies, ileal gene expression, and ileal, rectal, and faecal microbiota were assessed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5719489/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2008, the Risk Stratification and Identification of Immunogenetic and Microbial Markers of Rapid Disease Progression in Children with Crohn’s Disease (RISK) study was initiated to characterise prospectively the natural history of newly diagnosed Crohn’s disease in children presenting with an uncomplicated disease state.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28259484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5719489/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients younger than 18 years old with suspected inflammatory bowel disease were enrolled between Nov 1, 2008, and June 30, 2012 (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier NCT00790543; appendix).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000722> "A prospective inception cohort of patients younger than 18 years with suspected inflammatory bowel disease, enrolled at diagnosis between 2008 and 2012 at 28 sites in the United States and Canada (mostly Crohn's disease, also ulcerative colitis, unclassified IBD and non-inflamed controls), to characterise the natural history of newly diagnosed paediatric Crohn's disease and predict its complications from clinical, serological, genomic and microbial markers at diagnosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10200223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, TARCC aims to bridge health disparities by incorporating minority populations in Texas such as the Hispanic community, in particular MAs, into research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10379967/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TARCC is a longitudinally followed convenience sample of elderly persons diagnosed with AD, MCI, or control subjects recruited from five Texas medical schools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A novel and important strength of the TARCC database is its longitudinal nature, wherein participants were studied annually.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over time, the TARCC sites enrolled a cohort of more than 3,600 study participants representing over 14,500 visits (an average of four annual visits for each subject).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Texas Harris Alzheimer’s Research Study began in June of 2005 with the goal of establishing a comprehensive research cohort of well characterized subjects to address improved diagnosis, treatment, and, ultimately, prevention of AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36872777") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.txalzresearch.org/research/the-texas-harris-alzheimers-research-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The research study resulted in a large, standardized and well-curated research database containing integrated psychometric, medical and genetic data, biological markers, whole blood, serum, plasma and DNA from TARCC study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000723> "A longitudinal research cohort begun in June 2005 by the Texas Alzheimer's Research and Care Consortium, which has enrolled more than 3,600 older adults with Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition, with deliberate inclusion of Mexican Americans, at the consortium's Texas sites and followed annually with clinical, neuropsychological, genetic and blood biomarker assessments, to improve the diagnosis, treatment and prevention of Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6767399/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ethical clearance for the study was provided by the University of York, Department of Psychology's Ethics Committee and the NHS Research Ethics Committee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> "A longitudinal cohort of children at family risk of dyslexia, children with preschool language difficulties and typically developing controls, recruited from about age 3½ in 2007–2009 from York and neighbouring regions of northern England by the University of York and followed to study the development of language, reading and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6767399/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were recruited to the study between 2007 and 2009 from the City of York and neighboring regions within Yorkshire and the northeast of England.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> "A longitudinal cohort of children at family risk of dyslexia, children with preschool language difficulties and typically developing controls, recruited from about age 3½ in 2007–2009 from York and neighbouring regions of northern England by the University of York and followed to study the development of language, reading and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6767399/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this article, we use data from a longitudinal study of children at high risk of dyslexia from age 3½ to 8 years to trace the development of word‐level reading problems from an early stage in development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> "A longitudinal cohort of children at family risk of dyslexia, children with preschool language difficulties and typically developing controls, recruited from about age 3½ in 2007–2009 from York and neighbouring regions of northern England by the University of York and followed to study the development of language, reading and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30676649+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We followed children at family risk of dyslexia and children with preschool language difficulties from age 3½, comparing them with controls (N = 234).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> "A longitudinal cohort of children at family risk of dyslexia, children with preschool language difficulties and typically developing controls, recruited from about age 3½ in 2007–2009 from York and neighbouring regions of northern England by the University of York and followed to study the development of language, reading and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30676649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "York is a longitudinal cohort, in which reading- and language-related traits were assessed at multiple specific ages using various tools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000724> "A longitudinal cohort of children at family risk of dyslexia, children with preschool language difficulties and typically developing controls, recruited from about age 3½ in 2007–2009 from York and neighbouring regions of northern England by the University of York and followed to study the development of language, reading and dyslexia.")

