# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9687061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 2019 to February 2022, 200 pregnant women who attended the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Virgen de la Victoria de Málaga, after a positive 50 g oral glucose load, were included to participate in the project “Effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of the mother and the offspring during the first 1000 days.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38350951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10865541/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 32 (16 GDM, 16 non-GDM) pregnant women were selected from EPIDG cohort, which started in 2019 and is still recruiting participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38350951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10865541/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPIDG cohort has a total of 230 Mediterranean (South European) pregnant women who attended the Unit of Diabetes and Pregnancy at University Hospital Virgen de la Victoria, Málaga, Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11730480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, pregnant women, with a positive O’Sullivan test, attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy unit at Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria were recruited for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11730480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were drawn from the EPIDG cohort, comprising women with and without GDM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36421415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39408904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39806399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11730480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were selected based on their order of recruitment and whether they had attended both the postpartum visit (8–10 weeks after birth) and the one-year follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000728> "A prospective cohort of Mediterranean (southern European) pregnant women attending the Diabetes and Pregnancy Unit of Hospital Universitario Virgen de la Victoria in Málaga, Spain, after a positive glucose screening test, recruited from 2019 with and without gestational diabetes and followed with their offspring to one year after birth, to study the effect of gestational diabetes on the epigenome of mother and child during the first 1000 days.")

