AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38025163") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38025163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10630666/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the 6-year incidence of visual impairment (VI) and identify risk factors associated with VI in a multiethnic Asian population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000763> "A multiethnic population-based cohort of Malay, Indian and Chinese adults in Singapore, recruited at baseline through the Singapore Malay Eye Study (2004–2006), the Singapore Indian Eye Study (2007–2009) and the Singapore Chinese Eye Study (2009–2011) and re-examined about six years later (SEED-2), to study the incidence and risk factors of eye diseases and visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38025163") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38025163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10630666/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a multiethnic population-based cohort study using subjects recruited from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases (SEED) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000763> "A multiethnic population-based cohort of Malay, Indian and Chinese adults in Singapore, recruited at baseline through the Singapore Malay Eye Study (2004–2006), the Singapore Indian Eye Study (2007–2009) and the Singapore Chinese Eye Study (2009–2011) and re-examined about six years later (SEED-2), to study the incidence and risk factors of eye diseases and visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38025163") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5738399/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Disease (SEED) studies are population-based cohort studies, designed to evaluate the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of major eye disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000763> "A multiethnic population-based cohort of Malay, Indian and Chinese adults in Singapore, recruited at baseline through the Singapore Malay Eye Study (2004–2006), the Singapore Indian Eye Study (2007–2009) and the Singapore Chinese Eye Study (2009–2011) and re-examined about six years later (SEED-2), to study the incidence and risk factors of eye diseases and visual impairment.")

