# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8004670/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One hundred and seventy-eight patients with diagnosis of stages I–III NSCLC who completed the 3-month follow-up were selected from the RADIOGEN-Lung cohort (a study on the genomic influence in patients undergoing RT) that comprises 514 Galician individuals (northwest Spain).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8004670/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited at the Radiation Oncology Department of the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Spain, between March 2008 and May 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One hundred and ninety-three Galician individuals (NW Spain) integrate the RADIOGEN-head and neck cohort (Study on the genomic influence in patients undergoing RT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11887099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals were recruited into the RADIOGEN-Prostate study, initiated in 2005, which collects blood samples, dosimetry data, clinical information and toxicity data [7, 8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11887099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An epigenome-wide association study of post-RT toxicities was performed using the Illumina MethylationEPIC BeadChip, adjusting for age and cell type composition.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33810047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11887099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples for this study were obtained from prospective selected Galician prostate cancer patients who were treated at the Radiation Oncology Department of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago de Compostela (northwest Spain).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000791> "A Spanish cohort of cancer patients treated with radiotherapy at the Clinical University Hospital of Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, with prostate (RADIOGEN-Prostate, from 2005), lung (RADIOGEN-Lung, 2008–2015) and head and neck cancer sub-cohorts, collecting blood samples, dosimetry, clinical and toxicity data to identify genetic and epigenetic predictors of radiotherapy toxicity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22471860+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Religious Orders Study is a longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of aging and Alzheimer's disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3409291/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are without known dementia and agree to annual clinical evaluation and brain donation (some in the Chicago area also agree to donate, spinal cord, nerve, and muscle).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3409291/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Religious Orders Study enrolls Catholic nuns, priests and brothers, from more than 40 groups across the United States (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28322283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5608624/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants are required to sign an informed consent and an Anatomical Gift Act at enrollment, agreeing to donate their brains (ROS) or brains, spinal cords, and select nerves and muscles (MAP) to the study upon death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28322283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5608624/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects consisted of participants from two longitudinal cohort studies operated out of The Rush Alzheimer’s Disease Center in Chicago, the Religious Order Study (ROS) and the Rush Memory and Aging Project (MAP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29865057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6380522/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ROS started in 1994 and enrolls nuns priests and brothers from across the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000792> "A longitudinal clinical-pathologic cohort study of ageing and Alzheimer's disease run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1994 has enrolled older Catholic nuns, priests and brothers from across the United States who are free of dementia at enrolment and agree to annual clinical evaluations and brain donation at death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35012447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35012447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8744290/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAGE aggregated data containing common measures from three large scale studies in the substance abuse field: the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism (COGA), the Family Study of Cocaine Dependence (FSCD), and the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence (COGEND).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793> "A genome-wide association study dataset that aggregates common measures from three large substance-abuse studies, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism, the Family Study of Cocaine Dependence and the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence, funded as part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35012447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10503129/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Funding support for the Study of Addiction: Genetics and Environment (SAGE) was provided through the NIH Genes, Environment and Health Initiative [GEI] (U01 HG004422).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793> "A genome-wide association study dataset that aggregates common measures from three large substance-abuse studies, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism, the Family Study of Cocaine Dependence and the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence, funded as part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35012447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10503129/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAGE is one of the genome-wide association studies funded as part of the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) under GEI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793> "A genome-wide association study dataset that aggregates common measures from three large substance-abuse studies, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism, the Family Study of Cocaine Dependence and the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence, funded as part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35012447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37715138") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000092.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overarching goal is to identify novel genetic factors that contribute to addiction through a large-scale genome-wide association study of DSM-IV alcohol dependent (and frequently illicit drug dependent) cases and non-dependent, unrelated control subjects of European and African American descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000793> "A genome-wide association study dataset that aggregates common measures from three large substance-abuse studies, the Collaborative Study on the Genetics of Alcoholism, the Family Study of Cocaine Dependence and the Collaborative Genetic Study of Nicotine Dependence, funded as part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")

