AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood and urine samples were collected for biochemical analyses and further stored for future studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796> "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From a list of 16,069 names provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs, age-stratified random sampling was used to select 5,600 names (1,400 people from each decade of 40-49, 50-59, 60-69, and 70-79 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796> "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent standardized interview and assessment of blood pressure, anthropometry, presenting and best-corrected visual acuity, subjective refraction, ocular biometry, Goldmann tonometry, slit-lamp biomicroscopy, optic disc imaging, digital lens, and retinal photography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796> "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sampling frame consisted of all Malays aged 40-79 living in designated study areas in southwestern Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796> "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17365815") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17365815+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study provides population-based data on the prevalence of and risk factors for age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity in Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000796> "A population-based study of Malay adults aged 40–79 years living in south-western Singapore, selected by age-stratified random sampling and examined with standardised interviews, ocular and systemic assessments and stored blood and urine samples, to measure the prevalence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases in people of Malay ethnicity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19478234") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3159381/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information included sociodemographic characteristics; smoking habits; occupational, residential, and medical histories; and family history of cancer (questionnaire available online: http://www.creal.cat/fitxers/epicuro/epicuro%20questionnaires.htm).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer (the EPICURO study) that enrolled patients newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder in 1998–2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and individually matched hospital controls, to study environmental, occupational and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3372921/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, we reported on 1,991 individuals from the Spanish Bladder Cancer/EPICURO population-based case-control study in which we had performed a GWAS of adult-onset bladder cancer using DNA obtained from blood or buccal samples16.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer (the EPICURO study) that enrolled patients newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder in 1998–2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and individually matched hospital controls, to study environmental, occupational and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33517887") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7849104/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To increase statistical power, we included controls from the Spanish Bladder Cancer (SBC)/EPICURO study, carried out in the same geographical areas where PanGenEU study was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer (the EPICURO study) that enrolled patients newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder in 1998–2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and individually matched hospital controls, to study environmental, occupational and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Spanish study included cases newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder between 1998 and 2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and hospital controls individually matched to the cases on age at diagnosis/interview, sex, and hospital (706 White cases and 772 White controls with complete exposure information and genotyping data).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer (the EPICURO study) that enrolled patients newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder in 1998–2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and individually matched hospital controls, to study environmental, occupational and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35536285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9088962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed data from two large case–control studies—the New England Bladder Cancer Study (n/n=989 cases/1,162 controls), a population-based study, and the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study (n/n=706 cases/772 controls), a hospital-based study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000797> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer (the EPICURO study) that enrolled patients newly diagnosed with urothelial carcinoma of the bladder in 1998–2001 at 18 hospitals in five regions of Spain and individually matched hospital controls, to study environmental, occupational and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population encompassed 70 739 pregnancies from Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital of Shenzhen City (referred to as Longgang) and 50 948 pregnancies from Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital (referred to as Baoan).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We focus on identifying genes (1) associated with platelet count during pregnancy, (2) contributing to altering platelet counts, and (3) involved in GT development during pregnancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10904416/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we recruited 30,699 Chinese pregnant women who visited Shenzhen Baoan Women’s and Children’s Hospital (Shenzhen, China) for maternity check-ups and received an NIPT test in the first or second trimester between 2017 and 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12053562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These participants underwent NIPT with an average of 0.17x sequencing depth during the first or second trimester (mean gestational age: 16 weeks) between 2017 and 2021.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12053562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We incorporated NIPT data with glycemic traits and comprehensive laboratory and electronic medical records (Supplementary Data 1) to investigate the genetic architecture of GDM and the related glycemic traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12053562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 121,556 pregnancy participants from Shenzhen Baoan Women’s and Children’s Hospital (referred to as Baoan) and Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital of Shenzhen City (referred to as Longgang).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000798> "A hospital-based cohort of more than 100,000 Chinese pregnant women who had non-invasive prenatal testing at Longgang District Maternity and Child Healthcare Hospital and Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose low-depth NIPT sequencing data are linked to laboratory and electronic medical records to study the genetics of pregnancy traits and complications.")

