AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A range of health-related data have been collected as well as measures concerning child development, cognitive ability and educational attainment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, the MCS data have been linked to administrative data resources including health records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MCS is nationally representative and 18 552 families (18 827 children) were recruited to the cohort in the first sweep.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Millennium Cohort Study (MCS) is an observational, multidisciplinary cohort study that was set up to follow the lives of children born at the turn of the new century.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data also include a wealth of information describing the social, economic and demographic characteristics of the cohort members and their families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24550246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24550246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There have currently been five main sweeps of data collection, at ages 9 months and 3, 5, 7 and 11 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000801> "A nationally representative UK observational cohort of 18,827 children from 18,552 families, born at the turn of the century, followed through repeated sweeps of data collection from age 9 months onwards on health, development, cognitive ability, education and social and economic circumstances, with linkage to administrative health records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000802> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000802>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, radiation-induced toxicity and patient-rated outcome measures (PROM) were prospectively assessed weekly during RT and after completion of RT course, up to 6 weeks for acute toxicity, and at 6, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48 and 60 month for late toxicity (3).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000802> "A prospective cohort of patients with head and neck cancer treated with primary or postoperative radiotherapy, with or without chemotherapy, from 2007 to 2020 at the Department of Radiation Oncology of the University Medical Center Groningen, all enrolled in the UMCG head and neck cancer prospective data registration programme (NCT02435576), with prospective assessment of radiation-induced toxicity and patient-rated outcome measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients were included in the UMCG-HNC prospective data registration program (NCT02435576, clinicaltrials.gov) in which baseline patient-, tumour-, and treatment-characteristics were determined before starting the RT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000802> "A prospective cohort of patients with head and neck cancer treated with primary or postoperative radiotherapy, with or without chemotherapy, from 2007 to 2020 at the Department of Radiation Oncology of the University Medical Center Groningen, all enrolled in the UMCG head and neck cancer prospective data registration programme (NCT02435576), with prospective assessment of radiation-induced toxicity and patient-rated outcome measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36191651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0167814022044863-mmc1.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "University Medical Center Groningen Head and Neck cancer Study (UMCG-HANS) cohort consisted of 1,429 HNC patients treated with primary or postoperative RT either or not combined with chemotherapy (CH-RT) from 2007 to 2020 at the department of Radiation Oncology of the UMCG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000802> "A prospective cohort of patients with head and neck cancer treated with primary or postoperative radiotherapy, with or without chemotherapy, from 2007 to 2020 at the Department of Radiation Oncology of the University Medical Center Groningen, all enrolled in the UMCG head and neck cancer prospective data registration programme (NCT02435576), with prospective assessment of radiation-induced toxicity and patient-rated outcome measures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3365264/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AD cases (mean age-at-onset (AAO) 72.6±6.4 years; 65.6% women; 23.5% autopsy-confirmed) were derived from the University of Pittsburgh ADRC, all of whom met the National Institute of Neurological and Communication Disorders and Stroke (NINCDS)/Alzheimer's Disease and Related Disorders Association (ADRDA) criteria for probable or definite AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803> "A cohort of Alzheimer disease patients, about a quarter of them autopsy-confirmed, and cognitively normal controls from the same area, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer's Disease Research Center in Pittsburgh, United States, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3365264/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were cognitively normal subjects that were recruited from the same geographical area as the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803> "A cohort of Alzheimer disease patients, about a quarter of them autopsy-confirmed, and cognitively normal controls from the same area, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer's Disease Research Center in Pittsburgh, United States, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3365264/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we used 2229 samples from the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer's Disease Research Center (ADRC) that were genotyped using the Illumina Omni1-Quad chip to examine the extent of associations of the recently implicated nine non-APOE risk loci for LOAD in this sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803> "A cohort of Alzheimer disease patients, about a quarter of them autopsy-confirmed, and cognitively normal controls from the same area, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer's Disease Research Center in Pittsburgh, United States, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22832961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were evaluated at the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer Disease Research Center (PITT ADRC), Pittsburgh, PA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000803> "A cohort of Alzheimer disease patients, about a quarter of them autopsy-confirmed, and cognitively normal controls from the same area, recruited by the University of Pittsburgh Alzheimer's Disease Research Center in Pittsburgh, United States, and genotyped for genome-wide association studies of late-onset Alzheimer disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4866875/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All 335 participants completed required elements of the protocol, including fasting blood work, physical examination/frailty assessment, questionnaires, neuropsychological assessment, brain MRI, cardiac MRI, and echocardiogram.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> "A case-control longitudinal study of vascular health and brain aging launched in 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, USA, which enrolled 335 adults aged 60–92 with mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition from 2012 to 2014 for repeated clinical, cardiac, brain imaging and CSF assessments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4866875/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From September 2012 to November 2014, 335 participants age 60–92 were enrolled, including 168 individuals with mild cognitive impairment (MCI, 73 ± 8 years, 41% female) and 167 age-, sex-, and race-matched cognitively normal controls (NC, 72 ± 7 years, 41% female).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> "A case-control longitudinal study of vascular health and brain aging launched in 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, USA, which enrolled 335 adults aged 60–92 with mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition from 2012 to 2014 for repeated clinical, cardiac, brain imaging and CSF assessments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4866875/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Longitudinal follow-up of the cohort is underway with procedures repeating at 18-month intervals for a minimum of 3 years (i.e., baseline, 18-month follow-up, and 36-month follow-up).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> "A case-control longitudinal study of vascular health and brain aging launched in 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, USA, which enrolled 335 adults aged 60–92 with mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition from 2012 to 2014 for repeated clinical, cardiac, brain imaging and CSF assessments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4866875/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Such detailed vascular phenotyping is coupled with a serum, plasma, and CSF biosample repository and neuropsychological assessment and multimodal brain MRI acquisition at repeat time points.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> "A case-control longitudinal study of vascular health and brain aging launched in 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, USA, which enrolled 335 adults aged 60–92 with mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition from 2012 to 2014 for repeated clinical, cardiac, brain imaging and CSF assessments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26967211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4866875/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vanderbilt Memory & Aging Project is a case-control longitudinal study investigating vascular health and brain aging launched in September 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, TN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000804> "A case-control longitudinal study of vascular health and brain aging launched in 2012 at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, USA, which enrolled 335 adults aged 60–92 with mild cognitive impairment or normal cognition from 2012 to 2014 for repeated clinical, cardiac, brain imaging and CSF assessments.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000805> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000805>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32776978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32776978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7416942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, the study recruited 720 adolescents and adults with SCD at 10 clinical centers in the United States (U.S.) and United Kingdom (UK) between 2007–2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000805> "A cohort of patients with sickle cell disease enrolled at ten centres in the United States and the United Kingdom and screened by echocardiography and laboratory tests for pulmonary hypertension to assess eligibility for a randomised clinical trial of sildenafil.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32776978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32776978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7416942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Walk-PHaSST study was designed to assemble a large cohort of patients with SCD and to screen their eligibility for a randomized clinical trial of sildenafil via echocardiographic and laboratory screening for pulmonary hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000805> "A cohort of patients with sickle cell disease enrolled at ten centres in the United States and the United Kingdom and screened by echocardiography and laboratory tests for pulmonary hypertension to assess eligibility for a randomised clinical trial of sildenafil.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During 1980–1982, 996 individuals were examined with subsequent examinations made on the cohort at 4 (1984–1986), 10 (1990–1992), 14 (1995–1996), 20 (2000–2001), and 25 (2005–2007) years after the baseline examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, 10,135 patients with diabetes who were receiving primary care in an 11-county area in southern Wisconsin during 1979–1980 were classified as “older” and “younger” onset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conclusion, this U.S. population-based report showed a lower prevalence and incidence of ESRD among those more recently diagnosed, explained by improvements in glycemic and blood pressure control over the last several decades.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898749/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the population-based Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR) cohort, we sought to examine whether a decline in the prevalence and incidence of end-stage renal disease (ESRD) was evident with increasing calendar year of type 1 diabetes diagnosis among people followed for 25 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9422925") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1722309") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Dia- betic Retinopathy (WESDR) is a population based study of the prevalence and incidence of diabetic retinopathy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24026564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2761813/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this report, we extend our previous observations by describing the 25-year progression and regression of DR, the incidence of proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR), and changes in the prevalence of PDR in a large cohort of persons with type 1 diabetes mellitus participating in the Wisconsin Epidemiologic Study of Diabetic Retinopathy (WESDR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000806> "A population-based cohort of people with diabetes receiving primary care in an 11-county area of southern Wisconsin, United States, in 1979–1980, followed for decades to study the incidence and progression of diabetic retinopathy and other diabetes complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000807> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000807>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10727334/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established through several recruitment waves, participants were first recruited in 1992 from a random sample of Medicare‐eligible adults (aged ≥65 years) residing in the neighborhoods of Washington Heights and Inwood in northern Manhattan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000807> "A prospective, population-based study of aging and dementia in Medicare-eligible adults aged 65 and over living in the Washington Heights and Inwood neighborhoods of northern Manhattan, New York, first recruited in 1992 by random sampling and extended in later recruitment waves.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10727334/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHICAP (Washington Heights–Inwood Columbia Aging Project) study is a prospective, population‐based study of aging and dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000807> "A prospective, population-based study of aging and dementia in Medicare-eligible adults aged 65 and over living in the Washington Heights and Inwood neighborhoods of northern Manhattan, New York, first recruited in 1992 by random sampling and extended in later recruitment waves.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3173859/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These included all HapMap Phase I and II samples, along with further samples from the same four populations: individuals from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collected in Utah, USA, with ancestry from northern and western Europe (CEU); Han Chinese in Beijing, China (CHB); Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (JPT); and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Han Chinese individuals in Beijing, China, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3173859/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This expanded public resource of genome variants in global populations supports deeper interrogation of genomic variation and its role in human disease, and serves as a step towards a high-resolution map of the landscape of human genetic variation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Han Chinese individuals in Beijing, China, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33575800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8248963") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These LCLs were derived from 178 individuals from the Yoruba population in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI), 178 individuals with European ancestries from Utah, USA (CEU), and 90 individuals from a combined pop- ulation of Han Chinese from Beijing, China, and Japanese from Tokyo, Japan (ASN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Han Chinese individuals in Beijing, China, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3042601/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4.9 Tb of DNA sequence was generated in nine sequencing centres using three sequencing technologies, from DNA obtained from immortalised lymphoblastoid cell lines") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000808> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Han Chinese individuals in Beijing, China, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3173859/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These included all HapMap Phase I and II samples, along with further samples from the same four populations: individuals from the Centre d’Etude du Polymorphisme Humain collected in Utah, USA, with ancestry from northern and western Europe (CEU); Han Chinese in Beijing, China (CHB); Japanese in Tokyo, Japan (JPT); and Yoruba in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Japanese individuals in Tokyo, Japan, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3173859/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This expanded public resource of genome variants in global populations supports deeper interrogation of genomic variation and its role in human disease, and serves as a step towards a high-resolution map of the landscape of human genetic variation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Japanese individuals in Tokyo, Japan, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33575800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8248963") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These LCLs were derived from 178 individuals from the Yoruba population in Ibadan, Nigeria (YRI), 178 individuals with European ancestries from Utah, USA (CEU), and 90 individuals from a combined pop- ulation of Han Chinese from Beijing, China, and Japanese from Tokyo, Japan (ASN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Japanese individuals in Tokyo, Japan, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3042601/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4.9 Tb of DNA sequence was generated in nine sequencing centres using three sequencing technologies, from DNA obtained from immortalised lymphoblastoid cell lines") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000809> "A collection of DNA samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines from Japanese individuals in Tokyo, Japan, that forms one of the four founding population samples of the International HapMap Project and is used as a reference for human genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3439198/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Older persons without known dementia must agree to an assessment of risk factors, blood donation, and a detailed clinical evaluation each year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22471867+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Memory and Aging Project is a longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of aging with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3439198/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants are primarily recruited from retirement communities throughout northeastern Illinois") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3439198/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study design is similar to the Religious Orders Study in that it enrolls persons without dementia who agree to annual clinical evaluation and organ donation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28322283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5608624/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ROS and MAP studies are maintained and the data are collected by a single group of researchers at the Rush Alzheimer’s Disease Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22471867") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6380522/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAP started in 1997 and enrolls lay persons from across northeastern Illinois.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000810> "A longitudinal, epidemiologic clinical-pathologic cohort study of common chronic conditions of ageing run by the Rush Alzheimer's Disease Center, which since 1997 has enrolled older lay persons without dementia, mainly from retirement communities across northeastern Illinois, who agree to annual clinical evaluations and organ donation, with an emphasis on decline in cognitive and motor function and risk of Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9005349/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This research was carried out under the auspices of the Social Science Genetic Association Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> "A consortium founded in 2011 of medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genome-wide association studies of social-science outcomes such as educational attainment across more than 100 contributing cohorts and promotes harmonised phenotype measurement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4500051/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Social Science Genetic Association Consortium (SSGAC) reported on a 126,559 person GWAS that detected three genome-wide significant SNPs associated with completion of college (rs11584700 and rs4851266) and years of schooling (rs9320913).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> "A consortium founded in 2011 of medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genome-wide association studies of social-science outcomes such as educational attainment across more than 100 contributing cohorts and promotes harmonised phenotype measurement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SSGAC also promotes the collection of harmonized and well-measured phenotypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> "A consortium founded in 2011 of medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genome-wide association studies of social-science outcomes such as educational attainment across more than 100 contributing cohorts and promotes harmonised phenotype measurement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SSGAC is a cooperative enterprise among medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genetic association studies for social science outcomes and provides a platform for interdisciplinary collaboration and cross-fertilization of ideas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> "A consortium founded in 2011 of medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genome-wide association studies of social-science outcomes such as educational attainment across more than 100 contributing cohorts and promotes harmonised phenotype measurement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.thessgac.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The consortium in numbers 29 publications 47 phenotypes in the PGI Repository 11 datasets in the PGI Repository 100+ contributing cohorts") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000811> "A consortium founded in 2011 of medical researchers and social scientists that coordinates genome-wide association studies of social-science outcomes such as educational attainment across more than 100 contributing cohorts and promotes harmonised phenotype measurement.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Examination included measurements of traditional vascular risk factors (blood pressure, glycaemia, lipids, etc.), cognitive functions, and subclinical vascular diseases using carotid ultrasound and cerebral magnetic resonance imaging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> "A population-based longitudinal study of adults aged 65 and over recruited in three French cities, Bordeaux, Dijon and Montpellier, and followed from 1999 to 2012 with repeated examinations of vascular risk factors, cognition and subclinical vascular disease to study the relation between vascular diseases and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent regular extensive examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> "A population-based longitudinal study of adults aged 65 and over recruited in three French cities, Bordeaux, Dijon and Montpellier, and followed from 1999 to 2012 with repeated examinations of vascular risk factors, cognition and subclinical vascular disease to study the relation between vascular diseases and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from three French cities: Bordeaux (South-West), Dijon (North-East) and Montpellier (South-East).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> "A population-based longitudinal study of adults aged 65 and over recruited in three French cities, Bordeaux, Dijon and Montpellier, and followed from 1999 to 2012 with repeated examinations of vascular risk factors, cognition and subclinical vascular disease to study the relation between vascular diseases and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3C Study extended from 1999 to 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> "A population-based longitudinal study of adults aged 65 and over recruited in three French cities, Bordeaux, Dijon and Montpellier, and followed from 1999 to 2012 with repeated examinations of vascular risk factors, cognition and subclinical vascular disease to study the relation between vascular diseases and dementia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Three-City Study (3C Study) is a population-based longitudinal study of the relation between vascular diseases and dementia in persons aged 65 years and older") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000812> "A population-based longitudinal study of adults aged 65 and over recruited in three French cities, Bordeaux, Dijon and Montpellier, and followed from 1999 to 2012 with repeated examinations of vascular risk factors, cognition and subclinical vascular disease to study the relation between vascular diseases and dementia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2585099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age- and sex-matched controls were recruited at two regional Health Examination Centres; all were ≥ 40 years old and had no family history of colorectal cancer or polyps.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813> "A case-control study of sporadic colorectal cancer in the Pays de la Loire region of France, which recruited about 1,000 patients diagnosed at age 40 or over in regional hospitals and clinics and about 1,100 age- and sex-matched controls at regional health examination centres in 2002–2006, to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2585099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From December 2002 to March 2006, two groups of 1023 patients (632 males and 391 females; mean ± SD age at diagnosis 65.7 ± 10.1 years) and 1121 controls (609 males and 512 females; mean ± SD age at inclusion 61.9 ± 10. years), all of Caucasian origin, were recruited within the Pays de la Loire region of France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813> "A case-control study of sporadic colorectal cancer in the Pays de la Loire region of France, which recruited about 1,000 patients diagnosed at age 40 or over in regional hospitals and clinics and about 1,100 age- and sex-matched controls at regional health examination centres in 2002–2006, to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2585099/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In short, all cases were patients recruited in regional hospitals and clinics, with a personal history of colorectal cancer diagnosed at an age of ≥ 40 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813> "A case-control study of sporadic colorectal cancer in the Pays de la Loire region of France, which recruited about 1,000 patients diagnosed at age 40 or over in regional hospitals and clinics and about 1,100 age- and sex-matched controls at regional health examination centres in 2002–2006, to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18992148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18992148+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through a large genetic association study based on 1023 patients with sporadic CRC and 1121 controls, we tested a panel of these low-penetrance alleles to find out whether they could determine \"genotypic profiles\" at risk for CRC among individuals of the French population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000813> "A case-control study of sporadic colorectal cancer in the Pays de la Loire region of France, which recruited about 1,000 patients diagnosed at age 40 or over in regional hospitals and clinics and about 1,100 age- and sex-matched controls at regional health examination centres in 2002–2006, to study genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000814> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000814>)

