AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10984493/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We identified 115 pathology‐confirmed cases of rpAD in NPDPSC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000838> "A set of about 115 autopsied people referred with rapidly progressive dementia resembling prion disease to the National Prion Disease Pathology Surveillance Center at Case Western Reserve University between 2009 and 2017, in whom neuropathology, prion protein typing, PRNP sequencing and record review excluded prion disease and confirmed Alzheimer's disease, whole-genome sequenced from frozen brain tissue for genetic studies of rapidly progressive Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10984493/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole genome sequencing (WGS) was performed on the Illumina platform, using the Isaac alignment 37 and Strelka variant caller for single nucleotide variants and small indels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000838> "A set of about 115 autopsied people referred with rapidly progressive dementia resembling prion disease to the National Prion Disease Pathology Surveillance Center at Case Western Reserve University between 2009 and 2017, in whom neuropathology, prion protein typing, PRNP sequencing and record review excluded prion disease and confirmed Alzheimer's disease, whole-genome sequenced from frozen brain tissue for genetic studies of rapidly progressive Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38184787") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10984493/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "all cases were referred with rapidly progressive dementia resembling prion disease; neuropathology examinations, immunohistochemistry, molecular typing of the PrPSc protein, sequencing of the prion protein gene (PRNP), and medical records review to rule out sporadic and familial prion diseases") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000838> "A set of about 115 autopsied people referred with rapidly progressive dementia resembling prion disease to the National Prion Disease Pathology Surveillance Center at Case Western Reserve University between 2009 and 2017, in whom neuropathology, prion protein typing, PRNP sequencing and record review excluded prion disease and confirmed Alzheimer's disease, whole-genome sequenced from frozen brain tissue for genetic studies of rapidly progressive Alzheimer's disease.")

