AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4923737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "769 consecutive patients, with mean disease duration of 1.3 years, were assessed using a broad range of motor, cognitive and non-motor metrics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4923737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Full details of this cohort are described elsewhere, [5] with participants being recruited between September 2010 and September 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4923737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Future evaluation will determine whether patients retain their initial clinical phenotype or whether changing from one clinical phenotype to another is an important marker of subsequent progression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4923737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PD patients diagnosed within the past 3.5 years were prospectively recruited as part of the Oxford Parkinson’s Disease Centre (OPDC) cohort study from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley covering a population of approximately 2.1 million (PD-Discovery, website: http://opdc.medsci.ox.ac.uk).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4923737/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Use a data-driven approach to unravel any heterogeneity in the Parkinson’s phenotype in a well-characterised, population-based incidence cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26405788") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11161485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Oxford Discovery is a prospective, longitudinal study led by the Oxford Parkinson Disease Centre52.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000840> "A population-based incidence cohort of people diagnosed with Parkinson's disease within the previous 3.5 years, recruited by the Oxford Parkinson's Disease Centre from 11 hospitals across the Thames Valley, England, between 2010 and 2014, and followed with motor, cognitive and non-motor assessments to study Parkinson's disease progression and subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3210694/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnostic interview and blood/buccal samples were obtained from sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> "A family sample of sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry, with diagnostic interviews and blood or buccal DNA, members of which were genotyped genome-wide to study genetic contributions to alcohol use and dependence and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3210694/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomewide SNP genotyping was performed with 8754 individuals [2062 alcohol dependent cases] selected for informativeness for alcohol use disorder and associated quantitative traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> "A family sample of sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry, with diagnostic interviews and blood or buccal DNA, members of which were genotyped genome-wide to study genetic contributions to alcohol use and dependence and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3210694/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given moderately strong genetic contributions to variation in alcoholism and heaviness of drinking (50–60% heritability), with high correlation of genetic influences, we have conducted a quantitative trait genomewide association study for phenotypes related to alcohol use and dependence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> "A family sample of sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry, with diagnostic interviews and blood or buccal DNA, members of which were genotyped genome-wide to study genetic contributions to alcohol use and dependence and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3210694/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Index cases from these families, their full siblings and parents were recruited for three coordinated studies: (i) the NAG (Nicotine Addiction Genetics) Study (28) which ascertained heavy smoking index cases;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> "A family sample of sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry, with diagnostic interviews and blood or buccal DNA, members of which were genotyped genome-wide to study genetic contributions to alcohol use and dependence and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21529783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001299.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The telephone diagnostic interview assessed DSM-IV and modified DSM-IIIR diagnoses (i.e., without time clustering) for nicotine dependence, alcohol and other drug dependence and abuse, major depression, and childhood conduct disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000841> "A family sample of sibships ascertained through the Australian Twin Registry, with diagnostic interviews and blood or buccal DNA, members of which were genotyped genome-wide to study genetic contributions to alcohol use and dependence and nicotine dependence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A web-based Data Management Resource facilitates rapid sharing of data and biosamples across the research community for additional biomarker projects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established November 2012, the PDBP seeks to identify biomarkers to improve therapeutic development in PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PDBP is building a resource of longitudinally collected data and biosamples from well-characterized patients with PD of different stages and duration, parkinsonism, and control participants, and includes hypothesis-driven biomarker discovery projects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PDBP has enrolled 1082 individuals, including 620 with PD, 101 with parkinsonism (46 PSP, 36 MSA, 19 parkinsonism with currently undetermined diagnosis), 23 with essential tremor, and 338 controls (72% of planned enrollment) as of 10/21/2014 (enrollment ends 8/31/2015).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Parkinson Disease Biomarkers Program (PDBP) is a consortium of laboratory and clinical biomarker discovery projects funded by the National Institute of Neurological Diseases and Stroke (NINDS, National Institutes of Health (NIH), United States).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26442452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4824671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There are standardized operating procedures for biospecimen collection and clinical assessments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000842> "A longitudinal multi-project collection of clinical data and biosamples from people with Parkinson's disease at different stages, other parkinsonism, essential tremor and controls, established in 2012 by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke as a consortium of biomarker discovery projects with standardized procedures and a shared data management resource.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A subset of carriers of NOTCH3 p.Arg1231Cys were contacted by the Center of Non-Communicable Diseases in Karachi Pakistan under protocols approved by the IRB committee of the Center for Non-Communicable Diseases (NIH registered IRB 00007048).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> "A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan with about 250,000 participants from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023 across some 50 phenotypes, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PGR is a growing biobank that aims to enroll 1 million participants across Pakistan and as of September 2023, ~250,000 participants across n = 48 clinical sites in n = 17 cities from all over Pakistan have been enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> "A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan with about 250,000 participants from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023 across some 50 phenotypes, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PGR is a national consortium of several case-control studies focused on 50 distinct phenotypes, including:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> "A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan with about 250,000 participants from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023 across some 50 phenotypes, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PGR 75 K individuals were recruited and consented in Pakistan for whole exome sequencing (WES) (n = 75,819), including a stroke case:control discovery cohort of 31 K") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> "A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan with about 250,000 participants from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023 across some 50 phenotypes, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11399414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of this study was to identify protein coding deleterious missense or loss-of-function (LoF) variants associated with stroke phenotypes in the Pakistani population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000843> "A growing biobank and national consortium of case–control studies in Pakistan with about 250,000 participants from 48 clinical sites in 17 cities by September 2023 across some 50 phenotypes, with whole-exome sequencing and recontact, used for genetic association and loss-of-function studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4480925/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Treatment-seeking smokers (1246: 662 slow metabolizers; 584 normal metabolizers) were randomized to 11-weeks of nicotine patch (active patch + placebo pill), varenicline (active pill + placebo patch), or placebo (placebo pill + patch), plus behavioral counseling; an intent-to-treat analysis was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844> "A multicentre, randomised, placebo-controlled smoking-cessation trial (NCT01314001) run from 2010 to 2014 at four academic medical centres in the United States and Canada, in which 1246 treatment-seeking smokers stratified by nicotine metabolite ratio were assigned to placebo, nicotine patch or varenicline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4480925/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted the clinical trial at four academic medical centers (University of Pennsylvania (UPenn), Centre for Addiction and Mental Health/University of Toronto, State University of New York at Buffalo, and MD Anderson Cancer Center); assessment of the NMR was performed at the University of Toronto.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844> "A multicentre, randomised, placebo-controlled smoking-cessation trial (NCT01314001) run from 2010 to 2014 at four academic medical centres in the United States and Canada, in which 1246 treatment-seeking smokers stratified by nicotine metabolite ratio were assigned to placebo, nicotine patch or varenicline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25588294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25588294+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1246 participants (662 slow metabolisers of nicotine, 584 normal metabolisers of nicotine) were enrolled and randomly assigned to the three interventions (408 placebo, 418 nicotine patch, 420 varenicline).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000844> "A multicentre, randomised, placebo-controlled smoking-cessation trial (NCT01314001) run from 2010 to 2014 at four academic medical centres in the United States and Canada, in which 1246 treatment-seeking smokers stratified by nicotine metabolite ratio were assigned to placebo, nicotine patch or varenicline.")
