# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37286573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals were recruited at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau of Barcelona (Spain) between 2012 and 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845> "A Spanish case-control study of venous thromboembolism, based at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, whose cases had a first venous thromboembolism and were sampled after 6–12 months of anticoagulant treatment, with healthy controls recruited from the general population, used to study genetic and plasma determinants of venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37286573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Spanish RETROVE study recruited cases from patients who had a prior first time VTE, sampled post-treatment (6–12 months anticoagulants), with healthy controls recruited from the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845> "A Spanish case-control study of venous thromboembolism, based at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, whose cases had a first venous thromboembolism and were sampled after 6–12 months of anticoagulant treatment, with healthy controls recruited from the general population, used to study genetic and plasma determinants of venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37286573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Riesgo de Enfermedad TROmboembólica VEnosa (RETROVE) study is a prospective case–control study of 400 consecutive patients with VTE (cancer associated thrombosis excluded) and 400 healthy control volunteers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845> "A Spanish case-control study of venous thromboembolism, based at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, whose cases had a first venous thromboembolism and were sampled after 6–12 months of anticoagulant treatment, with healthy controls recruited from the general population, used to study genetic and plasma determinants of venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37286573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10247781/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To explore if CFHR5 concentration in plasma was influenced by genetic variants, we first performed a meta-analysis of GWAS for dual binder assay based CFHR5 concentrations in individuals from the FARIVE (n = 1033), RETROVE (n = 668) and MARTHA (n = 1266) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000845> "A Spanish case-control study of venous thromboembolism, based at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, whose cases had a first venous thromboembolism and were sampled after 6–12 months of anticoagulant treatment, with healthy controls recruited from the general population, used to study genetic and plasma determinants of venous thromboembolism.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of these, 600 patients completed follow-up in September 2006 (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed and internally validated a clinical decision rule that may ultimately provide clinicians with guidance as to whether oral anticoagulation therapy can be discontinued after 5–7 months of treatment for an “unprovoked” venous thromboembolism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included patients whose first, objectively proven unprovoked thromboembolism (proximal deep vein thrombosis, or segmental or greater pulmonary embolism) occurred 5–7 months before enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a prospective clinical decision-rule derivation cohort study and a split-sample validation study that included consecutive unselected patients from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed an assessment 5–7 months after the index venous thromboembolism event while patients were receiving oral anticoagulant therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13240746/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18725614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2518177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We sought to determine clinical predictors to identify patients who are at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism who could safely discontinue oral anticoagulants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000846> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients with a first unprovoked major venous thromboembolism, enrolled from 12 tertiary care centres in 4 countries while on oral anticoagulation 5–7 months after the event and followed after stopping anticoagulation (to September 2006), to derive a clinical decision rule identifying patients at low risk of recurrent venous thromboembolism.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35470676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After the baseline visit (visit 1 [V1]), 1705 subjects were reassessed 20 years later on their last visit (visit 4 [V4]).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> "A single-centre longitudinal family cohort of 4,295 people from 1,006 families of the Lorraine region, recruited in 1993–1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, and re-examined over about 20 years, to study the familial and genetic determinants of cardiovascular and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35470676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, our aim was to (1) assess the heritability of SUA levels, (2) assess the relationship between SNPs (GWAS) and SUA levels, and (3) investigate the association between SNPs most associated with SUA and metabolic outcomes and target organ damage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> "A single-centre longitudinal family cohort of 4,295 people from 1,006 families of the Lorraine region, recruited in 1993–1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, and re-examined over about 20 years, to study the familial and genetic determinants of cardiovascular and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35470676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The STANISLAS study cohort is a single‐center longitudinal cohort recruited between 1993 and 1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, composed of 1006 families with 4295 subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> "A single-centre longitudinal family cohort of 4,295 people from 1,006 families of the Lorraine region, recruited in 1993–1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, and re-examined over about 20 years, to study the familial and genetic determinants of cardiovascular and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9594084") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9594084+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main objective of the Stanislas cohort is to study the role and the contribution of genetic and environmental factors to cardiovascular status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> "A single-centre longitudinal family cohort of 4,295 people from 1,006 families of the Lorraine region, recruited in 1993–1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, and re-examined over about 20 years, to study the familial and genetic determinants of cardiovascular and metabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9238600/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9594084") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9594084+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The principal variables studied are: a) blood pressure, cardiac mass, and wall thickness of carotid and femoral arteries, b) obesity and fat mass, c) indicators of lipid metabolism") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000847> "A single-centre longitudinal family cohort of 4,295 people from 1,006 families of the Lorraine region, recruited in 1993–1995 at the Center for Preventive Medicine in Nancy, France, and re-examined over about 20 years, to study the familial and genetic determinants of cardiovascular and metabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11904716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SHS cohort has completed 3 clinical examinations (phase I, 1989-1991; phase II, 1993-1995; and phase III, 1998-1999) and has collected comprehensive data on clinical, lifestyle, and physical measures") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848> "A cohort of 4,549 self-identified American Indian adults aged 45 years or older, recruited in 1989–1991 from tribal communities in Arizona, Oklahoma, North Dakota and South Dakota, United States, and followed through repeated examinations to estimate cardiovascular disease rates and risk factors in American Indians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11904716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Strong Heart Study (SHS) is a large American Indian cohort recruited from 1989 to 1991, with ongoing follow-up (phase VII).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848> "A cohort of 4,549 self-identified American Indian adults aged 45 years or older, recruited in 1989–1991 from tribal communities in Arizona, Oklahoma, North Dakota and South Dakota, United States, and followed through repeated examinations to estimate cardiovascular disease rates and risk factors in American Indians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11904716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This genetic association study used data from the SHS, a large, well-characterized cohort of 4549 self-identified American Indian adults aged 45 years or older, who were recruited from tribal communities in Arizona, Oklahoma, North Dakota, and South Dakota (1989-1991).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848> "A cohort of 4,549 self-identified American Indian adults aged 45 years or older, recruited in 1989–1991 from tribal communities in Arizona, Oklahoma, North Dakota and South Dakota, United States, and followed through repeated examinations to estimate cardiovascular disease rates and risk factors in American Indians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40072435") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/research/atherosclerosis") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Strong Heart Study (SHS) is the largest and longest running epidemiologic study of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors among American Indians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000848> "A cohort of 4,549 self-identified American Indian adults aged 45 years or older, recruited in 1989–1991 from tribal communities in Arizona, Oklahoma, North Dakota and South Dakota, United States, and followed through repeated examinations to estimate cardiovascular disease rates and risk factors in American Indians.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4873985/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutive recruitment of 1200 white patients of European ancestry from the same geographical region who presented with stroke to St George’s Hospital was carried out over the period October 2003 to July 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> "A stroke study in which black stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, and white stroke patients were recruited at St George’s Hospital from October 2003 to July 2009, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4873985/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment occurred between 1999 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> "A stroke study in which black stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, and white stroke patients were recruited at St George’s Hospital from October 2003 to July 2009, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4873985/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLESS is a prospective study that recruited 1200 consecutive black patients with stroke from a contiguous geographical area in South London in the UK, covered by three acute hospitals (Guy’s and St Thomas’ Hospitals, King’s College Hospital, and St George’s Hospital).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> "A stroke study in which black stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, and white stroke patients were recruited at St George’s Hospital from October 2003 to July 2009, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5354108/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment of controls was by random selection from general practice lists in the catchment areas of St George's, Guys and St Thomas, and King's College Hospital NHS Trusts between 1999 and 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> "A stroke study in which black stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, and white stroke patients were recruited at St George’s Hospital from October 2003 to July 2009, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27197724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28349126") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5354108/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We undertook genome-wide analyses of stroke and stroke subtypes in a population of black African and black African Caribbean individuals from London, United Kingdom, to identify genetic risk factors associated with stroke in this minority population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000849> "A stroke study in which black stroke patients were prospectively recruited between 1999 and 2010 from three hospitals covering a contiguous area of South London, United Kingdom, and white stroke patients were recruited at St George’s Hospital from October 2003 to July 2009, with black African and African Caribbean community controls from general practice lists in the same catchment area (1999–2012), to study stroke subtypes and the genetic and other risk factors for stroke in African and African Caribbean people.")

