AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15133743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1182086/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLIC study scanned 473 individuals from 98 nuclear families ascertained through epidemiological and clinical-based studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000850> "A collection of nuclear families, each ascertained through a proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the age norm, gathered by the SLI Consortium from five clinical and epidemiological sites across the United Kingdom for linkage and association studies of specific language impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15133743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1182086/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have reported elsewhere a full-genome scan in 98 nuclear families affected by this disorder, with the use of three quantitative traits of language ability") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000850> "A collection of nuclear families, each ascertained through a proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the age norm, gathered by the SLI Consortium from five clinical and epidemiological sites across the United Kingdom for linkage and association studies of specific language impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2725236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SLIC families were all selected on the basis of a single proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the normative mean for his or her age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000850> "A collection of nuclear families, each ascertained through a proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the age norm, gathered by the SLI Consortium from five clinical and epidemiological sites across the United Kingdom for linkage and association studies of specific language impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2725236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The association screen utilized 806 individuals from 211 families ascertained by the SLI Consortium (SLIC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000850> "A collection of nuclear families, each ascertained through a proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the age norm, gathered by the SLI Consortium from five clinical and epidemiological sites across the United Kingdom for linkage and association studies of specific language impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19646677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2725236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This nuclear-family cohort was collected from five sites across the UK (The Newcomen Centre at Guy's Hospital, London; the Cambridge Language and Speech Project (CLASP)13; the Child Life and Health Department at the University of Edinburgh14; the Department of Child Health at the University of Aberdeen; and the Manchester Language Study15,16)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000850> "A collection of nuclear families, each ascertained through a proband with receptive and/or expressive language skills more than 1.5 SD below the age norm, gathered by the SLI Consortium from five clinical and epidemiological sites across the United Kingdom for linkage and association studies of specific language impairment.")

