# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the starting point of the I.Family study, another follow-up examination (T3) was conducted in 2013-2014, when the age range of index children, i.e. of children who had already participated at T0 or T1, was between 5 and 17 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> "A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline examination (T0) between September 2007 and June 2008 included 16 228 children aged 2 to 9.9 years from eight European countries: Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> "A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The longitudinal perspective of the IDEFICS cohort allows identification of risk factors for metabolic disorders and other health outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> "A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The observational design of the IDEFICS study was complemented by a setting-based community-oriented intervention programme for primary prevention of obesity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> "A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28040744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37420130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10473990/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European IDEFICS (Identification and prevention of Dietary- and lifestyle-induced health EFfects In Children and infantS)/I.Family cohort is a multi-centre population-based children’s study that aimed to identify risk factors for diet- and lifestyle-related diseases, with a focus on childhood overweight and metabolic disorders [14, 15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000871> "A multi-centre European population-based cohort of 16,228 children aged 2 to 9 years examined in 2007–2008 in Belgium, Cyprus, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Spain and Sweden, with a community-based obesity-prevention intervention, followed into adolescence by the I.Family study to identify dietary and lifestyle risk factors for childhood overweight and metabolic disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Centers in San Antonio, Texas, and San Luis Valley, Colorado, recruited Hispanics from two ongoing population-based studies (the San Antonio Heart Study and the San Luis Valley Diabetes Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Predictors of incident diabetes were evaluated in Hispanic, non-Hispanic white, and African American participants in the Insulin Resistance Atherosclerosis Study (aged 40–69 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8680609+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Insulin resistance was assessed directly using the frequently sampled intravenous glucose tolerance test with minimal model analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8680609+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intimal-medial carotid artery wall thickness, an indicator of atherosclerosis, was measured using B-mode ultrasonography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8680609+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 1600 men and women were recruited from four geographic areas to represent a range of glucose tolerance (normal, impaired, and diabetic) and ethnicity (hispanic, non-Hispanic white, and African-American).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19808919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8680609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8680609+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Insulin Resistance Atherosclerosis Study (IRAS) is the first epidemiologic study designed to assess the relationships between insulin resistance, insulinemia, glycemia, other components of the insulin resistance syndrome, and prevalent cardiovascular disease (CVD) in a large multiethnic cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000872> "A multiethnic cohort of over 1,600 Hispanic, non-Hispanic white and African American men and women aged 40–69 years with normal, impaired or diabetic glucose tolerance, recruited at four clinical centres in California, Texas and Colorado, United States, to study the relationships between directly measured insulin resistance, atherosclerosis and cardiovascular disease.")

