AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12878005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected from 2006 to 2009, and included information on social support, activities of daily living, comorbidity, physical activity, quality of life, depressive symptoms, and cognitive function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000886> "A population-based study of 2,488 people aged 65 and older in the province of Toledo, Spain, selected by two-stage random sampling from the municipal census and covering institutionalised and community-dwelling persons in rural and urban settings, with data collected from 2006 to study frailty and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12878005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were taken from the Toledo Study for Healthy Aging, a population-based study conducted on 2,488 individuals aged 65 years and older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000886> "A population-based study of 2,488 people aged 65 and older in the province of Toledo, Spain, selected by two-stage random sampling from the municipal census and covering institutionalised and community-dwelling persons in rural and urban settings, with data collected from 2006 to study frailty and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12878005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were taken from the baseline assessment in the TSHA, a population-based longitudinal study of institutionalized and community dwelling individuals aged 65 years and over, residing in the province of Toledo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000886> "A population-based study of 2,488 people aged 65 and older in the province of Toledo, Spain, selected by two-stage random sampling from the municipal census and covering institutionalised and community-dwelling persons in rural and urban settings, with data collected from 2006 to study frailty and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12878005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were selected by a two-stage random sampling from the municipal census of Toledo, covering both institutionalized and community dwelling persons from rural and urban settings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000886> "A population-based study of 2,488 people aged 65 and older in the province of Toledo, Spain, selected by two-stage random sampling from the municipal census and covering institutionalised and community-dwelling persons in rural and urban settings, with data collected from 2006 to study frailty and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22159772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12878005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Toledo Study for Healthy Aging (TSHA) was set to assess the frequency of FS in the older adult population of Spain, and to examine its underlying mechanisms, risk factors, clinical and functional significance, and its impact on the health care system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000886> "A population-based study of 2,488 people aged 65 and older in the province of Toledo, Spain, selected by two-stage random sampling from the municipal census and covering institutionalised and community-dwelling persons in rural and urban settings, with data collected from 2006 to study frailty and healthy ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23505255+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline recruitment of the BASE-II cohort was recently completed and has led to the sampling of 1600 older adults (age range 60-80 years), as well as 600 younger adults (20-35 years) serving as the basic population for in-depth analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23505255+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify and characterize the factors associated with 'healthy' vs. 'unhealthy' ageing, we have launched the Berlin Aging Study II (BASE-II), a multidisciplinary and multi-institutional project that ascertains a large number of ageing-related variables from a wide range of different functional domains.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34162642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230995/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline recruitment of 2200 adult volunteers from the Berlin metropolitan area and baseline assessments were completed in 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34162642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230995/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is based on a follow-up examination of a subsample (older group) of the Berlin Aging Study II (BASE-II).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34162642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230995/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The follow-up assessments within the GendAge study took place between 22 June 2018 and 10 March 2020 at the Charité Universitaetsmedizin Berlin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23505255") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34162642") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230995/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "namely, geriatrics and internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000887> "A multidisciplinary, multi-institutional cohort of about 1,600 older adults aged 60–80 and 600 younger adults aged 20–35 recruited as volunteers in the Berlin metropolitan area, Germany, with baseline assessments completed in 2014 across geriatrics, internal medicine, immunology, genetics, psychology, sociology and economics, to identify factors associated with healthy versus unhealthy ageing; a subsample of the older group was re-examined in 2018–2020 in the GendAge study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2000, 3011 participants (out of 4472 invitees) who had become 55 years of age or moved into the study district since the start of the study were added to the cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> "The second cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of 3,011 inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, who had moved to the district or turned 55 since the first cohort began, enrolled from 2000 and re-examined about every 5 years to study determinants of chronic diseases in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study aims to unravel etiology, preclinical course, natural history and potential targets for intervention for chronic diseases in mid-life and late-life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> "The second cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of 3,011 inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, who had moved to the district or turned 55 since the first cohort began, enrolled from 2000 and re-examined about every 5 years to study determinants of chronic diseases in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12188677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, RS is a large prospective, population-based cohort study conducted among middle-aged and older people in the suburb Ommoord in Rotterdam, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> "The second cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of 3,011 inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, who had moved to the district or turned 55 since the first cohort began, enrolled from 2000 and re-examined about every 5 years to study determinants of chronic diseases in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12188677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2000, the RS was extended with a second subcohort (RS-II) of 3011 participants who moved to Ommoord or turned 55 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> "The second cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of 3,011 inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, who had moved to the district or turned 55 since the first cohort began, enrolled from 2000 and re-examined about every 5 years to study determinants of chronic diseases in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40563098") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12188677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RS-I-4 and RS-II-2 visits were conducted between 2002 and 2005, with participants invited for re-examination approximately every 5 years, while the younger RS-IV-1 cohort was examined between 2016 and 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000888> "The second cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of 3,011 inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, who had moved to the district or turned 55 since the first cohort began, enrolled from 2000 and re-examined about every 5 years to study determinants of chronic diseases in older adults.")

