AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244060/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants in EIMS/GEMS were asked to provide blood samples for genetic analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000909> "A Swedish population-based case-control study of multiple sclerosis in which prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria were identified from the Swedish MS registry and controls were randomly selected from the national population register, with lifestyle and environmental questionnaires and blood samples for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244060/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GEMS identified prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria from the Swedish National MS registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000909> "A Swedish population-based case-control study of multiple sclerosis in which prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria were identified from the Swedish MS registry and controls were randomly selected from the national population register, with lifestyle and environmental questionnaires and blood samples for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244060/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One control per case, matched by age, sex and region at the time of disease onset, was randomly selected from the national population register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000909> "A Swedish population-based case-control study of multiple sclerosis in which prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria were identified from the Swedish MS registry and controls were randomly selected from the national population register, with lifestyle and environmental questionnaires and blood samples for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244060/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EIMS and GEMS questionnaires on environmental exposures and lifestyle factors were similar, with most questions identically worded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000909> "A Swedish population-based case-control study of multiple sclerosis in which prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria were identified from the Swedish MS registry and controls were randomly selected from the national population register, with lifestyle and environmental questionnaires and blood samples for genetic analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36629499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244060/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from Epidemiological Investigation of Multiple Sclerosis (EIMS) and Genes and Environment in Multiple Sclerosis (GEMS), which are Swedish population-based, case-control studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000909> "A Swedish population-based case-control study of multiple sclerosis in which prevalent cases fulfilling the McDonald criteria were identified from the Swedish MS registry and controls were randomly selected from the national population register, with lifestyle and environmental questionnaires and blood samples for genetic analyses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6355367/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were recruited using family health history questionnaires obtained from a county-wide (Richmond County, Georgia) public school screening of children in kindergarten through grade 8 whose families were interested in health research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910> "A prospective cohort of normotensive children of African or European ancestry aged 5–16 years in 1989, recruited through a county-wide public school screening in Richmond County, Georgia, United States, and re-evaluated repeatedly into adulthood to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6355367/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, participants who met the following criteria were recruited: aged 5–16 years in 1989, African or European ancestry, normotensive for age and sex based on BP screening, and apparently healthy based on parental reports of the child’s medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910> "A prospective cohort of normotensive children of African or European ancestry aged 5–16 years in 1989, recruited through a county-wide public school screening in Richmond County, Georgia, United States, and re-evaluated repeatedly into adulthood to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6355367/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Georgia Stress and Heart Study, a prospective cohort study with repeated measures of PWV in youth and young adults, provides an excellent opportunity to examine the pattern and the rate of longitudinal change in PWV within and among individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910> "A prospective cohort of normotensive children of African or European ancestry aged 5–16 years in 1989, recruited through a county-wide public school screening in Richmond County, Georgia, United States, and re-evaluated repeatedly into adulthood to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30234784") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6355367/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were from the Georgia Stress and Heart (GSH) study, an ongoing longitudinal study designed to evaluate the development of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood, with evaluations conducted annually from 1989 to 2000 (visits 1–10), every 1.5 years from 2000 to 2006 (visits 11–14), and every 2 years from 2008 to 2012 (visits 15–16).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000910> "A prospective cohort of normotensive children of African or European ancestry aged 5–16 years in 1989, recruited through a county-wide public school screening in Richmond County, Georgia, United States, and re-evaluated repeatedly into adulthood to study the development of cardiovascular risk factors from childhood to adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MRC/Wits-Agincourt Unit’s HAALSI (Health and Aging in Africa: Longitudinal Studies of an INDEPTH community) cohort was designed to examine the biological, social and economic conditions that shape health in the ageing population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911> "A longitudinal population study of more than 5000 adults aged 40 and older in Bushbuckridge, rural Mpumalanga, South Africa, recruited in 2014–2015 within the Agincourt Health and Demographic Surveillance System, collecting socio-demographic, infection history and cognitive data to study health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10043003/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HAALSI was funded by the National Institute on Aging (P01 AG041710) nested within the Agincourt Health and Demographic Surveillance System supported by the University of the Witwatersrand and Medical Research Council, South Africa, and the Wellcome Trust, UK (grants 058893/Z/99/A; 069683/Z/02/Z; 085477/Z/08/Z; 085477/B/08/Z).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911> "A longitudinal population study of more than 5000 adults aged 40 and older in Bushbuckridge, rural Mpumalanga, South Africa, recruited in 2014–2015 within the Agincourt Health and Demographic Surveillance System, collecting socio-demographic, infection history and cognitive data to study health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10043003/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Socio-demographic data, infection history, and cognitive performance data were collected from 5059 consented participants (male (n = 2345) and female (n = 2714)) aged 40 years and older recruited from Bushbuckridge, Mpumalanga (November 2014 to November 2015) and a sub-set of 2246 of these participants (male (n = 935) and female (n = 1311)) had genotype data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911> "A longitudinal population study of more than 5000 adults aged 40 and older in Bushbuckridge, rural Mpumalanga, South Africa, recruited in 2014–2015 within the Agincourt Health and Demographic Surveillance System, collecting socio-demographic, infection history and cognitive data to study health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36973338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10043003/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health and Aging in Africa: A Longitudinal Study of an INDEPTH Community in South Africa (HAALSI) collected baseline cognition data for over 5000 older adults in Bushbuckridge, rural Mpumalanga, South Africa (SA)36.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000911> "A longitudinal population study of more than 5000 adults aged 40 and older in Bushbuckridge, rural Mpumalanga, South Africa, recruited in 2014–2015 within the Agincourt Health and Demographic Surveillance System, collecting socio-demographic, infection history and cognitive data to study health and ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3429877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Observational work includes cohorts focusing on different stages along the life course, evaluation of national policy at population, household and individual levels and examination of household responses to shocks and stresses and the resulting pathways influencing health and well-being.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> "A health and socio-demographic surveillance system of about 90,000 people in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, established in 1992, which updates resident status and vital events annually and hosts observational cohorts and trials across the life course on health, population and social transitions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3429877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ongoing trials target critical problems affecting the health and well-being of children and adolescents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> "A health and socio-demographic surveillance system of about 90,000 people in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, established in 1992, which updates resident status and vital events annually and hosts observational cohorts and trials across the life course on health, population and social transitions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3429877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Agincourt HDSS constitutes a platform for research programmes that elucidate causal pathways and test interventions across the life course.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> "A health and socio-demographic surveillance system of about 90,000 people in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, established in 1992, which updates resident status and vital events annually and hosts observational cohorts and trials across the life course on health, population and social transitions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3429877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Agincourt health and socio-demographic surveillance system (HDSS), located in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, was established in 1992 to support district health systems development led by the post-apartheid ministry of health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> "A health and socio-demographic surveillance system of about 90,000 people in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, established in 1992, which updates resident status and vital events annually and hosts observational cohorts and trials across the life course on health, population and social transitions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22933647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3429877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HDSS (90 000 people), based on an annual update of resident status and vital events, now supports multiple investigations into the causes and consequences of complex health, population and social transitions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000912> "A health and socio-demographic surveillance system of about 90,000 people in rural northeast South Africa close to the Mozambique border, established in 1992, which updates resident status and vital events annually and hosts observational cohorts and trials across the life course on health, population and social transitions.")

