AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254404+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 11,000 pairs of twins and multiples of all ages have been recruited into the registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254404+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Qingdao Twin Registry (QTR) was initiated in 1998 as part of the National Chinese Twin Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254404+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twin studies offer a unique opportunity to disentangle the genetic and environmental risk and protective factors for chronic disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23182450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23182450+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adult twins have been sampled for studying heritability of multiple phenotypes associated with metabolic disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23182450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23182450+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, an elderly twin cohort has been recruited with a focus on genetic studies of aging-related phenotypes using twin modeling and genome-wide association analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254404") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23182450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23182450+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since then new twin cohorts have been sampled, with one longitudinal cohort of adolescent twins selected to explore determinants of metabolic disorders and health behaviors during puberty and young adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000932> "A registry of twins and multiples of all ages in Qingdao, China, initiated in 1998 as part of the Chinese National Twin Registry, with adolescent, adult and elderly twin cohorts sampled for studies of chronic disease, metabolic disorders, health behaviours and ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17254402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254402+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chinese National Twin Registry is the first and largest population-based twin registry in China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933> "A population-based twin registry in China, established in 2001, which includes data on over 61,000 twin pairs from 11 provinces or cities and collects biological specimens from disease-concordant and disease-discordant twin pairs, to analyse genetic and environmental influences on chronic diseases, especially cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31270876+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, the CNTR has focused on collecting biologic specimens from disease-concordant or disease-discordant twin pairs or from twin pairs reared apart.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933> "A population-based twin registry in China, established in 2001, which includes data on over 61,000 twin pairs from 11 provinces or cities and collects biological specimens from disease-concordant and disease-discordant twin pairs, to analyse genetic and environmental influences on chronic diseases, especially cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31270876+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since its establishment in 2001, the CNTR has provided an important resource for analysing genetic and environmental influences on chronic diseases especially cardiovascular diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933> "A population-based twin registry in China, established in 2001, which includes data on over 61,000 twin pairs from 11 provinces or cities and collects biological specimens from disease-concordant and disease-discordant twin pairs, to analyse genetic and environmental influences on chronic diseases, especially cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31270876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31270876+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chinese National Twin Registry (CNTR) currently includes data from 61 566 twin pair from 11 provinces or cities in China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000933> "A population-based twin registry in China, established in 2001, which includes data on over 61,000 twin pairs from 11 provinces or cities and collects biological specimens from disease-concordant and disease-discordant twin pairs, to analyse genetic and environmental influences on chronic diseases, especially cardiovascular diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25231870") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25231870+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, using genome-wide and custom-genotyping arrays in up to 182,416 women of European descent from 57 studies, we found robust evidence (P < 5 × 10(-8)) for 123 signals at 106 genomic loci associated with age at menarche.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> "An international network of investigators that meta-analyses genome-wide association study data from many cohorts to identify genetic variants and genes affecting reproductive ageing and reproductive timing, such as age at menarche and age at natural menopause.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28436984") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5841952/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These comprised 40 studies from the ReproGen consortium (N = 179,117), in addition to the 23andMe (N = 76,831) and UK Biobank (N = 73,397) studies (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> "An international network of investigators that meta-analyses genome-wide association study data from many cohorts to identify genetic variants and genes affecting reproductive ageing and reproductive timing, such as age at menarche and age at natural menopause.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36572578") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36572578+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With the development of genomic technology, the Reproductive Genetics Consortium conducted several genome-wide association studies on ANM in people of European descent, and found that defects in DNA damage repair pathways were the main genetic mechanism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> "An international network of investigators that meta-analyses genome-wide association study data from many cohorts to identify genetic variants and genes affecting reproductive ageing and reproductive timing, such as age at menarche and age at natural menopause.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ReproGen consortium is an international network of investigators interested in better understanding the genetic basis of reproductive ageing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> "An international network of investigators that meta-analyses genome-wide association study data from many cohorts to identify genetic variants and genes affecting reproductive ageing and reproductive timing, such as age at menarche and age at natural menopause.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.reprogen.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use large-scale meta-analyses of Genome-wide Association Study (GWAS) data to highlight genetic variants and genes that impact reproductive timing in humans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000934> "An international network of investigators that meta-analyses genome-wide association study data from many cohorts to identify genetic variants and genes affecting reproductive ageing and reproductive timing, such as age at menarche and age at natural menopause.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3496122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Approval of the study was given by the ethical review board at the Karolinska Institute (Stockholm, Sweden) and six other ethical review boards in the respective regions in which the subjects were based.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women aged 50–74 born in Sweden, with incident cases identified through the Swedish regional cancer registries and controls randomly selected from the Swedish population register, enrolled in 1993–1995, with ethical approval at Karolinska Institutet and funding from Singapore (A*STAR) and the US.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected from the Swedish Total Population Register and were frequency matched to the expected age distribution of the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women aged 50–74 born in Sweden, with incident cases identified through the Swedish regional cancer registries and controls randomly selected from the Swedish population register, enrolled in 1993–1995, with ethical approval at Karolinska Institutet and funding from Singapore (A*STAR) and the US.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident cases from October 1993 to March 1995 identified via the 6 regional cancer registries in Sweden, to which reporting is mandatory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women aged 50–74 born in Sweden, with incident cases identified through the Swedish regional cancer registries and controls randomly selected from the Swedish population register, enrolled in 1993–1995, with ethical approval at Karolinska Institutet and funding from Singapore (A*STAR) and the US.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SASBAC study was supported by funding from the Agency for Science, Technology and Research of Singapore (A*STAR), the US National Institute of Health (NIH)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women aged 50–74 born in Sweden, with incident cases identified through the Swedish regional cancer registries and controls randomly selected from the Swedish population register, enrolled in 1993–1995, with ethical approval at Karolinska Institutet and funding from Singapore (A*STAR) and the US.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22226020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Singapore and Sweden Breast Cancer Study (SASBAC) is a population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women born in Sweden aged 50 to 74 years at the time of enrollment, which was between 1 October 1993 and 31 March 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000935> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal breast cancer in women aged 50–74 born in Sweden, with incident cases identified through the Swedish regional cancer registries and controls randomly selected from the Swedish population register, enrolled in 1993–1995, with ethical approval at Karolinska Institutet and funding from Singapore (A*STAR) and the US.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000936> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000936>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3607485") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SLRIc /Toronto 331 499 Toronto, Canada Hospital-based case–control 317 K 314285") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000936> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Toronto, Canada, run by the University of Toronto and the Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital, whose genome-wide genotyped cases and controls contribute to international lung cancer consortia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3607485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the lung cancer study from Canada (University of Toronto and Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute) (4)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000936> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Toronto, Canada, run by the University of Toronto and the Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital, whose genome-wide genotyped cases and controls contribute to international lung cancer consortia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4621033/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We applied META-GSA to pool the results of four case-control GWASs of lung cancer risk (Central European Study and Toronto/Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute Study; German Lung Cancer Study and MD Anderson Cancer Center Study), which had already been analyzed separately with four different GSA methods (EASE; SLAT, mSUMSTAT and GenGen).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000936> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Toronto, Canada, run by the University of Toronto and the Samuel Lunenfeld Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital, whose genome-wide genotyped cases and controls contribute to international lung cancer consortia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000937> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000937>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Against this background, we attempted to identify genetic variations associated with GC risk according to sex and histological type by combining and analyzing additional cohorts with our previous study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000937> "A hospital-based case–control cohort of patients with gastric cancer and non-cancer controls aged 26–80 recruited at the Digestive Disease Center of Seoul National University Bundang Hospital, South Korea, with genome-wide genotypes, Helicobacter pylori status and lifestyle data, used to study genetic risk of gastric cancer by histological type and sex.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following QC and imputation, we retained 4,962,361 variants from 968 participants (527 GC patients and 441 non-cancer controls) with complete data for cancer status, sex, age, H. pylori status, and smoking status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000937> "A hospital-based case–control cohort of patients with gastric cancer and non-cancer controls aged 26–80 recruited at the Digestive Disease Center of Seoul National University Bundang Hospital, South Korea, with genome-wide genotypes, Helicobacter pylori status and lifestyle data, used to study genetic risk of gastric cancer by histological type and sex.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39862296") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11842433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Seoul National University Bundang Hospital (SNUBH) cohort comprises 1,216 participants, consisting of 610 patients with GC and 606 non-cancer controls, with ages ranging from 26 to 80 years, who were recruited from the enrolled participants who visited the Digestive Disease Center, SNUBH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000937> "A hospital-based case–control cohort of patients with gastric cancer and non-cancer controls aged 26–80 recruited at the Digestive Disease Center of Seoul National University Bundang Hospital, South Korea, with genome-wide genotypes, Helicobacter pylori status and lifestyle data, used to study genetic risk of gastric cancer by histological type and sex.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7738642/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we established the Tohoku Medical Megabank (TMM) Project, which is conducted by Tohoku University Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (ToMMo) and Iwate Medical University Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization (IMM).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "87,865 gave their informed consent to join our study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were aged 20 years or over and living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort comprised a large sample size and it contains information on the natural disaster, genome information, and metabolome information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We asked participants to join our cohort in the health check-up settings and assessment center based settings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31932529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31932529+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established a community-based cohort study to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake on disaster victims and gene-environment interactions on the incidence of major diseases, such as cancer and cardiovascular diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000938> "A community-based cohort of adults aged 20 years or over living in Miyagi or Iwate Prefecture, Japan, of whom 87,865 consented to join through health check-ups and assessment centres of the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project, to assess the long-term impact of the Great East Japan Earthquake and gene–environment interactions in major diseases such as cancer and cardiovascular disease, with genome and metabolome information.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In accordance with the development of the genome cohort design, a birth and three-generation cohort study appears to be essential for unravelling how genes and the environment compound on one another to determine health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Then, we recruited the women’s partners (the fathers of the fetuses), their parents (the grandparents of the fetuses), their children (the siblings of the fetuses, if any) and their extended family members (Figure 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To our best knowledge, the TMM BirThree Cohort Study is the first study to involve a birth and three-generation cohort from an initial stage of cohort construction combined with genome and omics analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ToMMo and IMM have conducted the TMM Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study) since July 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have conducted the Tohoku Medical Megabank Project Birth and Three-Generation Cohort Study (TMM BirThree Cohort Study) since July 2013 in Miyagi Prefecture, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31504573") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7124511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited pregnant women and their fetuses as probands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000939> "A birth and three-generation cohort in Japan conducted since July 2013 by the Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization of Tohoku University and the Iwate Tohoku Medical Megabank Organization, recruiting pregnant women and their fetuses as probands together with the fathers, grandparents, siblings and extended family members, with genome and omics information, to study disease risk across generations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339762/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection in this cohort started a few years after the population cohort, in 2004, with the inclusion of 543 children (response rate 43%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> "A Dutch clinical cohort of 543 children who had been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands before the age of 11, enrolled from 2004 alongside the TRAILS population cohort and followed from about age 11 with repeated assessments of mental health and development into young adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339762/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical cohort consists of individuals who have been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands any time before the age of 11.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> "A Dutch clinical cohort of 543 children who had been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands before the age of 11, enrolled from 2004 alongside the TRAILS population cohort and followed from about age 11 with repeated assessments of mental health and development into young adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339762/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical cohort has been assessed four times over a period of 8 years, with retention rates ranging between 77% and 85%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> "A Dutch clinical cohort of 543 children who had been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands before the age of 11, enrolled from 2004 alongside the TRAILS population cohort and followed from about age 11 with repeated assessments of mental health and development into young adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339762/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "to contribute to the understanding of the determinants of adolescents’ mental (ill-)health and social development during adolescence and young adulthood, as well as the mechanisms underlying the associations between determinants and outcomes") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> "A Dutch clinical cohort of 543 children who had been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands before the age of 11, enrolled from 2004 alongside the TRAILS population cohort and followed from about age 11 with repeated assessments of mental health and development into young adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25431468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25431468+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TRAILS consists of a population cohort (N=2230) and a clinical cohort (N=543), both of which were followed from about age 11 years onwards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000940> "A Dutch clinical cohort of 543 children who had been referred to a child psychiatric outpatient clinic in the Northern Netherlands before the age of 11, enrolled from 2004 alongside the TRAILS population cohort and followed from about age 11 with repeated assessments of mental health and development into young adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5697951/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3699066") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TUDR study is a collaborative effort between Taichung Veterans General Hospital (VGH) in Taiwan and Cedars-Sinai Medical Center (CSMC) in the USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941> "A collection of Chinese people with type 2 diabetes in Taiwan, with and without proliferative diabetic retinopathy, assembled from 1996 to 2011 by Taiwanese and US investigators for genetic studies of diabetic retinopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5697951/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3699066") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery cohort that underwent GWAS consisted of Chinese subjects at the two ends of the DR spectrum, defined as having type 2 diabetes of greater than 8 years duration without DR (controls, n ¼ 570) and PDR (cases, n ¼ 437).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941> "A collection of Chinese people with type 2 diabetes in Taiwan, with and without proliferative diabetic retinopathy, assembled from 1996 to 2011 by Taiwanese and US investigators for genetic studies of diabetic retinopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5697951/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3978/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3978_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TUDR study is a cohort that enrolled subjects with T2DM receiving care at Taichung Veterans General Hospital, Taichung, Taiwan, and a small number of subjects were included from Tri-Service General Hospital, Taipei, Taiwan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941> "A collection of Chinese people with type 2 diabetes in Taiwan, with and without proliferative diabetic retinopathy, assembled from 1996 to 2011 by Taiwanese and US investigators for genetic studies of diabetic retinopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5697951/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5697951/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TUDRTaiwan1996–2011Chinese1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000941> "A collection of Chinese people with type 2 diabetes in Taiwan, with and without proliferative diabetic retinopathy, assembled from 1996 to 2011 by Taiwanese and US investigators for genetic studies of diabetic retinopathy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3185950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort members have been recruited by a participant referral method intended to assemble economically a large general population cohort from whom detailed questionnaire information and blood samples can be obtained repeatedly over decades, with high completeness of follow-up and inclusion of large numbers of related individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> "A UK general-population cohort started in 2003 that recruited 112,049 participants aged 16–102 by 2011 through a generational referral method, in which women recruited directly nominated female friends and relatives, collecting detailed questionnaires and blood samples repeatedly over decades to investigate breast cancer aetiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3185950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The method has successfully been used during 2003–2011 to recruit 112 049 motivated participants with a broad geographic and socioeconomic distribution, aged 16–102 years, who have completed detailed questionnaires; 92% of the participants gave blood samples at recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> "A UK general-population cohort started in 2003 that recruited 112,049 participants aged 16–102 by 2011 through a generational referral method, in which women recruited directly nominated female friends and relatives, collecting detailed questionnaires and blood samples repeatedly over decades to investigate breast cancer aetiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3185950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The rationale, design, recruitment and follow-up methods are described for the Breakthrough Generations Study, a UK cohort study started in 2003, targeted at investigation of breast cancer aetiology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> "A UK general-population cohort started in 2003 that recruited 112,049 participants aged 16–102 by 2011 through a generational referral method, in which women recruited directly nominated female friends and relatives, collecting detailed questionnaires and blood samples repeatedly over decades to investigate breast cancer aetiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3185950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They nominated female friends and family, whom we contacted, and those who joined (‘second generation’) nominated others, reiterated for up to 28 generations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> "A UK general-population cohort started in 2003 that recruited 112,049 participants aged 16–102 by 2011 through a generational referral method, in which women recruited directly nominated female friends and relatives, collecting detailed questionnaires and blood samples repeatedly over decades to investigate breast cancer aetiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21897394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3185950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "‘First-generation’ recruits were women contacted directly, or who volunteered directly, to join the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000942> "A UK general-population cohort started in 2003 that recruited 112,049 participants aged 16–102 by 2011 through a generational referral method, in which women recruited directly nominated female friends and relatives, collecting detailed questionnaires and blood samples repeatedly over decades to investigate breast cancer aetiology.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000943> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000943>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5477157/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DiaGene study is a multi-centre, prospective, extensively phenotyped type 2 diabetes cohort study with concurrent inclusion of diabetes-free individuals at baseline as controls in the city of Eindhoven, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000943> "A multicentre prospective cohort of people with type 2 diabetes, with diabetes-free controls included at baseline, in the city of Eindhoven, the Netherlands, extensively phenotyped to study the aetiology of type 2 diabetes and its micro- and macrovascular complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5477157/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main purpose of the DiaGene study is to study the analyses of genetic, biochemical and environmental determinants of T2DM and its complications.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000943> "A multicentre prospective cohort of people with type 2 diabetes, with diabetes-free controls included at baseline, in the city of Eindhoven, the Netherlands, extensively phenotyped to study the aetiology of type 2 diabetes and its micro- and macrovascular complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28649285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5477157/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This encompasses all anthropometric and laboratory measurements and data on metabolic, microvascular and macrovascular complications of T2DM and enables us to perform prospective analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000943> "A multicentre prospective cohort of people with type 2 diabetes, with diabetes-free controls included at baseline, in the city of Eindhoven, the Netherlands, extensively phenotyped to study the aetiology of type 2 diabetes and its micro- and macrovascular complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000944> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000944>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10319806/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPSAC2000 is a mother
child cohort where all the mothers had a history of a doctor’s diagnosis of asthma after 7 years of age
and thus this is a high risk asthma cohort comprising 411 children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000944> "A Danish clinical research programme, the Copenhagen Prospective Studies on Asthma in Childhood, made up of mother-child birth cohorts: COPSAC2000, a high-risk cohort of 411 children of mothers with a doctor's diagnosis of asthma, enrolled in the first month of life, and COPSAC2010, a cohort of 700 children born to unselected mothers from Denmark.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10319806/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COPSAC2010 is a mother child cohort comprising 700
children born to unselected mothers from Denmark as described previously in detail9,10
.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000944> "A Danish clinical research programme, the Copenhagen Prospective Studies on Asthma in Childhood, made up of mother-child birth cohorts: COPSAC2000, a high-risk cohort of 411 children of mothers with a doctor's diagnosis of asthma, enrolled in the first month of life, and COPSAC2010, a cohort of 700 children born to unselected mothers from Denmark.")
