# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer in Kaiser Permanente health plan members (7,783 cases, 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African-American, 7.0% East Asian, 7.8% Latino)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the ProHealth study focused on ascertaining KP Northern California African-American PCa cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were all men in GERA without PCa diagnosis; who could have had other cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RPGEH participants included men in the RPGEH Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging (GERA) cohort (dbGaP phs000674.v1.p1), as well as PCa cases with a DNA sample in the RPGEH biorepository but who were not part of GERA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26034056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4527942/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To further characterize PCa’s genetic basis, we undertook a GWAS using multiple study cohorts within Kaiser Permanente (KP), a fully integrated health care delivery system: the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health (RPGEH) cohort (dbGaP phs000674.p1), the ProHealth Study, and the California Men’s Health Study (CMHS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000945> "A multiethnic genome-wide association study sample of prostate cancer from Kaiser Permanente health plan members in California, combining prostate cancer cases from three Kaiser Permanente studies (the Research Program on Genes, Environment and Health, the ProHealth Study and the California Men's Health Study) with men of the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Aging cohort without a prostate cancer diagnosis as controls (7,783 cases and 38,595 controls; 80.3% non-Hispanic white, 4.9% African American, 7.0% East Asian and 7.8% Latino).")

