# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26050256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26050256+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All analyses were conducted within the Gene-Lifestyle Interactions and Dental Endpoints (GLIDE) Consortium in 13 studies from Europe and the USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6591304/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(11) Biobank Japan (BBJ) and (12) Tokyo Medical and Dental University Aggressive Periodontitis Study (TMDUAGP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6591304/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All meta-analyses within GLIDE used a fixed effects inverse-variance-weighted strategy implemented in METAL19 (Methods; Supplementary Data 1, Supplementary Data 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6591304/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide association studies (GWAS) were undertaken within the GLIDE consortium, using clinical measures of dental diseases and imputed genotype data, accounting for age-specific, sex-specific and other study-specific covariates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6591304/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we synthesise evidence from two sources; the Gene-Lifestyle Interactions in Dental Endpoints (GLIDE) consortium18, which is a unique collection of epidemiological cohorts with detailed information on clinical endpoints of dental diseases; and UKB, which contains less-refined self-reported oral health data at a larger scale.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31235808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6591304/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to achieve further understanding of genetic contributions to caries and periodontitis, a shift in analysis scale—afforded by a similar approach to measurement—is required.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000947> "An international consortium of epidemiological cohorts from Europe, the United States and Japan with detailed clinical information on dental diseases, within which genome-wide association studies of dental caries and periodontitis are conducted and meta-analysed.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592689/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All PET data is collected on a Siemens ECAT HR+ PET scanner at Massachusetts General Hospital (MGH), in Boston, MA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592689/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HABS collects a range of demographic information (e.g., age, sex, education, race), clinical assessments (e.g., CDR, MMSE, GDS, estimated IQ), neuropsychological testing (e.g., processing speed, executive function, memory), blood work (fasting blood draw for Creatinine, Cholesterol, HDL, LDL, Glucose), APOE genotyping, physiological measures (e.g., height, weight, blood pressure).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592689/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects undergo a thorough imaging protocol consisting of the following modalities: PiB-PET (C-11 Pittsburgh Compound-B; dynamic 0–60 min), FDG-PET (F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose; 45–75 min), 3D T1-weighted structural MRI, task fMRI, resting state fMRI, diffusion tensor imaging (DTI), 3D T2-weighted FLAIR, susceptibility weighted imaging (SWI), and pulsed arterial spin labeling (pASL).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4592689/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Harvard Aging Brain Study (HABS NIH-P01AG036694) is a longitudinal observational study designed to further our understanding of differentiating “normal” aging from preclinical Alzheimer’s Dementia (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4592689/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The criteria utilized for inclusion/exclusion ensures the HABS cohort is comprised of cognitively normal, healthy older individuals at study enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25843019") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37101235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s40478-023-01563-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we systematically analyzed the largest collection of amyloid imaging data (N = 13,409), across multiple ethnicities from multicenter cohorts (Knight ADRC, A4, DIAN, ADNI, ADNIDOD, UPitt, HABS, AIBL, Memento, MCSA, WRAP, Berkeley, Korean study, and MISSION-AD) as a quantitative trait to identify the functional variants and genes driving the association of AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000948> "A longitudinal observational study of cognitively normal older adults, designed to distinguish normal ageing from preclinical Alzheimer's disease, with demographic, clinical, neuropsychological, clinical biomarker and neuroimaging data, including amyloid PET acquired at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11509949/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1995 and 2010, a total of 9449 southern Chinese women and men were recruited from the community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> "A prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Southern Chinese women and men recruited from the community in Hong Kong between 1995 and 2010, with questionnaire, anthropometric and clinical assessments at baseline and long-term follow-up through linkage to the Hong Kong Hospital Authority's territory-wide electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11509949/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During baseline assessments, participants completed a questionnaire on lifestyle behaviors, dietary habits, and medical conditions, alongside anthropometric and clinical measurements [28].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> "A prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Southern Chinese women and men recruited from the community in Hong Kong between 1995 and 2010, with questionnaire, anthropometric and clinical assessments at baseline and long-term follow-up through linkage to the Hong Kong Hospital Authority's territory-wide electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11509949/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Electronic health records of the HKOS participants were retrieved from the CDARS until 15 January 2024, allowing us to follow the participants longitudinally with a median of 20 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> "A prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Southern Chinese women and men recruited from the community in Hong Kong between 1995 and 2010, with questionnaire, anthropometric and clinical assessments at baseline and long-term follow-up through linkage to the Hong Kong Hospital Authority's territory-wide electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11509949/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were also linked to the Clinical Data Analysis and Reporting System (CDARS), a territory-wide electronic health record database managed by the Hong Kong Hospital Authority, via anonymized unique reference keys.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> "A prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Southern Chinese women and men recruited from the community in Hong Kong between 1995 and 2010, with questionnaire, anthropometric and clinical assessments at baseline and long-term follow-up through linkage to the Hong Kong Hospital Authority's territory-wide electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39458530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11509949/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from the Hong Kong Osteoporosis Study (HKOS), which was the first prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Asia [28].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000949> "A prospective cohort study of osteoporosis and fracture in Southern Chinese women and men recruited from the community in Hong Kong between 1995 and 2010, with questionnaire, anthropometric and clinical assessments at baseline and long-term follow-up through linkage to the Hong Kong Hospital Authority's territory-wide electronic health records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36403896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10085828/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of enrollment, participants underwent a research evaluation, which included completing a detailed study questionnaire, performing lung function testing, and submitting blood samples for biobanking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36403896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10085828/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants had to be between the age of 12–56 years at the time of recruitment and have no prior history of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or congestive heart failure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36403896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10085828/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAPPHIRE cohort participants were recruited from a large health care system serving the entirety of southeast Michigan, including the Detroit metropolitan area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36403896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10085828/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Study of Asthma-related Phenotypes and Pharmacogenomic Interactions by Race-ethnicity (SAPPHIRE) is a longitudinal cohort study of individuals with and without asthma from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10550990/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Study of Asthma Phenotypes and Pharmacogenomic Interactions by Race-ethnicity (SAPPHIRE) is
an ongoing study that was approved by the Institutional Review Board of Henry Ford Health System.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAPPHIRE is an ongoing prospective cohort study to determine the genetic determinants of inhaled corticosteroid response and other asthma-related phenotypes") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000950> "An ongoing study at Henry Ford Health System of members of the health system aged 12–56, with and without a clinical diagnosis of asthma, from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, United States, enrolled with a staff-administered questionnaire and lung function testing to study asthma phenotypes and pharmacogenomic interactions across racial and ethnic groups.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3585827/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Anthropometric measurements (height, weight, skinfold thickness), blood pressure, urine sample, and a fasting blood sample for glucose, insulin, micronutrients (i.e. vitamin B12, RBC folate, plasma homocysteine, methylmalonic acid MMA), lipids and a buffy coat for future DNA extraction will be collected, and processed using a standardized protocol at 24-28 weeks of gestation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3585827/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort in urban Canada is recruited in the Peel Ontario Region where South Asians account for 18% of the population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3585827/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The rural cohort is drawn from Snehalaya Hospital located in the village of Solur, Karnataka State.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3585827/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women between 18-40 years of age who are pregnant with a single fetus who are either from rural or urban India, or are of South Asian origin living in Canada (defined as maternal and paternal grandparents originating from the Indian subcontinent) are eligible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23356884+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The South Asian Birth Cohort Study (START) will investigate the environmental and genetic basis of adiposity among 750 South Asian offspring recruited from highly divergent environments, namely, rural and urban India and urban Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23356884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23356884+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The mother and growing offspring are followed prospectively and information on the growth trajectory, adiposity and health behaviors will be collected annually up to age 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000951> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant South Asian women aged 18–40 and their offspring, recruited in urban Bangalore and rural Solur in Karnataka, India, and in the Peel region of Ontario, Canada, with questionnaires, anthropometry, a glucose tolerance test, and blood and DNA samples in pregnancy, newborn measurements and follow-up of the children to age 3, to study the environmental and genetic determinants of adiposity among South Asians.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5778986/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients ≥18 years of age were eligible for enrollment if they were hospitalized with decompensation of known chronic HF or newly diagnosed HF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> "The clinical cohort of the TRIUMPH biomarker programme: an observational prospective study of adults admitted with acute heart failure, newly diagnosed or decompensated chronic, to 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013, with repeated blood sampling during one year of follow-up to validate prognostic biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5778986/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TRIUMPH was designed as a translational study program, combining biological discovery of novel biomarkers, technologic advances, and clinical validation in patients presenting with acute HF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> "The clinical cohort of the TRIUMPH biomarker programme: an observational prospective study of adults admitted with acute heart failure, newly diagnosed or decompensated chronic, to 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013, with repeated blood sampling during one year of follow-up to validate prognostic biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5778986/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical validation study was an observational prospective study enrolling patients admitted with acute HF in 14 hospitals in The Netherlands, between September 2009 and December 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> "The clinical cohort of the TRIUMPH biomarker programme: an observational prospective study of adults admitted with acute heart failure, newly diagnosed or decompensated chronic, to 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013, with repeated blood sampling during one year of follow-up to validate prognostic biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5778986/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort study was designed to validate the clinical value of biomarkers successfully passing the bio‐informatics and early‐validation stages of TRIUMPH, and to further evaluate more established biomarkers of HF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> "The clinical cohort of the TRIUMPH biomarker programme: an observational prospective study of adults admitted with acute heart failure, newly diagnosed or decompensated chronic, to 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013, with repeated blood sampling during one year of follow-up to validate prognostic biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29187387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29187387+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Repeated blood samples (7) were drawn during 1-year follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000952> "The clinical cohort of the TRIUMPH biomarker programme: an observational prospective study of adults admitted with acute heart failure, newly diagnosed or decompensated chronic, to 14 hospitals in the Netherlands between September 2009 and December 2013, with repeated blood sampling during one year of follow-up to validate prognostic biomarkers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3651583/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ASGC controls were participants in the Hunter Community Study (HCS), a population-based cohort of individuals aged 55–85 years, predominantly of European ancestry and residing in the Hunter Region in New South Wales, Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953> "A case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes, comprising stroke patients of European ancestry admitted to four clinical centres in Australia (Gosford Hospital, John Hunter Hospital in Newcastle, The Queen Elizabeth Hospital in Adelaide and Royal Perth Hospital) between 2003 and 2008, and population controls from the Hunter Community Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3651583/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ASGC stroke cases comprised stroke patients of European ancestry who were admitted to four clinical centers across Australia (The Neurosciences Department at Gosford Hospital, Gosford; the Neurology Department at John Hunter Hospital, Newcastle; The Queen Elizabeth Hospital, Adelaide; and the Royal Perth Hospital, Perth) between 2003 and 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953> "A case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes, comprising stroke patients of European ancestry admitted to four clinical centres in Australia (Gosford Hospital, John Hunter Hospital in Newcastle, The Queen Elizabeth Hospital in Adelaide and Royal Perth Hospital) between 2003 and 2008, and population controls from the Hunter Community Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3651583/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ischemic stroke subtypes were assigned using TOAST criteria on the basis of clinical, imaging and risk factor data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953> "A case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes, comprising stroke patients of European ancestry admitted to four clinical centres in Australia (Gosford Hospital, John Hunter Hospital in Newcastle, The Queen Elizabeth Hospital in Adelaide and Royal Perth Hospital) between 2003 and 2008, and population controls from the Hunter Community Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22941190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3651583/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed GWAS of ischemic stroke and a major ischemic stroke subtype (large artery atherosclerosis, LAA) using 1,162 ischemic stroke cases (including 421 LAA cases) and 1,244 population controls from Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000953> "A case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes, comprising stroke patients of European ancestry admitted to four clinical centres in Australia (Gosford Hospital, John Hunter Hospital in Newcastle, The Queen Elizabeth Hospital in Adelaide and Royal Perth Hospital) between 2003 and 2008, and population controls from the Hunter Community Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Birth Length Summary Data (2014) Birth Weight Summary Data - Fetal GWAS (2013)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> "A consortium that facilitates joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies to identify human genomic loci influencing traits related to early growth, from the fetus to young adulthood, such as birth weight and length, gestational duration, head circumference, childhood body mass index and obesity, and pubertal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Childhood Obesity Summary Data (2012) Childhood Obesity Summary Data (2019) Childhood BMI Summary Data (2015) Childhood BMI Summary Data (2020) Head Circumference Summary Data (2012) Head Circumference Summary Data (2022) Pubertal Growth Summary Data (2013) Pubertal Growth Summary Data (2024) Longitudinal Growth Summary Data (2024) Tanner Stage Summary Data (2014) Gestational Duration Data - Fetal GWAS (2019)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> "A consortium that facilitates joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies to identify human genomic loci influencing traits related to early growth, from the fetus to young adulthood, such as birth weight and length, gestational duration, head circumference, childhood body mass index and obesity, and pubertal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Early Growth Genetics (EGG) Consortium exists to facilitate joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies in order to identify human genomic loci that impact a variety of human traits related to early growth (fetus to young adult).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> "A consortium that facilitates joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies to identify human genomic loci influencing traits related to early growth, from the fetus to young adulthood, such as birth weight and length, gestational duration, head circumference, childhood body mass index and obesity, and pubertal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-019-00502-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EGG consortium focuses on the genetic basis of growth-related phenotypes spanning from fetal life into adolescence, including birth weight, childhood obesity and pubertal development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> "A consortium that facilitates joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies to identify human genomic loci influencing traits related to early growth, from the fetus to young adulthood, such as birth weight and length, gestational duration, head circumference, childhood body mass index and obesity, and pubertal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://egg-consortium.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-019-00502-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To achieve the sample sizes required for genetic research, the Early Growth Genetics (EGG) and EArly Genetics and Lifecourse Epidemiology (EAGLE) consortia were established.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000954> "A consortium that facilitates joint analysis of genetic data from multiple studies to identify human genomic loci influencing traits related to early growth, from the fetus to young adulthood, such as birth weight and length, gestational duration, head circumference, childhood body mass index and obesity, and pubertal growth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000955> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000955>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6390174/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutive patients with transient ischaemic attack or stroke were prospectively recruited from April 1, 2002, to March 31, 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000955> "A population-based incidence study of all acute vascular events in a defined population covered by nine primary care practices in Oxfordshire, United Kingdom, in which patients presenting with such events, including transient ischaemic attack and stroke, have been ascertained prospectively since 2002 and followed up.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6390174/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up interviews were done by trained nurses or study physicians at 1 month, 6 months, 1 year, and 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000955> "A population-based incidence study of all acute vascular events in a defined population covered by nine primary care practices in Oxfordshire, United Kingdom, in which patients presenting with such events, including transient ischaemic attack and stroke, have been ascertained prospectively since 2002 and followed up.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30784556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6390174/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OxVasc is a longitudinal population-based incidence cohort of all acute vascular events occurring within a defined population of 92 728, covered by around 100 primary care physicians in nine primary care practices in Oxfordshire, UK (appendix).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000955> "A population-based incidence study of all acute vascular events in a defined population covered by nine primary care practices in Oxfordshire, United Kingdom, in which patients presenting with such events, including transient ischaemic attack and stroke, have been ascertained prospectively since 2002 and followed up.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-50313-y") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants had previously been enrolled in randomized placebo-controlled trials or had been screened for previous studies in Copenhagen or Aalborg at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956> "A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-50313-y") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper we conducted a genome wide association study (GWAS) and phenome wide association study (PheWAS) for the VICM biomarker using the Prospective Epidemiologic Risk Factor (PERF) study13, an observational cohort with 5855 women linked to the Danish health registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956> "A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-50313-y") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PERF is comprised of 5855 post-menopausal Danish women, enrolled at baseline (PERF I) between 1999 and 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956> "A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38155185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-023-50313-y") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the study was to identify potential risk factors associated with age-related diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000956> "A prospective observational cohort of postmenopausal Danish women enrolled in 1999–2001, all of whom had previously taken part in randomised placebo-controlled trials or been screened for earlier studies at the Center for Clinical and Basic Research in Copenhagen or Aalborg, established to identify risk factors for age-related diseases and linked to the Danish health registries.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32986714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32986714+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a case-control study of 4,769 self-identified African American (2,463 cases and 2,306 controls), 2,199 Japanese American (1,106 cases and 1,093 controls), and 2,147 Latin American (1,081 cases and 1,066 controls) individuals from the Multiethnic Genome-wide Scan of Prostate Cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study we plan to undertake a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of prostate cancer in the Multiethnic Cohort (MEC) Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident cases of cancer are identified by annual linkage to the SEER cancer registries in California and Hawaii.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are mainly from five self-reported racial/ethnic populations living in Hawaii and California: African Americans, Native Hawaiians, Japanese Americans, Latinos, and Whites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prostate cancer cases have an invasive prostate cancer diagnosis after (incident) entry into cohort Controls were matched to cases on race/ethnicity, area of residence (California or Hawaii) and age at entry into cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000306.v4.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is part of the Gene Environment Association Studies initiative (GENEVA, http://www.genevastudy.org) funded by the trans-NIH Genes, Environment, and Health Initiative (GEI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000957> "A nested case-control genome-wide association study of prostate cancer within the Multiethnic Cohort Study, in which men of African American, Japanese American and Latino ancestry living in Hawaii and California with incident invasive prostate cancer, found by linkage to the SEER cancer registries, and controls matched on ethnicity, area of residence and age at cohort entry were genotyped under the Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Army STARRS (2009–2014) and STARRS-LS (2015–2020) are designed to identify modifiable risk and resilience factors, in order to better target interventions for Army suicides and to expand the scientific knowledge of psychosocial and neurobiological risk and resilience factors for STB and their psychopathological correlates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The All Army Study (AAS), a cross-sectional SAQ survey representative of active duty soldiers around the world (exclusive of basic training), including a probability sample of soldiers stationed in Afghanistan, who were surveyed as they transitioned through Kuwait for mid-tour leave;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The New Soldiers Study (NSS), a representative survey of new soldiers in the first week of basic training with self-administered questionnaires (SAQs), computerized neurocognitive tests, and blood samples;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Soldier Health Outcomes Studies (SHOS), two retrospective case–control studies of hospitalized suicide attempters (SHOS-A) and suicide decedents (SHOS-B)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The work that began in Army STARRS continues in STARRS-LS (2015–2020), the longitudinal follow-up study funded by the DoD, which adds historical administrative data from 2010 to 2015 and reassessment of the original Army STARRS survey respondents via web- and telephone-based interviews.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30104726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6756108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "in 2008 the US Army and US National Institute of Mental Health funded the Army Study to Assess Risk and Resilience in Servicemembers (Army STARRS), a multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of risk and resilience factors for suicidal thoughts and behaviors, and their psychopathological correlates among Army personnel.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000958> "A multicomponent epidemiological and neurobiological study of United States Army soldiers, funded by the US Army and the National Institute of Mental Health and carried out in 2009–2014. Its component studies combined Army administrative records with representative surveys of new soldiers, of active-duty soldiers and of brigade combat teams deploying to Afghanistan, some with neurocognitive tests and blood samples, and case-control studies of suicide attempts and deaths, to identify risk and resilience factors for suicidal behaviour and related mental disorders; its survey respondents are followed up in the Army STARRS Longitudinal Study (STARRS-LS).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15940135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-48190-8/MediaObjects/41467_2024_48190_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1993, the Barbados Asthma Genetics Study (BAGS) was initiated on nuclear and extended asthmatic families who self-reported as African Caribbean, resulting in the first evidence for linkage for asthma and tIgE in an African-ancestry population, and the development of novel family-based methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959> "A family-based asthma genetics study initiated in Barbados in 1993 on nuclear and extended families, self-reported as African Caribbean, of paediatric asthmatic probands referred from local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department of the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, with recruitment continuing through the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15940135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-48190-8/MediaObjects/41467_2024_48190_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pediatric probands were recruited through referrals at local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, and their nuclear and extended family members were subsequently recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959> "A family-based asthma genetics study initiated in Barbados in 1993 on nuclear and extended families, self-reported as African Caribbean, of paediatric asthmatic probands referred from local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department of the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, with recruitment continuing through the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15940135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38714703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-48190-8/MediaObjects/41467_2024_48190_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment into the BAGS program was enhanced through its involvement in the international Genetics of Asthma International Network (1999-2001) and the current sample of >1300 participants continues to grow through the efforts of collaborators and nursing staff at the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000959> "A family-based asthma genetics study initiated in Barbados in 1993 on nuclear and extended families, self-reported as African Caribbean, of paediatric asthmatic probands referred from local polyclinics or the Accident and Emergency Department of the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, with recruitment continuing through the Chronic Disease Research Centre in Barbados.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A structured questionnaire was used during in-person interviews by trained nurses to obtain information on socio-demographic characteristics, menstrual and reproductive history, height, weight by decade of adult life starting at age 20, personal medical history, family history of cancer, history of residence, lifetime occupational history and dietary habits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among the 1731 eligible controls identified by phone, 1317 (76%) accepted to participate to an in-person interview, and 1055 (80%) accepted to have a blood draw and were included in the present study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were breast cancer patients below 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007, identified from the main cancer treatment centers in each area and from smaller public and private hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population controls were selected among women residing in the study areas at the time of the case diagnosis and were frequency-matched to the cases by 10-year age group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were recruited for the study during the same period as the cases in 2005–2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30669331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6351946/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a population-based case-control study on breast cancer in Côte d’Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, two administrative areas (départements) located in Eastern and Western part of France, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000960> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in two French départements, Côte d'Or and Ille-et-Vilaine, in which women under 75 years of age with invasive or in situ breast carcinoma diagnosed from April 2005 to March 2007 and population controls frequency-matched to them by age, recruited over the same period, were interviewed in person by trained nurses, most also giving a blood sample; it has been used to study occupational, environmental and genetic risk factors for breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7923508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited to the Cardiovascular Health Improvement Project (CHIP), a longitudinal cardiovascular biobank within the Michigan Medicine Frankel Cardiovascular Center, initiated in 2013; biobank recruitment is ongoing [15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961> "A longitudinal cardiovascular biobank of patients treated at the Frankel Cardiovascular Center of Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, which has recruited since 2013, mainly patients with aortic disease, and links their genotype data to electronic health records and family history data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7923508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cardiovascular Health Improvement Project is supported by the Frankel Cardiovascular Center, University of Michigan, Michigan Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961> "A longitudinal cardiovascular biobank of patients treated at the Frankel Cardiovascular Center of Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, which has recruited since 2013, mainly patients with aortic disease, and links their genotype data to electronic health records and family history data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7923508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary focus is to recruit patients with aortic disease; governance is provided by three executive committees (Additional file 1, Committees).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961> "A longitudinal cardiovascular biobank of patients treated at the Frankel Cardiovascular Center of Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, which has recruited since 2013, mainly patients with aortic disease, and links their genotype data to electronic health records and family history data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33648514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cardiovascular Health Improvement Project (CHIP) is a cohort of
individuals treated at Michigan Medicine with linked genotype, EHR, and family history data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000961> "A longitudinal cardiovascular biobank of patients treated at the Frankel Cardiovascular Center of Michigan Medicine, the University of Michigan health system, which has recruited since 2013, mainly patients with aortic disease, and links their genotype data to electronic health records and family history data.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the baseline assessment only those patients with a diagnosis of ICD-10 depressive episode F32 from the Clinical Interview Schedule-Revised (CIS-R)[19] and a Beck Depression Inventory (BDI)[20] score of ≥ 15, were eligible to continue in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GPs referred patients aged between 18–74 years presenting with a new episode of depression, who did not have any medical contraindications to antidepressant medication and who had no history of psychosis or alcohol/substance abuse.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GenPod trial started recruiting participants in September 2005, and is due to complete data collection in March 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of this paper is to describe the protocol for a randomised controlled trial (RCT) designed to investigate genetic and clinical predictors of treatment response to SSRIs and NaRIs in depressive illness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is a multi-centred randomised controlled trial (shown in figure 1) in which patients with depression, recruited in primary care, were randomly allocated to either an NaRI (Reboxetine) or an SSRI (Citalopram).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18498636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2426669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is being conducted in three centres within the UK; Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000962> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial in primary care in Bristol, Birmingham and Newcastle, United Kingdom, in which adults aged 18–74 with a new episode of depression (an ICD-10 depressive episode and a Beck Depression Inventory score of at least 15), recruited from September 2005, were randomly allocated to citalopram or reboxetine to identify genetic and clinical predictors of response to antidepressant treatment.")

