AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3859856/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases were 3242 women with incident, histologically confirmed breast cancer in two major hospitals interviewed between 2001 and 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3859856/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The parent study was the Seoul Breast Cancer Study (SeBCS), which is a multicenter case-control study of incident breast cancer patients and controls recruited from hospitals or the community that has been conducted beginning in 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4998747/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants gave written informed consent at the time of enrollment, and face-to-face interviews with trained interviewers were conducted using a structured questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4998747/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases (N = 4601) consisted of women diagnosed with breast cancer admitted to 3 university hospitals in Seoul from 2001 to 2007, which accounts for about 15% to 18% of the total treated breast cancer patients in Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4998747/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls (N = 4647) were recruited from health examinees without cancers in the same hospitals as the cases or in community health screening programs in urban areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22452962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24349656") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27057831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8156547/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a multicenter case-control study, 4040 women with histologically confirmed breast cancer were recruited between 2001 and 2007 from the Seoul National University Hospital and the Asan Medical Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000966> "A multicentre case-control study of female breast cancer conducted in Seoul, South Korea, since 1995, which recruited women with histologically confirmed incident breast cancer at university hospitals in Seoul, among them Seoul National University Hospital and Asan Medical Center, and cancer-free controls from health examinees at the same hospitals or in community health screening programmes, collecting risk-factor information by face-to-face interviews with a structured questionnaire.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2474696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were identified within ∼1 month of diagnosis by the Northern California Cancer Center's rapid case ascertainment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4136881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based case-control study of NHL (2,055 cases, 2,081 controls) that included incident cases diagnosed from 2001 through 2006 was conducted in the San Francisco Bay Area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4136881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood and/or buccal specimens were collected from eligible cases and controls that participated in the laboratory portion of the study (participation rates, 87% and 89%, respectively).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4136881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, eligible patients were identified through the cancer registry and met the following criteria at diagnosis: aged 20–85 years, resident of one of the six Bay Area counties and able to complete an in-person interview in English.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4136881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were identified by random digit dial and random sampling of Center for Medicare and Medicaid lists, met the same eligibility criteria as cases with the exception of NHL diagnosis, and were frequency-matched to patients by age in five-year age groups, sex and county of residence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18636124") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25133503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4136881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To confirm NHL diagnosis and for consistent classification of NHL subtypes using the WHO classification, the study’s expert hematopathologist re-reviewed patient diagnostic pathology materials (including diagnostic slides, pathology, immunohistochemistry and flow cytometry reports) for >98% of consenting cases") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000967> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the San Francisco Bay Area, California, that enrolled residents of six Bay Area counties aged 20-85 with incident non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from 2001 through 2006, identified through the cancer registry by rapid case ascertainment, and controls found by random-digit dialling and from Medicare lists, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and county, with in-person interviews, blood or buccal specimens and expert re-review of the cases' pathology.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0006322321015705-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Janssen lifetime suicide attempt cohort consisted of subjects of European ancestry and was drawn from multiple clinical trial samples (NCT00044681, NCT00397033, NCT00412373, NCT00334126, NCT01193153,NCT00094926)conductedbyJanssenResearch&Development,LLCaswellhealthycontrol samples from NINDS Human Genetics Repository") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> "A case-control sample for lifetime suicide attempt of people of European ancestry, drawn from participants of six clinical trials conducted by Janssen Research & Development, with clinician-diagnosed major depressive disorder, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder or bipolar disorder, and from control samples of the NINDS Human Genetics Repository at the Coriell Institute and of BioIVT, with lifetime suicide-attempt history taken from clinical interview and medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0006322321015705-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical diagnosis of MDD, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, and bipolar disorder in Janssen clinical studies were based on expert clinician interviews conducted using DSM-IV-TR criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> "A case-control sample for lifetime suicide attempt of people of European ancestry, drawn from participants of six clinical trials conducted by Janssen Research & Development, with clinician-diagnosed major depressive disorder, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder or bipolar disorder, and from control samples of the NINDS Human Genetics Repository at the Coriell Institute and of BioIVT, with lifetime suicide-attempt history taken from clinical interview and medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0006322321015705-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The lifetime suicide attempt history was based on detailed clinical interview and medical records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> "A case-control sample for lifetime suicide attempt of people of European ancestry, drawn from participants of six clinical trials conducted by Janssen Research & Development, with clinician-diagnosed major depressive disorder, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder or bipolar disorder, and from control samples of the NINDS Human Genetics Repository at the Coriell Institute and of BioIVT, with lifetime suicide-attempt history taken from clinical interview and medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0006322321015705-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "samples from NINDS Human Genetics Repository (neurologically normal Caucasian control panel NDPT020, NDPT079, NDPT084, NDPT090, NDPT093, NDPT094, NDPT095, NDPT096, NDPT098, and NDPT099) managed by Coriell Institute for Medical Research (Camden, NJ) and from BioIVT (Westbury, NY).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> "A case-control sample for lifetime suicide attempt of people of European ancestry, drawn from participants of six clinical trials conducted by Janssen Research & Development, with clinician-diagnosed major depressive disorder, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder or bipolar disorder, and from control samples of the NINDS Human Genetics Repository at the Coriell Institute and of BioIVT, with lifetime suicide-attempt history taken from clinical interview and medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8851871/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Janssen (EUR) 255 1684") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000968> "A case-control sample for lifetime suicide attempt of people of European ancestry, drawn from participants of six clinical trials conducted by Janssen Research & Development, with clinician-diagnosed major depressive disorder, schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder or bipolar disorder, and from control samples of the NINDS Human Genetics Repository at the Coriell Institute and of BioIVT, with lifetime suicide-attempt history taken from clinical interview and medical records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4008818/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In December 2009, a group of researchers expert in large-scale neuroimaging or large-scale genetics studies formed a network called “Enhancing NeuroImaging Genetics through Meta-Analysis” or ENIGMA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4008818/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Working groups (WGs) were formed to understand the effects on the brain of bipolar disorder, major depressive disorder (MDD), schizophrenia, by pooling and comparing data from many neuroimaging centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24399358+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ENIGMA's first project was a genome-wide association study identifying common variants in the genome associated with hippocampal volume or intracranial volume.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24399358+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Enhancing NeuroImaging Genetics through Meta-Analysis (ENIGMA) Consortium is a collaborative network of researchers working together on a range of large-scale studies that integrate data from 70 institutions worldwide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7083923/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ENIGMA’s genetic studies are now analyzing imaging and genetics data from more than 50,000 people to uncover genetic markers that most robustly associated with brain structure and function, or imaging derived neurobiological traits related to various disease conditions") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399358") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://enigma.ini.usc.edu/about-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32198361") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32198361+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This review summarizes the last decade of work by the ENIGMA (Enhancing NeuroImaging Genetics through Meta Analysis) Consortium, a global alliance of over 1400 scientists across 43 countries, studying the human brain in health and disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000969> "An international collaborative network of neuroimaging and genetics researchers at institutions worldwide, organised into working groups, that pools and meta-analyses brain MRI and genetic data from many sites, including patient populations, to find genetic and other factors that affect brain structure and function in health and disease; its first project was a genome-wide association study of hippocampal and intracranial volume.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230374/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the baseline survey, we selected a representative sample of 7200 residents of Tirschenreuth aged 14 years and older by means of a sex- and municipality-stratified random sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230374/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The county of Tirschenreuth, located in the northeastern part of Bavaria immediately adjacent to the Czech Republic, is known as one of the hot spots of SARS-CoV2 spread in Germany during spring and early summer 2020") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8230374/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TiKoCo was designed as prospective cohort study with a baseline survey to determine the SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence in the county of Tirschenreuth and two follow-up investigations four and nine months after baseline to monitor its temporal development, focusing on the durability of antibody responses, incidence of new infections, and potential secondary infections.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34200766+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To estimate seroprevalence, underreported infections, and IFR for the Tirschenreuth population aged ≥14 years in June/July 2020, we conducted a population-based study including home visits for the elderly, and analyzed 4203 participants for SARS-CoV-2 antibodies via three antibody tests.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35746640+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Herein, we provide results from a prospective population-based longitudinal follow-up (FU) SARS-CoV-2 serosurveillance study in Tirschenreuth, the county which was hit hardest in Germany in spring 2020 and early 2021.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34200766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35746640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35746640+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of 4203 individuals aged 14 years or older enrolled at baseline (BL, June 2020), 3546 participated at FU1 (November 2020) and 3391 at FU2 (April 2021).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000970> "A prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants aged 14 or older of the county of Tirschenreuth in north-eastern Bavaria, Germany, one of the German counties hardest hit by SARS-CoV-2 in spring 2020, randomly selected with stratification by sex and municipality, who gave blood samples and questionnaires at a baseline survey in June-July 2020 and at follow-ups in November 2020 and April 2021, to determine SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence and its course over time, including undetected infections, the durability of antibody responses and new infections.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6185853/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Amsterdam Cohort Studies (ACS) on HIV was initiated in 1984, and is an open, prospective cohort study among MSM [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6185853/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The authors gratefully acknowledge the Amsterdam Cohort Studies (ACS) on HIV infection and AIDS, which is a collaboration between the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, the Academic Medical Center of the University of Amsterdam, Sanquin Blood Supply Foundation, Medical Center Jan van Goyen, and the HIV Focus Center of the DC-Clinics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7789277/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These findings were based on data from the Amsterdam Cohort Studies (ACS), which had been established in 1985, with follow-up now spanning over three decades, and closed in 2016 [2].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33407562+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this manuscript, we describe how the Amsterdam Cohort Studies (ACS) among people who use drugs (PWUD) was conceived within the context of the Dutch HR approach, including the challenges scientists faced while establishing this cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9586643+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Amsterdam Cohort Studies (ACS) on HIV infection and AIDS are a collaborative effort between the Academic Medical Centre (departments of Retrovirology and Internal Medicine), the Central Laboratory of Netherlands Red Cross Blood Transfusion Service, and the Amsterdam Municipal Health Service.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30312336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407562") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9586643") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9586643+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aims of the ACS are to study the prevalence, incidence, and risk factors for HIV infection and AIDS, to study the natural history of HIV-1 infection, to carry out intervention studies, and to evaluate prevention programs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000971> "A prospective cohort study of HIV infection and AIDS in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, a collaboration of the Public Health Service of Amsterdam, Amsterdam University Medical Centers, Sanquin Blood Supply and other partners, which since 1984 has followed an open cohort of men who have sex with men and from 1985 until 2016 followed a cohort of people who use drugs, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of HIV infection and AIDS and the natural history of HIV-1 infection, and to carry out intervention studies and evaluate prevention programmes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-02072-3/MediaObjects/41588_2024_2072_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is a multi-study case control collection at the Broad institute focused on cardiovascular diseases including atrial fibrillation, mitral valve prolapse, Atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia (AVNRT), Supraventricular tachycardia (SVT) and Bradyarrhythmia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972> "A multi-study case–control collection at the Broad Institute, an extension of the Broad AF study, focused on cardiovascular diseases including atrial fibrillation, mitral valve prolapse, atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia, supraventricular tachycardia and bradyarrhythmia, whose samples' DNA was imported to the Broad and jointly genotyped. It was funded as part of a collaboration between the Broad Institute and Bayer AG.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-02072-3/MediaObjects/41588_2024_2072_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Broad CVDi study is an extension of the Broad AF study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972> "A multi-study case–control collection at the Broad Institute, an extension of the Broad AF study, focused on cardiovascular diseases including atrial fibrillation, mitral valve prolapse, atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia, supraventricular tachycardia and bradyarrhythmia, whose samples' DNA was imported to the Broad and jointly genotyped. It was funded as part of a collaboration between the Broad Institute and Bayer AG.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-02072-3/MediaObjects/41588_2024_2072_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Broad Cardiovascular Disease Initiative Study was funded as part of a collaboration between the Broad Institute and Bayer AG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972> "A multi-study case–control collection at the Broad Institute, an extension of the Broad AF study, focused on cardiovascular diseases including atrial fibrillation, mitral valve prolapse, atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia, supraventricular tachycardia and bradyarrhythmia, whose samples' DNA was imported to the Broad and jointly genotyped. It was funded as part of a collaboration between the Broad Institute and Bayer AG.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-02072-3/MediaObjects/41588_2024_2072_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DNA for each sample was imported to the Broad and jointly genotyped on the Infinium PsychArray-24 v1.2 array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000972> "A multi-study case–control collection at the Broad Institute, an extension of the Broad AF study, focused on cardiovascular diseases including atrial fibrillation, mitral valve prolapse, atrioventricular nodal reentrant tachycardia, supraventricular tachycardia and bradyarrhythmia, whose samples' DNA was imported to the Broad and jointly genotyped. It was funded as part of a collaboration between the Broad Institute and Bayer AG.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11199195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11199195+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Canadian Multicentre Osteoporosis Study (CaMos) is a prospective cohort study which will measure the incidence and prevalence of osteoporosis and fractures, and the effect of putative risk factors, in a random sample of 10,061 women and men aged > or = 25 years recruited in approximately equal numbers in nine centers across Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 25 years and older, recruited in 1995–1997 by random telephone contact from within 50 km of nine regional centres across Canada, and followed with annual mailed questionnaires, repeated interviews and bone density measurements to study osteoporosis and fractures; a youth cohort aged 16–24 was added in 2004–2006.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40560400") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40560400+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Medical and lifestyle history, including self-reported physical activity, was obtained by interview at baseline, year 5 and year 10.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 25 years and older, recruited in 1995–1997 by random telephone contact from within 50 km of nine regional centres across Canada, and followed with annual mailed questionnaires, repeated interviews and bone density measurements to study osteoporosis and fractures; a youth cohort aged 16–24 was added in 2004–2006.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A follow up mailed questionnaire was completed annually.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 25 years and older, recruited in 1995–1997 by random telephone contact from within 50 km of nine regional centres across Canada, and followed with annual mailed questionnaires, repeated interviews and bone density measurements to study osteoporosis and fractures; a youth cohort aged 16–24 was added in 2004–2006.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Bone density was measured using DXA (dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry) at the lumbar spine and hip, and ultrasound of the shin and wrist were taken.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 25 years and older, recruited in 1995–1997 by random telephone contact from within 50 km of nine regional centres across Canada, and followed with annual mailed questionnaires, repeated interviews and bone density measurements to study osteoporosis and fractures; a youth cohort aged 16–24 was added in 2004–2006.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://camos.org/protocol/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men and women, aged 25 years and older, recruited from 1995 to 1997, residing within a 50 km radius of one of nine designated clinical centres, contacted at random by phone.Youth cohort: men and women, aged 16-24 recruited from 2004-2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000973> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 25 years and older, recruited in 1995–1997 by random telephone contact from within 50 km of nine regional centres across Canada, and followed with annual mailed questionnaires, repeated interviews and bone density measurements to study osteoporosis and fractures; a youth cohort aged 16–24 was added in 2004–2006.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,958 participants were enrolled from November 2013 to May 2016 at the Severance Hospital in Seoul, Republic of Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, CMERC-HI is a prospective cohort study aimed at developing more specific preventive strategies for patients with a high risk of CVD (clinicaltrials.gov NCT02003781).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People aged > 20 years who met at least one of the inclusion criteria were enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "high-risk patients with hypertension [estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) > 60 mL/min/1.73 m2) with target organ damage, or eGFR ≤ 60 mL/min/1.73 m2]; patients with diabetes mellitus with albuminuria; anuric patients with end-stage renal disease (ESRD) who were undergoing dialysis;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "patients with rheumatoid arthritis aged > 40 years and taking methotrexate and steroid; patients with atrial fibrillation with CHA2DS2-VASc score ≥ 1; and kidney transplant recipients at > 3 months after transplantation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28740058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5827083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "relatives of patients with acute myocardial infarction (men < 55 years old; women < 65 years old); patients with asymptomatic atherosclerotic CVD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000974> "A prospective cohort of adults at high risk of cardiovascular disease, enrolled from November 2013 at Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, to develop preventive strategies for high-risk patients. Participants qualify through high-risk hypertension, diabetes with albuminuria, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, asymptomatic atherosclerotic disease, rheumatoid arthritis treated with methotrexate and steroids, atrial fibrillation, a kidney transplant, or being a relative of a patient with early acute myocardial infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Longitudinal data were obtained from electronic medical records or abstracted from the patients’ paper records, retrospectively before 2004 and prospectively after January 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975> "A cohort of patients with cystic fibrosis enrolled from January 2004 at participating CF centres across France to study modifier genes of the disease, with longitudinal clinical data abstracted from medical records retrospectively before 2004 and collected prospectively since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with CF treated in 38 participating CF centers between January 2004 and January 2017 were enrolled in the French CF Modifier Gene Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975> "A cohort of patients with cystic fibrosis enrolled from January 2004 at participating CF centres across France to study modifier genes of the disease, with longitudinal clinical data abstracted from medical records retrospectively before 2004 and collected prospectively since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In France, patients were recruited from 48 CF centers, and phenotypic information was available for 2,898 patients older than 6 years of age; further, only patients with both parents born in European countries were considered (n=2,627).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975> "A cohort of patients with cystic fibrosis enrolled from January 2004 at participating CF centres across France to study modifier genes of the disease, with longitudinal clinical data abstracted from medical records retrospectively before 2004 and collected prospectively since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30058245") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this manuscript, we have extended our study of CF gene modifiers by testing 2,921 additional patients from North America (n=1,699) and France (n=1,222).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000975> "A cohort of patients with cystic fibrosis enrolled from January 2004 at participating CF centres across France to study modifier genes of the disease, with longitudinal clinical data abstracted from medical records retrospectively before 2004 and collected prospectively since.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the German Dupuytren study cohort, blood samples were collected from case subjects from Germany and Switzerland by the German Dupuytren Study Group13 and DNA was extracted with standard procedures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren's disease from Germany and Switzerland who had undergone surgical treatment for it, whose blood samples were collected by the German Dupuytren Study Group for genetic studies of the disease, with population controls taken from the PopGen and KORA studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all cohorts, the DD-affected case subjects were individuals who had undergone surgical treatment for their disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren's disease from Germany and Switzerland who had undergone surgical treatment for it, whose blood samples were collected by the German Dupuytren Study Group for genetic studies of the disease, with population controls taken from the PopGen and KORA studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the replication phase, we genotyped 45 SNPs with p ≤ 1 × 10−5 in the discovery set, in a total of 4,041 case subjects and 8,251 control subjects from the UK, the Netherlands, and Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren's disease from Germany and Switzerland who had undergone surgical treatment for it, whose blood samples were collected by the German Dupuytren Study Group for genetic studies of the disease, with population controls taken from the PopGen and KORA studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German cohort consisted of 768 case subjects from the German Dupuytren Study and 1,353 control subjects from the PopGen and KORA studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000976> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren's disease from Germany and Switzerland who had undergone surgical treatment for it, whose blood samples were collected by the German Dupuytren Study Group for genetic studies of the disease, with population controls taken from the PopGen and KORA studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000977> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000977>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6039372/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, all patients fulfilled the AD DSM-IV criteria and were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatry and addiction medicine departments of psychiatric hospitals participating in the German addiction research network.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000977> "A case–control sample of men of German ancestry with severe alcohol dependence requiring hospitalisation, recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatry and addiction medicine departments of psychiatric hospitals in the German addiction research network, together with population-based controls, assembled for genetic studies of alcohol dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6039372/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The target sample comprised 1333 male patients with German ancestry having severe AD requiring hospitalization and 1307 population-based controls, previously described in Treutlein et al.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000977> "A case–control sample of men of German ancestry with severe alcohol dependence requiring hospitalisation, recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatry and addiction medicine departments of psychiatric hospitals in the German addiction research network, together with population-based controls, assembled for genetic studies of alcohol dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29901528") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6039372/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We calculated MDD-PRS in the GESGA sample using the PGC-MDD2 results following previously published methods (Ripke et al., 2014).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000977> "A case–control sample of men of German ancestry with severe alcohol dependence requiring hospitalisation, recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatry and addiction medicine departments of psychiatric hospitals in the German addiction research network, together with population-based controls, assembled for genetic studies of alcohol dependence.")

