AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For eligibility in the PCL WP5 genetic study, the following inclusion criteria were applied: (1) patients were younger than age 18 years at cancer diagnosis;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, the first international GWAS of cisplatin-induced hearing loss sets out to identify novel allelic variants in the largest European cohort assembled for such a genome-wide pharmacogenetics association study so far.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patient recruitment started in January 2015 and final inclusion was October 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were recruited through a network of 14 institutions from 7 countries: Switzerland, Italy, Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria, and the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These were (1) cancer treatment included upfront cisplatin, either cisplatin as the single platinum drug throughout the entire course of treatment or change from cisplatin to carboplatin during treatment, and (2) no radiotherapy administration to the brain or inner ear (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30888333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6444213/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WP4b used a subset of research subjects from WP5 and aimed to identify additional genetic risk markers of hearing loss by GWAS with better control of nongenetic risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000988> "A subgroup of the PanCareLIFE ototoxicity genetics study made up of patients diagnosed with cancer before age 18 who were treated with upfront cisplatin and had no radiotherapy to the brain or inner ear, recruited in 2015–2017 through data providers in Switzerland, Italy, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Germany, Austria and the Netherlands for a genome-wide association study of cisplatin-induced hearing loss.")

