AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The African American-Diabetes Heart Study (AA-DHS) is assessing ethnic differences and inherited factors that contribute to the development of CP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3061609") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, several studies are in the development stage, including an extension of the AA-DHS to encompass cerebrovascular disease and cognition (AA-DHS-Mind).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21409311+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A second, parallel study, the African American DHS, has expanded the sample of African Americans to investigate marked racial differences in subclinical CVD between European Americans and African Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8136717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AA-DHS includes African Americans with T2D recruited from two Wake Forest School of Medicine (WFSM) studies: the family-based Diabetes Heart Study (DHS) and unrelated individuals in the AA-DHS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8136717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AA-DHS started after DHS and enrolled unrelated African Americans using identical inclusion criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19825824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21409311") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34014961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8136717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The African American-Diabetes Heart Study (AA-DHS) was designed to investigate biologic relationships between vitamin D and its metabolites, subclinical atherosclerosis, and skeletal health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000990> "A study at Wake Forest School of Medicine that, after the family-based Diabetes Heart Study and in parallel with it, enrolled unrelated African Americans with type 2 diabetes under the same inclusion criteria and analyses them together with that study's African American participants, to investigate ethnic differences in and inherited contributions to calcified atherosclerotic plaque and related traits such as bone density, vitamin D and, in its MIND extension, brain structure and cognition.")

