AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28406166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5566649/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This medical check‐up is provided to general residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, and is specifically designed to evaluate ageing‐related disorders, including atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function, and mild cognitive impairment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000991> "A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, who since 2006 have attended the health check-up programme of the Anti-aging Center at Ehime University Hospital, designed to evaluate ageing-related disorders such as atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function and mild cognitive impairment, and who are followed in the Japan Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP), a longitudinal study of factors related to cardiovascular disease, dementia and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28406166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41440-018-0020-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AASC includes apparently healthy, middle-aged to elderly participants in the medical check-up program at the Ehime University Hospital Anti-aging Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000991> "A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, who since 2006 have attended the health check-up programme of the Anti-aging Center at Ehime University Hospital, designed to evaluate ageing-related disorders such as atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function and mild cognitive impairment, and who are followed in the Japan Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP), a longitudinal study of factors related to cardiovascular disease, dementia and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28406166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41440-018-0020-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP study) is a longitudinal study conducted by Ehime University Graduate School of Medicine evaluating factors related to cardiovascular disease (CVD), dementia, and death among several cohorts from the general population in Ehime Prefecture, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000991> "A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, who since 2006 have attended the health check-up programme of the Anti-aging Center at Ehime University Hospital, designed to evaluate ageing-related disorders such as atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function and mild cognitive impairment, and who are followed in the Japan Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP), a longitudinal study of factors related to cardiovascular disease, dementia and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28406166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10821963/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 2244 community residents who participated in the health check-up program between February 2006 and March 2023") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000991> "A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, who since 2006 have attended the health check-up programme of the Anti-aging Center at Ehime University Hospital, designed to evaluate ageing-related disorders such as atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function and mild cognitive impairment, and who are followed in the Japan Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP), a longitudinal study of factors related to cardiovascular disease, dementia and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28371474") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28406166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29491417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38280978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10821963/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants who gave informed consent for using their clinical information obtained at the health check-up program for a longitudinal study were enrolled in the Shimanami Health Promoting Program (the J-SHIPP study) conducted by Ehime University Graduate School of Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000991> "A cohort of middle-aged and older residents of Ehime Prefecture, Japan, who since 2006 have attended the health check-up programme of the Anti-aging Center at Ehime University Hospital, designed to evaluate ageing-related disorders such as atherosclerosis, cardiovascular disease, physical function and mild cognitive impairment, and who are followed in the Japan Shimanami Health Promoting Program (J-SHIPP), a longitudinal study of factors related to cardiovascular disease, dementia and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5526098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Potential subjects are initially contacted by mail, prescreened for eligibility by telephone and those meeting criteria for one of the cohorts are referred for clinical examination, cognitive tests, Aβ PET using 18F-labeled florbetapir, MRI (structural, diffusion tensor, and resting state functional), lumbar puncture for CSF markers of tau, phosphorylated tau (p-tau181), β-amyloid (Aβ42), and blood collection for genetic analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5526098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Potential subjects identified by Veterans Administration records underwent an initial telephone screen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5526098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study now includes cohorts of Vietnam Veterans, both with and without MCI, who have histories of TBI, PTSD, and both TBI and PTSD, as well as controls without PTSD/TBI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5526098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the relationship of a past history of TBI and PTSD on the development of AD, the Department of Defense funded three proposals:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28758146+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are using biomarkers to study Vietnam Veterans with/without mild cognitive impairment with a history of at least one TBI and/or ongoing PTSD to determine whether these contribute to the development of AD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28758146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42316769") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13311454/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DoD-ADNI is a multi-site extension of ADNI designed to investigate the effects of TBI and PTSD on AD-related pathology in Vietnam-era Veterans") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000992> "A multi-site extension of the Alzheimer's Disease Neuroimaging Initiative, funded by the US Department of Defense, that enrolled Vietnam War veterans with a history of traumatic brain injury and/or ongoing post-traumatic stress disorder, with or without mild cognitive impairment, and veteran controls without either, identified mainly through Veterans Affairs records, and studies them with ADNI's clinical, cognitive, imaging and fluid biomarker methods to find whether these conditions contribute to the development of Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30287268+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ANGI recruited from the United States (US), Australia/New Zealand (ANZ), Sweden (SE), and Denmark (DK).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30287268+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment was via national registers (SE, DK); treatment centers (US, ANZ, SE, DK); and social and traditional media (US, ANZ, SE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6338222/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ANGI is an international collaboration sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the National Institute of Mental Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6338222/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples and clinical information were collected from 13,364 individuals with lifetime AN and from controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6338222/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the Anorexia Nervosa Genetics Initiative (ANGI) was to rapidly expand available samples for genome-wide association studies (GWAS) of AN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6338222/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To this end, we report the validity of an online eating disorder questionnaire (ED100K-v1) designed to capture AN cases and controls for inclusion in ANGI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000993> "An international collaboration, sponsored by the Klarman Family Foundation and the US National Institute of Mental Health, that recruited individuals with a lifetime history of anorexia nervosa and controls in the United States, Australia, New Zealand, Sweden and Denmark, through treatment centres, national registers and traditional and social media, with blood samples and an online eating-disorder questionnaire, to rapidly expand the samples available for genome-wide association studies of anorexia nervosa.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10232430+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multicentre, prospective cohort study of childhood asthma was established in three European countries; the purpose of the project is the examination of factors which modify the relationship between allergen exposure in infant life and subsequent atopy and asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10232430+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dust samples were collected from the homes of 643 infants in a single town in the UK (the first cohort) and assayed for house dust mites (Der p 1) and cat allergen (Fel d 1) concentrations by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1746847") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 18 months and starting in late 1993, we approached (without exception) every woman who presented for antenatal care to three general practices in Ashford, Kent (UK).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10292845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It included 642 children born between 1992 and 1993. Participants were recruited prenatally and followed to age 14 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10292845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung function measurements and SPT was carried out at 5, 8, and 14 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10232430") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15454651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16950296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37227431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10292845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ashford study is an unselected birth cohort study established in 1991 in Ashford, UK (Atkinson et al., 1999).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000994> "An unselected birth cohort of children born in 1992–1993 in Ashford, Kent, England, whose mothers were recruited in pregnancy from 1991 as the UK cohort of the Asthma Multicentre Infant Cohort Study, with house-dust allergen measured in infancy and follow-up by questionnaire, lung function and skin prick tests to age 14 years and a questionnaire at about age 20, to study how early-life allergen exposure and other factors relate to the development of atopy, wheeze and asthma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6405680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were drawn at each study follow‐up visit, which were predefined and scheduled every 3 months (±1 month).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6405680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were included if aged ≥18 years, capable of understanding and signing informed consent, and if CHF had been diagnosed ≥3 months ago according to European Society of Cardiology guidelines.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6405680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Bio‐SHiFT (Serial Biomarker Measurements and New Echocardiographic Techniques in Chronic Heart Failure Patients Result in Tailored Prediction of Prognosis) study is a prospective cohort study of stable patients with CHF, conducted in Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6405680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We studied the prognostic value of temporal patterns of 14 cardiac remodeling biomarker candidates in stable patients with CHF from the Bio‐SHiFT (Serial Biomarker Measurements and New Echocardiographic Techniques in Chronic Heart Failure Patients Result in Tailored Prediction of Prognosis) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38045440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10689916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between August 2011 and January 2018, a total of 398 patients with CHF were enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30760105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01851538?fields=protocolSection.identificationModule,protocolSection.statusModule,protocolSection.descriptionModule,protocolSection.designModule,protocolSection.contactsLocationsModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38597740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11346355/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 173 patients with HFrEF, we performed 6-monthly echocardiography and trimonthly blood sampling during a median follow-up of 2.7 (inter-quartile range: 2.5–2.8) years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000995> "A prospective multicentre cohort of clinically stable adult outpatients with chronic heart failure, enrolled from 2011 at Erasmus MC, Rotterdam, and Northwest Clinics, Alkmaar, the Netherlands, and seen every three months for blood sampling and clinical assessment, with echocardiography in a subset, to assess whether serial measurements of biomarkers can track disease progression and predict prognosis in individual patients.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BoSCO | Bonn Study of COVID Genetics | Germany | EUR | Initial discovery (Data Freeze 4)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA from all participating individuals with or without long COVID as well as the population-based controls were genotyped on a GSAv3.0 array (Illumina), as part of the main COVID-19 analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In September 2021 we started to sent out a specific questionnaire on „Long COVID“ to those individuals that had given recontacting consent and whose primary infection was > 3 months back.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to be eligible for participation, individuals have to be at least 18 years old and have to have been infected with SARS-CoV-2 as confirmed by diagnostic testing (qPCR or antibody testing).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BoSCO study continuously recruits individuals from the general population through public announcements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02100-w/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2100_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Upon enrollment in the BoSCO study, participants are sent an initial basic questionnaire comprising > 70 questions on demographics, pre-existing conditions, and details on infection and disease course.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000996> "A study run by the Institute of Human Genetics, University of Bonn, Germany, that continuously recruits adults with SARS-CoV-2 infection confirmed by PCR or antibody testing from the general population through public announcements, collecting questionnaires on demographics, pre-existing conditions and the course of infection (and, from September 2021, on long COVID) and DNA for genotyping, to study host genetic factors in COVID-19.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a disease-oriented biobank based on high-quality biosamples and clinical data of hospitalized and non-hospitalized SARS-CoV-2 PCR positive and negative individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BQC19 is a multicentric biobanking infrastructure composed of a network of 11 hospitals in Québec and their five partnering academic institutions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For adults who have consented to participate in BQC19 but have not been hospitalized, a 60 mL of blood is drawn at each of the scheduled follow-up visits approximately in months 1, 3, 6, 12, 18 and 24.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "On March 26, 2020, the Fonds de recherche du Québec—Santé (FRQS) and Génome Québec announced the launch of a COVID-19 Québec Biobank program, named BQC19.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BQC19 has been designed as a cohort that includes SARS-CoV-2 PCR negative controls to prospectively study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34010280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8133500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The “Biobanque québécoise de la COVID-19” (BQC19) is a pan–provincial initiative undertaken in Québec, Canada to enable the collection, storage and sharing of samples and data related to the COVID-19 crisis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000997> "A province-wide biobank and prospective cohort in Québec, Canada, launched in March 2020 by the Fonds de recherche du Québec–Santé and Génome Québec, which recruits through a network of Québec hospitals adults and children with PCR-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, both hospitalised and non-hospitalised, and PCR-negative controls, with longitudinal biosamples and clinical data, to study the clinical and biological determinants of COVID-19 clinical trajectories.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10027502+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Childhood Asthma Management Program (CAMP) is a multicenter, randomized, double-masked clinical trial designed to determine the long-term effects of three inhaled treatments for mild to moderate childhood asthma:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10027502+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "budesonide (a glucocorticoid used daily) and albuterol (a short-acting beta-agonist bronchodilator used as needed); nedocromil (a nonsteroid anti-inflammatory agent used daily) and albuterol; and placebo and albuterol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8255344/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,041 participants were enrolled in the trial between 1993 and 1995 at age 5–12 years; follow-up continued to 2012 when participants were aged 22–30 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11178010/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CAMP study was approved by the Institutional Review Board of Partners Healthcare (Partners Human Research Committee; Protocol#: 1999-P-001549/29), by all 8 CAMP clinical centers and by the CAMP Data Coordinating Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2048676/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CAMP is a multicenter North American clinical trial designed to investigate the long-term effects of inhaled antiinflammatory medications in children with mild to moderate asthma (15, 16).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2048676/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Informed assent and consent were obtained from the study participants and their parents to collect DNA for genetic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10027502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34212545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001726") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11750448/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Childhood Asthma Management Program (CAMP) clinical trial was conducted across several centers in the United States and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000998> "A multicentre, randomized, double-masked clinical trial of long-term inhaled treatment for mild to moderate asthma (budesonide, nedocromil or placebo, each with albuterol as needed) in children aged 5–12 years, who were enrolled in 1993–1995 at eight clinical centres in the United States and Canada and followed after the trial into adulthood, with a genetic ancillary study of the children and their parents.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Summary-level study results were combined by using inverse variance-weighted meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> "A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts' genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects participating in the GWAS consisted of a total of 16,388 self-identified African-American individuals from 7 population-based cohorts (ARIC, CARDIA, JHS, WHI, HANDLS, Health ABC, and GeneSTAR) that belong to the Continental Origins and Genetic Epidemiology Network (COGENT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> "A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts' genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7749437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our intent is to foster collaborations for studies of populations that are underrepresented in GWAS, increase awareness of the challenges and opportunities in studying these populations, and promote more genomic research across increasingly diverse populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> "A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts' genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7749437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COGENT-Kidney Consortium was established in 2014 to undertake trans-ethnic meta-analysis of GWAS of kidney traits in diverse populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> "A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts' genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738479") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32571486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7749437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Consortium is modelled on the COGENT Blood Pressure Consortium, which is focused on genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in individuals of African ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0000999> "A network of cohorts of African ancestry and of other populations under-represented in genome-wide association studies, whose consortia meta-analyse the cohorts' genome-wide data to find genetic variants for complex traits, such as white blood cell count, blood pressure and hypertension in African-ancestry cohorts (COGENT-BP) and kidney traits across diverse ancestries (COGENT-Kidney, established in 2014).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2443132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An initial aim of COHRA is to determine the contributions of individual, family, and community factors to oral diseases in Appalachian children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> "The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2443132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The University of Pittsburgh Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA) was established in 2000, in partnership with West Virginia University, to address this gap in our knowledge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> "The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants in COHRA1 were recruited from rural Appalachia in West Virginia and Western Pennsylvania by using a household-based recruitment protocol and using the same data collection protocols for every site.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> "The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10048401/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COHRA1 is a population-based cohort established in 2000 that recruited northern Appalachian families aiming to understand contributing factors to oral diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> "The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36981009") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10048401/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COHRA2 is a longitudinal study and has been recruiting and prospectively following pregnant white women from Pennsylvania and West Virginia and their children starting in 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001000> "The cohort studies of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, established in 2000 by the University of Pittsburgh in partnership with West Virginia University to find the factors behind poor oral health in northern Appalachia. They are a family-based etiology study (COHRA1), which recruited households in West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, and a longitudinal cohort (COHRA2), which since 2011 has recruited pregnant women in Pennsylvania and West Virginia and followed them and their children.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17463246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17463246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17463246+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed 386,731 common single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in 1464 patients with T2D and 1467 matched controls, each characterized for measures of glucose metabolism, lipids, obesity, and blood pressure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes and related quantitative traits by the Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT, Lund University and the Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research. Its participants were patients with type 2 diabetes and matched non-diabetic controls from Finland and Sweden, genotyped and characterised for glucose metabolism, lipids, obesity and blood pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17463246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2570409/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, in the genome-wide association Diabetes Genetics Initiative (DGI) Study for 19 traits, including plasma lipids, we provided evidence that the glucokinase (GCK) regulatory protein gene (GCKR) region was a novel quantitative trait locus associated with plasma triglyceride concentration (1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes and related quantitative traits by the Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT, Lund University and the Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research. Its participants were patients with type 2 diabetes and matched non-diabetic controls from Finland and Sweden, genotyped and characterised for glucose metabolism, lipids, obesity and blood pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17463246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2570409/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DGI Study material consisting of 2,931 individuals from Finland and Sweden (1,464 patients with type 2 diabetes and 1,467 nondiabetic control subjects) was ascertained as previously described (1,11,12).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes and related quantitative traits by the Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT, Lund University and the Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research. Its participants were patients with type 2 diabetes and matched non-diabetic controls from Finland and Sweden, genotyped and characterised for glucose metabolism, lipids, obesity and blood pressure.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17463246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2570409/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Diabetes Genetics Initiative of the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard, Lund University, and Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research: Genome-wide association analysis identifies loci for type 2 diabetes and triglyceride levels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001001> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes and related quantitative traits by the Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT, Lund University and the Novartis Institutes for BioMedical Research. Its participants were patients with type 2 diabetes and matched non-diabetic controls from Finland and Sweden, genotyped and characterised for glucose metabolism, lipids, obesity and blood pressure.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9179018/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analyses of the European and East Asian ancestry components of DIAMANTE have previously been reported6,10.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> "A consortium established to assemble genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes across diverse ancestry groups. It meta-analyses them within its European and East Asian ancestry components and, together with African, Hispanic and South Asian ancestry studies, in a multi-ancestry meta-regression, to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9179018/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DIAMANTE (DIAbetes Meta-ANalysis of Trans-Ethnic association studies) Consortium was established to assemble T2D GWAS across diverse ancestry groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> "A consortium established to assemble genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes across diverse ancestry groups. It meta-analyses them within its European and East Asian ancestry components and, together with African, Hispanic and South Asian ancestry studies, in a multi-ancestry meta-regression, to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9179018/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aggregated association summary statistics via multi-ancestry meta-regression, implemented in MR-MEGA15, which models allelic effect heterogeneity correlated with genetic ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> "A consortium established to assemble genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes across diverse ancestry groups. It meta-analyses them within its European and East Asian ancestry components and, together with African, Hispanic and South Asian ancestry studies, in a multi-ancestry meta-regression, to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9179018/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use the term “ancestry group” to refer to individuals with similar genetic background: European ancestry (51.1% of the total effective sample size); East Asian ancestry (28.4%); South Asian ancestry (8.3%); African ancestry, including recently admixed African American populations (6.6%); and Hispanic individuals with recent admixture of American, African, and European ancestry (5.6%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> "A consortium established to assemble genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes across diverse ancestry groups. It meta-analyses them within its European and East Asian ancestry components and, together with African, Hispanic and South Asian ancestry studies, in a multi-ancestry meta-regression, to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35551307+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fine-mapping of these signals was enhanced by the increased sample size and expanded population diversity of the multi-ancestry meta-analysis, which localized 54.4% of T2D associations to a single variant with >50% posterior probability.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001002> "A consortium established to assemble genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes across diverse ancestry groups. It meta-analyses them within its European and East Asian ancestry components and, together with African, Hispanic and South Asian ancestry studies, in a multi-ancestry meta-regression, to discover and fine-map type 2 diabetes loci.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5012582/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DRIVE acknowledges the following GWASs and investigators that shared genome-wide summary data as part of the breast-cancer GWAS meta-analysis:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> "A breast cancer genetics consortium, one of the five projects funded in 2010 under the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) post-GWAS initiative. It meta-analysed genome-wide summary data shared by existing breast cancer GWAS and genotyped breast cancer cases and controls on the OncoArray, to replicate known and find new breast cancer susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Discovery, Biology, and Risk of Inherited Variants in Breast Cancer (DRIVE) was one of five projects funded in 2010 as part of the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) initiative (http://epi.grants.cancer.gov/gameon/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> "A breast cancer genetics consortium, one of the five projects funded in 2010 under the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) post-GWAS initiative. It meta-analysed genome-wide summary data shared by existing breast cancer GWAS and genotyped breast cancer cases and controls on the OncoArray, to replicate known and find new breast cancer susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GAME-ON's overall goal was to foster an intra-disciplinary and collaborative approach to the translation of promising research leads deriving from the initial wave of cancer GWAS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> "A breast cancer genetics consortium, one of the five projects funded in 2010 under the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) post-GWAS initiative. It meta-analysed genome-wide summary data shared by existing breast cancer GWAS and genotyped breast cancer cases and controls on the OncoArray, to replicate known and find new breast cancer susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specific goals included replication of previous GWAS findings and identification of new susceptibility loci through meta analyses of existing GWAS data and fine mapping of identified loci to better pinpoint causal variants; and identify germline variants that are associated with risk of multiple cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> "A breast cancer genetics consortium, one of the five projects funded in 2010 under the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) post-GWAS initiative. It meta-analysed genome-wide summary data shared by existing breast cancer GWAS and genotyped breast cancer cases and controls on the OncoArray, to replicate known and find new breast cancer susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27598322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001265/phs001265.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001265.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DRIVE data included under this dbGAP submission include OncoArray data from 60,015 breast cancer cases and controls genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research (CIDR), University of Cambridge, National Cancer Institute, University of Copenhagen, University of Southern California and Mayo Clinic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001003> "A breast cancer genetics consortium, one of the five projects funded in 2010 under the NCI's Genetic Associations and Mechanisms in Oncology (GAME-ON) post-GWAS initiative. It meta-analysed genome-wide summary data shared by existing breast cancer GWAS and genotyped breast cancer cases and controls on the OncoArray, to replicate known and find new breast cancer susceptibility loci.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5972779/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPIC-CVD is a multi centre case-cohort study nested within the EPIC cohort designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease (CVD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5972779/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included 18 816 incident CVD cases identified between March 1991 and December 2010 in the EPIC cohort and a random subcohort of 17 634 EPIC participants was used as a reference group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9075396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among all participants with a stored blood sample (n=385 747), a total of 13 603 incident CHD cases were ascertained during follow‐up, and a random subcohort of 18 249 center‐stratified participants was selected irrespective of future disease status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9075396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we chose a case‐cohort design in EPIC to enable efficient measurement of molecular factors (eg, biomarkers of metabolism, genetics) in a reference subcohort that serves as the comparator group for incidence of several different disease outcomes, including type 2 diabetes mellitus, CHD, stroke, and cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7618008/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPIC-CVD is a case-cohort study nested in the EPIC study comprising individuals from a random sub-cohort and all other EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease and stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29844013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34796724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40099743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7618008/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In EPIC-CVD, genotyping was performed using the Human Core Exome array, Omni Exome Express array, and Illumina 660 Quad array and genotype imputation was based on the Haplotype Reference Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001004> "A case-cohort study nested within the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition, designed to investigate the determinants of cardiovascular disease. EPIC participants with incident coronary heart disease or stroke, identified from 1991 to 2010, are compared with a centre-stratified random subcohort of EPIC participants with stored blood samples, in which molecular factors, including genotypes, are measured.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1997110/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with confirmed ischemic stroke are included as probands; after their informed consent is obtained, their parents, siblings, and unaffected spouses are recruited and screened by using the proband-initiated contact method [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1997110/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conclusion, the FISSIC program is a family-based genetic study of ischemic stroke, focusing on the genetic and environmental determinants and their interactions with comprehensive strategies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1997110/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The pedigrees of ischemic stroke with clear documentation are recruited by using the proband-initiated contact method, based on the stroke registry in hospital and communities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9775185/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FISSIC is an ongoing community observational study that started in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9775185/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the baseline data from phase II of the FISSIC from December 2011 to April 2012, in which 9540 participants aged ≥40 years were recruited either in response to recruitment posters or by phone calls if their health records were available at a community health center [15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17825112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31823830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36551856") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42259975") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13582842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2005 and 2012, FISSIC recruited 3486 families, including trios and siblings, who have been followed up every 2 years to date.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001005> "A family-based study of the genetic and environmental causes of ischaemic stroke, begun in June 2005 in the Fangshan District, a rural area southwest of Beijing, China. It recruited people with ischaemic stroke as probands, with their parents and siblings, through hospital and community stroke registries, and in a second phase in 2011–2012 enrolled participants aged 40 or over through posters and community health centre records. The families enrolled between 2005 and 2012 are followed up every two years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30739198+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established the international FTLD-TDP whole-genome sequencing consortium to thoroughly characterize the known genetic causes of FTLD-TDP and identify novel genetic risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12032271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase II, additional WGS of 507 patients with FTLD-TDP, svPPA, bvFTD/ALS, and 322 controls free of neurodegenerative disorders was performed at USUHS sequencing center or Mayo Clinic Rochester using the TruSeq DNA PCR-Free Library preparation Kit (Illumina), followed by Whole Genome Sequencing by synthesis (SBS) chemistry on HiSeq X Illumina platform using the HiSeq X Ten Reag. kit v2.5.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12032271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 985 pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP or presumed FTLD-TDP patients clinically presenting with svPPA or bvFTD/ALS, as well as 3153 neurologically normal controls passed all QC measures (Supplementary Data 25).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12032271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One of the most striking conclusions from this phase II FTLD-TDP GWAS is the distinct association signals among FTLD-TDP pathological subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12032271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To validate and identify new genetic risk factors, we doubled the original sample size of the FTLD-TDP WGS consortium by not only sequencing more pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP patients but also including clinically defined FTLD subtypes enriched for specific FTLD-TDP pathological subtypes at autopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30739198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40280976") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40280976+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report our comprehensive genome-wide association study as part of the International FTLD-TDP Whole-Genome Sequencing Consortium, including 985 patients and 3,153 controls compiled from 26 institutions/brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia, and meta-analysis with the Dementia-seq cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001006> "An international consortium, established to characterise the known genetic causes of frontotemporal lobar degeneration with TDP-43 inclusions (FTLD-TDP) and to find new genetic risk factors for it and its pathological subtypes. It whole-genome sequences people with pathologically confirmed FTLD-TDP (and, from its second phase, clinically diagnosed FTLD subtypes enriched for FTLD-TDP) and neurologically normal controls, compiled from institutions and brain banks in North America, Europe and Australia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1182024") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Full pedigree development and biospecimen collection were performed on 771 families with three or more first-degree relatives affected with lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148967/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency matched to cases on age (5-year groups), sex and smoking status as closely as possible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148967/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GELCC enrolled lung cancer cases with a family history of lung cancer from the following data collection sites: Karmanos Cancer Institute/Wayne State University, University of Cincinnati College of Medicine, Mayo Clinic, Medical College of Toledo, and Louisiana State University Health Sciences Center—New Orleans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6148967/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study questionnaire included basic demographics, health history including history of other lung diseases, smoking history, and family history of cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13259588/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GELCC is a U.S.-based research network studying FLC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of this research application is to identify genetic factors that confer a high risk for lung cancer and to characterize the mechanisms by which these factors influence lung cancer risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15272417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29924316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41390056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.gelcc.org/node/3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also have phenotype, genotype and smoking data available on over 700 unaffected individuals who are frequency matched to the cases on age and gender, most of whom are current or former smokers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001007> "A family study of lung cancer in the United States in which the recruitment sites of the Genetic Epidemiology of Lung Cancer Consortium enrolled lung cancer patients with a family history of the disease, relatives in families with several affected members, and unaffected controls frequency-matched to the cases on age and sex, collecting pedigrees, smoking histories and biospecimens to identify inherited factors that confer a high risk of lung cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35886043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12439737+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analysis of gene-treatment interactions in relation to outcomes include CHD, stroke, heart failure, and blood pressure lowering.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> "An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35886043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12439737+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenHAT is an ancillary study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial, ALLHAT, a double-blind, randomized trial of 42 418 hypertensives, 55 years of age or older, with systolic or diastolic hypertension and one or more risk factors for cardiovascular disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> "An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35886043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12439737+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics of Hypertension Associated Treatment (GenHAT) study will determine whether variants in hypertension susceptibility genes interact with antihypertensive medication to modify coronary heart disease (CHD) risk in hypertensives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> "An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35886043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3160956/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenHAT genotyped variants in several hypertension-related genes in the 39,114 ALLHAT participants with available DNA, making the study design a post-hoc subgroup analysis of a randomized clinical trial [29].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> "An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12439737") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21887284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35886043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26791477") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4956602/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were derived from the GenHAT study, an ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT).18 Both studies have been described.4, 18 Briefly, ALLHAT was a randomized, double-blind, clinical trial that was conducted from February 1994 to March 2002 in 623 North American centers in both the US and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001008> "An ancillary pharmacogenetic study of the Antihypertensive and Lipid-Lowering Treatment to Prevent Heart Attack Trial (ALLHAT), a double-blind randomised trial of antihypertensive drugs in people aged 55 or older with hypertension and at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, conducted in 1994–2002 at centres in the United States and Canada. GenHAT genotyped the ALLHAT participants with available DNA to test whether variants in hypertension genes modify the effect of the randomised treatment on coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4190389/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Norway GenKOLS study (Genetics of Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease, GSK code RES11080) and the ECLIPSE study (NCT00292552; GSK code SCO104960) were sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6662162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the patients were recruited from a hospital patient registry (n=662) and from the general population (n=250) with participants with reduced FEV1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6662162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Main inclusion criteria were age >40 years, >2.5 pack-years of smoking history, and a post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC <0.70 and FEV1<80% of the predicted (full inclusion and exclusion criteria are given in the online supplement).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7480432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenKOLS was a case–control study, and the subjects in the current analyses comprised the COPD cases only.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7480432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects in the current analyses were all participants in the GenKOLS study (Genetic COPD study) conducted between January 2003 and January 2005 in Bergen, Norway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25134640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25241909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32944202") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0321-7/MediaObjects/41588_2018_321_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with > 2.5 pack years of smoking history were recruited from Bergen, Norway; cases had pre-bronchodilator % predicted FEV1 < 80% predicted and FEV1/FVC < 0.7, while controls had normal spirometry; subjects with severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency and other lung diseases (aside from asthma) were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001009> "A genetic case-control study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease conducted in Bergen, Norway, in 2003–2005 and sponsored by GlaxoSmithKline, which enrolled current and former smokers aged 40 or older: patients with at least moderate COPD, recruited from a hospital patient registry and from the general population, and smokers with normal lung function as controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31715324+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants invited to join the study (via media campaigns) provide demographic, environmental and genetic data, and consent for medical record linkage and recontact.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31715324+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study (www.gladstudy.org.uk) recruits individuals with depression or anxiety into the NIHR Mental Health BioResource.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GLAD is led by researchers at the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) Mental Health BioResource (part of the NIHR BioResource) at King's College London, in collaboration with Queen's University Belfast, University of Edinburgh, and Cardiff University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Links to Anxiety and Depression (GLAD) Study is a project set up to support studies exploring risk factors for depression and/or anxiety.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To take part in the GLAD Study you must either: Have ever experienced anxiety or depressive disorders (with or without a medical diagnosis) Have never experienced any mental health disorder.AND you must:Be aged 16 or overLive in the United Kingdom") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31715324") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://gladstudy.org.uk/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "You will need to: 1Register on the GLAD website2 Read the information sheet and provide consent 3 Complete a 30-60 minute questionnaire 4 Complete your DNA saliva kit (for genetics research) and return it to us in the free envelope provided") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001010> "A recontactable cohort of people aged 16 or over living in the United Kingdom, run by the NIHR Mental Health BioResource at King's College London, which recruits online people with current or past depression or anxiety, and also people with no history of mental disorder, into the NIHR BioResource. Participants complete questionnaires, give saliva samples for genotyping and consent to medical record linkage and recontact, to support research on risk factors for depression and anxiety.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39792440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5293989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following on the success of a Wellcome Trust funded project Genetics of Share (goSHARE), which had successfully been run as a pilot in NHS Tayside") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> "A biobank sub-study of SHARE, the Scottish Health Research Register, in NHS Tayside and NHS Fife, Scotland, which collects, with consent, blood left over from registrants' routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics for genotyping linked to their anonymised electronic health records; it began as a Wellcome Trust-funded pilot in NHS Tayside.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39792440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5913637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GoSHARE is a parallel project which additionally aims to get permission to collect spare blood from people attending for routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics, that would otherwise to go to waste after the necessary tests had been performed [http://www.goshare.org.uk/].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> "A biobank sub-study of SHARE, the Scottish Health Research Register, in NHS Tayside and NHS Fife, Scotland, which collects, with consent, blood left over from registrants' routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics for genotyping linked to their anonymised electronic health records; it began as a Wellcome Trust-funded pilot in NHS Tayside.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39792440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10369131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GoSHARE currently comprises a biobank of ∼74,000 individuals across the National Health Service Fife and the National Health Service Tayside (19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> "A biobank sub-study of SHARE, the Scottish Health Research Register, in NHS Tayside and NHS Fife, Scotland, which collects, with consent, blood left over from registrants' routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics for genotyping linked to their anonymised electronic health records; it began as a Wellcome Trust-funded pilot in NHS Tayside.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39792440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10369131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of both cohorts provided a sample of blood for genetic analysis and informed consent to link their genetic information to anonymized electronic health records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> "A biobank sub-study of SHARE, the Scottish Health Research Register, in NHS Tayside and NHS Fife, Scotland, which collects, with consent, blood left over from registrants' routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics for genotyping linked to their anonymised electronic health records; it began as a Wellcome Trust-funded pilot in NHS Tayside.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28148535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29025058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37308106") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39792440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12453674/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genetics of the Scottish Health Research Register (GoSHARE)4 is a sub-study of the SHARE initiative where almost 75,000 individuals living in Scotland have linked EHRs and consented for genotyping analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001011> "A biobank sub-study of SHARE, the Scottish Health Research Register, in NHS Tayside and NHS Fife, Scotland, which collects, with consent, blood left over from registrants' routine clinical tests at hospital or GP clinics for genotyping linked to their anonymised electronic health records; it began as a Wellcome Trust-funded pilot in NHS Tayside.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6249284/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were 1,432 African American and Hispanic American children, ages 8 to 15 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6678051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subject recruitment and collection of phenotype data and DNA were completed for 1432 unrelated children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6678051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRaD study is a multisite, case–control study of RD in minority youth across the USA, Canada and Puerto Rico.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6678051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study is one of the first to examine the genetics of reading-related traits in an admixed population of Hispanic American and African–American children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11068914/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For reading outcomes we used the Woodcock–Johnson III - Letter-Word Identification and Word Attack47 to assess word reading accuracy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30631481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30995994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38702345") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11068914/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was part of a larger, multi-site US and Canadian collaborative Genes, Reading, and Dyslexia (GRaD) project led by Yale University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001012> "A multisite case-control study of reading disability (developmental dyslexia) in Hispanic American and African American children aged 8 to 15, led by Yale University at sites in the United States, Puerto Rico and Canada, in which the children were assessed with reading and reading-related measures and gave DNA for genetic studies of reading ability and dyslexia.")

