# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2661765/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1991 to 1998, the Principal Investigators and Co-Investigators were located at Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA, U01 MH46281; Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD, U01 MH46290; and University of Alabama at Birmingham, Birmingham, AL, U01 MH46373.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2661765/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The total sample is comprised of 437 independent families with at least two affected siblings, totaling 1,397 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9008509+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "310 families including 679 subjects with AD by NINCDS/ADRDA and/or Khachaturian criteria and 231 unaffected subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9008509+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three academic medical centers ascertained subjects from memory disorder clinics, nursing homes, and the local community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Requesting investigators receive a file of demographic and diagnostic variables necessary for genetic analysis, with accompanying documentation, access to DNA samples, a code manual listing additional clinical and demographic data, and pedigree drawings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18189239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9008509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nimh.nih.gov/about/advisory-boards-and-groups/namhc/reports/genetics-and-mental-disorders-report-of-the-national-institute-of-mental-healths-genetics-workgroup") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Initiative also enabled the establishment of a national repository of demographic, clinical, diagnostic, and genetic data from individuals with bipolar disorder, schizophrenia, or Alzheimer’s disease to aid researchers in identifying factors responsible for these disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001024> "A family study of Alzheimer's disease in the United States in which three academic medical centres (Massachusetts General Hospital, Johns Hopkins University and the University of Alabama at Birmingham) ascertained families with two or more members affected by Alzheimer's disease (mostly affected sibling pairs), together with unaffected relatives, from 1991 through memory disorder clinics, nursing homes and the community, using uniform procedures. It is the Alzheimer's disease collection of the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative, whose data and DNA are shared through the NIMH repository for genetic linkage and association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10713750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NorthShore invested in an institutional research biobank, the Genomic Health Initiative (GHI), that conducts translational, discovery research driven by the intersection of the electronic health record (EHR) and genomics data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10713750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GHI’s key operational learnings include using the EHR patient portal to streamline participant outreach, education, consenting, and automating blood collection at the next phlebotomy appointment without impeding primary care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12149594/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All studied individuals provided written or electronic informed consent to participate in GHI, including permitting access to electronic health records to extract demographic, laboratory, diagnostic, and other clinical information for research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12149594/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Germline DNA was isolated from blood samples and sequenced using low-coverage whole genome sequencing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12149594/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GHI is a US health care system–based biobank from the NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) with 16,341 participants in the currently analyzed cohort (Supplementary Table 1) [29].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38090148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40496845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41585861") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12828546/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GHI was initiated in 2014 and is ongoing where clinical information during follow-up can be extracted from the electronic health record (EHR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001025> "A healthcare-system-based research biobank of NorthShore University HealthSystem (now Endeavor Health) in Illinois, United States, started in 2014, which enrols patients of the health system who consent to give a blood sample for DNA and to linkage of their electronic health records, for translational and discovery research combining genomic and clinical data.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3043283/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LHA research team and their scientific collaborators secured MRC funding to invite study members to take part in their first adult clinic-based data collection to obtain new ageing outcomes, as well as repeat measures of health, function and life circumstances, previously collected by research nurses at home visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3043283/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing (LHA) was established in 2008 to maximize the scientific potential of the NSHD and develop it into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3637651/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NSHD is based on a social class stratified sample of 5,362 births of all singleton births that occurred within marriage in a week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3637651/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The oldest British birth cohort, the MRC National Survey of Health and Development (NSHD), recently celebrated its 65th birthday and completion of its 23rd follow-up") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5206260/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 24th and most recent follow-up, a postal questionnaire at 68 years followed by a home visit at 69 years, focused on morbidity and its consequences; and repeated functional and mental health assessments, updated reports of health and life circumstances, and collected a third blood sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21345808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23637643") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27995394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5206260/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work was supported by the UK Medical Research Council which provides core funding for the MRC National Survey of Health and Development") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001026> "A birth cohort of people born in one week in March 1946 in England, Scotland and Wales, selected as a social-class-stratified sample of the singleton births to married mothers that week and followed up repeatedly from birth into old age through home visits, questionnaires and clinic assessments. The oldest of the British national birth cohort studies, it is core-funded by the UK Medical Research Council and has been developed since 2008 by the MRC Unit for Lifelong Health and Ageing at UCL into an interdisciplinary study of ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3995281/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OIDSCS is the first prospective study to systematically determine blood counts, blood cell morphology, and GATA1 mutation status in neonates with DS with the aims of (1) identifying the population at risk of developing ML-DS; (2) defining the clinical and hematologic features associated with a mutant GATA1 clone in DS neonates; and (3) determining how best to define TAM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12391799/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each participant was followed-up from birth to 4 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12391799/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study comprised 434 newborns with DS from the ODSCS, a prospective cohort that enrolled children with DS between 2006 to 2017 from 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12391799/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address the question of why only a subset of DS newborns develop transient leukemia, we performed a comprehensive genetic epidemiology study of GATA1s mutations via whole-genome sequencing (WGS) plus targeted GATA1 sequencing of 434 children with DS in the Oxford Down Syndrome Cohort Study (ODSCS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12391799/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole-genome sequencing was performed on 434 children with DS from the Oxford DS Cohort Study previously screened for GATA1s mutations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40407036") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12278782") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples for this independent cohort were from the Oxford Down Syndrome Cohort Study (ODSCS) and includes 436 children with DS who were collected prospectively from birth, enrolled across 18 hospitals in the UK between 2006 and 2012, and with serial clinical and hematological data from birth to age 4 years") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001027> "A prospective cohort of newborns with Down syndrome enrolled at birth in 18 hospitals in the United Kingdom from 2006 to 2017, screened for GATA1 mutations and followed with serial clinical and haematological data from birth to 4 years of age, to study transient abnormal myelopoiesis, preleukaemic GATA1 mutations and the risk of myeloid leukaemia in children with Down syndrome.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7181574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The POST study began in 2018 as an extension to GENOA, with similar data collection protocol and inclusion criteria, barring participants now meeting criteria for OUD as diagnosed with the DSM-5 [12].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903683/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from 31 outpatient addiction clinics in Ontario, Canada, between May 2018 and January 2020, using the following inclusion criteria: patients diagnosed with OUD using Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition (DSM-5) criteria and receiving outpatient methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment [21].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903683/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prospective observational data used in this study were collected in the Pharmacogenetics of Opioid Substitution Treatment Response (POST) study in a collaboration between researchers at McMaster University and the clinical programs of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the POST study, patients were eligible to participate if they were 16 years or older and met the criteria for DSM-5 opioid use disorder (OUD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10724251/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the GENOA study provided a blood sample for DNA and participants in the POST study provided a saliva sample for DNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32326982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33622351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38102185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40527567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12182195/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "data for the study were collected from 54 clinical sites across Ontario, Canada, between May 2018 and January 2023.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001028> "A prospective cohort of patients aged 16 or older receiving methadone or buprenorphine–naloxone treatment for opioid use disorder at outpatient clinics of the Canadian Addiction Treatment Centres across Ontario, Canada, recruited by McMaster University researchers from May 2018 to January 2023 as an extension of the Genetics of Opioid Addiction study with a similar protocol. Participants were interviewed at entry, gave a saliva sample for DNA and were followed for up to 12 months through their medical records and urine drug screens, to study biopsychosocial and genetic factors in treatment outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02688-1/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2688_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All underwent a cardiovascular examination at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02688-1/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2688_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up assessments ceased until 2018, when the cohort was „revived“ for genotyping and a follow-up investigation was performed via mailed questionnaires in 2021.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02688-1/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2688_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For PROCAM-2, 17,312 employees were recruited in more than 50 regional companies and government authorities on a voluntary basis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02688-1/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2688_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this analysis, we used data of PROCAM-2, the study's second part in which participants were examined between 2000 and 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41380-024-02688-1/MediaObjects/41380_2024_2688_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study is a large, prospective epidemiological study of cardiovascular risk factors and diseases performed in an occupational cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38839884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11746137/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROCAM-2 Study was initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research (LIFA) at the University of Münster") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001029> "An occupational cohort of employees of regional companies and government authorities in and around Münster, Germany, who volunteered and underwent a cardiovascular examination in 2000–2007, forming the second part of the Prospective Cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) Study of cardiovascular risk factors and disease, initiated and conducted by the Leibniz Institute for Arteriosclerosis Research at the University of Münster. Follow-up lapsed until 2018, when the cohort was revived for genotyping, followed by a postal follow-up questionnaire in 2021.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6585634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At each study visit, venous blood samples are collected, permitting extraction of biomaterials such as DNA, RNA, plasma, and serum.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6585634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of writing, 18 different clinical centers participated in data collection of clinical participants, two of which additionally collect data from nonclinical (control) individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6585634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we present design and first results of the PsyCourse study (N = 891 individuals at baseline), an ongoing transdiagnostic study of the affective‐to‐psychotic continuum that combines longitudinal deep phenotyping and dimensional assessment of psychopathology with an extensive collection of biomaterial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6585634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants with a life‐time DSM‐IV diagnosis of SZ (295.10/295.20/295.30/295.60/295.90) or schizophreniform disorder (295.40), brief psychotic disorder (298.8), or SZA (295.70) constitute the group with predominantly psychotic symptoms, whereas those with a life‐time DSM‐IV diagnosis of BD (296.0x/296.4x/296.5x/296.6x/296.8x) or reMDD (296.3x) constitute the predominantly affective group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11733486/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PsyCourse Study aims to identifiy clinical, neurobiological and molecular genetic signatures of the longitudinal course of major psychiatric disorders, and comprises an extensive phenotyping battery as well as biomaterial at four equidistant time points over a period of 18 months (baseline, 6 months, 12 months, 18 months).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11733486/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from the longitudinal, naturalistic, multicentre PsyCourse Study, which was conducted in Germany and Austria (www.PsyCourse.de) from 2011 to 2019") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30070057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39721961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41398-023-02508-0") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adult participants were referred by the clinical staff or identified by querying patient registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001030> "A multicentre, naturalistic longitudinal study of adults with schizophrenia-spectrum, bipolar or recurrent depressive disorders and of healthy controls, recruited at clinical centres in Germany and Austria from 2011 to 2019 and assessed four times at six-month intervals over 18 months with deep phenotyping, dimensional ratings of psychopathology, cognitive tests and blood sampling, to identify clinical, neurobiological and genetic signatures of the course of major psychiatric disorders across the affective-to-psychotic continuum.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2002 and 2005, we re-contacted subjects from the four studies described above using a systematic procedure, as follows.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Q-MEGA brings together four population-based studies of CMM that were conducted in Queensland, Australia between 1987 and 1995 (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The QFMP was a large family and twin study initiated in 1987 to study the influence of genetic susceptibility, sunlight exposure, and their interaction in CMM etiology (Aitken et al., 1996).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The principal aim of Q-MEGA is to provide a large and well-described population-based sample of CMM cases and their families, with blood collection for genetic purposes and detailed information on sun exposure and phenotype to explore the effect that environmental and genetic factors, and their interaction, play in the etiology of CMM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This article describes the design and baseline characteristics of Q-MEGA, the Queensland study of Melanoma: Environmental and Genetic Associations, which followed-up four population-based samples of CMM patients in Queensland, including children, adolescents, men aged over 50, and a large sample of adult cases and their families, including twins.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18361720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Updated data on environmental and phenotypic risk factors, and 2,777 blood samples were collected from interviewed participants as well as a subset of relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001031> "A population-based study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, that brings together four earlier population-based studies of melanoma patients conducted in 1987–1995: the Queensland Familial Melanoma Project of adult cases and their families, including twins, and studies of melanoma in children, in adolescents and in men over 50. Their participants and some relatives were re-contacted in 2002–2005 for telephone interviews on sun exposure and phenotype and for blood samples, to investigate genetic and environmental factors, and their interaction, in the aetiology of melanoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8795929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This prospectively recruited cohort comprised consecutive ambulatory patients referred to clinic or for a cardiovascular magnetic resonance (CMR) scan at The Royal Brompton Hospital between 2009 and 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data collected may include clinical examination data (e.g. demographic information, height, weight, blood pressure, ECG, laboratory tests), cardiovascular imaging, and patient questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family members of Biobank participants may also be invited to donate samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Standard sample collection includes whole blood, serum and plasma, but other sample types including, cardiac tissue, saliva and urine may also be stored.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cardiovascular Research Centre Biobank collects samples and associated clinical data from adult and paediatric patients attending Royal Brompton & Harefield NHS Trust for investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35086919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38032570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/royal-brompton-harefield-cardiovascular-research-centre-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary purpose of the biobank is the identification of new genes or biomarkers linked to cardiovascular disease to aid in the diagnosis and provide information on the prognosis of both common and rare cardiovascular diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001032> "A research biobank of the Royal Brompton and Harefield hospitals in London, United Kingdom, which since 2009 has collected blood and other samples, including cardiac tissue, with clinical, imaging and follow-up data from adult and paediatric patients attending the hospitals for the investigation or treatment of cardiovascular conditions, and from their relatives, to find genes and biomarkers for the diagnosis and prognosis of cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001033> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001033>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29302764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5975608") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CCPS Chicago Cancer Prone Study 394 387 47 (12) 45 (11) 140 (45) 171 (55) BBCS Baltimore Breast Cancer Study 95 102 54 (14) 52 (13) 44 (49) 45 (51) SCCS Southern Community Cohort Study 220 430 57 (9) 57 (9) 66 (36) 118 (64)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001033> "A consortium for a genome-wide association study of breast cancer in women of African ancestry in Nigeria, Barbados and the United States, pooling the cases and controls of six epidemiological studies (the Nigerian Breast Cancer Study, the Barbados National Cancer Study, the Racial Variability in Genotypic Determinants of Breast Cancer Risk Study, the Chicago Cancer Prone Study, the Baltimore Breast Cancer Study and the Southern Community Cohort Study), genotyped together on the Illumina HumanOmni2.5 array.")
