# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3046454/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 1, 1992, through September 30, 1999, in Melbourne and from January 1, 1993, through December 31, 1998, in Sydney, women younger than 40 years of age at diagnosis were selected; after January 1, 1996, random samples of women ages 40-49 years and 50-59 years at diagnosis were selected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> "A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3046454/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Breast Cancer Family Registry (ABCFR) is a population-based, case control family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset breast cancer that is being carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia [9-11], and is part of the Breast Cancer Family Registry [12].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> "A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6697632/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the population-based Australian Breast Cancer Family Study which followed-up 1,196 women enrolled during 1992–99 when aged <60 years at diagnosis with a first primary invasive breast cancer") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> "A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8660783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the ABCFS probands were either breast cancer cases (identified through population-complete cancer registries) or age-matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> "A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21182766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30771221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were adult women living in the metropolitan areas of Melbourne and Sydney and selected from the electoral roll by use of proportional random sampling based on the expected age distribution of the case patients") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001048> "A population-based case-control-family study of breast cancer with an emphasis on early-onset disease, carried out in Melbourne and Sydney, Australia, which enrolled women with a first primary breast cancer identified through cancer registries in 1992-1999, with controls selected from the electoral roll; it is the Australian site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30529582+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed genetic data from 22,775 patients with CRC (cases) and 47,731 individuals without cancer (controls) from 14 studies in the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30529582+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a GWAS of East Asians to identify CRC risk loci and evaluate the generalizability of findings from GWASs of European populations to Asian populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6441622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2010, we initiated the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium (ACCC) to identify new genetic risk factors for CRC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6441622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Included in the current study are 22,775 CRC cases and 47,731 controls of East-Asian ancestry from 14 studies conducted in China, Japan, and South Korea") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Studies (listed with grant support) participating in the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium include the Shanghai Women's Health Study (US NIH, R37CA070867, UM1CA182910), the Shanghai Men's Health Study (US NIH, R01CA082729, UM1CA173640)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01222-9/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1222_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Japan BioBank Colorectal Cancer Study (grant from the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology of the Japanese government), the Aichi Colorectal Cancer Study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001049> "A consortium, initiated in 2010, that pools genome-wide genotype data on colorectal cancer cases and cancer-free controls of East Asian ancestry from studies in China, Japan and South Korea, among them the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies and colorectal cancer studies from Shanghai, Guangzhou, Aichi, BioBank Japan and several Korean centres, to identify genetic risk factors for colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14583845+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in past or present AACTG clinical trials may contribute DNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3235490/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in the HIV controllers (median VL, CD4 count, and disease duration of 241 copies/ml, 699 cells/mm3, and 10 years, respectively) and treatment-naïve chronically infected individuals with advanced disease (median VL and CD4 count of 61,698 copies/ml and 224 cells/mm3, respectively) enrolled in antiviral treatment studies led by the AIDS Clinical Trials Group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2671281+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, a group of oncologists conducting clinical trials in patients with AIDS-associated KS as part of a cooperative group established by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID) drafted such criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:3044083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3044083+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address many of these issues in the United States, the Federal Government has established an AIDS Clinical Trials Group (ACTG) program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ACTG is the world’s largest and longest running clinical trials network focused on HIV and other infectious diseases and the people living with them.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14583845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21051598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2671281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://actgnetwork.org/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Founded in 1987, it comprises thousands of dedicated researchers, staff, and community members who are pursuing research into novel treatments and cures for infectious diseases at 59 locations across four continents") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001050> "A clinical trials network founded in 1987 as a cooperative group of the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, the largest and longest-running network of trials in HIV and other infectious diseases, now with sites on four continents. Participants of its trials may give DNA to its DNA bank (protocol A5128) for genetic studies, and treatment-naive participants with advanced HIV disease from its antiviral treatment trials were the progressors of the International HIV Controllers Study genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A set of core data elements are collected, including basic demographic details, details about their MS, an address for dispatching the saliva kit and their NHS number for linkage to their medical records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment started in November 2021 and is currently expected to run until August 2031 pending long-term funding.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ADAMS project is an ongoing genetic cohort study of individuals with MS from diverse ancestral backgrounds living in the UK") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is focused on people with MS from diverse ancestral backgrounds, that is, people with recent non-European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work is being carried out at the Preventive Neurology Unit at Queen Mary University of London, which is partly funded by Barts Charity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37197821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10193065/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are recruiting individuals with self-reported MS via a bespoke online platform, clinical sites and the UK MS Register (UKMSR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001051> "A UK genetic cohort study, run by the Preventive Neurology Unit of Queen Mary University of London and recruiting since November 2021, of adults with multiple sclerosis from diverse, mostly non-European, ancestral backgrounds, enrolled online, at clinical sites and through the UK MS Register, who give saliva DNA for genotyping, questionnaire data and consent to health-record linkage, to study the genetics of multiple sclerosis susceptibility and severity; it has no controls of its own.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31339677+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1053 patients underwent randomization from February 2017 through May 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31339677+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria included an age of 12 years or older, no receipt of ART in the previous 6 months, a creatinine clearance of more than 60 ml per minute (>80 ml per minute in patients younger than 19 years of age), and an HIV type 1 (HIV-1) RNA level of 500 copies or more per milliliter.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31339677+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end point was the percentage of patients with a 48-week HIV-1 RNA level of less than 50 copies per milliliter (as determined with the Snapshot algorithm from the Food and Drug Administration; noninferiority margin, -10 percentage points).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31339677+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a 96-week, phase 3, investigator-led, open-label, randomized trial in South Africa,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31339677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03122262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35512135") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9624457/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1,053 HIV-positive, ART-naïve participants were randomly assigned to one of three treatment arms: 1) dolutegravir, tenofovir alafenamide (TAF) and emtricitabine; 2) dolutegravir, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) and emtricitabine; or 3) efavirenz, TDF and emtricitabine (8).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001052> "A randomised, open-label, investigator-led phase 3 non-inferiority trial of first-line antiretroviral therapy, run by the University of the Witwatersrand (study WRHI 060) at sites in Johannesburg, South Africa, which from February 2017 randomised people aged 12 years or older with HIV-1 who had not received antiretroviral therapy in the previous 6 months to dolutegravir and emtricitabine with either tenofovir alafenamide or tenofovir disoproxil fumarate, or to efavirenz, tenofovir disoproxil fumarate and emtricitabine, and followed them for 96 weeks, later extended to 192 weeks.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2733811/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between October 28, 2001 and December 31, 2003, a total of 3179 subjects was recruited from Kaiser Permanente of Northern California, a large integrated healthcare delivery system in the San Francisco and greater Bay area, and enrolled into three case groups and two control groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2733811/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, case groups included early onset CAD (AMI, angina pectoris with positive angiogram or revascularization procedure in men ≤45 or women ≤55 years old), incident stable exertional angina at an older age and incident AMI at an older age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2733811/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Older controls included men and women aged 60–69 years at the time of identification in June 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2733811/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The young control group included subjects between the ages of 30 and 45 for men or 30 and 55 for women as well as a subset of 479 participants from the Coronary Artery Risk Development in Young Adults (CARDIA) study (12) originally recruited at the Oakland field center and attending the study's Year 15 examination in 2000–2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2733811/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through a phone interview, an extensive self-administered questionnaire, and/or the use of the Kaiser electronic clinical databases, we documented the presence or absence and age of onset of clinically significant CAD, CVD and PAD, as well as all traditional cardiovascular risk factors in all participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18443000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21917174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27030599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/heartjnl-2015-309136") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Atherosclerotic Disease, VAscular FunctioN and GenetiC Epidemiology (ADVANCE) study was originally designed as a case-control investigation of genetic and non-genetic determinants of coronary artery disease (CAD) and mode of CAD presentation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001053> "A multi-ethnic case-control genetic association study of coronary artery disease by Stanford University and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, which from October 2001 to December 2003 enrolled Kaiser Permanente members in the San Francisco Bay area into three case groups (early-onset coronary artery disease, and incident stable exertional angina or myocardial infarction at an older age) and two control groups free of clinical cardiovascular disease (younger adults, including some CARDIA participants, and adults aged 60 to 69), with questionnaires, stored blood samples, cardiac computed tomography in older controls and later follow-up through health plan records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26084364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34203817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21125205+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2006-2008, 963 subjects from the 3C Study, aged 73 years or more, had an eye examination and will have follow-up eye examinations every 2 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> "A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26084364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34203817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21125205+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Alienor (Antioxydants, Lipides Essentiels, Nutrition et maladies OculaiRes) Study aims at assessing the associations of eye diseases with nutritional factors, determined from plasma measurements and estimation of dietary intakes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> "A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26084364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34203817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12346055/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ALIENOR participants were recruited from the Three-City (3C) study, a population-based longitudinal cohort that initially included 9294 adults aged ≥65 years (1999–2000) in 3 French cities (Bordeaux, Dijon, and Montpellier), among whom 2104 in Bordeaux.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> "A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26084364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34203817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12346055/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ALIENOR (Antioxydants, LIpides Essentiels, Nutrition et maladies OculaiRes) study (www.alienor-study.com) is a population-based longitudinal cohort study among adults aged ≥73 years in Bordeaux, France (2006 to 2020).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> "A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21125205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26084364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34203817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40808916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12346055/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To diagnose and classify intermediate and advanced AMD, participants underwent a comprehensive ophthalmic examination in the Department of Ophthalmology of Bordeaux University Hospital, approximately every 2 to 3 years from 2006 to 2020 (Fig 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001054> "A population-based cohort of elderly residents of Bordeaux, France, recruited from 2006 as an ophthalmological follow-up nested within the Three-City Study, assessing associations between eye diseases such as age-related macular degeneration and nutritional factors through plasma measurements, dietary-intake estimation and repeated eye examinations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "APDGC controls were volunteers, often spouses of patients with PD, without symptoms of parkinsonism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patient samples and a subset of the controls used in the analysis were contributed by 12 APDGC centers, which are listed in text e-1 on the Neurology® Web site at Neurology.org.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exclusion based on neuropathology included the following: 66 cases without Lewy bodies; 6 with excessive Alzheimer pathology; 7 had parkinsonism with other pathologies; 16 had dementia with Lewy bodies; and 9 cases were withdrawn at the request of the contributing sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria included clinical diagnosis of PD by a neurologist before death, moderate/severe neuronal loss in the substantia nigra, and the presence of Lewy bodies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To reduce potential pathologic heterogeneity, the Autopsy-Confirmed Parkinson Disease Genetics Consortium (APDGC) collected a set of individuals with PD that have neuropathologic confirmation of Lewy body PD pathology, as well as a set of “autopsy-confirmed” control individuals with no evidence of PD neuropathology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4352096/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While 977 APDGC samples were genotyped by the Center for Inherited Disease Research (CIDR), Johns Hopkins University, only 791 samples remained after neuropathologic review (484 cases, 307 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25663231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000394.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Udall Center of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, Baltimore, MD, USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001055> "A case-control sample assembled by a consortium of twelve US autopsy centres, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence in Parkinson's Disease Research, of people clinically diagnosed with Parkinson's disease whose diagnosis was confirmed at autopsy (nigral neuronal loss and Lewy bodies, with little Alzheimer pathology) and of neuropathologically normal controls, often patients' spouses, genotyped genome-wide at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease with less diagnostic misclassification.")
