# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22736162+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients, hospitalised for an acute depression episode, a random sample of the inhabitants of the city of Münster and patients with an acute coronary syndrome from the same area are recruited into three cohorts, examined in parallel with identical methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065391/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BiDirect is a prospective observational study that integrates three different cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065391/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to BiDirect-Baseline, three follow-up examinations are scheduled to be conducted over the course of 12 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065391/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were (i) age (≥35 and < 66 years) and (ii) acute myocardial infarction, or acute coronary syndrome requiring therapy, or treatment of cardiac disease due to myocardial infarction within the last three months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065391/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objectives of BiDirect are to investigate (i) whether depression contributes to the onset and severity of (subclinical) arteriosclerosis, and (ii) whether the severity of (subclinical) arteriosclerosis is related to incident depression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22736162") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24924233") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4065391/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This report includes the first data collection wave (BiDirect-Baseline), which was conducted from July 2010 to June 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001060> "A prospective observational study run by the University of Münster, Germany, of three cohorts of adults aged 35–65 examined in parallel with identical methods: patients treated for an acute depressive episode and patients after an acute myocardial infarction or acute coronary syndrome, recruited through psychiatric and cardiological hospitals and clinics in and around Münster, and reference participants randomly sampled from the city's population register, with a baseline examination in 2010–2013 and repeated follow-ups, to investigate the bidirectional relationship between depression and subclinical arteriosclerosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001061> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001061>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16623958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33732727") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16623958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1524813/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During 1999–2000, 1174 (85.2%) of this group participated in an extension study (BMES IIB).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001061> "A population-based cohort study of common eye diseases and other health outcomes among permanent residents aged 49 years or older of two postcode areas in the Blue Mountains, west of Sydney, Australia, identified through a census and examined at baseline in 1992–1994 and then every five years to 2007–2009, with newly eligible residents added in an extension study in 1999–2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16623958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33732727") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16623958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1524813/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were identified through a census and were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001061> "A population-based cohort study of common eye diseases and other health outcomes among permanent residents aged 49 years or older of two postcode areas in the Blue Mountains, west of Sydney, Australia, identified through a census and examined at baseline in 1992–1994 and then every five years to 2007–2009, with newly eligible residents added in an extension study in 1999–2000.")
