# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BRAINS-UK will recruit 1500 cases of ischaemic and haemorrhagic stroke patients >18 years of age from specialist stroke centres around the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By investigating the influence of genetic factors on stroke risk in European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations, BRAINS has the potential to improve our understanding of genetic differences between these groups and may lead to new population-specific therapeutic targets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRAINS (Bio-repository of DNA in stroke) study aims to recruit subjects with all subtypes of stroke as well as controls from UK, India, Sri Lanka and Qatar.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary outcome of the study is to establish a large DNA repository of highly phenotyped stroke patients in the South Asian (British, Indian and Sri Lankan) and Middle Eastern (Qatari) populations as well as a comparative European-descended population from the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These sites were specifically chosen in areas with a high South Asian density allowing them to not only recruit stroke patients of European ancestry but also those of British South Asian ethnicity (www.brainsgenetics.com).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37706299") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10811966/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included the UK, Indian, and Qatari arms of the ongoing large Bio-Repository of DNA in Stroke (BRAINS) international prospective hospital-based study for South Asian stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001063> "An ongoing international hospital-based DNA repository, run from Imperial College London, of adults with ischaemic or haemorrhagic stroke recruited at stroke centres in the United Kingdom (patients of European ancestry and British South Asians), India and Qatar, together with controls, to compare genetic risk factors for stroke between European, South Asian and Middle Eastern populations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001064> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001064>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency-matched to cases according to 5-year age group, inclusion in the universal Galician Public Health Service (SERGAS) registry database, and place of residence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001064> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted since 1997 in Vigo and Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, Spain, recruiting incident breast cancer cases from Galician hospitals with blood and tumour tissue samples and risk-factor questionnaires, and controls frequency-matched by age, public health registry inclusion and place of residence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BREast Oncology GAlicia Network (BREOGAN) is a population-based study conducted since 1997 in two main cities in Galicia, Spain (Vigo and Santiago de Compostela), which cover approximately 700,000 inhabitants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001064> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted since 1997 in Vigo and Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, Spain, recruiting incident breast cancer cases from Galician hospitals with blood and tumour tissue samples and risk-factor questionnaires, and controls frequency-matched by age, public health registry inclusion and place of residence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study currently includes 2,078 incident breast cancer cases diagnosed from 1997-2014 in two Galician hospitals with blood, tumour tissue and risk factor questionnaire, as well as clinical information, including pathology, survival and treatment variables.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001064> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted since 1997 in Vigo and Santiago de Compostela, Galicia, Spain, recruiting incident breast cancer cases from Galician hospitals with blood and tumour tissue samples and risk-factor questionnaires, and controls frequency-matched by age, public health registry inclusion and place of residence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00262691") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21150884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3062002") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kita-Nagoya Genomic Epidemiology (KING) study (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier: NCT00262691) is a population-based cross-sectional study based in Kita-Nagoya, Japan, for which a total of 3975 volunteers were recruited from participants of annual health checkups and which has been described in detail previously.30") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065> "An ongoing community-based prospective observational study of the genetic basis of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors, begun in 2005 by Nagoya University with Aichi Gakuin University, of local residents of Kitanagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan, aged 50 or older, enrolled at community-based annual health check-ups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00262691") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study considered a total of 1,400 Japanese individuals, comprising 200 subjects each from seven regions (prefectures or cities) in Japan: Amagasaki (in Hyogo Prefecture), Ehime, Fukuoka, Kita-Nagoya (in Aichi Prefecture), Okinawa, Shimane and Tokyo, apart from 85 unrelated Japanese subjects from Tokyo in Phase 3 of the International HapMap Project, abbreviated as HapMap JPT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065> "An ongoing community-based prospective observational study of the genetic basis of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors, begun in 2005 by Nagoya University with Aichi Gakuin University, of local residents of Kitanagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan, aged 50 or older, enrolled at community-based annual health check-ups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00262691") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6453927/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It recruited 3975 Japanese subjects aged 50–80 years who underwent community-based annual health checkups between May 2005 and December 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065> "An ongoing community-based prospective observational study of the genetic basis of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors, begun in 2005 by Nagoya University with Aichi Gakuin University, of local residents of Kitanagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan, aged 50 or older, enrolled at community-based annual health check-ups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00262691") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30993211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6453927/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kita-Nagoya Genomic Epidemiology (KING) Study (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier NCT00262691) is an ongoing community-based prospective observational study of the genetic basis of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors31,32.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001065> "An ongoing community-based prospective observational study of the genetic basis of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors, begun in 2005 by Nagoya University with Aichi Gakuin University, of local residents of Kitanagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan, aged 50 or older, enrolled at community-based annual health check-ups.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001066> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001066>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000820.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001189.v5.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32864809") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7754106/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome sequencing for the “NHLBI TOPMed: Cleveland Clinic Atrial Fibrillation (CCAF) Study” (phs001189.v1.p1) was performed at the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard (3R01HL092577‐06S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001066> "A collection of clinical and genetic data from patients with atrial fibrillation and controls enrolled at the Cleveland Clinic in its CV/Arrhythmia Biobank, including the Cleveland Clinic Lone Atrial Fibrillation GeneBank of patients with atrial fibrillation without significant structural heart disease, for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation; its early-onset cases were whole-genome sequenced in the NHLBI TOPMed programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000820.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001189.v5.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001189.v5.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case subjects were at least 18 years of age with atrial fibrillation onset at 60 years of age or less and no preexisting heart failure, MI, or overt structural heart disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001066> "A collection of clinical and genetic data from patients with atrial fibrillation and controls enrolled at the Cleveland Clinic in its CV/Arrhythmia Biobank, including the Cleveland Clinic Lone Atrial Fibrillation GeneBank of patients with atrial fibrillation without significant structural heart disease, for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation; its early-onset cases were whole-genome sequenced in the NHLBI TOPMed programme.")
