AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3854934/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Colorado Twin Registry (CTR) is housed at the Institute for Behavioral Genetics (IBG) at the University of Colorado at Boulder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3854934/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Longitudinal Twin Study is a prospective study designed to investigate the genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development (Emde & Hewitt, 2001).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3854934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four samples are currently drawn from the CTR: The Community Twin Sample (CTS), the Longitudinal Twin Sample (LTS), the Early Reading Development Sample (ERDS), and the Colorado Learning Sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3854934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information on cognition, temperament, social competence, family relations, and behavioral problems was collected almost yearly from the time the participants were 14-months-old through age 16.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13333102/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LTS participants, born between 1984 and 1990, were recruited in Colorado, and were followed from birth (Corley et al. 2019).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42223860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13333102/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study examined the relationship between PS and the three EFs using data from the Colorado Longitudinal Twin Study (LTS), which included PS and EF assessments in adolescence (mean age 16–17, LTS) and established adulthood (mean age 29).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001069> "A prospective longitudinal study of same-sex twin pairs born in 1984–1990 and recruited in Colorado, United States, from the Colorado Twin Registry of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado, assessed almost yearly from 14 months to age 16 and again in adulthood to investigate genetic and environmental influences on individual differences in psychological development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Alzheimer’s Disease Genetics Consortium (ADGC) Across all datasets used, AD cases and cognitively-normal elders (CNEs) were defined by either (a) pathological confirmation of the presence (cases) or absence (CNEs) of AD pathology") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> "A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer's disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CSDC: The Combined Small Datasets Collection is a harmonized dataset including all data from six separately ascertained datasets or waves of datasets already described above (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2, and WASHU2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> "A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer's disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Datasets or waves were incorporated into the CSDC if they included fewer than 100 cases and/or 100 CNEs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> "A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer's disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "None of these datasets were separately incorporated into analyses and were only analyzed in the CSDC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> "A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer's disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CSDC is a harmonized collection of merged small datasets (comprising the existing datasets of BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2, and WASHU2) used in common variant analyses to deal with small case and control counts within the individual studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001070> "A harmonized dataset of the Alzheimer's Disease Genetics Consortium that merges six separately ascertained datasets or dataset waves of Alzheimer's disease cases and cognitively normal elders (BIOCARD, CHAP2, EAS, RMAYO, ROSMAP2 and WASHU2), each too small to be analysed on its own, so that they can be analysed together in common-variant association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8497954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Columbia COVID-19 Biobank recruited consecutive COVID-19 cases (positive result from nasopharyngeal SARS-CoV-2 polymerase chain reaction test), regardless of age, sex, or race/ethnicity who received care at the Columbia University Irving Medical Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8497954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Columbia University COVID-19 Biobank collected residual blood and urine samples after clinical testing from every COVID-19 patient diagnosed at the Columbia University Irving Medical Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9428108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Biobank recruited COVID-19 cases (n = 1,166) of diverse ancestry among all patients who were treated at Columbia University Irving Medical Center between March and May 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9428108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Columbia University COVID-19 Biobank was established in response to the New York City infection surge in March 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34642645") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36062073") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-021-03767-x/MediaObjects/41586_2021_3767_MOESM6_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Columbia University COVID19 Biobank | United States | CU | EUR | 203 | 2149 | 453 | 2149 | 508 | 2149") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001071> "A biobank set up at Columbia University Irving Medical Center in New York City, United States, in response to the city's COVID-19 surge in March 2020, which kept residual blood and urine samples left over from clinical testing of consecutive patients with PCR-confirmed COVID-19, of any age, sex or ancestry, treated at the medical center.")

