AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2873937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A random sample of 4500 subjects aged 45-74 years, stratified according to gender, 10-year age groups (45-54, 55-64, and 65-74 years), and the three geographical areas, was selected from the National Population Register in August 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2873937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FIN-D2D survey was carried out in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, the Southern Ostrobothnia, and Central Finland between October and December 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2873937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort included 2766 Finnish subjects (45-74 years) from the population-based FIN-D2D survey.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3118241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a part of the evaluation, population-based health examination surveys with independent random samples from the population were conducted in the beginning and at the end of the project period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3118241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals aged 45-74 years, stratified according to sex, 10-year age groups (45-54, 55-64, and 65-74 years) and five geographical areas, were selected from the National Population Register at the beginning of the project (year 2002 for Northern Ostrobothnia and Northern Savo, and year 2004 for South Ostrobothnia, Central Finland, and Pirkanmaa) and at the end of the project (year 2007 for all five areas).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3118241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The implementation project of this program, FIN-D2D, focused mainly on the high-risk strategy, and the strategy of early diagnosis and treatment [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21595955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3605054/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of the study is to gather information about prevalence of diabetes and cardiovascular diseases and of the risk factors associated with these within the Finnish population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001072> "A population-based health examination survey of a random sample of people aged 45–74, drawn from the National Population Register and stratified by sex, age group and area, in the hospital districts of Pirkanmaa, South Ostrobothnia and Central Finland, Finland, examined in October–December 2007 at the end of FIN-D2D, the implementation project of Finland's national type 2 diabetes prevention programme, to measure the prevalence of diabetes, cardiovascular disease and their risk factors and to evaluate the programme.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For DietBB, cohort participants where included if they were dementia-free at baseline and available biomaterial for DNA analysis is available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 120 of these participants, dementia of the AD-type occurred at any follow up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to methylation, the DietBB samples has genome-wide genotype data which was included in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AgeCoDe study is a general practice (GP) registry-based longitudinal study in elderly individuals that recruited patients aged 75 years and above in six German cities from 2003 to 200410 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DietBB sample included in this GWAS is a subsample extracted from the AgeCoDe cohort in the context of an ongoing genome-wide methylation analysis for dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The additional 200 remain free of dementia until last follow up of AgeCoDe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001073> "A subsample of the German Study on Ageing, Cognition and Dementia in Primary Care Patients (AgeCoDe), a general-practice registry-based longitudinal study of people aged 75 and over recruited in 2002–2003 in six German cities, made up of participants who were free of dementia at baseline and had DNA available and who either developed Alzheimer-type dementia during follow-up or stayed free of dementia, selected for a genome-wide DNA methylation study of dementia and also genotyped genome-wide.")

