# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DPS is a clinical trial with five participating centers (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere, and Oulu) in Finland (NCT00518167).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion criteria were 1) age 40–64 years at screening, 2) BMI >25 kg/m2 at screening, and 3) the mean value of two 75-g oral glucose tolerance tests (OGTTs) in the IGT range based on World Health Organization 1985 criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants randomized to intensive lifestyle intervention were given individualized counseling by the study nutritionists to achieve the lifestyle goals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The randomization of participants started in 1993 and continued until 1998.A total of 522 overweight men and women were randomly allocated to one of the two treatment modalities, the intensive diet-exercise counseling group (n = 265, 66% were women) or the control group (n = 257, 69% were women).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These data are based on the follow-up of 4 years when active intervention was finished and on the 3 years of follow-up after active intervention with a total follow-up of an average of 6.2 years (median 7 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20980412") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40583490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12439282/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the DPS was to investigate the impact of lifestyle advice (diet, weight control, and physical activity) in participants with impaired glucose tolerance for the prevention of T2DM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001075> "A randomised controlled trial at five centres in Finland (Helsinki, Kuopio, Turku, Tampere and Oulu) that from 1993 to 1998 randomised overweight men and women aged 40–64 with impaired glucose tolerance to intensive individual diet and exercise counselling or to a control group, to test whether lifestyle change prevents type 2 diabetes, and whose participants continued to be followed with yearly visits after the trial.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From the initial 101 subjects (33 eAMD, 47 iAMD, and 21 controls) enrolled in a prospective, observational natural history study at Duke Eye Center, 70 completed the 24-month study visit (representing ∼15% dropout rate per year) (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with eAMD and iAMD were enrolled from the Duke Eye Center patient population, and control participants were enrolled from the Duke Optometry and Comprehensive Eye Clinics or were family members or friends of the AMD patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion of study participants in a single-center, prospective, longitudinal, observational study of eAMD (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier, NCT01822873), named “Duke study of Functional Endpoints for Age-related Macular Degeneration” (Duke FEATURE), has been previously described.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These structural and functional features represent potential end points for clinical trials in iAMD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used a mixed-effect repeated measure (MMRM) model to control for covariates (baseline value, age, coronary artery disease, dry eye, and cataract status) and to explore the cross-sectional performance of the different assessments at 6-month intervals and any longitudinal VF change over the period of 24 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36245764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01822873") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42560005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13452432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were required to be at least 50 years of age; no best-corrected VA (BCVA) requirement was required.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001076> "A single-centre, prospective, longitudinal observational natural-history study at the Duke Eye Center in Durham, North Carolina, United States, which from 2013 enrolled people aged 50 or over with early or intermediate (dry) age-related macular degeneration from the centre's patients, together with controls from Duke optometry and comprehensive eye clinics or the patients' family and friends, and assessed them with retinal imaging and with visual function tests repeated about every six months over 24 months, to find functional end points for clinical trials.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898362/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In search of additional common genetic variants, we conducted a two-stage GWAS of EC among women participating in studies that are part of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium (E2C2, details in Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> "An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As shown on the map below, more than 37 studies have joined E2C2 since its inception in 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> "An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study Design: 22 case-control and 15 cohort studies Geography: 1 Asia, 25 North America, 10 Europe, 1 Australia") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> "An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall objective of E2C2 is to build on resources from existing studies by combining data across studies in order to advance our understanding of the etiology of this disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> "An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://epi.grants.cancer.gov/eecc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000893.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To this end, we conducted a genome-wide association study to identify genes involved in endometrial cancer using studies from the NCI-supported Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium (E2C2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001077> "An NCI-supported consortium, begun in 2006, of case-control and cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia that combines data across its member studies, including in a genome-wide association study, to investigate the etiology of endometrial cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26061305+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a cross-sectional study among 572 Chinese and Malay patients from the ongoing Epidemiology of Dementia in Singapore (EDIS) Study, who underwent comprehensive examinations including neuropsychological testing and brain magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7021682/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first phase of the EDIS study, participants ≥60 years underwent cognitive screening using the Abbreviated Mental Test (AMT) and the Progressive Forgetfulness Questionnaire (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7021682/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Screen positives who provided consent (n = 957) participated in the second phase of the study, which included comprehensive clinical and neuropsychological evaluations, together with neuroimaging at the same session.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7021682/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EDIS study employs a cross-sectional design drawing participants who were long-term local citizens from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Disease (SEED) study, consisting of the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, Singapore Malay Eye Study-2, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study-2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7021682/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiology of Dementia in Singapore (EDIS) study is a subsample of a population-based study focusing on the risk factors and prevalence of dementia and cognitive impairment in the three major Asian ethnicities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32060376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39179981") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11342485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiology of Dementia in Singapore (EDIS) study recruited participants from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Disease (SEED) study, a study comprised the Singapore Chinese Eye Study from 2009 to 2011, the Singapore Malays Eye Study from 2010 to 2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study from 2013 to 2015 [30].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001078> "A population-based study of the prevalence and risk factors of cognitive impairment and dementia in Chinese, Malay and Indian adults in Singapore, which drew participants aged 60 and over from the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases study (the Singapore Chinese Eye Study, 2009–2011, the Singapore Malay Eye Study, 2010–2013, and the Singapore Indian Eye Study, 2013–2015). Participants were screened with the Abbreviated Mental Test and a history of progressive forgetfulness, and those who screened positive were invited for neuropsychological testing and brain MRI.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3181335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were patients from four different French medical centers (Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier, Paris) selected according to the same criteria as the MARTHA patients, except with the restriction on age of onset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3607886/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals participating in the EOVT study were genotyped for 317,139 SNPs using the Illumina Sentrix HumanHap300 Beadchip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3607886/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work was based on two French GWAS on VT, the Early-Onset Venous Thrombosis (EOVT) and the Marseille Thrombosis Association (MARTHA) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10506044/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were selected for having documented idiopathic isolated PE or DVT at age <50 years in the absence of acquired risk factors (including surgery, hospitalization, pregnancy, puerperium, oral contraception, cancer, and autoimmune disease) and at the time of VTE and thrombophilia defects (including antithrombin, protein C, or protein S deficiencies, and homozygosity for FV Leiden or FII-20210A).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21980494") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23509962") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37399490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10506044/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Early Onset Venous Thrombosis (EOVT) study was a case-control sample of 339 patients with VTE and 1327 healthy French persons from the Suvimax study.28") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001079> "A French case-control study of venous thrombosis whose cases, from medical centres in Grenoble, Marseille, Montpellier and Paris, had a documented idiopathic deep vein thrombosis or pulmonary embolism before the age of 50 without acquired risk factors or major thrombophilia defects, and whose controls were healthy French participants of the SU.VI.MAX study. It was genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of venous thrombosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over the following 2 years 2,000 women were recruited from a Family History Clinic (FHC) in Manchester with oversampling of previous breast cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7616752/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During their participation in the original FH-Risk study women gave their consent for DNA testing (used for SNP analysis) and for the calculation of their breast density.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7616752/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original FH-Risk study aimed to validated and improve breast cancer risk prediction models used in FHRPCs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7616752/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women who took part in the original FH-Risk study from 2010 to 2012 [13,14] were invited in 2022/23 to receive an update on their breast cancer risk which included breast density and a PRS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11523958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Updated BC risk information was obtained from a sub-set of FHRPC attendees enroled in the Family History Risk (FHRisk) Study in 2010–11 as described previously [21, 22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27559559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39356295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39516339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11523958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were eligible for the FHRisk Study if they were 20-79 years of age and had not previously had BC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001080> "A study of women aged 20–79 attending the Family History Risk and Prevention Clinic in Manchester, United Kingdom, recruited in 2010–2012, who completed risk-factor questionnaires and consented to DNA testing for SNP analysis and to breast density measurement, set up to validate and improve the breast cancer risk prediction models used in family history clinics.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02417-6/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnosis of aortic valve stenosis was based on echocardiography defined as thickening of the aortic valve and evidence of an increased peak velocity of >2.5 m/s using cw-doppler.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081> "A cohort of patients with aortic valve stenosis, diagnosed by echocardiography or by a history of valve replacement for severe stenosis, recruited from the German Heart Center Munich and the University of Bonn/Marburg, Germany, and genotyped for studies of the genetics of aortic stenosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02417-6/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, patients with a history of aortic valve replacement for severe aortic valve stenosis were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081> "A cohort of patients with aortic valve stenosis, diagnosed by echocardiography or by a history of valve replacement for severe stenosis, recruited from the German Heart Center Munich and the University of Bonn/Marburg, Germany, and genotyped for studies of the genetics of aortic stenosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02417-6/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotyping in the German aortic stenosis cohort was performed using the Illumina Global Screening Array (GSA) v3.0, and following standard genotyping quality control, the genotyped data were imputed using the TOPMed imputation server.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081> "A cohort of patients with aortic valve stenosis, diagnosed by echocardiography or by a history of valve replacement for severe stenosis, recruited from the German Heart Center Munich and the University of Bonn/Marburg, Germany, and genotyped for studies of the genetics of aortic stenosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02417-6/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German Aortic Stenosis Cohort recruited patients from the German Heart Center Munich and from the University of Bonn/Marburg and contains approximately 5732 participants with aortic valve stenosis recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001081> "A cohort of patients with aortic valve stenosis, diagnosed by echocardiography or by a history of valve replacement for severe stenosis, recruited from the German Heart Center Munich and the University of Bonn/Marburg, Germany, and genotyped for studies of the genetics of aortic stenosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5669157/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We reviewed stroke‐related diagnostic testing for first‐ever hospitalized ischemic strokes among residents of the Greater Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky (GCNK) 5‐county region of 1.3 million people during four 1‐year study periods (July 1993 to June 1994 and calendar years 1999, 2005, and 2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11179757/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "in brief, this is a population‐based study using retrospective ascertainment of physician‐adjudicated stroke cases in a sample of ≈1.3 million people across 5 counties in southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11179936/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adults with acute ischemic stroke presenting to an emergency department within 24 hours of last known normal during study epochs 2005, 2010, and 2015 within the Greater Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky Stroke Study were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11179936/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the GCNKSS is a prospective population‐based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment, and outcomes within a 5‐county region comprising approximately 1.3 million people.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9472883+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Greater Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky Stroke Study was designed to be the first large, population-based metropolitan study of temporal trends in stroke incidence rates and outcome within a biracial population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28645938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38700029") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9472883") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9472883+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are identifying all hospitalized and autopsied cases of stroke and transient ischemic attack (TIA) among the 1.3 million inhabitants of a five-county region of Greater Cincinnati/Northern Kentucky for the period 7/1/93-6/30/94.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001082> "A population-based study of stroke incidence, risk factors, treatment and outcomes in the biracial population of a five-county region of southwestern Ohio and northern Kentucky, United States, around Cincinnati, which ascertains all hospitalized and autopsied strokes and transient ischaemic attacks among residents during one-year study periods held since 1993 (July 1993 to June 1994, 1999, 2005, 2010 and 2015), to measure temporal trends in stroke incidence and outcome.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11446758/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our study, the patient cases were sourced from hospitals with an average age of 64.77 years, while controls were selected from the database of a genetic testing company, Genotek, with an average age of ~35 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11446758/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Instead, we defined controls as individuals aged 40 years or above who reported having COVID-19 but did not experience a severe course of the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11446758/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The individuals who were included in our analysis provided informed consent for their data to be used for research purposes and responded to an online questionnaire.Genotek customer data were added to the study cohort for further analysis as controls (N = 6,400).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11446758/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed the genetic data of 787 individuals, with 691 from the N.V. Sklifosovsky Research Institute for Emergency Medicine and 96 from the Ufa Federal Research Center of the Russian Academy of Sciences (UFRC RAS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotek | Genotek | Russia | EUR | Initial discovery (Data Freeze 4)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39364016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genotek clients included in our analyses provided informed consent for their data to be used for research purposes and responded to online questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001083> "Participants of the COVID-19 genetic studies of the Russian genetic testing company Genotek: its customers who consented to research use of their data and answered online questionnaires about COVID-19, studied for long COVID and, when aged 40 or over with non-severe COVID-19, as controls in a genome-wide association study of severe COVID-19 whose cases were patients hospitalised in Moscow and Ufa.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2770870/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics of Kidneys in Diabetes (GoKinD) study, an initiative supported by the Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation (JDRF) and by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, was conceived to address this bottleneck by assembling a large DNA collection that is suitable for genetic association studies of nephropathy in type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2770870/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The George Washington Biostatistics Center worked with Matthews Media Group to identify for this study in the United States and Canada volunteers who subsequently were directed to one of 27 clinical centers around the United States for examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2770870/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The set of control subjects consists only of individuals with normoalbuminuria despite 15 yr of type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2770870/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To be eligible as a case patient, a patient had to have type 1 diabetes (minimum 10 yr duration) and severe diabetic nephropathy (ESRD or persistent proteinuria).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2682673/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, subjects enrolled in GoKinD had type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31, began insulin treatment within 1 year of their diagnosis, and were between 18 and 59 years of age at the time of enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16775037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19252134") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2682673/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Section of Genetics and Epidemiology at the Joslin Diabetes Center (JDC) recruited and examined patients of the Joslin Clinic from New England who were already enrolled in the Joslin Kidney Study on the Genetics of Diabetic Nephropathy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001084> "A collection of DNA and clinical data for genetic association studies of diabetic nephropathy in type 1 diabetes, assembled with support from the JDRF, NIDDK and CDC by the Joslin Diabetes Center, from patients of its clinic in New England, and by the George Washington University Biostatistics Center, from volunteers across the United States and Canada. Participants aged 18–59 with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before age 31 were enrolled as cases with diabetic nephropathy (persistent proteinuria or end-stage renal disease) or as controls with normoalbuminuria after at least 15 years of diabetes, with both parents enrolled where possible to form family trios.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001085> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001085>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These include previously genotyped control groups from Sweden, Spain, the UK, and Austria to be paired with the cases to be genotyped from the two GRCs from Sweden (LUND and SAHLSIS), and from the GRCs from Spain (BASICMAR), the UK (BRAINS), and Austria (GRAZ).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001085> "A hospital-based series of patients with ischaemic stroke admitted to the stroke unit of the Department of Neurology of the Medical University of Graz, Austria, investigated with brain imaging and a standardised diagnostic protocol and subtyped by stroke neurologists, whose cases are compared in genetic studies of ischaemic stroke with participants of the Austrian Stroke Prevention Study from the same catchment area as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1994 and 2003, subjects with first-ever and recurrent ischemic strokes admitted to the stroke unit of the Department of Neurology, Medical University of Graz (Graz, Austria) were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001085> "A hospital-based series of patients with ischaemic stroke admitted to the stroke unit of the Department of Neurology of the Medical University of Graz, Austria, investigated with brain imaging and a standardised diagnostic protocol and subtyped by stroke neurologists, whose cases are compared in genetic studies of ischaemic stroke with participants of the Austrian Stroke Prevention Study from the same catchment area as controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Medical University of Graz supports the databases of the Graz Stroke Study and the Austrian Stroke Prevention Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001085> "A hospital-based series of patients with ischaemic stroke admitted to the stroke unit of the Department of Neurology of the Medical University of Graz, Austria, investigated with brain imaging and a standardised diagnostic protocol and subtyped by stroke neurologists, whose cases are compared in genetic studies of ischaemic stroke with participants of the Austrian Stroke Prevention Study from the same catchment area as controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4301458/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All people with a new diagnosis of head and neck cancer are eligible to join the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086> "A prospective clinical cohort of people newly diagnosed with head and neck cancer, recruited before treatment at NHS centres across the United Kingdom and coordinated from Bristol, with health, lifestyle, quality-of-life and sexual-history questionnaires, clinical data, blood, saliva and tumour tissue samples and follow-up, set up to evaluate the centralisation of head and neck cancer care and as a biomedical resource for translational and prognostic research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4301458/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper we describe the methods for a large UK-based clinical cohort study in head and neck cancer called Head and Neck 5000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086> "A prospective clinical cohort of people newly diagnosed with head and neck cancer, recruited before treatment at NHS centres across the United Kingdom and coordinated from Bristol, with health, lifestyle, quality-of-life and sexual-history questionnaires, clinical data, blood, saliva and tumour tissue samples and follow-up, set up to evaluate the centralisation of head and neck cancer care and as a biomedical resource for translational and prognostic research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4301458/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People have to be recruited before their treatment starts, unless their cancer treatment was is their diagnostic procedure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086> "A prospective clinical cohort of people newly diagnosed with head and neck cancer, recruited before treatment at NHS centres across the United Kingdom and coordinated from Bristol, with health, lifestyle, quality-of-life and sexual-history questionnaires, clinical data, blood, saliva and tumour tissue samples and follow-up, set up to evaluate the centralisation of head and neck cancer care and as a biomedical resource for translational and prognostic research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4301458/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prior to treatment we give participants three questionnaires on health and lifestyle, quality of life and sexual history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001086> "A prospective clinical cohort of people newly diagnosed with head and neck cancer, recruited before treatment at NHS centres across the United Kingdom and coordinated from Bristol, with health, lifestyle, quality-of-life and sexual-history questionnaires, clinical data, blood, saliva and tumour tissue samples and follow-up, set up to evaluate the centralisation of head and neck cancer care and as a biomedical resource for translational and prognostic research.")
