# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16614111+AND+SRC%3AMED@A@format=json@A@resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multicenter case-control study comprising 811 upper aerodigestive tract cancer cases and 1,083 controls was conducted in: Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banska Bystrika (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16614111+AND+SRC%3AMED@A@format=json@A@resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This increase is likely to be due to patterns of alcohol and tobacco consumption. Genetic susceptibility to upper aerodigestive tract cancer in relation to such exposures is an important aspect that should be investigated among populations in this region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3060072/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the central European lung cancer study, the controls overlapped with the central European UADT cancer study for Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banska Bystrika (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3060072/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) central europe study [14], [37], [34] conducted from 2000 to 2002, in 6 centers from 5 countries") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3356135/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hospital-based studies in our study exclude individuals with previous or malignant disease, including respiratory disease (France, Rome, North Carolina, Northeast US, India), tobacco or alcohol related diseases (Central Europe and Western Europe) or from hospital visitors (Houston).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16614111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22655231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3356135/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To increase power, we included all controls selected for lung and kidney cancers in the Central Europe multicenter case–control study, in addition to the head and neck cancer controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001087> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract (oral cavity, pharynx, larynx and oesophagus), coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), Moscow (Russia), Banská Bystrica (Slovakia), and Olomouc and Prague (Czech Republic) to investigate genetic susceptibility to these cancers and its interaction with alcohol and tobacco use. It is the upper aerodigestive tract arm of IARC's central European multicentre case–control study of lung, head and neck and kidney cancers, and part of its controls are shared with the lung cancer arm.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3854934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Colorado Twin Registry (CTR) is a population based registry housed at the Institute for Behavioral Genetics (IBG) at the University of Colorado. Recruitment began in 1982 and includes twins born from 1968 to the present.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3854934/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Colorado Twin Registry (CTR) is housed at the Institute for Behavioral Genetics (IBG) at the University of Colorado at Boulder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23158098+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The paper provides an overview of CAP's history, how subjects were ascertained, recruited, and retained, and the domains of assessment that have been explored since the CAP's initiation in 1975.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23158098+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This paper describes the Colorado Adoption Project (CAP), an ongoing genetically informative longitudinal study of behavioral development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0890856722001794-mmc2.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two cohort studies from the Institute for Behavioral Genetics (IBG) supplied information for this project: The Colorado Adoption Project (http://ibgwww.colorado.edu/cap/) and the Colorado Twin Registry (https://www.colorado.edu/ibg/research/human-research-studies/colorado-twin-registry)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23092589") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23158098") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35378236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10859168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 22 cohorts, multiple univariate genome-wide association studies (GWASs) were performed using repeated assessments of internalizing symptoms, in a total of 64,561 children and adolescents between 3 and 18 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001088> "A combined sample of two longitudinal family studies of the Institute for Behavioral Genetics at the University of Colorado Boulder, United States: the Colorado Adoption Project, a prospective adoption study of behavioural development begun in 1975, and the Colorado Twin Registry, a population-based registry of twins born since 1968 that has recruited since 1982. Their genotyped participants are analysed together in genome-wide association meta-analyses of childhood and adolescent psychiatric traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patient material was collected at multiple clinical centers across North America, Europe, Australia and Africa (a list of contributing cohort studies and centers is given at the end of the paper).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV was established as a platform to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets obtained on HIV-1 infected individuals worldwide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3723635/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We here describe a large study of human genetic determinants of HIV-1 acquisition, performed under the auspices of the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV, a collaborative research effort bringing together the HIV-1 host genetics community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10393222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide autosomal genotypes and clinical data were obtained on a total of 9,705 PLWH from the ICGH (19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10393222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This collaboration consists of a collection of HIV natural history of disease cohorts from 17 independent studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37097752") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10393222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a sex-stratified GWAS of autosomes and the X chromosome to identify sex-specific genetic variants associated with HIV spVL and HIV control phenotypes in PLWH of European and African descent participating in the ICGH study (19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001089> "An international collaboration of the HIV host genetics community, established to combine all available genome-wide SNP data sets on people living with HIV-1 worldwide, which pools genotype and clinical data from HIV cohorts and studies in North America, Europe, Australia and Africa, many of them natural-history cohorts, to study host genetic influences on HIV-1 acquisition, viral load and spontaneous control.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32423502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36914876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36914876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10042257/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a meta-analysis of 24 GWAS with a total effective sample size of 206,106 (60,674 cases and 701,926 controls) of European (98%: Europe, USA, Australia), and East Asian (2%: Japan) ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090> "An international consortium of research groups studying the genetics of endometriosis, which pools genome-wide association data from studies in Europe, the United States, Australia and Japan, with cases identified by surgical confirmation, medical records or self-report, in meta-analyses of endometriosis risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32423502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36914876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42056605") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13195585/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IEGC is a collaborative effort that aggregates data from multiple international studies to investigate the genetic factors of endometriosis4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090> "An international consortium of research groups studying the genetics of endometriosis, which pools genome-wide association data from studies in Europe, the United States, Australia and Japan, with cases identified by surgical confirmation, medical records or self-report, in meta-analyses of endometriosis risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32423502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36914876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42056605") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13195585/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This meta-analysis included 23 cohorts with variable endometriosis case definitions including EHRs, surgically confirmed endometriosis, and self-reported information, and most studies applied logistic regression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001090> "An international consortium of research groups studying the genetics of endometriosis, which pools genome-wide association data from studies in Europe, the United States, Australia and Japan, with cases identified by surgical confirmation, medical records or self-report, in meta-analyses of endometriosis risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2761731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Around 60% of the modern descendants, still living in the 7 main villages of the valley or in the nearby areas, have been recruited based on their ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2761731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a part of a research program aimed at the identification of genes and variants associated to common disorders, we present here the analysis of a cohort of 1803 adult subjects from Val Borbera, selected based on their ancestry to represent the general population in the valley.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2761731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data and anthropometric measurements were collected by a team of MDs from the San Raffaele Hospital and by a local nurse.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2761731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the present study is to characterize the population isolate of the upper Val Borbera, a large valley localized within the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, in the Northwest of Italy, geographically secluded from the surrounding areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2761731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study, including the overall plan and the informed consent form was reviewed and approved by the institutional review boards of San Raffaele Hospital in Milan and by the Regione Piemonte ethical committee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19847309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37174278") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10178705/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All three populations belong to the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates (INGI), a project aimed at studying the genetic basis of complex diseases and phenotypes (including eating habits) [41].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001091> "A population-based cohort of adults descended from the inhabitants of the upper Val Borbera, a genetically isolated valley in the Apennine mountains of Piedmont, north-west Italy, recruited on the basis of their ancestry in the valley's villages and nearby areas, with clinical and anthropometric data collected by physicians of San Raffaele Hospital, Milan, to identify genes and variants underlying common disorders and quantitative traits; one of the isolated populations of the Italian Network of Genetic Isolates.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC184375/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients are evaluated at academic medical centers in the United States and compared with sex- and age-matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC184375/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stroke subtypes are determined by central blinded adjudication using standardized, validated mechanistic and syndromic classification systems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC184375/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ischemic Stroke Genetic Study is a prospective, multicenter genetic association study in adults with recent first-ever ischemic stroke confirmed with computed tomography or magnetic resonance imaging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC184375/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruit controls mainly from among spouses and unrelated friends of the patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC184375/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We restrict enrollment to within 30 days after onset of symptoms from the first-ever stroke to avoid potential survival bias [20-23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12848902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17845914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17845914+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ISGS is a prospective case-control genetic association study of patients with first-ever ischemic stroke at 5 US tertiary stroke centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001092> "A prospective multicentre case–control study, funded by the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, of adults with a first-ever ischaemic stroke confirmed by CT or MRI and enrolled within 30 days of onset at five academic medical centres in the United States, with centrally adjudicated stroke subtypes, and of stroke-free controls matched by age and sex and recruited mainly among the patients' spouses and unrelated friends, to investigate genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All women invited for screening from January 2011 to March 2013, at the four hospitals, were invited to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline blood samples were collected from the vast majority of the KARMA participants (69 440; 98%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The KARMA project is a prospective cohort study comprising women attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The KARMA study aims to study and determine the roles and interactions of mammographic density, genetic determinants and lifestyle in the risk of breast cancer to build a comprehensive risk prediction model including all known and established risk factors for breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were recruited from the Stockholm South General Hospital (50%), Helsingborg Hospital (27%), Skåne University Hospital, Lund, (14%) and Landskrona Hospital (9%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28180256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837703/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The platform currently holds variables and information on lifestyle factors through questionnaires, mammographic density from mammograms, genetic variants through genotyping, extensive information from health care registers and research results.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001093> "A prospective cohort of women recruited in 2011–2013 when attending mammography screening or clinical mammography at four hospitals in Sweden (in Stockholm, Helsingborg, Lund and Landskrona), with questionnaires, mammograms, blood samples and linkage to Swedish health registers, established to determine how mammographic density, genetic factors and lifestyle influence breast cancer risk and to build risk prediction models for individualised prevention and screening.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kconfab.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based in Australia, the primary aim of kConFab is to facilitate high-quality research by amassing a large and comprehensive resource of epidemiological and clinical data with biospecimens from individuals at high risk of breast and/or ovarian cancer, and from their close relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> "A research resource of epidemiological, family-history, lifestyle and clinical data and biospecimens collected since 1997 from affected and unaffected members of families with multiple cases of breast and/or ovarian cancer, recruited by research nurses through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand, and made available to researchers anywhere in the world for studies of familial breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kconfab.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Epidemiological, family history and lifestyle data, as well as biospecimens, are collected from multiple-case breast cancer families ascertained through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> "A research resource of epidemiological, family-history, lifestyle and clinical data and biospecimens collected since 1997 from affected and unaffected members of families with multiple cases of breast and/or ovarian cancer, recruited by research nurses through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand, and made available to researchers anywhere in the world for studies of familial breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kconfab.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families are recruited by research nurses located in all the largest FCCs in Australia and New Zealand into five categories described in Table 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> "A research resource of epidemiological, family-history, lifestyle and clinical data and biospecimens collected since 1997 from affected and unaffected members of families with multiple cases of breast and/or ovarian cancer, recruited by research nurses through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand, and made available to researchers anywhere in the world for studies of familial breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kconfab.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 1997, kConFab has been recruiting multiple individuals (affected and unaffected by cancer) from families that have presented to FCCs with evidence of high familial risk of breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> "A research resource of epidemiological, family-history, lifestyle and clinical data and biospecimens collected since 1997 from affected and unaffected members of families with multiple cases of breast and/or ovarian cancer, recruited by research nurses through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand, and made available to researchers anywhere in the world for studies of familial breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kconfab.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16507150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These kConFab resources are available to researchers anywhere in the world, who may apply to kConFab for biospecimens and data for use in ethically approved, peer-reviewed projects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001094> "A research resource of epidemiological, family-history, lifestyle and clinical data and biospecimens collected since 1997 from affected and unaffected members of families with multiple cases of breast and/or ovarian cancer, recruited by research nurses through family cancer clinics in Australia and New Zealand, and made available to researchers anywhere in the world for studies of familial breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All consecutive subjects with ischemic stroke (fulfilling WHO criteria12 (3)) who were admitted to the Stroke Unit at the Jagiellonian University (Krakow, Poland) and who provided informed consent were included in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects were of European origin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on clinical presentation and results from the diagnostic work-up, cases were classified into ischemic stroke etiologic subtypes according to modified TOAST criteria10 by a single reviewer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this on-going, prospective single-center, hospital-based study participants with first ever or recurrent strokes were recruited from January 22, 2002 to September 9, 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to this primary classification, cases were reclassified using CCS.11") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group included unrelated subjects taken from the population of southern Poland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001095> "An ongoing, prospective, single-centre, hospital-based study of consecutive consenting patients of European origin with first-ever or recurrent ischaemic stroke admitted since 2002 to the Stroke Unit of the Jagiellonian University in Krakow, Poland, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST and CCS criteria, together with unrelated stroke-free controls from the population of southern Poland; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because suitable control groups with available GWAS genotyping could not be identified from Poland and Belgium, controls from the KRAKOW and LEUVEN GRCs will also be genotyped as part of SiGN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5950843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The following baseline variables were collected: treatment with thrombolysis, age, baseline glycemia, diabetes mellitus, ischemic heart disease, hypertension, AF, hyperlipidemia, active smoking status, and stroke etiology according to TOAST criteria (cardio embolic, large artery atherosclerosis, small artery occlusion, other causes, and undetermined etiology) (16).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5950843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is an analysis within the prospective Leuven Stroke Genetics Study (15).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants from the LSGS study underwent brain imaging (MRI in 91% of patients, CT in the remainder) and a standardized protocol including lab examination, carotid ultrasound or CTA and cardiac examination (echocardiography and ambulatory ECG monitoring) in all patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases of European descent with cerebral ischemia, defined as a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation or a TIA with a new ischemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging, who were admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals (Leuven, Belgium) were enrolled in the LSGS between 2005 and 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29867722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control individuals were recruited in the same population amongst healthy individuals, spouses of patients suffering from neurological diseases (amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, ischemic stroke or multiple sclerosis), and from the Leuven University Gerontology Database as previously described.27") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001096> "A prospective hospital-based study of patients of European descent with cerebral ischaemia (a clinical stroke with imaging confirmation, or a transient ischaemic attack with a new ischaemic lesion on diffusion-weighted imaging) admitted to the Stroke Unit of the University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, from 2005 to 2009, with standardised diagnostic work-up and TOAST subtyping, together with controls recruited from the same population; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency matched to patient cases by age, ascertained through nonurology and nononcology clinics") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible patients with CaP, ascertained in urology and oncology clinics or through primary referral, must have had a histologically confirmed first primary CaP of any stage, grade, or pathologic classification.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Figure 1 depicts the MADCaP Network’s organizational structure, which has seven participant accrual centers in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal, and South Africa with several SSA and US centers partnered to enhance capacity building and offer mentorship.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this clinic-based case-control study, eligible participants were men older than age 30 years residing in each MADCaP center’s catchment area and self-identifying as black African with no known or self-reported European, Middle Eastern, or Asian ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed common data elements and instruments, regulatory infrastructure, and biosample collection, processing, and shipping protocols.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30260755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6223491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate Network, which includes seven SSA centers partnering with five US centers to study the genetics and epidemiology of CaP in SSA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001097> "A multicentre, clinic-based case-control study of prostate cancer run since 2016 by the Men of African Descent and Carcinoma of the Prostate (MADCaP) Network at seven accrual centres in Ghana, Nigeria, Senegal and South Africa, with partner institutions in the United States, which under common eligibility criteria, instruments and biosample protocols enrols men over 30 who self-identify as black African: incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases from urology and oncology clinics, and cancer-free controls frequency-matched by age from other clinics in the same catchment areas, to study the genetics and epidemiology of prostate cancer in sub-Saharan Africa.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2390537/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An analytical data set was put together for these analyses from our studies conducted in Jamaica, US (Maywood, Il) and Nigeria during the period 1994–1999 and resulted in a final data set consisting of a total of 3, 460 participants of which 1,409 were from Jamaica, 809 were from the US and 1,242 individuals were from Nigeria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2390537/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants from the US were recruited into the Genetic Study of Hypertension in Blacks between 1995–1999 and the Fat Reduction Intervention Trial in African-Americans (FRITAA) between 1995–1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2883343/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples were obtained from a larger cohort of families enrolled in the studies of blood pressure at Loyola University in Maywood, IL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2883343/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The survey enrolled a representative random sample of the population between the ages of 18 and 74, regardless of obesity phenotype.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433493") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28430825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5419579/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Maywood cohort consisted of African Americans from Maywood, IL, who were enrolled in studies of blood pressure at the Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine, Maywood, IL, USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001098> "A cohort of African-American families in Maywood, Illinois, United States, recruited from 1995 by Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine from a representative random sample of residents aged 18 to 74 for its family studies of blood pressure and the genetics of hypertension in populations of West African origin, in which Maywood was the United States site alongside Nigeria and Jamaica.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001099> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001099>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10613336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10613336") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10613336+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Minnesota Breast Cancer Family Study is a historical cohort study of relatives of a consecutive series of 426 breast cancer cases (probands) identified between 1944 and 1952.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001099> "A historical cohort of multigenerational families in Minnesota, United States, ascertained through a consecutive, family-history-unselected series of breast cancer probands diagnosed from 1944 to 1952 at the University of Minnesota, followed up by telephone interview and mailed questionnaire to measure cancer incidence and risk factors in their relatives (sisters, daughters, granddaughters, nieces and marry-ins).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10613336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10613336") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10613336+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The incidence of cancer and the measurement of risk factors in sisters, daughters, granddaughters, nieces, and marry-ins was determined through telephone interviews and mailed questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001099> "A historical cohort of multigenerational families in Minnesota, United States, ascertained through a consecutive, family-history-unselected series of breast cancer probands diagnosed from 1944 to 1952 at the University of Minnesota, followed up by telephone interview and mailed questionnaire to measure cancer incidence and risk factors in their relatives (sisters, daughters, granddaughters, nieces and marry-ins).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10613336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1186%2Fs13058-022-01524-0/MediaObjects/13058_2022_1524_MOESM1_ESM.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Almost all (99%) women in the 426 families were Caucasian and from Minnesota.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001099> "A historical cohort of multigenerational families in Minnesota, United States, ascertained through a consecutive, family-history-unselected series of breast cancer probands diagnosed from 1944 to 1952 at the University of Minnesota, followed up by telephone interview and mailed questionnaire to measure cancer incidence and risk factors in their relatives (sisters, daughters, granddaughters, nieces and marry-ins).")
