AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects with clinical suspicion of a stroke were admitted through the emergency room to a dedicated stroke unit supervised by a vascular neurologist.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001100> "A prospective hospital-based registry of adults with ischaemic stroke, of any ethnic or racial group, admitted through the emergency room to the dedicated stroke unit of the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute at JFK Medical Center in Edison, New Jersey, United States, which enrolled first-ever and recurrent strokes of any severity from 2000 to 2009 with standardised investigations and TOAST subtyping; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2000 to 2009, 1,139 subjects with ischemic strokes were enrolled in this registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001100> "A prospective hospital-based registry of adults with ischaemic stroke, of any ethnic or racial group, admitted through the emergency room to the dedicated stroke unit of the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute at JFK Medical Center in Edison, New Jersey, United States, which enrolled first-ever and recurrent strokes of any severity from 2000 to 2009 with standardised investigations and TOAST subtyping; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MCISS was initiated as a prospective hospital based stroke registry at the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute (Edison, NJ, U.S.A.).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001100> "A prospective hospital-based registry of adults with ischaemic stroke, of any ethnic or racial group, admitted through the emergency room to the dedicated stroke unit of the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute at JFK Medical Center in Edison, New Jersey, United States, which enrolled first-ever and recurrent strokes of any severity from 2000 to 2009 with standardised investigations and TOAST subtyping; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There was no selection criterion based upon stroke severity, and both first-ever and recurrent strokes were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001100> "A prospective hospital-based registry of adults with ischaemic stroke, of any ethnic or racial group, admitted through the emergency room to the dedicated stroke unit of the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute at JFK Medical Center in Edison, New Jersey, United States, which enrolled first-ever and recurrent strokes of any severity from 2000 to 2009 with standardised investigations and TOAST subtyping; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two independent investigators (one of which was a board-certified neurologist with expertise in vascular neurology) reviewed the data, and all strokes were classified into etiological subtypes using TOAST criteria10 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001100> "A prospective hospital-based registry of adults with ischaemic stroke, of any ethnic or racial group, admitted through the emergency room to the dedicated stroke unit of the New Jersey Neuroscience Institute at JFK Medical Center in Edison, New Jersey, United States, which enrolled first-ever and recurrent strokes of any severity from 2000 to 2009 with standardised investigations and TOAST subtyping; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12588707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical and neuropsychological assessments were conducted annually from baseline (Year 0) to Year 5 follow-up, while brain MRI scans were performed every 2 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12588707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From August 2010 to February 2020, a total of 700 patients consented to participate and were enrolled in the Harmonization study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12588707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were eligible and invited to participate if they were: (i) aged 50 years and above; (ii) able to undergo brain MRI; (iii) not diagnosed with aphasia or dysarthria that affected neuropsychological assessments; and (iv) diagnosed with no cognitive impairment, cognitive impairment no dementia and dementia due to AD, VaD or both.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12588707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Harmonization study is an ongoing prospective study which recruited patients from memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St. Luke’s Hospital in Singapore, aiming to examine cognitive deterioration and associated biomarkers in older Asian individuals with cognitive impairment and dementia due to AD and/or cerebrovascular disease (CeVD).8,9") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12588707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are indebted to staff of the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University Health System, Singapore, for their efforts in recruiting and assessing Harmonization participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38038215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40796328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41988974") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41160443") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41160443+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This manuscript reviewed the rationale, unique positioning, design, methodology, and findings from the HARMONISATION study, a prospective observational study of VCI and AD in multi-ethnic Asians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001101> "A prospective observational cohort of older multi-ethnic Asian patients aged 50 or over with no cognitive impairment, mild cognitive impairment or dementia due to Alzheimer's disease and/or cerebrovascular disease, recruited from 2010 at the memory clinics of the National University Hospital and St Luke's Hospital in Singapore and assessed by the Memory Aging and Cognition Centre, National University of Singapore, with annual clinical and neuropsychological follow-up for up to five years and brain MRI, retinal and blood biomarker data, to study vascular cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31551913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4,253 additional CCS-phenotyped cases from 10 GRCs across Europe and the US have been previously genotyped prior to initiating SiGN (BRAINS, EDIN, GASROS, GEOS, ISGS, NHS, MUNICH, OXVASC, ST GEORGE’S, and SWISS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> "A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31551913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4056331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GASROS Boston, USA Hospital-based 2003–2009") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> "A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31551913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were all consecutive patients aged 18 years presenting with ischemic stroke and admitted to the Massachusetts General Hospital (MGH) Stroke Unit through the Emergency Department, or evaluated in the MGH Neurology outpatient clinics, as well as on the inpatient Medical and Vascular Surgical services from January 2003 to July 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> "A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31551913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were recruited among the stroke-free adults presenting to the MGH outpatient clinics and matched with the stroke cases on the basis of age, sex and ancestry information obtained from principal component analysis of GWAS data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> "A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31551913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genes Affecting Stroke Risk and Outcome Study (GASROS) is a single-center prospective cohort that enrolled cases with acute ischemic stroke, aged more than 18 years who presented to MGH from 2003 to 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001102> "A hospital-based study at the Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, United States, that from 2003 enrolled adults with acute ischaemic stroke (consecutive patients admitted to its stroke unit through the emergency department, or seen in its neurology clinics or on other inpatient services), with stroke-free controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics matched on age, sex and ancestry, to study genetic influences on the risk and outcome of ischaemic stroke; one of the genetic research centres of the Stroke Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32716505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9446843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this study, the primary endpoint was death from melanoma which was ascertained through MIA clinical records and linkage to Australian Cancer Registries (including the New South Wales Cancer Registry), electoral rolls, and the Birth and Death Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> "A cohort of patients with histopathologically confirmed cutaneous melanoma managed at Melanoma Institute Australia in Sydney, Australia, identified with written informed consent from the institute's Biospecimen Bank and Research Database, whose germline DNA was genotyped genome-wide in phases from 2014 and who are followed prospectively for outcomes including death from melanoma, ascertained from clinical records and linkage to Australian cancer registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32716505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9446843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were genotyped in phases using the Oncoarray in 2014 and 2016, and the Global Screening Array in 2018 (Illumina, San Diego).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> "A cohort of patients with histopathologically confirmed cutaneous melanoma managed at Melanoma Institute Australia in Sydney, Australia, identified with written informed consent from the institute's Biospecimen Bank and Research Database, whose germline DNA was genotyped genome-wide in phases from 2014 and who are followed prospectively for outcomes including death from melanoma, ascertained from clinical records and linkage to Australian cancer registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32716505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9446843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants’ clinical and biospecimen data were captured and prospectively collected follow- up for outcomes including death due to melanoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> "A cohort of patients with histopathologically confirmed cutaneous melanoma managed at Melanoma Institute Australia in Sydney, Australia, identified with written informed consent from the institute's Biospecimen Bank and Research Database, whose germline DNA was genotyped genome-wide in phases from 2014 and who are followed prospectively for outcomes including death from melanoma, ascertained from clinical records and linkage to Australian cancer registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32716505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9446843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples for this cohort were derived from the Melanoma Institute Australia (MIA) Biospecimen Bank (protocol HREC/10/RPAH/530) and patient information from the MIA Research Database (protocol HREC/11/RPAH/444).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> "A cohort of patients with histopathologically confirmed cutaneous melanoma managed at Melanoma Institute Australia in Sydney, Australia, identified with written informed consent from the institute's Biospecimen Bank and Research Database, whose germline DNA was genotyped genome-wide in phases from 2014 and who are followed prospectively for outcomes including death from melanoma, ascertained from clinical records and linkage to Australian cancer registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32716505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36064556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9446843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With written, informed consent, patients with histo-pathological confirmed CM cases managed at MIA, Sydney, Australia were identified from this Biospecimen Bank and Database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001103> "A cohort of patients with histopathologically confirmed cutaneous melanoma managed at Melanoma Institute Australia in Sydney, Australia, identified with written informed consent from the institute's Biospecimen Bank and Research Database, whose germline DNA was genotyped genome-wide in phases from 2014 and who are followed prospectively for outcomes including death from melanoma, ascertained from clinical records and linkage to Australian cancer registries.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2009–2011, 1153 participants from the 3 Cities Study, aged 75 years or more, had an initial eye examination and were scheduled for eye examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of the Montrachet Study were recruited from an ongoing population‐based study, the Three‐City (3C) Study, which examined the vascular risk factors for dementia (2003).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Technicians conducted the eye examination in the Department of Ophthalmology, University Hospital Dijon, France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Montrachet (Maculopathy Optic Nerve nuTRition neurovAsCular and HEarT diseases) Study is a population‐based study designed to find associations between age‐related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly as a primary objective.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The eye examination comprised visual acuity, refraction, visual field, ocular surface assessment, photographs and OCT of the macula and the optic disc, measurement of intra‐ocular pressure, central corneal thickness and macular pigment assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26466845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5057364/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, from 22 October 2009, until 31 March 2013, 900 volunteers with an MRI and 253 without an MRI were recruited in the Montrachet Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001104> "A population-based study of people aged 75 years or older in Dijon, France, recruited from 2009 to 2013 among participants of the Three-City (3C) Study, who had eye examinations, including photographs and optical coherence tomography of the macula and optic disc, at Dijon University Hospital, designed to find associations between age-related eye diseases and neurologic and heart diseases in the elderly.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001105> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001105>)

