AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22306652") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were consecutive European Caucasians recruited from a single dedicated Stroke Unit at the Department of Neurology, Klinikum Großhadern, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Munich.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001105> "A hospital-based collection of consecutive patients of European ancestry with ischaemic stroke, recruited from 2002 to 2009 at the dedicated stroke unit of the Department of Neurology, Klinikum Großhadern, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Munich, Germany, with stroke subtypes assigned by TOAST criteria; the cases were genotyped genome-wide in the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 ischaemic stroke study and contribute to METASTROKE, the Stroke Genetics Network (SiGN) and MEGASTROKE.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.66") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hence, the first wave of data collection was carried out in 2007, in a sample of female twin pairs (n = 874) living in the region of Murcia, who were born between 1940 and 1966 (age range: 40 to 67).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.66") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information about the individuals comes from the computerized databases available at the regional health system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.66") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MTR was born in 2006 based on an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.66") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Murcia Twin Registry (MTR) is a population-based twin registry of adult multiples in the region of Murcia, located in southeast of Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.66") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The general goal of this initiative was to constitute a basic research tool for the analysis of the relative contribution of genetic and environmental factors to the development of complex phenotypes, focusing on health and health-related behaviors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41913940") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23046559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23046559+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There have been three waves of data collection and today the MTR databases include questionnaire and anthropometric data as well as biological samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001106> "A population-based register of adult twins and other multiples from the region of Murcia, southeast Spain, created in 2006 through an agreement between the University of Murcia and the Murcia Health Council, which identifies twins in the computerised databases of the regional health system and collects interview, questionnaire and anthropometric data in successive waves, with a biobank, for research on genetic and environmental influences on health and health-related behaviours; it began with female twins born 1940-1966 and later added male and opposite-sex twins.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HMS participants were recruited from nursing homes in 24 municipalities in one county in middle Norway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NEXGENS is a collaboration between the following 5 institutions: University of Exeter, King’s College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, University of Oslo, and Stavanger University Hospital which undertakes secondary analysis of data from Alzheimer’s disease patients from cohort studies and patient registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REDIC-NH participants were recruited at admission to one of 47 nursing homes in 4 counties in Norway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AddNeuroMed study involves six cross-European collection study sites; London (United Kingdom), Toulouse (France), Perugia (Italy), Kuopio (Finland), Lodz (Poland), and Thessaloniki (Greece) and has been described previously.24") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PADR study is affiliated to NorCog.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38784964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11114588/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "and from the following outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece (Italian and Greek Hospital Outpatients): Centre for Neurodegenerative Disorders, University of Brescia; IRCCS Casa Sollievo della Sofferenza, Neuropsychiatry Clinic of the Eginition Hospital, Athens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001107> "A collaboration of the University of Exeter, King's College London, Innlandet Hospital Trust, the University of Oslo and Stavanger University Hospital that undertakes secondary analysis of data on patients with Alzheimer's disease from cohort studies and patient registries, to study the genetics of neuropsychiatric symptoms such as psychosis in dementia. Its sources are the Norwegian registry of persons assessed for cognitive symptoms (NorCog) with the affiliated Progression of Alzheimer's Disease and Resource Use study, the REDIC-NH and Health and Memory Study nursing-home cohorts in Norway, AddNeuroMed, and hospital outpatient clinics in Italy and Greece.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2930111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were community volunteers and patient spouses; 353 (ages 67–90; mean 86.3±4.1 years) were evaluated by neurologists in Oregon and were free of neurodegenerative disease, the remaining 1633 (ages 21–90, mean 67.0±12.0 years) self-reported as neurologically healthy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2930111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PD-HLA association was uniform across genetic and environmental risk strata, and strong in sporadic (P=5.5×10−10) and late-onset (P=2.4×10−8) PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2930111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were diagnosed using the modified UK Brain Bank criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2930111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were recruited from the NGRC clinics in Oregon, Washington, New York and Georgia, using uniform criteria for diagnosis,23 subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation.2–5") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20711177+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a genome-wide association study of 2,000 individuals with Parkinson's disease (cases) and 1,986 unaffected controls from the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (NGRC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20711177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32566740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7293233/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnosis, subject selection, and data collection were performed by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium (NGRC) investigators at the four NGRC-affiliated movement disorder clinics, using standardized methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001108> "A case-control sample of people with Parkinson's disease, diagnosed by modified UK Brain Bank criteria, and neurologically healthy controls (community volunteers and patients' spouses), recruited by the NeuroGenetics Research Consortium at affiliated neurology and movement disorder clinics in Oregon, Washington, Georgia and New York, United States, with uniform, standardised methods for diagnosis, subject selection, data collection and DNA preparation, for genetic and gene-environment studies of Parkinson's disease, and genotyped genome-wide.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21573225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21998595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2883343/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we report a comprehensive GWA study of two anthropometric traits, height and body mass index (BMI), in two population samples of predominantly West African ancestry: African-Americans from Maywood, IL, and Nigerians from Igbo-Ora and Ibadan, Nigeria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21573225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21998595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3353888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both projects were reviewed and approved by the Institutional Review Board of the sponsoring US institutions (Loyola University Chicago and Howard University) and the Joint Ethical Committee of the University of Ibadan/University College Hospital, Ibadan, Nigeria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21573225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21998595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3353888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were recruited from Yoruba-speaking communities in southwest Nigeria as part of a long-term study on the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21573225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21998595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3353888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants from Idikan were controls in the Africa-America Diabetes Mellitus (AADM) Study recruited from Ibadan [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400458") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21573225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21998595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22615923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3353888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample is comprised of unrelated adults with normal or elevated blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town with a population of about 50,000; and from Idikan, a low-income neighborhood in the near-by city of Ibadan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001109> "A Loyola University Chicago project on the genetics of hypertension in people of West African origin, whose genome-wide association sample consists of unrelated Yoruba-speaking adults with normal or raised blood pressure from Igbo-Ora, a rural town, and Idikan, a low-income neighbourhood of Ibadan, in southwest Nigeria, recruited as part of a long-term study of the environmental and genetic factors underlying hypertension; the Idikan participants were controls of the Africa America Diabetes Mellitus study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All these lung cancer cases were histologically confirmed as incident NSCLC by at least two pathologists, who had not received chemo- or radio-therapy before diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> "A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer-free controls were selected from those participants in the community screening of non-communicable diseases, frequency- matched to cases by age, sex, and geographic regions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> "A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the present study, we newly performed genome-wide scan for 19,546 samples (NJMU GSA project: 10,248 cases and 9,298 controls) using Illumina Global Screening Array (GSA), which included three studies") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> "A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7015703") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nanjing GSA study: 4,149 cases and 3,198 controls from Nanjing and Shanghai; Beijing GSA study: 2,155 cases and 2,035 controls from Beijing and Tianjin; and Guangzhou GSA study: 3,944 cases and 4,065 controls from Guangdong") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> "A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31326317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42152146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13348699/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, these included the NJMU Global Screening Array project (10,248 cases and 9,298 controls), with participants recruited from five major cities in China (Nanjing, Shanghai, Beijing, Tianjin, and Guangzhou);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001110> "A case-control sample of Chinese patients with histologically confirmed incident non-small cell lung cancer, untreated by chemotherapy or radiotherapy before diagnosis, and cancer-free controls from community screening for non-communicable diseases, frequency-matched on age, sex and region, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array by Nanjing Medical University, China; it combines three regional case-control studies, from Nanjing and Shanghai, from Beijing and Tianjin, and from Guangdong.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4724255/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seven tests that were administered by at least seven of the eight sites (with the exception of the Montreal Cognitive Assessment [MoCA] which was administered at six of the eight sites) were defined as the “core battery” (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4724255/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled and clinically assessed 1,424 participants with PD in studies at eight sites which together comprise the PD Cognitive Genetics Consortium (PDCGC; Appendix e-1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5056861/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pacific Northwest Udall Center (PANUC), Portland, Oregon, and Seattle, Washington (all 6 are Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson’s Disease Research); and Rush University Medical Center, Chicago, Illinois.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical and genetic data for the project are stored and managed at the Coordinating Center at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each patient has undergone a detailed neurological evaluation and cognitive testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26296077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27571329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38870440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001664.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are presently undertaking a large-scale, two-stage study designed to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001111> "A consortium of academic Parkinson's disease research centres in the United States, several of them Morris K. Udall Centers of Excellence for Parkinson's Disease Research, that pools patients with Parkinson's disease enrolled in the centres' studies, each given a detailed neurological evaluation and a shared core battery of cognitive tests, with a coordinating centre at the University of Washington and VA Puget Sound Health Care System in Seattle, to identify genetic risk factors for cognitive impairment in Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21673961") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21673961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108970/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "POC (Polish Ovarian Cancer Study) Szczecin, Poznan, Opole and Rzeszow, Poland Population-based case-control 545 55.0 (0.5) 525 57.5 (0.5)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112> "A case-control study of ovarian cancer in Poland, with participants from Szczecin, Poznań, Opole and Rzeszów, that is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21673961") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21673961") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108970/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The association of ovarian carcinoma risk with the polymorphism rs1271572 in the estrogen receptor beta (ESR2) gene was examined in 4946 women with primary invasive ovarian carcinoma and 6582 controls in a pooled analysis of ten case-control studies within the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (OCAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001112> "A case-control study of ovarian cancer in Poland, with participants from Szczecin, Poznań, Opole and Rzeszów, that is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38412344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.99") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SALTY study was a collaborative effort between STR and researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113> "A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38412344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.99") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data collection began in the fall of 2008 by sending an extensive questionnaire to 24,914 Swedish twins, and it was completed in the summer of 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113> "A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38412344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.99") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data collection consisted of three parts: (1) an extensive self-report paper questionnaire; (2) saliva collection for DNA extraction (see under biobanking) and (3) a request to participate in a web-based investigation that included questions on musical experience, tendency to experience psychological flow and creative achievement, as well as tests of cognitive and motor performance.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113> "A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38412344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747977") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.99") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The target population was the younger part of the SALT cohort born between 1943 and 1958.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001113> "A study of the younger part of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study (SALT) cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry, twins born 1943–1958, who in 2008–2010 were sent an extensive self-report questionnaire, a request for saliva for DNA and an invitation to a web-based investigation, carried out by the registry with researchers in epidemiology, medicine, political science and economics.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17208583+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Severe Asthma Network (Severe Asthma Research Program) was established by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2001 to advance collectively the study of severe asthma to determine factors that differentiated these patients or subjects from those with milder asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5832534/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2001 to 2012 the NIH/NHLBI supported the Severe Asthma Research Program (SARP) I and II cohorts to study mechanisms differentiating severe from non-severe asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5832534/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In November 2012 the NIH/NHLBI formed SARP III, a network of U.S. investigators and a data coordinating center (DCC) located at regional academic health centers involved in severe asthma research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5832534/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The selection of specific features to examine with age was exploratory to generate hypotheses to be tested further in the longitudinal protocol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5832534/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To accomplish this goal, a cohort of adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma was recruited for detailed characterization and enrollment into an observational study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17208583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28866107") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8665111/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome Sequencing for “NHLBI TOPMed: Severe Asthma Research Program (SARP)” (phs001446.v1.p1) was performed at NYGC Genomics (HHSN268201500016C).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001114> "A research programme of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, established in 2001 (also called the Severe Asthma Network), in which a network of investigators at academic health centres in the United States recruits adults and children with severe and non-severe asthma for detailed phenotypic characterization, in the SARP I and II cohorts (2001–2012) and the longitudinal SARP III cohort (from 2012), to study the mechanisms that distinguish severe from non-severe asthma; the genomes of some of its participants were sequenced in NHLBI's Trans-Omics for Precision Medicine programme.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29797644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biological samples are banked for future genomics and proteomics studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29797644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initiated in 2014, the SCCRIP study prospectively recruits patients diagnosed with SCD and includes retrospective and longitudinal collection of clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial, and health outcomes data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29797644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Jude Children's Research Hospital established the Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program (SCCRIP), to conduct research in a clinically evaluated cohort of individuals with SCD across their lifetime.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11652775/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SCCRIP evaluates the health outcomes of patients with SCD throughout their life span to understand the disease progression and long-term effects of therapies and interpret the role of various genetic and environmental factors on health outcomes to improve their quality of life.15") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29797644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39373640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41870384") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13139885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Jude Children's Research Hospital (coordinating site), Methodist Comprehensive Sickle Cell Center, The Regional One Health Diggs‐Kraus Sickle Cell Clinic, and three St. Jude affiliate sites (clinicaltrials.gov #NCT02098863) [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001115> "A lifespan cohort study of people with sickle cell disease in the United States, established in 2014 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, that prospectively enrols patients at St. Jude (the coordinating site), two other sickle cell centres and St. Jude affiliate sites, collects retrospective and longitudinal clinical, neurocognitive, geospatial, psychosocial and health-outcome data and banks biological samples, to study disease progression from childhood into adulthood and the long-term effects of therapies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16900881+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all, 1,892 subjects were enrolled to participate in the family-based study; 1,623 of these subjects belong to 324 families, each of which has at least 2 siblings affected with T2DM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16900881+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase I of the Sikh Diabetes Study (SDS) was launched to build the population resources required to initiate a large-scale genetic epidemiological study of diabetes in an Asian Indian population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16900881+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SDS is focused on the Khatri Sikh population of North India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All AIDHS/SDS participants were recruited from the northern part of India between 2003 to 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Asian Indian Diabetic Heart Study/Sikh Diabetes Study (AIDHS/SDS) is a case-control study designed to investigate the association between genetic and environmental factors and their risk on type 2 diabetes (T2D) and cardiovascular disease in a population of Punjabi ancestry from India.60, 61") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16900881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38152657") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion was based on those with Sikh surnames of North Indian origin, and speaking the Punjabi language.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001116> "A genetic epidemiological study of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease in Punjabi-speaking Sikhs of North Indian origin, begun as a family-based study of Khatri Sikh families with at least two siblings affected by type 2 diabetes and extended as a case-control study, with participants recruited in northern India from 2003, to investigate genetic and environmental risk factors for type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001117> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001117>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34283174") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34283174") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8341359/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Jude Children’ Research Hospital Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program (SCCRIP) longitudinal cohort study (clinicaltrials.gov #NCT02098863).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001117> "A cohort of individuals with sickle cell disease recruited from Baylor College of Medicine and from the Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program (SCCRIP) cohort at St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, whose whole genomes were sequenced to define genotype-phenotype relations in sickle cell disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34283174") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34283174") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8341359/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To better define genotype–phenotype relations in SCD, we initiated the Sickle Cell Genome Project (SGP) by performing whole-genome sequencing (WGS) on participants from Baylor College of Medicine (BCM)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001117> "A cohort of individuals with sickle cell disease recruited from Baylor College of Medicine and from the Sickle Cell Clinical Research and Intervention Program (SCCRIP) cohort at St. Jude Children's Research Hospital, whose whole genomes were sequenced to define genotype-phenotype relations in sickle cell disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582024/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all cases, ischemic stroke was defined as a focal neurological deficit lasting >24 hours; in 1 cohort (St George's), cases of transient ischemic attack with associated recent brain infraction were also included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke, including some with transient ischaemic attack and recent brain infarction, recruited at St George's in London, United Kingdom, from 1995 to 2008, genotyped in the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 ischaemic stroke study and one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582024/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 (WTCCC2) ischemic stroke study comprises ischemic stroke cases recruited from 3 centers in the United Kingdom (St George's London, Oxford, and Edinburgh) and 1 center in Munich, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke, including some with transient ischaemic attack and recent brain infarction, recruited at St George's in London, United Kingdom, from 1995 to 2008, genotyped in the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 ischaemic stroke study and one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4056331/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4,253 additional CCS-phenotyped cases from 10 GRCs across Europe and the US have been previously genotyped prior to initiating SiGN (BRAINS, EDIN, GASROS, GEOS, ISGS, NHS, MUNICH, OXVASC, ST GEORGE’S, and SWISS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke, including some with transient ischaemic attack and recent brain infarction, recruited at St George's in London, United Kingdom, from 1995 to 2008, genotyped in the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 ischaemic stroke study and one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4056331/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ST GEORGE’S London, England Hospital-based 1995–2008 684 18–102 47 100 0") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001118> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke, including some with transient ischaemic attack and recent brain infarction, recruited at St George's in London, United Kingdom, from 1995 to 2008, genotyped in the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 ischaemic stroke study and one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20570912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3378688/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study recruitment commenced in October 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119> "A family study in the United Kingdom that from October 2002 recruited women attending the Cambridge and Huntingdon NHS breast screening services who had one or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts or nieces) who had also had screening mammograms, with further families found through newspaper and radio advertisements, to map genes underlying quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular mammographic breast density and sex steroid hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20570912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were also ascertained through newspaper and radio advertisements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119> "A family study in the United Kingdom that from October 2002 recruited women attending the Cambridge and Huntingdon NHS breast screening services who had one or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts or nieces) who had also had screening mammograms, with further families found through newspaper and radio advertisements, to map genes underlying quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular mammographic breast density and sex steroid hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20570912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Sisters in Breast Screening Study (SIBS) was designed to study the genetic basis of quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular breast density and sex-hormone levels [Varghese et al., 2012; Kataoka et al., 2009].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119> "A family study in the United Kingdom that from October 2002 recruited women attending the Cambridge and Huntingdon NHS breast screening services who had one or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts or nieces) who had also had screening mammograms, with further families found through newspaper and radio advertisements, to map genes underlying quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular mammographic breast density and sex steroid hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20570912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9006574/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women who attended the local Cambridge and Huntingdon Breast Screening Services to have mammographic examinations under the National Health Service (NHS) Breast Screening Program were identified and invited to participate in the study if they had 1 or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts, or nieces) who had also undergone mammographic screening.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001119> "A family study in the United Kingdom that from October 2002 recruited women attending the Cambridge and Huntingdon NHS breast screening services who had one or more female blood relatives (sisters, half-sisters, first cousins, aunts or nieces) who had also had screening mammograms, with further families found through newspaper and radio advertisements, to map genes underlying quantitative phenotypes related to breast cancer, in particular mammographic breast density and sex steroid hormone levels.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following provision of informed consent, SJLIFE participants (both in the original and expanded cohorts) are invited to return to SJCRH at least once every 5 years for protocol-based medical evaluations and assessments of neurocognitive function, physical performance status and patient-reported outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2015, the criteria were expanded to include survivors of any age at the time of evaluation who had lived ≥5 years post diagnosis and who had been diagnosed through 30 June 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Jude Children’s Research Hospital (SJCRH) established in 2007 the prospective St. Jude Lifetime (SJLIFE) cohort, open to survivors of all paediatric cancer subtypes representing the spectrum of paediatric, adolescent and young adult cancers, as well as frequency-matched community controls,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SJLIFE study utilizes a retrospective cohort study design with prospective follow-up and ongoing accrual of patients diagnosed and treated at SJCRH over five decades (1962–2012).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original inclusion criteria, as established in 2007, were limited to adults ≥18 years of age at the time of evaluation who were treated at SJCRH and had lived ≥10 years from initial cancer diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21370418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33374007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8453382/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "including collection of comprehensive treatment data on all participants, provision of protocol-based medical assessments, assessment of patient-reported outcomes, validation of self-reported medical events, performance of periodic longitudinal evaluations and collection of biologic specimens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001120> "A retrospective cohort with prospective follow-up, established in 2007 by St. Jude Children's Research Hospital in Memphis, Tennessee, of survivors of paediatric cancer diagnosed and treated there between 1962 and 2012 who have survived at least five years from diagnosis (until 2015, only adults who had survived ten years), with frequency-matched community controls, who are invited back to the hospital at least every five years for protocol-based medical assessments, patient-reported outcomes and biospecimen collection, to study late health outcomes of childhood cancer and its treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2939779/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The case cohort was composed of 1786 consecutive CRC patients of Swedish origin recruited through the Swedish Low-Risk CRC Study Group from 14 different hospitals from central Sweden during 2004–2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11756881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants included in 2004–2006 were invited to fill out a self-administered lifestyle questionnaire on study inclusion (n = 1,767).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11756881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were interviewed by the same interviewer on family history of CRC and other malignancies on study inclusion and pedigrees were constructed for the families of the index-person.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11756881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five hundred thirty-six cancer-free spouses of participants, without a family history of cancer and 1,106 blood donors from Karolinska University Hospital were used as controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11756881/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted 5 haplotype-based genome-wide association analyses using sporadic stage I–IV CRC patients with lifestyle factors known to confer an increased risk of CRC as cases and healthy spouses or blood donors as controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20648012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39543761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39665592") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6483948/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the years 2004-2009 more than 3300 consecutive patients operated on for colorectal cancer (CRC) in 14 hospitals in and around Stockholm and Uppsala were included in the Swedish Colorectal Cancer Low-risk study, and gave informed consent and blood for genetic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001121> "A multicentre study in central Sweden of consecutive patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited between 2004 and 2009 at 14 hospitals by the Swedish Low-Risk Colorectal Cancer Study Group and interviewed on their family history of cancer, with a lifestyle questionnaire for those recruited in 2004–2006 and cancer-free spouses of participants serving as controls; its cases and controls are used in genetic studies of colorectal cancer risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4082340/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were enrollees in the Group Health Cooperative (Seattle, Washington) aged 24–79 years who received a colonoscopy from 1998 to 2007, donated a buccal or blood sample, and completed a structured questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> "A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4082340/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and persons who were polyp-free at the index colonoscopy (controls) were systematically recruited during both phases of recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> "A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4082340/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study recruitment took place in 2 phases, with phase 1 occurring in 1998–2003 and phase 2 occurring in 2004–2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> "A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2 | SMS_AD | Screening Markers for Colorectal Cancer Study (advanced adenomas) | case-control | USA | Illumina Oncoarray+custom iSelect | 171 | 41 (0) | 16 (39) |   F: 65.6 (10.7) M: 63.4 (9.3) |  | 130 | 73 (56.2) |   F: 58.9 (11.3) M: 62.5 (11.2)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> "A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24875374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were enrollees in an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State (Kaiser Permanente Washington (formerly Group Health Cooperative, Seattle, Washington)) aged 24–79 years who underwent an index colonoscopy for any indication between 1998 and 2007 and donated a buccal-cell or blood sample for genotyping analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001122> "A two-phase case-control study of colorectal polyps among enrollees of Group Health Cooperative (now Kaiser Permanente Washington), an integrated health-care delivery system in western Washington State, United States, aged 24–79 years who had an index colonoscopy for any indication in 1998–2003 or 2004–2007, comprising patients diagnosed with adenomas or serrated polyps and polyp-free controls who gave buccal-cell or blood samples and completed a structured questionnaire; its advanced-adenoma cases and matched polyp-free controls were genotyped for consortium genome-wide studies of colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11882254+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After giving informed consent, without violating privacy among other family members, the proband invites siblings concordant and discordant for stroke to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> "A family-based study of ischaemic stroke that from 1999 to 2011 enrolled, at clinical centres in the United States and Canada, adult probands with radiographically confirmed ischaemic stroke who had at least one living full sibling with stroke, together with their stroke-affected siblings, confirmed by central review of medical records, and where possible a stroke-free sibling, confirmed by structured telephone interview, all contacted through the proband, to search the genome for genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke by linkage and family-based association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11882254+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Screening at multiple clinical centers identifies patients (probands) with radiographically confirmed ischemic stroke and a family history of at least 1 living full sibling with stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> "A family-based study of ischaemic stroke that from 1999 to 2011 enrolled, at clinical centres in the United States and Canada, adult probands with radiographically confirmed ischaemic stroke who had at least one living full sibling with stroke, together with their stroke-affected siblings, confirmed by central review of medical records, and where possible a stroke-free sibling, confirmed by structured telephone interview, all contacted through the proband, to search the genome for genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke by linkage and family-based association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11882254+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Siblings With Ischemic Stroke Study (SWISS) aims to conduct a genome-wide scan in sibling pairs concordant or discordant for ischemic stroke to identify novel genetic risk factors through linkage analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> "A family-based study of ischaemic stroke that from 1999 to 2011 enrolled, at clinical centres in the United States and Canada, adult probands with radiographically confirmed ischaemic stroke who had at least one living full sibling with stroke, together with their stroke-affected siblings, confirmed by central review of medical records, and where possible a stroke-free sibling, confirmed by structured telephone interview, all contacted through the proband, to search the genome for genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke by linkage and family-based association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11882254+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The diagnosis of ischemic stroke in potentially concordant siblings is confirmed by systematic centralized review of medical records. The stroke-free status of potentially discordant siblings is confirmed by validated structured telephone interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> "A family-based study of ischaemic stroke that from 1999 to 2011 enrolled, at clinical centres in the United States and Canada, adult probands with radiographically confirmed ischaemic stroke who had at least one living full sibling with stroke, together with their stroke-affected siblings, confirmed by central review of medical records, and where possible a stroke-free sibling, confirmed by structured telephone interview, all contacted through the proband, to search the genome for genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke by linkage and family-based association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11882254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21940970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21940970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Siblings With Ischemic Stroke Study enrolled 312 probands with ischemic stroke from 70 US and Canadian centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001123> "A family-based study of ischaemic stroke that from 1999 to 2011 enrolled, at clinical centres in the United States and Canada, adult probands with radiographically confirmed ischaemic stroke who had at least one living full sibling with stroke, together with their stroke-affected siblings, confirmed by central review of medical records, and where possible a stroke-free sibling, confirmed by structured telephone interview, all contacted through the proband, to search the genome for genetic risk factors for ischaemic stroke by linkage and family-based association analysis.")
