# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Half of the adolescents were exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Saguenay Youth Study (SYS) is a two-generational study of adolescents and their parents (n = 1029 adolescents and 962 parents) aimed at investigating the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort is family based (481 families), including only adolescents who have one or more siblings of similar age (12 to 18 years) and both biological parents of the French-Canadian origin born in the region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was recruited via adolescents attending high schools in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada. The region is home to the largest genetic founder population in North America.11–14") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data collection took place during 2003–12 in adolescents (full) and their parents (partial), and during 2012–15 in parents (full).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17469173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27018016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5837575/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ‘non-exposed’ adolescents were matched to the ‘exposed’ adolescents by the level of maternal education and by the high school attended.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001124> "A two-generation, family-based study in the Saguenay–Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec, Canada, a genetic founder population, of adolescent sibships aged 12–18 of French-Canadian origin recruited through high schools in 2003–2012, half of them exposed prenatally to maternal cigarette smoking and matched with non-exposed adolescents for maternal education and school, and of their parents (partly assessed in 2003–2012 and fully in 2012–2015), with extensive phenotyping including brain and abdominal MRI, cardiometabolic assessments and genome-wide genotyping, to investigate the aetiology, early stages and trans-generational trajectories of common cardiometabolic and brain diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10828500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, we conducted case-control GWASs of high TSH versus reference range TSH and low TSH versus reference range TSH assessing thyroid dysfunction in up to 6,712 cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10828500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we performed much larger GWAS meta-analyses on a comprehensive collection of TH traits, including TSH within the reference range, FT4, free and total T3 concentrations, and free and total T3/FT4 ratio in up to 271,040 euthyroid individuals of European ancestry from the joint collaboration of the ThyroidOmics Consortium (www.thyroidomics.com).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10828500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The summary statistics from the GWAS meta-analyses as well as the complete colocalization results and regional association plots of the fine-mapping analyses generated in this project are available on the ThyroidOmics Consortium website (http://www.thyroidomics.com) at the Datasets section (https://transfer.sysepi.medizin.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/datasets/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10828500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted GWAS meta-analyses of reference range thyroid function including up to 271,040 euthyroid individuals from European ancestry across 46 predominantly population-based cohorts from the ThyroidOmics Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ThyroidOmics Consortium was formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function, using various omics technologies in multiple large and well-phenotyped cohort studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30367059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://genepi.med.uni-greifswald.de/thyroidomics/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The available omics include genomics, epigenomics, transcriptomics, proteomics and metabolomics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001125> "An international consortium of large, well-phenotyped cohort studies, mostly population-based, formed to study the determinants and effects of thyroid diseases and thyroid function with genomic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data, which meta-analyses genome-wide association data from its member cohorts on thyroid-stimulating hormone, free thyroxine, triiodothyronine, thyroid dysfunction and related traits and makes the summary statistics available.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3478667/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TODAY study compared metformin monotherapy with two alternative approaches, one combining metformin with a second pharmacologic agent (rosiglitazone) and one combining metformin with an intensive lifestyle-intervention program, to test the hypothesis that combination therapy initiated early in the course of youth-onset type 2 diabetes would maintain acceptable glycemic control better than metformin alone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3478667/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility criteria included an age of 10 to 17 years, type 2 diabetes according to American Diabetes Association criteria for less than 2 years, a body-mass index (BMI) at or above the 85th percentile for age and sex, a negative test for diabetes-related autoantibodies (glutamic acid decarboxylase 65 and tyrosine phosphatase),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3478667/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment started in July 2004 and ended in February 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3478667/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Treatment Options for Type 2 Diabetes in Adolescents and Youth (TODAY) study was a multicenter, randomized clinical trial funded by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11570374/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After the clinical trial (2004-2011), an observational follow-up study (TODAY2) was conducted in 2 phases (phase 1, 2011-2014; phase 2, 2014-2020).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17448130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22540912") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38815053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11570374/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 699 participants, 10 to 17 years old, diagnosed with type 2 diabetes by American Diabetes Association criteria, with duration 2 years or less, body mass index (BMI) ≥ 85th percentile for age and sex, were enrolled across 15 clinical centers in the United States (15).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001126> "A multicentre randomized clinical trial funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases that from 2004 to 2009 enrolled children and adolescents aged 10–17 years with type 2 diabetes of less than two years' duration, a body-mass index at or above the 85th percentile and no diabetes autoantibodies at 15 clinical centres in the United States, and compared metformin alone with metformin plus rosiglitazone or plus an intensive lifestyle intervention for durable glycaemic control until 2011; its participants were then followed into adulthood in the observational TODAY2 study (2011–2020).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "72 sites in the UK providing secondary care treatment for PD patients as part of the UK National Health Service (NHS) (and in selected sites, their linked academic institutions) are participating, with multicentre ethics committee and local research and development department approvals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical assessments were made in out-patient clinics, using standardized and validated scales, to document the motor and non-motor features, quality of life and drug responsiveness of the enrolled subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Grant funding is from Parkinson’s UK, the national patient care and research organization.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment of first degree relatives, to a target of 840 unaffected siblings, is underway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Tracking Parkinson’s is a multicentre prospective longitudinal epidemiologic and biomarker study of PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26485428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4927877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Young onset cases were diagnosed at or below age 50 years, and recent onset cases were diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001127> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal epidemiological and biomarker study of Parkinson's disease in the United Kingdom, funded by Parkinson's UK, that recruited patients aged 18–90 with a clinical diagnosis of Parkinson's disease of recent onset (diagnosed within the preceding 3.5 years) or young onset (diagnosed at or before age 50) at 72 National Health Service secondary-care sites, together with unaffected siblings of patients, and follows them with repeated motor, non-motor and quality-of-life assessments, genotyping and biosamples, to explain variation in the clinical phenotype of Parkinson's disease, including its relation to genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001128> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001128>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42237039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-026-02583-1/MediaObjects/41588_2026_2583_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UKS cohort is a thoroughly diagnosed case-control cohort from Universitatsklinikum Saarlandes, consisting of individuals clinically diagnosed with sporadic Alzheimer’s disease (N = 596; age-at-onset [mean ± SD]: 72.2 ± 6.6 years) and cognitively healthy, age-, gender-, and ethnicity-matched population-based controls (N = 170; age-at-exam: 64.1 ± 3.0 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001128> "A case-control cohort from Universitatsklinikum Saarlandes, Germany, consisting of individuals clinically diagnosed with sporadic Alzheimer's disease together with cognitively healthy, age-, gender- and ethnicity-matched population-based controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As per January 1, 2007 there were approximately 50,000 men aged 65-74 years in the Mid Region of Denmark, which is located from coast to coast in the middle of Jutland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the case of PAD the participant is informed of the relatively positive prognosis of leg survival and the need to initiate suitable prophylactic measures including walking/exercise, smoking cessation, low-fat diet, aspirin and statin treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the timeframe of October 2008 until October 2010 approximately 50,000 65-74 year-old Danish men will be randomized to either receive an invitation for vascular screening or being a control (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Viborg Vascular (VIVA) screening trial is a randomized, clinically controlled study designed to evaluate the benefits of vascular screening and modern vascular prophylaxis in a population of 50,000 men aged 65-74 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objective of this study is to assess the efficacy and the cost-effectiveness of a combined screening program for AAA, PAD and hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2891736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary outcome variable is all-cause mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001129> "A randomised controlled screening trial of Viborg Hospital in which the men aged 65-74 living in the Central Denmark Region were randomised, from October 2008, either to an invitation to combined screening for abdominal aortic aneurysm, peripheral arterial disease and hypertension, with preventive treatment for those found to have disease, or to no invitation, to assess the effect of screening on all-cause mortality and its cost-effectiveness.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001130> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001130>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41969536") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.un.org/unispal/document/auto-insert-204882/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20957630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20957630+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All incidence cases of childhood cancers (under the age 15) from 1998 to 2007 were collected from the West Bank Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001130> "The cancer registry of the West Bank, kept by the Palestinian Ministry of Health, which records incident cancer cases among West Bank residents; it continues the West Bank part of the population-based Palestinian Cancer Registry, established in 1996 and working regularly from 1998, which was split into separate West Bank and Gaza registries in 2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41969536") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.un.org/unispal/document/auto-insert-204882/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41969536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13068369/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2007, the conflict between the two main Palestinian political parties, Fatah and Hamas, resulted in two entirely separate cancer registries, one in Gaza and the other in the West Bank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001130> "The cancer registry of the West Bank, kept by the Palestinian Ministry of Health, which records incident cancer cases among West Bank residents; it continues the West Bank part of the population-based Palestinian Cancer Registry, established in 1996 and working regularly from 1998, which was split into separate West Bank and Gaza registries in 2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41969536") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.un.org/unispal/document/auto-insert-204882/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.un.org/unispal/document/auto-insert-204882/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Palestinian Cancer Registry (PCR) is a population-based registry established in 1996 under the umbrella of the Ministry of Health and started its regular work in 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001130> "The cancer registry of the West Bank, kept by the Palestinian Ministry of Health, which records incident cancer cases among West Bank residents; it continues the West Bank part of the population-based Palestinian Cancer Registry, established in 1996 and working regularly from 1998, which was split into separate West Bank and Gaza registries in 2007.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Demographic and clinical data were collected prospectively during the hospitalization and at 90 days, by phone or in person.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genetic samples were derived from subjects enrolled in 3 different studies: (a) Acute tPA pharmacogenomics study (Ischemic stroke cases who received tPA and were admitted to BJH/Washington University; serial NIHSS scores,19 and data on hemorrhagic transformation was collected)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were identified for the genetic studies by screening admissions at our tertiary care hospital (both in the Emergency Department and on the Inpatient Stroke Service) without regard to age, race or ethnicity, including both first-ever and recurrent strokes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke Study (ReGenesIS, Ischemic stroke cases with NIHSS > 3 points without underlying chronic neurological disease, and expected survival up to 3 months after stroke)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WUSTL patient collection included ischemic stroke cases admitted to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center (St. Louis, MO, U.S.A.) for genetic studies starting from August 1, 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24021684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Cognitive Recovery and Rehabilitation Group (CRRG) Registry (all ischemic stroke cases admitted to BJH/Washington University who consent to entering their clinical data into a stroke registry, and the collection of blood for genetic analysis).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001131> "A hospital-based collection of ischaemic stroke patients admitted from August 2008 to Barnes-Jewish Hospital/Washington University Medical Center in St. Louis, Missouri, identified by screening emergency department and inpatient stroke service admissions regardless of age, race or ethnicity and followed up at 90 days, whose DNA came from an acute tPA pharmacogenomics study, the Recovery Genomics after Ischemic Stroke (ReGenesIS) study and the Cognitive Rehabilitation and Recovery Group (CRRG) stroke registry; one of the genetic research centres of the NINDS Stroke Genetics Network.")

