AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All case subjects met the UK Brain Bank Clinical Criteria for PD (26).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomic DNA for all cases was shipped to the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute (WTSI), Cambridge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control data set was that of the previously described WTCCC2 study (25)—totalling 2930 samples from the 1958 Birth Cohort (58C) and 2737 samples from the UK Blood Services Controls (NBS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples were collected through five UK-wide centres (Supplementary Material, Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To further understand the genetic basis of PD, we undertook a PD GWAS in the UK population as part of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 (WTCCC2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21044948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3005904/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK PD cases were randomly selected from population and hospital-based clinics with an emphasis on sporadic cases with no family history for this disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001133> "The Parkinson's disease genome-wide case-control study of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and the UK Parkinson's Disease Consortium: UK patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease meeting UK Brain Bank criteria, randomly selected from population- and hospital-based clinics through five UK centres and genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, compared with the WTCCC2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK Blood Services.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between June 2004 and April 2006, 602 patients were enrolled onto the study and 535 were treated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible patients had no prior therapy for advanced disease, Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status 0 to 2, no tumor invasion of adjacent organs, and no increased bleeding risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were randomly assigned with equal probability to gemcitabine plus bevacizumab or placebo, stratified by disease extent (locally advanced v metastatic), ECOG performance status (0/1 v 2), and prior radiation (no v yes).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The following institutions participated in this study: Delaware Christiana Care Community Clinical Oncology Program (CCOP)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end point was overall survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00088894") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20606091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2917317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These encouraging data led Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB) to conduct a double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized phase III trial of gemcitabine/bevacizumab versus gemcitabine/placebo in advanced pancreatic cancer patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001134> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomised phase III trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B that enrolled patients with previously untreated locally advanced or metastatic pancreatic cancer at its participating institutions in the United States between June 2004 and April 2006, comparing gemcitabine plus bevacizumab with gemcitabine plus placebo, with overall survival as the primary end point.")

