AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between May 2005 and December 2007, 1,050 patients were randomly assigned.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following US Food and Drug Administration approval of docetaxel and prednisone for mCRPC, a double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial was conducted to determine whether the addition of bevacizumab to docetaxel and prednisone would increase OS compared with docetaxel and prednisone alone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with chemotherapy-naive progressive mCRPC with Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group performance status ≤ 2 and adequate bone marrow, hepatic, and renal function were randomly assigned to receive docetaxel 75 mg/m2 intravenously (IV) over 1 hour for 21 days plus prednisone 5 mg orally twice per day (DP) with either bevacizumab 15 mg/kg IV every 3 weeks (DP + B) or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The following institutions (with supporting Grant No. in parentheses) participated in this study: Board of Regents of the University of Oklahoma, Oklahoma City, OK,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end point was overall survival (OS), and secondary end points were progression-free survival (PFS), 50% decline in prostate-specific antigen, objective response (OR), and toxicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00110214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22454414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3383121/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was designed by the CALGB, endorsed by the ECOG, and approved by the NCI Cancer Therapy Evaluation Program (CTEP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001135> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial designed by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B and endorsed by the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group that enrolled men with chemotherapy-naive progressive metastatic castration-resistant prostate cancer at participating institutions in the United States between May 2005 and December 2007, comparing docetaxel and prednisone with or without bevacizumab, with overall survival as the primary end point.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9526730/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients should have not received adjuvant therapy and a minimum follow up of three years was requested at the time of selection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Also, 50 samples from healthy colon mucosa obtained at colonoscopy from donors (M) without cancer were included and used as reference (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Colon cancer patients were retrospectively selected during 2012 from those that had received radical surgery in the Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) between January 1996 and December 2000, and had fresh frozen tumor samples in the hospital biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we present Colonomics (https://www.colonomics.org/), a multi-omics dataset that comprises 100 stage II colon cancer patients from which samples of tumoral tissue (T) and paired normal adjacent tissue (N) were obtained from the surgical specimen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One hundred patients were included, with the criteria of a confirmed adenocarcinoma of the colon, diagnosed in stage II and the tumor was microsatellite stable (tested with five markers).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were selected to have received only radical surgery, without adjuvant chemotherapy, which also reduces potential analysis to prognosis but not prediction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.colonomics.org/home/team/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36182938") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9526730/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Colonomics project aims to study the molecular basis of colon cancer through the integrative and large-scale analysis of different molecular data and to identify useful biomarkers of diagnosis and prognosis in colon cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001136> "A multi-omics colon cancer study run by the Catalan Institute of Oncology of patients with microsatellite-stable stage II colon adenocarcinoma who had radical surgery without adjuvant therapy at Bellvitge University Hospital (Barcelona, Spain) in 1996-2000 and were selected in 2012; their tumour and paired adjacent normal mucosa, with colon mucosa from healthy donors undergoing colonoscopy as reference, were profiled for gene expression, DNA methylation, SNPs, copy number and miRNAs to find diagnostic and prognostic biomarkers of colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00601900") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012690/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CALGB 40503 was initiated in 2008 as two parallel randomized trials to compare ET alone with ET plus bevacizumab as first-line endocrine therapy for hormone receptor–positive advanced-stage breast cancer:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> "A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00601900") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012690/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible patients included women age 18 years or older with locally advanced, unresectable, or metastatic breast cancer who were postmenopausal (or receiving ovarian suppression with a leuteinizing hormone-releasing hormone agonist).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> "A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00601900") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012690/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted Cancer and Leukemia Group B (CALGB, now known as Alliance) 40503, a randomized phase III trial, to determine whether bevacizumab can prolong progression-free survival (PFS) when added to first-line ET with letrozole for hormone receptor–positive advanced-stage breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> "A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00601900") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012690/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women with hormone receptor–positive MBC were randomly assigned 1:1 in a multicenter, open-label, phase III trial of letrozole (2.5 mg orally per day) with or without bevacizumab (15 mg/kg intravenously once every 3 weeks) within strata defined by measurable disease and disease-free interval.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> "A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00601900") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27138575") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5012690/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a phase III study with letrozole as ET with a primary end point of PFS and a phase II study with tamoxifen as ET with toxicity as the primary end point (results will be reported separately).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001137> "A randomised, multicentre trial of the Cancer and Leukemia Group B (now the Alliance for Clinical Trials in Oncology), begun in the United States in 2008, of first-line endocrine therapy alone or with bevacizumab for women with hormone receptor-positive advanced-stage breast cancer who were postmenopausal or receiving ovarian suppression: a phase III comparison with letrozole, run in parallel with a phase II comparison with tamoxifen.")

