AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6428856/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants filled a web-based survey, designed by Chengdu 23Mofang Biotechnology Co., Ltd.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001138> "A research cohort of customers of 23Mofang (Chengdu 23Mofang Biotechnology Co., Ltd.), a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company, who were genotyped through its personal genome service and consented to the research use of their genotypes and of traits they self-reported in the company's web-based surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6428856/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants have electronically signed the Informed Consent Form to allow their survey responses and genotypic information for the use of research purposes only.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001138> "A research cohort of customers of 23Mofang (Chengdu 23Mofang Biotechnology Co., Ltd.), a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company, who were genotyped through its personal genome service and consented to the research use of their genotypes and of traits they self-reported in the company's web-based surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13175889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from 23Mofang Inc.—a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company—through organic posts on their official app.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001138> "A research cohort of customers of 23Mofang (Chengdu 23Mofang Biotechnology Co., Ltd.), a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company, who were genotyped through its personal genome service and consented to the research use of their genotypes and of traits they self-reported in the company's web-based surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30899065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13175889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort comprised 47,305 self-reported myopic people and 8,209 nonmyopic people, all of whom provided informed consent and underwent genotyping as part of the 23Mofang Personal Genome Services.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001138> "A research cohort of customers of 23Mofang (Chengdu 23Mofang Biotechnology Co., Ltd.), a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company, who were genotyped through its personal genome service and consented to the research use of their genotypes and of traits they self-reported in the company's web-based surveys.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4841760/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A brief demographic questionnaire was then administered to capture the participant’s self-reported age, sex, ancestry, height and weight.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4841760/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For all of the reasons highlighted above, the 3D Facial Norms (3DFN) project was initiated in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium (https://www.facebase.org), a National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research (NIDCR) initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4841760/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals were recruited for the 3DFN project at four US sites across the country: Pittsburgh PA; Seattle, WA; Houston, TX; and Iowa City, IA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4841760/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The principal goal of the 3DFN project was to construct a large, web-based, interactive craniofacial normative database comprised of 3D facial images, morphometric variables, qualitative descriptors, and genomic markers for both the clinical and research community (https://www.facebase.org/facial_norms).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6206510/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, for the Pittsburgh 3DFN cohort, DNA was extracted from saliva samples and genotyped along with 72 HapMap control samples on the Illumina HumanOmniExpress + Exome v1.2 array (Illumina, San Diego, CA, United States) plus custom content by the Center for Inherited Disease Research (CIDR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26492185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27110347") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6206510/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pittsburgh 3DFN cohort consists of 2297 participants (age 3–40 years) of self-reported Western-European descent without a history of facial defects or craniofacial surgery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001139> "A normative craniofacial study begun in 2009 as part of the FaceBase Consortium of the US National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research, which recruited healthy people aged 3 to 40 of self-reported European ancestry and without craniofacial conditions at four US sites (Pittsburgh, Seattle, Houston and Iowa City), collecting 3D facial surface images, anthropometric measurements, a demographic questionnaire and saliva DNA for genome-wide genotyping, and shares the data through a web-based repository.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9684086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2018 data for 4D-SZ volunteers who were already included in the initial cohort were excluded and will be published in a future study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9684086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the 4D-SZ cohort (trans-omics, with more time points in future studies, based in China), we also comprehensively measured the parameters including fecal/salivary microbiomes, plasma metabolites, medical test data, immune indices, physical fitness test, and facial skin imaging, as well as female life history questionnaire, lifestyle questionnaire, and psychological questionnaire (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9684086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the first time point for the vagino-cervical microbiome of the 4D-SZ cohort, 516 Chinese volunteers joined from May to July during an annual physical examination in 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8648780/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the adult Chinese individuals in this cohort were recruited for a multi-omics study, with some volunteers providing samples from as early as 2015, which would constitute the time dimension in “4D”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8648780/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort included 2984 individuals with blood samples collected during a physical examination in 2017 in the city of Shenzhen, and all these individuals were enlisted for high-depth whole-genome sequencing (Supplementary Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33563976") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34118463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34873157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8648780/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The effects of environmental factors and host genes on oral microbiome composition were investigated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001140> "A multi-omics cohort of Chinese volunteers in Shenzhen, China, run by BGI-Shenzhen and recruited largely at annual physical examinations from 2017 (some gave samples from 2015), with sampling repeated over time, combining whole-genome sequencing, metagenomes of the gut, mouth and other body sites, plasma metabolites, medical tests and questionnaires on diet and lifestyle, to study how host genetics and environment shape the microbiome and health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1473211/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to collecting natural history data, AREDS includes a clinical trial of high-dose vitamin and mineral supplements for AMD and a clinical trial of high-dose vitamin supplements for cataract.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1473211/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Age-Related Eye Disease Study, a long-term multicenter, prospective study of 4757 persons age 55 to 80 years is designed to assess the clinical course, prognosis, and risk factors of both AMD and cataract.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1473211/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Eye Institute (NEI) of the National Institutes of Health (NIH) provides primary support for the study through contract intramural research funds, with additional support from Storz Ophthalmic Pharmaceuticals, currently owned by Bausch and Lomb Pharmaceuticals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13157973/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 4757 participants aged 55 to 80 years were recruited between 1992 and 1998 at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13157973/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AREDS cohort was followed between 1992 and 2005, during which questionnaires, regular eye examinations, and genotyping were performed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10588299") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11594942") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000001.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39826679") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13157973/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The remaining 4629 took part in the cataract trial, and were randomly assigned to placebo, antioxidants, zinc, or the combination of antioxidants and zinc, depending on AMD status.8") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001142> "A multicentre prospective study sponsored by the US National Eye Institute that recruited people aged 55 to 80, with or without age-related macular degeneration or lens opacities, at 11 retinal specialty clinics in the United States from 1992 to 1998 and followed them to 2005. It studied the clinical course and risk factors of age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and included randomised, placebo-controlled trials of high-dose antioxidant vitamins and zinc for these conditions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485447/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment began in October 2006 and continued through September 2008 at the 82 clinical sites across the US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485447/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary purpose of Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2 (AREDS2) is to evaluate the efficacy and safety of lutein+zeaxanthin (L+Z) and/or omega-3 long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acid (LCPUFA) supplementation in reducing the risk of developing advanced AMD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485447/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study will also assess the reduction in zinc and the omission of beta-carotene from original AREDS formulation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485447/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is supported by the intramural program funds and contracts from the National Eye Institute/National Institutes of Health (NEI/NIH), Department of Health and Human Services, Bethesda, MD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22840421") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23644932") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23644932+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Age-Related Eye Disease Study 2 (AREDS2), a multicenter, randomized, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 study with a 2 × 2 factorial design, conducted in 2006-2012 and enrolling 4203 participants aged 50 to 85 years at risk for progression to advanced AMD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001143> "A multicentre, randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial sponsored by the US National Eye Institute and run from 2006 to 2012 at 82 clinical centres in the United States. It enrolled people aged 50 to 85 at risk of progressing to advanced age-related macular degeneration to test whether adding lutein plus zeaxanthin or omega-3 fatty acids to the AREDS supplement formulation, or removing beta carotene or lowering zinc, changes that risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In South Africa, the study will be located within the Medical Research Council/University of the Witwatersrand Rural Public Health and Health Transitions Research Unit in Agincourt, Bushbuckridge sub-district of Mpumalanga province.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Uganda, the study will be based in the General Population Cohort (GPC), originally established in 1989 [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the proposed study, we will use iohexol excretion in a population sample of 3000 participants with and without CKD to measure GFR and determine the optimal equation to estimate GFR in Uganda, Malawi and South Africa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first is Karonga District in rural northern Malawi, predominantly subsistence farmers, fishermen and informal traders. The second site is Area 25 of Lilongwe, the capital city of Malawi.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This will consist of cross-sectional studies embedded within ongoing cohorts in Malawi and Uganda and a longitudinal study in South Africa, all with serial bio-banking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35839814") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941441") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6964098/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will measure GFR (mGFR) by plasma clearance of iohexol at 120, 180 and 240 min.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001144> "A study of kidney function in adults with and without chronic kidney disease in sub-Saharan Africa, run by the African Research on Kidney Disease collaboration within existing population cohorts in Malawi (Karonga and Lilongwe), South Africa (the Agincourt health and demographic surveillance site) and Uganda (the General Population Cohort). It measured glomerular filtration rate by iohexol plasma clearance to test equations for estimating it, with serial biobanking, cross-sectionally in Malawi and Uganda and longitudinally in South Africa.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5842784/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Young adults and cognitively normal older adults were recruited from the community via newspaper advertisements as part of the Berkeley Aging Cohort (BAC) at UC Berkeley.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10369372/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BACS Aß imaging was performed at the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory, participants underwent dynamic [11C]-PiB PET imaging over a 90 min interval after ∼15 mCi tracer injection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11032527/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All BACS participants undergo a standard battery of neuropsychological assessment at baseline and at each follow‐up time point to assess cognition including verbal and visual memory, working memory, language, executive function, and processing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11032527/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent longitudinal 1.5T magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), Pittsburgh compound B (PiB) PET, flortaucipir (FTP) PET, and cognitive assessments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11032527/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seventy‐eight cognitively healthy OA were recruited through the Berkeley Aging Cohort Study (BACS), an ongoing longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging in community‐dwelling older adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29527500") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37502020") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38334195") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40441049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13257327/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All BACS participants are cognitively normal older adult volunteers who were recruited into the cohort via advertisements and word of mouth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001145> "A longitudinal study of typical cognitive aging at the University of California, Berkeley, and Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It recruits cognitively normal older adults (and some young adults) living in the community in the San Francisco Bay Area through advertisements and word of mouth, and follows them with repeated neuropsychological testing, MRI, and PET imaging of amyloid and tau, to study brain changes in normal aging and early Alzheimer's disease pathology.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20595243") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1226067/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All families studied were of white European ancestry and resided in either the United Kingdom or the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> "A repository of DNA samples from British families of European ancestry with at least two siblings affected by type 1 diabetes, and their parents, recruited in the United Kingdom between 1989 and 1996 for the British Diabetic Association (now Diabetes UK) and made publicly available for genetic linkage and association studies of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20595243") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1226067/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The combined sample of 831 ASPs, all with both parents genotyped, provided 90% power to detect linkage for loci with λs = 1.3 at P=7.4×10-4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> "A repository of DNA samples from British families of European ancestry with at least two siblings affected by type 1 diabetes, and their parents, recruited in the United Kingdom between 1989 and 1996 for the British Diabetic Association (now Diabetes UK) and made publicly available for genetic linkage and association studies of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20595243") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1226067/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two collections of DNA samples from families with T1D are publicly available for genetic linkage studies, the Diabetes UK Warren 1 repository of samples from the United Kingdom and the HBDI collection of samples largely from the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> "A repository of DNA samples from British families of European ancestry with at least two siblings affected by type 1 diabetes, and their parents, recruited in the United Kingdom between 1989 and 1996 for the British Diabetic Association (now Diabetes UK) and made publicly available for genetic linkage and association studies of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20595243") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15049939+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1989 and 1996, 505 British families with at least two siblings affected by Type 1 diabetes were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> "A repository of DNA samples from British families of European ancestry with at least two siblings affected by type 1 diabetes, and their parents, recruited in the United Kingdom between 1989 and 1996 for the British Diabetic Association (now Diabetes UK) and made publicly available for genetic linkage and association studies of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11507694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15049939") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20595243") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16470599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16470599+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, the affected family-based control (AFBAC) association test and the transmission disequilibrium analysis of multiplex families of European descent from the British Diabetes Association (BDA) Warren Repository indicated that the association was stronger in -1123G > C compared to +1858C > T.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001146> "A repository of DNA samples from British families of European ancestry with at least two siblings affected by type 1 diabetes, and their parents, recruited in the United Kingdom between 1989 and 1996 for the British Diabetic Association (now Diabetes UK) and made publicly available for genetic linkage and association studies of type 1 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4348510/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All school children (n = 5,019) without special needs in grades 2 through 4 (7–10 y of age) were invited to participate, and families of 2,897 (59%) children agreed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4348510/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cognitive development was assessed through long-term change in working memory and attention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4348510/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 2012 to March 2013, children were evaluated every 3 mo over four repeated visits, using computerized tests in series lasting approximately 40 min in length.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4348510/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to assess the relationship between long-term exposure to traffic-related air pollutants at school and cognitive development measurements in primary school children within the BREATHE (Brain Development and Air Pollution Ultrafine Particles in School Children) project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4348510/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a prospective study of children (n = 2,715, aged 7 to 10 y) from 39 schools in Barcelona (Catalonia, Spain) exposed to high and low traffic-related air pollution, paired by school socioeconomic index; children were tested four times (i.e., to assess the 12-mo developmental trajectories) via computerized tests (n = 10,112).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25734425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31539824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31539824+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among the children recruited through a set of representative schools of the city of Barcelona, (Spain) in the Brain Development and Air Pollution Ultrafine Particles in School Children (BREATHE) study, 186 typically developing participants aged 8-12 years underwent brain MRI on the same 1.5 T MR unit over a 1.5-year period (October 2012-April 2014).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001147> "A prospective cohort of children aged 7–10 years in grades 2 to 4 at 39 primary schools in Barcelona, Spain, selected as pairs with high and low traffic-related air pollution, whose working memory and attention were tested four times, every three months, from January 2012 to March 2013, with brain MRI in a subsample, to study the effects of traffic-related air pollution on cognitive and brain development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16341085+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of this consortium is to characterize variations in approximately 50 genes that mediate two pathways that are associated with these cancers--the steroid-hormone metabolism pathway and the insulin-like growth factor signalling pathway--and to associate these variations with cancer risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2440354/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the consortium includes large well-established cohorts assembled in the United States or Europe that have DNA for genotyping and extensive questionnaire data from cohort members.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3044744/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Except for the MCCS study, the BPC3 consists of a series of matched nested case-control studies within each cohort; controls were matched to cases on a number of potential confounding factors, such as age, ethnicity, and region of recruitment, depending on the cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3044744/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MCCS used a case-cohort design, with a randomly sampled sub-cohort serving as controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23255287+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used 2,782 aggressive prostate cancer cases and 4,458 controls from the NCI Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium aggressive prostate cancer GWAS to infer 5.8 million well-imputed autosomal single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16341085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18596909") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21390317") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23255287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24523857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24523857+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected 3079 SNPs associated with a human complex trait or disease at genome-wide significance level (P<5 × 10(-8)) to perform a secondary analysis of an ER-negative GWAS from the National Cancer Institute's Breast and Prostate Cancer Cohort Consortium (BPC3), including 1998 cases and 2305 controls from prospective studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001148> "A consortium of large prospective cohorts in the United States, Europe and Australia, among them ATBC, CPS-II, EPIC, HPFS, the Multiethnic Cohort, NHS, PHS, PLCO and WHS, which pools nested case–control and case–cohort studies of breast and prostate cancer with DNA and prospectively collected questionnaire data, first to relate variation in genes of the steroid-hormone metabolism and insulin-like growth factor pathways to cancer risk, and later for genome-wide association studies of aggressive prostate cancer and oestrogen receptor-negative breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11871359/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Includes patients aged 16+ with chronic plaque psoriasis and started a course of systemic therapy (implies moderate-severe disease).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BSTOP is an ongoing prospective observational study of patients with a primary diagnosis of moderate‒severe plaque psoriasis across > 70 UK dermatology centres, which includes biological sample collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study participants donate blood which is used to extract DNA, and a subset of participants is invited to donate additional samples such as skin and bloods to monitor RNA, serum and immune cells. The biological data extracted from these samples is paired with clinical data such as medical history, previous psoriasis treatments, and length and severity of condition.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BSTOP seeks to identify and characterise biomarkers of response to systemic and biologic treatments for psoriasis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 80 sites throughout the UK are part of BSTOP and we are open to new dermatology departments interested in recruiting to the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.kcl.ac.uk/research/bstop") Annotation(rdfs:comment "is a non-commercial observational study established in 2011") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001149> "An ongoing prospective observational study and biobank of people aged 16 or over with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis starting systemic or biologic therapy, established in 2011 at the St John's Institute of Dermatology, Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust, and recruiting at more than 80 dermatology centres across the United Kingdom. It pairs DNA from every participant, and further blood and skin samples from some, with clinical data, captured partly through the British Association of Dermatologists Biologics and Immunomodulators Register, to identify biomarkers of response to psoriasis treatments.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15824551") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15824551+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were derived from the Black Women's Health Study, a U.S. prospective cohort study of black women who complete biannual mailed health questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11885530/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Black Women’s Health Study (BWHS) is a U.S. prospective cohort study of 59,000 United States Black women who enrolled in the study in 1995 and have been followed by biennial questionnaires since then.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Some participants are contacted to ask for consent to review their medical records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BWHS gathers information on many conditions that affect Black women — breast cancer, lupus, premature birth, hypertension, colon cancer, diabetes, uterine fibroids — the list is long.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There are also different cancer subtypes, which is why we review cancer registry data for information on subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40050615") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bu.edu/bwhs/history/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With the funding secured, in 1995 we sent health questionnaires to subscribers to Essence magazine, women who had participated in the feasibility studies, members of the Black Nurses’ Association, and friends and relatives of respondents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001150> "A prospective cohort of Black women in the United States, run by the Slone Epidemiology Center at Boston University, who enrolled in 1995 by returning health questionnaires mailed to subscribers of Essence magazine, members of the Black Nurses' Association, participants in its feasibility studies, and friends and relatives of respondents. The women are followed by repeated mailed questionnaires, with medical record and cancer registry review, to study the causes of illnesses common in Black women, such as breast cancer, hypertension, diabetes, lupus and uterine fibroids.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CACTI was designed to examine the prevalence of subclinical atherosclerosis in adults with type 1 diabetes and a comparable group of controls without any diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data for this analysis were collected as part of the prospective cohort study Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes (CACTI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Electron-beam computed tomography was used to measure CAC at baseline and follow-up exams.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3898750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was performed at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes in Denver, CO, and at the Clinical Translational Research Center at the University of Colorado Hospital, Aurora, CO.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6448314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study enrolled 1416 individuals between 19 and 56 years of age, with no known history of CHD: 652 subjects with type 1 diabetes and 764 nondiabetic control subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14578303") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23340891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24130360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30943964") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6448314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using data from the Coronary Artery Calcification in Type 1 Diabetes (CACTI) study [n = 1257; T1D: n = 568; non-diabetic controls: n = 689] collected between March 2000 and April 2002, we examined cross-sectional (baseline) and longitudinal (six-year follow-up in 2006–2008) associations of dietary fiber and HbA1c.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001151> "A prospective cohort of adults aged 19–56 years without known coronary heart disease, with long-standing type 1 diabetes or without diabetes (controls, mostly spouses, friends and neighbours of those with diabetes), examined from March 2000 to April 2002 at the Barbara Davis Center for Childhood Diabetes and the University of Colorado in Denver, United States, and re-examined about six years later. Coronary artery calcification was measured by electron-beam computed tomography, to study the prevalence and progression of subclinical coronary atherosclerosis in type 1 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.311/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng311_MOESM30_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Note that, although case definitions are broadly comparable, control definitions varied slightly by site: some sites used controls known to be free of psoriasis and other auto- immune disorders, others focused on psoriasis free controls only and yet others relied on population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.311/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng311_MOESM30_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "nearly all cases were collected in dermatology clinics and had their diagnosis confirmed by a dermatologist") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2745122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases and controls were of white European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2745122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Perlegen Sciences (Mountain View, CA, USA) genotyped discovery samples using four proprietary, high-density oligonucleotide arrays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2745122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify additional psoriasis susceptibility loci, we carried out a genome-wide association scan of 1,409 psoriasis cases and 1,436 controls in partnership with the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN)6 (see Table 1 and Supplementary Table 1 for details of case and control collections).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19169254") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000019.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of this collaborative study is to combine the resources and expertise of three groups with long-standing studies of psoriasis genetics in order to identify new genetic susceptibility factors for psoriasis, a common inflammatory skin disease that affects over 4 million Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001152> "A case–control collection of people of white European ancestry, with psoriasis diagnosed by dermatologists and controls without psoriasis, that pooled the long-standing psoriasis genetics collections of three United States groups, at the University of Michigan, the University of Utah and Washington University in St. Louis. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Perlegen platform through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) to identify psoriasis susceptibility loci.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29580111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29580111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6625507/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This five-year, population-based study was designed to assess the prevalence and risk factors associated with VI, blindness, lens opacities, glaucoma, AMD and DR in 6500 non-institutionalized AAs, aged 40 years and older, in and around Inglewood, California, within Los Angeles County.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29580111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8148035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For men of African ancestry, GRS replication was conducted among 1,586 cases and 1,086 controls from California and Uganda (CA UG Study) genotyped with the Illumina H3 Africa array and imputed using Phase 3 of the 1000 Genomes Project15 as the reference panel and Minimac4 on the Michigan Imputation Server27 (Supplementary Table 1 and 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29580111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01534-4/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1534_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer-free controls were from the African American Eye Disease Study and patients in other clinics at Mulago") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29580111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37945903") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01534-4/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1534_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases from Los Angeles, CA through SEER registry and Incident cases from Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001153> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in men of African ancestry, genotyped on the Illumina H3Africa array. It combines African American cases from Los Angeles, California, identified through the SEER cancer registry, and cancer-free controls from the African American Eye Disease Study in Inglewood, California, with incident cases and controls from other clinics at Mulago Hospital in Kampala, Uganda.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6186860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Infant length (to nearest 0.1 cm using length board and plastic tape) and weight (kilograms, measured with electronic scale; TANITA, HD-314) were obtained every 3 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6186860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mirpur, Dhaka is a relatively poor, urban neighborhood [12, 13], and Mirzapur is a rural subdistrict located 60 km northwest of Dhaka, as previously described [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6186860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women in their second trimester were identified.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6186860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Single, fresh stool specimens were collected from children every month (monthly surveillance) and during episodes of diarrhea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6186860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thereafter, field research assistants performed twice-weekly, in-home visits to interview caregivers and collect information regarding child morbidity and diarrhea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29897482") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32019797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40488529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12455312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a continuation of the study on Cryptosporidiosis and Enteropathogens in Bangladesh (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier NCT02764918) where Mirpur and Mirzapur children were enrolled within 1 week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001154> "A prospective birth cohort of children enrolled within a week of birth between June 2014 and March 2016 in Mirpur, an urban neighbourhood of Dhaka, and Mirzapur, a rural subdistrict north-west of Dhaka, Bangladesh, whose mothers were identified in the second trimester of pregnancy. The children were followed with twice-weekly home visits for diarrhoea, monthly stool samples and three-monthly growth measurements, to study the incidence of cryptosporidiosis, the immune response to it, host genetic susceptibility and its effect on child growth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2677920/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, the cohort provides a critical framework and resource for epidemiologists and biologists to investigate current and future questions regarding consequences of therapy, genetic association, disease processes and causation, and quality of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2677920/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To provide a comparison population, a cohort of siblings of survivors was constructed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19364948+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1994, the US National Cancer Institute funded the Childhood Cancer Survivor Study, a multi-institutional research initiative designed to establish a large and extensively characterized cohort of more than 14,000 5-year survivors of childhood and adolescent cancer diagnosed between 1970 and 1986.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7190022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initially inclusive of survivors with a diagnosis through 1986, the cohort was expanded to include survivors of childhood cancer with a diagnosis over three decades, from 1 January 1970 through 31 December 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7190022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Childhood Cancer Survivor Study is a multi-institutional retrospective cohort study with longitudinal follow-up of five year survivors of the most common childhood cancers") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19364948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31941657") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7190022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "diagnosed before age 21 years at one of 27 participating institutions in the United States and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001155> "A multi-institutional retrospective cohort, with longitudinal follow-up, of five-year survivors of the most common childhood cancers diagnosed before age 21 at participating paediatric centres in the United States and Canada, with a comparison cohort of their siblings. It was funded by the US National Cancer Institute in 1994 for survivors diagnosed in 1970-1986 and later expanded to those diagnosed in 1987-1999, as a resource for research on the long-term effects of childhood cancer and its treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1227/neu.0000000000000575") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the core data study, we will create and maintain well-curated biorepositories for analysis by the participants and to provide for legacy research with future new methodologies or longer follow-up of outcome (supported by future grant funding).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1227/neu.0000000000000575") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in Traumatic Brain Injury (CENTER-TBI) core data study and CENTER-TBI registry (NCT02210221) form part of the CENTER-TBI project: a large-scale project supported by the European Union Framework 7 program (grant 602150).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25525693+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Advanced neuroimaging and genomic and biomarker data will be used to improve characterization, and analyses will include neuroinformatics approaches to address variations in process and clinical care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25525693+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This multicenter, longitudinal, prospective, observational study in 22 countries across Europe and Israel will collect detailed data from 5400 consenting patients, presenting within 24 hours of injury, with a clinical diagnosis of TBI and an indication for computed tomography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25525693+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To improve characterization and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care, using comparative effectiveness research approaches.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25525693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31526754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34351445") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8486724/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Collaborative European NeuroTrauma Effectiveness Research in TBI (CENTER-TBI, registered at clinicaltrials.gov NCT02210221) study is a prospective cohort study conducted in 63 centers from 18 countries across Europe and Israel between December 2014 and December 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001156> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort of patients with traumatic brain injury who presented to hospital within 24 hours of injury with an indication for CT, recruited between December 2014 and December 2017 at centres in 18 countries across Europe and in Israel. Funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, it comprises a core study, with neuroimaging, biospecimens and outcome assessment, and a broader registry, and aims to improve the characterisation and classification of TBI and to identify best clinical care through comparative effectiveness research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38536042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WGS on 5,199 samples was performed by the Broad Institute Sequencing Center using their PCR-free Illumina sequencing-by-synthesis protocol (supplemental methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157> "A Johns Hopkins University study that enrolled people with cystic fibrosis both with and without cystic fibrosis-related diabetes; its participants are among those whose genomes were sequenced by the Cystic Fibrosis Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38536042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Modifiers of CF-Related Diabetes Study (CFRD Study) is based at Johns Hopkins and enrolls subjects with CF who do and do not have CFRD.15") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157> "A Johns Hopkins University study that enrolled people with cystic fibrosis both with and without cystic fibrosis-related diabetes; its participants are among those whose genomes were sequenced by the Cystic Fibrosis Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38536042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9606479/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with CF were recruited from five cohorts: CF Twin and Sibling Study (TSS)16 and Cystic Fibrosis-Related Diabetes (CFRD) Study8 (Johns Hopkins University);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001157> "A Johns Hopkins University study that enrolled people with cystic fibrosis both with and without cystic fibrosis-related diabetes; its participants are among those whose genomes were sequenced by the Cystic Fibrosis Genome Project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001158> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001158>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25287419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 246 twins or triplets and 1840 siblings with CF and 1373 parents in 1018 families were recruited from a total of 128 centers throughout the United States and four sites in Israel, Australia, and Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001158> "A family-based cohort of living twins, triplets and siblings who all have cystic fibrosis, and their parents, recruited from 2000 by Johns Hopkins University through CF care centres mostly in the United States and also in Australia, Israel and Scotland, to assess genetic and environmental modifiers of clinical outcomes in CF.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25287419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cystic Fibrosis Twin and Sibling Study (CF TSS) is based at Johns Hopkins and began enrolling subjects with CF who had at least one affected living sibling in 2000.14") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001158> "A family-based cohort of living twins, triplets and siblings who all have cystic fibrosis, and their parents, recruited from 2000 by Johns Hopkins University through CF care centres mostly in the United States and also in Australia, Israel and Scotland, to assess genetic and environmental modifiers of clinical outcomes in CF.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25287419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36206743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35647563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the study is to assess the genetic and non-genetic contributions to variation in the traits that form the CF phenotype using family-based approaches.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001158> "A family-based cohort of living twins, triplets and siblings who all have cystic fibrosis, and their parents, recruited from 2000 by Johns Hopkins University through CF care centres mostly in the United States and also in Australia, Israel and Scotland, to assess genetic and environmental modifiers of clinical outcomes in CF.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14646025+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One feature is that clinical evaluation for Alzheimer's disease is confined to a stratified random sample of all participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11623384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An additional 4,644 participants who later became age-eligible were recruited in successive cohorts, leading to a total study population of 10,802 participants by 2012.30,33 All CHAP participants were interviewed in their homes, both at baseline and all follow-up cycles (i.e., visits), which occurred roughly every 3 y post baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11623384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study was set in the Chicago Health and Aging Project (CHAP), a population-based longitudinal study (1993–2012) of older adults living in four adjacent neighborhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois.30,33") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11623384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The founding purpose of the CHAP was to be a longitudinal study of common late-life chronic conditions, particularly those that increase the risk of dementia, in a cohort of Black and White older adults who were at least 65 y of age.33") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11623384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "they also enrolled a small subset (n=235) who were 61–64.9 y of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14646025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39641998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40575494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12199416/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited through a door-to-door census in the four communities of focus") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001159> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of Black and White adults predominantly aged 65 and over living in four adjacent neighbourhoods on the south side of Chicago, Illinois, recruited through a door-to-door census from 1993, with later age groups entered as residents turned 65, whose participants were followed until 2012 with in-home interviews every three years and clinical evaluation of stratified random samples, to study common chronic conditions of late life, especially risk factors for Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33096046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41321066") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33096046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7674631/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data on social circumstances, health, development and wellbeing of the participants was obtained from the cohort at birth, four months, one year, annually to age 16 years, and at 18, 21, 25, 30, and 35 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160> "A population-based longitudinal birth cohort of the children born in the Christchurch urban region of New Zealand during a four-month period from April to August 1977, studied by the University of Otago, Christchurch, at birth, 4 months, 1 year, annually to age 16 and at intervals into adulthood (to age 40), on their health, development, social circumstances and wellbeing across the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33096046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41321066") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11984572/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data in this study were collected as part of the Christchurch Health and Development Study (CHDS), a prospective birth-cohort study comprised of 1265 children born in the Christchurch, New Zealand urban region during a 4-month period from April to August 1977.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160> "A population-based longitudinal birth cohort of the children born in the Christchurch urban region of New Zealand during a four-month period from April to August 1977, studied by the University of Otago, Christchurch, at birth, 4 months, 1 year, annually to age 16 and at intervals into adulthood (to age 40), on their health, development, social circumstances and wellbeing across the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33096046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41321066") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11984572/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort has been studied on 24 occasions from birth to age 40 years using a combination of interviews with parents and participants, standardised testing, teacher report, and medical record data (Buchanan et al., 2023).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160> "A population-based longitudinal birth cohort of the children born in the Christchurch urban region of New Zealand during a four-month period from April to August 1977, studied by the University of Otago, Christchurch, at birth, 4 months, 1 year, annually to age 16 and at intervals into adulthood (to age 40), on their health, development, social circumstances and wellbeing across the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33096046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41321066") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41321066") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41321066+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study members from the Christchurch Health and Development Study, a population-based New Zealand birth cohort study (N = 1265 at birth) were followed to age 40 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001160> "A population-based longitudinal birth cohort of the children born in the Christchurch urban region of New Zealand during a four-month period from April to August 1977, studied by the University of Otago, Christchurch, at birth, 4 months, 1 year, annually to age 16 and at intervals into adulthood (to age 40), on their health, development, social circumstances and wellbeing across the life course.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3481179/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between March 13, 2007 and May 28, 2010, a total of 1,741 PD participants from 45 sites in the U.S. and Canada were randomized 1:1 to either 10-gm creatine/day or matching placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23079770+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A randomized, multicenter, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled phase III study of creatine (10 g daily) in participants with early, treated PD, the Long-term Study-1 (LS-1), is being conducted by the National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease network.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4259292/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NINDS NET-PD LS-1 is a randomized, multicenter, double-blind study of 10 grams of oral creatine/day versus matching placebo in adults with early treated PD enrolled within five years of PD diagnosis (clinicaltrials.gov identifier# NCT00449865).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25668262+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were enrolled from March 2007 to May 2010 and followed up until September 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7851242/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All NET-PD LS-1 subjects were followed systematically for an average of 3.5 years, and a subset consented for genomic DNA banking for future analyses, offering a well-characterized dataset for BDNF SNP genotyping and analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23079770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25486269") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25668262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33215284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7851242/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples from NET-PD LS-1 subjects were obtained from the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001161> "A randomised, multicentre, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase III trial population of adults with early, treated Parkinson's disease (within five years of diagnosis and receiving dopaminergic therapy). Participants were enrolled at 45 sites in the United States and Canada from March 2007 to May 2010 by the NINDS Exploratory Trials in Parkinson's Disease (NET-PD) network, to test whether creatine slows long-term clinical decline, and were followed until September 2013. DNA from the participants who consented to banking is held in the Coriell Institute for Medical Research biorepository.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4412685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Day-long assessments (called phases) have been conducted at ages 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 18, 21, 26, 32, and most recently at age 38 years (in 2010–2012) when 95 % of the living Study members took part.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4412685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants (n = 1037) were born between April 1st 1972 and March 30, 1973 and first followed up at age three, forming the base sample for the longitudinal study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4412685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Study (hereafter the Dunedin Study) is an ongoing longitudinal investigation of health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4412685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To be eligible for inclusion participants had to be living in the greater Dunedin Metropolitan area 3 years after their birth at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital—the only maternity hospital in Dunedin at the time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25835958") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42101744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11357-026-02282-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit is based at the University of Otago within the Ngāi Tahu tribal area, whom we acknowledge as first peoples, tangata whenua (transl. people of this land).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001162> "A longitudinal study of the health and behaviour of a complete birth cohort: children born at Queen Mary Maternity Hospital, Dunedin, New Zealand, between April 1972 and March 1973 and still living in the greater Dunedin area at age 3. They were assessed in day-long multidisciplinary phases from age 3 through childhood and adolescence into midlife, by the Dunedin Multidisciplinary Health and Development Research Unit of the University of Otago.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6355980/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In ECRHS I, each participant was sent a brief questionnaire (stage 1) and from those who responded, a random population-based sample was selected to undergo a more detailed clinical examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6355980/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical phase of ECRHS I and II was performed during 1991–1994 and 1998–2002, respectively. ECRHS III is the second follow-up and was performed from February 2011 to January 2014 [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6376659/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ECRHS III was the third wave of data collection on the cohort, beginning in 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6376659/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Community Respiratory Health Survey (ECRHS) is a multicentre population-based cohort study that began in 1990–1994.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8050554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8050554+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, the survey is designed to estimate variations in the prevalence of asthma, asthma-like symptoms and airway responsiveness; to estimate variations in exposures to known or suspected risk factors for asthma, and assess to what extent these variations explain the variations in the prevalence of disease; and to estimate differences in the use of medication for asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28974648") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30723731") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30764884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-i") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-ii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iii") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ecrhs.org/ecrhs-iv") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC119432") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We gathered data from the 30 centres within regions: United Kingdom and Republic of Ireland), northern Europe (Iceland, Norway, Sweden), central Europe (Belgium, France, the Netherlands), southern Europe (Italy and Spain), Australia and New Zealand, and United States (Portland was the only area in the United States).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001163> "A multicentre, population-based cohort of adults aged 20 to 44 years who were selected at random from population registers in 1990-1994 in centres mainly in Western Europe, and also in Australia, New Zealand, the United States and elsewhere, and surveyed with a standardised protocol (a screening questionnaire, then a clinical examination of a random subsample and of those reporting asthma symptoms) to compare the prevalence of asthma and allergic disease, their risk factors and their treatment across countries. Those examined were followed up in ECRHS II (1998-2002), ECRHS III (2008-2014) and ECRHS IV (from 2021) to study the incidence and prognosis of asthma and allergy, lung function decline and COPD.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age more than or equal to18 yearsThe participants will either have or be suspected to have digestive disorder/diseasesParticipants must be able to give informed consent") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prospective patients are also enrolled in this project since 2001 and all patients are monitored and followed on a continuous basis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The University of Pittsburgh’s Early Detection Research Network (EDRN) Colorectal and Pancreatic Neoplasm Virtual Biorepository was funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The key objective of this initiative is to design and develop a colorectal and pancreatic neoplasm virtual bioreposity that provides high-quality clinically annotated colorectal and pancreatic neoplasm biospecimens for the support of translational research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "at different centers in the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) hospital networks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21031013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2956178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "patients who have been regularly managed and followed-up from 1990 to 2000 either for regular colorectal cancer screening or gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases and pancreatic and colorectal cancers") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001164> "A University of Pittsburgh biorepository, funded by the National Cancer Institute in 2001 as an Early Detection Research Network resource, of clinically annotated biospecimens and data from adults with, or suspected of having, digestive diseases who were managed in University of Pittsburgh Medical Center hospitals for colorectal cancer screening or for gastrointestinal malignancies, premalignant conditions, inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases or pancreatic and colorectal cancers. Patients followed from 1990 to 2000 were gathered retrospectively and new patients have been enrolled prospectively since 2001 and followed continuously, to support translational research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1586017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data on health behaviour like physical activity, tobacco and alcohol consumption were obtained by means of a questionnaire, documentation of anthropometric data, abdominal ultrasound and blood specimens for assessment of chemical parameters.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1586017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original aim of assessing the prevalence of E. multilocularis infection was amended by additional aims in the field of public health and internal medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1586017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The survey was conducted from November 4th to December 7th, 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1586017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm have cooperated to design and initiate the Echinococcus Multilocularis and Internal Diseases in Leutkirch (EMIL) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6423886/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2013, following data analysis and matching cases and controls according to gender, age, body mass index (BMI), and the presence or absence of hepatic steatosis, we recruited a subpopulation of 484 out of the original EMIL subjects for the follow-up study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16981990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30885181") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6423886/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In that year, 4000 people aged between 10 and 65 years randomly selected from the residents’ registration office in Leutkirch were contacted for the study, of whom 2445 subjects formed the study population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001165> "A population-based study of the residents of the town of Leutkirch in Baden-Württemberg, south-western Germany, designed by the State Health Department of Baden-Württemberg and the University of Ulm, for which inhabitants aged 10 to 65 years were selected at random from the municipal population register and examined in November and December 2002 (EMIL-I) with a questionnaire, anthropometry, abdominal ultrasound and blood sampling. Its original aim, the prevalence of infection with the fox tapeworm Echinococcus multilocularis, was extended to internal diseases and public health, and a subsample was re-examined in 2013 (EMIL-II).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783320/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CF patients ≤12 years of age at the time of enrollment were eligible if they had no prior isolation of Pa from respiratory cultures, or if prior history of isolation of Pa from respiratory cultures, at least a two-year period with Pa negative cultures (documented by at least 1 culture annually) or were concurrently enrolled in the EPIC-CT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783320/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples extracted from whole blood are being collected and banked from participants and their parents of origin for a separate planned evaluation of genetic factors that may be associated with CF pathogenesis, disease progression, and clinical outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783320/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, Pa isolates and serum samples from observational participants are banked for future studies to enhance the understanding of microbiological aspects of early CF lung disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783320/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPIC-OBS study is made possible by the existence of this resource: data collection occurs at each encounter and via an annual family survey utilizing an augmented version of the CFF Registry containing the standard Registry data collection forms as well as additional, study-specific forms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783320/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of EPIC-OBS is the identification of risk factors associated with early age at first isolation of Pa from respiratory cultures and with the early emergence of mucoid and antibiotic-resistant strains of Pa, in particular, modifiable exposures, such as environmental tobacco smoke, breastfeeding and daycare.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19470318") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22554417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39260370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26061914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5462119/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children with an established diagnosis of CF 0 to 12 years of age and with no prior lifetime respiratory isolation of Pa or Pa negative for ≥ 2 years were enrolled at 59 accredited U.S. CF care centers between 2004 and 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001166> "A prospective, multicentre observational cohort of children with cystic fibrosis aged 12 years or younger who were free of Pseudomonas aeruginosa at enrolment (no earlier positive respiratory culture, or at least two years of negative cultures) or were taking part in the companion Early Pseudomonas Infection Control clinical trial, enrolled in 2004-2006 at 59 cystic fibrosis care centres in the United States and led from the University of Washington and Seattle Children's Hospital. Participants were followed through encounter-based data collection built on the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation Patient Registry, annual family surveys, respiratory cultures and banked serum, bacterial isolates and DNA, to identify risk factors for early acquisition of P. aeruginosa and to describe its clinical consequences.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12220285/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were recruited to represent the UK population with newborns in the 1990s, to ensure adequate numbers of children in disadvantaged homes and to avoid an excess of twins born to well‐educated women using assisted reproduction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12220285/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample was drawn from a larger birth register of twins born in England and Wales in 1994–1995. 39 Full details about the sample are reported elsewhere. 40 Briefly, the E‐Risk sample was constructed in 1999–2000, when 1116 families (93% of those eligible) with same‐sex 5‐year‐old twins participated in home‐visit assessments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "E-Risk was proposed in 1997") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1998 E-Risk began by constructing a nationally representative 2-year birth cohort of 2,232 same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Environmental Risk (E-Risk) Longitudinal Twin Study aims to build knowledge around the question of how environmental and genetic factors contribute to the development of behaviours, health, and mental health problems from childhood through to adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40350583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.eriskstudy.com/about-the-e-risk-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "has been funded by the Medical Research Council (MRC) from 1998 through to 2027.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001167> "A nationally representative birth cohort of same-sex twins born in England and Wales in 1994-1995, drawn from a birth register of twins and recruited to represent UK families with newborns in the 1990s (ensuring enough children in disadvantaged homes and avoiding an excess of twins born to well-educated women after assisted reproduction). Proposed in 1997, funded by the Medical Research Council from 1998 and based at King's College London, it assessed the families at home when the twins were 5 (1999-2000), 7, 10, 12 and 18 years old, surveyed them online in their mid-twenties and planned a further assessment at age 30 for 2024-2025, to study how environmental and genetic factors contribute to behaviour, health and mental health problems from childhood into adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7527829/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were screened between Nov 30, 2015, and March 6, 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7527829/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (GaPP2) took place in 39 UK hospital centres.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7527829/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This project was funded by the Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, a Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research partnership (grant 13/52/04).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32979978+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were randomly assigned in a 1:1 ratio to receive gabapentin (titrated to a maximum dose of 2700 mg daily) or matching placebo for 16 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11384074/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For inclusion in this study, participants were able to optionally provide a saliva sample at entry to the GaPP2 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32979978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39258169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11384074/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, eligible participants for the GaPP2 trial were women aged 18–50 years with chronic pelvic pain lasting at least three months (with or without dysmenorrhoea and/or dyspareunia), and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001168> "The participants of a multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial at 39 UK hospital centres, funded by the Medical Research Council and National Institute for Health Research Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, in which women aged 18-50 years with chronic pelvic pain of at least three months and no obvious pelvic pathology at laparoscopy, screened between November 2015 and March 2019, were randomly assigned to gabapentin or matching placebo for 16 weeks to measure the efficacy and safety of gabapentin. Participants could give a saliva sample for genetic study at trial entry.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30770926+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A cohort study of pregnant women was initiated in May 2015 at the civil hospital in Gurugram, Haryana, India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30770926+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objectives are to identify clinical, epidemiologic, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic, and microbial correlates; discover molecular-risk markers by using an integrative -omics approach; and generate a risk-prediction algorithm for preterm birth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30770926+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We describe here the longitudinal study design, methodology of data collection, and the repositories of data, biospecimens, and ultrasound images being created.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work was funded by the Department of Biotechnology, Ministry of Science and Technology, Govt. of India (BT/PR9983/MED/97/194/2013)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363490/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women were enrolled in a single-centre prospective cohort (GARBH-Ini: interdisciplinary Group for Advanced Research on BirtH outcomes – DBT India Initiative) established at Gurugram Civil Hospital (GCH), a secondary hospital in Gurugram district of Haryana, India, after providing the written informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30770926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39030058") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363490/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These women were enrolled before 20 weeks of their gestational age as confirmed by standard ultrasonography (USG) dating protocols.
They were followed during pregnancy until delivery and once within 6 months of post-partum period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001169> "A single-centre prospective pregnancy cohort at Gurugram Civil Hospital, a secondary-care hospital in Gurugram district, Haryana, north India, that from May 2015 enrolled pregnant women before 20 weeks' gestation (dated by ultrasound) and followed them through pregnancy to delivery and once within six months after delivery, building repositories of clinical data, biospecimens and ultrasound images. Coordinated by the Translational Health Science and Technology Institute and funded by India's Department of Biotechnology, it aims to identify clinical, epidemiological, genomic, epigenomic, proteomic and microbial correlates of preterm birth and to develop risk-prediction tools for it.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After standard quality control and the estimation of ancestry groups (Table S1), GWASs stratified by ancestry and sex were conducted in each biobank (Table S2) with the first 20 genetic PCs adjusted as covariates, which are continuous measures of sample ancestries (STAR Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GBMI meta-analyzes summary statistics from GWASs generated using harmonized genotypes and phenotypes from member biobanks for 14 exemplar diseases and endpoints.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GBMI represents 2.2 million research participants with health and genetic data from 23 biobanks: one from Australia, one from West Asia, four from East Asian countries, eight from European countries, and nine from North America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2019, we formed the GBMI, bringing together 23 biobanks to work together to understand the genetic basis of human health and disease (Figure 1; Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The all-biobank meta-analysis results and plots for the 14 endpoints (including both ancestry-specific and cross-ancestry meta-analyses and sex-stratified meta-analyses) are available for downloading at https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/resources and browsing at the browser http://results.globalbiobankmeta.org.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.globalbiobankmeta.org/parcipating-biobanks") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36777996") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9903716/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We introduce the Global Biobank Meta-analysis Initiative (GBMI)—a collaborative network of 23 biobanks from 4 continents representing more than 2.2 million consented individuals with genetic data linked to electronic health records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001170> "A collaborative network of biobanks and genomics initiatives, formed in 2019 by 23 biobanks from four continents (North America, Europe, East and West Asia, and Australia) and since joined by others, whose participants have genotypes linked to electronic health records or other health data. Member biobanks run genome-wide association studies with harmonised phenotype definitions and methods, stratified by ancestry and sex, and GBMI meta-analyses the summary statistics across biobanks and ancestries, beginning with 14 diseases and endpoints, and releases them publicly, to increase the power and ancestral diversity of genetic studies of human disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21546499+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LNH2003-3 study was a phase II trial including diffuse large B-cell lymphoma patients with 2 or 3 International Prognostic Index factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22118442+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Intensified chemotherapy with ACVBP plus rituximab versus standard CHOP plus rituximab for the treatment of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (LNH03-2B): an open-label randomised phase 3 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23235801+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Untreated patients younger than 66 years with stage I or II DLBCL and no adverse prognostic factors of the age-adjusted International Prognostic Index were randomly assigned to receive three cycles of ACVBP plus sequential consolidation with or without the addition of four infusions of rituximab.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23578722+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dose-dense rituximab-CHOP compared with standard rituximab-CHOP in elderly patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (the LNH03-6B study): a randomised phase 3 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3105/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng3105_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Treatment program of DLBCL patients from the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA) consisting in GELA 576 525 Cases from randomized clinical trial with Patients recruited in the study that consented to DNA analysis Controls were from EPIC") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21482186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21546499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22118442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23235801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23578722") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36273105") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25261932") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4213349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GELA study was conducted on cases only; controls were drawn from a pool of 928 individuals from the French component of the EPIC cohort, who were previously scanned on Illumina HumanHap 660W or 610K47,48.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001171> "Patients with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) enrolled in the LNH03 (LNH 2003) programme of treatment trials of the Groupe d'Etude des Lymphomes de l'Adulte (GELA, later the Lymphoma Study Association, LYSA), who consented to DNA analysis. The programme's trials, opened from December 2003 at centres mainly in France and Belgium for patients of different ages and prognostic risk, were the randomised trials LNH03-1B, LNH03-2B and LNH03-6B, the phase 2 trial LNH03-3B, LNH03-39B and a phase 2 trial of R-miniCHOP in patients over 80. The patients' germline DNA was genotyped as the case series of GELA's genome-wide association study of DLBCL, with controls drawn from the French component of EPIC.")

