# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20039012+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENICA study involved interviews to assess shift work information in 857 breast cancer cases and 892 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3677984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood-derived DNA samples of all cases and controls were genotyped for UGT1A6_19_T>G and UGT1A6_541_A>G by matrix-assisted laser desorption/ionization mass spectrometry (MALDI-TOF MS; Sequenom, San Diego, CA) as described previously (The MARIE-GENICA Consortium, 2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3677984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were selected from population registries from 31 communities in the greater Bonn area; matched to cases in 5-year age classes from 2001 to 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3677984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident breast cancer cases were enrolled from 2000 to 2004 from the Greater Bonn area (from all hospitals within the study region); cases were enrolled within 6 months of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25229211+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GENICA is a population-based case-control study on breast cancer conducted in the Greater Region of Bonn.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20039012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25229211") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25229211+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we analyzed genetic polymorphisms in genes of cellular clocks, melatonin biosynthesis and signaling and their association with breast cancer as well as gene-gene and gene-night work interactions in a German case-control study on breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001173> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in women of the Greater Bonn region, Germany, run by the GENICA network of German research institutions, in which incident cases, enrolled from all hospitals of the region in 2000–2004 within six months of diagnosis, and controls drawn from the population registries of 31 communities of the region and matched in five-year age classes were interviewed and gave blood, to study how genes and environmental exposures interact in breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3136364/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Membership in the QFP was defined as having four grandparents with French-Canadian family names who were born in the Province of Québec, Canada, or in adjacent areas of the Provinces of New Brunswick and Ontario or in New England or New York State.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174> "A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3136364/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Canadian population sample used for panel D consisted of 762 psoriasis patients and 994 controls, sampled from the Québec founder population (QFP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174> "A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3136364/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We imputed both datasets, that is, the CASP dataset, which was genotyped by Perlegen Sciences, and the Canadian dataset, which was generated using the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip, were imputed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174> "A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.")
