AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40021644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-025-56719-8/MediaObjects/41467_2025_56719_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 18 contributing studies included 15 datasets with psoriasis cases ascertained via dermatologists or other secondary care specialist physicians (five previously analysed1 : CASP, ExomeChip, Genizon, PsA and WTCCC2; ten newly genotyped: BSTOP, Erlangen, Estonia, Kiel, Manchester, Michigan, Newfoundland, Scotland, Toronto and UCSF)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001174> "A case-control sample of people with psoriasis, ascertained through dermatologists or other secondary-care specialists, and controls, all drawn from the Québec founder population (people whose four grandparents had French-Canadian family names and were born in Québec or neighbouring areas), assembled by Genizon BioSciences of Saint-Laurent, Québec, and genotyped genome-wide on the Illumina Human 1M BeadChip; it is one of the European-ancestry GWAS datasets of the international psoriasis genetics meta-analyses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001175> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001175>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29083406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4355615/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENUFAD study (Genetic Analysis of Nuclear Families with Atopic Dermatitis) recruited complete nuclear families with at least two children affected with early-onset (<2 years of age) and moderate to severe AD as previously described [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001175> "A family-based genetic study of atopic dermatitis run from Charité Universitätsmedizin Berlin, which recruited complete nuclear families, mostly German and a few Swedish, through at least two children with physician-diagnosed, moderate to severe atopic dermatitis that began before the age of two, and in its extended phase also unrelated children with such early-onset disease, recording asthma and hay fever at recruitment, for genetic studies of atopic dermatitis and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29083406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4355615/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENUFAD study contributed 522 complete German nuclear families to the Central European study and 32 Swedish families to the Northern European data set.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001175> "A family-based genetic study of atopic dermatitis run from Charité Universitätsmedizin Berlin, which recruited complete nuclear families, mostly German and a few Swedish, through at least two children with physician-diagnosed, moderate to severe atopic dermatitis that began before the age of two, and in its extended phase also unrelated children with such early-onset disease, recording asthma and hay fever at recruitment, for genetic studies of atopic dermatitis and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29083406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37794016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29083406") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3985/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3985_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children of the extended GENUFAD study were recruited through early onset eczema (<2years) with moderate to severe disease expression, which was diagnosed by a physician according to standard criteria 36 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001175> "A family-based genetic study of atopic dermatitis run from Charité Universitätsmedizin Berlin, which recruited complete nuclear families, mostly German and a few Swedish, through at least two children with physician-diagnosed, moderate to severe atopic dermatitis that began before the age of two, and in its extended phase also unrelated children with such early-onset disease, recording asthma and hay fever at recruitment, for genetic studies of atopic dermatitis and allergic disease.")
