# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2719290/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 875 case subjects in the German MI Family Study were persons who had myocardial infarction before the age of 60 years and at least one first-degree relative with premature coronary artery disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2275796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, we identified families from all parts of Germany with accumulation of premature MI or severe CAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were from the population-based Augsburg KORA S4/F4 study and PopGen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GerMIFS II: patients had a validated MI with a strong genetic component as documented by an early age of onset (prior to the age of 60 years) and a positive family history for CAD in 59.4% of patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GerMIFS III (KORA): cases of non-fatal MI were identified in the KORA registry with DNA available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18398472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20923989") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36474045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GerMIFS IV cases consist of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography, classified as CAD or MI cases based on the coronary angiogram (at least a 50% stenosis in one major coronary vessel) and age of onset (<65 years in males, and <70 years in females).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001176> "A series of German case collections for genetic studies of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease, numbered GerMIFS I to VII, that began as a family study recruiting, from all parts of Germany, people with myocardial infarction before the age of 60 and relatives with premature coronary artery disease. Later collections added patients with early-onset myocardial infarction, non-fatal myocardial infarction cases from the KORA registry of the Augsburg region, and patients with coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction referred for coronary angiography, mostly compared with population controls from other German studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3012192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All GLACIER participants underwent detailed health and lifestyle examinations as part of the Västerbotten Intervention Programme, an ongoing population-based prospective cohort study focused on type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, and common cancers (20,22).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3012192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline examinations for GLACIER participants were undertaken from 1985 through 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3012192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 16,330 participants free from diabetes and other major chronic diseases at baseline, 4,059 had undergone a 10-year follow-up examination between January 1995 and December 2007 and were included in the longitudinal analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3012192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 1985, all residents of the county of Västerbotten have been invited to visit their primary care center for a clinical examination in the year of their 40th, 50th, and/or 60th birthday.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3012192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GLACIER Study is a prospective, population-based cohort study comprising 19,547 adults from the northern Swedish county of Västerbotten, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study (20).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20870969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26625858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25396097") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4225623/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established in 2008, the GLACIER Study comprises a cohort suitable for studies on the genetics of complex cardio-metabolic traits and gene-environment interactions, nested within the NSHDS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001177> "A prospective population-based cohort of adults from the county of Västerbotten in northern Sweden, nested within the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, whose members had baseline health and lifestyle examinations in the Västerbotten Intervention Programme between 1985 and 2004, in the years of their 40th, 50th or 60th birthdays, with a repeat examination about ten years later. It was established in 2008 to study the genetics of cardiometabolic traits and interactions between genes and lifestyle.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following six clinical evaluations in the first 2 years, the study participants were assessed once every year from age 3 until 13, and thereafter at 15 and 20 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German Multicentre Allergy Study began with the recruitment of 1314 newborns between January and December 1990 in maternity wards from university hospitals in 5 German cities – Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich – and has been described in detail elsewhere 19 including follow‐up methods 7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MAS birth cohort was risk‐enriched with 38% (n = 499) ‘high‐risk’ children, defined as having two immediate family members (parents or siblings) with asthma, allergic rhinitis or eczema, or an elevated cord blood immunoglobulin E (IgE) ≥0.9 kU/l, as compared to approximately 19% ‘high‐risk’ children in the source population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4744942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The remaining 62% (n = 815) were drawn as a random sample from all ‘low‐risk’ children of all study centres.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26011739+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Allergic multimorbidity at each time point was defined as the coexistence of at least 2 of the following diseases in one participant: asthma, allergic rhinitis and eczema.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25757221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29664587") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26011739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26011739+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Symptoms, medication and doctor's diagnoses of allergic diseases have been assessed using standardized questionnaires including validated ISAAC questions in 19 follow-up assessments up to age 20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001178> "A birth cohort of children born in 1990 and recruited in the maternity wards of university hospitals in five German cities (Berlin, Düsseldorf, Freiburg, Mainz and Munich), enriched for newborns at high risk of allergy, with two allergic immediate family members or raised cord-blood IgE, alongside a random sample of low-risk newborns, and followed with repeated examinations and questionnaires from infancy into adulthood to study the course of asthma, allergic rhinitis, eczema and allergic sensitisation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16207846+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We first tested 808 patients who were homozygous for the DeltaF508 mutation and were classified as having either severe or mild lung disease, as defined by the lowest or highest quartile of forced expiratory volume in one second (FEV1), respectively, for age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2995003/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Although the US samples included patients distributed across 48 US states, the majority of the subjects were collected from the eastern US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3296486/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Modifier Study (GMS) consists of unrelated patients homozygous for the common CF allele F508del (HGVS nomenclature: p.Phe508del), recruited from extremes of lung function9.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we use genome-wide association analysis to identify genetic modifiers of CF lung disease, the primary cause of mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4589222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, the majority of the GMS subjects were recruited as unrelated extremes-of-phenotype (lung disease severity, mild versus severe), whereas a subset of patients were recruited as a population-based sample at the Children’s Hospital of Denver, Wisconsin, and Boston, and also from the multicenter study UNC/CWRU GMS cohort (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16207846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20681990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9136666/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gene Modifier Study (GMS) originated at University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case
Western Reserve University in 2000 to enroll and characterize individuals with CF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001179> "A case-control study of genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease, led by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and Case Western Reserve University, that enrolled unrelated patients homozygous for F508del whose lung function for age was at either extreme (severe or mild disease) from cystic fibrosis centres across the United States, together with a smaller population-based sample from children's hospitals in Denver, Wisconsin and Boston.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3711243/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CFLD was defined as cirrhosis in patients ≥ 2 years of age, confirmed by imaging (ultrasound, CT, MRI) showing hepatic parenchymal abnormalities of portal hypertension (esophageal varices, portal-systemic collaterals, splenomegaly) in the absence of another cause for liver disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3711243/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of the CF controls were ascertained from the GMS Lung Study population (DF508 homozygotes; 92.6%)5, Most of the other controls had biallelic PI mutations (see online supplement, Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19738092+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the initial study, 124 patients with CFLD (enrolled January 1999-December 2004) and 843 control patients without CFLD were studied by genotyping 9 polymorphisms in 5 genes previously studied as modifiers of liver disease in CF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19738092+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two-stage case-control study enrolling patients with CF and severe liver disease with portal hypertension (CFLD) from 63 CF centers in the United States as well as 32 in Canada and 18 outside of North America, with the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill as the coordinating site.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3711243/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 191 CF patients evaluated for CFLD (portal hypertension; enrolled 1/2005–2/2007), there were 139 CF patients who fulfilled criteria from 35 CF Centers in 10 countries (Argentina, 5; Australia, 5; Canada, 24; Chile, 1; France, 9; Ireland, 8; Israel, 7; Italy, 14; United Kingdom, 4; and U.S., 62).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27062904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30307979") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19738092") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3711243/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our initial study compared polymorphic genotypes in these candidate modifier genes in CF subjects with CFLD and “control” CF patients (without CFLD, who were at least 15 years of age).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001180> "A two-stage case-control study of genetic modifiers of severe liver disease in cystic fibrosis, coordinated by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, which from January 1999 enrolled people with cystic fibrosis and cirrhosis with portal hypertension from cystic fibrosis centres in the United States, Canada and other countries of Europe, Australia, South America and the Middle East, and compared them with people with cystic fibrosis aged 15 or over without liver disease, many of them from the Genetic Modifier Study of lung disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16841623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23091423") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35712048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16841623") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16841623+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adult outpatients with moderate to severe DSM-IV-defined MDD and normal sexual functioning were randomly assigned to receive bupropion XL (300-450 mg/day; N = 276), escitalopram (10-20 mg/day; N = 281), or placebo (N = 273) for up to 8 weeks") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181> "A pharmacogenetic sample of adult outpatients of white European ancestry with moderate to severe major depressive disorder who completed escitalopram treatment in two identically designed randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled GlaxoSmithKline trials run in the United States in 2003–2004 to compare bupropion XL with escitalopram for antidepressant efficacy and effects on sexual functioning; GlaxoSmithKline contributed their DNA to the NEWMEDS consortium for genetic studies of antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16841623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23091423") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35712048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23091423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3472989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study aims to test the hypothesis that common genetic variants can predict response to antidepressants in a clinically meaningful way.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001181> "A pharmacogenetic sample of adult outpatients of white European ancestry with moderate to severe major depressive disorder who completed escitalopram treatment in two identically designed randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled GlaxoSmithKline trials run in the United States in 2003–2004 to compare bupropion XL with escitalopram for antidepressant efficacy and effects on sexual functioning; GlaxoSmithKline contributed their DNA to the NEWMEDS consortium for genetic studies of antidepressant response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16841623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23091423") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35712048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23091423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3472989/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Out of the 210 patients in
