AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25086665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/cancer-types/pancreas/panscan") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The third phase of PanScan (PanScan III) was conducted using recently identified incident pancreatic cancer cases drawn from fourteen cohorts from the cohort consortium, including nine prospective cohorts who participated in PanScan I, and five newly joined cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218> "A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute's Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25086665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/cancer-types/pancreas/panscan") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study, also known as \"PanScan\", is funded by the National Cancer Institute (NCI) and involves conducting a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of common genetic variants to identify markers of susceptibility to pancreatic cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218> "A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute's Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25086665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/cancer-types/pancreas/panscan") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the framework of the NCI-sponsored Cohort Consortium, investigators from 12 prospective epidemiologic cohorts formed the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium in 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001218> "A consortium formed in 2006 within the US National Cancer Institute's Cohort Consortium by investigators of 12 prospective cohort studies to run PanScan, a multi-stage genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer funded by the NCI. PanScan I genotyped cases and controls from the cohorts and one case-control study, PanScan II (from 2007) those of eight case-control studies, and PanScan III new incident cases from 14 cohorts and from case series and case-control studies, mostly people of European ancestry from the United States and Europe.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4422072/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A new genome-wide association study was conducted in prostate cancer cases and controls of European ancestry from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4422072/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4,600 cases and 2,941 controls of European ancestry from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial were genotyped using the Illumina HumanOmni2.5 Beadchip and passed rigorous quality control criteria (see Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4422072/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4,838 prostate cancer cases and 3,053 controls of European ancestry, matched on age and year of randomization, were selected for stage 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4422072/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All prostate cancer cases detected during screening or reported during the trial were pathologically confirmed, and information on stage and grade was abstracted from medical records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4422072/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To discover additional loci associated with risk and to identify loci specific for aggressive prostate cancer, here we conduct a multistage GWAS for prostate cancer among men of European ancestry using the Illumina HumanOmni2.5 Beadchip, which provides greater coverage of uncommon SNPs for individuals of European ancestry than microarrays used in previous GWAS of prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25939597") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28139693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30287866") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6172280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PEGASUS was supported by the Intramural Research Program, Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics, National Cancer Institute, National Institutes of Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001219> "A genome-wide association study of prostate cancer run by the Division of Cancer Epidemiology and Genetics of the US National Cancer Institute as a nested case-control study within the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian (PLCO) Cancer Screening Trial, in which men of European ancestry with pathologically confirmed prostate cancer detected during screening or reported during the trial, and men of the trial without prostate cancer matched to them on age and year of randomization, were genotyped genome-wide to find prostate cancer susceptibility loci, including loci for aggressive disease.")

