AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19287092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3297116/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A nested case-control GWAS study of angiographic CAD was done in PennCath (n=1401 white patients).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001220> "A hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for coronary artery disease at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center, United States, which from July 1998 to March 2003 recruited consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation and coronary angiography. A nested case-control genome-wide association study of angiographic coronary artery disease in its white patients is one of the core studies of the CARDIoGRAM consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19287092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3297116/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between July 1, 1998, and March 31, 2003, PennCath recruited 3815 consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001220> "A hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for coronary artery disease at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center, United States, which from July 1998 to March 2003 recruited consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation and coronary angiography. A nested case-control genome-wide association study of angiographic coronary artery disease in its white patients is one of the core studies of the CARDIoGRAM consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19287092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3297116/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Discovery studies were PennCath and MedStar (webappendix p 2), which recruited patients before coronary angiography at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center (Penn) and Washington Hospital Center (WHC), respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001220> "A hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for coronary artery disease at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center, United States, which from July 1998 to March 2003 recruited consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation and coronary angiography. A nested case-control genome-wide association study of angiographic coronary artery disease in its white patients is one of the core studies of the CARDIoGRAM consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19287092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3297116/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PennCath is a hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for CAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001220> "A hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for coronary artery disease at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center, United States, which from July 1998 to March 2003 recruited consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation and coronary angiography. A nested case-control genome-wide association study of angiographic coronary artery disease in its white patients is one of the core studies of the CARDIoGRAM consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19287092") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26343929") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5019244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Notably, PennCATH is one of the core GWA studies nested within the Coronary ARtery DIsease Genome‐wide Replication And Meta‐analysis (CARDIoGRAM) consortium meta‐data and serves as a representative regional population with no admixture 20, 21.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001220> "A hospital-based study of genes and biomarkers for coronary artery disease at the University of Pennsylvania Medical Center, United States, which from July 1998 to March 2003 recruited consecutive patients undergoing cardiac catheterisation and coronary angiography. A nested case-control genome-wide association study of angiographic coronary artery disease in its white patients is one of the core studies of the CARDIoGRAM consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4628902/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Multimodal neuroimaging data, developmental histories, behavioral and cognitive assessments, and/or genome-wide genotypes are now available for 1493 children and adolescents, aged 3 to 21 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4628902/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main objective of the multi-site Pediatric Imaging, Neurocognition, and Genetics (PING) study was to create a large repository of standardized measurements of behavioral and imaging phenotypes accompanied by whole genome genotyping acquired from typically-developing children varying widely in age (3 to 20 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4628902/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The repository contains aggregated data collected at 10 sites in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25937488+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cross-sectional study produced sharable data from 1493 children, and these data have been described in several publications focusing on brain and cognitive development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4628902/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited through local postings and outreach activities conducted in the greater metropolitan areas of Baltimore, Boston, Honolulu, Los Angeles, New Haven, New York, Sacramento, and San Diego.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25937488") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35998220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9436320/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PING data are disseminated by the PING Coordinating Center at the Center for Human Development, University of California, San Diego.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001221> "A multi-site cross-sectional study of typically developing children, adolescents and young adults aged 3 to 20 years, recruited through local postings and outreach in eight metropolitan areas of the United States and assessed at ten US sites, with its coordinating centre at the University of California, San Diego, that collected developmental histories, cognitive assessments, multimodal brain imaging and genome-wide genotypes to create a shared repository for studying brain and cognitive development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204770/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (pKARMA)Sweden5,53754343672702") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5517429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were breast cancer-free participants recruited between 2010 and 2011 from Helsingborg and Stockholm in Sweden, a subset of the KARMA study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5517429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Libro1 consists of female primary breast cancer cases diagnosed in Stockholm between January 2001 and December 2008 identified via the Regional Cancer register61.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5517429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We constructed celiac disease PRS profiles (celiac-PRS) using individual level genotype data for subjects in the pKARMA study genotyped as part of the iCOGS initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5517429/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "pKARMA is made up of 5,002 invasive breast cancer cases (from the Linne-Brost 1 (Libro1) study) and 5,433 controls (from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA60)).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28725034") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38366028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11160497/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KARMA and pKARMA participants donated blood samples at study enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001222> "A Swedish breast cancer case-control study, known as prevalent KARMA, that combines women diagnosed with primary breast cancer in Stockholm between 2001 and 2008, identified through the regional cancer register for the LIBRO-1 study, with breast-cancer-free women from the Karolinska Mammography Project for Risk Prediction of Breast Cancer (KARMA) cohort as controls, all of whom gave blood samples, and whose genotypes contribute to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium's studies of breast cancer risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17881719+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consenting PD patients not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy (n = 806) were randomized equally to CEP-1347 in dosages of 10 mg BID, 25 mg BID, or 50 mg BID, or matching placebo, and were evaluated blindly and prospectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2574855/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PRECEPT study was designed to determine whether this drug could slow the progression of early PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2574855/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PRECEPT study was stopped early following a pre-specified interim analysis for futility.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2574855/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants (n=806) were enrolled between April 2002 and April 2004 at 65 sites across the United States and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2574855/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a longitudinal cohort investigation among participants in the PRECEPT study, a two-year double-blind, randomized trial of oral CEP-1347, an antiapoptotic mixed lineage kinase inhibitor that had been found to be neuroprotective in animal models of PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17881719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18413464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5244667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "two well‐phenotyped, failed phase III clinical trials with longitudinal, observational extension studies (Deprenyl and Tocopherol Antioxidative Therapy of Parkinsonism [DATATOP]15; Parkinson Research Examination of CEP‐1347 Trial/A Longitudinal Follow‐up of the PRECEPT Study Cohort [PreCEPT/PostCEPT]13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001223> "A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial run by the Parkinson Study Group, which enrolled people with early Parkinson's disease not yet requiring dopaminergic therapy at 65 sites in the United States and Canada between April 2002 and April 2004 to test whether the mixed lineage kinase inhibitor CEP-1347 could slow disease progression; the trial was stopped early for futility in 2005, and its participants were then followed in the observational PostCEPT study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8295407") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited from seven psychiatric hospitals in Sweden (Danderyd, Huddinge, Hudiksvall, Sahlgrenska, Umeå, Uppsala, and Örebro).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8295407/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All blood samples were sent to Karolinska Institutet Biobank where DNA was extracted and stored.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36069021+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2013 and 2017, patients who had at least one treatment series recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT were invited to provide a blood sample for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10113810/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, a letter of invitation was sent to patients ≥18 years old registered in Q-ECT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10113810/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Local hospital staff routinely enter data on each treatment series into the register via a web-based platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33483693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36069021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10113810/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those who volunteered to participate completed a telephone interview and donated blood that was sent via overnight mail to Karolinska Institutet Biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001224> "A Swedish study that between 2013 and 2017 recruited adults who had received electroconvulsive therapy (ECT) recorded in the Swedish National Quality Register for ECT, inviting registered patients by letter to a telephone interview and blood sampling and recruiting others at Swedish psychiatric hospitals before an ECT series, and that links their DNA, stored at the Karolinska Institutet Biobank, to the register's data on each treatment series, to study predictors of ECT outcome, including genetic ones, and the genetics of severe depressive episodes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were recruited from three of Mirpur's northern wards, which are predominantly low-SES households living in slum conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROVIDE study was a randomized controlled clinical trial with two vaccine interventions, which enrolled a birth cohort of 700 children and their mothers, and followed the children for their first 2 years of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objectives of the PROVIDE study (in Bangladesh) were to determine: 1) the efficacy of a 2-dose Rotarix® oral rotavirus vaccine (given at 10 and 17 weeks of age) to prevent rotavirus diarrhea in the first year of life and 2) OPV efficacy when a single inactivated polio vaccine (IPV) dose replaced the fourth dose of trivalent OPV (tOPV).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The rationale for the design of the “Performance of Rotavirus and Oral Polio Vaccines in Developing Countries” (PROVIDE) study was to carefully evaluate factors that could interfere with oral vaccine efficacy in an environment characterized by poverty, urban overcrowding, and poor sanitary conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study had a 2 × 2 factorial design (Table 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35420468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38524222") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25711607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4385767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within 7 days after giving birth, screening for eligibility and study consenting occurred in the household by trained FRAs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001225> "A birth cohort of children enrolled with their mothers within seven days of birth in low-income wards of Mirpur, Dhaka, Bangladesh, from May 2011, into a randomized controlled trial with a two-by-two factorial design, conducted by the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) with the University of Vermont and the University of Virginia, that tested a delayed-dose oral rotavirus vaccine and the replacement of one oral polio vaccine dose by an injectable polio vaccine, and followed the children through their first two years of life to study why oral vaccines underperform in children living with poverty, poor sanitation and overcrowding.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32546850") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4580993/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the QTR, we split the sample into three sets of families to maximize the intersection of the SNPs genotyped on all family members: QTR610—families in which all individuals had been genotyped on the Illumina Human610 or Human660W chip; QTR370—families in which at least one individual had been genotyped on the Illumina CNV370 chip; QTRCoreExome—families in which all individuals had been genotyped on the HumanCoreExome chip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> "A population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages living in Australia, established in 2006 at the QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose members are invited into twin research projects on health and disease; genetic studies drawing on QIMR Berghofer's genotyped twin and family samples report them under the registry's name.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32546850") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By joining, you are making yourself available to participate in interesting and exciting research projects and be a part of scientific discoveries about health and disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> "A population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages living in Australia, established in 2006 at the QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose members are invited into twin research projects on health and disease; genetic studies drawing on QIMR Berghofer's genotyped twin and family samples report them under the registry's name.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32546850") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Contact will only come from scientific researchers whose research has been carefully reviewed and subsequently approved by the Human Research Ethics Committee at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> "A population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages living in Australia, established in 2006 at the QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose members are invited into twin research projects on health and disease; genetic studies drawing on QIMR Berghofer's genotyped twin and family samples report them under the registry's name.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32546850") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Queensland Twin Registry (QTwin) Study is a population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages, living in Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> "A population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages living in Australia, established in 2006 at the QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose members are invited into twin research projects on health and disease; genetic studies drawing on QIMR Berghofer's genotyped twin and family samples report them under the registry's name.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26242864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32546850") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.qimrb.edu.au/studies/queensland-twin-registry-(qtwin)-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Queensland Twin Registry (QTwin) was established in 2006") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001226> "A population-based registry of identical and non-identical twins and triplets of all ages living in Australia, established in 2006 at the QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose members are invited into twin research projects on health and disease; genetic studies drawing on QIMR Berghofer's genotyped twin and family samples report them under the registry's name.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37952397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38958117") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10663385/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the family-based ascertainment of REAAADI, interested participants are eligible if they are 50 years of age or older, identify as AA, and have at least two family members with concerns of memory or cognitive problems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227> "A multi-site US study of African Americans, a sub-study of the Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project run by investigators at North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University, Wake Forest School of Medicine, the University of Miami, Columbia University and Case Western Reserve University, that ascertains African American families affected by Alzheimer's disease through community outreach and collects blood or saliva samples, medical and family histories and cognitive assessments, to identify rare variants, genes and pathways associated with Alzheimer's disease in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37952397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38958117") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10663385/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REAAADI was designed to identify rare variant enriched genes and genetic pathways associated with AD among AAs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227> "A multi-site US study of African Americans, a sub-study of the Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project run by investigators at North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University, Wake Forest School of Medicine, the University of Miami, Columbia University and Case Western Reserve University, that ascertains African American families affected by Alzheimer's disease through community outreach and collects blood or saliva samples, medical and family histories and cognitive assessments, to identify rare variants, genes and pathways associated with Alzheimer's disease in African Americans.")
