AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37952397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38958117") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10663385/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Standard study procedures consists of blood sample collection via venipuncture or saliva collection and clinical data collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227> "A multi-site US study of African Americans, a sub-study of the Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project run by investigators at North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University, Wake Forest School of Medicine, the University of Miami, Columbia University and Case Western Reserve University, that ascertains African American families affected by Alzheimer's disease through community outreach and collects blood or saliva samples, medical and family histories and cognitive assessments, to identify rare variants, genes and pathways associated with Alzheimer's disease in African Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37952397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38958117") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37212603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10663385/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical protocol includes medical and family history interviews as well as objective measurements of cognitive abilities (e.g., assessments from the National Alzheimer’s Coordinating Center’s Uniform Data Set 2.0),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001227> "A multi-site US study of African Americans, a sub-study of the Alzheimer's Disease Sequencing Project run by investigators at North Carolina Agricultural and Technical State University, Wake Forest School of Medicine, the University of Miami, Columbia University and Case Western Reserve University, that ascertains African American families affected by Alzheimer's disease through community outreach and collects blood or saliva samples, medical and family histories and cognitive assessments, to identify rare variants, genes and pathways associated with Alzheimer's disease in African Americans.")
