# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15687363+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 3740 patients diagnosed between October 1, 1999, and August 30, 2002, with incident malignant lymphomas, including non-Hodgkin lymphoma, chronic lymphocytic leukemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma, and 3187 population controls provided detailed information on history of UV exposure and skin cancer and information on other possible risk factors for lymphomas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4268499/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 586 patients diagnosed with cHL according to the WHO classification in the study period and 3,187 controls representing 91% and 71% of eligible cases and controls, respectively, participated in the study, which included telephone interview and blood sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4268499/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population encompassed Danish and Swedish speaking residents aged 18-74 with no history of HIV infection, solid organ transplantation or previous hematopoietic malignancy in Denmark from June 1, 2000 to August 30, 2002, and in Sweden from October 1, 1999, to April 15, 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4411784/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, SCALE is a population-based case–control study of the etiology of malignant lymphomas conducted in Sweden and Denmark 1999 to 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4411784/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through a rapid case ascertainment network, the patients were identified shortly after diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15687363") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21037568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25294155") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2652/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2652_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Frequency matched (age in 10 year intervals, sex and country) population controls prospectively identified every 6 months in nationwide population registers (incidence density sampling).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001230> "A population-based case-control study of the causes of malignant lymphomas (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, including chronic lymphocytic leukaemia, and Hodgkin lymphoma) among residents of Denmark and Sweden aged 18–74, recruited in 1999–2002, with incident cases identified shortly after diagnosis through a rapid case-ascertainment network and controls sampled from the national population registers, and with a telephone interview and blood sampling.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35708486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39361370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35708486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9652109/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our GWAS constitutes the largest study on COVID-19 genetic risk factors conducted in Spain, with an intrinsic design benefit that SCOURGE includes detailed clinical and genetic information gathered homogeneously across the country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231> "A cohort of COVID-19 patients with detailed clinical information, recruited from hospitals across Spain from March to December 2020 and in Latin America from March 2020 to July 2021 by a Spanish research consortium launched in May 2020 to study host genetic factors in COVID-19 and find biomarkers of its course and prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35708486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39361370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35708486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9652109/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through diverse nested sub-studies, the Spanish Coalition to Unlock Research on Host Genetics on COVID-19 (SCOURGE) consortium was launched in May 2020 aiming to find biomarkers of evolution and prognosis that can have an immediate impact on clinical management and therapeutic decisions in SARS-CoV-2 infections.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231> "A cohort of COVID-19 patients with detailed clinical information, recruited from hospitals across Spain from March to December 2020 and in Latin America from March 2020 to July 2021 by a Spanish research consortium launched in May 2020 to study host genetic factors in COVID-19 and find biomarkers of its course and prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35708486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39361370") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39361370") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11449485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Spanish Coalition to Unlock Research on Host Genetics on COVID-19 (SCOURGE) recruited COVID-19 patients between March and December 2020 from hospitals across Spain and from March 2020 to July 2021 in Latin America (https://www.scourge-covid.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001231> "A cohort of COVID-19 patients with detailed clinical information, recruited from hospitals across Spain from March to December 2020 and in Latin America from March 2020 to July 2021 by a Spanish research consortium launched in May 2020 to study host genetic factors in COVID-19 and find biomarkers of its course and prognosis.")

