# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5390547/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the original 9704 white women, 7008 (96% of active participants) completed at least the questionnaire component of a Year 10 examination (between 1997 and 1998).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5390547/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SOF enrolled 9704 women aged ≥65 years between September 1986 and October 1988 for participation in the baseline examination [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5390547/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subsequently, at the Year 10 SOF examination conducted between 1997 and 1998, 662 African-American women were enrolled in the study increasing the total cohort enrollment to 10,366 women [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-023-04869-0/MediaObjects/42003_2023_4869_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SOF participants were followed up every four months by postcard or telephone to ascertain the occurrence of falls, fractures and changes in address.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-023-04869-0/MediaObjects/42003_2023_4869_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Study of Osteoporotic Fractures (SOF) is a prospective multicenter study of risk factors for vertebral and non-vertebral fractures 21 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28465840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37619450") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37402774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-023-04869-0/MediaObjects/42003_2023_4869_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "recruited from populations-based listings in four U.S. areas: Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001236> "A prospective multicentre cohort of community-dwelling women aged 65 or older in the United States, whose original, white members were recruited from population-based listings in four areas (Baltimore, Maryland; Minneapolis, Minnesota; Portland, Oregon; and the Monongahela Valley, Pennsylvania) between September 1986 and October 1988 and were joined by African American women enrolled at the Year 10 examination in 1997–1998, followed by regular contacts and repeat examinations to study risk factors for osteoporotic fractures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35580588") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10918580/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All twins responded to web-based surveys, including assessments of ACEs and depressive symptoms, with response rates of 60.0%, 42.0%, and 69.0%, respectively, in the 3 cohorts.39 Cohorts were additionally linked to nationwide health registers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> "A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35580588") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10918580/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Namely, we used the Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment (STAGE) comprising 25 313 twins (born 1959-1985) surveyed 2005 to 2006,37,38") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> "A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35580588") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12117053/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All twins were born in Sweden and were originally eligible for participation in either of two health screening survey studies conducted by the Swedish Twin Registry; the Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development (TCHAD)34 and the Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment (STAGE)35, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> "A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35580588") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12859210/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2012 and 2013, a web survey was administered to the STAGE cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> "A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35580588") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38446452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40425723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41624966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12859210/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 'Study of Twin Adults: Genes and Environment’ (STAGE) is a cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry at the Karolinska Institute in Stockholm, of approximately 32,000 twin individuals, born between 1959 and 1985.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001237> "A cohort of the Swedish Twin Registry made up of twins born in Sweden between 1959 and 1985, who were invited to a web-based health screening survey in 2005–2006 and have since been followed through linkage to national health registers and further web surveys.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00021528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15061154+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "STAR*D is a multisite, prospective, randomized, multistep clinical trial of outpatients with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> "A multisite, prospective, randomised, multistep clinical trial, funded by the US National Institute of Mental Health through the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas, that from 2001 enrolled adult outpatients aged 18 to 75 with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder from primary and specialty (psychiatric) care practices across the United States, to determine which treatments work best for those who do not respond adequately to initial treatment with citalopram.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00021528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15061154+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study compares various treatment options for those who do not attain a satisfactory response with citalopram, a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor antidepressant.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> "A multisite, prospective, randomised, multistep clinical trial, funded by the US National Institute of Mental Health through the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas, that from 2001 enrolled adult outpatients aged 18 to 75 with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder from primary and specialty (psychiatric) care practices across the United States, to determine which treatments work best for those who do not respond adequately to initial treatment with citalopram.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00021528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15061154+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study enrolls 4000 adults (ages 18-75) from both primary and specialty care practices who have not had either a prior inadequate response or clear-cut intolerance to a robust trial of protocol treatments during the current major depressive episode.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> "A multisite, prospective, randomised, multistep clinical trial, funded by the US National Institute of Mental Health through the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas, that from 2001 enrolled adult outpatients aged 18 to 75 with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder from primary and specialty (psychiatric) care practices across the United States, to determine which treatments work best for those who do not respond adequately to initial treatment with citalopram.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00021528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23377640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10416089/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The STAR*D study was funded by NIMH via contract N01MH90003 to the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> "A multisite, prospective, randomised, multistep clinical trial, funded by the US National Institute of Mental Health through the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas, that from 2001 enrolled adult outpatients aged 18 to 75 with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder from primary and specialty (psychiatric) care practices across the United States, to determine which treatments work best for those who do not respond adequately to initial treatment with citalopram.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15061154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27519822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00021528") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23377640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10416089/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included 4,041 treatment-seeking adult outpatients, recruited in 18 primary care and 23 psychiatric clinical sites across the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001238> "A multisite, prospective, randomised, multistep clinical trial, funded by the US National Institute of Mental Health through the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center at Dallas, that from 2001 enrolled adult outpatients aged 18 to 75 with nonpsychotic major depressive disorder from primary and specialty (psychiatric) care practices across the United States, to determine which treatments work best for those who do not respond adequately to initial treatment with citalopram.")

