# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17539366+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish Twin study of CHild and Adolescent Development (TCHAD) is a longitudinal study of how genes and environments contribute to development of health and behavioral problems from childhood to adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17539366+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The last data collection was in 2005 when the twins were 19 to 20 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5581816/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based prospective cohort study including all twins from the Swedish Twin Registry who were born in Sweden 1985–1986 (N = 2960) [19] was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5581816/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twins and/or their parents were contacted on four occasions (i.e., Waves); when the twins were 8–9, 13–14, 16–17, and 19–20 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6133086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Swedish Twin study of Child and Adolescent Development (TCHAD), we have followed 1,500 twin pairs from age 8 to age 20 with 4 waves of questionnaires to both parents and twins (1994, 1999, 2002, 2006) and we just completed a follow-up (November 2013) at age 26.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17539366") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28638965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29845340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ki.se/en/meb/twin-study-of-child-and-adolescent-development-tchad") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37289452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10251215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were originally included in a population-based longitudinal twin study, the Twin Study of Child and Adolescent Development (TCHAD),34 comprising all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986 (2960 children in total).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001240> "A population-based longitudinal study, run from Karolinska Institutet, of all twins born in Sweden between May 1985 and December 1986, identified through the Swedish Twin Registry, in which the twins and their parents completed questionnaires in four waves from 1994 to 2005, when the twins were aged 8–9, 13–14, 16–17 and 19–20, with a further follow-up at age 26, to study how genes and environments contribute to the development of health and behavioural problems from childhood to adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23815563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3814815/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SFGH investigators at the University of California San Francisco, Brain and Spinal Injury Center served as the TRACK-TBI Coordinating Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8927841/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of patients in the US cohort were recruited between 2014 and 2018 to TRACK-TBI, a NIH-NINDS funded prospective multicenter study aimed at improving the characterization of TBI through the collection of clinical and genetic data, plasma biomarkers, as well as neuroimaging and other multidimensional outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10028488/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria for TBI participants in the parent study were presentation within 24 hours of injury to a participating level I trauma center with clinical suspicion of TBI (ie, head computed tomography [CT] scan ordered)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10028488/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OTCs presented within 24 hours of injury with orthopedic injuries and were excluded if they had physical signs of head trauma or met any criteria for TBI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10028488/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TRACK-TBI is a prospective, multicenter study recruiting participants from 18 level I trauma centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35301180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02119182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36939699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10028488/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TRACK-TBI study enrolled participants within 24 hours of injury from 2/26/2014 – 7/27/2018 with the initial study designed to follow participants until 1 year post-injury.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001241> "A prospective, multicentre, longitudinal observational cohort study, led from the University of California, San Francisco, with funding from the US National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, that from February 2014 to July 2018 enrolled patients presenting within 24 hours of a traumatic brain injury who received a clinically indicated head CT scan, together with orthopaedic trauma controls, at 18 level I trauma centres in the United States, and collected clinical, neuroimaging, blood biomarker, genetic and outcome data to improve the characterisation, diagnosis and prognosis of traumatic brain injury.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In TN01 (renamed Pathway to Prevention) >250,000 relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes have been screened for autoantibodies (Fig. 1), and Pathway to Prevention remains the largest long-running cohort study of both children and adults at risk for disease with 8,937 individuals enrolled in monitoring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> "A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TN05 study was a randomized, double-blind study where participants with new-onset type 1 diabetes were treated with a four-dose course of the B-cell-depleting agent rituximab.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> "A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TrialNet actively screens relatives of individuals with type 1 diabetes, but other individuals who do not have a relative with the disease may join TN01 if they are found to have positive islet autoantibodies in an outside laboratory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> "A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12178618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "When the Pathway to Prevention study initiated testing in March 2003, screening included measurement of GADA, IAA, and IA2A.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> "A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40272284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40272284+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases (NIDDK) in 2001, Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet (TrialNet) is an international consortium of clinical research centers that studies the development of type 1 diabetes and performs clinical studies aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001242> "A cohort of people with or at risk of type 1 diabetes recruited since 2001 by Type 1 Diabetes TrialNet, an international network of clinical research centres established by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases: chiefly relatives of people with type 1 diabetes who are screened for islet autoantibodies and followed for progression in its Pathway to Prevention natural-history study, and people at risk of or newly diagnosed with type 1 diabetes enrolled in its trials aimed at delaying or preventing the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21194473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10667470+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based consecutive incident cases of breast and ovarian cancer were invited to participate in the University of California, Irvine breast and ovarian family registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> "A population-based breast cancer case-control study run from the University of California, Irvine, whose cases were breast cancer patients diagnosed in Orange County, California, in the year from March 1994, ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County and enrolled as probands in the UCI population-based breast and ovarian cancer family registry, and whose controls were Orange County residents recruited in 1998–2003 by random digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21194473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10882857+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population under study was all breast cancer cases diagnosed in Orange County, CA, during the 1-year period beginning 1 March 1994 and all ovarian cancer cases diagnosed in Orange County during the 2-year period beginning 1 March 1994.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> "A population-based breast cancer case-control study run from the University of California, Irvine, whose cases were breast cancer patients diagnosed in Orange County, California, in the year from March 1994, ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County and enrolled as probands in the UCI population-based breast and ovarian cancer family registry, and whose controls were Orange County residents recruited in 1998–2003 by random digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21194473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10882857+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This report focuses on the first consecutively ascertained 802 participating probands enrolled in the study, of which 9 were male breast cancer probands, 673 were female breast cancer probands and 120 were ovarian cancer probands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> "A population-based breast cancer case-control study run from the University of California, Irvine, whose cases were breast cancer patients diagnosed in Orange County, California, in the year from March 1994, ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County and enrolled as probands in the UCI population-based breast and ovarian cancer family registry, and whose controls were Orange County residents recruited in 1998–2003 by random digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21194473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases diagnosed in Orange County, California from 1994-1995; ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County California (CSPOC)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> "A population-based breast cancer case-control study run from the University of California, Irvine, whose cases were breast cancer patients diagnosed in Orange County, California, in the year from March 1994, ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County and enrolled as probands in the UCI population-based breast and ovarian cancer family registry, and whose controls were Orange County residents recruited in 1998–2003 by random digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10667470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10882857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21194473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruited from 1998-2003 using random digit dialling among Orange County residents; frequency matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001243> "A population-based breast cancer case-control study run from the University of California, Irvine, whose cases were breast cancer patients diagnosed in Orange County, California, in the year from March 1994, ascertained through the population-based Cancer Surveillance Program of Orange County and enrolled as probands in the UCI population-based breast and ovarian cancer family registry, and whose controls were Orange County residents recruited in 1998–2003 by random digit dialling and frequency-matched to cases by age and race/ethnicity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27544330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5071147/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, participants were mailed self-administered questionnaires during the following four time periods: 1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005, and 2012–2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6041262/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the US National Cancer Institute, in collaboration with the University of Minnesota and the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT), is studying cancer incidence and mortality among 146,022 (106,953 women) US radiologic technologists who were certified for at least two years during 1926–198241.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6041262/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four different questionnaires were administered during the periods 1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005, and 2012–2014 to collect information on health outcomes (including self-reports of glaucoma and macular degeneration, except in the first questionnaire), work history, demographic and lifestyle characteristics, and medical histories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Rad Tech Study began in 1982 by identifying 146,022 current and former radiologic technologists who were certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT) for at least two years from 1926 through 1982.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort has also been a valuable resource for investigating the effects of ultraviolet light exposure and other lifestyle factors on cancer and other health outcomes, including the growing prevalence of obesity and the nature of the relationship between body mass index and all-cause mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29992993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://dceg.cancer.gov/research/who-we-study/cohorts/us-radiologic-technologists") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objectives of the study are to assess risks for cancer and other diseases from Long-term low-dose occupational and personal medical ionizing radiation exposures") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001244> "A cohort of current and former radiologic technologists in the United States, women and men certified by the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists for at least two years between 1926 and 1982, assembled in 1982 by the US National Cancer Institute with the University of Minnesota and the Registry and followed through four mailed questionnaires (1983–1989, 1994–1998, 2003–2005 and 2012–2014), to assess risks of cancer and other diseases from protracted low-dose occupational and personal medical ionising radiation and other exposures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5589236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Future studies may be able to use this sub-phenotype to help localize the mechanism of AF when investigating newly discovered clinical and genetic associations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5589236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Post-ablation monitoring for arrhythmia recurrence included a 12-lead ECG and use of an ambulatory ECG monitor at 3, 6, and 12-months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5589236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pulmonary vein anatomy was assessed by pre-ablation imaging with a cardiac MRI or CT angiogram.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5589236/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VAFAR is a prospective, observational clinical biorepository [4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with AF referred for AF ablation are prospectively enrolled. A detailed clinical history is recorded, along with imaging data (cardiac MRI or CT). Blood samples are obtained for DNA extraction at the time of ablation. Details of the ablation procedure are recorded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28880943") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02404415") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000997.v6.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vanderbilt Atrial Fibrillation Ablation Registry (VAFAR) was founded in 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001245> "A prospective clinical and genetic biorepository at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, founded in 2011, that enrols adults scheduled for catheter ablation of atrial fibrillation, recording their medical history, pre-ablation imaging and procedure details, collecting blood for DNA at the time of ablation and following them for arrhythmia recurrence at 3, 6 and 12 months, to identify predictors of response to ablation and to support research on the mechanisms of atrial fibrillation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.125") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All VETSA participants are men and all were in some branch of military service at some time between 1965 and 1975.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.125") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection for VETSA wave 1 began in 2003 with 5- to 6-year follow-ups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.125") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VETSA participants are all part of the Vietnam Era Twin Registry, from which they were randomly selected from a large prior study that attempted to enroll all available twins") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.125") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VETSA selection criteria were (1) being in one’s 50s at the time of recruitment, and (2) both twins in a pair had to be willing to participate in the baseline assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31933447+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vietnam Era Twin Study of Aging (VETSA) is a longitudinal behavioral genetic study with a primary focus on cognitive and brain aging in men, particularly early identification of risk for mild cognitive impairment (MCI) and Alzheimer's disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23110957") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31933447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39036434") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11257108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection occurred at two sites (San Diego, CA, and Boston, MA) using identical protocols.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001246> "A longitudinal behavioural genetic study of cognitive and brain aging in men, and later of early risk of mild cognitive impairment and Alzheimer's disease, whose participants are twins randomly selected from the Vietnam Era Twin Registry of male twin pairs who both served in the US military between 1965 and 1975, recruited in their 50s and assessed at two sites, San Diego and Boston, from 2003, with follow-up waves every 5 to 6 years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001247> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001247>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4912948/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VHIR-FMT-BARCELONA Spain HumanCore ExomeChip EUR 545 320") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001247> "A case-control collection from Barcelona, Spain, of European-ancestry patients with non-lacunar ischaemic stroke confirmed by neuroimaging within 7 days, a subset of those enrolled in the Genetic contribution to functional Outcome and Disability after Stroke (GODS) project, and of controls over 40 years old without ischaemic stroke, collected in Barcelona primary care centres and Spanish network hospitals for the ISSYS and GRECOS studies, genotyped together and used as a case-control set in ischaemic stroke genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26708676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the samples (cases and controls) were genotyped using the Infinium Human Core Exome Chip (Illumina).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001247> "A case-control collection from Barcelona, Spain, of European-ancestry patients with non-lacunar ischaemic stroke confirmed by neuroimaging within 7 days, a subset of those enrolled in the Genetic contribution to functional Outcome and Disability after Stroke (GODS) project, and of controls over 40 years old without ischaemic stroke, collected in Barcelona primary care centres and Spanish network hospitals for the ISSYS and GRECOS studies, genotyped together and used as a case-control set in ischaemic stroke genome-wide association studies.")
