AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30271950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001032.v7.p2") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30271950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6123807/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At enrollment into the registry, a detailed medical and drug history was obtained from all patients and patients were also asked to complete a symptom questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001249> "A clinical and genetic registry at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, founded in 2001, that prospectively enrols patients with atrial fibrillation together with affected and unaffected family members, recording a detailed medical and drug history, an atrial fibrillation symptom severity assessment and a blood sample for DNA, and follows them with serial symptom assessments; its early-onset cases were whole-genome sequenced by the NHLBI TOPMed programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30271950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001032.v7.p2") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30271950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6123807/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped novel atrial fibrillation variants in an atrial fibrillation sample set (759 cases and 759 controls) from the Vanderbilt Atrial Fibrillation Registry, a clinical and genetic registry at the Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001249> "A clinical and genetic registry at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, founded in 2001, that prospectively enrols patients with atrial fibrillation together with affected and unaffected family members, recording a detailed medical and drug history, an atrial fibrillation symptom severity assessment and a blood sample for DNA, and follows them with serial symptom assessments; its early-onset cases were whole-genome sequenced by the NHLBI TOPMed programme.")
