AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5430735/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA extraction and genotyping were performed on saliva samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8371358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through WeGene, we conducted an online survey with its customer base.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8371358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WeGene is a leading private genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, which provides direct-to-consumer genetic testing and personalized healthcare information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11464942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided informed consent online and participated in the research online through organic posts on WeGene online platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11464942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 14,675 adult participants drawn from the customer base of WeGene, a personal genetic company, who had been genotyped by ∼700,000 SNPs on microarrays (38% on Affymetrix WeGene V1 array and 62% on Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array-24 v2.0 BeadChip array) as part of the WeGene Personal Genome Services (Kang et al., 2020).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28442769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34457340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39359028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42009823") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13175889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from WeGene Inc.—a Chinese direct-to-consumer genetic testing company.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001250> "A research cohort of customers of WeGene, a direct-to-consumer genetic testing company based in Shenzhen, China, who were genotyped from saliva on microarrays through the WeGene Personal Genome Services and consented to take part in research online, answering surveys posted on WeGene's online platform, website and WeChat channels.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Although the focus of the WSCS was sleep apnea, data have been collected on other sleep disorders including restless legs, insomnia, and narcolepsy, as well as sleep patterns.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the epidemiological project of the SCOR application from the University of Wisconsin, we proposed the Wisconsin Sleep Cohort Study (WSCS), a longitudinal epidemiology study designed to investigate the natural history of SDB by conducting overnight PSG, repeated at 4-year intervals, on a random sample of the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Stage 1, a mailed survey on sociodemographic factors, lifestyle, health history, and sleep characteristics was sent to a random sample of 6000 state employees aged 30-60 years (84% response).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Payroll files of Wisconsin state employees served as the sampling frame.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2858234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Survey respondents were then ranked on risk of SDB based on self-report of snoring. All high-risk respondents were selected for recruitment, along with an age- and sex-frequency matched random sample of low-risk respondents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19743755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35670608") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10091093/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All employees of 5 Wisconsin state agencies, ages 30–60 years at study initiation, were mailed a survey on sleep habits, health, and demographics in 1988.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001251> "A population-based longitudinal cohort study of the University of Wisconsin-Madison in which Wisconsin state employees aged 30 to 60, sampled from state payroll files, answered a mailed sleep and health survey in 1988, after which all respondents at high risk of sleep-disordered breathing by self-reported snoring, with an age- and sex-matched random sample of the others, were invited to overnight in-laboratory polysomnography repeated at about 4-year intervals, to study the natural history and health consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and other sleep disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After enrollment, 10 trained and calibrated clinical examiners (registered dental hygienists or dentists) conducted comprehensive examinations of participating children in their preschools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At enrollment, children’s legal guardians completed a one-page, self-administered, paper-and-pen questionnaire that included 15 demographic and oral health-related questions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children were eligible to participate in ZOE 2.0 if they were between the ages of 3–5 years and currently enrolled in a North Carolina Head Start program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nearly all (98%) examined children provided sufficient DNA from saliva for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, the ZOE 2.0 study population was children attending public preschools (Head Start) in North Carolina, United States, between August 2016 and February 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33139633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7663650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The genome-wide association study (GWAS) of ECC (“ZOE 2.0”) is a community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional, genetic epidemiologic study seeking to address this knowledge gap.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001252> "A community-based, multi-ethnic, cross-sectional genetic epidemiologic study of early childhood oral health, run by the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, that enrolled children aged 3 to 5 attending public preschools (Head Start programmes) across North Carolina, United States, from August 2016 to February 2019, examining their teeth in the preschools and collecting guardian questionnaires, saliva for genotyping and dental plaque, to study the genomics of early childhood caries.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16512801+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since January 2002, the European Commission is funding a large project, 'Protection against Allergy--Study in Rural Environments' (PASTURE; contract no. QLK4-2001-00250), under the Fifth Framework Program in the field of epidemiology of allergic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8111016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In both cohorts, the same questionnaires were administered at the end of pregnancy and when the children were 2, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 60, and 72 months of age to obtain information on frequencies of wheeze, parental atopic status, and environmental exposures with a focus on farming and nutrition (5, 8).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8111016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PASTURE recruited 1133 children in 2002-2005 from rural areas in 5 European countries: Austria, Finland, France, Germany, and Switzerland (6).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9907754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fecal samples were collected from children’s diapers during the home visit at 2 and 12 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, pregnant women were invited to participate during their third trimester of pregnancy and the children from the participating women were recruited at birth. Children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms at birth of the child was assigned to the farm group. The nonfarm group included children of mothers from the same rural areas but not living on a farm.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16512801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33986744") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36356926") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S009167492600093X-mmc3.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PASTURE study is a prospective birth cohort study started in 2002 and is conducted in children from rural areas of 5 European countries (Austria, Finland, France, Germany, and Switzerland) (58). The study was designed to evaluate risk and preventive factors for atopic diseases and was approved by the local research ethics committees in each country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001253> "A prospective birth cohort, begun in 2002 within an EU-funded project, of children from rural areas of Austria, Finland, France, Germany and Switzerland whose mothers were invited during the third trimester of pregnancy in 2002-2005, children of mothers living on family-run livestock farms forming the farm group and children of mothers from the same rural areas not living on a farm the reference group, followed from birth into school age with questionnaires, biological samples and clinical measurements to evaluate risk and protective factors, particularly farm exposures, for asthma and allergic diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4339753") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1st trimester (9.9 weeks of gestation) In person Questionnaire and interview Diet questionnaire Blood sample 2nd trimester (27.9 weeks of gestation) In person Questionnaire and interview Diet questionnaire Blood sample") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339753/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annually between visits, we mail questionnaires to mothers, as well as to children beginning at age 9 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339753/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From April 1999 through November 2002, we recruited women seen for prenatal care at eight urban and suburban practices of a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339753/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are currently conducting an early teen in-person visit (∼12–13 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339753/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established Project Viva to examine prenatal diet and other factors in relation to maternal and child health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4339753/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We saw mothers and children in the hospital during the delivery admission and during infancy (median age 6.3 months), early childhood (median 3.2 years) and mid-childhood (median 7.7 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24639442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37012456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-023-01343-9/MediaObjects/41588_2023_1343_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1999 and 2002, the study recruited women in early pregnancy from eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multispecialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001254> "A prospective pre-birth cohort, run from Harvard Medical School and the Harvard Pilgrim Health Care Institute, of women recruited in early pregnancy at eight obstetric offices of Atrius Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, a multi-specialty group practice in eastern Massachusetts, United States, from April 1999 to November 2002, and their children, followed with in-person visits during pregnancy, at delivery, in infancy, early and mid-childhood and early adolescence and with annual mailed questionnaires, to examine prenatal diet and other early-life factors in relation to maternal and child health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GERO cohort aims the recruitment of 300 elderly subjects (> 70 years) from Santiago (Chile), following them up for at least 3 years. Eligible people are adults not diagnosed with dementia with subjective cognitive complaint, which are reported either by the participant, a proxy or both.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort recruits the potential participants from the general population, using a door-to-door strategy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fieldwork started in November 2017 and is expected to finish at the middle of 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objective of the GERO cohort is to analyze the rate of functional decline and progression to clinical dementia and their associated risk factors in a community-dwelling elderly with subjective cognitive complaint, through a population-based study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The protocol for evaluation is based on a multidimensional approach including socio-demographic, biomedical, psychosocial, neuropsychological, neuropsychiatric and motor assessments. Neuroimaging, blood and stool samples are also obtained. This multidimensional evaluation is carried out in a baseline and 2 follow-ups assessments, at 18 and 36 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33238908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7690082/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample framework corresponds to the territories assigned to three primary healthcare centers selected by convenience according to their socioeconomic heterogeneity, which belong to three different districts in Santiago (Chile): Macul, Peñalolen and La Reina.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001255> "A population-based cohort of community-dwelling adults aged 70 or over without dementia but with a subjective cognitive complaint. They were recruited door to door from 2017 in three districts of Santiago, Chile (Macul, Peñalolén and La Reina), by the Geroscience Center for Brain Health and Metabolism (GERO), and are followed at 18 and 36 months with clinical, neuropsychological, neuroimaging, blood and stool assessments to study the rate of functional decline and progression to dementia and their risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gaaindata.org/getPartner?project=AGA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6355764/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with AD and without cognitive impairment older than 60 years were recruited from outpatient Neurology Departments of the following hospitals: Instituto de Investigaciones Médicas “Alfredo Lanari” and Hospital de Clínicas (Buenos Aires City), Hospital Interzonal General de Agudos “Eva Perón” (General San Martín county), Hospital El Cruce “Dr.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> "A multisite case-control study of sporadic Alzheimer's disease in Argentina, recruiting since 2013. Older people with Alzheimer's disease and cognitively unimpaired controls are enrolled at outpatient neurology departments of hospitals in the city and province of Buenos Aires and at centres in Jujuy, Córdoba and Mendoza provinces, to identify genes for susceptibility to sporadic Alzheimer's disease and genes that modify its phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gaaindata.org/getPartner?project=AGA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10276158/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AGA-ALZAR samples were recruited in the Buenos Aires, Jujuy, Córdoba, and Mendoza provinces.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> "A multisite case-control study of sporadic Alzheimer's disease in Argentina, recruiting since 2013. Older people with Alzheimer's disease and cognitively unimpaired controls are enrolled at outpatient neurology departments of hospitals in the city and province of Buenos Aires and at centres in Jujuy, Córdoba and Mendoza provinces, to identify genes for susceptibility to sporadic Alzheimer's disease and genes that modify its phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gaaindata.org/getPartner?project=AGA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10917041/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Argentinian samples were recruited in the context of the Alzheimer's Genetics in Argentina–Alzheimer Argentina consortium (AGA‐ALZAR, https://www.gaaindata.org/partner/AGA), from the following centers: Medical Research Institute A.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> "A multisite case-control study of sporadic Alzheimer's disease in Argentina, recruiting since 2013. Older people with Alzheimer's disease and cognitively unimpaired controls are enrolled at outpatient neurology departments of hospitals in the city and province of Buenos Aires and at centres in Jujuy, Córdoba and Mendoza provinces, to identify genes for susceptibility to sporadic Alzheimer's disease and genes that modify its phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gaaindata.org/getPartner?project=AGA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10917041/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lanari (C1427ARO, Buenos Aires), Hospital de Clínicas José de San Martín (C1120AAF, Buenos Aires), Hospital HIGA‐Eva Perón (B1650NBN, General San Martín), Hospital El Cruce (B1888AAE, Florencio Varela), and several geriatric centers across Jujuy and Mendoza provinces, organized and coordinated by their respective Public Ministry of Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> "A multisite case-control study of sporadic Alzheimer's disease in Argentina, recruiting since 2013. Older people with Alzheimer's disease and cognitively unimpaired controls are enrolled at outpatient neurology departments of hospitals in the city and province of Buenos Aires and at centres in Jujuy, Córdoba and Mendoza provinces, to identify genes for susceptibility to sporadic Alzheimer's disease and genes that modify its phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30705288") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37333771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.gaaindata.org/getPartner?project=AGA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37985413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10917041/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed GWAS on sporadic Alzheimer's disease (AD) including 539 patients and 854 controls from Argentina and Chile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001256> "A multisite case-control study of sporadic Alzheimer's disease in Argentina, recruiting since 2013. Older people with Alzheimer's disease and cognitively unimpaired controls are enrolled at outpatient neurology departments of hospitals in the city and province of Buenos Aires and at centres in Jujuy, Córdoba and Mendoza provinces, to identify genes for susceptibility to sporadic Alzheimer's disease and genes that modify its phenotypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3377679/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1031 healthy pregnant women who gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway were included in the study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3377679/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each pregnant woman had four antenatal visits (visit 1–4), scheduled at weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38 of pregnancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3377679/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The STORK study is a prospective cohort study including 1031 healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583865/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In short, the STORK-cohort consists of women of Scandinavian heritage (n = 1031) who registered for obstetric care at Oslo University Hospital - Rikshospitalet from 2001–2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583865/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Oral glucose tolerance test (75 g –2 hour) was undertaken twice, at weeks 14–16 and 30–32.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22723995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23460863") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3583865/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present work was performed in a subcohort (n = 207) of the STORK study, an observational, prospective study on the determinants of fetal growth and birth weight in healthy pregnancies") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001257> "A prospective cohort of healthy pregnant women of Scandinavian heritage with singleton pregnancies who registered for obstetric care and gave birth at Oslo University Hospital, Rikshospitalet, Norway, in 2001–2008, with four antenatal visits (weeks 14–16, 22–24, 30–32 and 36–38), fasting blood sampling, ultrasound at the final three visits and oral glucose tolerance tests at weeks 14–16 and 30–32, to study the determinants of fetal growth and birthweight in healthy pregnancies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3058917/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SALSA participants were the oldest members, aged 65 and older, of the San Antonio Heart Study (SAHS) cohort who were recruited for the SALSA baseline examination conducted from 1992 to 1996.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3058917/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SALSA baseline and follow-up examinations consisted of a comprehensive home-based assessment, conducted in the participant’s home, and a performance-based assessment, conducted at a clinical research center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3058917/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three follow-up exams were conducted between 2000 and 2005, 18 months apart.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3024332/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current study uses longitudinal data from the San Antonio Longitudinal Study of Aging (SALSA), a community-based study of disablement in a biethnic cohort of Mexican Americans and European Americans") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25597562+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Socioeconomically and ethnically diverse neighborhoods in San Antonio, Texas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21054295") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21216857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25597562") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25597562+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were randomly sampled from three types of neighborhoods that varied in ethnic composition and economic environment: barrio (low-income, exclusively MA), transitional (middle-income, equal proportion MAs and European Americans (EAs)) and suburban (upper-income, predominantly EA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001258> "A community-based longitudinal study of the disablement process in older Mexican Americans and European Americans in San Antonio, Texas. Its participants, the oldest members (aged 65 and over) of the San Antonio Heart Study cohort, had been randomly sampled from low-, middle- and high-income (barrio, transitional and suburban) neighbourhoods. They had a baseline examination in 1992–1996, combining a home-based assessment with a performance-based assessment at a clinical research center, and three follow-up examinations 18 months apart in 2000–2005.")

