AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35922517") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35922517") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9352569/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide assessment of the gene variants associated with severe COVID-19 phenotype in Iran | Iran | IranCovid | MID | - | - | 210 | 183 | - | - | Cases 48 years Controls 44.4 years | Digestive Disease Research Institute, Tehran University of Medical Sciences, Tehran, Iran | Yes | Illumina GSA24 | N/A | N/A |  | R6") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001260> "A case-control genetic association study of COVID-19 severity in Iran, based at Shariati Hospital, Tehran University of Medical Sciences. It genotyped people of Middle Eastern ancestry hospitalised with COVID-19, and controls, on the Illumina Global Screening Array, and contributed them to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative's meta-analyses of COVID-19 severity and of long COVID.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35922517") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12165857/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COVID-19 Ioannina Biobank (Ioannina), Genome-wide assessment of the gene variants associated with severe COVID-19 phenotype in Iran (IrCovid), Japan COVID-19 Task Force (JapanTaskForce)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001260> "A case-control genetic association study of COVID-19 severity in Iran, based at Shariati Hospital, Tehran University of Medical Sciences. It genotyped people of Middle Eastern ancestry hospitalised with COVID-19, and controls, on the Illumina Global Screening Array, and contributed them to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative's meta-analyses of COVID-19 severity and of long COVID.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35922517") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40399555") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12165857/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IrCovid | Genome-wide assessment of the gene variants associated with severe COVID-19 phenotype in Iran | Iran | MEA | Initial discovery (Data Freeze 4) | 114 | - | 242 | 242") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001260> "A case-control genetic association study of COVID-19 severity in Iran, based at Shariati Hospital, Tehran University of Medical Sciences. It genotyped people of Middle Eastern ancestry hospitalised with COVID-19, and controls, on the Illumina Global Screening Array, and contributed them to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative's meta-analyses of COVID-19 severity and of long COVID.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC524366/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between October 1997 and October 1999, all YH1 subjects were invited to participate in the third, hospital-based screening phase (YH3), and a 48.2% response rate was achieved.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC524366/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the initial screening (YH1), conducted in 1989/1990, surveyed 1015 adolescents (12-year old boys, n 251;12-year old girls, n 258; 15-year old boys, n 252; and 15-year old girls, n 254) randomly selected from post-primary schools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC524366/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1992/93, a follow up study (YH2) was undertaken, in which subjects from the original 12 year old cohort were reassessed using procedures identical to those used in YH1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC524366/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Young Hearts Project (YH) is an ongoing longitudinal study evaluating the prevalence of CVD risk factors in young people living in Northern Ireland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2958312/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Young Hearts Project 2000 had a total of 2,017 participants from Northern Ireland, consisting of 12- and 15-year-olds from 36 nationally representative schools; the response rate was 65.4%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15462676") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20864003") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2958312/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Young Hearts Project 2000 is a cross-sectional cohort study which took place in 1999–2001 following a previous study, Young Hearts I, described in detail elsewhere [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001261> "A longitudinal study of cardiovascular disease risk factors in young people in Northern Ireland, which screened a random sample of 12- and 15-year-olds from post-primary schools in 1989–1990, re-examined the younger group at age 15 in 1992–1993, and invited the whole sample back for examination as young adults in 1997–1999. A second school sample of 12- and 15-year-olds was surveyed in 1999–2001 as Young Hearts 2000.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22286726+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Longitudinal study of 3 cohorts of older adults from Santiago: the SABE cohort including 1235 people born before 1940; the Alexandros cohort including 950 people born between 1940 and 1948 from Primary Health Care centers and the ISAPRES cohort of 266 people from private health insurance registries (ISAPRES) born before 1947.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> "A longitudinal study of community-dwelling people aged 60 years and older in Santiago, Chile, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity. It follows three cohorts: Santiago participants of the SABE survey, born before 1940 and first recruited in 1999–2000; people born in 1940–1948, recruited from public primary health care centre registries in 2005–2008; and people of high socioeconomic status selected from private health insurance registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9319397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(b) 950 people born between 1940–1948 recruited between 2005 and 2008, randomly selected from 28 Public Primary healthcare center registries and (c) 266 people of high socio-economic status, born before 1949, randomly selected from the private health insurance system registries and recruited in 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> "A longitudinal study of community-dwelling people aged 60 years and older in Santiago, Chile, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity. It follows three cohorts: Santiago participants of the SABE survey, born before 1940 and first recruited in 1999–2000; people born in 1940–1948, recruited from public primary health care centre registries in 2005–2008; and people of high socioeconomic status selected from private health insurance registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9319397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly Alexandros is a longitudinal study of people ≥ 60 years that includes three cohorts of different demographic origin and socioeconomic status: (a) 1173 Subjects born before 1940 recruited in the frame of The SABE study [29] (in 1999–2000 through a probabilistic sampling),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> "A longitudinal study of community-dwelling people aged 60 years and older in Santiago, Chile, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity. It follows three cohorts: Santiago participants of the SABE survey, born before 1940 and first recruited in 1999–2000; people born in 1940–1948, recruited from public primary health care centre registries in 2005–2008; and people of high socioeconomic status selected from private health insurance registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9319397/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up study done in the context of Alexandros (Active Life Expectancy, Aging and Disorders Related to Obesity Study) after a mean follow up of 9078 person/years (mean 9.59 ± 3.5, min 5.0 max 15.0), a cohort study of community-dwelling people 60 years and older living in Santiago, Chile, previously described [28].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> "A longitudinal study of community-dwelling people aged 60 years and older in Santiago, Chile, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity. It follows three cohorts: Santiago participants of the SABE survey, born before 1940 and first recruited in 1999–2000; people born in 1940–1948, recruited from public primary health care centre registries in 2005–2008; and people of high socioeconomic status selected from private health insurance registries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35887574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36013179") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9410389/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ALEXANDROS cohort, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity in community dwelling people 60y and older, has already been described [66].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001262> "A longitudinal study of community-dwelling people aged 60 years and older in Santiago, Chile, designed to study disability and dementia associated with obesity. It follows three cohorts: Santiago participants of the SABE survey, born before 1940 and first recruited in 1999–2000; people born in 1940–1948, recruited from public primary health care centre registries in 2005–2008; and people of high socioeconomic status selected from private health insurance registries.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6865235/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADAGES indicates African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study; AGGP, African Glaucoma Genetics Project; GWAS, genome-wide association study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6865235/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Abbreviations: ADAGES, African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study; GERA, Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging; GWAS, genome-wide association study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6865235/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First Validation Women’s Health Initiative 23.1 20.8 1720 6067 Kaiser Permanente GERA 23.3 18.4 300 2700 ADAGES 24.3 21.4 1890 2205 South Africa 13.0 14.4 297 147 Tanzania 30.1 28.3 366 329") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6865235/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the GWAS discovery stage, study participants of African ancestry were recruited from Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, and Duke University (Durham, NC), where the same phenotype definition was applied to diagnose primary open-angle glaucoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31688885+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were recruited from Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru, and Mali from 2003 to 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31688885+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The validation stage included an additional 6937 affected individuals and 14 917 unaffected individuals using multicenter clinic- and population-based participant recruitment approaches.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31688885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31688885+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To perform a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of African ancestry populations and evaluate potential mechanisms of pathogenesis for loci associated with primary open-angle glaucoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001263> "A multicentre research consortium formed to carry out genome-wide association studies of primary open-angle glaucoma in people of African ancestry, which brought together case-control collections recruited in 2003–2018 through clinics and population-based studies in Ghana, Nigeria, South Africa, the United States, Tanzania, Britain, Cameroon, Saudi Arabia, Brazil, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Morocco, Peru and Mali. Besides its own site collections, it included participants of African ancestry from existing studies such as the Women's Health Initiative, the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging cohort and the African Descent and Glaucoma Evaluation Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3596061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Collaboration on Ovarian Neoplasms 7 (ICON7) trial is a Gynecologic Cancer Intergroup phase 3 trial that assessed the effects of adding bevacizumab, concurrently and as a continuation, to standard chemotherapy with carboplatin and paclitaxel in patients with primary peritoneal carcinoma, fallopian tube carcinoma, and epithelial ovarian carcinoma (ovarian cancer).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> "An international, open-label, randomised phase 3 trial of the Gynecologic Cancer InterGroup, led by the UK Medical Research Council, in which women with newly diagnosed high-risk early-stage or advanced epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer were recruited in 2006–2009 at centres in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand and randomised to carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy with or without concurrent and maintenance bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4648090/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between Dec 18, 2006, and Feb 16, 2009, seven GCIG groups recruited 1528 women with ovarian cancer from 263 centres across Europe, Canada, Australia, and New Zealand; these women were enrolled and randomly assigned to receive standard carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy (n=764) or standard chemotherapy plus bevacizumab (n=764; figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> "An international, open-label, randomised phase 3 trial of the Gynecologic Cancer InterGroup, led by the UK Medical Research Council, in which women with newly diagnosed high-risk early-stage or advanced epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer were recruited in 2006–2009 at centres in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand and randomised to carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy with or without concurrent and maintenance bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4648090/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible patients were aged 18 years or older; with newly diagnosed epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube, or primary peritoneal cancer; an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0–2; FIGO 1988 stage IIb–IV or high-risk (grade 3 or clear cell histology) stage I–IIa disease;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> "An international, open-label, randomised phase 3 trial of the Gynecologic Cancer InterGroup, led by the UK Medical Research Council, in which women with newly diagnosed high-risk early-stage or advanced epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer were recruited in 2006–2009 at centres in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand and randomised to carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy with or without concurrent and maintenance bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4648090/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ICON7 was an international, phase 3, open-label, randomised trial undertaken at 263 centres in 11 countries across Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> "An international, open-label, randomised phase 3 trial of the Gynecologic Cancer InterGroup, led by the UK Medical Research Council, in which women with newly diagnosed high-risk early-stage or advanced epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer were recruited in 2006–2009 at centres in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand and randomised to carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy with or without concurrent and maintenance bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23333117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26115797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4648090/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Randomisation was done centrally by a computer system based at the Medical Research Council Clinical Trials Unit (London, UK) accessed via the web or telephone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001264> "An international, open-label, randomised phase 3 trial of the Gynecologic Cancer InterGroup, led by the UK Medical Research Council, in which women with newly diagnosed high-risk early-stage or advanced epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer were recruited in 2006–2009 at centres in Europe, Canada, Australia and New Zealand and randomised to carboplatin and paclitaxel chemotherapy with or without concurrent and maintenance bevacizumab.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/cjn.2021.40") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects were recruited from 10 specialty Movement Disorders Centers/Neurology clinics across India over a 2-year period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/cjn.2021.40") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This report is part of a multicenter study titled “Genetics Of Pan-Indian Young Onset Parkinson’s Disease (GOPI-YOPD)” conducted under the aegis of the Parkinson Research Alliance of India (PRAI) and MedGenome Labs Pvt Ltd.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33685545+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients under follow-up of movement disorders specialists and meeting United Kingdom (UK) Brain Bank criteria for PD were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33685545+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a 2-year, pan-India, multicenter collaborative study to analyze clinical patterns of JP, YOPD, and EOPD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GOPI-YOPD is a prospective multicenter, collaborative study to analyze clinical and genetic patterns of JOPD, YOPD, and EOPD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33685545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/06/22/2023.06.18.23291407.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mdsabstracts.org/abstract/genetics-of-parkinsons-in-india-young-onset-parkinsons-disease-gopi-yopd-genetics-of-juvenile-young-and-early-onset-parkinsons-disease/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To determine the genetic and demographic patterns of juvenile-onset (JOPD, <20 years), young-onset (YOPD, 20-40 years), and early onset (EOPD, 40-50 years) Parkinson’s disease (PD) in India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001265> "A prospective, pan-India, multicentre study of people with juvenile-, young- and early-onset Parkinson's disease (onset by about 50 years of age), started by the Parkinson Research Alliance of India, which over two years recruited patients under the care of movement disorder specialists at ten specialty movement disorder centres and neurology clinics across India, to study the clinical and genetic patterns of early-onset Parkinson's disease in India.")

