AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34597274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35052684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9585783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were offered to participate in a follow-up study three to six months after discharge from ICU with questionnaires and a personal visit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001266> "A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34597274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35052684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9585783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery set was taken from the Pronmed cohort that consists of 374 critically ill COVID-19 patients admitted to the intensive care unit (ICU) at Uppsala University Hospital, in Uppsala, Sweden between March 13, 2020 and June 30, 2021 (Fig. 2A).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001266> "A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34597274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35052684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9585783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study was based on a discovery analysis of the prospective observational cohort Pronmed with critically ill COVID-19 patients from the ICU at Uppsala University Hospital (A).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001266> "A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.")
