AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34597274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35052684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study SweCovid, received funding from the National SciLifeLab-KAW COVID-19 Research Program in both 2020 and 2021 to investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001266> "A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34597274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35052684") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.scilifelab.se/news/uppsala-researchers-contributes-to-the-global-covid-19-host-genetics-initiative/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is a collaboration between researchers at Uppsala University and The Karolinska Institute, and today results from this study are included in findings presented in the Nature publication Mapping the human genetic architecture of COVID-19 by worldwide meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001266> "A study of patients with critical COVID-19 admitted from March 2020 to the intensive care unit of Uppsala University Hospital, Sweden, who were enrolled in the prospective observational PronMed cohort and invited to follow-up three to six months after discharge, in which researchers at Uppsala University and Karolinska Institutet investigate the mechanisms of acute and long-term organ dysfunction in critical COVID-19, including its host genetics.")

