AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29884306+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of the Placental Abruption Genetic Epidemiology (PAGE) study, a population based case-control study of PA conducted in Lima, Peru, were genotyped using the Illumina HumanCore-24 BeadChip platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5995331/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PAGE study participants were recruited among women who were admitted for obstetrical services to antepartum wards, emergency room, and labor and delivery wards of participating hospitals between March 2013 and December 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30194050") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6497388/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were selected randomly from eligible pregnant women who delivered at the same participating hospitals as the AP cases during the study period and who did not have a diagnosis of AP in the current pregnancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30194050") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6497388/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participating hospitals were Instituto Nacional Materno Perinatal, Hospital Edgardo Rebagliati Martins, Hospital San Bartolome, Hospital Hipolito Unanue, Hospital Arzobispo Loayza, Hospital Dos de Mayo, and Hospital Maria Auxiliadora.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study included data from the PAGE study which were 292 2,212 women, 933 of whom were PTB cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29884306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2023/11/22/2023.11.22.23298891.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted among participants of the Placental Abruption Genetic Epidemiology 449 study (PAGE), a case-control study from Lima, Peru, designed to investigate the genetic and 450 environmental determinants of placenta abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes like 451 preterm birth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001268> "A population-based case-control study of women admitted for obstetric care at seven hospitals in Lima, Peru, between March 2013 and December 2015, with cases of placental abruption and of preterm birth and controls selected at random from women delivering at the same hospitals, designed to investigate the genetic and environmental determinants of placental abruption and other adverse pregnancy outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21062840+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based cohort study of pregnant women attending the Child Health Clinics (CHC) in Groruddalen, Oslo, and their offspring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21062840+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Questionnaire data, blood pressure, anthropometric measurements, and fasting blood and urine samples are collected (gestational weeks 8-20 and 28, and 12 weeks postpartum) and an oral glucose tolerance test (28 weeks).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21062840+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The STORK Groruddalen research programme: A population-based cohort study of gestational diabetes, physical activity, and obesity in pregnancy in a multiethnic population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21062840+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have set up a research programme to identify predictors for GDM and fetal growth in a multiethnic population in Oslo to improve the identification of high risk pregnancies and reduce adverse short and long-term outcomes for mothers and offspring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8362992/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPIPREG (n = 480) is a sub-study of the larger STORK Groruddalen (STORK G) study, which is a population-based cohort of 823 healthy women with different ethnic origin (European, South Asian, African, Middle Eastern and South American) attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in the multi-ethnic area of Groruddalen, Oslo, Norway, 2008–2010 [30].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21062840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22108914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34388220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8362992/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measurements of weight and length/height were collected during routine follow-up at the Mother—and Child Health Clinics when the children were 6 weeks old and thereafter at the 3, 6, 12, 15, 24 and 48 months visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001269> "A population-based cohort of pregnant women of diverse ethnic origin attending three public Child Health Clinics for antenatal care in Groruddalen, a multi-ethnic area of Oslo, Norway, recruited in 2008–2010 and followed with their offspring through pregnancy and after birth, to study gestational diabetes, physical activity and obesity in pregnancy and to identify predictors of gestational diabetes and fetal growth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-020-1004-3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this Correspondence, we provide an account of a 49-day period during which we built a COVID-19 research biobank with samples from patients hospitalized in a large New York City health system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41591-020-1004-3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our mandate was to design a sample-collection protocol to serve as the backbone for COVID-19 research by yielding high-quality source material for sensitive molecular assays (e.g., RNA sequencing and CyTOF) that cannot be performed on clinical discards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood collection was performed in conjunction with routine clinical blood draws throughout participants’ hospital stays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, 567 individuals (495 hospitalized with COVID-19 and 72 healthy and hospitalized controls) were enrolled in the Mount Sinai COVID-19 Biobank Study between April and June 2020 (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients presenting to the Mount Sinai Health System between April and June 2020 were enrolled through daily manual review of new hospitalizations for COVID-19.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719485") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36482101") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9873574/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Six months or more after discharge from COVID-19 hospitalization (median = 363 days), 232 individuals (165 with RNA-seq) completed a self-reported checklist assessing for the emergence of PASC (Table 1, Supplementary Table 1a,b and Fig. 2a,b; checklist items referred to as symptoms).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001270> "A research biobank of patients hospitalised with COVID-19 in the Mount Sinai Health System in New York City, enrolled from April to June 2020 through daily review of new admissions together with a smaller group of healthy and hospitalised controls, whose blood was sampled repeatedly alongside routine clinical draws during their hospital stay for multi-omic study of the host response to SARS-CoV-2, and whose survivors were later surveyed for post-acute sequelae of COVID-19.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10412782+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Die Deutsche Diabetes Dialyse Studie is a prospective randomized placebo-controlled trial that tests the hypothesis that atorvastatin, a hydroxymethyl-glutaryl coenzyme A reductase inhibitor, decreases the rate of cardiovascular mortality and of nonfatal myocardial infarction in patients with type 2 diabetes who have been on hemodialysis treatment for no more than two years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10539202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 4D Study started in 1998") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10539202/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 4D Study was a multicentre, randomized, double-blind, prospective study enrolling 1255 participants with T2DM receiving maintenance HD at 178 centres who were randomly assigned to receive 20 mg of atorvastatin or matching placebo daily.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37779851+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During a median follow-up of 4 years, a total of 548 MACEs occurred, with 469 first and 79 recurrent events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10627490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, aged 18–80 years, who had received maintenance hemodialysis for less than 2 years were included by 178 dialysis centers in Germany into the 4 D study (Die Deutsche Diabetes Dialyse Studie/German Diabetes and Dialysis Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10412782") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37779851") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37806305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10627490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary endpoint included the following events: death from cardiac causes, nonfatal myocardial infarction, fatal stroke, or nonfatal stroke, whichever occurred first.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001271> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, begun in 1998 at dialysis centres throughout Germany, of adults aged 18–80 with type 2 diabetes who had been on maintenance haemodialysis for less than two years, which tested whether atorvastatin lowers the risk of cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke, and followed its participants for a median of four years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19752422+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective, multicenter observational cohort study of 1221 participants of African descent and European descent with no glaucoma (normal), suspected glaucoma, and glaucoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2761830/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment began January 2003 and ended July 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2761830/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3-site collaboration includes the Hamilton Glaucoma Center at the Department of Ophthalmology, University of California, San Diego (UCSD) (data coordinating center), the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary, and the Department of Ophthalmology, University of Alabama, Birmingham (UAB).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2761830/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall aim of the study is to identify clinical factors that explain the differences in glaucoma onset and rate of progression found between individuals of African descent and those of European descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29361356+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three thousand two hundred sixty-six glaucoma patients and control participants without glaucoma of African or European descent were recruited from 5 study centers in different regions of the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19752422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30352225") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29361356") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6050158/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall goal of ADAGES III is to identify the genetic factors associated with primary open angle glaucoma (POAG) in individuals of African descent (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001272> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort study, which from 2003 enrolled people of African descent and of European descent without glaucoma, with suspected glaucoma or with glaucoma at the University of California San Diego, the New York Eye and Ear Infirmary and the University of Alabama at Birmingham, United States, and followed them with repeated visual function testing and optic nerve imaging to identify why glaucoma onset and progression differ between people of African and European descent. Its third phase (ADAGES III) recruited, in 2014–2016 at five US centres, patients with primary open-angle glaucoma and controls of African or European descent, with DNA, to study the genetics of the disease in people of African descent.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Archived newborn dried blood spots (DBS) with matching birth certificate information held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health were obtained for cases and calendar birth year-, sex-, and race/ethnicity-matched (based on mother’s race/ethnicity) controls with no cancer history were obtained as a part of a larger population-based case-control study with linked cancer registry information through the Michigan Cancer Surveillance Program56.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baylor College of Medicine additionally provided biobanked saliva-based DNA specimens from race/ethnicity-matched controls completing well-child or sports physical visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children with a pathologically-verified diagnosis of B-ALL (ICD-O-3 histology 9811-9818, 9820, 9823, 9826, 9827, 9831-9837, 9940, 9948) at 0-25 years of age who identified as Black or African American from the ADMIRAL study were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Germline DNA samples were obtained from either: (a) COG frontline ALL protocols; (b) the Michigan BioTrust for Health; or (c) multiple institutional academic hospital ALL biobanks (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12546916/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we show differences in the genetic architecture of childhood B-ALL risk in African ancestral populations with an analysis of 4200 African American children, including 840 B-ALL cases, as a part of the ADMIxture and Risk of Acute Leukemia (ADMIRAL) Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41125582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-64337-7") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These novel risk variants were associated with specific B-ALL biological subtypes and overall survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001273> "A case-control study of B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia in Black or African American children and young adults diagnosed at ages 0–25 in the United States, run from the University of Minnesota, which gathered germline DNA of cases from Children's Oncology Group frontline trials, from newborn dried blood spots held by the Michigan BioTrust for Health and linked to the state cancer registry, and from hospital leukaemia biobanks, with controls matched on sex and ancestry from Michigan newborn blood spots and paediatric well-child visits. It investigates African ancestry-specific genetic susceptibility to B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia and its relation to disease subtype and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15899951+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This observational study included participants in the Amish Family Osteoporosis Study, begun in 1997 to identify genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis in the OOA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16939402+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BMD was measured at the spine, hip, and radius using DXA in 964 participants (mean age, 50.2 +/- 16.3 [SD] years; range, 18-99 years) from large multigenerational families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16939402+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Amish Family Osteoporosis Study was designed to identify genes affecting bone health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3390364/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Amish Family Osteoporosis Study (AFOS) study was designed to identify genetic determinants of osteoporosis in the Old Order Amish (OOA) population from Lancaster County, PA USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5940677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After the identification of individuals with osteoporosis by BMD, family members were recruited including first-degree relatives aged 20 years and older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15899951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16939402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29739999") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5940677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Spouses were also invited to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001274> "A family study of the Old Order Amish of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, United States, begun by the University of Maryland in 1997, which identified Amish adults with osteoporosis by bone mineral density screening and recruited their first-degree relatives aged 20 and over and their spouses, measuring bone density by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, to find genetic and clinical determinants of osteoporosis and bone health in large multigenerational families.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21572416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3158568/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network (AGEN) is a consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of cardiovascular disease related phenotypes, such as BP (or hypertension), diabetes, and obesity, conducted among Asian populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21572416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3158568/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network BP (AGEN-BP) work group was established to facilitate the identification of genetic variants influencing BP among populations of East Asian ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22797727+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we report a meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies for kidney function-related traits, including 71,149 east Asian individuals from 18 studies in 11 population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts, conducted as part of the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network (AGEN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we sought to find common genetic variants at novel loci that are associated with blood HbA1c level in the consortium of the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network (AGEN; http://www.agenconsortium.org/), which consists of East Asian cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7292783/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a fixed-effect inverse-variance weighted GWAS meta-analysis combining 23 studies imputed to the 1000 Genomes Phase 3 reference panel from the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network (AGEN) consortium (Supplementary Tables 1–3).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22797727") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23105927") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499647") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37859345") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37859345+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a cross-ancestry adiponectin GWAS meta-analysis in ≤46,434 individuals from the Metabolic Syndrome in Men (METSIM) cohort and the ADIPOGen and AGEN consortiums.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001275> "A consortium of genetic epidemiology studies of type 2 diabetes and related traits in people of East Asian ancestry, mostly population-, hospital- or family-based cohorts in East and South-East Asia, which meta-analyses its member studies' genome-wide association results in trait-specific groups (such as AGEN-T2D and AGEN-BP) for type 2 diabetes, glycaemic traits, adiposity, adiponectin, blood pressure and kidney function.")

