AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940340/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nine samples containing AD phenotypes from seven independent studies participating in the Anxiety NeuroGenetics STudy (ANGST) Consortium were included in the meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278> "A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940340/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We applied two phenotypic strategies aimed at capturing common (pleiotropic) genetic effects shared across the five core ADs: GAD, PD, social phobia, agoraphobia, and specific phobias.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278> "A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26754954+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify genetic variants contributing to genetic susceptibility shared across interview-generated DSM-based ADs") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278> "A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26754954") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26754954+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted genome-wide association analyses in nine samples of European ancestry from seven large, independent studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001278> "A consortium of seven independent studies of people of European ancestry in the United States, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Germany and Australia (the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia control sample, PsyCoLaus, the Rotterdam Study, the Study of Health in Pomerania, the QIMR twin sample, TRAILS and NESDA/NTR), with interview-based DSM diagnoses of anxiety disorders, formed to meta-analyse genome-wide association studies of generalized anxiety disorder, panic disorder, social phobia, agoraphobia and specific phobia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were of self-reported white European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery sample population included 1128 Australian, 74 New Zealand and 753 British women, between 55–85 years of age, five or more years postmenopausal") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080863/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report here a GWAS using a novel study design focusing on women of a specific age (postmenopausal women, age 55–85 years), with either extreme high or low hip BMD (age- and gender-adjusted BMD z-scores of +1.5 to +4.0, n = 1055, or −4.0 to −1.5, n = 900), with replication in cohorts of women drawn from the general population (n = 20,898).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21533022+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide association study using extreme truncate selection identifies novel genes affecting bone mineral density and fracture risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2249/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2249_MOESM26_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A consortium of investigators who have collected unrelated individuals with extreme BMD phenotypes (z scores +1.5 to +4; or ‐1.5 to ‐4) as a powerful strategy for gene discovery in quantitative traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2249/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2249_MOESM26_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AOGC Anglo‐Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium Extreme truncate selection Population‐based, clinical‐based Australia, New Zealand, United Kingdom") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001279> "A sample of postmenopausal women aged 55–85 of white European ancestry with extreme high or extreme low hip bone mineral density, recruited from population-based and clinical sources at centres in Australia, New Zealand and the United Kingdom by the Anglo-Australasian Osteoporosis Genetics Consortium and genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of bone mineral density and fracture that used extreme truncate selection.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6116430/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This investigator-led study is funded by the NIHR EME programme (NIHR EME 13/50/17 APRICOT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9255857/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrolment into APRICOT (Anakinra for Pustular Psoriasis: Response in a Controlled Trial) was conducted across 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9255857/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, eligible participants were aged ≥ 18 years with a diagnosis of PPP with disease of a sufficient severity to require systemic therapy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34411292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was a randomized (1 : 1), double-blind, two-staged, adaptive, UK multicentre, placebo-controlled trial") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34411292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To determine whether anakinra (an IL-1 receptor antagonist) delivers therapeutic benefit in PPP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30157880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34411292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34411292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Treatment was 8 weeks of anakinra or placebo via daily, self-administered subcutaneous injections.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001280> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled, two-stage adaptive trial, funded by the NIHR Efficacy and Mechanism Evaluation programme, that enrolled adults with palmoplantar pustulosis severe enough to need systemic therapy at 16 sites in England, Scotland and Wales between October 2016 and January 2020, to test whether 8 weeks of the interleukin-1 receptor antagonist anakinra reduces disease severity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28716989") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28716989+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the prospective ARCADIA registry (Assessment of Renal and Cervical Artery Dysplasia), symptomatic patients with renal artery (RA) FMD underwent tomographic- or magnetic resonance-angiography from the aortic arch to the intracranial arteries and those with cervical FMD from the diaphragm to the pelvis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8483547/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, included patients were women or men aged ≥18 years diagnosed with renal, cervical, or intracranial artery FMD, who were prospectively recruited at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium from 2009 to 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8483547/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All imaging studies from patients diagnosed locally with multisite FMD were centrally reviewed by a core imaging committee to confirm multisite status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FMD patients were included from the ARCADIA (Assessment of Renal and Cervical Artery DysplasIA) register, a national FMD registry at the Georges Pompidou European Hospital, APHP, Paris8.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ARCADIA study was sponsored by the Assistance Publique-Hôpitaux de Paris") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02884141") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The meta-analysis included participants of European ancestry from six studies: ARCADIA8/3C51 GWAS, Mayo Vascular Disease Biorepository52, DEFINE-FMD study16, ARCADIA-POL53/WOBASZ II54 study, University of Michigan/Cleveland Clinic Foundation (UM/CCF) study31,55 and FEIRI7/ASKLEPIOS56 study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001281> "A prospective national registry, sponsored by Assistance Publique–Hôpitaux de Paris and coordinated at the Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou in Paris, of adults with renal, cervical or intracranial artery fibromuscular dysplasia recruited from 2009 to 2014 at 16 university hospitals in France and Belgium, with standardised clinical and imaging data and leukocyte DNA collected to study multisite disease and to search for susceptibility genes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35069183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8769168/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of 19,342 hypertensive patients (40–79 years of age with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors) who were randomized to one of two antihypertensive regimens in ASCOT, 10,305 with non-fasting TC concentrations of 6.5 mmol/l or less (measured at the non-fasting screening visit) had been randomly assigned additional atorvastatin 10 mg or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10984564/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prevention of cardiovascular events with an antihypertensive regimen of amlodipine adding perindopril as required versus atenolol adding bendroflumethiazide as required, in the Anglo-Scandinavian Cardiac Outcomes Trial-Blood Pressure Lowering Arm (ASCOT-BPLA): a multicentre randomised controlled trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10984564/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Nordic countries, participants were recruited from 686 family practices and in the UK and Ireland, most participants were referred from family practices to the regional centres for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10984564/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were originally recruited between February 1998 and May 2000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12322408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ASCOT was a prospective randomised controlled trial of two different blood pressure-lowering strategies in 19 342 hypertensive subjects with three additional risk factors for CV disease—ASCOT Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm (BPLA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38291599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40139683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12322408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a factorial design, a subgroup of participants (n=10 305) with total cholesterol <6.5 mmol/L were re-randomised in a double-blind manner to receive either atorvastatin 10 mg or placebo—referred to as the lipid-lowering arm (LLA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001282> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial that recruited hypertensive men and women aged 40–79 with at least three other cardiovascular risk factors, mostly through family practices in the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordic countries between February 1998 and May 2000, to compare an amlodipine-based with an atenolol-based antihypertensive regimen for preventing coronary and other cardiovascular events (the Blood Pressure-Lowering Arm), those with total cholesterol of 6.5 mmol/L or less being also randomised to atorvastatin or placebo in a factorial Lipid-Lowering Arm.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All controls underwent the same evaluation as cases, which included a medical history, Unified Parkinson's Disease Rating Scale (UPDRS) and Mini Mental State Exam (MMSE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> "A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson's disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson's Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, for the PD EPI and AJ study, PD cases were recruited from the Center for PD and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> "A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson's disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson's Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, we used our AJ case-control population as a discovery dataset") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> "A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson's disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson's Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AJ GWAS dataset was created by combining participants from two studies the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> "A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson's disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson's Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21812969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3166909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we applied a GWAS approach to a relatively homogeneous Ashkenazi Jewish (AJ) population living in the New York area to search for both 'rare' and 'common' genetic variants that confer risk of PD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001283> "A case-control sample of people of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry from the New York area, with Parkinson's disease cases recruited at the Center for Parkinson's Disease and Other Movement Disorders at Columbia University and controls evaluated in the same way, assembled from two Columbia University studies, the Genetic Epidemiology of PD study (PD EPI) and the AJ Study, for a genome-wide association study of Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2944247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Supported by research grants U01-DK082223, U01-DK082185, U01DK082192 and U01DK082183 from the National Institute of Digestive, Diabetes and Kidney Diseases of the National Institutes of Health") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2944247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "three Clinical Research Center networks through Kaiser Permanente Northern California (Oakland, CA; San Francisco, CA; Walnut Creek, CA), Vanderbilt University (Nashville, TN), and the Translational Research Investigating Biomarker Endpoints in Acute Kidney Injury (TRIBE-AKI) network (New Haven, CT; Cincinnati, OH; London, Ontario; Montreal, Quebec).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20799966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Assessment, Serial Evaluation, and Subsequent Sequelae of Acute Kidney Injury (ASSESS-AKI) Study was established to examine how a hospitalized episode of AKI independently affects the risk of chronic kidney disease development and progression, cardiovascular events, death, and other important patient-centered outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20799966+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This prospective study will enroll a cohort of 1100 adult participants with a broad range of AKI and matched hospitalized participants without AKI at three Clinical Research Centers, as well as 100 children undergoing cardiac surgery at three Clinical Research Centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32707221+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "adults from four clinical centers surviving three months and more after hospitalization with or without AKI who were matched on center, pre-admission CKD status, and an integrated priority score based on age, prior cardiovascular disease or diabetes mellitus, preadmission estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) and treatment in the intensive care unit during the index hospitalization between December 2009-February 2015") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20799966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32707221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32707221+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "between December 2009-February 2015, with follow-up through November 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001284> "A prospective, matched cohort study, funded by the US National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, that enrolled hospitalised adults with and without acute kidney injury (AKI), matched on clinical research centre, pre-admission chronic kidney disease and other risk factors, at centres in the United States and Canada between December 2009 and February 2015, together with children undergoing cardiac surgery, and followed them after discharge to examine how an episode of AKI affects the development and progression of chronic kidney disease, cardiovascular events and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4617905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AugUR is specifically designed as a research platform to host studies of late onset diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4617905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the baseline survey, we obtain a random sample from the local registries of residence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4617905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we set out to establish a study platform using population-based recruitment of mobile elderly individuals in and around the east Bavarian city of Regensburg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10511022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AugUR is designed as a population-based cohort study with the follow-up ongoing until 2025.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10511022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AugUR recruitment was conducted in two independent baseline surveys (AugUR1, 2013-2015 and AugUR2, 2017-2019).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26489512") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37721739") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10511022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, inhabitants of the city and county of Regensburg, Germany, with ≥ 70 years of age, were identified by local registries and invited by a mailed written invitation letter to the study center at the University Hospital Regensburg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001285> "A population-based cohort of mobile people aged 70 and over from the city and county of Regensburg in eastern Bavaria, Germany, invited from random samples of the local residents' registries and examined at the University Hospital Regensburg in two baseline surveys (2013–2015 and 2017–2019), with interviews, medical and eye examinations, biobanking and genotyping and later follow-up, set up by the University of Regensburg as a research platform for late-onset chronic diseases and their genetic and non-genetic causes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522641/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All measures were performed with individuals wearing light clothing and no shoes in the baseline and repeated in the participants who survived in 2000 and 2002 [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522641/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline data collection was performed from February to May 1997, comprising standardized interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements, and electrocardiograms (ECGs).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522641/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the baseline cohort population comprised 1,606 (92.2%) of all the 1,742 residents aged 60 years or more on January 1st, 1997, who were identified by means of a complete census carried out in the city.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522641/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Deaths reported by next of kin during the annual follow-up interview were ascertained through the Brazilian mortality information system (Sistema de Informações sobre Mortalidade) with the permission of the Ministry of Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522641/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted in the Bambuí City (approximately 15,000 inhabitants), located in the state of Minas Gerais in the southeast region of Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23251690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were 1,450 (90.2% from total) individuals aged 60 years and over from the community-based Bambuí (Brazil) Cohort Study of Ageing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33633342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.maelstrom-research.org/study/bcsa") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objective of the Bambuí (Brazil) Cohort Study of Ageing is to examine the separate and joint effects of chronic Trypanosoma cruzi infection and non-communicable diseases on health outcomes in old age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001286> "A population-based cohort of the residents aged 60 and over of the town of Bambuí, in Minas Gerais, south-eastern Brazil, identified by a complete census on 1 January 1997 and examined at baseline in February–May 1997 with interviews, blood tests, blood pressure measurements and electrocardiograms, then followed with annual interviews, repeated examinations and death ascertainment to study health and mortality in older adults.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6830667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BASIC is a population-based, prospective cohort study at the Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology at Uppsala University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6830667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between September 2009 and November 2018, women during 31 687 pregnancies have been invited to the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6830667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to internet-based surveys with self-report instruments, participants contribute with biological samples, for example, blood samples (maternal and from umbilical cord), biopsies (umbilical cord and placenta) and microbiota samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6830667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the county of Uppsala, all pregnant women are referred to Uppsala University Hospital for a routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18, and 97% of women choose to attend.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6830667/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are followed-up at multiple points from baseline at gestational week 16–18 through 1-year postpartum (figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31641004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31641004+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With the population-based, prospective Biology, Affect, Stress, Imaging and Cognition (BASIC) cohort, we aim to investigate the biopsychosocial aetiological processes involved in perinatal depression (PND) and to pinpoint its predictors in order to improve early detection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001287> "A population-based prospective cohort of pregnant women in Uppsala County, Sweden, invited at their routine ultrasound examination at gestational week 16–18 at Uppsala University Hospital from September 2009 to November 2018 and followed to one year postpartum with web surveys, biological samples and medical-record data, to study the biopsychosocial causes and predictors of perinatal depression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001288> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001288>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3324445") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency-matched to cases by race and age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001288> "A case-control study of breast cancer in the greater Baltimore area, Maryland, United States, in which incident breast cancer cases and controls frequency-matched to them on race and age were recruited from February 1993 to August 2003 at six hospitals, including the University of Maryland Medical Center and the Baltimore Veterans Affairs Medical Center, to identify and characterise markers of disease aggressiveness and poor outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3324445") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident breast cancer cases and controls were recruited between February of 1993 and August of 2003 in six hospitals in the greater Baltimore area, including the University of Maryland Medical Center, the Baltimore Veterans Affairs Medical Center, Union Memorial Hospital, Mercy Medical Center and the Sinai Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001288> "A case-control study of breast cancer in the greater Baltimore area, Maryland, United States, in which incident breast cancer cases and controls frequency-matched to them on race and age were recruited from February 1993 to August 2003 at six hospitals, including the University of Maryland Medical Center and the Baltimore Veterans Affairs Medical Center, to identify and characterise markers of disease aggressiveness and poor outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3324445") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Baltimore Breast Cancer Study is a case–control study of breast cancer designed to identify and characterize markers of disease aggressiveness and poor outcome (29).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001288> "A case-control study of breast cancer in the greater Baltimore area, Maryland, United States, in which incident breast cancer cases and controls frequency-matched to them on race and age were recruited from February 1993 to August 2003 at six hospitals, including the University of Maryland Medical Center and the Baltimore Veterans Affairs Medical Center, to identify and characterise markers of disease aggressiveness and poor outcome.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4402933/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, a private census identified 5924 persons living in the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin aged 43–86 years, of which 4926 participated in the baseline examination in 1988–1990 and in up to four follow-up examinations in 1993–1995, 1998–2000, 2003–2005 and 2008–2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29242907+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SIF was measured with the SCOUT DS skin fluorescence spectrometer in a cross-sectional cohort study of 969 persons aged 68 to 102 years from the 1181 who participated in the 25-year follow-up examination in the Beaver Dam Eye Study (BDES) in 2014 to 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6133235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, a private census was conducted in the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, beginning in 1987.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6133235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The census identified 5924 residents between the ages of 43 and 84 from 3715 households.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8344102/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of the BDES was to collect information on the prevalence, incidence, and potential causes or risk factors associated with AMD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25905023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29242907") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30208419") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32200810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8344102/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "initiate this population-based study that included comprehensive eye examinations and centrally graded fundus photographs") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001289> "A population-based cohort of the residents of the city and township of Beaver Dam, Wisconsin, United States, aged 43 to 84 years at a private census begun in 1987. They were examined at baseline in 1988–1990 and re-examined about every five years (up to a 25-year follow-up in 2014–2016) by the University of Wisconsin-Madison, to study the prevalence, incidence and risk factors of age-related eye diseases, such as age-related macular degeneration and cataract, and of visual impairment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3165130/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical studies using the newest technologies have been initiated, including the BioImage Study in which novel approaches are tested in a typical health plan population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3165130/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BioImage Study (NCT00738725) is a prospective, observational study designed to evaluate associations among imaging and circulating biomarkers (cross-sectional) and their ability to predict atherothrombotic events (longitudinal) in asymptomatic at-risk subjects in the primary prevention of myocardial infarction and stroke [33].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3165130/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the BioImage Study is to identify imaging biomarkers that predict near-term (3-year) atherothrombotic events, with incremental improvement over traditional risk assessment (Framingham Risk Score).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3165130/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To ensure a diverse study population, enrollment occurred in two cities: Chicago, IL and Fort Lauderdale, FL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9558840/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BioImage study (NCT00738725) is a multi-ethnic, observational study aimed at characterizing subclinical atherosclerosis in 6,699 US adults (55-80 years at baseline, 2008- 2009) at risk for, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21800090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35234888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00738725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3978/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3978_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between January 2008 and June 2009, the BioImage Study enrolled 7,687 asymptomatic men 55 to 80 years of age and women 60 to 80 years of age who were members of the Humana Health System and residents of the Chicago, Illinois, or Fort Lauderdale, Florida, metropolitan areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001290> "A prospective observational cohort of asymptomatic adults at risk of, but without, clinical atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (men aged 55–80 and women aged 60–80). They were recruited in 2008–2009 by the High-Risk Plaque Initiative from members of the Humana health plan in Chicago, Illinois, and Fort Lauderdale, Florida, United States, and examined with vascular imaging and blood sampling, to identify imaging and circulating biomarkers that predict near-term atherothrombotic events.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2659620/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BNCS is a population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18814239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Barbados National Cancer Study (BNCS) is a nationwide case-control study investigating environmental and genetic factors for breast cancer (BC) in a predominantly African-origin population with similar ancestry as African-Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2659620/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases for the BC component of the study included all histologically confirmed incident BC that were identified by the country’s only Pathology Department at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital between July, 2002 and March, 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2659620/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were women of at least 21 years of age without cancer, who were randomly selected from a national database and frequency matched (2:1) to the cases by 5-year age groups based on the age at the time of diagnosis of the case.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22357627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18814239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2659620/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BNCS, funded by the National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI), with contribution from the Office for Minority Health, includes a Coordinating Center (University Medical Center, Stony Brook, NY), a Clinical Center (Ministry of Health and University of the West Indies, Bridgetown, Barbados, West Indies), a Local Laboratory Center (University of the West Indies)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001291> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of breast and prostate cancer in Barbados-born residents of Barbados. It was run by Stony Brook University with the Barbados Ministry of Health and the University of the West Indies and funded by the US National Human Genome Research Institute. Its breast cancer arm enrolled every histologically confirmed incident breast cancer identified by the island's only pathology department, at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, from July 2002 to March 2006, with controls randomly selected from a national database and frequency-matched by age. The aim was to study environmental and genetic risk factors in this predominantly African-origin population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31002669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22429277") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3446437/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BRASS is a prospective, observational, single-center cohort with RA patients diagnosed by board-certified rheumatologists at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> "A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31002669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8048846/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patient data were collected from self‐administered patient questionnaires, physician reports, radiographs, and blood samples, as described previously (13).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> "A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31002669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8048846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients in BRASS are followed in the clinic at least annually and are sent questionnaires 6 months into the intervening period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> "A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31002669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37237405") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10224608/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were considered eligible to enroll in the registry if they were 18 to 70 years old with an RA diagnosis made by a board-certified rheumatologist and were registered at the Robert Breck Brigham Arthritis Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> "A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31002669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33002337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01793103") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40977501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12904143/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRASS registry is a single-center, prospective observational cohort that enrolled participants from the Brigham and Women’s Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, MA from March 2003 – May 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001292> "A single-centre prospective observational registry cohort of adults with rheumatoid arthritis diagnosed by a rheumatologist, enrolled from March 2003 at the Brigham and Women's Hospital Arthritis Center in Boston, Massachusetts, United States. Participants are followed with annual visits, semi-annual questionnaires and stored blood samples, to find biomarkers that predict drug response, toxicity, disease activity and prognosis and to describe the natural history of treated rheumatoid arthritis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diseased fascial samples removed at surgery were immediately placed in EMEM media (Lonza) and transferred by overnight courier to our laboratory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the BSSH-GODD cohort, salivary samples were collected using the Oragene-OG250 salivary DNA collection kit (DNA Genotek).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all cohorts, the DD-affected case subjects were individuals who had undergone surgical treatment for their disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591021/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We wish to thank the collaborators of the BSSH-GODD group, the GODDAF group, and the German Dupuytren Study Group for recruitment of case subjects") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28886342+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We undertook the largest GWAS to date in individuals with a surgically validated diagnosis of DD from the UK, with replication in British, Dutch, and German individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://metadata.ega-archive.org/studies/EGAS00001001206") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6358194") Annotation(rdfs:comment "U.K. patients were recruited as part of the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren’s Disease study, and controls were recruited from the U.K.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001293> "A UK collection of adults with Dupuytren's disease who had been treated surgically for it. Saliva samples for DNA, and diseased palmar fascia removed at surgery, were collected by the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren's Disease (BSSH-GODD) consortium for genetic studies of the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14691062+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have used multiple sources to identify a population-representative cohort of newly diagnosed patients with parkinsonism and Parkinson's disease in the UK over a 2-year period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23781007+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical, neuropsychological and genetic testing were performed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23781007+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CamPaIGN study has been the first to prospectively track disease evolution from diagnosis in an unselected population-representative incident cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7063985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cambridgeshire Parkinson's Incidence from GP to Neurologist (CamPaIGN) cohort is an unbiased incident population‐based PD cohort comprising newly diagnosed cases recruited within the county of Cambridgeshire, UK, between December 2000 and December 2002.12 This study was established to provide comprehensive and true‐to‐life data on the natural history of idiopathic PD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11161485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "New cases of parkinsonism between 2000 and 2002 in Cambridgeshire were referred to the study through multiple sources (general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, PD specialist nurses, and hospital discharge coding departments).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11161485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cambridgeshire Parkinson’s Incidence from GP to Neurologist (CamPaIGN) study is an observational, longitudinal study of incident PD patients in the county of Cambridgeshire, UK55,56.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14691062") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23781007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31965629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://data.dpuk.ukserp.ac.uk/CohortDirectory/Item?fingerPrintID=CamPaIGN") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institution Name University of Cambridge Department Name Clinical Neurosciences, John van Geest Centre for Brain Repair City Cambridge") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001294> "An observational, longitudinal, population-representative incident cohort of people newly diagnosed with parkinsonism or Parkinson's disease in the county of Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, between December 2000 and December 2002. Cases were referred through general practitioners, neurologists, geriatricians, Parkinson's disease specialist nurses and hospital discharge coding, and were followed from diagnosis by the University of Cambridge with clinical, neuropsychological and genetic assessments, to describe the natural history of Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6462308/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was managed by the University of British Columbia Cardiology Research group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6462308/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we designed the Canadian SCAD cohort study, a large, observational, prospective, cohort study, to describe the natural history of SCAD and to provide the justification and foundation for future randomized clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6462308/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a multicentre, prospective, observational study of consecutive patients with non-atherosclerotic SCAD from 20 centres across Canada and two centres in the United States (Supplementary material online, Appendix S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30698711+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a multicentre, prospective, observational study of patients with non-atherosclerotic SCAD presenting acutely from 22 centres in North America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30698711+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We prospectively enrolled 750 SCAD patients from June 2014 to June 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02188069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04906356") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30698711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30698711+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recorded baseline demographics, in-hospital characteristics, precipitating/predisposing conditions, angiographic features (assessed by core laboratory), in-hospital major adverse events (MAE), and 30-day major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001295> "A multicentre, prospective, observational cohort of patients presenting with acute non-atherosclerotic spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD), run from the University of British Columbia and enrolled at cardiac centres in Canada and the United States since June 2014, whose precipitating stressors, predisposing conditions and core-laboratory-reviewed angiograms are recorded and who are followed for cardiovascular events, to establish the natural history of SCAD and the outcomes of its treatment. Its first phase, the Canadian SCAD Cohort Study (enrolment 2014 to 2018, three-year follow-up), was extended from December 2018 as the Canadian SCAD Study, with international enrolment, a genetic sub-study and follow-up of up to ten years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4625209/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary population was a random sample of almost 20,000 men and women 20–93 years old, drawn from a population of approximately 90,000 inhabitants aged 20 years or older living within 10 wards (the entire of Østerbro and 1/3 of Nørrebro) surrounding Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4625209/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using the unique personal identification number (Central-Personal-Register-code), consisting of date of birth and a registration number, the sample was age-stratified within 5-year age groups, with the main emphasis on the age groups from 35 to 70 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26779513+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the years many other aspects have been added to the study: pulmonary diseases, heart failure, arrhythmia, alcohol, arthrosis, eye diseases, allergy, epilepsia, dementia, stress, vital exhaustion, social network, sleep-apnoe, ageing and genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26779513+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Copenhagen City Heart Study, also known as \"Østerbroundersøgelsen\", is a large prospective cardio-vascular population study of 20,000 women and men that was launched in 1975") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26779513+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original purpose of the study was to focus on prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26779513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9005347/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CCHS is a prospective study of the Danish general population initiated in 1976-78 with follow-up examinations in 1981-83, 1991-94, 2001-03, and 2011-13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001296> "A prospective cardiovascular population study of an age-stratified random sample of adults aged 20 years or older living in the Østerbro district and part of Nørrebro around Rigshospitalet in Copenhagen, Denmark, launched in 1975 with a first examination in 1976–1978 and re-examinations in 1981–1983, 1991–1994, 2001–2003 and 2011–2013, whose participants are followed through the Danish national registers. Its original purpose was the prevention of coronary heart disease and stroke; lung disease, dementia, ageing, genetics and other topics were added later.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2908678/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with histologically confirmed breast cancer were enrolled through the Cancer Risk Clinic at the University of Chicago.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2908678/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls without breast cancer were gender and age-matched with cases and enrolled from patients who visit the same hospital and are wiling to donate blood for genetic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2908678/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Early-onset cases and African Americans were oversampled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2908678/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "drawn from the Chicago Cancer Prone Study (CCPS), which is an ongoing hospital-based case∶control investigation designed to study the genetics of breast cancer in young patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12818384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, CCPS is a local registry of diverse high‐risk families at a hospital‐based preventive oncology clinic that has registered 5685 participants as of September 2024 since its establishment in 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20661439") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792352") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41373161") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12818384/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CCPS registry participants underwent genetic testing and counseling upon enrollment, and the average number of years between genetic testing and the current study was 10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001297> "A registry of individuals and families at high risk of cancer, established in 1992 at the Cancer Risk Clinic, a hospital-based preventive oncology clinic of the University of Chicago, United States, whose participants receive genetic testing and counselling at enrolment. It is also run as a hospital-based case-control study of the genetics of breast cancer in young patients, enrolling women with histologically confirmed breast cancer through the clinic, with early-onset cases and African Americans oversampled, and cancer-free controls matched on sex and age from patients of the same hospital, with questionnaires adopted from the Breast Cancer Family Registry and blood samples.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5046828/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a result, the CSCC Center Directors, with support from the NHLBI, endorsed expansion of the C-Data Project to include the collection, testing, and storage of blood and DNA samples from participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5046828/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Statistics and Data Management Center (SDMC) of the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (NHLBI) Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers (CSCC) Program was charged in 2003 with establishing a database of clinical, quality of life, and outcomes data to support development of multi-center research on SCD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2911637/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adult and pediatric patients with all forms of SCD at participating CSCC Centers and satellite sites were considered eligible for C-Data Project enrollment if seen within the last 24 months and were expected to return for care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2911637/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nine CSCC centers, representing 19 clinical sites, participated in the C-Data Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Once a year, participants took part in a short interview about their health and lifestyle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study Period March 2005 – September 2008") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Collaborative Data Project (C-Data) was established to create a comprehensive database of children and adults receiving medical care at participating Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers (CSCC) who would potentially be eligible for inclusion in SCD clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19902523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20658620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/cscc_c_data/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00528203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00529061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs004820.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "4) To evaluate the relationship between sickle cells patients' characteristics and medical events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001298> "A multicentre observational cohort and database of children and adults with sickle cell disease receiving care at the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's Comprehensive Sickle Cell Centers in the United States, run from March 2005 to September 2008 at nine of the centres and their satellite sites, which collected clinical data abstracted from medical records, yearly health and lifestyle interviews and quality-of-life questionnaires, and from 2007 blood and DNA samples for a genotype-phenotype repository, to describe the disease's complications and identify participants for future clinical trials.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5063388/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between November 2000, and March 2011, 2693 study subjects were enrolled from Cardiovascular Genome Center, Yonsei University College of Medicine, Seoul, Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5063388/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomic DNA was extracted from the peripheral blood samples by QuickGene SNP Kit DNA (Fuji film, Tokyo, Japan).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5063388/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients underwent coronary angiography depending on the relevant chest symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5063388/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained nurses obtained the clinical data, including demographic parameters and medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8965428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among the patients who visited Severance Hospital for chest symptoms, risk-factor control, or a health checkup, 1300 patients were administered ACEIs and were followed up for more than 6 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24142632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27736948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35352885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35793981") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10164599/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients who visited the Division of Cardiology at a university hospital, for a health check-up or due to chest symptoms from January 2001 to August 2009 were included in the CGC cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001299> "A hospital-based registry cohort of the Cardiovascular Genome Center of Yonsei University College of Medicine, enrolling from November 2000 patients who visited the cardiology division of Severance Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, for chest symptoms, cardiovascular risk-factor control or a health check-up, with clinical data collected by trained nurses, blood samples for DNA and, where symptoms warranted, coronary angiography, for genetic research on coronary artery disease and other cardiovascular and metabolic conditions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3493132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We initially genotyped 1183 cases of postmenopausal invasive breast cancer and 1185 individually-matched controls from the Nurses’ Health Study (NHS) cohort, using the Illumina HumanHap500 array, as part of the National Cancer Institute CGEMS (Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility) Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3493132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we attempted to replicate the initial associations in the GWAS in an additional 1,776 cases and 2,072 controls from breast cancer case-control studies nested in three prospective cohorts") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21573004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21573004+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We attempted to identify common genetic variants associated with log relative telomere length using genome-wide genotyping data on 3,554 individuals from the Nurses' Health Study and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial that took part in the National Cancer Institute Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility initiative for breast and prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3374121/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage I studies are the following: CPS-II American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, ATBC Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, CeRePP Centre de Recherche pour les Pathologies Prostatiques, and PLCO Prostate, Lung Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A critical requirement of the CGEMS project is to share raw data and analysis results from the study with the cancer research community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A new NCI initiative, Cancer Genetic Markers of Susceptibility (CGEMS), is a three-year study designed to identify common genetic variations associated with risk for prostate and breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17529973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22271044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2291937/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/cgems-id-genetic-risks-two-cancers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3562712/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the five individual study populations from the CGEMS study5,7 (ACS = American Cancer Society Prevention Study II (US); ATBC = Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Prevention Study (Finland); FPCC: CeRePP French Prostate Case-Control Study (France);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001300> "A three-year initiative of the US National Cancer Institute, begun in 2006, that ran multi-stage genome-wide association studies of prostate and breast cancer in case-control sets drawn from existing studies (for prostate cancer, men from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal, and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II, the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study and the French Prostate Case-Control Study; for breast cancer, postmenopausal women from the Nurses' Health Study, with replication in further cohorts), and shared its genotype data and results with the research community.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2248329") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The resource consists of DNA and plasma samples from CF patients and parents as well as demographic and clinical data from patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2248329/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CF patients and their family members were recruited from 37 specialized CF clinics across Canada (shown in Supplemental Table 5), during a period from 2003 to 2006, as participants in the Canadian CF Modifier Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2248329/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patient cohort was recruited from a population-based sample representing nearly 75% of the current Canadian CF population (34).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6407791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A subset (n = 101) of the Canadian CF Gene Modifier cohort that mirrored the Canadian severe CF population also underwent whole genome sequencing by Complete Genomics (CG) at an average of 30X coverage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7236628/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CGS participants were recruited from CF centers in Canada without regard to genotype or lung function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18292811") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23670970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26417704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30807572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31697830") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7236628/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase 2 subjects included individuals from the 3 cohorts (TSS, CGS, and GMS) who were recruited or acquired CFRD phenotype information since phase 1, or who were excluded from phase 1 for relatedness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001301> "A population-based study of people with cystic fibrosis and their parents in Canada, led from the Hospital for Sick Children in Toronto, which recruited patients without regard to genotype or lung function through specialised CF clinics across the country, first from 2003 to 2006 and then in a second phase, with clinical data from clinic records and DNA for genome-wide genotyping and sequencing, to identify genetic modifiers of cystic fibrosis lung disease and of complications such as meconium ileus, liver disease and CF-related diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2791220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited between 1984 and 2007 in one of the 9 cohorts forming the Euro-CHAVI Consortium (N = 1397, including 486 subjects that were included in our previous study [3], 75.7% male, median age: 33 years) or in the MACS cohort (N = 1157, 100% male, median age: 33 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2838940/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Euro-CHAVI cohort represents a consortium of 8 European cohorts and 1 Australian cohort that agreed to participate in the Host Genetic Core initiative of the Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2838940/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study includesHIV-1 infected African American adult subjects enrolled in either the U.S. military (DoD) HIV Natural History Study (NHS)or in the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study(MACS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24910414+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nine site-affiliated laboratories in Africa and the USA collected and processed PBMCs, and cryopreserved PBMC were shipped to CHAVI repositories in Africa and the USA for long-term storage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24910414+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI) consortium was established to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and containment of virus replication, with the goal of advancing the development of an HIV protective vaccine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20041166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20205591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21160409") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24910414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-023-06370-4/MediaObjects/41586_2023_6370_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Center for HIV/AIDS Vaccine Immunology (CHAVI) is a consortium of universities and academic medical centers that was established by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases (NIAID) from 2005-2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001302> "A consortium of universities and academic medical centres established by the US National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases from 2005 to 2012 and led from Duke University, to determine the host and virus factors associated with HIV transmission, infection and control and so advance HIV vaccine development. Its clinical studies enrolled participants at sites in Africa and the United States, and its Host Genetics Core assembled genome-wide genotyped samples of people with HIV-1 from existing cohorts, including the European and Australian cohorts of the Euro-CHAVI consortium and participants of the US Military HIV Natural History Study and the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Demographic details, socioeconomic characteristics, lifestyle, disease history, surgical history, family history, and visual and social function data are being collected using questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "General physical examination, eye examination, biological specimen collection, and first-degree relative data were collected and analyzed in the present study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CKC cohort is hospital-based and dynamic and was established in Zhengzhou, China; KC patients (n = 1114) from a large geographical area were enrolled from January 2019 to June 2023, with a mean age of 22.23 years (6‒57 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chinese keratoconus (CKC) cohort study is a population-based longitudinal prospective cohort study in the Chinese population involving a clinical database and biobanks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38703249+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The follow-up of the CKC cohort study is expected to include data collection at 3 months, 6 months, and 1 year after the initial examination and then at the annual follow-up examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38703249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40642536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39186261") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11361386/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 958 patients from the Chinese Keratoconus (CKC) cohort study were recruited from Henan Eye Hospital to explore gene‒environment interactions in KC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001303> "A hospital-based, dynamic, longitudinal prospective cohort of patients with keratoconus, established at Henan Eye Hospital in Zhengzhou, China, which since January 2019 has enrolled patients from a large geographical area, collecting questionnaire data on demographics, lifestyle, eye rubbing, medical, surgical and family history and visual function, eye and general examinations, biological specimens and data on patients' first-degree relatives, with follow-up at 3, 6 and 12 months and yearly thereafter, to study genes, environment and their interaction in keratoconus progression and its prevention.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annually, a physical examination documenting height, weight, Tanner stage, and standardized BP is conducted, and cognitive function, quality of life, nutritional, and behavioral questionnaires are completed by the parent or the child.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples of serum, plasma, urine, hair, and fingernail clippings are stored in biosamples and genetics repositories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CKiD prospective cohort study has clinical coordinating centers (principal investigators) at Children’s Mercy Hospital and the University of Missouri-Kansas City") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CKiD study consists of two clinical coordinating centers in Baltimore, MD, and Kansas City, MO, which include 57 clinical sites") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The specific aims of the CKiD study are to (1) identify novel and traditional risk factors for the progression of CKD; (2) characterize the impact of a decline in kidney function on neurodevelopment, cognitive abilities, and behavior; (3) identify the prevalence and the evolution of cardiovascular (CV) disease risk factors in children with CKD; and (4) examine the effects of declining GFR on growth") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3630231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With funding from the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases, in collaboration with the National Institute of Neurologic Disorders and Stroke, the National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, we have established a prospective cohort study of children with CKD, called the Chronic Kidney Disease in Children (CKiD) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17699320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00327860") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35518833") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9062328/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CKiD Study is an ongoing cohort of children, adolescents, and young adults with a diagnosis of CKD in the United States and Canada with participants enrolled between ages 0.5 and 16 years starting in 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001304> "A multicentre prospective observational cohort of children with chronic kidney disease in the United States and Canada, funded since 2003 by the National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases and coordinated from Children's Mercy Hospital in Kansas City and Johns Hopkins (later the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia), which since 2005 has enrolled children aged 6 months to 16 years at paediatric nephrology centres and later also young adults. Participants have annual visits with measured glomerular filtration rate, questionnaires on cognition, behaviour and quality of life, cardiovascular assessments and stored biosamples and DNA, to identify risk factors for the decline of kidney function and its effects on cardiovascular risk, neurocognitive function and behaviour, and growth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5139672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For both healthy and patient groups, participants were men or women ages 21–50 years; NIH racial/ethnic category either White, not Hispanic or Latino; or Hispanic or Latino, of any racial group") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5139672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy adults were recruited by community advertisements from the Los Angeles area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5139672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants with adult ADHD, bipolar disorder, and schizophrenia were recruited using a patient-oriented strategy involving outreach to local clinics and online portals (separate from the methods used to recruit healthy volunteers).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5139672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CNP was one of 9 Interdisciplinary Research Consortia supported by the NIH Roadmap Initiative from 2007–2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5139672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine these domains the CNP collected interviews and rating scales, self-report measures, neurocognitive exams using both paper-pencil and computerized tests, and neuroimaging data comprising structural MRI (sMRI), high angular resolution diffusion imaging (HARDI), and functional MRI (fMRI) both at rest (rsfMRI) and during five different cognitive activation paradigms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27922632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618088/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants who were included underwent a neuropsychological battery and submitted blood samples for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001305> "A sample of adults aged 21–50 studied at the University of California, Los Angeles, by the Consortium for Neuropsychiatric Phenomics, one of the NIH Roadmap interdisciplinary research consortia of 2007–2012: mainly healthy White non-Hispanic or Hispanic adults recruited by community advertisement in the Los Angeles area, with smaller groups with schizophrenia, bipolar disorder or ADHD recruited through local clinics and online portals. Participants had diagnostic interviews, neurocognitive testing and blood sampling for genotyping, and a subset had structural, diffusion and functional MRI, to study memory and response-inhibition phenotypes dimensionally from genome to syndrome.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5936002/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 159 patients diagnosed with moderate-to-severe COPD were initially selected from the cohort of COPD in Dusty Areas (CODA), a Korean study that was designed to observe the clinical outcomes of patients living near cement factories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35886039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9318537/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were chosen from two cohorts: 500 subjects (324 COPD patients and 176 controls) from the COPD in dusty areas (CODA) cohort [8] and 474 subjects (235 COPD patients and 239 matched controls) from the KoGES-Ansan cohort [9,10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12835267/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the CODA study was to investigate the clinical outcomes of Koreans with COPD living near cement plants in six regions, Gangneung (GN), Danyang (DY), Donghae (DH), Samcheok (SC), Yeongwol (YW), and Jecheon (JC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.e-trd.org/journal/view.php?doi=10.4046/trd.2019.0006") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At baseline examinations, data on the medical interview, survey questionnaire, spirometry, physical examination, blood/urine samples, and computed tomography were obtained from all participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.e-trd.org/journal/view.php?doi=10.4046/trd.2019.0006") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the CODA study enrolled participants living in six areas near cement plants in the Kangwon and Chungbuk provinces of South Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29750028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31172706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41136451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41436567") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.e-trd.org/journal/view.php?doi=10.4046/trd.2019.0006") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Overall, 504 participants (362 males and 142 females) were enrolled between 2012 and 2017 for baseline examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001306> "A longitudinal observational cohort, begun in 2012 and based at Kangwon National University Hospital, of residents of six districts with cement plants in Gangwon (Kangwon) and Chungbuk provinces, South Korea, comprising people with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease or airflow limitation and volunteers with normal spirometry, examined with questionnaires, spirometry, chest CT and blood and urine sampling, to study the clinical course and outcomes of COPD in people exposed to cement dust.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11893754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "According to protocol, follow-up visits were conducted at 1-month and 6-month after transplantation, and then every 6 months for a period of up to 5 years for biological sample (blood) collection, and up to 10 years for clinical data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11893754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COLT was a prospective study, which included patients from twelve clinical centers between September 2009 to December 2018: CHU Nantes, Hospices Civils de Lyon, Assistance Publique-Hôpitaux de Marseille, Hôpital Foch (Paris), Hôpital Européen Georges Pompidou (Paris), CHU Grenoble, CHRU Strasbourg, CHU Bordeaux, Hôpital Bichat (Paris), Hôpital Marie Lannelongue (Paris area) and CHU Toulouse from France, as well as the Erasme Hospital (Brussels, Belgium).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11893754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenCOLT collected DNA, high-quality GWAS (genome-wide association study) genotyping and robust HLA data for donors and recipients to supplement COLT clinical data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11893754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical records and follow-up data from each participating center are centralized in a secured online database coordinated by the Nantes University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/medicine/articles/10.3389/fmed.2023.1126697/full") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main objective of COLT was the discovery of early factors able to predict CLAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36968829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39164465") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/medicine/articles/10.3389/fmed.2023.1126697/full") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The method was to set a prospective cohort of patients included before the transplant, then regularly followed over a period of 10 years of inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001307> "A prospective multicentre cohort of lung transplant candidates enrolled before transplantation at eleven French lung transplant centres and the Erasme Hospital in Brussels between September 2009 and the end of 2018, coordinated by Nantes University Hospital, with clinical data and biological samples from recipients, and samples from their organ donors, followed every six months after transplantation (samples for up to five years, clinical data for up to ten), set up to discover early predictors of chronic lung allograft dysfunction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9502612/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study enrollment ended in 1988, and it involved data collection at 23 university-based institutions in a uniform, standardized fashion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 4,085 participants, ranging in age from newborns to adults, were enrolled in Phase 1 from 23 centers across the US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both mild and hospital-based sickle cell patients were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CSSCD was a multicenter, prospective study on the natural history of sickle cell disease and participant enrollment into Phase 1 of the CSSCD began in 1978.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participant entry ended in 1981 for all patients greater than six months of age; however, infants continued to be enrolled until 1988.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase 2A of the study sought to examine the progression of organ damage in the heart, lung, kidney and liver in adult cohort patients (born before 1/1/56) enrolled in phase 1 of the study between 3/79 and 5/81.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36138487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7114401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/csscd/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease was initiated in 1977 to determine the natural history of sickle cell disease (SCD) from birth to death in order to identify those factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001308> "A multicentre prospective study of the natural history of sickle cell disease, initiated in 1977, that enrolled patients with sickle cell disease of all ages, from newborns to adults and from mild to hospital-based cases, at 23 centres across the United States from 1978 (patients older than six months until 1981, infants until 1988), and followed them with standardised examinations and records of acute and chronic complications and organ damage, later phases following the infant cohort and adult participants until 1998, to identify the factors contributing to the morbidity and mortality of the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15194016+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A probability-based sample of Dallas County residents aged 18 to 65 years was surveyed with an extensive household health interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15194016+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dallas Heart Study was designed as a single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample to (1) produce unbiased population estimates of biologic and social variables that pinpoint ethnic differences in cardiovascular health at the community level and (2) support hypothesis-driven research on the mechanisms causing these differences using genetics, advanced imaging modalities, social sciences, and clinical research center methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3969786/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DHS was approved by the Institutional Review Board of the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, and all subjects provided written informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3969786/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DHS-2 cohort was augmented by voluntary participation of friends and spouses of the original participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3969786/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dallas Heart Study (DHS) is a multiethnic population-based probability sample of Dallas County residents, weighted to include 50% African-American and 50% non-African-American participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15194016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24531328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33619548") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8118582/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measurements were obtained on 3538 participants collected in 2000 to 2002 (DHS-1) and on 3283 participants collected in 2007 to 2009 (DHS-2), including 2131 participants with paired measurements in DHS-1 and DHS-2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001309> "A single-site, multiethnic, population-based probability sample of residents of Dallas County, Texas, aged 18 to 65, weighted to be about half African American and run by the University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center, surveyed and examined in 2000–2002 (DHS-1) and re-examined in 2007–2009 together with spouses and other new participants (DHS-2), designed to produce unbiased estimates of ethnic differences in cardiovascular health and to support research on their biological and social mechanisms using genetics, imaging, and clinical and social-science methods.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5826343/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, we included 5,367 of these patients treated in the period between January 1, 1984, and December 31, 2007, as we aimed for a long observational period facilitating the study of late effects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5826343/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish Testicular Cancer Late Treatment Effects Cohort (DaTeCa-LATE) consists of a combination of data derived from the clinical database DaTeCa (1984–2007) (11), national health and sociodemographic registries (1977–2016), a biobank with blood and sputum samples, and an 167-item questionnaire containing patient reported outcome measures (PROMs) obtained in 2014–2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5826343/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish Testicular Cancer Late Treatment Effects Cohort is a nationwide and population-based cohort and is located at the Department of Oncology, Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, Denmark.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29515973+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data for this cross-sectional study were collected between January 1, 2014, and December 31, 2016, among living Danish TCS and 60% agreed to participate in the cohort (N = 2,572).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29515973+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was set up in order to analyze late effects in long-term testicular cancer survivors (TCS) and to contribute to the design of future follow-up programs addressing and potentially preventing late effects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37568739") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29515973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29515973+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study also included data obtained through linkages to Danish registries, a biobank, and clinical data from hospital files and pathology reports originating from the Danish Testicular Cancer Database (DaTeCa).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001310> "A nationwide, population-based cohort of long-term testicular cancer survivors treated in Denmark in 1984–2007, identified in the Danish Testicular Cancer (DaTeCa) clinical database and surveyed by questionnaire on late effects in 2014–2016 by the Department of Oncology at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, with linked hospital, pathology and national registry data and a biobank of blood and sputum samples, set up to analyse late effects of treatment and inform future follow-up programmes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5107608/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Maternal, paternal and child health are investigated through longitudinal measurements of risk factors in seven areas (environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological) that may impact on child health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5107608/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DCHS is a population-based birth cohort study in the Drakenstein area in Paarl, a peri-urban area, 60 km outside Cape Town, South Africa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25228292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women from a poor, peri-urban community with high exposure to infectious diseases and environmental risk factors are enrolled with 1000 mother-child pairs followed for at least 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25228292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We describe a unique multidisciplinary South African birth cohort, the Drakenstein Child Health Study (DCHS), to investigate the incidence, risk factors, aetiology and long-term impact of early lower respiratory tract infection (LRTI) on child health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31751344") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6874071/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consenting pregnant women were enrolled from March 2012 to March 2015 and followed through childbirth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25228292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31751344") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6874071/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were enrolled in their second trimester (20–28 weeks gestation) at 2 public sector primary health care clinics, one serving a predominantly mixed ancestry population (TC Newman) and the other serving a predominantly Black African population (Mbekweni).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001311> "A population-based birth cohort run by the University of Cape Town in the Drakenstein area of Paarl, a poor peri-urban community 60 km from Cape Town, South Africa, which enrolled pregnant women at 20–28 weeks' gestation at two primary health clinics (TC Newman and Mbekweni) between March 2012 and March 2015 and follows the mother–child pairs from pregnancy until the children are at least five years old, to investigate early-life determinants of child health, first among them early lower respiratory tract infection, through environmental, infectious, nutritional, genetic, psychosocial, maternal and immunological measures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Dental SCORE, an extended dental and periodontal examination was performed following the same protocols as in the COHRA1 study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9378791/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fourth cohort (Dental SCORE, n = 548) is a subset of a larger project, Heart SCORE, which is an ongoing cardiovascular disease study of 2,000 middle aged White and African Americans in the Pittsburgh region of Pennsylvania [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12475168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dental assessments and related data collection were carried out between 2007 and 2010 on a subgroup of 552 participants, known as the Dental Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation (Dental SCORE) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12475168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were age 45 to 75, lived in the greater Pittsburgh metropolitan area, and free of known health conditions likely to restrict life expectancy to less than five years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12475168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The research participants were recruited through a community-based study called Heart Strategies Concentrated on Risk Evaluation (Heart SCORE) that began in 2003 and enrolled 2,000 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35172313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41006734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12475168/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study’s primary goal was to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001312> "A sub-study of Heart SCORE (Heart Strategies Concentrating on Risk Evaluation), a community-based cohort begun in 2003 of White and African American adults aged 45–75 in the greater Pittsburgh area, Pennsylvania, set up to investigate racial disparities in cardiovascular disease, in which a subgroup of participants had extended dental and periodontal examinations following the COHRA1 protocols and gave blood or saliva for DNA in 2007–2010, run by the University of Pittsburgh.")

