AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diabetic subjects were recruited at the UMR8090 CNRS unit in Lille (N=271) and at the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital during medical examination (N=423).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from volunteers insured by the French social security system, which offers periodic health examinations free of charge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage 1: Inclusion criteria for cases were (i) T2DM according to 1997 American Diabetes Association (ADA) criteria1 ; (ii) family history of diabetes in first degree relatives; (iii) BMI < 30 kg/m².") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Inclusion criteria for controls were; (i) age at exam ≥ 45 yr.; (ii) normal fasting glucose according to 1997 ADA criteria; (iii) BMI < 27 kg/m².") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control subjects were participants in the Data from an Epidemiological Study on the Insulin Resistance syndrome (DESIR) program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35551307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature05616/MediaObjects/41586_2007_BFnature05616_MOESM286_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17293876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17293876+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested 392,935 single-nucleotide polymorphisms in a French case-control cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001313> "A French case–control sample of people of European ancestry assembled for a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes: people with type 2 diabetes, a family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives and a BMI below 30, recruited at the CNRS UMR8090 unit in Lille and the Endocrinology-Diabetology Department of the Corbeil-Essonnes Hospital, and normoglycaemic controls drawn mostly from the D.E.S.I.R. cohort of volunteers attending French health examination centres.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10834390/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among this group, individuals with two or more recorded diagnoses of T2D and at least one HbA1c value ≥6.5% were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10834390/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of enrollment, participants underwent a detailed evaluation that included completing a research survey, a clinical examination, and specimen collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10834390/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible DIAMOND participants were aged ≥18 years, were members of the health system and possessed affiliated health insurance with pharmaceutical coverage, and resided in southeast Michigan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10834390/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were from the Diabetes Multi-omic Investigation of Drug Response (DIAMOND), a diverse cohort of individuals with T2D from southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10834390/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts included in this study were approved by the institutional review boards of the Henry Ford Health System; the University of California, San Francisco; and Kaiser Permanente.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37639712+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DIAMOND participants had genome-wide genotype data and longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37639712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs003350.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The intent of the DIAMOND study is to use genomic profiling, drug exposure information, and electronic health record (EHR) derived outcome data to identify genetic predictors of treatment response.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001314> "A diverse cohort of adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of the Henry Ford Health System with pharmacy-covered health insurance and live in southeast Michigan and the Detroit metropolitan area, invited on the basis of two or more recorded diagnoses of type 2 diabetes and an HbA1c of at least 6.5%, who at enrolment completed a research survey, clinical examination and specimen collection, and whose genome-wide genotypes are linked to longitudinal electronic records of laboratory results and medication fills to study the genetics of response to diabetes drugs.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3383758/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Detroit Neighborhood Health Study (DNHS) recruited 1,547 adults aged 18 years or older at baseline from the city of Detroit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12975512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this investigation, we utilized data from the DNHS, a prospective population-based longitudinal cohort consisting of individuals residing in Detroit, Michigan") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12975512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent structured telephone interviews annually between 2008 and 2013 to assess various aspects, including perceptions of their neighborhoods, mental and physical health status, social support, exposure to traumatic events, symptoms of PTSD, depression and generalized anxiety, as well as alcohol and tobacco use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12975512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DNHS includes extensive data on social adversities collected in five annual waves from 2008 to 2013 along with biospecimens collected in a subset of participants in four of the five sampling waves.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12975512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the DNHS was to examine how biological variation, stressful and traumatic life experiences, and environmental factors contribute to the prediction of psychopathology and behavior.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12975512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To test this hypothesis, we leveraged longitudinal data from the Detroit Neighborhood Health Study, a community-based, prospective cohort of predominantly African Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22745713") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38177345") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41821625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000560.v3.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort participants were selected with a dual-frame probability design, using telephone numbers obtained from the U.S. Postal Service Delivery Sequence Files as well as a listed-assisted random-digit-dial frame.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001315> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 18 or older living in the city of Detroit, Michigan, most of them African American, drawn from a random probability sample of the city's households and interviewed by telephone in annual waves from 2008 to 2013, with blood specimens collected from a subset, to study how biological variation, stressful and traumatic experiences and environmental factors contribute to post-traumatic stress disorder, depression and other psychopathology.")

