AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16870633+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "handgrip strength dropped from 24.2 kg in Southern Denmark to 20.8 kg in Languedoc-Roussillon, France and 14.2 kg in Calabria, Italy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/5201950") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 234 trios composed by one centenarian, his/her child and a child of his/her concordant or discordant sib were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/5201950") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population pools of 1.6, 2.3 and 2.0 million inhabitants were screened, respectively, in Denmark, France and Italy to identify families matching the design requirements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/5201950") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the genetic contribution to familial similarity in longevity, we set up a novel experimental design where cousin-pairs born from siblings who were concordant or discordant for the longevity trait were analyzed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20584770+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this substudy of the European Challenge for Healthy Aging study, handgrip strength was measured in 290 subjects aged 90 years and older and in one of their offspring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16870633") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17989723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20584770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42176242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11357-026-02334-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The oldest subjects (90-plus individuals) were enrolled in two European projects investigating genetic and environmental factors associated with aging: the European Challenge for Healthy Aging (ECHA) project [24] and the GEnetics of Healthy Ageing (GEHA) project [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001317> "A European family study of longevity that recruited people aged 90 or older, many of them centenarians, in Southern Denmark, Languedoc-Roussillon in France and Calabria in Italy, together with one of their children and, in a cousin-pair design, a child of a sibling who was or was not also long-lived, to investigate genetic and environmental factors in longevity and healthy ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3478551/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 933 individuals were studied, with 658 participating in the EDC study baseline examination between 1986 and 1988 and 130 completing questionnaires only.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3478551/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were diagnosed or seen within 1 year of diagnosis at Children’s Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3478551/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pittsburgh EDC study is a prospective cohort study of childhood-onset (age <17 years) type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11932817/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical examinations were conducted biennially for the first 10 years of follow-up and at 18, 25, and 30 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11932817/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Questionnaires were administered biennially over the entire follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22851572") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37533055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39932735") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11932817/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EDC is a well-characterized, prospective study with long-term follow-up, designed to systematically ascertain incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001318> "A prospective cohort study of people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes (onset before age 17) who were diagnosed, or seen within a year of diagnosis, at Children's Hospital of Pittsburgh between 1950 and 1980, followed since a baseline examination in 1986–1988 with biennial examinations and questionnaires for ten years and later questionnaires and examinations, to ascertain the incidence of and risk factors for complications of type 1 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26691988") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17634448") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17634448+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To test for replication of the most significant findings, we genotyped a set of Scottish cases and controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319> "A clinic-based case-control study of age-related macular degeneration in Scotland, collected by a group in Edinburgh with funding from the Chief Scientist Office (Scotland), whose cases with advanced or intermediate AMD and controls were ascertained by fundus examination or photography; its cases and controls replicated the association of complement C3 with AMD and were contributed to the International AMD Genomics Consortium's genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26691988") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26691988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3448/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3448_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Edinburgh Clinic Clinic Clinic Yes Yes Yes No International 8") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319> "A clinic-based case-control study of age-related macular degeneration in Scotland, collected by a group in Edinburgh with funding from the Chief Scientist Office (Scotland), whose cases with advanced or intermediate AMD and controls were ascertained by fundus examination or photography; its cases and controls replicated the association of complement C3 with AMD and were contributed to the International AMD Genomics Consortium's genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17634448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26691988") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26691988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3448/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3448_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Edinburgh group using the Scottish AMD study was funded by the Chief scientists Office (Scotland) CSO reference number: CZB/4/79") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001319> "A clinic-based case-control study of age-related macular degeneration in Scotland, collected by a group in Edinburgh with funding from the Chief Scientist Office (Scotland), whose cases with advanced or intermediate AMD and controls were ascertained by fundus examination or photography; its cases and controls replicated the association of complement C3 with AMD and were contributed to the International AMD Genomics Consortium's genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A second visit of interviews and examinations is under way (2012–14) to enrich the assessment of cohort exposures and to detect initial incident events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All active or retired employees of the six institutions (and, in a few instances, also of related educational or health institutions), of both sexes, and with ages between 35 and 74 years, were eligible for the study, totalling, in 2008, 52 137 potential participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annual telephone interviews include questions on self-rated health, new diagnosis of conditions of interest, hospitalizations and specific medical procedures such as dialysis, revascularization and cancer biopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline assessment (2008–10) included detailed interviews and measurements to assess social and biological determinants of health, as well as various clinical and subclinical conditions related to diabetes, cardiovascular diseases and mental health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, the Brazilian Longitudinal Study of Adult Health (in Portuguese, ‘Estudo Longitudinal de Saúde do Adulto’, ELSA-Brasil) aims to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases, over a long-term follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24585730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4339754/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a group of Brazilian epidemiologists and clinicians from six institutions (Federal Universities of Bahia, Espírito Santo, Minas Gerais and Rio Grande do Sul; University of São Paulo; and Oswaldo Cruz Foundation), led by the authors of this article, organized the Study in centres located in state capitals of the north-eastern, south-eastern and southern regions of Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001320> "A multicentre cohort of active and retired employees aged 35–74 years of six Brazilian universities and research institutions, with study centres in state capitals of north-eastern, south-eastern and southern Brazil, examined at baseline in 2008–2010 and at later visits and followed by annual telephone interviews, to investigate the development of chronic diseases, primarily diabetes and cardiovascular diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31054214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6829037/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two regions were selected per country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31054214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6829037/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our EMBLEM study demonstrated the feasibility of conducting a networked, multisite population-based case-control study of eBL in in Uganda, Tanzania, and Kenya.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31054214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6829037/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we enrolled suspected eBL cases and population-based controls in six rural malaria-endemic areas in Northern Uganda, Northeastern Tanzania, and Western Kenya (Figure 1) in the Epidemiology of Burkitt Lymphoma in East African Children and Minors (EMBLEM) study during 2010–2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36595676") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9926229/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EMBLEM is a case–control study of eBL from 2010 through 2016 in six regions of Kenya, Uganda, and Tanzania.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EMBLEM is a case control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma (BL) designed to investigate risk factors of BL in malaria-endemic areas of Uganda, Tanzania, and Kenya.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EMBLEM was designed to enroll representative cases and controls (0-15 years) from defined geographical areas and use questionnaire, serological, and genetic methods to study BL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40646133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://emblem.cancer.gov/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiology of Burkitt lymphoma in East African children and minors (EMBLEM) is a research study sponsored by the Intramural Research program of the National Cancer Institute under Protocol #: 10-C-N133 during 2010-2016 to comprehensively investigate infections, immunological, and genetic risk factors of Burkitt lymphoma (BL).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001321> "A case-control study of childhood Burkitt lymphoma in malaria-endemic East Africa, sponsored by the US National Cancer Institute's intramural research program, that in 2010–2016 enrolled population-based cases and controls aged 0–15 years from six rural regions, two each in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, and used questionnaires, blood samples and genetic data to investigate infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for Burkitt lymphoma.")

