AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29410079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30267149") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38036604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39112778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42598116") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42598116") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13471357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MACS is a two-center research consortium studying the neurobiological foundations of affective disorders that recruited participants aged 18-65 years with West-European ancestry from January 09, 2015 to May 11, 2018 via newspaper advertisements or local psychiatric hospitals") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001330> "The human cohort of the German Research Foundation (DFG) research unit FOR2107 on the neurobiology of the major psychoses, recruited between 2014 and 2018 at the Universities of Marburg and Münster, Germany, through local psychiatric hospitals and newspaper advertisements: adults aged 18–65 with major depressive disorder, bipolar disorder, schizoaffective disorder or schizophrenia, healthy people at genetic and/or environmental risk, and healthy controls, deeply phenotyped with MRI, clinical course, neuropsychology, personality, risk and protective factors and biomaterials (blood, stool, urine, hair, saliva) at baseline and again at a 2-year follow-up, to identify how genetic and environmental factors shape brain structure and function and the course of these disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3545809") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify additional quantitative trait loci (QTL) for VWF antigen variation and to minimize the impact of age and illness- related environmental factors, we studied two independent healthy young cohorts, the Genes and Blood-Clotting Study (GABC, n = 1,152) and the Trinity Student Study (TSS, n = 2,310) (21–23).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25208887+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to identify genetic factors affecting the natural variation of plasminogen levels, we performed a genome-wide association study and linkage analysis in a sample of 3456 young healthy individuals who participated in the Genes and Blood Clotting Study (GABC) or the Trinity Student Study (TSS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11897800/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the study's phenotypic assessment, data on a series of common morphological traits was captured, including fifth finger clinodactyly.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11897800/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was focused on identifying genetic factors involved in blood clotting and recruited healthy individuals from the University of Michigan undergraduate and graduate population as well as their biological siblings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12314372/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1189 healthy individuals (ages 14-35) representing 507 sibships (with 2-6 siblings per family) from the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, were recruited between June 26, 2006, and January 30, 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23267103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25208887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40071514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40756183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12314372/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using the sibling structure in the GABC cohort and siblings in the TSS cohort, we performed linkage analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001331> "A family-based study of healthy young people aged 14–35, recruited at the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, United States, between June 2006 and January 2009 from the university's undergraduate and graduate students together with their biological siblings, with blood samples for measuring plasma haemostatic proteins (such as von Willebrand factor and plasminogen), genome-wide genotyping and a survey of common morphological traits, to identify the genetic factors behind variation in blood clotting in healthy people, using its sibling structure for linkage as well as association analysis.")

