AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3749730") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GAP consortium contributed to sample collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3749730/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For all samples, psoriasis was defined as psoriasis vulgaris (chronic plaque type psoriasis) the commonest manifestation of the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3510312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples of the Psoriasis/Arthritis Genetics Extension (PAGE) and the Genetic Analysis of Psoriasis Consortium (GAPC) datasets (Supplementary Table 1 and 2) were collected from subjects of European Caucasian descent at the participating institutions after obtaining informed consent in adherence with the Declaration of Helsinki Principles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3510312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GAPC cases and the Irish and Spanish controls were genotyped at the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute (WTSI) and all samples were provided by the relevant groups given in Supplementary Table 2 and listed in the GAP consortium members list (Supplementary Note 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3510312/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We combined three existing GWAS datasets (hereafter referred to as Kiel3, CASP4 and WTCCC25) with two independent European-descent case-control datasets genotyped on the Immunochip: the Psoriasis Association Genetics Extension (PAGE: 3,580 cases and 5,902 controls) and the Genetic Analysis of Psoriasis Consortium (GAPC: 2,997 cases and 9,183 controls) (datasets are described in Supplementary Tables 1 and 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20953190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2467/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2467_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GAPC Immunochip UK KCL/Glasgow/Sheffield WTCCC2 207 4822 Finland Helsinki DILGOM 240 490 Spain Barcelona Barcelona 269 202 The Netherlands Nijmegan Groningen 152 1,107 Austria Graz - 310 0 Sweden Gothenburg/Stockholm - 859 0 Italy Rome Groningen 73 509 Germany Erlangen PopGen 826 1,984 Ireland Dublin Dublin 61 69") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001332> "An international consortium of psoriasis genetics research groups in the United Kingdom, Ireland, Austria, Finland, Germany, Italy, the Netherlands, Spain and Sweden, with a management committee chaired from King's College London, that pools its members' collections of people of European descent with psoriasis vulgaris, together with controls from national control collections, for genetic association studies of psoriasis, including a genome-wide association study with the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 and an Immunochip case–control study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28295287+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biopsy tissue for cases prior to neoadjuvant therapy (if given), blood, saliva and fecal samples were sought for study subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28295287+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore conducted a population-based case-control study in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana, enrolling 2,202 women with lesions suspicious for breast cancer and 2,161 population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6467449/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A collaboration between the National Cancer Institute and three major hospitals in Ghana, the GBHS is a case-control study that aims to examine risk associations and estimate the population prevalence of known and novel breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6467449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, eligibility requirements for all study participants (cases and controls) included being: (i) female; (ii) 18 to 74 years old; (iii) a resident within one of the 22 defined municipal districts for at least one year prior to enrollment; and (iv) able to complete an in-person interview in either English or Twi language.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6467449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were defined as: women being recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy at one of the three major cancer treatment hospitals in Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital in Accra, and Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, and Peace and Love Hospital in Kumasi); or women presenting for treatment of pathologically-confirmed breast cancer at Korle Bu, Komfo Anokye, or Peace and Love Hospitals within one year of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30990841+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A pool of potential controls (women aged 18 to 74 years, never diagnosed with breast cancer) was selected from the enumeration using systematic random sampling and frequency-matched to the anticipated distributions of age and residence among cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28295287") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30990841") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38082317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38082317+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using data from 1071 invasive pathologically confirmed breast cancer cases and 2096 controls from the Ghana Breast Health Study conducted from 2013 to 2015, we investigated associations with mosquito control products to reduce the spread of mosquito-borne diseases, such as malaria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001333> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer, a collaboration of the US National Cancer Institute with three major hospitals in Accra and Kumasi, Ghana (Korle Bu Teaching Hospital, Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and Peace and Love Hospital), that in 2013–2015 enrolled women aged 18–74 recommended for biopsy of a breast lesion suspicious for malignancy, or treated for breast cancer, at these hospitals, and population controls sampled by household enumeration of the surrounding districts and frequency-matched on age and district, collecting interviews and tumour tissue, blood, saliva and faecal samples to study breast cancer risk factors in a West African population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4398999/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All international sites began active recruitment of participants in September 2012 with an aim to collect a total of 5,000 participants, recruited both prospectively and from existing repositories of participating centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4398999/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study inclusion–exclusion criteria require that participants must have had alcohol consumption averaging at least 80 g per day (for men) or 50 g per day (for women), for at least 10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25872595+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Extensive phenotypic data are obtained using semistructured interviews and patient records, and blood samples are collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25872595+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this National Institutes of Health/National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism funded study, we are recruiting high-risk drinkers who are either cases (with alcoholic cirrhosis) or controls (drinking comparable amounts over similar time, but free of significant liver disease).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25872595+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GenomALC Consortium comprises researchers from Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, United Kingdom, and United States, with a joint aim of exploring the genetic and genomic basis of alcoholic cirrhosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25872595") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11093576/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GenomALC-2 DNA samples and project-specific data were donated by research groups who had independently collected them for prior genetic studies of alcohol-associated liver disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001334> "A multicentre international case–control study of alcohol-related cirrhosis, run by the GenomALC Consortium of researchers in Australia, France, Germany, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and the United States with funding from the US National Institute on Alcohol Abuse and Alcoholism, that from September 2012 recruited, at liver and alcohol treatment clinics and from existing repositories of the participating centres, people who had drunk heavily (at least 80 g of alcohol a day for men or 50 g for women) for at least ten years, with alcoholic cirrhosis (cases) or without significant liver disease (controls), with interviews, clinical records and blood samples, to find genetic factors that predispose drinkers to cirrhosis. A second sample, GenomALC-2, added DNA and data that research groups in these countries and Belgium had collected for earlier genetic studies of alcohol-related liver disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20876876+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included 815 CDKN2A mutation carriers (473 affected, and 342 unaffected, with melanoma) from 186 families from 15 centers in Europe, North America, and Australia who participated in the Melanoma Genetics Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3251256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 14 GenoMEL groups contributed DNA samples from cases and controls of European (or Israeli) ethnicity (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3251256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase 1 was based on 1,650 cases from Australian and European populations chosen to have a phenotype argued to “enrich” for genetic susceptibility (early onset, multiple primaries, or modest family history of melanoma).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenoMEL was an FP6 project and, as such, was funded by the European Commission GenoMEL has also received substantial support from the National Cancer Institute (NCI) of the US National Institutes of Health (NIH) (CA83115).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Determine how those genes interact with environmental factors such ultraviolet radiation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20876876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21983787") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://genomel.org/research/programme-and-aims/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This non-profit consortium was established in 1997 and comprises the majority of research groups worldwide who are working on the genetics of familial melanoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001335> "An international non-profit consortium, established in 1997, of most of the research groups working on the genetics of familial melanoma, in Europe, North America, Australia and elsewhere, funded by the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme and the US National Cancer Institute, which pools data and samples from its members' melanoma-prone families and case–control series to find melanoma susceptibility genes and how they interact with environmental factors such as ultraviolet radiation. Its genome-wide association study combined melanoma cases, prioritised for family history, multiple primaries or early onset, and controls from the same populations, contributed by member groups in Europe, Israel and Australia, with French and UK population controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29987654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1186%2Fs13054-022-04208-5/MediaObjects/13054_2022_4208_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEN-SEP study [1], used for the first stage, is a national, multicenter, observational study conducted in a Spanish network of post-surgical units and ICUs recruiting unrelated adult (>18 years old) patients of European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336> "A multicentre observational cohort of adult patients of European ancestry with sepsis of any cause admitted to a network of intensive care units in Spain, recruited through the GEN-SEP Network of Spanish investigators in two periods (2002–2015 and 2016–2019) and followed for the development of acute respiratory distress syndrome and for 28-day survival, whose DNA is used in genetic studies of sepsis-associated ARDS and sepsis outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29987654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9637317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEN-SEP study, used for the first stage, included 475 (146 non-survivors) European ancestry patients considered for a previous GWAS of sepsis-associated ARDS [20] recruited between 2002 and 2015 for which follow-up records of 28-day survival were available (1st GEN-SEP period).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336> "A multicentre observational cohort of adult patients of European ancestry with sepsis of any cause admitted to a network of intensive care units in Spain, recruited through the GEN-SEP Network of Spanish investigators in two periods (2002–2015 and 2016–2019) and followed for the development of acute respiratory distress syndrome and for 28-day survival, whose DNA is used in genetic studies of sepsis-associated ARDS and sepsis outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29987654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12516505/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEN-SEP and SepNet studies comprised cases of clinically defined sepsis-associated ARDS (Berlin definition)2 and controls with sepsis who did not develop ARDS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336> "A multicentre observational cohort of adult patients of European ancestry with sepsis of any cause admitted to a network of intensive care units in Spain, recruited through the GEN-SEP Network of Spanish investigators in two periods (2002–2015 and 2016–2019) and followed for the development of acute respiratory distress syndrome and for 28-day survival, whose DNA is used in genetic studies of sepsis-associated ARDS and sepsis outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29987654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36335405") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41033104") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12516505/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GEN-SEP is a multicentre, observational study conducted in a Spanish network of ICUs comprising adult patients with all-cause sepsis of European ancestry recruited in two periods (in 2002-2015 and in 2016-2019)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001336> "A multicentre observational cohort of adult patients of European ancestry with sepsis of any cause admitted to a network of intensive care units in Spain, recruited through the GEN-SEP Network of Spanish investigators in two periods (2002–2015 and 2016–2019) and followed for the development of acute respiratory distress syndrome and for 28-day survival, whose DNA is used in genetic studies of sepsis-associated ARDS and sepsis outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582818/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Characteristics of the 1737 GEOS study participants (830 cases - 43% African-American and 907 controls - 39% African-American) are summarized in Table 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582818/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were subjects with no history of stroke identified by random-digit dialing and were matched to cases by age (within ten years) and geographic region of residence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10718488/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stroke cases aged 15–49 years old at the time of ischemic stroke were recruited from the greater Baltimore-Washington area over 4 time periods between 1992 and 2008, along with age and sex matched controls") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with a first-ever ischemic stroke were identified by discharge surveillance from one of 59 hospitals in the U.S. greater Baltimore- Washington area and by direct referral from regional neurologists.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEOS study is a population-based case-control study designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischemic stroke and to characterize interactions of stroke- associated genes with environmental risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459313") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38094903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/wnl/c/wnl_2022_08_08_mitchell_1_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.downstate.edu/research/centers-departments/henri-begleiter-neurodynamics-laboratory/_documents/2012-Hartz-IncreasedgeneticvulnerabilitytosmokingatCHRNA5inearly-onsetsmokers-Supplement.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "University of Maryland: The Genetics of Early Onset Stroke (GEOS) Study: The Genetics of Early Onset Stroke (GEOS) study is a population-based case-control study designed to identify the genetic determinants of ischemic stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001337> "A population-based case–control study of early-onset ischaemic stroke, run from the University of Maryland, Baltimore, that recruited women and men aged 15–49 with a first ischaemic stroke, identified by discharge surveillance at 59 hospitals of the greater Baltimore–Washington area of the United States and by referral from regional neurologists, in four periods between 1992 and 2008, together with controls without stroke found by random-digit dialling and matched on age and region of residence, in a biracial sample of European American and African American participants; it was designed to identify the genetic determinants of early-onset ischaemic stroke and their interactions with environmental risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we conducted a GWAS meta-analysis across knee, hip, finger, thumb, and spine osteoarthritis phenotypes in 826,690 individuals of European and East Asian descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8459317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two of the cohorts are of East Asian and 11 of the cohorts are of European descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35644035") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9541521/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GO consortium performed a large‐scale GWAS meta‐analysis for OA in 826,690 participants across 13 cohorts worldwide in 10 different OA phenotypes (Supplementary Table 1, https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/art.42246).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FinnGen study, launched in Finland in the autumn of 2017, is a study that combines genome information with digital health care data from national registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The deCODE genetics osteoarthritis study is an ongoing population based study in Iceland that was initiated in 1997.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GO aims to bring together all globally available genetic studies of osteoarthritis in order to make new discoveries possible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34450027") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/contributing-studies/contributing-studies/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.genetics-osteoarthritis.com/themenmenue/home/index.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics of Osteoarthritis (GO) consortium is a global collaboration with a focus on progressing our understanding of the genetic underpinning of osteoarthritis and related traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001338> "A global collaboration that aims to bring together all available genetic studies of osteoarthritis, meta-analysing genome-wide association data on osteoarthritis at different joint sites (hip, knee, hand, finger, thumb and spine) and related traits from its contributing cohorts and biobanks in Europe, East Asia, North America and Australia, among them UK Biobank, arcOGEN, deCODE, the HUNT Study, the Estonian Biobank, the Rotterdam Study, FinnGen and the Million Veteran Program.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(for GO-CAT, reference 2017-3978 and 2016-2675 for osteosarcoma and brain tumor cohorts, respectively)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As pediatric cancer is relatively rare, an international collaboration between the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment (GO-CAT) consortium and United Kingdom Molecular Genetics of Adverse Drug Reactions in Children (MAGIC) study was initiated to establish an international cohort that is sufficient to perform statistically meaningful analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participating centers included Radboud university medical center (Nijmegen, Netherlands), University Medical Center of Groningen (Groningen, Netherlands), Leiden University Medical Center (Leiden, Netherlands), Academic Medical Center (Amsterdam, Netherlands), Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Nazionale Tumori (Milan, Italy) and The Children’s Hospital at Westmead (Sydney, Australia).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients from the GO-CAT cohort were treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, whereas patients from the United Kingdom MAGIC cohort were primarily treated with cisplatin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GO-CAT cohort consisted of 136 patients with osteosarcoma (52.1%), 79 with medulloblastoma (30.3%) and 46 with low-grade glioma (17.6%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36699085") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9870026/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GO-CAT cohort is a multinational retrospective cohort of pediatric cancer patients, treated between 1975 and 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001339> "A multinational retrospective cohort of paediatric cancer patients treated between 1975 and 2020 at hospitals in the Netherlands, Italy and Australia, made up of osteosarcoma and brain tumour cohorts and mostly treated with cisplatin or carboplatin, assembled by the Genetics of Childhood Cancer Treatment consortium for pharmacogenetic research such as studies of platinum-induced hearing loss.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6358194/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Bilateral disease was the most common diathesis feature, reported at 63 percent and 40 percent in the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren’s Disease study and the Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease and Associated Fibromatosis study, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6358194/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was obtained from patients’ saliva (British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren’s Disease study) and blood (Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease and Associated Fibromatosis study)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6358194/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease and Associated Fibromatosis study, we imputed the missing data using the same method as in the British Society for Surgery of the Hand Genetics of Dupuytren’s Disease study, with the additional variable ectopic disease included in the imputation chain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6358194/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients in the Dutch Genetic Origin of Dupuytren Disease and Associated Fibromatosis study were also recruited from hand surgery clinics; this recruitment has also been described previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10876167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, phenotype and genotype data of total of 1669 DD patients were collected between 2007 and 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28886342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30688894") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37257093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37257093+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phenotype data include age at onset, recurrence, and family history of disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001340> "A case collection of people with Dupuytren disease recruited from 2007 through plastic and hand surgery clinics in the Netherlands, with blood samples for DNA and surgeon-recorded clinical data such as age at onset, family history, bilateral and ectopic disease and recurrence, for genetic studies of Dupuytren disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5204128/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In general, the sample can be characterized as individuals of European ancestry in their early twenties with low levels of alcohol and other drug use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5204128/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from the general community at both sites and also from the Department of Psychology undergraduate human subjects research pool at the University of Georgia site (n=426; 34% of the total sample).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5204128/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The battery comprised a delay discounting task, Monetary Choice Questionnaire, Conners Continuous Performance Test, Go/NoGo Task, Stop Signal Task, Barratt Impulsivity Scale, and the UPPS-P Impulsive Behavior Scale.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5742029/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was collected via a saliva sample for DNA collection in an Oragene DNA kit (DNA Genotek Inc., Kanata, ON, Canada).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5742029/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were English fluency, age 18 – 30 years, and self-reported Caucasian race and non-Hispanic ethnicity to minimize population stratification.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27449350") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29120849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37582857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10618088/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genetic, cognitive and behavioral data were similarly collected in the Genetics of Impulsivity (GOI) project, performed at the University of Georgia and the University of Chicago.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001341> "A study of healthy young adults aged 18–30 of self-reported Caucasian, non-Hispanic ancestry with low levels of alcohol and drug use, recruited from the community at the University of Chicago and the University of Georgia in the United States, and from the Georgia site's undergraduate research pool, who completed a laboratory battery of impulsivity measures (delay discounting, response inhibition, risk-taking and impulsive personality traits) and gave saliva DNA for genotyping, to study the genetic basis of impulsivity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22330960+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diabetic retinopathy was assessed by fundus photography and graded using modified Airlie House classification.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342> "A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years' duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3343221/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From October 2007 to December 2010, a cross-sectional study of 473 Hispanic type II diabetic subjects were recruited in a joint study of Cedars-Sinai Medical Center (CSMC) and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center (HUMC), following informed consent and approval by the Institutional Review Board (IRB)/Ethics Committee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342> "A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years' duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4212555/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GOLDR study is a family-based study assessing diabetes and diabetic complications in families (siblings and/or parents) of a proband, defined as having type 2 diabetes and either known DR or a diabetes duration of ≥10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342> "A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years' duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22330960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25452868") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4212555/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are all Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin, recruited, and studied at the Los Angeles BioMedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center (HUMC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001342> "A family-based study of Latinos of Mexican or Central American origin in the Los Angeles area, run jointly by Cedars-Sinai Medical Center and the Los Angeles Biomedical Research Institute at Harbor-UCLA Medical Center, which from 2007 recruited probands with type 2 diabetes and either diabetic retinopathy or diabetes of at least ten years' duration together with their siblings and parents, with retinopathy graded from fundus photographs, to study the genetics of diabetic retinopathy and other complications of diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Broadly, there are 2 scientific arms to GP2, one centered in genetically complex, typical PD and the other in monogenic disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the most part, GP2 will use existing or ongoing patient and cohort collections and will work with established PD consortia; however, in some instances GP2 will support the collection of additional patients, particularly from underserved communities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Furthermore, this work will be extended, for the first time at scale, to underrepresented populations from around the world.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GP2 is the first supported resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's (ASAP) initiative, an audacious effort supporting PD research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is also worth noting that the majority of GP2 genotyping will be centered on persons with PD because abundant data on controls already exist; however, some of our genetic resources will be centered on generating genetic data in controls") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37633302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33513272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9290711/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will also generate whole‐genome sequence data from more than 10,000 individuals to determine the genetic cause in as yet unsolved monogenic cases and to generate much needed reference data sets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001343> "A worldwide programme, the first resource project of the Aligning Science Across Parkinson's initiative, that genotypes and sequences people with Parkinson's disease, and some controls, from existing and newly collected patient and cohort collections, working with established Parkinson's disease consortia and focusing on populations under-represented in genetic research, and shares the harmonised data to find genetic causes of and risk factors for typical and monogenic Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3606015/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, two independent populations of African descent ascertained through physician’s diagnosed asthma, have been recruited by a consortium entitled Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora (GRAAD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344> "A case-control collection of self-reported African American children and adults with physician-diagnosed asthma and non-asthmatic controls from the Baltimore–Washington, DC metropolitan area, brought together by the Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora consortium from eight NIH-funded asthma studies and one study of healthy African Americans, to study genetic contributions to asthma and its disparities in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3606015/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These subjects comprised the consortium for ‘Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora’ (GRAAD) and represent eight separate, NIH-funded studies of asthma in pediatric and adult African American populations, plus one study on healthy African Americans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344> "A case-control collection of self-reported African American children and adults with physician-diagnosed asthma and non-asthmatic controls from the Baltimore–Washington, DC metropolitan area, brought together by the Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora consortium from eight NIH-funded asthma studies and one study of healthy African Americans, to study genetic contributions to asthma and its disparities in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19910028+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We sought to test the hypothesis that some genes might contribute to the profound disparities in asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344> "A case-control collection of self-reported African American children and adults with physician-diagnosed asthma and non-asthmatic controls from the Baltimore–Washington, DC metropolitan area, brought together by the Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora consortium from eight NIH-funded asthma studies and one study of healthy African Americans, to study genetic contributions to asthma and its disparities in people of African descent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19910028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34536413") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.888/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng888_MOESM5_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora study consists of 498 asthma cases and 500 non-asthmatic controls from the Baltimore-Washington, D.C. metropolitan area who self-reported as African American.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001344> "A case-control collection of self-reported African American children and adults with physician-diagnosed asthma and non-asthmatic controls from the Baltimore–Washington, DC metropolitan area, brought together by the Genomic Research on Asthma in the African Diaspora consortium from eight NIH-funded asthma studies and one study of healthy African Americans, to study genetic contributions to asthma and its disparities in people of African descent.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26153726+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genomic Research in Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency and Sarcoidosis α1 Study is a prospective, multicenter, cross-sectional study of adults older than age 35 years with PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4627423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the lung microbiome is likely to have a critical role in the pathobiology of immunologic lung diseases such as sarcoidosis, the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute solicited applications for the Genomic Research in Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deﬁciency and Sarcoidosis (GRADS) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4627423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants with a conﬁrmed diagnosis of sarcoidosis undergo a baseline visit with self-administered questionnaires, chest computed tomography, pulmonary function tests, and blood and urine testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4627423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This multicenter study involves a collaborative effort of a Genomics Informatics Center (GIC) and seven clinical centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4627423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are conducting an observational cohort study to explore the role of microbiome and genomic regulation as they relate to speciﬁc sarcoidosis clinical phenotypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26153726") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35806883") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26193069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26193069+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genomic Research in Alpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency and Sarcoidosis (GRADS) study is an observational cohort study designed to explore the role of the lung microbiome and genome in these two diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001345> "A multicentre observational study in the United States, solicited by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute and run by a genomics and informatics centre with several clinical centres, that enrolled adults with sarcoidosis across defined clinical phenotypes and adults over 35 with the PiZZ or PiMZ alpha-1 antitrypsin genotypes, with questionnaires, chest CT, lung function tests, bronchoalveolar lavage and blood samples, to study the role of the lung microbiome and genome-wide gene expression in the two diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38146367") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3131268/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For that, we exploited the GRIV cohort, comprising subjects exhibiting extreme profiles of AIDS progression (LTNP, long-term non-progressors and RP, rapid progressors) [20], [22], [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38146367") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3664380/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 275 GRIV LTNP, defined by a CD4+ T-cell count above 500/μL for more than 8 years after HIV infection in absence of antiretroviral therapy, were compared to 1,352 HIV-1 seronegative individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38146367") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4569262/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Only white individuals of European descent living in France were eligible for enrolment to reduce confounding effects by population substructure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38146367") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4569262/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRIV cohort, established in 1995 in France, is a collection of DNA samples used to identify host genes associated with slow progression and with rapid progression to AIDS [7,10,52].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38146367") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26367535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4569262/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the Data from an Epidemiological Study on Insulin Resistance Syndrome (DESIR) program as a control group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001346> "A collection of DNA samples, established in France in 1995, from HIV-1-infected people of European descent living in France with extreme courses of infection: long-term non-progressors (infected for more than eight years with CD4 T-cell counts above 500/mm3 and no symptoms) and rapid progressors. It is used to identify host genes associated with slow and rapid progression to AIDS, with genetic analyses comparing its members with seronegative French controls from another study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17254403+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "About 1000 pairs of twins living close to the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center were invited for the first phenotyping examination, questionnaire administration and DNA collection in July and August 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23186635+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2006 onward, phenotype and DNA collection have been completed for more than 1,200 twin pairs and their parents or siblings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/guangzhou-twin-eye-study-2019-update/90C6A3D2A49870EAE5B24D73E37F1263") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At present, there are 1291 sets of twins enrolled, and 11 year’s follow-up visits were completed in 2018 (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32014069+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Progressive phenotypes, such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, have been collected annually.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32014069+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 2006, approximately 1300 pairs of twins, aged 7-15 years, were enrolled at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17254403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23186635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41117591") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32014069") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32014069+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the Guangzhou Twin Eye Study (GTES) is to explore the impact that genes and environmental inﬂuences have on common eye diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001347> "A longitudinal twin study in Guangzhou, China, that from 2006 enrolled twin pairs aged 7 to 15 years from the population-based Guangzhou Twin Registry, living near the Zhongshan Ophthalmic Center, together with some of their parents or siblings. It collected DNA and baseline eye measurements, then examined the twins annually until 2018 for progressive traits such as cycloplegic refraction, axial length, height and weight, to study the genetic and environmental causes of common eye diseases, particularly myopia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001348> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001348>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37524447") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37524447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://bjo.bmj.com/content/108/6/865") Annotation(rdfs:comment "enrolled participants from the Guangzhou cohort, performed the animal and in vitro experiments and the genotyping and sequencing experiments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001348> "A cohort of high myopes and hyperopes recruited in Guangzhou, China, one of three Chinese cohorts combined in a genome-wide association meta-analysis of ocular axial length.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37524447") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37524447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37524447+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study meta-analysis was conducted in totalling 2644 Chinese individuals from 3 cohorts: the Guangzhou cohort (GZ, 537 high myopes and 151 hyperopes), Wenzhou cohort (334 high myopes and 6 hyperopes) and Guangzhou Twin Eye Study (1051 participants with normally distributed AL).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001348> "A cohort of high myopes and hyperopes recruited in Guangzhou, China, one of three Chinese cohorts combined in a genome-wide association meta-analysis of ocular axial length.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were histopathologically confirmed patients with CRC recruited from Sun Yat-Sen University Cancer Center between January 2002 and January 2012 and controls were cancer-free men and women recruited from the physical examination centers of several large hospitals in Guangdong during the same time period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in Guangzhou-1 (n = 1,603) were included in stage 1, Guangzhou-2 (n = 809) and Guangzhou-3 (n = 2,408) in stage 2 and Guangzhou-4 (n = 1,791) in stage 4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Guangzhou CRC Study: This study consisted of four case-control collections, Guangzhou- 1, Guangzhou-2, Guangzhou-3 and Guangzhou-4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24836286+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a genome-wide association study of CRC in East Asians with 14,963 cases and 31,945 controls and identified 6 new loci associated with CRC risk") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4068797/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, stage 1 (GWAS discovery) consisted of five studies: Shanghai CRC Study 1 (Shanghai-1, n = 3,102), Shanghai CRC Study 2 (Shanghai-2, n = 908), Guangzhou CRC Study 1 (Guangzhou-1, n = 1,603), Aichi CRC Study 1 (Aichi-1, n =1,346), and Korean Cancer Prevention Study-II CRC (KCPS-II, n = 1,301).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10545678/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "| Guangzhou1 | 638 | 971 |  | Guangzhou CRC Study | Case-control | China |") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001349> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer in Guangzhou, China. Its cases are patients with histopathologically confirmed colorectal cancer recruited at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center between 2002 and 2012, and its controls are cancer-free men and women recruited in the same period from the physical examination centres of several large hospitals in Guangdong. Its four case-control collections (Guangzhou-1 to Guangzhou-4) were genotyped for genome-wide association studies of colorectal cancer in East Asians.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11075607+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HGDS is a multicenter study of the growth and development, neurological, neuropsychological, and immune functioning of a cohort of children and adolescents, 62% of whom were infected with HIV through the use of clotting factor concentrates, and their non-hemophiliac, non-HIV infected male siblings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-023-06370-4/MediaObjects/41586_2023_6370_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were prospectively collected in 14 U.S. hemophilia treatment centers through 1996/97.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-023-06370-4/MediaObjects/41586_2023_6370_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HGDS is a multicenter study of hemophilia and its complications that was established in 1988.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8498644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data are being collected from a group of non-HIV infected non-hemophiliac siblings for comparison.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8498644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sixty-nine percent (n = 333) of a population of males between the ages of 6 and 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia participated in a comprehensive baseline examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11075607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8498644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8498644+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study design, research questions, and baseline data are presented from a multicenter longitudinal epidemiologic investigation of the impact of human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection on three areas of functioning in children and adolescents with hemophilia: physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001350> "A multicentre longitudinal study, established in 1988 at 14 hemophilia treatment centres in the United States, of boys and young men aged 6 to 19 years with moderate to severe hemophilia, HIV-infected through clotting factor concentrates or HIV-uninfected, with their non-hemophiliac, HIV-uninfected male siblings as a comparison group, followed until 1996/97 to study the impact of HIV on physical growth and sexual maturation, immune function, and neurological and neuropsychological functioning.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20843863") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20843863+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The health status of nonparticipants in a population-based health study: the Hordaland Health Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11053069/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1997–99, previous participants born 1950–51 and 1925–27 were reinvited, in addition to all residents in Hordaland County born 1953–57.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11053069/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hordaland Health Study (HUSK) is a community-based study in Western Norway conducted as a collaboration between the University of Bergen, the Norwegian Health Screening Service and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland (https://husk-en.w.uib.no/)53. In 1992–93 and 1997–99 participants were invited based on year of birth and site of residence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(rdfs:comment "I 2018 startet HUSK3 som et samarbeid mellom Universitetet i Bergen og Helse Bergen HF. Tannhelsetenesta kompetansesenter – TkVestland er også samarbeidspartner. Denne gangen inviteres kun kvinner / menn født 1950-51 som deltok i både HUSK1 og HUSK2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hordaland Health Studies (HHS) were conducted in 1992/93 (The Homocysteine study) and in 1997/99 (HUSK).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671141") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://husk.w.uib.no") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://husk-en.w.uib.no/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main focus of the studies is on chronic diseases including cadiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001351> "A population-based health study of residents of Hordaland County in Western Norway, begun in 1992-93 as the Hordaland Homocysteine Study by the Norwegian Health Screening Service, the University of Bergen and the Municipal Health Service in Hordaland, which invited residents by year of birth and place of residence, re-examined part of them together with further birth cohorts in 1997-99, and since 2018 has re-examined those born in 1950-51 who took part in both surveys, to study chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, cancer, osteoporosis, anxiety and depression and their prevention.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257606/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the participating children were ethnic Chinese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257606/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HKCES was designed to determine the occurrence and development of eye disorders, including refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia, and allergic disease, and to identify their environmental and genetic determinants11–13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257606/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The schools in each cluster region were randomly assigned an invitation priority according to the ranking numbers generated by computer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8257606/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study subjects were recruited from the Hong Kong Children Eye Study (HKCES)7–10, which is a population-based cohort study of eye conditions among children aged 6–8 years old in Hong Kong.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9856878/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Hong Kong Children Eye Study, an ongoing population-based cohort study on eye conditions in children aged 6 to 8 years recruited from primary schools in Hong Kong.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31981300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34226578") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36542383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36542383+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This population-based, cross-sectional study included participants from familial trios, each comprising a child aged 6 to 8 years and both parents, recruited from the Hong Kong Children Eye Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001352> "A population-based cohort study of eye conditions, run by the Chinese University of Hong Kong since 2015, that recruits ethnic Chinese children aged 6 to 8 years from randomly selected primary schools across Hong Kong, together with their parents, and follows the children up, to determine the occurrence and development of refractive errors, strabismus, amblyopia and other eye disorders and their environmental and genetic determinants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11732878/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals were invited for participation and prospective follow-up at the time of their regular structured assessment of risk factors, biochemical control and presence of diabetes complications, based on the modified European DIABCARE protocol [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11732878/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initiated in 2014, the HKDB enrolled participants from 11 diabetes centres at major public hospitals across Hong Kong using similar enrolment and assessment methods, aiming to establish a multicentre diabetes register and biobank for biomarker discovery using a transomics approach [12], as well as a platform to validate and compare known biomarkers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11732878/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Once enrolled, participants were prospectively followed until their death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11732878/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HKDB is a multicentre prospective cohort study co-ordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong (NCT05282680).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11732878/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HKDB was set up using a similar design to that of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register (HKDR), established at the Prince of Wales Hospital (PWH) and the Chinese University of Hong Kong in 1995, with regular comprehensive assessment of diabetes-related risk factors and also comprehensive screening of diabetes complications, as previously described [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32722720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39508878") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT05282680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7893928/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hong Kong Diabetes Biobank (HKDB) was established as a territory-wide diabetes registry and biobank for large-scale replication of genetic and epigenetic markers identified in the project since 2014") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001353> "A multicentre prospective cohort and biobank of adults with diabetes, started in 2014 and coordinated by the Chinese University of Hong Kong, which enrols people attending routine diabetes complication assessment at the diabetes centres of major public hospitals across Hong Kong, with the assessment methods of the Hong Kong Diabetes Register, and follows them for diabetes-related outcomes, to serve as a territory-wide diabetes register and biobank for epidemiological research and for the discovery and replication of genetic, epigenetic and other biomarkers of diabetes and its complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12561000/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood and serum specimens from the participants were collected at the enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354> "A newly established community-based prospective cohort in Zhejiang Province, China, which since June 2021 has been enrolling participants from urban and rural areas at several project sites, among them people attending routine physical examinations, and collecting blood and serum at enrolment.")
