AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12561000/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HOPE Cohort is a newly established community-based prospective cohort enrolling participants from both urban and rural areas in Zhejiang Province, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354> "A newly established community-based prospective cohort in Zhejiang Province, China, which since June 2021 has been enrolling participants from urban and rural areas at several project sites, among them people attending routine physical examinations, and collecting blood and serum at enrolment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13444103/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were drawn from one project site of the Healthy Zhejiang One Million People Cohort (HOPE), a newly established prospective cohort initiated in Zhejiang Province, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354> "A newly established community-based prospective cohort in Zhejiang Province, China, which since June 2021 has been enrolling participants from urban and rural areas at several project sites, among them people attending routine physical examinations, and collecting blood and serum at enrolment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40728933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42324270") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13444103/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline survey at this project site was conducted in the Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University School of Medicine, where individuals undergoing routine physical examinations were enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001354> "A newly established community-based prospective cohort in Zhejiang Province, China, which since June 2021 has been enrolling participants from urban and rural areas at several project sites, among them people attending routine physical examinations, and collecting blood and serum at enrolment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5914782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A major strength of the H-PEACE study is its structured and organised database, which not only includes data widely used in medical check-ups but also data from sophisticated high-quality advanced examinations, such as colonoscopy, brain MRI, abdominal CT and abdominal fat CT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5914782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 91 336 health examinees were included in the cohort, and we repeatedly measured and collected information for 50.9% (n=46 484) of the cohort members.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5914782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The H-PEACE study collected data from 91 336 Koreans aged 45.5±11.7 years (50 507 men and 40 829 women) who received a health check-up between October 2003 and December 2014 at the SNUH Gangnam Center") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5914782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Health and Prevention Enhancement (H-PEACE) study was designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results, biomarkers and the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases (NCDs), such as malignancies and metabolic diseases, in an average-risk population in Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5914782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Under the passive follow-up systems, >99% of participants are followed up for their new cancer development and death annually.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29674364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29674364+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Health and Prevention Enhancement (H-PEACE): a retrospective, population-based cohort study conducted at the Seoul National University Hospital Gangnam Center, Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001355> "A retrospective, population-based cohort of Koreans who had health check-ups at the Healthcare System Gangnam Center of Seoul National University Hospital in Seoul, South Korea, from October 2003, with repeated check-up data, advanced diagnostic imaging and record linkage for cancer and death, designed to investigate the association of diagnostic imaging results and biomarkers with the predisease stage of non-communicable diseases such as cancers and metabolic diseases in an average-risk population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3001778") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All determinations were centralized (Verona General Hos- pital, Central Laboratory).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3001778") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the INCIPE study 6200 patients, all Caucasians, ⱖ40-years old by January 1, 2006, were randomly chosen from the lists of patients of 62 randomly selected general practitioners (GPs) based in four geographical areas in the Veneto region, NE Italy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3001778") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The albumin to creatinine ratio in urine and estimated GFR from calibrated creatinine (SCr) were determined.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3001778") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To assess the prevalence of CKD in Italy, in 2006, in NE Italy, we launched the “INCIPE” study (Initiative on Nephropathy, of relevance to public health, which is Chronic, possibly in its Initial stages, and carries a Potential risk of major clinical End- points).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC9972819") Annotation(rdfs:comment "randomly selected general practitioners sited in four geographical areas (Verona,two in Padova,Venice) in the Veneto") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20813860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21711121") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36865011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9972819/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two independent subgroups of individuals of the INCIPE cohort were previously genotyped using either the Illumina Human Omni Express chip array (893 individuals, INCIPE-1) [13] or the Illumina Human Core Exome chip array (2153 individuals, INCIPE-2) [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001356> "A population-based survey of Caucasian adults aged 40 years or older, randomly selected in 2006 from the patient lists of randomly chosen general practitioners in four areas of the Veneto region (Verona, Padova and Venice) in north-eastern Italy, with centralised laboratory measurement of kidney function and albuminuria, set up at the University of Verona to determine the prevalence of chronic kidney disease and its risk factors; two subsets of its participants were genotyped for genetic studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8715184") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As an independent reference dataset, we obtained 1,345 clinically ascertained developmental stuttering patients (965 male and 380 female) collected from Curtin University Stuttering Center in Perth, Australia, the SpeechMatters Clinic in Dublin, Ireland, the Stuttering Research Laboratory at the University of Pittsburgh,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8756529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ISP cases and controls were genotyped using the Illumina Expanded Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array (MEGAex) at Vanderbilt University Medical Center’s core facility, VANTAGE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8756529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ISP comprises 1,345 clinically ascertained developmental stuttering cases collected from the Curtin Stuttering Treatment Clinic in Perth, Australia; the SpeechMatters Clinic and the Irish Stammering Association, in Dublin, Ireland; the National Stuttering Association, USA; online recruitment on reddit.com;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41105951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12614926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established in 2020, the International Stuttering Project (ISP) is an international collaboration of scientists and speech-language pathologists who specialize in stuttering, many of whom run clinics, practices, and therapy centers for stuttering.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Formed in 2020, the ISP continues to collate global outbred populations of people who stutter, specifically to illuminate genetic etiology and broaden investigations of its diverse and variable phenotype.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34861174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35047858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.theinternationalstutteringproject.com/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We are continually recruiting study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001357> "A continually recruiting collection of people with clinically ascertained developmental stuttering, assembled by the International Stuttering Project, a collaboration of researchers and clinicians in the United States, Australia and Ireland formed in 2020 to illuminate the genetic aetiology of stuttering, which recruits through stuttering clinics, research laboratories and stuttering associations in these countries and online and genotypes its participants at Vanderbilt University Medical Center.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15364185+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The relation of smoking, history of hypertension or diabetes, waist/hip ratio, dietary patterns, physical activity, consumption of alcohol, blood apolipoproteins (Apo), and psychosocial factors to myocardial infarction are reported here.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15364185+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, the effect of such factors on risk of coronary heart disease in most regions of the world is unknown.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15364185+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established a standardised case-control study of acute myocardial infarction in 52 countries, representing every inhabited continent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15364186+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used a case-control design with 11119 patients with a first myocardial infarction and 13648 age-matched (up to 5 years older or younger) and sex-matched controls from 262 centres in Asia, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, Australia, and North and South America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident acute MI, presenting to a hospital within 24 hours of symptom Age and sex matched hospital and community based, with no Nature Genetics: doi:10.1038/ng.2480 30 onset previous diagnosis of heart disease or history of exertional chest pain") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15364186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37414411") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10361015/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The INTERHEART study was a standardized case–control study involving 11 931 cases of first acute MI and 14 260 controls from 52 countries on 6 continents enrolled between February 1999 and March 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001358> "A standardised case-control study of first acute myocardial infarction, which from February 1999 to March 2003 enrolled patients presenting to hospital with a first myocardial infarction and age- and sex-matched hospital- or community-based controls without heart disease at 262 centres in 52 countries on every inhabited continent, to establish the importance of modifiable and psychosocial risk factors for myocardial infarction in all regions of the world.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ITHGC includes 12 case–control GWAS from nine countries in Europe, Africa, and Asia (total of 14,153 pulmonary TB cases and 19,536 healthy controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359> "A consortium established to study the host genetics of tuberculosis through collaborative, equitable data sharing, combining case-control genome-wide association studies from nine countries across Europe, Africa and Asia in a multi-ancestry meta-analysis of tuberculosis susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address these challenges, we established the International Tuberculosis Host Genetics Consortium (ITHGC) to study the host genetics of disease through collaborative and equitable data sharing (Naranbhai, 2016).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359> "A consortium established to study the host genetics of tuberculosis through collaborative, equitable data sharing, combining case-control genome-wide association studies from nine countries across Europe, Africa and Asia in a multi-ancestry meta-analysis of tuberculosis susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38224499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10789494/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established the International Tuberculosis Host Genetics Consortium to perform a multi-ancestry meta-analysis of GWAS, including 14,153 cases and 19,536 controls of African, Asian, and European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001359> "A consortium established to study the host genetics of tuberculosis through collaborative, equitable data sharing, combining case-control genome-wide association studies from nine countries across Europe, Africa and Asia in a multi-ancestry meta-analysis of tuberculosis susceptibility.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5886212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants from this study were collected with approval from the Institutional review board of Indiana University IRB00000222; Protocol number 1409306349.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5886212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "US sample consists of 743 unrelated volunteers (498 females, 245 males) recruited in the USA, who were of European (98%), and non-European ancestry (2% South American/South Asian/Middle Eastern).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00741-7/MediaObjects/41588_2020_741_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similar to the PSU sample cohort, no restrictions were placed on the recruitment of participants") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00741-7/MediaObjects/41588_2020_741_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IUPUI sample includes 3D images and genotypic data from individuals recruited in Indianapolis, IN and Twinsburg, OH (IUPUI IRB 1409306349). Participants self-reported information on age, height, weight, and ancestry at the time of the collection. Individuals who were below 18 years of age were included if they had a parent or legal guardian’s signature.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7796995/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The US samples originated from the 3D Facial Norms cohort55 (3DFN) and studies at the Pennsylvania State University (PSU) and Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis (IUPUI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29220522") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33288918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33692830") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7937973/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IUPUI personnel, data collection, and analyses were supported by the National Institute of Justice") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001360> "A collection of 3D facial images, self-reported age, height, weight and ancestry, and DNA from volunteers recruited without restriction on ancestry (minors with a parent's or guardian's consent) in Indianapolis, Indiana and in Twinsburg, Ohio under one Indiana University-Purdue University Indianapolis ethics protocol, with support from the US National Institute of Justice, and genotyped to study the genetics of facial shape and of other visible traits such as head hair shape.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18330919+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, PharmGKB has embraced a new role--broker of pharmacogenomic data for data sharing consortia. In particular, we have helped create the International Warfarin Pharmacogenetics Consortium (IWPC), which is devoted to pooling genotype and phenotype data relevant to the anticoagulant warfarin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2722908") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Warfarin Pharmacogenetics Consortium comprises 21 research groups from 9 countries and 4 continents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2722908") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The research groups contributed clinical and genetic data for a total of 5700 patients who were treated with warfarin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2722908") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These data were curated (i.e., collected, formatted, and subjected to quality control) by staff at the Pharmacogenetics and Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB, www.pharmgkb.org) and by members of the consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19228618+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed and used an algorithm for estimating the appropriate warfarin dose that is based on both clinical and genetic data from a broad population base.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18330919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19228618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20203262") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23755828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3759580/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples from African-American adults (aged ≥18 years) who were taking a stable maintenance dose of warfarin were obtained at International Warfarin Pharmacogenetics Consortium (IWPC) sites and the University of Alabama at Birmingham (Birmingham, AL, USA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001361> "A consortium of research groups in North and South America, Europe and Asia, formed with the Pharmacogenomics Knowledge Base (PharmGKB) as its data broker, that pools and curates the clinical and genetic data of warfarin-treated patients from its members' centres, to develop and evaluate pharmacogenetic algorithms for estimating the stable warfarin dose and to study the genetic determinants of warfarin dose across populations, including a genome-wide association study of African Americans from its US sites.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15345109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26082817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8909613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KARBAC1 (n = 394) is a hospital cohort of consecutive breast cancer cases recruited from October 1998 until May 2000 [21].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362> "A breast cancer case-control study in Stockholm, Sweden, whose cases are consecutive breast cancer patients treated at the oncology departments of Huddinge and Söder hospitals from 1998 to 2000 and women with familial breast cancer without BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations seen at the Department of Clinical Genetics of Karolinska University Hospital from 2000, and whose controls are blood donors from the same region, used to study inherited susceptibility to breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15345109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26082817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8909613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KARBAC2 (n = 109) is a BRCA1- and BRCA2 negative breast cancer cohort recruited from a clinical genetic counselling department from February 2000 until January 2012 [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362> "A breast cancer case-control study in Stockholm, Sweden, whose cases are consecutive breast cancer patients treated at the oncology departments of Huddinge and Söder hospitals from 1998 to 2000 and women with familial breast cancer without BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations seen at the Department of Clinical Genetics of Karolinska University Hospital from 2000, and whose controls are blood donors from the same region, used to study inherited susceptibility to breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15345109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26082817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8909613/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we were prompted to reanalyze two Swedish breast cancer cohorts—KARMA and KARBAC—consisting of 3200 invasive breast cancer cases and 5021 controls previously analyzed within the BCAC consortium [8,9,10,16,17,18,19].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362> "A breast cancer case-control study in Stockholm, Sweden, whose cases are consecutive breast cancer patients treated at the oncology departments of Huddinge and Söder hospitals from 1998 to 2000 and women with familial breast cancer without BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations seen at the Department of Clinical Genetics of Karolinska University Hospital from 2000, and whose controls are blood donors from the same region, used to study inherited susceptibility to breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15345109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24943594") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26082817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35267517") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KARBAC Karolinska Breast Cancer Study Sweden 1. Familial cases from Department of Clinical Genetics, Karolinska University Hospital , Stockholm. 2. Consecutive cases from Department of Oncology, Huddinge & Söder Hospital, Stockholm 1998-2000. Blood donors of mixed gender from same geographical region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001362> "A breast cancer case-control study in Stockholm, Sweden, whose cases are consecutive breast cancer patients treated at the oncology departments of Huddinge and Söder hospitals from 1998 to 2000 and women with familial breast cancer without BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations seen at the Department of Clinical Genetics of Karolinska University Hospital from 2000, and whose controls are blood donors from the same region, used to study inherited susceptibility to breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of these initial 1,727 participants who were enrolled in this study, 56 individuals with an incomplete semiquantitative food frequency questionnaire (SQFFQ) and 15 individuals with an implausible total energy intake (< 500 or > 4,000 kcal/day) were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases were recruited among patients who were diagnosed with early GC within the preceding 3 months with confirmed invasive carcinoma in the CGC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group comprised individuals who underwent health screening check-ups at the CCPD at the same hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The genotyping was performed using an Affymetrix Axiom® Exome 319 Array containing 318,983 SNPs (Affymetrix Inc., Santa Clara, CA, USA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7902036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-control study was conducted at the Center for Gastric Cancer (CGC) and the Center for Cancer Prevention & Detection (CCPD) of the National Cancer Center (NCC) in Korea between March 2011 and December 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33634021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37340842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38810984") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38810984+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dietary mercury intake, the IL23R rs10889677 polymorphism, and the risk of gastric cancer in a Korean population: a hospital-based case-control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001363> "A hospital-based case-control study of gastric cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, that from March 2011 to December 2014 recruited patients recently diagnosed with gastric cancer at its Center for Gastric Cancer as cases and cancer-free people attending health-screening check-ups at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection as controls, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and blood DNA genotyped on an exome array, to study dietary and genetic risk factors for gastric cancer.")

