AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2985/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng2985_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Korean-National Cancer Center CRC Study: This study (Korea-NCC) is a hospital- based case-control study of CRC conducted in South Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24836286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4068797/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage 4 consisted of five studies: Guangzhou CRC Study 4 (Guangzhou-4, n = 1,791), Aichi CRC Study 2 (Aichi-2, n = 708), Korean-National Cancer Center CRC Study (Korea-NCC, n = 2,721), Seoul CRC Study (Korea-Seoul, n = 1,522), and Hwasun Cancer Epidemiology Study-Colon and Rectum Cancer (HCES-CRC, n = 7,930).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "290 participants were excluded due to incomplete data from the semiquantitative food frequency questionnaire (SQFFQ) or general questionnaire") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were defined as those who newly diagnosed with CRC between August 2010 and September 2020 at the Center for Colorectal Cancer of the NCC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369566/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were selected from people visiting the Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection at the same hospital for the health check-up program provided by the National Health Insurance Cooperation from October 2007 to December 2022.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30529582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765848") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38514198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38514198+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotyping was performed using an Illumina MEGA-Expanded Array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001364> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer at the National Cancer Center in Goyang, South Korea, whose cases are patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at its Center for Colorectal Cancer from 2010 and whose controls are people attending the national health check-up programme at its Center for Cancer Prevention and Detection, with lifestyle and food-frequency questionnaires and genome-wide genotyping, contributing to the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's studies of genetic susceptibility to colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30514630+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were randomly assigned in a 1:1:1:1 ratio to receive 0.05%, 0.025%, and 0.01% atropine eye drops, or placebo eye drop, respectively, once nightly to both eyes for 1 year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41525-025-00504-5/MediaObjects/41525_2025_504_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LAMP is a randomized, placebo-controlled, double-masked trial, which aims to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low- concentration atropine eye drops at different concentrations. This study was conducted from January 2016 to November 2017 at the CUHK Eye Centre of the Chinese University of Hong Kong, Hong Kong, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12925536/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, children aged 4 to 12 years with a myopic refractive error of at least –1.0 diopter (D) in both eyes, astigmatism of <2.5 D, and documented myopic progression of ≥0.5 D in the previous year were enrolled in the LAMP trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12925536/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase II (i.e., the second year), all children in the placebo group of phase I were switched over to receive 0.05% atropine eye drops at the beginning of the second year until the end of the fifth year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12925536/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase III (i.e., the third year), the children in each of the 3 original treatment groups of phase II (0.05%, 0.025%, and 0.01% atropine eye drops) were randomized in a 1:1 ratio into (a) a continued treatment subgroup and (b) a treatment cessation subgroup.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30514630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40410244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41732593") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12925536/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While children from the LAMP study had been followed up for 5 years, all participants in the continued treatment groups from the originally studied concentration were switched to 0.05% atropine after the third year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001365> "A randomised, double-masked, placebo-controlled trial at the Chinese University of Hong Kong Eye Centre that from 2016 to 2017 enrolled children aged 4 to 12 with myopia in both eyes, limited astigmatism and documented myopic progression in the previous year, assigned them to nightly 0.05%, 0.025% or 0.01% atropine eye drops or placebo, and followed them in later phases (placebo switched to atropine, re-randomisation to continued treatment or washout, and longer-term follow-up), to evaluate the efficacy and safety of low-concentration atropine for slowing myopia progression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04491344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10350850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the obesity-enriched Leipzig Childhood Obesity Cohort (recruited from the local obesity outpatient clinic, IRB-Nr: 007/04, NCT04491344)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> "An obesity-enriched cohort of children and adolescents from the Leipzig area, Germany, recruited through the paediatric obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center and run by its Center for Pediatric Research, with oral glucose tolerance tests, serum and DNA samples collected at clinic visits and regular follow-up, some into adulthood, to identify genetic variants and biomarkers underlying childhood obesity and its metabolic consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04491344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12575610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children and adolescents from the area around Leipzig were referred to the obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center for evaluation and treatment of overweight/obesity and included in the study with subsequent regular follow-ups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> "An obesity-enriched cohort of children and adolescents from the Leipzig area, Germany, recruited through the paediatric obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center and run by its Center for Pediatric Research, with oral glucose tolerance tests, serum and DNA samples collected at clinic visits and regular follow-up, some into adulthood, to identify genetic variants and biomarkers underlying childhood obesity and its metabolic consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04491344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12575610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from an adulthood follow-up of the Leipzig childhood obesity cohort (N = 209, mean age at follow-up 24.9 years) were analyzed and related to the respective childhood data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> "An obesity-enriched cohort of children and adolescents from the Leipzig area, Germany, recruited through the paediatric obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center and run by its Center for Pediatric Research, with oral glucose tolerance tests, serum and DNA samples collected at clinic visits and regular follow-up, some into adulthood, to identify genetic variants and biomarkers underlying childhood obesity and its metabolic consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04491344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9771800/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the type of mutation escapes standard genetic screening algorithms, we rescreened the Leipzig Childhood Obesity cohort of 1,745 patients and identified four additional patients with the identical mutation, ectopic ASIP expression and a similar phenotype.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> "An obesity-enriched cohort of children and adolescents from the Leipzig area, Germany, recruited through the paediatric obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center and run by its Center for Pediatric Research, with oral glucose tolerance tests, serum and DNA samples collected at clinic visits and regular follow-up, some into adulthood, to identify genetic variants and biomarkers underlying childhood obesity and its metabolic consequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37465325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41168416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT04491344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7581004/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LEIPZIG childhood obesity cohort/LIFE Child Obesity is an obesity enriched subset with additional metabolic and cardiovascular phenotyping including OGTT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001366> "An obesity-enriched cohort of children and adolescents from the Leipzig area, Germany, recruited through the paediatric obesity outpatient clinic of Leipzig University Medical Center and run by its Center for Pediatric Research, with oral glucose tolerance tests, serum and DNA samples collected at clinic visits and regular follow-up, some into adulthood, to identify genetic variants and biomarkers underlying childhood obesity and its metabolic consequences.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11282926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients from the LORD cohort provided written informed consent to participate in our local biobank") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11282926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data including demographics, pathology report, surgical procedure and self-reported smoking history at the time of surgery were collected in a local database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11282926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LORD consists of a single site case-only cohort based on a 20-year data collection (1999–2021) of patients who underwent lung cancer surgery at IUCPQ-UL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11282926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung Oncology Research & Discovery (LORD) is an ongoing translational research program towards precision medicine in lung cancer diagnosis, management and treatment conducted at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (IUCPQ-UL or “Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec—Université Laval”), located in Quebec City, Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11282926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung cancer diagnosis was confirmed by pathological examination using resected specimens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38970920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40209611") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40209611+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Frequency of targetable genetic alterations in resectable lung adenocarcinoma: Results from the LORD project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001367> "An ongoing single-site, case-only cohort of patients who have undergone lung cancer surgery since 1999 at the Quebec Heart and Lung Institute (Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval) in Quebec City, Canada, with diagnoses confirmed by pathology of the resected specimens, clinical data and consent to the institute's biobank, assembled by a translational research programme towards precision medicine in lung cancer and used for germline genetic and tumour molecular studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3300281+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By the time of the participants' initial evaluation (April 1984-April 1985), infection with the human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) had occurred in higher proportions of men in Los Angeles (51%) and Chicago (43%) than in Baltimore/Washington, DC (31%) and Pittsburgh (21%)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3300281+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nearly 5,000 homosexual men volunteered for semiannual interview, physical examination, and laboratory testing in four metropolitan areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A3300281+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study was designed to elucidate the natural history of the infection causing acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS), identify risk factors for occurrence and clinical expression of the infection, and establish a repository of biologic specimens for future study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8484936") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2019, the National Institutes of Health combined the Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study (MACS) and the Women’s Interagency HIV Study (WIHS) into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study (MWCCS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8484936/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MACS targeted enrollment of men who have sex with men (MSM), with initial enrollment during 1984–1985 in 4 cities across the United States (2) and additional enrollment waves in 1987–1990 and 2001–2003, and limited replenishment enrollment from 2010 to 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:3300281") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33675224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-023-06370-4/MediaObjects/41586_2023_6370_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Multicenter AIDS Cohort Study (MACS) is an ongoing prospective study of the natural and treated histories of HIV-1 infection in homosexual and bisexual men conducted by sites located in Baltimore, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001368> "A prospective multicentre cohort study of gay and bisexual men with and without HIV-1 infection, first enrolled in 1984–1985 at sites in Baltimore/Washington DC, Chicago, Pittsburgh and Los Angeles in the United States, with later enrolment waves, and followed with interviews, physical examinations, laboratory testing and specimen banking every six months, to study the natural and treated history of HIV infection and AIDS and its risk factors; in 2019 it was combined with the Women's Interagency HIV Study into the MACS/WIHS Combined Cohort Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6585285/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The service was delivered by the lung cancer team at Wythenshawe Hospital, Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, in partnership with Alliance Medical.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6585285/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Manchester, we developed a community-based ‘Lung Health Check’ (LHC) approach to target high-risk smokers in deprived areas. LHCs were nurse-led and included calculation of lung cancer risk using the PLCOM2012 risk model.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6585285/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, ever smokers aged 55–74 at participating general practices (n=14) were invited to a LHC; this consisted of 6-year lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOM2012), symptom assessment, smoking cessation advice and spirometry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35430354+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Manchester Lung Health Check (LHC) programme invited ever smokers, age 55-80, to a lung cancer risk assessment in which their 6-year risk was calculated (using the PLCOM2012 model).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The M-LHC was a pilot of community-based targeted lung cancer screening for ever-smokers aged 55–74 invited by letter from 14 primary care practices in socioeconomically deprived parts of Manchester, commencing in 2016. Free Lung Health Checks were offered on mobile units, during which lung cancer risk assessments and LDCT screening were performed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30420406") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35430354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40046247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11880782/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Manchester Lung Health Check (M-LHC) pilot was based in areas of high socio-economic deprivation and offered annual LDCT screening to individuals at high risk. In this study, both high risk, screened (PLCOm2012 6-year ≥1.51%) and low risk, unscreened (PLCOm2012<1.51%) M-LHC participants were followed systematically for lung cancer occurrence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001369> "A community-based targeted lung cancer screening programme in socioeconomically deprived areas of Manchester, England, run by Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust, which began as a pilot in 2016 and continued in later programmes. It invites ever-smokers registered with local general practices (aged 55–74 in the pilot, 55–80 later) to a nurse-led Lung Health Check on mobile units, with lung cancer risk calculation (PLCOm2012), symptom assessment, spirometry and smoking cessation advice, offers annual low-dose CT screening to those at high risk, and follows attendees for lung cancer outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963733/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A questionnaire on sociodemographic information, cardiovascular health history, physical activity, lifestyle, past medical history and family history, was given to each participant at the time of consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963733/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a step towards identifying novel genetic and circulating biomarkers, we describe our approach to create an electronic medical record (EMR)-linked vascular disease-specific biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963733/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutive adult patients with known or suspected CAS, AAA, or PAD, referred for non-invasive vascular ultrasound or lower extremity arterial evaluation, were approached for participation in the biorepository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24689004+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AVD phenotypes, relevant risk factors and comorbid conditions were ascertained by electronic medical record (EMR)-based electronic algorithms that included diagnosis and procedure codes, laboratory data and text searches to ascertain medication use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24689004+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vascular Disease Biorepository at Mayo Clinic was established to archive DNA, plasma, and serum from patients with suspected AVD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24689004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26343387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mayo Vascular Disease Biorepository (VDB) at the Mayo Clinic was established to archive DNA, plasma, and serum from patients with suspected atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) referred for noninvasive vascular evaluation and exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center from January 14, 2006 to July 24, 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001370> "An electronic medical record-linked biorepository at Mayo Clinic, begun in 2006, that archives DNA, plasma and serum and a questionnaire from consecutive adult patients with known or suspected atherosclerotic vascular disease (such as carotid artery stenosis, abdominal aortic aneurysm or peripheral arterial disease) referred for non-invasive vascular evaluation or exercise stress testing at the Mayo Clinic Gonda Vascular Center, ascertaining disease and comorbidities with electronic phenotyping algorithms, to discover genetic and circulating biomarkers of atherosclerotic vascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Before new patients are recruited to the Biobank, a Biobank Technician will take informed consent from patients to use theirsurplus tissue and data about them for research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Biobank will collect tissue, blood and other samples from patients admitted to hospitals in the Greater Manchester area, who are undergoing an operation to remove tissue where cancer is a possible diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At most sites, sample collection is primarily focussed on patients undergoing surgery where surplus tissue can be collected in addition to matched blood and other fluid samples, such as urine or other fluids.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established in 2008, the MCRC Biobank has transformed the way biological samples are collected and supplied for ground-breaking cancer research projects within the Manchester Cancer Research Centre and beyond.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Regulated under The Christie NHS Foundation Trust Human Tissue Authority Licence for Research, the MCRC Biobank maintains the highest standards of regulatory compliance with respect to patient consent, secure sample storage and sample tractability whilst a robust Access Policy ensures that samples are released for high quality scientific research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/manchester-cancer-research-centre-biobank-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mcrc.manchester.ac.uk/research/mcrc-biobank/about-the-mcrc-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MCRC Biobank brings together organised tissue, blood and other sample collection across four NHS Trusts under one centralised infrastructure and governance framework, to facilitate the provision of samples of highest quality as efficiently as possible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001371> "A research tissue bank of the Manchester Cancer Research Centre, established in 2008 and run from The Christie NHS Foundation Trust, that collects tissue, blood and other samples, with consent to use them and data about the donors for research, from patients at four NHS trusts in Greater Manchester, mainly people undergoing surgery where cancer is a possible diagnosis, to supply samples for cancer research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4566921/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, melanoma patients were recruited between 1992 and 2011 through a nationwide network of French Dermatology Departments and Oncogenetic clinics that constitute the French Melanoma Study Group and MELARISK collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4566921/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information on demographic and clinical characteristics, family history of melanoma and known melanoma risk factors was collected through interview and clinical examination, extraction of medical records and by completing a questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4566921/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MELARISK patients were histologically confirmed melanoma cases of European ancestry who had been enrolled for the presence of family history of melanoma, multiple primaries and/or diagnosis before 40 years of age, in order to enrich the case series for genetic susceptibility.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4566921/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based controls were recruited from the same various parts of France as the cases and had genotyping data provided by the Centre National de Génotypage (CNG, Evry, France).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4566921/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This analysis strategy was applied to two large case-control studies of melanoma with genome-wide SNP data: the French MELARISK study, that comprised of 3,976 subjects of European-ancestry, and served as the discovery dataset") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25892537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32341527") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27347659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5116391/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MELARISK study comprised of 1,244 European-ancestry melanoma cases who were recruited through a nationwide network of French Dermatology Departments and Oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001372> "A French study of genetic susceptibility to cutaneous melanoma that recruited histologically confirmed melanoma patients of European ancestry, enrolled for a family history of melanoma, multiple primary melanomas or diagnosis before age 40, through a nationwide network of French dermatology departments and oncogenetic clinics between 1992 and 2011, with interview, clinical examination and questionnaire data on melanoma risk factors; in genome-wide association studies its cases were compared with population-based French controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2929328/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this cohort all HCV-seropositive individuals with hemophilia, aged 13 years or older, at one of the 52 participating hemophilia treatment centers, were invited to participate between April 2001 and April 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2929328/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MHCS-II is funded by the Intramural Research Program, National Cancer Institute (NCI), National Institutes of Health (NIH)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2929328/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the MHCS-II was established to quantify the impact of hepatitis C (HCV), hepatitis B (HBV) and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV-1) infections on persons with hemophilia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10848312/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I) evaluated and prospectively followed patients with hemophilia or a related coagulation disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8106967+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We studied human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) infection incidence over time in a 16-center cohort of hemophiliacs in the United States and Europe and estimated the most likely date of seroconversion for all seropositive subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20337924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8106967") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-023-06370-4/MediaObjects/41586_2023_6370_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initiated in 1982, 55 this study particularly sought to understand the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS in this population, which was at high risk for development of AIDS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001373> "A prospective cohort study of the US National Cancer Institute of people with hemophilia or related congenital coagulation disorders at hemophilia treatment centres: the first Multicenter Hemophilia Cohort Study (MHCS-I), begun in 1982 at 16 centres in the United States and Europe, followed its participants to study the cause and natural history of HIV infection and AIDS, and the second (MHCS-II) invited all HCV-seropositive patients aged 13 or older at 52 participating centres in 2001–2005, to quantify the impact of hepatitis C, hepatitis B and HIV infections.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6318225/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients who were young and fit to tolerate autologous stem-cell transplantation (transplantation eligible) entered the intensive treatment pathway. Older and less fit patients (transplantation ineligible) entered the non-intensive treatment pathway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> "A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6318225/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Randomisation occurred between May 26, 2010, and April 20, 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> "A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6318225/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants will potentially undergo three randomisations: i. At presentation (randomised to induction chemotherapy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> "A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30559051+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lenalidomide maintenance versus observation for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma (Myeloma XI): a multicentre, open-label, randomised, phase 3 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> "A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30559051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30559051+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Myeloma XI trial was an open-label, randomised, phase 3, adaptive design trial with three randomisation stages done at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales, and Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001374> "A UK open-label, randomised, phase 3 adaptive-design trial for patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma at 110 National Health Service hospitals in England, Wales and Scotland, recruiting from 2010, which assigned patients by age and fitness to intensive (transplantation) or non-intensive pathways and had three randomisation stages, including induction regimens and lenalidomide maintenance against observation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3639680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After completion of induction therapy, patients underwent peripheral blood stem-cell mobilisation and harvest, high-dose melphalan treatment (200 mg/m2), and autologous stem-cell transplantation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3639680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the MRC Myeloma IX trial, adult patients of age 18 years or older who had newly diagnosed and histologically confirmed symptomatic multiple myeloma were enrolled from 120 centres in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3639680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first randomisation, patients in the intensive pathway were allocated to receive either clodronic acid or zoledronic acid plus induction chemotherapy with either CVAD or CTD, and patients in the non-intensive pathway were allocated to receive either clodronic acid or zoledronic acid plus induction") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3639680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this open-label trial, no investigators, staff at participating centres, or patients were masked to treatment allocation apart from individuals analysing treatment response from laboratory results.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3639680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we designed the MRC Myeloma IX trial, an innovative study with two randomisation steps to allow comparison of both first-line and maintenance treatments for adult patients with newly diagnosed multiple myeloma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21131037+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1970 patients were enrolled between May, 2003, and November, 2007, of whom 1960 were eligible for intention-to-treat analysis") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001375> "A UK Medical Research Council open-label randomised trial that enrolled adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed symptomatic multiple myeloma at 120 UK centres between May 2003 and November 2007, allocating them to an intensive pathway (induction followed by high-dose melphalan and autologous stem-cell transplantation) or a non-intensive pathway, and randomising first-line bisphosphonate (zoledronic versus clodronic acid) with induction chemotherapy and, later, maintenance treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7188951/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DNA extraction was divided evenly between the Laboratorio de Genómica de Enfermedades Psiquiátricas y Neurodegenerativas of the Instituto Nacional de Medicina Genómica and the Departamento de Farmacogenómica of the Instituto Nacional de Psiquiatría Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7188951/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All of the geographic regions where more than half of the population speaks a Native American (NA) language were excluded. The survey was carried out in two phases, with the sampling performed in the second phase.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7188951/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a household survey like the Encodat 2016, collecting biological samples is problematic because it cannot be done under the controlled conditions of a clinical environment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7188951/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were questionnaires in each phase: the first focused on sociodemographic, social, and interpersonal information, with a section on patterns of alcohol, tobacco, and drug use, and the second on screening for psychiatric symptomatology. In the second phase, a sample of buccal epithelial cells was also collected") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7188951/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study analyzed a subsample of the Mexican Genomic Database for Addiction Research (MxGDAR/Encodat), derived from the Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39787278") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39787278+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample included 2,012 individuals from the Mexican Genomic Database for Addiction Research (MxGDAR/Encodat) cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs003558.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second administration of the survey included a subsample of 13,130 respondents who agreed to give a saliva sample for DNA analysis, to be used in analyzing the relationship of mental health, addiction, and genetics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32390825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs003558.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This sample was weighted according to selection probability to be representative on the national level.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001376> "A genomic database drawn from the second phase of the 2016 Mexican National Survey of Tobacco, Alcohol, and Drug Use (Encodat 2016), a nationwide household survey that excluded regions where most people speak a Native American language, whose participants answered questionnaires on substance use and psychiatric symptoms and gave buccal DNA samples, assembled by Mexico's National Institute of Psychiatry Ramón de la Fuente Muñiz and National Institute of Genomic Medicine for genetic studies of addiction and related psychiatric and pharmacogenetic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057087/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on earlier questionnaires, ever-smoking concordant twin pairs and their family members were recruited in 2001–2005 for the Nicotine Addiction Genetics (NAG) Finland study, as part of the consortium including Finland, Australia, and USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24927283+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twin pairs concordant for smoking history were recruited along with their family members, as part of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26407342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4583245") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NAG-FIN sample was ascertained from the Older Finnish Twin Cohort consisting of adult twins born in 1938–1957.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the study sample was drawn from the population‐based Finnish Twin Cohort Study, which consists altogether of 35 834 adult twins born in 1938–1957.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were assessed by DNA sample collection and a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview resulting in detailed phenotypic information on multiple smoking behavior traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twin pairs concordant for ever‐smoking were identified and recruited along with their family members (mainly siblings) for the Nicotine Addiction Genetics (NAG) Finland study. Priority was given to heavier smokers. The data collection took place in 2001–2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001377> "The Finnish arm of the multisite Nicotine Addiction Genetics consortium (Finland, Australia and the United States), in which twin pairs from the older Finnish Twin Cohort (born 1938–1957) concordant for ever-smoking, with priority to heavier smokers, were recruited in 2001–2005 together with their family members, mainly siblings, and assessed by a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview and DNA sampling to study the genetics of smoking behaviour and nicotine dependence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Apart from cognitive tasks, participants were asked to complete an online behavioral questionnaire concerning life events, personality, environmental factors and behavioural conditions, which included ADHD traits and autistic traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants volunteered in the Netherlands Study of Cognition, Environment and Genes (NESCOG), which comprises a general population sample (sample 1) and a genetically informative, family-based sample (sample 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sample 1 (S1, n = 837) was recruited through media advertisement or through the Science Live Program of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam (www.sciencelive.nl).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Central Committee on Research Involving Human Subjects in The Netherlands provided institutional review board (IRB) approval for both NESCOG samples in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738022/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of NESCOG is to study individual differences in cognition and cognitive-related disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257114+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data on Attention Problems (AP) were collected in a population-based family sample of twins and siblings (S2, n = 560).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001378> "A Dutch study of individual differences in cognition and cognition-related disorders. It has a general-population sample of volunteers recruited through media advertisements or the Science Live research programme of the NEMO Science Center in Amsterdam, who performed cognitive tasks and completed an online questionnaire on life events, personality, environment and behaviour, and a genetically informative family sample of twins and their siblings.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2000 and 2005, 1,066 subjects, aged 10–16 years, who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 years, were recruited throughout four English regions (East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol, and Oxford) for detailed phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Parents of the NFS children were also recruited, and they underwent clinical assessment, including height and weight.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3064014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1986 and 1996, the ORPS recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes aged <16 years in the geographic region of the Oxford Health Authority") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3064014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2000 and 2005, the NFS recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes throughout England (8).Both cohorts have been monitored with annual assessments of A1C and the albumin/creatinine ratio (ACR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21335371+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Serially collected samples for A1C measurement were available for 1,232 subjects with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes recruited to the Oxford Regional Prospective Study and the Nephropathy Family Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21335371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5280020/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GWAS discovery stage included 3135–5156 subjects with T1D, depending on phenotypic comparison (Supplemental Figure 1), from four studies: FinnDiane,23 the EURODIAB Family Study,24 the Scania Diabetes Registry (SDR),25 and the UK Nephropathy Family Study and Oxford Regional Prospective Study (NFS-ORPS/Cambridge)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001379> "A combined sample of two cohorts of young people with childhood-onset type 1 diabetes in England, analysed as one study in genome-wide association studies of diabetic kidney disease and type 1 diabetes. The Oxford Regional Prospective Study recruited children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region in 1986–1996. The Nephropathy Family Study recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years with type 1 diabetes, and their parents, in four English regions in 2000–2005. Both cohorts were followed with annual measurements of HbA1c and the urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2660471/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The longitudinal study schedule comprised annual collection of three consecutive early-morning urine specimens for centralized measurement of albumin-to-creatinine ratio (ACR) and blood samples for measurements of A1C and lipids.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> "A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2000 and 2005, 1,066 subjects, aged 10–16 years, who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 years, were recruited throughout four English regions (East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol, and Oxford) for detailed phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> "A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Parents of the NFS children were also recruited, and they underwent clinical assessment, including height and weight.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> "A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NFS was set up in 2000 as part of the Juvenile Diabetes Research Foundation/Wellcome Trust Diabetes Inflammation Laboratory: Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> "A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19918004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2809284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population was composed of young people with type 1 diabetes and their parents recruited in the Nephropathy Family Study (NFS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001380> "A longitudinal study of young people with type 1 diabetes in England, set up in 2000 within the Genetic Resource Investigating Diabetes (GRID) study of the JDRF/Wellcome Trust Diabetes and Inflammation Laboratory. In 2000–2005 it recruited adolescents aged 10–16 years who had developed type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in East Anglia, Birmingham, Bristol and Oxford, together with their parents. It followed them with annual urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratios and HbA1c measurements for phenotypic and genetic study of the early pathogenesis of microalbuminuria.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6161833/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, all cases were diagnosed and histologically confirmed as invasive breast cancer by pathologists at the University College Hospital in Ibadan, Nigeria, a tertiary hospital that serves southwestern Nigeria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study participants were women aged 18 years or older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were enrolled through general outpatient and ophthalmology clinics as well as from several communities randomly selected from a list of all communities in the catchment area of University College Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Starting in 2014, cases were enrolled at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital using the same NBCS questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NBCS started enrolling women with breast cancer (hereafter cases) and women without breast cancer (hereafter controls) in Nigeria in 1998 and, in 2011, enrollment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda using the same questionnaire and protocol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20716701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30130155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40249615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008756/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained interviewers administered structured questionnaires, measured height and weight, and obtained blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001381> "A case-control study of breast cancer in women aged 18 or older, begun in 1998 in Ibadan, Nigeria. Women with invasive breast cancer are recruited at University College Hospital, Ibadan (from 2014 also at Lagos State University Teaching Hospital). Women without cancer are enrolled as controls from the hospital's outpatient clinics and from communities randomly selected in its catchment area. Enrolment was extended to Cameroon and Uganda in 2011 with the same questionnaire and protocol. It collects questionnaire data and biospecimens to study epidemiological and inherited risk factors for breast cancer in African women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15826420") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15826420+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Joint Registry (NJR) for England and Wales was launched in April 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15826420") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15826420+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Department of Health (DoH) awarded the contract to run the NJR to Atomic Energy Authority (AEA) Technology in September 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23188900") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23188900+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients with osteoarthritis who had an Exeter V40/Contemporary THR (Stryker) implanted before 31 December 2010 and recorded in the National Joint Registry for England and Wales were included in the analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30273415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6123669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NJR hip dysplasia base population comprised 5411 adult individuals (4095 females) living in England who had undergone a hip replacement recorded in the NJR by the operating surgeon as being for the indication of hip dysplasia and who had given written permission for re-contact for research purposes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.njrcentre.org.uk/about-the-njr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30273415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6123669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Joint Registry for England, Wales, Northern Ireland, and the Isle of Man (NJR, http://www.njrcentre.org.uk/) was established in 2003 to collect audit data on all hip and knee replacement surgery in these regions") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001382> "A national registry of joint replacement surgery, set up by the Department of Health and the Welsh Government, that has recorded hip and knee replacements since April 2003 (ankle, elbow and shoulder replacements since 2010–2012) in NHS and independent hospitals in England and Wales, joined by Northern Ireland in 2013, the Isle of Man in 2015, Guernsey in 2019 and Jersey in 2025. Each procedure is recorded with the implant used and, with the patient's consent, the patient's details, to monitor the outcomes of implants, hospitals and surgeons.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4678416/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the PsA GWAS, 1,526 PsA case subjects and 1,508 unaffected control subjects were recruited by four collection centers—Michigan, Toronto, Newfoundland, and the National Psoriasis Foundation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "But although the biobank was retired in 2025, it remains a landmark achievement") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2006, the National Psoriasis Foundation led the creation of the Victor Henschel Biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "More than a collection of biological samples and clinical information, this pioneering piece of psoriatic disease research infrastructure intended to advance psoriatic disease genetic research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Moreover, unlike other resources, the data from the biobank would be made available broadly to an international community of researchers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NPF, with the generosity of patient volunteers and the financial backing of the Henschel family, launched the biobank with the ambitious goal of securing 2000 samples in its first year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26626624") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32725812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.psoriasis.org/victor-henschel-biobank/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Today, research studies using the biobank have honed our understanding of the common genetic influences on psoriasis and uncovered rare family lineages that allowed the discovery of genes with exceptional impact on the development of psoriasis and psoriatic arthritis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001383> "A biobank of biological samples, including DNA, and clinical information from volunteers in the United States with psoriasis or psoriatic arthritis and from unaffected controls. The National Psoriasis Foundation created it in 2006, with the financial backing of the Henschel family, to advance genetic research on psoriatic disease. Its samples were made available to researchers internationally for case-control and family studies until the biobank was retired in 2025.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8740935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fingerprints were collected using rolled ink prints on paper, or using an electronic fingerprint scanner in TZL (Greenbit DactyScan26) and NSPT (DactyScan40i) cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> "A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China's National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10351707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were photographed using a Canon EOS700D camera.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> "A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China's National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10351707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Survey of Physical Traits Study (NSPT) is part of the National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, which contained four sub-cohorts collected from three different regions of China in different years: Taizhou, Jiangsu province in 2015 and 2019, Zhengzhou, Henan province in 2017, Nanning, Guangxi province in 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> "A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China's National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.")
