AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12645165/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we systematically measured DNA methylation, protein expression, and metabolite levels, conducting a multiomics integration analysis for diabetes in the National Survey of Physical Traits (NSPT) cohort of 3,451 individuals from the Chinese population") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> "A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China's National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34995520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37459304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40938633") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12645165/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples in the NSPT cohort included 3,557 Chinese individuals recruited as volunteers from three regional districts in China: Zhengzhou, Taizhou, and Nanning.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001384> "A population-based prospective cohort of Han Chinese adults, a sub-project of China's National Science & Technology Basic Research Project, recruited as volunteers in four sub-cohorts in Taizhou (Jiangsu province; 2015 and 2019), Zhengzhou (Henan province; 2017) and Nanning (Guangxi province; 2018). Participants were photographed and assessed for physical traits such as facial, ear and fingerprint features, and gave blood for genotyping and for DNA methylation, proteomic and metabolomic profiling, to study the genetic and molecular basis of human physical traits and common diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All samples were sent for library preparation and sequencing at the NYGC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood and autopsy tissue samples were obtained from 41 ALS clinics and research institutions spanning the USA, the UK, the Netherlands, Greece, and Israel (Fig. 1A).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data on each patient as provided by each institution was harmonized by a team at NYGC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we present the full NYGC ALS Consortium dataset, comprising WGS on 4,746 donors and RNA-seq from 8 major brain and spinal cord tissues from a cohort of 695 individuals presenting with ALS, other neurological diseases, and non-neurological controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The New York Genome Center (NYGC) ALS Consortium was formed in 2015 to address this challenge, bringing together clinicians, basic scientists, geneticists, and computational biologists globally from 41 institutions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This partnership established a framework to generate whole genome sequencing (WGS) and bulk tissue RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) data and apply functional genomics approaches to survey the genetic, molecular, and cellular basis of ALS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.29.26350889v1.full-text") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have built a comprehensive and openly accessible resource of genomic and clinical data from ALS patients to enable the research community to answer critical scientific questions, accelerate biological discovery, and advance the development of novel therapeutics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001385> "A consortium formed in 2015 around the New York Genome Center, through which 41 ALS clinics and research institutions in the United States, the United Kingdom, the Netherlands, Greece and Israel contribute blood and post-mortem brain and spinal cord tissue from people with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, other neurological diseases and non-neurological controls. The samples are whole-genome and RNA sequenced at the New York Genome Center and their clinical data harmonised into an openly accessible genomic resource for ALS research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Approximately 80% had undergone surgical AAA repair (typically AAA’s > 50-55 mm in diameter).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited New Zealand men and women with a proven history of AAA (infra-renal aortic diameter ≥ 30 mm proven on ultrasound or CT scan).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group underwent an abdominal ultrasound scan to exclude (>25 mm) concurrent AAA and Anglo-European ancestry was required for inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The vast majority of cases (>97%) were of Anglo- European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5833524/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were also screened for peripheral artery disease (PAD; using ankle brachial index), carotid artery disease (ultrasound) and other cardiovascular risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27899403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5833524/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NZ GWAS 2 consisted of 397 AAA patients (332 male) and 384 elderly controls (308 male), genotyped using the Illumina Infinium Omni2.5 BeadChip array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001386> "A case-control study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) in New Zealand. The Vascular Research Consortium of New Zealand recruited men and women with AAA (infrarenal aortic diameter of at least 30 mm on ultrasound or CT scan, about 80% after surgical repair), nearly all of Anglo-European ancestry, and elderly Anglo-European controls in whom AAA was excluded by abdominal ultrasound and who were also screened for peripheral and carotid artery disease. Its participants were genotyped in two genome-wide case-control sets for genetic studies of AAA.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3387822") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eight studies [7–14] (including the unpublished Louisiana State University study) were conducted in North America, two in Europe [15, 16], and one in China [17], and one was the International Agency for Research on Cancer- coordinated Surveillance of Environmental Aspects Related to Cancer in Humans (SEARCH) study from Canada, Europe, and Australia [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22104574+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cigarette smoking and pancreatic cancer: an analysis from the International Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (Panc4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4520746/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, genome-wide genotyping of 8052 subjects from nine studies within the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4) (Supplementary Table 1) was conducted using the HumanOmniExpressExome-8v1 array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26646264+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Alcohol use equal to or greater than 26 g daily also was associated with increased risk of EOPC (odds ratio, 1.49; 95% confidence interval, 1.21-1.84), and there appeared to be a dose- and age-dependent effect of alcohol on risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26646264+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family history of PC, diabetes mellitus, smoking, obesity, and pancreatitis were associated with EOPC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22104574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26098869") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26646264") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4710562/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4) (http://www.panc4.org), is an international group of researchers organized to pool data from individual case-control studies of pancreatic cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001387> "An international consortium that pools data from case-control studies of pancreatic cancer, conducted in North America, Europe, China and Australia, to study risk factors such as tobacco and alcohol use, diabetes and pancreatitis; cases and controls from several member studies were also genotyped together for a genome-wide association study of pancreatic cancer.")

