AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19483682+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a genome-wide scan among 277 TGCT cases and 919 controls and found that seven markers at 12p22 within KITLG (c-KIT ligand) reached genome-wide significance") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2865677/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All controls were from the Philadelphia region, 90% were 46 years or older and had already passed the peak age of TGCT development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2865677/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were 277 white, non-Hispanic men with pathologically defined TGCT seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System (UPHS) or Fox Chase Cancer Center (FCCC) in Philadelphia, PA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2865677/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male controls (n=932) were selected from PennCATH, a UPHS single-center, hospital-based study of angiographic coronary artery disease (CAD) in almost 4,000 subjects undergoing cardiac catheterization.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2634/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2634_MOESM32_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 349 TGCT cases recruited from the University of Pennsylvania (Abramson Cancer Center) and Fox Chase Cancer Center were genotyped and compared to a control group of 919 men enrolled in the University of Pennsylvania Catherterization Study (PennCATH)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19483682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001307.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will analyze the contribution of genetic variants in these pathways to TGCT risk using a population-based case-control study in the Philadelphia metropolitian area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001388> "A case-control study of inherited susceptibility to testicular germ cell tumour at the University of Pennsylvania, Philadelphia, whose genome-wide association scan compared men with testicular germ cell tumour seen at the University of Pennsylvania Health System or Fox Chase Cancer Center with male controls from the Philadelphia region drawn from the PennCATH study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11415817/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with ALS were enrolled (between 2014 and 2019) at 12 centers in the United States and 1 center in South Africa through the prospective Phenotype-Genotype-Biomarker (PGB) study (registered at clinicaltrials.gov NCT02327845) of the Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development (CReATe) Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11415817/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Independent Ethics Committee (IEC) of the University of Tubingen approved the study in Germany (IEC-Project Number: 361/2017B01), but none of the Tubingen participants met eligibility criteria for this analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS)Frontotemporal dementia (FTD)Primary lateral sclerosis (PLS)Hereditary Spastic Paraplegia (HSP)Progressive Muscular Atrophy (PMA)Multi-System Proteinopathy (MSP)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family members of patients with apparently sporadic disease (ie, no family history) may also participate through a remote-evaluation process in which they provide limited information about their medical history as well as biological samples (blood and urine).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is broadly inclusive, enrolling patients with both familial and sporadic forms of disease. All enrolled patients will undergo five in-person evaluations at one of the CReATe consortium clinical sites as well as annual remote evaluations. In-person evaluations will include motor, cognitive and functional assessments as well as collection of biological fluids.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39270623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02327845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://create.rarediseasesnetwork.org/research-study/8001") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The third goal will be accomplished by laboratory testing of biological samples (blood, urine and spinal fluid) that are collected from study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001389> "A prospective, longitudinal observational study of the CReATe Consortium (Clinical Research in ALS and Related Disorders for Therapeutic Development), led from the University of Miami, that from 2014 enrolled patients with familial or sporadic amyotrophic lateral sclerosis or a related disorder (primary lateral sclerosis, progressive muscular atrophy, hereditary spastic paraplegia, frontotemporal dementia or multisystem proteinopathy), and some of their family members, at clinical sites in the United States, South Africa and Germany, with repeated motor, cognitive and functional assessments and collection of blood, urine and cerebrospinal fluid, to study phenotype-genotype relationships and develop biomarkers for therapy development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19332184+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PLATO is an international, randomized, double-blind, event-driven trial involving >18,000 patients hospitalized for ST-elevation ACS with scheduled primary percutaneous coronary intervention or for non-ST-elevation ACS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19332184+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The phase III PLATelet inhibition and patient Outcomes (PLATO) trial is designed to test the hypothesis that ticagrelor compared with clopidogrel will result in a lower risk of recurrent thrombotic events in a broad patient population with ACS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3117310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PLATO trial recruited 18 624 patients with acute coronary syndrome (with or without ST elevation) from 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3117310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary efficacy end point was the composite of death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction, or stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3117310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This work was supported by AstraZeneca, who funded the PLATO trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19332184") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21685437") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36869765") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36869765+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GWAS and MR were performed in patients with ACS from PLATO (n = 10 013) and FRISC-II (n = 2952), and with CCS from the STABILITY trial (n = 10 786).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001390> "An international, phase III, randomised, double-blind trial funded by AstraZeneca that enrolled patients hospitalised with acute coronary syndrome (ST-elevation ACS scheduled for primary percutaneous coronary intervention, or non-ST-elevation ACS) at 862 centres in 43 countries between October 2006 and July 2008, to compare ticagrelor with clopidogrel for preventing death from vascular causes, myocardial infarction and stroke; blood samples from its genetic and biomarker substudies have been used for genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6403101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "through the Anakinra in Pustular Psoriasis, Response in a Controlled Trial (APRICOT) clinical trial (EudraCT no. 2015-003600-23) and its sister mechanistic study, Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms (PLUM).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> "A UK research study sponsored by Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients' relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7495329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The remaining 161 patients were enrolled between 2016 and 2020 through the sister research study Pustular Psoriasis, Elucidating Underlying Mechanisms (PLUM).11 A total of 23 dermatology centers located across the UK were involved in the recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> "A UK research study sponsored by Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients' relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In PLUM we aim to identify and understand the genes that may have an influence on the development of pustular psoriasis, related immune pathways and responses to treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> "A UK research study sponsored by Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients' relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sponsor organisationGuy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> "A UK research study sponsored by Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients' relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30036598") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32936291") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/plum/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will recruit patients, disease controls, healthy volunteers and relations of patients and invite them to donate blood samples, and optional skin and hair pluck samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001391> "A UK research study sponsored by Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust and run as the sister mechanistic study of the APRICOT trial of anakinra, which recruited people with pustular psoriasis through specialist dermatology centres across the UK, together with disease controls, healthy volunteers and patients' relatives, and collected blood and optional skin and hair samples to identify genes, immune pathways and treatment responses involved in pustular psoriasis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25576993+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based, cross-sectional, case-control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25576993+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To describe the baseline characteristics of the Primary Open-Angle African American Glaucoma Genetics (POAAGG) study cohort, the largest African American population with primary open-angle glaucoma (POAG) recruited at a single institution (University of Pennsylvania [UPenn], Department of Ophthalmology, Scheie Eye Institute) to date.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4372490/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria include age over 35 years and self-identification as Black (African-American, African descent, or African Caribbean).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5512952/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Glaucoma specialists classified subjects as cases, controls, or suspects (suspected cases) based on previously published criteria [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5512952/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to meet the enrollment goal for the initial discovery cohort (n = 5500), the study implemented four new recruitment methods: (1) outreach in the local community, (2) in-house screening of community members (“in-reach”), (3) expansion to external sites, and (4) sampling of the Penn Medicine Biobank (PMBB).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25576993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28705151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40782885") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40782885+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from ophthalmology clinics in Philadelphia between July 2010 and August 2024.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001392> "A case-control genetic study of primary open-angle glaucoma led by the University of Pennsylvania's Scheie Eye Institute, which since July 2010 has enrolled self-identified Black adults (African American, African descent or African Caribbean) aged 35 or over from the Philadelphia region, mainly from University of Pennsylvania eye clinics and also through community screenings, two other Philadelphia ophthalmology practices and the Penn Medicine Biobank, with glaucoma specialists classifying them as cases, controls or glaucoma suspects, to identify genetic and clinical risk factors for the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6138692/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Project MinE seeks to obtain sequencing data in 15,000 ALS patients and 7,500 matched controls with the aim of identifying new loci associated to ALS risk, fine-map known and novel loci, and provide a publicly-available summary-level dataset that will enable further genetic research of this and other diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6138692/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Project MinE consortium includes ALS research groups from 16 different countries") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6138692/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This design means that samples and sample-affiliated data (e.g., dense phenotyping) from partners are collected, processed and stored according to the same protocol") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6138692/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the consortium, ALS patients and controls are ascertained through clinics affiliated to the research groups. At these clinics, neurologists obtain a standardized core clinical data set with phenotypic information (Supplementary Table 1) and blood is drawn for DNA isolation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29955173+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we report on the design of Project MinE and pilot analyses of successfully sequenced 1169 ALS patients and 608 controls drawn from the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29955173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36589292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://projectmine.com/about/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One of the main goals of Project MinE is to have its dataset accessible to all qualified researchers conducting health-related research in the public interest, ensuring fair and unbiased availability without preferential or exclusive access.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001393> "An international collaboration of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis research groups from about 16 countries, coordinated from the ALS Centre Netherlands at University Medical Center Utrecht and begun with a pilot in Dutch patients, in which people with ALS and matched controls are recruited through the groups' ALS clinics under a common protocol with a standardised core clinical data set and their whole genomes sequenced, to identify and fine-map genetic risk loci for ALS and share the data with researchers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2649356") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective multicenter study of 310 patients aged 3-20 years old with sickle cell disease under basal conditions and 54 matched controls was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2649356") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An unencour- aged 6-minute walk test was conducted according to the guidelines of the American Thoracic Society.19 Complete blood count and reticulocyte count were measured") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2649356") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients (n=310) 3 to 20 years of age with sickle cell disease confirmed by hemoglobin electrophoresis or high performance liquid chromatography were recruited at the Children’s National Medical Center and Howard University Hospital, Washington DC, and University of Michigan, Ann Arbor Michigan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2776981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were matched by age, sex and ethnicity to every sixth patient with sickle cell disease enrolled in the study and included individuals with hemoglobin AA, hemoglobin AS or hemoglobin AC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2776981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Doppler echocardiography was employed to estimate systolic pulmonary artery pressure through measurement of the tricuspid regurgitation velocity") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19211639") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19956689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2776981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pulmonary Hypertension and Hypoxic Response in Sickle Cell Disease (PUSH) Study is an on-going multicenter observational study that was designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children with sickle cell disease that are predictors of cardiopulmonary complications and that therefore are potential mechanistic targets for early preventive intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001394> "A prospective multicentre observational study of children and adolescents aged 3–20 years with sickle cell disease, examined at steady state, and of controls without the disease matched by age, sex and ethnicity, recruited at Howard University Hospital and Children's National Medical Center in Washington, DC, and the University of Michigan in Ann Arbor, with echocardiography, six-minute walk tests and blood markers, designed to identify factors in pre-symptomatic children that predict pulmonary hypertension and other cardiopulmonary complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12455559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12455559+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To assess the accuracy of a clinical diagnosis of multiple system atrophy (MSA) and compare it to the Quinn and Consensus criteria for MSA using neuropathologically examined cases from the Queen Square Brain Bank for Neurological Disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12784275+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seventy-three patients with a neuropathological diagnosis of PSP autopsied at the Queen Square Brain Bank for Neurological Disorders in London were collected between 1989 and 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11161485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Queen Square Brain Bank for Neurological Disorders (QSBB) is an archive of brains and tissue from individuals with neurodegenerative disease and neurologically normal controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Brain, spinal cord, cerebrospinal fluid and blood are collected from donors nationwide who have had a variety of neurological and neurodegenerative diseases. Our donors are registered via our donor scheme during life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Establishment organisationUCL Institute of Neurology, University College London") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12784275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38849413") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hra.nhs.uk/planning-and-improving-research/application-summaries/research-summaries/queen-square-brain-bank-for-neurological-disorders-qsbb-and-neurores/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over many years the QSBB and NeuroResource have facilitated research into neurodegenerative conditions by providing well characterised tissue samples to the scientific community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001395> "A research tissue bank at the UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology in London that archives brains and other tissue from donors across the UK, registered through its donor scheme during life, who had neurological and mostly neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease, multiple system atrophy and progressive supranuclear palsy, and from neurologically normal controls, and supplies well-characterised tissue and data for research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5840407/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples and aortic valves were collected from patients with severe aortic valve stenosis undergoing aortic valve replacement at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec (QUEBEC-CAVS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5840407/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In parallel, an ethnically matched control group was recruited from patients that underwent cardiac surgery, mostly for isolated coronary artery bypass (> 98%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5840407/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GWAS includes 1009 severe cases of tricuspid CAVS confirmed at surgery and 1017 ethnically matched controls with normal aortic valve that underwent cardiac surgery (QUEBEC-CAVS cohort).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-46639-4/MediaObjects/41467_2024_46639_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec calcific aortic valve stenosis cohort phase 1 (QUEBEC-CAVS-1) is a case-control study including patients with severe aortic valve stenosis undergoing aortic valve replacement at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-46639-4/MediaObjects/41467_2024_46639_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group consists of participants of European ancestry without valvular heart disease from the CARTaGENE cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29511167") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31141105") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38494474") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10944835/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Aortic valve tissues were collected from patients undergoing cardiac surgery at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval between 1998 and 2019 (QUEBEC-CAVS-RNA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001396> "A case-control study of calcific aortic valve stenosis at the Institut universitaire de cardiologie et de pneumologie de Québec – Université Laval, Canada, in which blood and aortic valve tissue are collected from patients undergoing aortic valve replacement for the disease and compared with controls (in its first phase, patients without valve disease undergoing cardiac surgery, mostly coronary artery bypass, at the same institute; in its second, CARTaGENE participants without valvular heart disease), to identify genetic susceptibility to the disease; its valve tissues, collected in 1998–2019, are also used for gene expression studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8019534/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Six patient care sites are included: (1) Fundação Hemominas in the three cities of Belo Horizonte (HBH), Juiz de Fora (JFO) and Montes Claros (MOC) in the state of Minas Gerais, (2) Fundação Hemorio in Rio de Janeiro in the state of Rio de Janeiro, (3) Fundação Hemope in Recife in the state of Pernambuco and, (4) Instituto da Criança, Hospital das Clínicas da Faculdade de Medicina da Universidade de São Paulo (HCFMUSP) in São Paulo in the state of São Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30027669+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A biorepository of blood samples was created and comprehensive demographic and clinical outcome data were entered in a centralized electronic database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30027669+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A large, multi-centre cohort was established to characterise clinical outcomes in the Brazilian SCD population and create the infrastructure to perform genotype-phenotype association studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30027669+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 2795 participants at six Brazilian sites were enrolled between 2013 and 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30027669+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible patients were randomly selected from participating sites and recruited at routine visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30027669") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36602125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10155195/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brazil SCD Cohort Study is part of the National Institutes of Health, National Heart Lung and Blood Institute (NHLBI) REDS-III program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001397> "A cohort of children and adults with sickle cell disease, randomly sampled from the active patients of six care sites in the Brazilian states of Minas Gerais (Belo Horizonte, Juiz de Fora and Montes Claros), Rio de Janeiro, Pernambuco (Recife) and São Paulo and enrolled in 2013–2015 as the Brazilian component of the NHLBI REDS-III programme, with clinical data, a blood biorepository and genome-wide genotyping, to characterise the clinical and transfusion outcomes of sickle cell disease in Brazil and support genotype–phenotype studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23301674+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the 20-year follow-up participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment that included visual acuity, orthoptic assessment and cycloplegic autorefraction, as well as several ocular biometric variables and multiple ophthalmic photographs of the anterior and posterior segments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> "The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort's 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23301674+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Raine Eye Health Study (REHS) was conceived to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults, and to characterize ocular biometric parameters in a young adult cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> "The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort's 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23301674+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Western Australian Pregnancy Cohort (Raine) Study originated as a randomized-controlled trial of 2900 women recruited from the state's largest maternity hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> "The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort's 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23301674+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Their offspring (N = 2868) have been followed at birth, ages 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 14, 17 and 20 years of age in a prospective cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> "The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort's 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23301674") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36596879") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9810640/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Generation-2 20-year follow-up of the Raine Study was funded by the National Health and Medical Research Council (NHMRC), Australia: project grant no.: 1 021 105.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001398> "The eye study of the offspring (Generation 2) of the Raine Study pregnancy cohort in Western Australia, in which participants completed a comprehensive eye assessment at the cohort's 20-year follow-up, including visual acuity, orthoptic assessment, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and anterior and posterior segment photography, to determine the prevalence of and risk factors for eye disease in young adults and characterise their ocular biometric parameters.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34706928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast cancer cases were identified in the University of Pennsylvania Health System and Karmanos Cancer Institute. Local advertisement was also put to recruit breast cancer cases living in the Philadelphia and Detroit area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399> "A hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted in the Philadelphia and Detroit metropolitan areas of the United States from 1999 to 2003, whose cases, diagnosed with invasive ductal breast cancer within 18 months of recruitment and over-sampled for diagnosis before age 40, were identified in the University of Pennsylvania Health System and the Karmanos Cancer Institute or recruited through local advertisement, with controls without breast cancer recruited in the same way.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34706928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were recruited in the same way as cases except that they did not have breast cancer. Patients with breast cancer had to be diagnosed within 18 months of recruitment and have invasive ductal cancer. The study over-sampled women diagnosed with breast cancer under age of 40 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399> "A hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted in the Philadelphia and Detroit metropolitan areas of the United States from 1999 to 2003, whose cases, diagnosed with invasive ductal breast cancer within 18 months of recruitment and over-sampled for diagnosis before age 40, were identified in the University of Pennsylvania Health System and the Karmanos Cancer Institute or recruited through local advertisement, with controls without breast cancer recruited in the same way.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34706928") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RVGBC is a hospital-based case-control study conducted in Philadelphia and Detroit metropolitan areas from 1999 to 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001399> "A hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer conducted in the Philadelphia and Detroit metropolitan areas of the United States from 1999 to 2003, whose cases, diagnosed with invasive ductal breast cancer within 18 months of recruitment and over-sampled for diagnosis before age 40, were identified in the University of Pennsylvania Health System and the Karmanos Cancer Institute or recruited through local advertisement, with controls without breast cancer recruited in the same way.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4292846/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim was to sample adults from villages within all four census regions of Samoa: Apia Urban Area (AUA), Northwest Upolu (NWU), Rest of Upolu (ROU), and Savaii (SAV).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4292846/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The recruitment and measurement of the study participants took place from February to July 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4292846/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study had a population-based design targeting approximately 3,500 adults aged 24.5 to <65 years with target participation numbers for each Samoan census region based upon the national population distribution described in the 2006 census.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4292846/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thirty-three villages were included in the study: nine from the AUA, eight from NWU, eight from ROU, and eight from SAV.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4292846/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To be included in the study, participants were of Samoan origin, which was determined by having four Samoan grandparents (based on self-report)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24799123") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000914") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Anthropometric, fasting blood biomarkers and detailed dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic variables were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001400> "A population-based cross-sectional study of adults with four Samoan grandparents, recruited from February to July 2010 in 33 villages across all four census regions of the independent nation of Samoa (Apia Urban Area, Northwest Upolu, the rest of Upolu and Savai'i), with anthropometry, fasting blood biomarkers, dietary, physical activity, health and socio-demographic data and genome-wide genotyping, to identify genetic variation that increases susceptibility to obesity and cardiometabolic traits in Samoans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/45157534") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7994529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sanford Health is the largest rural non-profit health system in the United States, serving more than 2 million patients through 46 medical centers, more than 200 clinics and 2,500 providers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> "A hospital-based biobank of adult patients of Sanford Health, a rural health system of the Upper Midwest of the United States based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, who since 2011 have elected to provide specimens for research, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array and linked to the health system's clinical records for genetic studies such as of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/45157534") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13055487/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Identification of controls and CAD cases was by International Classification of Diseases, Tenth Revision, Clinical Modification (ICD‐10‐CM) codes from the linked electronic medical record (Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> "A hospital-based biobank of adult patients of Sanford Health, a rural health system of the Upper Midwest of the United States based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, who since 2011 have elected to provide specimens for research, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array and linked to the health system's clinical records for genetic studies such as of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/45157534") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13055487/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were genotyped by use of the Illumina 550k, 610k, or Global Screening Array version 1 arrays, or the Affymetrix Genome‐Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> "A hospital-based biobank of adult patients of Sanford Health, a rural health system of the Upper Midwest of the United States based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, who since 2011 have elected to provide specimens for research, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array and linked to the health system's clinical records for genetic studies such as of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/45157534") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13055487/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sanford Health includes members from the states of North Dakota, South Dakota, Minnesota, and Nebraska.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> "A hospital-based biobank of adult patients of Sanford Health, a rural health system of the Upper Midwest of the United States based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, who since 2011 have elected to provide specimens for research, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array and linked to the health system's clinical records for genetic studies such as of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33777099") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/45157534") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41669951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13055487/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The biobank cohort includes participants aged ≥18 years from the Sanford Health system who elected to provide a specimen to the Sanford Biobank for research purposes, starting in 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001401> "A hospital-based biobank of adult patients of Sanford Health, a rural health system of the Upper Midwest of the United States based in Sioux Falls, South Dakota, who since 2011 have elected to provide specimens for research, genotyped on the Illumina Global Screening Array and linked to the health system's clinical records for genetic studies such as of cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1559717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Application of the main questionnaire, anthropometric survey, and stool and dust sample collection were completed in 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1559717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Salvador-SCAALA project described here is a longitudinal study involving children aged 4–11 years living in the city of Salvador, Northeastern Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1559717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This first study was originally designed to enrol three separate cohorts of children aged 0–3 years recruited from 24 small geographical areas selected to represent the population without sanitation in Salvador, called sentinel-areas [16,17] These three cohorts were recruited in 1997, 2001 and 2003, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1559717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This will be completed with data on dust collection (to dust mite and endotoxin), skin test to most common allergens, stool examinations to helminth and parasites, blood samples (to infection, total and specific IgE, and immunological makers), formaldehyde, physical inspection to diagnoses of eczema, and anthropometric measures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1559717/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the participants of the evaluation of impact of the sanitation programme were recruited as the study population of the present study on allergic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16796729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37497783") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://arca.fiocruz.br/bitstreams/11d752b4-81df-4cf2-86c3-6dac88008f5a/download") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Single- nucleotide variants were genotyped for the SCAALA population using the commercial Illumina HumanOmni2.5– 8 Kit BeadChip panel (www.illumina.com).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001402> "A cohort of children from 24 low-income areas of Salvador, Bahia, in north-eastern Brazil, first enrolled aged 0–3 years in 1997, 2001 and 2003 to evaluate the health effects of the city's sanitation programme and followed from 2005, at ages 4–11, with further surveys (questionnaires, anthropometry, stool, blood and house-dust samples, skin prick tests and, later, genome-wide genotyping), to study social, environmental, infectious, immunological and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergic diseases; it is the Brazilian study of the Social Changes, Asthma and Allergy in Latin America (SCAALA) programme.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1546772+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Identification of AIDS cases and deaths in the cohort was determined through multiple sources, including the national AIDS surveillance registry and the National Death Index.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1664363") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each cohort member who agreed to participate in AIDS follow up studies was testedforantibodies to HIV-I andaskedforpermission to test stored serum samples from the earlier hepatitis studies for HIV-I antibodies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1664363") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These participants were interviewed regarding behavioural and biological risk factors for HIV-I infection and AIDS, examined by a physician, and testedforantibodies to HIV-I eachyear or until a diagnosis ofAIDS was made.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2261554+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort included 6705 homosexual and bisexual men originally recruited from 1978 to 1980 for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2261554+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1546772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37532928") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2261554") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2261554+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To characterise the natural history of sexually transmitted HIV-I infection in homosexual and bisexual men.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001403> "A cohort of homosexual and bisexual men recruited in 1978–1980 at the San Francisco municipal sexually transmitted disease clinic for studies of sexually transmitted hepatitis B, whose stored serum specimens, follow-up examinations and questionnaires, and linkage to AIDS surveillance and death registries were later used to study the natural history, transmission and cofactors of HIV infection and AIDS.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25140956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this randomized, single-blind clinical trial, we randomly assigned children with sickle cell anemia to receive regular blood transfusions (transfusion group) or standard care (observation group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25140956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were between 5 and 15 years of age, with no history of stroke and with one or more silent cerebral infarcts on magnetic resonance imaging and a neurologic examination showing no abnormalities corresponding to these lesions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25140956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested the hypothesis that the incidence of the recurrence of an infarct would be lower among children who underwent regular blood-transfusion therapy than among those who received standard care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4195437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were an age of 5 to 15 years, confirmed diagnosis of hemoglobin SS or hemoglobin Sβ0 thalassemia, and at least one infarct-like lesion on the screening MRI scan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4195437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment began in December 2004 and continued through the end of May 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39293085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25140956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4195437/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted at 29 clinical centers in the United States, Canada, France, and the United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001404> "A multicentre, single-blind randomised clinical trial at 29 centres in the United States, Canada, France and the United Kingdom, which from December 2004 to May 2010 screened children aged 5 to 15 years with sickle cell anaemia (haemoglobin SS or Sβ0 thalassaemia) and no history of stroke by brain MRI, and randomly assigned those with silent cerebral infarcts to regular blood transfusions or standard care, to test whether transfusion therapy reduces the recurrence of cerebral infarcts.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, recruitment began in December 2009 and ended in April 2012 in Lausanne, in October 2012 in Geneva, and in April 2013 in Bern.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were as follows: (a) minimum age of 18 years; (b) of European descent (defined as having both parents and grandparents born in a restricted list of countries); (c) at least one, and ideally three, first degree family members also willing to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Index cases were randomly selected from the population-based CoLaus study [27] in Lausanne, and from the population-based Bus Santé study in Geneva [28]. In Bern, index participants were randomly selected using the cantonal phone directory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3963885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SKIPOGH is part of the larger family-based international EPOGH study (European Project on Genes in Hypertension).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12902508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study used data from SKIPOGH, a multicenter, family- and general population–based cohort designed to examine genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure and kidney function [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24663506") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41325371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41695656") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41695656+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A follow-up visit was performed 3 years later.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001405> "A multicentre family- and population-based study of adults of European descent in Switzerland, in which index participants drawn at random from population samples in the city of Lausanne (the CoLaus study), the canton of Geneva (the Bus Santé study) and the canton of Bern (the cantonal phone directory) were recruited from December 2009 to April 2013 together with their first-degree relatives and re-examined about three years later, to study genetic and environmental determinants of blood pressure, kidney function and other cardiometabolic outcomes; it is the Swiss part of the European Project on Genes in Hypertension.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5967359/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, 1967 DNA samples from five studies will be genotyped; BAMSE (n = 400), BREATHE (n = 92), PAGES (n = 514), GoShare (n = 561) and SLOVENIA (n = 400).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8399629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study (GWAS) of the change in lung function after 6 weeks of ICS treatment was performed in 166 asthma patients from the SLOVENIA study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8399629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children and young adults (5–18 years old) of Slovenian origin were included in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8399629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma from the SLOVENIA study were included in the GWAS of change in lung function after ICS treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8503671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Asthma was defined by having a physician-diagnosis of symptoms prior to recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28639505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34442380") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8503671/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLOVENIA study is a case-control cohort (age: 5–18) and includes asthmatic children and young adults recruited from tertiary health centers from Murska Sobota, Slovenia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001406> "A clinical study of children and young people aged 5–18 of Slovenian origin with a physician diagnosis of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma and hospital records at tertiary health centres in Slovenia, part of them regularly treated with inhaled corticosteroids under medical supervision, with lung function measured after six weeks of inhaled corticosteroid treatment. It is one of the asthma studies enrolled in the Pharmacogenomics in Childhood Asthma (PiCA) consortium, which studies the genetics of response to asthma treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24662965+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data for this study are from 725 community-dwelling adolescents participating in the Santiago Longitudinal Study, a study of substance using behaviors among urban adolescents in Santiago") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32276183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A32276183+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data are from 1,039 participants of the Santiago Longitudinal Study who were studied in childhood (M age 10 years), adolescence (14-17 years), and young adulthood (21-26 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7282289/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1991 and 1996, infants were recruited for an infancy iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial18 or neuromaturation study.19 Inclusion criteria for the infancy studies included full-term infants (greater than or equal to 37 weeks gestational age (GA)) with birth weight ≥3.0 kg, vaginal birth, no major health problems for the infant") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7282289/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data in this study are drawn from the Santiago Longitudinal Study, a cohort study from low-income to middle-income neighbourhoods in Santiago, Chile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9063300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will capitalize on a prospective birth cohort (the Santiago Longitudinal Study, SLS) of ≈1000 Chileans at 30-31y, 50% females, of low- to middle SES, who participated in research related to nutrition and development as infants with follow-up at 1y, 5y, 10y, 12y, 14y, 16y, 21y, and 23y (see Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24662965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32499257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34556688") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35501766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39885687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11875162/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Santiago Longitudinal Study (SLS) is a cohort of participants recruited from community clinics in Santiago, Chile, at infancy between 1991 and 1996 for participation in a randomized trial of iron supplementation to prevent iron deficiency anemia, as described previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001407> "A cohort of healthy, full-term infants from low- to middle-income neighbourhoods of Santiago, Chile, recruited through community clinics in 1991–1996 for an iron-deficiency anaemia preventive trial or a neuromaturation study, and followed up through childhood, adolescence and adulthood in studies of nutrition, development, substance use and cardiometabolic risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28135196") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35621206") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28135196") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28135196+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted this study using data from Shanghai Men's Health Study (SMHS) and Shanghai Women's Health Study (SWHS), two population-based prospective cohorts of middle-aged and elderly Chinese adults in urban Shanghai, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408> "The Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study taken together: two population-based prospective cohorts of middle-aged and elderly Chinese adults in urban Shanghai, China, which recruited women in 1996–2000 and men in 2002–2006 and whose data and biospecimens are often analysed jointly, for example in nested case–control and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28135196") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35621206") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35621206") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35621206+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We identified genetic determinants of plasma 2-AAA through meta-analysis of genome-wide association study data in 5456 individuals of European, African, and Asian ancestry from the Framingham Heart Study, Diabetes Prevention Program, Jackson Heart Study, and Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408> "The Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study taken together: two population-based prospective cohorts of middle-aged and elderly Chinese adults in urban Shanghai, China, which recruited women in 1996–2000 and men in 2002–2006 and whose data and biospecimens are often analysed jointly, for example in nested case–control and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28135196") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35621206") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12277705/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "urban Chinese residents, respectively, aged 40–74 years old, recruited during 1996–2000 and 2002–2006") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408> "The Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study taken together: two population-based prospective cohorts of middle-aged and elderly Chinese adults in urban Shanghai, China, which recruited women in 1996–2000 and men in 2002–2006 and whose data and biospecimens are often analysed jointly, for example in nested case–control and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28135196") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35621206") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40576378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40576378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a case-control study nested within the Shanghai Women's and Men's Health Studies to prospectively investigate the association between urinary metabolites and kidney cancer risk to understand its etiology and the underlying biological mechanisms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001408> "The Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study taken together: two population-based prospective cohorts of middle-aged and elderly Chinese adults in urban Shanghai, China, which recruited women in 1996–2000 and men in 2002–2006 and whose data and biospecimens are often analysed jointly, for example in nested case–control and genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26007630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27363682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31363079") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27363682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4932178/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Swedish/Norwegian GWAS5 was based on 1,668 and 157 MM patients from the Swedish National Myeloma Biobank (Skåne University Hospital, Lund, Sweden) and the Norwegian Biobank for Myeloma (Trondheim, Norway), respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409> "A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients' germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26007630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27363682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31363079") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31363079") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6667490/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients had been previously genotyped in genome-wide association studies using population-based samples from the Swedish National Myeloma Biobank (Skåne University Hospital, Lund)6,7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409> "A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients' germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26007630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27363682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31363079") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39103364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-50932-7/MediaObjects/41467_2024_50932_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our aim is to undertake a large-scale GWAS to find risk alleles for MM in the Swedish population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409> "A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients' germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26007630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27363682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31363079") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39103364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-024-50932-7/MediaObjects/41467_2024_50932_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This project is made feasible by that fact that our constellation is closely involved in coordinating the Swedish Myeloma Biobank as well as clinical studies on MM and MGUS in Sweden and the Nordic region, providing access to samples from patient cohorts that are sufficiently large to allow a GWAS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001409> "A national biobank of samples from patients with multiple myeloma in Sweden, based at Skåne University Hospital in Lund, whose patients' germline DNA has been genotyped for genome-wide association studies of inherited susceptibility to multiple myeloma.")

