# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "708 subjects were enrolled between May 2011 and March 2016, and 705 subjects were analyzed, as 3 were determined to be ineligible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Jewish Health, Denver, Colorado; University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences and Arkansas Children’s Hospital, Little Rock, Arkansas; and Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine, Baltimore, Maryland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided responses regarding their medical history, with verification of the EoE diagnosis and history by the study teams.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were recruited from the 5 US sites forming CoFAR: Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, New York; Duke University Medical Center, Durham, North Carolina") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This registry was part of a study conducted by CoFAR, the primary aim of which was to establish the genetic basis of EoE, and was conducted in conjunction with the Cincinnati Children’s Hospital Medical Center, which performed the genetic analysis on blood or saliva samples collected from the subjects at the time of enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01323803") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075341") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6132253/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was a multi-site, single visit registry of subjects 6 months to 65 years of age of any race, gender or ethnicity, with documented EoE, diagnosis based on histology demonstrating peak intraepithelial esophageal eosinophils ≥15/ high power field (HPF) and symptoms of esophageal dysfunction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001429> "A registry of children and adults aged 6 months to 65 years with biopsy-confirmed eosinophilic esophagitis, enrolled at a single visit in 2011–2016 at the five US sites of the NIAID-funded Consortium of Food Allergy Research (in New York, North Carolina, Denver, Little Rock and Baltimore), with medical history questionnaires and blood or saliva samples genotyped at Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center, to characterise the disease and establish its genetic basis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10038917/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All recruitment materials indicated that participants must be at least 18 years old and speak English fluently to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10038917/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants first completed a brief musical engagement questionnaire, followed by a brief headphone test in which participants heard sounds of different volumes (used in sensitivity analyses), two auditory tasks (musical rhythmic perception and speech perception), and the demographic questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10038917/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Reddit.com (i.e., Ask Me Anything events on the subdomains reddit.com/r/AskScience and reddit.com/r/Science), Facebook advertising, and social media sharing") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10038917/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Saliva collection kits were sent to 2,286 of these participants meeting the following criteria: they had completed the entire survey, reported that their data was usable, and had a valid US mailing address.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10038917/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vanderbilt Online Musicality Study is a worldwide sample of adults recruited from five sources: ResearchMatch.org (primary recruitment source, see Supporting Material for example advertisement text) in addition to advertisements in newsletters and research mailing lists at Vanderbilt University Medical Center,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41715922") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36718543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36718543+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current study used genome-wide complex trait analysis and polygenic score (PGS) approaches utilizing genotype data to examine genetic influences on two musicality traits (rhythmic perception and music engagement) in N = 1792 unrelated adults in the Vanderbilt Online Musicality Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001430> "An online study of adults aged 18 or over who speak English fluently, conducted by researchers at Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, and recruited worldwide, mainly through ResearchMatch and also through Vanderbilt newsletters and research mailing lists, Reddit, Facebook advertising and social media sharing. Participants completed web-based questionnaires on music engagement and auditory tasks of musical rhythm and speech perception, and those with a US mailing address were invited to return mail-in saliva samples for genotyping, to study the genetics of musicality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16960181+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Viva la Familia Study was designed to genetically map childhood obesity and its comorbidities in the Hispanic population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each family was ascertained on an obese proband, defined as a BMI>95th percentile, between the ages 4–19 y.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Family recruitment and phenotyping were conducted in 2000–2005 in Houston, TX.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In-depth phenotyping was performed to characterize the children, including anthropometry, body composition, growth, metabolites, hormones, inflammation, diet, energy expenditure and substrate utilization and physical activity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Once identified, the obese proband and all siblings, 4 to 19 y of age, and their parents were invited to the Children’s Nutrition Research Center for a tour and full explanation of the study prior to consenting.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16960181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23251661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3522587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cross-sectional, longitudinal study design consisted of baseline measurements, with a one-year follow-up to track children’s growth and body compositional changes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001431> "A family study of Hispanic children in Houston, Texas, conducted at the USDA/ARS Children's Nutrition Research Center of Baylor College of Medicine, which in 2000–2005 recruited families through a proband aged 4–19 with a BMI above the 95th percentile, together with the proband's siblings aged 4–19 and their parents. The children were phenotyped in depth (anthropometry, body composition by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, diet, physical activity, energy expenditure and metabolic risk factors) and followed up after one year, to map genetic and environmental contributions to childhood obesity and its comorbidities.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001432> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001432>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26237428") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21474410+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data consisted of all pathological data recorded by the cancer registry and the questionnaire, administered by telephone interview, covered major risk factors for melanoma, such as sun exposure history and skin type.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001432> "A population-based collection of adult melanoma cases resident in Western Australia and diagnosed between January 2006 and September 2009, identified through the Western Australian Cancer Registry and invited by mail with their diagnosing doctor's consent, with registry pathology data, a telephone questionnaire on melanoma risk factors such as sun exposure and skin type, and blood samples for DNA, RNA and serum, established to investigate the genetic epidemiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26237428") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21474410+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical, questionnaire-based phenotypic and blood samples for extraction of DNA, RNA and serum were collected from consenting cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001432> "A population-based collection of adult melanoma cases resident in Western Australia and diagnosed between January 2006 and September 2009, identified through the Western Australian Cancer Registry and invited by mail with their diagnosing doctor's consent, with registry pathology data, a telephone questionnaire on melanoma risk factors such as sun exposure and skin type, and blood samples for DNA, RNA and serum, established to investigate the genetic epidemiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26237428") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21474410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21474410+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Once the diagnosing doctor's consent was obtained, all eligible, resident Western Australian, adult cases of melanoma diagnosed between January 2006 and September 2009, were contacted by mail and invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001432> "A population-based collection of adult melanoma cases resident in Western Australia and diagnosed between January 2006 and September 2009, identified through the Western Australian Cancer Registry and invited by mail with their diagnosing doctor's consent, with registry pathology data, a telephone questionnaire on melanoma risk factors such as sun exposure and skin type, and blood samples for DNA, RNA and serum, established to investigate the genetic epidemiology of melanoma.")
