AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39163621") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03512080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://warpath.info/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9537548/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from 12 outpatient clinics and hospital departments in Uganda and South Africa between June 2018 and March 2020") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001433> "An observational study of adults taking warfarin at a stable maintenance dose for venous thromboembolism, atrial fibrillation or valvular heart disease, Black African and, in South Africa, also of mixed ancestry, recruited from June 2018 to March 2020 at outpatient clinics and hospital departments in Uganda and South Africa by the NIHR Global Health Research Group on warfarin anticoagulation in sub-Saharan Africa (the University of Liverpool, the Infectious Diseases Institute in Kampala and the University of Cape Town), with clinical data and blood samples for genotyping, to develop clinical and genetic warfarin dosing algorithms for sub-Saharan African patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39163621") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03512080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://warpath.info/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9537548/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study included warfarin-treated adult (≥18 years) participants of self-reported black-African ethnicity who were recruited as part of an observational study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001433> "An observational study of adults taking warfarin at a stable maintenance dose for venous thromboembolism, atrial fibrillation or valvular heart disease, Black African and, in South Africa, also of mixed ancestry, recruited from June 2018 to March 2020 at outpatient clinics and hospital departments in Uganda and South Africa by the NIHR Global Health Research Group on warfarin anticoagulation in sub-Saharan Africa (the University of Liverpool, the Infectious Diseases Institute in Kampala and the University of Cape Town), with clinical data and blood samples for genotyping, to develop clinical and genetic warfarin dosing algorithms for sub-Saharan African patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39163621") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03512080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://warpath.info/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39163621") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11493193/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, participants had to maintain an international normalized ratio (INR) within the therapeutic range (2.0-3.0 for venous thromboembolism/atrial fibrillation, and 2.5-3.5 for valvular heart disease) at both visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001433> "An observational study of adults taking warfarin at a stable maintenance dose for venous thromboembolism, atrial fibrillation or valvular heart disease, Black African and, in South Africa, also of mixed ancestry, recruited from June 2018 to March 2020 at outpatient clinics and hospital departments in Uganda and South Africa by the NIHR Global Health Research Group on warfarin anticoagulation in sub-Saharan Africa (the University of Liverpool, the Infectious Diseases Institute in Kampala and the University of Cape Town), with clinical data and blood samples for genotyping, to develop clinical and genetic warfarin dosing algorithms for sub-Saharan African patients.")
