AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36210801") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39163621") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT03512080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://warpath.info/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://warpath.info/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is funded by the National Institute for Health Research, UK and is shared work between the University of Liverpool, United Kingdom, the University of Cape Town, South Africa and the Infectious Disease Institute, Kampala, Uganda.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001433> "An observational study of adults taking warfarin at a stable maintenance dose for venous thromboembolism, atrial fibrillation or valvular heart disease, Black African and, in South Africa, also of mixed ancestry, recruited from June 2018 to March 2020 at outpatient clinics and hospital departments in Uganda and South Africa by the NIHR Global Health Research Group on warfarin anticoagulation in sub-Saharan Africa (the University of Liverpool, the Infectious Diseases Institute in Kampala and the University of Cape Town), with clinical data and blood samples for genotyping, to develop clinical and genetic warfarin dosing algorithms for sub-Saharan African patients.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC400669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility in the etiology of breast cancer, we designed a case-control study nested within five population-based cancer registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were identified through eight population-based cancer registries: six in the USA, one in Canada and one in Denmark (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls in WECARE I and II were eligible for inclusion if the first breast cancer was invasive with no disease spread beyond regional lymph nodes and diagnosed during 1985–2008 before age 55 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls were individually matched in triplets (one case and two controls) in WECARE I and in pairs in WECARE II by age at first breast cancer (5-year strata), calendar-year of first diagnosis (4-year strata), cancer registry, and race/ethnicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4940926/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Selected from a large cohort of women diagnosed with an invasive breast cancer, case patients were diagnosed with CBC and control patients were diagnosed with unilateral breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15084244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27400983") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38263039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10807183/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WECARE Study is a multi-center, population-based case–control study of CBC conducted in two phases: the WECARE I Study (2001–2004) and WECARE II Study (2009–2012) [12, 13].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001434> "A population-based case-control study of contralateral breast cancer, designed to examine the joint roles of radiation exposure and genetic susceptibility, in which women diagnosed before age 55 with a first primary invasive breast cancer who later developed contralateral breast cancer were individually matched to women with unilateral breast cancer. Participants were identified through population-based cancer registries in the United States, Canada and Denmark and recruited in two phases, WECARE I (2001–2004) and WECARE II (2009–2012).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12226357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, since metastatic potential is a key determinant of clinical outcomes, we aimed to identify loci with differential effects on M3 and D3 cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> "A case-control study of uveal melanoma run at the University of Pennsylvania for a genome-wide association study of the cancer and of differences between tumours with monosomy and disomy of chromosome 3, whose cases were patients treated at Wills Eye Hospital in Philadelphia, recruited through the UPenn Genetic Diagnostic Laboratory with blood samples and clinical and tumour data, and whose controls were selected from participants of the Penn Medicine Biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12226357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wills Eye Hospital GWAS was approved by the institutional review board of the Perelman School of Medicine, University of Pennsylvania; other studies were approved as described in the original publications.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> "A case-control study of uveal melanoma run at the University of Pennsylvania for a genome-wide association study of the cancer and of differences between tumours with monosomy and disomy of chromosome 3, whose cases were patients treated at Wills Eye Hospital in Philadelphia, recruited through the UPenn Genetic Diagnostic Laboratory with blood samples and clinical and tumour data, and whose controls were selected from participants of the Penn Medicine Biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12226357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also selected 937 controls originally recruited as part of the Penn Medicine Biobank.18") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> "A case-control study of uveal melanoma run at the University of Pennsylvania for a genome-wide association study of the cancer and of differences between tumours with monosomy and disomy of chromosome 3, whose cases were patients treated at Wills Eye Hospital in Philadelphia, recruited through the UPenn Genetic Diagnostic Laboratory with blood samples and clinical and tumour data, and whose controls were selected from participants of the Penn Medicine Biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12226357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected blood samples and patients’ sex, age, metastasis status, chromosome 3 status, tumor stage, tumor location, and eye color.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> "A case-control study of uveal melanoma run at the University of Pennsylvania for a genome-wide association study of the cancer and of differences between tumours with monosomy and disomy of chromosome 3, whose cases were patients treated at Wills Eye Hospital in Philadelphia, recruited through the UPenn Genetic Diagnostic Laboratory with blood samples and clinical and tumour data, and whose controls were selected from participants of the Penn Medicine Biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40495383") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12226357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped cases and controls at 826,804 variants using the Affymetrix Axiom Precision Medicine Research Array and performed quality control, removing individuals with sex mismatch or high missingness (>5%), and SNPs with a genotype call rate <95%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001435> "A case-control study of uveal melanoma run at the University of Pennsylvania for a genome-wide association study of the cancer and of differences between tumours with monosomy and disomy of chromosome 3, whose cases were patients treated at Wills Eye Hospital in Philadelphia, recruited through the UPenn Genetic Diagnostic Laboratory with blood samples and clinical and tumour data, and whose controls were selected from participants of the Penn Medicine Biobank.")
