# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WOBASZ II is the newest Polish population based survey, performed in 2013-2014 to evaluate prevalence, control, treatment, and morbidity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WOBASZ II study was planned as a cross-sectional survey of a random sample of Polish residents aged over 20 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The selection, using the National Identity Card Registry of the Ministry of Internal Affairs, was made as a three-stage sampling, stratified according to administrative units (voivodeships), type of urbanisation (commune), and gender.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26620680+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WOBASZ II was coordinated by the Department of Epidemiology, Cardiovascular Diseases Prevention and Health Promotion of the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw in cooperation with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz, and Poznan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8521585/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study protocol consisted of a questionnaire used in face-to-face interviews, physical examination, and blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26620680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41144382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12558468/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, the individual samples drawn were independent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001436> "A cross-sectional national health examination survey of a random sample of residents of Poland aged over 20, drawn from the national identity card registry by three-stage sampling stratified by voivodeship, type of urbanisation and gender, and examined in 2013–2014 with face-to-face questionnaire interviews, physical examinations and blood samples to assess the prevalence, treatment and control of cardiovascular diseases and their risk factors. It continued the first WOBASZ survey of 2003–2005 with a new, independent sample and was coordinated by the Institute of Cardiology in Warsaw with medical universities in Gdansk, Katowice, Krakow, Lodz and Poznan.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were collected for centralised measurement of glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1986 to 1997, 91% (n=527) of eligible children were recruited at a mean age 8.8 (SD 4.0) years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Research nurses assessed participants annually from the first year of diagnosis and recorded height, weight, blood pressure, and collected three consecutive early morning (first void) urine specimens for the measurement of albumin:creatinine ratio.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Oxford regional prospective study is a population based inception cohort of children with type 1 diabetes designed to determine prospectively the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Oxford regional prospective study was established in 1986.13") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10097935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18349042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2276285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study identified children aged under 16 in the Oxford Health Authority over a 10 year period from the St Bartholomew’s Oxford diabetes register and recruited children within three months of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001437> "A population-based inception cohort of children diagnosed with type 1 diabetes before the age of 16 in the Oxford Health Authority region of the United Kingdom, established in 1986, who were recruited within three months of diagnosis until 1997 and followed prospectively with annual measurements of HbA1c and urinary albumin excretion to determine the natural course of microalbuminuria during childhood and adolescence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20541252+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to identify common genetic variants affecting vitamin D concentrations and risk of insufficiency.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> "A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5772647/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we expand the previous SUNLIGHT Consortium GWAS discovery sample size from 16,125 to 79,366 (all European descent).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> "A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5772647/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have performed a large 25-hydroxyvitamin D meta-GWAS involving 31 studies with a total of 79,366 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> "A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5772647/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It represents a collaboration of more than 30 studies from the United Kingdom, United States, Canada, Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy, and Finland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> "A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20541252") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-02662-2/MediaObjects/41467_2017_2662_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29343764") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5772647/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SUNLIGHT consortium (Study of Underlying Genetic Determinants of Vitamin D and Highly Related Traits) was formed in 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001438> "A consortium, formed in 2008, of cohort studies from the United Kingdom, the United States, Canada, the Netherlands, Germany, Sweden, Italy and Finland that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results for circulating 25-hydroxyvitamin D concentration in people of European descent, to identify genetic determinants of vitamin D status and insufficiency.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001439> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001439>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30150663") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was recruited via 12- to 18-year old adolescents attending high schools in the Saguenay Lac-Saint-Jean region of Quebec (Canada).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001439> "A consortium established to combine the results of genome-wide association studies from cohorts in Europe, the United States, Canada and Australia, beginning with lifetime cannabis use, in order to identify the genetic variants underlying individual differences in cannabis use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30150663") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4872459/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Currently, the combined International Cannabis Consortium sample size for lifetime cannabis is 32 330 individuals from 13 cohorts from Europe, the United States and Australia, along with four independent replication samples comprising 5627 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001439> "A consortium established to combine the results of genome-wide association studies from cohorts in Europe, the United States, Canada and Australia, beginning with lifetime cannabis use, in order to identify the genetic variants underlying individual differences in cannabis use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30150663") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27023175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4872459/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In response to this need, the International Cannabis Consortium was established to combine the results of multiple GWASs to identify the genetic variants underlying individual differences in cannabis use phenotypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001439> "A consortium established to combine the results of genome-wide association studies from cohorts in Europe, the United States, Canada and Australia, beginning with lifetime cannabis use, in order to identify the genetic variants underlying individual differences in cannabis use.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2443132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A family had to have at least one parent-child pair in which the participating child was the biological child of a participating parent and was between the ages of 1 – 18.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2443132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An initial aim of COHRA is to determine the contributions of individual, family, and community factors to oral diseases in Appalachian children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2443132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families participated in a comprehensive assessment protocol involving interviews, questionnaires, a clinical oral health assessment, a microbiological assessment, and collection of DNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4461765/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Reflecting the overall goal of COHRA to address individual-, family-, and community-level factors influencing oral health, participants in the COHRA1 cohort were enrolled according to a household-based strategy that targeted biological parent-child pairs, with all additional household members invited to participate regardless of biological or legal relationships.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36672800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858612/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA1) is a cross-sectional study comprising members of households living in rural West Virginia and Western Pennsylvania—a region with a high prevalence of poor oral health outcomes [4,15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18522740") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26106416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000095.v3.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment for the study began in 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001440> "A cross-sectional, family-based study, the first cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, that from 2003 recruited households with at least one biological parent–child pair (the child aged 1–18 years), together with all other household members, mainly in rural counties of central West Virginia and western Pennsylvania, United States, and assessed them by interviews, questionnaires, oral health and microbiological examinations and DNA collection to study how individual, family and community factors contribute to oral disease in Appalachia.")

