AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29207502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30086711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34347822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35633918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36599956") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29207502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5748769/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population of the Shika study consisted of 4121 individuals from 40 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001441> "A longitudinal community-based observational study, commissioned by the town and conducted since 2011 by Kanazawa University, of residents of Shika Town on the Noto Peninsula, Ishikawa Prefecture, Japan, which aims to find ways of preventing lifestyle-related diseases: residents aged 40 and over in four model districts of the town complete questionnaires on diet, lifestyle and health and undergo a comprehensive health examination, with blood taken for biochemical tests and DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29207502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30086711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34347822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35633918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36599956") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29207502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5748769/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected four model districts in Shika town for the study including Horimatsu, Higashi-masuho, Tsuchida and Togi with a population in 2016 of 7183 and 2592 households [32].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001441> "A longitudinal community-based observational study, commissioned by the town and conducted since 2011 by Kanazawa University, of residents of Shika Town on the Noto Peninsula, Ishikawa Prefecture, Japan, which aims to find ways of preventing lifestyle-related diseases: residents aged 40 and over in four model districts of the town complete questionnaires on diet, lifestyle and health and undergo a comprehensive health examination, with blood taken for biochemical tests and DNA.")
