AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29207502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30086711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34347822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35633918") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36599956") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35633918") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9139339/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shika study is a longitudinal community-based observational study that has been conducted since 2011 among the residents of Shika town, which is located on the Noto Peninsula in Ishikawa prefecture, Japan.17") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001441> "A longitudinal community-based observational study, commissioned by the town and conducted since 2011 by Kanazawa University, of residents of Shika Town on the Noto Peninsula, Ishikawa Prefecture, Japan, which aims to find ways of preventing lifestyle-related diseases: residents aged 40 and over in four model districts of the town complete questionnaires on diet, lifestyle and health and undergo a comprehensive health examination, with blood taken for biochemical tests and DNA.")
