# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://heart.bmj.com/content/108/14/1114") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants have been identified by review of clinic and discharge letters.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9240330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A venous blood sample (30 mL) was obtained from each participant for the purpose of DNA extraction (QIAsymphony DSP DNA Midi kit/automatic device).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9240330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Demographic and clinical data were collected using purposefully designed questionnaires (REDCap).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9240330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnosis of BAV was confirmed by review of cardiac MRI (cMRI), trans-oesophageal echocardiography (TOE) or unequivocal transthoracic echocardiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9240330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with positive familial history were offered cascade echocardiographic screening.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32720365") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35288444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9240330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population of our study were participants of the University of Leicester Bicuspid aoRtic vAlVe gEnetic research (BRAVE)—an ongoing, multicentre recruitment of patients with BAV disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001442> "An ongoing multicentre genetic study led by the University of Leicester, United Kingdom, with support from the NIHR Leicester Biomedical Research Centre, that recruits patients with bicuspid aortic valve disease, identified from clinic and discharge letters and confirmed by cardiac imaging, together with relatives of patients with a family history of the disease, who are offered cascade echocardiographic screening, and collects clinical questionnaire data and blood for DNA to study the genetic causes of bicuspid aortic valve disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6918065") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the blood draw, 20mL of blood are collected: 10mL is collected into ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) tubes and is reserved for de- oxyribonucleic acid (DNA) extraction, while 10mL is collected in EDTA-anticoagulated (plasma) and non-anticoagulated (serum) tubes") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6918065") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy controls are recruited from the general population and are pre-screened by the same clinical team and matched to FMD cases according to age, sex, race/ethnicity, and body mass index (BMI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12413977") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both the CAUSE and DEFINE-FMD studies are observational, case-controlled, cross-sectional studies, and both were approved by the institutional review board of the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12413977") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given the challenges surrounding FMD we initiated DEFINE-FMD (NCT01967511), a systems genetics study leveraging blood samples and fibroblasts obtained by skin biopsy to disclose key FMD gene regulatory co-expression networks with disease drivers and causal pathways.19") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12413977") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria for entry into DEFINE-FMD include ≥ 18 years of age, being freely willing to participate, and fluency in English.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12413977") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While DEFINE-FMD was recently expanded and is now also enrolling subjects with spontaneous coronary artery dissection (SCAD) or cervical artery dissection (CvAD) in the absence of typical multifocal FMD, these subjects with isolated SCAD or CvAD were not included in this analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31424497") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39271816") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01967511") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs003674.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2013 we initiated the DEFINE study (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT01967511), which has now recruited > 440 subjects and which aims to unravel the pathobiological mechanisms of this disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001443> "An observational case-control study at the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, New York, United States, that since 2013 has enrolled adults with fibromuscular dysplasia and, since its expansion, adults with spontaneous coronary artery dissection or cervical artery dissection, together with healthy controls from the general population matched to the fibromuscular dysplasia cases by age and sex, and collects blood (DNA, plasma and serum) and skin-biopsy fibroblasts for a systems-genetics study of the key drivers of these arterial diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy US Caucasian women who are in the 12th to 29th weeks of pregnancy are potentially eligible for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COHRA2 protocol is presented in detail, including inclusion criteria (healthy, adult, pregnant, US Caucasian, English speaking, and nonimmunocompromised women), recruiting (two sites: Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and West Virginia, USA), assessments (demographic, medical, dental, psychosocial/behavioral, and oral microbial samples and DNA)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA) has been enrolling pregnant women and their babies since 2011 in the COHRA2 study of genetic, microbial, and environmental factors involved in oral health in Northern Appalachia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia (COHRA) was established in 2000 as a collaboration between the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University to study the high rates of oral health problems seen in Northern Appalachia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4451284/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Under the COHRA2 study protocol, we collect data on women during their pregnancy and follow them and their babies longitudinally through the early years of the baby's life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26089906") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38404680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10890941/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COHRA2 is a mother-child pair prospective study of English-speaking pregnant White women aged 18 years and older residing in Northern and North Central Appalachia, specifically in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and throughout the state of West Virginia.10") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001444> "A prospective mother–child cohort of the Center for Oral Health Research in Appalachia, a collaboration of the University of Pittsburgh and West Virginia University, that since 2011 has enrolled healthy, English-speaking, White pregnant women aged 18 and over in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and across West Virginia, United States, and follows the women and their children from pregnancy into early childhood with oral examinations, questionnaires and oral microbial and DNA samples, to study the genetic, microbial and environmental factors in oral health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4718515/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, to be included in this study, a family was required to have at least 10 living individuals in 3 or more generations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4718515/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were selected through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia, which was defined as recurrent thrombotic events (at least one of which was spontaneous), a single spontaneous thrombotic episode plus a first-degree relative also affected, or onset of thrombosis before age 45.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4718515/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to the Genetic Analysis of Idiopathic Thrombophilia 1 (GAIT-1) Project [3,20], we initiated another project—the Genetic Analysis of Idiopathic Thrombophilia 2 (GAIT-2) Project, using a new set of families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4718515/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Spanish families in our study were recruited in the GAIT-2 Project at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau of Barcelona, Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4718515/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These results indicate that the study of the genetic basis of thrombin generation phenotypes should identify novel genetic factors involved in the risk of VTE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26784699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35272364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9251712/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All of the individuals were recruited at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau (Barcelona, Spain) from 2006 to 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001445> "A family-based study, run at the Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau in Barcelona, of extended Spanish families recruited from 2006 to 2010 through a proband with idiopathic thrombophilia (recurrent thrombosis, a spontaneous thrombosis with an affected first-degree relative, or thrombosis before age 45, with known biological causes excluded), each family having at least ten living members in three or more generations. It follows the GAIT-1 Project with a new set of families and studies the genetic basis of thrombosis risk and of intermediate phenotypes such as thrombin generation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7612120/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In some cases we used summary statistics from our first GWAS of AFB and NEB8 on discovery cohorts (see Supp Note Tables S1-S3b).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446> "A consortium of cohort studies that carries out genome-wide association meta-analyses of human reproductive behaviour, such as age at first sex, age at first birth, number of children ever born and childlessness, in people of European ancestry; after a first study of age at first birth and number of children ever born, it meta-analysed cohorts for age at first sex and age at first birth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7612120/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This consortium is a collaboration studying the GWAS of human reproductive behaviour including age at first sex and birth, number of children ever born, childlessness and related traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446> "A consortium of cohort studies that carries out genome-wide association meta-analyses of human reproductive behaviour, such as age at first sex, age at first birth, number of children ever born and childlessness, in people of European ancestry; after a first study of age at first birth and number of children ever born, it meta-analysed cohorts for age at first sex and age at first birth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34211149") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7612120/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a meta-analysis of GWAS results from 36 cohorts for AFS and AFB in individuals of European ancestry (defined by genetic principal components).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001446> "A consortium of cohort studies that carries out genome-wide association meta-analyses of human reproductive behaviour, such as age at first sex, age at first birth, number of children ever born and childlessness, in people of European ancestry; after a first study of age at first birth and number of children ever born, it meta-analysed cohorts for age at first sex and age at first birth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12875989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Before blood sampling, participants in the SerGenCovid-19 project were asked to provide health, anamnestic, and lifestyle information through a secure, access-restricted online questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12875989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sample collection was conducted between May 2021 and February 2022.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12875989/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples used in this study are part of the SerGenCovid-19 project (https://sergencovid19.d4science.org), an initiative of the Italian National Research Council (Consiglio Nazionale delle Ricerche, CNR) aimed at identifying the genetic and serological factors involved in response to vaccination against COVID-19 and susceptibility to SARS-CoV-2 infection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(rdfs:comment "I volontari potranno recarsi presso uno dei sette centri individuati su base nazionale (Sicilia, Calabria, Sardegna, Campania, Lazio, Toscana, Lombardia), per un prelievo di sangue che sarà ripetuto dopo 5 e 10 mesi”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inoltre consentirà di costruire una sieroteca e una genoteca che seguiranno gli stringenti standard della infrastruttura pan-europea di biobanche e risorse di ricerca biomolecolare (BBMRI)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A partire da 100.000 soggetti reclutati nell’ambito dello studio Epicovid-19, che hanno manifestato la disponibilità ad essere ricontattati per ulteriori studi, sono stati selezionati 10.000 partecipanti, distribuiti omogeneamente in tutto il paese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41659846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cnr.it/it/comunicato-stampa/10010/parte-il-progetto-sergen-covid-19") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.irib.cnr.it/progetti/virus-memory/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Il prelievo si è ripetuto dopo 5 mesi (T1) e dopo ulteriori 5 mesi (T2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001447> "A cohort of adult volunteers living across Italy, selected by the Italian National Research Council (CNR) from respondents to its EPICOVID-19 web survey who had agreed to be recontacted, who completed an online health and lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood at collection centres in several Italian regions, with repeat sampling about 5 and 10 months later, between May 2021 and February 2022. It was set up to study the serological and genetic factors in the immune response to SARS-CoV-2 infection and COVID-19 vaccination and in susceptibility to infection, and to build a serum and DNA biobank.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33981951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4500830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Bevacizumab was given at 10 mg/kg on days 1 and 15 of each cycle until March 2011, when an amendment allowed optional use to be declared at the time of random assignment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> "A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33981951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4500830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility included patients age ≥ 18 years with histologically documented stage IV or stage IIIC BC not amenable to local therapy, ECOG performance status of 0 to 1, and life expectancy ≥ 12 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> "A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33981951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4500830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end point was PFS defined as the interval from date of registration until date of first disease progression or death as a result of any cause; patients were censored at the last date they were assessed to be progression free.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> "A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33981951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4500830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was activated in October 2008 and was closed to accrual in November 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> "A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33981951") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00785291") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26056183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4500830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "trial was a three-arm randomized phase III trial comparing paclitaxel once per week to nanoparticle albumin-bound nab-paclitaxel once per week and to ixabepilone as first-line chemotherapy with bevacizumab for locally recurrent or metastatic BC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001448> "A randomised, three-arm phase III trial led by the Cancer and Leukemia Group B, with the North Central Cancer Treatment Group (as N063H), the Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group and the Southwest Oncology Group taking part, that enrolled patients aged 18 or over with locally recurrent (stage IIIC) or metastatic (stage IV) breast cancer and no prior chemotherapy for metastatic disease at institutions in the United States from 2008 to 2011, comparing first-line paclitaxel once per week with nab-paclitaxel or ixabepilone once per week, each given with bevacizumab (optional from March 2011), with progression-free survival as the primary end point.")
