# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17446795+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 2524 participants (1301 women) are a representative cohort of 35-55-year-old individuals, free from overt cardiovascular disease at study initiation, randomly sampled from the twinned Belgian communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17446795+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Asklepios Study is a longitudinal population study focusing on the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in (preclinical) cardiovascular disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5916889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on the population lists of the twinned Belgian Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken communities (provided by local authorities), subjects within the age group of 35 to 55 years (8,104 eligible) were randomly sampled and invited by tiered direct postal mailing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5916889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From the onset of the study, also partners and relatives (when living in Erpe-Mere – Nieuwerkerken) were eligible for participation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6723474/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measurements of round 2 [29] were performed during a continuous period, between 2011 and 2016 at the same single study site in Erpe–Mere and essentially mirrored all examinations performed in round 1") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17446795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29695838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31357728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6723474/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study uses measurements from round 2 of the study (2011–2016) as no spirometry was performed in round 1 (2002–2004).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001449> "A longitudinal population study by investigators of Ghent University, Belgium, of men and women aged about 35 to 55 and free from overt cardiovascular disease, randomly sampled from the population lists of the twinned communities of Erpe-Mere and Nieuwerkerken (partners and relatives living there were also eligible), examined at a single local study site in 2002–2004 and again in 2011–2016, to study the interplay between ageing, cardiovascular haemodynamics and inflammation in preclinical cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4091794/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CORtisol NETwork Consortium is funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government (grant CZB-4-733) and the British Heart Foundation (grant RG11/4/28734).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4091794/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a discovery meta-analysis of genome-wide association studies (GWAMA) of morning plasma cortisol levels, investigating ∼2.5 M SNPs in 12,597 men and women, aged 14–102 years, of European origin (Table S1 for participant characteristics).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4091794/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Raine Western Australia Pregnancy Cohort (Raine) 902 797 51.9 17.1(0.29) 16.01-18.91") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cortisol was measured by immunoassay in blood samples collected from study participants between 0700 and 1100 h in all cohorts except for in TwinsUK which measured cortisol using liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CORNET consortium extended its genome-wide association meta-analysis for morning plasma cortisol from 12,597 to 25,314 subjects and from ~2.2M to ~7M SNPs, in 17 population-based cohorts of European ancestries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25010111") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33469137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8144017/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established the CORtisol NETwork (CORNET) consortium with the initial aim of identifying genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in HPA axis function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001450> "A consortium of population-based cohorts in Europe and Australia with genome-wide genotypes and morning plasma cortisol measured in blood sampled at a controlled time of day, funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government and the British Heart Foundation, that combines their participants of European ancestry in genome-wide association meta-analyses of morning plasma cortisol, formed to identify genetic determinants of inter-individual variation in hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33441111") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7805191/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were obtained from the Amsterdam Born Children and their Development (ABCD) study, a large prospective birth cohort in Amsterdam, the Netherlands [36].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12808570/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women living in Amsterdam between January 2003 and March 2004 were eligible to participate in the Amsterdam Born Children and their Development cohort study (n = 12,393) and were recruited at the first prenatal visit (n = 8266) [44].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12808570/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data in this article are part of the Amsterdam Born Children and their Development cohort: a multi-ethnic birth study, which follows the health, growth and development of approximately 8000 children born in Amsterdam.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children are followed from the womb to young adulthood: their health and development is measured at a few timepoints during this period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main objective of the ABCD study is to identify and analyse factors in early life (during pregnancy and early childhood) that may explain later health and health inequalities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41550966") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://abcd.amsterdamumc.nl/en/background-information-abcd-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, the ABCD study pays specific attention to explaining health differences between children of different ethnic origins.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001451> "A prospective, multi-ethnic birth cohort run from Amsterdam UMC that recruited pregnant women living in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, at their first prenatal visit between January 2003 and March 2004, and follows their children from pregnancy into young adulthood to identify factors in pregnancy and early childhood that explain later health and health inequalities, with particular attention to differences between ethnic groups.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(4) consent to donation of a blood sample and (5) consent to (at least) two home-visits from a researcher, which includes an interview and neuropsychological testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Centenarians are followed annually until death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this reason, we extended the 100-plus Study with a second phase in 2017, in which we also include first-degree family-members of centenarians and their partners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this, we initiated the 100-plus Study in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam in the Netherlands (www.100plus.nl).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 100-plus Study includes (1) Dutch-speaking centenarians who can (2) provide official evidence for being aged 100 years or older, (3) self-report to be cognitively healthy, which is confirmed by an informant (i.e. a child or close relation),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30362018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6290855/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify the characteristics associated with the escape or delay of cognitive decline, we initiated the 100-plus Study (www.100plus.nl).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001452> "An ongoing prospective cohort study, started in 2013 at the Alzheimer Center Amsterdam (Amsterdam UMC), of Dutch-speaking centenarians in the Netherlands who report being cognitively healthy, as confirmed by an informant, and since 2017 also of their first-degree family members and partners, set up to identify characteristics associated with escaping or delaying cognitive decline. Centenarians are visited at home for interviews, neuropsychological testing and blood sampling, followed annually until death, and offered post-mortem brain donation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3634553/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Two Sister Study is a family-based retrospective study of environmental and genetic factors related to young-onset breast cancer, which was developed from the Sister Study (http://www.sisterstudy.org/2Sisters_English/2Sisters.htm).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> "A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3634553/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted the Two Sister Study, a sister-matched case–control study, by enrolling 1422 women between September 2008 and December 2010, who were younger than age 50 years at diagnosis with breast cancer and were enrolled within 4 years of diagnosis, and 1669 breast cancer–free control sisters from the Sister Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> "A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(rdfs:comment "About 1,300 of the sisters with young-onset breast cancer completed all of the study requirements (all questionnaires and saliva sample) and are now being followed prospectively along with Sister Study participants who developed breast cancer after joining the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> "A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study, conducted by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> "A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22773825") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://sisterstudy.niehs.nih.gov/English/2sis.htm") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women who were younger than 50 when they were diagnosed with breast cancer, were diagnosed recently, and had a sister enrolled in the Sister Study were invited to participate in the Two Sister Study, along with their parents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001453> "A family-based study of young-onset breast cancer, conducted by the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences as an offshoot of the Sister Study, that in 2008–2010 enrolled women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 who had a sister in the Sister Study, together with their parents, and used the breast cancer-free Sister Study sisters as matched controls, to study genetic and environmental causes of young-onset breast cancer. The affected women are followed prospectively as breast cancer survivors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7444809/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All questionnaires collected after January 2014 were World Endometriosis Research Foundation Endometriosis Phenome and Biobanking Harmonization Project (WERF EPHect) compliant [16], which are available online (http://endometriosisfoundation.org/ephect).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7444809/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annual questionnaires were collected via the same methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7444809/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, endometriosis cases were enrolled from Boston Children’s Hospital (BCH) and Brigham and Women’s Hospital (BWH) and were eligible if they were 1) female; 2) aged 7–55 years; and 3) had a surgical diagnosis of endometriosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7444809/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, controls were women without a surgical diagnosis of endometriosis and were recruited from clinics at BCH and BWH and from the local Boston community through local advertisement, online postings, and/or word of mouth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11043576/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Women's Health Study: From Adolescence to Adulthood (A2A) is a longitudinal observational cohort study that enrolled 1,549 participants [n = 787 surgically confirmed women with endometriosis (cases) and n = 762 controls] from November 2012–June 2018, enrolling 85% of those who were eligible to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32833998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38495219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38665804") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10940847/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Urine samples were collected at baseline in compliance with the WERF EPHect standardized fluids tools, 23 with the exception that we did not require clean catch collection of urine samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001454> "A longitudinal cohort of the Boston Center for Endometriosis (Boston Children's Hospital and Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston) that in 2012–2018 enrolled adolescent and adult females aged 7–55 with surgically diagnosed endometriosis at the two hospitals, together with participants without endometriosis from their clinics and the local community, collected blood and urine samples at enrolment, and follows participants with annual questionnaires, compliant since 2014 with the World Endometriosis Research Foundation's EPHect standards.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11284829") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the genetic data consisted of three main components: whole genome sequencing data, newly generated genotyping data using the Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array (MEGA), and genotyping data from existing studies or consortia (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11284829") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, we analyzed whole-genome sequenced and high-density genotyped data from 18,034 female cases with breast cancer and 22,104 female controls of African ancestry from 26 studies participating in the AABCG, with 85.3% of participants from the United States and 14.7% from the African continent and Barbados.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC11284829") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we used genetic data from the AABCG, a consortium for a genetic study of breast cancer for females of African ancestry, including genetic data from over 20 studies conducted in the U.S. and Africa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01736-4/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1736_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GAME-ON OncoArray consortium consists of samples from NBHS, CBCS, NC-BCFR, MEC, PLCO, 2SISTER, SISTER, USRT, and WAABCS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13007722/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The genotype datasets used in this study are publicly available via dbGaP (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gap/) including AABC under accession code phs000851.v1.p1, ONCO under accession code phs001265.v1.p1, AMBER under accession code phs000669.v1.p1, ROOT under accession code phs000383.v1.p1, and GBHS under accession code phs002387.v1.p1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38741014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41629673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41629673+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed PRS models for overall BC, estrogen receptor (ER)-positive, ER-negative and triple-negative BC (TNBC) in African-ancestry women using data from the African Ancestry Breast Cancer Genetics consortium (17,391 cases and 18,800 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001455> "A consortium for genetic studies of breast cancer in women of African ancestry that pools whole-genome sequencing data, new Multi-Ethnic Genotyping Array genotypes and existing genotype data on breast cancer cases and controls from more than 20 studies in the United States, Africa and Barbados, among them the samples of the AMBER, ROOT, AABC and GAME-ON OncoArray consortia, for genome-wide association analyses and polygenic risk prediction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3517659/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium was supported by the Australian National Health and Medical Research Council (613627).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> "An Australian research consortium, supported by the National Health and Medical Research Council, that pooled genotyped physician-diagnosed asthma cases and controls of European ancestry from several Australian studies, among them studies of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Lung Institute of Western Australia, the Busselton Health Study and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study, into a genome-wide association study of asthma first reported in 2011. Its data have since been used in international meta-analyses of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3517659/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Next, to prioritise loci for replication, results from the Australian GWAS were combined with those published and made publicly available by the GABRIEL consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> "An Australian research consortium, supported by the National Health and Medical Research Council, that pooled genotyped physician-diagnosed asthma cases and controls of European ancestry from several Australian studies, among them studies of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Lung Institute of Western Australia, the Busselton Health Study and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study, into a genome-wide association study of asthma first reported in 2011. Its data have since been used in international meta-analyses of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4280183/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 2,669 case subjects of European ancestry with physician-diagnosed asthma and 4,528 control subjects of European ancestry without asthma were genotyped for a recent GWAS of asthma described in detail elsewhere.14") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> "An Australian research consortium, supported by the National Health and Medical Research Council, that pooled genotyped physician-diagnosed asthma cases and controls of European ancestry from several Australian studies, among them studies of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Lung Institute of Western Australia, the Busselton Health Study and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study, into a genome-wide association study of asthma first reported in 2011. Its data have since been used in international meta-analyses of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4280183/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and control subjects were drawn from 4 studies: the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (n = 921), the Lung Institute of Western Australia (n = 475), the Busselton Health Study (n = 445), and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study (n = 296).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> "An Australian research consortium, supported by the National Health and Medical Research Council, that pooled genotyped physician-diagnosed asthma cases and controls of European ancestry from several Australian studies, among them studies of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Lung Institute of Western Australia, the Busselton Health Study and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study, into a genome-wide association study of asthma first reported in 2011. Its data have since been used in international meta-analyses of asthma and allergic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24388013") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium (AAGC) Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium AAGC European Australia Population-based and case-control studies 2110 3857") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001456> "An Australian research consortium, supported by the National Health and Medical Research Council, that pooled genotyped physician-diagnosed asthma cases and controls of European ancestry from several Australian studies, among them studies of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Lung Institute of Western Australia, the Busselton Health Study and the Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study, into a genome-wide association study of asthma first reported in 2011. Its data have since been used in international meta-analyses of asthma and allergic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001457> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001457>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Aarhus Aarhus Prostate Cancer Study Aarhus Denmark Hospital-based, Retrospective, Observational") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001457> "A hospital-based, retrospective case-control study of prostate cancer at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are men treated for prostate adenocarcinoma at the hospital's Department of Urology in Skejby and whose controls are age-matched men treated for myocardial infarction or undergoing coronary angioplasty with no prostate cancer diagnosis in the Danish Cancer Register or the Danish Cause of Death Register. It is one of the studies of the PRACTICAL consortium and was genotyped in the consortium's prostate cancer OncoArray project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age-matched males treated for myocardial infarction or undergoing coronary angioplasty, but with no prostate cancer diagnosis based on information retrieved from the Danish Cancer Register and the Danish Cause of Death Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001457> "A hospital-based, retrospective case-control study of prostate cancer at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are men treated for prostate adenocarcinoma at the hospital's Department of Urology in Skejby and whose controls are age-matched men treated for myocardial infarction or undergoing coronary angioplasty with no prostate cancer diagnosis in the Danish Cancer Register or the Danish Cause of Death Register. It is one of the studies of the PRACTICAL consortium and was genotyped in the consortium's prostate cancer OncoArray project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients treated for prostate adenocarcinoma at Department of Urology, Aarhus University Hospital, Skejby (Aarhus, Denmark)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001457> "A hospital-based, retrospective case-control study of prostate cancer at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are men treated for prostate adenocarcinoma at the hospital's Department of Urology in Skejby and whose controls are age-matched men treated for myocardial infarction or undergoing coronary angioplasty with no prostate cancer diagnosis in the Danish Cancer Register or the Danish Cause of Death Register. It is one of the studies of the PRACTICAL consortium and was genotyped in the consortium's prostate cancer OncoArray project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001458> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001458>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20520800") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4754625/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast cancer patients diagnosed before age 50 in 2003-2009 at the NKI-AVL; and (ABCS-F) All non-BRCA1/2 breast cancer cases from the family cancer clinic of the NKI-AVL tested in the period 1995-2009; all ages and diagnosed with breast cancer in 1965-2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001458> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study run from the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital (NKI-AVL) in Amsterdam, whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 (operable invasive cancers diagnosed in 1970–1994 in four Dutch hospitals and, for the iCOGS and OncoArray genotyping, patients diagnosed in 1995–2011 at the NKI-AVL) and whose controls are women recruited through the Sanquin blood bank. A familial arm, ABCS-F, adds breast cancer patients without BRCA1/2 mutations from the NKI-AVL family cancer clinic, and the study contributes to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20520800") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4754625/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based cohort of women recruited through the Sanquin blood bank, all ages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001458> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study run from the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital (NKI-AVL) in Amsterdam, whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer before age 50 (operable invasive cancers diagnosed in 1970–1994 in four Dutch hospitals and, for the iCOGS and OncoArray genotyping, patients diagnosed in 1995–2011 at the NKI-AVL) and whose controls are women recruited through the Sanquin blood bank. A familial arm, ABCS-F, adds breast cancer patients without BRCA1/2 mutations from the NKI-AVL family cancer clinic, and the study contributes to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
