# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4754625/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast cancer patients diagnosed before age 50 in 2003-2009 at the NKI-AVL; and (ABCS-F) All non-BRCA1/2 breast cancer cases from the family cancer clinic of the NKI-AVL tested in the period 1995-2009; all ages and diagnosed with breast cancer in 1965-2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> "The familial arm of the Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study, whose cases are breast cancer patients of any age without a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation who were counselled and tested from 1995 at the family cancer clinic of the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital in Amsterdam, and whose controls are healthy women from the general population recruited through the blood bank. The Breast Cancer Association Consortium lists it as a study separate from the main ABCS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4948019/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ABCS-F cases (N = 1,769) were selected from the linked databases of the Division of Diagnostic Oncology and the Tumor Registry of the Antoni van Leeuwenhoek hospital in Amsterdam32.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> "The familial arm of the Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study, whose cases are breast cancer patients of any age without a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation who were counselled and tested from 1995 at the family cancer clinic of the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital in Amsterdam, and whose controls are healthy women from the general population recruited through the blood bank. The Breast Cancer Association Consortium lists it as a study separate from the main ABCS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4948019/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ABCS-F controls (N = 1,968) are healthy women of all ages (median age was 49 years (range 18–69 years)) from the general population and were recruited through the blood bank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> "The familial arm of the Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study, whose cases are breast cancer patients of any age without a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation who were counselled and tested from 1995 at the family cancer clinic of the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital in Amsterdam, and whose controls are healthy women from the general population recruited through the blood bank. The Breast Cancer Association Consortium lists it as a study separate from the main ABCS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4948019/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included female breast cancer patients of all ages (median age was 42 years (range 14–79 years)), without a pathogenic BRCA1/2 mutation or unclassified variant, who were counselled in the Family Cancer Clinic and diagnosed and/or treated with cancer in the Antoni van Leeuwenhoek hospital in the period 1995–2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> "The familial arm of the Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study, whose cases are breast cancer patients of any age without a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation who were counselled and tested from 1995 at the family cancer clinic of the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital in Amsterdam, and whose controls are healthy women from the general population recruited through the blood bank. The Breast Cancer Association Consortium lists it as a study separate from the main ABCS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27424772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ABCS-F | Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study – Familial | Netherlands | Case-only study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001459> "The familial arm of the Amsterdam Breast Cancer Study, whose cases are breast cancer patients of any age without a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation who were counselled and tested from 1995 at the family cancer clinic of the Netherlands Cancer Institute – Antoni van Leeuwenhoek Hospital in Amsterdam, and whose controls are healthy women from the general population recruited through the blood bank. The Breast Cancer Association Consortium lists it as a study separate from the main ABCS.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001460> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001460>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25496151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30554720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31263747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31263747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6597578/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fresh frozen tumors and matching blood samples were accessed from the Brisbane Breast Bank (BBB) at the University of Queensland Centre for Clinical Research (UQCCR) and from the Australian Breast Cancer Tissue Bank (ABCTB) based at the Westmead Institute for Medical Research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001460> "A breast cancer biobank, headquartered at the Westmead Institute for Medical Research of the University of Sydney, that since 2006 has collected tumour tissue, blood and linked clinical and follow-up data from consenting patients with breast cancer at collection sites across Australia, provides them for research and contributes breast cancer cases to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25496151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30554720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31263747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.aa") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Central Management hub based at Westmead Millennium Institute, University of Sydney, Hawkesbury Road, Westmead, NSW 2145, Australia Collection nodes across Australia") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001460> "A breast cancer biobank, headquartered at the Westmead Institute for Medical Research of the University of Sydney, that since 2006 has collected tumour tissue, blood and linked clinical and follow-up data from consenting patients with breast cancer at collection sites across Australia, provides them for research and contributes breast cancer cases to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25496151") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25855707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30554720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31263747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://openbioresources.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/ojb.aa") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Donors are consented according to standard ethical principles for use of their material for unspecified future research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001460> "A breast cancer biobank, headquartered at the Westmead Institute for Medical Research of the University of Sydney, that since 2006 has collected tumour tissue, blood and linked clinical and follow-up data from consenting patients with breast cancer at collection sites across Australia, provides them for research and contributes breast cancer cases to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
