# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18621558") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22055160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18621558") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2697027/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To exploit the new molecular technologies, an international group of investigators from Australia, New Zealand and the UK have formed “The Aneurysm Consortium” and recently obtained funding to carry out a GWAS of AAA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463> "A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18621558") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22055160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AC: Aneurysm Consortium (AC), cases of AAA together with available DNA recruited in eight centers in the UK, Australia, and New Zealand and also samples from the United Kingdom Small Aneurysm Trial from inpatient populations, outpatient clinics, or population screening programs in the participating centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463> "A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18621558") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22055160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PRS validation set 2: This set includes 1887 cases from AC and 5437 controls from WTCCC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463> "A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18621558") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22055160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37845353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10632148/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WTCCC2: Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 data used included samples from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and from the UK National Blood Service.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001463> "A consortium of investigators in the United Kingdom, Australia and New Zealand formed to carry out a genome-wide association study of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA). Its GWAS dataset pools AAA cases with DNA from eight centres in those countries and from the UK Small Aneurysm Trial, recruited from inpatients, outpatient clinics and population screening programmes, and compares them with Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2 controls from the 1958 British Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07999/MediaObjects/41586_2009_BFnature07999_MOESM226_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All ASD subjects utilized for the case- control analysis were diagnosed with the ADOS (Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule), ADI (Autism Diagnostic Interview) or ADI-R (Autism Diagnostic Interview- Revised) diagnostic tools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07999/MediaObjects/41586_2009_BFnature07999_MOESM226_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we were left with 1,453 samples that met the study criteria of either positive ADI/ADI-R, ADOS or both.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2943511/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To boost power for identifying these associations, we examined an Autism Case-Control cohort (ACC cohort, Table 1), comprising 1,453 subjects with ASDs from several US sites, and 7,070 control subjects without ASDs from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, who were also genotyped on the same platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2925224/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All genome-wide SNP genotyping was performed using the InfiniumII HumanHap550 BeadChip at the Center for Applied Genomics at The Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2925224/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fifty-four per cent were from simplex families, the rest were from multiplex families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404256") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19404257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2925224/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assembled an Autism Case-Control (ACC) cohort by collecting 859 ASD cases (from a total of 1,246 ACC cases, parents, and siblings) of European ancestry, and 1,409 healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001464> "A case-control collection for genome-wide studies of autism spectrum disorders assembled at the Center for Applied Genomics of the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia, combining people with autism spectrum disorders from several US sites, diagnosed with the Autism Diagnostic Interview and/or Autism Diagnostic Observation Schedule and from simplex and multiplex families (with some of their parents and siblings), with control subjects without autism spectrum disorders from the Children's Hospital of Philadelphia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17599422+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Action to Control Cardiovascular Risk in Diabetes (ACCORD) trial is a randomized, multicenter, double 2 x 2 factorial design study involving 10,251 middle-aged and older participants with type 2 diabetes who are at high risk for CVD events because of existing CVD or additional risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 10,251 participants with type 2 diabetes were recruited from seven clinical networks in the U.S. and Canada between 2001 and 2005 and randomized in a 1:1 ratio to receive intensive glucose-lowering treatment, aiming for an HbA1c level below 6%, or to standard treatment, aiming for an HbA1c level between 7.0% and 7.9%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Half of the participants were additionally randomized to a subtrial of intensive versus standard antihypertensive therapy (ACCORD-BP) (23) and the other half to a subtrial of fenofibrate + simvastatin versus simvastatin alone (ACCORD-Lipid) (24).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similarly, none of the ACCORD randomized interventions (i.e., intensive vs. standard glycemic control, fenofibrate + simvastatin vs. placebo + simvastatin, and intensive vs. standard blood pressure control) showed a significant interaction with the GRS on MCE (all P for interaction > 0.1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ACCORD study (ClinicalTrials.gov identifier NCT00000620) was supported by National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute contracts N01-HC-95178, N01-HC-95179, N01-HC-95180, N01-HC-95181, N01-HC-95182, N01-HC-95183, and N01-HC-95184 as well as IAA #Y1-HC-9035 and IAA #Y1-HC-1010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17599422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30262460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6196830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ACCORD trial was aimed at evaluating whether intensive treatments targeting hyperglycemia, elevated blood pressure, and dyslipidemia could reduce the risk of major adverse cardiovascular events among patients with high-risk type 2 diabetes (22).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001465> "A randomised, multicentre, double 2×2 factorial trial cohort of middle-aged and older adults with type 2 diabetes at high risk of cardiovascular events because of existing cardiovascular disease or additional risk factors, recruited in 2001–2005 through seven clinical networks in the United States and Canada with funding from the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. All participants were randomised to intensive or standard glycaemic control and, in two sub-trials, to intensive or standard blood-pressure control or to fenofibrate or placebo added to simvastatin, to test whether these strategies reduce major cardiovascular events.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16256881+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Peripheral and central blood pressure, augmentation pressure (AP), and AIx were determined in 4,001 healthy, normotensive individuals, aged 18 to 90 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> "A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18426997+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seated peripheral (brachial) and central (aortic) blood pressures were assessed, and the ratio between aortic and brachial pulse pressure (pulse pressure ratio, ie, 1/amplification) was calculated in healthy individuals, diabetic subjects, patients with cardiovascular disease, and in individuals with only 1 of the following: hypertension, hypercholesterolemia, or smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> "A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5330867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Height and weight were assessed and a medical history questionnaire, including details of medication was completed. Following 15 min of supine rest, brachial blood pressure and carotid and femoral artery pressure waveforms were recorded, and aPWV determined. Blood samples (20 mL) were then drawn from the antecubital fossa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> "A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5330867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, we explored the relationship between TL and aortic stiffness in two distinct groups of healthy individuals; those aged less than 30 years and those over 50 years, who were pre‐selected on the basis of having aPWV in the lower or upper extremes for their age group and sex.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> "A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16256881") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18426997") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28247509") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12553408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were drawn from the ACCT (Anglo‐Cardiff Collaborative Trial) population, which consists of >12 000 individuals, selected at random from local general practice lists and open‐access Cardiovascular Risk Assessment Clinics across East Anglia and Wales.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001466> "A population of adults in East Anglia and Wales, United Kingdom, selected at random from local general practice lists and open-access cardiovascular risk assessment clinics and studied by investigators in Cambridge and Cardiff, comprising healthy people as well as people with cardiovascular risk factors or disease, whose peripheral and central blood pressure, wave reflection and aortic pulse wave velocity were measured, with questionnaires and blood samples, to study vascular ageing, arterial stiffness and central blood pressure across the adult lifespan.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33310085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26482880+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We identified variants in the MBOAT7 (P = 1.03 × 10(-9)) and TM6SF2 (P = 7.89 × 10(-10)) genes as new risk loci and confirmed rs738409 in PNPLA3 as an important risk locus for alcohol-related cirrhosis (P = 1.54 × 10(-48)) at a genome-wide level of significance.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33310085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26482880+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a genome-wide association study for alcohol-related cirrhosis in individuals of European descent (712 cases and 1,426 controls) with subsequent validation in two independent European cohorts (1,148 cases and 922 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33310085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11093576/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The summary statistics from GWAS of 712 ALC cases and 1466 drinking controls were obtained from http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/ to be meta-analyzed with GenomALC-1 plus NIAAA cohort’s GWAS results.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33310085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide association meta-analysis of 712 cases with alcohol-related cirrhosis and 1,466 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26482880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33310085") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://gengastro.med.tu-dresden.de/suppl/alc_cirrhosis/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3417/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Germany GWAS 1 (n=904) United Kingdom GWAS 2 (n=425) Germany (n=629) Belgium (n=677) Germany (n=730) Belgium (n=654) Case (n=213) Control (n=691) Case (n=243) Control (n=182) Case (n=272) Control (n=417) Case (n=533) Control (n=144)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001467> "A genome-wide association study of alcohol-related cirrhosis in people of European descent that meta-analysed two case–control data sets, one from Germany and one from the United Kingdom, comparing patients with alcohol-related cirrhosis with drinking controls to find genetic risk loci for the disease; its discovery results were published in 2015 and its summary statistics have been reused by later studies of cirrhosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3182557/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place in Newcastle and Greater Manchester between 1983 and 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3182557/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The University of Manchester Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre (ACPRC) programme began in 1983 and this study has documented longitudinal trajectories in cognitive function in a large sample of older adults in the North of England, UK17.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6091034/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For all participants, 50 ml of blood was collected in the morning, after 2 h of fasting, including EDTA blood for DNA isolation, plasma, and buffy coat, clotted blood for serum, and Paxgene tubes for RNA isolation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6091034/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2003, a subsample of 500 Manchester volunteers underwent detailed physical examination and provided samples of saliva, serum, and plasma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12411609/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort recruited healthy, community-dwelling older adults of British European ancestry, which may limit the generalizability of the findings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21826061") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30075734") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796669") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34113784") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40908294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12411609/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed data from 2945 community-dwelling older adults from the University of Manchester Longitudinal Study of Cognition in Normal Healthy Old Age, with up to five repeated assessments of meal timing and health behaviors conducted between 1983 and 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001468> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy community-dwelling volunteers in middle and old age, recruited in Greater Manchester and Newcastle upon Tyne, England, between 1983 and the early 1990s by the University of Manchester's Age and Cognitive Performance Research Centre to chart trajectories of cognitive function in normal old age; participants took alternating batteries of cognitive tests every two years until 2003, with questionnaires on health and behaviour repeated until 2017. Blood was collected for DNA extraction, a Manchester subsample was physically examined and gave saliva, serum and plasma in 2003, and some participants donated their brains to the Manchester Brain Bank.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data and samples were collected using structured interviews, self-rated questionnaires, blood and cerebrospinal fluid samples, magnetic resonance imaging, and neuropsychological tests.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up visits are conducted 7 and 14 years after baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each included patient, age- and sex-matched controls were randomly selected by Statistics Sweden [6] and contacted by mail.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subsequently, in 2009, a second study center was started through a partnership between the Sahlgrenska University hospital in Gothenburg and the Institute of Neuroscience and Physiology at the University of Gothenburg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SBP was established through a collaboration between the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic at the Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28468681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39746340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11965871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The St. Göran Bipolar Project (SBP) is a longitudinal outpatient study investigation aimed at identifying predictive factors associated with long-term outcomes in individuals with bipolar disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001469> "A longitudinal naturalistic cohort of outpatients with bipolar disorder, launched in 2005 by the Karolinska Institutet and the St. Göran bipolar outpatient clinic (the Affective Center) of Northern Stockholm Psychiatry in Stockholm, Sweden, with a second centre in Gothenburg from 2009, which consecutively enrols patients treated at these clinics, with age- and sex-matched population controls randomly selected by Statistics Sweden. It combines clinical ratings, cognitive testing, blood and cerebrospinal fluid sampling, brain imaging and genetics, with follow-up planned at 7 and 14 years, to identify predictors of long-term outcome in bipolar disorder.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10362776/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sporadic AD and control plasma samples [n = 504 control, 912 EOAD (onset < 65 years), 492 LOAD (onset > 65 years)] were a subset of the AD Cardiff Cohort, collected between 2004 and 2020 from individuals recruited from UK community and hospital settings using MRC, Moondance Foundation, and Health and Care Research Wales (HCRW) funding (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> "A case–control cohort of people with sporadic early- or late-onset Alzheimer's disease and elderly controls screened for dementia, recruited from community and hospital settings in the United Kingdom between the early 2000s and 2020 with funding from the Medical Research Council, the Moondance Foundation and Health and Care Research Wales, and assessed with a standardised clinical and neuropsychological protocol. Its longitudinal clinical and cognitive data and blood samples support genome-wide genotyping, plasma biomarker and induced pluripotent stem cell studies of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12365843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All elderly controls were screened for dementia and were chosen to match case samples for sex and ethnicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> "A case–control cohort of people with sporadic early- or late-onset Alzheimer's disease and elderly controls screened for dementia, recruited from community and hospital settings in the United Kingdom between the early 2000s and 2020 with funding from the Medical Research Council, the Moondance Foundation and Health and Care Research Wales, and assessed with a standardised clinical and neuropsychological protocol. Its longitudinal clinical and cognitive data and blood samples support genome-wide genotyping, plasma biomarker and induced pluripotent stem cell studies of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12365843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Anonymized detailed clinical, cognitive, and non-cognitive longitudinal data and genome-wide microarray data (Illumina 610 or global screening array) from the selected donors will be available upon application via the Dementia Platforms UK website (https://portal.dementiasplatform.uk).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> "A case–control cohort of people with sporadic early- or late-onset Alzheimer's disease and elderly controls screened for dementia, recruited from community and hospital settings in the United Kingdom between the early 2000s and 2020 with funding from the Medical Research Council, the Moondance Foundation and Health and Care Research Wales, and assessed with a standardised clinical and neuropsychological protocol. Its longitudinal clinical and cognitive data and blood samples support genome-wide genotyping, plasma biomarker and induced pluripotent stem cell studies of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12365843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following identification, cryopreserved peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) were used to generate iPSC lines from the samples, with recent (“fresh”) donations prioritized, as detailed in Tables 1 and 2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> "A case–control cohort of people with sporadic early- or late-onset Alzheimer's disease and elderly controls screened for dementia, recruited from community and hospital settings in the United Kingdom between the early 2000s and 2020 with funding from the Medical Research Council, the Moondance Foundation and Health and Care Research Wales, and assessed with a standardised clinical and neuropsychological protocol. Its longitudinal clinical and cognitive data and blood samples support genome-wide genotyping, plasma biomarker and induced pluripotent stem cell studies of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35383826") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37480051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40614728") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12365843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort collection used a standardized clinical and comprehensive neuropsychological assessment to diagnose either EOAD or LOAD (see supplemental information).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001470> "A case–control cohort of people with sporadic early- or late-onset Alzheimer's disease and elderly controls screened for dementia, recruited from community and hospital settings in the United Kingdom between the early 2000s and 2020 with funding from the Medical Research Council, the Moondance Foundation and Health and Care Research Wales, and assessed with a standardised clinical and neuropsychological protocol. Its longitudinal clinical and cognitive data and blood samples support genome-wide genotyping, plasma biomarker and induced pluripotent stem cell studies of Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01351961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19246701+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective, dedicated, cross-sectional population of 198 elderly hypertensive patients (mean age 69.3+/-6.2 years) with subjective memory complaints underwent a full set of cognitive function assessments, brain MRI with semiquantification of WMH, carotid ultrasonography, carotid-femoral pulse wave velocity, brachial endothelial function, and plasma von Willebrand Factor measurements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> "A single-centre cohort study at Nancy University Hospital, France, of older treated hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints, recruited in the early 2000s through local press advertisements and general practitioners of the Inserm clinical investigation centre network, who had cognitive testing, brain MRI for white matter hyperintensities, measurements of arterial stiffness, carotid structure and endothelial function, and DNA and serum banking, and were re-examined about eight years later (ADELAHYDE-2), to identify genetic, environmental and vascular determinants of leukoaraiosis and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01351961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5738235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This ancillary PET/MRI study was extracted from the ADELAHYDE longitudinal single-center study, which aimed at identifying factors associated with cognitive decline and white matter diseases in older hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> "A single-centre cohort study at Nancy University Hospital, France, of older treated hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints, recruited in the early 2000s through local press advertisements and general practitioners of the Inserm clinical investigation centre network, who had cognitive testing, brain MRI for white matter hyperintensities, measurements of arterial stiffness, carotid structure and endothelial function, and DNA and serum banking, and were re-examined about eight years later (ADELAHYDE-2), to identify genetic, environmental and vascular determinants of leukoaraiosis and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01351961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7175941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria for ADELAHYDE were age 60–85 years with arterial hypertension (>1 year from diagnosis, receiving antihypertensive treatment for at least one month), presenting with low-grade subjective memory complaints (SMCs) defined as a McNair scale >15 (revised validated French version of 26 items).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> "A single-centre cohort study at Nancy University Hospital, France, of older treated hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints, recruited in the early 2000s through local press advertisements and general practitioners of the Inserm clinical investigation centre network, who had cognitive testing, brain MRI for white matter hyperintensities, measurements of arterial stiffness, carotid structure and endothelial function, and DNA and serum banking, and were re-examined about eight years later (ADELAHYDE-2), to identify genetic, environmental and vascular determinants of leukoaraiosis and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01351961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7175941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were initially (V1) recruited in 2005 by local press advertisements or referral by general practitioners from an investigator network of the Inserm Clinical Investigation Centre.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> "A single-centre cohort study at Nancy University Hospital, France, of older treated hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints, recruited in the early 2000s through local press advertisements and general practitioners of the Inserm clinical investigation centre network, who had cognitive testing, brain MRI for white matter hyperintensities, measurements of arterial stiffness, carotid structure and endothelial function, and DNA and serum banking, and were re-examined about eight years later (ADELAHYDE-2), to identify genetic, environmental and vascular determinants of leukoaraiosis and cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332706") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29276677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01351961") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32039844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7175941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ADELAHYDE study was a prospective, longitudinal, single-center study, with two visits (visit 1, V1 and visit 2, V2) separated by approximately 8 years, investigating the role of vascular factors in the evolution of cognitive impairment and dementia in a cohort of elderly hypertensive patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001471> "A single-centre cohort study at Nancy University Hospital, France, of older treated hypertensive patients with subjective memory complaints, recruited in the early 2000s through local press advertisements and general practitioners of the Inserm clinical investigation centre network, who had cognitive testing, brain MRI for white matter hyperintensities, measurements of arterial stiffness, carotid structure and endothelial function, and DNA and serum banking, and were re-examined about eight years later (ADELAHYDE-2), to identify genetic, environmental and vascular determinants of leukoaraiosis and cognitive decline.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11889014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11889014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11889014+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the present longitudinal study was to compare the progression of aortic stiffness over a 6-year period in treated hypertensive subjects and normotensive subjects, and to evaluate the determinants of this progression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472> "A longitudinal study of the determinants of arterial ageing in French adults of a Paris cohort followed at the Centre d'Investigations Préventives et Cliniques, re-examined years apart with measurements of aortic stiffness and carotid atherosclerosis, and with leukocyte telomere length measured at successive examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11889014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5903283/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a longitudinal study, comprising 154 French men and women (aged 31–76 years at baseline), carotid plaques were quantified by echography and telomere length on leucocytes was measured by Southern blots at baseline and follow-up examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472> "A longitudinal study of the determinants of arterial ageing in French adults of a Paris cohort followed at the Centre d'Investigations Préventives et Cliniques, re-examined years apart with measurements of aortic stiffness and carotid atherosclerosis, and with leukocyte telomere length measured at successive examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11889014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5903283/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were from a Parisian cohort that had been followed at the Centre d’Investigations Préventives et Cliniques.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472> "A longitudinal study of the determinants of arterial ageing in French adults of a Paris cohort followed at the Centre d'Investigations Préventives et Cliniques, re-examined years apart with measurements of aortic stiffness and carotid atherosclerosis, and with leukocyte telomere length measured at successive examinations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11889014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28630210") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5903283/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This research draws on the Evolution de la Rigidité Artérielle (ERA) study, which examined determinants of arterial aging24.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001472> "A longitudinal study of the determinants of arterial ageing in French adults of a Paris cohort followed at the Centre d'Investigations Préventives et Cliniques, re-examined years apart with measurements of aortic stiffness and carotid atherosclerosis, and with leukocyte telomere length measured at successive examinations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnpp.2014.267/MediaObjects/41386_2015_BFnpp2014267_MOESM62_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients were adults of Caucasian origin, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d’Hebron located in Barcelona (Spain), and met Diagnostic and Statistical Manual for Mental Disorders-IV (DSM-IV) criteria for ADHD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473> "A case–control collection of the Psychiatric Genetics Unit of the Vall d'Hebron Research Institute (VHIR) in Barcelona, Spain, of adults of European origin with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, and of unrelated blood donors screened for lifetime ADHD symptoms, genotyped genome-wide to identify loci conferring susceptibility to persistent ADHD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnpp.2014.267/MediaObjects/41386_2015_BFnpp2014267_MOESM62_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control sample consisted of two subsets: (i) 584 unrelated blood donors frequency-matched for gender with the ADHD group in which DSM-IV life- time ADHD symptoms were excluded") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473> "A case–control collection of the Psychiatric Genetics Unit of the Vall d'Hebron Research Institute (VHIR) in Barcelona, Spain, of adults of European origin with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, and of unrelated blood donors screened for lifetime ADHD symptoms, genotyped genome-wide to identify loci conferring susceptibility to persistent ADHD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4330505/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conclusion, we performed a two-step GWAS to identify genetic risk factors for persistent ADHD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473> "A case–control collection of the Psychiatric Genetics Unit of the Vall d'Hebron Research Institute (VHIR) in Barcelona, Spain, of adults of European origin with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, and of unrelated blood donors screened for lifetime ADHD symptoms, genotyped genome-wide to identify loci conferring susceptibility to persistent ADHD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25284319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4330505/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery sample included 607 ADHD cases and 584 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001473> "A case–control collection of the Psychiatric Genetics Unit of the Vall d'Hebron Research Institute (VHIR) in Barcelona, Spain, of adults of European origin with attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder, recruited and evaluated at the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, and of unrelated blood donors screened for lifetime ADHD symptoms, genotyped genome-wide to identify loci conferring susceptibility to persistent ADHD.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s001250100612") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADVANCE is designed to provide reliable evidence on the balance of benefits and risks conferred by blood pressure lowering therapy and intensive glucose control therapy in high-risk diabetic patients, regardless of initial blood pressure or glucose concentrations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16075030+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADVANCE (Action in Diabetes and Vascular disease: Preterax and Diamicron-MR Controlled Evaluation) is a large-scale, 2 x 2 factorial, randomised clinical trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3220831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, subjects had type 2 diabetes diagnosed at ≥30 years of age, were ≥55 years of age at entry to the study, and had either existing cardiovascular disease or at least one risk factor for that disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3220831/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were randomized to 1) the fixed combination of the ACE inhibitor, perindopril, and the diuretic, indapamide (2 mg/0.625 mg, doubled to 4 mg/1.25 mg after 3 months) or matching placebos and 2) intensive (gliclazide MR based, to an HbA1c target of ≤6.5%) or standard (usual care) glucose control.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7496988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ADVANCE‐ON was a follow‐up study that continued observation of people who were alive after their randomized therapies ceased 17.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11596665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16075030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21972410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31967344") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7496988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NCT00145925, clinicaltrials.gov) was a double‐blind RCT, conducted by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries between July 2001 and January 2008, involving 11 140 people with type 2 diabetes mellitus 16.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001474> "A multinational randomised controlled trial with a 2×2 factorial design, conducted from 2001 by 215 collaborating centres in 20 countries in Asia, Australasia, Europe and North America among people with type 2 diabetes diagnosed at age 30 or older, aged 55 or older and with cardiovascular disease or at least one other cardiovascular risk factor, which compared a fixed combination of perindopril and indapamide with placebo, whatever the initial blood pressure, and an intensive gliclazide modified-release-based glucose control regimen targeting an HbA1c of 6.5% or less with standard glucose control, for their effects on major macrovascular and microvascular events; surviving participants were followed after the trial in ADVANCE-ON.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20720431+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients are followed for 3 years after surgery for occurring cardiovascular events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20720431+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The large amount of structurally stored tissue and blood combined with clinical characteristics and follow-up provide an excellent soil for indepth pathophysiological analyses, with assessment of AAA heterogeneity in combination with postoperative clinical outcome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20720431+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study commenced in 2003 in 2 medical centers and currently holds information and material of >300 AAA patients, making it the largest reported aneurysm biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4220929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Aneurysm-Express study (which is a derivative of the previously mentioned Athero-Express study) is a longitudinal biobank study that includes aneurysm tissue from all patients undergoing open surgical abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) repair in two Dutch hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4220929/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Aneurysm-Express study was approved by the institutional review boards of both participating hospitals (University Medical Center Utrecht, Utrecht, The Netherlands, and St. Antonius Hospital, Nieuwegein, The Netherlands) and patients gave written informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20720431") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25372389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31882626") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6934821/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Aneurysm-Express is a biobank study that contains aneurysm sac tissue from patients undergoing open surgical repair of arterial aneurysms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001475> "A biobank study at University Medical Center Utrecht and St. Antonius Hospital Nieuwegein, the Netherlands, set up in 2003 as a derivative of the Athero-Express, of patients undergoing open surgical repair of abdominal aortic and other arterial aneurysms, which stores aneurysm wall tissue collected during surgery together with blood, clinical data and three years of follow-up for cardiovascular events, to study aneurysm heterogeneity in relation to postoperative outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28416818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31113362") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32078373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31113362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6528378/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AFLMU (Germany) 3573 Ongoing registry of AF patients from a large arrhythmia clinic AF 16–93 69% Recurrent AF following intervention (Follow-up available for part of the cohort) ongoing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476> "A biobank and ongoing prospective registry of patients with atrial fibrillation from the arrhythmia clinic of the Department of Medicine I, University Hospital Munich, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Germany, established within the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU with support from the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, which collects blood samples and clinical data and follows patients for recurrence of atrial fibrillation after rhythm-control interventions such as catheter ablation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28416818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31113362") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32078373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32078373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7080569/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AFLMU Biobank has been established at the Department of Medicine I at the University Hospital Munich of the Ludwig-Maximilians-University of Munich Germany with the support of the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research (BMBF).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476> "A biobank and ongoing prospective registry of patients with atrial fibrillation from the arrhythmia clinic of the Department of Medicine I, University Hospital Munich, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Germany, established within the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU with support from the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, which collects blood samples and clinical data and follows patients for recurrence of atrial fibrillation after rhythm-control interventions such as catheter ablation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28416818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31113362") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32078373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7455124/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were collected during the ablation from a groin puncture site and before access to the left atrium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476> "A biobank and ongoing prospective registry of patients with atrial fibrillation from the arrhythmia clinic of the Department of Medicine I, University Hospital Munich, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Germany, established within the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU with support from the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, which collects blood samples and clinical data and follows patients for recurrence of atrial fibrillation after rhythm-control interventions such as catheter ablation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28416818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31113362") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32078373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32814717") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7455124/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients underwent systematic rhythm follow-up with 24-hour Holter monitoring every 3 months (AFACT and MARK AF) or 7-day Holter monitoring (AFLMU; Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001476> "A biobank and ongoing prospective registry of patients with atrial fibrillation from the arrhythmia clinic of the Department of Medicine I, University Hospital Munich, Ludwig-Maximilians-University, Germany, established within the Arrhythmia-Biobank-LMU with support from the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, which collects blood samples and clinical data and follows patients for recurrence of atrial fibrillation after rhythm-control interventions such as catheter ablation.")
