# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10552-011-9894-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ANECS was a population-based case–control study conducted from 2005 to 2007, in which 1,399 women with newly diagnosed histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer and 740 control women provided risk factor information via telephone interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10552-011-9894-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were women aged 18–79 years living in Australia with histologically confirmed epithelial endometrial cancer newly diagnosed between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10552-011-9894-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control women were sampled from the national electoral roll (enrollment in Australia is compulsory) to match the state and age distribution (in 5-year bands) of the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10552-011-9894-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study (ANECS) is an Australia-wide, population-based case–control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10552-011-9894-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were recruited by nurses who liaised with the treatment clinics and state-based cancer registries across Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22245995") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40033780") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29533022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5920223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Overall, 125 (17%) women died during the follow-up period (range, 3.0–8.5 years), 89 of EC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001486> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Australia, run by a study group at QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, whose cases are women aged 18–79 years newly diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary endometrial cancer between July 2005 (May 2005 in Queensland) and December 2007, identified through major hospitals and state cancer registries, and whose controls are women randomly selected from the Australian Electoral Roll and frequency-matched to the cases by state of residence and five-year age group; participants gave risk-factor information by telephone interview and blood samples, and the cases were followed for survival, to study the causes and outcomes of endometrial cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples from all patients were obtained during angiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "No CAD or non-obstructive CAD was defined by absence of lesions or by lesions without significant luminal narrowing of the coronary arteries (<50%)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted as part of the Lübeck Registry of Structural Heart Disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2958814/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the first replication step, additional German DCM cases (mean age 53±13 years; n = 564, n = 440 men, n = 124 women) were recruited from different German study centers: Berlin, n = 64; Lübeck, n = 96 (Angio-Lueb); Marburg, n = 61 (EUROGENE); Münster, n = 101 (EUROGENE); Regensburg, n = 150 (EUROGENE); Regensburg, n = 92 (GoKard).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Lübeck Registry of Structural Heart Disease /KORA (Kooperative Gesundheitsforschung in der Region Augsburg) survey S3/F3 datasets included cases selected from consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography, which were classified as CAD/MI based on the coronary angiogram; cases were < 65 y in males or < 70 y in females.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19348677") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20975947") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23202125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27150028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4858885/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled patients presenting with acute symptom onset at the emergency department at the University Hospital of Schleswig–Holstein, Campus Lübeck, Germany who were diagnosed with central PE (location of the embolism in the pulmonary trunk and/or main pulmonary artery/ies) by CT-pulmonary angiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001487> "A registry of patients with heart disease treated at the University of Lübeck hospital (University Hospital Schleswig-Holstein, Campus Lübeck) in Germany, with blood samples and clinical data, whose angiography sample (Angio-Lueb) consists of consecutive patients referred for coronary angiography and classified from the angiogram as having coronary artery disease or myocardial infarction or not. It has provided cases for genetic association studies of coronary artery disease, with population controls from KORA, and of dilated cardiomyopathy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19525955+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify multiple sclerosis (MS) susceptibility loci, we conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) in 1,618 cases and used shared data for 3,413 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> "A multiple sclerosis case-control collection assembled for genome-wide association studies by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene), a collaboration of multiple sclerosis research groups in Australia and New Zealand, whose cases are people with multiple sclerosis of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand; its genome-wide scan compared them with shared genotype data from controls of European ancestry from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States, and further ANZgene cases and controls were collected for replication and fine-mapping, to identify genetic variants that influence susceptibility to multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19525955+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed replication in an independent set of 2,256 cases and 2,310 controls, for a total of 3,874 cases and 5,723 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> "A multiple sclerosis case-control collection assembled for genome-wide association studies by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene), a collaboration of multiple sclerosis research groups in Australia and New Zealand, whose cases are people with multiple sclerosis of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand; its genome-wide scan compared them with shared genotype data from controls of European ancestry from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States, and further ANZgene cases and controls were collected for replication and fine-mapping, to identify genetic variants that influence susceptibility to multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3035668/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analysis of genotype data from a genome-wide association study which consisted of 1618 MS cases and 3413 healthy controls conducted by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> "A multiple sclerosis case-control collection assembled for genome-wide association studies by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene), a collaboration of multiple sclerosis research groups in Australia and New Zealand, whose cases are people with multiple sclerosis of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand; its genome-wide scan compared them with shared genotype data from controls of European ancestry from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States, and further ANZgene cases and controls were collected for replication and fine-mapping, to identify genetic variants that influence susceptibility to multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3035668/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following quality control as outlined in the ANZgene GWAS [28], this dataset consisted of 1618 MS cases of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand, and 3413 healthy controls of European ancestry from Australia, the UK and the US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> "A multiple sclerosis case-control collection assembled for genome-wide association studies by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene), a collaboration of multiple sclerosis research groups in Australia and New Zealand, whose cases are people with multiple sclerosis of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand; its genome-wide scan compared them with shared genotype data from controls of European ancestry from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States, and further ANZgene cases and controls were collected for replication and fine-mapping, to identify genetic variants that influence susceptibility to multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525955") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21347448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26990204") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4798184/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3268 MS cases and 3579 healthy controls genotyped for the fine-mapping component of this study formed part of a larger ANZgene MS loci fine-mapping study, and were phenotyped according to established criteria [27].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001488> "A multiple sclerosis case-control collection assembled for genome-wide association studies by the Australia and New Zealand Multiple Sclerosis Genetics Consortium (ANZgene), a collaboration of multiple sclerosis research groups in Australia and New Zealand, whose cases are people with multiple sclerosis of European ancestry from Australia and New Zealand; its genome-wide scan compared them with shared genotype data from controls of European ancestry from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States, and further ANZgene cases and controls were collected for replication and fine-mapping, to identify genetic variants that influence susceptibility to multiple sclerosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22171965+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical information and blood are collected from participants after referral by eye practitioners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22171965+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples are collected across Australia and New Zealand using postage kits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22171965+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian and New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma is a prospective study that aims to develop a large cohort of glaucoma cases with severe visual field loss to identify novel genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23453510+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cascade genetic testing was made available for relatives of participants found to carry a Myocilin mutation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23453510+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One thousand sixty individuals with advanced POAG (103 with age at onset of 40 years or younger) and 320 with nonadvanced POAG all recruited by the Australian and New Zealand Registry of Advanced Glaucoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22171965") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23453510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://anzrag.com.au/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28513611") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5520071/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with ARM were recruited in the ANZRAG regardless of their glaucoma status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001489> "A prospective registry, run from the Department of Ophthalmology at Flinders University in Adelaide, of people with glaucoma referred by their eye practitioners across Australia and New Zealand: mainly people with advanced glaucoma (chiefly primary open-angle glaucoma with severe visual field loss), but also with less advanced, secondary and developmental glaucomas such as Axenfeld–Rieger malformation, whose clinical information and blood or saliva samples are collected by post. It was set up to find genetic risk factors for glaucoma blindness, and relatives of participants who carry myocilin mutations are offered cascade genetic testing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3794544/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were sampled from an ongoing study of ovarian histological types comprising approximately 1,000 women with ovarian carcinomas (300 endometrioid, 300 clear cell, 300 mucinous, and 100 high-grade serous).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3794544/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were identified from the Alberta Cancer Registry, a population-based registry that records and maintains data on all new cancer cases and cancer deaths occurring in the province of Alberta, Canada, and for whom we are collecting detailed pathologic assessment, tumor tissue, and clinical data from medical chart abstraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4264456/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annual updates are performed for vital statisticsPathology reports and histological slides reviewed by gynaecologic pathologist") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4264456/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a large study evaluating FOLR1 expression with survival in different histological types of OvCa.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13219410/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "studies used anonymized data, had a retrospective design with no active subject recruitment, clinical interventions or impact on patient care, and used archival pathology specimens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24175302") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25349970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41922350") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13219410/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AOV | Alberta Ovarian Tumor Types Study  | Canada | 1978-2010 | Population-based Alberta Cancer Registry;  annual updates are performed for vital statistics | Pathology reports and histological slides review by the study pathologist") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001490> "A population-based, retrospective study of the histological types of ovarian carcinoma in the province of Alberta, Canada, whose cases are women with ovarian carcinoma identified through the Alberta Cancer Registry and sampled by histological type (endometrioid, clear cell, mucinous and high-grade serous carcinoma), with archival tumour tissue and pathology reports reviewed by a gynaecological pathologist, clinical data abstracted from medical charts and yearly updates of vital status, to study molecular and clinical differences between the types and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20615888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20615888+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "three laboratories within the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource tissue banking network.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3435290/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, from 2004 onwards, 1349 histopathologically-confirmed prostate cancer cases were recruited through private and public urologists in Queensland, Australia via three prostate cancer studies or resources:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3435290/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is well known that genetic variation has the potential to affect gene expression and/or various protein characteristics and hence we sought to investigate the possible role of single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in the KLK4 gene in prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738112/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood was collected according to the APCB's standard operating procedures, which have been reviewed within Australia and by the International Society of Biological and Environmental Repositories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3738112/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource (APCB) collected biological samples and clinical data from men undergoing RP at the Royal Adelaide Hospital (RAH) and St Vincent's Hospital (SVH), Sydney.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23846169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29703916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37370825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10296524/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was a retrospective assessment of men with prostate cancer who had consented to provide radical prostatectomy tissue block samples to the Adelaide node of the Australian Prostate Cancer Bioresource (APCB) between January 2006 and August 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001491> "A national prostate cancer tissue bank in Australia, organised as a network of nodes in several states (among them Queensland, New South Wales and South Australia), that since the mid-2000s has collected radical prostatectomy tissue, blood, and clinical, pathology and follow-up data from men with prostate cancer, recruited through their urologists at diagnosis or before surgery at participating hospitals under common standard operating procedures, and supplies them for research, including genetic association studies of prostate cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3330223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BMD measurements were made at the initial baseline visit (V1), which took place between 1990 and 1994 when the women were aged 45–54 years (n=5114), and from a follow-up visit (V2) between 1997 and 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3330223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was extracted from peripheral blood obtained during the second visit using standard techniques as described previously.43") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3330223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited at random using Community Health Index records from within a 25-mile radius of Aberdeen, a city in the North East of Scotland with a population of ∼250 000.41, 42") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3330223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The longitudinal APOSS is a population-based screening programme for osteoporotic fracture risk in females.40") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28702941+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women from the Aberdeen Prospective Osteoporosis Screening Study (2007-2011, n = 2129, age = 66 years (2.2)) provided dietary intake using a food frequency questionnaire; 37 food groups were created.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22234152") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32547728") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7273562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A second health visit occurred between 1997 and 1999 (n = 3883, now aged 50–62 years) and a third between 2007 and 2011 (n = 2126, aged 60–73 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001492> "A population-based osteoporosis screening study and longitudinal cohort of women from the Aberdeen area of north-east Scotland, selected at random from Community Health Index (primary care) records within 25 miles of Aberdeen and invited, when aged 45–54, to a baseline health visit with bone density measurement in 1990–1994, with further visits in 1997–1999, when blood was taken for DNA, and in 2007–2011, to study bone loss, osteoporotic fracture risk and falls and their dietary, medical and genetic determinants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20211292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were randomly assigned in a 1:1 ratio to receive apixaban or warfarin using a double-blind, double-dummy design.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20211292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of ARISTOTLE is to determine if the factor Xa inhibitor, apixaban, is noninferior to warfarin at reducing the combined endpoint of stroke (ischemic or hemorrhagic) and systemic embolism in patients with AF and at least 1 additional risk factor for stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20211292+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have randomized 18,206 patients from over 1,000 centers in 40 countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23563134") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23563134+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Plasma samples at randomization were available from 14,892 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4908974/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, ARISTOTLE was a multicentre, double blind, double dummy trial comparing apixaban with warfarin performed in 2006-11.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20211292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27306620") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00412984") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39046333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39046333+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Key subgroup analyses from the phase 3 ARISTOTLE trial (NCT00412984) are presented using data from patients who received either concomitant inhibitors or inducers of cytochrome P450 3A4 and/or P‑glycoprotein.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001493> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, double-dummy phase 3 trial, sponsored by Bristol-Myers Squibb and Pfizer, in which patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter and at least one additional risk factor for stroke, enrolled from 2006 at over 1,000 centres in about 40 countries, were randomly assigned to apixaban or warfarin to test whether apixaban is non-inferior to warfarin in preventing stroke or systemic embolism. The trial ended in 2011; its participants' baseline blood samples and genotypes have since been used in biomarker and genetic studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001494> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001494>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16475872") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22504420") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24516880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.gefos.org/?q=content/aarhus-osteoporosis-study-0") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-006-0059-6") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BMD was assessed using dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry (DXA) on a Hologic 1000 (Hologic, Vilvourde, Belgium) or Norland (Gammatec; Varlcse, Denmark) bone densitometer at the lumbar spine and the following standard sites at the hip: femoral neck, trochanter, intertrochanteric region, and Ward’s triangle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001494> "A case–control study of osteoporosis at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are osteoporotic men and women with vertebral fractures or low bone mineral density and whose controls are normal individuals, assessed with dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, radiographs and bone turnover markers and genotyped for candidate-gene studies and for replication of genome-wide association findings on bone mineral density and fracture, which took part in the GENOMOS consortium and in the GEFOS meta-analysis of bone mineral density and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16475872") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22504420") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24516880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.gefos.org/?q=content/aarhus-osteoporosis-study-0") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-006-0059-6") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The case group consisted of 462 osteoporotic patients, defined by a T score of <−2.5 or at least one nontraumatic fracture of the spine, referred to the Department of Endocrinology at Aarhus University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001494> "A case–control study of osteoporosis at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are osteoporotic men and women with vertebral fractures or low bone mineral density and whose controls are normal individuals, assessed with dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, radiographs and bone turnover markers and genotyped for candidate-gene studies and for replication of genome-wide association findings on bone mineral density and fracture, which took part in the GENOMOS consortium and in the GEFOS meta-analysis of bone mineral density and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16475872") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22504420") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24516880") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.gefos.org/?q=content/aarhus-osteoporosis-study-0") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17205326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00223-006-0059-6") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated if the polymorphisms in the IL-1α gene affect the risk of osteoporotic fractures, bone mineral density (BMD), and bone turnover in 462 osteoporotic patients and 336 normal controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001494> "A case–control study of osteoporosis at Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark, whose cases are osteoporotic men and women with vertebral fractures or low bone mineral density and whose controls are normal individuals, assessed with dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, radiographs and bone turnover markers and genotyped for candidate-gene studies and for replication of genome-wide association findings on bone mineral density and fracture, which took part in the GENOMOS consortium and in the GEFOS meta-analysis of bone mineral density and fracture.")
