# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ARREST is aimed at identifying genetic, clinical, pharmacological and environmental determinants of OHCA in the community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ARREST is an ongoing, prospective observational registry of all OHCAs in the study region North Holland, a province of The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After each resuscitation attempt, EMS paramedics routinely send the continuous ECG and impedance recordings from their manual defibrillators to the study centre by modem.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are drawn from a registry that contains drug dispensing records from community pharmacies (PHARMO Institute for Drug Outcomes Research, Utrecht, the Netherlands http://www.pharmo.nl/),10 25 and from a database that contains the complete medical records of >60 000 people from a large group of GPs in the study area (HAG-net-AMC).9 26") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, we include DNA samples from OHCA victims with documented ventricular tachycardia/fibrillation during the resuscitation attempt since July 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pure.amsterdamumc.nl/en/datasets/arrest-amsterdam-resuscitation-studies/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25332818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4189338/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of all OHCA victims since June 2005, we prospectively collect medical history (through hospital and general practitioner), and current and previous medication use (through community pharmacy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001495> "An ongoing prospective, community-based registry, set up in June 2005 and run from the Academic Medical Center in Amsterdam, of all out-of-hospital cardiac arrests with a resuscitation attempt by emergency medical services in the province of North Holland, the Netherlands, which collects resuscitation and ECG data, outcomes, medical history from hospitals and general practitioners, medication use from community pharmacies and, since July 2007, DNA from patients with documented ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation. It studies the outcome and the clinical, pharmacological, environmental and genetic determinants of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest, taking controls from pharmacy and general-practice databases for case–control analyses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23990795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3674800/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Alzheimer's Research UK (formerly the Alzheimer's Research Trust)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> "A collaboration of United Kingdom Alzheimer's disease research groups at the Universities of Nottingham, Manchester, Southampton and Bristol, Queen's University Belfast and the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing, funded by the Alzheimer's Research Trust (renamed Alzheimer's Research UK, after which the collaboration is called the ARUK Consortium), that pooled DNA from people with probable or post-mortem-confirmed Alzheimer's disease and from elderly controls into a DNA bank hosted at the University of Nottingham. Its cases and controls formed one of the sample collections of the GERAD genome-wide association study of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23990795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5937907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All case samples were diagnosed as either definite (post mortem confirmed) or probable Alzheimer’s disease (AD)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> "A collaboration of United Kingdom Alzheimer's disease research groups at the Universities of Nottingham, Manchester, Southampton and Bristol, Queen's University Belfast and the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing, funded by the Alzheimer's Research Trust (renamed Alzheimer's Research UK, after which the collaboration is called the ARUK Consortium), that pooled DNA from people with probable or post-mortem-confirmed Alzheimer's disease and from elderly controls into a DNA bank hosted at the University of Nottingham. Its cases and controls formed one of the sample collections of the GERAD genome-wide association study of Alzheimer's disease.")
