AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23990795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7145452/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The University of Nottingham Group is funded by ARUK and hosts the ARUK Consortium DNA Bank, with the members given in the Appendix I below.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> "A collaboration of United Kingdom Alzheimer's disease research groups at the Universities of Nottingham, Manchester, Southampton and Bristol, Queen's University Belfast and the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing, funded by the Alzheimer's Research Trust (renamed Alzheimer's Research UK, after which the collaboration is called the ARUK Consortium), that pooled DNA from people with probable or post-mortem-confirmed Alzheimer's disease and from elderly controls into a DNA bank hosted at the University of Nottingham. Its cases and controls formed one of the sample collections of the GERAD genome-wide association study of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23990795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were drawn from the MRC genetic resource for AD; the ART Collaboration; Competence Network of Dementia and Department of Psychiatry, University of Bonn; Aristotle University of Thessaloniki; a Belgian sample derived from a prospective clinical study at the Memory Clinic and Department of Neurology, ZNA Middelheim, Antwerpen10 ; and the University of Munich.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> "A collaboration of United Kingdom Alzheimer's disease research groups at the Universities of Nottingham, Manchester, Southampton and Bristol, Queen's University Belfast and the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing, funded by the Alzheimer's Research Trust (renamed Alzheimer's Research UK, after which the collaboration is called the ARUK Consortium), that pooled DNA from people with probable or post-mortem-confirmed Alzheimer's disease and from elderly controls into a DNA bank hosted at the University of Nottingham. Its cases and controls formed one of the sample collections of the GERAD genome-wide association study of Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19734902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23990795") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29675612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32274467") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery sample included 4,113 cases and 1,602 elderly screened controls genotyped at the Sanger Institute on the Illumina 610-quad chip, referred to collectively hereafter as the 610 group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001496> "A collaboration of United Kingdom Alzheimer's disease research groups at the Universities of Nottingham, Manchester, Southampton and Bristol, Queen's University Belfast and the Oxford Project to Investigate Memory and Ageing, funded by the Alzheimer's Research Trust (renamed Alzheimer's Research UK, after which the collaboration is called the ARUK Consortium), that pooled DNA from people with probable or post-mortem-confirmed Alzheimer's disease and from elderly controls into a DNA bank hosted at the University of Nottingham. Its cases and controls formed one of the sample collections of the GERAD genome-wide association study of Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-010-0519-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were general hospital surgery in-patients and orthopaedic and traumatology patients aged 30–79.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00420-010-0519-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, cases were defined as being new cases of skin (non-melanoma), bladder and kidney cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3346769/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Arsenic Health Risk Assessment and Molecular Epidemiology (ASHRAM) study, a case–control study, was conducted in areas of Hungary, Romania, and Slovakia with reported presence of iAs in groundwater.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3346769/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, controls were frequency matched to all potential cancer cases by sex, 5-year age band, and residence in the same county/region of the study area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3346769/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Urinary metabolites of iAs, methylarsonic acid [MA, MA(V) unless otherwise noted] and dimethylarsinic acid [DMA, DMA(V) unless otherwise noted] were measured with high-performance liquid chromatography with inductively coupled plasma/mass spectrometry (Lindberg et al. 2006).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20401490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22436128") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Arsenic Health Risk Assessment and Molecular Epidemiology study in Central Europe (ASHRAM) 43, 44 London School Of Hygiene And Tropical Medicine, UK Case-control Hospital based in Slovakia and Hungary 2002- 2004 89 425** 84 399** 610Q 317K CNG CNG") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001497> "A hospital-based case–control study of basal cell carcinoma of the skin and of bladder and kidney cancers in relation to low-level inorganic arsenic in drinking water, funded by the European Commission and conducted in 2002–2004 in counties of Hungary, Romania and Slovakia with arsenic in groundwater. Its incident cases, and its controls drawn from general surgery, orthopaedic and trauma in-patients of hospitals across the same areas and frequency matched to the cases by age, sex and county, all aged 30–79, were assessed for lifetime arsenic exposure, urinary arsenic metabolites and genetic susceptibility.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2572614/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the Athens Study of Psychosis Proneness and Incidence of Schizophrenia (ASPIS) examined 2243 randomly selected young male conscripts aged 18 to 24 years from the Greek Air Force in their first 2 weeks of admission to the National Basic Air Force Training Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2572614/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Their associations with self-rated schizotypy (SPQ), vigilance, verbal, spatial working memory and antisaccade eye performance were tested with regressions in a representative population of 2,243 young male military conscripts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22503357+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Then, 2 years later (T(2)-second assessment), at the time of military discharge, they were tested for NSS with the Neurological Evaluation Scale (NES) and reevaluated with the SPQ, the SCL-90-R and additionally the Structured Clinical Interview for Personality Disorders (SCID-II) for the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders Third Edition, Revised (DSM-III-R).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3796069/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Military service is compulsory in Greece, and all healthy men are recruited and assigned to the different army corps by random assignment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3796069/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants at the time of data collection were undergoing a mandatory military training program at the Greek Air Force during the first 2 weeks of admission to the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, Greece.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18834502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22503357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23155182") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3796069/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the ASPIS (Athens Study of Psychosis Proneness and Incidence of Schizophrenia), 8 such consecutive separate waves of conscripts were assessed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001498> "A study of young men aged 18–24 doing compulsory military service in Greece, randomly selected in successive waves during their first two weeks at the National Basic Air Force Training Center in Tripolis, who completed self-rated questionnaires on schizotypy and psychopathology and computerised neurocognitive and eye-movement tasks and gave DNA, a subgroup being reassessed at discharge two years later. Led from the University Mental Health Research Institute in Athens, it studies psychosis proneness and its cognitive and genetic correlates in the general population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4115148/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all subjects, post-cycloplegic refraction (following instillation of tropicamide 1%) for both eyes was measured using a Humphrey-598 automatic refractor (Carl Zeiss Meditec, Inc.).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.96") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ATES and GEM studies have undertaken studies into the genetic influences on a number of ophthalmic traits through the use of heritability studies, linkage studies, genome-wide association studies, and candidate gene-based studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.96") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first stage of recruitment involved directly approaching twins who had already agreed to participate in the Tasmanian Asthma Study (TAS) and the Tasmanian Infant Health Survey (THIS);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2012.96") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second wave of recruitment into the ATES was conducted through the ATR, beginning in 2001 through an application entitled the ‘Twin study of ophthalmic screening parameters’.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4141707/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similarly to the TwinsUK samples, they were genotyped with HumanHap610-Quad array (Illumina) at CIDR.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20835236") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23116649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23599335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4141707/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian Twin Eye Study comprises participants examined as part of the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania (TEST) or the Brisbane Adolescent Twins Study (BATS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001499> "An Australian twin study of eye traits that combines twins, and some of their siblings, given an eye examination in the Twins Eye Study in Tasmania or in the Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, with measures such as cycloplegic refraction, intraocular pressure and retinal photographs and with genome-wide genotypes, used in heritability, linkage and genome-wide association studies of ophthalmic traits. Its participants were recruited through the Australian Twin Registry, existing twin studies, schools and publicity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2700867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between November 1996 and June 2000, 1,303 CAD patients (75% males, mean age: 61.7 ± 0.3 years) were recruited at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz at the occasion of a diagnostic coronary angiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2700867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy control subjects (n = 484, 73% males, mean age 60.0 ± 0.4 years) were recruited either from general practitioners’ offices in the course of a routine check-up or by newspaper announcement.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3523004/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Athero Gene study is a prospective cohort of CAD patients enrolled during several successive phases of recruitment between November 1996 and February 2004 [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4496051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AtheroGene study is a prospective, multicenter, clinical cohort study including patients with known CAD (at least one stenosis over 30%) as diagnosed by coronary angiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4496051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the AtheroGene study was to elucidate clinical, genetic and laboratory factors associated with progression of coronary atherosclerosis and outcome during follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19495570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23136988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26154343") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32321351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7428563/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During a median follow‐up of 4.0 years, 10.3% of the subjects had a nonfatal MI and/or cardiovascular death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001500> "A prospective clinical cohort of patients with coronary artery disease (at least one coronary stenosis over 30% on angiography), from stable angina to acute coronary syndromes, enrolled in successive phases from November 1996 to early 2004 when they underwent coronary angiography at the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz or the Bundeswehrzentralkrankenhaus Koblenz, Germany, and followed for cardiovascular death and non-fatal myocardial infarction. It studies clinical, genetic and laboratory determinants of the progression and outcome of coronary atherosclerosis, and for genetic case–control analyses also recruited healthy controls from the Rhein-Main area.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases and controls were unrelated; one individual was selected from each family.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed migraine data were collected by means of semi-structured telephone interviews, with a mean age at interview of 37.5 years [SD = 11.3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ATM study includes data from Australian twins and their families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases (N = 2,825; 752 [27%] male, 2,073 [73%] female) were preferentially selected from each family based on migraine severity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population controls (N = 3,525; 1,814 [51%] male, 1,711 [49%] female) were randomly selected from families containing no known migraine cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2676/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2676_MOESM11_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24081561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3947136/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects were drawn from the QIMR GWA cohort of over 19,000 individuals genotyped using a variety of Illumina GWA arrays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001501> "A genome-wide association case–control sample of unrelated Australians of European descent, one from each family, drawn from the twins and their relatives studied at the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) who were genotyped genome-wide: migraine cases, identified in semi-structured telephone interviews based on the International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-II) or by self-report and chosen preferentially for severity, and population controls from families with no known migraine. It is one of the studies of the International Headache Genetics Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study was undertaken in 933 European ancestry individuals with severe asthma based on Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA) criteria 3 or above and 3346 clean controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> "A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 3353 control subjects without history of asthma or wheeze (clean controls) were collected from the UK and Western Australia, all of whom were of European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> "A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of this study was to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and to evaluate whether susceptibility to severe asthma differs from that of mild to moderate asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> "A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We acknowledge support of Asthma UK, the Wellcome Trust and the Medical Research Council.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> "A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://thorax.bmj.com/content/67/9/762") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped 1026 individuals of European ancestry with severe asthma based on the Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA) criteria.18 Only subjects in classes 3–5 were included, recruited across UK-based centres.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001502> "A genetic study of severe asthma in the United Kingdom, supported by Asthma UK, which recruited people of European ancestry with severe asthma (Global Initiative for Asthma classes 3–5) at UK centres and compared them in genome-wide association studies with controls without asthma or wheeze, to identify genetic determinants of severe asthma and whether they differ from those of mild to moderate asthma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11631763/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Amsterdam UMC (AUMC) dataset, AUMC samples were omitted from the PRS training data, and PRS was used to discriminate clinical DCM cases (N = 783) from referents (N = 6,978).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01975-5/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1975_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this study we have received data from unrelated individuals from NTR.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01975-5/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1975_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Other inclusion criteria included the presence of a DNA sample for genotyping and an age older than 18 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01975-5/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1975_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with DCM in the Amsterdam UMC cohort were defined as index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to the Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for DCM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01975-5/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1975_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group was sourced from the Dutch Twin Register (NTR)10 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39572784") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-024-01975-5/MediaObjects/41588_2024_1975_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The diagnosis of DCM was confirmed for all patients by manual examination of the medical chart, with a required left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) of less than 50% to indicate hypocontractility9 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001503> "A case–control dataset for genome-wide association studies of dilated cardiomyopathy assembled at Amsterdam UMC, the Netherlands. Its cases are adult index patients referred by secondary or tertiary cardiologists to Amsterdam UMC for genetic testing for dilated cardiomyopathy, with the diagnosis confirmed from the medical chart and a left ventricular ejection fraction below 50%, and its controls are unrelated participants of the Netherlands Twin Register.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients have been studied repeatedly every 1 to 1.5 years to improve the phenotype.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment was done consecutively in the outpatient departments of these two hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Austrian Diabetic Nephropathy Study (AusDiane) was initiated in 2012 in the state of Salzburg in Austria, and is part of the InterDiane Consortium (please see also the InterDiane cohort description).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane) was initiated in 2010 based on the protocol of the FinnDiane Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the study is to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications in patients with T1D.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients have been studied during a regular visit at two hospitals (Department of Internal Medicine 1, Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001504> "A clinic-based cohort study of patients with type 1 diabetes in the state of Salzburg, Austria, initiated in 2012 as the Austrian study of the International Diabetic Nephropathy Consortium (InterDiane), which follows the protocol of the Finnish Diabetic Nephropathy Study to identify risk factors for diabetic nephropathy and other chronic complications of type 1 diabetes. Patients are recruited consecutively at the outpatient departments of Paracelsus Medical University Hospital Salzburg and Diakonissen-Wehrle Hospital Salzburg, with clinical data drawn mainly from the Type 1 diabetes Registry of the state of Salzburg, and are re-examined every 1 to 1.5 years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19089808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20801717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24964207") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30232950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19089808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19089808+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of our study is to explore the association of DTNBP1 with BD and with a sub phenotype, presence/absence of psychotic symptoms, in a sample of 515 patients with BD (ICD10/DSMIV) and 1,316 ethnically matched control subjects recruited from the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505> "A case–control genetic association study of bipolar disorder in the United Kingdom, funded by GlaxoSmithKline, whose cases are people with bipolar disorder recruited in London and diagnosed with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry (SCAN) interview and the Operational Criteria Checklist, and whose controls are ethnically matched subjects recruited in the UK; its control group has also served as UK controls in genome-wide association studies of other disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19089808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20801717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24964207") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30232950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20801717") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3257853/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected samples from patients with sporadic ALS from 20 UK hospitals and obtained UK control samples from the control groups of the Depression Case Control study, the Bipolar Affective Case Control Study, and the British 1958 birth cohort DNA collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505> "A case–control genetic association study of bipolar disorder in the United Kingdom, funded by GlaxoSmithKline, whose cases are people with bipolar disorder recruited in London and diagnosed with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry (SCAN) interview and the Operational Criteria Checklist, and whose controls are ethnically matched subjects recruited in the UK; its control group has also served as UK controls in genome-wide association studies of other disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19089808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20801717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24964207") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30232950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24964207") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4309466/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the Bipolar Affective Disorder Case Control Study (BACCs) (n = 470) were recruited in London, United Kingdom in the same manner and assessed for diagnosis using the SCAN interview and Operational Criteria Checklist for Psychotic Illness Program [McGuffin et al., 1991].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505> "A case–control genetic association study of bipolar disorder in the United Kingdom, funded by GlaxoSmithKline, whose cases are people with bipolar disorder recruited in London and diagnosed with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry (SCAN) interview and the Operational Criteria Checklist, and whose controls are ethnically matched subjects recruited in the UK; its control group has also served as UK controls in genome-wide association studies of other disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19089808") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20801717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24964207") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30232950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30232950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6429240/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GlaxoSmithKline Research and Development funded BaCCs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001505> "A case–control genetic association study of bipolar disorder in the United Kingdom, funded by GlaxoSmithKline, whose cases are people with bipolar disorder recruited in London and diagnosed with the Schedules for Clinical Assessment in Neuropsychiatry (SCAN) interview and the Operational Criteria Checklist, and whose controls are ethnically matched subjects recruited in the UK; its control group has also served as UK controls in genome-wide association studies of other disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Most BBDP subjects are enrolled as cognitively normal volunteers residing in the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix, Arizona.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specific recruitment efforts are also directed at subjects with Alzheimer’s disease, Parkinson’s disease and cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement disorders assessments during life and more than 90% receive full pathological examinations by medically licensed pathologists after death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BBDP is a longitudinal clinicopathological study of AD, PD and normal aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brain and Body Donation Program (BBDP) at Banner Sun Health Research Institute (http://www.brainandbodydonationprogram.org) started in 1987 with brain-only donations and currently has banked more than 1600 brains.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25619230") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4593391/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The collective academic output of the BBDP is now described as the Arizona Study of Aging and Neurodegenerative Disorders (AZSAND).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001506> "A brain and body donation programme and clinicopathological study of ageing and neurodegenerative disorders at Banner Sun Health Research Institute in Arizona, United States, started in 1987. Its participants, mostly cognitively normal volunteers from the retirement communities of metropolitan Phoenix together with people recruited because they have Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease or cancer, receive standardized general medical, neurological, neuropsychological and movement-disorder assessments during life and, for most, a full pathological examination after death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, we report the results of the BARCODE1 Pilot, which was set up as a feasibility study to examine the acceptability of the study to men in the UK community prior to opening the main BARCODE1 study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men in the top 10% of the study population’s genetic risk distribution are offered screening with MRI of the prostate followed by systematic and targeted biopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BARCODE1 Pilot has shown this community study in the UK to be feasible, with an overall uptake of 26%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BARCODE1 study (NCT03857477) is enrolling men of European ancestry from the community via their GPs to undergo a germline genetic profile test utilising 130 PCa risk SNPs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main BARCODE1 study is now open and will recruit 5000 men.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34214236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9292247/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was co‐ordinated and managed by the Oncogenetics Team at The Institute of Cancer Research, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001507> "A community-based prostate cancer risk-screening study in the United Kingdom, coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research, that invites men of European ancestry via their general practitioners to undergo a germline genetic profile test of prostate cancer risk single nucleotide polymorphisms. Men in the highest genetic-risk stratum are offered MRI-led prostate screening and targeted biopsy; the study began with a feasibility pilot before opening to wider recruitment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of enrollment, 1132 of these subjects had a diagnosis of remitting-relapsing MS according to the McDonald criteria, and 208 had a diagnosis of CIS with MRI signs suggestive of demyelination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> "A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "But empirically, the effect may be modest: The distribution of wGRS in the derivation sample is plotted in Figure 1, along with that of the validation sample collection assembled from several therapeutic trials (TT) that has not previously been used in genome-wide association studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> "A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotypes for the TT and MIGEN subjects were available from genome-wide genotyping data collected using Affymetrix Genechip 6.0 arrays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> "A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similarly, details on the first validation set that includes subjects assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from its therapeutic trials include a total of 1340 cases (Table 1b).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> "A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19879194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3099419/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They come from 3 studies evaluating IFNβ-1b and one study evaluating a CCR1-antagonist.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001508> "A collection of patients with relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis or a clinically isolated syndrome with MRI signs of demyelination, assembled by Bayer Schering Pharma from four of its clinical trials: three studies of interferon beta-1b (BENEFIT, BEYOND and the 16-year long-term follow-up of the pivotal interferon beta-1b trial in relapsing–remitting multiple sclerosis) and one of a CCR1 antagonist. It was genotyped genome-wide and used as multiple sclerosis cases in genetic studies of susceptibility.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17030683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19696694+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two thousand and eighty-nine (2089) Caucasian women without preexisting diabetes and preexisting hypertension with singleton pregnancies delivering consecutively at the Charité obstetrics department participated in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> "A birth cohort of mother–child pairs recruited at delivery in the 2000s from women with singleton pregnancies giving birth consecutively at the obstetrics department of the Charité university hospital in Berlin, Germany, with maternal blood, umbilical cord blood, placentas and birth measurements collected at birth. It is used to study maternal and fetal influences, including genetic ones, on birth weight, pregnancy outcomes and maternal physiology in pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17030683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29309628+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The identified associations indicate that genetic effects on maternal glucose, cytochrome P450 activity and gestational duration, and potentially on maternal blood pressure and immune function, are relevant for fetal growth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> "A birth cohort of mother–child pairs recruited at delivery in the 2000s from women with singleton pregnancies giving birth consecutively at the obstetrics department of the Charité university hospital in Berlin, Germany, with maternal blood, umbilical cord blood, placentas and birth measurements collected at birth. It is used to study maternal and fetal influences, including genetic ones, on birth weight, pregnancy outcomes and maternal physiology in pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17030683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31954177+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Associations between maternal smoking behavior and 163 cord blood metabolites and associations between newborn head circumference and concentrations of smoking behavior related metabolites were analysed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> "A birth cohort of mother–child pairs recruited at delivery in the 2000s from women with singleton pregnancies giving birth consecutively at the obstetrics department of the Charité university hospital in Berlin, Germany, with maternal blood, umbilical cord blood, placentas and birth measurements collected at birth. It is used to study maternal and fetal influences, including genetic ones, on birth weight, pregnancy outcomes and maternal physiology in pregnancy.")
