AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17030683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6976643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Placental samples were collected directly after delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> "A birth cohort of mother–child pairs recruited at delivery in the 2000s from women with singleton pregnancies giving birth consecutively at the obstetrics department of the Charité university hospital in Berlin, Germany, with maternal blood, umbilical cord blood, placentas and birth measurements collected at birth. It is used to study maternal and fetal influences, including genetic ones, on birth weight, pregnancy outcomes and maternal physiology in pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17030683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19696694") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29309628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31954177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31969597") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6976643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted in 1023 mothers with singleton pregnancies delivering at the Charité obstetrics department, Berlin, Germany from 2000 to 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001509> "A birth cohort of mother–child pairs recruited at delivery in the 2000s from women with singleton pregnancies giving birth consecutively at the obstetrics department of the Charité university hospital in Berlin, Germany, with maternal blood, umbilical cord blood, placentas and birth measurements collected at birth. It is used to study maternal and fetal influences, including genetic ones, on birth weight, pregnancy outcomes and maternal physiology in pregnancy.")

