# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17722095+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated PCBs and organochlorine pesticides and risk of NHL in a population-based case-control study in British Columbia, Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2788526/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All HIV-negative NHL cases diagnosed in British Columbia from March 2000 to February 2004, residing in the Greater Vancouver Regional District and greater Victoria (Capital Regional District), aged 20 to 79 were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2788526/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population controls were identified from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health and were frequency matched to cases by sex, age, and area of residence in a 1:1 ratio.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2788526/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To systematically investigate the role of NBS1, MRE11, RAD50 and BLM in susceptibility to NHL, we carried out re-sequencing of these four genes to establish the spectrum of genetic variation in NHL cases, and genotyped 797 NHL cases and 793 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17722095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19917125") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41375-022-01711-0/MediaObjects/41375_2022_1711_MOESM1_ESM.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First primary NHL diagnosis from Vancouver and Victoria metropolitan areas identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-infected and post-transplant cases)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001512> "A population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in British Columbia, Canada, which invited residents of Greater Vancouver and Greater Victoria aged 20–79 with non-Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed from March 2000 to February 2004, identified through the BC Cancer Registry (excluding HIV-positive and post-transplant cases), together with population controls from the Client Registry of the British Columbia Ministry of Health frequency-matched to the cases on sex, age and area of residence, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://bcmj.org/articles/british-columbia-familial-hypercholesterolemia-registry") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27931859+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this study was to characterize the clinical features, current treatment patterns, and CV outcomes of patients with HeFH in British Columbia, Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> "A registry of people with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in British Columbia, Canada, based at the Healthy Heart Program Prevention Clinic of St. Paul's Hospital in Vancouver, which enrols clinic patients meeting the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria, invites their relatives for evaluation and follows adult participants prospectively as an open observational cohort. Set up as the first such registry in Canada to improve the identification and management of the condition, it is also used to study its cardiovascular outcomes and genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://bcmj.org/articles/british-columbia-familial-hypercholesterolemia-registry") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7889287/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The British Columbia Familial Hypercholesterolemia (BCFH) cohort is a prospective, longitudinal, open observational study of adults (≥18 years) with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolemia (FH) in the Canadian province of British Columbia, Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> "A registry of people with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in British Columbia, Canada, based at the Healthy Heart Program Prevention Clinic of St. Paul's Hospital in Vancouver, which enrols clinic patients meeting the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria, invites their relatives for evaluation and follows adult participants prospectively as an open observational cohort. Set up as the first such registry in Canada to improve the identification and management of the condition, it is also used to study its cardiovascular outcomes and genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://bcmj.org/articles/british-columbia-familial-hypercholesterolemia-registry") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7889287/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The library preparation, sequencing, and variant analysis for our targeted next-generation sequencing workflow for assessing FH- associated variants in individuals from the BCFH cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> "A registry of people with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in British Columbia, Canada, based at the Healthy Heart Program Prevention Clinic of St. Paul's Hospital in Vancouver, which enrols clinic patients meeting the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria, invites their relatives for evaluation and follows adult participants prospectively as an open observational cohort. Set up as the first such registry in Canada to improve the identification and management of the condition, it is also used to study its cardiovascular outcomes and genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://bcmj.org/articles/british-columbia-familial-hypercholesterolemia-registry") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11846310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FH patients were initially screened with information available within the FH registry (age, location, Dutch Lipid Clinic Network Score (DLCNS), presence of comorbidities, listed as ‘active,’ consented for research purposes).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> "A registry of people with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in British Columbia, Canada, based at the Healthy Heart Program Prevention Clinic of St. Paul's Hospital in Vancouver, which enrols clinic patients meeting the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria, invites their relatives for evaluation and follows adult participants prospectively as an open observational cohort. Set up as the first such registry in Canada to improve the identification and management of the condition, it is also used to study its cardiovascular outcomes and genetic causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://bcmj.org/articles/british-columbia-familial-hypercholesterolemia-registry") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39987058") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11846310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FH patients were recruited from the British Columbia Familial Hypercholesterolemia Registry (Healthy Heart Program - Prevention Clinic, St. Paul’s Hospital, Vancouver, Canada).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001513> "A registry of people with clinically diagnosed heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia in British Columbia, Canada, based at the Healthy Heart Program Prevention Clinic of St. Paul's Hospital in Vancouver, which enrols clinic patients meeting the Dutch Lipid Clinic Network criteria, invites their relatives for evaluation and follows adult participants prospectively as an open observational cohort. Set up as the first such registry in Canada to improve the identification and management of the condition, it is also used to study its cardiovascular outcomes and genetic causes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC468645/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Geographic area Philadelphia New York, New Jersey, Connecticut Salt Lake City Melbourne, Sydney Province of Ontario") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC468645/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male with breast cancer; female with breast or ovarian cancer diagnosed at age <45; female with breast and ovarian cancer diagnosed at any age; two first- or second-degree or three first-, second-, or third-degree relatives with breast or ovarian cancer; BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation carrier") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All sites collected the following: family history data from probands; epidemiological and dietary data, and blood samples (or mouthwash samples if venipuncture was declined) from probands and selected relatives; and clinical and treatment data, tumor blocks and pathology reports for probands and relatives with a personal history of breast or ovarian cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinic-based families, including those of Ashkenazi Jewish ancestry, were recruited from their local populations in the USA by Columbia University in New York City, New York") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1064100/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 1995 the MNYR has been recruiting families with breast and/or ovarian cancers in clinical and community settings within the metropolitan New York area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11018378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642171") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29244822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5731703/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In terms of follow-up, we contacted at least one participant from each family annually to update personal and family cancer histories and deaths, as well as some exposures addressed in the core epidemiology questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001514> "The New York site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, known as the Metropolitan New York Registry and run from Columbia University in New York City, which from 1995 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through clinical and community settings in the New York metropolitan area (New York, New Jersey and Connecticut), including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, several relatives were affected or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")

