AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All sites collected the following: family history data from probands; epidemiological and dietary data, and blood samples (or mouthwash samples if venipuncture was declined) from probands and selected relatives; and clinical and treatment data, tumor blocks and pathology reports for probands and relatives with a personal history of breast or ovarian cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001515> "The Philadelphia site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, run from Fox Chase Cancer Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, which from 1996 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through family cancer clinics and community outreach in the Philadelphia area, including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 35, both cancers, or bilateral breast cancer first diagnosed before 50, a man had breast cancer, affected relatives spanned two generations or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC468645/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the clinic-based families in the USA, at least one participant from each family is contacted annually to update personal and family cancer histories and deaths, as well as some exposures addressed in the core epidemiology questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001515> "The Philadelphia site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, run from Fox Chase Cancer Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, which from 1996 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through family cancer clinics and community outreach in the Philadelphia area, including Ashkenazi Jewish and minority families, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 35, both cancers, or bilateral breast cancer first diagnosed before 50, a man had breast cancer, affected relatives spanned two generations or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are contacted annually for follow-up, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
