# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001516> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001516>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26174520") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26538066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.bcfamilyregistry.org/for-participants/participating-sites") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15217505") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC468645/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male with breast cancer; female with breast or ovarian cancer diagnosed at age <45; female with breast and ovarian cancer diagnosed at any age; three individuals in two generations with breast or ovarian cancer, one diagnosed at age <45; BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation carrier") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001516> "The Utah site of the Breast Cancer Family Registry, run from the Huntsman Cancer Institute at the University of Utah in Salt Lake City, which from 1996 enrolled families with breast or ovarian cancer through family cancer clinics and community outreach in the Salt Lake City area, and later further families carrying BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations, when a woman had breast or ovarian cancer before age 45 or both cancers, a man had breast cancer, three relatives in two generations were affected (one before age 45) or a BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation was known. Affected and unaffected probands and their relatives gave family-history and epidemiological questionnaires and blood samples and are followed up by annual contact and by linkage to population-based cancer registries, for studies of the genetic epidemiology of breast cancer.")
