# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12791629+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were the offspring, who were aged 23-27 y at follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3313975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A follow-up of the 951 participants who had completed the original trial at 5 years was conducted between 1997 and 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3313975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Barry Caerphilly Growth (BCG) cohort study is a long-term follow-up of a randomized controlled trial of 1,163 infants born consecutively between March 1972 and October 1974 in two populations from the towns of Barry and Caerphilly in South Wales [15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1627387") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1972 the opportunity was taken to set up a randomised controlled trial to investigate the effect on thegrowthofchildren, fromearlyinpregnancy to 5 years, ofentitlement to a daily supplement ofmilk comparablewiththatwhichhadbeenavailableunder the Welfare Food Act, 1940.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1627387") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In each town contact was made through general practitioners with a consecutive series of just over 700 newly pregnant women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12791629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17921364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23790346") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7030223") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1627387") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The infants were visited by specially trained nurses at 10 days, at 6 weeks, and at 3, 6, 9 and 12 months and thereafter at 6-monthly intervals until their fifth birthdays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001517> "A cohort of children born consecutively from March 1972 to October 1974 in the towns of Barry and Caerphilly, South Wales, whose mothers were recruited early in pregnancy through general practitioners into a randomised controlled trial, set up in 1972 by the Medical Research Council Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and the Welsh National School of Medicine in Cardiff, of milk tokens for pregnant women and their children up to five years of age, with the children examined by trained nurses at intervals from birth to five years. The children who completed the trial were traced and re-examined at 23–27 years of age in 1997–1999 to study how birth size, infant feeding, early growth and childhood illness relate to adult blood pressure, adiposity, insulin resistance, haemostatic factors and lung function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20567021+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Breast Cancer in Northern Israel Study is a population-based case-control study in northern Israel of patients with breast cancer and age-, clinic-, and ethnic-group matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5764256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast and colon cancer free controls, matched on age, sex, ethnicity and residence (primary care clinic) were randomly selected from the same source population (living in the same area).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5764256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutively diagnosed patients, with colorectal and breast cancer, residing in a geographically defined area of northern Israel at time of diagnosis were eligible to participate in these studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5764256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In both studies participants provided IRB approved written informed consent at the time of enrollment and were interviewed to obtain information about their personal history of cancer, medical history, medication use, education, and health habits including alcohol consumption, smoking, and physical activity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5764256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment to the MECC Study started March 31, 1998 and recruitment to the BCINIS started at January 1, 2000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20567021") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21952991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37451831") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29324747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5764256/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While patients with cancer were from the entire eligible population, the sampling frame of controls was from Clalit Health Services (CHS) register of insurees residing at the same area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001518> "A population-based case-control study of breast cancer in northern Israel, conducted by the Clalit National Cancer Control Center in Haifa with family medicine, surgery, pathology and oncology teams across the region, which since January 2000 has enrolled consecutively diagnosed breast cancer patients living in a defined area of northern Israel and cancer-free controls randomly selected from the Clalit Health Services register of insured people in the same area, matched on age, ethnic group and primary care clinic. Participants are interviewed about their medical history, medication use and health habits and give a blood sample, for studies of breast cancer risk factors, including genetic ones.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34925446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BCX is comprised of more than 134,021 participants from 24 discovery cohorts and five ancestries: European, African American, Hispanic, East Asian, and South Asian.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> "An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34925446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BCX is interested in the genetics of all main hematological measures and is divided into three main working groups: RBC, white blood cell (WBC),21 and platelet (PLT).20") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> "An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34925446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Blood-Cell Consortium (BCX) aims to identify novel common and rare variants associated with blood-cell traits using an exome array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> "An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34925446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5005438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We meta-analyzed ExomeChip results for seven RBC-related phenotypes (RBC count, HCT, HGB, MCH, MCHC, MCV, and RDW) available in up to 130,273 individuals from 24 studies and 5 ancestries (Tables S1–S3 and Figure S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> "An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346685") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27346686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34925446") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888494") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7482360/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Blood Cell Consortium Phase 2 (BCX2) continues to identify novel common and rare variants associated with blood cell traits using imputed genotype data based on Haplotype Reference Consortium (HRC) or the 1000 Genomes Project (Phase 3, version 5) for European ancestry cohorts and non-European ancestry cohorts, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001519> "An international consortium of cohort studies and biobanks, organised in red blood cell, white blood cell and platelet working groups, that meta-analyses genetic associations with blood-cell counts and indices in participants of European, African, Hispanic/Latino, East Asian and South Asian ancestry, first with exome-array genotypes and later (its second phase, BCX2) with genome-wide imputed data, to identify common and rare variants that influence blood-cell traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were either incident cases referred to the University Hospital Erlangen by surrounding practitioners (66% of the case sample set), or prevalent cases that were outpatients in follow-up care approached within 6.2 (±4.6 SD) years after treatment for primary endometrial cancer in the same hospital (34% of the case sample set).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520> "A single-centre case-control study of endometrial cancer at the University Hospital Erlangen in Bavaria, Germany, conducted between 2002 and 2008 to investigate genetic and epidemiological risk factors for endometrial cancer, whose cases were incident cases referred to the hospital by surrounding practitioners or prevalent cases approached during follow-up care after treatment there for primary endometrial cancer, with epidemiological information from a structured interview questionnaire and clinical data from health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Epidemiological information was collected by a structured questionnaire completed during an interview and clinical data for the cases was obtained from clinical health records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520> "A single-centre case-control study of endometrial cancer at the University Hospital Erlangen in Bavaria, Germany, conducted between 2002 and 2008 to investigate genetic and epidemiological risk factors for endometrial cancer, whose cases were incident cases referred to the hospital by surrounding practitioners or prevalent cases approached during follow-up care after treatment there for primary endometrial cancer, with epidemiological information from a structured interview questionnaire and clinical data from health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Bavarian Endometrial Cancer Cases and Controls Study (BECS) is a single-center case-control study, conducted between 2002 and 2008, with the aim of investigating genetic and epidemiological risk factors for endometrial cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520> "A single-centre case-control study of endometrial cancer at the University Hospital Erlangen in Bavaria, Germany, conducted between 2002 and 2008 to investigate genetic and epidemiological risk factors for endometrial cancer, whose cases were incident cases referred to the hospital by surrounding practitioners or prevalent cases approached during follow-up care after treatment there for primary endometrial cancer, with epidemiological information from a structured interview questionnaire and clinical data from health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13537468/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Replication analysis in the German population included 221 cases from the Bavarian Endometrial Cancer Study (BECS) and 251 healthy controls aged 55 years and older from the Bavarian Breast Cancer Cases and Controls (BBCC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001520> "A single-centre case-control study of endometrial cancer at the University Hospital Erlangen in Bavaria, Germany, conducted between 2002 and 2008 to investigate genetic and epidemiological risk factors for endometrial cancer, whose cases were incident cases referred to the hospital by surrounding practitioners or prevalent cases approached during follow-up care after treatment there for primary endometrial cancer, with epidemiological information from a structured interview questionnaire and clinical data from health records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2813048/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A trained research nurse (A.M.) saw all the subjects at home on at least two visits, took medical history, anthropometric measurements and blood samples") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2813048/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Associations between blood pressure, anthropometric indices and sodium were investigated in 495 apparently healthy, community-living participants (age 90, SD 4.8; range 80–106), from the cross-sectional Belfast Elderly Longitudinal Free-living Aging STudy (BELFAST) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2902418/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, subjects gave blood samples for DNA and other laboratory variables, responded to nutrition, life style and medical history questionnaires and had Blood Pressure and anthropometric measurements taken [2,4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2902418/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the BELFAST study, 90 year old subjects, who are 'very good' for their age, also called 'elite' (approximately 500), were recruited through their General Practitioners, from the Greater Belfast area [1,2].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2902418/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Belfast Longevity Group enlisted the help of 500 community-living, mobile, mentally competent, 'elite' nonagenarians, as part of an ongoing study of ageing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19496022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20388089") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25773008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20507630") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2902418/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed some immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors and some aspects of their interaction in this group of 'oldest old'.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001521> "A longitudinal study of ageing by the Belfast Longevity Group of Queen's University Belfast, Northern Ireland, of 'elite' octogenarians and nonagenarians, and some centenarians: community-living, apparently well, independently mobile and mentally competent people recruited through their general practitioners in the Greater Belfast area and seen at home by a research nurse, who took their medical history, anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and blood samples for DNA and laboratory tests, with nutrition and lifestyle questionnaires, to study the immunological, cardiovascular, nutritional and genetic factors of healthy ageing and longevity.")

