AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24958192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40078479") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3265835/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After written informed consent, blood samples were obtained for genomic DNA extraction, generation of EBV cell lines and plasma and serum collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001522> "A case-control cohort for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease, drawn from a prospective study of Alzheimer's disease in Flanders, Belgium, whose genetic studies are run from the University of Antwerp: unrelated patients with early- or late-onset possible or probable Alzheimer's disease, diagnosed by consensus of at least two neurologists at the memory clinics of the Hospital Network Antwerp (Middelheim and Hoge Beuken) and the University Hospitals Leuven and at other neurology centres of the Belgian Neurology (BELNEU) consortium, and healthy unrelated control individuals from Belgium, patients' partners or community volunteers, with blood samples for DNA, cell lines and plasma and, for some patients, cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24958192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40078479") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3265835/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consensus diagnosis of possible or probable AD was given by at least two neurologists, based on the NINCDS/ADRDA criteria.24") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001522> "A case-control cohort for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease, drawn from a prospective study of Alzheimer's disease in Flanders, Belgium, whose genetic studies are run from the University of Antwerp: unrelated patients with early- or late-onset possible or probable Alzheimer's disease, diagnosed by consensus of at least two neurologists at the memory clinics of the Hospital Network Antwerp (Middelheim and Hoge Beuken) and the University Hospitals Leuven and at other neurology centres of the Belgian Neurology (BELNEU) consortium, and healthy unrelated control individuals from Belgium, patients' partners or community volunteers, with blood samples for DNA, cell lines and plasma and, for some patients, cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24958192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40078479") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3265835/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Flanders–Belgian control group consisted of 844 healthy, unrelated individuals from Belgium (mean age at inclusion 65.4±14.8 years, 57.0% women).23") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001522> "A case-control cohort for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease, drawn from a prospective study of Alzheimer's disease in Flanders, Belgium, whose genetic studies are run from the University of Antwerp: unrelated patients with early- or late-onset possible or probable Alzheimer's disease, diagnosed by consensus of at least two neurologists at the memory clinics of the Hospital Network Antwerp (Middelheim and Hoge Beuken) and the University Hospitals Leuven and at other neurology centres of the Belgian Neurology (BELNEU) consortium, and healthy unrelated control individuals from Belgium, patients' partners or community volunteers, with blood samples for DNA, cell lines and plasma and, for some patients, cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers.")
