AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21403675") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24958192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40078479") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35379992") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-022-01024-z/MediaObjects/41588_2022_1024_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients were ascertained at the memory clinic of Middelheim and Hoge Beuken (Hospital Network Antwerp, Belgium) and at the memory clinic of the University Hospitals of Leuven, Belgium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001522> "A case-control cohort for genetic studies of Alzheimer's disease, drawn from a prospective study of Alzheimer's disease in Flanders, Belgium, whose genetic studies are run from the University of Antwerp: unrelated patients with early- or late-onset possible or probable Alzheimer's disease, diagnosed by consensus of at least two neurologists at the memory clinics of the Hospital Network Antwerp (Middelheim and Hoge Beuken) and the University Hospitals Leuven and at other neurology centres of the Belgian Neurology (BELNEU) consortium, and healthy unrelated control individuals from Belgium, patients' partners or community volunteers, with blood samples for DNA, cell lines and plasma and, for some patients, cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15539711+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort of 139 probands in the Boston Early-Onset COPD Study was recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics between September 1994 and July 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19300482") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2650282/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BEOCOPD subjects were recruited through COPD probands with age <53 years, FEV1 <40% predicted, and without severe α1-antitrypsin deficiency [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age at enrollment: 10 years or greater First or second-degree relative of an EOCOPD proband, or first-degree relative of another affected pedigree member") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Extended pedigrees are enrolled, primarily in New England, although some more geographically distant subjects have been included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15539711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000946.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Boston Early-Onset COPD was started in 1994 in an effort to find genetic determinants of COPD other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001523> "A family study begun in 1994 at Brigham and Women's Hospital, Boston, to find genetic determinants of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease other than alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, which enrols extended pedigrees, mainly in New England, ascertained through probands with severe COPD (FEV1 at most 40% predicted) before age 53 and without severe alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, recruited from lung transplant and general pulmonary clinics, together with their first- and second-degree relatives aged 10 years or older.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BEST is a 2×2 full factorial double-blind randomized controlled trial of 7,000 adults having manifest arsenical skin lesions evaluating the efficacy of 6-year supplementation with alpha-tocopherol (100 mg daily) and L-selenomethionine (200 μg daily) for the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For study administrative purposes, we stratified randomization by study site and gender, utilizing Araihazar and Matlab as the two main study strata since we have centralized field offices located in those sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals were recruited from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali, and Chandpur districts of Bangladesh.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were randomly assigned to receive identical-appearing tablets containing vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol, 100 mg daily), selenium (L-selenomethionine, 200 μg daily), vitamin E and selenium, or placebo (all supplied by Kabco Inc, Amityville, NY) for 6 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Secondary endpoints include all-cause and cancer-related mortality, diabetes mellitus, and oxidative stress biomarkers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23590571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3953314/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were 7,000 participants enrolled in the trial between April 2006 and August 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001524> "A population-based, 2×2 factorial, double-blind randomised controlled chemoprevention trial in Bangladesh that enrolled adults with manifest arsenical skin lesions from the Narayanganj, Comilla, Noakhali and Chandpur districts, through field offices in Araihazar and Matlab, between April 2006 and August 2009, and gave them vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol), selenium (L-selenomethionine), both or placebo for six years to test the prevention of non-melanoma skin cancer, with all-cause and cancer mortality, diabetes and oxidative stress biomarkers as secondary endpoints.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4666784/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at or before age 50 from 2009 to 2012 were recruited to the study through the Florida Cancer Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12686358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study aimed to assess the association between the timing of BRCA testing and surgical management among young Black women with breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12686358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population was derived from the Black Women with Breast Cancer: Etiology, Survival, and Treatment Outcomes (BEST) study, a population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at or below age 50 between 2005 and 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12686358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were recruited through state cancer registries in Florida and Tennessee, spoke English, and were alive at the time of recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13244119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we evaluated the demographic and clinicopathologic characteristics of HBC in a cancer registry‐based collection of young Black women with breast cancer, including distribution of GPVs across HBC genes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26287763") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33947654") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41360000") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42252839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13244119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were asked to provide informed consent, sign a medical records and tissue/tumor release, provide a saliva sample for HBC testing, and complete a questionnaire, which collected data on sociodemographic, epidemiologic, and lifestyle factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001525> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of self-identified Black women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at age 50 or younger, identified through the state cancer registries of Florida and Tennessee (diagnoses from 2005 to 2018; its first phase recruited women diagnosed in Florida in 2009–2012), who completed a questionnaire on sociodemographic, reproductive, epidemiologic and lifestyle factors, released their medical records and tumour tissue and gave saliva for germline genetic testing, now based at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, to study the causes, inherited predisposition, treatment and survival of breast cancer, including triple-negative breast cancer, in young Black women.")

