AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3609646/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baltic Familial Breast Ovarian Cancer Consortium (BFBOCC): BFBOCC is partly supported by Lithuania (BFBOCC-LT), Research Council of Lithuania grant LIG-19/2010, and Hereditary Cancer Association (Paveldimo vėžio asociacija).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526> "A collection of carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants from families seen in clinical cancer genetics services in Lithuania and Latvia, gathered by a collaboration of Lithuanian (BFBOCC-LT) and Latvian (BFBOCC-LV) hereditary breast and ovarian cancer research groups and contributed as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2, for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3609646/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Latvia (BFBOCC-LV) is partly supported by LSC grant 10.0010.08 and in part by a grant from the ESF Nr.2009/0220/1DP/1.1.1.2.0/09/APIA/VIAA/016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526> "A collection of carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants from families seen in clinical cancer genetics services in Lithuania and Latvia, gathered by a collaboration of Lithuanian (BFBOCC-LT) and Latvian (BFBOCC-LV) hereditary breast and ovarian cancer research groups and contributed as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2, for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8755508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variant carriers were recruited through 40 studies from 19 countries participating in the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (CIMBA) (24).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526> "A collection of carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants from families seen in clinical cancer genetics services in Lithuania and Latvia, gathered by a collaboration of Lithuanian (BFBOCC-LT) and Latvian (BFBOCC-LV) hereditary breast and ovarian cancer research groups and contributed as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2, for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8755508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of male carriers were ascertained through families attending cancer genetic clinics (96.9%; Supplementary Tables 1 and 2, available online).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526> "A collection of carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants from families seen in clinical cancer genetics services in Lithuania and Latvia, gathered by a collaboration of Lithuanian (BFBOCC-LT) and Latvian (BFBOCC-LV) hereditary breast and ovarian cancer research groups and contributed as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2, for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8755508/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BFBOCC Latvia/Lithuania 100.0 3 0 1 4 0 0 0 0") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001526> "A collection of carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants from families seen in clinical cancer genetics services in Lithuania and Latvia, gathered by a collaboration of Lithuanian (BFBOCC-LT) and Latvian (BFBOCC-LV) hereditary breast and ovarian cancer research groups and contributed as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2, for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2) being below age 65 for healthy controls (except where they were spouses/partners of participants with dementia)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BDR is a network of 6 dementia research centers (based at the universities of King’s College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and the associated university brain banks handling the donations (Cardiff brain donations were banked in London).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brains for Dementia Research (BDR) cohort and program was for planned brain donation across five UK brain banks and one donation point, with standardized operating procedures, following longitudinal clinical and psychometric assessments for people with no cognitive impairment as well as those with dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These factors, combined with the shortage of control brain tissue, led to BDR (brainsfordementiaresearch.org.uk) being established in 2008, through funding from the Alzheimer’s Research UK (ARUK) and Alzheimer’s Society (AS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30452415") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6294579/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This encompassed recruitment of participants without dementia via a variety of means, provided informed consent for regular assessment and their consent to donate their brain for research upon death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001527> "A longitudinal brain-donation cohort in the United Kingdom, established in 2008 with funding from Alzheimer's Research UK and the Alzheimer's Society, of volunteers with dementia and volunteers without cognitive impairment (the latter aged 65 or over, apart from spouses or partners of participants with dementia), recruited through a network of six dementia research centres (King's College London, Bristol, Manchester, Oxford, Cardiff and Newcastle) and their university brain banks, who undergo standardised clinical and psychometric assessments during life and have consented to donate their brains for dementia research after death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3590244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each affected subject was asked to identify members of close family aged 16–25 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3590244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following informed consent, unaffected individuals with at least one first degree, or two second degree relatives with bipolar I disorder were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3590244/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Unaffected, unrelated comparison subjects with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder were identified from the social networks of the high-risk subjects and matched for age, sex and premorbid IQ to the high-risk group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7479500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Assessments at timepoint 1, timepoint 2 and timepoint 4 included an MRI session, although only MRI measurements at timepoint 1 and timepoint 2 were considered within this study to restrict to a single scanner.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7479500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of the SBFS were invited every two years for a total of four assessments over six years") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23483904") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25229638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27418025") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32954013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7479500/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We were therefore interested in determining from longitudinal prospective data of young individuals, whether a comprehensive and spatially unconstrained measure of brain structure aging trajectory across the brain was related to concurrent mood disorder onset and/or to familial risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001528> "A prospective longitudinal study based at the University of Edinburgh of young people aged 16–25 at entry who were well but at high familial risk of mood disorder, having at least one first-degree or two second-degree relatives with bipolar I disorder (identified through patients with bipolar I disorder referred by psychiatrists across Scotland), and of unrelated controls with no personal or family history of bipolar disorder drawn from their social networks, assessed clinically on four occasions about two years apart and with brain MRI at the first, second and fourth assessments to study changes that precede the onset of mood disorders.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18717640+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By use of a whole-population ascertainment scheme, 822 individuals were enrolled from a schistosomiasis-endemic area in Conde, Bahia, in Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3345031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Regression models using GEE to account for family membership and family-based quantitative transmission disequilibrium tests (QTDT) were used to evaluate associations with total serum IgE (tIgE) levels and S. mansoni fecal egg counts adjusted for non-genetic covariates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The dataset is comprised of 2 large pedigrees with 535 and 310 members collapsed into 318 nuclear families (aged 5-85 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Association statistics were generated by means of inverse-variance meta-analysis of CAAPA studies with mean African ancestry percentage < 50% (BIAS, PGCA, ProAR, GALA II).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were recruited July – September, 2004, from five communities (Buri, Camarao, Genipapo, Sempre Viva, and Cobo), and follow-up visits continue.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18717640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22574126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27725671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30787307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brazilian Immunogenetics of Asthma and Schistosomiasis (BIAS) study is a whole-population ascertainment designed study of asthma and schistosomiasis in the rural district of Conde, Bahia, located 200 km north of Salvador, Brazil [14-16].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001529> "A family-based study of asthma and schistosomiasis in five rural communities of the district of Conde, Bahia, north-eastern Brazil, an area endemic for Schistosoma mansoni about 200 km north of Salvador, in which residents aged 5 to 85, most of them members of two large pedigrees, were enrolled by whole-population ascertainment from July to September 2004 by the Federal University of Bahia and Johns Hopkins University, with later follow-up visits, to study the genetic control of total serum IgE, S. mansoni infection intensity and asthma; it is one of the studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,013 participants were enrolled in BICWALZS from October 2016 to December 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of five institutions participated: Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital, and Chonnam National University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given the above, the Biobank Innovations for Chronic Cerebrovascular Disease with ALZheimer’s Disease Study (BICWALZS) was planned and initiated in 2016 by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BICWALZS is a prospective and longitudinal study assessing various clinical and biomarker characteristics in older adults with cognitive complaints.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original goal of BICWALZS was to facilitate, regulate, and ensure optimal research use of human biospecimens and data in the field of AD, chronic CVD, and mixed pathology for mild cognitive impairment (MCI) and dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35042283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8898610/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We planned to follow all participants annually with brief assessments and participants who had cortical amyloid burden, subcortical vascular pathology, apolipoprotein E4 allele, or significant cognitive decline biannually with an expanded assessment including neuropsychological tests, actigraphy measurements, and brain MRI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001530> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre biobank cohort of older adults with cognitive complaints (subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment, Alzheimer's disease, vascular and other dementias) enrolled from October 2016 to December 2020 at five South Korean university hospitals (Ajou University Hospital, Samsung Medical Center, Inha University Hospital, Pusan National University Hospital and Chonnam National University Hospital), planned and funded by the Korea Disease Control and Prevention Agency for the Korea Biobank Project to bank biospecimens and data for research on Alzheimer's disease, chronic cerebrovascular disease and mixed pathology; participants have clinical and neuropsychological assessments and blood tests, subsets have brain MRI, amyloid PET, Korea Biobank Array genotyping, actigraphy and skin fibroblast sampling, and follow-up is planned annually.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Unselected cases recruited from University College Hospital Galway and surrounding hospitals in the West of Ireland since 2001") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531> "A case-control study of breast cancer in the West of Ireland whose cases are unselected breast cancer patients recruited from University College Hospital Galway and surrounding hospitals in the West of Ireland since 2001, and whose controls are women over 60 years of age with no personal history of any cancer and no family history of breast or ovarian cancer, identified from retirement groups in the West of Ireland in 2001–2008; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women > 60 years with no personal history of any cancer and no family history of breast or ovarian cancer identified from retirement groups in the West of Ireland between 2001- 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001531> "A case-control study of breast cancer in the West of Ireland whose cases are unselected breast cancer patients recruited from University College Hospital Galway and surrounding hospitals in the West of Ireland since 2001, and whose controls are women over 60 years of age with no personal history of any cancer and no family history of breast or ovarian cancer, identified from retirement groups in the West of Ireland in 2001–2008; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3035981/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genetic component of the Bipolar Consortium, termed the ‘Bipolar Genome Study (BiGS),’ was initiated in 2006 to conduct a GWA study of BD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3035981/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The US National Institutes of Mental Health–sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium (Bipolar Consortium) has collected over 3,500 subjects with BD during 1990-2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3035981/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a GWA study of BD separately in individuals of European ancestry (EA) and of African ancestry (AA) using a variety of methods to control for population substructure and admixture among the individuals of AA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128104/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All eleven collection sites in the BiGS Consortium received IRB approval for subject ascertainment, assessment, and collection of DNA for genetic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128104/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data and biomaterials from the NIMH GI (Genetics Initiative) MGS2 (Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia) control sample were collected by NorthShore University HealthSystem, Evanston, IL") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21738484") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3128104/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "However, while most of the samples in GAIN were collected as part of extended families or sib-pairs, the TGEN samples were primarily selected without regard to family history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001532> "A case-control genetic study of bipolar disorder in the United States, initiated in 2006 as the genetic component of the NIMH-sponsored Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder Consortium to carry out genome-wide association studies: cases with bipolar disorder of European and African American ancestry, collected through the consortium's eleven US collection sites (mostly from multiplex families or sibling pairs for the first, GAIN-funded genotyping; without regard to family history for the later TGen genotyping), and controls from the NIMH Genetics Initiative control sample collected for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(3) saliva samples for genetic and epigenetic (methylation) analyses; (4) hair samples to measure cortisol, dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) and testosterone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility criteria were: (1) family who left Syria because of the war within the 4 years prior to recruitment; (2) child aged 8–16 years old; and (3) primary caregiver available to participate (typically the mother, or the caregiver who spent most time with the child).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, we aim to explore the interplay between those psychosocial and biological factors found to be most important in predicting risk and resilience.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were families displaced by the Syrian civil war that began in March 2011 and were living as refugees in ITSs in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study employs a longitudinal cohort design with baseline data assessment and follow-up 1 year later.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37933522") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35041012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8960581/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sponsor, Queen Mary University of London, reviewed the study for compliance with all relevant legal and regulatory requirements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001533> "A longitudinal cohort of Syrian refugee children aged 8–16 and their primary caregivers, from families who had fled the war in Syria within the previous four years and were living in informal tented settlements in the West and Central Beqaa regions of Lebanon, recruited by purposive cluster sampling from October 2017 to January 2018 and followed up once a year later, with interviews of children and caregivers and children's saliva (for genotyping and DNA methylation) and hair (for cortisol, DHEA and testosterone), to study how psychosocial and biological factors shape resilience and mental health problems; it was funded by the US National Institute of Child Health and Human Development and sponsored by Queen Mary University of London.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8545920/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals treated with PD in participating facilities who had undergone a PET within six months of starting PD were eligible for enrollment, without regard to duration of PD treatment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8545920/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in Bio-PD were prospectively enrolled from 54 centers in four countries (Australia, 2; Canada, 5; United Kingdom, 32; and United States, 15 centers) from September 2013 through November 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8545920/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Peritoneal Dialysis Competitive Risk Analysis for Long-Term Outcomes (PD-CRAFT) that enrolled participants from 42 centers in the United Kingdom from August 2012 through December 2014 (n=1355)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8545920/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To bridge this gap in knowledge, we undertook the Biological Determinants of PD (Bio-PD) study to perform a GWAS to test the hypothesis that common genetic variants explain some of the inter-individual variability in PSTR in people with kidney failure treated with PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12807162/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was procured for participants enrolled in other studies from 36 centers (n=2140; Belgium, Hong Kong, Sweden, and the United Kingdom).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12807162/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "members of the research team at the University of Washington that coordinated the international study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34197840") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40669005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02694068") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs002996.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria included adults over the age of 20 who are able to provide consent and had a record of a PET within 6 months of starting PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001534> "An international observational cohort study, led from the University of Washington, of adults with kidney failure treated with peritoneal dialysis who had a peritoneal equilibration test soon after starting it, set up to find common genetic variants that influence peritoneal solute transfer rate and ultrafiltration. Participants were enrolled prospectively at centres in Australia, Canada, the United Kingdom and the United States from 2013 to 2018, and DNA and clinical data were added from earlier peritoneal dialysis studies in the United Kingdom (PD-CRAFT), Belgium, Sweden and Hong Kong.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27126231+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By using a novel systems biology approach, incorporating demographics, biomarkers, genome-wide analysis, and proteomics, a model that predicts response to therapy will be developed") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7319410/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The prospective, observational, international BIOSTAT‐CHF study included 2516 patients with heart failure from 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7375987/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, BIOSTAT-CHF was a multicentre, multinational, prospective observational study, in which 2516 patients with new-set or worsening signs and/or symptoms of heart failure from 11 European countries, who were on suboptimal guideline recommended treatment (i.e., ≤ 50% of target doses of ACEi/ARBs and beta-blockers), were enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7375987/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Physicians could enrol patients if they anticipated uptitration or initiation of ACEi/ARB and beta-blockers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8318449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a validation cohort of 1738 HF patients was recruited from six centres in Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31919934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32002631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32825781") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33998162") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8318449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "patients ≥18 years old with diagnosed HF with either echocardiographic evidence of left ventricular systolic dysfunction or a previous documented admission to hospital with HF requiring furosemide, currently treated with furosemide ≥20 mg/day or equivalent") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001535> "A multicentre, prospective, observational European study of adults with new-onset or worsening heart failure who were treated with loop diuretics but received no more than half the target doses of ACE inhibitors or angiotensin receptor blockers and/or beta-blockers, and whose physicians intended to start or up-titrate these drugs. Its index cohort was enrolled at 69 centres in 11 European countries between December 2010 and December 2012 and its validation cohort at six centres in Scotland between October 2010 and April 2014; funded by the European Commission's Seventh Framework Programme, it combined clinical data, biomarkers, genome-wide genotyping and proteomics to find patient profiles that predict response to guideline-recommended therapy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3662650/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MalariaGEN partners in Gambia, Malawi and Kenya collected blood samples from children diagnosed with severe malaria, including cerebral malaria and severe malarial anaemia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,815 children (aged 2 months - 14 years) admitted to the national hospital in Blantyre, Malawi, were enrolled into an unmatched case-control study during 1994-2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a background comparator population, DNA from cord bloods was collected from 3,777 infants born in the same hospital during 2006-2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 (CP1) along with those of 11 other case-control studies from a total of 11 malaria-endemic countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was also obtained from blood samples collected from the parents of a number of cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-malawi/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme (MLW) together with the Blantyre Malaria Project (BMP) recruited severe malaria cases, healthy controls and parents from the Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital (QECH) in Blantyre, Malawi.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001536> "An unmatched case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria at Queen Elizabeth Central Hospital, Blantyre, Malawi, run by the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Trust Clinical Research Programme with the Blantyre Malaria Project. Its cases are children aged 2 months to 14 years admitted with severe malaria (cerebral malaria or severe malarial anaemia) in 1994-2007, its controls are cord-blood samples from infants born at the same hospital in 2006-2007, and blood was also taken from some cases' parents; it is the Malawi partner study of the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and its genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6035076/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, unselected participants of the German screening colonoscopy program are recruited by gastroenterology practices in southern Germany in this multicenter study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6035076/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of every age undergoing screening colonoscopy, which is reimbursed in the German health-care system since October 2002 to individuals aged ≥55 years, are informed about the study at a preparatory visit, usually one week prior to colonoscopy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6035076/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients are invited to provide stool and blood samples prior to colonoscopy and to complete a standardized questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Actual study start date: 2005-11-08") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Primary Sponsor Address: Deutsches Krebsforschungszentrum Heidelberg") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29574091") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35060941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38704818") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://drks.de/search/en/trial/DRKS00008737") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will compare the results from blood and stool and tests to the results of the colonoscopy in order to determine the performance of novel tests in detection of adenomas and early colorectal cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001537> "An ongoing, prospective, multicentre diagnostic study of participants in the German screening colonoscopy programme, recruited since November 2005 at a preparatory visit before colonoscopy at gastroenterology practices in southern Germany, who donate blood and stool samples and answer a questionnaire. Run from the German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ) in Heidelberg, it evaluates new blood and stool tests for the early detection of colorectal cancer and advanced adenomas against the findings of screening colonoscopy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178591/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Bloodomics partners from AMC (The Netherlands), LURIC (Germany), the University of Cambridge (UK), and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute (UK) received funding through the 6th Framework funded Integrated Project Bloodomics (grant LSHM-CT-2004-503485).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3178591/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch component of the BLOODOMICS collaboration comprises of cases drawn from the Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study, with controls ascertained from the Sanquin Common Controls (SANQUIN-CC) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3178591/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German component of the BLOODOMICS collaboration comprises of cases and controls from the LUdwigshafen RIsk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study, supplemented by additional controls from the Mannheim study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Coordinated by CHANCELLOR MASTERS AND SCHOLARS OF THE UNIVERSITY OF CAMBRIDGE United Kingdom") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start date 1 June 2004 End date 30 November 2008") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21966275") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/503485") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project will generate population genetics data providing insight into the causes of CAD & AT through the identification of tributory genes and gene variants, proteins and intracellular signalling pathways.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001538> "A European Union Sixth Framework Programme integrated project (June 2004 to November 2008), coordinated by the University of Cambridge with clinical coronary artery disease centres, genomics groups and the Wellcome Trust Sanger Institute, that sought genes and pathways of atherothrombosis in coronary artery disease through platelet transcriptome and proteome analysis and exon resequencing. For genetic association studies it assembled a Dutch case-control collection, with cases from the Academic Medical Center Amsterdam Premature Atherosclerosis Study (AMC-PAS) and the AGNES study of first ST-elevation myocardial infarction and controls from Sanquin blood donors, and a German one, with cases and controls from the Ludwigshafen Risk and Cardiovascular Health (LURIC) study and additional blood-donor controls from Mannheim.")

