AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21639959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28346442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28346442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3826/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3826_MOESM68_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BEL: Nationaal Kankerplan") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001541> "A hospital-based case-control study of ovarian cancer at University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, funded by the Belgian National Cancer Plan (Nationaal Kankerplan). It is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code BEL) and contributes cases and controls to its genome-wide association studies of ovarian cancer risk and to its analyses of ovarian cancer outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21639959") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28346442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BEL Belgian Ovarian Cancer Study (BELOCS) Belgium Cases attending the Gynecologic Oncology Unit at the Leuven University Hospital diagnosed with incident ovarian cancer from 2009 onwards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001541> "A hospital-based case-control study of ovarian cancer at University Hospitals Leuven, Belgium, funded by the Belgian National Cancer Plan (Nationaal Kankerplan). It is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code BEL) and contributes cases and controls to its genome-wide association studies of ovarian cancer risk and to its analyses of ovarian cancer outcome.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32231276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0090-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_90_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BOMA 1-3 | boma | Germany | Consecutive inpatients; SCID or SADS interview; medical records | POPGEN & KORA population-based | DSM-IV MDD; German ancestry; ≥18yo | BIP, hypomania, NAP, MDD related to SUD | Unscreened") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32231276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0090-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_90_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "mdd_boma_eur | Bonn-Mannheim MDD study | Germany | No | Prohibited by national law | NA | NA | Available via collaboration with PIs") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32231276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2008.125/MediaObjects/41380_2009_BFmp2008125_MOESM452_ESM.doc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases for the Bonn/Mannheim MDD study were ascertained from consecutive admissions to the inpatient units of the Department of Psychiatry and Psychotherapy at the University of Bonn and at the Central Institute for Mental Health in Mannheim, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32231276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2008.125/MediaObjects/41380_2009_BFmp2008125_MOESM452_ESM.doc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "medical records, and the family history method.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29700475") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32231276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fmp.2008.125/MediaObjects/41380_2009_BFmp2008125_MOESM452_ESM.doc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "were made by a consensus best-estimate procedure based on all available information, including a structured interview (SCID-I)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001542> "A German case-control study of major depressive disorder whose cases were consecutive admissions with a DSM-IV lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder to the psychiatric inpatient units of the University of Bonn and of the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, diagnosed by best-estimate consensus from a structured interview (SCID-I or SADS), medical records and family history and excluding bipolar disorder, non-affective psychosis and substance-related depression, and whose controls came from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the cohorts of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's major depressive disorder working group (cohort code boma).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21353194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21353194") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21353194+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the GWAS, we investigated 499,494 autosomal and 12,484 X-chromosomal SNPs in 682 patients with BD and in 1300 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543> "A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's bipolar disorder working group.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21353194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.943/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng943_MOESM29_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases for the BOMA-Bipolar Study were ascertained from consecutive admissions to the inpatent units of the Department of Psychiatry and Psychotherapy at the University of Bonn and at the Central Institute for Mental Health in Mannheim, University of Heidelberg, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543> "A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's bipolar disorder working group.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21353194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.943/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng943_MOESM29_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were ascertained from three population-based studies in Germany (PopGen, KORA, and Heinz-Nixdorf-Recall Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543> "A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's bipolar disorder working group.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21353194") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.943/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng943_MOESM29_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DSM-IV lifetime diagnoses of bipolar I disorder were assigned using a consensus best-estimate procedure, based on all available information, including a structured interviews Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV-TR-axis I disorders and Schedule of Affective Disorders1 and Schizophrenia- Lifetime version2 (SCID-I, SADS-L), medical records, and the family history method.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001543> "A German case-control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder, from the University of Bonn and the Central Institute of Mental Health in Mannheim, whose cases, nearly all with bipolar I disorder diagnosed by DSM-IV best-estimate consensus from structured interviews (SADS-L or SCID), were recruited from consecutive admissions to psychiatric inpatient units, and whose controls were drawn from the German population-based studies PopGen, KORA and Heinz Nixdorf Recall. It is one of the samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium's bipolar disorder working group.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After signing an informed consent, a sample of whole-blood already collected for 297 in-hospital biochemical analysis or SARS-CoV-2 serology was used for genomic DNA 298 extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, early in 2021, the Covid-19 77 Host Genetics Initiative (HGI) has brought together 49.562 cases and 2 million controls, 78 from populations with different ancestries across the world to elucidate the genetic 79 determinants of SARS-CoV-2 infection and severity including 853 samples from the 80 BRACOVID study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, Covid-19 patients were enrolled 291 after hospitalization in one of the following tertiary care centers in the metropolitan area 292 of Sao Paulo, Brazil: Instituto do Coração, and Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas 293 da Faculdade de Medicina da Universidade de São Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Non-hospitalized cases were 294 selected by serological studies surveys for previous SARS-CoV-2 infection or SARS- 295 CoV-2 PCR test among health professionals or the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants responded to a detailed questionnaire aimed at collecting 300 demographic, risk factors, symptoms, and prior clinical information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2021/10/07/2021.10.06.21264631.full.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRACOVID study was designed to identify and characterize genetic risk 97 factors for Covid-19 severity in the Brazilian population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001544> "A genetic study of COVID-19 severity in Brazil, based at the University of São Paulo Medical School, which enrolled people infected with SARS-CoV-2 in the São Paulo metropolitan area: patients hospitalised with COVID-19 at the Instituto do Coração (InCor) and the Instituto Central do Hospital das Clínicas, and people with a previous infection who were not hospitalised, found through serological surveys or SARS-CoV-2 PCR testing of health professionals and the general population. DNA came from blood samples already taken for clinical tests or serology, with questionnaire or hospital-record data; it was designed to identify genetic risk factors for COVID-19 severity in the Brazilian population and contributes to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3580526/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients eligible for the BRAGGSS cohort were initially identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register (BSRBR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3580526/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRAGGSS cohort was developed for the study of genetic predictors of response to anti-TNF biologic therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4334684/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BRAGGSS is a multicentre study collecting clinical, laboratory and adherence data on patients with RA who are starting treatment with biologic therapy in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6150911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Collaborations have been established between some of the larger referring centres to form the Biologics in Rheumatoid Arthritis Genetics and Genomics Study Syndicate (BRAGGSS; www.braggss.co.uk), which collects blood samples from biologic treated RA patients for DNA, RNA and cellular studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12854005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BRAGGSS recruited patients with a clinical diagnosis of RA from 53 centers across England from November 2008 to December 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23039402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25213131") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40567118") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40567118+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Biologics in Rheumatoid Arthritis Genetics and Genomics Study Syndicate is a nationwide observational cohort study recruiting patients from 53 centers across the United Kingdom before the initiation of biologic treatment and following them up prospectively for 12 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001545> "A multicentre observational study of patients with rheumatoid arthritis treated with biologic drugs at rheumatology centres across the United Kingdom, which collects their blood samples for DNA, RNA and cellular studies together with clinical, laboratory and adherence data, to study genetic and other predictors of response to biologic therapy. Its first patients, starting anti-TNF therapy, were identified through the British Society for Rheumatology Biologics Register; from November 2008 patients were recruited before starting a biologic and followed up prospectively for 12 months.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls have been recruited within 48 h of recruiting index cases, and they are “frequency-matched” to cases by sex and age (in 5-year age bands).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were individuals without a previous self-reported history of cardiovascular disease (as defined above) drawn from individuals concurrently identified in the same hospital as index cases, and recruited in the following order of priority: (1) visitors of patients attending the out-patient department;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following screening by medically-qualified research officers, patients (male or female; aged at least 20 years) admitted to the emergency rooms of the NICVD hospital are eligible for inclusion as MI cases") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRAVE study was established in 2011 by the Department of Public Health and Primary Care at the University of Cambridge (the study’s international coordinating centre)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Bangladesh Risk of Acute Vascular Events (BRAVE) study is an epidemiological bioresource established to examine environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of CHD among the Bangladeshi population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39811539") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25930055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4516898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "in collaboration with the Chronic Non-communicable Disease Unit at the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Bangladesh.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001546> "A case-control study of first-onset acute myocardial infarction in Bangladesh, established in 2011 by the University of Cambridge with the International Centre for Diarrhoeal Disease Research, Bangladesh (icddr,b) and the National Institute of Cardiovascular Disease (NICVD) in Dhaka, whose cases are adults admitted to the NICVD's emergency rooms with a first myocardial infarction and whose controls, frequency-matched by age and sex, are hospital visitors without cardiovascular disease; with questionnaire data, electrocardiograms and stored blood samples, it was set up to study environmental, genetic, lifestyle and biochemical determinants of coronary heart disease in Bangladeshis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16504378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the association between occupational exposure to polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons, aromatic amines and diesel and bladder cancer risk and the modification by smoking and metabolic polymorphisms, have we recruited 200 cases and 385 population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3042097/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases included in the study were incident cases identified with histologically confirmed transitional cell carcinoma (TCC) of the bladder between 1999 and 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3042097/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, our study was a population-based case–control study conducted in the Belgian province of Limburg consisting of 200 bladder cancer cases and 386 healthy control subjects [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3042097/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were derived from the Limburg Cancer Registry (LIKAR) and invited to participate in the study by urologists and general practitioners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3042097/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since strict Belgian privacy laws preclude direct access to population registers, control subjects were selected through the Belgian authority, Kruispuntbank van de Sociale Zekerheid (Crossroads Bank of Social Security).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16380991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16504378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27386115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21203820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3042097/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This was done via simple random sampling, stratified by municipality and social economic status among inhabitants from the province of Limburg who were 50 years of age and older, without a diagnosis of transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001547> "A population-based case-control study of bladder cancer in the Belgian province of Limburg, whose cases are people with histologically confirmed incident transitional cell carcinoma of the bladder diagnosed between 1999 and 2004, identified through the Limburg Cancer Registry and invited by their urologists and general practitioners, and whose controls are inhabitants of the province aged 50 or over sampled at random through the Crossroads Bank of Social Security, stratified by municipality and socioeconomic status; it was used to study occupational, dietary and genetic risk factors for bladder cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001548> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001548>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BSUCH Breast Cancer Study of the University Clinic Heidelberg 13 Germany All cases diagnosed with breast cancer in 2007- 2009 at the University Women`s Clinic Heidelberg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001548> "A case-control study of breast cancer in Germany whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer in 2007-2009 at the University Women's Clinic Heidelberg and whose controls are female blood donors recruited in the same years at the Institute of Transfusion Medicine and Immunology in Mannheim; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Female blood donors recruited in 2007- 2009 at the Institute of Transfusion Medicine & Immunology, Mannheim.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001548> "A case-control study of breast cancer in Germany whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer in 2007-2009 at the University Women's Clinic Heidelberg and whose controls are female blood donors recruited in the same years at the Institute of Transfusion Medicine and Immunology in Mannheim; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23535729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23535729+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These SNPs were genotyped in 45,290 cases and 41,880 controls of European ancestry from 41 studies in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001548> "A case-control study of breast cancer in Germany whose cases are women diagnosed with breast cancer in 2007-2009 at the University Women's Clinic Heidelberg and whose controls are female blood donors recruited in the same years at the Institute of Transfusion Medicine and Immunology in Mannheim; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25993007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stage 2 samples for replication testing of 96 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) consisted of 13,517 unrelated Chinese Hans (6,570 T2D case and 6,947 nondiabetic control subjects) from the Guizhou-Bijie Type 2 Diabetes Study (GBTDS), the Beijing Type 2 Diabetes Studies (BTDS), and the Hubei Type 2 Diabetes Studies (HTDS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of unrelated Han Chinese from Beijing, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, used in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and glycaemic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25993007") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25993007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4439071/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project is a cross-sectional study within the framework of the “Longevity and Health of Aging Population in Guangxi China (LHAPGC)” and “Beijing Type 2 Diabetes Studies (BTDS)” [20, 21].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001549> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of unrelated Han Chinese from Beijing, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, used in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and glycaemic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24949998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5540428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first two waves of data were collected in the clinic, following an assessment of Melanocyte Naevi (moles) around the twelfth (TWin Mole study visit 1: TW1) and fourteenth birthday of the twins (TWin Mole study visit 2: TW2) [6, 37–39]") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24949998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40576277+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were re-examined 2 years later, and a subset was seen 20 years after the initial exam.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24949998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A40576277+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Brisbane Twin Nevus Study recorded sun behaviours and counted naevi on annual new samples of 12-year-old twins (and siblings nearest in age) from 1992 to 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24949998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13106845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort comprises a sample of predominantly adolescent twins (age 9–23 years) and their parents from Southeastern Queensland, Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24949998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28764680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40576277") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41807453") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13106845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested whether our PRS for cutaneous nevi was associated with iris nevi scored in the QIMR Brisbane Twin Nevus Study (BTNS) cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001550> "A study of the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) in Brisbane, Australia, that from 1992 to 2016 examined annual new samples of 12-year-old twins from south-east Queensland, with their siblings nearest in age, counting their naevi and recording their sun behaviour, and re-examined them two years later; set up to investigate genetic factors in naevus development and other risk factors for melanoma, it also includes the twins' parents and is the twin mole study of the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10209490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first letter mailed to a potential subject, the selected individual was asked to indicate the day and time that would be convenient to come to the mobile unit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10209490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from the Bus Santé study, an ongoing yearly population-based cross-sectional study of adults living in the state of Geneva, Switzerland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11286997/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Every year since 1992, a stratified random sampling procedure according to age and sex distributions in the population of reference extracts a representative sample of the Canton’s noninstitutionalized residents from a local government residential list.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11286997/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fasting blood samples were collected and glucose, total and high–density lipoprotein (HDL), plasma cholesterol and triglycerides were assayed using commercially available enzymatic kits (Bayer Technicon Diagnostics, CV 1.4 %, 1.2 %, and 1.5 %, for glucose, cholesterol, and triglycerides, respectively).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11286997/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants completed self–administered, standardized questionnaires covering a series of risk factors for major lifestyle–related chronic conditions, sociodemographic characteristics, educational and occupational histories, dietary intake, and physical activity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37250185") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40235578") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39081844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11286997/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from the Bus Santé study, a repeated cross–sectional population–based health survey in Geneva Canton, Switzerland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001551> "A repeated cross-sectional population-based health examination survey of adults living in the canton of Geneva, Switzerland, which since 1992 has examined in a mobile unit, each year, a new random sample of residents drawn from the cantonal residents list and stratified by age and sex, collecting questionnaires, physical measurements and blood samples on risk factors for cardiovascular and other lifestyle-related chronic diseases.")

