AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3157552/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A GWA study using the Genome-Wide Human SNP 6.0 Array (Affymetrix, Santa Clara, USA) was conducted to discover SNPs associated with CAD in the CADomics study (Coronary Artery Disease and Genomics), a case-control study of CAD (2,078 CAD cases and 2,953 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3157552/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CADomics is a case-control study including the hospital-based catheter-lab AtheroGene Registry and the population-based Gutenberg-Heart Study (GHS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between June 1999 and February 2004, patients with documented CAD referred to the Department of Medicine II of the Johannes Gutenberg-University in Mainz, Germany and the Department of Medicine of the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital, Koblenz, were enrolled in the AtheroGene study registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CADomics (Coronary Artery Disease and genomics) is a German-based case-control study of CAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample was drawn randomly from the governmental local registry offices which contains all citizens in the city of Mainz and the district of Mainz-Bingen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21606135") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3070269/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CADomics Coronary Artery Disease and Omics 2078/2952 58.3 21.9/50.5 60.8 (10.1)/55.3 (10.8) 29.4 (5.1)/27.0 (4.7) CAD: >50% stenosis in 1 major coronary artery and/or MI based on ECG and enzymes Population sample with no history of MI") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001554> "A German case-control study of coronary artery disease that pools patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease from the hospital catheter-laboratory-based AtheroGene Registry, enrolled in 1999–2004 at Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz and the German Federal Armed Forces Central Hospital in Koblenz, with controls without a history of myocardial infarction from the population-based Gutenberg Heart Study of the city of Mainz and the Mainz-Bingen district, assembled for genome-wide association studies of coronary artery disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5295119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data-collection phases were at 5-year intervals: 1979–1983 (phase 1), 1984–1988 (phase 2), 1989–1993 (phase 3), 1993–1997 (phase 4), and 2002–2005 (phase 5).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5295119/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CaPS was set up to study the influence of CVD risk factors in the development of coronary heart disease (CHD) [12], and recruited an initial 2512 men, aged 45 to 59 years living in the town of Caerphilly and five adjacent villages, South Wales, UK (response rate 89%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888493") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Caerphilly Prospective Study was undertaken by the former MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) and was funded by the Medical Research Council of the United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10582873/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Beginning in phase 3 (age 55–69 years), cognitive assessments were added, including the Cambridge Cognitive Examination (CAMCOG),21 the Alice Heim 4 (AH4) test22 and the Rivermead Behavioural Memory Test (RBMT,23 which includes immediate recall of a 21-clause story and delayed recall after 20 min).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10582873/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men aged 45–59 were identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists in Caerphilly and surrounding villages in South Wales, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28106791") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0092867420308229-mmc1.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.thl.fi/publications/morgam/cohorts/full/uk/unk-caea.htm") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37844990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10582873/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current paper uses a prospective cohort of men in Wales, with in-depth cognitive assessments and data spanning over three decades, to examine the prevalence of sSCD, prospective associations from potential causal factors, and objective cognitive change.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001555> "A population-based prospective cohort of men aged 45–59 years from the town of Caerphilly and its surrounding villages in South Wales, United Kingdom, identified from electoral rolls and general practice lists and first examined in 1979–1983 by the MRC Epidemiology Unit (South Wales) to study risk factors for coronary heart disease, then re-examined in later phases that added cognitive testing and follow-up for dementia and other chronic diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3458872/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from 5745 individuals consecutively enrolled in the population-based setting, which is known as Amagasaki Study [26], 4990 individuals without receiving current treatment for dyslipidemia were included in the present study (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> "An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged over 18 years in Amagasaki, Hyogo Prefecture, Japan, consecutively enrolled for a baseline examination between September 2002 and August 2003, which is one of the member studies of the Cardio-metabolic Genome Epidemiology (CAGE) Network and whose samples are used in genetic studies of blood pressure, lipids and other cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Amagasaki Study is an ongoing population-based cohort study of 5,743 individuals (3,435 males and 2,310 females), aged >18 years and recruited for a baseline examination between September 2002 to August 200329.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> "An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged over 18 years in Amagasaki, Hyogo Prefecture, Japan, consecutively enrolled for a baseline examination between September 2002 and August 2003, which is one of the member studies of the Cardio-metabolic Genome Epidemiology (CAGE) Network and whose samples are used in genetic studies of blood pressure, lipids and other cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study considered 1,400 Japanese individuals which is a subset of the 3,933 subjects in Asian Diversity Project (ADP), comprising 200 subjects each from seven regions (prefectures or cities): Amagasaki (in Hyogo Prefecture), Ehime, Fukuoka, Kita-nagoya (in Aichi Prefecture), Okinawa, Shimane and Tokyo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> "An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged over 18 years in Amagasaki, Hyogo Prefecture, Japan, consecutively enrolled for a baseline examination between September 2002 and August 2003, which is one of the member studies of the Cardio-metabolic Genome Epidemiology (CAGE) Network and whose samples are used in genetic studies of blood pressure, lipids and other cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional panels of 3,294 hypertensive subjects and 6,831 normotensive controls were selected from the CAGE Network (hospital-‐based and population-‐based samples from the Amagasaki Study, Fukuoka Cohort Study, and KING Study) to test the strength of the hypertension association1 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> "An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged over 18 years in Amagasaki, Hyogo Prefecture, Japan, consecutively enrolled for a baseline examination between September 2002 and August 2003, which is one of the member studies of the Cardio-metabolic Genome Epidemiology (CAGE) Network and whose samples are used in genetic studies of blood pressure, lipids and other cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23050023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.834/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng834_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3158568/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The associations with SBP/DBP, BMI, fasting plasma glucose, and lipids were analyzed in CAGE-Amagasaki Study (for 5 SNPs) and CAGE-Fukuoka Study (for rs11066280 and rs671 alone) samples with and without adjustment for alcohol intake;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001556> "An ongoing population-based cohort of people aged over 18 years in Amagasaki, Hyogo Prefecture, Japan, consecutively enrolled for a baseline examination between September 2002 and August 2003, which is one of the member studies of the Cardio-metabolic Genome Epidemiology (CAGE) Network and whose samples are used in genetic studies of blood pressure, lipids and other cardiometabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20205615") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20205615+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data were derived from the baseline survey of the Kyushu University Fukuoka Cohort Study, and included 12,020 Japanese men and women aged 49-76 years who were free of chronic liver diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> "A community-based prospective cohort of middle-aged and older Japanese men and women in Fukuoka, Japan, run by Kyushu University, who took part in a baseline survey with a questionnaire and DNA collection between February 2004 and August 2007 and are followed up to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3022068/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Residents aged 49 to 76 years in the East Ward of Fukuoka City were invited to participate in the study by mail.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> "A community-based prospective cohort of middle-aged and older Japanese men and women in Fukuoka, Japan, run by Kyushu University, who took part in a baseline survey with a questionnaire and DNA collection between February 2004 and August 2007 and are followed up to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From this cohort, 12,569 subjects completed the questionnaire and also provided DNA for genotyping of SNPs to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility of the so-called lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer, and diabetes mellitus.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> "A community-based prospective cohort of middle-aged and older Japanese men and women in Fukuoka, Japan, run by Kyushu University, who took part in a baseline survey with a questionnaire and DNA collection between February 2004 and August 2007 and are followed up to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kyushu University Fukuoka Cohort Study is a community-based prospective epidemiologic cohort of 12,959 subjects, who participated in the baseline survey during the period from February 2004 to August 200732.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> "A community-based prospective cohort of middle-aged and older Japanese men and women in Fukuoka, Japan, run by Kyushu University, who took part in a baseline survey with a questionnaire and DNA collection between February 2004 and August 2007 and are followed up to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21297916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34313618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34313618+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We evaluated the association between baseline characteristics and outcomes (diagnosis of osteoporosis or incidence of fracture) in 4,427 postmenopausal women who participated in the Kyushu University Fukuoka Cohort Study on lifestyle-related diseases (baseline: February 2004 to August 2007; follow-up: February 2010 to December 2012).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001557> "A community-based prospective cohort of middle-aged and older Japanese men and women in Fukuoka, Japan, run by Kyushu University, who took part in a baseline survey with a questionnaire and DNA collection between February 2004 and August 2007 and are followed up to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Center for Global health and Medicine hospital-based cohort study (CAGE-NCGM) aims to prospectively investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558> "A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital's clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Non-diabetic subjects were chosen from the clinical practice or the annual medical checkup of the NCGM hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558> "A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital's clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were enrolled for the detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer, and diabetes mellitus.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558> "A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital's clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26648100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4673465/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects in the Tokyo district were selected from participants in the Hospital-based Cohort Study at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine (NCGM), Tokyo, to investigate lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility for lifestyle-related diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001558> "A hospital-based prospective cohort at the National Center for Global Health and Medicine in Tokyo, Japan, whose participants, drawn from the hospital's clinical practice and annual medical check-ups, are enrolled for detailed examination of lifestyle and lifestyle-related diseases such as cardiovascular diseases, cancer and diabetes mellitus to investigate the relationship between genetic and non-genetic factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ambulant, community-dwelling women aged ≥70 years were recruited from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, a citizenship requirement that covers >98% of this age group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dementia outcomes were captured through the Western Australian Data Linkage System over 14.5 years (from 1998 to 2013) and retrieved from the Western Australia Hospital Morbidity Data Collection and mortality records from death certificates, similar to previous publications.12,13") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following the five-year intervention (1998–2003), women participated in two subsequent follow-up observational studies (2003–2013), resulting in a total follow-up of 14.5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This post-hoc analysis of a five-year double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of calcium supplements for primary fracture prevention evaluated the long-term risk for dementia in older women, randomised to either calcium supplements or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12673806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women who were randomised to the calcium group received 600 mg of calcium as carbonate twice daily (1200 mg calcium per day) over a period of five years and were advised to consume the supplements with their morning and evening meals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38477757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41346785") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After CAIFOS, women were observed for a further 10 yr, with the entire study known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women (PLSAW).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001559> "A five-year randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily calcium carbonate supplementation for fracture prevention in ambulant, community-dwelling women aged 70 years or older, recruited in 1998 from the general population of Western Australia through the electoral roll, whose participants were followed after the trial ended in 2003 in two observational studies to 2013 and through linked Western Australian hospital and death records, the whole study being known as the Perth Longitudinal Study of Ageing Women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2639618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, of the eligible subjects, 396 girls participated in the laboratory tests one to eight times during a maximum period of 8 years (mean duration of total follow-up was 7.5 years and mean age at last follow-up was 18.3 years;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2639618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the 396 girls, 258 participated in a calcium and vitamin D intervention during the first 2 years [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2639618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects were first contacted via class teachers teaching grades 4 to 6 (age 9 to 13 years old) in 61 schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (96% of all the schools in these areas).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2639618/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used sibling data to estimate the broad sense heritability of body composition with a linear mixed-effects model (n = 456 individuals, including brothers and sisters of the girls) [20,21].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4184839/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 235 Finnish young women (mean age 18.3 yrs, range 16.1–21.4 yrs) participated in the laboratory tests in the year 2007–8. In addition, 40 brothers, 214 mothers, 121 fathers, 120 grandmothers and 65 grandfathers of these girls were also invited to participate in the measurements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19171028") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24358145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279460") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26439744") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30158200") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6113773/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Calex-family study Cohort Finland Jyväskylä and its surrondings Northern European General population 994 The Calex-family study is a family- based study to study Fractures in Puberty - Causes and Implications in Old Age") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001560> "A Finnish three-generation family study run by researchers at the University of Jyväskylä, built on the Calex study, a cohort of girls recruited in school grades 4 to 6 through schools in the city of Jyväskylä and its surroundings in Central Finland (some of whom first took part in a two-year randomised calcium, vitamin D and dairy supplementation trial) and followed through puberty for about 7.5 years; in 2007–2008 the girls, then young women, and their brothers, mothers, fathers, grandmothers and grandfathers were invited to the same bone, body-composition and blood measurements, to study the heritability and determinants of bone mass, body composition and related metabolic traits across generations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/public-health-nutrition/article/adherence-to-the-world-cancer-research-fundamerican-institute-for-cancer-research-cancer-prevention-recommendations-and-breast-cancer-risk-in-the-cancer-de-mama-cama-study/FC8C93652680936392587C5C112B03F4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(i) patients with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of BC, regardless of the stage of disease; (ii) patients with no previous treatment such as radiotherapy, chemotherapy or anti-oestrogens such as tamoxifen during the previous 6 months;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/public-health-nutrition/article/adherence-to-the-world-cancer-research-fundamerican-institute-for-cancer-research-cancer-prevention-recommendations-and-breast-cancer-risk-in-the-cancer-de-mama-cama-study/FC8C93652680936392587C5C112B03F4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were randomly selected by multiple-step random sampling and were frequency-matched to cases according to 5-year age groups, health-care institution and region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085630/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In both the patients and the controls, blood samples and anthropometric measurements were obtained at participating hospitals by personnel following standardized procedures and who were blinded to the study hypotheses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085630/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, the CAMA study included consecutive women with incident BC (cases (n = 1000)), aged 35–69 years, who were required to have had a minimum of 5 years of residency in the study cities and who were recruited from 12 public hospitals") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085630/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In-person interviews were conducted at the hospital with the patients and at the homes of the controls to obtain information on their sociodemographics, reproductive health, breast pathology, lifestyle, and co-morbidities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20084545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25805146") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30092822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085630/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study is derived from the population-based case-control study “Risk factors for BC in Mexico: mammographic patterns, C-peptide, and growth factors, a multicenter study” (CAMA), which was conducted in three cities of Mexico (Monterrey, Veracruz, and Mexico City) from January 2004 to December 2007 [42].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001561> "A population-based case–control study of breast cancer in Mexican women aged 35 to 69, carried out from January 2004 to December 2007 in Mexico City, Monterrey and Veracruz by investigators of the Mexican National Institute of Public Health, in which women with newly diagnosed, untreated breast cancer were recruited at twelve public hospitals of the Mexican Social Security Institute, the Institute of Security and Social Services of State Workers and the Ministry of Health, and controls, frequency-matched to the cases by age, health-care institution and region, were chosen by multistage random household sampling; participants were interviewed on health, diet and physical activity, measured and gave blood samples, to study risk factors for breast cancer in Mexico.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2916850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CAMSCHMainland China28728756.3 (11.6)56.3 (10.0)Case-control") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562> "A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2916850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Replication of the strongest signal, rs2736100 was performed in the remaining subjects of the GELAC study [13] as well as six studies of never-smoking Asian women with lung adenocarcinoma in East Asia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562> "A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2916850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The additional replication studies included the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences Cancer Hospital study (CAMSCH) [16], Wuhan lung cancer study (WHLCS) [17], Seoul National University study (SNU) [18], Korea University Medical Center study (KUMC) [19], Kyungpook National University Hospital study (KNUH) [20] and Shanghai Women's Health Cohort Study (SWHS) [21], [22] (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001562> "A lung cancer case–control study of ethnic Han Chinese, carried out from 1997 to 2008, in which cases were recruited from Beijing and surrounding provinces at the Cancer Hospital of the Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences in Beijing, China, and cancer-free controls from the same region and period were drawn from a community nutritional survey, to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer; its never-smoking women take part in the genome-wide association studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
