AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931544") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16931544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16931544+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate this, the authors undertook a case-control study (n = 1,012) of the association between NSAIDs and more advanced prostate cancer in Ohio men recruited between 2001 and 2004 and evaluated whether this association was modified by a functional polymorphism in the lymphotoxin alpha (LTA) gene (LTA C+80A, where the CC genotype results in higher LTA production).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001564> "A case–control study of more aggressive prostate cancer in men recruited from 2001 to 2004 at the major medical institutions of Cleveland, Ohio, United States (the Cleveland Clinic, University Hospitals of Cleveland and their affiliates), in which cases were newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancers of higher grade, stage or prostate-specific antigen level, and age-matched controls were men without prostate cancer undergoing standard annual medical examinations at the same institutions, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for aggressive prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931544") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21602798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21602798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.839/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng839_MOESM33_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects were recruited and frequency-matched on the major medical institutions in Cleveland, Ohio (i.e., the Cleveland Clinic, University Hospitals of Cleveland, and their affiliates) between 2001 and 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001564> "A case–control study of more aggressive prostate cancer in men recruited from 2001 to 2004 at the major medical institutions of Cleveland, Ohio, United States (the Cleveland Clinic, University Hospitals of Cleveland and their affiliates), in which cases were newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancers of higher grade, stage or prostate-specific antigen level, and age-matched controls were men without prostate cancer undergoing standard annual medical examinations at the same institutions, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for aggressive prostate cancer.")
