# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19566956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10891016+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 545 high-risk infants (at least 1 first-degree relative with asthma or 2 first-degree relatives with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19566956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10891016+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Avoidance of house dust mite and pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding, and supplementation with a partially hydrolyzed formula.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19566956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10891016+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prospective, prenatally randomized, controlled study with follow-up through the age of 1 year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19566956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15100668+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast-feeding was encouraged with formula supplementation if necessary, and introduction of solid foods was delayed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy.")
