AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10891016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15100668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19566956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35686384") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9796543/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Current asthma and allergy sensitization were based on a pediatric allergist's clinical decision and skin prick test results, respectively, at age 1‐, 2‐, 7‐, and 15‐years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001565> "A prenatally randomised controlled trial, begun in 1995 at university hospital-based centres in Vancouver and Winnipeg, Canada, of infants at high risk of asthma (with at least one first-degree relative with asthma or two with other IgE-mediated allergic diseases) identified before birth, whose families were assigned either to a multifaceted intervention in the first year of life (avoidance of house dust mite, pet allergens and environmental tobacco smoke, encouragement of breastfeeding with partially hydrolysed formula supplementation, and delayed introduction of solid foods) or to a control group, and whose children were followed as a birth cohort with paediatric allergist assessments to age 15, to test the primary prevention of asthma and allergy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16339465+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Carotid Atherosclerosis Progression Study (CAPS; n=5056; age range 19 to 90 years; mean age 50.1 years), common carotid artery (CCA) IMT, bifurcation IMT, internal carotid artery IMT and vascular risk factors were evaluated at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16339465+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The incidence of stroke, myocardial infarction (MI), and death was determined prospectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17332447+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 3000 individuals from the prospective community-based Carotid Atherosclerosis Progression Study (CAPS) were genotyped for single nucleotide polymorphisms: TLR2 (Arg753Gln, -16934 A/T) and TLR4 (D299G, T399I).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17332447+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Associations were determined with common carotid artery intima-media thickness (IMT) at baseline and also progression of IMT over the 3-year follow-up period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4254855/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Carotid Atherosclerosis Progression Study (CAPS), members of a German primary healthcare scheme were invited of whom 6,962 participants (attendance rate 21%) agreed to take part.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15243147") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16339465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17332447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431077") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22617119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22617119+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the 10-year follow-up of 4995 subjects, strokes, transient ischaemic attacks (TIA) and deaths were recorded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001566> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Germany in which adults aged about 19 to 90, volunteers from among the members of a German primary health-care scheme, had vascular risk factors and carotid intima–media thickness measured by ultrasound at baseline and again after about three years, and were followed for about ten years for myocardial infarction, stroke, transient ischaemic attack and death, to study the progression of early carotid atherosclerosis and its value in predicting vascular events.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3518149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, from October 2000 to December 2010, a standard protocol was used to recruit incident cases of histologically confirmed lung cancer at Asturias’ four main hospitals (the Cabueñes Hospital in Gijón, San Agustin Hospital in Avilés, General Hospital in Oviedo and Álvarez-Buylla Hospital in Mieres).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3518149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, controls were selected from patients admitted to those hospitals with diagnoses unrelated to the exposures of interest and individually matched by ethnicity, gender, age (± 5 years) and hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3518149/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CAPUA (Lung Cancer in Asturias [Cáncer de Pulmón en Asturias], Spain) study is a hospital-based, case–control study conducted by the Molecular Epidemiology Cancer Unit at the University Institute of Oncology (University of Oviedo).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were incident cases of histologically confirmed lung cancer between 30 and 85 years of age and residents in the geographical area of each participating hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Structured questionnaires collected information on sociodemographic characteristics, recent and prior tobacco use, environmental exposure (air pollution and passive smoking), diet, personal and family history of cancer, and occupational history from each participant.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5560148/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A quality control of 50 blood and mouthwash samples from the same participants was used to confirm the reliability of the genotyping results using the mouthwash samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5560148/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, a total of 877 incident lung cancer cases aged 30-85 years were recruited and interviewed in four main hospitals of Asturias in northern Spain from October 2000 to December 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23013535") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28819433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5560148/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The questionnaires collected information from the participants about age, sex, sociodemographic characteristics, tobacco history, diet (including alcohol consumption), occupation, and personal and family (first-degree relatives) history of cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001567> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Asturias, northern Spain, run by the Molecular Epidemiology of Cancer Unit of the University Institute of Oncology of the University of Oviedo, which from October 2000 used a standard protocol to recruit incident, histologically confirmed lung cancer cases aged 30 to 85 living in the areas of the main hospitals of Asturias (in Gijón, Avilés, Oviedo and Mieres), with controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to the exposures studied and individually matched by ethnicity, sex, age and hospital; participants were interviewed on tobacco, diet, occupation and environmental exposures and gave blood or mouthwash samples, to study lifestyle, occupational and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11918622+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Collaborative AtoRvastatin Diabetes Study (CARDS) is a multicentre, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind clinical trial of primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in patients with Type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11918622+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This paper describes the design of a collaborative clinical trial between Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, that addresses this question.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15325833+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2838 patients aged 40-75 years in 132 centres in the UK and Ireland were randomised to placebo (n=1410) or atorvastatin 10 mg daily (n=1428).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15325833+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study entrants had no documented previous history of cardiovascular disease, an LDL-cholesterol concentration of 4.14 mmol/L or lower, a fasting triglyceride amount of 6.78 mmol/L or less, and at least one of the following: retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking, or hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15325833+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial was terminated 2 years earlier than expected because the prespecified early stopping rule for efficacy had been met.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11918622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15325833") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25899452") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4472939/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001568> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of atorvastatin 10 mg daily for the primary prevention of cardiovascular disease in men and women aged 40–75 with type 2 diabetes, no history of cardiovascular disease, LDL cholesterol of 4.14 mmol/l or less and at least one further risk factor (retinopathy, albuminuria, current smoking or hypertension), who were randomised between November 1997 and June 2001 at centres in the United Kingdom and Ireland. It was run as a collaboration of Diabetes UK, the NHS Research and Development Directorate and Pfizer UK, and was stopped early when its prespecified efficacy criterion was met.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bmj.com/content/332/7555/1426") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men and postmenopausal women were eligible if they had had an acute myocardial infarction 3-20 months before the study, low density lipoprotein cholesterol concentrations of 3.0-4.5 mmol/l, fasting glucose concentrations of no more than 12.2 mmol/l, left ventricular ejection fractions of no less than 25%, no symptoms of congestive heart failure, and were 21-75 years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bmj.com/content/332/7555/1426") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were stratified according to clinical centre and randomly assigned in a double blinded fashion to receive either 40 mg of pravastatin (Pravachol, Bristol Myers Squibb) or placebo once daily.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bmj.com/content/332/7555/1426") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CARE study was initiated by the investigators and was funded by Bristol-Myers-Squibb.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1746424+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cholesterol and Recurrent Events trial is testing whether pravastatin, a hydroxymethylglutaryl coenzyme A reductase inhibitor, will decrease the sum of fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction (MI) in patients who have recovered from a MI and who have normal total cholesterol levels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7572695+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial was designed to have a median follow-up of 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16714328") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7572695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8801446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9841599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9841599+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "80 hospitals and affiliates in the United States and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001569> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled secondary-prevention trial of pravastatin 40 mg daily in men and postmenopausal women aged 21–75 who had had a myocardial infarction 3 to 20 months earlier and had average cholesterol levels (total cholesterol below 240 mg/dl and LDL cholesterol of 115–174 mg/dl), enrolled at 80 hospitals and affiliated centres in the United States and Canada and followed for about five years to test whether lowering cholesterol reduces fatal coronary heart disease and nonfatal myocardial infarction. It was initiated by its investigators and funded by Bristol-Myers Squibb.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15157730+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to promote innovative research in asthma therapies, the National Heart, Lung and Blood Institute created the Childhood Asthma Research and Education Network in 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PACT was designed to compare three contemporary asthma controller regimens as first-line therapy for the management of mild-to-moderate persistent asthma in school-aged children.45") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PEAK was a three year long, double blind, randomized, parallel group design trial in which children ages 2–3 years with a positive modified asthma predictive index (API) were treated for two years with either fluticasone 44 mcg/puff MDI, 2 puffs twice daily via a spacer and face mask, or matching placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CARE Network was next developed in 1999 and consisted of five clinical centers (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and one data coordinating center (Penn State University, Hershey).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objectives of these clinical research networks are to conduct multiple, well designed clinical trials for rapid evaluation of new and existing therapeutic approaches to asthma and to disseminate laboratory and clinical findings to the health care community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15157730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17141853") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2742212/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, the CARE Network designed the CLIC trial42 to examine the variability of responses to both ICSs and LTRAs in children with asthma to identify patient features that would serve as indicators for selection of the controller medications most likely to achieve a favorable response in individual patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001570> "A paediatric asthma clinical research network created in 1999 by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, made up of five clinical centres (University of California, San Diego; University of Arizona, Tucson; Washington University, St. Louis; University of Wisconsin, Madison; National Jewish Medical and Research Center, Denver) and a data coordinating centre at Penn State University, Hershey, to evaluate new and existing asthma therapies in children through multicentre randomised clinical trials. Its trial cohorts include the Prevention of Early Asthma in Kids (PEAK) trial in preschool children at high risk of asthma and the CLIC and PACT trials in school-aged children with mild-to-moderate persistent asthma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1844268+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARET is a multi-center collaboration, with participants recruited in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8137335+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As of April 30, 1993, CARET had randomized 1,845 participants in the 1985-1988 pilot phase plus 13,260 \"efficacy\" participants since 1989; of these, 4,000 are asbestos-exposed males and 11,105 are smokers and former smokers (44% female).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARET began in 1985, and the intervention was halted in January 1996, 21 months ahead of schedule, with the twin conclusions for definitive evidence of no benefit and substantial evidence of a harmful effect of the intervention on both lung cancer incidence and total mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARET continued to follow and collect endpoints on their participants through 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the active intervention phase of CARET, serum, plasma, whole blood, and lung tissue specimens were collected on participants. These biospecimens make up the CARET Biorepository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15572756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1844268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8137335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8602180") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Carotene and Retinol Efficacy Trial (CARET) was a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of the cancer prevention efficacy and safety of a daily combination of 30 mg of beta-carotene and 25,000 IU of retinyl palmitate in 18,314 persons at high risk for lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001571> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of daily beta-carotene (30 mg) plus retinyl palmitate (25,000 IU) for the primary prevention of lung cancer in people at high risk of it, namely male and female heavy smokers and former smokers and asbestos-exposed men, recruited at centres in Seattle, Portland, San Francisco, Irvine, Baltimore and New Haven, United States, in a pilot phase from 1985 and an efficacy phase from 1989. The intervention was stopped in January 1996, 21 months early, because it increased lung cancer incidence and mortality; participants were followed through 2005, and the serum, plasma, whole blood and lung tissue collected during the trial form the CARET Biorepository.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12908658+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Institute of Mental Health initiated the Clinical Antipsychotic Trials of Intervention Effectiveness (CATIE) program to evaluate the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in typical settings and populations so that the study results will be maximally useful in routine clinical situations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16172203+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1493 patients with schizophrenia were recruited at 57 U.S. sites and randomly assigned to receive olanzapine (7.5 to 30 mg per day), perphenazine (8 to 32 mg per day), quetiapine (200 to 800 mg per day), or risperidone (1.5 to 6.0 mg per day) for up to 18 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3910086/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases were participants in the CATIE project (NIMH contract NO1 MH90001) which was conducted between 1/2001-12/2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3910086/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study inclusion criteria were: definite diagnosis of SCZ (28, 29), age 18–67 years, clinical decision that oral medication was appropriate, adequate decisional capacity, and provision of written informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3910086/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The optional genetic sub-study began about a year after the trial began and 51% of CATIE participants donated a DNA sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12908658") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16172203") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18347602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19721433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2888895/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CATIE assessments began with a baseline assessment followed by Phase 1, a double-blinded randomized clinical trial comparing treatment with the second generation antipsychotics olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone, or ziprasidone versus perphenazine (a midpotency first generation antipsychotic).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001572> "A multiphase randomised trial of the effectiveness of antipsychotic drugs in adults aged 18–67 with chronic schizophrenia, run under the US National Institute of Mental Health's CATIE programme in 2001–2004 at 57 clinical sites across the United States (public mental health, academic, Veterans Affairs and managed care settings), whose double-blind first phase compared the first-generation drug perphenazine with the second-generation drugs olanzapine, quetiapine, risperidone and ziprasidone for up to 18 months, with all-cause treatment discontinuation as the primary outcome. Participants could join an optional genetic sub-study by donating DNA.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4740268/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Neighborhood controls, individuals with little or no lifetime opioid misuse, were recruited from socially disadvantaged neighborhoods in geographic proximity to OST clinics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4740268/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Opioid dependent individuals, aged 18 or older, were recruited from opioid substitution therapy (OST) clinics in the greater Sydney region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection began in 2004 and candidate gene genotyping was completed in 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants provided blood samples as a source of DNA and completed a comprehensive psychiatric diagnostic interview based on the Semi-Structured Assessment of the Genetics of Alcoholism - Australia (SSAGA-OZ) augmented with sections drawn from other instruments assessing childhood trauma exposure, family history, and screening for borderline personality disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Comorbidity and Trauma Study was funded in 2003 by NIDA as a collaboration of investigators at Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre, University of New South Wales.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23245376") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26239289") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a retrospective case-control study examining genetic and environmental factors contributing to heroin dependence liability.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001573> "A retrospective case–control study of genetic and environmental contributions to heroin dependence, funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse in 2003 and run by Washington University, the Queensland Institute of Medical Research and the National Drug and Alcohol Research Centre (University of New South Wales), which from 2004 recruited opioid-dependent adults from opioid substitution (maintenance) treatment clinics in the greater Sydney area, Australia, and neighbourhood controls with little or no lifetime opioid use from socially disadvantaged areas served by the same clinics. Participants gave blood for DNA and completed a psychiatric diagnostic interview (SSAGA-OZ) with added assessments of childhood trauma, family history and borderline personality disorder.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3774761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "594 controls were selected from the ‘10,001 Dalmatians’ study, an ongoing genetic study in Croatia. This study includes approximately three thousand individuals from the general population of Split and from Vis and Korčula Islands in Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3774761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Although both are located in Zagreb, these tertiary care hospitals attract patients from across the country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3774761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were picked randomly, but with constrains regarding age (+/- 5 years) and sex. Participants with personal history of malignant disease were excluded from the control group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3774761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the period from November 2008 to July 2009, a total of 338 colorectal cancer cases were recruited at departments of surgery in two hospitals in Zagreb, Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24066093+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped four variants previously associated with CRC: rs10795668, rs16892766, rs3802842 and rs4939827.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24066093") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6517433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DACHS study samples were genotyped using the Illumina OncoArray, CORSA study sampels were genotyped on the Affymetrix Axiom Genome-Wide CEU 1 Array, and Croatia study samples were genotyped on Illumina OmniExpressExome BeadChip 8v1.1 or 8v1.3.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001574> "A case–control study of colorectal cancer in Croatia, whose cases are patients with colorectal cancer recruited from November 2008 at the surgery departments of two tertiary hospitals in Zagreb that receive patients from across the country, and whose population controls without a history of cancer were drawn at random, by age and sex, from the '10,001 Dalmatians' study of the general population of Split and the islands of Vis and Korčula. Its participants were genotyped for known colorectal cancer risk variants and later genome-wide, for European colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC212698/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases were a random sample of Europid men and women with Type 2 diabetes, aged 47–75 years, from a population-based diabetes register in a geographically defined region in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cambridgeshire, Ely, ADDITION, EPIC-Norfolk, and the Norfolk Diabetes studies were funded by the MRC with support from NHS Research & Development and the Wellcome Trust.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were randomly selected from general practitioner diabetes registers in Cambridgeshire, UK, and T2D was defined as onset of diabetes after the age of 30 y and without insulin use in the first year after diagnosis [12].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames, and individually matched to cases for age, sex, and general practitioner practice.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diabetes was excluded in controls by medical record search and by a glycated haemoglobin measurement of less than 6%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12045211") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14551916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cambridgeshire case-control study is a population-based study of T2D cases, aged 45–76 y, and age- and sex-matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001575> "A population-based case–control study of type 2 diabetes in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, whose cases are Europid men and women with type 2 diabetes (onset after age 30 without insulin treatment in the first year after diagnosis) randomly selected from general practice diabetes registers in a geographically defined region of Cambridgeshire, and whose controls were recruited at random from the same population sampling frames and individually matched to cases for age, sex and general practice, with diabetes excluded by medical record search and an HbA1c below 6%. It was funded by the Medical Research Council with support from NHS Research and Development and the Wellcome Trust.")

