AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7474092/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2010 and 2015, adult subjects with mFMD (Nunrelated = 412) were enrolled with IRB approval in the Cleveland Clinic FMD Biorepository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001577> "A biorepository of DNA and clinical data from adults with fibromuscular dysplasia enrolled at the Cleveland Clinic, Cleveland, Ohio, United States, from consecutive patients seen at its dedicated fibromuscular dysplasia referral clinic, each giving a blood or saliva sample, used in genetic studies of fibromuscular dysplasia and of arterial dissection, including spontaneous coronary artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7474092/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each research participant contributed either a blood or saliva sample via standard K+ EDTA blood collection tubes or commercial saliva collection kits (Oragene, DNAGenotek).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001577> "A biorepository of DNA and clinical data from adults with fibromuscular dysplasia enrolled at the Cleveland Clinic, Cleveland, Ohio, United States, from consecutive patients seen at its dedicated fibromuscular dysplasia referral clinic, each giving a blood or saliva sample, used in genetic studies of fibromuscular dysplasia and of arterial dissection, including spontaneous coronary artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34654805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32887874") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7474092/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given the overlap of FMD and SCAD diagnoses in some individuals, we hypothesized that alleles discovered by our GWAS would be associated with SCAD events in individuals with mFMD and tested this in a cohort of individuals with mFMD consecutively enrolled at presentation to subspecialty clinics with angiographic evidence of mFMD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001577> "A biorepository of DNA and clinical data from adults with fibromuscular dysplasia enrolled at the Cleveland Clinic, Cleveland, Ohio, United States, from consecutive patients seen at its dedicated fibromuscular dysplasia referral clinic, each giving a blood or saliva sample, used in genetic studies of fibromuscular dysplasia and of arterial dissection, including spontaneous coronary artery dissection.")
