# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3490334/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases were phenotyped by an experienced stroke neurologist according to TOAST criteria, based on relevant clinical imaging and available information on cardiovascular risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3490334/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are Italian individuals enrolled within the PROCARDIS Study, with no personal or sibling history of coronary heart disease before age 66 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3490334/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Italian cases were genotyped using Illumina Human610-Quad v1_B or Human660W-Quad v1_A chips.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3490334/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study Includes consecutive Italian patients referred to Besta Institute from 2000 to 2009 with stroke and included in the Besta Cerebrovascular Diseases Registry (CEDIR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582024/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cerebrovascular Diseases Registry (CEDIR), Milan, Italy;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23381943") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3582024/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Besta Cerebrovascular Diseases Registry (CEDIR) was supported by the Italian Ministry of Health, years 2007-2010 (Annual Research Funding; Grant Numbers: RC 2007/LR6, RC 2008/LR6; RC 2009/LR8; RC 2010/LR8).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001582> "A registry of stroke patients at the Carlo Besta Neurological Institute (Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Carlo Besta), Milan, Italy, including consecutive Italian patients with stroke referred to the institute from 2000 to 2009, funded by the Italian Ministry of Health; its imaging-confirmed ischaemic stroke cases, subtyped by stroke neurologists with the TOAST criteria, were genotyped and studied with Italian PROCARDIS participants as controls in genome-wide association studies of stroke.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19753122") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21540858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22113997") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1097 newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed, renal parenchymal cancers (ICD-O-2 code C64) between 20 and 79 years of age were recruited during August 1999 and January 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583> "A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, with an exception for benign prostatic hyperplasia, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC's lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies; its participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region's high kidney cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19753122") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21540858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22113997") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible controls (n=1476) were admitted to the same hospitals as the cases for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disorders (except for benign prostatic hyperplasia) between August 1998 and March 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583> "A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, with an exception for benign prostatic hyperplasia, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC's lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies; its participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region's high kidney cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19753122") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21540858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22113997") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This hospital-based case–control study was conducted in seven centres (Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland), and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice, and Brno (Czech Republic)).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583> "A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, with an exception for benign prostatic hyperplasia, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC's lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies; its participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region's high kidney cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19753122") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21540858") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22113997") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19034282") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2600689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained interviewers used standardised questionnaires at all centres to elicit information on demographic background, smoking, alcohol drinking, dietary practices, height, weight, medical history, family history of cancer, residential history, and occupational history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001583> "A hospital-based multicentre case–control study of renal cell carcinoma conducted by the International Agency for Research on Cancer and the US National Cancer Institute at seven centres in Moscow (Russia), Bucharest (Romania), Lodz (Poland) and Prague, Olomouc, Ceske Budejovice and Brno (Czech Republic), which recruited newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed cases aged 20–79 between August 1999 and January 2003 and controls admitted to the same hospitals for conditions unrelated to smoking or genitourinary disease, with an exception for benign prostatic hyperplasia, some of them recruited in parallel for IARC's lung and head and neck cancer case–control studies; its participants were interviewed with standardised questionnaires on lifestyle, diet and medical, residential and occupational history and gave blood for DNA, to study the causes of the region's high kidney cancer rates.")
