# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681020/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A structured personal interview was performed with the child and one or preferably both parents by a trained interviewer during the time period 2006–2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681020/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CEFALO is an interview-based case–control study in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, including children and adolescents aged 7–19 years with primary intracranial brain tumours diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and matched population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681020/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CEFALO study is a multinational case–control study conducted in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, with the primary aim to investigate the possible association between CABT risk and mobile phone use and other relevant exposures (Aydin et al, 2011).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681020/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two controls per case were randomly selected from nationwide population registries in Scandinavia and in Switzerland from communal registries, and were individually matched by age (Denmark, Switzerland and Sweden: month of birth; Norway: year of birth), gender and region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681020/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "cases were identified both at hospitals and in country-specific disease registries") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21795665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23652309") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26014354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26014354+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Saliva DNA from 245 cases and 489 controls, aged 7-19 years at diagnosis/reference date, was extracted and genotyped for 29 SNPs reported by GWAS to be significantly associated with risk of adult glioma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001584> "An international population-based case–control study of primary intracranial brain tumours in children and adolescents aged 7–19 in Denmark, Norway, Sweden and Switzerland, whose cases were diagnosed between 2004 and 2008 and identified through hospitals and national cancer registries, and whose controls were drawn at random from population registries and matched by age, sex and region. The children and their parents were interviewed in person, mainly to find out whether mobile phone use and other exposures raise the risk of brain tumours; saliva DNA from part of the participants was genotyped in candidate-gene studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6880438/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals in the technical concordance cohort and clinical cohort gave electronic informed consent that Color may author publications using non-aggregated, de-identified information, either on its own or in collaboration with academic or commercial third parties.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> "A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6880438/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals in the technical concordance cohort and clinical cohort gave electronic informed consent to have their de-identified information and sample used in anonymized studies (Western Institutional Review Board, #20150716).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> "A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6880438/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All phenotypic information was self-reported by the individual through an online, interactive health history tool.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> "A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6880438/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical cohort included DNA samples from 11,502 individuals whose healthcare provider had ordered a Color multi-gene panel test (Fig. 1b).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> "A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31771638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32820175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7441381/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a breast cancer case-control study consisted of 19,264 women (1920 cases and 17,344 controls) who underwent clinical grade genetic testing for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndrome at a commercial testing laboratory (Color Genomics; Burlingame, CA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001585> "A research cohort of people whose healthcare provider ordered clinical-grade multi-gene panel testing for inherited disease risk, such as hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, from Color Genomics, a commercial genetic testing laboratory in Burlingame, California, and who gave electronic informed consent, under a Western Institutional Review Board protocol, for their de-identified samples, sequence data and health histories, self-reported through an online tool, to be used in research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3048024/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "genotyping of assembled DNA samples using three platforms: Sequenom for the Pilot Study, the ITMAT-Broad-CARe (IBC) array for candidate gene studies, and the Affymetrix 6.0 array for genome-wide association studies;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048024/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CARe has assembled DNA samples for more than 40,000 individuals self-identified as European-American, African-American, Hispanic, or Chinese-American, with accompanying data on hundreds of phenotypes that have been standardized and deposited in the CARe Phenotype Database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048024/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CARe Study was initiated by the NHLBI in 2006. DNA samples and phenotypic information from the nine NHLBI cohorts—ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, CHS, CSSCD, FHS, JHS, MESA, and SHHS—were sent to the Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard and deposited in the CARe Phenotype Database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3048024/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute’s Candidate Gene Association Resource (CARe), a planned cross-cohort analysis of genetic variation in cardiovascular, pulmonary, hematological, and sleep-related traits, comprises more than 40,000 participants representing four ethnic groups in nine community-based cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from individual cohorts is available to approved investigators through dbGaP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000283.v6.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, a genome wide association study using a 1,000K SNP Chip was conducted on approximately 8,900 African American participants drawn from five CARe cohorts: ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, JHS, and MESA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001586> "A shared genotype–phenotype resource set up by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute in 2006, which brought DNA samples and phenotype data from nine NHLBI cohort studies (ARIC, CARDIA, the Cleveland Family Study, the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Cooperative Study of Sickle Cell Disease, the Framingham Heart Study, the Jackson Heart Study, MESA and the Sleep Heart Health Study) to the Broad Institute, genotyped their European American, African American, Hispanic and Chinese American participants on a candidate-gene array (the ITMAT-Broad-CARe array) and the African American participants of five of the cohorts genome-wide, and makes the data available to approved researchers, to find genetic variants associated with cardiovascular, pulmonary, haematological and sleep-related traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9583631/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were obtained at baseline (study inclusion) from a self-administered questionnaire reviewed together with an investigator on the day of attendance, a physical examination and from blood samples including DNA extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9583631/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals participating in the study were by linkage to the Danish registries followed with information on diagnosis codes, emigration status and information from the causes of death registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9960719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A follow-up examination began in 2014 and is still ongoing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9960719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All individuals aged 40 years and above, and 25% of individuals aged 20 to 39 years from the greater Copenhagen area (municipalities of Herlev, Ballerup, Gladsaxe, Gentofte, Rødovre, Furesø, Lyngby-Tårbæk, Copenhagen, Egedal, Rudersdal, Allerød, Glostrup, Albertslund, Hørsholm, and Frederikssund) were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9960719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study design, the Copenhagen General Population Study (Herlev/Østerbroundersøgelsen) was initiated in 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36214322") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36852012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36891075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9986766/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the Copenhagen General Population Study are invited to participate by random selection on the basis of the national Danish Civil Registration System to reflect the Danish population aged 20 to 100 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001587> "A prospective general-population cohort run from Herlev and Gentofte Hospital, Copenhagen University Hospital, and modelled on the Copenhagen City Heart Study, which from 2003 to 2015 invited adults aged 20–100 living in the greater Copenhagen area, identified through the Danish Civil Registration System (all those aged 40 or over and a quarter of those aged 20–39), and examined them with a questionnaire, a physical examination, lung function tests and blood sampling with DNA extraction. Participants are re-examined in a second round that began in 2014 and are followed through the national Danish health registries for cardiovascular, pulmonary and other diseases and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7249710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The China MUCA 1998 cohort was established in 1998 with cluster random sampling and included about 500 men and 500 women aged 35 to 59 years in each of the 15 clusters.[17]") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> "A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study's 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7249710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was based on the project of Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR), which was a large collaborative study to investigate the epidemic of CVDs and identify the risk factors in the general Chinese population") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> "A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study's 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8315380/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The China MUCA (1992–1994) and the China MUCA (1998) selected 14,392 (9 clusters) and 11,480 participants (11 clusters) aged 35–59 years using cluster random sampling method in 1992–1994 and 1998, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> "A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study's 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "According to a uniform protocol, both InterASIA and ChinaMUCA-1998 cohorts were first followed up during 2007–08, and all three cohorts were further followed up in 2012–15 and 2018–20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> "A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study's 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37305106") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10249193/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the China Multi‐Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (China MUCA‐1998), which employed a cluster random sampling method to select 11 clusters aged 35–59 years in nine provinces,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001588> "A population-based cohort of Chinese men and women aged 35–59, selected in 1998 by cluster random sampling in several provinces of China for the 1998 survey of the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (a separate sample from that study's 1992–1994 cohort), whose participants were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 under the uniform protocol of the China-PAR project to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12891-020-3073-3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, the Chingford Study was started in Chingford, North London, United Kingdom by contacting all women 45 to 64 years of age from a register of a large general practice in 1988 to 1989.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8449034/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The women have been assessed annually and are representative of women from the UK population in terms of demographic characteristics (25).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8982643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chingford study women were linked to the Office for National Statistics that provided the cause of death information from the death certificates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11029301/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It ran from 1989 to 2010, having over 20 years of follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11029301/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chingford study was a population-based prospective cohort study that aimed to assess musculoskeletal disease in the female population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32005116") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34288584") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34537387") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38637130") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3691951/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Chingford Study was established in 1989 when 1003 women, aged 44-67 years, derived from the register of a large general practice in Chingford, North London, were recruited to a prospective population-based longitudinal study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001589> "A prospective population-based cohort of women aged 45–64 registered with a large general practice in Chingford, North-East London, United Kingdom, recruited in 1988–1989 to study osteoarthritis, osteoporosis and other musculoskeletal disease and assessed annually for over 20 years (to 2010) with clinical examinations, nurse-administered questionnaires, hand and knee radiographs and bone density measurements; deaths are traced through the Office for National Statistics.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In association with the Prostate Cancer Association Group to Investigate Cancer Associated Alterations in the Genome (PRACTICAL) consortium for prostate cancer predisposition study [6, 8, 15], we investigated genetic predisposition to prostate cancer in men of Han Chinese ancestry using the custom Illumina single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNP) array (iCOGS) [8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in Han Chinese men run by the CHIPGECS collaborative group of Chinese hospitals and universities with Barts Cancer Institute, Queen Mary University of London, which recruited hospital patients with a pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer and cancer-free men of comparable age from the community or from hospital attendees having routine physical examinations, in several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, central and northeast), and whose samples were genotyped with the PRACTICAL consortium on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similar numbers of cancer-free controls and cases were recruited from the community or hospital subjects undergoing routine physical examination in each recruitment region in China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in Han Chinese men run by the CHIPGECS collaborative group of Chinese hospitals and universities with Barts Cancer Institute, Queen Mary University of London, which recruited hospital patients with a pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer and cancer-free men of comparable age from the community or from hospital attendees having routine physical examinations, in several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, central and northeast), and whose samples were genotyped with the PRACTICAL consortium on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases were hospital based with pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in Han Chinese men run by the CHIPGECS collaborative group of Chinese hospitals and universities with Barts Cancer Institute, Queen Mary University of London, which recruited hospital patients with a pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer and cancer-free men of comparable age from the community or from hospital attendees having routine physical examinations, in several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, central and northeast), and whose samples were genotyped with the PRACTICAL consortium on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These male Han Chinese subjects were recruited from several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, middle and northeast) by members of the Chinese Prostate Cancer Genetic and Environmental Correlation Study (CHIPGECS) collaborative group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in Han Chinese men run by the CHIPGECS collaborative group of Chinese hospitals and universities with Barts Cancer Institute, Queen Mary University of London, which recruited hospital patients with a pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer and cancer-free men of comparable age from the community or from hospital attendees having routine physical examinations, in several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, central and northeast), and whose samples were genotyped with the PRACTICAL consortium on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26881390") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5008293/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped 495 prostate cancer cases and 640 age matched non-cancer male controls (Supplementary Table S1) using the iCOGS SNP array [8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001590> "A case–control study of prostate cancer in Han Chinese men run by the CHIPGECS collaborative group of Chinese hospitals and universities with Barts Cancer Institute, Queen Mary University of London, which recruited hospital patients with a pathological diagnosis of primary prostate cancer and cancer-free men of comparable age from the community or from hospital attendees having routine physical examinations, in several regions of China (south, southeast, southwest, central and northeast), and whose samples were genotyped with the PRACTICAL consortium on the iCOGS and OncoArray arrays.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Building on these preliminary findings, the ChooseWell 365 study was a randomized clinical trial that tested a 12-month automated, personalized behavioral intervention to prevent weight gain and improve diet in hospital employees.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ChooseWell 365 was a randomized clinical trial of a behavioral intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Employees were potentially eligible for the study if they were between the ages of 20 and 75 years and used their ID for cafeteria purchases on the main campus at least 4 times a week for at least 6 weeks over a 12-week period prior to enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For 12 months, participants in the intervention group received 2 emails per week with feedback on previous cafeteria purchases and personalized health and lifestyle tips and 1 letter per month with peer comparisons and financial incentives for healthier purchases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and took part over 24 months, with a 12-month intervention period plus 12 months of follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30414448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097048") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8185595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This randomized clinical trial was conducted on the main campus of Massachusetts General Hospital (MGH), a large academic teaching hospital in Boston, Massachusetts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001591> "A randomized clinical trial among employees of Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston, Massachusetts, aged 20 to 75, who regularly paid for food at the hospital's traffic-light-labelled cafeterias with their employee ID, enrolled between September 2016 and February 2018 and followed for 24 months to test whether a 12-month automated, personalized intervention (feedback on their cafeteria purchases, health and lifestyle tips, social norm comparisons and financial incentives) prevented weight gain and improved diet.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4311073/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Beginning from study entry and continuing until high school graduation, yearly questionnaires assessed the development of respiratory symptoms and current activity patterns.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4311073/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, more than 11,000 school children were selected from classrooms in 16 communities in multiple waves of subject recruitment starting in 1993 to maximize the differences in regional air pollution concentrations and mixtures (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4311073/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Children’s Health Study (CHS) is a continuing series of longitudinal studies that first began in 1993 and has focused on demonstrating the chronic impacts of air pollution on respiratory illnesses from early childhood through adolescence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25738666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4430551/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For cohorts C and D, pulmonary-function testing was performed annually from 4th through 12th grade (mean ages, 10 to 18 years), with the use of rolling-seal spirometers. In cohort E, pulmonary-function testing was performed every other year, when the children were approximately 11, 13, and 15 years of age, with the use of pressure transducer–based spirometers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25738666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4430551/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The two earlier cohorts (cohorts C and D) enrolled fourth-grade students in 1992–1993 and 1995–1996, respectively, from elementary schools in 12 southern California communities.13 The third cohort (cohort E) enrolled kindergarten and first-grade students in 2002–2003") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20371422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25694817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://healthstudy.usc.edu/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The USC Children’s Health Study begins 1993 About 3,600 students from 4th, 7th and 10th grades join the study from 12 communities across Southern California 1996 900 participating students graduate from high school 2,100 new 4th grade students join the study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001592> "A prospective study of schoolchildren in southern California, run by the University of Southern California, that from 1993 recruited successive cohorts from school classrooms in 16 communities chosen to differ in regional air pollution (fourth, seventh and tenth graders in 1993, fourth graders in 1996, and kindergarten and first-grade children in 2002–2003) and followed them through school with yearly questionnaires and repeated lung function tests (yearly from fourth grade in the fourth-grade cohorts of 1993 and 1996, every other year in the 2002–2003 cohort), to study the chronic effects of air pollution and other environmental and genetic factors on children's respiratory health, asthma and lung function growth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22563304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22698489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25406188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22563304") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3341326/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-control study comprises 5,270 patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital during the period 1991–2009 and 5,270 unmatched controls without IHD randomly sampled from the CGPS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593> "A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22563304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22698489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25406188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22698489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4606982") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, instrumental variable analysis by 2-stage least-squares regression was used to assess a potential causal relationship between elevated nonfasting glucose levels and increased IHD and MI risk using genetic variants as instruments for elevated nonfasting glucose levels in an additive model; we used the CCHS, CGPS, and CIHDS combined to obtain maximal power.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593> "A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22563304") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22698489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25406188") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22698489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4606982") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to a diagnosis of IHD, these patients also had stenosis/atherosclerosis on coronary angiography and/or a positive exercise electrocardiography test, and/or MI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001593> "A hospital-based case-control study of ischaemic heart disease in Denmark whose cases are patients from the greater Copenhagen area referred for coronary angiography to Copenhagen University Hospital from 1991 onwards, with ischaemic heart disease documented by coronary stenosis or atherosclerosis on angiography, a positive exercise electrocardiogram or myocardial infarction, and whose controls without ischaemic heart disease are sampled from the Copenhagen General Population Study; with the Copenhagen City Heart Study and the Copenhagen General Population Study it is used in genetic and Mendelian randomization studies of cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31888885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7249710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR), which was a large collaborative study to investigate the epidemic of CVDs and identify the risk factors in the general Chinese population") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> "A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31888885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7249710/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CIMIC was a large, community-based cohort that was established from 2007 to 2008 and selected four survey sites from three provinces (Shandong, Henan, and Jiangsu) with different economic development levels in China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> "A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31888885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8315380/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CIMIC is a large community-based study, which recruited 86,428 participants aged ≥18 years by a 3-stage cluster random sampling method in 2007–2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> "A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31888885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "According to a uniform protocol, both InterASIA and ChinaMUCA-1998 cohorts were first followed up during 2007–08, and all three cohorts were further followed up in 2012–15 and 2018–20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> "A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31888885") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32433046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The validation cohorts were derived from three cohorts in the China-PAR project, including the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA), the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (ChinaMUCA-1998), and Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study (CIMIC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001594> "A community-based cohort of Chinese adults aged 18 or over recruited in 2007–2008 by three-stage cluster random sampling at four survey sites, in Shandong, Henan and Jiangsu provinces, chosen for their different levels of economic development; it is one of the sub-cohorts of the Prediction for Atherosclerotic Cardiovascular Disease Risk in China (China-PAR) project, followed up with the other sub-cohorts under a uniform protocol in 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 to study cardiovascular risk factors and incident cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4350512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Association analyses were conducted in the discovery sample of 225 alcohol-dependent subjects treated with acamprosate for 3 months in community-based treatment programs in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4350512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both men and women between the ages of 18 and 80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence based on DSM-IV-TR criteria with the last drink 5 or more days before enrollment were included in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4350512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In accordance with these considerations, we conducted an open label, naturalistic prospective study investigating genetic markers associated with abstinence in alcohol-dependent subjects treated with acamprosate in community-based programs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4350512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programs affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and the Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin, Minnesota, Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin (Supplementary Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9270258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, we applied a pharmaco-omics-informed genomic strategy during which we utilized plasma samples from 442 AUD subjects enrolled in the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism Study to assay circulating FGF21.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25290263") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00662571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35752286") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9270258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism recruited 442 AUD subjects with clinical data, and DNA samples were obtained prior to treatment [8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001595> "A pharmacogenomic study of acamprosate response in alcohol dependence, conducted from 2008 to 2013 by the Mayo Clinic Center for the Individualized Treatment of Alcoholism, which enrolled men and women aged 18–80 with a primary diagnosis of current alcohol dependence (DSM-IV-TR) whose last drink was at least 5 days before enrolment, from community-based residential and outpatient treatment programmes affiliated with Mayo Clinic in Rochester, Minnesota, and Mayo Clinic Health System sites in Austin and Albert Lea, Minnesota, and La Crosse, Wisconsin, treated them with acamprosate for 3 months in an open-label, naturalistic prospective design and collected DNA and plasma to identify biomarkers of treatment response.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases are children aged ≤18 years with a diagnosis of JIA by 16 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are healthy children aged ≤18 years, born in the state of Victoria, undergoing a minor elective surgical procedure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper we present data collected to CLARITY from February 2008 (study commencement) until December 2010, for a comparison of collected data pertaining to socio-demographics, lifestyle and birth between cases and controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident cases are defined as children recruited within six months of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prevalent cases are defined as those children diagnosed more than 6 months before recruitment, and since 1997.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23153063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3551677/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have established a JIA biobank in Melbourne, Australia called CLARITY – ChiLdhood Arthritis Risk factor Identification sTudY, with the broad aim of identifying genomic and environmental disease risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001596> "A case-control study and biobank of juvenile idiopathic arthritis at the Royal Children's Hospital in Melbourne, Victoria, Australia, begun in February 2008, whose cases are children aged 18 or under with juvenile idiopathic arthritis diagnosed by age 16, recruited at hospital clinic visits within six months of diagnosis (incident) or later (prevalent, diagnosed since 1997), and whose controls are healthy Victorian-born children undergoing minor elective surgery at the hospital's Day Surgery Unit; families complete questionnaires on clinical, epidemiological and environmental factors and the children give a blood sample, to identify genomic and environmental risk factors for the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Electronic data sources can be used to follow the participants for updated contact information from membership files, cancer diagnoses through cancer registry databases, and deaths of through linkage with health plan mortality databases derived from state death certificate files.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2002 – 2003, we established the California Men's Health Study (CMHS), a multiethnic cohort of 84 170 men ages 45 to 69 years who are members of the northern and southern California regions of Kaiser Permanente, the largest managed care organization in California.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Members were also offered the option to complete the questionnaires electronically in English on a secure website (NCS Pearson, Inc.).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established a male, multiethnic cohort primarily to study prostate cancer etiology and secondarily to study the etiologies of other cancer and non-cancer conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We linked study data with clinical data, including laboratory, hospitalization, and cancer data, from electronic health plan files.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16813653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1569841/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We obtained baseline data from the men using a two-stage mailed survey, and we employed unique recruitment techniques to enrich the cohort with non-white men.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001597> "A prospective multiethnic cohort of men aged 45 to 69 who were members of the northern and southern California regions of the Kaiser Permanente health plan, recruited in 2002–2003 through a two-stage mailed or online questionnaire with mailing strategies to enrich the cohort with non-white men, and followed through linkage with the health plan's electronic clinical, laboratory, hospitalisation, cancer registry and mortality data, mainly to study the causes of prostate cancer and also of other cancers and non-cancerous conditions in men.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0109973") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO), Madrid, Spain") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> "A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4229095/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Second, we further investigated 42 SNPs with suggestive evidence for association using 41,785 cases and 41,880 controls from 41 studies included in the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> "A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32424353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CNIO-BCS | Spanish National Cancer Centre Breast Cancer Study | Spain | Case-control study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> "A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(i) consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo; (ii) cases with at least one affected first degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid (2000-2005)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> "A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25390939") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women attending the Menopause Research Centre, Madrid and female members of the College of Lawyers attending a free, targeted medical check-up in Madrid, all free of breast cancer and all in Madrid between 2000-2005") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001598> "A case-control study of breast cancer of the Spanish National Cancer Research Centre (CNIO) in Madrid, Spain, whose cases, recruited in 2000–2005, are consecutive breast cancer patients from three public hospitals, two in Madrid and one in Oviedo, and women with at least one affected first-degree relative recruited through the CNIO family cancer clinic in Madrid, and whose controls are women free of breast cancer attending the Menopause Research Centre in Madrid or a free medical check-up for female members of the College of Lawyers in Madrid; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28391914+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objectives of this cross-sectional cohort study are twofold: to identify the strongest predictors of CVD in patients with FH and to develop a new score to identify FH patients at very high CVD risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28391914+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We screened 20,434 patients with dyslipidemia to identify carriers of an FH-causing mutation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28456682+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among the 20,434 subjects attending the lipid clinic, we identified and included 725 individuals who carried an FH causing mutation in this retrospective cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7889287/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CNMA cohort used a 4-week washout period before obtaining a lipid profile to reduce confounding caused by cholesterol-lowering medication.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7889287/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed the influence of an LDL-C polygenic score on levels of LDL-C and risk of ASCVD for individuals with monogenic FH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28456682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33079599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7889287/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic, Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal, Montréal, Quebec") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001599> "A retrospective clinic-based cohort of patients with familial hypercholesterolaemia caused by a known mutation, identified by genetic screening among the patients with dyslipidaemia attending the lipid clinic (Nutrition, Metabolism and Atherosclerosis Clinic) of the Institut de recherches cliniques de Montréal in Montreal, Canada, whose clinical records and lipid profiles, measured after a washout of cholesterol-lowering medication, are used to study genetic and clinical modifiers of lipid levels and cardiovascular disease in familial hypercholesterolaemia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21316118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3048494/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All enrolled patients were pathologically confirmed at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital between January 2000 and August 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> "A case–control study of lung cancer based at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea. From 2000 it enrolled consecutive patients, all ethnic Koreans, with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed incident lung cancer, excluding secondary or recurrent tumours, and compared them with population-based controls to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21316118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3048494/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population consisted of 3938 patients with newly diagnosed lung cancer and 1700 population-based controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> "A case–control study of lung cancer based at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea. From 2000 it enrolled consecutive patients, all ethnic Koreans, with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed incident lung cancer, excluding secondary or recurrent tumours, and compared them with population-based controls to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
