AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21316118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with secondary or recurrent tumors were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> "A case–control study of lung cancer based at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea. From 2000 it enrolled consecutive patients, all ethnic Koreans, with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed incident lung cancer, excluding secondary or recurrent tumours, and compared them with population-based controls to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21316118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CNULCS was conducted in the Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea and has been previously described15 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> "A case–control study of lung cancer based at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea. From 2000 it enrolled consecutive patients, all ethnic Koreans, with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed incident lung cancer, excluding secondary or recurrent tumours, and compared them with population-based controls to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21316118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21342495") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4169232/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Internal sets (HKS, SNU, CNULCS, SWHS, YLCS and components of samples from Japan and GELAC) were genotyped at the NCI Cancer Genomic Research (CGR) Laboratory using the Illumina 660W SNP microarray.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001600> "A case–control study of lung cancer based at Chonnam National University Hwasun Hospital in Jeollanam-do, South Korea. From 2000 it enrolled consecutive patients, all ethnic Koreans, with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed incident lung cancer, excluding secondary or recurrent tumours, and compared them with population-based controls to study genetic susceptibility to lung cancer. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2862011/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Elligble subjects were then enrolled and examined in the Clinical Research Center at the Medical University South Carolina (MUSC), Charleston SC or four off-site centers approved by the MUSC Institutional Review committee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2862011/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were screened from an established cohort study of diabetes among Gullah African Americans (Project SuGar22), regularly scheduled community health fairs, recruitment events at local churches, and other community events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2862011/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects were recruited from June 2004 to May 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2862011/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study assessed the previously unknown prevalence of periodontal disease among a sample of Gullah African Americans with diabetes and investigated the association between diabetes control and presence of periodontal disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4212267/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Building upon the positive community partnership developed by Project SuGar, the first Center for Oral Health Research (COHR) project funded through the Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health mechanism became the second successful community-engaged genetic project under the SIFP umbrella.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19563285") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23966867") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25364473") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4212267/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first project was a genetic/epidemiologic cross-sectional study that investigated the prevalence of caries and periodontal disease in the T2DM Gullah population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001601> "A cross-sectional genetic and epidemiological study of periodontal disease and caries in Gullah African Americans with type 2 diabetes from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina. The Medical University of South Carolina ran it as the first project funded through its NIH Center of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE) for Oral Health. Participants were recruited in 2004–2006 from Project SuGAR, community health fairs and churches, were examined at MUSC in Charleston or at four off-site centres and gave blood for DNA, so that periodontal disease could be related to diabetes control, cytokine genes and inflammation. Their data form one of the studies of the Sea Islands Genetics Network.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6300273/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this report we calculated a genetic risk score using coefficients from a prior GWAS study and analyzed the relation between the genetic risk score and both presence and severity of CHD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6364925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Copenhagen Cardiovascular Genetic study (COGEN) is a biobank that has collected superfluous whole blood from patients admitted to six cardiology departments in the Capital region of Copenhagen from 2010–2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8213191/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline characteristics and results from the CAG were obtained from the Eastern Danish Heart Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8213191/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Copenhagen Cardiovascular Genetic study (COGEN) is comprised of approximately 80,000 patients admitted to six cardiology departments in the capital region of Copenhagen, Denmark, from 2010–2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8213191/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study is based on the first subset of COGEN participants that were genotyped, including patients with stable/unstable angina pectoris, non-ST elevation myocardial infarction (NSTEMI) or ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI) who were referred to a coronary angiography (CAG) in the period 2010–2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30566436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30726294") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34480422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8712846/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the nine case collections, seven were primarily focused on HF while two identified HF cases from an at‐risk population (COGEN and LURIC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001602> "A biobank of whole blood left over from the clinical care of patients admitted in 2010–2017 to six cardiology departments in the Capital Region of Denmark, around Copenhagen. The samples are linked to Danish clinical registries such as the Eastern Danish Heart Registry, and genotyped subsets of the patients, for example those who underwent coronary angiography in 2010–2014, are used to study the genetics of coronary artery disease, heart failure and other cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2394344/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 160 patients, who were approached to participate in the COGS study between February 1999 and July 2000, were eligible to participate in the patient feedback study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2394344/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients expressing interest were visited in their own home by the local study recruitment nurse to: discuss the COGS study; provide genetic counselling by constructing a detailed pedigree and producing an estimated risk of HNPCC for their relatives (low/moderate/high) based on Scottish guidelines (Haites et al, 2000); gain written consent; take a blood sample for genetic testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2394344/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Colorectal Cancer Genetic Susceptibility (COGS) study aims to evaluate a new Scottish-wide research strategy for identifying individuals at high risk of developing HNPCC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2293/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2293_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were sampled from the Scottish population NHS registers, matched by age (±5 years), gender and area of residence within Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4747430/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Scotland1 GWAS consisted of genotyping 1,012 early-onset Scottish CRC cases and 1,012 controls using the Illumina HumanHap300 and HumanHap240S arrays (COGS Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14562005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15931596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6135234/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Scotland1 COGS (Colorectal Cancer Susceptibility Study) Edinburgh University Scottish population-based incidence cases aged <55 at diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001603> "A Scotland-wide study run from Edinburgh from 1999 that approached patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer at age 55 or younger. Research nurses visited them at home to take a family pedigree, give genetic counselling and take blood for genetic testing, to evaluate a strategy for finding families with hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer and to study inherited susceptibility to colorectal cancer. Population controls matched by age, sex and area of residence were recruited through the Scottish NHS. Its early-onset cases and controls formed the Scotland1 genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6420345/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ColoCare Study participants agree to complete a baseline questionnaire and provide biological specimens at the time of enrollment and over the course of 5 years of follow-up, as outlined below.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6420345/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients are recruited before surgery (baseline).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6420345/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "with short-term and long-term patient-reported and clinical outcomes (e.g., therapy-induced toxicities, recurrence, survival and quality of life, etc.) among patients with colorectal cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6420345/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ColoCare (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT02328677) is an international, multi-center prospective cohort study among women and men newly diagnosed with a primary invasive colorectal cancer of any stage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6420345/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Center for Tumor Diseases and University Hospital of Heidelberg (Heidelberg, Germany) in 2010, Huntsman Cancer Institute (Salt Lake City, Utah, USA) in 2015") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30523039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC6420345/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was initially developed at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center (Seattle, Washington, USA) in 2007, with subsequent consortium sites at the H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center and Research Institute (Tampa, Florida, USA) in 2009") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001604> "An international, multicentre prospective cohort of adults newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal cancer of any stage. It began at the Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center in Seattle in 2007 and from 2009 added sites in Tampa, Heidelberg (Germany), Salt Lake City, Los Angeles, St. Louis and Memphis. Patients are enrolled before surgery. They complete questionnaires and give blood, urine and stool at enrolment and repeatedly during five years of follow-up, tumour and adipose tissue are collected at surgery, and treatment and outcome data are abstracted from medical records, so that biomarkers and modifiable lifestyle factors that predict recurrence, survival, treatment toxicity and quality of life can be found.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4046039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Division of Human Nutrition, Wageningen University, Wageningen, The Netherlands") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited in 2010–2020 at 11 hospitals in the Netherlands by investigators at Wageningen University. Participants complete questionnaires on diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, body weight and quality of life and give blood at diagnosis and 6 months, 2 years and 5 years later, while clinical data come from the Netherlands Cancer Registry and hospital records. The aim is to learn how diet and other lifestyle factors influence recurrence, survival and quality of life after colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4046039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information on clinical characteristics is gathered from linkage with the Netherlands Cancer Registry and with hospital databases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited in 2010–2020 at 11 hospitals in the Netherlands by investigators at Wageningen University. Participants complete questionnaires on diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, body weight and quality of life and give blood at diagnosis and 6 months, 2 years and 5 years later, while clinical data come from the Netherlands Cancer Registry and hospital records. The aim is to learn how diet and other lifestyle factors influence recurrence, survival and quality of life after colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4046039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main aim of this study is to assess associations of diet and other lifestyle factors, with colorectal cancer recurrence, survival and quality of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited in 2010–2020 at 11 hospitals in the Netherlands by investigators at Wageningen University. Participants complete questionnaires on diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, body weight and quality of life and give blood at diagnosis and 6 months, 2 years and 5 years later, while clinical data come from the Netherlands Cancer Registry and hospital records. The aim is to learn how diet and other lifestyle factors influence recurrence, survival and quality of life after colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4046039/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Upon recruitment, after 6 months, 2 years and 5 years, patients fill out food-frequency questionnaires; questionnaires about dietary supplement use, physical activity, weight, height, and quality of life; and donate blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited in 2010–2020 at 11 hospitals in the Netherlands by investigators at Wageningen University. Participants complete questionnaires on diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, body weight and quality of life and give blood at diagnosis and 6 months, 2 years and 5 years later, while clinical data come from the Netherlands Cancer Registry and hospital records. The aim is to learn how diet and other lifestyle factors influence recurrence, survival and quality of life after colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24886284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41212533") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13016977/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COLON study is a prospective cohort study among 2107 adults newly diagnosed with stage I-IV CRC, recruited between 2010 and 2020 via 11 hospitals throughout the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001605> "A multicentre prospective cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer of any stage, recruited in 2010–2020 at 11 hospitals in the Netherlands by investigators at Wageningen University. Participants complete questionnaires on diet, dietary supplements, physical activity, body weight and quality of life and give blood at diagnosis and 6 months, 2 years and 5 years later, while clinical data come from the Netherlands Cancer Registry and hospital records. The aim is to learn how diet and other lifestyle factors influence recurrence, survival and quality of life after colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "COLUMBUS is a population-based case–control study of breast cancer conducted in four cities: Bogota, Ibague and Neiva, from the Central Colombian Andes region, and Pasto, from the Colombian South.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer-free controls were recruited through the same institutions and were matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin using a genealogical interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident cases with invasive breast cancer aged 18–75 years have been recruited in two population registries and two large cancer hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4204111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment started in 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7301155/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of note, the COLUMBUS substudies (Colombia and Mexico) were analyzed as separate datasets, given differences in study populations and genotyping methods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25327703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39625644") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31553449") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7301155/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From Mexico City, Mexico, we analyzed data from 481 cases aged 25-89 and diagnosed 2010-2018 at the Social Security Hospital in Mexico City, the largest cancer hospital in the country. As controls, we included 453 blood donors without breast cancer recruited from the same hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001606> "A case–control study of breast cancer in Latin American women, led by investigators at the Universidad del Tolima in Ibagué, Colombia, and the University of California, Davis. From 2011 it recruited women with incident invasive breast cancer, through population cancer registries and large cancer hospitals in Bogotá, Ibagué and Neiva in central Colombia and Pasto in the south, together with cancer-free controls from the same institutions matched on education, socioeconomic status and local origin. A Mexican arm comprises cases diagnosed from 2010 at the Social Security hospital in Mexico City, with blood-donor controls from the same hospital. The study investigates inherited and environmental causes of breast cancer, and its Colombian and Mexican arms, genotyped on different arrays, are analysed as separate datasets.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34562747+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were siblings or partners of cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11393909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from the Victorian and Queensland Cancer Registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11393909/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included Australian residents diagnosed between 2009 and 2015 with a histologically confirmed RCC (ICD-10 C64) at age 18–74 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CONFIRM Kidney Study (whose scientific title is Consortium for the Investigation of Renal Malignancies) and its Queensland arm, The CARE Study ( C ollaborative Australian Renal Cell Carcinoma Epidemiology), are run by Cancer Council Victoria as part of a consortium including hospitals, universities and research institutions in Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The studies are investigating whether lifestyle choices (such as diet or exercise) and environmental factors (such as exposure to sunlight or certain chemicals) can affect the risk of developing kidney cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28598434") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34562747") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39272843") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20221025011857/https://www.cancervic.org.au/research/epidemiology/cec-programs/confirm.html") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a strong family history of kidney cancer (two or more 1 st or 2 nd degree relatives), OR a confirmed or suspected kidney cancer syndrome") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001607> "A kidney cancer study run by Cancer Council Victoria with QIMR Berghofer, the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries and hospitals and familial cancer clinics across Australia; its Queensland arm is called the CARE Study. Its population-based case–control family component recruited, through the Victorian and Queensland cancer registries, people diagnosed in 2009–2015, at age 18–74, with histologically confirmed renal cell carcinoma, with siblings and partners of cases as controls. The study also enrolled people with a strong family history of kidney cancer or a hereditary kidney cancer syndrome. Participants completed questionnaires on health, lifestyle and family and medical history and gave blood, so that lifestyle, environmental and genetic causes of kidney cancer could be investigated.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4655913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1976, all Danish counties (formerly the main administrative level, replaced by regions in 2007) were requested to submit these data to a central national hospital registry, which formed the basis for the DNPR (Danish, Landspatientregisteret).23 This registry was established in 1977 and achieved complete nationwide coverage in 1978.24") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4655913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It has recorded information on all patients discharged from Danish nonpsychiatric hospitals since 1977 and on psychiatric inpatients and emergency department and outpatient specialty clinic contacts since 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4655913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DNPR provides a data source to identify diseases, examinations, certain in-hospital medical treatments, and surgical procedures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4655913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The availability of patient-identifiable data in the DNPR makes it technically easy to link to other Danish data sources using the CPR number.20") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4655913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim is continuous monitoring of hospital and health services utilization for the Danish Health and Medicines Authority, thus providing a tool for health care planning.26 The registry is also increasingly used to monitor the occurrence of diseases and use of treatments,27 for quality assurance in the hospital sector,28 and for medical research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26604824") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://english.sundhedsdatastyrelsen.dk/health-data-and-registers/national-health-registers") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish Health Data Authority is responsible for the national health registers that contain data related to the health of the entire Danish population and the services of the healthcare system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001608> "A nationwide Danish hospital register, established in 1977 from the hospital discharge records that Denmark's counties were asked to submit and now kept by the Danish Health Data Authority, that records every patient discharged from Danish non-psychiatric hospitals since 1977 and psychiatric inpatients and emergency-department and outpatient specialty-clinic contacts since 1995, with diagnoses, examinations, treatments and surgical procedures. Kept primarily to monitor hospital use for health-care planning, it is also used, through linkage by personal identification number, for disease monitoring, quality assurance and research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5591318/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA extraction and genotyping were performed through 23andMe by the National Genetics Institute, a CLIA-certified clinical laboratory and subsidiary of Laboratory Corporation of America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6961964/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Most, but not all, participants were Duke University students at the time of data collection; the sample includes a small number of students from nearby universities as well.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6961964/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants included a subset of individuals (N = 312) having completed the Duke Neurogenetics Study (DNS), which was designed to identify biomarkers of risk for psychopathology amongst young adult university students.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6838553/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were available from 798 undergraduate students (452 women, age range 18–22 years, mean age = 19.65 years) who successfully completed the Duke Neurogenetics Study (DNS) between January 25th, 2010 and November 12th, 2013 including structural and diffusion magnetic resonance imaging scans, as well as self-reported childhood stress and trait anxiety.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11071117/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from 1,307 university student volunteers (751 women, 19.7 ± 1.3 years of age) who successfully completed the DNS between January 2010 and November 2016 were included in the present analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28887539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31629936") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31677585") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38711811") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11071117/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exclusion criteria did not include history of diagnosis for psychiatric disorders classified by the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fourth Edition (50).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001609> "A study of young adult university students aged 18–22, most of them Duke University undergraduates recruited on campus in Durham, North Carolina, United States, who between 2010 and 2016 completed self-report and behavioural measures and functional and structural brain MRI as part of research in Duke University's Laboratory of NeuroGenetics and were genotyped externally, without excluding people with psychiatric diagnoses, to relate variation in behaviour, brain and genes to risk for psychopathology.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC554111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, in 1989, all men and women aged 60 or above living in Dubbo, a city of approximately 32,000 people 400 km north west of Sydney (Australia), were invited to participate in the DOES.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC554111/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dubbo was selected for the study site because the age and gender distribution of the population closely resembles the Australian population and it is relatively isolated in terms of medical care, so that virtually complete ascertainment of all fractures occurring in the target population is possible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10494511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As there were some differences between the participants recruited before and after 2000,( 25 ) this cohort only included participants recruited from the year 2000 onward (DOES2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10494511/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Every 2–3 years, participants were assessed for medical and lifestyle factors and had a DXA scan performed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10940110/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All fractures were ascertained from the 2 or 3 radiology centres servicing the Dubbo area, and circumstances surrounding fracture were ascertained by personal interview following the fracture event.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15727686") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37701154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38485241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10940110/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, DOES was designed as a prospective, population-based investigation that was operational from 1989 to 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001610> "A prospective population-based study of osteoporosis and fracture that in 1989 invited all men and women aged 60 or over living in Dubbo, New South Wales, Australia, a city chosen because its age and sex structure resembled Australia's and its isolation allowed near-complete ascertainment of fractures, and recruited further participants from 2000. Run by investigators of the Garvan Institute of Medical Research, Sydney, it reassessed participants every two to three years with interviews and bone densitometry and recorded fractures from the area's radiology services until 2020.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10340280+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1990 we initiated a 20 year, partly randomised study (Danish Osteoporosis Prevention Study, DOPS) in order to (a) evaluate clinical, biochemical and osteodensitometric variables as predictors of low bone mass and future osteoporotic fractures,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.e6409") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of these, 1006 were randomly allocated (open label) to receive hormone replacement therapy (n=502) or no treatment (n=504); the remaining 1010 women had a personal choice (of these, 221 opted for hormone replacement therapy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.e6409") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited by direct mailing to a random sample (n=47 720) of women from the general background population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.e6409") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Danish Osteoporosis Prevention Study is a prospective investigator initiated multicentre trial evaluating the effect of hormone replacement therapy as primary prevention of osteoporotic fractures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.e6409") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The analyses were carried out, with 1 august 2002 as the stopping date, about 10 years after randomization (when the randomised treatment was stopped).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10340280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23048011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj.e6409") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The criteria for inclusion in the study were healthy, recently postmenopausal white women aged 45-58, with last menstrual bleeding 3-24 months before study entry or perimenopausal symptoms (including irregular menstruations) in combination with recorded postmenopausal serum follicle stimulating hormone values (>2 standard deviations over the premenopausal mean).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001611> "An investigator-initiated, partly randomised multicentre trial in Denmark that in 1990–1993 enrolled healthy white women aged 45–58 in early menopause, recruited by direct mailing to a random sample of women from the general population, and allocated them, open label, to hormone replacement therapy or no treatment either at random or by their own choice. Planned to run for 20 years, with its randomised treatment stopped in 2002, it was set up to test whether hormone replacement therapy started soon after menopause prevents osteoporotic fractures and to find clinical, biochemical and densitometric predictors of low bone mass and fracture.")

