AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36203093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8755508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of male carriers were ascertained through families attending cancer genetic clinics (96.9%; Supplementary Tables 1 and 2, available online).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001623> "A Danish study at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, that recruits and genetically counsels carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants ascertained through cancer genetics clinics, under approval of the research ethics committees of the Capital Region of Denmark, and contributes them as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (CIMBA) for research on genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34320204") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36203093") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36203093") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9537519/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Department of Clinical Genetics, Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, Copenhagen, Denmark") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001623> "A Danish study at Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital, that recruits and genetically counsels carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 pathogenic variants ascertained through cancer genetics clinics, under approval of the research ethics committees of the Capital Region of Denmark, and contributes them as one study to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (CIMBA) for research on genetic modifiers of cancer risk in carriers.")

