AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34379666") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34379666") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8357137/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Corea (Genetics of COVID-related Manifestation) Data collection and coordination: Kangbuk Samsung Cohort Study (KSCS)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001625> "A South Korean case–control study of host genetic factors in COVID-19, contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative, that compares patients with COVID-19, among them hospitalised patients, with controls, all of Korean ancestry, under the ethics approval of Kangbuk Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Bundang Hospital and Seoul National University Hospital; its data collection was coordinated with the Kangbuk Samsung Cohort Study and its participants were genotyped on the Axiom Asia Precision Medicine Research Array.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5098601/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our previous analyses, based on two GWA studies from the UK (UK1/CORGI) and Scotland (Scotland1/COGS) have identified 10 common variants that are associated with CRC risk 2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5098601/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK4/CORGI2BCD samples comprised additional CRC cases and unaffected spouse/partner controls from the CORGI study collected since the UK1/CORGI samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3785128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All adenoma-only cases (N=503) had a first or second degree relative with CRC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3785128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All recruits had developed CRC at age ≤80, and/or “significant” colorectal adenoma(s) that fulfilled one or more of the following criteria: ≥3 in number; severe dysplasia; villous histology; and presentation at <45 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3785128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CORGI controls were 1,666 spouses/partners of CORGI cases and reported no personal or family history of colorectal tumours.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618284") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3785128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study has recruited through Clinical Genetics Departments from throughout the United Kingdom since 1999 and has to date enrolled 1,698 families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001626> "A UK family study that since 1999 has recruited, through Clinical Genetics Departments throughout the United Kingdom, members of families with colorectal tumours who developed colorectal cancer by age 80 or significant colorectal adenomas (three or more, with severe dysplasia or villous histology, or presenting before age 45; adenoma-only cases having a first- or second-degree relative with colorectal cancer), with their unaffected spouses or partners as controls, to identify genes that predispose to colorectal tumours. Its cases and controls formed the first UK genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer (UK1) and later sample sets.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001627> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001627>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21789208") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24879436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30988369") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21789208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3137628/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the subjects were recruited from the cities of Xi'an/Changsha and their vicinity with the purposes of searching for genetic factors for osteoporosis related phenotypes (such as BMD, BS, bone geometry).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001627> "A genetic study of osteoporosis-related traits in unrelated Han Chinese adults recruited in and around the cities of Xi'an and Changsha, China, whose bone mineral density was measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, set up to identify genes underlying osteoporosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21789208") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24879436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30988369") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21789208") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3137628/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample for the initial genome-wide CNV analysis consisted of 1,627 unrelated Chinese Han adults including 825 women and 802 men.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001627> "A genetic study of osteoporosis-related traits in unrelated Han Chinese adults recruited in and around the cities of Xi'an and Changsha, China, whose bone mineral density was measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, set up to identify genes underlying osteoporosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21789208") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24879436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30988369") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24879436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4039436/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three studies(OOS, KCOS and COS) were originally designed to identify potential genes underlying osteoporosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001627> "A genetic study of osteoporosis-related traits in unrelated Han Chinese adults recruited in and around the cities of Xi'an and Changsha, China, whose bone mineral density was measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry, set up to identify genes underlying osteoporosis.")
