# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9678085/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollees in the CPDR database are military health care beneficiaries who are eligible for TRICARE‐for‐life health care coverage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9678085/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Informed consent was obtained at the time of transrectal ultrasound‐guided biopsy (TRUS) for suspicion of PCa, as described previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10216554/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Demographics, clinical characteristics, pathology information, and all treatment data were obtained from the CPDR multicenter national clinical database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Frozen tissue, blood, and bone marrow samples have been collected from prostate cancer patients under institutional review boardapproved protocols at Walter Reed Army Medical Center since 1993 and at other sites more recently.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences (USUHS), Bethesda, Maryland, was designated to provide for the establishment and administration of the Center for Prostate Disease Research (CPDR) as authorized in public law no. 102-172.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35616266") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35638719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36743401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37239075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://medschool.usuhs.edu/sur/research/center-for-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/department-defense-center-prostate-disease-research") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The triservice Multicenter Prostate Cancer Longitudinal Database, which began as a prospective data collection system at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, has now expanded to 11 other locations and also includes retrospective data collection back to 1980.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001629> "A longitudinal clinical research database of military health care beneficiaries who consent to enrolment, typically at prostate biopsy for suspected prostate cancer, at United States military treatment facilities (Walter Reed and other Army, Navy and Air Force medical centres, now with one civilian centre), run by the Department of Defense Center for Prostate Disease Research of the Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences, which records their demographic, clinical, pathology, treatment, quality-of-life and outcome data. It began as prospective data collection at Walter Reed Army Medical Center in January 1994, with retrospective data back to 1980, and is linked to a biospecimen bank of blood and tissue collected at Walter Reed since 1993.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23668689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3132306/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5669824/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23668689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4053164/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The California Pacific Medical Center Breast Health Cohort is linked to the San Francisco Mammography Registry, part of the NCI Breast Cancer Surveillance Consortium that collects demographic and risk factor data on women receiving mammography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630> "A cohort of women having screening mammography at the Breast Health Center of California Pacific Medical Center in San Francisco, California, United States, an imaging facility of the San Francisco Mammography Registry (part of the NCI Breast Cancer Surveillance Consortium), who completed the registry's demographic and risk-factor questionnaire and, from 2004 to 2011, were asked to give blood for research and consent to genotyping; breast cancers are ascertained by linkage to the California Cancer Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23668689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3132306/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5669824/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5033764/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All women presenting for mammography completed a questionnaire with demographic information and risk factor data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630> "A cohort of women having screening mammography at the Breast Health Center of California Pacific Medical Center in San Francisco, California, United States, an imaging facility of the San Francisco Mammography Registry (part of the NCI Breast Cancer Surveillance Consortium), who completed the registry's demographic and risk-factor questionnaire and, from 2004 to 2011, were asked to give blood for research and consent to genotyping; breast cancers are ascertained by linkage to the California Cancer Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23668689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3132306/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5669824/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5033764/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnosis of breast cancer was ascertained by linkage to the California Cancer Registry (CCR), with last linkage on October 31, 2013; women without breast cancer at this time were considered controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630> "A cohort of women having screening mammography at the Breast Health Center of California Pacific Medical Center in San Francisco, California, United States, an imaging facility of the San Francisco Mammography Registry (part of the NCI Breast Cancer Surveillance Consortium), who completed the registry's demographic and risk-factor questionnaire and, from 2004 to 2011, were asked to give blood for research and consent to genotyping; breast cancers are ascertained by linkage to the California Cancer Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23668689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3132306/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5669824/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27565998") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5033764/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2004-2011, women were also asked to provide blood samples for research and written informed consent to undergo genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001630> "A cohort of women having screening mammography at the Breast Health Center of California Pacific Medical Center in San Francisco, California, United States, an imaging facility of the San Francisco Mammography Registry (part of the NCI Breast Cancer Surveillance Consortium), who completed the registry's demographic and risk-factor questionnaire and, from 2004 to 2011, were asked to give blood for research and consent to genotyping; breast cancers are ascertained by linkage to the California Cancer Registry.")
