AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21799935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38966335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3440341/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DHCS is still ongoing, thus consecutively enrolling new HIV-infected individuals and immigrants with HIV infection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001665> "A nationwide, prospective, population-based cohort of all people with HIV aged 16 or older treated at Denmark's specialised HIV centres since 1 January 1995, which keeps enrolling newly diagnosed people and immigrants with HIV and records demographic, clinical and laboratory data on their infection and care, linkable to the Danish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21799935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38966335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3440341/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DHCS, which has been described in detail elsewhere [27], is a nationwide, prospective, population-based cohort study of all Danish HIV-infected individuals treated in one of the above mentioned centers since 1 January 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001665> "A nationwide, prospective, population-based cohort of all people with HIV aged 16 or older treated at Denmark's specialised HIV centres since 1 January 1995, which keeps enrolling newly diagnosed people and immigrants with HIV and records demographic, clinical and laboratory data on their infection and care, linkable to the Danish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21799935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38966335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3440341/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the unique 10-digit civil registration number assigned to all individuals in Denmark at birth or upon immigration to link data from the following registers:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001665> "A nationwide, prospective, population-based cohort of all people with HIV aged 16 or older treated at Denmark's specialised HIV centres since 1 January 1995, which keeps enrolling newly diagnosed people and immigrants with HIV and records demographic, clinical and laboratory data on their infection and care, linkable to the Danish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21799935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22984529") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38966335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38966335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11223088/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DHCS is a complete record of all PWH 16 years of age and older receiving care at one of the eight HIV centres in Denmark since January 1, 19954 and includes data regarding demographics as well as other information related to HIV infection and care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001665> "A nationwide, prospective, population-based cohort of all people with HIV aged 16 or older treated at Denmark's specialised HIV centres since 1 January 1995, which keeps enrolling newly diagnosed people and immigrants with HIV and records demographic, clinical and laboratory data on their infection and care, linkable to the Danish national registers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001666> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001666>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21775348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38654257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41835011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21775348") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21775348+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It includes information about citizens, providers, and health services but minimal clinical information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001666> "A national administrative register of the services provided under Denmark's public health insurance by the contractors of primary health care (general practitioners, practising specialists, dentists, physiotherapists, psychologists and others), which covers everyone living in Denmark with data from 1990 and records the citizen, the provider and the service but little clinical information; collected for administrative and research purposes, it is linked by personal identification number to the other national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21775348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38654257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41835011") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21775348") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21775348+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The register contains data collected for administrative and scientific purposes from health contractors in primary health care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001666> "A national administrative register of the services provided under Denmark's public health insurance by the contractors of primary health care (general practitioners, practising specialists, dentists, physiotherapists, psychologists and others), which covers everyone living in Denmark with data from 1990 and records the citizen, the provider and the service but little clinical information; collected for administrative and research purposes, it is linked by personal identification number to the other national registers.")
