AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The (non-overlapping) population-based series has been recruited in 2009. Patients were identified through the population-based regional cancer registry held by the Comprehensive Cancer Centre East, Nijmegen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001673> "A case–control study of renal cell carcinoma in the region of Nijmegen, the Netherlands, run by Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre with the Comprehensive Cancer Centre East, whose cases of European descent form a hospital-based series (patients of the hospital's outpatient urology clinic who had given blood and lifestyle data from 1999 onwards for studies of gene–environment interactions in urological disease and were found through the cancer registry to have renal cell carcinoma) and a population-based series recruited in 2009 through the regional cancer registry (patients diagnosed in 1995–2008 before the age of 75). Its controls are participants of the population-based Nijmegen Biomedical Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21131975") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.723/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng723_MOESM3_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch RCC series (N=748) consists of a population-based series (N=417) and a hospital-based series (N=331)50 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001673> "A case–control study of renal cell carcinoma in the region of Nijmegen, the Netherlands, run by Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre with the Comprehensive Cancer Centre East, whose cases of European descent form a hospital-based series (patients of the hospital's outpatient urology clinic who had given blood and lifestyle data from 1999 onwards for studies of gene–environment interactions in urological disease and were found through the cancer registry to have renal cell carcinoma) and a population-based series recruited in 2009 through the regional cancer registry (patients diagnosed in 1995–2008 before the age of 75). Its controls are participants of the population-based Nijmegen Biomedical Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11198615/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the current study, adult heterozygous carriers of a HeFH variant and free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (defined as stroke and/or coronary artery disease) at time of enrollment, and who provided written informed consent for additional genetic analysis and linkage of health records, were included (n = 1,343) (Supplemental Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> "A prospective cohort drawn from the Dutch national cascade-screening programme for heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, which enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013: adult carriers of a heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia variant free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at enrolment who consented to genetic analysis and linkage of their health records, together with relatives from the same families confirmed as non-carriers and matched to them by age and sex, followed for incident coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11198615/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to compare CAD risk in HeFH variant carriers to noncarriers, a control group consisting of relatives confirmed to be noncarriers and derived from the same families as the carriers, was matched based on age and sex in a 1:1 ratio.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> "A prospective cohort drawn from the Dutch national cascade-screening programme for heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, which enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013: adult carriers of a heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia variant free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at enrolment who consented to genetic analysis and linkage of their health records, together with relatives from the same families confirmed as non-carriers and matched to them by age and sex, followed for incident coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11198615/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Its association with incident CAD was assessed over a median follow-up time of 10.2 and 10.9 years in the Dutch HeFH Cohort and UK Biobank, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> "A prospective cohort drawn from the Dutch national cascade-screening programme for heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, which enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013: adult carriers of a heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia variant free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at enrolment who consented to genetic analysis and linkage of their health records, together with relatives from the same families confirmed as non-carriers and matched to them by age and sex, followed for incident coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11198615/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch National HeFH cascade-screening program enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> "A prospective cohort drawn from the Dutch national cascade-screening programme for heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, which enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013: adult carriers of a heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia variant free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at enrolment who consented to genetic analysis and linkage of their health records, together with relatives from the same families confirmed as non-carriers and matched to them by age and sex, followed for incident coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38938725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11198615/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed data from a prospective cohort study of 1,315 individuals who carried a HeFH variant and 1,315 matched family noncarriers derived from a nationwide screening program in the Netherlands, with subsequent replication in 151,009 participants of the UK Biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001674> "A prospective cohort drawn from the Dutch national cascade-screening programme for heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, which enrolled participants between 1994 and 2013: adult carriers of a heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia variant free of atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease at enrolment who consented to genetic analysis and linkage of their health records, together with relatives from the same families confirmed as non-carriers and matched to them by age and sex, followed for incident coronary artery disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3086278/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These height case-control samples have been described previously12.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3086278/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a collection of 3,207 adults sampled from the near-extremes of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and 90th to 95th percentiles; Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20881960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects gave informed consent, and approval was obtained from the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20881960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects in the Polish panel were born in Poland, and all grandparents were born in Europe or Russia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20881960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For additional validation, we genotyped randomly chosen SNPs representing 33 of the 207 associated loci in an independent samples of 2,181 European-American and 1,009 Polish subjects from the tails of the height distribution (5-10th and 90-95th percentile).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17767157") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20881960") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09410/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09410_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For both panels, all individuals were self-described \"white\" or \"Caucasian.\" For the US panel, all subjects were born in the US, and all of their grandparents were born in either the US or Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001675> "Two case-control panels of self-described white adults sampled from the tails of the height distribution (the 5th to 10th and the 90th to 95th percentiles), one of European Americans born in the United States and one of people born in Poland, studied under the approval of the Institutional Review Board of Children's Hospital, Boston, and genotyped to validate variants associated with adult height.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1917239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Arterial disease was assessed in 1592 participants by means of the WHO questionnaire on intermittent claudication and measurement of the ankle brachial systolic pressure index (ABPI) and change in ankle systolic pressure during reactive hyperaemia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> "A study of peripheral arterial disease in the general population of Edinburgh, Scotland, based on an age-stratified sample of 1,592 men and women aged 55 to 74 selected from the age-sex registers of ten general practices in the city and assessed by questionnaire and ankle brachial pressure index, funded by the British Heart Foundation and genotyped for genetic studies such as the DIAGRAM consortium’s meta-analysis of type 2 diabetes and the UCLEB consortium’s Mendelian randomisation analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1917239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this paper is to describe the prevalence of both asymptomatic and symptomatic disease and relation to ischaemic heart disease in the Edinburgh Artery Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> "A study of peripheral arterial disease in the general population of Edinburgh, Scotland, based on an age-stratified sample of 1,592 men and women aged 55 to 74 selected from the age-sex registers of ten general practices in the city and assessed by questionnaire and ankle brachial pressure index, funded by the British Heart Foundation and genotyped for genetic studies such as the DIAGRAM consortium’s meta-analysis of type 2 diabetes and the UCLEB consortium’s Mendelian randomisation analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2383/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2383_MOESM31_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EAS was funded by the British Heart Foundation (RG/98002).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> "A study of peripheral arterial disease in the general population of Edinburgh, Scotland, based on an age-stratified sample of 1,592 men and women aged 55 to 74 selected from the age-sex registers of ten general practices in the city and assessed by questionnaire and ankle brachial pressure index, funded by the British Heart Foundation and genotyped for genetic studies such as the DIAGRAM consortium’s meta-analysis of type 2 diabetes and the UCLEB consortium’s Mendelian randomisation analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5841831/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EAS is funded by the British Heart Foundation (Programme Grant RG/98002), with Metabochip genotyping funded by a project grant from the Chief Scientist Office of Scotland (Project Grant CZB/4/672).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> "A study of peripheral arterial disease in the general population of Edinburgh, Scotland, based on an age-stratified sample of 1,592 men and women aged 55 to 74 selected from the age-sex registers of ten general practices in the city and assessed by questionnaire and ankle brachial pressure index, funded by the British Heart Foundation and genotyped for genetic studies such as the DIAGRAM consortium’s meta-analysis of type 2 diabetes and the UCLEB consortium’s Mendelian randomisation analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1917239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22885922") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25979724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5841831/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Edinburgh Artery Study (EAS) is an age-stratified random sample of men and women, aged 55-74 years, which was selected between August 1987 and September 1988 from the age-sex registers of ten general practices with a geographical and socio-economical catchment population spread throughout the city of Edinburgh, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001677> "A study of peripheral arterial disease in the general population of Edinburgh, Scotland, based on an age-stratified sample of 1,592 men and women aged 55 to 74 selected from the age-sex registers of ten general practices in the city and assessed by questionnaire and ankle brachial pressure index, funded by the British Heart Foundation and genotyped for genetic studies such as the DIAGRAM consortium’s meta-analysis of type 2 diabetes and the UCLEB consortium’s Mendelian randomisation analyses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3274508") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Generic control subjects were selected on the basis of country of the case patient recruitment from several previously published genome-wide association studies of other cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3274508/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide genotyping of cHL case patient samples was performed using the Illumina Infinium Human660-Quad BeadChip (Illumina Inc, San Diego, CA) at the Centre National de Génotypage (Evry, France; http://www.cng.fr/), as described previously (22).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3274508/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These studies included the Alcohol Related Cancers and Genetic Susceptibility in Europe Study (15); the International Agency for Research on Cancer Central Europe Study (16); the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium (17); the Nijmegen Biomedical Study (18); the Nord-Trøndelag Health Study and Tromsø IV Studies (19,20); and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium (21).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4055950/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Collaborative Study, presented elsewhere, included 1,241 HL cases aged 13–80 (median age = 33 years) from five European-based HL studies and 5,726 generic controls aged 17–94 (mean age = 62) used in the initial GWAS scan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4055950/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery meta-analysis was undertaken by 2 centers (IARC and USC) and was based on summary data from 3 previously reported GWAS providing genotype data on 1,816 HL cases and 7,877 controls of European descent: The European Collaborative GWAS, and the University of Southern California (USC)/University of Chicago (UC) GWAS studies, which were combined for a single meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4055950/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The distribution of cases among the five European-based HL studies is: the EPILYMPH Study (N = 196), the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group and the Young Adult Hodgkin’s Disease Case–Control Study (N = 397), the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study (SCALE) (N = 344), and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study (N = 304).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001678> "A European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma that genotyped, at the Centre National de Génotypage in France, cases from five European Hodgkin lymphoma studies (the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin's Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study) and compared them with generic controls chosen by country from earlier genome-wide association studies of other cancers in populations of European ancestry, among them ARCAGE, the IARC Central Europe Study, the Pancreatic Cancer Cohort Consortium, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and the Wellcome Trust Case–Control Consortium. It was the European discovery sample of the 2014 Hodgkin lymphoma GWAS meta-analysis with the University of Southern California and University of Chicago GWAS.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11040019+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ECTIM (étude cas-temoin de l'infarctus myocarde) extension study was established to determine whether a previously implicated polymorphism of the P-selectin gene was associated with myocardial infarction risk in men and women in Belfast and Glasgow.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1534257+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male patients aged 25-64 years with myocardial infarction (MI) and control subjects sampled from the general population were recruited in the four centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1534257+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ECTIM study, which is based on WHO MONICA centers in Belfast (Northern Ireland), Strasbourg (eastern France), Toulouse (southwestern France), and Lille (northern France), has been established to investigate this striking difference.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1534257+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The incidence of coronary heart disease (CHD) in middle-aged men is more than three times higher in Northern Ireland than in France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7789377+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the ECTIM Study, the medical treatment given to male patients (25-64 years) 3 to 9 months after myocardial infarction (MI) were analysed in France and Northern Ireland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11040019") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12081984") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1534257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7789377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8633596") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8633596+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The effect of alcohol consumption was assessed in 561 men with myocardial infarction and 643 healthy controls recruited from France and Northern Ireland between 1988 and 1991 in the ECTIM Study (Enquête Cas-Témoins de I'Infarctus du Myocarde).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001679> "A multicentre case-control study of myocardial infarction based on the WHO MONICA centres of Belfast (Northern Ireland) and Lille, Strasbourg and Toulouse (France), set up to investigate why coronary heart disease is more than three times as common in middle-aged men in Northern Ireland as in France. Between 1988 and 1991 it recruited men aged 25–64 who had had a myocardial infarction, examined 3 to 9 months after the event, and control men sampled from the general population. Its cases and controls have been used in many candidate-gene studies of myocardial infarction and lipids, and an extension study later recruited men and women in the MONICA areas of Belfast and Glasgow.")

