AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28213371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24425039+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A cohort of Caribbean Hispanics with familial LOAD was recruited in a different study at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer's Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic as part of the EFIGA study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683> "A family study of Caribbean Hispanics from families multiply affected by late-onset Alzheimer's disease, recruited at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer's Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic, with follow-up of unaffected family members, to study the genetics of familial late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28213371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4000602/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since then, large multiplex families with multiple individuals at risk of LOAD have been recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683> "A family study of Caribbean Hispanics from families multiply affected by late-onset Alzheimer's disease, recruited at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer's Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic, with follow-up of unaffected family members, to study the genetics of familial late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28213371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4000602/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, we estimated the annual incidence rates of LOAD in previously unaffected individuals in the NIA-LOAD/NCRAD and EFIGA families and assessed the effects of demographic variables, such as age at onset, sex, and APOE genotype, on those rates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683> "A family study of Caribbean Hispanics from families multiply affected by late-onset Alzheimer's disease, recruited at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer's Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic, with follow-up of unaffected family members, to study the genetics of familial late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28213371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24425039") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4000602/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To study the underlying genetic architecture of LOAD in Caribbean Hispanics, the Estudio Familiar de Influencia Geneticaen Alzheimer(EFIGA)was initiated, and recruitment began in 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001683> "A family study of Caribbean Hispanics from families multiply affected by late-onset Alzheimer's disease, recruited at the Taub Institute for Research on Alzheimer's Disease and the Aging Brain in New York and from clinics in the Dominican Republic, with follow-up of unaffected family members, to study the genetics of familial late-onset Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ars.els-cdn.com/content/image/1-s2.0-S0140673610619964-mmc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Emory Genebank Study (Atlanta, Georgia, USA): Study participants were enrolled at the Emory University Hospital, Crawford Long Hospital, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital, all in Atlanta, Georgia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were enrolled at the Emory University Hospital, Emory University Hospital Midtown, Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with no evidence of coronary artery disease on cardiac catheterization and no prior history of MI or CAD were defined as controls (n=146).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with ≥ 50% stenosis in one or more coronary arteries or with prior history of MI, CABG or percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) were defined as cases (n=321).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21239051") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21270820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079521/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Emory Genebank Study was designed to investigate the relationship between biochemical and genetic factors with CAD in subjects undergoing cardiac catheterization.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001684> "A study of patients undergoing cardiac catheterization at Emory University hospitals, the Emory Clinic and Grady Memorial Hospital in Atlanta, Georgia, United States, designed to investigate the relationship of biochemical and genetic factors with coronary artery disease; patients with angiographic coronary artery disease or a history of myocardial infarction or coronary revascularisation serve as cases and those without coronary artery disease on catheterization as controls in genetic studies.")

