AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20081857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on WHO oral glucose tolerance testing criteria, participants were confirmed as controls (n = 1,606) or classified as cases (n = 91).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001686> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in the United Kingdom whose cases had previously undiagnosed type 2 diabetes, defined by World Health Organization oral glucose tolerance test criteria, found by population-based stepwise screening of 40- to 69-year-olds in the UK Cambridge arm of the ADDITION study or by oral glucose tolerance testing in the MRC Ely Study, and whose controls were participants of the MRC Ely Study, a population-based cohort of white European adults without diagnosed diabetes from a similar sampling frame as the cases, confirmed free of diabetes by oral glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20081857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were identified from the Medical Research Council (MRC) Ely study, a population-based cohort of white European men and women aged 35 to 79 y without diagnosed diabetes and from a similar sampling frame as the cases [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001686> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in the United Kingdom whose cases had previously undiagnosed type 2 diabetes, defined by World Health Organization oral glucose tolerance test criteria, found by population-based stepwise screening of 40- to 69-year-olds in the UK Cambridge arm of the ADDITION study or by oral glucose tolerance testing in the MRC Ely Study, and whose controls were participants of the MRC Ely Study, a population-based cohort of white European adults without diagnosed diabetes from a similar sampling frame as the cases, confirmed free of diabetes by oral glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20081857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Previously undiagnosed prevalent cases of T2D, defined using World Health Organization oral glucose tolerance testing criteria, were identified via a population-based stepwise screening strategy among 40- to 69-y olds participating in the UK Cambridge arm of the ADDITION study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001686> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in the United Kingdom whose cases had previously undiagnosed type 2 diabetes, defined by World Health Organization oral glucose tolerance test criteria, found by population-based stepwise screening of 40- to 69-year-olds in the UK Cambridge arm of the ADDITION study or by oral glucose tolerance testing in the MRC Ely Study, and whose controls were participants of the MRC Ely Study, a population-based cohort of white European adults without diagnosed diabetes from a similar sampling frame as the cases, confirmed free of diabetes by oral glucose tolerance test.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18372903") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20081857") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used three T2D case-control studies (Cambridgeshire, ADDITION-Ely, and Norfolk Diabetes) and the population-based EPIC-Norfolk cohort for genetic analysis, and the EPIC-Norfolk cohort for blood-based analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001686> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in the United Kingdom whose cases had previously undiagnosed type 2 diabetes, defined by World Health Organization oral glucose tolerance test criteria, found by population-based stepwise screening of 40- to 69-year-olds in the UK Cambridge arm of the ADDITION study or by oral glucose tolerance testing in the MRC Ely Study, and whose controls were participants of the MRC Ely Study, a population-based cohort of white European adults without diagnosed diabetes from a similar sampling frame as the cases, confirmed free of diabetes by oral glucose tolerance test.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18328041+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EMAS will provide new population-based data concerning the main features that characterize ageing in men and its critical determinants, particularly with reference to age-related changes in hormone levels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18328041+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men aged 40-79 years were recruited from eight European centres: Florence (Italy), Leuven (Belgium), Lodz (Poland), Malmö (Sweden), Manchester (UK), Santiago de Compostela (Spain), Szeged (Hungary) and Tartu (Estonia).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18328041+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects were recruited from population registers and those who agreed to take part completed a detailed questionnaire including aspects of personal and medical history, lifestyle factors and sexual function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18328041+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Male Ageing Study (EMAS) is a multicentre prospective cohort designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men, including their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18328041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18653627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18653627+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each centre recruited an age-stratified sample of men aged 40-79 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001687> "A multicentre prospective population-based cohort of men aged 40–79 years recruited from population registers in eight European centres (Florence, Leuven, Lodz, Malmö, Manchester, Santiago de Compostela, Szeged and Tartu) with an age-stratified sample at each centre, who completed a detailed questionnaire on personal and medical history, lifestyle and sexual function, designed to examine the prevalence, incidence and geographical distribution of gender-specific and general symptoms of ageing in men and their endocrine, genetic and psychosocial predictors, particularly age-related changes in hormone levels.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6033314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals are eligible for inclusion in EMBRACE if they (i) carry a pathogenic mutation in BRCA1 or BRCA2, (ii) are noncarriers in families with a pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation, or (iii) are potential carriers but opt not to undergo a predictive genetic test.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688> "A prospective cohort study in the United Kingdom and the Republic of Ireland, coordinated in Cambridge, of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, non-carrier relatives from carrier families and untested potential carriers, recruited through regional cancer genetics centres around the time of genetic testing, to characterise cancer risks in BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers and their relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6033314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment is organized through regional cancer genetics centers, generally close to the time of genetic testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688> "A prospective cohort study in the United Kingdom and the Republic of Ireland, coordinated in Cambridge, of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, non-carrier relatives from carrier families and untested potential carriers, recruited through regional cancer genetics centres around the time of genetic testing, to characterise cancer risks in BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers and their relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6033314/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiological Study of Familial Breast Cancer (EMBRACE) study is a prospective cohort study in the United Kingdom and Republic of Ireland, aiming to characterize cancer risks in BRCA1/BRCA2 mutation carriers and their relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688> "A prospective cohort study in the United Kingdom and the Republic of Ireland, coordinated in Cambridge, of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, non-carrier relatives from carrier families and untested potential carriers, recruited through regional cancer genetics centres around the time of genetic testing, to characterise cancer risks in BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers and their relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23544012") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29565421") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4661791/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Coordinating Centre, Cambridge:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001688> "A prospective cohort study in the United Kingdom and the Republic of Ireland, coordinated in Cambridge, of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, non-carrier relatives from carrier families and untested potential carriers, recruited through regional cancer genetics centres around the time of genetic testing, to characterise cancer risks in BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers and their relatives.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2760125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all, 822 cases (397 NHL, 149 LH, 168 SLP and 108 MM) and 752 controls were included and described 5481 and 5188 first degree relatives, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> "A French multicentre hospital-based case-control study of lymphoid neoplasms (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Hodgkin lymphoma, lymphoproliferative syndromes and multiple myeloma), conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004, whose cases were recently diagnosed patients aged 18 to 75 living in each hospital's catchment area and whose controls were patients of the same hospitals, mainly from orthopaedic and rheumatology departments, to study environmental, infectious and genetic risk factors for these neoplasms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2760125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lymphoid neoplasm (LN), including Hodgkin’s lymphoma (HL), non-Hodgkin’s lymphoma (NHL), multiple myeloma (MM) and lymphoproliferative syndromes (LPS) are among the most common cancers in France after smoking-related cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> "A French multicentre hospital-based case-control study of lymphoid neoplasms (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Hodgkin lymphoma, lymphoproliferative syndromes and multiple myeloma), conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004, whose cases were recently diagnosed patients aged 18 to 75 living in each hospital's catchment area and whose controls were patients of the same hospitals, mainly from orthopaedic and rheumatology departments, to study environmental, infectious and genetic risk factors for these neoplasms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2760125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ENGELA study is a French multicenter hospital-based case-control study that was conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004 in order to investigate for environmental, infectious and genetics risk factors for LN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> "A French multicentre hospital-based case-control study of lymphoid neoplasms (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Hodgkin lymphoma, lymphoproliferative syndromes and multiple myeloma), conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004, whose cases were recently diagnosed patients aged 18 to 75 living in each hospital's catchment area and whose controls were patients of the same hospitals, mainly from orthopaedic and rheumatology departments, to study environmental, infectious and genetic risk factors for these neoplasms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2760125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were patients with no prior history of LN, recruited in the same hospital as the cases, mainly in orthopaedic and rheumatologic departments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> "A French multicentre hospital-based case-control study of lymphoid neoplasms (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Hodgkin lymphoma, lymphoproliferative syndromes and multiple myeloma), conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004, whose cases were recently diagnosed patients aged 18 to 75 living in each hospital's catchment area and whose controls were patients of the same hospitals, mainly from orthopaedic and rheumatology departments, to study environmental, infectious and genetic risk factors for these neoplasms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19058175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2760125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The eligible cases were subjects aged between 18 and 75 years old, recently diagnosed with LN, and residing in the catchment area of each hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001689> "A French multicentre hospital-based case-control study of lymphoid neoplasms (non-Hodgkin lymphoma, Hodgkin lymphoma, lymphoproliferative syndromes and multiple myeloma), conducted in the main hospitals of Bordeaux, Brest, Caen, Nantes, Lille and Toulouse from September 2000 to December 2004, whose cases were recently diagnosed patients aged 18 to 75 living in each hospital's catchment area and whose controls were patients of the same hospitals, mainly from orthopaedic and rheumatology departments, to study environmental, infectious and genetic risk factors for these neoplasms.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001690> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001690>)

