AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MCCS- RFPCS- EOPCFS Melbourne, Australia") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001690> "A population-based study of early-onset prostate cancer run by Cancer Council Victoria in Melbourne, Australia, whose participants are men diagnosed with prostate cancer before the age of 56, ascertained through the Victorian Cancer Registry.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12668699+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were randomly assigned to eplerenone (25 mg per day initially, titrated to a maximum of 50 mg per day; 3319 patients) or placebo (3313 patients) [correction] in addition to optimal medical therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, added to optimal medical therapy in patients enrolled 3 to 14 days after an acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (ejection fraction of 40% or less) and heart failure or diabetes, followed for death and cardiovascular hospitalisation; a biomarker substudy of its patients has serial blood measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12668699+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end points were death from any cause and death from cardiovascular causes or hospitalization for heart failure, acute myocardial infarction, stroke, or ventricular arrhythmia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, added to optimal medical therapy in patients enrolled 3 to 14 days after an acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (ejection fraction of 40% or less) and heart failure or diabetes, followed for death and cardiovascular hospitalisation; a biomarker substudy of its patients has serial blood measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12668699+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a double-blind, placebo-controlled study evaluating the effect of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, on morbidity and mortality among patients with acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction and heart failure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, added to optimal medical therapy in patients enrolled 3 to 14 days after an acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (ejection fraction of 40% or less) and heart failure or diabetes, followed for death and cardiovascular hospitalisation; a biomarker substudy of its patients has serial blood measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00392-019-01500-3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the biomarker substudy of EPHESUS, circulating plasmatic biomarker determinations were performed in 476 patients at randomization (i.e., 3 to 14 days after MI diagnosis), and months 1, 3, 6 and 9.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, added to optimal medical therapy in patients enrolled 3 to 14 days after an acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (ejection fraction of 40% or less) and heart failure or diabetes, followed for death and cardiovascular hospitalisation; a biomarker substudy of its patients has serial blood measurements.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12668699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31250134") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31482613") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6837025/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPHESUS included 6632 patients with an acute MI (3‐14 days after the MI), and a LVEF ≤ 40% plus HF or diabetes to receive either eplerenone (25 mg per day initially, titrated to a maximum of 50 mg per day) or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001691> "A double-blind, placebo-controlled randomised trial of eplerenone, a selective aldosterone blocker, added to optimal medical therapy in patients enrolled 3 to 14 days after an acute myocardial infarction complicated by left ventricular dysfunction (ejection fraction of 40% or less) and heart failure or diabetes, followed for death and cardiovascular hospitalisation; a biomarker substudy of its patients has serial blood measurements.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10807638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case identification was made in all private and public cancer centers in the department of Hérault.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in the Hérault département in the south of France, whose cases are men under 75 newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in 2012-2013 while living in Hérault, identified in all of its public and private cancer centres, and whose controls are men without prostate cancer randomly selected from Hérault's general population with quotas on age and socioeconomic status, set up to study environmental and genetic risk factors for prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10807638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected from the general population in the department of Hérault that were not diagnosed with prostate cancer and living in the same department at the time of inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in the Hérault département in the south of France, whose cases are men under 75 newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in 2012-2013 while living in Hérault, identified in all of its public and private cancer centres, and whose controls are men without prostate cancer randomly selected from Hérault's general population with quotas on age and socioeconomic status, set up to study environmental and genetic risk factors for prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10807638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EPICAP (Epidemiological study of prostate cancer) is a population‐based case–control study conducted in the department of Hérault located in the south of France between 2012 and 2014 to investigate the role of environmental and genetic factors in the occurrence of prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in the Hérault département in the south of France, whose cases are men under 75 newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in 2012-2013 while living in Hérault, identified in all of its public and private cancer centres, and whose controls are men without prostate cancer randomly selected from Hérault's general population with quotas on age and socioeconomic status, set up to study environmental and genetic risk factors for prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10807638/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer between 2012 and 2013 who were under the age of 75 and living in the department of Hérault at the time of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in the Hérault département in the south of France, whose cases are men under 75 newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in 2012-2013 while living in Hérault, identified in all of its public and private cancer centres, and whose controls are men without prostate cancer randomly selected from Hérault's general population with quotas on age and socioeconomic status, set up to study environmental and genetic risk factors for prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38174802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3936778/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls are selected from the general population in the département of Hérault, using quotas defined for age and socioeconomic status (SES).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001692> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in the Hérault département in the south of France, whose cases are men under 75 newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in 2012-2013 while living in Hérault, identified in all of its public and private cancer centres, and whose controls are men without prostate cancer randomly selected from Hérault's general population with quotas on age and socioeconomic status, set up to study environmental and genetic risk factors for prostate cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001693> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001693>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19079261") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2669167/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each GWA study performed linear regression (additive model) to test for association between each SNP and BMI Z score using PLINK (WTCCC-T2D, WTCCC-UKBS, WTCCC-CAD, CoLauS), SAS/Genetics 9.1 (EPIC-Obesity Study), STATA 8.1 (British 1958 BC) or R (WTCCC-HT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001693> "A representative sample of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort (men and women of European descent aged 39 to 79, recruited in Norfolk, United Kingdom, in 1993-1997), genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of body mass index and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19079261") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2669167/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotypes were called using the CHIAMO genotype calling software for all studies, apart from the EPIC-Obesity and CoLauS studies, for which the BRLMM algorithm was used.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001693> "A representative sample of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort (men and women of European descent aged 39 to 79, recruited in Norfolk, United Kingdom, in 1993-1997), genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of body mass index and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19079261") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2669167/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPIC Obesity study comprises a representative sample (n = 2,566) nested within the EPIC-Norfolk Study, a population-based cohort study of 25,663 men and women of European descent aged 39–79 y recruited in Norfolk, UK between 1993 and 1997.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001693> "A representative sample of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort (men and women of European descent aged 39 to 79, recruited in Norfolk, United Kingdom, in 1993-1997), genotyped genome-wide for genetic association studies of body mass index and obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20638935+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The replication set was an independent, prospective, multicenter Spanish cohort (EPICOLON II) of 895 patients with newly diagnosed CRC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It recruited consecutive, unselected, population-based colorectal cancer (CRC) cases and control subjects matched by age and gender without personal or familial history of cancer all over Spain with the main goal of gaining knowledge in Lynch syndrome and familial CRC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPICOLON consortium was initiated in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterology Association.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22294762+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This epidemiological, prospective and multicentre study collected extensive clinical data and biological samples from ∼2000 CRC cases and 2000 controls in Phases 1 and 2 involving 25 and 14 participating hospitals, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hospital-based controls were recruited through the blood collection unit of each hospital, together with cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20638935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22294762") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EPICOLON Consortium comprises a prospective, multicentre and population-based epidemiology survey of the incidence and features of CRC in the Spanish population23 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001694> "A prospective, multicentre, population-based study of colorectal cancer across Spain, started in 1999 by the Gastrointestinal Oncology Group of the Spanish Gastroenterological Association, which in two phases (EPICOLON I in 25 hospitals and EPICOLON II in 14) recruited consecutive unselected patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer and hospital controls matched by age and sex with no personal or family history of cancer, mainly to study Lynch syndrome and familial colorectal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2631192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants aged between 25 and 65 years were contacted via the registers of three primary care practices located in socio-economically diverse areas of North-West England.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2631192/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects free of CWP at baseline were followed up 15 months later, when pain status, threatening life events and HRQoL (SF-12) were assessed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.3899/jrheum.080541") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were followed up twice by further postal questionnaires at 15 months and 4 years from baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.3899/jrheum.080541") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a 4-year prospective population-based study of pain in the North-West of England known as the Epidemiology of Functional Disorders (Epifund) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2927682/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pain and psychological data was collected at three time points over a 4-year period via a postal survey as part of a prospective population-based cohort study, EPIFUND (for ‘Epidemiology of Functional Disorders’).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19059720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19369469") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19723618") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20400346") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22956598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3691951/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stage 2b studies (CHINGFORD, EPIFUND and HCS) performed de novo genotyping, using both Sequenom iPLEX and TaqMan-based assays (supplementary methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001695> "A prospective population-based study of pain in North West England, in which adults aged 25 to 65 years recruited from the registers of three general practices in socio-economically diverse areas answered postal questionnaires on pain and psychological factors at baseline and were followed up at about 15 months and 4 years; it has been used to study the onset, persistence and genetics of chronic widespread pain.")

