AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2901865/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our analysis sample of 721 AJ SZ probands and 720 AJ controls was collected by the Johns Hopkins Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry (http://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/epigen/), and has been described in detail elsewhere.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4363491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases and controls were ascertained reporting four grandparents of known AJ descent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4363491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Screened controls were recruited over a four-year period (2003–2007) at Jewish community professional meetings, community centers and synagogues.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4363491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 1996, recruitment has focused on Ashkenazi Jewish (AJ) individuals in the U.S affected with SZ or BP, their families and screened controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4363491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects included research participants with a diagnosis of SZ (including schizoaffective) or BP diagnosis recruited over a 15-year period (1996–2011) through advertisements, talks, letters to leaders service providers of the Jewish community and a study web site.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20431428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25781172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4363491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients were interviewed in-person and diagnosed through a consensus procedure described in detail elsewhere [30,31].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001696> "A case-control sample of Ashkenazi Jewish people with schizophrenia, including schizoaffective disorder, and screened Ashkenazi Jewish controls, all reporting four grandparents of Ashkenazi Jewish descent, recruited in the United States by the Epidemiology-Genetics Program in Psychiatry of Johns Hopkins University: the cases through advertisements, talks and letters to the Jewish community and a study website, interviewed in person and diagnosed by consensus, and the controls at Jewish community meetings, community centres and synagogues.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EpiHealth is a population-based, multicenter longitudinal cohort study in subjects aged 45–75 years in which exposures (lifestyle factors and genes) are collected at a baseline investigation aiming for 300,000 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, a collection of data on lifestyle factors by self-assessment using an internet-based questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Second, a visit to a test center where blood samples are collected and physiological parameters recorded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The date of including the first patient in the study was April 26th 2011 in Uppsala, and in January 9th 2012 the test center in Malmö started to include subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objectives of the EpiHealth cohort study is to provide a resource to study interactions between genotypes and lifestyle factors in a large cohort (aim is 300,000 individuals) derived from the Swedish population in the age range 45–75 years regarding development of common degenerative disorders (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38965493") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23435790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10654-013-9787-x") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Third, the sample is followed for occurrence of outcomes using nationwide medical registers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001697> "A Swedish population-based cohort study of men and women aged 45 to 75, recruited from 2011 through test centres in Uppsala and Malmö, who answered an internet-based lifestyle questionnaire and gave blood samples and physiological measurements at the test centre, and who are followed for disease outcomes through nationwide medical registers, set up to study interactions between genes and lifestyle in common diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16702371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17087949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17087949") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17087949+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In-person interviews were conducted to collect data on demographic, medical, and family history as well as environmental exposures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698> "A multicentre case-control study of incident lymphoma conducted in 1998–2004 in the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy and Spain, whose controls were frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and country and drawn at random from population registers in Germany and Italy and from patients of the cases' hospitals elsewhere, and whose participants were interviewed in person about their medical and family history and environmental exposures, to investigate risk factors for lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16702371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17087949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7351167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency matched by 5-year age groups, sex and country of residence and randomly selected from population registries in Italy and Germany (population-based recruitment) and among patients admitted to the same hospital as cases in the remaining countries (hospital-based recruitment).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698> "A multicentre case-control study of incident lymphoma conducted in 1998–2004 in the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy and Spain, whose controls were frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and country and drawn at random from population registers in Germany and Italy and from patients of the cases' hospitals elsewhere, and whose participants were interviewed in person about their medical and family history and environmental exposures, to investigate risk factors for lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16702371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17087949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7351167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Epilymph is a case-control study of incident lymphoma conducted between 1998 and 2004 in the Czech-Republic, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy, and Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698> "A multicentre case-control study of incident lymphoma conducted in 1998–2004 in the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy and Spain, whose controls were frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and country and drawn at random from population registers in Germany and Italy and from patients of the cases' hospitals elsewhere, and whose participants were interviewed in person about their medical and family history and environmental exposures, to investigate risk factors for lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16702371") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17087949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32649712") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7351167/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we examine the association between medical diagnostic IR exposure and lymphoma risk in the multicentre European lymphoma case-control study Epilymph.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001698> "A multicentre case-control study of incident lymphoma conducted in 1998–2004 in the Czech Republic, France, Germany, Ireland, Italy and Spain, whose controls were frequency-matched to cases on age, sex and country and drawn at random from population registers in Germany and Italy and from patients of the cases' hospitals elsewhere, and whose participants were interviewed in person about their medical and family history and environmental exposures, to investigate risk factors for lymphoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2931495/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were identified from the medical records of the Sun Yat-Sen University Cancer Center, the largest centre for cancer prevention and treatment in southern China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2931495/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility criteria included the following: 1) histological confirmation of NPC, 2) age less than 80 years, 3) no previous diagnosis of or treatment for NPC, and 4) residence in Guangdong province. Among all eligible NPC patients identified between October 2005 and October 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2931495/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The centre is located in Guangzhou, the capital of Guangdong province, and it draws patients from all areas of Guangdong Province.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2931495/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were recruited from people who requested health examinations in the centers of physical examination of the largest general hospitals in Guangdong province. All subjects were required to be Guangdong residents without any history of malignancy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2931495/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To evaluate the association between dietary factors and NPC risk in Guangdong, China, a large-scale, hospital-based case-control study was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20727127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29905022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35414057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31241250") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6712476/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present hospital‐based case‐only study was conducted on the basis of a case‐control study named as EPI‐NPC‐2005 project conducted during October 2005 and October 2007, which was designed to assess the interaction between EBV, environmental factors and genetic determinants in the pathogenesis and progression of NPC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001699> "A hospital-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in Guangdong, southern China, whose cases are Guangdong residents under 80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed nasopharyngeal carcinoma identified at Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center in Guangzhou between October 2005 and October 2007, and whose frequency-matched controls are Guangdong residents without cancer recruited among people attending health examinations at large general hospitals of the province; it was set up to study dietary, environmental and genetic risk factors for the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257687+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on this information, participants were assigned to screening groups, and selected participants were invited for in-person examination (n = 623).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> "A population-based cohort set up in 2010 in Lübeck, Germany, in which inhabitants screened by mailed questionnaire were assigned to groups ranging from healthy controls to people with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism, alongside Parkinson's disease patients, and selected participants were examined in person and followed up, to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257687+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this, we included several control groups with decreasing contrast from Parkinson's disease patients. Group definitions ranged from healthy control subjects to those with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> "A population-based cohort set up in 2010 in Lübeck, Germany, in which inhabitants screened by mailed questionnaire were assigned to groups ranging from healthy controls to people with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism, alongside Parkinson's disease patients, and selected participants were examined in person and followed up, to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257687+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first-year follow-up examination was performed either in person using the same protocol or via mailed questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> "A population-based cohort set up in 2010 in Lübeck, Germany, in which inhabitants screened by mailed questionnaire were assigned to groups ranging from healthy controls to people with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism, alongside Parkinson's disease patients, and selected participants were examined in person and followed up, to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257687+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort was set up in 2010 to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> "A population-based cohort set up in 2010 in Lübeck, Germany, in which inhabitants screened by mailed questionnaire were assigned to groups ranging from healthy controls to people with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism, alongside Parkinson's disease patients, and selected participants were examined in person and followed up, to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23257687") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23257687+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using a mailed questionnaire, we screened 5838 inhabitants of Lübeck, Germany, out of a target population of 10 000 citizens, enquiring about motor impairment, pain, quality of life, comorbidities, somatization and demographics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001700> "A population-based cohort set up in 2010 in Lübeck, Germany, in which inhabitants screened by mailed questionnaire were assigned to groups ranging from healthy controls to people with suspected early motor signs of parkinsonism, alongside Parkinson's disease patients, and selected participants were examined in person and followed up, to investigate the specificity of non-motor symptoms for Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10657417+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We randomly sampled subjects between 60 and 90 years old from 2 population-based follow-up studies in which subjects had their baseline examinations in 1975 to 1978 (midlife) and in 1990 to 1993 (late life).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> "A population-based follow-up study begun in 1975 in Zoetermeer, the Netherlands, which examined inhabitants aged from 5 to 91 years to study the determinants of chronic diseases; participants aged 60 to 90 were later sampled for brain MRI in 1995–1996 and rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9143207") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9143207+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All residents of 5 or more years who were living in two districts in the Dutch town of Zoetermeer were invited to participate in a study on indicators for chronic diseases between 1975 and 1978.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> "A population-based follow-up study begun in 1975 in Zoetermeer, the Netherlands, which examined inhabitants aged from 5 to 91 years to study the determinants of chronic diseases; participants aged 60 to 90 were later sampled for brain MRI in 1995–1996 and rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It includes 10,361 subjects between 5 and 91 years old and originally focused on determinants of various chronic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> "A population-based follow-up study begun in 1975 in Zoetermeer, the Netherlands, which examined inhabitants aged from 5 to 91 years to study the determinants of chronic diseases; participants aged 60 to 90 were later sampled for brain MRI in 1995–1996 and rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent baseline MRI scanning in 1995–1996 and were rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008 [29], [30].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> "A population-based follow-up study begun in 1975 in Zoetermeer, the Netherlands, which examined inhabitants aged from 5 to 91 years to study the determinants of chronic diseases; participants aged 60 to 90 were later sampled for brain MRI in 1995–1996 and rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10657417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4879491/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiological Prevention study Of Zoetermeer (EPOZ) is a population-based follow-up study that was initiated in 1975 [28].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001702> "A population-based follow-up study begun in 1975 in Zoetermeer, the Netherlands, which examined inhabitants aged from 5 to 91 years to study the determinants of chronic diseases; participants aged 60 to 90 were later sampled for brain MRI in 1995–1996 and rescanned in 1999–2000 and 2008.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7280960/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Included patients were diagnosed with ALL or lymphoblastic lymphoma (LBL) between 1998 and 2013 in Australia, aged between 1 and 18 years inclusive, and treated on one of the following BFM-based protocols: ANZCCSG study 7, ANZCHOG study 8, BFM-95, COG A5971, or AIEOP-BFM study 9 [30,31,32,33,34].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8883571/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical cohort consisted of 1,251 children with ALL/LBL (Online Supplementary Figure S1) from six tertiary Australian pediatric oncology centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8883571/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a national Australian retrospective review of children diagnosed with ALL or lymphoblastic lymphoma (LBL).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8883571/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a systematic, retrospective review of 1,251 consecutive Australian children enrolled on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols between 1998-2013.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2025.288939") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ERASE study collected mTRT data across two major ALL treatment platforms, creating an opportunity to undertake the first study of clinical and genetic risk factors for mTRT in pediatric ALL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32438682") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33567813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41163570") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13040163/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In ERASE (Evaluation of Risk of ALL Treatment-related Side-Effects), we undertook a retrospective study of Australian pediatric ALL patients diagnosed between 1998-2013, including annotation of treatment, survival, TRT and a germline GWAS (Online Supplementary Tables S1, S2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001704> "A national retrospective study of children aged 1 to 18 years diagnosed with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoblastic lymphoma between 1998 and 2013 at six tertiary paediatric oncology centres in Australia and treated on Berlin-Frankfurt-Münster- or Children's Oncology Group-based protocols, with annotation of treatment, survival and treatment-related toxicities and a germline genome-wide association study, to find clinical and genetic risk factors for side-effects of treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five other centers (Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain and Switzerland) joined the study between 1994 and 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In short, eligible subjects (men aged 50–74 years of age at time of randomization) were identified from population registers and randomization was performed individually based on random numbers (with 1:1 allocation, except in Finland where an intervention/control ratio of approximately 1:1.5 was used).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ERSPC is a multi-center, randomized screening trial with the main goal to compare PCa mortality between an intervention arm invited to screening and a control arm with no intervention offered.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Randomized study of Screening for Prostate Cancer (ERSPC) is a randomized multi-center trial with a predefined centralized database, analysis plan and core age group (55–69 years) evaluating prostate-specific antigen (PSA) testing in eight European countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The screening interval of four years (two years in Sweden) was chosen on the basis of lead time estimated as >8 years at the time of trial initiation10, 11.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25108889") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4427906/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial was initiated in 1993 in the Netherlands and in Belgium6, 7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001705> "A multicentre randomised trial of prostate-specific antigen (PSA) screening, begun in 1993 in the Netherlands and Belgium and joined by centres in Sweden, Finland, Italy, Spain, Switzerland and France, in which men aged 50 to 74 identified from population registers were randomly assigned to screening, generally every four years, or to no intervention, and followed for prostate cancer incidence and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17330239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18396378+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ESCALE included all children in France less than 15 years old with a diagnosis of acute leukaemia, lymphoma, malignant CNS tumor, or neuroblastoma (2003-2004).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> "A nationwide registry-based case-control study carried out in France in 2003–2004 of children under 15 years old diagnosed with acute leukaemia, lymphoma, a malignant central nervous system tumour or neuroblastoma, and population controls frequency-matched to them on age and sex, whose mothers were interviewed by standardised telephone questionnaire, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for childhood cancers and leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17330239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A national registry–based case–control study [ESCALE (Etude Sur les Cancers et les Leucémies de l’Enfant, Study on Environmental and Genetic Risk Factors of Childhood Cancers and Leukemia)] carried out in France was used to assess the effect of exposure to road traffic exhaust fumes on the risk of childhood leukemia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> "A nationwide registry-based case-control study carried out in France in 2003–2004 of children under 15 years old diagnosed with acute leukaemia, lymphoma, a malignant central nervous system tumour or neuroblastoma, and population controls frequency-matched to them on age and sex, whose mothers were interviewed by standardised telephone questionnaire, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for childhood cancers and leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17330239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over the study period, 2003–2004, 763 cases and 1,681 controls < 15 years old were included, and the controls were frequency matched with the cases on age and sex.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> "A nationwide registry-based case-control study carried out in France in 2003–2004 of children under 15 years old diagnosed with acute leukaemia, lymphoma, a malignant central nervous system tumour or neuroblastoma, and population controls frequency-matched to them on age and sex, whose mothers were interviewed by standardised telephone questionnaire, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for childhood cancers and leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17330239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ESCALE data were collected by a standardized telephone interview of the mothers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> "A nationwide registry-based case-control study carried out in France in 2003–2004 of children under 15 years old diagnosed with acute leukaemia, lymphoma, a malignant central nervous system tumour or neuroblastoma, and population controls frequency-matched to them on age and sex, whose mothers were interviewed by standardised telephone questionnaire, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for childhood cancers and leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17330239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18396378") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21147599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3080942/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ESCALE study is a national study conducted in 2003 and 2004 in mainland France (11 million children < 15 years of age) to investigate the role of infectious, environmental, and genetic factors in four childhood neoplastic diseases (acute leukemia, lymphoma, neuroblastoma, and brain tumor) (Brosselin et al. 2009; Rudant et al. 2007, 2008, 2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001707> "A nationwide registry-based case-control study carried out in France in 2003–2004 of children under 15 years old diagnosed with acute leukaemia, lymphoma, a malignant central nervous system tumour or neuroblastoma, and population controls frequency-matched to them on age and sex, whose mothers were interviewed by standardised telephone questionnaire, to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors for childhood cancers and leukaemia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2137937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "487 extremely obese children and adolescents (‘cases’) were recruited in hospitals specialized for the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity (Table 2; mean BMI Z score: 4.63±2.27) while 442 healthy lean individuals (‘controls’) were ascertained at the University of Marburg (Table 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2137937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GWA (Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 5.0 comprising 440,794 single nucleotide polymorphisms) for early onset extreme obesity based on 487 extremely obese young German individuals and 442 healthy lean German controls;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2137937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have performed a genome wide association study (GWA) for early onset (extreme) obesity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.140/MediaObjects/41588_2008_BFng140_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Statistical analyses – The association between rs17782313 and obesity case‐control status was performed using logistic regression, adjusted for age and sex with SPSS 14.0 software (SPSS, Chicago, IL, USA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ESSEN study is not a (birth) cohort study and information on year of birth is sometimes lacking; the study is a cross-sectional study with cases that are on average more extreme than the ≥95th percentile;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18159244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18454148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2247/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2247_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Essen Obesity Study (Essen Obesity Trios) is a nuclear family study with 705 obese offspring (54.9% female; mean age 13.4 ± 3.0 years; age range 3-24 years; mean BMI 32.0 ± 5.8 kg/m2 ; mean BMI-SDS 4.2 ± 2.0) who were ascertained like the cases in the case-control study; in addition the 2x705 biological parents of the offspring were ascertained15 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001708> "A German cross-sectional study of early-onset extreme obesity, made up of a case-control study of extremely obese children and adolescents recruited in hospitals specialised in the inpatient treatment of extreme obesity, with healthy lean controls ascertained at the University of Marburg, and a nuclear family study of obese children and adolescents ascertained in the same way together with both their biological parents (the Essen Obesity Trios), whose genotypes have been used in genome-wide association studies of obesity and body mass index.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At baseline, data were collected for all participants on discharges from non-psychiatric, non-obstetric wards in Scottish hospitals between 1981 and September 2007 using record linkage to the SMR01 scheme (acute hospital admissions) at the Information and Services Division of NHS Scotland [13].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up cognitive, vascular and liver assessments are scheduled for 2010–2011 when subjects will have been in the study for 4 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants recruited at baseline (2006–2007) constitute 1066 men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes, living in the Lothian region of central Scotland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People aged between 60 and 74 years on 1st August 2006 were selected by sex and 5-year age bands from computer-randomised lists of eligible subjects extracted from the LDR.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Edinburgh Type 2 Diabetes Study is a large prospective cohort study that has the potential to identify factors that are important for the development and progression of less well-characterised complications of type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19077235") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2621220/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Edinburgh Type 2 Diabetes Study was established in 2006 in order to investigate the role of potential risk factors in these complications, as well as to further investigate mechanisms underlying the development and progression of micro and macrovascular disease in type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001710> "A prospective cohort of men and women aged 60 to 75 years with established type 2 diabetes living in the Lothian region of central Scotland, randomly selected by sex and age band from the Lothian Diabetes Register and recruited in 2006–2007, established to investigate risk factors for, and mechanisms of, the development and progression of micro- and macrovascular complications of type 2 diabetes and of its less well-characterised complications, with follow-up examinations and linkage to hospital records.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16753010+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EUDRAGENE: European collaboration to establish a case-control DNA collection for studying the genetic basis of adverse drug reactions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> "A European collaboration, supported by the European Commission's 5th Framework Programme, that established a DNA case-control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to serious adverse drug reactions, ascertaining cases mainly through adverse drug reaction reports to pharmacovigilance centres; its cases have been used in genetic studies of drug-induced liver injury, statin-induced myopathy and other reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2526236/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have therefore established a network (EUDRAGENE) to establish a DNA case–control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to various classes of ADR, based on case ascertainment through the pharmacovigilance system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> "A European collaboration, supported by the European Commission's 5th Framework Programme, that established a DNA case-control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to serious adverse drug reactions, ascertaining cases mainly through adverse drug reaction reports to pharmacovigilance centres; its cases have been used in genetic studies of drug-induced liver injury, statin-induced myopathy and other reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3129430/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adult (≥18 years) AC-DILI cases identified retrospectively and prospectively from European pharmacovigilance centre adverse drug reaction reports were collected from November 2006 to August 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> "A European collaboration, supported by the European Commission's 5th Framework Programme, that established a DNA case-control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to serious adverse drug reactions, ascertaining cases mainly through adverse drug reaction reports to pharmacovigilance centres; its cases have been used in genetic studies of drug-induced liver injury, statin-induced myopathy and other reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3129430/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EUDRAGENE collaboration has received support from the EC 5th Framework program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> "A European collaboration, supported by the European Commission's 5th Framework Programme, that established a DNA case-control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to serious adverse drug reactions, ascertaining cases mainly through adverse drug reaction reports to pharmacovigilance centres; its cases have been used in genetic studies of drug-induced liver injury, statin-induced myopathy and other reactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753010") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18637888") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21570397") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31220337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6896237/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All 585 CPRD statin‐tolerant controls and 19 patients with myopathy from the EUDRAGENE cohort were genotyped for statistically significant association signals identified in the case‐control discovery GWAS (P < 5 × 10−5)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001711> "A European collaboration, supported by the European Commission's 5th Framework Programme, that established a DNA case-control collection for studying the genetic basis of susceptibility to serious adverse drug reactions, ascertaining cases mainly through adverse drug reaction reports to pharmacovigilance centres; its cases have been used in genetic studies of drug-induced liver injury, statin-induced myopathy and other reactions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001712> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001712>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7096091") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were ascertained through 28 centres across Europe some of which had participated in the EURODIAB Prospective Complications Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001712> "A European genetic study of diabetic nephropathy and retinopathy in type 1 diabetes, combining a family-based design of affected offspring and their family members with a larger case-control component, whose participants were ascertained through 28 centres across Europe, some of which had taken part in the EURODIAB Prospective Complications Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7096091") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The family study involves both a family based design with affected off- spring and family members and also a larger case control component that is the subject of this report.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001712> "A European genetic study of diabetic nephropathy and retinopathy in type 1 diabetes, combining a family-based design of affected offspring and their family members with a larger case-control component, whose participants were ascertained through 28 centres across Europe, some of which had taken part in the EURODIAB Prospective Complications Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27647854") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16163567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7096091") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objective of the EURODIAB FS is to identify genes and pathways involved in the pathogenesis of nephropathy (DN) and retinopathy (DR) in type 1 DM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001712> "A European genetic study of diabetic nephropathy and retinopathy in type 1 diabetes, combining a family-based design of affected offspring and their family members with a larger case-control component, whose participants were ascertained through 28 centres across Europe, some of which had taken part in the EURODIAB Prospective Complications Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2687074/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All EUROSPAN cohorts were genotyped using Illumina 317K platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> "A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2687074/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Special Populations Network (EUROSPAN) consortium consists of five population samples: (i) the Erasmus Ruchpen Family (ERF) study conducted in The Netherlands, (ii) the MICROS study conducted in Italy, (iii) the Northern Swedish Population (NSP), (iv) the Orkney Complex Disease Study (ORCADES; Scotland) and (v) the Vis study conducted in Croatia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> "A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19060911+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we report the first GWA analysis of loci affecting total cholesterol (TC), low-density lipoprotein (LDL) cholesterol, high-density lipoprotein (HDL) cholesterol and triglycerides sampled randomly from 16 population-based cohorts and genotyped using mainly the Illumina HumanHap300-Duo platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> "A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.609/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng609_MOESM31_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls were ascertained from four genetically isolated European populations recruited from: South Tyrol, Italy (MICROS: Study of Micro-isolates in South Tyrol); Vis island, Croatia; Rucphen, Netherlands (ERF: the Erasmus Rucphen Family study); and Orkney Islands, Scotland (ORCADES: Orkney Complex Disease Study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> "A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19060911") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3303225/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CROATIA Studies (Croatia-Vis, Croatia-Korcula, Croatia-Split) were supported by grants from the Medical Research Council UK and Ministry of Science, Education and Sport of the Republic of Croatia (No. 108-1080315-0302) and CROATIA-Vis by the European Union framework program 6 European Special Populations Research Network (EUROSPAN) project (contract LSHG-CT-2006-018947).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001713> "A consortium of family-based genetic studies of isolated European populations, funded as a European Union Sixth Framework Programme project, whose samples (the Erasmus Rucphen Family study in the Netherlands, MICROS in South Tyrol, Italy, the Northern Swedish Population Health Study, the Orkney Complex Disease Study in Scotland and the Vis study in Croatia) were genotyped on a common platform and analysed together in genome-wide association studies.")

