AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26407342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26407342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4583245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FinnTwin16 is a population–based longitudinal study of five consecutive birth cohorts (1975–1979) of Finnish twins and their families [25, 26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001727> "A population-based longitudinal study of Finnish twins from five consecutive birth cohorts (1975–1979) and their families, one of the three cohorts of the Finnish Twin Cohort Study, begun in 1991 with baseline assessments of the twins and their parents when the twins were aged 16 and followed with questionnaire waves at ages 17 and 18½, in young adulthood and later, the fifth wave also assessing the twins' spouses or partners.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12537859+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They have participated since 1975 in mail surveys, in clinical examinations for subsamples, and have been followed-up for morbidity using national medical registers; 2) The older Twin Cohort was expanded in 1996 to include opposite-sex pairs born 1938-1957 (c. 8000 pairs);") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.54") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Earlier questionnaires were mailed in 1975 and 1981 to all twins born before 1958 and living in Finland, identified from the population register of Finland; the 1990 third-wave questionnaire was targeted to twins born in 1930–1957 who had responded to either earlier questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.54") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fourth wave of assessments was done in three parts, with a questionnaire study of twins born during 1945–1957 in 2011–2012, while older twins were interviewed and screened for dementia in two time periods, between 1999 and 2007 for twins born before 1938 and between 2013 and 2017 for twins born in 1938–1944.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1017/thg.2019.54") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The older Finnish Twin Cohort (FTC) was established in 1974.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11046842/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants of this study were from the older Finnish Twin Cohort study, which is a longitudinal population-based study of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958 (N=13,888) [24, 25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537859") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23298696") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31462340") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38671483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/finntwin16-a-longitudinal-study-from-age-16-of-a-populationbased-finnish-twin-cohort/066CB09103674DBA0210715C3AECC560") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Finnish Twin Cohort comprises three different cohorts: the Older Twin Cohort established in the 1970s and the FinnTwin12 and FT16 initiated in the 1990s.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001728> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of twins from same-sex pairs born in Finland before 1958, identified from the population register and established in 1974, who answered health questionnaires in 1975, 1981, 1990 and 2011–2012, were screened for dementia in later waves, took part in clinical studies of subsamples and are followed up through national medical registers; it was expanded to opposite-sex pairs born 1938–1957, and is the oldest of the three Finnish Twin Cohorts.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2570409/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FINRISK97 study is a population-based cross-sectional survey which consists of 8,191 people aged 25–74 years from five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu, and Kuopio regions) (21).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> "The 1997 survey of the National FINRISK Study, a population-based cross-sectional survey of a stratified random sample of people aged 25–74 living in five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu and Kuopio regions), examined for chronic-disease risk factors and followed up for incident cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4210840") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the follow-up, hospitalization and mortality data were obtained from the Finnish National Hospital Discharge Register and the Finnish National Causes-of-Death Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> "The 1997 survey of the National FINRISK Study, a population-based cross-sectional survey of a stratified random sample of people aged 25–74 living in five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu and Kuopio regions), examined for chronic-disease risk factors and followed up for incident cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4210840") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FINRISK surveys have been conducted every 5 years since 1972 to monitor the risk of chronic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> "The 1997 survey of the National FINRISK Study, a population-based cross-sectional survey of a stratified random sample of people aged 25–74 living in five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu and Kuopio regions), examined for chronic-disease risk factors and followed up for incident cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4210840") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each survey, a stratified random sample was selected from the 25-74 year old inhabitants in different regions in Finland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> "The 1997 survey of the National FINRISK Study, a population-based cross-sectional survey of a stratified random sample of people aged 25–74 living in five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu and Kuopio regions), examined for chronic-disease risk factors and followed up for incident cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18678614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23599444") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31431621") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6702196/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To determine whether the identified biomarkers are indicators of disease-specific mortality risk, we also explored the associations of the biomarkers with cardiovascular, cancer, and infection-related mortality in the FINRISK 1997 cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001729> "The 1997 survey of the National FINRISK Study, a population-based cross-sectional survey of a stratified random sample of people aged 25–74 living in five geographical areas of Finland (the Helsinki, southwestern Finland, North Karelia, Oulu and Kuopio regions), examined for chronic-disease risk factors and followed up for incident cardiovascular disease and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001730> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001730>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33051487") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33051487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7553910/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 80,458 men aged 55–67 years were enrolled during 1996–1999, with 32,000 randomised to the screening arm and invited to PSA-based screenings at four-year intervals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001730> "A randomised trial of prostate-cancer screening in Finland, the largest component of the European Randomized Study of Screening for Prostate Cancer, enrolling men aged 55–67 during 1996–1999 and inviting those randomised to its screening arm to prostate-specific-antigen-based screening at four-year intervals.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33051487") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33051487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7553910/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of them, 2283 were clinical cases from the Pirkanmaa Hospital District, and 455 were from the Finnish Randomized Study of Screening for Prostate Cancer (FinRSPC)22, which is the largest component of the European Randomized Study of Screening for Prostate Cancer (ERSPC)23.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001730> "A randomised trial of prostate-cancer screening in Finland, the largest component of the European Randomized Study of Screening for Prostate Cancer, enrolling men aged 55–67 during 1996–1999 and inviting those randomised to its screening arm to prostate-specific-antigen-based screening at four-year intervals.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001731> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001731>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2820168/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finland SO replicationb 83 365 Sequenom iPlex Gold") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001731> "A Finnish case-control sample of multiple sclerosis patients with at least one parent born in Southern Ostrobothnia, the internal isolate on the western coast of Finland with an increased prevalence of multiple sclerosis, and anonymous population controls collected at the Central Hospital of Seinäjoki in Southern Ostrobothnia, that was genotyped as the isolate replication set of a 2010 genome-wide association study of multiple sclerosis in that isolate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2820168/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MS samples included in the genome-wide analysis originated from the MS high-risk isolate located on the western coast of Finland (Southern Ostrobothnia, SO) with ∼2-fold prevalence and higher familial clustering of MS compared to other regions of Finland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001731> "A Finnish case-control sample of multiple sclerosis patients with at least one parent born in Southern Ostrobothnia, the internal isolate on the western coast of Finland with an increased prevalence of multiple sclerosis, and anonymous population controls collected at the Central Hospital of Seinäjoki in Southern Ostrobothnia, that was genotyped as the isolate replication set of a 2010 genome-wide association study of multiple sclerosis in that isolate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20159113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2820168/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MS cases have at least one parent born within SO, and anonymous population controls were collected from the Central Hospital of Seinajoki in Southern Ostrobothnia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001731> "A Finnish case-control sample of multiple sclerosis patients with at least one parent born in Southern Ostrobothnia, the internal isolate on the western coast of Finland with an increased prevalence of multiple sclerosis, and anonymous population controls collected at the Central Hospital of Seinäjoki in Southern Ostrobothnia, that was genotyped as the isolate replication set of a 2010 genome-wide association study of multiple sclerosis in that isolate.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001732> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001732>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00433927") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25088940+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between Jan 23, 2007, and Sept 19, 2012, 592 patients with KRAS exon 2 wild-type tumours were randomly assigned and received treatment (297 in the FOLFIRI plus cetuximab group and 295 in the FOLFIRI plus bevacizumab group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001732> "An open-label, randomised phase 3 trial, led from the Ludwig-Maximilians-University of Munich, that from January 2007 to September 2012 recruited patients aged 18–75 with KRAS (exon 2) wild-type metastatic colorectal cancer at centres in Germany and Austria and assigned them to first-line FOLFIRI plus cetuximab or FOLFIRI plus bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00433927") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25088940+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FOLFIRI plus cetuximab versus FOLFIRI plus bevacizumab as first-line treatment for patients with metastatic colorectal cancer (FIRE-3): a randomised, open-label, phase 3 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001732> "An open-label, randomised phase 3 trial, led from the Ludwig-Maximilians-University of Munich, that from January 2007 to September 2012 recruited patients aged 18–75 with KRAS (exon 2) wild-type metastatic colorectal cancer at centres in Germany and Austria and assigned them to first-line FOLFIRI plus cetuximab or FOLFIRI plus bevacizumab.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT00433927") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25088940") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25088940+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this open-label, randomised, phase 3 trial, we recruited patients aged 18-75 years with stage IV, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer, an Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance status of 0-2, an estimated life expectancy of greater than 3 months, and adequate organ function, from centres in Germany and Austria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001732> "An open-label, randomised phase 3 trial, led from the Ludwig-Maximilians-University of Munich, that from January 2007 to September 2012 recruited patients aged 18–75 with KRAS (exon 2) wild-type metastatic colorectal cancer at centres in Germany and Austria and assigned them to first-line FOLFIRI plus cetuximab or FOLFIRI plus bevacizumab.")

