# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28304224") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28304224+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our trial, inhibition of PCSK9 with evolocumab on a background of statin therapy lowered LDL cholesterol levels to a median of 30 mg per deciliter (0.78 mmol per liter) and reduced the risk of cardiovascular events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (TIMI 59) of whether adding the PCSK9 inhibitor evolocumab to statin therapy reduces major cardiovascular events in patients aged 40 to 85 with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (a history of myocardial infarction, non-haemorrhagic stroke or symptomatic peripheral artery disease) and raised LDL or non-HDL cholesterol.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8058781/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FOURIER trial was a multinational, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of the efficacy of evolocumab in patients with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (TIMI 59) of whether adding the PCSK9 inhibitor evolocumab to statin therapy reduces major cardiovascular events in patients aged 40 to 85 with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (a history of myocardial infarction, non-haemorrhagic stroke or symptomatic peripheral artery disease) and raised LDL or non-HDL cholesterol.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC8058781/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The key inclusion criteria for the trial were an age between 40 and 85 years, LDL-C ≥70 mg/dl or non–high-density lipoprotein cholesterol ≥100 mg/dl, and a history of either myocardial infarction, nonhemorrhagic stroke, or symptomatic peripheral artery disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (TIMI 59) of whether adding the PCSK9 inhibitor evolocumab to statin therapy reduces major cardiovascular events in patients aged 40 to 85 with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (a history of myocardial infarction, non-haemorrhagic stroke or symptomatic peripheral artery disease) and raised LDL or non-HDL cholesterol.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC13014400") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Further Cardiovascular Outcomes Research with PCSK9 Inhibition in Subjects with Elevated Risk (FOURIER) trial, adding the PCSK9 monoclonal antibody evolocumab to statin therapy achieved a median LDL-C of 30 mg dl−1 (ref. 2), a level lower than has been seen in any previous major clinical trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (TIMI 59) of whether adding the PCSK9 inhibitor evolocumab to statin therapy reduces major cardiovascular events in patients aged 40 to 85 with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (a history of myocardial infarction, non-haemorrhagic stroke or symptomatic peripheral artery disease) and raised LDL or non-HDL cholesterol.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31707849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40011692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10310983/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FOURIER (TIMI 59) (Further Cardiovascular Outcomes Research With PCSK9 Inhibition in Subjects With Elevated Risk).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001739> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (TIMI 59) of whether adding the PCSK9 inhibitor evolocumab to statin therapy reduces major cardiovascular events in patients aged 40 to 85 with clinically evident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (a history of myocardial infarction, non-haemorrhagic stroke or symptomatic peripheral artery disease) and raised LDL or non-HDL cholesterol.")

