# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001745> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001745>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18243582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18243582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2384165/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One full sibling for each case and community-based subject participated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001745> "A family study of cocaine dependence at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis, Missouri, in which adults with cocaine dependence recruited from chemical dependency treatment centres in the St. Louis area, and community controls matched to them on age, ethnicity, gender and zip code and recruited through driver's licence records, each took part with a full sibling, to study family, neighbourhood and genetic contributions to substance dependence; recruitment targeted equal numbers of men and women and of European-Americans and African-Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18243582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18519132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2582594/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cocaine dependent subjects were recruited from chemical dependency treatment centers in the St. Louis area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001745> "A family study of cocaine dependence at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis, Missouri, in which adults with cocaine dependence recruited from chemical dependency treatment centres in the St. Louis area, and community controls matched to them on age, ethnicity, gender and zip code and recruited through driver's licence records, each took part with a full sibling, to study family, neighbourhood and genetic contributions to substance dependence; recruitment targeted equal numbers of men and women and of European-Americans and African-Americans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18243582") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18519132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2582594/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were recruited through driver’s license records maintained by the Missouri Family Registry, housed at Washington University School of Medicine for research purposes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001745> "A family study of cocaine dependence at Washington University School of Medicine in St. Louis, Missouri, in which adults with cocaine dependence recruited from chemical dependency treatment centres in the St. Louis area, and community controls matched to them on age, ethnicity, gender and zip code and recruited through driver's licence records, each took part with a full sibling, to study family, neighbourhood and genetic contributions to substance dependence; recruitment targeted equal numbers of men and women and of European-Americans and African-Americans.")
