# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001746> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001746>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In stage 1, we tested the association with T2D of 2,234,194 genotyped and imputed SNPs that passed all QC criteria in 3,712 Chinese Hans from Beijing and Shanghai, of which 1,839 were case subjects, and 1,873 were control subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001746> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Han Chinese from Beijing or Shanghai, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, that was one of the four sample sets of the stage 1 genome-wide scan of a 2013 genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese Hans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stage 1 samples for the GWA scan included 1,999 T2D case subjects and 1,976 nondiabetic control subjects drawn from the Nutrition and Health of Aging Population in China (NHAPC) study (312 case and 815 control subjects), the Gut Microbiota and Obesity Study (GMOS) (82 case and 163 control subjects), the Fudan-Huashan Study (807 case and 339 control subjects), and the Beijing Diabetes Survey (798 case and 659 control subjects).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001746> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Han Chinese from Beijing or Shanghai, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, that was one of the four sample sets of the stage 1 genome-wide scan of a 2013 genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese Hans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001747> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001747>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants underwent clinical examination, including ECG, echocardiography, and blood draw, from which DNA has been extracted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001747> "A Norwegian study of early-onset lone atrial fibrillation that enrolled, between 2009 and 2016, people diagnosed with atrial fibrillation before age 50 in the absence of clinical or echocardiographic signs of cardiovascular disease, hypertension, or metabolic or pulmonary disease; all participants had a clinical examination with ECG and echocardiography and gave blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lone AF was defined as AF in the absence of clinical or echocardiographic findings of cardiovascular disease, hypertension, and metabolic or pulmonary disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001747> "A Norwegian study of early-onset lone atrial fibrillation that enrolled, between 2009 and 2016, people diagnosed with atrial fibrillation before age 50 in the absence of clinical or echocardiographic signs of cardiovascular disease, hypertension, or metabolic or pulmonary disease; all participants had a clinical examination with ECG and echocardiography and gave blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics in AF (GENAF) study enrolled individuals with early-onset lone AF before age 50 in Norway between 2009 and 20168 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001747> "A Norwegian study of early-onset lone atrial fibrillation that enrolled, between 2009 and 2016, people diagnosed with atrial fibrillation before age 50 in the absence of clinical or echocardiographic signs of cardiovascular disease, hypertension, or metabolic or pulmonary disease; all participants had a clinical examination with ECG and echocardiography and gave blood for DNA.")

