AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17728769") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17898773") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) initiative of the US Foundation for the National Institutes of Health, we conducted a genomewide association study of 435,291 SNPs genotyped in 1,738 MDD cases and 1,802 controls selected to be at low liability for MDD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001749> "A public-private partnership of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health that, through a series of collaborative genome-wide association studies, genotyped samples from case-control studies of bipolar disorder, diabetic nephropathy, major depressive disorder, psoriasis and schizophrenia and a trio study of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and made the resulting individual genotype and phenotype data available to researchers through dbGaP.")
