AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12028118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16391567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16443614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17847005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18177490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12028118") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12028118+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "100 Norwegian families (426 subjects) of 7-35-year-old sibling-pairs with asthma and their parents underwent questionnaire/interview (medical and exposure history), skin prick test (SPT) to common local inhalant allergens and German cockroach, and IgE specific to mites, mosquito, shrimp and cockroach.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001750> "A multinational family study of asthma that in 1999-2001 recruited, at centres in Europe (among them the United Kingdom, Greece and Norway), Australia and the United States, nuclear families of probands aged 7-35 years with physician-diagnosed asthma and their symptomatic siblings, together with their parents, who were assessed by questionnaire, lung function and allergen skin prick testing, to search for asthma susceptibility loci and quantitative asthma phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12028118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16391567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16443614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17847005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18177490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16391567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16391567+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families with at least two siblings with asthma were collected from Europe, Australia and the US.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001750> "A multinational family study of asthma that in 1999-2001 recruited, at centres in Europe (among them the United Kingdom, Greece and Norway), Australia and the United States, nuclear families of probands aged 7-35 years with physician-diagnosed asthma and their symptomatic siblings, together with their parents, who were assessed by questionnaire, lung function and allergen skin prick testing, to search for asthma susceptibility loci and quantitative asthma phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12028118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16391567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16443614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17847005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18177490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16443614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2082729/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 232 families with at least one asthmatic child (aged 7–18 years) were recruited via an asthmatic proband from the two centres (North Staffordshire and Sheffield) between January 1999 and December 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001750> "A multinational family study of asthma that in 1999-2001 recruited, at centres in Europe (among them the United Kingdom, Greece and Norway), Australia and the United States, nuclear families of probands aged 7-35 years with physician-diagnosed asthma and their symptomatic siblings, together with their parents, who were assessed by questionnaire, lung function and allergen skin prick testing, to search for asthma susceptibility loci and quantitative asthma phenotypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12028118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16391567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16443614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17847005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18177490") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18177490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18177490+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Factor analysis was used to identify distinct phenotypes from questionnaire, clinical, and laboratory data, including baseline pulmonary function, allergen skin prick test (SPT).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001750> "A multinational family study of asthma that in 1999-2001 recruited, at centres in Europe (among them the United Kingdom, Greece and Norway), Australia and the United States, nuclear families of probands aged 7-35 years with physician-diagnosed asthma and their symptomatic siblings, together with their parents, who were assessed by questionnaire, lung function and allergen skin prick testing, to search for asthma susceptibility loci and quantitative asthma phenotypes.")
