AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3035981/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data and biomaterials were collected as part of ten projects that participated in the National Institute of Mental Health (NIMH) Bipolar Disorder Genetics Initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3035981/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The initial BiGS GWA study was funded through the Foundation for the National Institutes of Health Genetic Information Association Network (GAIN) initiative (http://www.genome.gov/19518664) and we report the results of this GWA study here.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3035981/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify Bipolar Disorder (BD) genetic susceptibility factors, we conducted two genome-wide association (GWA) studies: one involving a sample of individuals of European ancestry (EA; n = 1,001 cases; n = 1,033 controls) and one involving a sample of individuals of African ancestry (AA; n = 345 cases; n = 670 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178836/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls for both the GAIN-BP and BiGS samples were ascertained throughout the United States and genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array as part of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia II (MGS2) Collaboration") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178836/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were matched by ethnicity, age and sex to the BP cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178836/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotyping in both efforts was performed using the Affymetrix 6.0 array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19488044") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21305692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3178836/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Unrelated cases were genotyped in two separate efforts described in detail elsewhere, the Genetic Association Information Network Bipolar Sample (GAIN-BP)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001751> "The sample of the first genome-wide association study of the Bipolar Genome Study, funded through the Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN): unrelated cases with bipolar disorder of European American and African American ancestry from the collections of the NIMH Genetics Initiative for Bipolar Disorder in the United States, and controls matched by ethnicity, age and sex who were ascertained throughout the United States for the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia collaboration, all genotyped on the Affymetrix 6.0 array.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18197199+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper, we briefly review linkage studies of MDD and then describe the large-scale nationwide biological sample collection in Dutch twin families from the Netherlands Twin Register (NTR) and in participants in the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety (NESDA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional cases were from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS (25), ARIADNE (26), and the NTR.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were a lifetime diagnosis of DSM-IV MDD (1) as diagnosed via the Composite International Diagnostic Interview psychiatric interview (27), age 18-65 years, and self-reported western European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MDD cases were mainly from NESDA, a longitudinal cohort study designed to be representative of individuals with depressive and/or anxiety disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were N=1,703 controls from the NTR and additional controls from NESDA (N=133 from general practice, N=24 from ARIADNE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18197199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065144") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2717726/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This GWAS was one of the six initial Genetic Association Information Network (GAIN) studies sponsored by the Foundation for the NIH (19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001752> "A case-control genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder in the Netherlands, one of the six initial studies of the Genetic Association Information Network of the Foundation for the US National Institutes of Health, whose cases, with a lifetime diagnosis of major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety and also from the population-based cohorts NEMESIS, ARIADNE and the Netherlands Twin Register, and whose controls, selected for low genetic liability to major depressive disorder, came mainly from the Netherlands Twin Register and also from the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety.")

