# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1769317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between July 1, 2001 and December 31, 2004 we attempted to enroll 863 men who had been diagnosed with prostate cancer within the last two years and 668 agreed to participate (77%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between July 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1769317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The over sampling of cases compared with controls was done because the primary objective of the study was to evaluate gene-environment interaction using a statistically more efficient case-only analytic approach [30].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between July 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1769317/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we studied 637 prostate cancer cases and 244 controls of White and African-American race from the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between July 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3102736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected from the same HFHS population base from which cases were drawn.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between July 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17067754") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21637779") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3102736/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Henry Ford Health System (HFHS) recruited cases diagnosed with adenocarcinoma of the prostate of Caucasian or African American race, less than 75 years of age, and living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area [41].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001765> "A case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Henry Ford Health System in Detroit, Michigan, United States, which enrolled men of Caucasian or African American race younger than 75 years with adenocarcinoma of the prostate living in the metropolitan Detroit tri-county area, and controls randomly selected from the same Henry Ford Health System population base, between July 2001 and December 2004, to study gene-environment interaction in prostate cancer risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3609892/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the NIDA-funded Gene-Environment-Development Initiative (GEDI) our goal is to identify exactly which genes, which environments, and which developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3609892/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four data sets were used whose common characteristics include (1) general population samples including males and females; (2) repeated measures across adolescence and young adulthood; (3) assessment of nicotine, alcohol and cannabis use and addiction; (4) measures of family and environmental risk; and (5) consent for genotyping DNA from blood or saliva.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3609892/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This representative study of psychiatric illness and service use in African American and White youth took place in four rural counties in the southeastern USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30482948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Christchurch Health and Development study (CHDS)2,3 is a longitudinal study of a birth cohort of 1,265 children collected in mid-1977 from urban Christchurch, New Zealand.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30482948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Duke arm of the NIDA-funded Gene-Environment-Development Initiative (GEDI) combined existing phenotypic and environmental data from two large prospective studies, the Great Smoky Mountains Study (GSMS) and the Caring for Children in the Community (CCC) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30482948") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VCU arm of the NIDA-funded Gene-Environment-Development Initiative (GEDI) combined existing phenotypic and environmental data from the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development (VTSABD) study, a population-based multi-wave, cohort-sequential twin study of adolescent psychopathology and its risk factors,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23461817") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8956679") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8956679+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multistage, overlapping cohorts design was used, in which 4500 of the 11758 children aged 9, 11, and 13 years in an 11-county area of the southeastern United States were randomly selected for screening for psychiatric symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001766> "A consortium funded by the US National Institute on Drug Abuse that brought together four existing longitudinal, general-population studies with repeated assessments across childhood, adolescence and young adulthood, the Virginia Twin Study of Adolescent Behavioral Development, the Great Smoky Mountains Study and the Caring for Children in the Community study in the United States and the Christchurch Health and Development Study in New Zealand, to identify which genes, environments and developmental transitions together predict the development of drug use and misuse.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10644212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, patients with lung cancer included ethnically Han Chinese individuals who were aged 18 years or older with histologically confirmed incident primary lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767> "A genetic epidemiological study of lung cancer in Taiwan whose case-control component, from September 2002, recruited ethnically Han Chinese patients aged 18 years or older with histologically confirmed incident primary lung cancer from six medical centres, together with cancer-free controls matched on age, gender and ethnicity from the health-examination departments of the same hospitals, to evaluate questionnaire-based and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10644212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals categorized as controls were matched on age (±2 years), gender, and ethnic background and were cancer-free and randomly selected from the health-examination departments during the same time and from the same 6 hospitals as case recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767> "A genetic epidemiological study of lung cancer in Taiwan whose case-control component, from September 2002, recruited ethnically Han Chinese patients aged 18 years or older with histologically confirmed incident primary lung cancer from six medical centres, together with cancer-free controls matched on age, gender and ethnicity from the health-examination departments of the same hospitals, to evaluate questionnaire-based and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10644212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited between September 17, 2002, and March 30, 2011, from 6 medical centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767> "A genetic epidemiological study of lung cancer in Taiwan whose case-control component, from September 2002, recruited ethnically Han Chinese patients aged 18 years or older with histologically confirmed incident primary lung cancer from six medical centres, together with cancer-free controls matched on age, gender and ethnicity from the health-examination departments of the same hospitals, to evaluate questionnaire-based and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37955902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10644212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study used the case-control component of GELAC in Taiwan, which aimed to evaluate the associations between questionnaire-based and genetic risk factors and lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001767> "A genetic epidemiological study of lung cancer in Taiwan whose case-control component, from September 2002, recruited ethnically Han Chinese patients aged 18 years or older with histologically confirmed incident primary lung cancer from six medical centres, together with cancer-free controls matched on age, gender and ethnicity from the health-examination departments of the same hospitals, to evaluate questionnaire-based and genetic risk factors for lung cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After GELCAPS was incorporated into the NCRN (National Cancer Research Network) portfolio in March 2002 it was subsequently rolled out across England after individual centers had obtained local ethical permissions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004 were eligible for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Coupled with patient recruitment their spouses/partners who had no known past or current history of malignancy were invited to participate for the purposes of contributing to the generation of a control series.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GELCAPS was one of the first genetic epidemiological trials in the UK to be adopted by the National Cancer Research Network (NCRN) onto its portfolio with the participation of over 100 oncology departments specialising in the management of lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To create a resource for identifying low penetrance alleles for lung cancer we established GELCAPS (GEnetic Lung CAncer Predisposition Study) in March 1999 to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data from a large series of lung cancer cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18715499") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2535604/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We established GEnetic Lung CAncer Predisposition Study (GELCAPS) to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data from a large series of cases and a series of spouse/partner controls, thereby generating a key resource for the identification of low risk alleles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001768> "A case-control DNA resource for lung cancer established in March 1999 by the Institute of Cancer Research and adopted in 2002 onto the portfolio of the National Cancer Research Network, through which oncology departments across England recruited patients diagnosed with lung cancer between March 1999 and July 2004, and their spouses or partners without a history of cancer as controls, to collect DNA and clinico-pathological data for identifying low-penetrance susceptibility alleles for lung cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were selected from the same hospital, frequency-matched by 10-year age groups and admitted or seen in the hospital within 30 days of the date of diagnosis of the corresponding case.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were Chinese women with a diagnosis of primary lung carcinoma (all histological types).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEL-S study is a case-control study carried out in the 5 major public-sector hospitals in Singapore5 (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer, Singapore Study (GEL-S)5") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4169232/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To gain insight into the etiology of lung cancer among never-smoking women, we formed the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia (FLCCA), which includes studies drawn from mainland China, South Korea, Japan, Singapore, Taiwan, and Hong Kong.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36530673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34750403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8575905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data for the present analysis was obtained from the Genes and Environment in Lung Cancer (GEL) study, a case–control study conducted in public hospitals from 2005 to 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001769> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in ethnic Chinese women in Singapore, recruited from 2005 to 2008 in the major public-sector hospitals (Changi General Hospital, National Cancer Centre, National University Hospital, Singapore General Hospital and Tan Tock Seng Hospital), with cases of primary lung carcinoma of all histological types and controls from the same hospitals frequency-matched by 10-year age group; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10449117+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants in the Genetic Epidemiology of Migraine Study were comprised of 6,491 adults, age 20 to 65 years, selected randomly from two county population registries in the Netherlands to participate in a general health survey (52.7% response).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2566523/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A semi-structured telephone interview was obtained in a random sample of (83%) screen-positive and (5%) screen-negative participants to clarify the signs and symptoms of migraine headache and aura reported in the stage 2 questionnaire, and to validate the earlier questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2566523/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Screen-positive participants completed a more detailed questionnaire that focused on signs and symptoms of migraine headache and aura as outlined in the IHS criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2566523/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEM cohort is embedded within the ‘MORGEN’ project—a population-based study designed to monitor risk factors for and the prevalence of chronic diseases of public health importance in Dutch adults 20-65 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2566523/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEM sample has been used for genetic and clinical research, including assessing the cardiovascular risk profile and impact of migraine on quality of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10449117") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18676988") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19025553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3268125/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, from a population-based survey of 6491 Dutch adults aged 20–60 years living in two representative Dutch municipalities (Maastricht and Doetinchem) 863 migraineurs and 5628 controls were identified according to the IHS-criteria (1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001770> "A Dutch population-based study of migraine embedded in the MORGEN project, in which adults aged 20 to 65 randomly selected from two Dutch county population registries (Maastricht and Doetinchem) to take part in a general health survey were screened for headache history, screen-positives were given a detailed headache questionnaire and a random subset a semistructured telephone clinical interview, and migraine was diagnosed by International Headache Society criteria, to study the prevalence, characteristics, cardiovascular risk profile and genetics of migraine.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30430080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6220051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GEMO participants are from HBOC families ascertained prospectively through family cancer clinics and tested positive for a confirmed PV in BRCA1/2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> "A multicentre study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, run through the French National Cancer Genetics Network of the UNICANCER Genetic Group, coordinated from Lyon (Hospices Civils de Lyon and Centre Léon Bérard) and the Institut Curie in Paris, with contributing cancer genetics centres across France and at Creighton University in Omaha, United States, to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in these carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30430080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6220051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEMO coordinating center was located at Centre Léon Bérard (Lyon) until September 2015 and is currently held at Institut Curie (Paris).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> "A multicentre study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, run through the French National Cancer Genetics Network of the UNICANCER Genetic Group, coordinated from Lyon (Hospices Civils de Lyon and Centre Léon Bérard) and the Institut Curie in Paris, with contributing cancer genetics centres across France and at Creighton University in Omaha, United States, to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in these carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30430080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6220051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Modifiers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 (GEMO) Group is the French multidisciplinary, collaborative framework for the investigation of genetic factors modifying cancer risk in Hereditary Breast and Ovarian cancer (HBOC) families segregating BRCA1/2 PVs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> "A multicentre study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, run through the French National Cancer Genetics Network of the UNICANCER Genetic Group, coordinated from Lyon (Hospices Civils de Lyon and Centre Léon Bérard) and the Institut Curie in Paris, with contributing cancer genetics centres across France and at Creighton University in Omaha, United States, to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in these carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30430080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6220051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Modifiers of Cancer Risk in BRCA1/2 Mutation Carriers (GEMO) study is a study from the National Cancer Genetics Network UNICANCER Genetic Group, France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> "A multicentre study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, run through the French National Cancer Genetics Network of the UNICANCER Genetic Group, coordinated from Lyon (Hospices Civils de Lyon and Centre Léon Bérard) and the Institut Curie in Paris, with contributing cancer genetics centres across France and at Creighton University in Omaha, United States, to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in these carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30430080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6220051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Today, GEMO involves 32 clinics and the 17 diagnostics laboratories from the GGC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001771> "A multicentre study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants, run through the French National Cancer Genetics Network of the UNICANCER Genetic Group, coordinated from Lyon (Hospices Civils de Lyon and Centre Léon Bérard) and the Institut Curie in Paris, with contributing cancer genetics centres across France and at Creighton University in Omaha, United States, to identify genetic modifiers of cancer risk in these carriers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible families consisted of a minimum of two siblings (an affected sib-pair) with atherogenic dyslipidemia (ADL), which was defined by the simultaneous presence of high triglyceride (≥75% percentile for age, sex, and country) and low HDL-cholesterol (HDL-C) (≤25% percentile for age, sex, and country) levels in plasma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were recruited into the GEMS Study from six study sites, located in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland, and the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first arm of the GEMS Study, two sets of families with differing ancestral origins (i.e., families of Turkish and southern European (TSE) origin and of Northern and Western European (NWE) origin) were recruited for the purpose of carrying out linkage analysis of metabolic syndrome and related traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the second arm of the GEMS Study, a set of 1,025 cases with ADL and 1,008 normolipidemic controls were recruited from the five GEMS sites with subjects of NWE origin for a case–control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEMS Study was initiated in 1999 for the purpose of identifying genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15642551") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25164947") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19165155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4028785/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Epidemiology of Metabolic Syndrome (GEMS) Study is a multicenter study designed to identify the genetic determinants of metabolic syndrome and related traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001772> "A multicentre, multinational family-based study initiated in 1999 to identify genes associated with the metabolic syndrome and related traits, in which affected status was defined by atherogenic dyslipidaemia (low HDL cholesterol with elevated triglycerides for age, sex and country). Its first arm recruited families of Turkish and southern European and of Northern and Western European origin at six sites in Australia, Canada, Finland, Turkey, Switzerland and the United States for linkage analysis; its second arm recruited unrelated cases with atherogenic dyslipidaemia and normolipidaemic controls of Northern and Western European origin at five of the sites for genome-wide association analysis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01714440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11142483/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After the weights of the SNPs were estimated in the DeKAF Genomics cohort, the PRS was then validated in another independent cohort, the Genomics of Kidney Transplantation (GEN-03).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> "A prospective observational cohort of kidney or kidney-pancreas transplant recipients, enrolled within 10 days of transplantation, and kidney donors, recruited from 2012 to 2016 at transplant centres in the United States (University of Alabama in Birmingham, University of Minnesota, Hennepin County Medical Center and Mayo Clinic) and Canada (University of Alberta) in a study sponsored by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases with the Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program, to investigate the relationship between genetic variation and kidney transplant outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01714440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11142483/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Kidney transplant clinical information and genotyping data was collected from two cohort studies: DeKAF Genomics (2005–2011, NCT00270712) and GEN-03 (2012–2016, NCT01714440).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> "A prospective observational cohort of kidney or kidney-pancreas transplant recipients, enrolled within 10 days of transplantation, and kidney donors, recruited from 2012 to 2016 at transplant centres in the United States (University of Alabama in Birmingham, University of Minnesota, Hennepin County Medical Center and Mayo Clinic) and Canada (University of Alberta) in a study sponsored by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases with the Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program, to investigate the relationship between genetic variation and kidney transplant outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01714440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001667/phs001667.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001667.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Kidney (or kidney-pancreas) transplant recipient no more than 10 days post-transplant, or kidney donor no more than 30 days post-transplant") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> "A prospective observational cohort of kidney or kidney-pancreas transplant recipients, enrolled within 10 days of transplantation, and kidney donors, recruited from 2012 to 2016 at transplant centres in the United States (University of Alabama in Birmingham, University of Minnesota, Hennepin County Medical Center and Mayo Clinic) and Canada (University of Alberta) in a study sponsored by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases with the Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program, to investigate the relationship between genetic variation and kidney transplant outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01714440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/dbgap/studies/phs001667/phs001667.v1.p1/GapExchange_phs001667.v1.p1.xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specimens were originally collected from the NIAID funded Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program (GTCRP); GEN-03; Genomics of Kidney Transplantation") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> "A prospective observational cohort of kidney or kidney-pancreas transplant recipients, enrolled within 10 days of transplantation, and kidney donors, recruited from 2012 to 2016 at transplant centres in the United States (University of Alabama in Birmingham, University of Minnesota, Hennepin County Medical Center and Mayo Clinic) and Canada (University of Alberta) in a study sponsored by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases with the Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program, to investigate the relationship between genetic variation and kidney transplant outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01714440") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6597284/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two prospective, observational, multicenter cohorts were used in this study; a discovery cohort used to identify genetic variants associated with TAC trough blood concentrations and immunosuppressant adverse effects and a confirmation cohort used to validate those variants identified in the discovery cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001773> "A prospective observational cohort of kidney or kidney-pancreas transplant recipients, enrolled within 10 days of transplantation, and kidney donors, recruited from 2012 to 2016 at transplant centres in the United States (University of Alabama in Birmingham, University of Minnesota, Hennepin County Medical Center and Mayo Clinic) and Canada (University of Alberta) in a study sponsored by the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases with the Genomics of Transplantation Cooperative Research Program, to investigate the relationship between genetic variation and kidney transplant outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17378724+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this school-based cross-sectional study, more than 400 variables describing anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and other lifestyle characteristics were collected from participating children and their families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> "A school-based cross-sectional study of fifth- and sixth-grade children aged 10 to 14 years, enrolled between November 2005 and June 2006 from primary schools in the Attica region of Greece, which collected anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and lifestyle data from the children and their families to evaluate the contributions and interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity factors in childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17378724+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "So far, 920 participants have been enrolled and the final projected sample is 1000 fifth- and sixth-grade students from selected elementary schools in Attica (10-14 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> "A school-based cross-sectional study of fifth- and sixth-grade children aged 10 to 14 years, enrolled between November 2005 and June 2006 from primary schools in the Attica region of Greece, which collected anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and lifestyle data from the children and their families to evaluate the contributions and interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity factors in childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17378724+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gene-Diet Attica Investigation on childhood obesity (GENDAI) evaluates the contributions to and pivotal interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity variables on children's weight.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> "A school-based cross-sectional study of fifth- and sixth-grade children aged 10 to 14 years, enrolled between November 2005 and June 2006 from primary schools in the Attica region of Greece, which collected anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and lifestyle data from the children and their families to evaluate the contributions and interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity factors in childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2807029/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1138 children were recruited from November 2005 to June 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> "A school-based cross-sectional study of fifth- and sixth-grade children aged 10 to 14 years, enrolled between November 2005 and June 2006 from primary schools in the Attica region of Greece, which collected anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and lifestyle data from the children and their families to evaluate the contributions and interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity factors in childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17378724") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19403283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2807029/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENDAI cohort consists of young children of both sexes attending school in the area of Attica, Greece.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001774> "A school-based cross-sectional study of fifth- and sixth-grade children aged 10 to 14 years, enrolled between November 2005 and June 2006 from primary schools in the Attica region of Greece, which collected anthropometric, dietary, clinical, genetic, sociodemographic and lifestyle data from the children and their families to evaluate the contributions and interactions of genetic, dietary and physical activity factors in childhood obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC507978") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A cross-sectional study was conducted prospectively in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium (see list in Acknowledgments) from May 1994 to April 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC507978") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A review committee (see composition in Acknowledgments), not aware of patients’ origin, reviewed all case records to validate patient selection criteria and to grade the renal involvement of each patient.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC507978") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All inpatients and outpatients attending these clinics were asked to participate in the study if they fullfilled two criteria: (a) insulin-dependent diabetes before the age of 35 yr, and (b) past or present proliferative diabetic retinopathy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537649") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9120002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9120002+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As angiotensin II increases glomerular pressure, we studied the relationship between genetic polymorphisms in the renin-angiotensin system-angiotensin I converting enzyme (ACE), angiotensinogen (AGT), and angiotensin II, subtype 1, receptor-and the renal involvement of insulin-dependent diabetic subjects with proliferative retinopathy: those exposed to the risk of nephropathy due to diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001775> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of people with insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes and proliferative diabetic retinopathy, and so exposed to the risk of diabetic nephropathy, conducted from May 1994 to April 1995 in 17 diabetic clinics in France and Belgium, in which participants were classified by the severity of their renal involvement, to study the genetic determinants of diabetic nephropathy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were of northern-European ancestry and matched as a group, proportionally with cases according to age (±5 years), gender.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group consisted of unrelated individuals, primarily spouses/partners, friends and other volunteers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study cohort was ascertained through a prospective multi-center effort initiated in 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study recruited patients of northern-European ancestry, preferentially with a relapsing onset of MS, although individuals with all clinical subtypes of the disease participated, including clinically isolated syndrome (CIS), relapsing remitting MS (RRMS), secondary progressive MS (SPMS), primary progressive MS (PPMS) and progressive relapsing MS (PRMS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three MS clinical centers were involved in patient enrollment and biological specimen collection using identical inclusion criteria, two in Europe (Vrije Universiteit Medical Center, Amsterdam; and University Hospital Basel) and one in the USA (University of California San Francisco).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3247076/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five strata (IMSGC-US, IMSGC-UK, GeneMSA-US, GeneMSA-NL, and GeneMSA-CH) were taken from a previously published meta-analysis.3") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001776> "The Swiss site sample, recruited at University Hospital Basel, Switzerland, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")

