AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study recruited patients of northern-European ancestry, preferentially with a relapsing onset of MS, although individuals with all clinical subtypes of the disease participated, including clinically isolated syndrome (CIS), relapsing remitting MS (RRMS), secondary progressive MS (SPMS), primary progressive MS (PPMS) and progressive relapsing MS (PRMS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001778> "The United States site sample, recruited at the University of California San Francisco, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4334814/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three MS clinical centers were involved in patient enrollment and biological specimen collection using identical inclusion criteria, two in Europe (Vrije Universiteit Medical Center, Amsterdam; and University Hospital Basel) and one in the USA (University of California San Francisco).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001778> "The United States site sample, recruited at the University of California San Francisco, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19010793") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19525953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570697") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22190364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3247076/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five strata (IMSGC-US, IMSGC-UK, GeneMSA-US, GeneMSA-NL, and GeneMSA-CH) were taken from a previously published meta-analysis.3") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001778> "The United States site sample, recruited at the University of California San Francisco, of people with multiple sclerosis and controls enrolled in the Genetic Multiple Sclerosis Associations (GeneMSA) study, a prospective case-control study of multiple sclerosis started in 2003 and funded by GlaxoSmithKline at three clinical centres with identical inclusion criteria, of patients of northern-European ancestry with any clinical subtype of multiple sclerosis (preferentially relapsing onset) and unrelated controls (mainly spouses or partners, friends and other volunteers) group-matched on age and sex, to study genetic influences on susceptibility and on clinical and MRI phenotype; used as a separate stratum in genome-wide meta-analyses of multiple sclerosis.")

