AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27515689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16751059+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A continuously expanding biorepository has been created consisting of frozen lymphocytes and DNA isolated from patients treated with radiotherapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001779> "A biorepository of frozen lymphocytes and DNA from patients treated with radiotherapy for cancer, with a database of their diagnosis, treatment and outcome, run from the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, whose patients include men treated for prostate cancer at the Mount Sinai Hospital in New York and patients treated in Tokyo and Chiba, Japan, and which was set up to find genetic variants that predict adverse effects of radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27515689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16751059+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conjunction with this biorepository, a database is maintained with detailed clinical information pertaining to diagnosis, treatment, and outcome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001779> "A biorepository of frozen lymphocytes and DNA from patients treated with radiotherapy for cancer, with a database of their diagnosis, treatment and outcome, run from the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, whose patients include men treated for prostate cancer at the Mount Sinai Hospital in New York and patients treated in Tokyo and Chiba, Japan, and which was set up to find genetic variants that predict adverse effects of radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27515689") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16751059") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16751059+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The validation of a test capable of predicting which patients would be most likely to develop adverse responses to radiation treatment, based on the possession of specific genetic variants, would therefore be of value.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001779> "A biorepository of frozen lymphocytes and DNA from patients treated with radiotherapy for cancer, with a database of their diagnosis, treatment and outcome, run from the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, whose patients include men treated for prostate cancer at the Mount Sinai Hospital in New York and patients treated in Tokyo and Chiba, Japan, and which was set up to find genetic variants that predict adverse effects of radiotherapy.")
