AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783544/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Non-Hispanic white subjects were recruited from Tecumseh, Michigan, and African-American subjects were recruited from Maywood, Illinois.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783544/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Once the proband was identified, an attempt was made to enroll all siblings and parents of the proband, irrespective of their blood pressure or hypertension treatment status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2783544/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Probands were defined as individuals aged 18–50 years with blood pressures in the upper 20th to 25th percentile of the age/gender-specific blood pressure distribution.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3405908/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenNet recruited African American, Caucasian, and Mexican American nuclear families ascertained through young/middle-aged probands with untreated high-normal BP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3405908/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1995 the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute established a collaboration of 4 multicenter networks, known as the Family Blood Pressure Program (FBPP), to investigate the genetic determinants of inter-individual BP variation in Asians, African Americans, Mexican Americans, and Caucasians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16076393") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21151011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3405908/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FBPP pooled data derive from the 4 separate multicenter Networks: GenNet, GENOA, HyperGEN, and SAPPHIRe (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001785> "A family study of the genetics of blood pressure and hypertension in the United States, one of the four networks of the NHLBI Family Blood Pressure Program, which from 1995 recruited nuclear families through young and middle-aged probands with blood pressure in the upper part of the distribution and enrolled their siblings and parents regardless of blood pressure: European Americans in Tecumseh, Michigan, African Americans in Maywood, Illinois, and also Mexican American families.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/genomeutwin-a-strategy-to-identify-genetic-influences-on-health-and-disease/339E85B99573B6E157333A7076AE31E7") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This international study, reaching beyond the geographical borders of Europe, is based on linkage and association strategies designed to identify genetic contributors to health and disease using integrated expertise of participating groups in genetics, epidemiology and biostatistics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786> "A European Community-funded research project that joined eight large twin registers (the national twin cohorts of Denmark, Finland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden, the UK TwinsUK cohort and an Australian twin cohort) with the multinational MORGAM population cohort, to identify genetic and lifestyle contributors to common diseases by linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14624719+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By merging information from numerous epidemiological and genetic databases, GenomEUtwin will create an intellectual and technical infrastructure for future genetic epidemiological studies aiming to define genetic and life style risks for common human diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786> "A European Community-funded research project that joined eight large twin registers (the national twin cohorts of Denmark, Finland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden, the UK TwinsUK cohort and an Australian twin cohort) with the multinational MORGAM population cohort, to identify genetic and lifestyle contributors to common diseases by linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14624719+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this issue of Twin Research, we describe different facets of a European Community funded effort, GenomEUtwin, which capitalises on eight of the world's largest and best characterised twin registers and a multi-national population cohort, MORGAM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786> "A European Community-funded research project that joined eight large twin registers (the national twin cohorts of Denmark, Finland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden, the UK TwinsUK cohort and an Australian twin cohort) with the multinational MORGAM population cohort, to identify genetic and lifestyle contributors to common diseases by linkage and association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14624719") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twin samples were drawn from the GenomEUtwin project23 , which is comprised of the Danish, Dutch, Finnish, Italian, Norwegian, and Swedish national twin cohorts, an Australian twin cohort, and the UK-based TwinsUK cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001786> "A European Community-funded research project that joined eight large twin registers (the national twin cohorts of Denmark, Finland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway and Sweden, the UK TwinsUK cohort and an Australian twin cohort) with the multinational MORGAM population cohort, to identify genetic and lifestyle contributors to common diseases by linkage and association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23280790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28411264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38103737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23280790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23280790+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to find genetic variations associated with hemorrhagic transformation (HT) and mortality rates after t-PA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787> "A multicentre Spanish study of patients of European ancestry with acute ischaemic stroke, admitted to the emergency rooms of Vall d'Hebron Hospital in Barcelona and other Spanish hospitals and treated with recombinant tissue plasminogen activator (r-tPA), set up to find genetic variants associated with haemorrhagic transformation and death after thrombolysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23280790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28411264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38103737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8305811/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutive Caucasian patients with acute ischemic stroke who were admitted to the emergency room and received recombinant tissue-type plasminogen activator (r-tPA) within 4.5 hours of symptom onset were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787> "A multicentre Spanish study of patients of European ancestry with acute ischaemic stroke, admitted to the emergency rooms of Vall d'Hebron Hospital in Barcelona and other Spanish hospitals and treated with recombinant tissue plasminogen activator (r-tPA), set up to find genetic variants associated with haemorrhagic transformation and death after thrombolysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23280790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28411264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38103737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8305811/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were enrrolled at Spanish hospitals (Vall d’Hebron University Hospital, Hospital Clinic, Hospital Universitari de Girona Doctor Josep Trueta, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, Hospital Universitari Germans Trias I Pujol, Hospital Universitari del Mar, Hospital de Basurto) between 2002 to 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787> "A multicentre Spanish study of patients of European ancestry with acute ischaemic stroke, admitted to the emergency rooms of Vall d'Hebron Hospital in Barcelona and other Spanish hospitals and treated with recombinant tissue plasminogen activator (r-tPA), set up to find genetic variants associated with haemorrhagic transformation and death after thrombolysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23280790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28411264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34300314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38103737") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38103737") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11103592/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenoTPA is a multicenter GWAS of European-ancestry patients with IS admitted to the emergency room at Spanish hospitals and treated with r-tPA alone (N = 2045).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001787> "A multicentre Spanish study of patients of European ancestry with acute ischaemic stroke, admitted to the emergency rooms of Vall d'Hebron Hospital in Barcelona and other Spanish hospitals and treated with recombinant tissue plasminogen activator (r-tPA), set up to find genetic variants associated with haemorrhagic transformation and death after thrombolysis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.479/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng479_MOESM310_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases had RA consistent with 1987 ACR criteria, and only those patients that were CCP positive were used in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.479/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng479_MOESM310_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU university medical center, the Jan van Breemen institute, and the AMC/University of Amsterdam, all situated in the Amsterdam region in the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.479/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng479_MOESM310_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy controls were recruited from blood donors from the same region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.479/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng479_MOESM310_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam (GENRA) provided a collection of Dutch cases recruited through from the greater Amsterdam region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3610685/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ABCoN, GENRA are prospective cohorts, BeSt, eRA and TEAR are randomized controlled trial (RCT), and rest of REF group are observational cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23555300") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23555300+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To understand the biological basis of response to anti-TNF therapy, we conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) meta-analysis of more than 2 million common variants in 2,706 RA patients from 13 different collections.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001788> "A prospective collection of Dutch patients with rheumatoid arthritis meeting the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, recruited from the outpatient rheumatology clinics of the VU University Medical Center, the Jan van Breemen Institute and the Academic Medical Center/University of Amsterdam in the Amsterdam region of the Netherlands, together with healthy blood-donor controls from the same region, which the Genetics Network Rheumatology Amsterdam contributed to genetic studies of rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility and of response to anti-TNF therapy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12707949+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biological materials and blinded clinical data will be made available through the NIMH cell repository program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> "A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with DSM-IV major depressive disorder that was recurrent or consisted of one episode lasting at least three years, beginning before age 31, and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository; its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12707949+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a study of a large sample of families with recurrent major depressive disorder (DSM-IV) beginning by the age 30 in probands or 40 in relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> "A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with DSM-IV major depressive disorder that was recurrent or consisted of one episode lasting at least three years, beginning before age 31, and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository; its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.")
