AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6486400/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GenRED I recruited affected sibling pair families for linkage studies10, 15, 16, and GenRED II is currently recruiting additional cases for association studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> "A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with DSM-IV major depressive disorder that was recurrent or consisted of one episode lasting at least three years, beginning before age 31, and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository; its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12953334/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood specimens were collected from interviewed subjects, their available parents, and, if fewer than two parents were available, up to two siblings without a known major depressive disorder, as reported in the Family Interview for Genetic Studies [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> "A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with DSM-IV major depressive disorder that was recurrent or consisted of one episode lasting at least three years, beginning before age 31, and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository; its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12707949") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20125088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40285827") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12953334/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Probands were recruited from 6 major U.S. sites [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001789> "A collaborative study run at six sites in the United States with NIMH support that recruited people with DSM-IV major depressive disorder that was recurrent or consisted of one episode lasting at least three years, beginning before age 31, and a parent or sibling with recurrent major depression beginning before age 41, as a sample for molecular genetic studies of depression whose biological materials and clinical data are made available through the NIMH repository; its first phase (GenRED I) recruited families with affected sibling pairs, with their parents and some unaffected siblings, for linkage studies, and its second (GenRED II) further probands for association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genomics Research in Cardiovascular disease (GenRIC) is an East Asian study were participants were recruited in Seoul, South Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> "A Korean case-control study of coronary artery disease whose cases are patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (myocardial infarction, stable or unstable angina) from three teaching hospitals in Seoul (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine), and whose controls come from the Health Examinees (HEXA) population cohort of the Korean Genome Epidemiology Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "2,690 controls from HEXA (Health Examinee) which is one of the KoGES (Korean Genome Epidemiology Study) population based cohorts that were initiated in 2001 aiming to identify genetic risk factors of complex diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> "A Korean case-control study of coronary artery disease whose cases are patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (myocardial infarction, stable or unstable angina) from three teaching hospitals in Seoul (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine), and whose controls come from the Health Examinees (HEXA) population cohort of the Korean Genome Epidemiology Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CAD was confirmed by standard coronary angiography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> "A Korean case-control study of coronary artery disease whose cases are patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (myocardial infarction, stable or unstable angina) from three teaching hospitals in Seoul (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine), and whose controls come from the Health Examinees (HEXA) population cohort of the Korean Genome Epidemiology Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects of GenRIC (Genomics Research in Cardiovascular Disease) study is composed of 2,099 CAD patients from three teaching hospitals (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> "A Korean case-control study of coronary artery disease whose cases are patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (myocardial infarction, stable or unstable angina) from three teaching hospitals in Seoul (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine), and whose controls come from the Health Examinees (HEXA) population cohort of the Korean Genome Epidemiology Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2480/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2480_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with myocardial infarction (31%), stable angina (41%) and unstable angina (28%) were classified as CAD subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001790> "A Korean case-control study of coronary artery disease whose cases are patients with angiographically confirmed coronary artery disease (myocardial infarction, stable or unstable angina) from three teaching hospitals in Seoul (Samsung Medical Center, Seoul National University Hospital and Yonsei University College of Medicine), and whose controls come from the Health Examinees (HEXA) population cohort of the Korean Genome Epidemiology Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEP is a clinic-based case-control set, and the NHS and HPFS are case-control sets nested within population-based studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the GEP, cases were derived predominantly from the Glaucoma Service at MEEI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Other controls were identified from regional glaucoma screenings held throughout Massachusetts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic Etiologies of POAG was initiated in 1996 with funding from the National Eye Institute") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of controls were patients who presented to the MEEI comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examination or from spouses of MEEI patients with secondary forms of glaucoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overarching goal is to identify novel genetic factors that contribute to primary open-angle glaucoma through large-scale genome-wide association studies of three well-characterized cohorts of cases and controls, some in matched pairs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001793> "A clinic-based case-control study of primary open-angle glaucoma, begun at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary in 1996 with National Eye Institute funding to find genetic loci for the disease, whose cases came mainly from the infirmary's Glaucoma Service and whose controls were mostly patients attending its comprehensive ophthalmology service for routine eye examinations or spouses of patients, with others found at regional glaucoma screenings in Massachusetts.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25534375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27611952") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28715532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24794243") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24794243+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The addition of neoadjuvant carboplatin to a regimen of a taxane, an anthracycline, and targeted therapy significantly increases the proportion of patients achieving a pathological complete response.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794> "A multicentre, randomised, open-label phase II neoadjuvant trial run in Germany by the German Breast Group in patients with triple-negative or HER2-positive early breast cancer, which tested whether adding carboplatin to anthracycline- and taxane-based chemotherapy (given with trastuzumab and lapatinib for HER2-positive and bevacizumab for triple-negative disease) increases the rate of pathological complete response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25534375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27611952") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28715532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27611952") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5356512/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed prospectively collected pre-therapeutic core biopsies from the phase II randomized neoadjuvant GeparSixto trial that investigated intense anthracycline/taxane-based chemotherapy with or without carboplatin together with targeted agents (bevacizumab in TNBC or trastuzumab/lapatinib in HER2-positive disease).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794> "A multicentre, randomised, open-label phase II neoadjuvant trial run in Germany by the German Breast Group in patients with triple-negative or HER2-positive early breast cancer, which tested whether adding carboplatin to anthracycline- and taxane-based chemotherapy (given with trastuzumab and lapatinib for HER2-positive and bevacizumab for triple-negative disease) increases the rate of pathological complete response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25534375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27611952") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28715532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GeparSixto Randomized phase II trial investigating the addition of carboplatin to neoadjuvant therapy for triple-negative and HER2-positive early breast cancer109 Multicenter, prospective, randomized, open-label phase II study Germany") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794> "A multicentre, randomised, open-label phase II neoadjuvant trial run in Germany by the German Breast Group in patients with triple-negative or HER2-positive early breast cancer, which tested whether adding carboplatin to anthracycline- and taxane-based chemotherapy (given with trastuzumab and lapatinib for HER2-positive and bevacizumab for triple-negative disease) increases the rate of pathological complete response.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25534375") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27611952") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28715532") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature24284/MediaObjects/41586_2017_BFnature24284_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6347624/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEPARSIXTO study was conducted by the German Breast Group GmbH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001794> "A multicentre, randomised, open-label phase II neoadjuvant trial run in Germany by the German Breast Group in patients with triple-negative or HER2-positive early breast cancer, which tested whether adding carboplatin to anthracycline- and taxane-based chemotherapy (given with trastuzumab and lapatinib for HER2-positive and bevacizumab for triple-negative disease) increases the rate of pathological complete response.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10333435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11793707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Likewise, the families from the German Asthma Genetics Group were also ascertained through two siblings with asthma at multiple centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10333435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC548502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on a previous analysis of a genome-wide scan of asthma [7,8] with inconsistent chromosomal findings to earlier studies, we decided to expand the initial sample with additional families by the same core protocol for clinical examination and using the same set of microsatellite markers [7,8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10333435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC548502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained staff from 3 university hospitals as well as 6 pediatric pulmonary practices carried out an identical phenotyping procedure as described previously [7].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10333435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.323/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng323_MOESM13_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sib-pairs from the Germany II sample set were analyzed assuming mendelian inheritance under the null hypothesis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10333435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11793707") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15634351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fejhg.2010.38/MediaObjects/41431_2010_BFejhg201038_MOESM31_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German sib-pair study consisted of two hundred and one families of at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001796> "A family study of asthma in Germany whose families have at least two children with confirmed clinical asthma, ascertained at multiple centres and phenotyped by trained staff to a common protocol for the German Asthma Genetics Group; its families were used for genome-wide linkage scans of asthma and later as a replication sample in genetic association studies of asthma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001797> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001797>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11065005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11065005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11065005+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based case control family study of breast cancer among women diagnosed by the age of 50, conducted in two geographic areas in Germany, was used to evaluate the effect of breastfeeding on risk of breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001797> "A population-based case-control family study of breast cancer in women diagnosed before age 50 in Germany, whose cases were all incident breast cancers diagnosed in 1992–1995 in two regions, Rhein-Neckar-Odenwald and Freiburg, identified by surveying the clinics serving those regions, and whose controls were residents of the study regions selected at random from population registries and matched to cases by age and region.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11065005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GESBC Genetic Epidemiology Study of Breast Cancer by Age 50 21 Germany All incident cases diagnosed <50 years of age in 1992-5 in two regions: Rhein-Neckar-Odenwald and Freiburg, by surveying the 38 clinics serving these regions") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001797> "A population-based case-control family study of breast cancer in women diagnosed before age 50 in Germany, whose cases were all incident breast cancers diagnosed in 1992–1995 in two regions, Rhein-Neckar-Odenwald and Freiburg, identified by surveying the clinics serving those regions, and whose controls were residents of the study regions selected at random from population registries and matched to cases by age and region.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11065005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Selected from random lists of residents of the study regions supplied by population registries; two controls were selected for each case, matched by age and study region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001797> "A population-based case-control family study of breast cancer in women diagnosed before age 50 in Germany, whose cases were all incident breast cancers diagnosed in 1992–1995 in two regions, Rhein-Neckar-Odenwald and Freiburg, identified by surveying the clinics serving those regions, and whose controls were residents of the study regions selected at random from population registries and matched to cases by age and region.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001798> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001798>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24001461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24476587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42308041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02410-z/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2410_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24001461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24001461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from questionnaire, health examination, biochemical measurements and public registers were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001798> "A general population study of residents aged over 20 of Næstved municipality in Zealand, Denmark, recruited in 2010–2013, whose participants underwent a health examination, completed questionnaires and gave blood samples at baseline, with linkage to public registers for follow-up, established to facilitate epidemiological and genetic research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24001461") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24476587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42308041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02410-z/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2410_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24001461") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24001461+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were more frequently women, had a higher median age, a higher frequency of marriage/registered partnerships, but had a lower frequency of co-morbidities and death in the follow-up period (January 2010-May 2011 (diseases)/June 2011 (death) than the non-participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001798> "A general population study of residents aged over 20 of Næstved municipality in Zealand, Denmark, recruited in 2010–2013, whose participants underwent a health examination, completed questionnaires and gave blood samples at baseline, with linkage to public registers for follow-up, established to facilitate epidemiological and genetic research.")
