# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with AF (n=1108) were included in 3 registry cohorts at the University Medical Center (www.atrialfibrillationresearch.nl), and Maastricht University Medical Center (AF-Risk n=6).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AF-Risk study (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT01510210) is an observational hospital-based cohort (n=500; in GGAF 339) to seek for markers of severity of atrial remodeling and predict outcome of a rhythm control treatment strategy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Biomarker AF study (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT01510197) is an observational hospital-based cohort (n=500; in GGAF 458) to identify a risk profile to guide AF therapy in all-comers with AF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GGAF cohort (n=2207) is a genotype and phenotype repository of individuals with AF and age- and sex-matched controls from 5 different sources.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PREVEND cohort study (www.prevend.org) is a community-based cohort study including 8592 inhabitants of the city of Groningen, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Young-AF study is an observational hospital-based cohort (n=500; in GGAF 311) to seek describe the phenotypic profile of patients with AF onset at age <60 years and the occurrence of AF progression during 5 years follow up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001800> "A collection of individuals with atrial fibrillation and age- and sex-matched controls, assembled at the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, as a genotype and phenotype repository for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation, whose cases come from three hospital-based atrial fibrillation cohorts (the AF-Risk, Young-AF and Biomarker-AF studies) and whose controls come from the GIPS-III trial and the PREVEND community cohort of Groningen.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18376349+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Standardized anthropometric, biochemical, and clinical procedures and extensive questionnaires were used to assess health parameters and lifestyle factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801> "A cross-sectional health and nutrition study of urban Greek adults aged 60 years and over, a randomly selected group of members of the Centers of Open Protection for the Elderly in the Athens region recruited between 2004 and 2008, assessed with standardized anthropometric, biochemical and clinical procedures and extensive questionnaires to investigate the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological and biochemical factors that determine the health status of elderly Greeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18376349+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The \"GHRAS\" study is aimed at investigating the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological, and biochemical factors determining the health status of elderly Greeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801> "A cross-sectional health and nutrition study of urban Greek adults aged 60 years and over, a randomly selected group of members of the Centers of Open Protection for the Elderly in the Athens region recruited between 2004 and 2008, assessed with standardized anthropometric, biochemical and clinical procedures and extensive questionnaires to investigate the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological and biochemical factors that determine the health status of elderly Greeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20693352") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2004 and 2008, a randomly selected group of 800 adults, who were members of the “Centers of Open Protection for the Elderly” in the Athens region, were selected to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801> "A cross-sectional health and nutrition study of urban Greek adults aged 60 years and over, a randomly selected group of members of the Centers of Open Protection for the Elderly in the Athens region recruited between 2004 and 2008, assessed with standardized anthropometric, biochemical and clinical procedures and extensive questionnaires to investigate the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological and biochemical factors that determine the health status of elderly Greeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18376349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20693352") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2992213/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GHRAS is a cross-sectional health and nutrition study conducted in elderly (≥60 y) urban Greek adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001801> "A cross-sectional health and nutrition study of urban Greek adults aged 60 years and over, a randomly selected group of members of the Centers of Open Protection for the Elderly in the Athens region recruited between 2004 and 2008, assessed with standardized anthropometric, biochemical and clinical procedures and extensive questionnaires to investigate the interactions among socioeconomic, lifestyle, dietary, psychological and biochemical factors that determine the health status of elderly Greeks.")

