AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5053363/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the primary scan (German-GWAS), 1,001 cHL cases, ascertained by the German Hodgkin Study Group during 1998–2007, were genotyped using the Illumina Human OmniExpress-12 v1.0 arrays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001802> "A clinical trials group, whose Trial Coordination Center belongs to Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne, Germany, that runs controlled, prospective, randomized trials for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, recruiting patients from across Europe, to optimise diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care; genetic studies use Hodgkin lymphoma patients ascertained through it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For over 30 years now, the German Hodgkin Study Group (GHSG) has been committed to optimizing diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care in Hodgkin lymphoma, and so far over 15,000 patients have participated in its trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001802> "A clinical trials group, whose Trial Coordination Center belongs to Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne, Germany, that runs controlled, prospective, randomized trials for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, recruiting patients from across Europe, to optimise diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care; genetic studies use Hodgkin lymphoma patients ascertained through it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It recruits patients from all across Europe to include them in its clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001802> "A clinical trials group, whose Trial Coordination Center belongs to Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne, Germany, that runs controlled, prospective, randomized trials for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, recruiting patients from across Europe, to optimise diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care; genetic studies use Hodgkin lymphoma patients ascertained through it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GHSG’s Trial Coordination Center belongs to the Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001802> "A clinical trials group, whose Trial Coordination Center belongs to Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne, Germany, that runs controlled, prospective, randomized trials for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, recruiting patients from across Europe, to optimise diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care; genetic studies use Hodgkin lymphoma patients ascertained through it.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://en.ghsg.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With the results of its various large-scale trials (controlled, prospective, randomized trials) for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, the GHSG has contributed decisively to the great progress that has been made in Hodgkin lymphoma therapy over the years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001802> "A clinical trials group, whose Trial Coordination Center belongs to Department I of Internal Medicine of the University of Cologne, Germany, that runs controlled, prospective, randomized trials for all stages of Hodgkin lymphoma, recruiting patients from across Europe, to optimise diagnostics, therapy and follow-up care; genetic studies use Hodgkin lymphoma patients ascertained through it.")
