# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age 18–80 years at diagnosis Ability to speak the local language Cases were recruited within 1 year of diagnosis and consented to participation at their clinic visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diagnosis of histologically confirmed, supratentorial, intracranial glioma (World Health Organization (WHO) grades II–IV)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we briefly describe the Glioma International Case-Control (GICC) Study (recruitment, 2010–2013), a study being conducted by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium that integrates data from multiple data collection sites, uses a common protocol and questionnaire, and includes biospecimen collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seven sites recruited visitors accompanying cancer patients as controls, 4 sites recruited clinic-based controls, and 3 sites used population-based controls (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study's comprehensive questionnaire data will allow for examination of putative risk factors identified from prior literature (i.e., radiation exposure, atopy, childhood infections), which can be reexamined in detail and validated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30482874") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4874516/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To our knowledge, the GICC Study is the largest glioma study to date that includes collection of blood samples, which will allow for genetic analysis and interrogation of gene-environment interactions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001803> "A multisite case-control study of glioma run by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium, which in 2010–2013 recruited, under a common protocol and questionnaire with blood sample collection, adults aged 18–80 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed glioma and controls (visitors accompanying cancer patients, clinic-based or population-based controls, depending on the site) at 14 sites in the United States, Denmark, Israel, Sweden and the United Kingdom, to study environmental and genetic risk factors for glioma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23742623+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the GIFT study, 201 families were recruited consisting of 438 siblings with an objectively confirmed VTE at a young age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804> "An affected-sibling family study of venous thromboembolism based at Leiden University Medical Center, the Netherlands, which recruited small thrombophilic families in which at least two siblings had objectively confirmed venous thromboembolism at a young age (before 45), to identify new genetic susceptibility loci for venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23742623+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aimed to identify novel thrombosis susceptibility alleles in a large panel of small thrombophilic families: the Genetics In Familial Thrombosis (GIFT) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804> "An affected-sibling family study of venous thromboembolism based at Leiden University Medical Center, the Netherlands, which recruited small thrombophilic families in which at least two siblings had objectively confirmed venous thromboembolism at a young age (before 45), to identify new genetic susceptibility loci for venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GIFT and the MEGA studies were approved by the Medical Ethics Committee of the Leiden University Medical Center, Leiden, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804> "An affected-sibling family study of venous thromboembolism based at Leiden University Medical Center, the Netherlands, which recruited small thrombophilic families in which at least two siblings had objectively confirmed venous thromboembolism at a young age (before 45), to identify new genetic susceptibility loci for venous thromboembolism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23742623") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5695603/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients with familial VTE comprised of 36 unrelated cases with familial VTE from the GENES study [17], and 434 cases with VTE from 201 families from the GIFT study, which included affected sibs with thrombosis before the age of 45, in the absence of known thrombophilia [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001804> "An affected-sibling family study of venous thromboembolism based at Leiden University Medical Center, the Netherlands, which recruited small thrombophilic families in which at least two siblings had objectively confirmed venous thromboembolism at a young age (before 45), to identify new genetic susceptibility loci for venous thromboembolism.")

