AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/nn.4228") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GIG (Genomic Imaging Göttingen) sample was established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry at Göttingen University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5026735") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were Caucasians with European ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5026735") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exclusion criteria were past or present psychiatric disorders according to ICD-10, a positive family history of psychiatric disorders, substance abuse during the last month, cannabis abuse during the last 2 weeks, mental retardation, dementia, neurological or metabolic diseases, and pregnancy in women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5026735") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy young adults aged 18–31 years were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5026735/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the Genomic Imaging Goettingen (GIG) study (n=299) were recruited by advertisements in intern online student networks and local newsletters in the Georg-August-University Goettingen and the University Medical Center Goettingen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27184339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27184339+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A large homogenous sample of 224 young (aged 18-31 years) participants was genotyped and underwent functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001805> "A sample of healthy young adults of European ancestry, established at the Center for Translational Research in Systems Neuroscience and Psychiatry of the University of Göttingen and recruited through advertisements at the University of Göttingen and the University Medical Center Göttingen, excluding people with past or present psychiatric disorders, a family history of psychiatric disorders, recent substance abuse, or neurological or metabolic disease, who are genotyped and undergo brain magnetic resonance imaging, including functional MRI.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16283990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a sample-based prospective study, 2,095 probands with myopia of -0.50 DS or worse and a positive family history of myopia were contacted via the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group (MELG) database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16283990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Probands and family members recruited into the study undertook a detailed assessment including questionnaire, best-corrected visual acuity, objective and subjective refraction, axial length, anterior chamber depth, keratometry readings, slit-lamp examination, height, weight and head circumference measurements, and blood sample collection for DNA analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16283990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEM study has used a targeted approach to identify an Australian cohort with a diverse spread of myopia, ranging from low to extreme.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16283990+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genes in Myopia (GEM) Study aims to recruit probands with myopia and their family members to allow genetic analysis of myopia to be undertaken.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18552384+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All twins from Victoria aged 18 years or older were invited to participate in the Genes in Myopia (GEM) twin study through the Australian Twin Registry (ATR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16283990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18552384") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20576483") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20576483+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to explore the potential role of genetic determinants in refractive error the \"GEnes in Myopia (GEM) study\" was established in 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001806> "An Australian family and twin study of the genetics of myopia and other refractive errors, established in Melbourne in 2004, which recruited probands with myopia and a family history of it (contacted through the database of the Melbourne Excimer Laser Group) together with their family members, and adult twins from Victoria through the Australian Twin Registry, with a detailed eye examination, ocular biometry, questionnaire and blood sample for DNA.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3585435/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the GISHEAL project of the 6th Framework Program of the European Commission (EU contract LSHP-CT-2007-037616)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3664380/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, the French-Italian GISHEAL cohort recruited 144 LTNP defined by a CD4+ T-cell count above 500/μL for more than 7 years after HIV infection in the absence of antiretroviral therapy (Figure 3) (Guergnon et al., 2012).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plospathogens/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.ppat.1003515.s001") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GISHEAL is a collaborative European consortium focusing on long-term nonprogressors (LTNP), with particular regard to the host genetic background and gene expression profiling and to the adaptive and innate immunological responses to the infection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5484768/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide association studies were performed on the HIC included in this study as part of the collaborative GISHEAL study, along with 139 others who fulfilled LTNP criteria from the French asymptomatic long term, Italian evaluation of LTNP viro-immunologic study (ELVIS), and additional patients from the Chelsea and Westminster cohort (11, 15, 16)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5484768/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SNP of interest, recently shown to correlate with non-progressive HIV-1 infection (11), were identified by comparing profiles of atypical progressors with the control French PRIMO cohort (11, 17).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23459797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23750159") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23935489") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702030") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766982/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we performed a GWAS on a cohort of 160 HIV-1 infected Caucasian Long Term Non Progressors (LTNP) from the EC-funded European-African ''GISHEAL'' Consortium in order to explore whether novel genetic factors could account for the LTNP phenotype") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001807> "A European-African consortium project of the European Commission's Sixth Framework Programme on the genetics and immunology of HIV-1 long-term non-progression, and its French-Italian cohort of untreated, HIV-1-infected Caucasian long-term non-progressors (CD4+ T-cell counts above 500/μL for more than seven years after infection without antiretroviral therapy) drawn from the French asymptomatic long-term cohort, the Italian ELVIS study and the Chelsea and Westminster cohort. The cohort was genotyped genome-wide and compared with seroconverters of the French PRIMO cohort to find host genetic factors of long-term non-progression, and it contributed to the International Collaboration for the Genomics of HIV.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10465168+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From October, 1993, to September, 1995, 11,324 patients surviving recent") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808> "A multicentre Italian randomized trial of the Gruppo Italiano per lo Studio della Sopravvivenza nell'Infarto miocardico (GISSI) in which patients surviving a recent (3 months or less) myocardial infarction, with no limits of age and sex, were randomly assigned from October 1993 to September 1995 in a factorial design to supplements of n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids, vitamin E, both, or none for 3.5 years, with death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke as the combined primary endpoint.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10465168+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated the effects of these substances as supplements in patients who had myocardial infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808> "A multicentre Italian randomized trial of the Gruppo Italiano per lo Studio della Sopravvivenza nell'Infarto miocardico (GISSI) in which patients surviving a recent (3 months or less) myocardial infarction, with no limits of age and sex, were randomly assigned from October 1993 to September 1995 in a factorial design to supplements of n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids, vitamin E, both, or none for 3.5 years, with death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke as the combined primary endpoint.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2871267/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GISSI-P and IGLOO are both multicentre Italian studies approved by the local ethics committees of the participating hospitals (see references 16,17 for the complete list).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808> "A multicentre Italian randomized trial of the Gruppo Italiano per lo Studio della Sopravvivenza nell'Infarto miocardico (GISSI) in which patients surviving a recent (3 months or less) myocardial infarction, with no limits of age and sex, were randomly assigned from October 1993 to September 1995 in a factorial design to supplements of n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids, vitamin E, both, or none for 3.5 years, with death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke as the combined primary endpoint.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10465168") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20403154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2871267/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, GISSI-P patients were selected on the basis of a clinical diagnosis of recent (< = 3 months) MI, with no limits of age and distinction of sex.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001808> "A multicentre Italian randomized trial of the Gruppo Italiano per lo Studio della Sopravvivenza nell'Infarto miocardico (GISSI) in which patients surviving a recent (3 months or less) myocardial infarction, with no limits of age and sex, were randomly assigned from October 1993 to September 1995 in a factorial design to supplements of n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids, vitamin E, both, or none for 3.5 years, with death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and stroke as the combined primary endpoint.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients underwent brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound in accordance with a standard clinical protocol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, Scotland, recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke, all with brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound, analysed against shared WTCCC controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort in the MEGASTROKE consortium’s genome-wide association study of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with ischemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, were recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, Scotland, recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke, all with brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound, analysed against shared WTCCC controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort in the MEGASTROKE consortium’s genome-wide association study of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0058-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_58_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were drawn from shared WTCCC controls obtained from the 1958 Birth Cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, Scotland, recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke, all with brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound, analysed against shared WTCCC controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort in the MEGASTROKE consortium’s genome-wide association study of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5968830/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were drawn from 29 studies with genome-wide genotypes imputed to 1000 Genomes Project (1000G) phase 1v3 or similar14 (MEGASTROKE consortium; Supplementary Note and Supplementary Tables 1 and 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, Scotland, recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke, all with brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound, analysed against shared WTCCC controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort in the MEGASTROKE consortium’s genome-wide association study of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29531354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29531354+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a multiancestry genome-wide-association meta-analysis in 521,612 individuals (67,162 cases and 454,450 controls) and discovered 22 new stroke risk loci, bringing the total to 32.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001809> "A hospital-based collection of patients with ischaemic stroke attending the cerebrovascular service of the Western Infirmary, Glasgow, Scotland, recruited between 1990 and 2004 as part of an ongoing study of genetic and circulating biomarkers in stroke, all with brain imaging and extracranial carotid ultrasound, analysed against shared WTCCC controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort in the MEGASTROKE consortium’s genome-wide association study of stroke.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases and controls for both studies were residents of the continental United States and were of mainly European ancestry, which was confirmed by principal component analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify genes that predispose to glaucomatous optic nerve disease, we completed two GWAS for POAG: the GLAUGEN (Glaucoma Genes and Environment) GWAS that is part of the GENEVA (GENEVA Genes Environment Association) studies [16] and the NEIGHBOR (NEI Glaucoma Human genetics collaBORation) GWAS [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23869166") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GEP is a clinical case-control study from Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary while the NHS and HPFS contain cases and controls nested within population-based cohorts at risk for POAG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23869166") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GLAUGEN study contains POAG cases and controls derived from the Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma (GEP) study, the Nurses’ Health Study (NHS), and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study (HPFS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the Glaucoma Gene Environment Initiative (GLAUGEN), funded by the Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI), is to discover genetic loci associated with POAG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3343074/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3712669/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000308.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The secondary aim of GLAUGEN, funded by NHGRI and the National Eye Institute, is to discover gene environment interactions in POAG.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001810> "A case-control genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma in the United States, part of the NIH Gene Environment Association Studies (GENEVA) initiative, which assembled cases and controls from three studies: the clinic-based Genetic Etiologies of Primary Open-Angle Glaucoma project of the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary, and cases and matched controls from the glaucoma-at-risk cohorts of the Nurses' Health Study and the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, to find genetic loci and gene–environment interactions for the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25652157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3615132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All living affected relatives were interviewed, and following consents, blood or saliva samples were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> "An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25652157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3615132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible probands were consented and completed a questionnaire (administered in-person or by telephone).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> "An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25652157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3615132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were identified through either a screening questionnaire administered to glioma patients in the clinic setting (verified for completeness through population registries in Europe), medical record review of glioma patients’ reported family history of brain tumours, or the Internet (www.gliogene.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> "An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.")
