AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25652157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3615132/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The eligibility criteria for inclusion were that the family had to have at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas, in 1st/2nd/3rd-degree relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> "An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25652157") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25482530") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4296199/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gliogene Consortium recruited 435 glioma families from 14 centers in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom, and Israel between 2007 and 2011 (7).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001812> "An international family study of non-syndromic glioma run by the Gliogene Consortium (Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium) to find glioma susceptibility genes, first by genome-wide linkage analysis: between 2007 and 2011 its 14 centres in the United States, Sweden, Denmark, the United Kingdom and Israel recruited families with at least two pathologically confirmed intracranial primary gliomas among first- to third-degree relatives, found by screening glioma patients in clinics, by review of medical records or through the internet, and collected questionnaires from probands and blood or saliva samples from living affected relatives.")

