# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As illustrated in the consort diagram in Supplementary Fig. 8 whole-genome sequencing data was collected from whole blood only from patients that signed the optional RBR ICF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By signing the optional RBR ICF, patients provided informed consent for study of inherited and non-inherited genetic variation from these whole blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients in the control arms received combinations of chemotherapies, bevacizumab, or sunitinib reflecting standard of care for the cancer indication in which the trial was conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aggregated endocrine system irAE across seven phase 3 trials testing atezolizumab combinations with chemotherapies and bevacizumab spanning six cancer indications:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We thank all of our Genentech colleagues involved in the Human Genetics Initiative") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34099659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8184890/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "metastatic urothelial carcinoma (IMvigor21115), squamous and non-squamous non-small cell lung cancer (IMpower15016, IMpower13017, IMpower13118), small cell lung cancer (IMpower13319), metastatic renal cell carcinoma (IMmotion15120), and triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC) (IMpassion13021,22) (Supplementary Tables 1–2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001816> "A collection of germline whole-genome sequencing data, assembled by Genentech's Human Genetics Initiative, from patients in seven Roche/Genentech phase 3 trials of the anti-PD-L1 antibody atezolizumab, alone or combined with chemotherapy or bevacizumab, and their standard-of-care control arms in six cancers (IMvigor211, IMpower150, IMpower130, IMpower131, IMpower133, IMmotion151 and IMpassion130), sequenced from blood samples given under the trials' optional research biosample consent.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this cohort, the original GNHS and another cohort study (the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures [CCFH]) have been integrated into the one GNHS project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GNHS baseline study conducted in China is the baseline study of the original GNHS (2008–2013) and the CCFH (2009–2015).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study (GNHS) aims to assess the determinants of metabolic disease in nutritional aspects, as well as other environmental and genetic factors, and explore possible biomarkers and mechanisms with multi-omics integration.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants in the original GNHS were recruited from multiple communities covering the majority of Guangzhou city via the following measures: local advertisements, health talks, and referrals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population-based sample of adults in Guangzhou, China (baseline: 40–83 years old; n = 5,118) was followed up about every 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37813622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11078596/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also measured multi-omics, including host genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome, gut microbiome (16S rRNA sequencing, metagenome, and internal transcribed spacer 2 sequencing), and fecal metabolome and proteome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001817> "A community-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 83 at baseline living in Guangzhou, China, which joins the original Guangzhou Nutrition and Health Study, recruited between 2008 and 2013 from communities across the city through local advertisements, health talks and referrals, with the controls of a case-control study of hip fractures recruited in 2009-2015. Participants are followed up about every three years with lifestyle, dietary, body composition, imaging and multi-omics assessments, including genome-wide genotyping, serum metabolome and proteome and gut microbiome, to study the nutritional, environmental and genetic determinants of metabolic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3112290/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects received face-to-face medical and psychiatric interviews in the subject’s language of choice (English or Spanish).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3112290/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the Genetics of Brain Structure Function study, all subjects received neuropsychological assessments and, those without contraindication, underwent magnetic resonance imaging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3112290/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study, the Genetics of Brain Structure and Function Study, recruited individuals from these two cohorts and children and grandchildren of probands who are now older than 16 years of age were also invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9531122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetics of Brain Structure (GOBS) dataset is a cross-sectional imaging archive aimed at localizing, identifying, and characterizing genes and quantitative trait loci associated with variations in brain structure and function.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9531122/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To minimize selection bias, participants were drawn from extended pedigrees of Mexican American families recruited at random from the San Antonio, Texas community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21557468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22028680") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36204553") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39757975") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11702472/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were part of the genetics of brain structure and function study (GOBS) (McKay et al. 2014; Olvera et al. 2011), a subset of individuals from the San Antonio Family Heart Study (Mahaney et al. 1995; Mitchell et al. 1996) and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study (Puppala et al. 2006).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001818> "A family-based imaging genetics study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, which recruited members of the extended pedigrees of the San Antonio Family Heart Study and the San Antonio Family Gallbladder Study, with the children and grandchildren of their probands, for brain magnetic resonance imaging and neuropsychological and psychiatric assessment at the University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio, to localise, identify and characterise genes and quantitative trait loci that influence brain structure and function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10525717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38989260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6045854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, a cohort of 1494 women was randomly recruited from the general population between 1993 and 1997 (77.1% participation) with a further 246 women aged 20–29 years recruited at the same time as the 10-year follow up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> "A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10525717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38989260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6045854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of this study was to describe the health literacy profile of a randomly recruited population-based sample of women participating in a cohort study based in south-eastern Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> "A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10525717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38989260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11234898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2001 and 2006, this study recruited a random age-stratified sample of 1540 men aged >20 years from the Barwon Statistical Division using the Australian electoral roll (Figure 1).27") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> "A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10525717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38989260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11234898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Change in BMD was calculated for L2–L4, and TH by subtracting BMD measured at follow-up (2016–2021) from BMD at baseline (2006–2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> "A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10525717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005608") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38989260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11234898/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Geelong Osteoporosis Study (GOS) is a prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001819> "A prospective, population-based cohort study of adults in south-eastern Australia, in which women were randomly recruited from the general population in 1993–1997, with further women aged 20–29 years recruited at the 10-year follow-up, and a random age-stratified sample of men aged over 20 years was recruited from the Barwon Statistical Division through the Australian electoral roll in 2001–2006, followed with repeated assessments of bone mineral density, fractures and other musculoskeletal and general health outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3516872/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects included in the GRADE (Genetic Risk Assessment of Defibrillator Events) study were at least 18 years of age, had an ejection fraction of ≤ 30%, and an implantable cardioverter-defibrillator (ICD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26231842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood was drawn at the time of enrollment for DNA extraction to investigate the correlation between genetic polymorphisms and outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26231842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrolling centers were the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center, the Pittsburgh VA Healthcare System, Emory University Hospitals, Atlanta VA Medical Center, Massachusetts General Hospital, Mid-Ohio Cardiology Group, and the Ohio State Medical Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26231842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients from the GRADE study, a prospective multicenter observational study that recruited 1808 subjects who received a new ICD implant or had an ICD generator change within the past 5 years, were retrospectively analyzed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26231842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were followed yearly for up to 5 years, with the primary end point being freedom from appropriate first ICD shock (a surrogate reflecting risk of sudden cardiac death)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22004663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26231842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4599449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a secondary end point being freedom from a combined outcome of death/heart transplant/VAD placement, a surrogate for death unrelated to arrhythmias in this population with ICDs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001820> "A prospective multicentre observational study at seven hospitals and practices in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Massachusetts and Ohio of adults with a left ventricular ejection fraction of 30% or less who had received a new implantable cardioverter-defibrillator or an ICD generator change within the previous five years, followed yearly for up to five years for appropriate ICD shocks and for death, heart transplant or ventricular assist device placement, with blood drawn at enrolment to relate genetic polymorphisms to these outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9429139/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39673281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected samples from cohort of the GRAND study, which is a prospective, multicenter, case–control study aimed to identify genetic factors related to EOCAD susceptibility and outcomes in Chinese [21].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> "A prospective multicentre, hospital-based, coronary angiography-based case-control study in China, coordinated from Zhongshan Hospital, Fudan University, that recruited adults at 38 cardiac centres between May 2017 and April 2019, centred on patients with early-onset coronary artery disease (onset at 45 years or younger) and older controls (65 years or older) without angiographically significant coronary disease, to identify genetic factors in the susceptibility to and outcomes of early-onset coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9429139/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39673281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "control subjects with no angiographically significant CAD (< 30% coronary stenosis) from the GRAND study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> "A prospective multicentre, hospital-based, coronary angiography-based case-control study in China, coordinated from Zhongshan Hospital, Fudan University, that recruited adults at 38 cardiac centres between May 2017 and April 2019, centred on patients with early-onset coronary artery disease (onset at 45 years or younger) and older controls (65 years or older) without angiographically significant coronary disease, to identify genetic factors in the susceptibility to and outcomes of early-onset coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9429139/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39673281") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "screened from 1950 patients with EOCAD (age ≤ 45 years, at least 50% stenosis of coronary artery by angiography), and selected control subjects from 1006 elder (age ≥ 65 years) with < 30% coronary stenosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> "A prospective multicentre, hospital-based, coronary angiography-based case-control study in China, coordinated from Zhongshan Hospital, Fudan University, that recruited adults at 38 cardiac centres between May 2017 and April 2019, centred on patients with early-onset coronary artery disease (onset at 45 years or younger) and older controls (65 years or older) without angiographically significant coronary disease, to identify genetic factors in the susceptibility to and outcomes of early-onset coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9429139/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRAND study recruited adult participants from 38 cardiac centers across China between May 2017 and April 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> "A prospective multicentre, hospital-based, coronary angiography-based case-control study in China, coordinated from Zhongshan Hospital, Fudan University, that recruited adults at 38 cardiac centres between May 2017 and April 2019, centred on patients with early-onset coronary artery disease (onset at 45 years or younger) and older controls (65 years or older) without angiographically significant coronary disease, to identify genetic factors in the susceptibility to and outcomes of early-onset coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11645474/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9429139/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40118068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12008806/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Genetic characteristics of coRonary Artery disease in ChiNese young aDults (GRAND) study is a multicenter, hospital-based observational clinical study.70") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001821> "A prospective multicentre, hospital-based, coronary angiography-based case-control study in China, coordinated from Zhongshan Hospital, Fudan University, that recruited adults at 38 cardiac centres between May 2017 and April 2019, centred on patients with early-onset coronary artery disease (onset at 45 years or younger) and older controls (65 years or older) without angiographically significant coronary disease, to identify genetic factors in the susceptibility to and outcomes of early-onset coronary artery disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For genetic analyses, control subjects, who gave written informed consent, were voluntary blood donors, recruited by the Department of Transfusion Medicine at the Georg-August-University of Göttingen according to national guidelines for blood donation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this purpose, 1085 patients were recruited between 2005 and 2010 by an invariable team of traveling investigators in a cross-sectional field study that comprised 23 German psychiatric hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRAS data collection comprises presently (as of August 2010) 1037 patients with confirmed diagnosis of schizophrenia (82.2%) or schizoaffective disorder (17.8%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were examined in different settings: 348 (32.1%) as outpatients, 474 (43.7%) as inpatients in psychiatric hospitals, 189 (17.4%) as residents in sheltered homes, 54 (5%) as patients in specific forensic units, and 20 (1.8%) as day clinic patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To launch PGAS, we had to establish a comprehensive phenotypical data base of schizophrenic patients, the GRAS (Göttingen Research Association for Schizophrenia) data collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20819981") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3002316/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With >3000 data points per schizophrenic subject, this data base of living patients, who are also accessible for follow-up studies, provides a wide-ranging and standardized phenotype characterization of as yet unprecedented detail.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001822> "A cross-sectional data collection of patients with schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder in Germany, recruited from 2005 by a single travelling team of investigators at 23 collaborating psychiatric hospitals, among them inpatients, outpatients, residents of sheltered homes and forensic patients, and phenotyped with more than 3,000 data points per patient, with healthy blood-donor controls recruited in Göttingen for genetic analyses, built as the basis for phenotype-based genetic association studies of schizophrenia.")

