# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21082022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21082022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2965757/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRECO protocol comprises integrated measurement of renal hemodynamics and extracellular volume as applied in an ongoing series of studies in healthy subjects [33], [34].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824> "An ongoing research programme at the renal function unit of the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, that hosts and harmonises a series of studies of renal hemodynamics, mainly in healthy volunteers, under a common protocol of integrated measurement of renal hemodynamics and extracellular volume, with standardised methods and calibration over time; participants are typically studied on a standardised dietary sodium intake.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21082022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4552520/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GRECO program hosts and harmonizes studies on renal hemodynamics at the renal function unit of the University Medical Center Groningen, by standardization of methodology, including harmonization of study protocols and calibration over time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824> "An ongoing research programme at the renal function unit of the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, that hosts and harmonises a series of studies of renal hemodynamics, mainly in healthy volunteers, under a common protocol of integrated measurement of renal hemodynamics and extracellular volume, with standardised methods and calibration over time; participants are typically studied on a standardised dietary sodium intake.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21082022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4552520/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population was recruited from the ongoing Groningen Renal Hemodynamic Cohorts (GRECO) program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824> "An ongoing research programme at the renal function unit of the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, that hosts and harmonises a series of studies of renal hemodynamics, mainly in healthy volunteers, under a common protocol of integrated measurement of renal hemodynamics and extracellular volume, with standardised methods and calibration over time; participants are typically studied on a standardised dietary sodium intake.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21082022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26149279") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4552520/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study protocol consisted of a 7-day period on a standardized sodium diet (aim: 200 mmol Na+/day).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001824> "An ongoing research programme at the renal function unit of the University Medical Center Groningen, the Netherlands, that hosts and harmonises a series of studies of renal hemodynamics, mainly in healthy volunteers, under a common protocol of integrated measurement of renal hemodynamics and extracellular volume, with standardised methods and calibration over time; participants are typically studied on a standardised dietary sodium intake.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(i) obtaining detailed family histories from individuals who are apparently from families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer or a syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer; (ii) documenting through medical records and through pathologist review of tissues the occurrence of cancer;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(iii) collecting, processing and storing biological samples, when possible, from Registry participants; and (iv) making the information and biological samples available for research under Institutional Review Board approved research protocols.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It was established in 1981 at the Roswell Park Cancer Institute") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gilda Radner Familial Ovarian Cancer Registry (GRFOCR) is a self-referred Registry of families with two or more ovarian cancer cases in blood relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary function of the Registry is to receive family cancer information voluntarily contributed throughout the United States by ovarian cancer patients, referring and concerned physicians, concerned women, and patients of the Roswell Park Cancer Institute (RPCI) Gynecologic Oncology Department.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29447163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8420680") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19536330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2694280/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed 1919 pedigrees derived from the Gilda Radner Familial Ovarian Cancer Registry (formerly referred to as the Familial Ovarian Cancer Registry) at the Roswell Park Cancer Institute (RPCI), Buffalo, New York, USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001825> "A self-referred registry of families with two or more cases of ovarian cancer among blood relatives, or with a cancer syndrome possibly related to ovarian cancer, established in 1981 at Roswell Park Cancer Institute in Buffalo, New York, United States, which receives family cancer information from throughout the United States, obtains detailed family histories, documents cancers through medical records and pathology review, and collects and stores biological samples from registry participants for research on familial ovarian cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4372188/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1991–2008, 3623 women consented to the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Program and the Women’s Cancer Program biorepository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4372188/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stored serum samples from women, who previously underwent genetic counseling and testing for BRCA mutations due to family histories of cancer, were obtained from the Women’s Cancer Program biorespository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9000920/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "3 female BRCA1mut patients’ LCLs were chosen from the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Program repository and BRCA1mut iPSC lines (Lines CS08i-BRCA-n5, CS70i-BRCA-n1 and CS79i-BRCA-n2) were generated at Cedars-Sinai Biomanufacturing Center iPSC Core.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11047303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As BRCA germline testing became clinically available, we offered testing to our Gilda Radner cohort and to our ovarian cancer patients and their families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11047303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "She was a patient at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center during my fellowship, and after completing my training, we launched the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23157996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25256924") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34965417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38230704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11047303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The program enrolled women at elevated risk due to their family histories of cancer, and participants underwent regular screenings with CA125 and ultrasound in an attempt to diagnose ovarian cancer before it had spread.1,2") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001826> "A research program at Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, launched as the Gilda Radner Hereditary Cancer Early Detection Program, that from 1991 enrolled women at elevated risk of cancer because of their family histories, among them carriers of BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations, offered them ovarian cancer screening and, once it became clinically available, BRCA genetic testing, and keeps their serum samples and lymphoblastoid cell lines in a biorepository for later studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001827> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001827>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6778823/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34887591") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-021-04064-3/MediaObjects/41586_2021_4064_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GRMIC | Greek Recurrent Myocardial Infarction Cohort | Greece | EUR | 173 | 0.82658959537572252 | 60.208791208791197 | Fasting | 22 individuals | 34.693641618497097 | 108.456647398844 | Measured | 149.306358381503 | 172.96531791907501 | Illumina Human Core Exome | Minimac | HRC and 1KGP3 | rvtests") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001827> "A cohort of survivors of myocardial infarction in Greece, followed for recurrent events, whose participants have been genotyped and profiled for gene expression after the index infarction to study the genetics of recurrent myocardial infarction and of cardiometabolic traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34887591") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6778823/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6778823/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five of the identified genes (CHD7, IST1, KIAA1958, MAP3K5, UBFD1) were also found to be differentially expressed six months after a MI in 39 MI survivors (Greek Recurrent Myocardial Infarction Cohort) that had not experienced any recurrent event during that period (p-adj ≤10-5).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001827> "A cohort of survivors of myocardial infarction in Greece, followed for recurrent events, whose participants have been genotyped and profiled for gene expression after the index infarction to study the genetics of recurrent myocardial infarction and of cardiometabolic traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2008 and 2012 young adults (ages 18 to 35) with normal or corrected-to-normal vision were recruited from the Boston community to participate in the GSP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By linking existing investigator-initiated studies to a common acquisition protocol, the GSP data aggregation strategy was able to accumulate over 3,000 unique data sets in under 4 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were asked to: 1) complete a basic set of demographic and health questionnaires just before, or directly after, the scan; 2) undergo a series of structural and functional MRI scans; 3) provide a saliva sample before and after the scan; and 4) complete a web-based battery of behavioral, cognitive, and personality assessments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Saliva was collected at the time of scan (for DNA extraction) along with core demographic and health information; a website link was provided for more extensive behavioral phenotyping that included IQ estimates, personality, social and emotional probes, and a series of additional cognitive tasks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Taking advantage of these innovations, the Brain Genomics Superstruct Project (GSP) was initiated to yield a dataset of structural, functional, behavioral, and genetic information on a large number of clinically normal participants that could be analyzed on its own or combined with other large-scale data collection efforts4–9.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26175908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4493828/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the Brain Genomics Superstruct Project (GSP) is to enable large-scale exploration of the links between brain function, behavior, and ultimately genetic variation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001829> "A neuroimaging genetics study of clinically normal participants, mostly young adults aged 18 to 35, recruited from the Boston community, United States, in 2008–2012 through ongoing research studies at Harvard University and Massachusetts General Hospital that shared a common acquisition protocol, who underwent structural and functional magnetic resonance imaging, gave saliva for DNA and completed demographic, health, behavioural, cognitive and personality assessments, to link individual differences in brain structure and function to behaviour and genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3632836") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples from these women were genotyped using an Illumina Infinium 660k array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3632836") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These samples were genotyped as part of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium (WTCCC2; see URLs)27.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3632836") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three thousand nine hundred and sixty breast cancer cases were used in stage 1, of which 3,652 were from cancer genetics clinics in the UK recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study (FBCS) and 308 were from oncology clinics in the UK recruited through the Prospective study of Outcomes in Sporadic versus Hereditary breast cancer (POSH) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3378688/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls used in this study were genotyped as part of the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium (WTCCC) study and were drawn from the 1958 Birth Cohort (a population-based study in the United Kingdom of individuals born in one week in 1958) and from the UK National Blood Service (9).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22266113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3378688/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To explore whether PMD and breast cancer have a shared genetic basis, we identified genetic variants most strongly associated with PMD in a published meta-analysis of five genome-wide association studies (GWAS) and used these to construct risk scores for 3628 breast cancer cases and 5190 controls from the UK2 GWAS of breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4229095") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK2 GWAS was funded by Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001832> "The second UK genome-wide association study of breast cancer, funded by the Wellcome Trust and Cancer Research UK, whose cases are women with breast cancer from UK cancer genetics clinics, recruited through the Familial Breast Cancer Study, and from UK oncology clinics, recruited through the POSH study, and whose controls come from the 1958 Birth Cohort and the UK National Blood Service, genotyped by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium 2.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among a total of 1,305 T2D controls, 633 subjects were selected from Health2 cohort according to the following inclusion criteria: (1) no past history of diabetes, (2) no anti-diabetic medicine, (3) fasting plasma glucose < 5.6 mmol/L and plasma glucose 2-h after ingestion of 75g oral glucose load < 7.8 mmol/L and (4) subjects older than 60 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Health2 cohort recruited a total of 8,500 participants aged 40-69 years from five regional cities in Korea based on the Korean Genome Epidemiologic Study (KoGES) project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KNIH H2T2DS Affy 6.0 Call rate > 0.95 IMPUTE V1.0 HapMap build 36 release 22 (CHB+JPT) proper_info > 0.5 na na") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KNIH H2T2DS Korean 1183 1305 2488 Population-based") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Remaining 672 T2D controls were selected from Health Examinee (HEXA) cohort shared control study that was initially designed in 2008 for the Korean cancer and coronary artery disease (CAD) GWA studies by randomly selecting approximately 3,700 of 1,200,000 subjects aged 40-69 from the HEXA cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "T2D cases were included according to the following criteria: (1) using diabetes medication, (2) fasting plasma glucose ≥ 7 mmol/L or plasma glucose 2-h after ingestion of 75g oral glucose load ≥ 11.1 mmol/L and (3) age of disease onset ≥ 40 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001834> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of Korean adults contributed by the Korea National Institute of Health to the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes meta-analysis. Its cases, with type 2 diabetes of onset at age 40 or older, were drawn from the population-based Health2 cohort of the Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study; its controls, without diabetes or anti-diabetic medication and with normal fasting glucose, came partly from the Health2 cohort (those older than 60 with a normal oral glucose tolerance test) and partly from the Health Examinee (HEXA) shared control study. It was genotyped genome-wide on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001835> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001835>)

