AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29937543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29937543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6068188/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were invited into the study after they became aware of their mutation carrier status through a clinical genetic test.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001850> "An ongoing nationwide retrospective cohort study with prospective follow-up of members of families carrying BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations in the Netherlands, begun in 1999, whose participants are invited once they learn their carrier status through clinical genetic testing at the Dutch university medical centres and family cancer clinics. It is run by the Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Research Group Netherlands, coordinated by the Netherlands Cancer Institute in Amsterdam, and collects data through questionnaires, medical records and linkage with the Netherlands Cancer Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29937543") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36271417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29937543") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6068188/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Questionnaires, clinical records and linkages with the Netherlands Cancer Registry were used to collect data on IVF exposure, risk-reducing surgeries and cancer diagnosis, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001850> "An ongoing nationwide retrospective cohort study with prospective follow-up of members of families carrying BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations in the Netherlands, begun in 1999, whose participants are invited once they learn their carrier status through clinical genetic testing at the Dutch university medical centres and family cancer clinics. It is run by the Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Research Group Netherlands, coordinated by the Netherlands Cancer Institute in Amsterdam, and collects data through questionnaires, medical records and linkage with the Netherlands Cancer Registry.")
