# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11698837/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were initially recruited to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and risk of adult diseases [24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11698837/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hertfordshire Cohort Study (HCS) is a population-based sample of men and women born between 1931 and 1939 in Hertfordshire, UK who still lived there at the time of the study [24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12942649/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Given the importance of nutrition to musculoskeletal health at older ages, we therefore evaluated the stability of diet quality in the Hertfordshire Cohort Study over a median of 17 years, from around the age of 65 up until the ninth decade.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12942649/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 178 individuals provided diet quality scores derived in 1998–2004, 2011 and 2017 (median age 64.0, 74.7 and 80.7) using principal component analysis of food frequency questionnaires") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39751886") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41754086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12942649/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hertfordshire Cohort Study consists of 1579 men and 1418 women who were born in Hertfordshire (UK) from 1931–1939, and who still lived there in 1998–2004 when they completed a home interview and clinic visit for a detailed health assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001855> "A population-based cohort of men and women born in 1931–1939 in Hertfordshire, United Kingdom, who still lived there in 1998–2004, when they completed a home interview and a clinic visit for a detailed health assessment, and some of whom were followed up in later waves, recruited initially to investigate the relationship between growth in infancy and the risk of adult diseases and since used to study musculoskeletal and general health in older age.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35995766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35995766") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9395431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HERITAGE enrolled a combination of self-identified white and Black family units, totaling 763 sedentary participants (38% Black) between the ages of 17–65 years, in a 20-week, graded endurance exercise training study across four clinical centers in the US and Canada in 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856> "A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35995766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7674877+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A consortium of five universities in the United States and Canada are involved in carrying out the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856> "A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35995766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7674877+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 90 Caucasian families and 40 African-American families with both parents and three or more biological adult offspring are being recruited, tested, exercise-trained in the laboratory with the same program for 20 wk, and re-tested.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856> "A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35995766") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7674877") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7674877+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HERITAGE family study (HEalth, RIsk factors, exercise Training And GEnetics) will document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic, and hormonal responses to aerobic exercise training.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001856> "A family study, run by a consortium of universities in the United States and Canada, of sedentary white and Black families (both parents and adult offspring aged 17 to 65) who were tested, put through the same 20-week graded aerobic exercise training programme and re-tested, designed to document the role of the genotype in the cardiovascular, metabolic and hormonal responses to regular exercise.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19351941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19351941") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2916661/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Usual care plus aerobic exercise training, consisting of 36 supervised sessions followed by home-based training, or usual care alone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857> "A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19351941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7738407/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HF-ACTION was a National Institute of Health funded randomized clinical trial that took place at 82 centers within the United States, Canada, and France from April 2003 through February 2007, enrolling a total of 2331 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857> "A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19351941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7738407/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the trial was to compare usual HFrEF care to usual HFrEF care plus exercise training, but it included a genetic sub-study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857> "A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19351941") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7738407/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial included adult HFrEF patients with LVEF ≤ 35% and NYHA class II to IV symptoms despite optimal heart failure therapy for at least 6 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001857> "A randomized controlled trial, funded by the US National Institutes of Health, that enrolled adult patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (left ventricular ejection fraction ≤35%) and NYHA class II-IV symptoms despite optimal therapy, at 82 centers in the United States, Canada and France from April 2003 to February 2007, comparing usual heart-failure care with usual care plus supervised and then home-based aerobic exercise training, and including a genetic sub-study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Approximately 4,200 twins aged 40-93 (μ=64, σ=7.9; 27.2% males), took part in a 2 years follow up the HLQ.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Attitude Ideology - US 1990 (MATR) 50 item scale (e.g., gun control, welfare, immigration, school prayer) 4,040") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample is a follow up of the 1988 MATR study above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4038932/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample, previously dubbed the Virginia 30K, consists of 29,682 individuals (8,636 families), including twins (14,753), non-twin siblings (3,184), parents (2,362), offspring spouses (4,390) and other relatives (4,993) aged 18-96 years (μ=49.5, σ=17.6; 43% males).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A large questionnaire on “Health and Life Styles” (HLQ), which contained measures of political attitudes and life events, among many other traits, was administered to the population in the late 1980’s.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24569950") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24860199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4031194/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population was drawn from Virginia’s Vital Records Office and further supplemented by a national mailer sent to the American Association of Retired Persons") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001858> "A 1990 follow-up survey of the twins of the Virginia 30,000 study of twins and their relatives (the 1988 Mid Atlantic Twin Registry study, a kinship sample drawn from Virginia's vital records and supplemented by a national mailing to members of the American Association of Retired Persons, which had answered a Health and Life Styles questionnaire in the late 1980s), in which twins aged 40 to 93 were surveyed again about two years later on many of the same measures, including a Wilson-Patterson inventory of political attitudes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HISLA stage 1 includes 17 studies and one consortium (Consortium for the Analysis of the Diversity and Evolution of Latin America [CANDELA]17)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hispanic/Latino Anthropometry (HISLA) Consortium is comprised of 27 studies/consortia of adult participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The studies of the HISLA Consortium were meta-analyzed in two stages: discovery (stage 1) and replication (stage 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address this knowledge gap, we analyzed densely imputed genetic data in a sample of Hispanic/Latino adults to identify and fine-map genetic variants associated with body mass index (BMI), height, and BMI-adjusted waist-to-hip ratio (WHRadjBMI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35399580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8990175/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru, or the US with self-reported heritage from across Spanish-speaking Latin America, or Native American heritage, primarily Pima and Zuni25 (Table S1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001860> "A consortium of studies and consortia of adults of Hispanic/Latino heritage, or of Native American heritage, from Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Peru and the United States, among them the CANDELA consortium, that meta-analyses their genome-wide association results in discovery and replication stages to find and fine-map genetic loci for anthropometric traits such as body mass index, height and waist-to-hip ratio.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Epidemiological data were obtained from questionnaires, and information on tumor stage and histology was obtained from pathology and clinical reports.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Interviews were conducted at either the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School, and peripheral blood was collected for the extraction of DNA from white blood cells.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hannover-Jena Endometrial Cancer Study (HJECS), a hospital-based case-control study, included 250 German women, aged 31-89 years, who were recruited either at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after having been diagnosed with histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM302_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BECS/HJECS | Bavarian Endometrial Cancer Study/Hannover-Jena Endometrial Cancer Study | Germany; hospital-based cases, population-based cases |  | Illumina Infinium iSelect | 137 | 112") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the iCOGS genotyping stage, 4,330 women with a confirmed diagnosis of endometrial cancer and European ancestry were recruited via 11 studies in Western Europe, North America and Australia, collectively called the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001861> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Germany, whose cases were women aged 31–89 recruited at the Friedrich Schiller University of Jena or at Hannover Medical School after a diagnosis of histologically confirmed primary incident endometrial carcinoma between 2004 and 2010, who were interviewed there and gave peripheral blood for DNA, with epidemiological data from questionnaires and tumour stage and histology from pathology and clinical reports. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")

