AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the Healthy Nevada Project undergo written and informed consent to having genetic information associated with electronic health information (EHR) in a de-identified manner.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase II was initiated in 2018, using the Helix Exome+ platform (Helix, San Diego, CA, United States).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HNP is a population health study of Nevadans, with specific targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically depressed Northern Nevada areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Healthy Nevada Project (HNP), a population health study developed in collaboration between Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno, Nevada, was established in 2016 to examine the effects genetics may have on Nevadan health outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Renown Health EHR system was instantiated in 2007 on the EPIC system (EPIC System Corporation, Verona, WI, United States), and contains lab results, diagnosis codes (ICD9/ICD10), and sociodemographic information of approximately 1.6 million hospital patient visits from 2005 to the present date.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33763119") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7982958/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project consists of two phases: Phase I began in 2016, in which genotyping was conducted on 10,000 adult volunteer participants as described in Read et al.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001869> "A population health study of adult volunteers in Nevada, established in 2016 by Renown Health and the Desert Research Institute in Reno with targeted recruitment in rural and socioeconomically deprived areas of northern Nevada, that links participants' genetic data (genotyping from 2016, Helix Exome+ sequencing from 2018) with their Renown Health electronic health records.")

