AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HAW Hawaii Ovarian Cancer Study United States Rapid case ascertainment through Hawaii Tumor Registry from 1993 onwards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001870> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer in Hawaii, USA, whose cases were identified by rapid case ascertainment through the Hawaii Tumor Registry from 1993 to 2008 and whose controls were randomly selected from the Hawaii Department of Health's annual survey of representative households and matched to cases on age and ethnicity, with data collected by interview; one of the member studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Randomly selected from Hawaii Department of Health Annual Survey of the representative households.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001870> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer in Hawaii, USA, whose cases were identified by rapid case ascertainment through the Hawaii Tumor Registry from 1993 to 2008 and whose controls were randomly selected from the Hawaii Department of Health's annual survey of representative households and matched to cases on age and ethnicity, with data collected by interview; one of the member studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.668/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng668_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2663409/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested the hypothesis that these SNPs were associated with the risk of ovarian cancer in a population-based case–control study in Hawaii, including 367 histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian cancer cases and 602 age- and ethnicity-matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001870> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer in Hawaii, USA, whose cases were identified by rapid case ascertainment through the Hawaii Tumor Registry from 1993 to 2008 and whose controls were randomly selected from the Hawaii Department of Health's annual survey of representative households and matched to cases on age and ethnicity, with data collected by interview; one of the member studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19768735") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8612442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19768735") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19768735+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hoorn study is a population-based cohort study on glucose metabolism and vascular disease initiated in 1989, with follow-up examinations in 1996-1998, 2000-2001 and 2005-2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871> "A population-based cohort study of glucose metabolism and vascular disease in the Netherlands, begun in 1989 with men and women aged 50-74 randomly selected from the population register of the town of Hoorn, who underwent oral glucose tolerance tests and were re-examined in 1996-1998, 2000-2001 and 2005-2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19768735") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8612442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8720611+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A survey of glucose tolerance was conducted in subjects aged 50-74 years, randomly selected from the registry of the middle-sized town of Hoorn in the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871> "A population-based cohort study of glucose metabolism and vascular disease in the Netherlands, begun in 1989 with men and women aged 50-74 randomly selected from the population register of the town of Hoorn, who underwent oral glucose tolerance tests and were re-examined in 1996-1998, 2000-2001 and 2005-2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19768735") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8612442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8720611+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on the mean values of two oral glucose tolerance tests subjects were classified in categories of glucose tolerance according to the World Health Organization criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871> "A population-based cohort study of glucose metabolism and vascular disease in the Netherlands, begun in 1989 with men and women aged 50-74 randomly selected from the population register of the town of Hoorn, who underwent oral glucose tolerance tests and were re-examined in 1996-1998, 2000-2001 and 2005-2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19768735") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8612442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8720611") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6448924/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The mean baseline age of the total study population was 60.3 (6.9) years and 54.6% were male.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001871> "A population-based cohort study of glucose metabolism and vascular disease in the Netherlands, begun in 1989 with men and women aged 50-74 randomly selected from the population register of the town of Hoorn, who underwent oral glucose tolerance tests and were re-examined in 1996-1998, 2000-2001 and 2005-2007.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165492/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3013232/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3454462/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this study was to describe the associations of aspirin, NA-NSAIDs, or acetaminophen use with ovarian cancer risk, using the data from Hormones and Ovarian Cancer Prediction (HOPE) study, the second-largest population-based case-control study on ovarian cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer run from the University of Pittsburgh, which enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer diagnosed from 2003 who lived in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and western New York State, identified from hospital tumour registries, clinical practices and pathology databases, and interviewed participants at home.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165492/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3013232/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3454462/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study protocol was approved by the University of Pittsburgh Institutional Review Board and by the human subject committees at each hospital where cases were identified.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer run from the University of Pittsburgh, which enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer diagnosed from 2003 who lived in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and western New York State, identified from hospital tumour registries, clinical practices and pathology databases, and interviewed participants at home.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165492/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3013232/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were identified from hospital tumor registries, clinical practices, and pathology databases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer run from the University of Pittsburgh, which enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer diagnosed from 2003 who lived in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and western New York State, identified from hospital tumour registries, clinical practices and pathology databases, and interviewed participants at home.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165492/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3013232/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants completed interviews at home with trained interviewers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer run from the University of Pittsburgh, which enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer diagnosed from 2003 who lived in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and western New York State, identified from hospital tumour registries, clinical practices and pathology databases, and interviewed participants at home.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165492/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3013232/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41416-026-03508-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HOPE study enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube, or peritoneal cancer between 2003 and 2008 who were residents of the contiguous region consisting of Western Pennsylvania, Eastern Ohio, and Western New York State [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001872> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer run from the University of Pittsburgh, which enrolled women with primary epithelial ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer diagnosed from 2003 who lived in western Pennsylvania, eastern Ohio and western New York State, identified from hospital tumour registries, clinical practices and pathology databases, and interviewed participants at home.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Coronary artery disease was defined as coronary artery stenosis 50 % or greater, old or acute myocardial infarction, or sudden cardiac death caused by plaque rupture and thrombosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874> "A Finnish forensic autopsy series of men aged 35 to 69 who died out of hospital, combining consecutive autopsies in Helsinki in 1991-1992 (the Helsinki Sudden Death Study) and in Tampere in 2001-2004 (the Tampere Coronary Study), in which coronary artery disease was assessed at autopsy from coronary stenosis of 50% or more, old or acute myocardial infarction, or sudden cardiac death from plaque rupture and thrombosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3396/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3396_MOESM57_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Helsinki Sudden Death Study (HSDS) and Tampere Coronary Study (TCS) are a series of consecutive forensic autopsies of men aged 35-69 who died out of hospital in Helsinki between 1991 and 1992 (HSDS) or in Tampere between 2001 and 2004 (TCS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001874> "A Finnish forensic autopsy series of men aged 35 to 69 who died out of hospital, combining consecutive autopsies in Helsinki in 1991-1992 (the Helsinki Sudden Death Study) and in Tampere in 2001-2004 (the Tampere Coronary Study), in which coronary artery disease was assessed at autopsy from coronary stenosis of 50% or more, old or acute myocardial infarction, or sudden cardiac death from plaque rupture and thrombosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001875> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001875>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For stage 2 replication, we genotyped 96 SNPs selected from stage 1 in three independent Chinese Han populations with 6,570 T2D case subjects and 6,947 control subjects from the GBTDS, BTDS, and HTDS studies using TaqMan SNP Genotyping Assays (Applied Biosystems, Foster City, CA) in the Fludigm EP1 platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001875> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of unrelated Han Chinese from Hubei province, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, genotyped as one of three independent replication populations in a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese Hans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3526061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stage 2 samples for replication testing of 96 single nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) consisted of 13,517 unrelated Chinese Hans (6,570 T2D case and 6,947 nondiabetic control subjects) from the Guizhou-Bijie Type 2 Diabetes Study (GBTDS), the Beijing Type 2 Diabetes Studies (BTDS), and the Hubei Type 2 Diabetes Studies (HTDS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001875> "A type 2 diabetes case-control sample of unrelated Han Chinese from Hubei province, China, made up of people with type 2 diabetes and nondiabetic controls, genotyped as one of three independent replication populations in a genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese Hans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001876> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001876>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30224653") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23372812") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3555935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, families were identified through essential hypertensive probands, categorised within the upper 5% of the population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001876> "A family cohort of white British nuclear and extended families from Oxford, United Kingdom, recruited from 1993 through a proband with essential hypertension in the upper 5% of the blood pressure distribution, with other family members collected regardless of their blood pressure, for quantitative genetic study of hypertension, left ventricular mass and other cardiovascular risk factors; families were recalled for further cardiovascular phenotyping, including electrocardiography, echocardiography and cardiac magnetic resonance imaging.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23372812") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30224653") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31537879") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30224653") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0205-x/MediaObjects/41588_2018_205_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HTO |  | population-based  | This family study in which probands were ascertained based on blood pressure, and family members were collected regardless of case or control status. | U.K Oxford cohort | 1265 | [PMID 18852390]") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001876> "A family cohort of white British nuclear and extended families from Oxford, United Kingdom, recruited from 1993 through a proband with essential hypertension in the upper 5% of the blood pressure distribution, with other family members collected regardless of their blood pressure, for quantitative genetic study of hypertension, left ventricular mass and other cardiovascular risk factors; families were recalled for further cardiovascular phenotyping, including electrocardiography, echocardiography and cardiac magnetic resonance imaging.")
