# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35252394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8888857/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data originate from the multicenter international study “HYPERGENES–European Network for Genetic-Epidemiological Studies: building a method to dissect complex genetic traits, using essential hypertension as a disease model,” funded by the European Union 7th Framework Programme (grant HEALTH-2007-201550) (18).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Regarding the present work, cases and controls were recruited within specific cohorts/networks: FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A classical two-stage case-control strategy was employed with a discovery phase of 1,865 cases and 1,750 controls (2,294 males, 1,321 females), all genotyped on the Illumina 1M Duo chip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls were recruited from extensively characterized cohorts using standardized clinical ascertainment, collected over many years in different European regions (balanced within North Europe, Continental Italy and Sardinia).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to perform a genetic association with continuous BP phenotypes, we considered two additional cohorts (FLEMENGHO-EPOGH, n=1514 and WHSS, n=306, see methods S2 (please see http://hyper.ahajournals.org) that provided population-based data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature11401/MediaObjects/41586_2012_BFnature11401_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272453/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HYPERGENES Project investigated associations between genetic variants and essential hypertension pursuing a two-stage study by recruiting cases and controls from extensively characterized cohorts recruited over many years in different European regions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001882> "A European Union Seventh Framework Programme project on the genetics of essential hypertension, coordinated from the University of Milan, that assembled hypertensive cases, normotensive controls and population samples from extensively characterised cohorts in different European regions (northern Europe, continental Italy and Sardinia), among them the FLEMENGHO/EPOGH cohort, the Wandsworth Heart and Stroke Study, the Milano-Sassari cohort and the SOPHIA cohort, for a two-stage genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001884> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001884>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3837431/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0090-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_90_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22472876") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3837431/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "i2b2 Center (Informatics for Integrating Biology and the Bedside), an NIH-funded National Center for Biomedical Computing based at Partners HealthCare System") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001884> "A major depressive disorder case-control sample of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium from the Partners HealthCare System in the United States, assembled with the i2b2 (Informatics for Integrating Biology and the Bedside) centre, whose cases were identified by natural language processing of electronic medical records with psychiatrist review (an ICD-9 diagnosis of major depressive disorder, confirmed on record review, with depression either responsive to an SSRI or unresponsive to at least two antidepressant trials) and whose controls came from neuroimaging studies, screened by self-reported psychiatric history.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3837431/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0090-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_90_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0090-3/MediaObjects/41588_2018_90_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "i2b2-TRD 13 | i2b3 | USA | Natural language processing of EMR; psychiatrist review | Controls from neuroimaging studies; self-report psychiatric history | ICD-9 MDD, EMR review, SSRI-responsive or unresponsive to ≥2 AD trials | BIP, NAP | MDD, BIP, NAP, SUDS, psych medication use") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001884> "A major depressive disorder case-control sample of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium from the Partners HealthCare System in the United States, assembled with the i2b2 (Informatics for Integrating Biology and the Bedside) centre, whose cases were identified by natural language processing of electronic medical records with psychiatrist review (an ICD-9 diagnosis of major depressive disorder, confirmed on record review, with depression either responsive to an SSRI or unresponsive to at least two antidepressant trials) and whose controls came from neuroimaging studies, screened by self-reported psychiatric history.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001887> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001887>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15770118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18331377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15770118") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15770118+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AD was assessed among 1201 probands and affected siblings with use of the Semi-Structured Assessment for the Genetics of Alcoholism and among 213 parents with use of a modified version of the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001887> "A family study of alcohol dependence in Ireland and Northern Ireland that between 1998 and 2002 recruited probands meeting DSM-IV criteria for alcohol dependence, ascertained in community alcoholism treatment facilities and public and private hospitals and with all four grandparents born in Ireland or Great Britain, together with their siblings and parents, all interviewed by clinically trained interviewers, probands and siblings with a modified Semi-Structured Assessment for the Genetics of Alcoholism and parents with a modified Structured Clinical Interview for DSM.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15770118") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18331377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41593-018-0275-1/MediaObjects/41593_2018_275_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18331377") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2665790/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After a prospective family was identified through probands, parents and potentially affected siblings whom the probands provided permission to contact were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001887> "A family study of alcohol dependence in Ireland and Northern Ireland that between 1998 and 2002 recruited probands meeting DSM-IV criteria for alcohol dependence, ascertained in community alcoholism treatment facilities and public and private hospitals and with all four grandparents born in Ireland or Great Britain, together with their siblings and parents, all interviewed by clinically trained interviewers, probands and siblings with a modified Semi-Structured Assessment for the Genetics of Alcoholism and parents with a modified Structured Clinical Interview for DSM.")
