# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6966793/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sixty-six percent of participants were enrolled through one of five ongoing nationwide studies in the UK and Ireland (Epidemiological Study of Familial Breast Cancer [EMBRACE]), France (Gene Etude Prospective Sein Ovaire [GENEPSO]), Netherlands (Hereditary Breast and Ovarian cancer study Netherlands [HEBON]), Australia and New Zealand (kConFab), and Austria (Medical University of Vienna [MUV]).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6966793/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were invited to complete a baseline questionnaire and a series of follow-up questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6966793/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The questionnaires requested detailed information on known or suspected risk factors for breast and ovarian cancer, including family history, reproductive history, and surgical interventions including RRM or RRSO.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7521995/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, where possible, passive follow-up by pathology (Denmark and Netherlands), cancer and death registry linkage (Denmark, Netherlands, Sweden and the United Kingdom), and validation of self-reported cancer diagnoses and preventive surgeries") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7521995/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IBCCS study participants were recruited between 1997 and 2011 from 18 European cancer genetics centres and Quebec, Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1186/bcr93") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IBCCS study includes data both from large parallel studies being conducted in the UK, Netherlands, and France, and from small individual centers in which the IBCCS is providing the impetus and some resources to collect the necessary data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001889> "An international collaborative prospective cohort study of carriers of BRCA1 or BRCA2 pathogenic variants that pools nationwide and centre-based carrier studies, including EMBRACE in the United Kingdom and Ireland, GENEPSO in France and HEBON in the Netherlands and smaller studies in other European countries and Quebec, Canada; participants were recruited from cancer genetics centres between 1997 and 2011 and followed actively by questionnaire and, where possible, by pathology, cancer and death registry linkage and medical records, to study breast and ovarian cancer risks and their modifiers in carriers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001890> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001890>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26732427") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the study donated a blood sample and answered a lifestyle questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001890> "A case-control sample of Icelanders assembled by deCODE genetics for genome-wide association studies of urinary bladder cancer, with cases identified through the Icelandic Cancer Registry and recruited from 2001 by trained nurses through special recruitment clinics, donating a blood sample and answering a lifestyle questionnaire, and controls drawn from other ongoing genome-wide studies at deCODE.")
