AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26732427") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Records of all UBC diagnoses were obtained from the Icelandic Cancer Registry (ICR) (http://www.krabbameinsskra.is).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001890> "A case-control sample of Icelanders assembled by deCODE genetics for genome-wide association studies of urinary bladder cancer, with cases identified through the Icelandic Cancer Registry and recruited from 2001 by trained nurses through special recruitment clinics, donating a blood sample and answering a lifestyle questionnaire, and controls drawn from other ongoing genome-wide studies at deCODE.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26732427") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment of UBC cases was initiated in 2001 and included all prevalent cases as well as newly diagnosed cases from that time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001890> "A case-control sample of Icelanders assembled by deCODE genetics for genome-wide association studies of urinary bladder cancer, with cases identified through the Icelandic Cancer Registry and recruited from 2001 by trained nurses through special recruitment clinics, donating a blood sample and answering a lifestyle questionnaire, and controls drawn from other ongoing genome-wide studies at deCODE.")
