AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After chart review, 121 participants were identified as having ALC and 470 patients with MASLD-cirrhosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Chronic liver disease cases were identified using ICD9/10 liver disease–specific codes and subsequently confirmed via electronic medical chart review (N=1033).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrolled participants’ medical information is obtained from the Indiana Network for Patient Care research database.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Indiana Biobank cohort participants were recruited in-person from participating clinics and consented to research under IB protocol approved by Institutional Review Boards at respective institutes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Liver disease–free controls from the Indiana Biobank (IB-Liver cohort) were identified as those without a liver-specific ICD9/10 code or laboratory data, suggesting a risk for liver injury or disease (ie, abnormal AST, alanine aminotransferase tests, positive HBsAg, or hepatitis C antibody).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38727677") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11093576/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IB-liver participants were recruited through the Indiana Biobank, which is a centralized statewide biobanking initiative at Indiana University, Purdue University, and the University of Notre Dame.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001891> "A case-control sample drawn from the Indiana Biobank, the statewide biobank of Indiana University, Purdue University and the University of Notre Dame whose participants are recruited in person from participating clinics and linked to the Indiana Network for Patient Care, comprising participants with chronic liver disease identified from ICD-9/10 codes and confirmed by chart review, among them patients with cirrhosis attributed to alcohol or to metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease, and liver disease-free controls without liver-specific codes or abnormal liver tests, assembled for genetic studies of cirrhosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each patient in the IBSEN cohort was matched for age and sex with five controls from the same geographical area at the time of diagnosis, randomly drawn from the Norwegian Population Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> "A population-based inception cohort of all patients newly diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease (ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease) from 1990 to 1993 while living in four counties of south-eastern Norway, each matched for age and sex with five controls drawn from the Norwegian Population Register, set up to establish the incidence of the disease in the region and followed prospectively for its natural course at 1, 5, 10, 20 and 30 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, the population-based inception cohort included 519 patients with UC and 237 with CD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> "A population-based inception cohort of all patients newly diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease (ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease) from 1990 to 1993 while living in four counties of south-eastern Norway, each matched for age and sex with five controls drawn from the Norwegian Population Register, set up to establish the incidence of the disease in the region and followed prospectively for its natural course at 1, 5, 10, 20 and 30 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "all newly diagnosed IBD patients from January 1, 1990 to December 31, 1993 residing in four geographically well-defined areas [counties] in Southeast Norway were included.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> "A population-based inception cohort of all patients newly diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease (ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease) from 1990 to 1993 while living in four counties of south-eastern Norway, each matched for age and sex with five controls drawn from the Norwegian Population Register, set up to establish the incidence of the disease in the region and followed prospectively for its natural course at 1, 5, 10, 20 and 30 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12791208/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were enrolled prospectively over a 4-year period, from January 1, 1990, to December 31, 1993, based on established international diagnostic criteria and a follow-up protocol encompassing 1, 5, 10, 20, and 30-year intervals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> "A population-based inception cohort of all patients newly diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease (ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease) from 1990 to 1993 while living in four counties of south-eastern Norway, each matched for age and sex with five controls drawn from the Norwegian Population Register, set up to establish the incidence of the disease in the region and followed prospectively for its natural course at 1, 5, 10, 20 and 30 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36239614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41531802") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12791208/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Inflammatory Bowel Disease in South-Eastern Norway (IBSEN) study group was initially established to ascertain the precise incidence of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) within a specific region of Norway, thereby contributing to a global initiative aimed at elucidating the increasing prevalence of these conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001892> "A population-based inception cohort of all patients newly diagnosed with inflammatory bowel disease (ulcerative colitis or Crohn's disease) from 1990 to 1993 while living in four counties of south-eastern Norway, each matched for age and sex with five controls drawn from the Norwegian Population Register, set up to establish the incidence of the disease in the region and followed prospectively for its natural course at 1, 5, 10, 20 and 30 years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4856228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recently, we integrated the reengineered TCCR with other registries, developed by the Biomedical Informatics Core Facility at the Fred and Pamela Buffett Cancer Center under the umbrella of the integrated Cancer Data Repository for Cancer research (iCaRe2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4856228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TCCR core data elements have formed the Common Core Questionnaire shared among all iCaRe2 registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4856228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first two registries, namely, Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry (PCCR) and the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry (BCCR), were described previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4856228/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To achieve this goal, we have been developing collaborative cancer-specific registries for the standardized collection of comprehensive demographic, lifestyle, physical activity, dietary habits, family history, and quality of life (QoL) data, as well as data on medical history, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6611482/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The collection of data and specimen used in this study was supported by the integrated Cancer Repository for Cancer Research (iCaRe2), developed and maintained by the Biomedical Informatics Core and the Clinical Trials Office at the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27168721") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31303884") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38672660") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11048743/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The US-based BC-positive cases (n = 321) were sourced from the integrated Cancer Repository for Cancer Research (iCaRe2) and the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry (BCCR), situated in the Midwestern United States [19].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001893> "An umbrella repository of collaborative cancer-specific registries, among them the Pancreatic Cancer Collaborative Registry, the Breast Cancer Collaborative Registry and the Thyroid Cancer and Tumor Collaborative Registry, developed and maintained by the Fred & Pamela Buffett Cancer Center at the University of Nebraska Medical Center in Omaha, through which participating hospitals in the Midwestern United States enrol cancer patients, high-risk individuals and controls and collect questionnaire data on a common core of demographic, lifestyle, family history and quality-of-life items, clinical and follow-up data and biospecimens for cancer research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001894> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001894>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29666432") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28072414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5545718/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were then genotyped at the Broad Institute.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001894> "A consortium of investigators in the United States, the United Kingdom and Sweden, established to accelerate genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder and its clinical subtypes by applying high-throughput phenotyping methods, which brings together bipolar disorder cases and unaffected controls from the Sweden Bipolar Disorder Cohort, the Bipolar Disorder Research Network in the United Kingdom, a University of Southern California collection and a Massachusetts General Hospital collection identified from electronic health records, all genotyped at the Broad Institute.")
