# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The collaborative work of the consortium has led to a repository of samples (DNA, plasma, and serum) of more than 17,000 subjects from two major ethnic groups in India (Indo-European and Dravidians) that have been well-characterized for anthropometric and clinical markers (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The consortium monitors the effects of urbanization on a population-in-transition by re-sampling at regular intervals from the same geographical locations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary goal of INDICO is to build resources and generate information to understand role of genetic, epigenetic as well as environmental factors in pathogenesis of T2D.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The time range of sample collection (2003–2011) coincides with the rapid increase in the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) growth of the Indian economy (World Development Indicator 2011).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11568-011-9157-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, we initiated a nation-wide collaborative effort by establishing the INdian DIabetes COnsortium (INDICO) for the systematic, comprehensive, and large-scale studies towards the understanding of T2D in India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23209189") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3581193/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control group included subjects who met the following criteria: 1) ≥40 years of age; 2) HbA1c level ≤6.0%; 3) fasting plasma glucose level <110 mg/dL (6.1 mmol/L); 4) no family history of diabetes in first-degree relatives; and 5) urban dwellers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23209189") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3581193/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects included randomly selected subjects with a 2-h plasma glucose level <140 mg/dL (7.8 mmol/L) and fasting plasma glucose <100 mg/dL (5.6 mmol/L).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23205164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23209189") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3581193/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were recruited based on the criteria as in stage 1, except that the fasting glucose level <100 mg/dL (5.6 mmol/L) was considered as the cutoff for subjects with missing information about HbA1c levels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001919> "A nationwide collaborative biorepository of DNA, plasma and serum from people with and without type 2 diabetes in India's two major ethnic groups (Indo-European and Dravidian speakers), collected from 2003 to 2011 with anthropometric and clinical measurements by the Indian Diabetes Consortium to study the genetic, epigenetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes in Indians undergoing socioeconomic transition, re-sampling the same areas at intervals to follow the effects of urbanisation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, cases and controls originate from the following population based or prospective cohort studies in agricultural dust and/or animal exposed environments: the Danish SUS study90,91 , the Dutch Omega92,93 and Veterinarian’s Health Study94 ;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prevalent cases and industry, gender and age matched study‐specific controls were included for the GWAS initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The populations come from industries with exposure to known major allergens and irritants; high molecular weight sensitizers (wheat flour, fungal alpha amylase, animal allergens), low molecular weight sensitizers (isocyanate monomers and oligomers) and irritants and inflammatory agents (isocyanates, organic dust, endotoxins, wood).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study base consists of several pooled surveys on occupational asthma from Denmark and The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "in wheat and amylase exposed environments: the bakers from the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project95 ;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "in wood dust exposed environments: workers in the Danish furniture industry of the Danish Wood Dust Cohort;96,97 and for isocyanate exposed workers: a population of Dutch industrial spray painters.98,99") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001920> "A Danish and Dutch occupational research group whose pooled surveys of occupational asthma, drawn from population-based or prospective cohort studies of workers exposed to allergens and irritants (agricultural dust or animals in the Danish SUS study, the Dutch Omega study and the Veterinarian’s Health Study; wheat flour and amylase in the Dutch Bakers health surveillance project; wood dust in the Danish Wood Dust Cohort of furniture workers; isocyanates in Dutch industrial spray painters), provided prevalent asthma cases and industry-, sex- and age-matched controls, as the INDUSTRIAL subgroup of the GABRIEL Consortium, to the genome-wide meta-analysis of asthma of the Trans-National Asthma Genetic Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16023150+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consortia have been initiated for head and neck cancer (International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium (INHANCE)) and lung cancer (International Lung Cancer Consortium (ILCCO)) with the aim to share comparable data, to focus on rare subgroups such as nonsmokers and to coordinate laboratory analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5131845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population comprised 6,034 cases and 6,585 controls derived from 12 epidemiological studies, the majority of case-control design and part of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium (INHANCE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5131845/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer in 6,034 cases and 6,585 controls from Europe, North America and South America;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28945835") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a pooled analysis using data from five studies within the INHANCE Consortium [15]: Milan (Italy), Rome (Italy), Western Europe involving three Italian centres [Aviano (Friuli Venezia Giulia), Padua (Veneto), Turin (Piemonte)], Sao Paulo (Brazil) and Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42011792") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The pooled analysis included 16 studies from the database with available individual‐level data on smoking cessation and all covariates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16023150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13340975/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5834132/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3060072/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To further investigate common genetic variation and susceptibility to UADT cancers, we have performed a genome-wide association study within the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology (INHANCE) consortium,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001922> "An international consortium of research groups leading epidemiological studies of head and neck cancer, mostly case–control studies in North and South America, Europe and Asia, which pools their individual-level data in a common database to share comparable data, study rare subgroups such as never smokers and coordinate laboratory analyses of the causes of head and neck cancer, including genome-wide association studies of cancers of the upper aerodigestive tract.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "High-risk French-Canadian breast and/or ovarian families were recruited into a research project started in 1996, which subsequently evolved into a large ongoing interdisciplinary research program designated INHERIT BRCAs [31,32].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants from families considered in the present study were first tested for a panel of 18 truncating mutations detected or reported in the French-Canadian population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This integrated clinical research program was composed of a network of referring clinicians across the province of Quebec.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also used this data set to estimate the risks for breast and ovarian cancer conferred by BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "or the family carried a deleterious mutation already identified in the BRCA1 or BRCA2 genes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2702391/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16417652") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1413985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the family had at least four individuals with breast and/or ovarian cancer diagnosed at any age in first-degree or second-degree relatives; the family had three first-degree relatives affected with breast and/or ovarian cancer at any age;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001923> "A research programme based at the Centre Hospitalier Universitaire de Québec and Laval University, Canada, that has recruited high-risk French-Canadian families with breast and/or ovarian cancer (several affected close relatives, or a known BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutation) through a network of referring clinicians across Quebec since 1996, for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation testing and studies of inherited susceptibility to breast and ovarian cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32816869") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data for this analysis were obtained from the electronic medical records of a tertiary care center for diabetes, which has 50 branches spread across nine states of India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076730/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The India–Scotland Partnership for Precision Medicine in Diabetes (INSPIRED) brings together data resources for the study of diabetes in India and Scotland (UK).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076730/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort includes white European individuals with type 2 diabetes from the East of Scotland (the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort [ESDC]), across the regions of Tayside and Fife.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076730/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This research was funded by the National Institute for Health Research (NIHR) (INSPIRED 16/136/102) using aid from the UK government to support global health research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7437708/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35247066") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076730/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two cohorts of Asian Indians, the ICMR-INDIAB cohort (Indian Council of Medical Research-India Diabetes Study) and the DMDSC cohort (Dr Mohan’s Diabetes Specialties Centre), and one of white Europeans, the ESDC (East Scotland Diabetes Cohort), were used.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001924> "A research partnership funded by the UK National Institute for Health Research between the University of Dundee, Scotland, and Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre and Madras Diabetes Research Foundation, Chennai, India, that brings together diabetes data resources from India and Scotland, chiefly a cohort of Asian Indians with type 2 diabetes from the electronic medical records of Dr Mohan's Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC) and the East Scotland Diabetes Cohort (ESDC) of white Europeans with type 2 diabetes from Tayside and Fife, for precision-medicine studies comparing type 2 diabetes in Asian Indians and white Europeans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14555879") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22751097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36988954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15132212+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multistage cluster sampling method was used to select a nationally representative sample of 15,838 adults, aged 35-74 years, in China, and 5,350 similarly aged adults in Thailand.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> "A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14555879") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22751097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36988954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15132212+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall objective of the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA) was to estimate the prevalence and distribution of cardiovascular disease risk factors, including hypertension, hypercholesterolemia, diabetes, obesity, cigarette smoking, and physical inactivity, in the general population of both China and Thailand.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> "A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14555879") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22751097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36988954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34327424") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8315380/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The InterASIA used a 4-stage stratified sampling method to enroll 15,540 participants aged 35–74 years from 10 provinces as nationally representative sample of China in 2000–2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> "A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14555879") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22751097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36988954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "According to a uniform protocol, both InterASIA and ChinaMUCA-1998 cohorts were first followed up during 2007–08, and all three cohorts were further followed up in 2012–15 and 2018–20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> "A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14555879") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15132212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22751097") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36988954") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35195259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9076396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The validation cohorts were derived from three cohorts in the China-PAR project, including the International Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Disease in Asia (InterASIA), the China Multi-Center Collaborative Study of Cardiovascular Epidemiology (ChinaMUCA-1998), and Community Intervention of Metabolic Syndrome in China and Chinese Family Health Study (CIMIC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001925> "A population-based survey of cardiovascular disease and its risk factors (hypertension, hypercholesterolaemia, diabetes, obesity, smoking and physical inactivity) in nationally representative samples of adults aged 35–74 in China and Thailand, selected in 2000–2001 by multistage stratified cluster sampling; its Chinese participants, from ten provinces, were followed up in 2007–2008, 2012–2015 and 2018–2020 as one of the three sub-cohorts of the China-PAR project on incident atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11137634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Reexaminations using the same metrics were performed from 2014 to 2016 in 1394 participants (of 2108 invited) who attended the baseline examination at Sahlgrenska University Hospital and were still alive.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11231701/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based cohort of 3614 adult individuals, aged 25 to 77, living in Västra Götaland County, Sweden, was examined in 2001–2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11231701/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The INTERGENE research programme was initiated to study the INTERplay between GENEtic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12959171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A random sample of 8626 adults aged 24–77 years was drawn from population registers, of whom 3614 (42%) accepted the invitation and underwent baseline clinical examination between 2001 and 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12959171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were followed through inpatient and outpatient records in the Swedish National Patient Register and death records in the Swedish Cause of Death Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38809556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38983451") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41741164") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12959171/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Interplay Between Genetic Susceptibility and External Factors (INTERGENE) study is a population-based prospective cohort established in western Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001926> "A population-based prospective cohort of the INTERGENE research programme, set up to study the interplay between genetic and environmental risk factors for chronic disease, in which a random sample of adults aged 24 to 77 drawn from the population registers of an urban-rural area of western Sweden (Västra Götaland County, about half of them living in Gothenburg) was examined in 2001-2004 and re-examined in 2014-2016, with follow-up of health outcomes through linkage to the Swedish national registers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9152-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multinational case–control study, INTERPHONE, was set-up to investigate whether mobile phone use increases the risk of cancer and, more specifically, whether the RF fields emitted by mobile phones are carcinogenic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9152-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A secondary objective was to evaluate the relation between these tumours and a number of known and potential risk factors, including ionising radiation, occupational exposure to electromagnetic fields and the subject’s personal and familial medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9152-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All residents in the study regions aged 30 to 59 were eligible for the study; additional eligibility criteria, such as citizenship and proficiency in the local language were imposed in some study centres (Web Annex Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9152-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sixteen study centres in thirteen countries (Australia; Canada: Montreal, Ottawa, Vancouver; Denmark; Finland; France; Germany; Israel; Italy; Japan; New Zealand; Norway; Sweden; and the UK: North and South) participated in INTERPHONE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9152-z") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus INTERPHONE was initiated as a set of multi-national case–control studies, focusing on four types of tumour: glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17636416") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34648614") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9082802/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study period for eligible diagnoses ranged 2–4 years during 2000–04, slightly varying by country.17") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001927> "A multinational case-control study of glioma, meningioma, acoustic neurinoma and parotid gland tumours in residents aged 30 to 59, carried out with a common core protocol by sixteen centres in thirteen countries (Australia, Canada, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Israel, Italy, Japan, New Zealand, Norway, Sweden and the United Kingdom) with cases diagnosed during 2000–2004, set up to investigate whether mobile phone use and the radiofrequency fields it emits increase the risk of these tumours, and also collecting information on other potential risk factors.")

