AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5707984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is supported by three main French universities: the Universities of Bordeaux, Versailles, and Nice.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6561426/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment started in February 2013 and is still ongoing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6561426/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline inquiry collected information on students’ health, personal and family medical histories, sociodemographic characteristics and lifestyle habits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6561426/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The eligibility criteria are to be officially enrolled at a university or higher education institution; to be at least 18 years of age; to be able to read and understand French; and to provide informed consent for participation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6561426/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objectives of the i-Share cohort are to evaluate important health aspects among university students over the course of 10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29113070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31167858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6561426/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is based on the internet-based Students Health Research Enterprise (i-Share, www.i-share.fr) project, a prospective population-based cohort study of students in higher education institutions in France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001935> "An ongoing prospective internet-based cohort (e-cohort) of students aged 18 or over who are enrolled at a university or other higher education institution in France and can read French, recruiting since February 2013 with the support of the universities of Bordeaux, Versailles and Nice, which collects online questionnaires on sociodemographic and academic characteristics, health status, personal and family medical history, lifestyle and mental health to study the health of university students over ten years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1487176/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A similar questionnaire was sent to their siblings and children older than 30 y, and to the spouses of those relatives, with blood sought from all those who completed a questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1487176/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The chief acknowledgement for the ISIS study is to the patients and their relatives who collaborated, to their general practitioners, and to the medical and nursing staff from more than 100 hospitals in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1746418+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fundamental aim of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group is to assess reliably the balance of any benefits and risks for widely practicable treatments that might produce moderate but worthwhile mortality reductions in patients with suspected acute myocardial infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bmj.com/content/311/7003/471") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood was to be taken from patients in ISIS-3 immediately after randomisation but before the trial treatments and collected in a 10 ml vacutainer containing 0.12 ml preservative (15% potassium EDTA with aprotinin 0.34 mmol/l: Becton Dickinson).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.bmj.com/content/311/7003/471") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were the survivors in the United Kingdom aged 30-79 from the ISIS-3 or ISIS-4 trials who completed an epidemiological questionnaire sent to them a few months after their infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16839190") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1746418") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19567438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7647641") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7647641+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the early 1990s responses to a postal questionnaire were obtained from 13,926 survivors of myocardial infarction (cases) recently discharged from hospitals in the United Kingdom and 32,389 of their relatives (controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001936> "The programme of the International Studies of Infarct Survival (ISIS) collaborative group, which ran large randomised trials of treatments for suspected acute myocardial infarction (ISIS-1 to ISIS-4) through collaborating hospitals, and its case-control study in more than 100 UK hospitals, in which blood was taken from ISIS-3 patients on admission and, in the early 1990s, surviving patients of the ISIS-3 and ISIS-4 trials aged 30-79, their siblings and children, and those relatives' spouses, who served as controls, completed postal questionnaires on smoking and other habits and were asked for blood, for studies of smoking, blood markers and genetic variants in relation to the risk of non-fatal myocardial infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19440188+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "I-SPY 2 (investigation of serial studies to predict your therapeutic response with imaging and molecular analysis 2) is a process targeting the rapid, focused clinical development of paired oncologic therapies and biomarkers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19440188+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "I-SPY 2 is a collaborative effort among academic investigators, the National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration, and the pharmaceutical and biotechnology industries under the auspices of the Foundation for the National Institutes of Health Biomarkers Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19440188+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The framework is an adaptive phase II clinical trial design in the neoadjuvant setting for women with locally advanced breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37188791") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC10185660") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The I-SPY 2 TRIAL is an ongoing clinical trial comparing multiple novel therapeutic agents for neoadjuvant treatment of locally advanced breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42530945+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants, continuously enrolled since 2010, were adaptively randomized from February 2, 2020, to December 9, 2021, to one of several experimental neoadjuvant therapies or control groups based on receptor subtypes defined by hormone receptor (HR), ERBB2 status, and MammaPrint (Agendia Inc) molecular risk, categorized as high (MP1) or ultrahigh (MP2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42530945") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A42530945+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The I-SPY2 (Investigation of Serial Studies to Predict Your Therapeutic Response With Imaging and Molecular Analysis 2) is an ongoing randomized clinical platform trial being conducted at multiple US clinical sites including patients with early-stage (II or III) ERBB2-negative, high-risk breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001937> "An ongoing adaptive phase II platform clinical trial, run collaboratively by academic investigators, the US National Cancer Institute, the US Food and Drug Administration and industry under the Foundation for the NIH Biomarkers Consortium, conducted at multiple clinical sites in the United States with participants continuously enrolled since 2010, testing novel neoadjuvant therapeutic agents and biomarkers in women with locally advanced, high-risk breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3661655/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed genome-wide association studies (GWAS) for metabolites in the RISC study, replicated the GWAS findings in the Botnia study, and carried out Mendelian randomization analyses in RISC, EUGENE2, and Stanford IST to test the associations of genetic variants with insulin sensitivity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> "A cohort of non-diabetic adults of European ancestry pooled from studies of insulin resistance carried out at Stanford University over about ten years, whose insulin sensitivity was measured directly by the insulin suppression test (as steady-state plasma glucose) and who were genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of insulin sensitivity and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2610/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2610_MOESM4_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample was drawn from multiple studies of insulin resistance at Stanford over the last ~10 years:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> "A cohort of non-diabetic adults of European ancestry pooled from studies of insulin resistance carried out at Stanford University over about ten years, whose insulin sensitivity was measured directly by the insulin suppression test (as steady-state plasma glucose) and who were genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of insulin sensitivity and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4030103/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sample collection for the Stanford IST Cohort was carried out in part in the Clinical and Translational Research Unit, Stanford University, with funds provided by the National Center for Research Resources, NIH grant 2 M01 RR000070, and the U.S.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> "A cohort of non-diabetic adults of European ancestry pooled from studies of insulin resistance carried out at Stanford University over about ten years, whose insulin sensitivity was measured directly by the insulin suppression test (as steady-state plasma glucose) and who were genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of insulin sensitivity and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4409020") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Stanford and SAPPHIRe studies, insulin sensitivity was measured by the IST, with a readout of steady-state plasma glucose (mmol/l).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> "A cohort of non-diabetic adults of European ancestry pooled from studies of insulin resistance carried out at Stanford University over about ten years, whose insulin sensitivity was measured directly by the insulin suppression test (as steady-state plasma glucose) and who were genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of insulin sensitivity and related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23378610") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23583979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24296717") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25798622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4409020/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed GWAS data from nondiabetic participants of European ancestry from 4 studies who provided DNA for genome-wide genotyping and underwent a direct measure of insulin sensitivity (Table 1), including either euglycemic-hyperinsulinemic clamp or IST.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001939> "A cohort of non-diabetic adults of European ancestry pooled from studies of insulin resistance carried out at Stanford University over about ten years, whose insulin sensitivity was measured directly by the insulin suppression test (as steady-state plasma glucose) and who were genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of insulin sensitivity and related traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each job lasting 1 year or more, specific questions asked for a short description of the employer’s trade, the daily tasks, the machines and tools used, and a self-report about exposures of interest for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In most centres, controls were hospitalized, cancer free patients from surgery wards, eye care departments, or hematology outpatients or patients suffering from trauma injuries, gastrointestinal disorders, cardiovascular disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Cagliari and Nuoro centers, controls were a random sample of the general population 2:1 frequency matched to the incident case by 5-year age and gender groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study protocol included a questionnaire interview to the incident cases of lymphoma (any subtype) and to 2:1 age and gender frequency matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The “Gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology” (ItGxE) multicentre case-control study took place in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres, namely Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33910586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8082925/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained interviewers conducted in person interviews at the hospital or at the residence of study subjects, using a modified version of the EpiLymph questionnaire [10], designed to gather information on a number of variables, including socio-demographic data, and a lifetime occupational history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001940> "A multicentre case-control study of lymphoma of any subtype carried out in 2011–2017 in six Italian centres (Perugia, Florence, Novara, Verona, Cagliari and Nuoro in Sardinia, and Bari and Taranto in Apulia), whose cases are incident lymphoma patients and whose controls, frequency-matched to cases by age and sex, are cancer-free hospital patients in most centres and a random sample of the general population in Cagliari and Nuoro, interviewed about lifetime occupational history and other exposures to study gene-environment interactions in lymphoma etiology.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adults had been followed in the clinic since birth, and those whose medical records indicated a history of at least three episodes of wheezing, at least one of which occurred after the age of six years, were also classified as having asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described previously [29], a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire which had been validated in the Jamaican population was administered.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children from Kingston, St. Andrew, and St. Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 as part of a child development study, and again at age 18.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants’ mothers were initially recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September—October 1986.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Jamaican Adolescent Asthma Study (JAAS) is a cross-sectional study on the prevalence of asthma and allergies in 897 Jamaican adolescents [29].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23554133") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The same pipeline was used to infer local ancestry of the CAAPA BASS and JAAS studies, genotyped on the MEGA, and an additional 393 BAGS subjects, genotyped on the Omni 2.5 array but not genotyped on the ADPC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001941> "A cross-sectional study of the prevalence of asthma and allergies in Jamaican adolescents whose mothers had been recruited into the Jamaica Perinatal Mortality Survey of 1986, which included all children born in Jamaica in September–October 1986; children from Kingston, St Andrew and St Catherine were contacted at ages 11 and 16 in a child development study and again at 18, and asthma was ascertained with a modified International Study of Asthma and Allergies in Childhood (ISAAC) questionnaire validated in the Jamaican population and, for adults followed in clinic since birth, from medical records. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20011587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20011587") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2788130/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ages of the extreme old were validated with birth certificates (in the case of the JCS, the Basic Resident Registration Card).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942> "A study of exceptional longevity, approved by the ethics committee of Keio University School of Medicine, that enrols centenarians from throughout Japan, with an emphasis on semi-supercentenarians aged 105 or more whose ages are validated with the Basic Resident Registration Card, together with referent subjects (spouses of centenarians' offspring and healthy younger volunteers), and whose genotyped cases and geographically matched controls serve as a Japanese case-control set in genetic studies of extreme old age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20011587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3808698/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The JCS enrolls Japanese centenarians from throughout Japan with an emphasis upon recruiting semi-supercentenarians (age 105+ years) and referent cohort subjects comprising spouses of centenarians' offspring and healthy younger volunteers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942> "A study of exceptional longevity, approved by the ethics committee of Keio University School of Medicine, that enrols centenarians from throughout Japan, with an emphasis on semi-supercentenarians aged 105 or more whose ages are validated with the Basic Resident Registration Card, together with referent subjects (spouses of centenarians' offspring and healthy younger volunteers), and whose genotyped cases and geographically matched controls serve as a Japanese case-control set in genetic studies of extreme old age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20011587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3808698/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The JCS study protocol is approved by the Ethical Committee of Keio University School of Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942> "A study of exceptional longevity, approved by the ethics committee of Keio University School of Medicine, that enrols centenarians from throughout Japan, with an emphasis on semi-supercentenarians aged 105 or more whose ages are validated with the Basic Resident Registration Card, together with referent subjects (spouses of centenarians' offspring and healthy younger volunteers), and whose genotyped cases and geographically matched controls serve as a Japanese case-control set in genetic studies of extreme old age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20011587") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24244950") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3808698/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Japanese Centenarian Study (JCS) included 513 long lived individuals (median survival 106 years; age range 100-114) and 561 geographically matched controls (median age 75 years; range: 26-89).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001942> "A study of exceptional longevity, approved by the ethics committee of Keio University School of Medicine, that enrols centenarians from throughout Japan, with an emphasis on semi-supercentenarians aged 105 or more whose ages are validated with the Basic Resident Registration Card, together with referent subjects (spouses of centenarians' offspring and healthy younger volunteers), and whose genotyped cases and geographically matched controls serve as a Japanese case-control set in genetic studies of extreme old age.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18854865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39428694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0058618") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the purpose of this study, the Stage 1 genome-wide association study (GWAS) dataset included 2024 subjects (1008 AD cases and 1016 controls) and the Stage 2 dataset included 1870 subjects (885 AD cases and 985 controls).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> "A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer's disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer's Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease in the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18854865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39428694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2986257/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were collected by the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for AD (JGSCAD): the members are listed in our recent publications.10, 11") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> "A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer's disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer's Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease in the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18854865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39428694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2986257/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Non-demented controls living in an unassisted manner in the local community were recruited from among elderly subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> "A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer's disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer's Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease in the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18854865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39428694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2986257/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LOAD patients were clinically validated, and satisfied the criteria of the National Institute of Neurological and Communicative Disorders and Stroke-Alzheimer's Disease and Related Disorders Association for a diagnosis of probable AD.12") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> "A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer's disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer's Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease in the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18854865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23565137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39428694") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2986257/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we here assessed whether or not the genetic association of GAB2 with LOAD can be reproduced in Japanese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001944> "A case-control collection of blood samples from Japanese patients with clinically validated late-onset Alzheimer's disease meeting the NINCDS-ADRDA criteria and from elderly people without signs of dementia living unassisted in the local community, gathered by the members of the Japanese Genetic Study Consortium for Alzheimer's Disease for candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of Alzheimer's disease in the Japanese population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001947> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001947>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "De-identifiable patient samples and clinical information were collected prior to ablation procedures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001947> "A clinical case collection of the Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine that since September 2008 has collected samples and clinical information from patients over 18 years of age referred for catheter ablation of symptomatic, drug-refractory atrial fibrillation, taken before the ablation procedure, for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine Atrial Fibrillation Genetics Cohort started collecting data in September 2008 on patients >18 years of age that were referred for catheter ablation of symptomatic drug refractory atrial fibrillation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001947> "A clinical case collection of the Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine that since September 2008 has collected samples and clinical information from patients over 18 years of age referred for catheter ablation of symptomatic, drug-refractory atrial fibrillation, taken before the ablation procedure, for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001598.v3.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "present an opportunity to significantly improve our understanding of (1) The relation of paroxysmal versus persistent AF with (a) structural left atrial changes (left/right atrial scar, wall thinning, pulmonary vein anomalies, and coronary sinus dilation) and with (b) candidate genetic variants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001947> "A clinical case collection of the Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine that since September 2008 has collected samples and clinical information from patients over 18 years of age referred for catheter ablation of symptomatic, drug-refractory atrial fibrillation, taken before the ablation procedure, for genetic studies of atrial fibrillation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8060327/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study subjects were recruited from approximately 3,500 adult patients (95% Caucasian) with T1D who received care at the Joslin Clinic (Boston, MA) between 1991 and 200978–80.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11529980/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants for this research were selected from among 3,500 individuals who were enrolled into the JKS between 1991 and 2009 and were followed until 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11529980/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current research consists of 2 case-control studies nested in the JKS cohort; one included individuals with T1D and Macro-albuminuria (T1D study exploratory panel) and the other included individuals with T2D and Albuminuria (Macro and Micro) (T2D study validation panel) (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11529980/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The JKS aimed to enroll all eligible participants with albuminuria and a similar number of individuals taken randomly from a much larger pool of eligible individuals with normoalbuminuria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11529980/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The JKS is a longitudinal observational study that aims to investigate the determinants of, and") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33883567") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11529980/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "to describe the natural history of kidney function decline in, T1D and T2D in the Joslin Clinic population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001948> "A longitudinal observational study, led from the Research Division of the Joslin Diabetes Center in Boston, of adults with type 1 or type 2 diabetes attending the Joslin Clinic, enrolled in several cohorts from 1991 onwards with the aim of taking all eligible patients with albuminuria and a similar number drawn at random from those with normoalbuminuria, and followed for the development and progression of diabetic kidney disease, including kidney function decline and end-stage kidney disease.")

