# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3145913/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At Visit 2 of the Jerusalem LRC [24], information was gathered on 2544 middle-aged individuals, of whom 69.2% were randomly sampled from Visit 1 participants and 30.8% were additionally sampled from Visit 1 subjects with elevated lipid levels") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3145913/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To do so, we analyzed data from the population-based Jerusalem Lipid Research Clinic (LRC) cohort study which was initiated in the 1970s as a cardiovascular prevalence study, using protocols of the North American LRC prevalence studies [24–26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0138036") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1976–1978 (phase 1) the Jerusalem Lipid Research Clinic (LRC) Study initially examined 8646 17-y-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem, representing full age cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0138036") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Measures of BMI (in kg/m2), blood pressure, heath behaviors and biochemistry were obtained from the baseline examination and interview at mean age 30y.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0138036") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Smoking status and BMI were also obtained from the follow-up visit at mean age 43y.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21220750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22237065") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26406330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7161042") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7161042+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Jerusalem Lipid Research Clinic examined 8,646 17-yr-old youngsters and 6,952 of their parents in order to obtain information on the distribution of plasma lipids and lipoproteins in the free-living multiethnic population of Jerusalem.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001950> "A population-based cohort study in Jerusalem, Israel, begun in 1976–1979 as a cardiovascular prevalence study that followed the protocols of the North American Lipid Research Clinics prevalence studies, examining full age cohorts of 17-year-old Jewish residents of Jerusalem and many of their parents to describe plasma lipids and lipoproteins; samples of both generations were re-examined in later phases, the young participants at about 30 and 43 years of age in its longitudinal study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5003412/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As a part of a series of nationally based cooperative projects, the Millennium Genome Project (Millennium GPJ), we conducted multiple candidate gene analyses to identify susceptible genes and polymorphisms for hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5003412/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 2 other cohorts, Yokohama and Matsuyama, are derived from employees of large manufacturing industries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5003412/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita, and Nomura studies are general population-based genetic epidemiological studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3405/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3405_MOESM35_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study subjects were recruited through a community-based or company- based annual medical check-up process, and all clinical data used in this study were obtained from the personal medical check-up records of the subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20921432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21909115") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3405/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3405_MOESM35_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Japanese Millennium Genome Project comprises seven independent study cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001951> "A Japanese collaborative sample, assembled within the nationally based cooperative Millennium Genome Project for genetic studies of hypertension, that combines seven independent cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors: the Ohasama, Shigaraki, Takashima, Suita and Nomura studies, general-population studies of community residents recruited through medical check-ups, and the Yokohama and Matsuyama cohorts of employees of large manufacturing industries.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3483265/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were recruited during a one-year period between June 2006 and May 2007 as part of a larger study of severe febrile illness in children [detailed in [21], [22]].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3483265/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted in Teule district hospital, Muheza, and surrounding villages in Muheza district, Tanga region, Tanzania, where mortality in children under 5 is estimated at 165 per 1000 (Tanzanian census 2002).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A matched case-control study (children aged 3 months-10 years) was carried out in Muheza, Tanzania between 2006-2008 with the aim of identifying the genes involved in protection against severe malaria, and the sub-phenotypes acidosis, severe malarial anaemia, cerebral malaria, shock, respiratory distress and bacteraemia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to the MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 (CP1) along with those of 11 other case-control studies from a total of 11 malaria-endemic countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Joint Malaria Programme together with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine recruited severe malaria cases and healthy participants from Teule Hospital and community, respectively, in Muheza, North East Tanzania.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23144702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29381699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-north-east-tanzania/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These were individually matched to cases for tribal origin of at least one parent, electoral ward of residence and within 3 years of age to a case.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001952> "A matched case-control study of severe malaria in children aged 3 months to 10 years in Muheza, Tanga region, north-eastern Tanzania, carried out in 2006–2008 by the Joint Malaria Programme (Kilimanjaro Christian Medical Centre, Moshi) with the London School of Hygiene and Tropical Medicine. Its cases were children admitted to Teule Hospital with severe malaria, recruited within a study of severe febrile illness, and its controls were healthy children from the community individually matched on parental tribal origin, ward of residence and age; its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1 and used in candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies of severe malaria.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For example, in the early 2000s, hay fever in school children was almost non-existent in Russian Karelia, and only 2% were sensitized to birch pollen compared with 27% in Finnish Karelia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In subsequent studies, it became apparent that on the Finnish side, healthy children had a more biodiverse living environment as well as greater diversity of certain bacterial classes on their skin than atopic children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Seropositivity to some pathogens, microbial content in house dust and drinking water seemed to confer allergy protection in Russia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Finnish and Russian Karelia are adjacent areas in northern Europe, socio-economically distinct but geoclimatically similar.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Karelia Allergy Study was commenced in 1998 to characterize the allergy profiles in the two areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25772429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25772429+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The key finding was that allergic symptoms and diseases were systematically more common in Finnish children and adults than in their Russian counterparts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001954> "A study begun in 1998 that compares allergic symptoms and diseases, atopic sensitisation and their environmental and microbial determinants in children and adults of the adjacent Finnish and Russian parts of Karelia, areas that are geoclimatically similar but socio-economically distinct.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4942950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For prostate cancer, the KARUPROSTATE study includes 623 cases (new cases of prostate cancer diagnosed in Guadeloupe between 2004 and 2007) and 671 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Guadeloupe, French West Indies, carried out between 2004 and 2007, whose cases are men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in Guadeloupe in that period and whose controls are a random sample of men over 44 years old invited to the free health screening programme of the French national health insurance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4942950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In KARUPROSTATE the control group is a random sample of men aged over 44 years summoned by the national health insurance for free and systematic health screening; a recruitment bias is unlikely.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Guadeloupe, French West Indies, carried out between 2004 and 2007, whose cases are men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in Guadeloupe in that period and whose controls are a random sample of men over 44 years old invited to the free health screening programme of the French national health insurance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4942950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fourth, called KARUPROSTATE and carried out between 2004 and 2007, is a case–control study (n = 623/671).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Guadeloupe, French West Indies, carried out between 2004 and 2007, whose cases are men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in Guadeloupe in that period and whose controls are a random sample of men over 44 years old invited to the free health screening programme of the French national health insurance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785499") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27406382") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KARUPROSTATE (n=749) French West Indies Prostate Cancer Study French West Indies Case-control") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001955> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Guadeloupe, French West Indies, carried out between 2004 and 2007, whose cases are men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer in Guadeloupe in that period and whose controls are a random sample of men over 44 years old invited to the free health screening programme of the French national health insurance.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33627073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between March 2017 and December 2018, a total of 1026 independent seniors were enrolled in the KAWP and a comprehensive baseline assessment, including assessment of physical, mental, and cognitive function as well as social participation was conducted (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33627073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project (KAWP) is a longitudinal cohort study of older adults aged between 85 and 89 with no physical disability at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33627073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion criteria of KAWP are: 1) being a resident of Kawasaki city, a city with a population of 1.5 million, located in the Greater Tokyo Area and aged between 85 and 89; 2) having no limitations in the basic activities of daily living (ADL); and 3) being able to visit the study site, the Kawasaki Municipal Hospitals independently.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33627073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The prime aim of the KAWP is to explore trajectories of functional decline, frailty, and cognitive impairment, and to identify genetic, biological, behavioral, and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify this deteriorating process at an advanced age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7903371/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36691746") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10346016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cross-sectional study used data from the Kawasaki Aging and Wellbeing Project (KAWP) conducted in Kawasaki city (Kanagawa Prefecture, Japan)(21).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001956> "A prospective longitudinal cohort study of community-dwelling residents of Kawasaki City in the Greater Tokyo Area, Japan, aged 85 to 89 and without limitations in basic activities of daily living at baseline, enrolled at hospitals in the city between March 2017 and December 2018, to study the trajectories of functional decline, frailty and cognitive impairment at advanced age and the genetic, biological, behavioural and socioenvironmental factors that delay or modify them.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30862124") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion and exclusion criteria for ADD, MCI, and CU in the KBASE-V were the same as those that were in the KBASE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30862124") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The validation cohort of KBASE (KBASE-V) is an independent nationwide cohort to reconfirm new potential biomarkers that were identified in the KBASE study and is intended to find risk and prognostic factors for AD as additional studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30862124") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have recruited 71 CN participants, 96 SCD, 72 MCI, and 56 ADD in nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33436035") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among 331 participants from nine memory clinics across South Korea (KBASE-V study participants; 71 cognitively normal (CN), 99 subjective cognitive decline (SCD), 89 mild cognitive impairment (MCI), and 72 probable AD), 139 (29 CN, 58 SCD, 29 MCI, and 23 AD) agreed to provide CSF.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6463169/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33436035") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7802266/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical assessments conducted at baseline and every year for 3 years included the Korean version of the Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE) in the CERAD assessment packet [17];") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001958> "The independent, nationwide validation cohort of the Korean Brain Aging Study for the Early Diagnosis and Prediction of Alzheimer's disease (KBASE), which recruited cognitively normal people and people with subjective cognitive decline, mild cognitive impairment or Alzheimer's disease dementia at nine memory clinics across South Korea from April 2015 to August 2016 under the same criteria as KBASE, and followed them annually for three years, to reconfirm biomarkers identified in KBASE and to find risk and prognostic factors for Alzheimer's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001959> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001959>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23148692+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30177847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6120908/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The KBCP controls were carefully selected from healthy individuals of the Savo region in Eastern Finland matching individually to each BC case by age and long-term place of living, thus originating from the same genetic background as the KBCP cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001959> "A breast cancer study in eastern Finland whose cases are women seen at Kuopio University Hospital between 1990 and 1995 because of a breast lump, mammographic abnormality or other breast symptom and found to have breast cancer, and whose controls were selected from the National Population Register over the same years, matched to cases by age and long-term area of residence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23148692+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Selected from the National Population Register between 1990-1995; age and long-term area-of- residence matched to cases") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001959> "A breast cancer study in eastern Finland whose cases are women seen at Kuopio University Hospital between 1990 and 1995 because of a breast lump, mammographic abnormality or other breast symptom and found to have breast cancer, and whose controls were selected from the National Population Register over the same years, matched to cases by age and long-term area of residence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23148692+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women seen at Kuopio University Hospital between 1990-1995 because of a breast lump, mammographic abnormality, or other breast symptom and who were found to have breast cancer") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001959> "A breast cancer study in eastern Finland whose cases are women seen at Kuopio University Hospital between 1990 and 1995 because of a breast lump, mammographic abnormality or other breast symptom and found to have breast cancer, and whose controls were selected from the National Population Register over the same years, matched to cases by age and long-term area of residence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001960> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001960>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Identified from the electoral rolls from across Australia as part of the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study in 2002-2006") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001960> "A breast cancer case-control set contributed to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) that combines, as cases, the index (youngest affected) cases of BRCA1- and BRCA2-mutation-negative multiple-case breast and breast-ovarian cancer families recruited since 1998 through family cancer clinics across Australia and New Zealand by the Kathleen Cuningham Foundation Consortium for Research into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab), and, as controls, women identified from the electoral rolls across Australia in 2002–2006 by the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study (AOCS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3653403/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Index (youngest affected) cases from BRCA1- and BRCA2-mutation-negative multiple-case breast and breast-ovarian families recruited though family cancer clinics from across Australia and New Zealand from 1998-present") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001960> "A breast cancer case-control set contributed to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) that combines, as cases, the index (youngest affected) cases of BRCA1- and BRCA2-mutation-negative multiple-case breast and breast-ovarian cancer families recruited since 1998 through family cancer clinics across Australia and New Zealand by the Kathleen Cuningham Foundation Consortium for Research into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab), and, as controls, women identified from the electoral rolls across Australia in 2002–2006 by the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study (AOCS).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-0609-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_609_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "KCONFAB/AOCS | Kathleen Cuningham Foundation Consortium for research into Familial Breast Cancer/Australian Ovarian Cancer Study | Australia and New Zeland | Case-control study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001960> "A breast cancer case-control set contributed to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC) that combines, as cases, the index (youngest affected) cases of BRCA1- and BRCA2-mutation-negative multiple-case breast and breast-ovarian cancer families recruited since 1998 through family cancer clinics across Australia and New Zealand by the Kathleen Cuningham Foundation Consortium for Research into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab), and, as controls, women identified from the electoral rolls across Australia in 2002–2006 by the Australian Ovarian Cancer Study (AOCS).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32152362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6707235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For all three body composition traits (BMI, WBFP, and ALMI), we identified significant geographical differences (p-values < 0.001) among the three datasets (LOS, KCOS and OOS), even when adjusted for age, height, weight, smoking, alcohol use, and regular physical activity (Table 3).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits, including bone mineral density and body composition, in randomly recruited adults of European ancestry living in and around Kansas City, Missouri.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32152362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6707235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The results indicate no significant geographical difference in BMD for males or females under the criteria of η2 > 0.01.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits, including bone mineral density and body composition, in randomly recruited adults of European ancestry living in and around Kansas City, Missouri.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32152362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6707235/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study used 11,315 randomly recruited Caucasian subjects, from three cross-sectional study cohorts: 5,939 from the Louisiana Osteoporosis Study (LOS, New Orleans and Baton Rouge area, Coordinates: ~30oN~90–91oW)39, 3,497 from the Kansas City Osteoporosis Study (KCOS, Kansas City area, Coordinates: ~39oN~94oW)40,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits, including bone mineral density and body composition, in randomly recruited adults of European ancestry living in and around Kansas City, Missouri.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32152362") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32152362") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7062907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The KCOS is a cross-sectional study of osteoporosis with 2,286 unrelated European ancestry participants living in and around Kansas City, Missouri, USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001961> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits, including bone mineral density and body composition, in randomly recruited adults of European ancestry living in and around Kansas City, Missouri.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4617542/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address this problem we conducted a large multi-centre case-control study of severe malaria across 12 locations in Burkina Faso, Cameroon, The Gambia, Ghana, Kenya, Malawi, Mali, Nigeria, Tanzania, Vietnam and Papua New Guinea (Supplementary Table 1, Supplementary Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4703047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We examined the effect of G6PD deficiency on the risk of malaria and other childhood diseases in children living within the area served by the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System in Kenya.6") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study was set in Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya.4 We investigated the effect of a range of candidate genes on risk for severe falciparum malaria, using a case-control approach.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included as cases children (aged <14 years) who presented to hospital with clinical features of severe malaria5, 6, 7 and were subsequently admitted to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included as controls infants (aged 3–12 months) who were born within the same study area as cases and who were recruits to a cohort study investigating genetic susceptibility to a range of childhood diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23717212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26686045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31844061") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30033078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6069675/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included as controls infants born in the local community between Aug 1, 2006, and Sept 30, 2010, who were part of a genetics study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001963> "A case-control study of severe Plasmodium falciparum malaria in children of Kilifi County on the coast of Kenya, carried out by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in the area of the Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System: its cases are children younger than 14 years admitted with severe malaria to the high-dependency ward of Kilifi County Hospital, and its controls are infants aged 3–12 months born in the same area between August 2006 and September 2010 who were recruited to a cohort study of genetic susceptibility to childhood diseases. It is the Kenyan partner study of the Malaria Genomic Epidemiology Network's multicentre case-control study of severe malaria (Consortial Project 1), whose samples were used in MalariaGEN's candidate-gene and genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10584889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among 5399 Arab patients, we optimize polygenic scores for 10 cardiometabolic traits, achieving a performance that is better than published scores and on par with performance in European-ancestry individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10584889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population included a disease cohort of 5399 individuals referred for cardiology care at the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center—a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh—from all five regions of Saudi Arabia,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10584889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was supported by a sponsored research agreement between King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center and Massachusetts General Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10584889/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a population reference cohort of 1017 individuals not known to have cardiometabolic disease and that are representative of 28 tribes of indigenous Arabs in Saudi Arabia") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13092120/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to blood samples for DNA extraction and genotyping array analyses, participants provided access to their electronic health records for phenotype data and shared socio-demographic information through a clinical research coordinator.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37852978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41844147") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13092120/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center (KFSH&RC) cohort consists of indigenous Arabs from Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care at KFSH&RC, a tertiary care hospital recognized throughout Saudi Arabia and the Middle East, for work-up of cardiac disease from all over the country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001964> "A hospital-based cohort of indigenous Arabs from all five regions of Saudi Arabia referred for cardiology care to the King Faisal Specialist Hospital and Research Center, a tertiary care hospital in Riyadh, who gave blood samples for genotyping and access to their electronic health records for phenotypes, together with a population reference group of indigenous Arabs without known cardiometabolic disease representing 28 Saudi tribes; it was set up with Massachusetts General Hospital to study polygenic scores for cardiometabolic disease in Arabs.")

