# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective, unmatched case-control study was conducted between August 2006 and December 2008 recruiting cases admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were also collected from the biological parents of children with severe malaria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases consist of children (aged 3 months - 12 years) with severe malaria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls consisted of cord blood samples collected from the labour ward of the same hospital at the same time as cases were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ethical clearance was obtained from the Committee on Human Research, Publications and Ethics of KATH / Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology, Kumasi (proposal numbers: ID GHS-ERC-03/9/06, CHRPF/07/01/06, CHRPE SMS UST/24/05/2007).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25261933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.malariagen.net/partner_study/human-genetic-determinants-severe-malaria-kumasi-ghana/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The studies were conducted in the Kumasi Metropolitan District of the Ashanti Region of Ghana where Kumasi is the capital city.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001969> "A prospective, unmatched case-control study of severe malaria conducted in August 2006 – December 2008 in the Kumasi Metropolitan District, Ashanti Region, Ghana, with ethics approval from Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital and the Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology. Its cases were children aged 3 months to 12 years with severe malaria admitted to the Paediatric Emergency Unit of Komfo Anokye Teaching Hospital, its controls were cord-blood samples collected in the same hospital's labour ward, and blood was also taken from the biological parents of cases (family trios); its clinical data and DNA samples were contributed to MalariaGEN Consortial Project 1.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001970> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001970>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124411") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729156") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27623749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40723014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124411") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3794088/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was performed as a part of the Korean Children-Adolescents Study (KoCAS), which has been monitored yearly since their entry into elementary school at age 7 in Gwacheon City or fourth grade at age 10 in Seoul and Gyeonggi Province, Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001970> "An open prospective cohort of Korean children, conducted by the Korea National Institute of Health, that enrolled children on entry to elementary school at age 7 (from 2005, at four elementary schools in Gwacheon) or in the fourth grade at age 10 in Seoul and Gyeonggi Province, and followed them annually from 2005 to 2020 except in 2015 to identify early risk factors for obesity and associated metabolic diseases; genotyped subsets were used in genome-wide association studies of childhood obesity and of liver enzyme levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124411") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729156") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27623749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40723014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24124411") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3794088/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a genome-wide association study to identify new genetic loci for liver enzyme levels in a Korean childhood cohort (n = 484).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001970> "An open prospective cohort of Korean children, conducted by the Korea National Institute of Health, that enrolled children on entry to elementary school at age 7 (from 2005, at four elementary schools in Gwacheon) or in the fourth grade at age 10 in Seoul and Gyeonggi Province, and followed them annually from 2005 to 2020 except in 2015 to identify early risk factors for obesity and associated metabolic diseases; genotyped subsets were used in genome-wide association studies of childhood obesity and of liver enzyme levels.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24124411") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729156") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27623749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40723014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26729156") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4728634/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted using data from the Korean Child-Adolescent Cohort Study (KoCAS), which followed a cohort of Korean students annually at four elementary schools in Gwacheon from entry into school at the age of seven years, in 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001970> "An open prospective cohort of Korean children, conducted by the Korea National Institute of Health, that enrolled children on entry to elementary school at age 7 (from 2005, at four elementary schools in Gwacheon) or in the fourth grade at age 10 in Seoul and Gyeonggi Province, and followed them annually from 2005 to 2020 except in 2015 to identify early risk factors for obesity and associated metabolic diseases; genotyped subsets were used in genome-wide association studies of childhood obesity and of liver enzyme levels.")
