# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Annual follow-up for cancer cases and follow-up at the 1st year for benign tumor cases are performing to evaluate treatment effect and progression.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Standardized questionnaires were administered by trained interviewers, including sections on socio-demographics characteristics, past medical history, medication usage, family history, lifetime consumption of alcohol and tobacco, diet, physical activity, and reproductive factors for women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of this paper was to report the protocol of the Ko-EVE study to examine epidemiological and molecular factors for ovarian cancer and benign neoplasms and to ascertain the major risk factors for ovarian cancer control in Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23098463+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case-control study covers incident epithelial ovarian cancers and benign neoplasms, four major centers participating in enrolling incident cases and 3 hospitals enrolling healthy controls among health examinees.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36789760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this database, patients with EOC were enrolled from 2008 to 2015 from seven general hospitals located in Seoul and Gyeonggi‐do, Korea") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23098463") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36789760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10134271/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected patients with EOC, aged over 20 years, who were histologically confirmed as having stages I–III EOC by pathologists at the time of enrollment. 16") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001972> "A hospital-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer and benign epithelial ovarian neoplasms in Korea, which enrolled women with incident, histologically confirmed epithelial ovarian tumours at major general hospitals in Seoul and Gyeonggi-do, and as controls women without ovarian cancer undergoing health screening at general hospitals, collecting standardized interview questionnaires and biological specimens and following up the cases, to study the epidemiological and molecular risk factors and natural history of epithelial ovarian cancer in Koreans.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1) patients with breast cancer and a family history of breast or ovarian cancer; 2) patients with breast cancer without a family history of breast or ovarian cancer who were ≤40 years of age at diagnosis, diagnosed with bilateral breast cancer or another primary malignancy related to BRCA mutations, or male; and 3) family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers [10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between June 2010 and May 2013, the second phase of the KOHBRA Study was performed to identify the clinical characteristics and prognostic indicators of BRCA-related breast cancer and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA mutations and to develop a Korean BRCA risk calculator and nationwide genetic counseling network for HBOC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between May 2007 and May 2010, 1967 subjects from 36 institutions were enrolled in the KOHBRA Study, and all subjects received genetic counseling and BRCA genetic testing [9].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between May 2007 and May 2010, the first phase of the KOHBRA Study was performed to estimate the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations among patients and their families at risk for HBOC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24155753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3800720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In May 2007, the Korean Hereditary Breast Cancer (KOHBRA) Study, a large, prospective, nationwide study, was established to acquire evidence for the accurate risk assessment and management of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer (HBOC) in the Korean population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001973> "A prospective, nationwide study of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer in Korea, established in May 2007, that enrols, at many hospitals across the country, breast cancer patients at high risk of carrying a BRCA1/2 mutation (those with a family history of breast or ovarian cancer, or diagnosed at 40 or younger, with bilateral breast cancer or another BRCA-related primary cancer, or male) and family members of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, all of whom receive genetic counselling and BRCA testing. Its first phase (2007–2010) estimated the prevalence of BRCA1/2 mutations, and its second (2010–2013) studied the clinical characteristics, prognosis and environmental and genetic modifiers of BRCA-related breast cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-022-32821-z/MediaObjects/41467_2022_32821_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The third KORA survey (KORA S3, n=3,996) is a population-based sample from the general population of the South-German city of Augsburg and surrounding counties from 1994/1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001974> "The ten-year follow-up examination of the KORA S3 survey, conducted in 2004/05, which re-examined participants of the 1994/95 S3 survey, a population-based random sample of residents aged 25–74 of the city of Augsburg and surrounding counties in southern Germany, within the KORA research platform.")
