AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15374369") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10732458/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9074345/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15374369") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15374369+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Leiden 85-plus study has investigated the prevalence of morbidity in the total population of the Dutch community of Leiden (population 105 000) aged 85 and over, including both independently living and institutionalized elderly.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001985> "A population-based prospective cohort study of the oldest old in the city of Leiden, the Netherlands, which enrolled inhabitants who turned 85 between September 1997 and September 1999 in the month of their 85th birthday and examined them with interviews and clinical examinations at baseline and yearly for five years, to study health, functioning and well-being in very old age; an earlier survey under the same name studied the prevalence of morbidity in the whole population of Leiden aged 85 and over, living independently or in institutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15374369") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10732458/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9074345/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35524168") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9074345/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Leiden 85-plus Study, an observational population-based prospective cohort study, examined health, functioning and well-being in very old adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001985> "A population-based prospective cohort study of the oldest old in the city of Leiden, the Netherlands, which enrolled inhabitants who turned 85 between September 1997 and September 1999 in the month of their 85th birthday and examined them with interviews and clinical examinations at baseline and yearly for five years, to study health, functioning and well-being in very old age; an earlier survey under the same name studied the prevalence of morbidity in the whole population of Leiden aged 85 and over, living independently or in institutions.")
