AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18431743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108163/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4203374/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this study, controls were women with at least one intact ovary, with no history of cancer except possibly non-melanoma skin cancer, and individually matched with patients on race/ethnicity (non-Hispanic White, African-American, Hispanic, Asians), and date of birth (+/- 5 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001988> "Population-based case-control studies of ovarian cancer among women resident in Los Angeles County, California, United States, run at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California, in which cases with newly diagnosed ovarian cancer were identified through the county's SEER cancer registry (the Cancer Surveillance Program) and controls were recruited from the cases' neighbourhoods and matched on race/ethnicity and age; the studies take part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the code USC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18431743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108163/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4203374/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Neighborhood controls were sought by one of our staff who physically canvassed the neighborhood of the case using a systematic algorithm based on the address of the case.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001988> "Population-based case-control studies of ovarian cancer among women resident in Los Angeles County, California, United States, run at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California, in which cases with newly diagnosed ovarian cancer were identified through the county's SEER cancer registry (the Cancer Surveillance Program) and controls were recruited from the cases' neighbourhoods and matched on race/ethnicity and age; the studies take part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the code USC.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18431743") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3108163/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19065661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4203374/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases were identified by the Cancer Surveillance Program (CSP), part of the National Cancer Institute's Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program, covering all residents of Los Angeles County.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001988> "Population-based case-control studies of ovarian cancer among women resident in Los Angeles County, California, United States, run at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California, in which cases with newly diagnosed ovarian cancer were identified through the county's SEER cancer registry (the Cancer Surveillance Program) and controls were recruited from the cases' neighbourhoods and matched on race/ethnicity and age; the studies take part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the code USC.")
