# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10604159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up visits and re-assessments of the status of complications of diabetes take place every three years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10604159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LatDiane recruits adult patients with T1D diagnosed before the age of 40 with insulin treatment initiated within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide levels below 0.3 nmol/L.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10604159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with a history of chronic kidney disease apart from DKD are excluded from LatDiane.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10604159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study protocol includes recording diabetes and other disease histories, basic clinical and anthropometric investigation, collection of blood samples for preparation of serum and plasma and DNA extraction, collection of urine, as well as assessment of dietary and physical activity habits, socioeconomic factors, and psychologic condition with the help of questionnaires") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10604159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is a part of the longitudinal LatDiane study, initiated in 2013 (and participating in the international InterDiane consortium).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35915454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37893052") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39720301") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cdn-links.lww.com/permalink/jsn/c/jsn_30_10_2022_12_07_salem_2019030218_sdc1.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Latvian Diabetic Nephropathy Study (LatDiane) was initiated in 2012 and is part of the InterDiane Consortium (please see also the InterDiane cohort description).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001989> "A longitudinal study, started in 2013, of adults in Latvia with type 1 diabetes diagnosed before the age of 40, with insulin treatment started within one year of diagnosis and C-peptide below 0.3 nmol/L, excluding those with chronic kidney disease other than diabetic kidney disease, who are examined, give blood and urine samples and answer questionnaires at baseline and at follow-up visits every three years, to study diabetic kidney disease and the other complications of diabetes. It is part of the InterDiane consortium.")

