AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, patients from the urology department of St James's University Hospital, Leeds, were recruited from August 2002 to March 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001990> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Leeds, England, whose cases were patients of the urology department of St James's University Hospital and whose controls came from the hospital's otolaryngology and ophthalmology departments, recruited from August 2002 to March 2006. It takes part in the International Consortium of Bladder Cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were recruited from the otolaryngology outpatients and ophthalmology inpatient and outpatient departments at St James's Hospital, Leeds, from August 2002 to March 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001990> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Leeds, England, whose cases were patients of the urology department of St James's University Hospital and whose controls came from the hospital's otolaryngology and ophthalmology departments, recruited from August 2002 to March 2006. It takes part in the International Consortium of Bladder Cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9835888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Cancer Institute (NCI) funded the Integrative Analysis of Cancer Risk and Etiology (INTEGRAL) U19 program, which includes an objective to develop early detection biomarkers and risk prediction tools for lung cancer screening.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9835888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Risk Biomarker project leverages resources from the Lung Cancer Cohort Consortium (LC3) [4], [5], [6], [7], [8] which was initially established in 2010 within the NCI Cohort Consortium [9].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9835888/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore leveraged the infrastructure from the Risk Biomarker project and the Lung Cancer Cohort Consortium to develop a comprehensive study database for lung cancer incidence and mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9835888/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the biomarker studies, lung cancer cases were defined using the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, Second Edition (ICD-O-2), and included all primary malignant cancers coded as C34.0-C34.9 with pre-diagnostic blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9849351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each case, one healthy, cancer-free control subject was matched by cohort, sex, race (US cohorts only), date of blood collection, date of birth, and self-reported smoking status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36404465") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36653422") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39179310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40212049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11985077/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this international prospective cohort consortium study, we used data from the Lung Cancer Cohort Consortium (LC3), which includes 20 prospective population cohorts from 16 countries in North America, Europe, Asia, and Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001991> "An international consortium of prospective cohort studies in North America, Europe, Asia and Australia, established in 2010 within the US National Cancer Institute Cohort Consortium, that pools harmonized risk-factor and lung cancer outcome data on the cohorts' participants, and prediagnostic blood samples of lung cancer cases and matched controls for biomarker studies, for research on lung cancer aetiology, risk prediction and early detection.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6659464") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative (KLCRI) was supported by the Department of Defense") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(for trace element analysis), urine, buffy coat, water, soil, and radon collection, residence GPS mapping, as well as an extensive epidemiologic, occupational, and health history questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer cases were recruited from the Kentucky Cancer Registry at the time of diagnosis and controls were recruited from a random digit dialing process from the same region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Newly diagnosed lung cancer cases and controls underwent blood, toenail") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study accrual began in January 5, 2012 and completed on September 5, 2014 and 520 subjects were recruited in a 4:1 ratio of controls: cases from Appalachian Kentucky.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kentucky Lung Cancer Research Initiative is a study conducted by the Markey Cancer Center Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky using a population-based, case- control framework to study the extraordinarily high rates of lung cancer in Southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001992> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer in southeastern, Appalachian Kentucky, United States, run by the Markey Cancer Center and the University of Kentucky with Department of Defense funding, which from January 2012 to September 2014 recruited newly diagnosed cases through the Kentucky Cancer Registry and controls from the same region by random-digit dialling, and collected blood, toenail, urine, water, soil and radon samples, residential GPS mapping and an epidemiologic, occupational and health-history questionnaire, to study the region's very high lung cancer rates.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001994> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001994>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19836008") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22899653") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24880342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19836008") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2775843/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Estonia 109 874 Estonia Hospital-based case-control 317K, 370Duo") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001994> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Estonia, whose cases were lung cancer patients enrolled in Estonian hospitals between 2002 and 2006 and whose controls were randomly selected from the population-based cohort of the Estonian Genome Project; genotyped genome-wide with support from the University of Tartu, it was one of the five case–control studies of the IARC lung cancer genome-wide association study and was pooled in the lung cancer meta-analyses of the TRICL consortium.")
