# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1271381/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases underwent a standardized clinical assessment performed by a neurologist subspecialized in movement disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1271381/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Department of Neurology of the Mayo Clinic in Rochester, MN, from June 1996 through May 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1271381/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was again shipped to Perlegen Sciences for whole-genome amplification and genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1271381/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They all resided within Minnesota or one of the surrounding four states (Wisconsin, Iowa, South Dakota, or North Dakota).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16252231+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a two-tiered, whole-genome association study of Parkinson disease (PD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16252231") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000048.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Criteria for Controls: Unaffected siblings of cases, matched on gender when able then on closest age at study (tier 1); or unrelated population controls, matched on gender and age at study (tier 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001995> "A two-tiered case-control study of Parkinson disease at the Mayo Clinic, Rochester, Minnesota, genotyped genome-wide on a Perlegen platform, whose cases were enrolled prospectively from the clinical practice of the Mayo Clinic's Department of Neurology from June 1996 to May 2004 among residents of Minnesota and the four surrounding states and assessed by a movement-disorders neurologist, and whose controls were unaffected siblings of cases (tier 1) or unrelated population controls matched on sex and age (tier 2), all screened for parkinsonism.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data for endometrial cancer patients were recorded during interview at the time of diagnosis, and from pathology reports.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases, identified by active surveillance of electronic patient files at the Leuven University Hospital, were white women aged 27-80 years diagnosed with endometrial cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Leuven Endometrial Study (LES) is a hospital based case-control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-018-05427-7/MediaObjects/41467_2018_5427_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LES | Leuven Endometrial Cancer Study | Belgium; hospital based cases | | Illumina OncoArray 534K | 528 | 382 | 142 | 69 | 26 | 11 | 7") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13537468/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Replication in the Belgian population included 528 cases from the Leuven Endometrial Cancer Study (LES) and 1,266 controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre Study (LMBC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001997> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer at the Leuven University Hospital in Belgium, whose cases were white women aged 27–80 diagnosed with endometrial cancer, identified by active surveillance of the hospital's electronic patient files, with clinical data recorded at interview at diagnosis and from pathology reports. In genetic analyses its cases were compared with controls from blood donors of the Leuven Multidisciplinary Breast Centre study, and they were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10225243") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10225243+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this prospective randomized trial using an intention-to-treat analysis, smokers with early COPD who were assigned to a smoking-cessation intervention had fewer respiratory symptoms after 5 years of follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2048803+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Lung Health Study is a randomized clinical trial designed to determine whether a smoking intervention program and prescription of an inhaled bronchodilator can reduce the annual rate of decline of FEV1 (FEV1 slope) in cigarette smokers with mild to moderate airflow limitation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41164942") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41164942+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed data from 5279 participants from the United States from the Lung Health Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41164942") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41164942+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We compared all-cause and cause-specific mortality at 32.5 years between the combined special intervention groups and usual care group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41527371+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1986 and 1989, the LHS enrolled 5887 smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction across ten North American sites and randomized them to a 10-day smoking cessation intervention with placebo inhaler, the same intervention with ipratropium bromide, or usual care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2048803") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41527371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7966841") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7966841+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ten clinical centers in the United States and Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0001998> "A randomized clinical trial run at ten clinical centres in the United States and Canada, which between 1986 and 1989 enrolled smokers aged 35-59 with mild-to-moderate airway obstruction and randomized them to a smoking-cessation intervention (with an inhaled bronchodilator or a placebo inhaler) or usual care, to determine whether smoking cessation and bronchodilator treatment reduce the rate of decline of lung function, with long-term follow-up of respiratory symptoms and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1023/A:1016387020854.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among case and control respondents who completed the interviewer- administered questionnaire, 98.2 and 97.6% self-completed the food frequency questionnaire; 73.0 and 73.3% donated a blood sample; and 93.0 and 83.3% donated a urine sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> "A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12206514+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among a random sample of case and control respondents who are long-term residents, samples of dust (83.6 and 83.0%); soil (93.5 and 89.7%); and water (94.3 and 93.9%) were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> "A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12206514+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Long Island Breast Cancer Study Project is a federally mandated, population-based case-control study to determine whether breast cancer risk among women in the counties of Nassau and Suffolk, NY, is associated with selected environmental exposures, assessed by blood samples, self-reports, and environmental home samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> "A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8751127/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Breast cancer cases were women from the Nassau and Suffolk Counties on Long Island, New York with newly diagnosed first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between 1 August 1996 and 31 July 1997 [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> "A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12206514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35010632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8751127/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Long Island Breast Cancer Study Project (LIBCSP) participants diagnosed with breast cancer between 1 August 1996 and 31 July 1997 and followed-up through 31 December 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002000> "A federally mandated, population-based case-control study of breast cancer among women living in Nassau and Suffolk counties on Long Island, New York, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with a first primary in situ or invasive breast cancer between August 1996 and July 1997; cases and controls were interviewed and gave blood and urine, and long-term residents gave household dust, soil and water samples, to determine whether breast cancer risk is associated with environmental exposures, and the cases were later followed up to study prognosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23181778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Full participant recruitment and complete data collection started in July 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23181778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LIFE Child study is part of LIFE, a life sciences research program of the University of Leipzig (Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases - LIFE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23181778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ‘Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) Child Study’ focuses on two main research objectives: (1) monitoring of normal growth, development and health; (2) non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity and its co-morbidities, atopy and mental health problems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23181778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This program includes clinical history (perinatal and past medical history, medications, allergies, immunizations, developmental history and family history) clinical examination, collection of blood, hair and urine samples, anthropometry and different age-dependent questionnaires (see Table 4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28144813+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LIFE Child study is a large population-based longitudinal childhood cohort study conducted in the city of Leipzig, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3533937/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28144813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28144813+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study consists of three interrelated cohorts; the birth cohort, the health cohort, and the obesity cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002001> "A population-based prospective longitudinal cohort study of children and adolescents in the city of Leipzig, Germany, run since July 2011 by the Leipzig Research Centre for Civilization Diseases (LIFE) at Leipzig University, made up of a birth cohort recruited in pregnancy, a health cohort and an obesity cohort, whose participants have repeated medical, psychological and sociodemographic assessments and give biological samples from fetal life to adulthood, to monitor normal growth, development and health and to study non-communicable diseases such as childhood obesity, atopy and mental health problems.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5715013/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we extend that approach in a genome-wide association meta-analysis (GWAMA) to discovery across UKB European- and African-ancestry populations and 24 further population studies (LifeGen), mainly from Europe, Australia and North America, to search for further genetic variants influencing longevity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> "A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants' genomes to the survival of those participants' parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5715013/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To facilitate standardisation across the GWAS consortium, residuals for GWAS were calculated in accordance with the analysis plan set out below using a common R protocol distributed to all groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> "A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants' genomes to the survival of those participants' parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5715013/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted an association test between parental survival (age and alive/dead status) and offspring genotype.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> "A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants' genomes to the survival of those participants' parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6333444/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our second dataset was the publicly available summary statistics from LifeGen, a consortium of 26 population cohorts investigating genomic effects on parental lifespans") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> "A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants' genomes to the survival of those participants' parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29030599") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30642433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6333444/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We carried out GWAS of survival in a sample of 1,012,240 parents (60% deceased) of European ancestry from UK Biobank and a previously published meta-analysis of 26 additional population cohorts") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002002> "A consortium of population studies, mainly from Europe, Australia and North America and of European or African ancestry, that ran a common protocol relating their genotyped participants' genomes to the survival of those participants' parents, and meta-analysed the results with UK Biobank in a genome-wide association study of human longevity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All controls were admitted to a single tertiary care hospital in Austria (Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder, Linz) because of minor health problems, such as vertebrogenic pain, cataract surgery, and non-arterial surgery (e.g. varicose vein extirpation, herniotomy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From April 2000 to April 2002 we consecutively enrolled all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic PAD admitted to a single tertiary care hospital in Austria (Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder, Linz).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January 2001 to July 2004 we recruited controls matched to the patients with lower extremity PAD in a 1:1 design by age (±2 years), sex, and diabetes mellitus status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mortality data for the entire cohort were obtained from the Austrian Mortality Registry, resulting in date of death and cause of death") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LIPAD study was prospectively designed and conducted to evaluate biomarkers for PAD by using a case–control design and to determine the long-term outcome of patients with established PAD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5692147/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5054299/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, although we had stringent selection criteria for our controls and excluded ‘significant’ atherosclerotic disease by history and by screening, we cannot exclude the presence of atherosclerotic disease per se in our controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002004> "A prospectively designed hospital-based case-control and follow-up study of lower extremity peripheral arterial disease in Linz, Austria, which enrolled consecutively, from April 2000 to April 2002, all patients with symptomatic chronic atherosclerotic peripheral arterial disease admitted to the Konventhospital Barmherzige Brueder Linz, and from 2001 to 2004 controls screened to exclude significant atherosclerotic disease admitted to the same hospital for minor health problems, matched by age, sex and diabetes status, to evaluate biomarkers and genetic variants for peripheral arterial disease and the long-term outcome of the patients through the Austrian Mortality Registry.")

