AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433484") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24704916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24704916") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3899950/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our molecular epidemiological study was conducted on blood samples of a well described sample population of 175 young cancer patients (LUng Cancer in the Young LUCY) and 623 relatives (mother, father, siblings and children) and spouses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020> "A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433484") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24704916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples are taken and DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines are prepared of all cases and controls and of parts of the relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020> "A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433484") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24704916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LUCY (LUng Cancer in the Young) is a multicenter study with 31 recruiting hospitals in Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020> "A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18433484") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24704916") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25644374") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LUCY-study provides access to a nationwide, population based family and a case-control sample (control population KORA, described below) of lung cancer patients aged 50 years or younger at diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002020> "A German multicentre study of lung cancer diagnosed at the age of 50 or younger, run by the Institute of Epidemiology of the Helmholtz Zentrum München and the Department of Genetic Epidemiology of the University of Göttingen with 31 recruiting clinics across Germany from 2000, which collected a nationwide family sample (young patients with their parents, siblings, children and spouses) and a case–control sample with population controls from the KORA surveys, with epidemiological data on medical history, education, occupation, family history of cancer and smoking, and blood samples from which DNA and lymphoblastoid cell lines were prepared.")
