AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537875") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23218199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31608855") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31608855") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/midatlantic-twin-registry-of-virginia-commonwealth-university/D6A17F0CECC43803BF9437EDDC2061EB") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mid-Atlantic Twin Registry (MATR) is a population-based registry of more than 60,000 twins primarily born or living in Virginia, North Carolina and South Carolina.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002034> "A population-based registry of twins and their families, primarily born or living in Virginia, North Carolina and South Carolina and ascertained mainly from birth records (and formerly school records), formed in 1997 by merging the Virginia Twin Registry (established around 1975) with the North Carolina Twin Registry, with South Carolina added in 1998; based at Virginia Commonwealth University, it recruits its twins into research studies, collects data and DNA, and keeps a DNA repository.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12537875") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23218199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31608855") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31608855") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/twin-research-and-human-genetics/article/midatlantic-twin-registry-of-virginia-commonwealth-university/D6A17F0CECC43803BF9437EDDC2061EB") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mid-Atlantic Twin Registry (MATR) is a population-based registry of twins and their families that was formed through the convergence of the Virginia Twin Registry (est. circa 1975) and the North Carolina Twin Registry in 1997 and the addition of South Carolina in 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002034> "A population-based registry of twins and their families, primarily born or living in Virginia, North Carolina and South Carolina and ascertained mainly from birth records (and formerly school records), formed in 1997 by merging the Virginia Twin Registry (established around 1975) with the North Carolina Twin Registry, with South Carolina added in 1998; based at Virginia Commonwealth University, it recruits its twins into research studies, collects data and DNA, and keeps a DNA repository.")

