AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Muenster cervical artery dissection collection was in part supported by Competence Net Stroke, Germany (BMBF), by the “Innovative Medizinische Forschung” (IMF) of the Medical Faculty of the University of Münster, by the Neuromedical Foundation, Münster and by the Leibniz Institute of Atherosclerosis Research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002040> "A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection at the University of Münster, Germany, one of the centres collaborating with the CADISP consortium that recruited patients of European origin, applying the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, for the second sample (CADISP-2) of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To increase the sample size for genetic analyses, an independent sample of 501 CeAD patients of European origin was recruited between 2008 and 2010, in some CADISP centers and additional 12 centers in 7 European countries and the United States (Supplementary Fig. 2), applying the same inclusion criteria as for the CADISP study (Supplementary Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002040> "A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection at the University of Münster, Germany, one of the centres collaborating with the CADISP consortium that recruited patients of European origin, applying the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, for the second sample (CADISP-2) of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "genotypes of 451 CeAD patients for CADISP-2 and 213 Finnish controls were obtained by Human660W-Quad BeadChip (Illumina).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002040> "A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection at the University of Münster, Germany, one of the centres collaborating with the CADISP consortium that recruited patients of European origin, applying the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, for the second sample (CADISP-2) of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children were diagnosed with asthma by a pediatric allergist at the referral clinic based on clinical symptoms and response to treatment [32].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children with asthma (aged 5–17) and their biological parents were recruited between June 1998 and November 2003 from a pediatric allergy specialty clinic at a large public hospital in central Mexico City, Hospital Infantil de Mexico Frederico Gomez.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoking, were completed by parents, nearly always the mother.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The clinical evaluation also included skin prick testing to measure atopy and pulmonary function testing, as previously described [6].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This research was supported by the Intramural Research Program of the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, National Institutes of Health, Department of Health and Human Services (Z01ES049019).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21804549") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26635092") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19714205") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2722731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a GWAS to identify novel candidate susceptibility genes associated with childhood asthma in case-parent trios from Mexico City and tested the most significantly associated SNPs in an independent study of trios of Mexican ethnicity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002041> "A case–parent trio study of childhood asthma in Mexico City, supported by the Intramural Research Program of the US National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, which recruited children aged 5 to 17 with asthma, diagnosed by a paediatric allergist from clinical symptoms and response to treatment, together with their biological parents, between June 1998 and November 2003 at the paediatric allergy clinic of the Hospital Infantil de México Federico Gómez, a large public hospital in central Mexico City; parents completed questionnaires on the children's asthma symptoms and risk factors, including environmental tobacco smoke, the children had skin prick tests and lung function tests, and blood was taken from children and parents for DNA, from which the trios were genotyped genome-wide.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23805179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3727653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data acquisition across multiple sites permitted the integration and cross-validation of clinical, cognitive, morphometric, and functional neuroimaging results gathered from unique samples of schizophrenia patients and controls using a common protocol across sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> "A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23805179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3727653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Expertly collected, well-curated data sets consisting of comprehensive clinical characterization and raw structural, functional and diffusion-weighted DICOM images in schizophrenia patients and sex and age-matched controls are now accessible to the scientific community through an on-line data repository (coins.mrn.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> "A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23805179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3727653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotyping on the blinded DNA was performed at the MRN (Mind Research Network) Neurogenetics Core Lab using the Illumina HumanOmni-Quad BeadChip.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> "A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23805179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3727653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Particular effort was made to recruit patients early in the course of their illness, at the onset of their symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> "A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23805179") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23760817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3727653/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute, now the Mind Research Network (MRN, www.mrn.org), comprised of investigators at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital, and the University of Iowa, conducted a cross-sectional study to identify quantitative neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002042> "A cross-sectional study of schizophrenia conducted by the Mental Illness and Neuroscience Discovery Institute (now the Mind Research Network) at the University of New Mexico, the University of Minnesota, Massachusetts General Hospital and the University of Iowa, which collected clinical, cognitive, structural, functional and diffusion MRI and genetic data under a common protocol from people with schizophrenia, recruited where possible early in their illness, and sex- and age-matched controls, to identify neuroimaging biomarkers of schizophrenia.")

