# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we present the largest GWAS for MDD to date, the MDD2000+ study comprising 2431 cases and 3673 screened controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MDD cases were recruited through in- and out-patient services of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland and were tertiary referrals from primary care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Only unrelated individuals were included in MDD2000+.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were provided by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR, Australia), The Netherlands Study of Anxiety and Depression (NESDA), The Netherlands Twin Registry (NTR), the University of Edinburgh (UK), and the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study (controls only, US).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study participants were adult twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry (http://www.twins.org.au).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21042317") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3252611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MDD2000+ project comprises a total of 2431 cases with MDD and 3673 screened controls from different sources and genotyped on different platforms (Tables 1 and 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002049> "A genome-wide association study of major depressive disorder that combined unrelated cases and screened controls from several sources genotyped on different platforms: Australian twins and their families recruited through the Australian Twin Registry by the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, the Netherlands Study of Depression and Anxiety, the Netherlands Twin Registry, patients of psychiatric hospitals in Scotland recruited by the University of Edinburgh, and controls from the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia study in the United States.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002050> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002050>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-018-05427-7/MediaObjects/41467_2018_5427_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MECS | Mayo Endometrial Cancer Study | USA; Clinic based cases |  | Illumina OncoArray 534K | 236 | 173 | 61") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002050> "A clinic-based series of women with endometrial cancer at Mayo Clinic in the United States, whose cases were contributed to the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we conduct a meta-GWAS including 12,906 endometrial cancer cases and 108,979 country-matched controls of European ancestry from 17 studies identified via the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC), the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium (E2C2) and the UK Biobank and report a further nine genome-wide significant endometrial cancer genetic risk regions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002050> "A clinic-based series of women with endometrial cancer at Mayo Clinic in the United States, whose cases were contributed to the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7592606/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using the newly-developed GPSCAD and bioinformatics framework, we next studied 1,800 CAD cases and 1,163 control individuals newly-recruited in India as part of a MedGenome study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051> "A case-control study of coronary artery disease conducted by MedGenome in India, whose cases and controls were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals in five Indian cities (Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore) and genotyped to test a framework for assessing a genome-wide polygenic score for coronary artery disease in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7592606/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent genotyping using the Illumina Global Screening Array Platform, of whom 1,800 CAD cases and 1,163 controls remained after quality control (Supplemental Appendix).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051> "A case-control study of coronary artery disease conducted by MedGenome in India, whose cases and controls were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals in five Indian cities (Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore) and genotyped to test a framework for assessing a genome-wide polygenic score for coronary artery disease in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7592606/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To provide a set of individuals to test the framework for GPSCAD assessment, a second set of individuals −1,826 CAD cases and 1,209 controls - were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals at 5 cities in India -- Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051> "A case-control study of coronary artery disease conducted by MedGenome in India, whose cases and controls were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals in five Indian cities (Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore) and genotyped to test a framework for assessing a genome-wide polygenic score for coronary artery disease in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32762905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7592606/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed and tested a new GPSCAD using three distinct South Asian studies, and provide a generalizable framework for ancestry-specific GPS assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002051> "A case-control study of coronary artery disease conducted by MedGenome in India, whose cases and controls were recruited from outpatient clinics and hospitals in five Indian cities (Kochi, Jaipur, Coimbatore, Chennai and Bangalore) and genotyped to test a framework for assessing a genome-wide polygenic score for coronary artery disease in South Asians.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25102180") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25102180") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4125087/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the parent studies (ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, CHS, eMERGE, FamHS, FIND, GeneSTAR, GENOA, HANDLS, Health ABC, HUFS, IPM Biobank, IRAS, IRASFS, JHS, MESA, MESA Family, SCCS, SIGNET-REGARDS, WFSM and WHI) of the MEDIA consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052> "A consortium of studies with African American participants that meta-analyses genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in African Americans to investigate the genetic architecture of the disease in this population; its parent studies include ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, CHS, eMERGE, FamHS, FIND, GeneSTAR, GENOA, HANDLS, Health ABC, HUFS, IPM Biobank, IRAS, IRASFS, JHS, MESA, MESA Family, SCCS, SIGNET-REGARDS, WFSM and WHI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25102180") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25102180") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25102180+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to investigate the genetic architecture of T2D in African Americans, the MEta-analysis of type 2 DIabetes in African Americans (MEDIA) Consortium examined 17 GWAS on T2D comprising 8,284 cases and 15,543 controls in African Americans in stage 1 analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002052> "A consortium of studies with African American participants that meta-analyses genome-wide association studies of type 2 diabetes in African Americans to investigate the genetic architecture of the disease in this population; its parent studies include ARIC, CARDIA, CFS, CHS, eMERGE, FamHS, FIND, GeneSTAR, GENOA, HANDLS, Health ABC, HUFS, IPM Biobank, IRAS, IRASFS, JHS, MESA, MESA Family, SCCS, SIGNET-REGARDS, WFSM and WHI.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MESCA is a population-based prospective study of childhood asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MESCA is the first prospective study to provide robust evidence for the link between childhood asthma and the development of COPD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited in 1964 in Melbourne, Australia, and followed up 8 times until the most recent follow-up in their sixth decade of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, with the initial aim of determining the prevalence and describing the natural history of childhood asthma and wheezy bronchitis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Severe asthma (SA)*83Children with persistent symptoms who had an onset before three years and/or barrel-chest deformity as well as reduced lung functions with FEV1/FVC ≤ 50%*this group was added at age 10 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21907864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41849083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13331842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using different sampling ratios, 401 children were selected into four groups (Table 1): a control group (C, n = 106) comprised of every 20th child out of those who had never wheezed") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002054> "A population-based prospective study of childhood asthma, also known as the Melbourne Asthma Study, initiated in 1964 by Howard Williams of the Royal Children’s Hospital, Melbourne, Australia, which recruited three asthma or wheeze groups and a control group of children aged 7, added a severe-asthma group at age 10, and has followed participants into their sixth decade, providing the first prospective evidence linking childhood asthma to the development of COPD, with participants contributing to the Australian Asthma Genetics Consortium’s genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19052638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5336269/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Betatrophin levels were analyzed in participants of the MesyBePo study follow-up cohort (Metabolic Syndrome Berlin-Potsdam) that included healthy control subjects as well as patients with impaired glucose metabolism including overt type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent nutritional assessment, with a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test and insulin measurements in those without diabetes, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19052638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5569105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants underwent physical examination and fasting blood test, as well as a standardized 3-h 75-g OGTT (unless no evident diagnosis of diabetes was existent) with insulin measurements in nondiabetic subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent nutritional assessment, with a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test and insulin measurements in those without diabetes, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19052638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5569105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cross-sectional Metabolic Syndrome Berlin Potsdam (MeSyBePo) study was approved by the ethics commissions of Berlin and Brandenburg, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent nutritional assessment, with a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test and insulin measurements in those without diabetes, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19052638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5569105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included 2364 participants, who were randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and surroundings, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent nutritional assessment, with a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test and insulin measurements in those without diabetes, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19052638") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28257453") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28835639") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5569105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the cross-sectional Metabolic Syndrome Berlin Potsdam (MeSyBePo) study, which includes nutritional assessments, was analyzed") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002055> "A cross-sectional study of the metabolic syndrome in Germany whose participants, randomly recruited from Berlin, Potsdam and their surroundings, underwent nutritional assessment, with a 75 g oral glucose tolerance test and insulin measurements in those without diabetes, and included people with normal glucose metabolism as well as people with impaired glucose metabolism or type 2 diabetes; part of it was later re-examined in a follow-up study.")
