# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants provided blood samples for GWAS genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> "A cohort of patients of Kaiser Permanente Northern California, United States, established with funding from GlaxoSmithKline in collaboration with the University of California San Francisco and Kaiser Permanente Northern California for a genome-wide association study of extreme responders to metformin: patients who met the study criteria were invited, gave blood samples for genotyping, and had their drug response taken from the electronic health record. Its participants with type 2 diabetes who had a sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy formed one of the data sets of the MetGen Plus and DIRECT genome-wide meta-analysis of glycaemic response to sulfonylureas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Drug response information was extracted from the electronic health record.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> "A cohort of patients of Kaiser Permanente Northern California, United States, established with funding from GlaxoSmithKline in collaboration with the University of California San Francisco and Kaiser Permanente Northern California for a genome-wide association study of extreme responders to metformin: patients who met the study criteria were invited, gave blood samples for genotyping, and had their drug response taken from the electronic health record. Its participants with type 2 diabetes who had a sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy formed one of the data sets of the MetGen Plus and DIRECT genome-wide meta-analysis of glycaemic response to sulfonylureas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Metformin Response (METRO) cohort was established through funding by GSK (GlaxoSmithKline) in collaboration with University of California San Francisco (UCSF), and Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) under a collaborative research agreement.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> "A cohort of patients of Kaiser Permanente Northern California, United States, established with funding from GlaxoSmithKline in collaboration with the University of California San Francisco and Kaiser Permanente Northern California for a genome-wide association study of extreme responders to metformin: patients who met the study criteria were invited, gave blood samples for genotyping, and had their drug response taken from the electronic health record. Its participants with type 2 diabetes who had a sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy formed one of the data sets of the MetGen Plus and DIRECT genome-wide meta-analysis of glycaemic response to sulfonylureas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prescriptions of sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy, along with HbA1c levels, dose and adherence were available for the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> "A cohort of patients of Kaiser Permanente Northern California, United States, established with funding from GlaxoSmithKline in collaboration with the University of California San Francisco and Kaiser Permanente Northern California for a genome-wide association study of extreme responders to metformin: patients who met the study criteria were invited, gave blood samples for genotyping, and had their drug response taken from the electronic health record. Its participants with type 2 diabetes who had a sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy formed one of the data sets of the MetGen Plus and DIRECT genome-wide meta-analysis of glycaemic response to sulfonylureas.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the cohort is to perform a genome- wide association of approximately 1000 extreme responders to metformin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002056> "A cohort of patients of Kaiser Permanente Northern California, United States, established with funding from GlaxoSmithKline in collaboration with the University of California San Francisco and Kaiser Permanente Northern California for a genome-wide association study of extreme responders to metformin: patients who met the study criteria were invited, gave blood samples for genotyping, and had their drug response taken from the electronic health record. Its participants with type 2 diabetes who had a sulfonylurea added to initial metformin therapy formed one of the data sets of the MetGen Plus and DIRECT genome-wide meta-analysis of glycaemic response to sulfonylureas.")
