AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3173859") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples from seven additional populations were also included: African ancestry in the southwestern USA (ASW); Chinese in metropolitan Denver, Colorado, USA (CHD); Gujarati Indians in Houston, Texas, USA (GIH); Luhya in Webuye, Kenya (LWK); Maasai in Kinyawa, Kenya (MKK); Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California, USA (MXL); and samples collected in Tuscany, Italy (TSI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002058> "A collection of DNA samples from people of Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California, one of the seven population samples added in phase 3 of the International HapMap Project and used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3173859") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected and studied an extended set of 1,184 samples from 11 populations (Supplementary Information).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002058> "A collection of DNA samples from people of Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California, one of the seven population samples added in phase 3 of the International HapMap Project and used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3173859") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the community of Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002058> "A collection of DNA samples from people of Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California, one of the seven population samples added in phase 3 of the International HapMap Project and used as a reference for human genetic variation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20811451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3173859/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This expanded public resource of genome variants in global populations supports deeper interrogation of genomic variation and its role in human disease, and serves as a step towards a high-resolution map of the landscape of human genetic variation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002058> "A collection of DNA samples from people of Mexican ancestry in Los Angeles, California, one of the seven population samples added in phase 3 of the International HapMap Project and used as a reference for human genetic variation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002059> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002059>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-023-41819-0/MediaObjects/41467_2023_41819_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "African American samples were genotyped using the Illumina 1M-Duo bead arrays (except 170 PLCO subjects on Illumina Omni 2.5M).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002059> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in African Americans, part of a 'Minority GWAS' effort alongside a Japanese study, that pooled African American cases and controls identified from the Multiethnic Cohort, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Southern Community Cohort Study, the MD Anderson Cancer Center, the University of North Carolina CanCORS and Rectal Cancer studies and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-023-41819-0/MediaObjects/41467_2023_41819_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second GWAS of African American samples (n = 6,597) (Supplementary Table 2) were identified from the MEC, CCFR, the Southern Community Cohort Study (SCCS), the MD Anderson Cancer Center, the University of North Carolina CanCORS study (UNCCanCORS) and Rectal Cancer Study (UNC-Rectal), and from the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening (PLCO) Trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002059> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in African Americans, part of a 'Minority GWAS' effort alongside a Japanese study, that pooled African American cases and controls identified from the Multiethnic Cohort, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Southern Community Cohort Study, the MD Anderson Cancer Center, the University of North Carolina CanCORS and Rectal Cancer studies and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-023-41819-0/MediaObjects/41467_2023_41819_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To discover additional risk loci for this cancer, we combine, via a meta-analysis, two GWAS of CRC in populations of Japanese and African American ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002059> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in African Americans, part of a 'Minority GWAS' effort alongside a Japanese study, that pooled African American cases and controls identified from the Multiethnic Cohort, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Southern Community Cohort Study, the MD Anderson Cancer Center, the University of North Carolina CanCORS and Rectal Cancer studies and the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002060> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002060>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These genome-wide data were obtained from healthy Norwegian individuals recruited through the Norwegian Bone Marrow Donor Registry held at the Institute of Immunology, Oslo University Hospital, Norway (http://www.nordonor.org/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002060> "A set of healthy Norwegian controls, recruited through the Norwegian Bone Marrow Donor Registry of the Institute of Immunology, Oslo University Hospital, whose genome-wide genotypes were generated on the Illumina 550 chip by the Myasthenia Gravis Genetic Consortium and shared as external control data for genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These samples were genotyped on the IIlumina 550 chip by the Myasthenia Gravis Genetic Consortium (MGGC) who generously provided these data as external controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002060> "A set of healthy Norwegian controls, recruited through the Norwegian Bone Marrow Donor Registry of the Institute of Immunology, Oslo University Hospital, whose genome-wide genotypes were generated on the Illumina 550 chip by the Myasthenia Gravis Genetic Consortium and shared as external control data for genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25812009") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4374872/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These CAMP MGH participants all underwent a 75-g OGTT in the absence of anti-hyperglycemic therapies, in which plasma glucose was measured by hexokinase assay (Abbott; Chicago, IL), and insulin international units were determined using a radio-immunoassay (Roche; Indianapolis, IN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5679734/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we sought to validate PGS for QT interval in two ‘real-world’ cohorts of European and African ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5679734/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals in the CAMP cohort were entirely outpatients, and underwent an ECG as an elective procedure, while subjects in the PHB population were more likely to have undergone an ECG to evaluate for cardiac disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5679734/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CAMP cohort was genotyped on Illumina Infinium HumanCoreExome-24 BeadChips, and imputed to 1000 Genomes Reference Panel (Phase1, v3) using Impute2 (version 2.3.1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5679734/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cardiovascular and Metabolic Patient (CAMP) cohort is composed of 3,756 individuals who underwent assessment of demographic data, past medical history, including medications, and a single resting ECG measurement.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28986454") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29295838") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5937525/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from the Cardiology and Metabolic Patient Cohort study at Massachusetts General Hospital (n=1,675) were used to validate genetic associations with insulin secretion as well as test the observational association of insulin secretion and BMI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002061> "A cohort of outpatients at Massachusetts General Hospital with recorded demographic data, medical and medication history and a resting electrocardiogram, many of whom also underwent an oral glucose tolerance test, genotyped genome-wide for genetic studies of cardiometabolic traits such as the QT interval, insulin secretion and body mass index.")

