AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37783704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood leukocyte DNA samples were genotyped on the Illumina 1M-Duo or the Illumina 660W-Quad arrays yielding, after quality control (QC) procedures, data for 323,852 SNPs available for all Japanese samples (see Methods and Supplementary Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002064> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in people of Japanese ancestry that pooled cases and controls from the Multiethnic Cohort Study, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study and case-control studies in Hawaii and in Fukuoka and Nagano, Japan, first analysed in a trans-ethnic meta-analysis with a parallel African American study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37783704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first GWAS, Japanese samples (n = 6,424) were identified from the Multiethnic Cohort study (MEC), the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry (CCFR), the Japan Public Health Center cohort study (JPHC) and three case-control studies in Hawaii (CR2&3) and in Fukuoka and Nagano, Japan (Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002064> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in people of Japanese ancestry that pooled cases and controls from the Multiethnic Cohort Study, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study and case-control studies in Hawaii and in Fukuoka and Nagano, Japan, first analysed in a trans-ethnic meta-analysis with a parallel African American study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37783704") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4180879/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To discover additional risk loci for this cancer, we combine, via a meta-analysis, two GWAS of CRC in populations of Japanese and African American ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002064> "A genome-wide association study of colorectal cancer in people of Japanese ancestry that pooled cases and controls from the Multiethnic Cohort Study, the Colorectal Cancer Family Registry, the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study and case-control studies in Hawaii and in Fukuoka and Nagano, Japan, first analysed in a trans-ethnic meta-analysis with a parallel African American study.")

