# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2681011") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stage 1 consisted of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium (MIGen), a collection of 2,967 cases of early-onset MI (in men ≤50 years old or women ≤60 years old) and 3,075 age- and sex-matched controls free of MI from six international sites: Boston and Seattle in the United States as well as Sweden, Finland, Spain, and Italy (Table 1 and Supplementary Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069> "An international consortium of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease case-control studies, formed for a genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction (men aged 50 or younger, women 60 or younger) and age- and sex-matched controls from sites in Boston and Seattle in the United States, Sweden, Finland, Spain and Italy, and later extended with further case-control cohorts for exome and gene sequencing studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2681011") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We designed a three-staged GWAS of early-onset MI with SNPs, common CNVs, and rare CNVs (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069> "An international consortium of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease case-control studies, formed for a genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction (men aged 50 or younger, women 60 or younger) and age- and sex-matched controls from sites in Boston and Seattle in the United States, Sweden, Finland, Spain and Italy, and later extended with further case-control cohorts for exome and gene sequencing studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5664181/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LPL gene was sequenced in 10 CAD case-control cohorts of the multinational Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium and a nested CAD case-control cohort of the Geisinger Health System DiscovEHR cohort between 2010 and 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069> "An international consortium of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease case-control studies, formed for a genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction (men aged 50 or younger, women 60 or younger) and age- and sex-matched controls from sites in Boston and Seattle in the United States, Sweden, Finland, Spain and Italy, and later extended with further case-control cohorts for exome and gene sequencing studies of coronary artery disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19198609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28267856") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5664181/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole exome sequencing of the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Consortium was performed at the Broad Institute (Cambridge, MA, USA) as previously described between 2010 and 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002069> "An international consortium of myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease case-control studies, formed for a genome-wide association study of early-onset myocardial infarction (men aged 50 or younger, women 60 or younger) and age- and sex-matched controls from sites in Boston and Seattle in the United States, Sweden, Finland, Spain and Italy, and later extended with further case-control cohorts for exome and gene sequencing studies of coronary artery disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27557300+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We sought to provide prospective evidence of the clinical utility of the addition of the 70-gene signature to standard clinical-pathological criteria in selecting patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> "A randomized phase III trial of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC 10041/BIG 3-04) that enrolled women aged 18–70 years with operable early-stage invasive breast cancer and up to three positive lymph nodes at institutions in nine European countries from 2007 to 2011, to test whether the 70-gene signature (MammaPrint), used with clinical-pathological criteria, can select patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7385160/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were enrolled in 112 participating institutions in nine European countries between February 2007 and September 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> "A randomized phase III trial of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC 10041/BIG 3-04) that enrolled women aged 18–70 years with operable early-stage invasive breast cancer and up to three positive lymph nodes at institutions in nine European countries from 2007 to 2011, to test whether the 70-gene signature (MammaPrint), used with clinical-pathological criteria, can select patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7385160/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MINDACT trial3,4, sponsored by the European Organization of Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) and country-associated clinical trial groups, enrolled women aged ≥18 years that were diagnosed with histologically proven operable TNM stage I–II invasive breast cancer and 0–3 positive lymph nodes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> "A randomized phase III trial of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC 10041/BIG 3-04) that enrolled women aged 18–70 years with operable early-stage invasive breast cancer and up to three positive lymph nodes at institutions in nine European countries from 2007 to 2011, to test whether the 70-gene signature (MammaPrint), used with clinical-pathological criteria, can select patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7385160/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The largest trial that collected full-transcriptome expression data is the MINDACT trial2,3, an international, multi-center, prospective, phase III randomized trial whose main objective was to prospectively validate the 70-gene MammaPrint signature as a prognostic tool for the clinical evaluation of patients to help avoid chemotherapy4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> "A randomized phase III trial of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC 10041/BIG 3-04) that enrolled women aged 18–70 years with operable early-stage invasive breast cancer and up to three positive lymph nodes at institutions in nine European countries from 2007 to 2011, to test whether the 70-gene signature (MammaPrint), used with clinical-pathological criteria, can select patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27557300") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32719399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36689693") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10082287/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MINDACT included women age 18-70 years with operable invasive breast cancer (T1-3), 0-3 positive lymph nodes (N0-1), and no distant metastasis (M0).23,24") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002070> "A randomized phase III trial of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC 10041/BIG 3-04) that enrolled women aged 18–70 years with operable early-stage invasive breast cancer and up to three positive lymph nodes at institutions in nine European countries from 2007 to 2011, to test whether the 70-gene signature (MammaPrint), used with clinical-pathological criteria, can select patients for adjuvant chemotherapy.")

