AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23932335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25897678") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28771617") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23932335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23932335+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We wanted to investigate if biomarkers could improve prediction of lymph node metastasis and outcome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002080> "A prospective multicentre study of women treated for endometrial cancer (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00598845), centred on Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, Norway, that between May 2001 and February 2013 enrolled consenting patients at ten hospitals in Norway, Belgium and Sweden within the European Network for Individualized Treatment of Endometrial Cancer (ENITEC), collecting preoperative curettage or biopsy specimens, tumour tissue, blood and clinical follow-up to study molecular markers of lymph node metastasis and prognosis for preoperative risk stratification.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23932335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25897678") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28771617") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25897678") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4430715/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 402 endometrial cancer patients were prospectively included when treated at the Department of Gynaecology and Obstetrics, Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, Norway, from May 2001 to March 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002080> "A prospective multicentre study of women treated for endometrial cancer (ClinicalTrials.gov NCT00598845), centred on Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, Norway, that between May 2001 and February 2013 enrolled consenting patients at ten hospitals in Norway, Belgium and Sweden within the European Network for Individualized Treatment of Endometrial Cancer (ENITEC), collecting preoperative curettage or biopsy specimens, tumour tissue, blood and clinical follow-up to study molecular markers of lymph node metastasis and prognosis for preoperative risk stratification.")
