# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002081> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002081>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24885863") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24885863") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4035696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MONA LISA (Monitoring National du Risque Artériel; National Monitoring of Arterial Risk) Lille study was a population-based, cross-sectional study of a representative sample of 1578 participants recruited from within the Lille urban area in northern France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002081> "A population-based cross-sectional survey of cardiovascular risk factors in France, in which women and men aged 35 to 74 years were randomly selected from electoral rolls between 2005 and 2007 in three areas: the Lille urban community in northern France, the Bas-Rhin department in eastern France and the Haute-Garonne department in southwestern France.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24885863") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485857") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40485857") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12143755/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between 2005 and 2007, women and men aged 35–74 years were randomly selected from electoral rolls in three French regions: Lille urban community in Northern France, Bas-Rhin department in Eastern France, and Haute-Garonne department in Southwestern France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002081> "A population-based cross-sectional survey of cardiovascular risk factors in France, in which women and men aged 35 to 74 years were randomly selected from electoral rolls between 2005 and 2007 in three areas: the Lille urban community in northern France, the Bas-Rhin department in eastern France and the Haute-Garonne department in southwestern France.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30804558") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, we utilized additional autism family samples (318 trios collected by investigators of the Autism Consortium and in Montreal) with genome-wide Affymetrix 5.0/500K array data also genotyped at the Genetic Analysis Platform of the Broad Institute using the same conditions, QC, and analysis pipelines (Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> "A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30804558") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place in Massachusetts and surrounding states through contacts with parent support and patient advocacy groups, brochures, newsletters, and the study web site.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> "A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30804558") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2772655/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects diagnosed with autism spectrum disorders with both of their parents were recruited from clinics specializing in the diagnosis of Pervasive Developmental Disorders (PDD), readaptation centers, and specialized schools in the Montreal and Quebec City regions, Canada, as described 31.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> "A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30804558") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5441062/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Support for the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair (EDSP) family sample (part of the MonBos collection) was provided by the NLM Family foundation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> "A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19812673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30804558") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5441062/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MonBos Collection study was funded in part through a grant from the Autism Consortium of Boston.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002082> "A collection of families of children with autism spectrum disorder, recruited in the Montreal and Quebec City regions of Canada and by investigators of the Autism Consortium of Boston in Massachusetts and surrounding states of the United States, including the Extreme Discordant Sib-Pair family sample. Funded in part by the Autism Consortium of Boston, its parent-offspring trios have been genotyped for autism genome-wide association studies, including those of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27694991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here we generate new and so far unpublished genome-wide SNP data from 2,266 clinically well-characterized patients with BD (∼76% BD type I) and 5,028 ethnically matched controls, derived from the MooDS (Systematic Investigation of the Molecular Causes of Major Mood Disorders and Schizophrenia) consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083> "A German research consortium, the Integrated Genome Research Network MooDS of the National Genome Research Network plus (NGFNplus), funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, whose groups collected and genotyped case-control samples for genome-wide association studies of schizophrenia in Germany and of bipolar disorder in Germany and in partner centres in Poland, Russia, Spain, Canada and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27694991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over the last 5 years, the MooDS consortium produced two waves of genome-wide data for BD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083> "A German research consortium, the Integrated Genome Research Network MooDS of the National Genome Research Network plus (NGFNplus), funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, whose groups collected and genotyped case-control samples for genome-wide association studies of schizophrenia in Germany and of bipolar disorder in Germany and in partner centres in Poland, Russia, Spain, Canada and Australia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26854805") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27694991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24618891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms4339") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples originate from four European countries, Canada and Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002083> "A German research consortium, the Integrated Genome Research Network MooDS of the National Genome Research Network plus (NGFNplus), funded by the German Federal Ministry of Education and Research, whose groups collected and genotyped case-control samples for genome-wide association studies of schizophrenia in Germany and of bipolar disorder in Germany and in partner centres in Poland, Russia, Spain, Canada and Australia.")
