AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC8899940") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Osteoporotic fractures in men (MrOS) and women (MsOS) Hong Kong represent the first large-scale prospective cohort studies conducted on bone health in East Asians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8899940/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At baseline (BL), 2,000 Chinese men and 2,000 Chinese women ≥65 years were recruited from the local communities from August 2001 to March 2003, to determine the relationship between anthropometric, lifestyle, medical and other factors with bone mineral density (BMD) at the hip and spine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9573629/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The target was to recruit a stratified sample that equally assigned the cohort into three age groups (65–69, 70–74, and ≥75 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10006108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For older women, our MsOS(Hong Kong) year-14 and year-18 follow-up studies suggest that, subjects with minimal osteoporotic-like vertebral fracture (OLVF) had an incident VF risk higher than subjects without baseline OLVF (Table 2) (8,9).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11151245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our osteoporotic fractures in women (MsOS) Hong Kong study [materials see (33), T-scores re-calculated with local Hong Kong women BMD reference], 1,900 Chinese women were followed up for 8.82±1.49 years, and 69 hip fractur were recorded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33159570") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35284274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36235568") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36915360") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38846307") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41097147") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12526030/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cognitive function was assessed based on the Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE) [23] at baseline and reassessed in the fourth year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002094> "The women's arm of the Mr. Osteoporosis and Ms. Osteoporosis Study in Hong Kong: a prospective cohort of community-dwelling Chinese women aged 65 years or older in Hong Kong, recruited in 2001–2003 in a sample stratified by age group, whose osteoporotic hip, spine and vertebral fractures have been followed up for about two decades, with other outcomes of ageing such as diet, cognition and mortality studied in the same cohort.")

