# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9108705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2392892+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A birth-record based Registry is nearing completion of some 8,000 pairs of twins born in Minnesota from 1936 to 1955, plus some 1,200 pairs of male twins born 1971-81.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> "A birth-record-based registry of twins born in Minnesota, United States, identified from Minnesota State birth certificates and enrolled by mailed questionnaires together with their parents, spouses, siblings and children, covering twins born 1904–1934, 1936–1955 and 1961–1964 who were assessed in middle and older adulthood, with subsets later assessed in person, as one of the studies of the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9108705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7056536/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MTR twins completed brief questionnaires via mail when they were enrolled, and subsets of MTR twins have completed subsequent in-person assessments; parents, spouses, same-sex siblings, and children of MTR twins were also recruited and completed brief questionnaires via mail at the time of the initial ascertainment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> "A birth-record-based registry of twins born in Minnesota, United States, identified from Minnesota State birth certificates and enrolled by mailed questionnaires together with their parents, spouses, siblings and children, covering twins born 1904–1934, 1936–1955 and 1961–1964 who were assessed in middle and older adulthood, with subsets later assessed in person, as one of the studies of the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9108705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7056536/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MTR twins were identified from Minnesota State birth certificates, which are publically available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> "A birth-record-based registry of twins born in Minnesota, United States, identified from Minnesota State birth certificates and enrolled by mailed questionnaires together with their parents, spouses, siblings and children, covering twins born 1904–1934, 1936–1955 and 1961–1964 who were assessed in middle and older adulthood, with subsets later assessed in person, as one of the studies of the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9108705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7056536/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The MCTFR includes the Minnesota Twin Registry (MTR), a cohort of twins who have completed assessments in middle and older adulthood;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> "A birth-record-based registry of twins born in Minnesota, United States, identified from Minnesota State birth certificates and enrolled by mailed questionnaires together with their parents, spouses, siblings and children, covering twins born 1904–1934, 1936–1955 and 1961–1964 who were assessed in middle and older adulthood, with subsets later assessed in person, as one of the studies of the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2392892") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9108705") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31796137") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7056536/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Minnesota Twin Registry (MTR) includes monozygotic (MZ) and same-sex dizygotic (DZ) twins born between 1904 and 1934 (1802 twins), 1936 and 1955 (8614 twins), and 1961 and 1964 (782 twins) who have completed assessments in middle and older adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002098> "A birth-record-based registry of twins born in Minnesota, United States, identified from Minnesota State birth certificates and enrolled by mailed questionnaires together with their parents, spouses, siblings and children, covering twins born 1904–1934, 1936–1955 and 1961–1964 who were assessed in middle and older adulthood, with subsets later assessed in person, as one of the studies of the Minnesota Center for Twin and Family Research.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All exome sequencing was performed at the Broad Institute of Harvard and MIT; samples sequence capture was performed using Illumina's ICE Capture reagent and sequencing was performed on an Illumina HiSeq 2000 or 2500.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> "A case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany, with cases who had a myocardial infarction before age 41 (men) or 56 (women) and controls from German population studies without myocardial infarction or coronary artery disease over age 65 (men) or 75 (women), exome-sequenced in the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Exome Sequencing Consortium to find genetic contributors to early myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were defined as men with myocardial infarction (MI) before age 41 and women with MI before age 56.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> "A case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany, with cases who had a myocardial infarction before age 41 (men) or 56 (women) and controls from German population studies without myocardial infarction or coronary artery disease over age 65 (men) or 75 (women), exome-sequenced in the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Exome Sequencing Consortium to find genetic contributors to early myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were selected from German population studies and were individuals without MI or coronary artery disease (CAD) over age 65 and 75 for men and women, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> "A case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany, with cases who had a myocardial infarction before age 41 (men) or 56 (women) and controls from German population studies without myocardial infarction or coronary artery disease over age 65 (men) or 75 (women), exome-sequenced in the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Exome Sequencing Consortium to find genetic contributors to early myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is focused on understanding the genetic contributors to early myocardial-infarction (MI) in the German population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> "A case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany, with cases who had a myocardial infarction before age 41 (men) or 56 (women) and controls from German population studies without myocardial infarction or coronary artery disease over age 65 (men) or 75 (women), exome-sequenced in the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Exome Sequencing Consortium to find genetic contributors to early myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000916.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Munich-MI study is a case-control cohort study recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002099> "A case-control study of early-onset myocardial infarction recruited at the German Heart Center in Munich, Germany, with cases who had a myocardial infarction before age 41 (men) or 56 (women) and controls from German population studies without myocardial infarction or coronary artery disease over age 65 (men) or 75 (women), exome-sequenced in the Myocardial Infarction Genetics Exome Sequencing Consortium to find genetic contributors to early myocardial infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24144296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32193507") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the Myopia Genomics Study of Hong Kong, unrelated individuals of Chinese descent aged between 18 and 45 years were recruited via the Optometry Clinic at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University with details as described previously23-25 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102> "A genetic study of myopia at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University, which recruited unrelated adults of Chinese descent aged 18 to 45 years through the university's Optometry Clinic, excluding people with signs of ocular disorders or of inherited disorders associated with myopia, measured their refraction by cycloplegic autorefraction together with corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length, and genotyped them genome-wide; it is a member study of the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia (CREAM).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24144296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32193507") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hong Kong Study (10 < age ≤ 25) Illumina HumanCNV370-Quadv3 IMPUTE v2.3.0 1000 Genome Reference panels 7419383 0.996") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102> "A genetic study of myopia at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University, which recruited unrelated adults of Chinese descent aged 18 to 45 years through the university's Optometry Clinic, excluding people with signs of ocular disorders or of inherited disorders associated with myopia, measured their refraction by cycloplegic autorefraction together with corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length, and genotyped them genome-wide; it is a member study of the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia (CREAM).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24144296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32193507") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ophthalmic examination was performed with refraction measured by cycloplegic autorefraction together with the measurement of other ocular components including corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102> "A genetic study of myopia at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University, which recruited unrelated adults of Chinese descent aged 18 to 45 years through the university's Optometry Clinic, excluding people with signs of ocular disorders or of inherited disorders associated with myopia, measured their refraction by cycloplegic autorefraction together with corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length, and genotyped them genome-wide; it is a member study of the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia (CREAM).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24144296") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32193507") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs42003-020-0802-y/MediaObjects/42003_2020_802_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with signs of ocular disorders or other inherited disorders associated with myopia were excluded from the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002102> "A genetic study of myopia at the Hong Kong Polytechnic University, which recruited unrelated adults of Chinese descent aged 18 to 45 years through the university's Optometry Clinic, excluding people with signs of ocular disorders or of inherited disorders associated with myopia, measured their refraction by cycloplegic autorefraction together with corneal curvature, lens thickness and axial length, and genotyped them genome-wide; it is a member study of the Consortium for Refractive Error and Myopia (CREAM).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26541979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30054336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26541979") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26541979+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From October 2008 to February 2015, we established a hospital-based cohort of ovarian cancer patients and the germline status of all 218 women with invasive epithelial ovarian cancer was tested using targeted amplification and sequencing of the intron-exon junctions and exonic sequences of BRCA1, BRCA2, PALB2 and TP53.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103> "A single-centre, hospital-based case cohort of women with ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer in Malaysia, recruited consecutively at a private hospital from October 2008 to February 2015 and tested for germline variants in BRCA1 and BRCA2; it takes part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the study code MAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26541979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30054336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7619263/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Malaysian Ovarian Cancer Genetic (MyOvCa) study, a single-centre hospital-based case cohort where consecutive cases from a private hospital were recruited between October 2008 and February 2015 (3),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103> "A single-centre, hospital-based case cohort of women with ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer in Malaysia, recruited consecutively at a private hospital from October 2008 to February 2015 and tested for germline variants in BRCA1 and BRCA2; it takes part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the study code MAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26541979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30054336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7619263/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study participants included women clinically diagnosed with ovarian, fallopian, or primary peritoneal cancer, recruited from two cohorts:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103> "A single-centre, hospital-based case cohort of women with ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer in Malaysia, recruited consecutively at a private hospital from October 2008 to February 2015 and tested for germline variants in BRCA1 and BRCA2; it takes part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the study code MAS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26541979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30054336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42013351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Malaysia Ovarian Cancer Study MAS Malaysia Need info 106 106 0 c -‐") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002103> "A single-centre, hospital-based case cohort of women with ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer in Malaysia, recruited consecutively at a private hospital from October 2008 to February 2015 and tested for germline variants in BRCA1 and BRCA2; it takes part in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium under the study code MAS.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17594470+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A cohort of 800 85 year olds from Newcastle and North Tyneside will be recruited at baseline and followed until the last participant has died.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17594470+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants will be visited in their current residence (own home or institution) by a research nurse at baseline, 18 months and 36 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Excepting these exclusions, all those remaining in the sampling frame were sent a letter of invitation by the study team, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of their state of health. Recruitment and assessment took place over a 17 month period during 2006-7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participation at baseline entailed a detailed multidimensional health assessment, comprising questionnaires, measurements, function tests, a fasting blood sample, and a review of medical records held by the general practice; participants could decline elements of the protocol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Newcastle 85+ Study aims to determine the full spectrum of health within an inception cohort of 85 year olds, selected without regard to health status, and to examine health trajectories and outcomes as the cohort ages and the association between these outcomes and a complex array of clinical, biological, and psychosocial factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17594470") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20028777") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797051/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sampling frame comprised all people born in 1921 who were permanently registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside primary care trusts in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002104> "A prospective inception cohort study of health and ageing in the very old in North East England, funded by the UK Medical Research Council and the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, which invited everyone born in 1921 (turning 85 in 2006) who was registered with a participating general practice in Newcastle upon Tyne or North Tyneside, whether living at home or in an institution and regardless of health, recruited them in 2006–2007, assessed them at home with a multidimensional health assessment, review of general practice records and fasting blood samples, with repeat assessments at 18 and 36 months and follow-up until death, to study health trajectories, their biological, medical and social determinants, and the biology of ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39858580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this regard, available data from 351 individuals in a Greek case–control NAFLD study were also used during following stages of our analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> "A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39858580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment was carried out at the Outpatient Clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine in Laiko General Hospital between 2012 and 2015.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> "A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39858580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study consisted of adult participants free of any secondary liver disease or injury while reporting no excessive alcohol intake.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> "A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39858580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was approved by the Ethics Committee of Harokopio University of Athens (38074/13-07-2012), based on the Helsinki Declaration, and all participants provided a written participant consent form prior to their enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> "A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39858580") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11765347/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Volunteer participants were classified as cases or controls according to the level of hepatic steatosis, if any.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002105> "A case-control study of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease run by Harokopio University of Athens in Greek adults without secondary liver disease or excessive alcohol intake, recruited between 2012 and 2015 at the outpatient clinics of the First Department of Propaedeutic and Internal Medicine, Laiko General Hospital, Athens, and classified as cases or controls by degree of hepatic steatosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3068622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A computer-assisted telephone interview adapted from the Semi-Structured Assessment for the Genetics of Alcoholism (SSAGA) was then administered.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3068622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, prior reports by index cases of smoking status and family structure (in surveys of two large Australian Twin Panel cohorts and of spouses of the older twin cohort) were used to ascertain families with a sib pair [containing at most one monozygotic (MZ) twin] concordant for heavy smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3068622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Interviewing was conducted from 2001-2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3068622/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Australian component of the NAG project, a collaboration between Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) and Washington University School of Medicine (WUSM) investigators, used data collection procedures approved by both institutions’ institutional review boards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4057087/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on earlier questionnaires, ever-smoking concordant twin pairs and their family members were recruited in 2001–2005 for the Nicotine Addiction Genetics (NAG) Finland study, as part of the consortium including Finland, Australia, and USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18519829") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19878140") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700436") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24927283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29532581") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6519128/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were assessed by DNA sample collection and a structured diagnostic psychiatric interview resulting in detailed phenotypic information on multiple smoking behavior traits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002106> "A multisite consortium of Finland, Australia and the United States for the genetics of nicotine dependence, coordinated from Washington University School of Medicine: its Australian component, run with the Queensland Institute of Medical Research, recruited families with a sib pair concordant for heavy smoking, identified from surveys of Australian Twin Registry cohorts, and interviewed them by telephone in 2001–2006, and its Finnish component recruited twin pairs from the Finnish Twin Cohort concordant for ever-smoking, with their family members (mainly siblings), in 2001–2005; participants were assessed with a structured diagnostic interview and gave DNA for linkage and association studies of nicotine dependence and related substance use.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21324183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One control was matched for each case by age (within 3 years) and by residential area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-0168-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were recruited between 2001 and 2005 at four hospitals in Nagano, and between 2001 and 2006 at eight hospitals in São Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-0168-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were a consecutive series of female patients aged 20–74 years with newly diagnosed and histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-0168-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the study in Nagano, eligible controls were selected from medical checkup examinees in two of the four hospitals and confirmed not to have cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3050759/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-0168-1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These multicenter, hospital-based case–control studies of breast cancer were designed to determine lifestyle factors and genetic susceptibility to the risk of breast cancer and to compare potential risk factors among Japanese living in Nagano, Japan, and Japanese Brazilians and non-Japanese Brazilians living in São Paulo, Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002107> "A multicentre hospital-based case-control study of breast cancer in Nagano, Japan, enrolling a consecutive series of women aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed invasive breast cancer at four hospitals and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees matched by age and residential area, designed to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors and, with a parallel study in São Paulo, Brazil, to compare Japanese, Japanese Brazilian and non-Japanese Brazilian women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By using a national registry and biobank established in 1996 with serial samples including the majority of Norwegian patients with Addison’s disease, we aimed to investigate the robustness of the 21OH-Abs assay and its clinical value in defining autoimmune PAI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110> "A national registry and biobank of patients with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease) in Norway, established in 1996 within the National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS) at Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, that collects clinical information, demographics and serial biological samples from most Norwegian patients with the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Norwegian Addison Registry (ROAS) collates clinical information, demographics, and biological samples from patients with PAI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110> "A national registry and biobank of patients with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease) in Norway, established in 1996 within the National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS) at Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, that collects clinical information, demographics and serial biological samples from most Norwegian patients with the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with POI were identified among AAD patients in the National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS), encompassing the Norwegian Addison Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110> "A national registry and biobank of patients with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease) in Norway, established in 1996 within the National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS) at Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, that collects clinical information, demographics and serial biological samples from most Norwegian patients with the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8052519/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8208662/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS), Department of Medicine, Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, Norway, for handling blood samples and analyzing autoantibodies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002110> "A national registry and biobank of patients with primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison's disease) in Norway, established in 1996 within the National Registry of Organ-Specific Autoimmune Diseases (ROAS) at Haukeland University Hospital, Bergen, that collects clinical information, demographics and serial biological samples from most Norwegian patients with the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NAROD | Women's College Research Institute Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer Study | CANADA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Its purpose is to better understand the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancers. We hope to gain a better understanding of the interaction between various hormonal, reproductive, and lifestyle factors that may be associated with the development of breast and ovarian cancer in high-risk families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was started in 1995") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To participate you will complete a questionnaire that asks questions about your health, menstrual cycle, lifestyle, etc. every two years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women who have learned that they have a mutation in either the BRCA1, BRCA2 or PALB2 gene are eligible, regardless of their personal cancer history Women who are 18 years of age or older") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.womensacademics.ca/active-studies/risk-factor-analysis-of-hereditary-breast-and-ovarian-cancer/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "participants from across Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean, and Latin America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002111> "A long-term study, started in 1995 at Women's College Hospital in Toronto, Canada, of women aged 18 or over carrying a BRCA1 or BRCA2 (later also PALB2) mutation, whatever their cancer history, recruited from Canada, the United States, Europe, Asia, the Caribbean and Latin America and followed by questionnaires every two years, to study hormonal, reproductive and lifestyle factors in the prevention and treatment of hereditary breast and ovarian cancer; it contributes carriers to CIMBA.")

