AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Most of these were also drawn from already existing DNA databases of ischemic stroke patients (SIFAP,15 SAHLSIS, Gothenburg,16 Nijmegen,17 Barcelona stroke genetics study6 )") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002120> "A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection, of European origin, at Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre, the Netherlands, drawn in part from the FUTURE study and meeting the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, which with controls from Nijmegen and the Rotterdam Study formed one of the follow-up samples of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25420145") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3154/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3154_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Netherlands Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Center/the FUTURE study Nijmegen 20 Netherlands Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Center and Rotterdam Study † Nijmegen (N=36) and Rotterdam (N=400) 436") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002120> "A collection of patients with cervical artery dissection, of European origin, at Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Centre, the Netherlands, drawn in part from the FUTURE study and meeting the inclusion criteria of the CADISP study, which with controls from Nijmegen and the Rotterdam Study formed one of the follow-up samples of the 2015 genome-wide association study of cervical artery dissection.")

