AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2883069/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "English school children (n= 792) aged between 7 and 9 years from an unselected population birth cohort (the North Cumbria Community Genetics Project) were examined, each on one occasion") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3316565/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples and data from this prospective, unselected, population-based cohort were collected between 1996 and 2003 at a single maternity unit in West Cumbria, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1051317") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The North Cumbria Community Genetics Project was first conceived in autumn 1993 at meetings between the University ofNewcastle (Department of Human Genetics and the Sir James Spence Institute of Child Health) and Westlakes Research Institute (Genetics Unit and the Department of Occupational Health and Medical Statistics).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1051317") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This encompassed methodology for the collection and storage of samples from newborns at the West Cumberland Hospital subject to informed maternal consent, together with a short lifestyle questionnaire to be completed by the mother.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9610806+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of the North Cumbria Community Genetics Project is to establish a store of DNA, plasma, and viable cells from a cohort of around 8000 Cumbrian infants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19681860") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22479380") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24098518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9610806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9610806+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To meet this objective, specimens of umbilical cord blood and tissue will be collected with maternal consent from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital, Whitehaven over a five year period from January 1996.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002121> "A prospective, unselected, population-based birth cohort in West Cumbria, England, set up by the University of Newcastle and the Westlakes Research Institute, which from January 1996 to 2003 collected umbilical cord blood and tissue, with maternal consent and a short maternal lifestyle questionnaire, from babies born at the West Cumberland Hospital maternity unit in Whitehaven, storing DNA, plasma and viable cells as a resource for genetic and epidemiological studies of gene–environment interaction and health, with some children followed up in childhood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A hospital-based case-control study 22 was conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples were collected at the same time as the questionnaire, and a buffy coat was preserved at –80°C until analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Dietary habits were investigated using a 141-item semi-quantitative food-frequency questionnaire, which was developed and validated in the Japanese population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were patients aged 20–74 years with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer during the survey at those hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy controls who were confirmed as not having any cancer were selected from medical checkup examinees in the four hospitals. Two controls were matched to each case on sex, age (within three years), hospital and residential area and 245 controls participated (participation rate = 99%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25105248") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms5613/MediaObjects/41467_2014_BFncomms5613_MOESM440_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants completed a self-administered questionnaire, which included questions on demographic characteristics, anthropometric factors, smoking habits, family history of cancer, and medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002122> "A hospital-based case-control study of colorectal cancer conducted between October 1998 and March 2002 at four hospitals in Nagano Prefecture, Japan, enrolling patients aged 20-74 with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed colorectal cancer and cancer-free controls from medical check-up examinees at the same hospitals, matched on sex, age, hospital and residential area, with self-administered and food-frequency questionnaires and blood samples.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3919005/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The New England Bladder Cancer Study (NEBCS) represents a single study comprises Maine (ME) and Vermont (VT) components genotyped in NCI-GWAS1, and the New Hampshire (NH) component genotyped in NCI-GWAS2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3919005/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the new bladder cancer GWAS was comprised 2422 cases genotyped with the HumanHap 660w and HumanHap 610 (Illumina, San Diego, CA, USA) and 5751 cancer-free controls selected from previously scanned studies at the NCI (NCI-GWAS2) (Fig. 1, Supplementary Material, Table S1) (9,16–21).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(specifically Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial, and The American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were defined as individuals having histologically confirmed primary carcinoma of the urinary bladder, including carcinoma in situ (ICD-0-2 topography codes C67.0-C67.9 or ICD9 codes 188.1-188.9).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Scan data were obtained from two case-control studies carried out in Spain and the United States (specifically, those in the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohort studies in Finland and the United States") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22238607") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24163127") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000346.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used data from 591,637 single nucleotide polymorphisms 3,532 affected individuals (cases) and 5,119 controls of European descent and replication including 8382 cases and 48275 controls from 16 studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002123> "The US National Cancer Institute's genome-wide association study of bladder cancer, which pooled cases with histologically confirmed bladder cancer and controls of European descent from two case-control studies in Spain and the United States (the Spanish Bladder Cancer Study and the Maine and Vermont components of the New England Bladder Cancer Study) and three prospective cohorts in Finland and the United States (the Alpha-Tocopherol, Beta-Carotene Cancer Prevention Study, the Prostate, Lung, Colorectal and Ovarian Cancer Screening Trial and the American Cancer Society Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort) in its first scan (NCI-GWAS1), and added a second scan (NCI-GWAS2) of further cases, including the New Hampshire component of the New England Bladder Cancer Study, with cancer-free controls from previously scanned NCI studies, to identify susceptibility loci for bladder cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002124> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002124>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15342441") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26956414") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29674426") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17588155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10552-007-9025-5") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls aged 65–74 years were randomly selected from Center for Medicare and Medicaid Services files of residents eligible for Medicare, also stratified on geographic area, sex, age, and race.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002124> "A multicentre population-based case-control study of non-Hodgkin lymphoma in the United States, run by the US National Cancer Institute, whose cases were people with a first primary non-Hodgkin lymphoma (excluding people infected with HIV) identified through four Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results cancer registries (Detroit, Iowa, Los Angeles and Seattle), and whose controls from the same areas were matched on area, age and race and found by random digit dialling (under 65) or from Medicare files (65 and over).")
