# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biospecimens were stored at each research site but with centralised management of biospecimen information by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Colorectal Cancer Patients Cohort (CRCPC) was a national, multicentre prospective cohort study, which was initiated in January 2015 and established at 16 hospitals (online supplemental table S1) from 11 provinces in China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In CRCPC, follow-up was conducted with both active and passive approaches at 6, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48 and 60 months after surgery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CRCSC was first launched in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, in January 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NCRCC study includes the Colorectal Cancer Screening Cohort (CRCSC), which recruited individuals who were at high risk of CRC between 2016 and 2020 and Colorectal Cancer Patients Cohort (CRCPC), which recruited newly diagnosed patients with CRC between 2015 and 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34903541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8672005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Colorectal Cancer Cohort (NCRCC) study aims to specifically assess risk factors and biomarkers related to endpoints across the colorectal cancer continuum from the aetiology through survivorship.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002127> "A prospective cohort study in China, coordinated by the Second Affiliated Hospital of Zhejiang University, of risk factors and biomarkers across the colorectal cancer continuum from aetiology to survivorship, made up of a screening cohort of people at high risk of colorectal cancer recruited from 2016 to 2020, first in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, and a multicentre cohort of patients newly diagnosed with colorectal cancer recruited from 2015 to 2020 at 16 hospitals in 11 provinces and followed up after surgery.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3201934/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Norfolk Diabetes case-control study is a study of men and women with T2D in Norfolk, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in Norfolk, UK, whose cases were men and women with type 2 diabetes identified through general practice diabetes registers and local hospital diabetes clinic and retinal screening programme registers in Norfolk, and whose controls, free of known diabetes, were randomly selected from participants of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3737432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 6,950 controls free of known diabetes at baseline or during follow-up were randomly selected from European Prospective Investigation of Cancer (EPIC)-Norfolk participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in Norfolk, UK, whose cases were men and women with type 2 diabetes identified through general practice diabetes registers and local hospital diabetes clinic and retinal screening programme registers in Norfolk, and whose controls, free of known diabetes, were randomly selected from participants of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3737432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All type 2 diabetes patients identified through general practice diabetes registers in Norfolk and local hospital diabetes clinic and retinal screening programme patient registers were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in Norfolk, UK, whose cases were men and women with type 2 diabetes identified through general practice diabetes registers and local hospital diabetes clinic and retinal screening programme registers in Norfolk, and whose controls, free of known diabetes, were randomly selected from participants of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22039354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23702607") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3737432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Norfolk Diabetes Case–Control Study is a study of men and women with type 2 diabetes in Norfolk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002128> "A type 2 diabetes case-control study in Norfolk, UK, whose cases were men and women with type 2 diabetes identified through general practice diabetes registers and local hospital diabetes clinic and retinal screening programme registers in Norfolk, and whose controls, free of known diabetes, were randomly selected from participants of the EPIC-Norfolk cohort.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15978930+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because presentation of EBV antigenic peptides can elicit vigorous immune responses, we investigated associations of the HLA region with EBV-positive and EBV-negative Hodgkin's lymphoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed in the northern Netherlands between 1987 and 2009, whose tumours were classified by WHO criteria and Epstein-Barr virus status and whose germline DNA, with that of first-degree relatives of patients diagnosed up to 2000, was used to study HLA associations with Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative Hodgkin lymphoma; its classical Hodgkin lymphoma cases were one of the five case series of the European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15978930+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Germline DNA was isolated from 200 patients diagnosed between 1987 and 2000 and from their first-degree relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed in the northern Netherlands between 1987 and 2009, whose tumours were classified by WHO criteria and Epstein-Barr virus status and whose germline DNA, with that of first-degree relatives of patients diagnosed up to 2000, was used to study HLA associations with Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative Hodgkin lymphoma; its classical Hodgkin lymphoma cases were one of the five case series of the European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15978930+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a retrospective, population-based study, patients with Hodgkin's lymphoma were reclassified according to the WHO classification, and EBV status was assessed by in-situ hybridisation of EBV-encoded small RNAs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed in the northern Netherlands between 1987 and 2009, whose tumours were classified by WHO criteria and Epstein-Barr virus status and whose germline DNA, with that of first-degree relatives of patients diagnosed up to 2000, was used to study HLA associations with Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative Hodgkin lymphoma; its classical Hodgkin lymphoma cases were one of the five case series of the European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3274508/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide genotyping was performed on cHL case samples from five European-based HL studies: the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin’s Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study, and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed in the northern Netherlands between 1987 and 2009, whose tumours were classified by WHO criteria and Epstein-Barr virus status and whose germline DNA, with that of first-degree relatives of patients diagnosed up to 2000, was used to study HLA associations with Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative Hodgkin lymphoma; its classical Hodgkin lymphoma cases were one of the five case series of the European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15978930") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24920014") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3274508/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study comprises a population-based case patient series of HL diagnosed in Northern Netherlands between January 1987 and April 2009 (8).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002129> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma diagnosed in the northern Netherlands between 1987 and 2009, whose tumours were classified by WHO criteria and Epstein-Barr virus status and whose germline DNA, with that of first-degree relatives of patients diagnosed up to 2000, was used to study HLA associations with Epstein-Barr virus-positive and -negative Hodgkin lymphoma; its classical Hodgkin lymphoma cases were one of the five case series of the European genome-wide association study of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2567988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information regarding recurrence, stage, grade and histology of endometrial cancer was collected from the medical records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data on reproductive and environmental risk factors including ethnicity was collected using self reported questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients presenting at this hospital-based site were captured by ANECS recruitment from 2005 onwards.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Newcastle Endometrial Cancer Study (NECS) includes histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases consecutively recruited from 1992 up to 2005 at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia15 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we conduct a meta-GWAS including 12,906 endometrial cancer cases and 108,979 country-matched controls of European ancestry from 17 studies identified via the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium (ECAC), the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium (E2C2) and the UK Biobank and report a further nine genome-wide significant endometrial cancer genetic risk regions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18822177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30093612") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6085317/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NECS | Newcastle Endometrial Cancer Study | Australia;  hospital-based cases |  | Illumina OncoArray 534K | 170 | 124 | 23") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002130> "A hospital-based series of histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases recruited consecutively from 1992 to 2005 among women presenting for treatment at the Hunter Centre for Gynaecological Cancer, John Hunter Hospital, in Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia, with reproductive and environmental risk factors (including ethnicity) from self-reported questionnaires and recurrence, stage, grade and histology from medical records; from 2005 patients at this site were recruited by the Australian National Endometrial Cancer Study. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All clinical data was reviewed and copies of the original visual field tests were re-evaluated for criteria meeting the case definition described below by the coordinating center at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls for the NEIGHBOR study were collected from 12 sites in parallel with the collection of cases and controls from 3 sites for the GLAUGEN study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls were at least 35 years old and were European-derived or Hispanic Caucasians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NEIGHBOR (NEI Glaucoma Human genetics collaBORation) consortium is a unique collaborative effort involving investigators at 12 institutions located throughout the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NEIGHBOR consortium includes samples from two landmark NEI-funded clinical trials (CIGTS, AGIS) investigating treatment outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22570617") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22828004") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3485429/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The consortium has harmonized clinical definitions and genotyping platforms with the GLAUGEN POAG GWAS that is part of the GENEVA consortium (22), allowing for inter-study validation and a combined meta-analysis of at least 3500 cases and 3500 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002131> "A case-control study for a genome-wide association study of primary open-angle glaucoma, run by a consortium of investigators at 12 institutions across the United States, whose cases and controls, aged 35 or over and of European or Hispanic white ancestry, were collected at the 12 sites. Most came from university glaucoma and general ophthalmology clinics, and some from other studies such as the Marshfield Personalized Medicine Research Project and the CIGTS and AGIS glaucoma trials. The case and control definitions were harmonised with the GLAUGEN study, and the clinical data were reviewed centrally at the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3482/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3482_MOESM79_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NEIGHBORHOOD, National Eye Institute Glaucoma Human Genetics Collaboration Heritable Overall Operational Database; NHS/HPFS, Nurses Health Study/Health Professionals Follow-up Study; MEEI, Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary; NEIGHBOR, National Eye Institute Glaucoma Human Genetics Collaboration; OHTS, Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study; WGHS, Women’s Genome Health Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> "A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses' Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women's Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For all 8 NEIGHBORHOOD studies cases were primarily defined as at least 1 reliable visual field showing loss consistent with glaucoma, without a secondary cause, or CDR (cup-to-disc ratio) ≥ 0.7 or CDR asymmetry ≥ 0.2 or documented progression of optic nerve degeneration (in the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study [OHTS]).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> "A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses' Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women's Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For stage 1 (discovery) we meta-analyzed summary data from 8 independent datasets (3,853 cases and 33,480 controls; Supplementary Table 1) with European ancestry from the United States collectively referred to as the National Eye Institute Glaucoma Human Genetics Collaboration Heritable Overall Operational Database (NEIGHBORHOOD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> "A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses' Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women's Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4731307/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the overall NEIGHBORHOOD (NBH), the summary value for the population cohorts (POP; NHS/HPFS/WGHS) are presented separately from the case/control cohorts (CC; Iowa, OHTS (Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study), Marshfield, MEEI, NEIGHBOR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> "A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses' Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women's Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26752265") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27760082") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5266624/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The national eye institute glaucoma human collaboration heritable overall operational database (NEIGHBORHOOD) dataset represents a genome-wide meta-analysis summary dataset from eight independent studies, including the Nurses’ Health Study, with a total of 3,853 POAG cases and 33,480 controls of European ancestry from the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002132> "A genome-wide meta-analysis resource for primary open-angle glaucoma that combines summary data from eight independent case-control and population-based datasets of European ancestry from the United States: the NEIGHBOR study, the Nurses' Health Study, the Health Professionals Follow-up Study, the Women's Genome Health Study, the Ocular Hypertension Treatment Study, and collections from Iowa, Marshfield and the Massachusetts Eye and Ear Infirmary. Cases in all datasets were defined by a harmonised glaucoma definition.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases with histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 using the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center (DHMC) Tumor Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer, based at Dartmouth College, among residents of northern and central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont, United States, in which cases of histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 through the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center Tumor Registry, and controls identified from a commercial database were matched to them on five-year age group, sex and county.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control participants were identified using a commercial database and matched to lung cancer cases within 5- year age groups, sex and county.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer, based at Dartmouth College, among residents of northern and central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont, United States, in which cases of histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 through the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center Tumor Registry, and controls identified from a commercial database were matched to them on five-year age group, sex and county.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NELCS New England Lung Cancer Study Dartmouth College") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002133> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer, based at Dartmouth College, among residents of northern and central New Hampshire counties and the bordering region of Vermont, United States, in which cases of histologically confirmed primary incident lung cancer were identified from 2005 to 2007 through the New Hampshire State Cancer Registry and the Dartmouth-Hitchcock Medical Center Tumor Registry, and controls identified from a commercial database were matched to them on five-year age group, sex and county.")
