AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20641046") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35913550") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42687372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9555130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9857790") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20641046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6878518/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "New topics not included in NEMESIS‐1 were added, e.g. impulse‐control disorders, and genetic correlates of mental disorders through gathering DNA from saliva samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002134> "A psychiatric epidemiological population study of non-institutionalised Dutch adults, conducted by the Trimbos Institute in Utrecht, that interviews representative samples drawn by multistage, stratified random sampling (NEMESIS-1 from 1996 and NEMESIS-2 from 2007, aged 18-64, the latter with DNA from saliva, and NEMESIS-3 from 2019, aged 18-75) with the Composite International Diagnostic Interview and follows them up to determine the prevalence, incidence, course and consequences of mental disorders.")
