AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over follow-up, data were collected on endoscopic screening practices and, if individuals have been diagnosed with 43 polyp, the polyps confirmed to be adenomatous by medical record review.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144> "The advanced colorectal adenoma case-control sample of the Nurses' Health Study, United States, genotyped for the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium: participants with an advanced adenoma (1 cm or larger, or with tubulovillous or villous histology, high-grade dysplasia or carcinoma in situ) confirmed by medical record review, matched to participants who had a lower endoscopy in the same period without an adenoma on year of birth, date of blood sampling, reason for the endoscopy and timing of any prior endoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples from HPFS, NHS, PHS, DACHS Set 2 were successfully genotyped using Illumina HumanOmniExpress.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144> "The advanced colorectal adenoma case-control sample of the Nurses' Health Study, United States, genotyped for the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium: participants with an advanced adenoma (1 cm or larger, or with tubulovillous or villous histology, high-grade dysplasia or carcinoma in situ) confirmed by medical record review, matched to participants who had a lower endoscopy in the same period without an adenoma on year of birth, date of blood sampling, reason for the endoscopy and timing of any prior endoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Advanced adenoma was defined as an adenoma 1 cm or larger in diameter and/or with tubulovillous, villous, or high grade dysplasia/carcinoma- in-situ histology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144> "The advanced colorectal adenoma case-control sample of the Nurses' Health Study, United States, genotyped for the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium: participants with an advanced adenoma (1 cm or larger, or with tubulovillous or villous histology, high-grade dysplasia or carcinoma in situ) confirmed by medical record review, matched to participants who had a lower endoscopy in the same period without an adenoma on year of birth, date of blood sampling, reason for the endoscopy and timing of any prior endoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to the CRC case-control set, a separate case-control set (NHS_5_AD) was constructed of participants diagnosed with advanced adenoma matched to control participants who underwent a lower endoscopy in the same time period and did not have an adenoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144> "The advanced colorectal adenoma case-control sample of the Nurses' Health Study, United States, genotyped for the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium: participants with an advanced adenoma (1 cm or larger, or with tubulovillous or villous histology, high-grade dysplasia or carcinoma in situ) confirmed by medical record review, matched to participants who had a lower endoscopy in the same period without an adenoma on year of birth, date of blood sampling, reason for the endoscopy and timing of any prior endoscopy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Matching criteria included year of birth (within 1 year) and month/ year of blood sampling (within 6 months), the reason for their lower endoscopy (screening, family history, or symptoms), and the time period of any prior endoscopy (within 2 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002144> "The advanced colorectal adenoma case-control sample of the Nurses' Health Study, United States, genotyped for the Genetics and Epidemiology of Colorectal Cancer Consortium: participants with an advanced adenoma (1 cm or larger, or with tubulovillous or villous histology, high-grade dysplasia or carcinoma in situ) confirmed by medical record review, matched to participants who had a lower endoscopy in the same period without an adenoma on year of birth, date of blood sampling, reason for the endoscopy and timing of any prior endoscopy.")

