AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25924736") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-020-15905-6/MediaObjects/41467_2020_15905_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clalit National Israeli Cancer Control Center- lung cancer study Carmel Medical Center & Technion Israel/Europe Pop.CC* 2005- ongoing 663 510 1173 This case-control study of newly diagnosed lung cancer cases of any histology and population age/sex/ethnicity-matched \"healthy\" controls 25924736") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002150> "An ongoing population-based case-control study of lung cancer in Israel, run since 2005 by the Clalit National Israeli Cancer Control Center with Carmel Medical Center and the Technion, of newly diagnosed lung cancer cases of any histology and controls matched to them on age, sex and ethnicity, all interviewed face to face and giving a blood sample, with histology, tumour blocks and clinical follow-up available for most cases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4667444/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using this in-depth genealogical information a large multi-generational Norfolk pedigree was reconstructed [1].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12940796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, volunteers from the Island (n = 601) were recruited via radio and newspaper announcements; gave informed consent prior to participation; answered a questionnaire on lifestyle, medical and family history; and provided anthropometric measurements and blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12940796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS) is a population-based cohort study supported by Australian NHMRC and NHF funding.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12940796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Norfolk Island Health Study (NIHS, n = 601) was established in 2000 to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases [6,7,8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12940796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort is derived from a small admixed founder group of male European and female Polynesian ancestry that originated from the 1789 mutiny on the HMS Bounty, and has remained genetically distinct due to historical isolation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26628212") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41751589") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12940796/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We sought to identify novel associations between candidate genetic coding variants and CVD traits in our isolated study cohort: the Norfolk Island Health Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002153> "A population-based study established in 2000 of volunteers from Norfolk Island, a genetic isolate descended from a small admixed founder group of European and Polynesian ancestry, with questionnaires on lifestyle, medical and family history, anthropometric measurements, blood samples and a reconstructed multi-generational pedigree, to investigate genetic risk factors for complex diseases such as cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From each available non-Ashkenazi European-origin family, when possible we selected 2 BP I siblings including the proband if available (n = 946 individuals in 473 sibling pairs); otherwise we selected a single BP I case (n = 184).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We excluded individuals with suspected major depression based on answers to questions related to depressive mood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected an additional 47 non-Ashkenazi European-origin BP I cases who met DSM-IV criteria from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected as controls 772 non-Ashkenazi European-origin individuals aged 20–70 years from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative Repository who reported they had not been diagnosed with or treated for BP or schizophrenia, and had not heard voices that others could not hear.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21926972") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29906448") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2678639/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We selected samples for previously-studied individuals from 2 sources: 1,130 Bipolar I (BP I) cases and 772 controls from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative Repository (http://zork.wustl.edu/nimh/) and 47 BP I cases from the University of Michigan Prechter Repository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002156> "A case–control sample for genome-wide association studies of bipolar disorder in the United States, assembled by the Pritzker Neuropsychiatric Disorders Research Consortium: its cases, of non-Ashkenazi European origin with bipolar I disorder, came from the NIMH Human Genetics Initiative repository, selected where possible as pairs of affected siblings from families collected in its multicentre bipolar family study, and from the University of Michigan Prechter Bipolar Genetics Repository; its controls came from the NIMH repository and reported no diagnosis of or treatment for bipolar disorder or schizophrenia and said they had not heard voices that others could not hear, with suspected major depression excluded. It is one of the bipolar disorder samples of the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium.")
