# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3761216/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Upper Midwest Health Study –National Institute forOccupational Safety and Health NIOSH-UMHS Case-control Population-basedcontrols frequencymatched 1.5:1 byage, sex, state Illumina 660W 300 542 1995-1997 USA (IA,MI, MN,WI) 48.68 56.06") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3406961/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls age 18–64 were randomly selected from state driver’s license/nondriver ID records, and those age 65–80 were selected from Health Care Financing Administration's (HCFA) Medicare data within 10-year age group strata, with the proportion/stratum determined by the age distribution of glioma cases in that state from 1992 to 1994.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3406961/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health developed the Upper Midwest Health Study (UMHS) as a case–control study of intracranial gliomas and pesticide uses among rural residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3406961/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included 798 histologically confirmed primary intracranial glioma cases (45 % with proxy respondents) and 1,175 population-based controls, all adult (age 18–80) non-metropolitan residents of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota, and Wisconsin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530494/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases diagnosed from January 1, 1995, through January 31, 1997, were identified through participating medical facilities and neurosurgeon offices.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15866761") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17131948") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561519") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22691464") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22715102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4530494/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1995, the National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health (NIOSH) initiated the Upper Midwest Health Study (UMHS), a population-based case–control study of glioma (brain cancer) risk in a non-metropolitan population [Davis-King et al., 1994].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002158> "A population-based case-control study of primary intracranial glioma, initiated in 1995 by the US National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health among adults aged 18 to 80 living in non-metropolitan counties of Iowa, Michigan, Minnesota and Wisconsin, to evaluate associations of glioma with farm and rural exposures, pesticides above all. Its cases had histologically confirmed glioma diagnosed from January 1995 to January 1997, and its controls, frequency-matched within state, were drawn from driver's licence and identification records (ages 18–64) and Medicare data (ages 65–80); its participants' DNA was later genotyped in National Cancer Institute genome-wide studies of glioma and of clonal mosaicism.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An independent NIPT PLUS pregnancy cohort was used to train the polygenic risk scores (PRSs) 198 model of platelet counts during the first, second, and third trimesters.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2020 and 2021, 199 5,733 pregnant women who participated in the pregnancy screening program from Shenzhen 200 Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital were recruited, all received Non-Invasive Prenatal 201 Testing (NIPT) and provided written informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The genotyping and quality control 203 processes of NIPT PLUS cohort participants were the same as Baoan and Longgang.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12053562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This cohort included 5897 individuals who underwent deeper sequencing (0.3x), comprising 795 GDM cases (22.3%) and 2770 controls with clear GDM diagnosis records before 20 weeks of gestation (detailed information is provided in the Supplemental Notes).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00125-023-06065-5/MediaObjects/125_2023_6065_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to the previously mentioned participants, we collected data from 4,688 individuals who sought maternity check-ups at Shenzhen Baoan Women’s and Children’s Hospital (Shenzhen, China) throughout the entire 40-week gestational period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38064665") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38372780") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40325049") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11033587/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00125-023-06065-5/MediaObjects/125_2023_6065_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Notably, these samples are characterized by a deeper sequencing depth in comparison to conventional NIPT, with an average depth of 0.3x.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002159> "A cohort of pregnant women recruited in 2020 and 2021 through the pregnancy screening programme of Shenzhen Baoan Women's and Children's Hospital in Shenzhen, China, whose non-invasive prenatal testing (NIPT) was sequenced at greater depth than conventional NIPT, and whose genotypes and hospital records are used to replicate and validate genetic studies of pregnancy traits such as platelet counts, gestational thrombocytopenia and gestational diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3196697/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were newly diagnosed histologically confirmed cases of invasive epithelial ovarian cancer identified between January 2004 and May 2008 through rapid case ascertainment by the New Jersey State Cancer Registry (NJSCR), a population-based SEER cancer registry that has collected data since 1978.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3196697/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a population-based case-control study, the NJ Ovarian Cancer Study, specifically designed to evaluate phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk in New Jersey, a population characterized by large ethnic diversity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3196697/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the controls from the EDGE Study and added ovarian cancer cases to form a new case-control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3196697/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women older than 21 years, able to understand English or Spanish, and residing in one of six New Jersey counties (Bergen, Essex, Hudson, Middlesex, Morris, and Union) were eligible to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10165492/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NJO: We thank all participants and research staff at the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey, the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21943063") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36688720") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3108163/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "New Jersey Ovarian Cancer Study NJOCS NJO USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002160> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer in New Jersey, United States, run by the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, whose cases were women with newly diagnosed invasive epithelial ovarian cancer living in six New Jersey counties, identified from January 2004 to May 2008 through the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, and whose controls were those of the EDGE (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer) Study. It was designed to study phytoestrogens and ovarian cancer risk and is one of the studies of the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (study code NJO).")

