AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27455348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33495596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33495596") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00762-2/MediaObjects/41588_2020_762_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group consisted of a previously genotyped Dutch control population from project Mine (cohort NL4") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163> "A case-control cohort from the population-based registry of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) in the Netherlands, one of the cohorts of the international ALS genome-wide association study linked to Project MinE, whose cases have probable or definite ALS diagnosed by neurologists at the tertiary referral centres University Medical Center Utrecht, Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam and Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen, and whose controls, free of neuromuscular disease and matched for age, sex and ethnicity, were ascertained through a population-based study of ALS in the Netherlands. Its genotyped controls have been reused as a Dutch control group in other genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27455348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33495596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were diagnosed with probable or definite ALS according to the revised El-Escorial Criteria by neurologists specialized in motor neuron diseases11 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163> "A case-control cohort from the population-based registry of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) in the Netherlands, one of the cohorts of the international ALS genome-wide association study linked to Project MinE, whose cases have probable or definite ALS diagnosed by neurologists at the tertiary referral centres University Medical Center Utrecht, Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam and Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen, and whose controls, free of neuromuscular disease and matched for age, sex and ethnicity, were ascertained through a population-based study of ALS in the Netherlands. Its genotyped controls have been reused as a Dutch control group in other genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27455348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33495596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control individuals were free of any neuromuscular disease and matched for age, gender and ethnicity ascertained through a population based study on ALS in the Netherlands2 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163> "A case-control cohort from the population-based registry of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) in the Netherlands, one of the cohorts of the international ALS genome-wide association study linked to Project MinE, whose cases have probable or definite ALS diagnosed by neurologists at the tertiary referral centres University Medical Center Utrecht, Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam and Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen, and whose controls, free of neuromuscular disease and matched for age, sex and ethnicity, were ascertained through a population-based study of ALS in the Netherlands. Its genotyped controls have been reused as a Dutch control group in other genetic association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27455348") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33495596") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3622/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3622_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Tertiary referral centers for ALS were University Medical Center Utrecht, Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam and Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002163> "A case-control cohort from the population-based registry of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS) in the Netherlands, one of the cohorts of the international ALS genome-wide association study linked to Project MinE, whose cases have probable or definite ALS diagnosed by neurologists at the tertiary referral centres University Medical Center Utrecht, Academic Medical Centre Amsterdam and Radboud University Medical Center Nijmegen, and whose controls, free of neuromuscular disease and matched for age, sex and ethnicity, were ascertained through a population-based study of ALS in the Netherlands. Its genotyped controls have been reused as a Dutch control group in other genetic association studies.")

