AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.573/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng573_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients who were diagnosed in one of three hospitals (Radboud University Nijmegen Medical Center and Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen and Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem) and who were alive at April 15th, 2008 were recruited for a study on gene-environment interactions in lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002164> "A Dutch sample of three groups from Nijmegen, the Netherlands: population controls from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, patients with urinary bladder cancer recruited for the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study, and patients with lung cancer identified through the population-based cancer registry of the Comprehensive Cancer Center IKO and recruited for a study of gene–environment interactions in lung cancer; it was one of the samples of the ENGAGE consortium's genome-wide association analysis of the number of cigarettes smoked per day.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.573/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng573_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with lung cancer were identified through the population-based cancer registry of the Comprehensive Cancer Center IKO, Nijmegen, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002164> "A Dutch sample of three groups from Nijmegen, the Netherlands: population controls from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, patients with urinary bladder cancer recruited for the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study, and patients with lung cancer identified through the population-based cancer registry of the Comprehensive Cancer Center IKO and recruited for a study of gene–environment interactions in lung cancer; it was one of the samples of the ENGAGE consortium's genome-wide association analysis of the number of cigarettes smoked per day.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20418888") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.573/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng573_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch series consists of 3 groups: population controls, patients with urinary bladder cancer, and patients with lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002164> "A Dutch sample of three groups from Nijmegen, the Netherlands: population controls from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, patients with urinary bladder cancer recruited for the Nijmegen Bladder Cancer Study, and patients with lung cancer identified through the population-based cancer registry of the Comprehensive Cancer Center IKO and recruited for a study of gene–environment interactions in lung cancer; it was one of the samples of the ENGAGE consortium's genome-wide association analysis of the number of cigarettes smoked per day.")
