# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All three other studies (i.e., POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, and the Radboudumc Urology Outpatient Clinic Epidemiology Study) were initiated to study genetic risk factors for disease and participants to these studies gave general informed consent for DNA-related research and linkage with disease registries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Nijmegen The Nijmegen Lung Cancer Study Radboud University Medical Centre") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients who were diagnosed in one of three hospitals (Radboud university medical center and Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen and Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem) since 1989 and who were still alive at April 15th, 2008 were recruited for a study on gene-environment interactions in lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Netherlands patients with lung cancer were identified through the population-based cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation in Nijmegen, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cancer-free controls (46% males) were selected from participants of the “Nijmegen Biomedical Study” (NBS;), an age- and sex-stratified random sample of the general population of the municipality of Nijmegen, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case series was expanded with 94 patients to a total of 552 by linking three other studies to the population-based cancer registry in order to identify new occurrences of lung cancer among the participants of these other studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002165> "A population-based case-control study of lung cancer run by Radboud University Medical Centre in Nijmegen, the Netherlands, to study gene-environment interactions. Its cases are patients diagnosed with lung cancer since 1989 at Radboud university medical center, Canisius Wilhelmina Hospital in Nijmegen or Rijnstate Hospital in Arnhem, identified through the cancer registry of the Netherlands Comprehensive Cancer Organisation, together with lung cancer cases found among participants of POLYGENE, the Nijmegen Biomedical Study and a Radboudumc urology outpatient study; its cancer-free controls are drawn from the Nijmegen Biomedical Study, a random sample of the general population of Nijmegen.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3081812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood was collected prior to diagnosis and treatment, and body size measures were ascertained by trained staff.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3081812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants were 40 years of age or older and had no prior prostate cancer diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3081812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this biomarker sub-study of the Nashville Men's Health Study (NMHS), we included 494 NMHS participants, consisting of 98 high-grade (Gleason≥7) and 100 low-grade cancer cases, 133 prostate intraepithelial neoplasia (PIN) cases, and 163 controls without cancer or PIN at biopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3081812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy between 2002 and 2008 at a Vanderbilt University Medical Center (Nashville, TN), the Tennessee Valley Veteran's Administration Hospital (Nashville, TN), or a large private urology practice in Nashville, were approached for recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3081812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nashville Men's Health Study (NMHS) utilizes a multi-centered, rapid-recruitment protocol to collect clinical, biological, behavioral, and body measurement data from men scheduled for diagnostic prostate biopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19286210") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21541018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26158673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4497718/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Considering the consistent evidence for an association between metabolic dysregulation and BPH, but the limited number of studies investigating genetic risk factors for BPH, our study provides the most thorough evaluation to date of the hypothesis that BPH and metabolism share common genetic determinants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002167> "A clinic-based study of men aged 40 or older with no previous prostate cancer diagnosis who were scheduled for a diagnostic prostate biopsy at Vanderbilt University Medical Center, the Tennessee Valley Veterans Administration hospital or a large private urology practice in Nashville, Tennessee, United States, recruited from 2002 under a multicentre rapid-recruitment protocol that collects clinical, biological, behavioural and body-measurement data and blood and urine, to study risk factors for prostate cancer, prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia and benign prostatic enlargement.")

