# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3837060/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited through a community-based annual medical check-up in 2002 and the study population consisted of 2,895 middle-aged and elderly residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3837060/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nomura cohort was based on a community (Nomura town) of 11,000 inhabitants in Ehime Prefecture, a largely rural area located in western Japan [4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3405/MediaObjects/41588_2015_BFng3405_MOESM35_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Japanese Millennium Genome Project comprises seven independent study cohorts for studies of cardiovascular diseases and related risk factors. Among them, four cohorts of general Japanese population, namely Nomura (Ehime University)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12701544/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this prospective, population-based cohort study, we examined the association between baseline Cr/BW ratio and survival over 10- and 22-year follow-up periods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12701544/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from rural communities in Ehime Prefecture, Japan, specifically individuals who routinely participated in annual community-based health checkups conducted at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24009259") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26390057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41393571") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12701544/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This prospective, population-based cohort study is part of the Nomura Study [17,18], which was initiated in 2002 for the first cohort and in 2014 for the second.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002171> "A community-based cohort of middle-aged and elderly residents of Nomura town, a largely rural community in Ehime Prefecture, western Japan, recruited through the annual community health check-ups at the Nomura Health and Welfare Center, with a first cohort enrolled in 2002 and a second in 2014 and followed up for mortality; run from Ehime University, it is one of the general-population cohorts of the Japanese Millennium Genome Project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002172> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002172>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3002853/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nordic Control database, NordicDB, has been set up as a unique resource in the Nordic area and the data are available for authorized users through the web portal (http://www.nordicdb.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002172> "A database and web portal set up in the Nordic countries that pools genome-wide SNP genotypes of control individuals from Finnish, Swedish and Danish studies, with country-specific allele frequencies, so that genetic association studies in the Nordic countries can use them as shared controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3002853/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current version of NordicDB pools together high-density genome-wide SNP information from ∼5000 controls originating from Finnish, Swedish and Danish studies and shows country-specific allele frequencies for SNP markers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002172> "A database and web portal set up in the Nordic countries that pools genome-wide SNP genotypes of control individuals from Finnish, Swedish and Danish studies, with country-specific allele frequencies, so that genetic association studies in the Nordic countries can use them as shared controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20664631") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3002853/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This allows scientists interested in studying Nordic populations to use their preferred platform to genotype new cases and use NordicDB to pick readily genotyped controls for their studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002172> "A database and web portal set up in the Nordic countries that pools genome-wide SNP genotypes of control individuals from Finnish, Swedish and Danish studies, with country-specific allele frequencies, so that genetic association studies in the Nordic countries can use them as shared controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10972367+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a prospective, randomised, open, blinded endpoint study, we enrolled 10,881 patients, aged 50-74 years, at health centres in Norway and Sweden, who had diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10972367+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We compared the effects of diltiazem with that of diuretics, beta-blockers, or both on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality in hypertensive patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8173702+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 12,000 patients will be recruited from about 480 primary Health Care Centers or hospital based Hypertension Units.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8173702+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Male and female patients, aged 50-69, with primary hypertension are randomly allocated to therapy starting with either diltiazem (180-360 mg daily) or conventional treatment (diuretics or beta-adrenergic blockers).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8173702+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NORDIL--the Nordic diltiazem intervention study was started in September 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10972367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8173702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8173702+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This trial is a prospective randomized open blinded-endpoint (PROBE) multicenter, parallel-group study conducted in Norway and Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002173> "A prospective, randomised, open, blinded-endpoint multicentre trial started in 1992 that enrolled patients aged 50-74 with primary hypertension and a diastolic blood pressure of 100 mm Hg or more at primary health care centres and hospital hypertension units in Norway and Sweden, and randomly assigned them to diltiazem or to conventional treatment with diuretics, beta-blockers or both, to compare their effects on cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18258609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CC 1986-2005 335 422 757 18258609") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> "A population-based case-control study of non-small cell lung cancer in Western Norway, run by the National Institute of Occupational Health (NIOH) in Oslo within its lung cancer genetics project, whose cases are patients of Norwegian origin with histologically confirmed early-stage non-small cell lung cancer admitted to Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, and whose healthy controls come from the same region and are frequency-matched to the cases on cumulative smoking; recruitment ran from 1986 to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18258609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Early-stage NSCLC cases and healthy controls at the time of enrollment were Caucasians of Norwegian origin and were recruited from the same geographical region (Western Norway).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> "A population-based case-control study of non-small cell lung cancer in Western Norway, run by the National Institute of Occupational Health (NIOH) in Oslo within its lung cancer genetics project, whose cases are patients of Norwegian origin with histologically confirmed early-stage non-small cell lung cancer admitted to Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, and whose healthy controls come from the same region and are frequency-matched to the cases on cumulative smoking; recruitment ran from 1986 to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18258609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Only patients with histologically confirmed early-stage NSCLC were included in our study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> "A population-based case-control study of non-small cell lung cancer in Western Norway, run by the National Institute of Occupational Health (NIOH) in Oslo within its lung cancer genetics project, whose cases are patients of Norwegian origin with histologically confirmed early-stage non-small cell lung cancer admitted to Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, and whose healthy controls come from the same region and are frequency-matched to the cases on cumulative smoking; recruitment ran from 1986 to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18258609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were recruited from the same geographical region of Western Norway and frequency-matched with cases on cumulative smoking dose (pack-years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> "A population-based case-control study of non-small cell lung cancer in Western Norway, run by the National Institute of Occupational Health (NIOH) in Oslo within its lung cancer genetics project, whose cases are patients of Norwegian origin with histologically confirmed early-stage non-small cell lung cancer admitted to Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, and whose healthy controls come from the same region and are frequency-matched to the cases on cumulative smoking; recruitment ran from 1986 to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18258609") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The patients were enrolled in the study, whenever practically feasible among patients admitted for lung cancer at the Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, Norway.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002174> "A population-based case-control study of non-small cell lung cancer in Western Norway, run by the National Institute of Occupational Health (NIOH) in Oslo within its lung cancer genetics project, whose cases are patients of Norwegian origin with histologically confirmed early-stage non-small cell lung cancer admitted to Haukeland University Hospital in Bergen, and whose healthy controls come from the same region and are frequency-matched to the cases on cumulative smoking; recruitment ran from 1986 to 2005.")
