# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3398416/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, within the Nottingham Smokers Study, for which we have in-depth phenotype data and know that individuals with asthma and never-smokers with airflow obstruction have been specifically excluded, we found similar effect estimates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3398416/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Nottingham Smokers Study, in which both pre- and postbronchodilation spirometry were measured, the positive predictive value of prebronchodilation-defined COPD for diagnosis of postbroncholidation-defined COPD was 98% (Table E2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4006731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung function measurements (FEV1 and FVC) were recorded at enrolment using a MicroLab ML3500 spirometer (Micro Medical Ltd, UK) recording the best of three satisfactory attempts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4006731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nottingham Smokers cohort is an ongoing collection in Nottingham using the following criteria; European ancestry, >40 years of age and smoking history of >10 pack years (currently n = 538).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5414061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 206 subjects with COPD defined by spirometry (forced expiratory volume (FEV)/forced vital capacity (FVC) <0.7, FEV1% <80%), over 40 years of age, and 338 controls, as part of the Nottingham Smokers Study.25") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21965014") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24786987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26952864") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.501/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng501_MOESM25_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nottingham Smokers cohort collection was funded by The University of Nottingham.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002176> "An ongoing collection, in Nottingham and funded by the University of Nottingham, of smokers of European ancestry over 40 years of age with a smoking history of more than 10 pack-years, whose lung function (FEV1 and FVC) was measured by spirometry at enrolment, before and after bronchodilation, and from which people with asthma were excluded; divided by spirometry into COPD cases and smoking controls, it has served as a follow-up sample in genetic association studies of lung function and COPD.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional versions of PRSfull and PRSfull-noHLA were constructed for comparative analysis of the UKB, BSTOP and Novartis secukinumab trial populations, further filtering input variants to those in the Novartis trials genotyping dataset") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177> "A pooled set of participants with psoriasis from five Novartis clinical trials of secukinumab (CAIN457A2302, CAIN457A2303, CAIN457A2304, CAIN457A2223 and CAIN457A2403), whose anonymized trial data and genotypes, collected by Novartis Pharmaceuticals, are analysed post hoc as a psoriasis-only cohort in genetic studies of psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Novartis data was collected from five clinical trials of secukinumab in psoriasis (details available on https://clinicaltrials.gov/): CAIN457A2302 (NCT01365455), CAIN457A2303 (NCT01358578), CAIN457A2304 (NCT01406938), CAIN457A2223 (NCT01537432), CAIN457A2403 (NCT03553823).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177> "A pooled set of participants with psoriasis from five Novartis clinical trials of secukinumab (CAIN457A2302, CAIN457A2303, CAIN457A2304, CAIN457A2223 and CAIN457A2403), whose anonymized trial data and genotypes, collected by Novartis Pharmaceuticals, are analysed post hoc as a psoriasis-only cohort in genetic studies of psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Novartis data was a post hoc analysis of existing anonymized clinical trial data collected by Novartis Pharmaceuticals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177> "A pooled set of participants with psoriasis from five Novartis clinical trials of secukinumab (CAIN457A2302, CAIN457A2303, CAIN457A2304, CAIN457A2223 and CAIN457A2403), whose anonymized trial data and genotypes, collected by Novartis Pharmaceuticals, are analysed post hoc as a psoriasis-only cohort in genetic studies of psoriasis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41408349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12857016/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two psoriasis-only cohorts, BSTOP and Novartis clinical trials of secukinumab, were used to compare psoriasis polygenic risk distributions to various UK Biobank sub-cohorts (severe psoriasis, non-severe psoriasis, any psoriasis, non-psoriasis and full population).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002177> "A pooled set of participants with psoriasis from five Novartis clinical trials of secukinumab (CAIN457A2302, CAIN457A2303, CAIN457A2304, CAIN457A2223 and CAIN457A2403), whose anonymized trial data and genotypes, collected by Novartis Pharmaceuticals, are analysed post hoc as a psoriasis-only cohort in genetic studies of psoriasis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5675616/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "13 cities/counties (Deqing, Fengkai, Gaoyao, Huaiji, Sihui, Zhaoqing, Guangning, Wuzhou, Cenxi, Cangwu, Tengxian, Pingnan, and Guiping) in Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region in southern China") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5675616/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected every six months from total population registries in the study area, with frequency matching to the expected five-year age and sex distribution of the cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5675616/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible subjects were those currently with a residence in the study area, which defined the source population; aged between 20 and 74 years") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5675616/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we undertook a large, population-based case-control study of NPC in southern China (the NPC Genes, Environment, and EBV (NPCGEE) study) with the specific aims of understanding the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures, and infection with the Epstein-Barr virus (EBV) in disease etiology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29152064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5675616/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected questionnaires and biospecimens from incident cases recruited between March 2010 and December 2013, and population-based controls between November 2010 and November 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002178> "A population-based case-control study of nasopharyngeal carcinoma in southern China, in which incident cases aged 20–74 years were recruited from March 2010 to December 2013, and randomly selected population controls from November 2010 to November 2014, among residents of 13 cities and counties of Guangdong Province and Guangxi Autonomous Region, with questionnaires and biospecimens collected to study the independent and interactive roles of genes, environmental exposures and Epstein–Barr virus infection in the disease; it was conducted by Sun Yat-sen University Cancer Center, Karolinska Institutet, Guangxi Medical University and collaborating institutions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9063108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1992 to 1996, 1621 of the original 2095 participants took part in a randomized trial of daily sunscreen application and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention [16, 18, 19].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9063108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nambour Skin Cancer Study was a prospective cohort study of 2095 randomly selected residents of the Nambour township in subtropical Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9063108/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was initiated in 1986 with skin examinations of all participants by dermatologists [16].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11112428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During follow-up, 488 participants died, including 188 from CVD, 151 from cancer and 170 from other causes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11112428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants aged 20–69 years were randomly selected from the electoral roll (voting is compulsory in Australia) for a survey of skin cancer prevalence in 1986.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35505292") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38680071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11112428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used dietary intake data collected using a self-administered, semi-quantitative FFQ completed by Nambour Study participants in 1992, 1994 and 1996.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002182> "A prospective community-based cohort of adults aged 20–69 years randomly selected from the electoral roll of the township of Nambour in subtropical Queensland, Australia, begun in 1986 with a survey of skin cancer prevalence and dermatologists' skin examinations; from 1992 to 1996 most participants took part in a randomised trial of daily sunscreen use and beta-carotene supplementation for skin cancer prevention, and the cohort has since been followed for skin cancers, diet and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27008869") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5868213") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four large genotyping studies, the ANECS, E2C2, NSECG and SEARCH, contributed a total of 16 852 women (4907 cases, 11 945 controls) of European ancestry with confirmed EC diagnosis to the meta-analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Study of the Genetics of Endometrial Cancer (NSECG) cases were identified from collaborating clinicians throughout the UK from 2008 to 2013, taking care not to recruit from centres involved in SEARCH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "acknowledge the invaluable help of the National Cancer Research Network with the collection of study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The National Study of Endometrial Cancer Genetics (NSECG) consisted of 925 histologically confirmed endometrial cancer cases from the UK; 86% with endometrioid-only histology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first was an independent GWAS; the National Study of Endometrial Cancer (NSECG), including 925 endometrial cancer cases genotyped using the Illumina 660W array, 1,286 cancer-free controls from the CORGI/SP1 GWAS11,12 and 2,674 controls from the 1958 Birth Cohort13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4907351/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify additional endometrial cancer risk loci, we re-analysed data from our previous GWAS (ANECS, SEARCH datasets10) and conducted a meta-analysis with two further studies (Supplementary Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002183> "A UK study of women with histologically confirmed endometrial cancer, identified through collaborating clinicians throughout the United Kingdom, with the help of the National Cancer Research Network, from 2008 to 2013 (avoiding centres that recruited to the SEARCH study) and coordinated from the University of Oxford, to find inherited genetic variants that influence endometrial cancer risk; its cases have been compared with controls from other UK studies, such as the CORGI study and the 1958 Birth Cohort.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002185> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002185>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12189166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20372189") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12189166") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12189166+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Association analysis in families recruited on the basis of affected sib pairs for asthma reveal significant association for both coding region polymorphisms with atopy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002185> "A family-based study of the genetics of asthma in Nottingham, United Kingdom, whose families were recruited on the basis of pairs of siblings affected by asthma and were used in association studies of candidate genes with atopy; its index cases, children with asthma of European ancestry, later served as childhood asthma cases in a genetic study of the 17q21 asthma locus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12189166") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20372189") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20372189") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2987388") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the phenotype–genotype relationship of the sequence variant at 17q21 with asthma, we genotyped tagging SNPs at this locus (including rs7216389) in samples obtained from Iceland, Australia, The Netherlands, Germany, the United Kingdom and Korea") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002185> "A family-based study of the genetics of asthma in Nottingham, United Kingdom, whose families were recruited on the basis of pairs of siblings affected by asthma and were used in association studies of candidate genes with atopy; its index cases, children with asthma of European ancestry, later served as childhood asthma cases in a genetic study of the 17q21 asthma locus.")
