AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with ages of onset under 35 years were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002190> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese adults in Taiwan, whose cases were patients with type 2 diabetes diagnosed by American Diabetes Association criteria (onset at age 35 or older) recruited from the metabolism clinics of National Taiwan University Hospital, Taipei, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance on a 75-g oral glucose tolerance test recruited from routine health examinations; it was a replication study of the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes genome-wide meta-analysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22158537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The glucose tolerant control subjects by 75-g oral glucose tolerance tests (OGTT) were recruited from routine health examinations, and type 2 diabetic patients were recruited from the metabolism clinics of the National Taiwan University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002190> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese adults in Taiwan, whose cases were patients with type 2 diabetes diagnosed by American Diabetes Association criteria (onset at age 35 or older) recruited from the metabolism clinics of National Taiwan University Hospital, Taipei, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance on a 75-g oral glucose tolerance test recruited from routine health examinations; it was a replication study of the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's type 2 diabetes genome-wide meta-analysis.")
