AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27542569") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702895") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30177847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30177847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6120908/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have demonstrated our approach on the Kuopio Breast Cancer Project (KBCP)22 and the Oulu Breast Cancer Study (OBCS) (University of Oulu/Oulu University Hospital, 2004)23 sample sets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002195> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study of the University of Oulu and Oulu University Hospital, Finland, whose cases are breast cancer patients from Northern Finland, unselected for age and family history, collected at Oulu University Hospital from 2000 onwards, and whose controls are healthy female blood donors of the Finnish Red Cross from the Oulu area; it studies inherited susceptibility to breast cancer and contributes to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27542569") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28702895") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30177847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2563/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2563_MOESM7_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OBCS Oulu Breast Cancer Study 29 Finland Consecutive incident cases diagnosed at the Oulu University Hospital between 2000-2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002195> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study of the University of Oulu and Oulu University Hospital, Finland, whose cases are breast cancer patients from Northern Finland, unselected for age and family history, collected at Oulu University Hospital from 2000 onwards, and whose controls are healthy female blood donors of the Finnish Red Cross from the Oulu area; it studies inherited susceptibility to breast cancer and contributes to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All tumors were assessed for mismatch repair (MMR) deficiency by microsatellite instability (MSI) testing and/or immunohistochemical (IHC) analysis at OSU, if not already completed in a Clinical Laboratory Improvement Amendments (CLIA)–approved laboratory for routine care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical inclusion criteria were CRC diagnosed under age 50 years, a personal history of synchronous or metachronous CRC and/or endometrial cancer (EC), or a family history of a first-degree relative with CRC or EC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those with MMR deficiency without MLH1 hypermethylation had either ColoSeq (January 1, 2013-July 31, 2016) or BROCA (August 1, 2016-December 31, 2016) MGPT through the University of Washington's Genetics and Solid Tumor Laboratory") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those with MMR-proficient tumors or MLH1-hypermethylated tumors meeting clinical inclusion criteria underwent myRisk MGPT through Myriad Genetics Inc using methods previously described.27") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three thousand three hundred ten unselected adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive CRC were prospectively accrued from 51 hospitals across Ohio between January 1, 2013, and December 31, 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42435229") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34250417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8232834/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To improve identification of hereditary cancer syndromes in individuals with colorectal cancer (CRC), a statewide initiative was created to provide universal tumor screening for Lynch syndrome (LS)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002196> "A prospective statewide study of adults who underwent surgical resection for primary invasive colorectal cancer at 51 hospitals across Ohio, United States, enrolled from 2013 to 2016, in which every tumour was screened for mismatch-repair deficiency and those with mismatch-repair-deficient tumours without MLH1 hypermethylation or with high-risk clinical criteria (diagnosis before 50, multiple primary colorectal or endometrial cancers, or a first-degree relative with colorectal or endometrial cancer) had multigene germline panel testing, to identify Lynch syndrome and other hereditary cancer syndromes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1868919/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initial efforts by CIMBA to identify modifiers of breast cancer risk for BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers have focused on validation of common genetic variants previously associated with risk in smaller studies of carriers or unselected breast cancers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> "A study of the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network, a Cancer Care Ontario-funded research network based at the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, that contributes carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants and their data to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1868919/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OCGN by Cancer Care Ontario,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> "A study of the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network, a Cancer Care Ontario-funded research network based at the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, that contributes carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants and their data to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5408990/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible study subjects included in the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) are female carriers of a pathogenic mutation in either BRCA1 or BRCA2 who are age 18 years or older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> "A study of the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network, a Cancer Care Ontario-funded research network based at the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, that contributes carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants and their data to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5408990/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We wish to thank members and participants in the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network for their contributions to the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> "A study of the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network, a Cancer Care Ontario-funded research network based at the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, that contributes carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants and their data to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17466083") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28376175") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3785/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3785_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "OCGN | Ontario Cancer Genetics Network | CANADA | 133 | 71 |  | 6 | 4") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002197> "A study of the Ontario Cancer Genetics Network, a Cancer Care Ontario-funded research network based at the Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute of Mount Sinai Hospital in Toronto, Ontario, Canada, that contributes carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants and their data to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of cancer risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11007659") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11007659+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ontario Familial Colon Cancer Registry (OFCCR) is a novel registry that collects family history information, epidemiologic data, blood samples and tumour specimens from a population-based sample of colorectal cancer patients and their families.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200> "A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute's Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Colorectal cancer cases (sampled based on family history) and all population controls were invited to complete a family history questionnaire, epidemiologic and food questionnaire and also provide a blood sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200> "A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute's Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls recruited by the OFCCR were comprised of a random sample of Ontario residents identified using two methods with the same eligibility criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002200> "A population-based familial colorectal cancer registry in Ontario, Canada, one of the sites of the US National Cancer Institute's Colon Cancer Family Registry, which recruited people aged 20 to 74 with colorectal cancer diagnosed from July 1997 to June 2000, identified through the Ontario Cancer Registry, and population controls randomly sampled from Ontario residents and frequency-matched to the cases by sex and five-year age group, who completed family-history, epidemiologic and food questionnaires and gave blood samples.")
