AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2900891/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, our study cohort for the initial GWA came from a US mid-west Caucasian population, living in Omaha, NE, USA, and its surrounding areas.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2900891/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we performed a genome-wide association scan for obesity by examining approximately 500 000 single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) in a sample of 1000 unrelated US Caucasians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2900891/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were normal healthy subjects defined by a comprehensive suite of exclusion criteria (48).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31444391") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18325910") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2900891/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This sample contains 1000 unrelated adults, which was randomly identified from our established and expanding genetic repertoire currently containing more than 6000 subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002209> "A cross-sectional study of osteoporosis and related traits in randomly recruited, healthy adult Caucasians living in Omaha, Nebraska, United States, and its surrounding areas, screened by exclusion criteria for chronic and metabolic diseases, with bone mineral density and body composition measured by dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry. Its unrelated genotyped members formed genome-wide association samples for obesity-related traits.")
