AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33034053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118516") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ovarian cancer Prognosis And Lifestyle study is a prospective population-based cohort of 958 Australian women with OC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210> "A national prospective population-based cohort of Australian women diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015, run from QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, who completed questionnaires at recruitment and repeatedly during follow-up and whose medical records were abstracted, to study how lifestyle factors relate to outcomes after an ovarian cancer diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33034053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118516") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women also completed questionnaires every 3 months for the first year, specifying their current weight, smoking, physical activity, and medication use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210> "A national prospective population-based cohort of Australian women diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015, run from QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, who completed questionnaires at recruitment and repeatedly during follow-up and whose medical records were abstracted, to study how lifestyle factors relate to outcomes after an ovarian cancer diagnosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33034053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40118516") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36744914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10165482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women completed a baseline questionnaire at recruitment, providing information about their ancestry, education, height, average weight during the 5 years prediagnosis, smoking habit, physical activity, preexisting conditions, and medication use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002210> "A national prospective population-based cohort of Australian women diagnosed with histologically confirmed invasive epithelial ovarian, primary peritoneal or fallopian tube cancer from 2012 to 2015, run from QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute in Brisbane, who completed questionnaires at recruitment and repeatedly during follow-up and whose medical records were abstracted, to study how lifestyle factors relate to outcomes after an ovarian cancer diagnosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(1) The University of Maryland at Baltimore, MD, with a nearby population 651,154; (2) The University of Buffalo, NY, with a nearby population of 292,648; (3) The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, NC, with a nearby population 48,715; and (4) The University of Florida at Gainesville, FL, with a nearby population of 95,447.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up questionnaires, completed once every three months, identify people who develop significant symptoms suggestive of TMD, with examinations then performed to determine presence or absence of TMD in those reporting significant symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place between May 2006 and November 2008, when healthy volunteers were sought from communities in and around each study site.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline case-control study recruited 185 people with chronic TMD, comparing them with 1,633 controls drawn from the enrollees in the prospective cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project “Orofacial Pain: Prospective Evaluation and Risk Assessment” (OPPERA) was designed to identify a broad range of genetic, physiologic, psychosocial and clinical characteristics that influence development of painful temporomandibular disorders (TMD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22074754") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22074749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3666856/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Volunteers aged 18-44 years were recruited at four US study sites: 3,263 people without TMD were enrolled into the prospective cohort study; 1,633 of them were selected as controls for the baseline case-control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002211> "A multicentre study of temporomandibular disorder (TMD) that from 2006 recruited community volunteers aged 18 to 44 years in and around four US academic health centres (in Baltimore, Buffalo, Chapel Hill and Gainesville) into a prospective cohort of people free of TMD, followed for first-onset TMD, and a baseline case-control study comparing people with chronic TMD with controls drawn from the cohort, to identify risk factors for TMD pain.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2363910/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan and Australia, and coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2363910/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present Cuban case-control study was part of an international study of oral cancer and HPV carried out in Italy") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14652239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate these associations, we conducted a multicenter case-control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx in nine countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14652239+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited 1670 case patients (1415 with cancer of the oral cavity and 255 with cancer of the oropharynx) and 1732 control subjects and obtained an interview, oral exfoliated cells, and blood from all participants and fresh biopsy specimens from case patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3685/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3685_MOESM17_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IARC  oral cancer  (ORC) | 175/168 | OC n=100 OPC n=68 | Canada, Italy, Poland, Spain |") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11437401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14652239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19190158") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21437268") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27749845") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3685/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3685_MOESM17_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Multicenter Hospital-based case-control") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002212> "An international hospital-based case–control study of cancer of the oral cavity and oropharynx, coordinated by the International Agency for Research on Cancer in nine countries (Italy, Spain, Northern Ireland, Poland, Canada, India, Sudan, Australia and Cuba), which interviewed its participants and collected oral exfoliated cells and blood from cases and controls, and fresh tumour biopsies from cases, to study the role of human papillomavirus in these cancers. It is one of the studies of the International Head and Neck Cancer Epidemiology Consortium, and participants from its centres in Canada, Italy, Poland and Spain were genotyped for a genome-wide association study of oral cavity and pharyngeal cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002213> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002213>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16545646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16731473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20360844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25227407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16545646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16545646+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases of SCD in Multnomah County, Oregon (population 660,486; 2002 to 2004) were prospectively ascertained in the ongoing Oregon Sudden Unexpected Death Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002213> "An ongoing prospective community-based study of out-of-hospital sudden cardiac arrest and sudden cardiac death in the Portland, Oregon metropolitan area (including Multnomah County), United States, running since 2002, which ascertains cases through first responders, emergency medical services, area hospitals and the county medical examiner, reviews their medical records, and compares them with geographically matched controls, including people with coronary artery disease, some of them with blood samples for genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16545646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16731473") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20360844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25227407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20360844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2845611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, patients with likely out of hospital SCA were referred from the regional emergency medical response system (EMS), the County Medical Examiner, and emergency departments of the 16 area hospitals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002213> "An ongoing prospective community-based study of out-of-hospital sudden cardiac arrest and sudden cardiac death in the Portland, Oregon metropolitan area (including Multnomah County), United States, running since 2002, which ascertains cases through first responders, emergency medical services, area hospitals and the county medical examiner, reviews their medical records, and compares them with geographically matched controls, including people with coronary artery disease, some of them with blood samples for genetic studies.")
