# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10206402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16080113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17498711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10206402") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10206402+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Oxford Endometriosis Gene (OXEGENE) study, an international collaborative project, seeks to identify the susceptibility loci using linkage analysis; the aim then is to use positional cloning techniques to identify genes that predispose women to the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224> "A United Kingdom-based international genetic study of endometriosis, run from the University of Oxford, that from 1995 to 2006 recruited women with surgically confirmed endometriosis, both families with two or more affected sisters and single cases, through collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland and the United States, advertisements and its website, to identify susceptibility genes by linkage analysis and positional cloning; with the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study it forms the International Endogene Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10206402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16080113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17498711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16080113") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1226203/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "our International Endogene Study (Treloar et al. 2002), which resulted from the merger of two independent groups: the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study and the United Kingdom–based, international Oxford Endometriosis Gene (OXEGENE) Study;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224> "A United Kingdom-based international genetic study of endometriosis, run from the University of Oxford, that from 1995 to 2006 recruited women with surgically confirmed endometriosis, both families with two or more affected sisters and single cases, through collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland and the United States, advertisements and its website, to identify susceptibility genes by linkage analysis and positional cloning; with the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study it forms the International Endogene Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10206402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16080113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17498711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17498711") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2939902/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, women were identified from the clinic databases of collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland, and the United States, or through advertisements, by the OXEGENE website, or research centers throughout the world.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224> "A United Kingdom-based international genetic study of endometriosis, run from the University of Oxford, that from 1995 to 2006 recruited women with surgically confirmed endometriosis, both families with two or more affected sisters and single cases, through collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland and the United States, advertisements and its website, to identify susceptibility genes by linkage analysis and positional cloning; with the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study it forms the International Endogene Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10206402") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16080113") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17498711") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21151130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.731/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng731_MOESM17_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1995-2006, the Oxford Endometriosis Gene (OXEGENE) study, Oxford, UK, recruited 245 families with ≥2 affected sisters with surgically confirmed endometriosis, and 785 single cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002224> "A United Kingdom-based international genetic study of endometriosis, run from the University of Oxford, that from 1995 to 2006 recruited women with surgically confirmed endometriosis, both families with two or more affected sisters and single cases, through collaborating clinicians in Britain, Ireland and the United States, advertisements and its website, to identify susceptibility genes by linkage analysis and positional cloning; with the Australian Genes Behind Endometriosis Study it forms the International Endogene Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC5642867") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institute of Biomedical and Clinical Science, University of Exeter Medical School, Exeter, U.K.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5642867/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Known monogenic diabetes and secondary diabetes cases were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5642867/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, we also tested the ability of a genetic risk score to predict severe insulin deficiency that requires insulin treatment within 3 years of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5642867/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed a cross-sectional cohort of people diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 years (n=223), who had diabetes for more than 3 years and self-reported as white European, from Devon and Cornwall in South West England.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26577414") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5642867/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We categorised people as severely insulin deficient if they received continuous insulin treatment <3 years from diagnosis and had a low measured C-peptide (non-fasting measured <0.6 nmol/L or equivalent fasting blood or post-home meal urine C-peptide creatinine ratio level) (Supplementary Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002225> "A cross-sectional cohort of white European adults from Devon and Cornwall in South West England who were diagnosed with diabetes between the ages of 20 and 40 and had had it for more than three years, excluding known monogenic and secondary diabetes, assembled by researchers at the University of Exeter to test whether a type 1 diabetes genetic risk score predicts progression to severe insulin deficiency (continuous insulin treatment within three years of diagnosis with low C-peptide).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3052/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng3052_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2270/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2270_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PACIFIC study: Pancreatic Cancer Investigation: Finding Causes PACIFIC Study Hospital- based Case- Control (Group Health (Seattle Puget Sound) and Kaiser Permanente Northern CA) 274 269 Blood Seattle, Washington and Northern California, USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226> "A case-control study of pancreatic cancer among members of two US health plans, Group Health in the Seattle Puget Sound area of Washington and Kaiser Permanente Northern California. It is one of the case-control studies of the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4) whose samples were genotyped in the PanScan genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3052/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng3052_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3808252/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pancreatic Cancer: Investigation into Finding Causes (PACIFIC) Study is a case-control study of pancreatic cancer based in the defined populations of two large health plans (Group Health Cooperative (GHC) in Seattle, WA and Kaiser Permanente Northern California, (KPNC)).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226> "A case-control study of pancreatic cancer among members of two US health plans, Group Health in the Seattle Puget Sound area of Washington and Kaiser Permanente Northern California. It is one of the case-control studies of the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4) whose samples were genotyped in the PanScan genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3052/MediaObjects/41588_2014_BFng3052_MOESM19_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000206.v5.p3") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The studies included in PanScan (PanScan II) from PanC4 are: PACIFIC Study of Group Health and Northern California Kaiser Permanente") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002226> "A case-control study of pancreatic cancer among members of two US health plans, Group Health in the Seattle Puget Sound area of Washington and Kaiser Permanente Northern California. It is one of the case-control studies of the Pancreatic Cancer Case-Control Consortium (PanC4) whose samples were genotyped in the PanScan genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13138623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, 1,782 participants (1,038 PAF cases and 744 controls) were included in the GWAS and PRS analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> "A multicentre case-control study of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in Japan, whose cases with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and unrelated controls with no history of atrial fibrillation, all Japanese inpatients and outpatients of the cardiology departments of seven hospitals (among them Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital and Jichi Medical University Hospital), were enrolled from March 2020 to December 2021 and genotyped for a genome-wide association study and polygenic risk scores of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13138623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomic DNA was extracted from peripheral blood samples and genotyped using the Infinium Asian Screening Array-24 v1.0 BeadChip (Illumina, Inc., San Diego, CA, USA), which covers 659,184 common SNPs, at Macrogen Japan (Tokyo, Japan).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> "A multicentre case-control study of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in Japan, whose cases with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and unrelated controls with no history of atrial fibrillation, all Japanese inpatients and outpatients of the cardiology departments of seven hospitals (among them Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital and Jichi Medical University Hospital), were enrolled from March 2020 to December 2021 and genotyped for a genome-wide association study and polygenic risk scores of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13138623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 2,604 participants were enrolled between March 1, 2020 and December 31, 2021, including inpatients and outpatients from the Department of Cardiology of Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital, Jichi Medical University Hospital,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> "A multicentre case-control study of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in Japan, whose cases with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and unrelated controls with no history of atrial fibrillation, all Japanese inpatients and outpatients of the cardiology departments of seven hospitals (among them Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital and Jichi Medical University Hospital), were enrolled from March 2020 to December 2021 and genotyped for a genome-wide association study and polygenic risk scores of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13138623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted in Japanese subjects, and participants were classified as PAF cases or controls; those in the control group were unrelated individuals without any history of AF, recruited from the same institutions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> "A multicentre case-control study of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in Japan, whose cases with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and unrelated controls with no history of atrial fibrillation, all Japanese inpatients and outpatients of the cardiology departments of seven hospitals (among them Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital and Jichi Medical University Hospital), were enrolled from March 2020 to December 2021 and genotyped for a genome-wide association study and polygenic risk scores of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42081549") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13138623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Yokohama City Minato Red Cross Hospital, Jichi Medical University Saitama Medical Center, Yokosuka Kyosai Hospital, National Hospital Organization Disaster Medical Center, and Tsuchiura Kyodo General Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002227> "A multicentre case-control study of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation in Japan, whose cases with paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and unrelated controls with no history of atrial fibrillation, all Japanese inpatients and outpatients of the cardiology departments of seven hospitals (among them Tokyo Medical and Dental University Hospital and Jichi Medical University Hospital), were enrolled from March 2020 to December 2021 and genotyped for a genome-wide association study and polygenic risk scores of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23206934+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "So far 2220 cases of pancreatic adenocarcinoma, a smaller number of cases of endocrine pancreatic tumours (n=86), chronic pancreatitis (n=272) and 3847 healthy controls have been collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> "A case-control consortium of basic and clinical research groups that pools biological samples and data from patients with pancreatic adenocarcinoma and other pancreatic diseases (endocrine pancreatic tumours, chronic pancreatitis) and from healthy controls, collected mainly in European countries and also in Brazil and Japan, to find genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23206934+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PANcreatic Disease ReseArch (PANDoRA) consortium was established to unite the efforts of different research groups; its aim is to create a large bio-database to uncover new genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment, and patient survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> "A case-control consortium of basic and clinical research groups that pools biological samples and data from patients with pancreatic adenocarcinoma and other pancreatic diseases (endocrine pancreatic tumours, chronic pancreatitis) and from healthy controls, collected mainly in European countries and also in Brazil and Japan, to find genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27579533") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5340084/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 15 promising variants (P < 5.0×10−6) were selected for replication in 1,912 pancreatic cancer cases and 3,763 control subjects from the European PANDoRA case-control consortium [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> "A case-control consortium of basic and clinical research groups that pools biological samples and data from patients with pancreatic adenocarcinoma and other pancreatic diseases (endocrine pancreatic tumours, chronic pancreatitis) and from healthy controls, collected mainly in European countries and also in Brazil and Japan, to find genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34926279") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8678088/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional samples belonging to the PANDoRA consortium, mostly from European populations, were selected for genotyping.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> "A case-control consortium of basic and clinical research groups that pools biological samples and data from patients with pancreatic adenocarcinoma and other pancreatic diseases (endocrine pancreatic tumours, chronic pancreatitis) and from healthy controls, collected mainly in European countries and also in Brazil and Japan, to find genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23206934") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37164172") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37164172+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PANDoRA is spread across 12 European countries, Brazil and Japan, bringing together 29 basic and clinical research groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002229> "A case-control consortium of basic and clinical research groups that pools biological samples and data from patients with pancreatic adenocarcinoma and other pancreatic diseases (endocrine pancreatic tumours, chronic pancreatitis) and from healthy controls, collected mainly in European countries and also in Brazil and Japan, to find genetic factors for pancreatic cancer risk, response to treatment and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:17636417%20AND%20SRC:MED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32791343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, subject recruitment took place between 1992 and 1995 at five general university hospitals in eastern Spain, where 602 patients with biliopancreatic diseases, including 185 incident cases of PDAC, were prospectively identified.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230> "A multicentre prospective hospital-based study of patients with pancreatic and biliary diseases, among them incident cases of exocrine pancreatic cancer, recruited from 1992 to 1995 at five general university hospitals in eastern Spain and followed for survival, to study the role of KRAS mutations and other genetic alterations, and of environmental exposures such as persistent organic pollutants and trace elements, in the diagnosis, prognosis and aetiology of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:17636417%20AND%20SRC:MED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32791343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up for all participants in the PANKRAS II study was 17.5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230> "A multicentre prospective hospital-based study of patients with pancreatic and biliary diseases, among them incident cases of exocrine pancreatic cancer, recruited from 1992 to 1995 at five general university hospitals in eastern Spain and followed for survival, to study the role of KRAS mutations and other genetic alterations, and of environmental exposures such as persistent organic pollutants and trace elements, in the diagnosis, prognosis and aetiology of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:17636417%20AND%20SRC:MED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32791343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "No previous studies have analyzed the combined influence of KRAS mutations, persistent organic pollutants (POPs), and trace elements upon survival in PDAC or in any other human cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230> "A multicentre prospective hospital-based study of patients with pancreatic and biliary diseases, among them incident cases of exocrine pancreatic cancer, recruited from 1992 to 1995 at five general university hospitals in eastern Spain and followed for survival, to study the role of KRAS mutations and other genetic alterations, and of environmental exposures such as persistent organic pollutants and trace elements, in the diagnosis, prognosis and aetiology of pancreatic cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:17636417%20AND%20SRC:MED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32791343") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7689512/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To analyze the individual and combined influence of KRAS mutations, POPs, and trace elements upon survival from PDAC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002230> "A multicentre prospective hospital-based study of patients with pancreatic and biliary diseases, among them incident cases of exocrine pancreatic cancer, recruited from 1992 to 1995 at five general university hospitals in eastern Spain and followed for survival, to study the role of KRAS mutations and other genetic alterations, and of environmental exposures such as persistent organic pollutants and trace elements, in the diagnosis, prognosis and aetiology of pancreatic cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CAP subjects were recruited from two clinical sites located in Los Angeles and San Francisco, California.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were Caucasians, aged 21 and older, who received 40 mg daily pravastatin for 12 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were Caucasians, aged 30 and above, who received open label 40 mg simvastatin daily for 6 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were two clinical populations in the PARC study, which has been described in detail previously38 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature09270/MediaObjects/41586_2010_BFnature09270_MOESM283_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These subjects were enrolled from 1,143 sites representing 49 states and the District of Columbia, with no single site enrolling more than 4 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002231> "A pharmacogenomic study of the response to statins that combines two clinical populations of white adults in the United States given a statin for a fixed period: participants of the Cholesterol and Atherosclerosis Pharmacogenetics (CAP) study, recruited at two clinical sites in Los Angeles and San Francisco and treated with simvastatin for six weeks, and participants of the Pravastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) trial, enrolled at sites across the country and treated with pravastatin for twelve weeks.")
