AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21741729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21912625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21741729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3172377/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Parkinson’s, Genes, and Environment (PAGE) study is a case-control study within the large prospective NIH-AARP Diet and Health Study cohort (Schatzkin, et al., 2001).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002232> "A case-control study of Parkinson's disease nested in the NIH-AARP Diet and Health Study, the prospective cohort established by the National Cancer Institute in 1995–1996, whose cases are cohort members who reported Parkinson's disease in the cohort's 2004–2006 follow-up survey and were confirmed by their treating physicians or by medical record review, and whose controls are randomly selected cohort members who did not report Parkinson's disease, frequency-matched to the cases on year of birth, sex and ethnicity, with DNA collected from saliva.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21741729") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21912625") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21741729") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3172377/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was established in 1995–1996 by the National Cancer Institute for cancer research, and collected comprehensive dietary and lifestyle information at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002232> "A case-control study of Parkinson's disease nested in the NIH-AARP Diet and Health Study, the prospective cohort established by the National Cancer Institute in 1995–1996, whose cases are cohort members who reported Parkinson's disease in the cohort's 2004–2006 follow-up survey and were confirmed by their treating physicians or by medical record review, and whose controls are randomly selected cohort members who did not report Parkinson's disease, frequency-matched to the cases on year of birth, sex and ethnicity, with DNA collected from saliva.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002234> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002234>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19020293") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246476") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27911342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19020293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19020293+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 196 non-demented, drug-naive patients who were recruited after an extensive search of all new cases of PD in the area and 201 healthy control subjects completed a battery of neuropsychological tests of verbal memory, visuospatial, and attentional-executive functioning.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002234> "A population-based longitudinal study of the incidence, neurobiology and prognosis of Parkinson’s disease in Norway, which recruited incident, untreated patients with Parkinson’s disease and control participants and follows them with a standardised examination programme; its patients contribute to genetic studies of Parkinson’s disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19020293") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246476") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27911342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27911342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5302042/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were derived from the Norwegian ParkWest project, a population-based longitudinal study of the incidence, neurobiology and prognosis of PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002234> "A population-based longitudinal study of the incidence, neurobiology and prognosis of Parkinson’s disease in Norway, which recruited incident, untreated patients with Parkinson’s disease and control participants and follows them with a standardised examination programme; its patients contribute to genetic studies of Parkinson’s disease progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19020293") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19246476") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27911342") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27911342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5302042/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, patients with newly diagnosed PD and NC subjects were recruited from four counties in Western and Southern Norway between 2004 and 2006, and followed prospectively by movement disorders neurologists with standardized clinical examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002234> "A population-based longitudinal study of the incidence, neurobiology and prognosis of Parkinson’s disease in Norway, which recruited incident, untreated patients with Parkinson’s disease and control participants and follows them with a standardised examination programme; its patients contribute to genetic studies of Parkinson’s disease progression.")
