AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36343223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39930085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3827723/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants will be evaluated by serial DRE, serum PSA, and prostate biopsies according to the timeline outlined in Table 3.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002236> "A multi-institutional prospective cohort and biorepository of men with clinically localized prostate cancer managed by active surveillance, enrolled from 2008 at clinical sites in the United States and Canada and followed under a protocol of regular prostate-specific antigen tests and surveillance biopsies, supported by the Canary Foundation to discover and confirm biomarkers that distinguish aggressive from indolent disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36343223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39930085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3827723/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Canary Prostate Active Surveillance Study (PASS) is a multicenter, prospective active surveillance study that is currently enrolling participants at Stanford University, University of California at San Francisco, University of British Columbia, University of Washington, and University of Texas Health Science Center at San Antonio.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002236> "A multi-institutional prospective cohort and biorepository of men with clinically localized prostate cancer managed by active surveillance, enrolled from 2008 at clinical sites in the United States and Canada and followed under a protocol of regular prostate-specific antigen tests and surveillance biopsies, supported by the Canary Foundation to discover and confirm biomarkers that distinguish aggressive from indolent disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36343223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39930085") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19758683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3827723/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Canary Prostate Active Surveillance Study(PASS) is a multicenter study and biorepository that will discover and confirm biomarkers of aggressive disease as defined by histologic, PSA, or clinical criteria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002236> "A multi-institutional prospective cohort and biorepository of men with clinically localized prostate cancer managed by active surveillance, enrolled from 2008 at clinical sites in the United States and Canada and followed under a protocol of regular prostate-specific antigen tests and surveillance biopsies, supported by the Canary Foundation to discover and confirm biomarkers that distinguish aggressive from indolent disease.")
