# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An extensive baseline interview is conducted, blood and saliva samples are collected, and body measurements are taken.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility includes any woman diagnosed with invasive breast cancer within KPNC, no previous diagnosis of other invasive cancer, age 21 years or older, and ability to speak English, Spanish, Cantonese, or Mandarin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pathways aims to examine the effect on recurrence and survival of 1) lifestyle factors such as diet, physical activity, quality of life, and use of alternative therapies and 2) molecular factors such as genetic polymorphisms involved in metabolism of chemotherapeutic agents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since January 9, 2006, women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer are being recruited from the KPNC patient population into the Pathways Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pathways Study is a prospective cohort study, with recruitment of women from the Kaiser Permanente Northern California (KPNC) patient population as soon after diagnosis of invasive breast cancer as possible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18478338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2581640/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women are typically enrolled within two months post-diagnosis during an in-person baseline interview.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002237> "A prospective cohort of women aged 21 or older newly diagnosed with invasive breast cancer at Kaiser Permanente Northern California, in the United States, recruited from January 2006 within two months of diagnosis, interviewed and sampled for blood and saliva at baseline and followed for recurrence and survival, to study how lifestyle and molecular factors affect breast cancer prognosis.")

