AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16676364+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical data are abstracted from medical records, diagnostic biopsies are reviewed and assayed, and tissue microarrays are constructed from prostatectomy samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16676364+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study nurses administer structured questionnaires and collect blood, adipose tissue, urine, and toenail samples during an in-home visit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16676364+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The North Carolina-Louisiana Prostate Cancer Project (PCaP) is a multidisciplinary study of social, individual, and tumor-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3934014/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PCaP is a population-based, case-only study designed to investigate social, individual, and tumor-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer that has been described.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3934014/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PCaP recruited 1130 black/ AA CaP cases between 40 and79 years of age with newly diagnosed, histologically-confirmed, adenocarcinoma of the prostate from North Carolina (NC) and Louisiana (LA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16676364") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24037755") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38758522") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11377453/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible PCaP participants included those aged 40–79 years old at diagnosis, were physically and mentally able to complete the interview, could complete the interview in English, and self-identified as at least part Black/African American or Caucasian/European American/White.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002238> "A population-based, case-only study of African American and European American men aged 40 to 79 with newly diagnosed prostate cancer in North Carolina and Louisiana, United States, who were interviewed at home and gave blood, adipose tissue, urine and toenail samples, with medical records and tumour tissue reviewed, to investigate the social, individual and tumour-level causes of racial differences in prostate cancer aggressiveness.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22936456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4087101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were residents of the island who were randomly selected from a national database, frequency age-matched (by 5-year age groups) to the cases, and free of PC at the time of the study visit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Barbados, West Indies, whose cases were male citizens with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancer identified from July 2002 to January 2011 and whose controls were age-matched residents randomly selected from a national database, designed to evaluate genetic and epidemiologic contributors to prostate cancer in this Afro-Caribbean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22936456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4087101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases for the PCBP study included all male citizens of Barbados with newly diagnosed and histologically confirmed PC identified between July, 2002 and January, 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Barbados, West Indies, whose cases were male citizens with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancer identified from July 2002 to January 2011 and whose controls were age-matched residents randomly selected from a national database, designed to evaluate genetic and epidemiologic contributors to prostate cancer in this Afro-Caribbean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22936456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4087101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Findings from the PCBP, a large nationwide case-control study of PC in Barbados, indicate that more than three-quarters of African-Barbadian men are DARC-negative, yet there does not appear to be an association between DARC expressivity and PC risk in this predominantly African-origin population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Barbados, West Indies, whose cases were male citizens with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancer identified from July 2002 to January 2011 and whose controls were age-matched residents randomly selected from a national database, designed to evaluate genetic and epidemiologic contributors to prostate cancer in this Afro-Caribbean population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22936456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24399209") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4087101/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prostate Cancer in a Black Population (PCBP) study was a large, population-based case-control study designed to evaluate genetic and epidemiologic contributors to PC in Barbados, West Indies, an Afro-Caribbean nation with relatively low admixture (7).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002239> "A nationwide population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Barbados, West Indies, whose cases were male citizens with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed prostate cancer identified from July 2002 to January 2011 and whose controls were age-matched residents randomly selected from a national database, designed to evaluate genetic and epidemiologic contributors to prostate cancer in this Afro-Caribbean population.")

