AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26387087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients of Clinic of Urology, Alexandrovska University Hospital, Sofia, Bulgaria, PrCa histopathologically confirmed 72 patients with verified BPH and PSA<3,5; 78 healthy controls from the MMC Biobank, no history of PrCa") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002240> "A hospital-based case–control study of prostate cancer in Sofia, Bulgaria, run by the Medical University of Sofia, whose cases are patients of the Clinic of Urology of Alexandrovska University Hospital with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer and whose controls are patients with benign prostatic hyperplasia and low PSA and healthy men from the MMC Biobank; it contributes genotyped cases and controls to the PRACTICAL consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22810146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1994 and 1997, 18,882 men from 210 study sites located throughout the United States and Canada were randomized in the PCPT to either the finasteride or placebo arm and followed yearly with a digital rectal exam (DRE) and PSA determination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22810146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following seven years of study participation, men without a diagnosis of prostate cancer were recommended to undergo an end-of-study biopsy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22810146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3058741/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prostate Cancer Prevention Trial (PCPT) was a phase III randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled clinical trial of finasteride in 18,882 men.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22810146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3139891/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 18,882 men aged 55 years or older with a normal digital rectal examination (DRE), a prostate-specific antigen (PSA) level of ≤ 3 ng/ml, and no prior history of prostate cancer, severe benign prostate hyperplasia, or other clinically significant coexisting conditions, were randomized to receiving finasteride (5 mg/day) or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21149329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22810146") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21667068") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3139891/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PCPT was a Phase III double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, that tested whether finasteride could reduce the period prevalence of prostate cancer during a 7-year intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002241> "A phase 3 randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, administered through the Southwest Oncology Group, in which generally healthy men aged 55 or older with a normal digital rectal examination and a PSA level of 3 ng/mL or less, recruited at sites across the United States and Canada from 1994 to 1997, were assigned to finasteride (5 mg a day) or placebo for seven years and offered an end-of-study prostate biopsy, to test whether finasteride prevents prostate cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A10052443+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pathobiological Determinants of Atherosclerosis in Youth Study, a multi-institutional autopsy study conducted in US medical centers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272499/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fifteen cooperating centers in eight communities adopted standardized procedures to collect tissue specimens and blood from individuals autopsied in the cooperating medical examiners’ laboratories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3272499/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PDAY study, initiated in 1987, assessed the relationship between established risk factors for coronary heart disease and pathologically defined atherosclerotic lesions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3272499/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pathobiological Determinants of Atherosclerosis in Youth (PDAY) study is a bi-racial investigation of the development and progression of atherosclerosis involving 3013 individuals aged 15–34 who underwent autopsy within 48 h following death from external causes including accidents, homicides, and suicide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5115850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pathobiological Determinants of Atherosclerosis in Youth (PDAY) is a unique NHLBI repository that includes of a total of 2876 study subjects, between 15 and 34 years old, black and white, men and women, who died of external, non-atherosclerosis related causes and underwent autopsy between June 1, 1987, and August 31, 1994.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:10052443") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22015179") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27861582") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5115850/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the NHLBI sponsored Pathobiological Determinants of Atherosclerosis in Youth (PDAY) study[4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002242> "A multi-institutional autopsy study, sponsored by the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, in which fifteen cooperating centres in eight US communities used standardised procedures to collect arteries, blood and other tissues from black and white males and females aged 15 to 34 who died of external causes (accidents, homicides and suicides) and were autopsied between 1987 and 1994, to relate established coronary heart disease risk factors to the extent of atherosclerotic lesions in youth.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27066548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2896763/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We thank the French Parkinson's Disease Genetics Study Group (PDG) and the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm for sample collection and preparation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> "A French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics, associating university hospitals across France, through which patients with Parkinson's disease of European origin, including early-onset index cases, and some healthy controls are recruited for genetic studies, with samples prepared by the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm in Paris.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27066548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3646288/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients were of European origin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> "A French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics, associating university hospitals across France, through which patients with Parkinson's disease of European origin, including early-onset index cases, and some healthy controls are recruited for genetic studies, with samples prepared by the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm in Paris.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27066548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3646288/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects with PD (n=1031) were recruited through the French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics associating 15 university hospitals across France.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> "A French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics, associating university hospitals across France, through which patients with Parkinson's disease of European origin, including early-onset index cases, and some healthy controls are recruited for genetic studies, with samples prepared by the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm in Paris.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27066548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3646288/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The healthy controls (n=2061) of the French sample came from either the French Three-City (3C) cohort (n=1933)13 or the Parkinson's disease genetics network (n=128).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> "A French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics, associating university hospitals across France, through which patients with Parkinson's disease of European origin, including early-onset index cases, and some healthy controls are recruited for genetic studies, with samples prepared by the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm in Paris.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20598272") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23408064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27066548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33841314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8027075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed data mining on a gene panel or whole-exome sequencing in 460 index cases with early-onset (≤ 40 years) Parkinson's disease, including 57 with autosomal recessive disease and 403 isolated cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002243> "A French network for the study of Parkinson's disease genetics, associating university hospitals across France, through which patients with Parkinson's disease of European origin, including early-onset index cases, and some healthy controls are recruited for genetic studies, with samples prepared by the DNA and cell bank of the CRicm in Paris.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants were invited to a follow-up investigation after approximately 10-yr (ie, age 35), of whom 794 (75% response) participated in the investigation (253 declined).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based cohort of young-adult women from Malmö, Sweden, who were invited in 1999–2004 at the age of 25 (excluding women pregnant then or in the previous 12 months) and invited again about ten years later at age 35, set up to explore the genetic, clinical and lifestyle factors associated with attaining peak bone mass and with later changes in bone mass, with bone density and body composition measured by DXA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, during 1999-2004, 25-yr-old women from Malmö, Sweden, were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based cohort of young-adult women from Malmö, Sweden, who were invited in 1999–2004 at the age of 25 (excluding women pregnant then or in the previous 12 months) and invited again about ten years later at age 35, set up to explore the genetic, clinical and lifestyle factors associated with attaining peak bone mass and with later changes in bone mass, with bone density and body composition measured by DXA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Criteria for inclusion were being age 25 yr and female; the criterion for exclusion was pregnancy (current or within 12 mo).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based cohort of young-adult women from Malmö, Sweden, who were invited in 1999–2004 at the age of 25 (excluding women pregnant then or in the previous 12 months) and invited again about ten years later at age 35, set up to explore the genetic, clinical and lifestyle factors associated with attaining peak bone mass and with later changes in bone mass, with bone density and body composition measured by DXA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12685719/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PEAK-25 cohort is a longitudinal, prospective, population-based study of young-adult women with the main purpose of exploring the relationship between genetic, clinical, and lifestyle factors associated with attainment of peak bone mass12 and subsequent changes in bone mass over time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based cohort of young-adult women from Malmö, Sweden, who were invited in 1999–2004 at the age of 25 (excluding women pregnant then or in the previous 12 months) and invited again about ten years later at age 35, set up to explore the genetic, clinical and lifestyle factors associated with attaining peak bone mass and with later changes in bone mass, with bone density and body composition measured by DXA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40581742") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-017-00031-7/MediaObjects/41467_2017_31_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants answered a detailed questionnaire regarding their general health; BMD and body composition was assessed by DXA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002244> "A longitudinal, prospective, population-based cohort of young-adult women from Malmö, Sweden, who were invited in 1999–2004 at the age of 25 (excluding women pregnant then or in the previous 12 months) and invited again about ten years later at age 35, set up to explore the genetic, clinical and lifestyle factors associated with attaining peak bone mass and with later changes in bone mass, with bone density and body composition measured by DXA.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12630196/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Polish Cancer Study was a large case–control study of endometrial, ovarian, and breast cancer that enrolled women aged 20–74 years from Warsaw or Łódź, Poland [12, 13].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12630196/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women with incident and pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer were identified through a hospital-based rapid identification system that covered approximately 85% of all cancer cases in Warsaw and Łódź; cancer registries were used to identify additional women with cancer for potential recruitment into the study [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12630196/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "women were selected from the Polish Electronic System, a database with demographic information for all residents of Poland [12].The control group was frequency matched to cases on study site and age group") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total, 551 of 695 eligible cases (79.3%) and 1925 of 2843 eligible controls (67.7%) were interviewed about demographic factors, reproductive history, exogenous hormone use, lifetime body size and physical activity, and medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our study subjects were derived from the Polish Endometrial Cancer Study, a large, population-based, endometrial case-control study (18) conducted among women residing in two Polish cities, Warsaw and Lodz, from 2001 to 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22730518") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24096698") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41094331") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3431573/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained study nurses collected venous blood from 85% of participating cases and 93% of participating controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002245> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer, the endometrial component of the US National Cancer Institute's Polish Cancer Study, that in 2001–2003 enrolled women aged 20–74 years in Warsaw and Łódź, Poland: cases with incident, pathologically confirmed endometrial cancer identified through a rapid hospital-based identification system and cancer registries, and controls selected from the Polish Electronic System and frequency-matched on site and age, all interviewed in person and a subset giving blood samples.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24655690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PEGASUS-TIMI 54 is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multinational clinical trial designed to evaluate the efficacy and safety of ticagrelor in addition to aspirin (75-150 mg) for the prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events in patients with a history of myocardial infarction and risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial that recruited patients with a spontaneous myocardial infarction one to three years earlier and additional risk factors from October 2010 to April 2013 and assigned them to ticagrelor 90 mg or 60 mg twice daily or matching placebo, all on low-dose aspirin, to test whether long-term ticagrelor reduces cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction or stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24655690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with a history of spontaneous myocardial infarction within 1 to 3 years are randomized in a 1:1:1 fashion to ticagrelor 90 mg twice daily, ticagrelor 60 mg twice daily, or matching placebo, all with low dose ASA, until the end of the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial that recruited patients with a spontaneous myocardial infarction one to three years earlier and additional risk factors from October 2010 to April 2013 and assigned them to ticagrelor 90 mg or 60 mg twice daily or matching placebo, all on low-dose aspirin, to test whether long-term ticagrelor reduces cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction or stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24655690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment began in October 2010 and completed in April 2013 with a sample size of over 21,000 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial that recruited patients with a spontaneous myocardial infarction one to three years earlier and additional risk factors from October 2010 to April 2013 and assigned them to ticagrelor 90 mg or 60 mg twice daily or matching placebo, all on low-dose aspirin, to test whether long-term ticagrelor reduces cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction or stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24655690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24655690+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary endpoint is a composite of cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, or stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002246> "A multinational, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial that recruited patients with a spontaneous myocardial infarction one to three years earlier and additional risk factors from October 2010 to April 2013 and assigned them to ticagrelor 90 mg or 60 mg twice daily or matching placebo, all on low-dose aspirin, to test whether long-term ticagrelor reduces cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction or stroke.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A blood sample was drawn by a certified phlebotomist at the INEN central laboratory.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each PEGEN-BC participant completed a standardized survey administered by a trained research coordinator at INEN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Peruvian Genetics and Genomics of Breast Cancer Study (PEGEN-BC) is a hospital-based cohort including patients from the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Tumor subtypes were defined using immunohistochemistry (IHC) markers by a certified pathologist at INEN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were invited to participate if they had a diagnosis of invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later and were between 21 and 79 years of age when diagnosed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36925912") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10013058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "genome-wide genotype data obtained with the Affymetrix Precision Medicine Array were pruned using PLINK v.1.9 (64)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002248> "A hospital-based cohort of women diagnosed with invasive breast cancer in 2010 or later at ages 21 to 79 and recruited at the Instituto Nacional de Enfermedades Neoplásicas (INEN) in Lima, Peru, who complete a standardised survey and give a blood sample for genotyping, with tumour subtypes from pathology at INEN, used to study genetic ancestry and other factors in breast cancer among Peruvian women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An additional 655 individuals in 167 nuclear and extended families were recruited through an asthmatic proband.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 836 unrelated asthma cases and 574 non- asthmatic controls were recruited from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centers in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described previously [19], asthma was defined using GINA criteria [23] by using a standardized questionnaire previously tested [24, 25] in patients with a history of physician-diagnosed asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Proyecto Genes Candidatos en Asma (PGCA) study is a population-based study conducted by the Institute for Immunological Research of The University of Cartagena (Colombia) to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies [16, 19, 21, 22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The control group comprised unrelated individuals without a personal or familiar history of asthma or allergies [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms12522/MediaObjects/41467_2016_BFncomms12522_MOESM1276_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-019-08469-7/MediaObjects/41467_2019_8469_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The diagnosis was confirmed by a physician belonging to the research staff, sustained on a clear clinical history with clinical symptoms and the presence of reversible airways disease on pulmonary function testing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002249> "A population-based study run by the Institute for Immunological Research of the University of Cartagena, Colombia, to identify environmental and genetic risk factors for asthma and allergies, which recruited unrelated people with asthma, diagnosed by GINA criteria with a standardised questionnaire and confirmed by a study physician from the clinical history and reversible airway obstruction on lung function testing, and unrelated controls without a personal or family history of asthma or allergies from the Social Security Clinic and outpatient health centres in Cartagena from 2002 to 2005, together with nuclear and extended families recruited through asthmatic probands. It is one of the asthma genetics studies of the Consortium on Asthma among African-ancestry Populations in the Americas (CAAPA).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2627511/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both studies (PROGENI and GenePD) initially ascertained multiplex PD families consisting of at least a sibling pair, both of whom were reported to be affected with PD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2627511/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both studies ascertained primarily Caucasian, non-Hispanic participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2627511/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control samples (n = 895) were obtained from the NINDS Human Genetics Resource Center at the Coriell Institute Coriell Cell Repositories (Camden, NJ); older individuals were preferentially selected in an effort to have the mean age at recruitment of the controls be similar to the mean age at onset of the PD cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2627511/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PD cases underwent a uniform neurological evaluation that employed PD diagnostic criteria based broadly on the United Kingdom PD Society Brain Bank Criteria (Gibb and Lees 1988), although modified by both studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2758866/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One PD case (n = 935) from each family recruited from two ongoing studies of familial PD, the GenePD study and the PROGENI study, was selected for the GWAS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18985386") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000126.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They all are negative for neurological disease based on self-report.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002250> "A genome-wide association sample of familial Parkinson's disease that combines unrelated cases, one per multiplex family, from two familial Parkinson's disease studies, PROGENI and GenePD, diagnosed by modified UK Parkinson's Disease Society Brain Bank criteria and primarily Caucasian and non-Hispanic, with Caucasian non-Hispanic controls without neurological disease from the NINDS repository at the Coriell Institute, genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research to find genetic risk factors for Parkinson's disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31656041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33234119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5399750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were followed up at 1 (visit 2 [V2]) and 12 months (visit 3 [V3]) postrecruitment, and annually thereafter until all participants had been followed up for at least 12 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> "A UK multicentre prospective observational cohort of patients hospitalised with a non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome (non-ST elevation myocardial infarction or unstable angina), run at 16 hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, whose participants were followed up at one and 12 months, and annually thereafter while the study ran, for further cardiovascular events; its medication, adherence, plasma drug-level and genome-wide genotype data are used in pharmacogenetic studies of secondary-prevention cardiovascular drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31656041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33234119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5399750/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This investigation utilizes a prospective CVD observational study that was conducted at 16 different UK hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, entitled the Pharmacogenetics of Acute Coronary Syndrome (PhACS) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> "A UK multicentre prospective observational cohort of patients hospitalised with a non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome (non-ST elevation myocardial infarction or unstable angina), run at 16 hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, whose participants were followed up at one and 12 months, and annually thereafter while the study ran, for further cardiovascular events; its medication, adherence, plasma drug-level and genome-wide genotype data are used in pharmacogenetic studies of secondary-prevention cardiovascular drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31656041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33234119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35356681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8958266/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,470 patients hospitalised with NSTE-ACS were prospectively recruited into the PhACS study from 16 sites in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> "A UK multicentre prospective observational cohort of patients hospitalised with a non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome (non-ST elevation myocardial infarction or unstable angina), run at 16 hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, whose participants were followed up at one and 12 months, and annually thereafter while the study ran, for further cardiovascular events; its medication, adherence, plasma drug-level and genome-wide genotype data are used in pharmacogenetic studies of secondary-prevention cardiovascular drugs.")
