AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31656041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33234119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35356681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8958266/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Steady-state plasma concentrations of bisoprolol were obtained in 653 patients with a NSTE-ACS at a median of one month after hospital discharge, and PK parameters were modelled using nonlinear mixed-effects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> "A UK multicentre prospective observational cohort of patients hospitalised with a non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome (non-ST elevation myocardial infarction or unstable angina), run at 16 hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, whose participants were followed up at one and 12 months, and annually thereafter while the study ran, for further cardiovascular events; its medication, adherence, plasma drug-level and genome-wide genotype data are used in pharmacogenetic studies of secondary-prevention cardiovascular drugs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28391887") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30005242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31656041") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33234119") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35356681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8958266/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "poor adherence to bisoprolol, defined as at least one pill missed in the week before visit 2 as assessed by the Brief Medication Questionnaire (BMQ)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002251> "A UK multicentre prospective observational cohort of patients hospitalised with a non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome (non-ST elevation myocardial infarction or unstable angina), run at 16 hospital sites between 2008 and 2013, whose participants were followed up at one and 12 months, and annually thereafter while the study ran, for further cardiovascular events; its medication, adherence, plasma drug-level and genome-wide genotype data are used in pharmacogenetic studies of secondary-prevention cardiovascular drugs.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between December 1997 and May 1999, we screened and enrolled subjects in Scotland, Ireland, and the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men and women aged 70-82 years were recruited if they had pre-existing vascular disease or were at increased risk of such disease because of smoking, hypertension, or diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PHArmacogenetic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk (PHASE) is a genome wide association study in the PROspective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at risk for vascular disease (PROSPER) that investigates the genetic variation responsible for the individual variation in drug response to pravastatin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The research leading to these results has received funding from the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme (FP7/2007-2013) under grant agreement n° HEALTH-F2-2009-223004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3207930/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This table shows that the genotyped subjects in the PROSPER/PHASE study are representative of the total study population of the PROSPER study, since no major discrepancies exist between the two study sets.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21977987") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22666496") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3364212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PROspective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk/PHArmacogenomic study of Statins in the Elderly at risk for cardiovascular disease (PROSPER/PHASE), a randomized placebo controlled study of pravastatin in the elderly.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002252> "A genome-wide association study within the Prospective Study of Pravastatin in the Elderly at Risk (PROSPER), a trial of pravastatin in men and women aged 70 to 82 screened in Scotland, Ireland and the Netherlands from 1997 to 1999, in which the trial's participants were genotyped genome-wide to find the genetic variation responsible for individual differences in response to pravastatin; it was funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme.")

