AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3729260/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PIC sampled a homogeneous population founded 500 years ago on two island archipelagos off the coast of Portugal (Pato et al, 2004; Sklar et al, 2004).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3729260/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The initial 10,000 GPC participants drawn from earlier studies include our Portuguese Island Collection (PIC) of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12888025") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In mainland Portugal, families were identified by collaborators at the University of Coimbra.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC12888025") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Azores and Madeira, all psychiatric and general hospitals participated and families were ascertained only if both parents and all four of the grandparents of proband were native to the islands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All of the subjects that provided DNA in this study were either thoroughly-screened psychiatric controls with no personal or familial history of mental illness or probands from families segregating bipolar disorder or SCZ in the Portuguese population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15704217") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23650244") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24123842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature07239/MediaObjects/41586_2008_BFnature07239_MOESM238_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This population consisted of subjects living in Portugal, the Azorean and Madeiran islands, or the direct (first or second generation) Portuguese immigrant population in the United States, as described in Sklar et al.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002257> "A collection of individuals and multiplex families with schizophrenia and/or bipolar disorder, with psychiatrically screened controls, sampled from the founder population of the Azores and Madeira archipelagos of Portugal through all the islands' psychiatric and general hospitals, taking families only if the proband's parents and four grandparents were native to the islands, with further families from mainland Portugal identified through the University of Coimbra and participants from the first- and second-generation Portuguese immigrant population of the United States; it was used in linkage and association studies of psychosis and became part of the Genomic Psychiatry Cohort.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/jnnp-2015-312581") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All general practitioners (GPs) and hospital specialists working with suspected/newly diagnosed PD operating in the county were regularly contacted by mail and electronically throughout the study period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1136/jnnp-2015-312581") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PICNICS study recruited newly diagnosed cases of PD and parkinsonism resident in Cambridgeshire between 1 April 2008 and 31 January 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7361014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments were completed at each time point including the Unified Parkinson’s Disease Rating Scale (UPDRS) in the CamPaIGN cohort, Movement Disorders Society UPDRS (MDS-UPDRS) in the PICNICS cohort") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7361014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PICNICS cohort was recruited between 2006 and 2013, and subjects have been followed up at 18 monthly intervals, so far for up to 11.4 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13387983/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ICICLE‐PD and PICNICS supplemented their incidence cohorts with additional non‐incident inception cases, which were excluded from the current analyses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26800710") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32303560") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33958783") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41964342") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-021-00847-6/MediaObjects/41588_2021_847_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PICNICS study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge/Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust UK and received funding from the Cure Parkinson’s Trust, the Van Geest Foundation, Parkinson’s UK, and the NIHR Cambridge Biomedical Research Centre.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002258> "A community-based cohort of people newly diagnosed with Parkinson's disease or other parkinsonism in Cambridgeshire, United Kingdom, recruited between 2006 and 2013: incident cases ascertained through general practitioners and hospital specialists between April 2008 and January 2010, in a second incidence study of the same base population as CamPaIGN, supplemented by other newly diagnosed (inception) cases. Participants are followed up every 18 months with motor, cognitive and neuropsychiatric assessments to study the natural history of Parkinson's disease; the study was sponsored by the University of Cambridge and Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Trust.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In particular, we are recruiting midlife and older Australians with high and low genetic risk of dementia to discover biological markers of early neuropathology, identify modifiable risk factors, and establish the very earliest phenotypic and neuronal signs of disease onset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Online surveys and cognitive testing are used to characterise an Australia-wide sample currently totalling over 3800 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PISA utilises genetic prediction to recruit and enrich a prospective cohort and follow them longitudinally.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants from a defined at-risk cohort and positive controls (clinical cohort of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early AD) are invited for onsite visits for detailed functional, structural and molecular neuroimaging, lifestyle monitoring, detailed neurocognitive testing, plus blood sample donation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PISA study protocol has approval from the Human Research Ethics Committees (HREC) of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute and the University of Queensland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40759756") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33341723") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7750170/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This prospective cohort study, “Prospective Imaging Study of Ageing: Genes, Brain and Behaviour” (PISA) seeks to characterise the phenotype and natural history of healthy adult Australians at high future risk of Alzheimer’s disease (AD).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002260> "A prospective cohort of healthy midlife and older adults from across Australia, recruited using genetic prediction to be enriched for high and low genetic risk of Alzheimer's disease and followed longitudinally with online surveys and cognitive testing, with at-risk participants and a clinical group of patients with mild cognitive impairment or early Alzheimer's disease invited for neuroimaging, detailed neurocognitive testing and blood sampling, to find the earliest signs and modifiable risk factors of Alzheimer's disease; approved by the ethics committee of QIMR Berghofer Medical Research Institute.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002262> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002262>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4636453/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second group of subjects came from the Pittsburgh Lung Screening Study (PLuSS), a Pittsburgh-based CT lung cancer screening study that enrolled, between 2002 and 2005, 50-79 year-old current or former cigarette smokers (≥half pack/day for ≥25 years, quit ≤10 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002262> "A prospective, Pittsburgh-based cohort of current and former cigarette smokers aged 50-79 (at least half a pack a day for 25 years and, for former smokers, quit within the last 10 years), enrolled in 2002-2005 for computed-tomography lung cancer screening and long-term follow-up.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4636453/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using PLuSS, an illustrative cohort of current and former cigarette smokers, we evaluated SNPs in GWAS-identified regions as predictors of lung cancer risk, an effort only possible with prospective data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002262> "A prospective, Pittsburgh-based cohort of current and former cigarette smokers aged 50-79 (at least half a pack a day for 25 years and, for former smokers, quit within the last 10 years), enrolled in 2002-2005 for computed-tomography lung cancer screening and long-term follow-up.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26352532") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4636453/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recalibrated both the risk factor score-only model and the risk factor score plus GWAS-region count variable model to four events per 100 (absolute 6-year lung cancer incidence observed in PLuSS; data not shown).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002262> "A prospective, Pittsburgh-based cohort of current and former cigarette smokers aged 50-79 (at least half a pack a day for 25 years and, for former smokers, quit within the last 10 years), enrolled in 2002-2005 for computed-tomography lung cancer screening and long-term follow-up.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3632/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3632_MOESM89_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a funded project to the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters (PMT) by the National Institute of Health (NIH) Pharmacogenomics Research Network (PGRN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6014560/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There was one cohort from European ancestry, which included combined samples from Genetics of Diabetes Audit and Research in Tayside Scotland (GoDARTS) and PMET1-EU (Pharmacogenomics of Metformin, cohort 1, of European ancestry; PMET1 was previously named PMT2) (REP1) (n = 6,963).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13403371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Change in HbA1c (ΔHbA1c = on‐treatment minus pre‐treatment) was regressed against: age at diabetes diagnosis, sex, pre‐treatment HbA1c, days from pre‐treatment measurement to sulfonylurea prescription, days from sulfonylurea prescription to on‐treatment measurement, average sulfonylurea dose, and interaction terms for metformin, insulin, and thiazolidinedione use.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pharmacogenomics of Metformin (PMET) cohort 1, was established to study the metformin response of patients with T2D.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants from the PMET1 cohort were selected from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort, a subsample of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health (RPEGH).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27500523") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29650774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34607834") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42504935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/30717650") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants from the PMET2 cohort were selected from the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health (RPEGH), using the criteria previously established for PMET1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002264> "A pharmacogenomic study of glycaemic response to metformin and sulfonylureas in adults with type 2 diabetes who are members of Kaiser Permanente in the United States, with drug response defined from HbA1c measurements and prescriptions in electronic health records. Its first cohort, PMET1 (previously named PMT2, from the Pharmacogenomics of Membrane Transporters project of the NIH Pharmacogenomics Research Network), was drawn from the Genetic Epidemiology Research on Adult Health and Aging (GERA) cohort of the Kaiser Permanente Research Program on Genes, Environment, and Health in Northern California; Kaiser Permanente Northern California also supplied the phenotype data of a second cohort, PMET2.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23266556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17671225") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17671225+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a case-control study to examine the relationship between PMH and CRC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal hormone use and colorectal cancer among women aged 50 to 74 in 13 counties of Washington State, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal adenocarcinoma between October 1998 and February 2002 and identified through the SEER cancer registry, and whose controls were randomly selected from driver's licence and Medicare rosters; run as a supplementary study to the Colon Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23266556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Community-based controls were randomly selected according to age distribution (in 5-year age intervals) of the eligible cases by using lists of licensed drivers from the Washington State Department of Licensing for individuals, ages 50 to 64 years, and rosters from the Health Care Financing Administration (now the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid) for individuals older than 64 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal hormone use and colorectal cancer among women aged 50 to 74 in 13 counties of Washington State, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal adenocarcinoma between October 1998 and February 2002 and identified through the SEER cancer registry, and whose controls were randomly selected from driver's licence and Medicare rosters; run as a supplementary study to the Colon Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23266556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible case patients included all female residents, ages 50 to 74 years, residing in the 13 counties in Washington State reporting to the Cancer Surveillance SEER program, who were newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal adenocarcinoma (ICD-O C18.0, C18.2-.9, C19.9, C20.0-.9) between October 1998 and February 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal hormone use and colorectal cancer among women aged 50 to 74 in 13 counties of Washington State, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal adenocarcinoma between October 1998 and February 2002 and identified through the SEER cancer registry, and whose controls were randomly selected from driver's licence and Medicare rosters; run as a supplementary study to the Colon Cancer Family Registry.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23266556") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fncomms8138/MediaObjects/41467_2015_BFncomms8138_MOESM787_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PMH-CCFR | Postmenopausal Hormones Supplementary Study to the Colon Cancer Family Registry | case-control | USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002266> "A population-based case-control study of postmenopausal hormone use and colorectal cancer among women aged 50 to 74 in 13 counties of Washington State, United States, whose cases were newly diagnosed with invasive colorectal adenocarcinoma between October 1998 and February 2002 and identified through the SEER cancer registry, and whose controls were randomly selected from driver's licence and Medicare rosters; run as a supplementary study to the Colon Cancer Family Registry.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002267> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002267>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32857771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32857771") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7454981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer patients were identified through surgical, medical, and radiation departments; and outpatient clinic visit schedules and had confirmed histological diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002267> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung and head and neck cancers conducted from 2008 in the Greater Toronto Area, Canada, at Mount Sinai Hospital (Sinai Health System) and Princess Margaret Cancer Centre, in which histologically confirmed cases seen at the hospitals' clinics and controls selected at random from family medicine clinic databases, frequency-matched on age and sex, were interviewed with a standard questionnaire on lifestyle, occupational, medical and family history.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32857771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32857771") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7454981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were patients diagnosed with lung or head and neck cancer, collectively termed as upper aero-digestive tract (UADT) cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002267> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung and head and neck cancers conducted from 2008 in the Greater Toronto Area, Canada, at Mount Sinai Hospital (Sinai Health System) and Princess Margaret Cancer Centre, in which histologically confirmed cases seen at the hospitals' clinics and controls selected at random from family medicine clinic databases, frequency-matched on age and sex, were interviewed with a standard questionnaire on lifestyle, occupational, medical and family history.")
