AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17697367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17697367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1995215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An additional recruitment category includes women aged 41 to 50 years who are found to be BRCA1 or BRCA2 gene carriers and were diagnosed with their first breast cancer during the study recruiting period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271> "A prospective cohort of women in the United Kingdom diagnosed with a first primary breast cancer at age 40 or younger, recruited between 2001 and January 2008 (with an additional category of BRCA1 or BRCA2 carriers diagnosed at 41 to 50), with family history, epidemiological and clinical data and blood collected and annual follow-up, to establish whether genetic status influences breast cancer prognosis independently of known prognostic factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17697367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20453838") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17697367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1995215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical information about diagnosis, treatment and clinical course is collected and blood is stored.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002271> "A prospective cohort of women in the United Kingdom diagnosed with a first primary breast cancer at age 40 or younger, recruited between 2001 and January 2008 (with an additional category of BRCA1 or BRCA2 carriers diagnosed at 41 to 50), with family history, epidemiological and clinical data and blood collected and annual follow-up, to establish whether genetic status influences breast cancer prognosis independently of known prognostic factors.")
