# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7360585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients recruited to the study were aged 18 years or older and signed an informed consent form") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7360585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PRECISESADS study is a European multi center, non-randomized, and observational clinical study with recruitment performed between December 2014 and December 2018 at 19 institutions in 9 countries (Austria, Belgium, France, Germany, Hungary, Italy, Portugal, Spain and Switzerland).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7360585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study had two types of patient recruitment that included a cross-sectional study and an inception prospective study with patients followed at two time points, registered with number NCT02890121 and NCT02890134 in ClinicalTrials.gov, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7360585/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The target number of included patients affected by systemic autoimmune diseases was 2005 (around 400 by disease or group of diseases: rheumatoid arthritis, scleroderma or systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren’s syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, and primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and 554 healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665668") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT02890134?fields=IdentificationModule,DescriptionModule,DesignModule,ContactsLocationsModule,StatusModule") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8192578/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report herein on the integrated molecular profiling of 304 pSS patients compared to 330 matched healthy volunteers (HV) performed using high-throughput multi-omics data collected within the PRECISESADS IMI JU project (genetic, epigenomic, transcriptomic, combined with flow cytometric data, multiplexed cytokines, as well as classical serology and clinical data).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002276> "A European multicentre observational study of the PRECISESADS project that recruited adults with systemic autoimmune diseases (rheumatoid arthritis, systemic sclerosis, primary Sjögren's syndrome, systemic lupus erythematosus, primary antiphospholipid syndrome, mixed connective tissue disease and undifferentiated connective tissue disease) and healthy controls at 19 institutions in nine countries between December 2014 and December 2018, in a cross-sectional cohort and a prospective inception cohort, to reclassify these diseases into molecular clusters using omics profiles.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, the PreFace study had a comprehensive biomaterial program, which collected germline DNA, plasma, serum and formalin-fixed paraffin embedded tumors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From February 2009 to January 2011, a total of 3529 patients were registered in the PreFace study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Postmenopausal hormone receptor-positive BC patients, for whom an upfront five-year therapy with letrozole (2.5 mg/day) was indicated, were eligible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PreFace Study (Evaluation of PREdictive FACtors Regarding the Effectivity of Aromatase Inhibitor Therapy, NCT01908556) was a prospective open label phase IV clinical trial in patients with HRpos early-stage breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted in multiple study sites across Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38344045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10853028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We here report the primary analysis of the PreFace study, which evaluated disease-free survival, overall survival and safety of upfront adjuvant letrozole treatment at the physician’s discretion in postmenopausal patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002277> "A prospective, open-label, multicentre phase IV clinical trial in Germany which in 2009-2011 enrolled postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive early breast cancer whose physician had indicated five years of upfront adjuvant letrozole, to evaluate predictive factors of aromatase inhibitor effectiveness, survival and safety, with a biomaterial collection of germline DNA, plasma, serum and tumour tissue.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood collection protocolDNA, plasma, serum") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent clinical evaluation including neuropsychological testing and various questionnaires, neuroimaging, and blood sampling for plasma biomarkers and genomic data analyses (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PREMIER consortium (May 2019 and December 2022) recruited a research cohort to establish an R&BD platform for the development of early diagnosis and precision medicine-based treatment of mild cognitive impairment (MCI) and dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11538854/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The three cohorts include the precision medicine platform for mild cognitive impairment based on multi-omics, imaging, evidence-based R&BD (PREMIER) consortium, the longitudinal/cohort study of patients with late onset dementia (LLOD) cohort, and the Samsung Medical Center (SMC) amyloid PET cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between May 2019 and May 2022, 1,700 participants were enrolled in the Precision Medicine Platform for MCI based on multi-omics, imaging, evidence-based R&BD (PREMIER) consortium, a large-scale, multi-center study involving 25 centers across South Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39113750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39254221") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39512701") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12046249/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included cognitively unimpaired (CU)11 individuals and dementia of the Alzheimer’s type (DAT)12 as normal and active control groups, respectively.11,12,13 Additionally, individuals with frontotemporal dementia14,15 were included as an active control group, without classification based on cognitive stage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002278> "A multicentre research cohort of the PREMIER consortium, which from 2019 to 2022 enrolled people with mild cognitive impairment, with cognitively unimpaired people and people with Alzheimer's-type or frontotemporal dementia as control groups, from memory clinics, regional dementia centres and hospitals across South Korea, and assessed them with neuropsychological tests, questionnaires, brain MRI, amyloid PET and blood samples (DNA, plasma, serum) to build a platform for the early diagnosis and precision-medicine treatment of mild cognitive impairment and dementia; it is one of the cohorts of K-ROAD.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11376301+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lipid profiles and hs-CRP levels will be obtained at baseline, 12 weeks, and 24 weeks in all study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11376301+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PRavastatin Inflammation CRP Evaluation (PRINCE) is an investigator-initiated, multicenter, community-based trial that will evaluate the effects of pravastatin on hs-CRP in up to 1182 individuals with coronary artery disease and up to 1702 individuals without coronary artery disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11434828+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Community-based, prospective, randomized, double-blind trial including 1702 men and women with no prior history of cardiovascular disease (primary prevention cohort) and open-label study including 1182 patients with known cardiovascular disease (secondary prevention cohort) who provided at least baseline and 12-week blood samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11434828+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the double-blind primary prevention trial were randomly assigned to receive 40 mg/d of pravastatin (n = 865) or placebo (n = 837) for 24 weeks.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11434828+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted in US office-based practices from February to December 2000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11376301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11434828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20339536") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2842298/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples were collected from 1536 PRINCE participants including 1362 that were self-identified as Caucasian [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002279> "An investigator-initiated, multicentre, community-based trial in office-based practices in the United States that from February to December 2000 evaluated the effect of pravastatin 40 mg/d on C-reactive protein: men and women with no prior cardiovascular disease (the primary prevention cohort) were randomly assigned, double-blind, to pravastatin or placebo for 24 weeks, and patients with known cardiovascular disease (the secondary prevention cohort) received open-label pravastatin, with lipid profiles and high-sensitivity C-reactive protein measured at baseline, 12 and 24 weeks. DNA collected from participants was later used in genome-wide studies of the lipid-lowering response to statins.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38109351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11062611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we aimed to study the prevalence, causes, and consequences of reduced left or right ventricular (RV) EF in a prospective cohort of healthy young elite endurance athletes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12305178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consecutive athletes are recruited through the national center for sports cardiology via 1 of 2 pathways: (a) ostensibly healthy athletes and (b) athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias based on symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12305178/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ProAFHeart study is a multicentre prospective trial aiming to determine the prevalence and 2-year incidence of arrhythmias and athletic remodeling in endurance athletes 16–80 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Actual 2/02/2017") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Endurance athletes will be aged and gender matched to healthy non-athletic controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40273982") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?ACTRN=12618000711213") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This will be assessed by comparing three groups: (1) young athletes adapting to elite training, (2) middle-aged athletes during end of career detraining, and (3) retired athletes with more than 10 years of competition at national or international level.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002280> "A multicentre prospective study in Australia and Belgium, enrolling since 2017, of atrial and ventricular remodelling and the prevalence and incidence of arrhythmias, especially atrial fibrillation, in endurance athletes aged 16 to 80 (young elite, retiring and retired athletes, including athletes referred with known or suspected arrhythmias) and in age- and sex-matched non-athletes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additional inclusion criteria were diagnostic serum PSA < 20 ng/mL, local tumor stage T1-T2, no signs of lymph node metastasis (NX or N0), or bone metastasis (MX or M0), and being ≤70 years of age at diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, study participants were derived from a retrospective nationwide cohort study of men with localized prostate cancer, the National Prostate Cancer Register (NPCR) of Sweden Follow-up Study (Stattin et al., 2008).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men in the NPCR of Sweden Follow-up Study who were still alive in 2007 (n = 7075) were eligible for and invited to participate in the PROCAP study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men with a registered localized prostate cancer in the Swedish NPCR between 1 January 1997 (1 January 1998, in one region) and 31 December 2002 were eligible for participation in the NPCR of Sweden Follow-up Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants responded to a questionnaire assessing lifestyle factors either on the web (50%) or in paper format (50%) and donated a blood sample for genetic analysis between January 2007 and June 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7012357/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We aim to study the association between leisure time sitting after a prostate cancer diagnosis and overall and prostate cancer-specific mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002281> "A nationwide Swedish cohort of men with localized prostate cancer, drawn from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden Follow-up Study (men registered in 1997-2002 with localized disease, PSA below 20 ng/mL and age 70 or younger at diagnosis), whose members still alive in 2007 answered a lifestyle questionnaire and gave a blood sample for genetic analysis in 2007-2008, to study genetic and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer progression and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were collected from Continental Italy (excluding Sardinia) as part of the PROGEMUS (PROgnostic GEnetic factors in MUltiple Sclerosis) project, 87% of cases were collected in North-West Italy (Novara, Torino, Milano, Pavia) and 13% in Central Italy (Rome).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These patients were all recruited from hospital based clinics; mean participation rate was approximately 60% (range 20%-90%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1347 consecutive Italian MS patients diagnosed according to McDonald criteria [4], were ascertained by two Italian consortia, PROGEMUS (N = 1002), and PROGRESSO (N = 345).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients born in Sardinia, of non-Italian ancestry, or refusing permission to DNA testing were not ascertained.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3681825/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROGEMUS study was approved by the Ethical Committee of the AOU Maggiore della Carità, Novara (Coordinating Centre)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23785401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29587799") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38927672") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11203028/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study included Caucasian patients with relapsing–remitting RRMS diagnosed according to McDonald’s criteria [18] who were originally enrolled from 2010 to 2013 in a cross-sectional multicenter study (PROGEMUS—PROgnostic GEnetic factors in MUltiple Sclerosis); they were regularly followed-up for at least 10 years after diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002282> "A cross-sectional multicentre study of multiple sclerosis in continental Italy (excluding Sardinia), coordinated from Novara (the AOU Maggiore della Carità and the University of Piemonte Orientale), in which consecutive patients with multiple sclerosis of Italian ancestry, mostly from north-west Italy, were recruited through hospital-based clinics and gave DNA, to study genetic factors in multiple sclerosis, in particular prognostic ones.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19279319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26595808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2677501") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,325 individuals with PD from 566 multiplex families were ascertained through a pair of siblings, both of whom were reported to have PD (PROGENI study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283> "A genetic study of familial Parkinson's disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson's disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19279319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26595808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2677501") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All available affected individuals were seen by a movement disorder specialist at one of 59 Parkinson Study Group sites located throughout North America (table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283> "A genetic study of familial Parkinson's disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson's disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19279319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26595808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19279319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2690967/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of an ongoing study designed to identify genes contributing to PD susceptibility (PROGENI Study), subjects with PD were recruited through the Parkinson Study Group (PSG), a network of 65 participating clinical centers located throughout North America.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283> "A genetic study of familial Parkinson's disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson's disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson's disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18987351") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19279319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26595808") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26595808") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4946647/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families with at least 1 pair of living siblings diagnosed as having PD were evaluated by Parkinson Study Group movement disorder neurologists.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002283> "A genetic study of familial Parkinson's disease, run through the Parkinson Study Group, that ascertains multiplex families through a pair of living siblings who both have Parkinson's disease and has the affected family members examined by movement disorder specialists at Parkinson Study Group clinical centres throughout North America, to identify genes contributing to susceptibility to Parkinson's disease.")

