# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria requires the presence of either ocular hypertension (defined as IOP, >24 mmHg; central corneal thickness, <555 μm; and Disc Damage Likelihood Scale [DDLS] grade, 0 or 1),13 an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma (DDLS grade, ≥1)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in the PROGRESSA study were genotyped on HumanCoreExome arrays (Illumina)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROGRESSA study is a longitudinal, prospective, multicenter observational cohort study of patients with early glaucoma and patients with suspected glaucoma in Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We reviewed the baseline Humphrey Visual Field (HVF) 24-2 Swedish Interactive Threshold Algorithm Standard tests for all eyes included in the study to classify participants as having either perimetric glaucoma or suspected glaucoma at study enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9559075/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "enrolled in the PROGRESSA study between May 2012 and January 2021 were reviewed for evidence of baseline structural defects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30517101") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36246177") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36249683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9560531/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROGRESSA study is a prospective longitudinal cohort study of >2000 individuals with suspect or early manifest glaucoma that was designed to investigate genetic and clinical associations with glaucoma progression (as previously described).50, 51, 52 Participants within this cohort undergo 6-month routine ophthalmic examinations that include SD OCT imaging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002285> "A prospective, longitudinal, multicentre observational cohort study in Australia, led from Flinders University in South Australia and enrolling since 2012, of people with suspected glaucoma (an optic disc suspicious of glaucoma or ocular hypertension) or early manifest primary open-angle glaucoma, who are genotyped and examined every six months with optical coherence tomography and visual field testing, to identify clinical and genetic predictors of glaucoma progression.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(1) To identify the impact of training load and genotype on the variance of EICR in elite endurance athletes and (2) determine how EICR and its determinants are associated with physical performance, health benefits and cardiac pathology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cardiac phenotyping will be repeated at 2, 5, 10 and 20 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Endurance athletes are recruited from state and national sports programs from the age of 14 to 23 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Non-athletes consist of age and gender matched university and college students recruited from Australian and Belgian universities in addition to social media campaigns.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three hundred elite endurance athletes aged 14–23 years will have comprehensive cardiovascular phenotyping using echocardiography, cardiac MRI, 12-lead ECG, exercise-ECG and 24-hour-Holter monitoring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35368514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8935177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "collaborators in Australia (Baker Heart and Diabetes Institute Melbourne, St Vincent’s Hospital Melbourne, University of Adelaide, Royal Adelaide Hospital, Royal Melbourne Hospital and Victor Chang Cardiac Research Institute) and Belgium (University Hospitals Leuven, University Hospital Antwerp and Jessa Hospital Hasselt).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002287> "An international multicentre prospective cohort study in Australia and Belgium of young competitive endurance athletes aged 14 to 23, recruited from elite endurance sports programmes, and of matched non-athletes, who undergo echocardiography, cardiac MRI, ECG, exercise testing and Holter monitoring repeated over 20 years, to assess how training load and genotype determine exercise-induced cardiac remodelling and its consequences for performance, health and heart disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2606883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Project SuGAR enlisted medical clinics, churches, and established organizations on the Sea Islands to aid in identifying patients with type 2 diabetes who belonged to families with multiple affected members (6).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2606883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Gullah-speaking African American population from the Sea Islands of South Carolina is characterized by a low degree of European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes and diabetic complications.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2606883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Type 2 diabetes–affected sibling, half-sibling, or parent-child pairs were recruited and assessed for medical, anthropometrical, and metabolic phenotypes in affected and nonaffected family members to conduct a whole-genome linkage scan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2606883/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also thank multiple personnel in the Division of Endocrinology at the Medical University of South Carolina") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19783527+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped 5,974 SNPs in 979 subjects from 418 pedigrees and used the variance component approach to compute heritability estimates, genetic and environmental correlations, and linkage analyses for selected lipoprotein subclasses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18835935") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19783527") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25279862") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25279862+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1995 and 2003, 1321 Gullah African Americans with a high prevalence of diabetes mellitus from the South Carolina Sea Islands consented to and enrolled in the Sea Islands Genetic African American Registry (Project SuGAR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002288> "A registry of Gullah-speaking African American families from the Sea Islands and coastal low country of South Carolina, a population with little European admixture and high rates of type 2 diabetes, run from the Division of Endocrinology of the Medical University of South Carolina. Between 1995 and 2003 it enrolled families with several members affected by type 2 diabetes (affected sibling, half-sibling or parent-child pairs, with their affected and unaffected relatives), identified with the help of medical clinics, churches and community organisations on the Sea Islands, and assessed them for medical, anthropometric and metabolic traits for genetic studies such as genome-wide linkage scans of type 2 diabetes and lipoprotein subclasses.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4957617/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the ProMPT (Prostate Mechanisms of Progression and Treatment) collaboration which is supported by the National Cancer Research Institute (NCRI) formed by the Department of Health, the Medical Research Council and Cancer Research UK (G0500966/75466).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> "A UK prostate cancer study run from Cambridge as a National Cancer Research Institute and Medical Research Council collaborative linked to the ProtecT trial, which collected biological samples (including tissue and urine) and data from men with and without prostate cancer attending hospital outpatient clinics, for a bio-repository used to study the mechanisms of prostate cancer progression and treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ProMPT: A study to collect samples and data from subjects with and without prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> "A UK prostate cancer study run from Cambridge as a National Cancer Research Institute and Medical Research Council collaborative linked to the ProtecT trial, which collected biological samples (including tissue and urine) and data from men with and without prostate cancer attending hospital outpatient clinics, for a bio-repository used to study the mechanisms of prostate cancer progression and treatment.")
