AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ProtecT trial and its linked ProMPT and CAP (Comparison Arm for ProtecT) studies are supported by Department of Health, England; Cancer Research UK grant number C522/A8649, Medical Research Council of England grant number G0500966, ID 75466, and The NCRI, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> "A UK prostate cancer study run from Cambridge as a National Cancer Research Institute and Medical Research Council collaborative linked to the ProtecT trial, which collected biological samples (including tissue and urine) and data from men with and without prostate cancer attending hospital outpatient clinics, for a bio-repository used to study the mechanisms of prostate cancer progression and treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We also acknowledge the support of the NIHR Cambridge Biomedical Research Centre, the DOH HTA (ProtecT grant), and the NCRI/MRC (ProMPT grant) for help with the bio-repository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> "A UK prostate cancer study run from Cambridge as a National Cancer Research Institute and Medical Research Council collaborative linked to the ProtecT trial, which collected biological samples (including tissue and urine) and data from men with and without prostate cancer attending hospital outpatient clinics, for a bio-repository used to study the mechanisms of prostate cancer progression and treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27225428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We would also like to acknowledge the support of the National Cancer Research Prostate Cancer: Mechanisms of Progression and Treatment (PROMPT) collaborative (grant code G0500966/75466) which has funded tissue and urine collections in Cambridge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002289> "A UK prostate cancer study run from Cambridge as a National Cancer Research Institute and Medical Research Council collaborative linked to the ProtecT trial, which collected biological samples (including tissue and urine) and data from men with and without prostate cancer attending hospital outpatient clinics, for a bio-repository used to study the mechanisms of prostate cancer progression and treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analyses were performed in data of the SCOPA-PROPARK cohort, a 5-year hospital-based longitudinal cohort of over 400 PD patients who have been examined annually.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At baseline (2003–2005) and the five subsequent annual visits all patients received standardized assessments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In view of the fact that we aimed to obtain information on the full spectrum of the disease, a recruitment strategy based on age at onset (< or ≥50 years) and disease duration (< or ≥10 years) was applied.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western part of The Netherlands and all fulfilled the United Kingdom Parkinson’s disease Society Brain Bank criteria for idiopathic PD [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROPARK cohort study includes over 400 PD patients who have been examined annually and followed for 5 years (i.e., six assessments) on a broad range of motor and non-motor features [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27717005") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27126456") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4893359/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The majority of patients were evaluated at the Leiden University Medical Center, but more severely affected patients were offered the possibility to be examined at their homes to prevent selective dropout.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002290> "A hospital-based longitudinal cohort of patients with idiopathic Parkinson's disease, recruited from neurology clinics of university and regional hospitals in the western Netherlands across strata of age at onset and disease duration and examined mainly at Leiden University Medical Center, who were assessed on a broad range of motor and non-motor features at baseline in 2003-2005 and annually for five years, to profile the clinical course of the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between Oct 1, 2001, and Jan 20, 2009, 228,966 men were invited to attend an appointment with a specialist nurse.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consenting participants with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring (surveillance strategy), radical prostatectomy, or three-dimensional conformal external-beam radiotherapy by a computer-generated allocation system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this randomised phase 3 trial, men aged 50-69 years registered at 337 primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited to attend a specialist nurse appointment for a serum prostate-specific antigen (PSA) test.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prostate biopsies were offered to men with a PSA concentration of 3·0 μg/L or higher.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report the study design, participant sociodemographic and clinical characteristics, and the initial results of the testing and diagnostic phase of the Prostate testing for cancer and Treatment (ProtecT) trial, which aims to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25163905") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25163905+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "With the addition of 247 pilot study participants recruited between 1999 and 2001, 2664 men were eligible for the treatment trial and 1643 (62%) agreed to be randomly assigned (545 to active monitoring, 545 to radiotherapy, and 553 to radical prostatectomy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002291> "A randomised phase 3 trial in the United Kingdom in which men aged 50–69 registered at primary care centres in nine UK cities were invited for PSA testing (a pilot from 1999, the main phase from 2001 to 2009), men with a raised PSA were offered prostate biopsy, and those with clinically localised prostate cancer were randomly assigned to active monitoring, radical prostatectomy or radiotherapy, to investigate the effectiveness of treatments for localised prostate cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were all patients newly diagnosed with primary histologically confirmed prostate cancer, actively ascertained through pathology departments across seven French-speaking hospitals in the Montreal area between 2005 and 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Concurrent to case recruitment, controls were randomly selected from the electoral list of French-speaking men residing in the Montreal area and frequency-matched to cases in 5-year age groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible subjects were men, younger than 76 years of age at the time of diagnosis or selection, residents of the greater Montreal area, registered on Quebec’s permanent electoral list (continually updated) and Canadian citizens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In-person interviews, conducted with 1,916 histologically confirmed prostate cancer cases and 1,985 population controls, elicited information on a wide range of socio-demographic, lifestyle, and medical factors, including PSA screening.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6131535/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prostate Cancer & Environment Study (PROtEuS), described previously (Blanc-Lapierre et al., 2015), is a population-based case-control study conducted in Montreal, Canada, to assess the role of environmental and lifestyle factors in prostate cancer risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24655933") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30233396") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs001391.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the conception of the genetic component of PROtEuS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002292> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in Montreal, Quebec, Canada, in which men aged 75 or under with histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed in 2005–2009 were ascertained across Montreal's French-language hospitals and controls were randomly selected from the provincial electoral list of French-speaking men, frequency-matched on age, and interviewed in person on sociodemographic, lifestyle, environmental and medical factors, with a genetic component.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10552-016-0848-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases in the PROVAQ study included women aged 18–79 years with incident primary borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube, or peritoneum, diagnosed between 2010 and 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10552-016-0848-9") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases and controls were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area and able to communicate in either French or English.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cases and controls participated in an in-person interview during which information on personal and family medical history, and sociodemographic, reproductive, and lifestyle characteristics, including multiple vitamin D determinants, was collected for each year during the entire adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among 652 incident cases of histologically confirmed epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube, or peritoneum from 7 Montreal hospitals, 507 patients (78%) agreed to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population controls were identified from the Quebec electoral list and recruited in an approximate 2:1 ratio to cases, frequency-matched to cases by 5-year age group and Montreal region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28102526") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38509513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38754871") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11369219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prevention of Ovarian Cancer in Quebec (PROVAQ) study is a population-based case-control study of female Canadian citizens aged 18-79 years conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002293> "A population-based case-control study of epithelial ovarian cancer conducted in Montreal, Canada, from 2011 to 2016, in which women aged 18–79 who were Canadian citizens living in the greater Montreal area, with incident borderline or invasive epithelial cancer of the ovary, fallopian tube or peritoneum identified at seven Montreal hospitals, and controls sampled from the Quebec electoral list and frequency-matched to them by age and region of Montreal, were interviewed in person.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14980229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15007110+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary end point was a composite of death from any cause, myocardial infarction, documented unstable angina requiring rehospitalization, revascularization (performed at least 30 days after randomization), and stroke.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294> "A double-blind randomised trial in patients hospitalised for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days that compared standard statin therapy (pravastatin 40 mg daily) with intensive statin therapy (atorvastatin 80 mg daily), and long-term treatment with the antibiotic gatifloxacin with placebo, for the prevention of death and major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14980229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15007110+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled 4162 patients who had been hospitalized for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days and compared 40 mg of pravastatin daily (standard therapy) with 80 mg of atorvastatin daily (intensive therapy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294> "A double-blind randomised trial in patients hospitalised for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days that compared standard statin therapy (pravastatin 40 mg daily) with intensive statin therapy (atorvastatin 80 mg daily), and long-term treatment with the antibiotic gatifloxacin with placebo, for the prevention of death and major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14980229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15843667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects received 400 mg of gatifloxacin daily during an initial 2-week course of therapy that began 2 weeks after randomization, followed by a 10-day course every month for the duration of the trial (mean duration, 2 years), or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294> "A double-blind randomised trial in patients hospitalised for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days that compared standard statin therapy (pravastatin 40 mg daily) with intensive statin therapy (atorvastatin 80 mg daily), and long-term treatment with the antibiotic gatifloxacin with placebo, for the prevention of death and major cardiovascular events.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14980229") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15007110") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15843667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15843667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled 4162 patients who had been hospitalized for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days and evaluated the efficacy of long-term treatment with gatifloxacin, a bactericidal antibiotic known to be effective against C. pneumoniae, in a double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002294> "A double-blind randomised trial in patients hospitalised for an acute coronary syndrome within the preceding 10 days that compared standard statin therapy (pravastatin 40 mg daily) with intensive statin therapy (atorvastatin 80 mg daily), and long-term treatment with the antibiotic gatifloxacin with placebo, for the prevention of death and major cardiovascular events.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34246321") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1216054/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects from whom DNA was obtained were recruited from volunteers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> "A collection of DNA samples and Epstein-Barr virus-transformed cell lines from healthy Japanese volunteers, recruited through the Pharma SNP Consortium in Tokyo, whose health was checked through the consortium; the samples were used for a database of SNPs and haplotypes in drug-related genes and as controls in genetic association studies of the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34246321") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1216054/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, we have provided a database of SNPs and haplotype blocks of 199 drug-related genes using samples from 752 subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> "A collection of DNA samples and Epstein-Barr virus-transformed cell lines from healthy Japanese volunteers, recruited through the Pharma SNP Consortium in Tokyo, whose health was checked through the consortium; the samples were used for a database of SNPs and haplotypes in drug-related genes and as controls in genetic association studies of the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34246321") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3228237/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A large number of control subjects (96.7%) was recruited through the Pharma SNP consortium (PSC) in Japan (http://www.jpma.or.jp/psc/frame-e.html).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> "A collection of DNA samples and Epstein-Barr virus-transformed cell lines from healthy Japanese volunteers, recruited through the Pharma SNP Consortium in Tokyo, whose health was checked through the consortium; the samples were used for a database of SNPs and haplotypes in drug-related genes and as controls in genetic association studies of the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34246321") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3228237/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through the consortium, their health and absence of diabetes were intensively checked.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> "A collection of DNA samples and Epstein-Barr virus-transformed cell lines from healthy Japanese volunteers, recruited through the Pharma SNP Consortium in Tokyo, whose health was checked through the consortium; the samples were used for a database of SNPs and haplotypes in drug-related genes and as controls in genetic association studies of the Japanese population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15202072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18199129") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34246321") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22291604") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3266877/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EBV-transformed lymphoblastoid cell lines (n = 62) were established by Pharma SNP Consortium (Tokyo, Japan) using peripheral blood lymphocytes of Japanese healthy individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002295> "A collection of DNA samples and Epstein-Barr virus-transformed cell lines from healthy Japanese volunteers, recruited through the Pharma SNP Consortium in Tokyo, whose health was checked through the consortium; the samples were used for a database of SNPs and haplotypes in drug-related genes and as controls in genetic association studies of the Japanese population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3486297") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To comprehensively analyze genetic factors underlying the resistant phenotype in the Pumwani sex worker cohort, we conducted an exploratory study with low-resolution genome-wide SNP analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3486297/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is an open prospective cohort located in the heart of the Pumwani slum.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3486297/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Pumwani sex worker cohort was established in Nairobi, Kenya, in 1985 (27, 48) and has become well known for a small group of women who remain seronegative and PCR negative to HIV despite repeated exposure through active high-risk sex work.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4081595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects involved in this study are enrollees of Pumwani sex worker Cohort, an open cohort with biannual follow-ups, established in 1985 in Nairobi, Kenya [5], [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4081595/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We examined the effect of HLA class I haplotypes on HIV-1 seroconversion and disease progression in the Pumwani sex worker cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22915813") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24992306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9840285") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29295533") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5795417/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The University of Manitoba, as well as University of Nairobi ethics review panels, have approved studies with these subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002298> "An open cohort of female sex workers in Pumwani, Nairobi, Kenya, established in 1985 with follow-up visits twice a year and studied with the University of Nairobi and the University of Manitoba, in which a subgroup of women remain uninfected by HIV-1 despite heavy exposure through sex work; it is used to study natural resistance to HIV-1 infection, seroconversion and disease progression, including host genetic studies of HLA and other variants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19540385+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individual data collection includes medical history, lifestyle behaviors (physical activity and dietary profile), blood collection and storage for biochemistry and future genetic analysis, electrocardiogram, and anthropometric measures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19540385+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PURE study has been recruiting since 2002 and has enrolled 139,506 individuals by March 31, 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24093842+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PURE study was established to investigate associations between social, behavioural, genetic, and environmental factors and cardiovascular diseases in 17 countries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24093842+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within communities, representative samples of adults aged 35 to 70 years and their household members (n = 424,921) were invited for participation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8674745/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PURE is a prospective cohort study of individuals aged 35 to 70 years at baseline in 27 countries across 5 continents, with baseline and follow-up data in 160 967 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19540385") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24093842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34910150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40519856") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12166863/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Prospective Urban Rural Epidemiology (PURE) study was an investigator-initiated study funded by the Population Health Research Institute (PHRI), Hamilton Health Sciences Research Institute, the Canadian Institutes of Health Research, and the Heart and Stroke Foundation of Ontario.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002299> "A large international prospective epidemiological cohort study, funded by the Population Health Research Institute (Hamilton, Canada) with Canadian research funders, that has recruited since 2002 adults aged 35 to 70 years, with their household members, from representative samples of urban and rural communities in low-, middle- and high-income countries on five continents (17 countries at first, 27 later), to examine how societal influences and social, behavioural, genetic and environmental factors relate to lifestyle, cardiovascular risk factors and chronic non-communicable diseases, above all cardiovascular disease. Participants give medical history, lifestyle, anthropometric and electrocardiogram data and blood stored for biochemistry and genetic analysis, and are followed up for at least 10 years for events and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23460355+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PURIFICAR is the first and only familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico providing these services to families affected with familial cancer syndromes promoting education, testing and surveillance of at-risk family members, and focusing on cancer prevention efforts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4217335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consented probands complete a comprehensive baseline questionnaire capturing medical, environmental exposures and cancer family history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4217335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals with either personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer and/or polyposis are referred to PURIFICAR by gastroenterologists, oncologists, and colorectal surgeons.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4217335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pedigrees for each proband are completed to trace the number of affected relatives with polyposis and/or cancer using PROGENY software (http://www.progenygenetics.com/) [18].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4217335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects enrolled in PURIFICAR are US Hispanic individuals with a clinical and/or genetic diagnosis of FAP, attenuated FAP (AFAP), hamartomatous polyposis syndromes, or Lynch syndrome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23460355") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25389437") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4217335/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This registry was established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center (UPRCCC) and has received direct or in kind support from the National Institutes of Health, UPRCCC, the Puerto Rico Gastroenterology Association (http://www.gastropr.org/), and the Puerto Rico Colorectal Cancer Coalition (http://cancercolonpr.org/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002300> "A familial cancer registry established in 2006 at the University of Puerto Rico Comprehensive Cancer Center, the first familial cancer registry in Puerto Rico, which enrols Hispanic individuals with a clinical or genetic diagnosis of a hereditary colorectal cancer or polyposis syndrome (familial adenomatous polyposis, attenuated FAP, hamartomatous polyposis syndromes or Lynch syndrome), referred with a personal or family history of possible familial colorectal cancer or polyposis by gastroenterologists, oncologists and colorectal surgeons. Consenting probands complete questionnaires on medical history, environmental exposures and cancer family history, their pedigrees are traced, and the registry offers affected families education, genetic testing and surveillance.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants will receive 12 weeks of varenicline in combination with 6 sessions of smoking cessation counseling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study visits will be completed at Swope Health Central, a Federally Qualified Health Center located in Kansas City, Missouri.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants are non-Hispanic African American or White adults, 18 years of age or older who smoke 3–20 cigarettes per day on 25 days or more during the preceding month, and are interested in quitting smoking, taking varenicline for 3 months, have a functioning telephone, and are willing to complete all study-related requirements.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Quit2Live is, to our knowledge, the first head-to-head trial designed with the primary aim of examining African American-White disparities in quitting smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Secondary aims are to identify mechanisms that mediate and/or moderate the relationship between race and quitting.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33300144") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies/NCT01836276") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26667382") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4818177/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study procedures are approved and monitored by the University of Kansas Medical Center (KUMC) IRB (#00001602).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002301> "A smoking-cessation clinical trial run by the University of Kansas Medical Center in Kansas City, United States, from 2013 to 2017, in which adult non-Hispanic African American and White smokers of 3–20 cigarettes a day who wanted to quit were treated with varenicline, to study racial differences in quitting smoking and their causes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After obtaining doctor's consent, a brief family history questionnaire was mailed to all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8791274+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Queensland Familial Melanoma Project was undertaken to investigate (a) the role of genetic susceptibility as indicated by skin type, pigmentation and the prevalence of naevi and (b) exposure to solar ultraviolet radiation, and their interaction in the aetiology of familial melanoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "12,016 histologically-confirmed primary invasive or in situ CMMs were recorded by the Queensland Cancer Registry (QCR) between January 1, 1982 and December 31, 1990 (notification of cancer has been compulsory in Queensland since 1982).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, we sampled index cases among patients that agreed to be contacted again, including all twins, all patients reporting at least one first-degree relative with CMM, and a random sample of the remaining patients who reported no first-degree relatives with CMM.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Risk factor questionnaires were then mailed to 7,619 relatives aged 18–75 years for whom the index cases provided contact details, and 5,158 of them responded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8791274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3677021/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The QFMP was a large family and twin study initiated in 1987 to study the influence of genetic susceptibility, sunlight exposure, and their interaction in CMM etiology (Aitken et al., 1996).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002302> "A population-based family and twin study of cutaneous melanoma in Queensland, Australia, begun in 1987, in which all Queensland residents with a first primary cutaneous melanoma diagnosed between 1982 and 1990, identified through the Queensland Cancer Registry, were sent a family-history questionnaire and familial cases, twins, a sample of non-familial cases and the cases' relatives were then studied, to investigate genetic susceptibility (skin type, pigmentation and naevi), solar ultraviolet exposure and their interaction in the aetiology of melanoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families were all of French descent and were living for the most part within 80 km of Quebec City.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase 1 of the study (1979 to 1982), a total of 1650 individuals from 375 families (nuclear families with biological or adopted offspring and uncle/aunt when available) were recruited and assessed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase 2 (1989–1997), 385 subjects from 105 phase 1 families were retested, and an additional 74 families ascertained for obesity (at least one parent and one offspring with a body mass index of 32 kg/m2 or higher) were added to the cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase 3 (1998–2002), 44 new families ascertained for obesity were added, while 204 subjects from phase 1 were tested a third time and 113 subjects from phase 2 were tested a second time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main goal of the Quebec Family Study (QFS) as originally planned was to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health related behavior.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24533236") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3920031/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from the Quebec Health Research Council in 1978 and the study was launched at Laval University (Quebec City, Canada) the same year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002303> "An observational family study launched at Laval University in Quebec City, Canada, in 1978 to investigate the role of genetic factors in physical fitness, body composition, risk factors for common diseases and health-related behaviour, which in 1979–1982 recruited nuclear families of French descent living mostly near Quebec City (with biological or adopted offspring) irrespective of body weight. As the study turned to the genetics of obesity, families ascertained through obese members were added in 1989–1997 and 1998–2002, and it has been used to study the familial and genetic determinants of obesity, body fat distribution and energy balance.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the Quebec lung cancer screening program, the Lung-RADS grading system (version 2022) was used to guide management decisions, such as close follow-up with LDCT or biopsy, consistent with previous reports [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From this high-risk group, participants were selected for the SYNERGIQC project, 2974 provided blood samples for research purposes to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In SYNERGIQC, blood samples were collected during the first or second visit following enrolment in the screening program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident lung cancer was defined by pathological confirmation or LDCT diagnosis in SYNERGIQC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SYNERGIQC originates from the Quebec lung cancer screening program [17], a provincial multicenter pilot-study launched in 2021 for ever-smokers aged 55–74.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41990546") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13096907/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The program initially enrolled participants, of whom 3542 were classified as high-risk based on a PLCOm2012norace risk score of ≥2%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002304> "A research cohort of ever-smokers aged 55–74 at high clinical risk of lung cancer (a PLCOm2012norace risk of 2% or more) enrolled in the provincial multicentre pilot lung cancer screening program of Quebec, Canada, launched in 2021, who gave blood samples to the AIRS biobank at the IUCPQ and CUSM sites at their first or second screening visit and are followed for incident lung cancer after low-dose CT screening managed with Lung-RADS.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3435290/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1349 histopathologically-confirmed prostate cancer cases were recruited through private and public urologists in Queensland, Australia via three prostate cancer studies or resources: the Retrospective Queensland Study (N = 154; [26]), the Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project (ProsCan, N = 857; [25]) and from the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00748-0/MediaObjects/41588_2020_748_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Acquired through the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource (APCB), where cases were recruited through local urologists at the time of diagnosis .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00748-0/MediaObjects/41588_2020_748_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "QLD = A longitudinal cohort study (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project: ProsCan)conducted in Queensland, through which men newly diagnosed with prostate cancer from 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals were directly referred to ProsCan at the time of diagnosis by their treating clinician (age range 43-88 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00748-0/MediaObjects/41588_2020_748_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "QLD = Controls comprised healthy male blood donors with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through (i) the Australian Red Cross Blood Services in Brisbane (age range 19-76 years) and (ii) the Australian Electoral Commission (AEC) (age and post-code/ area matched to ProsCan, age range 54-90 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-020-00748-0/MediaObjects/41588_2020_748_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Retrospective Queensland Study (QLD) and the Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project (ProsCan)                              |  QLD           | PRACTICAL iCOGS") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22970239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26992435") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33398198") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "QLD (n=4564) Queensland Study Brisbane, Australia Case-control") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002305> "A case-control study of prostate cancer in Queensland, Australia, contributed to the PRACTICAL consortium, whose cases were men with histopathologically confirmed prostate cancer recruited through urologists in Queensland from the Retrospective Queensland Study, the ProsCan (Prostate Cancer Supportive Care and Patient Outcomes Project) cohort of men newly diagnosed at 26 private practices and 10 public hospitals, and the Queensland node of the Australian Prostate Cancer BioResource. Its controls were healthy men with no personal history of prostate cancer, recruited through the Australian Red Cross Blood Service in Brisbane or, matched to the cases by age and postcode, through the Australian Electoral Commission.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27660192+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adjuvant capecitabine plus bevacizumab versus capecitabine alone in patients with colorectal cancer (QUASAR 2): an open-label, randomised phase 3 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27660192+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between April 25, 2005, and Oct 12, 2010, 1952 eligible patients were enrolled, of whom 1941 had assessable data (968 in the capecitabine alone group and 973 in the capecitabine and bevacizumab group).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27660192+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the open-label, randomised, controlled QUASAR 2 trial, which was done at 170 hospitals in seven countries, we recruited patients aged 18 years or older with WHO performance status scores of 0 or 1 who had undergone potentially curative surgery for histologically proven stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27660192+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were randomly assigned (1:1) to receive eight 3-week cycles of oral capecitabine alone (1250 mg/m2 twice daily for 14 days followed by a break for 7 days) or the same regimen of oral capecitabine plus 16 cycles of 7·5 mg/kg bevacizumab by intravenous infusion over 90 min on day 1 of each cycle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27660192+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated whether bevacizumab could improve disease-free survival in the adjuvant setting after resection of the primary tumour.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27660192") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.isrctn.com/api/query/format/default?q=ISRCTN45133151") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Public University of Oxford (UK) University/education") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002306> "An open-label randomised phase 3 trial in which patients aged 18 or older who had undergone potentially curative surgery for stage III or high-risk stage II colorectal cancer were recruited at 170 hospitals in seven countries, led from the United Kingdom, between 2005 and 2010 and randomly assigned to adjuvant capecitabine alone or capecitabine plus bevacizumab, to test whether bevacizumab improves disease-free survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4407390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 3,244 participants (2,434 depressed patients and 810 healthy controls) were recruited from the Radiant study, which included the Depression Network (DeNT) study [14], the Depression Case–Control (DeCC) study [15], and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) study [16].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4407390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants in the DeNT and DeCC studies experienced two or more episodes of major depression of at least moderate severity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4407390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DeCC study is a case–control study which recruited unrelated patients from three sites in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4407390/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DeNT study is a family study which recruited sibling pairs affected with recurrent unipolar depression from eight clinical sites across Europe and one in the USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotyping of the RADIANT study was funded by a joint grant from the UK Medical Research Council and GlaxoSmithKline (G0701420).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25903154") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642257") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00439-013-1370-8") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants came from two studies on recurrent depression [the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study and the Depression Network (DeNT) study] and a pharmacogenetic study [the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs from Depression (GENDEP) study], which have been described in more detail previously (Cohen-Woods et al. 2009; Farmer et al. 2004; Uher et al. 2009).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002307> "A collection of clinically ascertained depression samples genotyped together for genome-wide association studies of major depressive disorder, made up of the Depression Network (DeNT) study of sibling pairs with recurrent unipolar depression recruited at clinical sites in Europe and one in the United States, the Depression Case Control (DeCC) study of unrelated patients with recurrent depression recruited at three UK sites, and the Genome-Based Therapeutic Drugs for Depression (GENDEP) pharmacogenetic study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3419947") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To be realistic components of a predictive algorithm for adverse reactions to radiotherapy, genetic effects will need to be robust in terms of replication and the central question will be their effect on an individual not a population, i.e., positive predictive value is more important than population attributable risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3419947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients in the Cambridge Intensity Modulated Radiotherapy (IMRT) and Manchester prospective trials were offered recruitment to RAPPER when they enroled in the component study; blood was taken for RAPPER before radiotherapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3419947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RAPPER study (UKCRN1471) is a large UK sample collection study, opened in 2005, which recruits patients from clinical trials and other well-designed studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3419947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Toxicity data for all patients were collected prospectively within the component clinical trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26510858") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26510858+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SNP genotypes were determined in female breast cancer patients from the RAPPER (Radiogenomics: Assessment of polymorphisms for predicting the effects of radiotherapy) study using the Illumina CytoSNP12 genome-wide array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22767148") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27070714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29892016") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5036513/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RAPPER cohort comprises individuals and data recruited into the RT01 and CHHiP UK radiotherapy trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002308> "A UK multicentre sample collection study, opened in 2005, that collects blood samples and prospectively recorded radiotherapy toxicity data from cancer patients, among them breast and prostate cancer patients, enrolled in radiotherapy clinical trials (such as RT01 and CHHiP) and other studies, to identify genetic variants that predict the adverse effects of radiotherapy on normal tissue.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1049/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1049_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RBCS Rotterdam Breast Cancer Study 36 Netherlands Familial breast cancer patients selected from the clinical genetics center at Erasmus Medical Center between 1994-2005 Spouses or mutation-negative siblings of heterozygous Cystic Fibrosis mutation carriers selected from the clinical genetics centre at Erasmus Medical Center between 1996-2006") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each family, the youngest breast cancer patient who had been tested for BRCA1 and BRCA2 was assigned to be the index case and included in RBCS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RBCS cases (N = 2,751) were selected from the database of the Clinical Genetics Centre at Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam, representing the Southwestern part of the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Selected families included all families counselled between 1994 and 2014 that presented with at least two cases of female breast cancer or at least one case of female breast cancer and one case of ovarian cancer in first- or second-degree relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The RBCS control population (N = 1,159) was geographically matched and included women from cystic fibrosis families who were either spouses of individuals at risk of being carrier of a CFTR mutation or individuals who were tested negative for a CFTR mutation and were counselled between 1996 and 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22267197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/srep30026") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The samples included in this study were from two Dutch breast cancer case-control studies: RBCS and ABCS-F.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002309> "A hospital-based breast cancer case-control study in the southwest of the Netherlands, whose cases are index patients from families with breast or breast and ovarian cancer counselled at the Clinical Genetics Centre of Erasmus University Medical Centre in Rotterdam from 1994, and whose geographically matched controls are women from cystic fibrosis families counselled at the same centre; it is one of the studies of the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22085902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24076602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31961910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38880029") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22085902") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3283173/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trio family samples were collected through REFGENSEP, whereas samples for multiplex families were obtained from both REFGENSEP and CCPGSMS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310> "A French national network for the genetic study of multiple sclerosis that since 1992 has recruited people with multiple sclerosis, with the parents and siblings of patients in trio and multiplex families, through physicians at hospital centres across France and through advertising campaigns run with patient associations, confirming each diagnosis by a network physician and collecting clinical information and a blood sample, and whose biological resource centre keeps DNA and cell lines for genetic studies of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22085902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24076602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31961910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38880029") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24076602") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2770/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2770_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical information, informed consent and a blood sample were collected under the supervision of a trained physician.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310> "A French national network for the genetic study of multiple sclerosis that since 1992 has recruited people with multiple sclerosis, with the parents and siblings of patients in trio and multiplex families, through physicians at hospital centres across France and through advertising campaigns run with patient associations, confirming each diagnosis by a network physician and collecting clinical information and a blood sample, and whose biological resource centre keeps DNA and cell lines for genetic studies of multiple sclerosis.")
