AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22085902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24076602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31961910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38880029") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature10251/MediaObjects/41586_2011_BFnature10251_MOESM243_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All volunteers are examined by a REFGENSEP physician to confirm the diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310> "A French national network for the genetic study of multiple sclerosis that since 1992 has recruited people with multiple sclerosis, with the parents and siblings of patients in trio and multiplex families, through physicians at hospital centres across France and through advertising campaigns run with patient associations, confirming each diagnosis by a network physician and collecting clinical information and a blood sample, and whose biological resource centre keeps DNA and cell lines for genetic studies of multiple sclerosis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21833088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22085902") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24076602") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31961910") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38880029") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/all/collections/REFGENSEP") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The BRC has already compiled DNA and lymphoblastoid cells from: 860 simplex, 130 multiplex families, 1332 cases and 790 controls which are available for genetic studies, and the collection is still going on.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002310> "A French national network for the genetic study of multiple sclerosis that since 1992 has recruited people with multiple sclerosis, with the parents and siblings of patients in trio and multiplex families, through physicians at hospital centres across France and through advertising campaigns run with patient associations, confirming each diagnosis by a network physician and collecting clinical information and a blood sample, and whose biological resource centre keeps DNA and cell lines for genetic studies of multiple sclerosis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12231538/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Circulating biomarkers, DNA methylation, microRNAs, and proteomics have been measured in a cohort subset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12231538/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the 2005 and 2018 surveys, a random sample of participants was obtained from the city of Girona and rural towns (three in 2005 and two in 2018), each town with fewer than 10 000 inhabitants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12231538/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Moreover, follow-up information on CV and non-CV events and cause-specific mortality was obtained by linking the REGICOR cohort with hospital admissions, the mortality registry, and primary care records through the PADRIS program.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12231538/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Girona Heart Registry (REGICOR) population cohort was established to study cardiovascular (CV) risk factor prevalence and control, investigate novel risk factors associated with the incidence of CV diseases, and develop CV risk prediction models.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12231538/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The REGICOR cohort integrates the participants of four population-based surveys conducted in 1995, 2000, 2005, and 2018 in the Girona province (North-Eastern Spain), with a current reference population of approximately 790 000 inhabitants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16371198") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781316") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40611603") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7588921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7588921+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed changes in 28-day and 3-year survival after a first myocardial infarction between 1978-85 and 1986-88 in the REGICOR (Registre GIroní del COR) registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002311> "A population-based study of cardiovascular disease in the province of Girona, north-eastern Spain, run by the REGICOR study group of the Hospital del Mar Research Institute, Barcelona. It began as a registry of patients with myocardial infarction in Girona, with data from 1978, and its population cohort, established in 1995 to study the prevalence and control of cardiovascular risk factors, novel risk factors and biomarkers of cardiovascular disease and cardiovascular risk prediction, combines participants of four surveys (1995, 2000, 2005 and 2018) randomly sampled from towns of the province and the city of Girona. Participants were re-examined, followed up for cardiovascular and other events and death, including by linkage to electronic health records, and genotyped, with other omics measured in subsets.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4029977/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All women from Stockholm County, Sweden with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred to the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Karolinska University Hospital, Stockholm, Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4029977/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Histological verification of cancer diagnoses in relatives was obtained from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records and/or death certificates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4029977/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those who accepted (index patients) completed two questionnaires: one regarding diagnoses and age of onset of colorectal, breast, ovarian and other cancers in their family (i.e., the index patient, her first- and, second-degree relatives and first cousins), and a second questionnaire on their own risk factors") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For each patient, the following was collected: blood and tumor samples; detailed family history and formulation of a pedigree where all suspected cancer cases were verified in medical records/pathology report if possible; questionnaire covering relevant environmental factors underlying endometrial cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients (n=520) who underwent surgery for endometrial cancer at Karolinska University hospital Solna, Sweden between 2008 and 2011 were included in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24851142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40101186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27135401") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3562/MediaObjects/41588_2016_BFng3562_MOESM301_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Registry of Endometrial Cancer in Sweden (RENDOCAS) is a hospital based case- control study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002312> "A hospital-based case-control study of endometrial cancer in Sweden, whose patients underwent surgery for uterine cancer from 2008 at Karolinska University Hospital, Solna, in Stockholm, to which women of Stockholm County with newly diagnosed uterine cancer are referred, and gave blood and tumour samples, questionnaires on their own risk factors and on cancers in their families, and pedigrees in which cancers in relatives were verified from the Swedish Cancer Registry, medical records or death certificates where possible. Its cases were genotyped in the genome-wide association studies of the Endometrial Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40207047") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30928825") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30928825+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Randomized Trial to Prevent Vascular Events in HIV (REPRIEVE) (A5332) is a prospective, randomized, placebo-controlled trial of a statin strategy for the primary prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE) in PWH with low to moderate traditional risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313> "A multicentre, international, phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (ACTG A5332) of pitavastatin calcium for the primary prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events in adults with HIV on antiretroviral therapy and at low-to-moderate traditional cardiovascular risk, which enrolled participants from 2015 to 2019 at sites in 12 countries across five Global Burden of Disease regions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40207047") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11179771/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria included age ≥40 and ≤75 years, on any ART regimen for at least 6 months before study entry, CD4+ T‐cell count >100 cells/mm3, and fasting LDL‐C meeting specific thresholds depending on the 10‐year ASCVD risk score estimated by the 2013 American College of Cardiology/American Heart Association PCEs (Figure S1B).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313> "A multicentre, international, phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (ACTG A5332) of pitavastatin calcium for the primary prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events in adults with HIV on antiretroviral therapy and at low-to-moderate traditional cardiovascular risk, which enrolled participants from 2015 to 2019 at sites in 12 countries across five Global Burden of Disease regions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40207047") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11179771/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PRSs for CAD (GPSMult) and lipid traits were calculated in a global cohort of people with HIV treated with antiretroviral therapy with low‐to‐moderate atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease risk enrolled in REPRIEVE (Randomized Trial to Prevent Vascular Events in HIV).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313> "A multicentre, international, phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (ACTG A5332) of pitavastatin calcium for the primary prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events in adults with HIV on antiretroviral therapy and at low-to-moderate traditional cardiovascular risk, which enrolled participants from 2015 to 2019 at sites in 12 countries across five Global Burden of Disease regions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38533953") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39435321") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40207047") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39435321") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11493083/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REPRIEVE (NCT02344290) enrolled 7769 participants from March 2015 to July 2019 in 12 countries across 5 Global Burden of Disease (GBD) regions [11] in a multicenter phase 3 trial based on a prospective, double-blind, placebo-controlled design to evaluate pitavastatin calcium (4 mg daily) vs placebo among PWH undergoing ART [9, 10].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002313> "A multicentre, international, phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (ACTG A5332) of pitavastatin calcium for the primary prevention of major adverse cardiovascular events in adults with HIV on antiretroviral therapy and at low-to-moderate traditional cardiovascular risk, which enrolled participants from 2015 to 2019 at sites in 12 countries across five Global Burden of Disease regions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31146072+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "An international, prospective cohort study recruited cancer patients in 26 hospitals in eight countries between April 2014 and March 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31146072+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were followed for a minimum of 12 (lung) or 24 (breast/prostate) months and summary descriptive statistics were generated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31146072+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REQUITE aimed to establish a resource for multi-national validation of models and biomarkers that predict risk of late toxicity following radiotherapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A31146072+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The centralised, accessible database includes: physician- (47,025 forms) and patient- (54,901) reported outcomes; 11,563 breast photos; 17,107 DICOMs and 12,684 DVHs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7593843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In order to address previous limitations in pooling data, in using common toxicity scoring systems and in collecting standardized data, REQUITE carried out an international, multi-center, prospective observational study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31146072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33178576") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37862240") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10653584/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REQUITE received funding from the European Union’s Seventh Framework Programme for research, technological development, and demonstration under grant agreement No. 601826.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002314> "An international, prospective, observational cohort study, funded by the European Union's Seventh Framework Programme, that between April 2014 and March 2017 recruited patients with breast, prostate or lung cancer planned for potentially curative radiotherapy at 26 hospitals in eight countries in Europe and the United States. With standardised data collection across centres, it gathered pre-treatment blood samples, treatment and dosimetry data and physician- and patient-reported outcomes during follow-up of at least 12 (lung) or 24 (breast, prostate) months, in a centralised database and biobank with genotype data, as a resource for validating models and biomarkers, including genetic ones, that predict toxicity after radiotherapy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11167223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12928689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11054002+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1,635 randomly selected residents of Reykjavik, Iceland, were enrolled, and among them, 1,045 responded and took part in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315> "A population-based epidemiological study of eye disease, run by Icelandic and Japanese study groups, in which citizens of Reykjavik, Iceland, aged 50 years and older, randomly selected from the national population census, were given ophthalmological examinations to determine the prevalence of lens opacities, refractive error and visual acuity, and open-angle glaucoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11167223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12928689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11054002+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based cataract epidemiological study, the Reykjavik Eye Study, was conducted to determine the prevalence and characteristics of lens opacities in Iceland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315> "A population-based epidemiological study of eye disease, run by Icelandic and Japanese study groups, in which citizens of Reykjavik, Iceland, aged 50 years and older, randomly selected from the national population census, were given ophthalmological examinations to determine the prevalence of lens opacities, refractive error and visual acuity, and open-angle glaucoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11167223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12928689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11167223") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11167223+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1700 persons were randomly selected from the national population census.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315> "A population-based epidemiological study of eye disease, run by Icelandic and Japanese study groups, in which citizens of Reykjavik, Iceland, aged 50 years and older, randomly selected from the national population census, were given ophthalmological examinations to determine the prevalence of lens opacities, refractive error and visual acuity, and open-angle glaucoma.")
