AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11054002") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11167223") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12928689") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12928689") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12928689+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To establish the age- and sex-specific prevalence of open-angle glaucoma (OAG) subsuming pseudoexfoliation (PEX) in the city of Reykjavik.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002315> "A population-based epidemiological study of eye disease, run by Icelandic and Japanese study groups, in which citizens of Reykjavik, Iceland, aged 50 years and older, randomly selected from the national population census, were given ophthalmological examinations to determine the prevalence of lens opacities, refractive error and visual acuity, and open-angle glaucoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants completed a detailed lifestyle questionnaire which included questions about occupational exposures, education, medical history and family history of cancer and lung disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung cancer cases diagnosed at ages older than 60 years were recruited if they reported a family history of lung cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants also donated blood samples for DNA extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Resource for the Study of Lung Cancer Epidemiology in North Trent is an ongoing study conducted in Sheffield from 2006 and due to complete recruitment in 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cases and matched controls were recruited through several major cancer treatment centres, however, the majority were recruited in North Trent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study recruited pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 years or younger and family matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002316> "A case-control study of lung cancer epidemiology run from Sheffield, England, since 2006, which recruits pathologically confirmed lung cancer cases diagnosed at age 60 or younger (or older with a family history of lung cancer) and family-matched controls through several cancer treatment centres, mostly in North Trent, collecting a lifestyle, occupational-exposure and family-history questionnaire and blood for DNA.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7529994/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1991–1992, 23,820 participants aged 30 to 65 years old from seven townships in Taiwan enrolled in the study, completed questionnaires, and underwent health examinations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC7529994/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The REVEAL-HBV and -HCV cohort studies are based in the same community-based survey, which was conducted to examine the characteristics and risk factors for HCC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10548479/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HCC diagnosis was determined by transabdominal ultrasound and α-fetoprotein testing or by data linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry or the National Death Certification profiles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10548479/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of the study enrollees, 4,155 (17.4%) were hepatitis B virus surface antigen (HBsAg) seropositive and were followed as part of the REVEAL-HBV study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10548479/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Regular examinations consisting of blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography occurred every 6–12 months through December 31, 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29600553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32406072") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36878686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC10548479/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similarly, 1,095 (4.6%) persons were anti-HCV seropositive and were followed as part of the REVEAL-HCV study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002317> "A community-based prospective cohort in Taiwan made up of the participants of the REVEAL study who were seropositive for hepatitis B surface antigen: the REVEAL study enrolled residents aged 30 to 65 years from seven townships in Taiwan in 1991–1992, who gave blood samples, completed questionnaires and had health examinations at enrolment, and its HBsAg-seropositive participants were followed with blood collection and abdominal ultrasonography every 6–12 months and by linkage to the Taiwan National Cancer Registry and death certification, to study the risk factors for hepatocellular carcinoma in chronic hepatitis B virus carriers. Its sister cohort, REVEAL-HCV, followed the participants seropositive for antibodies to hepatitis C virus.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002318> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002318>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24386513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Risk Factors for Prostate Cancer Study (RFPCS) is a population based case- control study that in the period 1994-1997 recruited through State Cancer Registries men resident in Perth and Melbourne diagnosed with prostate cancer at age less than 70 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002318> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Cancer Council Victoria, which in 1994-1997 recruited men resident in Melbourne and Perth, Australia, who were diagnosed with prostate cancer before age 70, through the state cancer registries, together with controls identified from government electoral rolls and frequency-matched to the cases by age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24386513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2846760/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were selected from the RFPCS study, in which they were identified through government electoral rolls and frequency matched to the age distribution of the RFPCS cases (n=667), together with a random sample from the MCCS cohort (n=981).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002318> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Cancer Council Victoria, which in 1994-1997 recruited men resident in Melbourne and Perth, Australia, who were diagnosed with prostate cancer before age 70, through the state cancer registries, together with controls identified from government electoral rolls and frequency-matched to the cases by age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19767753") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24386513") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.450/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng450_MOESM22_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24386513") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3877662/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We analyzed NKX3.1 genotype and serum IGF-I in a second group of cases and controls from the Risk Factors for Prostate Cancer Study of the Victoria Cancer Council (RFPCS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002318> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer run by the Cancer Council Victoria, which in 1994-1997 recruited men resident in Melbourne and Perth, Australia, who were diagnosed with prostate cancer before age 70, through the state cancer registries, together with controls identified from government electoral rolls and frequency-matched to the cases by age.")

