AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17615053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19050702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20949628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22076443") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19050702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2607223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These controls (1136 men, 1702 women; mean age 59.8 years; s.d.±10.8) were the spouses or unrelated friends of patients with malignancies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002323> "A collection of DNA samples from people with cancer, among them colorectal cancer patients, and from healthy people who were the spouses or unrelated friends of patients with malignancies, recruited from 1999 through the Institute of Cancer Research and the Royal Marsden Hospital NHS Trust in the United Kingdom for genetic epidemiological studies of cancer susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17615053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19050702") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20949628") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22076443") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22076443") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3263985/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK2 (NSCCG) consisted of 2854 CRC cases (58% male, mean age at diagnosis 59.3 years; SD± 8.7) ascertained through two ongoing initiatives at the Institute of Cancer Research/Royal Marsden Hospital NHS Trust (RMHNHST) from 1999 onwards—The National Study of Colorectal Cancer Genetics (NSCCG) and the Royal Marsden Hospital Trust/Institute of Cancer Research Family History and DNA Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002323> "A collection of DNA samples from people with cancer, among them colorectal cancer patients, and from healthy people who were the spouses or unrelated friends of patients with malignancies, recruited from 1999 through the Institute of Cancer Research and the Royal Marsden Hospital NHS Trust in the United Kingdom for genetic epidemiological studies of cancer susceptibility.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At baseline, the participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities with different characteristics: 1350 participants from an urban region in Itabashi, Tokyo; 864 participants from a mountainous region in Hidakagawa, Wakayama; and 826 participants from a coastal region in Taiji, Wakayama.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2005, we established a large-scale population-based OA cohort study called the Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability (ROAD) with the goal of establishing epidemiologic indices to evaluate clinical evidence for the development of a disease-modifying treatment for skeletal diseases [6,7].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ROAD study was a prospective investigation of OA conducted among population-based cohorts in various cities across Japan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline survey of the Research on Osteoarthritis/Osteoporosis Against Disability (ROAD) study was conducted from 2005 to 2007; 3040 participants (1061 men and 1979 women; mean age 70.3 years) completed all OA examinations, including a questionnaire of medical information in the present/past and radiographic examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using the data acquired from the ROAD study, we reported the prevalence of osteoporosis and hip OA [7,8].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19410032") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39968102") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11834036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We initially enrolled 3040 participants (1061 men and 1979 women; mean age 70.3 years; range 23–95 years) during the baseline period and have since conducted multiple follow-up surveys since 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002325> "A population-based cohort study of osteoarthritis and osteoporosis in Japan, established in 2005 to build epidemiological indices for skeletal diseases, whose participants were recruited from resident registration listings in three communities (urban Itabashi in Tokyo, and mountainous Hidakagawa and coastal Taiji in Wakayama Prefecture) for a baseline survey in 2005–2007 with radiographic examinations and questionnaires, and have been re-examined in follow-up surveys since.")

