AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16835332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17169636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6685438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort enrollment began in 2000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002335> "A prospective population-based cohort of healthy male volunteers enrolled in San Antonio and South Texas since 2000 by the San Antonio Center of Biomarkers of Risk for Prostate Cancer of the National Cancer Institute's Early Detection Research Network, screened annually or biannually by digital rectal examination and serum prostate-specific antigen, with prostate biopsy recommended after an abnormal result, to study prostate cancer risk and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16835332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17169636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6685438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SABOR study is a National Cancer Institute Early Detection Research Network-sponsored Clinical and Epidemiologic Validation Center that includes a multi-ethnic cohort of 3880 men from San Antonio and South Texas area without prior diagnosis of PCa") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002335> "A prospective population-based cohort of healthy male volunteers enrolled in San Antonio and South Texas since 2000 by the San Antonio Center of Biomarkers of Risk for Prostate Cancer of the National Cancer Institute's Early Detection Research Network, screened annually or biannually by digital rectal examination and serum prostate-specific antigen, with prostate biopsy recommended after an abnormal result, to study prostate cancer risk and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16835332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17169636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6685438/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We herein investigate the relationship between consumption of various nutrients including types of dietary fat using a validated food frequency questionnaire (FFQ) and the future risk for PCa taken one time at baseline in men participating in a community-based screening cohort called the San Antonio Biomarkers of Risk (SABOR) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002335> "A prospective population-based cohort of healthy male volunteers enrolled in San Antonio and South Texas since 2000 by the San Antonio Center of Biomarkers of Risk for Prostate Cancer of the National Cancer Institute's Early Detection Research Network, screened annually or biannually by digital rectal examination and serum prostate-specific antigen, with prostate biopsy recommended after an abnormal result, to study prostate cancer risk and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16835332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17169636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7028127/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were examined annually/biannually by digital rectal exam and serum prostate‐specific antigen level, and prostate biopsy was recommended for men with positive results.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002335> "A prospective population-based cohort of healthy male volunteers enrolled in San Antonio and South Texas since 2000 by the San Antonio Center of Biomarkers of Risk for Prostate Cancer of the National Cancer Institute's Early Detection Research Network, screened annually or biannually by digital rectal examination and serum prostate-specific antigen, with prostate biopsy recommended after an abnormal result, to study prostate cancer risk and its biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16835332") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17169636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30385837") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31226226") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7028127/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SABOR is a cohort study which has been enrolling healthy male volunteers in San Antonio and South Texas area since 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002335> "A prospective population-based cohort of healthy male volunteers enrolled in San Antonio and South Texas since 2000 by the San Antonio Center of Biomarkers of Risk for Prostate Cancer of the National Cancer Institute's Early Detection Research Network, screened annually or biannually by digital rectal examination and serum prostate-specific antigen, with prostate biopsy recommended after an abnormal result, to study prostate cancer risk and its biomarkers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16123354+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study was initiated to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1380282/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All of the probands’ first-, second-, and third-degree relatives aged ⩾18 years were invited to participate in the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recalled twice for a total of up to three examinations per person.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAFDGS also began in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study [2] and recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in an earlier epidemiologic survey, the San Antonio Heart Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second recall began the gallbladder component of the study, recruited new family members, and added 8 newly recruited families [3,4].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16123354") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16400619") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These family data were obtained from two studies: the San Antonio Family Heart Study (SAFHS) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (SAFDGS), which are together referred to as the San Antonio Family Studies (SAFS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002336> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, United States, begun in 1991 as the San Antonio Family Diabetes Study to identify susceptibility genes for type 2 diabetes, which recruited low-income Mexican Americans with type 2 diabetes identified in the San Antonio Heart Study and their extended families, examined them repeatedly, and at its second recall added a gallbladder disease component and further families; with the San Antonio Family Heart Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recalled for up to four examinations over an approximately 20-year period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, begun in 1991, that recruited low-income Mexican Americans aged 40 to 60, selected at random without regard to disease from Mexican American census tracts, together with their extended families, and followed them with repeated examinations to study the genetic and environmental contributions to cardiovascular disease risk factors. With the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAFHS began in 1991 with 40- to 60-year-old low-income Mexican Americans, selected at random without regard to presence or absence of disease, who were almost exclusively from Mexican American census tracts in San Antonio, Texas [1].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, begun in 1991, that recruited low-income Mexican Americans aged 40 to 60, selected at random without regard to disease from Mexican American census tracts, together with their extended families, and followed them with repeated examinations to study the genetic and environmental contributions to cardiovascular disease risk factors. With the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4145406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These family data were obtained from two studies: the San Antonio Family Heart Study (SAFHS) and the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study (SAFDGS), which are together referred to as the San Antonio Family Studies (SAFS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, begun in 1991, that recruited low-income Mexican Americans aged 40 to 60, selected at random without regard to disease from Mexican American census tracts, together with their extended families, and followed them with repeated examinations to study the genetic and environmental contributions to cardiovascular disease risk factors. With the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8901667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among Mexican Americans from San Antonio (Tex), we quantified the relative contributions of both genetic and environmental influences to a large panel of cardiovascular risk factors, including serum levels of lipids, lipoproteins, glucose, hormones, adiposity, and blood pressure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, begun in 1991, that recruited low-income Mexican Americans aged 40 to 60, selected at random without regard to disease from Mexican American census tracts, together with their extended families, and followed them with repeated examinations to study the genetic and environmental contributions to cardiovascular disease risk factors. With the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25519314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8901667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8901667+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Members of 42 extended families were studied, including 1236 first-, second-, and third-degree relatives of randomly ascertained probands and their spouses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002337> "A family study of Mexican Americans in San Antonio, Texas, begun in 1991, that recruited low-income Mexican Americans aged 40 to 60, selected at random without regard to disease from Mexican American census tracts, together with their extended families, and followed them with repeated examinations to study the genetic and environmental contributions to cardiovascular disease risk factors. With the San Antonio Family Diabetes/Gallbladder Study it makes up the San Antonio Family Studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=19416140&retmode=xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SAGE study captures the complete longitudinal healthcare records of children born in 1995 and contains detailed information on early-life exposures, such as antibiotic utilization and immunization, in relationship to the development of asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19416140") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=19416140&retmode=xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "to genotype children for genes likely associated with the development of asthma and to study the epigenetic regulation of pre-established protective vs allergic immune responses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All children in the asthma and allergy stratawere invited to participate in thecase‐control study, as were a random sample (n=200) from the strata of children with neither condition.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2002, a one‐page survey was mailed to families to enquire about their health and home environment exposure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Parents were asked for permission to be contacted for further study and to link the survey data to their child’s health care database records.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29273806") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Study of Asthma Genes and Environment Study (SAGE5 ) is a population‐based sample of 16,320 children, born in the province of Manitoba, Canada in the year of 1995.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002338> "A population-based cohort of children born in the province of Manitoba, Canada, in 1995, whose families were surveyed in 2002 about the child's health and home environment, with linkage to the child's health care records, and from which children with asthma or allergy and a random sample of children with neither were invited to a nested case-control study of the early-life genetic and environmental origins of asthma. It is one of the Canadian cohorts of the ALLERGEN consortium.")

