# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this ongoing cohort study we investigate individuals with SCD, without major psychiatric of neurological disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants undergo extensive assessment, including cerebrospinal fluid collection and optional amyloid positron emission tomography scan, with annual follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SCIENCe inclusion started in June 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Strengths of the study include the highly standardized assessment of a broad range of factors potentially related to SCD, including various biomarkers, as well as repeated collection of blood and CSF for biobanking to be able to evaluate biomarkers longitudinally.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Subjective Cognitive Impairment Cohort (SCIENCe) is a prospective cohort study including consecutive patients with SCD presenting at the Alzheimer Center of the VU University Medical Center Amsterdam.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30081935") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6080529/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They receive standardized dementia screening at the memory clinic, including an interview with a neurologist, physical and neurological examination, neuropsychological assessment, as well as routine analyses of blood, CSF, and brain magnetic resonance imaging (MRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002351> "A prospective cohort study, with inclusion from June 2014, of consecutive patients with subjective cognitive decline, without major psychiatric or neurological disorders, who presented at the memory clinic of the Alzheimer Center of VU University Medical Center Amsterdam, the Netherlands. After the clinic's standardised dementia screening they are followed annually, with repeated blood and cerebrospinal fluid collection for biobanking and optional amyloid PET, to study clinical progression and the factors contributing to subjective cognitive decline.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18483556") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2367449/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NHS was established in 1976, when 121,700 female U.S. registered nurses between the ages of 30 and 55, residing in 11 larger U.S. states, completed and returned the initial self-administered questionnaire on their medical histories and baseline health-related exposures, forming the basis for the NHS cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2699349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A common control series was randomly selected from participants who gave a blood sample and were free of diagnosed skin cancer up to and including the questionnaire cycle during which the case was diagnosed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2699349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases in this study consisted of women with incident skin cancer from the subcohort of the NHS who gave a blood specimen in 1989–1990 (n = 32,826), including SCC and BCC cases with a diagnosis any time after blood collection up to June 1, 1998 and melanoma cases up to June 1, 2000 with no previously diagnosed skin cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2699349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the skin cancer nested case-control study, natural skin color and other sun exposure-related information were collected by the retrospective supplementary questionnaire in 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2699349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One or two controls were matched to each case by year of birth (± 1 year).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16943234") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19500394") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2699349/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The nested case-control study consisted of 218 incident melanoma cases, 285 incident SCC cases, a sample of 300 BCC cases from the large number of incident cases, and 870 age-matched controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002352> "A case-control study of skin cancer nested within the Nurses' Health Study in the United States, in which women of the cohort's blood subcohort (blood given in 1989-1990) with incident melanoma, squamous cell carcinoma or basal cell carcinoma diagnosed after blood collection, and no earlier skin cancer, were compared with a common series of controls randomly selected from blood donors free of diagnosed skin cancer and matched by year of birth, with pigmentation and sun exposure information collected by a retrospective supplementary questionnaire.")

