AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15623754") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15623754+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To determine the incidence and progression rates of myopia in young Singaporean children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16234459+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Yearly eye examinations involving biometry measures were performed in the schools.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7726587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children 7 to 9 years of age were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7726587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cycloplegic autorefraction was performed at every visit.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7726587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SCORM study was initiated in three schools in Singapore from 1999 to 2001.11,23,24 The methodology has been described previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7726587/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this study was to investigate the association between 1-year myopia progression and subsequent 2-year myopia progression amongst myopic children in the Singapore Cohort Study of the Risk Factors for Myopia (SCORM).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234459") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33344056") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8322707/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SCORM is a prospective cohort whereby children from grades 1 to 3 were recruited from 3 Singapore schools in 1999 and 2001 (n = 1979), and has been described previously.19–21") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002354> "A school-based cohort study of myopia in Singapore children, begun in three Singapore schools in 1999–2001, which recruited children aged 7 to 9 years and examined them yearly in their schools, with cycloplegic autorefraction and ocular biometry, to study the risk factors for the onset and progression of myopia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases diagnosed with primary invasive prostate cancer between October 1999 and September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry (SCCCR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were randomly sampled from the 1999 Health Care Financing Administration (HCFA) Medicare beneficiary file.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were frequency matched to cases on age (five-year age groups), race (Caucasian, African-American), and geographical region (western, middle and eastern third of the state).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases were South Carolina residents, aged 65–79, whose prostate cancer was histologically confirmed, and whose physicians had given permission for research staff to contact their patient.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The questionnaire collected information on demographic characteristics, socioeconomic status, stress, coping, alcohol and tobacco use, physical activity, diet, medical history, family history of cancer, history of sexually transmitted infections, and farm-related work activities and exposures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15150583") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16912087") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29117387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15280622") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5521001/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Trained interviewers from the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory conducted computer-assisted telephone interviews with subjects who provided consent with the understanding that written consent would be obtained.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002355> "A population-based case-control study of prostate cancer in older African American and white men in South Carolina, United States, funded by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Men aged 65–79 with incident, histologically confirmed prostate cancer diagnosed from October 1999 to September 2001 were identified through the South Carolina Central Cancer Registry, and controls of the same ages, frequency-matched on age, race and region, were sampled from the Medicare beneficiary file; both were interviewed by telephone by the University of South Carolina Survey Research Laboratory about lifestyle, diet, medical and family history and farm work.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls for the discovery phase were 1,710 non-diabetic female controls from the SBCS (for further details, see Text S1, online).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA samples were genotyped using the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 590,887 SNPs genotyped in 1,019 T2D cases and 1,710 controls selected from Chinese women in Shanghai, we selected the top 2,100 SNPs that were not in linkage disequilibrium (r2<0.2) with known T2D loci for in silico replication in three T2D GWAS conducted among European Americans, Koreans, and Singapore Chinese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2940731/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The discovery stage included 1,019 T2D cases, 886 incident T2D cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study (SWHS), an ongoing, population-based, prospective cohort study of women living in Shanghai, and 133 prevalent T2D cases identified among controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), who were recruited in Shanghai during approximately the same period as the SWHS [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 1710 controls used in this GWAS were shared with a GWAS of breast cancer that was recently completed and was based primarily based on the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22158264") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23406970") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3779367/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 6,922 women (aged 25–70 years) with both anthropometrics and genomic DNA samples who participated in three ongoing, GWA studies: 1) the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study (SBCGS), 2) the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Genetics Study (SECGS), and 3) the Shanghai Diabetes Genetics Study (SDGS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002356> "A genome-wide association study of type 2 diabetes in Chinese women in Shanghai, contributed by Vanderbilt University and the Shanghai Cancer Institute, whose cases were incident type 2 diabetes cases from the Shanghai Women's Health Study and prevalent cases found among the controls of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, and whose controls were women from the general population free of cancer and diabetes, shared with the Shanghai Breast Cancer Genetics Study. Genotyped on the Affymetrix Genome-Wide Human SNP Array 6.0, it has also been pooled with the Shanghai breast and endometrial cancer genetics studies for genetic analyses of other traits in women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16284367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3750988/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BE patients were prospectively identified from the private and public pathology laboratories servicing metropolitan Brisbane.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> "A population-based case-control study of Barrett's oesophagus and reflux-related conditions in Brisbane, Australia, whose cases were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18 to 79 with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of Barrett's oesophagus, with or without dysplasia, between February 2003 and June 2006, identified through the pathology laboratories serving the city, and whose controls were people randomly selected from the Australian electoral roll and matched to the cases by age and sex, together with endoscopy patients whose biopsies showed only oesophageal inflammation consistent with reflux and no Barrett's oesophagus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16284367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3750988/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, eligible cases for the Study of Digestive Health were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18–79 years with a new (incident) histologically confirmed diagnosis of BE (for nondysplastic BE cases) or dysplasia (for dysplastic BE cases) between 1 February 2003 and 30 June 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> "A population-based case-control study of Barrett's oesophagus and reflux-related conditions in Brisbane, Australia, whose cases were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18 to 79 with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of Barrett's oesophagus, with or without dysplasia, between February 2003 and June 2006, identified through the pathology laboratories serving the city, and whose controls were people randomly selected from the Australian electoral roll and matched to the cases by age and sex, together with endoscopy patients whose biopsies showed only oesophageal inflammation consistent with reflux and no Barrett's oesophagus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16284367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3750988/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To derive the prediction model, we used data from participants in the Study of Digestive Health, a population-based study of BE and reflux-related conditions conducted in Brisbane, Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> "A population-based case-control study of Barrett's oesophagus and reflux-related conditions in Brisbane, Australia, whose cases were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18 to 79 with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of Barrett's oesophagus, with or without dysplasia, between February 2003 and June 2006, identified through the pathology laboratories serving the city, and whose controls were people randomly selected from the Australian electoral roll and matched to the cases by age and sex, together with endoscopy patients whose biopsies showed only oesophageal inflammation consistent with reflux and no Barrett's oesophagus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16284367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3750988/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two separate control groups were recruited for the Study of Digestive Health: ‘inflammation controls’ (i.e., patients who underwent endoscopy but for whom the histology report identified only esophageal inflammatory changes consistent with GER and no other pathological or macroscopic changes including no evidence of BE), and population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> "A population-based case-control study of Barrett's oesophagus and reflux-related conditions in Brisbane, Australia, whose cases were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18 to 79 with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of Barrett's oesophagus, with or without dysplasia, between February 2003 and June 2006, identified through the pathology laboratories serving the city, and whose controls were people randomly selected from the Australian electoral roll and matched to the cases by age and sex, together with endoscopy patients whose biopsies showed only oesophageal inflammation consistent with reflux and no Barrett's oesophagus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16284367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22787114") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26090820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4474428/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected from the same geographical regions from the Australian Electoral Roll (enrolment is compulsory by law in Australia) and matched for sex and age (in 5-year categories) of the cases with Barrett’s esophagus.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002357> "A population-based case-control study of Barrett's oesophagus and reflux-related conditions in Brisbane, Australia, whose cases were residents of metropolitan Brisbane aged 18 to 79 with a new histologically confirmed diagnosis of Barrett's oesophagus, with or without dysplasia, between February 2003 and June 2006, identified through the pathology laboratories serving the city, and whose controls were people randomly selected from the Australian electoral roll and matched to the cases by age and sex, together with endoscopy patients whose biopsies showed only oesophageal inflammation consistent with reflux and no Barrett's oesophagus.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-009-1594-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In stage 1, we recruited 1,892 unrelated type 2 diabetic patients from the inpatient database of Shanghai Diabetes Institute and 1,808 unrelated controls who had been recruited from the general population by the Shanghai Diabetes Studies [25, 26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-009-1594-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Upon approval by our institutional review board, we recruited 6,771 case–control participants of Han Chinese ancestry in Shanghai using a two-stage approach for this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3198055/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In stage 1, we recruited 1,276 type 2 diabetic patients from the Shanghai Diabetes Institute Inpatient Database of Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People’s Hospital (10,11) and examined them for diabetic retinopathy and nephropathy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function, and diabetic complications were collected8-10 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current study included 5,950 patients of type 1 diabetes, T2D or some genetic syndromes related to diabetes (e.g., Parder Willi, Rabson Manderhall).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19937226") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21911749") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22961080") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1019/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1019_MOESM23_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People’s Hospital beginning in 2001.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002358> "The inpatient database of the Shanghai Diabetes Institute at Shanghai Jiao Tong University Affiliated Sixth People's Hospital, Shanghai, China: Han Chinese inpatients of the hospital's Department of Endocrinology and Metabolism, recruited from 2001, with type 2 diabetes, type 1 diabetes or genetic syndromes related to diabetes, for whom detailed phenotypes of glucose and lipid metabolism, blood pressure, liver and kidney function and diabetic complications were collected. Its type 2 diabetes patients have served as cases, with controls from the community-based Shanghai Diabetes Studies, in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and its complications.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12406920+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Aiming at primary prevention of the disease, the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Program (SDPP) was developed as a joint program between the Departments of Endocrinology, Social Medicine and Epidemiology at the Karolinska Institute.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9363331/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A health examination, including anthropometric and blood pressure measurements and an oral glucose tolerance test (OGTT), as well as a questionnaire on lifestyle factors and a food frequency questionnaire (FFQ) were carried out at baseline and both follow-up occasions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9363331/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By design, the cohort was enriched by 50% with subjects that had family history of diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9363331/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, men and women of appropriate age, residing in the selected study areas, participated in a baseline survey during 1992–1994 for men and 1996–1998 for women (Supplementary Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9363331/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants of the baseline survey were invited to a first follow-up after 8–10 years, in 2002–2004 for men and in 2004–2006 for women, and to a second follow-up in 2014–2017 (9–15 years after the first follow-up).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12406920") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35435501") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9363331/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study is part of the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Program (SDPP), a prospective cohort study that comprised men and women 35–56 years old at baseline, without previously diagnosed diabetes, from five municipalities in Stockholm County.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002360> "A population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 35–56 without previously diagnosed diabetes from five municipalities of Stockholm County, Sweden, surveyed at baseline in 1992–1994 (men) and 1996–1998 (women) with the sample enriched to about half with a family history of diabetes, and re-examined after 8–10 years and again in 2014–2017 with health examinations, oral glucose tolerance tests and questionnaires, set up at the Karolinska Institute to study the determinants of prediabetes and type 2 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2988223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After randomisation between September 1998, and October 2001, participants were to be seen in study clinics at 2, 4, 8, and 12 months and then 6-monthly until final follow-up visits between October 2007, and June 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> "A randomised trial cohort of men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction, recruited from 1998 through special clinics at 88 UK hospitals and coordinated by the Clinical Trial Service Unit in Oxford, which compared 80 mg with 20 mg simvastatin daily and, in a two-by-two factorial design, folic acid plus vitamin B12 with placebo, and whose participants also served for the identification of an SLCO1B1 variant associated with simvastatin-induced myopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2988223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Compliant individuals who did not have a serious problem during the run-in, and agreed to participate, were randomly allocated to receive either 80 mg or 20 mg simvastatin daily with a double-dummy approach to mask the treatment allocation (and separately, in a two-by-two factorial design, 2 mg folic acid plus 1 mg vitamin B12 daily or matching placebo).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> "A randomised trial cohort of men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction, recruited from 1998 through special clinics at 88 UK hospitals and coordinated by the Clinical Trial Service Unit in Oxford, which compared 80 mg with 20 mg simvastatin daily and, in a two-by-two factorial design, folic acid plus vitamin B12 with placebo, and whose participants also served for the identification of an SLCO1B1 variant associated with simvastatin-induced myopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2988223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Medical collaborators from 88 UK hospitals appointed senior nurses to run special clinics for the study (see Acknowledgments).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> "A randomised trial cohort of men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction, recruited from 1998 through special clinics at 88 UK hospitals and coordinated by the Clinical Trial Service Unit in Oxford, which compared 80 mg with 20 mg simvastatin daily and, in a two-by-two factorial design, folic acid plus vitamin B12 with placebo, and whose participants also served for the identification of an SLCO1B1 variant associated with simvastatin-induced myopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2988223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SEARCH allowed the identification of a common variant (estimated population prevalence of 0·15) in the SLCO1B1 gene that was associated with a particularly high risk of myopathy.12") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> "A randomised trial cohort of men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction, recruited from 1998 through special clinics at 88 UK hospitals and coordinated by the Clinical Trial Service Unit in Oxford, which compared 80 mg with 20 mg simvastatin daily and, in a two-by-two factorial design, folic acid plus vitamin B12 with placebo, and whose participants also served for the identification of an SLCO1B1 variant associated with simvastatin-induced myopathy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21067805") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2988223/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We undertook a double-blind randomised trial in 12 064 men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002361> "A randomised trial cohort of men and women aged 18–80 years with a history of myocardial infarction, recruited from 1998 through special clinics at 88 UK hospitals and coordinated by the Clinical Trial Service Unit in Oxford, which compared 80 mg with 20 mg simvastatin daily and, in a two-by-two factorial design, folic acid plus vitamin B12 with placebo, and whose participants also served for the identification of an SLCO1B1 variant associated with simvastatin-induced myopathy.")

