# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1454 eligible endometrial cancer patients were identified during the study period, of which 1204 patients (82.8%) completed in-person interviews.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cancer patients were identified through the population-based Shanghai Cancer Registry that has virtually complete ascertainment of all incident cases diagnosed among residents of urban Shanghai [1,7].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were randomly selected from the general population in Shanghai using the Shanghai Resident Registry, a population registry containing demographic information for all residents of urban Shanghai and matched to cases according to the age distribution of endometrial cancer cases in 1996.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, this study consisted of 1204 incident endometrial cancer cases diagnosed between 30 and 69 years of age and 1212 age frequency-matched community controls recruited from 1997 to 2003.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of those who completed the in-person interviews, 860 cases and 861 controls donated a blood sample and 285 cases and 281 controls provided a buccal cell sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17315164") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.318/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng318_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17301695") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2238679/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study is a population-based case–control study conducted among Chinese women in Shanghai.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002365> "A population-based case-control study of endometrial cancer among Chinese women in urban Shanghai, China, conducted from 1997 to 2003, in which women aged 30-69 with newly diagnosed endometrial cancer, identified through the Shanghai Cancer Registry, and age frequency-matched controls randomly selected from the general population through the Shanghai Resident Registry were interviewed in person and gave blood or buccal cell samples, to study risk factors for endometrial cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC4260321") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We did find a suggestive association with rs1837253 on chromosome 5, situated within the TSLP gene, among patients with severe asthma in the SEVERE study (P = 3×10−6; odds ratio, 0.56), but this association was not replicated among patients with severe asthma in the AUGOSA (Asthma UK Genetics of Severe Asthma) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> "A collection of children and adults with severe or refractory asthma recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics in England, the adult and paediatric clinics of the Royal Brompton Hospital, London, and the adult clinic of the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester, where they were characterised under the clinics' severe asthma protocols, assembled as the severe asthma group of the GABRIEL consortium's genome-wide association study of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GABRIEL Severe asthma study SEVERE European United Kingdom Case-control study 290 974") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> "A collection of children and adults with severe or refractory asthma recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics in England, the adult and paediatric clinics of the Royal Brompton Hospital, London, and the adult clinic of the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester, where they were characterised under the clinics' severe asthma protocols, assembled as the severe asthma group of the GABRIEL consortium's genome-wide association study of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients attending the Glenfield Hospital clinics had full characterisation and were deemed to have severe/refractory asthma according to a specialised protocol involving parameters of airway inflammation, airway physiology, as well as quality of life and control of symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> "A collection of children and adults with severe or refractory asthma recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics in England, the adult and paediatric clinics of the Royal Brompton Hospital, London, and the adult clinic of the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester, where they were characterised under the clinics' severe asthma protocols, assembled as the severe asthma group of the GABRIEL consortium's genome-wide association study of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SEVERE: Severe/refractory cases of asthma were recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics; adult and childhood clinics based at the Royal Brompton Hospital, London and an adult clinic at the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> "A collection of children and adults with severe or refractory asthma recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics in England, the adult and paediatric clinics of the Royal Brompton Hospital, London, and the adult clinic of the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester, where they were characterised under the clinics' severe asthma protocols, assembled as the severe asthma group of the GABRIEL consortium's genome-wide association study of asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20860503") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-017-0014-7/MediaObjects/41588_2017_14_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those attending Royal Brompton Hospital adult clinics were also fully characterised, with severe asthma defined according to the ATS and ERS definition of severe asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002366> "A collection of children and adults with severe or refractory asthma recruited through three specialist severe asthma clinics in England, the adult and paediatric clinics of the Royal Brompton Hospital, London, and the adult clinic of the Glenfield Hospital, Leicester, where they were characterised under the clinics' severe asthma protocols, assembled as the severe asthma group of the GABRIEL consortium's genome-wide association study of asthma.")

