AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age and gender-matched population-based controls were ascertained from two population lists—controls under age 65 years were recruited through driver’s license lists; controls 65-74 years were selected from Health Care Finance Administration files.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng2089/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng2089_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Epidemiology/family history questionnaires (same as for the OFCCR and NFCCR) were completed on all respondents over the telephone using a CATI format.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2739726/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Seattle Familial Colorectal Cancer Registry identified incident population-based CRC cases aged 20–74 in 3 Washington state counties through the Puget Sound SEER program; controls were recruited through drivers license lists (age, <65 y) and through health care finance files (age, 65–74 y).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4890809/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Seattle CCFR is a population-based registry that includes primary invasive colorectal cancer cases diagnosed through Puget Sound Region Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) cancer registry, and their first degree relatives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12891059/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the SCCFR, we enrolled study participants who were diagnosed with incident invasive CRC between 1998 and 2007 while residing in western Washington State; in Phase I (1998–2002), we enrolled those who were diagnosed at ages 20–74 years while residing in a three county region") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17618283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19245865") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27253385") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12349377/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Seattle Colon Cancer Family Registry (SCCFR) is a population-based case–control study in Washington State, one of seven centers forming the Colon Cancer Family Registry (www.coloncfr.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002367> "A population-based colorectal cancer family registry in western Washington State, United States, one of the sites of the Colon Cancer Family Registry, which enrolled people aged 20 to 74 with incident colorectal cancer in three Washington State counties, identified through the Puget Sound SEER cancer registry, together with their first-degree relatives, and age- and sex-matched population controls recruited from driver's licence lists (under 65) and health care finance files (65 to 74), all of whom completed epidemiology and family-history questionnaires by telephone.")

