# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility is assessed with the following criteria: (1) a diagnosis of breast carcinoma in situ or invasive breast cancer; (2) citizens or permanent residents of Singapore; and (3) aged 21 years and above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment started at National University Hospital (NUH, a tertiary academic hospital) in April 2010. Subsequently, recruitment sites extended to five other tertiary hospitals,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SGBCC was first established as a cohort with both retrospective and prospective components.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Self-reported data on sociodemographic and lifestyle, reproductive risk factors, medical history and family history of breast or ovarian cancer is collected using a structured questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Singapore Breast Cancer Cohort (SGBCC), an ongoing multi-ethnic cohort established with the overarching goal to identify genetic markers for breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response, as well as to understand the ethnic differences in disease risk and outcome in an Asian setting.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33901219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8075208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Vital status and cause of death are obtained via linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths in accordance to the audit cycle at each hospital [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002369> "An ongoing multi-ethnic cohort of breast cancer patients aged 21 years and over who are citizens or permanent residents of Singapore, recruited from April 2010 at the National University Hospital and later at five other public tertiary hospitals in Singapore, with retrospective and prospective components, questionnaire, medical record and biospecimen data and follow-up through linkage with the Registry of Births and Deaths, established to identify genetic markers of breast cancer risk, prognosis and treatment response and to study ethnic differences in breast cancer risk and outcome in Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9674971+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Also, the allele frequencies of 73% of the marker loci differed significantly (P < .01) between individuals of European and African ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9674971+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Millennium Schizophrenia Consortium has completed a genome-wide scan to detect susceptibility loci for schizophrenia in 244 individuals from the nuclear families of 92 independent pairs of schizophrenic sibs ascertained by the NIMH Genetics Initiative.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9674971+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NIMH Genetics Initiative on Schizophrenia, a multisite collaborative study, was established as a national resource with a centralized clinical data base and cell repository.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9674973+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The schizophrenia families were collected by three sites: Washington University, Harvard University, and Columbia University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fnature08192/MediaObjects/41586_2009_BFnature08192_MOESM270_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly: SGI subjects (2.4%) were recruited by three research groups in the United States (see Acknowledgments) in a study designed to collect families with affected sibling pairs (and other affected members when available), ascertaining through probands with schizophrenia recruited through clinical settings.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23936182") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674971") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9674973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000167.v1.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases met criteria for schizophrenia (SCZ) or schizoaffective disorder (SA) per the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders version IV (DSM-IV) for all three collections (SGI, MGS1, and MGS2) comprising these cases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002370> "A family collection of the US National Institute of Mental Health Genetics Initiative, a multisite study set up as a national resource with a centralised clinical database and cell repository, in which Washington University, Harvard University and Columbia University ascertained, from 1991 to 1997, nuclear families of European and African ancestry with siblings affected by schizophrenia or schizoaffective disorder, for genetic linkage and association studies of schizophrenia; its cases later formed one of the three collections of the Molecular Genetics of Schizophrenia genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GWAS genotyping was performed at the Vanderbilt Microarray Shared Resource (VMSR) and Affymetrix Research Services Laboratory (ARSL) using the Affymetrix Genome- Wide Human SNP Array 6.0 (Affy6.0) platform, following Affymetrix’s protocols.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shanghai genome-wide association studies include participants of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (SECS), Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3288728/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Shanghai Genome Wide Associations Studies (SGWAS) would like to thank the dedicated investigators and staff members from the research teams at Vanderbilt University, the Shanghai Cancer Institute, and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, and most of all, the study participants for their contributions to the studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4168820/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participating studies (grant support) in the Shanghai Genome-Wide Association Studies (SGWAS) are as follows: Shanghai Women's Health Study (R37CA070867 to W.Z.), Shanghai Men′s Health Study (R01CA082729 to X.-O.S.), Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (R01CA064277 to X.-O.S.) and Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study (R01CA092585 to X.-O.S.).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4168820/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To evaluate the possible modifying effect of alcohol consumption on the association between ALDH2 and BMI, we analyzed the association of BMI with rs671 by gender and alcohol consumption status (drinkers versus. non-drinkers) using data from the two studies (SGWAS for Chinese and KCPS-II for Koreans) for which we had direct access to individual data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24861553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27931260") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5146840/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "5152 Chinese women (2867 cases and 2285 controls) from the Shanghai Genome-Wide Association Studies (SGWAS) who were participants in the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study (SBCS), the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study (SBCSS), and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002373> "A collection of the genome-wide genotyping of Chinese participants of population-based studies in Shanghai, China, run by Vanderbilt University with the Shanghai Cancer Institute and the Shanghai Institute of Preventive Medicine, that pools the scans of the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, the Shanghai Breast Cancer Survival Study, the Shanghai Endometrial Cancer Study, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study for genetic association studies of breast cancer and other traits such as body mass index.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3390407/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A genome-wide association study (GWAS) of BDR, quantified as percent change in baseline FEV1 after administration of a β2-agonist, was performed with 1,644 non-Hispanic white asthmatic subjects from six drug clinical trials: CAMP, LOCCS, LODO, a medication trial conducted by Sepracor, CARE, and ACRN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> "A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each of the childhood asthma studies has a majority of children participating as part of a parent-child trio.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> "A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) Asthma Resource project (SHARP) is conducting a genome-wide analysis in adults and children who have participated in National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute's clinical research trials on asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> "A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ACRN (adult) studies are probands alone.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> "A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792082") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000166.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This includes 1041 children with asthma who participated in the Childhood Asthma Management Program (CAMP), 994 children who participated in one or five clinical trials conducted by the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, and 701 adults who participated in one of six clinical trials conducted by the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002374> "A genome-wide genotyping project of the NHLBI SNP Health Association Resource (SHARe) that collects children and adults with asthma who took part in NHLBI asthma clinical trials: children of the Childhood Asthma Management Program and of trials of the Childhood Asthma Research and Education (CARE) network, most of them with their parents as parent-child trios, and adults of trials of the Asthma Clinical Research Network (ACRN), for genetic studies of asthma and of response to asthma treatment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2465514") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One control per case was randomly selected at the time of case incidence from the study base after stratification for age, sex and hospital catchment area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> "A population-based case-control study of risk factors for a first myocardial infarction, whose study base was all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years without a previous myocardial infarction living in Stockholm County, Sweden, in 1992–1994: cases were identified through the coronary and intensive care units of the catchment-area hospitals, hospital discharge records and death certificates, controls were drawn at random from the study base matched on age, sex and hospital catchment area, and the patients were followed for recurrent cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2465514") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were identified through a special organisation set up at the coronary and intensive care units of the hospitals in the catchment areas, and from hospital discharge records and death certificates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> "A population-based case-control study of risk factors for a first myocardial infarction, whose study base was all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years without a previous myocardial infarction living in Stockholm County, Sweden, in 1992–1994: cases were identified through the coronary and intensive care units of the catchment-area hospitals, hospital discharge records and death certificates, controls were drawn at random from the study base matched on age, sex and hospital catchment area, and the patients were followed for recurrent cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2465514") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SHEEP study is a population-based case–control study of risk factors for incident myocardial infarction and has been described in detail elsewhere.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> "A population-based case-control study of risk factors for a first myocardial infarction, whose study base was all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years without a previous myocardial infarction living in Stockholm County, Sweden, in 1992–1994: cases were identified through the coronary and intensive care units of the catchment-area hospitals, hospital discharge records and death certificates, controls were drawn at random from the study base matched on age, sex and hospital catchment area, and the patients were followed for recurrent cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2465514") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study base included all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years, with no prior clinically diagnosed myocardial infarction event, living in Stockholm County during 1992–4.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> "A population-based case-control study of risk factors for a first myocardial infarction, whose study base was all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years without a previous myocardial infarction living in Stockholm County, Sweden, in 1992–1994: cases were identified through the coronary and intensive care units of the catchment-area hospitals, hospital discharge records and death certificates, controls were drawn at random from the study base matched on age, sex and hospital catchment area, and the patients were followed for recurrent cardiovascular events and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17108306") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34551078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34551078+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were followed for cardiovascular events and mortality for a median of 14 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002375> "A population-based case-control study of risk factors for a first myocardial infarction, whose study base was all Swedish citizens aged 45–70 years without a previous myocardial infarction living in Stockholm County, Sweden, in 1992–1994: cases were identified through the coronary and intensive care units of the catchment-area hospitals, hospital discharge records and death certificates, controls were drawn at random from the study base matched on age, sex and hospital catchment area, and the patients were followed for recurrent cardiovascular events and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9493915+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Sleep Heart Health Study (SHHS) is a prospective cohort study designed to investigate obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) and other sleep-disordered breathing (SDB) as risk factors for the development of cardiovascular disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9493915+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study is designed to enroll 6,600 adult participants aged 40 years and older who will undergo a home polysomnogram to assess the presence of OSA and other SDB.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During exam cycle 3 (January 2001- June 2003), a second polysomnogram (SHHS-2) was obtained in 3295 of the participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In all, 6441 individuals were enrolled between November 1, 1995 and January 31, 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in SHHS were recruited from nine existing NHLBI epidemiological studies in which data on cardiovascular risk factors had been collected previously.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9493915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://biolincc.nhlbi.nih.gov/studies/shhs/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To determine the cardiovascular and other consequences of sleep-disordered breathing and to test whether sleep-disordered breathing is associated with an increased risk of coronary heart disease, stroke, all-cause mortality and hypertension by examining subjects from well-characterized and established epidemiologic cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002376> "A multicentre prospective cohort study of the US National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute that enrolled adults aged 40 years or older in 1995–1998 from existing epidemiological cohorts (sites of the Atherosclerosis Risk in Communities Study and the Cardiovascular Health Study, the Framingham Offspring Cohort, the Strong Heart Study, the New York Hypertension Cohorts and two Tucson studies) and added an in-home polysomnogram at baseline and again in 2001–2003 to their data, to study obstructive sleep apnoea and other sleep-disordered breathing as risk factors for cardiovascular disease, hypertension and death.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19995197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood, tear, and urine samples were collected for biochemical analyses, and stored for genetic and proteomic studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19995197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Examination procedures included interviews, measurement of blood pressure, anthropometry, presenting and best-corrected visual acuity, subjective refraction, ocular biometry, Goldmann applanation tonometry, slit-lamp biomicroscopy, optic disc imaging and digital photography of the lens and retina, using a standardized protocol.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19995197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From two lists of 12,000 names of each ethnic group provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs, age-stratified random sampling was used to select 6,350 names in each group, with a target sample size of 3,300.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19995197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conjunction with the Singapore Malay Eye Study, the SICC study will permit an in-depth evaluation of the prevalence, risk factors, and impact of major eye diseases in Chinese, Indians and Malays, three distinct Asian ethnic groups, whose combined numbers represent half the world's population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19995197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SICC examined a population-based cross-sectional sample of 3,300 ethnic Indians and 3,300 ethnic Chinese aged 40-80+ years residing in the South-Western part of Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19995197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39051044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23964661") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3852120/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the Singapore Indian Eye Study (SINDI), which is part of the Singapore Indian Chinese Cohort Eye Study (SICC) [42], consists of 2538 Indian subjects aged 40 and above") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002378> "A population-based eye study of ethnic Indian and ethnic Chinese adults aged 40 years and older living in south-western Singapore, sampled by age-stratified random sampling from name lists provided by the Ministry of Home Affairs and examined with standardised interviews, eye examinations and laboratory investigations, with blood, tear and urine samples stored for genetic and proteomic studies, to quantify ethnic differences in the prevalence, risk factors and impact of major eye diseases; its Indian component is the Singapore Indian Eye Study, and together with the Singapore Malay Eye Study it covers Singapore's three main ethnic groups.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "3) diagnosed with hypertension at age >30 years; 4) have a fasting blood glucose level of <7 mmol/L and no family members with a diagnosis of diabetes; and 5) have a BMI <27 kg/m2 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379> "A hospital-based case-control genome-wide association study of hypertension among Han Chinese adults aged 37–84 living in the Shanghai metropolitan area, approved by the ethics committee of Ruijin Hospital. Its cases had hypertension diagnosed after age 30 and at least two family members with hypertension, and its controls were normotensive adults over 40; both groups had a BMI under 27 kg/m2 and cases had no diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls had to meet the following eligibility criteria: 1) normal blood pressure measurement (systolic blood pressure <=120 mmHg and diastolic blood pressure <=80 mmHg); 2) be aged >40 years; and 3) have a BMI <27 kg/m2 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379> "A hospital-based case-control genome-wide association study of hypertension among Han Chinese adults aged 37–84 living in the Shanghai metropolitan area, approved by the ethics committee of Ruijin Hospital. Its cases had hypertension diagnosed after age 30 and at least two family members with hypertension, and its controls were normotensive adults over 40; both groups had a BMI under 27 kg/m2 and cases had no diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study included a total of 446 hypertension cases (224 men/222 women) and 455 controls (230 men, 225 women) aged 37-84 years, which were Chinese Han origin residing in the Shanghai metropolitan area and gave written informed consent to donating blood samples for genetic analysis and related assays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379> "A hospital-based case-control genome-wide association study of hypertension among Han Chinese adults aged 37–84 living in the Shanghai metropolitan area, approved by the ethics committee of Ruijin Hospital. Its cases had hypertension diagnosed after age 30 and at least two family members with hypertension, and its controls were normotensive adults over 40; both groups had a BMI under 27 kg/m2 and cases had no diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22344219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a case-control GWAS investigating the genetic variants associated with hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002379> "A hospital-based case-control genome-wide association study of hypertension among Han Chinese adults aged 37–84 living in the Shanghai metropolitan area, approved by the ethics committee of Ruijin Hospital. Its cases had hypertension diagnosed after age 30 and at least two family members with hypertension, and its controls were normotensive adults over 40; both groups had a BMI under 27 kg/m2 and cases had no diabetes.")
