# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study subjects were ethnic Koreans.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were recruited from the patient pool at the Kyungpook National University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Lung cancer patients were recruited from the patient pool at the Genomic Research Center for Lung and Breast/Ovarian Cancer and the Inha University Medical Center.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SKLCS: South Korea Multi-Center Lung Cancer Study (includes Seoul National University Study; Korean University Medical Center Study; and Kyungpook National University Hospital Study)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SKLCS study of lung cancer in Korea consists of several studies conducted at multiple study centers, which have been previously described6-8 , as follows:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28025329") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The lung cancer patients were recruited from patients at Seoul National University Hospitals in Seoul and Bundang, while the age- and sex-matched controls were participants in the health checkup program of Inha University Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002387> "A South Korean multi-centre lung cancer study that brings together three previously described case-control studies of ethnic Koreans, the Seoul National University study, the Korea University Medical Center study and the Kyungpook National University Hospital study, which recruited lung cancer patients at university hospitals and a lung cancer research centre and controls from hospital health check-up programmes; it takes part in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia as one study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27303699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4863607/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study used samples from the SKOT cohorts, in which 311 (SKOT I) and 184 (SKOT II) Danish children were followed for the first 3 years after birth, with the overall aim of investigating relationships between early diet, growth development, and later disease risks, especially obesity and metabolic syndrome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5493126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In short, based on random selection from the National Danish Civil Registry of infants born in the greater Copenhagen area, 330 children were enrolled in the study between April 2007 and May 2008 at age 8.5 months and examined at 9, 18, and 36 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5493126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were being a singleton infant born at term (≥37 weeks of gestation), with no diseases expected to affect growth or nutritional intake.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6773597") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For SKOT-II, the mothers had participated in the TOP-study [36] (Treatment of Obese Pregnant Woman at Hvidovre Hospital in the Copenhagen area) i.e. they had a pre-pregnancy BMI >30kg/m2, and their infants fulfilled the same inclusion criteria as the SKOT-I cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6773597") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 9 months examination was conducted at the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, University of Copenhagen as described in detail elsewhere [28;29;35].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28666428") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30887376") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29961064") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC6773597") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study sample was drawn from the two prospective observational cohorts; SKOT-I and SKOT-II mainly differing in the pre-pregnancy BMI of the mothers but using similar protocols for data-collection making it possible to combine the cohorts [35].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002388> "An observational cohort of healthy, singleton, term-born young children from the greater Copenhagen area, Denmark, run by the Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports at the University of Copenhagen, which followed them from 9 to 36 months of age: SKOT I enrolled infants selected at random from the Danish Civil Registry in 2007–2008 and examined them at 9, 18 and 36 months, and SKOT II enrolled, under the same protocol, infants of obese mothers from a trial of obese pregnant women at Hvidovre Hospital, to study diet, growth, body composition, development and early determinants of overweight.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797795/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients were all unrelated ethnic Han Chinese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797795/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the same time controls were selected from cancer-free patients with other lung diseases but free of cancer history and symptom. Controls were all non-smoking females and frequency matched to cases on age (± 5 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797795/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, we describe a case-control study of lung adenocarcinoma in non-smoking female population in Shenyang, China") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2797795/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this hospital-based case-control study, the case group consisted of 285 diagnosed nonsmoking female patients (between January 2002 and November 2007) with histologically confirmed lung adenocarcinoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLCS was carried out in the Liaoning Province in Northeast China and has been previously described9 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20003391") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33385923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8378844/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our primary analysis included 1,472 lung adenocarcinoma cases and 1,497 controls from the Genetic Epidemiological Study of Lung Adenocarcinoma (GELAC) (Jou et al., 2009), the Shenyang Lung Cancer Study (SLCS) (Yin et al., 2009), and the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) (Zhang et al., 2007; Zheng et al., 2005).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002389> "A hospital-based case-control study of lung cancer in never-smoking ethnic Chinese women in Shenyang, Liaoning Province, northeast China, whose cases had histologically confirmed lung cancer and whose controls were non-smoking women with other lung diseases but free of cancer, frequency-matched to the cases on age; it is one of the studies pooled in the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")

