AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21874001") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.921/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng921_MOESM16_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21874001") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.921/MediaObjects/41588_2011_BFng921_MOESM16_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SLYDS case sample was augmented with 176 diabetes cases from SLDCS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002390> "A Sri Lankan type 2 diabetes case-control study whose cases came mostly from the Sri Lankan Young Diabetes Study of patients with early-onset diabetes recruited from the three largest hospitals in Sri Lanka, augmented with diabetes cases from the Sri Lankan Diabetes Cardiovascular Study, and whose controls were participants in the Sri Lankan Diabetes Cardiovascular Study, a cross-sectional nationally representative epidemiological investigation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18438839+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because of the unique homogeneous nature of the Gullah, we sought to define the genetic and environmental factors contributing to systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) in this population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18438839+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using data from our ongoing cohort study of lupus in the Gullah population, which we established in 2003, disease characteristics and serologic profiles were summarized for 184 patients with SLE, 144 unaffected first-degree relatives, and 144 matched unrelated, unaffected control subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3535475/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, eligible cases were: 1) age two years and above, 2) self-identified as African American ‘Gullah’ from the Sea Island region of South Carolina, 3) diagnosed with SLE by meeting at least four of the 11 classification criteria as designated by the ACR") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3535475/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This case–control study was nested in a longitudinal observational cohort called SLE in Gullah Health (SLEIGH), which was started in 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8286328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Interdisciplinary research teams from the Medical University of South Carolina (MUSC) developed community‐engaged research projects between the academic researchers and Gullah African Americans residing in rural South Carolina, leading to the formation of SIFP Citizen Advisory Committee") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18438839") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22031537") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30326636") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34008864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8286328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "and the Systemic Lupus Erythematosus in Gullah Health (SLEIGH) Study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002391> "A longitudinal observational cohort study of systemic lupus erythematosus among the Gullah African Americans of the Sea Island region of South Carolina, United States, run from the Medical University of South Carolina, which enrols self-identified Gullah patients with lupus meeting the American College of Rheumatology classification criteria, their relatives, and unrelated unaffected Gullah controls, to study the genetic and environmental factors that contribute to lupus in this population. It is one of the community-engaged Sea Island Families Project studies.")

