AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16931632+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Study of Myocardial Infarctions Leiden (SMILE) that included 560 men younger than age 70 with a first myocardial infarction and 646 control subjects, we investigated the risk of myocardial infarction for levels of factor XI (factor XIc) and factor XII (factor XIIc).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17053057+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We measured plasma ADAMTS13 and VWF antigen levels by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) in a large population-based case-control study (Study of Myocardial Infarctions Leiden [SMILE]), consisting of 560 men with a first myocardial infarction (MI) and 646 control subjects.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2688572") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects were frequency matched on 10-year age groups to the patients and were men without a history of myocardial infarction") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2688572") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, the recruited patients were men who had a first myocardial infarction between January 1990 and January 1996, who were below the age of 70.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2688572/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition we studied the effect of plasma TAFI levels, as determined by a functional assay, and the -438G/A, 505A/G, 1040C/T, and i4 + 164A/C SNP in the TAFI gene on the risk of a first myocardial infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16931632") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17053057") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19377074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28393470") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC9797027/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Study of Myocardial Infarctions Leiden (SMILE), which was a case–control study of men born in the Netherlands, higher FIXc was associated with increased risk of a first MI among men aged < 70 years, with the highest risk being seen among men aged < 55 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002393> "A population-based case-control study from Leiden, the Netherlands, of men born in the Netherlands, comparing men younger than 70 years who had a first myocardial infarction between 1990 and 1996 with control men without a history of myocardial infarction, frequency-matched on 10-year age groups, used to study coagulation and fibrinolytic factors, their genetic variants and cardiovascular risk factors as risk factors for myocardial infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15359994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1972546") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this paper, we describe the actual survival experience of unselected high and intermediate grade non-Hodgkin's lym- phoma (HIG NHL) patients treated with standard UK chemotherapy and radiotherapy protocols by the multicentre Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group (SNLG).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma in Scotland and northern England, collected through the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, a clinical collaborative group that registered lymphoma patients in these regions prospectively on a shared database from 1979; the genetic series comprises the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, a case–control study conducted in 1993–1997, and a local case series collected prospectively in 1992–2008, and its cases were genotyped in European genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15359994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2069849+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1979 and 1987 the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group registered 972 adults with Working Formulation high or intermediate grade non-Hodgkin's lymphoma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma in Scotland and northern England, collected through the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, a clinical collaborative group that registered lymphoma patients in these regions prospectively on a shared database from 1979; the genetic series comprises the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, a case–control study conducted in 1993–1997, and a local case series collected prospectively in 1992–2008, and its cases were genotyped in European genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15359994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A2069849+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinical, pathological and investigational data were recorded prospectively on a computer database allowing analysis for prognostic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma in Scotland and northern England, collected through the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, a clinical collaborative group that registered lymphoma patients in these regions prospectively on a shared database from 1979; the genetic series comprises the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, a case–control study conducted in 1993–1997, and a local case series collected prospectively in 1992–2008, and its cases were genotyped in European genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15359994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC3274508") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome-wide genotyping was performed on cHL case samples from five European-based HL studies: the EPILYMPH Study, the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, the Young Adult Hodgkin’s Disease Case–Control Study, the Scandinavian Lymphoma Etiology Study, and the Northern Dutch Hodgkin Lymphoma Study (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma in Scotland and northern England, collected through the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, a clinical collaborative group that registered lymphoma patients in these regions prospectively on a shared database from 1979; the genetic series comprises the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, a case–control study conducted in 1993–1997, and a local case series collected prospectively in 1992–2008, and its cases were genotyped in European genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15359994") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:2069849") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22286212") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3274508/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group includes the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, which is a case–control study conducted in Scotland and Northern England between January 1993 and July 1997 (6), and the “local case series,” a prospectively collected series of patients within those regions between January 1992 and March 2008 (9).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002394> "A population-based series of patients with Hodgkin lymphoma in Scotland and northern England, collected through the Scotland and Newcastle Lymphoma Group, a clinical collaborative group that registered lymphoma patients in these regions prospectively on a shared database from 1979; the genetic series comprises the Scotland and Newcastle Epidemiological Study of Hodgkin's Disease, a case–control study conducted in 1993–1997, and a local case series collected prospectively in 1992–2008, and its cases were genotyped in European genome-wide association studies of classical Hodgkin lymphoma.")

