# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33846372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA methylation information was profiled with the Illumina’s Infinium MethylationEPIC BeadChip (Illumina catalog number WG-317-1003), after sample normalization to 500 ng and bisulfite conversion with EZ-96 DNA Methylation Kit, as recommended by the manufacturer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33846372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA was normalized to 200–400 ng and genotyped with Illumina’s Infinium GSA-24.v3.0 BeadChip (Illumina catalog number 20030771), following manufacturer’s recommendations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
