AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33846372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genotypes summary statistics can be accessed through COVID-19 Host Genetic Initiative web page (https://www.covid19hg.org/), included in the project “Determining the Molecular Pathways and Genetic Predisposition of the Acute Inflammatory Process Caused by SARS-CoV-2 (SPGRX)”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33846372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole blood samples from SARS-CoV-2 RT-PCR negative (101) and positive lab tested individuals (473) were obtained from two clinical centers (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid, discovery cohort and Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga, replication cohort).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33846372") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35933486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9357033/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole blood was sampled upon arrival to the emergency ward, within a week after first symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002404> "A Spanish study of the molecular pathways and genetic predisposition behind the acute inflammatory response to SARS-CoV-2, run from the GENYO Centre for Genomics and Oncological Research in Granada, whose participants, patients with laboratory-confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection whose blood was sampled on arrival at the emergency ward of the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Valladolid (from March 2020) or the Hospital Regional Universitario de Málaga (from August 2020), together with SARS-CoV-2 PCR-negative individuals, were genotyped on the Illumina Infinium Global Screening Array and profiled for whole-blood DNA methylation; it contributed to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20446946") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22931315") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20446946") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20446946+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SPS3 is an ongoing Phase III multicentre secondary prevention trial focused on preventing recurrent stroke in patients with small vessel ischaemic stroke, or lacunes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406> "A randomised, multicentre phase III secondary-prevention trial in patients with recent, MRI-confirmed symptomatic lacunar (small subcortical) stroke, recruited between 2003 and 2011 at clinical centres in North America, Latin America and Spain, which tested in a two-by-two factorial design aspirin plus clopidogrel against aspirin alone and a lower against a higher systolic blood-pressure target for preventing recurrent stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20446946") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22931315") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23726159+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients were recruited between March, 2003, and April, 2011, and randomly assigned, according to a two-by-two multifactorial design, to a systolic-blood-pressure target of 130-149 mm Hg or less than 130 mm Hg.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406> "A randomised, multicentre phase III secondary-prevention trial in patients with recent, MRI-confirmed symptomatic lacunar (small subcortical) stroke, recruited between 2003 and 2011 at clinical centres in North America, Latin America and Spain, which tested in a two-by-two factorial design aspirin plus clopidogrel against aspirin alone and a lower against a higher systolic blood-pressure target for preventing recurrent stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20446946") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22931315") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3979302/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, SPS3 was a randomized, multicenter clinical trial conducted in 81 clinical centers in North America, Latin America, and Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406> "A randomised, multicentre phase III secondary-prevention trial in patients with recent, MRI-confirmed symptomatic lacunar (small subcortical) stroke, recruited between 2003 and 2011 at clinical centres in North America, Latin America and Spain, which tested in a two-by-two factorial design aspirin plus clopidogrel against aspirin alone and a lower against a higher systolic blood-pressure target for preventing recurrent stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20446946") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22931315") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23726159") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3979302/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SPS3 trial tested two randomized interventions in a 2-by-2 factorial design in patients with recent symptomatic MRI-confirmed lacunar stroke: clopidogrel and aspirin vs. aspirin alone and two target levels of systolic BP.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002406> "A randomised, multicentre phase III secondary-prevention trial in patients with recent, MRI-confirmed symptomatic lacunar (small subcortical) stroke, recruited between 2003 and 2011 at clinical centres in North America, Latin America and Spain, which tested in a two-by-two factorial design aspirin plus clopidogrel against aspirin alone and a lower against a higher systolic blood-pressure target for preventing recurrent stroke.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17925548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3650102/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15547181+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After a median follow-up of 23 months, both groups had similar progression-free survival (medians of 15.0 months for docetaxel-carboplatin and 14.8 months for paclitaxel-carboplatin; hazard ratio [HR] docetaxel-paclitaxel = 0.97, 95% confidence interval [CI] = 0.83 to 1.13; P = .707), overall survival rates at 2 years (64.2% and 68.9%, respectively;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408> "An international multicentre phase III randomised trial (SCOTROC1) of first-line docetaxel-carboplatin versus paclitaxel-carboplatin chemotherapy for stage Ic–IV epithelial ovarian or primary peritoneal cancer, coordinated through a clinical trials unit in Glasgow and recruiting patients in the United Kingdom, elsewhere in Europe, the United States and Australasia, whose patients were followed for progression-free and overall survival and whose DNA has been used in pharmacogenetic studies and in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's studies of ovarian cancer outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17925548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3650102/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15547181+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We compared the combination of docetaxel-carboplatin with the combination of paclitaxel-carboplatin as first-line chemotherapy for stage Ic-IV epithelial ovarian or primary peritoneal cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408> "An international multicentre phase III randomised trial (SCOTROC1) of first-line docetaxel-carboplatin versus paclitaxel-carboplatin chemotherapy for stage Ic–IV epithelial ovarian or primary peritoneal cancer, coordinated through a clinical trials unit in Glasgow and recruiting patients in the United Kingdom, elsewhere in Europe, the United States and Australasia, whose patients were followed for progression-free and overall survival and whose DNA has been used in pharmacogenetic studies and in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's studies of ovarian cancer outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17925548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3650102/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16314640+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One thousand seventy-seven patients were recruited (UK, n = 689; Europe, United States, and Australasia, n = 388).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408> "An international multicentre phase III randomised trial (SCOTROC1) of first-line docetaxel-carboplatin versus paclitaxel-carboplatin chemotherapy for stage Ic–IV epithelial ovarian or primary peritoneal cancer, coordinated through a clinical trials unit in Glasgow and recruiting patients in the United Kingdom, elsewhere in Europe, the United States and Australasia, whose patients were followed for progression-free and overall survival and whose DNA has been used in pharmacogenetic studies and in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's studies of ovarian cancer outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15547181") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17925548") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3650102/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16314640") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16314640+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We explored this within the context of a large, international, prospective, randomized trial of first-line chemotherapy in advanced ovarian cancer (docetaxel-carboplatin v paclitaxel-carboplatin; SCOTROC-1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002408> "An international multicentre phase III randomised trial (SCOTROC1) of first-line docetaxel-carboplatin versus paclitaxel-carboplatin chemotherapy for stage Ic–IV epithelial ovarian or primary peritoneal cancer, coordinated through a clinical trials unit in Glasgow and recruiting patients in the United Kingdom, elsewhere in Europe, the United States and Australasia, whose patients were followed for progression-free and overall survival and whose DNA has been used in pharmacogenetic studies and in the Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium's studies of ovarian cancer outcome.")
