# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22784820+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the South Stockholm Ischemic Stroke Study, 928 ICVD patients and 602 controls were genotyped for 100 different gene polymorphisms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409> "A case-control study of ischaemic cerebrovascular disease in southern Stockholm, Sweden, whose stroke patients underwent clinical investigation and standardised blood tests and whose patients and controls were genotyped for 100 polymorphisms in 47 candidate susceptibility genes to study the genetic profile of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22784820+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we examined the conventional risk factors and the distribution of 100 polymorphisms in 47 suspected susceptibility genes for ICVD in stroke patients with or without a PFO.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409> "A case-control study of ischaemic cerebrovascular disease in southern Stockholm, Sweden, whose stroke patients underwent clinical investigation and standardised blood tests and whose patients and controls were genotyped for 100 polymorphisms in 47 candidate susceptibility genes to study the genetic profile of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22784820+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The stroke patients also underwent relevant investigation and standardized blood tests.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409> "A case-control study of ischaemic cerebrovascular disease in southern Stockholm, Sweden, whose stroke patients underwent clinical investigation and standardised blood tests and whose patients and controls were genotyped for 100 polymorphisms in 47 candidate susceptibility genes to study the genetic profile of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22784820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3490334/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Swedish patients with ischemic stroke attending the stroke unit or the stroke outpatient clinic at Karolinska University Hospital, Huddinge unit in Stockholm, Sweden, were recruited from 1996 to 2002 as part of an ongoing genetic epidemiology study, the South Stockholm Ischemic Stroke Study (SSISS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002409> "A case-control study of ischaemic cerebrovascular disease in southern Stockholm, Sweden, whose stroke patients underwent clinical investigation and standardised blood tests and whose patients and controls were genotyped for 100 polymorphisms in 47 candidate susceptibility genes to study the genetic profile of ischaemic stroke and its subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-021-03767-x/MediaObjects/41586_2021_3767_MOESM6_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomic epidemiology of SARS-Cov-2 and host genetics in Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) | United States | Stanford | EUR | - | - | - | - | 169 | 190 | Cases 42.4 years  Controls 44.13 years | Stanford University IRB, Panel #8 | Consent waiver for initial data collection but consent for survey data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9426371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Host whole genome sequencing was aligned and called using methods for low pass data12–14 (mean of mean coverages: 2.56X ± 2.50X(SD), Fig. 1D), followed by phasing and imputation with GLIMPSE (Supplementary Fig. 1A, B)15.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9426371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to this analysis, we examined viral variants, host immunity (e.g., HLA typing), and the microbiome as covariates of majority ancestry to identify important potential contributors to disease severity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9426371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Residual viral transport media (VTM) from SARS-CoV-2 clinical diagnostic tests were prospectively collected from March 2020 to July 2020 from Stanford Health Care in northern California, USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9426371/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Swabs were selected approximately consecutively from SARS-CoV-2 positive and negative individuals and linked to structured clinical information from the electronic health record.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36042219") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36042219+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We leverage a pandemic tracking strategy in which we sequence viral and host genomes and transcriptomes from nasopharyngeal swabs of 1049 individuals (736 SARS-CoV-2 positive and 313 SARS-CoV-2 negative) and integrate them with digital phenotypes from electronic health records from a diverse catchment area in Northern California.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002410> "A COVID-19 pandemic-tracking study at Stanford Health Care in northern California that, from March to July 2020, collected the residual nasopharyngeal swab media of clinical SARS-CoV-2 tests from approximately consecutive SARS-CoV-2-positive and -negative patients, linked them to electronic health record data, and sequenced the patients' genomes at low coverage together with viral genomes and transcriptomes, to study host genetic, viral and clinical correlates of COVID-19 severity; it contributed its host genetic data to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3979485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All eye examinations were performed from May 2006 to November 2008 by trained eye professionals, with assessments conducted at two convenient clinic sites within the study area: the Singapore National Eye Center (SNEC) or the Jurong Medical Centre, Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3979485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eye examinations were conducted by trained ophthalmologists, optometrists, and orthoptists and included visual acuity assessment, ocular motility tests (cover testing, ocular movements, stereoacuity, and fixation preference), cycloplegic autorefraction, biometry examination, and fundus photography.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3979485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Parental questionnaires were administered.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19933197+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Door-to-door recruitment of participants was used, with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month increments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23860760+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Strabismus, Amblyopia, and Refractive Error Study in Singaporean Chinese Preschoolers (STARS) family study conducted from 2008 to 2010, a total of 727 participants (304 parent-child pairs, 83 sibling pairs, and 87 spouse pairs) were included in the analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19426960") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19933197") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22064996") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23860760") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34319387") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8322707/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Strabismus, Amblyopia, and Refractive Error Study (STARS) is a population-based survey of Chinese families with children aged 6 to 72 months residing in the southwestern and western region of Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002411> "A population-based study of Chinese children aged 6 to 72 months living in south-western and western Singapore, recruited door to door from 2006 to 2008 with disproportionate random sampling in 6-month age bands, who had parental questionnaires and eye examinations including visual acuity, cycloplegic autorefraction, ocular biometry and retinal photography, to study strabismus, amblyopia and refractive error in preschool children; a family study in 2008-2010 added parents and siblings.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22032547+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first is a genome-wide association and copy number variation analysis using the diagnostic phenotype of schizophrenia and cognitive phenotypes, and a joint genome-wide analysis performed by combining our data with other datasets to increase the power to detect genetic risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22032547+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second is a prospective study of a large group of individuals who are assessed to be at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and the third is a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in patients with schizophrenia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22032547+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This paper describes the rationale, aims and development of the Singapore Translational and Clinical Research in Psychosis, which is a 5-year programme.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9954179/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants consisted of both outpatients and inpatients recruited as part of the Singapore Translational and Clinical Research Psychosis (STCRP) program at the Institute of Mental Health, Singapore.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9954179/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were included if they were of Chinese ethnicity, 21 to 55 years of age, completed a minimum of six years of primary school education, and had a diagnosis of schizophrenia ascertained on the Structured Clinical Interview for DSM-IV-TR Axis I Disorders [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22032547") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36831758") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9954179/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted from 2008 to 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002412> "A five-year national flagship research programme on psychosis in Singapore, based at the Institute of Mental Health, made up of three linked studies: a genome-wide association and copy-number study of schizophrenia and its cognitive phenotypes, a prospective study of people at ultra-high risk of psychosis, and a randomized controlled trial to improve neurocognition in schizophrenia. Its schizophrenia study recruited outpatients and inpatients of Chinese ethnicity aged 21 to 55 with DSM-IV schizophrenia at the Institute of Mental Health from 2008 to 2011.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002413> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002413>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_json/PMC4503229/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41467-021-21287-0/MediaObjects/41467_2021_21287_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "STHM2 (n=4524) Stockholm 2 Stockholm, Sweden Population- based, observational 1491 3033") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002413> "A population-based cohort of men referred for prostate-specific antigen testing in laboratories in Stockholm County, Sweden, who were invited at the blood-sampling visit between 2010 and 2012, with prostate cancer diagnoses and biopsy results taken from the National Prostate Cancer Register and regional records; it supplied prostate cancer cases and controls to international genetic studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_json/PMC4503229/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4503229/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, this database consists of all men in Stockholm County who had at least one PSA analyzed since 2003 together with their biopsy records and prostate cancer history as recorded by the National Prostate Cancer Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002413> "A population-based cohort of men referred for prostate-specific antigen testing in laboratories in Stockholm County, Sweden, who were invited at the blood-sampling visit between 2010 and 2012, with prostate cancer diagnoses and biopsy results taken from the National Prostate Cancer Register and regional records; it supplied prostate cancer cases and controls to international genetic studies.")
