AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All variables were assessed during the baseline health check-up, which included medical and clinical examinations, blood and urine analyses, ECG, and questionnaires assessing lifestyle and medical history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As described elsewhere [20, 21], the Suita Study is a population-based study with a prospective cohort design, aimed at investigating CVD risk factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, 546 volunteers were recruited between 1992 and 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One group was recruited in 1989 (6485 people) and the other in 1998 (1329 people).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were then asked to return to the NCVC every two years for follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40383629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9056605") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40898037") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12403414/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Suita population consisted of two randomly selected groups from Osaka, Japan, based on 10-year age and sex categories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002418> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents of Suita, an urban city in Osaka, Japan, made up of two groups randomly selected from the general population by sex and 10-year age group (recruited in 1989 and 1998) and a volunteer group (recruited 1992-2006), who had a baseline health examination with questionnaire, clinical examination, blood and urine analysis and electrocardiogram at the National Cerebral and Cardiovascular Center and return there every two years for follow-up, to investigate risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9503043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15557412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15557412+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants took a single daily capsule of a combination of 120 mg of ascorbic acid, 30 mg of vitamin E, 6 mg of beta carotene, 100 mug of selenium, and 20 mg of zinc, or a placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for a median of 7.5 years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9503043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15557412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15557412+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Median follow-up time was 7.5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for a median of 7.5 years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9503043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15557412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15557412+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Supplementation en Vitamines et Mineraux Antioxydants (SU.VI.MAX) study is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary prevention trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for a median of 7.5 years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9503043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15557412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15557412+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We tested the efficacy of nutritional doses of supplementation with a combination of antioxidant vitamins and minerals in reducing the incidence of cancer and ischemic cardiovascular disease in the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for a median of 7.5 years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9503043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9683310") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9683310+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "this 8-year cohort study, which started in 1994 in France; 12,735 eligible subjects (women aged 35-60, and men aged 45-60) were included in 1994") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002419> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled primary-prevention trial in the general adult population of France, which in 1994 enrolled women aged 35 to 60 and men aged 45 to 60 and followed them for a median of 7.5 years to test whether daily supplementation with antioxidant vitamins (vitamin C, vitamin E and beta-carotene) and minerals (selenium and zinc) at nutritional doses reduces cancers and cardiovascular diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002420> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002420>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24001895") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/3972802/bin/NIHMS514903-supplement-1.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24001895") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3972802/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In-silico or de novo replication genotyping and association analyses were conducted in up to six additional samples of 28,783 participants (Table 1, Supplementary Note).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002420> "A cross-sectional survey of hypertension carried out in 2010 in four urban communities and four rural villages of the Jinchang district of Suzhou, Jiangsu province, China, whose 3,061 participants were Han Chinese adults aged 30 years or older without end-organ damage, chronic renal disease, tumours or urinary tract infections, with questionnaire, anthropometric and blood pressure data. All its participants were genotyped as a de novo replication sample of the Asian Genetic Epidemiology Network's genome-wide association meta-analysis of mean arterial and pulse pressure.")
