AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 758 cancer-free controls were derived from the SWHS/SMHS and frequency- matched to CRC cases by age and sex.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421> "A colorectal cancer case-control study nested in two population-based cohorts in urban Shanghai, China, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study, whose cases were colorectal cancer patients identified among the cohorts' participants and whose controls were cancer-free participants of the same cohorts frequency-matched to the cases by age and sex. Its samples, with additional community controls from the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, were genotyped as the Shanghai-1 and Shanghai-2 sets of the discovery stage of the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23263487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2505/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2505_MOESM12_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Colorectal cancer (CRC) cases for the project were derived from the Shanghai Women’s Health Study (SWHS) and the Shanghai Men’s Health Study (SMHS), both population-based cohort studies which are being conducted in urban Shanghai, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002421> "A colorectal cancer case-control study nested in two population-based cohorts in urban Shanghai, China, the Shanghai Women's Health Study and the Shanghai Men's Health Study, whose cases were colorectal cancer patients identified among the cohorts' participants and whose controls were cancer-free participants of the same cohorts frequency-matched to the cases by age and sex. Its samples, with additional community controls from the Shanghai Breast Cancer Study, were genotyped as the Shanghai-1 and Shanghai-2 sets of the discovery stage of the Asia Colorectal Cancer Consortium's genome-wide association study.")
