AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33623038") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0142-8/MediaObjects/41588_2018_142_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Identified through linkage to the Finnish Cancer Registry and patient records; and the Finnish arm of the ERSPC study Cohort participants without a diagnosis of cancer") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002435> "A population-based prostate cancer case–control study in Finland, run from Tampere, whose cases were identified through linkage to the Finnish Cancer Registry, patient records and the Finnish arm of the European Randomized Study of Screening for Prostate Cancer (ERSPC), and whose controls are ERSPC cohort participants without a cancer diagnosis; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome sequencing (WGS) was performed at the HudsonAlpha Institute for Biotechnology on either the Illumina HiSeq X platform, or the Illumina NovaSeq platform.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genomes from 900 Colombian individuals with Alzheimer’s disease (AD) [n = 376], frontotemporal lobar degeneration-motor neuron disease continuum (FTLD-MND) [n = 197], early-onset dementia not otherwise specified (EOD) [n = 73], and healthy participants [n = 254] were analyzed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited or referred to the “Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia,” University of Antioquia, Colombia for “The Admixture and Neurodegeneration Genomic Landscape” (TANGL) study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Healthy participant cohort (n = 254) included individuals related and unrelated to the patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The recruitment targeted patients with early-onset dementia and families in which multiple first-degree relatives were affected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35260199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8902761/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "When patients had familial forms of dementia, their relatives with neurological and psychiatric disorders were recruited along with healthy family members.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002436> "A genome sequencing study of Colombians with neurodegenerative disease, chiefly early-onset or autosomal dominant Alzheimer's disease, the frontotemporal lobar degeneration–motor neuron disease spectrum and other early-onset dementias, together with affected and healthy relatives and unrelated healthy participants, recruited or referred to the Grupo de Neurociencias de Antioquia of the University of Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia, with recruitment targeting early-onset dementia and families with several affected first-degree relatives, to study the admixture and rare disease-causing variants underlying neurodegeneration in Colombia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41287073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12642085/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the latter group, screening allocation was determined by a composite risk score incorporating age, sex, family history of CRC, smoking status, and body mass index, with high-risk participants referred for colonoscopy and low-risk participants for FIT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After providing written informed consent, participants were randomized in a 1:2:2 ratio to one-time colonoscopy (n = 3,937), annual FIT screening (n = 7,858), or a risk-adapted screening strategy (n = 7,787).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants were adults aged 50–74 years recruited from community-based screening programs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participant recruitment began in May 2018, and four screening rounds (baseline and three annual follow-up rounds) were completed by October 2023.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41851747") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13123215/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TARGET-C study (Comparative Evaluation of Novel Screening Strategies for Colorectal Cancer Screening) is a multicenter randomized controlled trial conducted in six study centers across five provinces in China (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan, and Yunnan).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002437> "A multicentre randomised controlled trial of colorectal cancer screening at six study centres in five Chinese provinces (Jiangsu, Zhejiang, Anhui, Hunan and Yunnan), which from May 2018 recruited adults aged 50–74 years from community-based screening programmes and randomised them to one-time colonoscopy, annual faecal immunochemical testing or a risk-adapted strategy (colonoscopy for high-risk and faecal immunochemical testing for low-risk participants), over four annual screening rounds completed in 2023.")

