AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were identified from the TCR.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll, frequency matched by five-year age groups to the cases, and checked bi-annually against the TCR for PrCa diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Families with more than two affected first-degree relatives spanning two or more generations were identified through interrogation of the Menzies Genealogical database and the Tasmanian Cancer Registry (TCR), in addition to collaboration with local clinicians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study included 73 PrCa families comprising DNA from 379 affected men and 471 unaffected male and female relatives of Northern European heritage [22,23,24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was initiated in Tasmania in the late 1990s, prior to the implementation of wide-spread prostate-specific antigen (PSA) testing as a PrCa screening tool.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33436325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39001544") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11240467/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Australian resource, consisting of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002439> "The prostate cancer resource of the Menzies Institute for Medical Research, University of Tasmania, in Hobart, made up of the Tasmanian Familial Prostate Cancer Study, begun in the late 1990s, of prostate cancer families of Northern European descent identified through the Menzies Genealogical database, the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and local clinicians, and the population-based Tasmanian Prostate Cancer Case-Control Study, whose cases were ascertained through the Tasmanian Cancer Registry and whose male controls were selected at random from the Tasmanian electoral roll; it contributes to the PRACTICAL consortium.")

