AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TBCS Torino Bladder Cancer Study 401 379 100 Italy: hospital-based (48)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002440> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Torino (Turin), Italy, whose cases were men living in the Torino metropolitan area newly diagnosed with bladder cancer between 1994 and 2006 in the urology departments of the San Giovanni Battista Hospital, and whose controls were men from the same area treated in the same hospital for benign diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were all Caucasian men, aged 40–75 years (median 63 years) and living in the Torino metropolitan area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002440> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Torino (Turin), Italy, whose cases were men living in the Torino metropolitan area newly diagnosed with bladder cancer between 1994 and 2006 in the urology departments of the San Giovanni Battista Hospital, and whose controls were men from the same area treated in the same hospital for benign diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sources of cases for the Torino bladder cancer study were two urology departments of the main hospital in Torino, the San Giovanni Battista Hospital (32).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002440> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Torino (Turin), Italy, whose cases were men living in the Torino metropolitan area newly diagnosed with bladder cancer between 1994 and 2006 in the urology departments of the San Giovanni Battista Hospital, and whose controls were men from the same area treated in the same hospital for benign diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sources of controls are urology, medical and surgical departments of the same hospital in Torino. All controls are Caucasian men resident in the Torino metropolitan area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002440> "A hospital-based case-control study of bladder cancer in Torino (Turin), Italy, whose cases were men living in the Torino metropolitan area newly diagnosed with bladder cancer between 1994 and 2006 in the urology departments of the San Giovanni Battista Hospital, and whose controls were men from the same area treated in the same hospital for benign diseases.")
