# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3874/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3874_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-020-2263-3/MediaObjects/41586_2020_2263_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fasting blood samples were collected before cardiac catheterization while 10 ml of peripheral blood was collected in the catheter lab specifically for buffy coat isolation and DNA extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443> "An ongoing hospital-based cohort of patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention for stable angina pectoris or prior myocardial infarction at National Taiwan University Hospital, enrolling patients both in the north of Taiwan, where the main hospital is, and at a branch of the hospital in south-central Taiwan, with electronic medical records, fasting blood samples taken before cardiac catheterisation and blood collected in the catheter laboratory for DNA. It is one of the seven Taiwan-based cohorts of the TAICHI consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3874/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3874_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-020-2263-3/MediaObjects/41586_2020_2263_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are not only from the north of Taiwan where the main NTU medical school/hospital is located, but also from Yulin branch of NTUH, located in south/central Taiwan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443> "An ongoing hospital-based cohort of patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention for stable angina pectoris or prior myocardial infarction at National Taiwan University Hospital, enrolling patients both in the north of Taiwan, where the main hospital is, and at a branch of the hospital in south-central Taiwan, with electronic medical records, fasting blood samples taken before cardiac catheterisation and blood collected in the catheter laboratory for DNA. It is one of the seven Taiwan-based cohorts of the TAICHI consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3874/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3874_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-020-2263-3/MediaObjects/41586_2020_2263_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TCAGEN (Taiwan Coronary Artery Disease GENetic) study is an ongoing cohort study that has been enrolling patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous intervention at the National Taiwan University Hospital (NTUH) in the setting of either stable angina pectoris or prior myocardial infarction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443> "An ongoing hospital-based cohort of patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention for stable angina pectoris or prior myocardial infarction at National Taiwan University Hospital, enrolling patients both in the north of Taiwan, where the main hospital is, and at a branch of the hospital in south-central Taiwan, with electronic medical records, fasting blood samples taken before cardiac catheterisation and blood collected in the catheter laboratory for DNA. It is one of the seven Taiwan-based cohorts of the TAICHI consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3874/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3874_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-020-2263-3/MediaObjects/41586_2020_2263_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2797/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2797_MOESM43_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The hospital uses an elaborate electronic medical record system that provides access to clinic visit notes, diagnostic codes of clinic encounters, prescriptions, and laboratory data in a searchable form.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002443> "An ongoing hospital-based cohort of patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention for stable angina pectoris or prior myocardial infarction at National Taiwan University Hospital, enrolling patients both in the north of Taiwan, where the main hospital is, and at a branch of the hospital in south-central Taiwan, with electronic medical records, fasting blood samples taken before cardiac catheterisation and blood collected in the catheter laboratory for DNA. It is one of the seven Taiwan-based cohorts of the TAICHI consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5344981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By linking genome-wide data to the existing databank of TLGS participants, which includes comprehensive behavioral, biochemical, and clinical data on each participant since cohort inception in 1999, the TCGS will also allow exploration of gene-gene and gene-environment interactions as they relate to disease status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5344981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TCGS was designed in collaboration with the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences and the genetic company deCODE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5344981/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aim of the Tehran Cardiometabolic Genetic Study (TCGS) is to create a comprehensive genome-wide database of at least 16,000 Tehranians, who are participants of the ongoing Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study (TLGS) cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10175059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TCGS cohort focuses on cardiovascular, endocrine, metabolic abnormalities, cancers, and some inherited diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10175059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TCGS has created a comprehensive database comprising 20,367 participants born between 1911 and 2015 selected from four main ongoing studies in a family-based longitudinal framework.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28232301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37169991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10175059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tehran cardiometabolic genetic study (TCGS) is a large population-based cohort study that conducts periodic follow-ups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002445> "A family-based, population-based genetic cohort in Tehran, Iran, designed by the Research Institute for Endocrine Sciences in collaboration with deCODE genetics, that genotyped participants of the Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study genome-wide and links their genotypes to the behavioural, biochemical and clinical data collected since 1999, later extended to participants of four ongoing studies with periodic follow-up, to identify genetic factors in cardiometabolic risk factors, cancers and other non-communicable diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3284120/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible participants were Caucasians from Poland between 40 and 80 years of age with at least 10 pack-years of cigarette smoking history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5716321/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All TCGS subjects were over the age of 40 with at least 10 pack-years of cigarette smoking history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5716321/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases had severe to very severe airflow obstruction with post-bronchodilator forced expiratory volume in 1 second (FEV1) <50% predicted and FEV1/forced vital capacity (FVC) <0.7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5716321/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Control subjects demonstrated normal lung function (post-bronchodilator FEV1 ≥80% predicted and FEV1/FVC ≥0.7).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5716321/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TCGS subjects in Poland were enrolled by the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases (Warsaw, Poland),6 and subjects in Korea participated at four university hospitals in Korea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22140090") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29238186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5716321/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled severe COPD subjects and smoker controls in Korea and Poland in the Transcontinental COPD Genetics Study (TCGS) and severe COPD cases in a study of frequent and infrequent exacerbators from the USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002446> "A case-control genetic study of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease made up of two case-control studies, one in Poland, enrolled through the Institute of Tuberculosis and Lung Diseases in Warsaw, and one in Korea, at four university hospitals, which recruited smokers aged 40 to 80 with at least 10 pack-years of smoking: cases with severe to very severe airflow obstruction and controls with normal lung function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002447> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002447>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17354224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39977302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11734643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the source population for TCPS was patients between 45 and 70 years of age undergoing colonoscopy at the Vanderbilt Gastroenterology Clinic and the Veteran's Affairs Tennessee Valley Health System in Nashville.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002447> "A colonoscopy-based case-control study of colorectal polyps conducted by Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, from 2003 to 2010, which enrolled patients undergoing colonoscopy at the Vanderbilt gastroenterology clinic and the Nashville Veterans Affairs medical centre, taking those found to have adenomatous or hyperplastic polyps as cases and polyp-free patients as controls, to study dietary, lifestyle and genetic risk factors for colorectal polyps.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17354224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39977302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11734643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases presented with polyps (i.e., adenomas, hyperplastic polyps, or both) and controls were polyp‐free.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002447> "A colonoscopy-based case-control study of colorectal polyps conducted by Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, from 2003 to 2010, which enrolled patients undergoing colonoscopy at the Vanderbilt gastroenterology clinic and the Nashville Veterans Affairs medical centre, taking those found to have adenomatous or hyperplastic polyps as cases and polyp-free patients as controls, to study dietary, lifestyle and genetic risk factors for colorectal polyps.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17354224") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39977302") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39812514") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11734643/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Tennessee Colorectal Polyp Study (TCPS), a colonoscopy‐based case‐control study of adenomatous polyps conducted at Vanderbilt University Medical Center (VUMC) from 2003 to 2010 in Nashville, Tennessee.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002447> "A colonoscopy-based case-control study of colorectal polyps conducted by Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville, Tennessee, from 2003 to 2010, which enrolled patients undergoing colonoscopy at the Vanderbilt gastroenterology clinic and the Nashville Veterans Affairs medical centre, taking those found to have adenomatous or hyperplastic polyps as cases and polyp-free patients as controls, to study dietary, lifestyle and genetic risk factors for colorectal polyps.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17850472+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Six clinical centers in the USA and Europe will screen 361,588 newborns, of which it is anticipated that 17,804 will be eligible for enrollment with just over 7,800 followed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17850472+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Environmental Determinants of Diabetes in the Young (TEDDY) is an observational cohort study in which newborns who are younger than 4 months and have high-risk human leukocyte antigen alleles in the general population or are first-degree relatives (FDRs) of patients affected with T1DM will be enrolled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6415767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Clinic visits occur quarterly until age 4, and then every 6 months through age 15.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6415767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TEDDY aims to identify environmental factors that trigger or protect against the development of IA and T1D.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6415767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TEDDY includes three US clinical centers in Denver, Seattle, and Augusta as well as centers in Turku (Finland), Malmö (Sweden), and Munich (Germany).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17850472") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32770166") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30353256") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6415767/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Environmental Determinants of Diabetes in the Young (TEDDY) Study follows from birth 8676 children with T1D risk HLA-DR-DQ genotypes in the USA, Finland, Germany, and Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002448> "A multicentre, multinational prospective birth cohort study, run from six clinical centres in the United States, Finland, Germany and Sweden, that screened newborns from the general population and first-degree relatives of people with type 1 diabetes for high-risk HLA genotypes, enrolled eligible children before four months of age and follows them to age 15, to identify infectious, dietary and other environmental exposures associated with islet autoimmunity and type 1 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14756462+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From January through October 2001, more than 400 US pulmonologists and allergists enrolled patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> "A 3-year multicentre observational cohort study of patients aged 6 years or older with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma, enrolled from January to October 2001 by more than 400 pulmonologists and allergists in the United States and sponsored by Genentech and Novartis, with data on demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, asthma triggers and quality of life collected semiannually and annually to characterise the natural history of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A14756462+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of The Epidemiology and Natural History of Asthma: Outcomes and Treatment Regimens (TENOR) study is to better understand the natural history of asthma in these patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> "A 3-year multicentre observational cohort study of patients aged 6 years or older with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma, enrolled from January to October 2001 by more than 400 pulmonologists and allergists in the United States and sponsored by Genentech and Novartis, with data on demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, asthma triggers and quality of life collected semiannually and annually to characterise the natural history of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2824608/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TENOR study was a multi-center observational and longitudinal cohort study of 4,756 asthmatics described as “severe or difficult-to-treat” by their physicians, sponsored by Genentech and Novartis [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> "A 3-year multicentre observational cohort study of patients aged 6 years or older with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma, enrolled from January to October 2001 by more than 400 pulmonologists and allergists in the United States and sponsored by Genentech and Novartis, with data on demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, asthma triggers and quality of life collected semiannually and annually to characterise the natural history of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3622643/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data assessed semiannually and annually included demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, asthma-related health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, self-reported asthma triggers, and asthma-related quality of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> "A 3-year multicentre observational cohort study of patients aged 6 years or older with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma, enrolled from January to October 2001 by more than 400 pulmonologists and allergists in the United States and sponsored by Genentech and Novartis, with data on demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, asthma triggers and quality of life collected semiannually and annually to characterise the natural history of the disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:14756462") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20159242") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22694932") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3622643/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Epidemiology and Natural History of Asthma: Outcomes and Treatment Regimens (TENOR) study was a large, 3-year, multicenter, observational cohort study of 4756 patients (n = 3489 adults ≥18 years of age, n = 497 adolescents 13-17 years of age, and n = 770 children 6-12 years of age) with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002449> "A 3-year multicentre observational cohort study of patients aged 6 years or older with severe or difficult-to-treat asthma, enrolled from January to October 2001 by more than 400 pulmonologists and allergists in the United States and sponsored by Genentech and Novartis, with data on demographics, medical history, comorbidities, asthma control, health care use, medication use, lung function, IgE levels, asthma triggers and quality of life collected semiannually and annually to characterise the natural history of the disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As we wished to utilise ophthalmic instrumentation that was difficult to access due to associated expense and limited availability, we used private or hospital ophthalmology clinics out of hours (weekends and early evenings).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Commencing in late 2000, twins who had been involved in the Menzies Centre for Population Health Research (now Menzies Research Institute) Tasmanian Infant Health Study (TIHS) were recruited as our initial cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five separate avenues for cohort recruitment were adopted: 1) piggy-backing existing studies where twins had been recruited; 2); utilising the national twin registry; 3) word of mouth and local media publicity; 4) directly approaching schools; and finally 5) collaborating with other research groups studying twins.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In total 55 triples (19 sets of triplets, where two sets had only two siblings attended) and 196 siblings were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The twins we examined in the Twins Eye Study Tasmania (TEST) were recruited in several waves, many overlapping with each other.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19803772") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3855231/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We asked all twins aged five years and older to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002450> "A study of the eyes of twins, begun in 2000 by the University of Tasmania and the Centre for Eye Research Australia, that recruited twins aged five years and over and some of their siblings, mostly in Tasmania, Australia, through earlier Tasmanian cohort studies, the Australian Twin Registry, schools and local publicity, and gave them ophthalmic examinations, to find genes for blinding eye diseases and quantitative eye traits.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002455> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002455>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31852448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31852448") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6921553/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first discovery stage, 1707age (± 3 years) and sex matched controls (BMI < 35 kg/m2) were included from Han-Chinese Cell and Genome Bank in Taiwan (HanBKT) established from October 1, 2002, to January 14, 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002455> "A biobank of healthy Han Chinese people in Taiwan, recruited between October 2002 and January 2004 by stratified three-stage probability cluster sampling through the registries of the non-aboriginal townships and city districts of Taiwan, whose DNA has served as population controls for genetic association studies, among them the Taiwan Super Control Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31852448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.1087/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng1087_MOESM24_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Han-Chinese Cell and Genome Bank in Taiwan21 includes more than 3,300 healthy controls who were recruited via a stratified, 3-staged probability clustering sampling scheme through a registry of all the 329 non-aboriginal townships or city districts in Taiwan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002455> "A biobank of healthy Han Chinese people in Taiwan, recruited between October 2002 and January 2004 by stratified three-stage probability cluster sampling through the registries of the non-aboriginal townships and city districts of Taiwan, whose DNA has served as population controls for genetic association studies, among them the Taiwan Super Control Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31852448") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4284402/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Taiwan Super Control Study (TWSC) included 1000 randomly selected individuals, of which genetic data were extracted from the Han-Chinese Cell and Genome Bank in Taiwan [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002455> "A biobank of healthy Han Chinese people in Taiwan, recruited between October 2002 and January 2004 by stratified three-stage probability cluster sampling through the registries of the non-aboriginal townships and city districts of Taiwan, whose DNA has served as population controls for genetic association studies, among them the Taiwan Super Control Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002456> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002456>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18629629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21908515") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18629629") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-9998-0") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age (±5 years) frequency-matched controls were recruited from women who attended health screening in the Center of Health Examination in the same hospital during the same period without any evidence of cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002456> "A hospital-based case–control study of breast cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were women with histopathologically diagnosed primary breast cancer recruited consecutively from the Department of Breast Surgery of Tianjin Cancer Institute and Hospital, Tianjin Medical University, and whose controls were women without evidence of cancer who attended health screening at the same hospital, frequency-matched to the cases on age; all participants were unrelated ethnic Han Chinese women who were permanent residents of urban Tianjin. Its study period was 2004 to 2008, and it is one of the participating studies of the Asia Breast Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18629629") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21908515") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18629629") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10549-008-9998-0") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients and control subjects were genetically unrelated, ethnic Han Chinese women from permanent residents of the urban area of Tianjin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002456> "A hospital-based case–control study of breast cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were women with histopathologically diagnosed primary breast cancer recruited consecutively from the Department of Breast Surgery of Tianjin Cancer Institute and Hospital, Tianjin Medical University, and whose controls were women without evidence of cancer who attended health screening at the same hospital, frequency-matched to the cases on age; all participants were unrelated ethnic Han Chinese women who were permanent residents of urban Tianjin. Its study period was 2004 to 2008, and it is one of the participating studies of the Asia Breast Cancer Consortium.")
