# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16644310+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a prospective single-blinded multicenter trial, 824 symptomatic patients, CHF hospitalization within the last year and elevated NT-BNP, are randomized to an intensified versus a standard medical therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16644310+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It will provide unique information comparing two treatment strategies in two age groups irrespective of ejection fraction regarding prognosis, quality of life, as well as resource utilization and costs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16644310+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "to evaluate the medical management of very old patients (> or = 75 years) with CHF compared with younger patients (60-74 years)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7738407/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TIME-CHF was a randomized controlled trial that took place at 15 centers in Switzerland and Germany from January 2003 to June 2008 that enrolled a total of 622 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16644310") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33012170") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7738407/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the trial was to compare N-terminal pro-B-type natriuretic peptide (NTproBNP)–guided versus symptom-guided treatment for heart failure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002457> "A prospective, single-blinded, multicentre randomised trial, run at centres in Switzerland and Germany from 2003 to 2008, in which patients aged 60 years or over with symptomatic congestive heart failure, a heart-failure hospitalisation within the previous year and raised NT-proBNP were randomised to NT-proBNP-guided (intensified) or symptom-guided (standard) medical therapy, to compare the two strategies in patients aged 75 or over and aged 60 to 74, with reduced or preserved ejection fraction.")

