AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23839018") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28604730") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.3892/MediaObjects/41588_2017_BFng3892_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Total Cancer Care™ is a multi-institutional observational study of cancer patients that prospectively collects self-reported demographic and clinical data, medical record information and blood samples for research purposes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002458> "A hospital-based, case-only study of the molecular epidemiology of lung cancer survival at the H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center in Tampa, Florida, United States, whose participants are lung cancer patients recruited from Moffitt's Thoracic Oncology Clinic between April 2006 and August 2010 under the centre's Total Cancer Care protocol, which collects self-reported, medical record and cancer registry data and blood samples.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All subjects were ethnic Chinese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were recruited from patients who underwent regular health check-up during the same time when cases were recruited and lived in the same neighborhoods or nearby communities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients with a previous medical history of cancer, or previous radiotherapy or chemotherapy were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TLCS enrolled patients with newly diagnosed and histologically confirmed primary non- small cell lung cancer from Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital in Tianjin, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The controls were frequency-matched to cases on gender and age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4169232/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify new susceptibility loci in Asian never-smoking women, we conducted a lung cancer GWAS in 14 studies (13 case-control studies and 1 cohort study, Supplementary Note, Supplementary Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002459> "A case–control study of lung cancer in Tianjin, China, whose cases were patients with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed primary non-small cell lung cancer at Tianjin Medical University Cancer Hospital, excluding those with a previous cancer or earlier radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were people attending regular health check-ups in the same period who lived in the same or nearby neighbourhoods, frequency-matched to the cases on sex and age; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2656492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 15005 individuals aged 3 years and over who were residence of district No.13 of Tehran and were under the coverage of three medical health centers, were selected using multistage cluster random sampling method.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2656492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In phase II of the TLGS, lifestyle interventions were implemented in 5630 people and 9375 individuals served as controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2656492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase II is a prospective follow-up study which has begun from January 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2656492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tehran Lipid and Glucose Study (TLGS) is a large scale community based prospective study performed on a representative sample of residents of district-13 of Tehran, capital of Iran.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6289309/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TLGS was first designed in 1997 and implemented in 1999 with the aim of studying epidemiology of NCD risk factors and outcomes of NCDs in a manner that was previously unprecedented in Iran (4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19166627") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30584442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6289309/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This population was selected through a multistage stratified cluster random sampling technique from the population of district 13 in Tehran.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002460> "A community-based prospective study of a representative sample of residents of district 13 of Tehran, Iran, aged 3 years and over and selected by multistage stratified cluster random sampling, designed in 1997 and begun in 1999 as a cross-sectional survey of non-communicable disease risk factors; from 2002 it became a long-term longitudinal study, including a controlled community lifestyle intervention, with follow-up examinations about every three years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A19187325+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tasmanian Longitudinal Health Study (TAHS) is a population-based cohort (n=8583) study of respiratory disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12926821/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the baseline survey was carried out to assess the respiratory illnesses of 8583 offspring born in 1961, who were attending schools in Tasmania, Australia, in 1968.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12926821/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up studies were performed when the offspring were at mean ages of 13, 18, 30, 43, 50 and 53 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12926821/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TAHS commenced in 1968 (baseline) and gathered comprehensive respiratory health data from probands (referred to as “offspring” in this paper), from childhood until the sixth decade of life [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12926821/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The parents completed the baseline survey for their offspring and provided information about their own history of respiratory illnesses and demographic characteristics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19187325") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41736738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42480573") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9240942/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At mean age=53, 3609 (58.9%) respondents completed the questionnaire and 2719 (43.9%) underwent lung function testing including prebronchodilator/postbronchodilator spirometry and lung gas transfer measurements, on average 46 years later (figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002461> "A population-based cohort study of respiratory health that began in 1968 with a survey of the children born in 1961 who were attending school in Tasmania, Australia, and has followed these probands with repeated surveys and lung function testing from age 7 into their sixth decade, with their parents also surveyed.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Importantly, genotype data from a subset of these cases and controls have previously been used in association studies involving a number of these SNPs by the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Triple Negative Breast Cancer Consortium (TNBCC), 22 common breast cancer susceptibility variants were investigated in 2,980 Caucasian women with triple negative breast cancer and 4,978 healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These included cases from the KBCP and POSH cohort studies, cases and controls from the MCCS cohort study, and cases and controls from established population-based breast cancer case-control studies (BBCS, GENICA, MARIE, SEARCH)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These subjects were ascertained by 22 studies in 10 different countries: United States, Australia, Great Britain, Finland, Germany, Netherlands, Greece, Ireland, and Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Triple negative (TN) breast cancers are a biologically and clinically distinct subtype of breast cancer, defined as tumors that exhibit low or no expression of estrogen receptor (ER), progesterone receptor (PR), and human epidermal growth factor receptor-2 (HER2) (1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29058716") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21844186") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3327299/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "hospital or clinic based case-control studies (ABCS, BIGGS, LMBC, MCBCS, OBCS, SBCS, and RPCI), case-only studies with geographically matched controls (BBCC, KARBAC, SKKDKFZS, FCCC), and unselected cases identified in tumor collections (DFCI, ABCTB, DEMOKRITOS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002462> "An international consortium of case-control, cohort, case-only and tumour-collection studies of breast cancer in the United States, Australia and Europe that pools women with triple-negative (estrogen receptor-, progesterone receptor- and HER2-negative) breast cancer and controls to study inherited susceptibility to triple-negative breast cancer, and that contributes its case series to the Breast Cancer Association Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC552310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects aged between 50 and 79 years were selected randomly from the electoral roll of Southern Tasmania, with an equal number of males and females.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC552310/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Tasmanian Older Adult Cohort Study (TASOAC), an ongoing prospective population-based study aimed at identifying the environmental, genetic, and biochemical factors associated with the development and progression of OA at multiple sites (hand, knee, hip, and spine), which commenced in 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10571432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Tasmanian Older Adult Cohort (TASOAC) is a prospective study in southern Tasmania, Australia [19].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10571432/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current study included 394 participants who had data on smoking status and underwent MRI assessments at baseline and the 2.6-year follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11889593/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between March 2002 and September 2004, 1099 individuals out of 1904 older adults were randomly chosen from the electoral roll in Southern Tasmania (population 229,000) and enrolled in this cohort, resulting in a response rate of 57 %.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15720725") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37833699") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40061840") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11889593/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data souce of this study was the Tasmania Older Adult Cohort (TASOAC), a longitudinal, prospective observational study involving community-dwelling older adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002463> "A prospective population-based cohort of community-dwelling men and women aged 50 to 79, selected at random in equal numbers by sex from the electoral roll of southern Tasmania, Australia, and enrolled between March 2002 and September 2004, with follow-up assessments, to identify environmental, genetic and biochemical factors in the development and progression of osteoarthritis at multiple sites.")

