AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21592732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35650188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37310336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21592732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21592732+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a web-based cross-sectional study we obtained detailed information about cannabis use and subclinical psychiatric experiences using the Community Assessment of Psychic Experiences (CAPE).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002477> "A cohort of young Dutch adults recruited online through a project website launched in 2006, who reported their cannabis use and psychotic-like experiences in a web-based survey; to increase power for gene-environment interaction, a genotyped subset combines participants from the general population with participants selected from the top or bottom quintile of psychotic-like experience scores who were either cannabis non-users or heavy users.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21592732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35650188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37310336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35650188") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9160238/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Utrecht Cannabis Cohort (UCC) consists of 1262 Dutch young adults of European ancestry aged from 18 to 25 years, recruited using a project website launched in 2006 [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002477> "A cohort of young Dutch adults recruited online through a project website launched in 2006, who reported their cannabis use and psychotic-like experiences in a web-based survey; to increase power for gene-environment interaction, a genotyped subset combines participants from the general population with participants selected from the top or bottom quintile of psychotic-like experience scores who were either cannabis non-users or heavy users.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21592732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35650188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37310336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37310336") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10106286/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To increase power for gene × environment interactions in previous studies (Boks et al., 2007), data from individuals from the general population were combined with data of participants selected from the top or bottom quintile of total PLE scores, who are either non-users (<2 lifetime exposures to cannabis) or heavy users (i.e. current expenditure for personal cannabis use exceeded €10 weekly).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002477> "A cohort of young Dutch adults recruited online through a project website launched in 2006, who reported their cannabis use and psychotic-like experiences in a web-based survey; to increase power for gene-environment interaction, a genotyped subset combines participants from the general population with participants selected from the top or bottom quintile of psychotic-like experience scores who were either cannabis non-users or heavy users.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21592732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35650188") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37310336") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Ftp.2016.36/MediaObjects/41398_2016_BFtp201636_MOESM267_ESM.doc") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Of these individuals, 1000 genome imputed whole genome genotyping data was available for 2,137 individuals of which 2,078 could be used for genetic analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002477> "A cohort of young Dutch adults recruited online through a project website launched in 2006, who reported their cannabis use and psychotic-like experiences in a web-based survey; to increase power for gene-environment interaction, a genotyped subset combines participants from the general population with participants selected from the top or bottom quintile of psychotic-like experience scores who were either cannabis non-users or heavy users.")

