# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6868237/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, patients with BD, their first-degree family members and healthy controls were recruited via clinicians, the Dutch BD patients’ association, pharmacies, advertisements, and through individuals who previously participated in scientific studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480> "A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients' association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6868237/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DB Cohort study, started in 2011, is a multicenter case–control study in the Netherlands, investigating genetic and phenotypic information of patients with BD type I, first-degree relatives, and controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480> "A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients' association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9542330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were acquired from the Dutch Bipolar Cohort (DBC), a large ongoing case‐control study started in June 2011, in a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles (UCLA) and the Dutch healthcare institutes of the University Medical Center Utrecht (UMC Utrecht)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480> "A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients' association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31748521") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34821429") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9542330/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Dutch healthcare institutes of the University Medical Center Utrecht (UMC Utrecht), GGZ Altrecht, GGz inGeest, University Medical Center Groningen, Delta Center for Mental Health Care, Dimence, Parnassia (PsyQ) and Reinier van Arkel Group.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002480> "A multicentre case-control study in the Netherlands, started in 2011 as a collaboration between the University of California Los Angeles and University Medical Center Utrecht with other Dutch mental health care institutes, that collects genetic and phenotypic information on patients with bipolar I disorder, their first-degree relatives and controls, recruited through clinicians, the Dutch bipolar disorder patients' association, pharmacies, advertisements and earlier research studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24423220+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LASER-AD longitudinal study of people with AD and their carers has contributed to our understanding of the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease, and to developing tools that help detect dementia earlier, and screen and identify problems experienced by carers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "London and the South East Region AD project (LASER-AD), University College London") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants and their carers were approached through local community mental health teams, dementia specialist nurses, the voluntary sector, memory clinics, nursing and residential homes, day hospitals, day centres and inpatient units.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited between July 2002 and January 2003 and followed up to 54 months; hence, the data are relatively old and the prevalence of agitations symptoms among people with AD may have changed over time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was purposively and prospectively recruited, using overall figures from a review of the epidemiology of AD, to be a representative sample of people with AD in terms of sex, living setting and severity of cognitive impairment in the community.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24423220") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.440/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng440_MOESM9_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4360590/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We calculated National Health Service (NHS) and personal social services (PSS) costs associated with different levels of agitation using data from a naturalistic prospective cohort study of people with AD, covering the London and the South East Region of the UK (LASER-AD study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002481> "A naturalistic, prospective cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease and their carers in London and the South East Region of the UK, run from University College London, recruited in 2002-2003 through community mental health teams, memory clinics, care homes, day hospitals and the voluntary sector to be representative of people with Alzheimer's disease in the community by sex, living setting and severity, and followed for up to 54 months to study the progression, characteristics and costs of the disease and the problems of carers.")

