# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5852207/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We determined the capacity for a combined genetic risk score (GRS) to discriminate disease-risk subgroups in a racially and ethnically diverse cohort from the southeastern U.S. including 637 T1D patients, 46 at-risk relatives having two or more T1D-related autoantibodies (≥2AAb+), 790 first-degree relatives (≤1AAb+), 68 second-degree relatives (≤1 AAb+), and 405 controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> "A cross-sectional collection of serum and genomic DNA from people with type 1 diabetes, their first- and second-degree relatives, islet autoantibody-positive at-risk individuals and unaffected controls, recruited from the general population and from outpatient clinics at the University of Florida in Gainesville, Nemours Children's Hospital in Orlando and Emory University in Atlanta, United States, and banked by the University of Florida Diabetes Institute for studies of type 1 diabetes genetic risk and biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5852207/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We emulated this model to assess its capacity to stratify subgroups (i.e., controls, low- and high-risk relatives, type 1 diabetes patients) using cumulative genetic risk in our regional cross-sectional cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> "A cross-sectional collection of serum and genomic DNA from people with type 1 diabetes, their first- and second-degree relatives, islet autoantibody-positive at-risk individuals and unaffected controls, recruited from the general population and from outpatient clinics at the University of Florida in Gainesville, Nemours Children's Hospital in Orlando and Emory University in Atlanta, United States, and banked by the University of Florida Diabetes Institute for studies of type 1 diabetes genetic risk and biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11749058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Peripheral blood was collected from consented study participants recruited from the general population and outpatient endocrinology clinics at the University of Florida (Gainesville, Florida), Nemours Children’s Hospital (Orlando, Florida), and Emory University (Atlanta, Georgia).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> "A cross-sectional collection of serum and genomic DNA from people with type 1 diabetes, their first- and second-degree relatives, islet autoantibody-positive at-risk individuals and unaffected controls, recruited from the general population and from outpatient clinics at the University of Florida in Gainesville, Nemours Children's Hospital in Orlando and Emory University in Atlanta, United States, and banked by the University of Florida Diabetes Institute for studies of type 1 diabetes genetic risk and biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11749058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Serum and genomic DNA samples were stored at −20°C in the University of Florida Diabetes Institute (UFDI) Study Bank as previously described.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> "A cross-sectional collection of serum and genomic DNA from people with type 1 diabetes, their first- and second-degree relatives, islet autoantibody-positive at-risk individuals and unaffected controls, recruited from the general population and from outpatient clinics at the University of Florida in Gainesville, Nemours Children's Hospital in Orlando and Emory University in Atlanta, United States, and banked by the University of Florida Diabetes Institute for studies of type 1 diabetes genetic risk and biomarkers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29540798") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39755561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11749058/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collectively evaluated seven such biomarkers, combined with islet autoantibodies (AAb) and genetic risk score (GRS2), for their utility in predicting AAb/T1D status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002487> "A cross-sectional collection of serum and genomic DNA from people with type 1 diabetes, their first- and second-degree relatives, islet autoantibody-positive at-risk individuals and unaffected controls, recruited from the general population and from outpatient clinics at the University of Florida in Gainesville, Nemours Children's Hospital in Orlando and Emory University in Atlanta, United States, and banked by the University of Florida Diabetes Institute for studies of type 1 diabetes genetic risk and biomarkers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15921047+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to participate in the Utrecht Health Project (UHP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Leidsche Rijn, a newly developed residential area of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, in which all new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to take part, receive a baseline individual health profile from research nurses, and are followed up through continuous linkage with the general practitioners' electronic medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15921047+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Follow-up data are collected through continuous linkage with the computerized medical files recorded by the general practitioners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Leidsche Rijn, a newly developed residential area of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, in which all new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to take part, receive a baseline individual health profile from research nurses, and are followed up through continuous linkage with the general practitioners' electronic medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15921047+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Informed consent is obtained and an individual health profile (IHP) is made by dedicated research nurses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Leidsche Rijn, a newly developed residential area of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, in which all new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to take part, receive a baseline individual health profile from research nurses, and are followed up through continuous linkage with the general practitioners' electronic medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15921047+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This formed the basis for a new study initiated in a newly developed large residential area in Leidsche Rijn, part of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Leidsche Rijn, a newly developed residential area of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, in which all new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to take part, receive a baseline individual health profile from research nurses, and are followed up through continuous linkage with the general practitioners' electronic medical records.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15921047") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16887835") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16887835+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline data of 4950 adult participants of the Utrecht Health Project, a community-based prospective cohort study, were used to calculate sensitivity and specificity of self-reported hypertension and diabetes with the results of blood pressure measurements and blood glucose levels, corrected for current medication use, as the reference standard.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002490> "A community-based prospective cohort study in Leidsche Rijn, a newly developed residential area of the city of Utrecht, the Netherlands, in which all new inhabitants are invited by their general practitioner to take part, receive a baseline individual health profile from research nurses, and are followed up through continuous linkage with the general practitioners' electronic medical records.")

