# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18502301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3095685/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK-resident subjects with Type 2 diabetes (n = 892) were recruited to the UKADS from Birmingham and Coventry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493> "A study of patients with type 2 diabetes in general practices in Birmingham and Coventry, United Kingdom, carried out in 2004-2007, made up of a community-based cluster randomised controlled trial of a culturally sensitive enhanced care package for patients of south Asian origin and a parallel cohort study of cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian and white European patients; its south Asian participants have also contributed to genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18502301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4060842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EuroQol EQ-5D measure was administered to 1,978 patients with type 2 diabetes in the UK Asian Diabetes Study (UKADS): 1,486 of south Asian origin (Indian, Pakistani, Bangladeshi or other south Asian) and 492 of white European origin.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493> "A study of patients with type 2 diabetes in general practices in Birmingham and Coventry, United Kingdom, carried out in 2004-2007, made up of a community-based cluster randomised controlled trial of a culturally sensitive enhanced care package for patients of south Asian origin and a parallel cohort study of cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian and white European patients; its south Asian participants have also contributed to genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18502301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4060842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main study, carried out in 2004–2007, recruited a total of 1486 south Asian and 492 white European patients from 25 general practices in Birmingham (16 practices) and Coventry (9 practices).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493> "A study of patients with type 2 diabetes in general practices in Birmingham and Coventry, United Kingdom, carried out in 2004-2007, made up of a community-based cluster randomised controlled trial of a culturally sensitive enhanced care package for patients of south Asian origin and a parallel cohort study of cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian and white European patients; its south Asian participants have also contributed to genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18502301") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21294771") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24902492") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4060842/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a community-based, cluster randomized controlled trial that evaluated the effectiveness of a culturally sensitive enhanced care package in UK general practice in improving cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian patients with type 2 diabetes, plus a parallel cohort study of cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian and white European patients with type 2 diabetes[3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002493> "A study of patients with type 2 diabetes in general practices in Birmingham and Coventry, United Kingdom, carried out in 2004-2007, made up of a community-based cluster randomised controlled trial of a culturally sensitive enhanced care package for patients of south Asian origin and a parallel cohort study of cardiovascular risk factors in south Asian and white European patients; its south Asian participants have also contributed to genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were ascertained from regional cancer registries and directly from consultants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> "A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Generations Study (UK-GS) is a long-term prospective cohort study of breast cancer aetiology involving >113,000 women from the UK, recruited between 2003 and 2013 (4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> "A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MBCS controls were from two sources – male non-blood relatives of cases, and male spouses of women taking part in the UK-GS (described below).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> "A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Potential cases were all men resident in England and Wales with invasive or in situ breast cancer diagnosed at ages 18-79 since 1st January 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> "A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32785646") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8023850/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK-BCN-MBCS is a national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales that was established at the Institute of Cancer Research (ICR), London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men and to illuminate, from a novel angle, aetiology in women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002494> "A national population-based case-control study of male breast cancer in England and Wales, set up at the Institute of Cancer Research, London, in 2007 to investigate the aetiology of breast cancer in men, whose cases are men resident in England and Wales diagnosed with invasive or in situ breast cancer at ages 18–79 from 2005 onwards, found through regional cancer registries and consultants, and whose controls are male non-blood relatives of cases and male spouses of women in the Generations Study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4593935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the UK Biobank Lung Exome Variant Evaluation (UK BiLEVE) study, we undertook nested case-control studies in individuals of European ancestry from UK Biobank") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4593935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sampling was undertaken such that equal numbers of males and females were selected in total and the numbers of individuals selected from each age–sex band were proportional to the number of individuals in the band being sampled (appendix pp 3–5).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4593935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We report new loci associated with extremes of FEV1 and COPD, including evidence that a genomic region of complex structural variation has an effect on lung function and airflow obstruction in the general population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4593935/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We undertook genome-wide genotyping of variants using a new custom Affymetrix Axiom array (UK BiLEVE array; Santa Clara, CA, USA; appendix pp 5–8)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26423011+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We sampled individuals of European ancestry from UK Biobank, from the middle and extremes of the forced expiratory volume in 1 s (FEV1) distribution among heavy smokers (mean 35 pack-years) and never smokers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28166215") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30305743") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26423011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26423011+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used UK Biobank data to study the genetic causes of smoking behaviour and lung health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002495> "A sub-cohort of UK Biobank participants of European ancestry chosen from the middle and the extremes of the distribution of forced expiratory volume in 1 second among heavy smokers and among never smokers, sampled equally by sex, for nested case-control studies of the genetics of lung function, smoking behaviour and chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and genotyped on the custom UK BiLEVE Axiom array.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29551738") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2796/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2796_MOESM2_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK-wide excluding Northern Ireland (UK Gene Study) 0 759 0 759 759") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496> "A United Kingdom study, funded by a Medical Research Council programme grant, of people with Barrett's oesophagus identified at endoscopy with a histopathologically confirmed diagnosis of intestinal metaplasia and recruited across the UK excluding Northern Ireland, whose cases have been used in genetic association studies of Barrett's oesophagus and oesophageal adenocarcinoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29551738") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3840115/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "87 were genotyped in 874 histologically confirmed esophageal adenocarcinoma cases from the Stomach and Oesophageal Cancer Study (SOCS), 759 histologically confirmed Barrett’s esophagus cases from the UK Barrett’s Oesophagus Gene Study (UK Gene Study)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496> "A United Kingdom study, funded by a Medical Research Council programme grant, of people with Barrett's oesophagus identified at endoscopy with a histopathologically confirmed diagnosis of intestinal metaplasia and recruited across the UK excluding Northern Ireland, whose cases have been used in genetic association studies of Barrett's oesophagus and oesophageal adenocarcinoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29551738") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3840115/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Barrett’s esophagus cases were identified at endoscopy with a confirmed histopathological diagnosis of intestinal metaplasia from the UK Barrett’s Oesophagus Gene Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496> "A United Kingdom study, funded by a Medical Research Council programme grant, of people with Barrett's oesophagus identified at endoscopy with a histopathologically confirmed diagnosis of intestinal metaplasia and recruited across the UK excluding Northern Ireland, whose cases have been used in genetic association studies of Barrett's oesophagus and oesophageal adenocarcinoma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29551738") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24121790") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3840115/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Barrett’s oesophagus gene study was funded by a Medical Research Council Programme grant, the UK SOCS study was funded by CRUK as well as funding from the Cambridge NIHR biomedical research centre and the Cambridge Experimental Cancer Medicine Centre.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002496> "A United Kingdom study, funded by a Medical Research Council programme grant, of people with Barrett's oesophagus identified at endoscopy with a histopathologically confirmed diagnosis of intestinal metaplasia and recruited across the UK excluding Northern Ireland, whose cases have been used in genetic association studies of Barrett's oesophagus and oesophageal adenocarcinoma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17971770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18022173+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A multicenter, randomized, double-blind trial of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folate supplements (0.5 mg/day) to prevent colorectal adenoma recurrence was performed using a 2 x 2 factorial design.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in the United Kingdom and Denmark of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folic acid (0.5 mg/day) in a 2 x 2 factorial design for the prevention of colorectal adenoma recurrence, in patients who had had a colorectal adenoma removed in the six months before recruitment and who were followed up with a second colonoscopy after about three years; DNA from its participants has been used in genetic studies of adenoma risk and recurrence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17971770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18022173+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All patients had an adenoma (>/=0.5 cm) removed in the 6 months before recruitment and were followed-up at 4-month intervals with a second colonoscopy after approximately 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in the United Kingdom and Denmark of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folic acid (0.5 mg/day) in a 2 x 2 factorial design for the prevention of colorectal adenoma recurrence, in patients who had had a colorectal adenoma removed in the six months before recruitment and who were followed up with a second colonoscopy after about three years; DNA from its participants has been used in genetic studies of adenoma risk and recurrence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17971770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18413818") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A18413818+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We genotyped ODC G316A in 546 individuals in the United Kingdom Colorectal Adenoma Prevention trial of aspirin for CRA recurrence prevention and pooled our findings with data from two other randomized intervention trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in the United Kingdom and Denmark of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folic acid (0.5 mg/day) in a 2 x 2 factorial design for the prevention of colorectal adenoma recurrence, in patients who had had a colorectal adenoma removed in the six months before recruitment and who were followed up with a second colonoscopy after about three years; DNA from its participants has been used in genetic studies of adenoma risk and recurrence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17971770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37965303") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the ukCAP trial (Logan et al., 2008), participants were randomised to 500 μg/day folic acid versus placebo (with or without 300 mg aspirin/day) for 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in the United Kingdom and Denmark of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folic acid (0.5 mg/day) in a 2 x 2 factorial design for the prevention of colorectal adenoma recurrence, in patients who had had a colorectal adenoma removed in the six months before recruitment and who were followed up with a second colonoscopy after about three years; DNA from its participants has been used in genetic studies of adenoma risk and recurrence.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17971770") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18022173") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37965303") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10641704/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three studies were conducted in the US (AFPPS, NHS/HPFS and the trial by Jaszewski et al.) and one in the UK and Denmark (UkCAP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002498> "A multicentre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in the United Kingdom and Denmark of aspirin (300 mg/day) and folic acid (0.5 mg/day) in a 2 x 2 factorial design for the prevention of colorectal adenoma recurrence, in patients who had had a colorectal adenoma removed in the six months before recruitment and who were followed up with a second colonoscopy after about three years; DNA from its participants has been used in genetic studies of adenoma risk and recurrence.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.nature.com/articles/ng.2843") Annotation(rdfs:comment "International CLL Linkage Consortium (ICLLLC)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5253627/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "292 cases collected through the Newcastle CLL Consortium (181 male; mean age at diagnosis: 66 years) from patients attending six haematology units in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5253627/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CLL-UK2 comprised 1,403 cases collected from two ongoing initiatives: (i) 1,111 cases collected through a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the ICR") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5253627/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the UK controls, we used publicly accessible data generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium (WTCCC), the 1958 Birth Cohort (also known as the National Child Development Study) and UK Blood Service76.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5253627/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CLL-UK1 GWAS comprised 517 cases: (i) 155 cases (95 male; mean age at diagnosis: 59 years) from ICLLLC; and (ii) 362 cases (269 male; mean age at diagnosis: 63 years) from the Leukaemia Research CLL-4 trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24292274") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28165464") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28112199") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5253627/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls comprise of the WTCCC 1958 Birth Cohort (1958BC) and National Blood Service (NBS) which are split between UK-CLL1 and UK-CLL2 respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002499> "An aggregation of the two UK case-control genome-wide association studies of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia led by the Institute of Cancer Research: UK-CLL-1, whose cases came from the International CLL Linkage Consortium and the Leukaemia Research Fund CLL4 trial, and UK-CLL-2, whose cases came from a UK national study of CLL genetics coordinated by the Institute of Cancer Research and from the Newcastle CLL Consortium, using publicly available genotypes of UK controls generated by the Wellcome Trust Case Control Consortium, with 1958 Birth Cohort controls for UK-CLL-1 and UK Blood Service controls for UK-CLL-2.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002500> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002500>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.424/MediaObjects/41588_2009_BFng424_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UK Colorectal control NSCR UK Population based - 917") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002500> "A set of population-based controls from the United Kingdom, taken from a national colorectal cancer genetics study and genotyped on the Illumina HumanHap550 array for a colorectal cancer genome-wide association study, whose existing genotypes were reused as controls in the first stage of an ovarian cancer genome-wide association study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19011631") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC2844110/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Existing data from two sets of controls, genotyped on the Infinium 550k array, were used in stage 1 analyses: the Welcome Trust Case-Control Consortium 1958 birth cohort, and a national colorectal control study using Illumina platform Hap550 array.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002500> "A set of population-based controls from the United Kingdom, taken from a national colorectal cancer genetics study and genotyped on the Illumina HumanHap550 array for a colorectal cancer genome-wide association study, whose existing genotypes were reused as controls in the first stage of an ovarian cancer genome-wide association study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4106467/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For Stage 2 replication, we directly genotyped 3 lead SNPs representing 2 top novel independent (r2<0.25) association signals (CSNK2A2 and FER) in a UK CVD cohort available with RTL measures on 2,952 MI patients and healthy controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It comprises of 1014 subjects consecutively recruited from the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals in 2001–2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The European Atherosclerosis Research Study (EARS) II was undertaken to compare postprandial responses (oral glucose tolerance test [OGTT] and oral fat tolerance test [OFTT]) of male case subjects (n=407) between 18 and 28 years old whose father had a proven myocardial infarction before the age of 55 years and male control subjects (n=415) who were age‐matched and were recruited irrespective of family history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HIFMECH study comprises Caucasian male survivors of a first MI aged <60 years (excluding patients with FH and insulin‐dependent diabetes mellitus) and population‐based individuals of the same age and region recruited from four centres in Europe: Stockholm, Sweden and London, England for the North and Marseille, France and San Giovanni Retondo, Italy representing the South [1].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Simon Broome study is a cross‐sectional study comprising 410 Caucasian patients with treated heterozygous FH aged 18 years recruited from 6 lipid clinics in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24795349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/instance/4106467/bin/NIHMS595180-supplement-000412_-_Supplemental_Material.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UDACS is a cross‐sectional sample of diabetes patients designed to study the association between common genetic variants and biochemical risk factors implicated in coronary heart disease (CHD) in patients with diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002502> "A pooled sample of four European cardiovascular studies with leukocyte telomere length measures: the HIFMECH study (male survivors of a first myocardial infarction and population controls from four centres in Sweden, England, France and Italy), the Simon Broome study (patients with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia from six UK lipid clinics), the University College London Diabetes and Cardiovascular disease Study (UDACS, patients of the diabetes clinic at UCL Hospitals) and the European Atherosclerosis Research Study II (young men whose fathers had a myocardial infarction before the age of 55, and age-matched controls). Under this name its 2,952 myocardial infarction patients and healthy controls of European ancestry were the Stage 2 replication sample of a 2014 genome-wide association study of leukocyte telomere length in Punjabi Sikhs.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It has collected information from a large number of families where at least 2 people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment start: 01/08/1991 Recruitment end: 30/09/2009") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Supported by Cancer Research UKExperimental Cancer Medicine Centre (ECMC)University of Cambridge") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The general aim of the study was to look at familial factors that might be important in increasing the risk of ovarian cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The researchers collected medical information and family history details. They also collected blood and tissue samples from some of the people who took part.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19648919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://web.archive.org/web/20230402084624/https://www.cancerresearchuk.org/about-cancer/find-a-clinical-trial/a-study-looking-at-family-history-and-ovarian-cancer") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study started in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer. It later became the UK Familial Ovarian Cancer Register (FOCR).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002504> "A register of families in the United Kingdom in which at least two people have been diagnosed with ovarian cancer, begun in 1991 as the UKCCCR study of familial ovarian cancer and supported by Cancer Research UK and the University of Cambridge, which recruited until 2009 and collected medical information, family histories and, from some members, blood and tissue samples to study familial risk factors for ovarian cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16968788+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PATIENTS/OUTCOME MEASURES: We prospectively collected clinical/biochemical data as part of the protocol for a United Kingdom DNA collection for GD and HT.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> "The patients with Graves' disease of the United Kingdom's national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves' disease or Hashimoto's thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves' disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves' disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A16968788+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated, in 2805 Caucasian subjects, whether age at diagnosis, gender, family history (FH), smoking history, and presence of goiter influenced disease manifestations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> "The patients with Graves' disease of the United Kingdom's national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves' disease or Hashimoto's thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves' disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves' disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC2680141") Annotation(rdfs:comment "AITD national DNA collection of index cases and family members from centres including Birmingham, Bournemouth, Cambridge, Cardiff, Exeter, Leeds, Newcastle and Sheffield.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> "The patients with Graves' disease of the United Kingdom's national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves' disease or Hashimoto's thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves' disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves' disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3937134/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the Graves' disease analyses, cases were recruited from the United Kingdom Graves' disease cohort and controls from the British 1958 Birth Cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> "The patients with Graves' disease of the United Kingdom's national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves' disease or Hashimoto's thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves' disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves' disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16968788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17952073") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24586183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3937134/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Graves' disease cohort was funded by the Wellcome Trust grant 068181.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002505> "The patients with Graves' disease of the United Kingdom's national DNA collection for autoimmune thyroid disease (the AITD National Collection), a multicentre collection of Caucasian patients with Graves' disease or Hashimoto's thyroiditis and their family members, recruited at hospitals across the United Kingdom with clinical and biochemical data collected prospectively under a common protocol and funded by the Wellcome Trust. Its Graves' disease patients have served as cases in genetic association studies of Graves' disease, analysed against British 1958 Birth Cohort controls.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6517433/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the UK Genetic Prostate Cancer Study (UKGPCS) (age <65 years), a study conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> "A multi-institutional, longitudinal observational study of prostate cancer in the United Kingdom, conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust, that since 1992 has recruited men with histologically confirmed prostate cancer in a population-based arm and in arms enriched for young age at onset or a family history of the disease, together with cancer-free men from its clinics as controls, collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data to study inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9928632/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Genetic Prostate Cancer Study (UKGPCS)42 recruited individuals with histologically confirmed PCa in three arms: a population-based arm that recruited men independent of age or FH, and arms enriched for young-age-at-onset PCa or PCa FH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> "A multi-institutional, longitudinal observational study of prostate cancer in the United Kingdom, conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust, that since 1992 has recruited men with histologically confirmed prostate cancer in a population-based arm and in arms enriched for young age at onset or a family history of the disease, together with cancer-free men from its clinics as controls, collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data to study inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9928632/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used complex segregation analysis to fit genetic models for the observed cancer inheritance patterns in UKGPCS families.51") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> "A multi-institutional, longitudinal observational study of prostate cancer in the United Kingdom, conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust, that since 1992 has recruited men with histologically confirmed prostate cancer in a population-based arm and in arms enriched for young age at onset or a family history of the disease, together with cancer-free men from its clinics as controls, collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data to study inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9928632/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "from (1) men without PCa personal or FH recruited through UKGPCS participating clinics, and (2) ProtecT trial participants with PSA < 0.5 ng/mL.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> "A multi-institutional, longitudinal observational study of prostate cancer in the United Kingdom, conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust, that since 1992 has recruited men with histologically confirmed prostate cancer in a population-based arm and in arms enriched for young age at onset or a family history of the disease, together with cancer-free men from its clinics as controls, collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data to study inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31089142") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36493335") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36528478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36528478+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Genetic Prostate Cancer Study is a longitudinal, multi-institutional, observational study collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data since 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002506> "A multi-institutional, longitudinal observational study of prostate cancer in the United Kingdom, conducted through the Royal Marsden NHS Foundation Trust, that since 1992 has recruited men with histologically confirmed prostate cancer in a population-based arm and in arms enriched for young age at onset or a family history of the disease, together with cancer-free men from its clinics as controls, collecting baseline and follow-up clinical data to study inherited susceptibility to prostate cancer and its outcomes.")

