AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5289481/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "10,484 population control samples genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.0 were obtained from the Understanding Society Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002508> "A genome-wide association study sample of the UK IBD Genetics Consortium, analysed in a 2017 genome-wide association study of inflammatory bowel disease: British patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosed by accepted endoscopic, histopathological and radiological criteria and genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.1, with population controls from the Understanding Society project (the UK Household Longitudinal Study) genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5289481/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After quality control, data were available for 4,474 Crohn’s disease, 4,173 ulcerative colitis, 592 IBD-unclassified cases and 9,500 controls for 296,203 variants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002508> "A genome-wide association study sample of the UK IBD Genetics Consortium, analysed in a 2017 genome-wide association study of inflammatory bowel disease: British patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosed by accepted endoscopic, histopathological and radiological criteria and genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.1, with population controls from the Understanding Society project (the UK Household Longitudinal Study) genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5289481/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Following ethical approval by Cambridge MREC (reference: 03/5/012), 11,768 British IBD cases, diagnosed using accepted endoscopic, histopathological and radiological criteria, were consented into the study and genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002508> "A genome-wide association study sample of the UK IBD Genetics Consortium, analysed in a 2017 genome-wide association study of inflammatory bowel disease: British patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosed by accepted endoscopic, histopathological and radiological criteria and genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.1, with population controls from the Understanding Society project (the UK Household Longitudinal Study) genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.0.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28067908") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5289481/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Household Longitudinal Study is led by the Institute for Social and Economic Research at the University of Essex and funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002508> "A genome-wide association study sample of the UK IBD Genetics Consortium, analysed in a 2017 genome-wide association study of inflammatory bowel disease: British patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis or unclassified inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosed by accepted endoscopic, histopathological and radiological criteria and genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.1, with population controls from the Understanding Society project (the UK Household Longitudinal Study) genotyped on the Human Core Exome v12.0.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2564/MediaObjects/41588_2013_BFng2564_MOESM8_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "United Kingdom Ovarian Cancer Population Study UKO United Kingdom (England, Wales and Northern Ireland) Population based/ Case-‐control 718 1123 98.1 702(353)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases Women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer who are about to undergo surgery Women with a confirmed diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer Women with a probable diagnosis of primary invasive ovarian cancer who are not undergoing surgery") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls Women with a possible benign or borderline adnexal mass who are about to undergo surgery Apparently healthy women recruited from the Multimodal arm of UKCTOCS when they attend for annual screening") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The effort through UKOPS has been to identify novel markers that could aid CA125.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UKOPS has contributed to the international Ovarian Cancer Association Consortium (OCAC), an amalgamation of 47 groups from around the world and identified several of these factors that only increase the risks marginally compared to the BRCA1/2 mutations in the women at ‘high risk’ to answer the question ‘Why do some women develop ovarian cancer and not others?”.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23513043") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/ukops") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UKOPS is exploring which symptoms or medical complaints are common in women with ovarian cancer when compared to women who do not have the disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002511> "A population-based case-control study of ovarian cancer run from University College London at hospitals in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, whose cases are women with an adnexal mass suspicious of ovarian cancer about to undergo surgery or with a confirmed or probable diagnosis of primary invasive or borderline ovarian cancer, and whose controls are women with a possibly benign or borderline adnexal mass and apparently healthy women from the multimodal screening arm of UKCTOCS, set up to find genetic risk factors, markers to add to CA125 and early symptoms of ovarian cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1778353+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the main randomisation, those who were asymptomatic and had fasting plasma glucose under 15 mmol/l were allocated either to diet policy, or to active policy with either insulin or sulphonylurea aiming to reduce the fasting plasma glucose to under 6 mmol/l.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1778353+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Newly presenting Type 2 diabetic patients aged 25-65 years inclusive, median age 53 years, median body mass index 28 kg/m2 and median fasting plasma glucose 11.3 mmol/l, were recruited and treated initially by diet.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1778353+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hypertension in Diabetes Study has been included in a factorial design to assess whether improved blood pressure control will be advantageous. Patients with blood pressure greater than or equal to 160/90 mm Hg were randomly allocated to tight control aiming for less than 150/85 mm Hg with either an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor or a Beta-blocker or to less tight control") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A1778353+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UK Prospective Diabetes Study (UKPDS) is a multi-centre, prospective, randomised, intervention trial of 5100 newly-diagnosed patients with Type 2 (non-insulin-dependent) diabetes mellitus which aims to determine whether improved blood glucose control will prevent complications and reduce the associated morbidity and mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12140635/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, those who were overweight and randomized to the metformin arm had a reduced risk for any diabetes-related endpoint, diabetes-related death and all-cause mortality compared with those allocated to conventional therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:1778353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9742976") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40485651") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12140635/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study commenced in 1977 and included 600 patients in a pilot phase in five centres.2 By 1987, the study had expanded to 23 centres (15 centres in Glucose Study I and 8 in Glucose Study II), enrolling a total of 5,102 participants.3") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002512> "A multicentre randomised intervention trial in the United Kingdom, begun in 1977 and expanded to 23 centres by 1987, of patients aged 25–65 years with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes, who after initial diet treatment were randomly allocated to intensive blood-glucose control (with a sulphonylurea or insulin, or metformin for overweight patients) or to conventional diet-based treatment, with the Hypertension in Diabetes Study nested in a factorial design comparing tight with less tight blood-pressure control; its participants were followed for diabetic complications and death for decades after the intervention ended.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002513> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002513>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17982455") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20852893") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17982455") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2007.32/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng200732_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All other cases were recruited from NHS Rheumatology Clinics throughout the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002513> "A collection of adult patients with rheumatoid arthritis fulfilling the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, and of healthy controls, assembled for genetic studies by the UK Rheumatoid Arthritis Genetics consortium, a collaboration of six UK rheumatology research groups. Cases were recruited in Manchester, Aberdeen, Leeds, Sheffield, London and Oxford, mostly from NHS rheumatology clinics but also from the Arthritis Research Campaign National Repository of Family Material and the Norfolk Arthritis Register, and controls in five of these centres; its samples were used to replicate and extend rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility loci from genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17982455") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19898481") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20852893") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17982455") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2007.32/MediaObjects/41588_2007_BFng200732_MOESM20_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA from RA patients, over 18 years old and satisfying the American College of Rheumatology criteria for RA1 was available from 6 centres in the UK and 5 of these centres also provided DNA samples from healthy controls:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002513> "A collection of adult patients with rheumatoid arthritis fulfilling the 1987 American College of Rheumatology criteria, and of healthy controls, assembled for genetic studies by the UK Rheumatoid Arthritis Genetics consortium, a collaboration of six UK rheumatology research groups. Cases were recruited in Manchester, Aberdeen, Leeds, Sheffield, London and Oxford, mostly from NHS rheumatology clinics but also from the Arthritis Research Campaign National Repository of Family Material and the Norfolk Arthritis Register, and controls in five of these centres; its samples were used to replicate and extend rheumatoid arthritis susceptibility loci from genome-wide association studies.")
