AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4930126/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We obtained their Illumina HumanOmni2.5 genotypes, FTND scores and other phenotypic data via dbGaP accession number phs000404.v1.p1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002536> "A randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation trial of the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center, run at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention with participants recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States, in which adults who smoked 10 or more cigarettes a day and were motivated to quit were randomly assigned to placebo, nicotine patch, nicotine lozenge, sustained-release bupropion or a combination, and whose genotyped participants are used in genetic studies of nicotine dependence and smoking cessation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9575976/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each participant was randomly assigned to one of the six conditions: (1) placebo, (2) nicotine patch, (3) nicotine lozenge, (4) sustained-release bupropion, (5) nicotine patch and nicotine lozenge (combination nicotine replacement [C-NRT]), or (6) bupropion and nicotine lozenge.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002536> "A randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation trial of the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center, run at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention with participants recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States, in which adults who smoked 10 or more cigarettes a day and were motivated to quit were randomly assigned to placebo, nicotine patch, nicotine lozenge, sustained-release bupropion or a combination, and whose genotyped participants are used in genetic studies of nicotine dependence and smoking cessation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9575976/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TTURC participants were genotyped at the Center for Inherited Disease Research at Johns Hopkins University using the Illumina Omni2.5 microarray.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002536> "A randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation trial of the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center, run at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention with participants recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States, in which adults who smoked 10 or more cigarettes a day and were motivated to quit were randomly assigned to placebo, nicotine patch, nicotine lozenge, sustained-release bupropion or a combination, and whose genotyped participants are used in genetic studies of nicotine dependence and smoking cessation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9575976/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The TTURC study is a randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation clinical trial at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention focusing on the genetic association of time to relapse after quitting.13") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002536> "A randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation trial of the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center, run at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention with participants recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States, in which adults who smoked 10 or more cigarettes a day and were motivated to quit were randomly assigned to placebo, nicotine patch, nicotine lozenge, sustained-release bupropion or a combination, and whose genotyped participants are used in genetic studies of nicotine dependence and smoking cessation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26440539") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35170738") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3433845/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were eligible to participate if they were 18 years of age or older, smoked 10 or more cigarettes per day, and were motivated to quit smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002536> "A randomized, placebo-controlled smoking cessation trial of the University of Wisconsin Transdisciplinary Tobacco Use Research Center, run at the University of Wisconsin Center for Tobacco Research and Intervention with participants recruited in Madison and Milwaukee, Wisconsin, United States, in which adults who smoked 10 or more cigarettes a day and were motivated to quit were randomly assigned to placebo, nicotine patch, nicotine lozenge, sustained-release bupropion or a combination, and whose genotyped participants are used in genetic studies of nicotine dependence and smoking cessation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39715278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8387688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biological samples of study participants were stored at the Eurac Research Biobank (ERB) at the Bolzano-Bozen Hospital, Italy, as described in the Supplementary Material page 7.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537> "A population-based SARS-CoV-2 study in the Gardena valley (Val Gardena/Gröden) of South Tyrol, Italy, one of the areas most afflicted early in the COVID-19 pandemic, that invited a random sample of the inhabitants of its main municipalities (Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva), stratified by municipality, sex and age group, to answer a questionnaire and undergo a nasopharyngeal swab test and a serological antibody test between 26 May and 8 June 2020, towards the end of the first wave, and stored their biological samples at the Eurac Research Biobank; funded by the Healthcare System of the Autonomous Province of Bolzano/Bozen, it later contributed genotyped participants to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative and participants with confirmed infection to a whole-genome sequencing study of COVID-19 host genetics built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39715278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8387688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the initial phase of the SARS-CoV-2 pandemic, the Gardena valley, a well-known winter tourism destination located in South Tyrol (Italy), became one of the European regions most afflicted by the coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537> "A population-based SARS-CoV-2 study in the Gardena valley (Val Gardena/Gröden) of South Tyrol, Italy, one of the areas most afflicted early in the COVID-19 pandemic, that invited a random sample of the inhabitants of its main municipalities (Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva), stratified by municipality, sex and age group, to answer a questionnaire and undergo a nasopharyngeal swab test and a serological antibody test between 26 May and 8 June 2020, towards the end of the first wave, and stored their biological samples at the Eurac Research Biobank; funded by the Healthcare System of the Autonomous Province of Bolzano/Bozen, it later contributed genotyped participants to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative and participants with confirmed infection to a whole-genome sequencing study of COVID-19 host genetics built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39715278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8387688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Invited to the study were 2958 of the 9424 inhabitants of Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva, the main municipalities of the Gardena valley, following a one-stage random sampling design stratified by municipality, sex and age group (<6, 6–17, 18–34, 35–49, 50–64, 65+ years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537> "A population-based SARS-CoV-2 study in the Gardena valley (Val Gardena/Gröden) of South Tyrol, Italy, one of the areas most afflicted early in the COVID-19 pandemic, that invited a random sample of the inhabitants of its main municipalities (Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva), stratified by municipality, sex and age group, to answer a questionnaire and undergo a nasopharyngeal swab test and a serological antibody test between 26 May and 8 June 2020, towards the end of the first wave, and stored their biological samples at the Eurac Research Biobank; funded by the Healthcare System of the Autonomous Province of Bolzano/Bozen, it later contributed genotyped participants to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative and participants with confirmed infection to a whole-genome sequencing study of COVID-19 host genetics built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34237774") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39715278") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34645534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8387688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were invited via letter including the planned participation date; a link to the online questionnaire (with telephone support) covering demographic, clinical and socio-behavioural aspects (Supplementary Material page 2); a personalised password for use as pseudo-anonymisation code.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002537> "A population-based SARS-CoV-2 study in the Gardena valley (Val Gardena/Gröden) of South Tyrol, Italy, one of the areas most afflicted early in the COVID-19 pandemic, that invited a random sample of the inhabitants of its main municipalities (Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva), stratified by municipality, sex and age group, to answer a questionnaire and undergo a nasopharyngeal swab test and a serological antibody test between 26 May and 8 June 2020, towards the end of the first wave, and stored their biological samples at the Eurac Research Biobank; funded by the Healthcare System of the Autonomous Province of Bolzano/Bozen, it later contributed genotyped participants to the COVID-19 Host Genetics Initiative and participants with confirmed infection to a whole-genome sequencing study of COVID-19 host genetics built on the German COVID-19 Omics Initiative.")
