# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5085288/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Anthropometrics were obtained by physical examination, questionnaires, and interviews at the time of inclusion into the Biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> "A regional diabetes case-control biobank in Vejle, Denmark, established from 2007 to 2010, holding blood, DNA and urine samples and examination, questionnaire and interview data from patients with diabetes and an age- and sex-matched control population aged 25 to 75, linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, National Patient Registry and National Prescription Registry, for studies of the causes of diabetes and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5085288/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Behind the idea of establishing the Vejle Diabetes Biobank was an intention to increase the etiological knowledge about T2D and its comorbidities and to enhance the quality of diabetes care on the population level as well as for the individual patient.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> "A regional diabetes case-control biobank in Vejle, Denmark, established from 2007 to 2010, holding blood, DNA and urine samples and examination, questionnaire and interview data from patients with diabetes and an age- and sex-matched control population aged 25 to 75, linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, National Patient Registry and National Prescription Registry, for studies of the causes of diabetes and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5085288/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vejle Diabetes Biobank was established from 2007 to 2010 as a regional Biobank containing blood, DNA, and urine samples from patients with diabetes and a gender- and age-matched control population aged 25–75 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> "A regional diabetes case-control biobank in Vejle, Denmark, established from 2007 to 2010, holding blood, DNA and urine samples and examination, questionnaire and interview data from patients with diabetes and an age- and sex-matched control population aged 25 to 75, linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, National Patient Registry and National Prescription Registry, for studies of the causes of diabetes and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5085288/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort was linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, the Danish National Patient Registry, and the Danish National Prescription Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> "A regional diabetes case-control biobank in Vejle, Denmark, established from 2007 to 2010, holding blood, DNA and urine samples and examination, questionnaire and interview data from patients with diabetes and an age- and sex-matched control population aged 25 to 75, linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, National Patient Registry and National Prescription Registry, for studies of the causes of diabetes and its comorbidities.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27799821") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5085288/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The individuals for the control cohort were selected by the Danish Civil Registration System from the background population of the former County of Vejle, Denmark (n=360,921).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002542> "A regional diabetes case-control biobank in Vejle, Denmark, established from 2007 to 2010, holding blood, DNA and urine samples and examination, questionnaire and interview data from patients with diabetes and an age- and sex-matched control population aged 25 to 75, linked to the Danish Civil Registration System, National Patient Registry and National Prescription Registry, for studies of the causes of diabetes and its comorbidities.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2364177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A population-based, statewide study on diagnostic delay and late stage diagnosis was conducted among patients with various forms of cancer in Saarland, a state with about 1 million inhabitants in Western Germany (Verlauf der diagnostischen Abklärung, VERDI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2364177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the purpose of this study, all women aged 18 to 80 years who were residents of the state of Saarland with primary, symptomatic and invasive breast cancer of any histological type, diagnosed between 1 October, 1996 and 28 February, 1998, were eligible.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2364177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The interviews contained detailed questions concerning disease history from first complaint to definite diagnosis, general health status, health practices, availability of health services, social network and socio-economic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2364177/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Treating gynaecologists, surgeons, oncologists and radio-therapists from all hospitals in Saarland and all adjacent counties identified potential study participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4853774/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Gastric cancer cases included in the validation set were recruited in the context of the ESTHER II study and the VERDI study19,20.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11953844") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27140836") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30510241") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0286-6/MediaObjects/41588_2018_286_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ESTHER_VERDI | Epidemiologische Studie zu Chancen der Verhütung, Früherkennung und optimierten Therapie chronischer Erkrankungen in der älteren Bevölkerung; Verlauf der diagnotischen Abklärung bei Krebspatienten | case-control | Germany") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002544> "A population-based, statewide study of patients with newly diagnosed cancers of various sites in Saarland, Germany, identified in the late 1990s by their treating physicians at the hospitals of Saarland and adjacent counties and interviewed about the diagnostic process, to study diagnostic delay and late-stage diagnosis; conducted by epidemiologists of the University of Ulm and the German Centre for Research on Ageing with the Saarland Cancer Registry. It is distinct from the ESTHER cohort, with which consortia pool it as ESTHER/VERDI.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37173335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23544013") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3609646/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Studies by the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) have shown that a subset of common alleles influencing breast and ovarian cancer risk in the general population are also associated with cancer risk in BRCA1 mutation carriers [5]–[11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545> "A cancer clinic-based study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants in Victoria, Australia, assembled by the Victorian Familial Cancer Trials Group under the ethics approval of the Peter MacCallum Cancer Centre, which contributes carriers to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of breast and ovarian cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37173335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37173335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10182045/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Victorian Familial Cancer Trials GroupVFCTGAustraliaCancer clinic-based studyPeter MacCallum Cancer Centre Ethics CommitteeIRBa6752") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545> "A cancer clinic-based study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants in Victoria, Australia, assembled by the Victorian Familial Cancer Trials Group under the ethics approval of the Peter MacCallum Cancer Centre, which contributes carriers to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of breast and ovarian cancer risk.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28448241") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37173335") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37173335") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10182045/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed the PREDICT v 2.2 for prognosis of breast cancer patients with pathogenic germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants, using follow-up data from 5453 BRCA1/2 carriers from the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) and the Breast Cancer Association Consortium (BCAC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002545> "A cancer clinic-based study of carriers of pathogenic BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants in Victoria, Australia, assembled by the Victorian Familial Cancer Trials Group under the ethics approval of the Peter MacCallum Cancer Centre, which contributes carriers to the Consortium of Investigators of Modifiers of BRCA1/2 (CIMBA) for studies of genetic modifiers of breast and ovarian cancer risk.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2211406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was performed within the framework of the Verona Heart Project, a regional survey aimed to search for new risk factors for CAD and MI in subjects with objective angiographic documentation of their coronary vessels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> "An ongoing regional study at the university hospital of Verona, Italy, of adults from the Verona district who underwent coronary angiography, comprising patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and coronary artery disease-free subjects angiographed for other reasons (mainly valvular heart disease), with cross-sectional and prospective designs, to search for new risk factors for coronary artery disease and myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6497332/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1020 patients (723 men and 297 women) who lived in the District of Verona and for whom prospective data were available were included in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> "An ongoing regional study at the university hospital of Verona, Italy, of adults from the Verona district who underwent coronary angiography, comprising patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and coronary artery disease-free subjects angiographed for other reasons (mainly valvular heart disease), with cross-sectional and prospective designs, to search for new risk factors for coronary artery disease and myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6497332/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "On the basis of an angiographic evaluation, the patients were classified as CAD‐free (n=213, individuals who underwent coronary angiography for reasons other than suspected CAD, primarily valvular heart disease) and patients with CAD") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> "An ongoing regional study at the university hospital of Verona, Italy, of adults from the Verona district who underwent coronary angiography, comprising patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and coronary artery disease-free subjects angiographed for other reasons (mainly valvular heart disease), with cross-sectional and prospective designs, to search for new risk factors for coronary artery disease and myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6497332/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VHS is an ongoing survey that uses cross‐sectional and prospective designs aimed to search for new risk factors for CAD in patients using objective, angiographic documentation of their coronary vessels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> "An ongoing regional study at the university hospital of Verona, Italy, of adults from the Verona district who underwent coronary angiography, comprising patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and coronary artery disease-free subjects angiographed for other reasons (mainly valvular heart disease), with cross-sectional and prospective designs, to search for new risk factors for coronary artery disease and myocardial infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18253477") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30646800") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6497332/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ethics committee of our institution (Azienda Ospedaliera Universitaria Integrata, Verona, Italy) approved the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002546> "An ongoing regional study at the university hospital of Verona, Italy, of adults from the Verona district who underwent coronary angiography, comprising patients with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and coronary artery disease-free subjects angiographed for other reasons (mainly valvular heart disease), with cross-sectional and prospective designs, to search for new risk factors for coronary artery disease and myocardial infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20837956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completion of adjuvant therapy for stage II and III CRC were randomly assigned to receive rofecoxib (20 mg daily) or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20837956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of this study was to test whether the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib could reduce recurrence and improve survival when administered in the adjuvant setting of colorectal cancer (CRC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20837956+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial was terminated early because of the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.670/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng670_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VICTOR, post-treatment stage of a Phase III, randomised controlled trial of rofecoxib (VIOXX) in colorectal cancer patients after potentially curative therapy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5098601/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These trials recruited patients from throughout the United Kingdom.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20837956") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972440") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24062397") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22634755") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4747430/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VQ58 GWAS comprised 1,800 CRC cases from the UK-based VICTOR and QUASAR2 adjuvant chemotherapy clinical trials.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002547> "A phase III, placebo-controlled randomized trial of the COX-2 inhibitor rofecoxib (Vioxx) in patients from throughout the United Kingdom who had undergone potentially curative surgery and completed adjuvant therapy for stage II or III colorectal cancer, testing whether rofecoxib reduced recurrence and improved survival; it was terminated early by the worldwide withdrawal of rofecoxib. Its patients, together with those of the QUASAR2 trial, form the VQ58 case series of colorectal cancer genome-wide association studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20339479") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2844807/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples stored in the Medical Biobank enable investigation of a wide range of diseases in prospective case-referent and panel studies, including cancers, neurological, inflammatory and infectious diseases, and others, in addition to CVD and diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8993880/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A nested matched case-control sample was also selected from the VIP cohort based on age and time of blood draw, with cases being defined as those diagnosed with prostate cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8993880/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Herein, PRS for incident prostate cancer was evaluated in two population-based cohorts of unscreened middle-aged men linked to cancer and death registries: the Västerbotten Intervention Project (VIP) and the Malmö Diet and Cancer study (MDC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8993880/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VIP is an ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to receive a health examination at ages 40, 50, and 60 with blood drawn for cryopreservation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35396534") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41419686") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-025-02417-6/MediaObjects/41588_2025_2417_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study (NSHDS) comprises three sub-surveys, the Västerbotten Intervention Program (VIP), the Northerns Sweden MONICA study and the Mammography Screening Program (MSP), whereof VIP and MONICA are actively recruiting.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002549> "An ongoing population-based cohort study initiated in 1985 in which all residents of Västerbotten County, Sweden, are invited to a health examination at ages 40, 50 and 60, with blood drawn for cryopreservation; one of the three sub-surveys of the Northern Sweden Health and Disease Study, used for nested case–control studies of cancer and cardiovascular disease and for evaluating polygenic risk scores.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25512442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30586733") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3064946/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Results from the study will be used to develop clinically useful risk-stratification models for young AMI patients, explain sex differences in outcomes and identify targets for intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550> "An observational, multiethnic cohort study of young adults with acute myocardial infarction, aged 18 to 55, enrolled with more women than men at hospitals across the United States and Spain from 2008, to study sex differences in the presentation, treatment and outcomes of AMI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25512442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30586733") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3064946/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Variation in Recovery: Role of Gender on Outcomes of Young AMI Patients (VIRGO) is a large, observational study of the presentation, treatment and outcomes of young women and men with AMI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550> "An observational, multiethnic cohort study of young adults with acute myocardial infarction, aged 18 to 55, enrolled with more women than men at hospitals across the United States and Spain from 2008, to study sex differences in the presentation, treatment and outcomes of AMI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25512442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30586733") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25512442") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4322946/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Hospitalized patients with AMI ages 18-55 years were recruited between August 2008 and January 2012 to participate in the VIRGO Study, named IM-JOVEN in Spain, to reflect separate, public funding (U.S.: N=2,985, 2,009 women, 976 men; 103 sites; Spain: N= 516, 340 women, 176 men; 24 sites).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550> "An observational, multiethnic cohort study of young adults with acute myocardial infarction, aged 18 to 55, enrolled with more women than men at hospitals across the United States and Spain from 2008, to study sex differences in the presentation, treatment and outcomes of AMI.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21081748") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25512442") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30586733") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30586733") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6433484/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "VIRGO investigators enrolled a multiethnic population of patients presenting to one of 103 United States hospitals with a myocardial infarction between August 2008 and January 2012 using a 2:1 female-to-male enrollment design.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002550> "An observational, multiethnic cohort study of young adults with acute myocardial infarction, aged 18 to 55, enrolled with more women than men at hospitals across the United States and Spain from 2008, to study sex differences in the presentation, treatment and outcomes of AMI.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8621195") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33988330+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the frame of The Vobarno Study blood samples for hematochemistry and DNA extraction, clinic and 24-hour blood pressure measurements, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, and aortic stiffness were measured in all subjects, living in a small town (Vobarno) between Brescia and the Garda Lake (Italy), and randomly selected from electoral roles.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551> "A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8621195") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33988330+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study subjects were included in a long follow-up, lasting 25 years, and cardiovascular morbility and mortality were assessed up to 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551> "A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8621195") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A33988330+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vobarno Study represents the first observational study aimed to assess in a general population sample the relationship between parameters of cardiac and vascular structure (and function) and blood pressure values, measured in the clinic and during the 24 hours.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551> "A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33988330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:8621195") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:8621195") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A8621195+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In conclusion, in a general population of unselected middle-aged subjects, carotid wall thickness and LVMI were associated with each other and related to 24-hour BP levels although the major determinants of carotid wall and cardiac structure were different.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002551> "A population-based observational study of middle-aged residents of Vobarno, a small town between Brescia and Lake Garda in northern Italy, randomly selected from the electoral rolls and examined with clinic and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure measurement, cardiac and carotid ultrasound, aortic stiffness and blood sampling for biochemistry and DNA extraction, to relate cardiac and vascular structure and function to blood pressure; participants were followed for about 25 years for cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3501159/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information on area of residence, age, sex, smoking habits and respiratory symptoms was collected by the Dutch version of the UK MRC standard questionnaire, and spirometry was performed [20].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4824471/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen study is a general population based study on the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in a general population of exclusively white individuals of Dutch descent [18,19].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4824471/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study started in 1965, and participants had medical examinations every 3 years until the final survey in 1989/1990.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4824471/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We updated the vital status of all participants in the Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen study on December 31st, 2008, and evaluated the following mortality outcomes") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5362243/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were derived from Vlagtwedde/Vlaardingen cohort study, a population-based cohort of adult subjects of European ancestry in the Netherlands, recruited from 1965 with a follow-up of over 25 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23054033") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27055053") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28073367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28273074") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30845926") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6407273/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four separate GWASes were performed assessing the genetic associations between the two definitions of airflow obstruction, stratified by smoking status, for both the LifeLines (discovery) and Vlagtwedde-Vlaardingen (replication) studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002552> "A population-based cohort study of the epidemiology of pulmonary diseases in adults of Dutch descent from the general population of Vlagtwedde and Vlaardingen, the Netherlands, who from 1965 until the last survey in 1989/1990 had medical examinations with a respiratory questionnaire and spirometry every three years, and whose vital status was later updated; its genotyped participants have been used in genetic studies of lung function, airflow obstruction and respiratory symptoms.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11484155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1235485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All ascertained families include, at minimum, a sib pair with T2D, together with parents and additional siblings when available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11484155") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1235485/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Warren 2 Consortium was established by Diabetes UK (formerly the British Diabetic Association) to contribute to global efforts to identify T2D-susceptibility genes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1534014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects for the family-based analysis were recruited as part of a Warren 2 cohort from across the UK and were independent of subjects in the case-control analysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1534014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "These families consisted of either an affected proband with both parents (\"trios\"; in this study 17 out of the 395 trios were missing one parent) or an affected proband with one parent and at least one sibling (\"duos\"; 14 out of the 223 siblings in this study were affected).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1534014/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "probands from type 2 diabetic sibships from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 repository (W2SP; n = 499) [12,13]; and a more recent collection of cases with type 2 diabetes from the Diabetes UK Warren 2 repository (W2C; age at diagnosis 35–65 years; not selected for having a family history of diabetes; n = 1038).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16753056") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20459604") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19672314") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2720540/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Diabetes UK funded the Warren 2 resource utilised in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002553> "A collection, funded by Diabetes UK, of people with type 2 diabetes and their relatives recruited from across the United Kingdom for genetic studies of type 2 diabetes, comprising probands of affected sibships (sib pairs), parent-offspring trios and duos, and a later collection of cases diagnosed at 35 to 65 years who were not selected for a family history of diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15006283+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a factorial design, 8171 U.S. female health professionals aged >or=40 years were randomized to vitamin E, vitamin C, beta-carotene, or placebos.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "8,171 women were willing and eligible, were compliant during a 12-week run-in, and were randomized into the trial from June, 1995, through October, 1996 (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1998, approximately 2-3 years following randomization to the antioxidant arms, a folic acid/vitamin B6/B12 component was added to the trial, expanding it to a four-arm factorial trial.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were 40 years or older with a prior history of CVD or three or more CVD risk factors, and were followed an average 9.4 years, from 1995-96 to 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WACS is a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial evaluating the effects of vitamin C") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15006283") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17698683") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2034519/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WACS tested the effects of vitamins C (500 mg daily), E (600 IU every other day), and beta-carotene (50 mg every other day) on the combined outcome of myocardial infarction (MI), stroke, coronary revascularization, or CVD death among 8,171 female health professionals at increased risk in a 2×2×2 factorial design.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002554> "A randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled 2x2x2 factorial trial of vitamin C, vitamin E and beta carotene for the prevention of cardiovascular events among female health professionals in the United States aged 40 or older with a history of cardiovascular disease or at least three cardiovascular risk factors, randomised from June 1995 to October 1996, to which a folic acid, vitamin B6 and vitamin B12 component was added in 1998; participants were followed up by questionnaire to 2005.")

