AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16758424") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19690614") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22498169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24171102") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:7802978") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9586648") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:7802978") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A7802978+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Western Australian HIV Cohort Study; a prospective, single centre, population-based observational study of the natural history of HIV disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002555> "A prospective, single-centre, population-based observational study of the natural history of HIV disease among people with HIV attending the tertiary HIV service in Perth, Western Australia, whose clinical data, HIV sequences and host HLA and genome-wide genotypes have been used to study HIV immune escape, host genetic control of the virus, and prospective HLA-B*5701 screening to prevent abacavir hypersensitivity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766507/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because of all of the limitations of this approach, in 2006 we established collaboration with the New Jersey State Cancer Registry, based at the NJDHSS for rapid case ascertainment, and phased out recruitment in metropolitan New York, ending in December 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766507/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Because of the large, racially mixed population of women in metropolitan New York City (NYC) and eastern New Jersey (NJ), we are currently conducting a case-control study, the Women's Circle of Health Study (WCHS), with the goal of accruing 1200 AA and 1200 EA women with breast cancer and an equal number of controls, to specifically address these questions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766507/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To address this, we conducted a case-control study to evaluate risk factors for high-grade ER- disease in both AA and EA women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2766507/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the study has included two bases for recruitment and interviewing, one in NYC, based at Mount Sinai School of Medicine (MSSM), and one in NJ, based at The Cancer Institute of New Jersey (CINJ), with data and biospecimens sent to Roswell Park Cancer Institute (RPCI) in Buffalo, NY, for processing and storage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5658184/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls with no prior cancer history and matched to the cases by self-reported race, 5 year age categories and geographic residence were initially identified through random digit dialing (RDD), and later through community recruitment, especially to boost enrollment of AA controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19865486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24113797") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33024820") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29073238") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5658184/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WCHS was designed to study genetic and non-genetic factors in association with early and aggressive breast cancer risk in EA and AA women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002556> "A multi-site case-control study of breast cancer in African American and European American women in metropolitan New York City and New Jersey, with cases ascertained through hospitals and the New Jersey State Cancer Registry and controls identified first through random digit dialing and later also through community-based recruitment, recruited from bases at Mount Sinai School of Medicine and the Cancer Institute of New Jersey with data and biospecimens processed at Roswell Park Cancer Institute, to investigate genetic and lifestyle risk factors for aggressive (high-grade, estrogen receptor-negative) breast cancer and its earlier onset in African American women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All participants, including their parents and grandparents, were Han Chinese.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy NGT individuals were recruited from an unselected population undergoing a routine health check-up at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Replication set II samples included samples from the SWHS/SMHS (described above), Nutrition and Health of Aging Population in China (NHAPC), and Wuhan Diabetes Study (WDS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "T2D patients met the well-established diagnostic criteria recommended by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization incorporating both fasting plasma glucose and 2-h oral glucose tolerance test.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "T2D patients were consecutively recruited from men and women attending the outpatient clinics of Department of Endocrinology, Tongji Medical College Hospital, Wuhan, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22109280") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20862305") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1001127.s008") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The inclusion criteria for patients with newly diagnosed T2D were: age ≥ 30 years, no history of a diagnosis of diabetes, and no history of receiving pharmacological treatment for hyperlipidaemia or hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002559> "A hospital-based case-control study of type 2 diabetes in Han Chinese in Wuhan, China, whose cases were men and women aged 30 or older with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes (by American Diabetes Association and World Health Organization criteria, using fasting and 2-hour oral glucose tolerance test glucose), recruited consecutively from the endocrinology outpatient clinics of Tongji Medical College Hospital, and whose controls were people with normal glucose tolerance from an unselected population attending routine health check-ups at the same hospital between December 2004 and November 2007. It has been used for replication genotyping in genetic association studies of type 2 diabetes and obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002560> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002560>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11659911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study participants provided written informed consent, and the study was approved by the institutional review board of Westlake University, Hangzhou, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002560> "An ongoing prospective cohort that since August 2019 has recruited pregnant women aged 18 years or older with gestational diabetes at 24–28 weeks' gestation from the Hangzhou Maternity and Child Health Care Hospital in Hangzhou, China, who intend to deliver there and to stay in Hangzhou with their children for at least four years; it was approved by the institutional review board of Westlake University and integrates multi-omics with precision nutrition research on gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11659911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria for WeBirth involved pregnant women (1) who were aged 18 years or older and had received a diagnosis of GD, and with a gestational age ranging from 24 to 28 weeks; and (2) who intended to deliver at Hangzhou Women’s Hospital and remain in Hangzhou with their children for 4 or more years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002560> "An ongoing prospective cohort that since August 2019 has recruited pregnant women aged 18 years or older with gestational diabetes at 24–28 weeks' gestation from the Hangzhou Maternity and Child Health Care Hospital in Hangzhou, China, who intend to deliver there and to stay in Hangzhou with their children for at least four years; it was approved by the institutional review board of Westlake University and integrates multi-omics with precision nutrition research on gestational diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39699891") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11659911/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WeBirth is an ongoing prospective cohort study that recruits pregnant women with hyperglycemia from the Hangzhou Maternity and Child Health Care Hospital in Hangzhou, China, starting from August 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002560> "An ongoing prospective cohort that since August 2019 has recruited pregnant women aged 18 years or older with gestational diabetes at 24–28 weeks' gestation from the Hangzhou Maternity and Child Health Care Hospital in Hangzhou, China, who intend to deliver there and to stay in Hangzhou with their children for at least four years; it was approved by the institutional review board of Westlake University and integrates multi-omics with precision nutrition research on gestational diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fasting plasma glucose and HbA1c were measured using standard methods.19,20 Fasting C-peptide was measured by ELISA (Diagnostic Biochem Canade, ON, Canada).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Genome wide genotyping data was generated on WellGen and PMNS participants using Affymetrix SNP 6.0 Chips (Affymetrix, CA, USA)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Moreover, all the anthropometric and clinical measurements in WellGen and PMNS were performed in the same department using the same instruments and laboratory assays.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "People with T2D (n = 3111) being treated at the Diabetes Unit, KEM Hospital (Pune, India) and associated clinics were included in the WellGen cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10363502/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the overarching aim was to investigate associations of genetic risk scores of diabetes-related traits (insulin secretion, insulin resistance, etc.) generated from European studies with T2D and its subgroups in an Indian cohort (WellGen) so as to dissect the underlying aetiology of T2D in India.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37492423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00125-006-0502-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both the present study and Pune Maternal Nutrition Study (PMNS) are funded by the Wellcome Trust, London, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002561> "A genetic study of type 2 diabetes in India, funded in part by the Wellcome Trust, whose participants are people with type 2 diabetes treated at the Diabetes Unit of the King Edward Memorial (KEM) Hospital and Research Centre in Pune and associated clinics, with clinical, anthropometric and biochemical measurements made in that unit and genome-wide genotyping performed at the Centre for Cellular and Molecular Biology, Hyderabad.")

