AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12728163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12728163") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC1746660") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Three hundred and forty one white families were recruited from the Southampton area with at least two biological siblings (age 5–21 years) with a current physician diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication on a regular basis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002562> "A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician's diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12728163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3185108/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, the Wessex population consisted of families with at least two biologic siblings with a current physician’s diagnosis of asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002562> "A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician's diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12728163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3185108/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wessex Family Cohort was originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002562> "A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician's diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12728163") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21696813") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3185108/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Transmission disequilibrium tests (TDT) in the Wessex replication population confirmed the association of rs2275380 with asthma diagnosis (Table II).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002562> "A UK family-based collection of white families recruited from the Southampton area, each with at least two biological siblings aged 5 to 21 years with a current physician's diagnosis of asthma who were taking asthma medication regularly, originally recruited in collaboration with Genome Therapeutics Corporation and Schering-Plough for the study that identified ADAM33 as an asthma gene, and later used to test asthma genetic associations by transmission disequilibrium tests.")

