# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9933300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1993 to 1998, the WHI enrolled 161,808 women aged 50 to 79 in randomized clinical trials (CT) or an observational study (OS).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9933300/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHI OS examined predictors and important causes of morbidity and mortality [12], while WHI CT examined the effects of menopausal hormone therapy (HT) vs. placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation vs. placebo, and low-fat eating patterns vs. usual eating patterns.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Postmenopausal women ranging in age from 50 to 79 are enrolled at one of 40 WHI clinical centers nationwide into either a clinical trial (CT) that will include about 64,500 women or an observational study (OS) that will include about 100,000 women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "a low-fat eating pattern, hypothesized to prevent breast cancer and colorectal cancer and, secondarily, coronary heart disease;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "calcium and vitamin D supplementation, hypothesized to prevent hip fractures and, secondarily, other fractures and colorectal cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36797788") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:9492970") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A9492970+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "hormone replacement therapy, hypothesized to reduce the risk of coronary heart disease and other cardiovascular diseases and, secondarily, to reduce the risk of hip and other fractures, with increased breast cancer risk as a possible adverse outcome;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002566> "The randomised clinical trial component of the Women's Health Initiative, in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 enrolled from 1993 to 1998 at the 40 WHI clinical centres in the United States were randomised in three distinct interventions: menopausal hormone therapy versus placebo, calcium and vitamin D supplementation versus placebo, and a low-fat eating pattern versus usual diet, tested for the prevention of coronary heart disease, breast and colorectal cancer, and fractures.")

