# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3059994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, 27,347 postmenopausal women 50–79 years of age in areas surrounding 40 clinical centers were enrolled in one of two randomized, double-blind trials between 1993 and 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3059994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the E trial, which was open only to women without a uterus, participants were randomized to either oral conjugated equine estrogen (CEE) 0.25 mg/day or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24084921") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3963523/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "27,347 postmenopausal women ages 50 to 79 were recruited from 1993 to 1998 at 40 U.S. clinical centers; 16,608 women with a uterus were randomized to daily oral CEE (0.625 mg) plus MPA (2.5 mg) (Prempro) or placebo and 10,739 women with hysterectomy were randomized to daily oral CEE (0.625 mg) alone (Premarin) or placebo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6858581/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All WHI-HT participants subsequently continued to be followed without intervention until close-out.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21036692") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6858581/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHI-HT initially comprised 27,347 postmenopausal women who were randomized to receive either estrogen plus progestin or estrogen alone versus placebo until the trials were stopped early in July 2002 and March 2004, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002568> "The hormone therapy component of the Women's Health Initiative: two randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trials in which postmenopausal women aged 50 to 79 years were enrolled between 1993 and 1998 at 40 clinical centers across the United States and randomized to estrogen alone (women without a uterus) or estrogen plus progestin versus placebo; the estrogen plus progestin and estrogen-alone trials were stopped early in 2002 and 2004, and participants were then followed without intervention.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31676865") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHI-LLS (GWAS) sub-study consisted of the phase III cohort of additional eligible women who were added to the LLS study after the decision was made to expand the study population in 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7566285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 7,875 women between the ages of 63 and 99 years provided measures for the WHI-LLS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7566285/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WHI-LLS was a single in-person visit conducted in 2012–2013 to collect phlebotomy, anthropometry, and objective physical function measures in WHI Extension Study Participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9434234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BP was measured at an in-person home visit by certified staff with the use of standardized procedures and instruments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9434234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LLS had a one-time in-person visit conducted between March 2012 and May 2013 consisting of a blood draw, brief clinical assessment, BP measurement, and functional status assessment of WHI participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32680817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-019-0519-3/MediaObjects/41588_2019_519_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35522983") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9434234/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "who enrolled in the WHI-LLS, an ancillary study to the WHI.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002569> "An ancillary study of the Women's Health Initiative that between March 2012 and May 2013 made a one-time in-person home visit to women of the WHI Extension Study, then aged 63 to 99, to collect a blood sample, a brief clinical assessment, blood pressure, anthropometry and objective physical-function measures; the women added when its study population was expanded in 2012 were genotyped genome-wide as the WHI-LLS GWAS sub-study.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7087709") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Leidsche Rijn is a new residential area under con- struction near the city of Utrecht in the Netherlands,") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7087709/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Based on actual neonatal care practice and embedded in a larger epidemiological study, the Utrecht Health Project, WHISTLER will provide an unique framework to address issues in childhood respiratory disease that are currently insufficiently understood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7087709/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Baseline examination includes a questionnaire evaluating known risk factors for wheezing illnesses; anthropometric measurements; measurements of infant and parental lung function; and sampling of infant and parental DNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7087709/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants will be followed for respiratory events using data from a daily respiratory symptom questionnaire; visits to the general practitioner (primary health care visits, drugs prescriptions and hospital referral); viral sampling during wheezing episodes; and house dust sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7087709/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wheezing Illnesses Study Leidsche Rijn (WHISTLER) was initiated in December 2001 as a single-centre prospective birth cohort study and will include a population-based sample of at least 2000 healthy newborns.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15499901") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37713433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10503770/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2007, the original study design was expanded to include measurements of vascular characteristics (The WHISTLER-Cardio cohort study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002570> "A population-based prospective birth cohort of healthy newborns from Leidsche Rijn, a residential area near Utrecht in the Netherlands, begun in December 2001 from the University Medical Center Utrecht and embedded in the Utrecht Health Project, with infant and parental lung function, DNA, questionnaires and primary-care records collected to study the determinants of wheezing illnesses; in 2007 it was extended with vascular measurements (WHISTLER-Cardio).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3281313/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All civil servants aged 35-55 in 20 London based departments were invited to participate by letter, and 73% agreed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3281313/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Study inception (phase 1) was over the years 1985-8 and involved a clinical examination and a self administered questionnaire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3699448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This observation led to the initiation of the Whitehall II study in 1985 to investigate a range of possible mechanisms potentially underlying these socioeconomic inequalities in disease, most notably psychosocial stress.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3699448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We use data from the British Whitehall II study, a prospective occupational cohort of adults established in 1985.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5480222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since baseline, follow-up clinical examinations have taken place approximately every five years, with the latest one completed in 2012-13.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22223828") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23843750") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28642251") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5480222/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Whitehall II study is an ongoing cohort study of men and women originally employed by the British civil service in London based offices.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002571> "A prospective occupational cohort of British civil servants, men and women aged 35 to 55 working in 20 London-based civil service departments, recruited in 1985–1988 with a clinical examination and questionnaire and re-examined in repeated phases since, set up to investigate the mechanisms, notably psychosocial stress, underlying socioeconomic inequalities in disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All residents in the study communities aged between 18 and 80 years, living in the sampling buildings for more than 5 years are eligible to participate in the WHZH study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants are followed for physiological or pathological changes or incidence of cardiopulmonary diseases every 3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants underwent an extensive physical examination, including anthropometry, spirometry, electrocardiography, and measurements of blood pressure, heart rate, exhaled nitric oxide and carbon monoxide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wuhan-Zhuhai (WHZH) cohort study is designed to investigate the association between air pollutants exposure and physiological or pathological reactions on respiratory and cardiovascular system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort is a community-based prospective study that includes 4812 individuals aged 18–80 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25252923") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4247123/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The recruitment started in April and completed in May 2011, Wuhan city, and the same work was done in May 2012, Zhuhai city.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002572> "A community-based prospective cohort of residents aged 18 to 80 of sampled communities in Wuhan (Hubei province) and Zhuhai (Guangdong province), China, who had lived there for more than five years, recruited in April–May 2011 in Wuhan and May 2012 in Zhuhai with questionnaires, physical examination, spirometry and blood and urine samples, and followed up every three years to study how exposure to air particulate matter and other environmental pollutants affects the respiratory and cardiovascular systems.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2654370/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The current report represents a subanalysis of the Women's Insights and Shared Experiences Study, a pair of case-control studies examining associations between exogenous hormone use, parity, estrogen-related genes, and endometrial or breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2654370/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We performed a case-control study of white and African American women age 50 to 79 years in the Philadelphia area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2722148/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Incident breast cancer cases were identified through hospitals and validated via the Pennsylvania State Cancer Registry, and frequency-matched controls were identified from the community using random-digit dialing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2722148/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Potentially eligible cases were Caucasian and AA women ages 50–79 years old residing in these counties at the time of a new diagnosis of breast cancer between 1 July 1999 and 30 June 2002.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2722148/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The source population for this study was the three counties of Philadelphia (PA), Delaware (PA) and Camden (NJ).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18757329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19028704") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19124504") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2668570/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participating studies in this pooled analysis were six population-based case-control studies (Estrogen, Diet, Genetics, and Endometrial Cancer; Fred Hutchinson Cancer Research Center case-control study; Women's Insights and Shared Experiences;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002574> "A population-based pair of case-control studies, one of endometrial cancer and one of breast cancer, among white and African American women aged 50 to 79 in the Philadelphia area of Pennsylvania and New Jersey, United States, examining exogenous hormone use, parity and estrogen-related genes: cases diagnosed between July 1999 and June 2002 were identified through hospitals and the Pennsylvania Cancer Registry, and controls from the same area by random-digit dialling. Its endometrial cancer study is one of the studies of the Epidemiology of Endometrial Cancer Consortium.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002575> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002575>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1186%2Fs13229-017-0137-9/MediaObjects/13229_2017_137_MOESM1_ESM.docx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28540026") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1186%2Fs13229-017-0137-9/MediaObjects/13229_2017_137_MOESM1_ESM.docx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Analysis was limited to European-Americans (as determined by principal components analysis).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002575> "A combination of Californian autism spectrum disorder collections, namely the UCSF/Weiss trios and cases, the UCSF/Hendren cases, the USC/Levitt cases and controls, trios, cases and controls from the CHARGE study at UC Davis and cases and controls of the Autism Phenome Project of the UC Davis MIND Institute, whose samples were genotyped by the laboratory of L. A. Weiss at the University of California, San Francisco, on Affymetrix Axiom EUR arrays, and which contributed its European-American participants to the Psychiatric Genomics Consortium autism GWAS.")
