# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All controls were frequency matched to the cases by age, sex, and residential area (urban or countryside).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases were consecutively recruited from the Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls were cancer-free outpatients from other clinics in the same hospital during the same period when the cases were recruited.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The WLCS study was carried out in Wuhan, China and has been described elsewhere13 .") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2456/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2456_MOESM34_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "There were no restrictions based on age, sex, and histology, but patients with a previous cancer history or with unknown conditions of radiotherapy or chemotherapy were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20700438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23143601") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23143601+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To identify common genetic variants that contribute to lung cancer susceptibility, we conducted a multistage genome-wide association study of lung cancer in Asian women who never smoked.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002576> "A hospital-based case–control study of lung cancer in Wuhan, China, whose cases were consecutive patients with lung cancer at Wuhan Zhongnan Hospital, without restriction on age, sex or histology but excluding those with a previous cancer or an unknown history of radiotherapy or chemotherapy, and whose controls were cancer-free outpatients of other clinics of the same hospital in the same period, frequency-matched to the cases on age, sex and urban or rural residence; all participants were ethnic Chinese. Its never-smoking women were genotyped genome-wide as one of the studies of the Female Lung Cancer Consortium in Asia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05275-y/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5275_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5402460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Both sites are ∼4,100 m above sea level.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> "A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05275-y/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5275_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5402460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this study, we perform a large-scale genome-wide study to detect genetic signals of high-altitude adaptation in 3,008 Tibetans and 7,287 non-Tibetan individuals of Eastern Asian (EAS) ancestry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> "A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.")
