AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05275-y/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5275_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5402460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects were recruited at two separate sites (Seda and Litang) of the TP in Sichuan, western China (SI Appendix, Fig.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> "A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05275-y/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5275_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5402460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We extracted DNA from blood samples and performed genome-wide SNP genotyping assays using the Illumina CoreExome array, an SNP array with 264,909 tag SNPs with genome-wide coverage and 244,593 exome-focused SNPs (Materials and Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> "A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-05275-y/MediaObjects/41586_2022_5275_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28373541") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5402460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Seda subjects were recruited from people who came from diverse regions of the TP to study or work at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute and the Litang subjects were recruited from nomadic people who have lived in Litang and surrounding areas for many generations (Materials and Methods).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002577> "A collection of Tibetans recruited at two sites about 4,100 m above sea level on the Tibetan Plateau in Sichuan, western China: at Seda, among people studying or working at the Seda Larong Wuming Buddhist Institute who came from diverse regions of the plateau, and at Litang, among nomadic people who had lived in the area for generations; their blood DNA was genotyped on the Illumina CoreExome array for a study of high-altitude adaptation, and the genotype and phenotype data are held by the Wenzhou Medical University biobank.")

