AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5657532/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the monthly follow-up, dose, INR, and changes in concomitant medications that influence warfarin pharmacodynamics (antiplatelet agents) or pharmacokinetics (e.g. amiodarone) were documented.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5657532/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Herein we evaluate whether PTTR, risk of over-anticoagulation (INR>4) and risk of hemorrhage differs by race and assess the influence of clinical and genetic factors on these outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5657532/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants >20 years of age initiating warfarin therapy were enrolled in an inception warfarin pharmacogenetics cohort study if the target international normalized ratio (INR) range was 2–3 and therapy was managed at the anticoagulation clinic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC5657532/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To our knowledge, this is the first study to report PTTR and risk of hemorrhage among African American and European American warfarin users managed through an anticoagulation service.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9241245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The UAB WPC [31] is a prospective cohort of first-time warfarin users aged 19 years or older starting warfarin for anticoagulation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28806200") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000708.v1.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35765100") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9241245/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Warfarin therapy requiring a target international normalized ratio (INR) range of 2-3 was initiated in patients with venous thromboembolism, stroke/transient ischemic attacks, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction, and/or peripheral arterial disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002580> "A prospective inception cohort of adults starting chronic warfarin therapy with a target INR of 2–3 for venous thromboembolism, stroke or transient ischaemic attack, atrial fibrillation, myocardial infarction or peripheral arterial disease, enrolled at anticoagulation clinics by the University of Alabama at Birmingham and followed at monthly clinic visits for warfarin dose, INR, medications and outcomes, to study genetic and clinical determinants of warfarin response in African American and European American patients.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002581> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002581>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12721875") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15685490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36786861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15685490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15685490+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Forty-two hospitals participated in the study including 24 departments of neurology, 13 of internal medicine, and 5 of geriatric medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002581> "A regional hospital-based register of patients admitted with acute stroke to cooperating hospitals in Westphalia, north-west Germany, with departments of neurology, internal medicine and geriatric medicine taking part, which records a standardised data set of sociodemographic and clinical characteristics, diagnostic and treatment procedures, complications and status at discharge; its case ascertainment was part of the German Competence Net Stroke, and consecutive consenting ischaemic stroke patients recruited through it have been used in genetic studies of stroke.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12721875") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15685490") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23041239") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36786861") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15685490") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15685490+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stroke patients admitted to hospitals cooperating within the Westphalian Stroke Register between January 1, 2000 and December 31, 2001 were analyzed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002581> "A regional hospital-based register of patients admitted with acute stroke to cooperating hospitals in Westphalia, north-west Germany, with departments of neurology, internal medicine and geriatric medicine taking part, which records a standardised data set of sociodemographic and clinical characteristics, diagnostic and treatment procedures, complications and status at discharge; its case ascertainment was part of the German Competence Net Stroke, and consecutive consenting ischaemic stroke patients recruited through it have been used in genetic studies of stroke.")
