AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10181480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 10,858 adults aged ≥30 years old were recruited with random cluster sampling from 2 communities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002585> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 30 or older established in Wuxi city, Jiangsu Province, China, in April to June 2007 through random cluster sampling of residents of two communities, with a baseline questionnaire, physical measurements and blood sampling for DNA extraction, followed prospectively to study risk factors for non-communicable diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10181480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As previously described [23], all participants completed a face-to-face questionnaire, underwent physical measurements, and provided peripheral venous blood samples for further examinations and DNA extraction.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002585> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 30 or older established in Wuxi city, Jiangsu Province, China, in April to June 2007 through random cluster sampling of residents of two communities, with a baseline questionnaire, physical measurements and blood sampling for DNA extraction, followed prospectively to study risk factors for non-communicable diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10181480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information about incident T2D was collected through the local chronic non-communicable disease (NCD) registration system, health record management system, and hospital information system established by Wuxi Health Commission, Wuxi CDC, and the Wuxi Center for Health Statistics and Information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002585> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 30 or older established in Wuxi city, Jiangsu Province, China, in April to June 2007 through random cluster sampling of residents of two communities, with a baseline questionnaire, physical measurements and blood sampling for DNA extraction, followed prospectively to study risk factors for non-communicable diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37432247") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10181480/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Wuxi Non-Communicable Diseases cohort (Wuxi NCDs cohort) was established from April to June 2007 (baseline) in Wuxi city, Jiangsu Province, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002585> "A population-based cohort of adults aged 30 or older established in Wuxi city, Jiangsu Province, China, in April to June 2007 through random cluster sampling of residents of two communities, with a baseline questionnaire, physical measurements and blood sampling for DNA extraction, followed prospectively to study risk factors for non-communicable diseases such as type 2 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29439783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3645306/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This analysis used data from the breast cancer cases enrolled in the Wisconsin women’s health study (WWHS), a federally funded population-based case–control study designed to examine the associations of lifestyle factors and genetics with breast cancer risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> "A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29439783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3645306/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WWHS cases were incident breast cancer cases reported to the mandatory statewide cancer registry and interviewed for our study between 2004 and 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> "A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29439783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4112552/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During 1988-2003, controls were randomly selected in each state using lists of licensed drivers (ages <65) and Medicare beneficiaries (ages ≥65). Controls of all ages were selected only from lists of licensed drivers during 2004-2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> "A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29439783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4112552/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 40-minute telephone interview elicited information on reproductive history, alcohol consumption, smoking history, height and weight, use of oral contraceptive and postmenopausal hormones, personal and family medical history, and demographic factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> "A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22490319") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29439783") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24647890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC4112552/unicode") Annotation(rdfs:comment "and Wisconsin with a new diagnosis of invasive breast cancer (ICD-O version 2 C50.0-C50.9) reported to each state's cancer registry and aged <75 years at diagnosis between April 1988 and January 2008 were eligible for five consecutive phases of a case-control study collectively called the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002586> "A series of population-based case–control studies of breast cancer run at the University of Wisconsin, whose cases are Wisconsin women with incident breast cancer reported to the statewide cancer registry and whose controls are women without breast cancer randomly selected from lists of licensed drivers and, for women aged 65 or over until 2003, of Medicare beneficiaries, all interviewed by telephone about reproductive history, family cancer history and lifestyle, to study lifestyle and genetic risk factors for breast cancer; it is the Wisconsin part of the Collaborative Breast Cancer Study, which recruited Wisconsin cases from 1988 to 2008.")
