# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(2) an initial diagnosis of hypertension between 20 and 51 years of age;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(3) no secondary causes of hypertension") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(4) a fasting glucose level <126 mg/dl and no previous diagnosis of diabetes mellitus; (5) a body mass index <35 kg/m2; (6) having both sides of parents and grandparents identifying themselves as Han Chinese; (7) being a legal resident of Taiwan.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2674219/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We obtained complete genotypic and phenotypic data from 1,008 YOH individuals and established immortalized cell lines from their lymphocytes for the Academia Sinica Multi-Center YOH Genetic Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5789005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Age and sex matched normotensive controls were selected from “Han-Chinese Cell and Genome Bank in Taiwan”18 which has established by Institute of Biomedical Sciences of Academia Sinica.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19421330") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21771975") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23469169") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29379041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5789005/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Young-onset hypertensive patients were selected from “Academia Sinica Multi-Center Young-Onset Hypertension Genetic Study”, which had recruited 1023 non-aboriginal Taiwanese individuals with essential hypertension aged 20 to 50.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002591> "A multicentre study run from Academia Sinica, Taiwan, of Han Chinese patients with young-onset essential hypertension, first diagnosed between the ages of 20 and 51, with secondary hypertension, diabetes and a body mass index of 35 kg/m2 or more excluded. Lymphoblastoid cell lines were established for its patients, who, with normotensive controls from other Taiwanese studies, have been used in genome-wide association, gene-expression and candidate-gene studies of hypertension, blood pressure, adiponectin and ACE activity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20972438") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.687/MediaObjects/41588_2010_BFng687_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Zaragoza Bladder Cancer Study (ZBCS) 245 1,305 Hospital-based case-control, Zaragoza, Spain Cases diagnosed at the University Hospital in Zaragoza from 2007 to 2009 Individuals attending the University Hospital in Zaragoza for diseases other than cancer between 2001 and 2007") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592> "A hospital-based case–control study of urinary bladder cancer in Zaragoza, Spain, whose cases were patients with histologically proven urothelial cell carcinoma of the bladder recruited from the urology and oncology departments of Zaragoza Hospital from 2007 to 2009 and whose controls were individuals who had attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for diseases other than cancer from 2001 to 2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 246 patients with histologically proven urothelial cell carcinoma of the bladder were enrolled (response 77%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592> "A hospital-based case–control study of urinary bladder cancer in Zaragoza, Spain, whose cases were patients with histologically proven urothelial cell carcinoma of the bladder recruited from the urology and oncology departments of Zaragoza Hospital from 2007 to 2009 and whose controls were individuals who had attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for diseases other than cancer from 2001 to 2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 890 Spanish control individuals were part of a larger collection of control samples obtained from individuals who had attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza, Spain, for diseases other than cancer between November 2001 and May 2007.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592> "A hospital-based case–control study of urinary bladder cancer in Zaragoza, Spain, whose cases were patients with histologically proven urothelial cell carcinoma of the bladder recruited from the urology and oncology departments of Zaragoza Hospital from 2007 to 2009 and whose controls were individuals who had attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for diseases other than cancer from 2001 to 2007.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20972438") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21750109") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3188988/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Spanish study patients were recruited from the urology and oncology departments of Zaragoza Hospital between September 2007 and June 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002592> "A hospital-based case–control study of urinary bladder cancer in Zaragoza, Spain, whose cases were patients with histologically proven urothelial cell carcinoma of the bladder recruited from the urology and oncology departments of Zaragoza Hospital from 2007 to 2009 and whose controls were individuals who had attended the University Hospital in Zaragoza for diseases other than cancer from 2001 to 2007.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Each participant had undergone a high-quality colonoscopy examination.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593> "A Chinese genetic sample for colorectal neoplasia drawn from the population-based colorectal cancer screening programme of Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, made up of a one-to-one matched case-control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 and a cross-sectional colonoscopy screening study performed in 2014, whose participants were genotyped on the Illumina Asian Screening Array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from a cross-sectional screening study performed in 2014, as a part of the early work on the CRC screening program conducted in Jiashan County.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593> "A Chinese genetic sample for colorectal neoplasia drawn from the population-based colorectal cancer screening programme of Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, made up of a one-to-one matched case-control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 and a cross-sectional colonoscopy screening study performed in 2014, whose participants were genotyped on the Illumina Asian Screening Array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from a one-to-one matched case–control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 based on an ongoing population-based CRC screening program running in Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593> "A Chinese genetic sample for colorectal neoplasia drawn from the population-based colorectal cancer screening programme of Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, made up of a one-to-one matched case-control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 and a cross-sectional colonoscopy screening study performed in 2014, whose participants were genotyped on the Illumina Asian Screening Array.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38872215") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11170922/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects from ZJCRC case–control set and ZJCRC cross-sectional screening set were genotyped using the Illumina™ Asian Screening Array (ASA) system to identify potential susceptibility variants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002593> "A Chinese genetic sample for colorectal neoplasia drawn from the population-based colorectal cancer screening programme of Jiashan County, Zhejiang Province, made up of a one-to-one matched case-control study conducted from 2015 to 2022 and a cross-sectional colonoscopy screening study performed in 2014, whose participants were genotyped on the Illumina Asian Screening Array.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40619433") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs/history") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27459450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27459450+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have summarized the evolution of the Nurses' Health Study (NHS), a prospective cohort study of 121 700 married registered nurses launched in 1976; NHS II, which began in 1989 and enrolled 116 430 nurses; and NHS3, which began in 2010 and has ongoing enrollment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594> "An umbrella of three prospective cohorts of nurses: the original Nurses' Health Study established in 1976, Nurses' Health Study II, and Nurses' Health Study 3, which is still enrolling nurses and nursing students in the United States or Canada; together they count more than 275,000 participants and are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40619433") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs/history") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27459459") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A27459459+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through periodic assessment of diet by validated dietary questionnaires over 40 years, the NHSs have identified dietary determinants of diseases such as breast and other cancers; obesity; type 2 diabetes; cardiovascular, respiratory, and eye diseases; and neurodegenerative and mental health disorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594> "An umbrella of three prospective cohorts of nurses: the original Nurses' Health Study established in 1976, Nurses' Health Study II, and Nurses' Health Study 3, which is still enrolling nurses and nursing students in the United States or Canada; together they count more than 275,000 participants and are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40619433") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs/history") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40619433") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12232564/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NHS3, initiated in 2010, is an ongoing open-enrollment cohort of nurses and nursing students in the US or Canada.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594> "An umbrella of three prospective cohorts of nurses: the original Nurses' Health Study established in 1976, Nurses' Health Study II, and Nurses' Health Study 3, which is still enrolling nurses and nursing students in the United States or Canada; together they count more than 275,000 participants and are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40619433") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://nurseshealthstudy.org/about-nhs/history") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-025-08771-z/MediaObjects/41586_2025_8771_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nurses' Health Studies are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women (http://nurseshealthstudy.org/).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002594> "An umbrella of three prospective cohorts of nurses: the original Nurses' Health Study established in 1976, Nurses' Health Study II, and Nurses' Health Study 3, which is still enrolling nurses and nursing students in the United States or Canada; together they count more than 275,000 participants and are among the largest prospective investigations into the risk factors for major chronic diseases in women.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4974817/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected for the SAGE trial from 1990 to 2007 and for the ICGHD from 2004 to 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4974817/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The publicly available datasets used for analysis were obtained from dbGaP (http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gap) through accession numbers phs000092.v1.p and phs000277.v1.p1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cases and controls were obtained from the several large investigations including: The Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a Twin Study of Mole Development in Adolescence, and ongoing genetic studies of substance dependence conducted by investigators at Yale and collaborating institutions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Controls included assessed individuals who did not meet DSM-IV heroin dependence criteria and unassessed general population controls.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project uses a case-control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27028160") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/projects/gap/cgi-bin/study.cgi?study_id=phs000277.v2.p1") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This collaboration of Australian and American investigators aims to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002595> "A collaboration of Australian and American investigators to identify genes associated with liability for heroin dependence, using a case–control design in which cases met lifetime DSM-IV criteria for heroin dependence and controls were assessed individuals without heroin dependence or unassessed general population controls, with cases and controls drawn from several investigations including the Comorbidity and Trauma Study, Heroin Dependence in Western Australia, the OZ-ALC Study, a twin study of mole development in adolescence and genetic studies of substance dependence at Yale; its data, collected from 2004 to 2009, are held in dbGaP as phs000277.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5817954/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from the 4 Swedish cohorts from Stockholm (SNAC-K, SALT/Twin gene, 60 y/IMPROVE, and SDPP) as well as the 2 Dutch cohorts (EPIC-MORGEN and EPIC-PROSPECT) were pooled by the local analyst, and analyzed as single cohorts, named Cardiovascular Effects of Air Pollution and Noise in Stockholm (CEANS) and EPIC Netherlands (EPIC-NL), respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8438896/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme (SDPP) was designed as a population-based prospective cohort, and includes 3 128 men recruited between the years 1992 and 1994 and 4821 women recruited between the years 1996 and 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8438896/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fourth subcohort, the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen, included a random sample of inhabitants aged at least 60 years and residing in a central area of Stockholm City (N=3 363).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8438896/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The second subcohort named SIXTY consists of a population-based random sample of 60-year-old men and women (N=4 232) living within Stockholm County between August 1997 and March 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8909720/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study aims to estimate the exposure-lag response between air pollution exposure and risk for ischemic heart disease (IHD) and stroke incidence by applying distributed lag non-linear models (DLNMs).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29016987") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34497075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35270332") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40672052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12266180/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CEANS (Cardiovascular Effects of Air Pollution and Noise in Stockholm study) combined data from four sub-cohorts: The Screening Across the Lifespan Twin Study (SALT) sampled 7,043 individuals from the Swedish Twin Register born 1958 and earlier, who lived in Stockholm County [1].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002596> "A pooling of four population-based cohorts from Stockholm County, Sweden (the Stockholm Diabetes Prevention Programme, a random sample of 60-year-olds known as SIXTY, the Stockholm-resident participants of the Screening Across the Lifespan Twin study, and the Swedish National Study on Aging and Care in Kungsholmen), recruited between 1992 and 2004 and analysed together to study long-term exposure to ambient air pollution and noise as risk factors for cardiovascular disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All Danish residents 18 years and older with a valid digital signature (MitID) and an account with the digital receipt solution can donate information about their purchases for research purposes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Another strength is the ability to use the personal identification number provided by participants to collect key covariates from Danish registries, including household size, income, education, and social data, in addition to other exposure data and health outcomes, as detailed above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since June 2021, a GDPR-compliant, secure, encrypted web application developed by SSI, as part of the Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP), has been in operation21.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The My Purchases cohort has had ongoing recruitment since June 2021.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The consumer consents to transfer all previous digital receipts collected by the digital receipt solution and to transfer future receipts collected until they decide to leave the study or 2040, whichever comes first (the study page at https://mineindkob.ssi.dk/ has an option to leave the study).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/CON") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38062070") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10703931/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This framework allows us to follow key health determinants, such as tobacco, alcohol, dental products, and diet over time, and thereby investigate time-varying exposures, possible associations with health outcomes, and resultant targets of interventions24,34,35.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002597> "A cohort of adult Danish residents who, since June 2021, have consented through a web application run by Statens Serum Institut to donate the digital receipts of their consumer purchases, linked through their personal identification number to national health registers, to study how purchases, diet and household lifestyle exposures affect health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7227258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of the fifth measurement of the STREAM cohort (2015), a second cohort of participants was recruited, consisting of persons aged 45–49 years and employed persons in the other age groups (50–54, 55–59, 60–64).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> "A prospective cohort of persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands, stratified by age and employment status, followed from 2010 by the Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research TNO through online questionnaires on work characteristics, health, employment transitions, work ability and productivity, to study sustainable work participation of older workers; a second group was recruited in 2015.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7227258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From the inception of the cohort in 2010 (T1) onwards, participants completed an online questionnaire on topics such as work characteristics, health, employment status and transitions, work ability, and work productivity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> "A prospective cohort of persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands, stratified by age and employment status, followed from 2010 by the Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research TNO through online questionnaires on work characteristics, health, employment transitions, work ability and productivity, to study sustainable work participation of older workers; a second group was recruited in 2015.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7227258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "STREAM is an ongoing prospective cohort among persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands stratified by age and employment status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> "A prospective cohort of persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands, stratified by age and employment status, followed from 2010 by the Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research TNO through online questionnaires on work characteristics, health, employment transitions, work ability and productivity, to study sustainable work participation of older workers; a second group was recruited in 2015.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7227258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data that support the findings of this study are available from TNO Healthy Living (Leiden, the Netherlands) but restrictions apply to the availability of these data, which were used under license for the current study, and so are not publicly available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> "A prospective cohort of persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands, stratified by age and employment status, followed from 2010 by the Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research TNO through online questionnaires on work characteristics, health, employment transitions, work ability and productivity, to study sustainable work participation of older workers; a second group was recruited in 2015.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32414410") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7227258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The strength of STREAM is that a wide variety of variables important for sustainable work participation were collected that are not currently included in most occupational health surveys.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002598> "A prospective cohort of persons aged 45 to 64 years in the Netherlands, stratified by age and employment status, followed from 2010 by the Netherlands Organisation for Applied Scientific Research TNO through online questionnaires on work characteristics, health, employment transitions, work ability and productivity, to study sustainable work participation of older workers; a second group was recruited in 2015.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Results will help researchers understand factors that increase cancer risk and other diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination collects the cervical biospecimens and adds associated data from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cervical Screening Cohort enrols women screened for human papillomavirus (HPV) and cervical abnormalities within the capital region of Sweden from the organised screening program and the non-organised testing of cervical samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort is ideal for longitudinal, long-term follow-up studies due to its validated documentation and registry-derived information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort is systematically updated with individual-level data from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38926412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11208431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort started in 2011 and has enrolled more than 670,000 women, contributing with more than 1.2 million biobanked samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002599> "A cohort of women screened for human papillomavirus and cervical abnormalities in the capital region of Sweden, in the organised screening programme and in non-organised testing, enrolled from 2011 by the Center for Cervical Cancer Elimination at Karolinska Institutet and Karolinska University Hospital, with biobanked cervical samples and individual screening data updated from the Swedish National Cervical Screening Registry (NKCx), for long-term follow-up studies of cervical cancer and other diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7934722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch famine birth cohort consists of 2414 singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam around the time of the Dutch famine (1943–1947) whose birth records have been kept.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7934722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dutch famine birth cohort study was set up to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine during the specific stages of gestation on later health, with a particular focus on chronic cardiovascular and metabolic diseases, ageing and mental health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7934722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort has been interviewed and physically examined in several waves of data collection since that time, allowing repeated measures of a wide range of phenotypic information as well as the collection of biological samples (blood, urine, buccal swabs), functional testing (of heart, lungs, kidney, HPA axis) and imaging of the brain (MRI) and vasculature (ultrasound).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7934722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort has been traced and studied since 1994, when the first data collection started.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7934722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through linkage with registries, mortality and morbidity information of the entire cohort has been obtained.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33664071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.hongerwinter.nl/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Het Hongerwinter Onderzoek is een uniek onderzoek van het Amsterdam UMC naar de gezondheid van mannen en vrouwen die zijn geboren rond de tijd van de Hongerwinter (1944/1945) in het Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002600> "A historical birth cohort of singletons born alive and at term in the Wilhelmina Gasthuis in Amsterdam, the Netherlands, around the time of the 1944–1945 Dutch famine (1943–1947), traced and studied by Amsterdam UMC since 1994 through repeated interviews, examinations, biological samples, imaging and registry linkage, to investigate the effects of acute maternal undernutrition during specific stages of gestation on later health, particularly cardiovascular and metabolic disease, ageing and mental health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6060880/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Diabetes Prediction in Skåne (DiPiS) study is a prospective follow-up of children at risk of T1D in southern Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> "A prospective, population-based cohort of children born in Skåne, Sweden, between September 2000 and August 2004 who were screened as newborns for risk of type 1 diabetes, with children at increased risk followed with yearly capillary blood samples for islet autoantibodies from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, to investigate the genetic and environmental factors contributing to or triggering type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12264131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between September 2000 and August 2004, newborns in Skåne were screened for risk of developing type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> "A prospective, population-based cohort of children born in Skåne, Sweden, between September 2000 and August 2004 who were screened as newborns for risk of type 1 diabetes, with children at increased risk followed with yearly capillary blood samples for islet autoantibodies from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, to investigate the genetic and environmental factors contributing to or triggering type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12264131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children at increased risk of type 1 diabetes were invited to participate in follow-up from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, whichever occurred first15.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> "A prospective, population-based cohort of children born in Skåne, Sweden, between September 2000 and August 2004 who were screened as newborns for risk of type 1 diabetes, with children at increased risk followed with yearly capillary blood samples for islet autoantibodies from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, to investigate the genetic and environmental factors contributing to or triggering type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12264131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DiPiS was a prospective, population-based cohort study that investigated the genetic and environmental factors contributing to, or triggering, the development of type 1 diabetes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> "A prospective, population-based cohort of children born in Skåne, Sweden, between September 2000 and August 2004 who were screened as newborns for risk of type 1 diabetes, with children at increased risk followed with yearly capillary blood samples for islet autoantibodies from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, to investigate the genetic and environmental factors contributing to or triggering type 1 diabetes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29752553") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40664750") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12264131/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During follow-up, the children donated capillary blood samples for autoantibody analyses each year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002601> "A prospective, population-based cohort of children born in Skåne, Sweden, between September 2000 and August 2004 who were screened as newborns for risk of type 1 diabetes, with children at increased risk followed with yearly capillary blood samples for islet autoantibodies from two to 15 years of age or until diabetes onset, to investigate the genetic and environmental factors contributing to or triggering type 1 diabetes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELFE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7266552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 349 maternity units were randomly selected in metropolitan France and the children were recruited at birth from the 320 maternity units that agreed to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> "The first French national birth cohort, of children recruited at birth in 2011 in a random sample of maternity units in metropolitan France during 25 selected days spread over the year and followed by the French Institute for Demographic Studies (Ined), Inserm and the French Blood Agency, to study the determinants of development, health and socialisation of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELFE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7266552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ELFE is the first French national birth cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> "The first French national birth cohort, of children recruited at birth in 2011 in a random sample of maternity units in metropolitan France during 25 selected days spread over the year and followed by the French Institute for Demographic Studies (Ined), Inserm and the French Blood Agency, to study the determinants of development, health and socialisation of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELFE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7266552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Its objective is to study determinants of the development, health and socialization of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> "The first French national birth cohort, of children recruited at birth in 2011 in a random sample of maternity units in metropolitan France during 25 selected days spread over the year and followed by the French Institute for Demographic Studies (Ined), Inserm and the French Blood Agency, to study the determinants of development, health and socialisation of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELFE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7266552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place during 25 selected days in 2011, grouped into four periods over the year;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> "The first French national birth cohort, of children recruited at birth in 2011 in a random sample of maternity units in metropolitan France during 25 selected days spread over the year and followed by the French Institute for Demographic Studies (Ined), Inserm and the French Blood Agency, to study the determinants of development, health and socialisation of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31747017") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELFE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38172606") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10764867/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Elfe survey is a joint project between the Institut national des études démographiques (Ined) and the Institut national de la santé et de la recherche médicale (Inserm), in partnership with the Établissement français du sang (EFS)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002602> "The first French national birth cohort, of children recruited at birth in 2011 in a random sample of maternity units in metropolitan France during 25 selected days spread over the year and followed by the French Institute for Demographic Studies (Ined), Inserm and the French Blood Agency, to study the determinants of development, health and socialisation of children from birth to adulthood through a multidisciplinary approach.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41196593") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://limburgsgeboortecohort.be/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32396192") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7218490/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the framework of the Belgian birth cohort Environmental Influence on Early Aging (ENVIRONAGE) study, mother-newborn pairs were recruited on arrival for delivery at the East-Limburg Hospital in Genk, Belgium.21") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> "A prospective, population-based birth cohort of mother–newborn pairs recruited at delivery since February 2010 at East-Limburg Hospital (Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg) in Genk, in the province of Limburg, Belgium, with umbilical cord blood collected at birth and follow-up of the children at 4 to 6 years of age at Hasselt University, to study how environmental exposures in early life influence the biology of human ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41196593") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://limburgsgeboortecohort.be/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12634485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "EDTA-coated BD Vacutainer® K2E plastic whole blood tubes were used for drawing umbilical cord blood immediately after delivery at the proximal (neonatal) end of the umbilical cord (BD, Franklin Lakes, NJ, USA).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> "A prospective, population-based birth cohort of mother–newborn pairs recruited at delivery since February 2010 at East-Limburg Hospital (Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg) in Genk, in the province of Limburg, Belgium, with umbilical cord blood collected at birth and follow-up of the children at 4 to 6 years of age at Hasselt University, to study how environmental exposures in early life influence the biology of human ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41196593") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://limburgsgeboortecohort.be/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12634485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mother-child pairs are invited for follow-up when the child is between 4 and 6 years of age, at Hasselt University (Diepenbeek, Belgium).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> "A prospective, population-based birth cohort of mother–newborn pairs recruited at delivery since February 2010 at East-Limburg Hospital (Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg) in Genk, in the province of Limburg, Belgium, with umbilical cord blood collected at birth and follow-up of the children at 4 to 6 years of age at Hasselt University, to study how environmental exposures in early life influence the biology of human ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41196593") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://limburgsgeboortecohort.be/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12634485/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ENVIRONAGE birth cohort is still ongoing, having recruited mother-newborn pairs since February 2010 in the province of Limburg (Belgium).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> "A prospective, population-based birth cohort of mother–newborn pairs recruited at delivery since February 2010 at East-Limburg Hospital (Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg) in Genk, in the province of Limburg, Belgium, with umbilical cord blood collected at birth and follow-up of the children at 4 to 6 years of age at Hasselt University, to study how environmental exposures in early life influence the biology of human ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41106326") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41196593") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://limburgsgeboortecohort.be/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ENVIRONAGE") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within the ongoing population-based prospective birth cohort study ENVIRONAGE we explore new dimensions in the current understanding of human ageing and its interaction with the environment") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002603> "A prospective, population-based birth cohort of mother–newborn pairs recruited at delivery since February 2010 at East-Limburg Hospital (Ziekenhuis Oost-Limburg) in Genk, in the province of Limburg, Belgium, with umbilical cord blood collected at birth and follow-up of the children at 4 to 6 years of age at Hasselt University, to study how environmental exposures in early life influence the biology of human ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HPV") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25593103+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 11 Arm A communities 90% of participating girls and boys were assigned to receive HPV-16/18 vaccine, in 11 Arm B communities 90% of girls were assigned to receive HPV-16/18 vaccine - boys were assigned to receive hepatitis B-virus (HBV) vaccine, and in 11 Arm C communities all were assigned to receive HBV-vaccine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> "The participants of a community-randomised phase IV trial in which early adolescents born 1992–1995 and resident in 33 Finnish communities were invited in 2007–2009 and assigned by community to gender-neutral HPV16/18 vaccination, HPV16/18 vaccination of girls with hepatitis B vaccination of boys, or gender-neutral hepatitis B vaccination, and followed up with cervicovaginal sampling from 18.5 years of age, to compare the overall and herd effects of gender-neutral and girls-only HPV vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HPV") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25593103+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In two school-years (2007-2008 and 2008-2009) we invited 80,272 1992-1995 born early adolescents to a CRT in 33 communities a priori stratified by low, intermediate and high HPV-16/18 seroprevalence.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> "The participants of a community-randomised phase IV trial in which early adolescents born 1992–1995 and resident in 33 Finnish communities were invited in 2007–2009 and assigned by community to gender-neutral HPV16/18 vaccination, HPV16/18 vaccination of girls with hepatitis B vaccination of boys, or gender-neutral hepatitis B vaccination, and followed up with cervicovaginal sampling from 18.5 years of age, to compare the overall and herd effects of gender-neutral and girls-only HPV vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HPV") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25593103+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our cluster randomized trial (NCT00534638) assesses the overall and herd effects of vaccinating girls vs. girls and boys.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> "The participants of a community-randomised phase IV trial in which early adolescents born 1992–1995 and resident in 33 Finnish communities were invited in 2007–2009 and assigned by community to gender-neutral HPV16/18 vaccination, HPV16/18 vaccination of girls with hepatitis B vaccination of boys, or gender-neutral hepatitis B vaccination, and followed up with cervicovaginal sampling from 18.5 years of age, to compare the overall and herd effects of gender-neutral and girls-only HPV vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HPV") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A29055031+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Four years later (2010-14) 11,396 cervicovaginal samples obtained from 18.5 year-old women were tested for HPV DNA, and prevalence of cervical HPV infections by trial arm and birth cohort was the main outcome measure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> "The participants of a community-randomised phase IV trial in which early adolescents born 1992–1995 and resident in 33 Finnish communities were invited in 2007–2009 and assigned by community to gender-neutral HPV16/18 vaccination, HPV16/18 vaccination of girls with hepatitis B vaccination of boys, or gender-neutral hepatitis B vaccination, and followed up with cervicovaginal sampling from 18.5 years of age, to compare the overall and herd effects of gender-neutral and girls-only HPV vaccination.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25593103") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29055031") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HPV") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34097688") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID:34097688%20AND%20SRC:MED&resultType=core&format=json") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2007-2010, the 1992-1995 birth cohorts of 33 Finnish communities were randomized to receive gender-neutral HPV vaccination (Arm A), girls-only HPV vaccination (Arm B), or no HPV vaccination (Arm C) (11 communities per trial arm).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002604> "The participants of a community-randomised phase IV trial in which early adolescents born 1992–1995 and resident in 33 Finnish communities were invited in 2007–2009 and assigned by community to gender-neutral HPV16/18 vaccination, HPV16/18 vaccination of girls with hepatitis B vaccination of boys, or gender-neutral hepatitis B vaccination, and followed up with cervicovaginal sampling from 18.5 years of age, to compare the overall and herd effects of gender-neutral and girls-only HPV vaccination.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9194-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Members of the cohort are babies born to women in this source population who become aware of the study and volunteer to participate through registration on the study website (www.progettoninfea.it).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-007-9194-2") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NINFEA cohort is an Internet-based birth cohort established in Italy with the aim of investigating the effects of early life exposures on the health of newborns, infants, adolescents and adults.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A17955333+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this purpose we constructed a website (www.progettoninfea.it), with on-line questionnaires to be completed during pregnancy and at 6 and 18 months after delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4526937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NINFEA cohort started as a pilot study in the city of Turin, Italy, in July 2005 and has been gradually extended to the rest of Italy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39808632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11731713/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After delivery, mothers were invited to fill online follow-up questionnaires at 6 and 18 months of age of their child, and then when they turned four, seven, ten, thirteen and sixteen years old.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17955333") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26071071") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NINFEA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.progettoninfea.it/index_en") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39808632") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11731713/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NINFEA study is a prospective Italian birth cohort that recruited more than 7500 pregnant women (www.progettoninfea.it) [12,13] from 2005 to 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002605> "An Italian internet-based birth cohort of children born to pregnant women who volunteered through the study website, started as a pilot in Turin in July 2005 and extended to the rest of Italy, with recruitment until 2016 and online questionnaires completed by the mothers during pregnancy and repeatedly through the child's childhood and adolescence, set up to investigate the effects of pre-natal and early post-natal exposures on infant, child and adult health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407552") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4430416/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The present study is part of the “Rhea” project, a pregnancy cohort which examines prospectively a population-based cohort of pregnant women and their children at the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece [25].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606> "A population-based mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece, recruited at their first major ultrasound examination around week 12 of gestation at four prenatal clinics in Heraklion from February 2007 to February 2008, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy towards young adulthood to study how environmental, dietary and other early-life exposures affect the health of mothers and children, with a focus on childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407552") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4430416/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited pregnant women (Greek and immigrants) at the time of the first comprehensive ultrasound examination, around week 12 of gestation (mean: 12.1 weeks, SD: 0.7), from four prenatal clinics (two public and two private) in Heraklion city, during the twelve-month period from February 2007 until February 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606> "A population-based mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece, recruited at their first major ultrasound examination around week 12 of gestation at four prenatal clinics in Heraklion from February 2007 to February 2008, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy towards young adulthood to study how environmental, dietary and other early-life exposures affect the health of mothers and children, with a focus on childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407552") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Rhea study was established in 2007 in the island of Crete, aiming to recruit a representative sample of mother-child pairs from early pregnancy and to follow them up to young adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606> "A population-based mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece, recruited at their first major ultrasound examination around week 12 of gestation at four prenatal clinics in Heraklion from February 2007 to February 2008, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy towards young adulthood to study how environmental, dietary and other early-life exposures affect the health of mothers and children, with a focus on childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25970502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33407552") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/RHEA") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This has changed dramatically over the last 50 years, and the Rhea cohort was created in response to the rising concerns about the high rates of childhood obesity in Greece (more than 40% overweight and obese children at school age according to recent estimates).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002606> "A population-based mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the prefecture of Heraklion, Crete, Greece, recruited at their first major ultrasound examination around week 12 of gestation at four prenatal clinics in Heraklion from February 2007 to February 2008, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy towards young adulthood to study how environmental, dietary and other early-life exposures affect the health of mothers and children, with a focus on childhood obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7003818/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The third cohort includes inhabitants of the municipality of Ommoord, Rotterdam aged >45 years, and was recruited between 2006 and 2008.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2006, a further extension of the cohort was initiated in which 3932 subjects were included, aged 45–54 years, out of 6057 invited, living in the Ommoord district.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RS-III-1 refers to the baseline examination of all persons aged 45 years and over living in the study district that had not been examined already (i.e., mainly comprising those aged 45–60 years).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "RS-III-2 refers to the first re-examination of this third cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Rotterdam Study was designed as a prospective cohort study, initially comprising 7983 persons living in the well-defined Ommoord district in the city of Rotterdam in The Netherlands (78% of 10,215 invitees).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31638273") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32367290") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7250962/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study aims to unravel etiology, preclinical course, natural history and potential targets for intervention for chronic diseases in mid-life and late-life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002607> "The third cohort of the Rotterdam Study, a prospective population-based cohort of inhabitants of Ommoord, a suburb of Rotterdam in the Netherlands, aged 45 and over who had not already been examined in the study (mainly people aged 45 to 54), enrolled from 2006 to 2008 and re-examined periodically to study the causes and course of chronic diseases in mid-life and late life.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6843812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DNA, RNA, serum, plasma, placenta, cord blood, meconium, child and mother stools, living cells, milk, hair and repeated urine samples were collected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6843812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment took place between July 2014 and July 2017 in eight obstetrical ultrasonography practices located in Grenoble area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6843812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall aim of the cohort is to provide an improved characterization of the effect of time-varying prevalent environmental factors on continuous health and biological parameters related to respiratory health, growth and neurodevelopment, as well as to contribute to the unraveling of the underlying biological pathways possibly implied.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6843812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study subjects of SEPAGES cohort were pregnant women, their partner and future child.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6843812/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We developed a couple-child cohort relying on deep phenotyping and extended personal exposure assessment aiming to better characterize the effects of components of the exposome, including air pollutants and non-persistent endocrine disruptors, on child health and development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31615055") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34435564") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cohorte-sepages.fr/en") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mise en place dans la région grenobloise, la cohorte est coordonnée par une équipe de recherche en épidémiologie environnementale de l’Inserm (Institut national de la santé et de la recherche médicale) et de l’Université Grenoble Alpes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002608> "A French couple-child cohort of pregnant women, their partners and their children, recruited between July 2014 and July 2017 at eight obstetric ultrasonography practices in the Grenoble area, set up by Inserm, CNRS and University Grenoble Alpes as a research platform with repeated personal exposure measurements and biological sampling during pregnancy and early life, to study the effects of air pollutants, non-persistent endocrine disruptors and other exposures on child growth, respiratory health and neurodevelopment and the biological pathways involved.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21870174+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We evaluated whether a diet high in fatty fish, bilberries and wholegrain products (Healthy Diet) improves biomarkers reflecting inflammation and endothelial dysfunction in individuals with impaired glucose metabolism.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3938672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Altogether 131 subjects (40–70 y, BMI 26–39 kg/m2) with impaired glucose metabolism and features of the metabolic syndrome were randomized into three groups with 12-week periods according to a parallel study design.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3938672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Recruitment and screening were done during October 2007 - November 2008, and intervention periods were carried out during January 2008 - June 2009.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3938672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The trial was conducted at the Department of Clinical Nutrition, University of Eastern Finland (Kuopio, Finland).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3938672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They consumed either: a) wholegrain and low postprandial insulin response grain products, fatty fish 3 times a week, and bilberries 3 portions per day (HealthyDiet), b) wholegrain and low postprandial insulin response grain products (WGED), or c) refined wheat breads as cereal products (Control).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21870174") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00573781") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24587337") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3938672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We studied the combined effects of wholegrain, fish and bilberries on serum metabolic profile and lipid transfer protein activities in subjects with the metabolic syndrome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002609> "A 12-week randomised controlled dietary intervention trial of men and women aged 40 to 70 with impaired glucose metabolism and other features of the metabolic syndrome, recruited in 2007–2008 in the Kuopio area of Finland and run by the Department of Clinical Nutrition of the University of Eastern Finland, comparing a healthy Nordic-type diet rich in whole grain products, fatty fish and bilberries and a whole-grain-enriched diet with a control diet for effects on glucose and lipid metabolism, inflammation and endothelial function.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5727241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All women in Finland are at their 12th week of pregnancy offered screening for congenital infections (hepatitis B, HIV, and syphilis).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5727241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In summary, the FMC is a unique, accessible biobank for epidemiological, biomarker, and surveillance studies on cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5727241/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The residual serum samples are stored in the FMC 3.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37196097") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10681868/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The FMC includes 2 million biospecimens from >90% of pregnancies in Finland between 1983 and 2016; samples were collected during the late weeks of the first trimester or the early weeks of the second trimester of pregnancy [24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "FMC is linkable with population-based health registers including the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29071810") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Finnish Maternity Cohort (FMC) in Northern Finland Biobank Borealis is a collection of serum samples comprising virtually the entire population of Finnish females, who have been pregnant since 1983.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002610> "A nationwide population-based biobank cohort of the women in Finland who have been pregnant since 1983, made up of the early-pregnancy serum samples left over from the screening for congenital infections offered to all pregnant women, now held by the Northern Finland Biobank Borealis and linkable to national health registers such as the Finnish Cancer Registry and the Medical Birth Register, as a resource for epidemiological, biomarker and surveillance studies of cancer and other diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25948663+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All cohort members were volunteer participants and gave informed consent prior to inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25948663+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to an extensive questionnaire, blood and urine samples were collected for storage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25948663+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline data collection contains records for 13 172 individuals (2010-11), between 45 and 64 years of age, from the city of Kielce and surrounding rural area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A25948663+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study aims at providing information on determinants of health differences between Poland and other countries in the region, especially related to premature mortality.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5466582/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data collection was supported by the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund, Grant, PNRF-228-AI-1/07.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25948663") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28626626") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5466582/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Polish Norwegian Study (PONS) is a prospective community-based investigation of risk factors for chronic diseases, conducted in the Kielce region of south-east Poland (Manczuk et al., 2015).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002611> "A prospective community-based cohort of volunteer men and women aged 45–64 years recruited in 2010–2011 from the city of Kielce and its surrounding rural area in south-eastern Poland, with questionnaires and stored blood and urine samples, set up with support from the Polish-Norwegian Research Fund to study health, health-related behaviours and risk factors for chronic diseases and premature mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CVD morbidity was identified through linkage with the National Hospital Discharge Register (till 1 January 2006) based on information on the date of birth, gender and postal code using a validated probabilistic method [24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the Monitoring Project on Chronic Disease Risk Factors (MORGEN-project), baseline cardiovascular risk factor data were collected in 1993–1997 in 22 769 men and women aged 20–65 years [23], [24].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Monitoring Project on Risk Factors and Chronic Diseases in the Netherlands (MORGEN) study was supported by the Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport of the Netherlands, and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, Bilthoven, The Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The authors would like to thank the logistics and data managers of the Monitoring Project on Risk Factors for Chronic Diseases (MORGEN-project), and the epidemiologists and field workers of the Municipal Health Services in Amsterdam, Doetinchem and Maastricht for their important contribution to the data collection for these studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project was carried out in random population samples of Amsterdam (respons rate 33%), Maastricht (43%) and Doetinchem (68%) in the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3241680/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Vital status was checked by the national population register.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22194890") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.rivm.nl/doetinchem-cohort-studie/metingen") Annotation(rdfs:comment "naast hart- en vaatziekten en de klassieke risicofactoren (waaronder voeding), kwam er ook aandacht voor diabetes, kanker, astma en COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (chronische bronchitis of longemfyseem)) (onder andere testen van de longfunctie), migraine, klachten van het bewegingsapparaat en kwaliteit van leven.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002612> "A population-based study of men and women aged 20–65 years drawn as random samples of the populations of Amsterdam, Maastricht and Doetinchem in the Netherlands, whose cardiovascular and other chronic disease risk factors were measured by the Municipal Health Services in 1993–1997 in a project supported by the Dutch Ministry of Health, Welfare and Sport and the National Institute for Public Health and the Environment, and who were followed for disease through linkage with national registers.")

