AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35092330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9306822/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Generation R Next Study is conducted by the Erasmus University Medical Center in collaboration with the Erasmus University Rotterdam and the City of Rotterdam.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35092330") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9306822/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was embedded in the Generation R Next Study, a population‐based prospective cohort study from preconception onwards in Rotterdam, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11802838/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were enrolled in a population-based prospective cohort, the Generation R Next Study, from fetal life until adulthood in Rotterdam, the Netherlands.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11802838/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort is designed to enable the identification of early environmental and genetic causes and causal pathways leading to normal and abnormal growth, development and health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13368358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women and their partners residing in the Rotterdam area who were either planning pregnancy (within a year) or were pregnant (preferably less than 11 weeks) between August 2017 and July 2021 were eligible for inclusion.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39915565") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41762673") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GenR%20Next") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://generationr.nl/next") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Generation R Next is wereldwijd het eerste onderzoek dat een zo grote groep toekomstige ouders en kinderen volgt.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002613> "A population-based prospective cohort in Rotterdam, the Netherlands, of women enrolled from August 2017 before conception or during pregnancy, with their partners and children, followed from preconception and fetal life onwards by the Generation R group at Erasmus MC to study the growth, development and health of a new generation of children and their parents.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13235725/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NORDCAP study data were linked from different national registers and cover all individuals born in Finland during years 1987-2016 (~1 800 000 individuals) followed from birth to December 31, 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13235725/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a longitudinal, register-based total birth cohort study using data from the Nordic Children and Adolescents Born Preterm (NORDCAP) study, governed by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Nordic Children and Adults Born Preterm (NORDCAP) project was originally established to investigate how preterm birth and maternal pregnancy disorders predict offspring health, well-being and societal achievements of the offspring from childhood to adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition, the study examines the health and well-being of the children's parents, the intergenerational transmission of health, and childhood and adolescence factors as predictors of health and well-being.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Finnish study population includes all births in Finland during 1987–2023, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register, THL (approximately 2 100 000 children).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42241480") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/NORDCAP") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.oulu.fi/en/projects/nordic-children-and-adults-born-preterm-nordcap") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study started at the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare, but moved to University of Oulu in summer 2025.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002614> "A register-based cohort of all children born in Finland from 1987 onwards, identified from the Finnish Medical Birth Register and linked with other national health, social and population registers and with data on their parents, held by the University of Oulu (earlier by the Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare) to study how preterm birth, pregnancy disorders and other early-life factors predict health, well-being and societal outcomes from childhood to adulthood, and the intergenerational transmission of health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.10707225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8663864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A pilot study will be carried out on maternity exposure by monitoring pregnant women using an innovative wearable exposome sensor to generate personal health profiling of the participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy pregnant and non-pregnant women in Finland, enrolled by the University of Oulu from 2022 within the EU Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP) project and followed for at least four months with wearable personal exposome monitors and repeated biological sampling (blood, saliva, sweat, urine), to pilot personal profiling of chemical and biological exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.10707225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8663864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "an innovative wearable exposure sensor that collects airborne and toxic substances as well as particulate matters derived from virus, bacteria, fungal spores, animal debris, and plant pollens.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy pregnant and non-pregnant women in Finland, enrolled by the University of Oulu from 2022 within the EU Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP) project and followed for at least four months with wearable personal exposome monitors and repeated biological sampling (blood, saliva, sweat, urine), to pilot personal profiling of chemical and biological exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.10707225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Longitudinal cohort of pregnant and non-pregnant women for exposome estimation from blood, saliva, sweat and personal aerosols.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy pregnant and non-pregnant women in Finland, enrolled by the University of Oulu from 2022 within the EU Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP) project and followed for at least four months with wearable personal exposome monitors and repeated biological sampling (blood, saliva, sweat, urine), to pilot personal profiling of chemical and biological exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.10707225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PopulationContinents EuropeCountries Finland") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy pregnant and non-pregnant women in Finland, enrolled by the University of Oulu from 2022 within the EU Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP) project and followed for at least four months with wearable personal exposome monitors and repeated biological sampling (blood, saliva, sweat, urine), to pilot personal profiling of chemical and biological exposures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34909561") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://api.datacite.org/dois/10.5281/zenodo.10707225") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WDC") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start/End data collection 2022 until 2022") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002615> "A longitudinal cohort of healthy pregnant and non-pregnant women in Finland, enrolled by the University of Oulu from 2022 within the EU Human Exposome Assessment Platform (HEAP) project and followed for at least four months with wearable personal exposome monitors and repeated biological sampling (blood, saliva, sweat, urine), to pilot personal profiling of chemical and biological exposures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28812915+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kardiovize Brno 2030 study was designed as a prospective cohort study to investigate the complex relationships of cardiovascular disease and outcomes with a range of biological, psychosocial, environmental, behavioral, and economic factors in an urban population of the Czech Republic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616> "A prospective population-based cohort of a random, sex- and age-stratified 1% sample of residents of Brno, Czech Republic, aged 25–64 years, drawn from health insurance registries in 2013 and examined at St Anne's University Hospital in Brno, to study how biological, psychosocial, environmental, behavioural and economic factors relate to cardiovascular disease and its outcomes in a Central European urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28812915+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We randomly selected a 1% sample of the city of Brno residents aged 25-64 years stratified by sex and age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616> "A prospective population-based cohort of a random, sex- and age-stratified 1% sample of residents of Brno, Czech Republic, aged 25–64 years, drawn from health insurance registries in 2013 and examined at St Anne's University Hospital in Brno, to study how biological, psychosocial, environmental, behavioural and economic factors relate to cardiovascular disease and its outcomes in a Central European urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8488447/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Survey sampling was done in January 2013 with technical assistance from the largest (state‐run) health insurance company using the registries of all health insurance companies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616> "A prospective population-based cohort of a random, sex- and age-stratified 1% sample of residents of Brno, Czech Republic, aged 25–64 years, drawn from health insurance registries in 2013 and examined at St Anne's University Hospital in Brno, to study how biological, psychosocial, environmental, behavioural and economic factors relate to cardiovascular disease and its outcomes in a Central European urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28812915") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34631132") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8488447/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline health assessment, face‐to‐face health interview, and comprehensive questionnaire were performed by trained nurses and physicians at the International Clinical Research Center (ICRC) of the St. Anne's University Hospital (FNUSA) in Brno;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002616> "A prospective population-based cohort of a random, sex- and age-stratified 1% sample of residents of Brno, Czech Republic, aged 25–64 years, drawn from health insurance registries in 2013 and examined at St Anne's University Hospital in Brno, to study how biological, psychosocial, environmental, behavioural and economic factors relate to cardiovascular disease and its outcomes in a Central European urban population.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BCS70 began as the British Births Survey") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Fifty years of follow-up provide opportunities for new research on social, economic and health outcomes in mid-life, their antecedents and generational change.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 1970 British Cohort Study (BCS70) is an ongoing, multidisciplinary, longitudinal study of a cohort of over 17 000 births in England, Scotland and Wales.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10244059/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The initial sample comprised all births in Britain in a single week in 1970.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://cls.ucl.ac.uk/cls-studies/1970-british-cohort-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over the course of participants’ lives, BCS70 has collected information on health, physical, educational and social development, and economic circumstances among other factors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35849349") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BCS%201970") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BCS70 is designed and managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies, Social Research Institute, UCL and is core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002617> "A longitudinal birth cohort of the people born in England, Scotland and Wales in a single week of 1970, which began as the British Births Survey and has followed its members' health, physical, educational and social development and economic circumstances through childhood and adult life; it is managed by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London and core funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4000047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1985 and 1994 baseline examinations were conducted in 4874 women who were 55 years of age at time of recruitment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of women aged 55 years at recruitment from the industrialised Ruhr Area and rural areas north of it (Borken, Dülmen) in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, examined at baseline between 1985 and 1994 and followed up from 2006 onwards; initiated by the State Government of North Rhine-Westphalia to study the health effects of air pollution in women, and run by the IUF – Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine, Düsseldorf.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4000047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2006, a follow-up examination was conducted to assess the change in respiratory symptoms after a strong decline in concentrations of ambient air pollutants had taken place in the Ruhr Area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of women aged 55 years at recruitment from the industrialised Ruhr Area and rural areas north of it (Borken, Dülmen) in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, examined at baseline between 1985 and 1994 and followed up from 2006 onwards; initiated by the State Government of North Rhine-Westphalia to study the health effects of air pollution in women, and run by the IUF – Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine, Düsseldorf.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4000047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SALIA study was initiated in the early 1980s by the State Government of North-Rhine Westphalia to investigate the health effects of air pollution exposure in women.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of women aged 55 years at recruitment from the industrialised Ruhr Area and rural areas north of it (Borken, Dülmen) in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, examined at baseline between 1985 and 1994 and followed up from 2006 onwards; initiated by the State Government of North Rhine-Westphalia to study the health effects of air pollution in women, and run by the IUF – Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine, Düsseldorf.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4000047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The strength of the study is that SALIA is a population-based cohort of elderly women (not a cohort of either highly exposed or diseased and more susceptible subjects) with a detailed exposure assessment and an in-depth characterization of subclinical pulmonary inflammation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of women aged 55 years at recruitment from the industrialised Ruhr Area and rural areas north of it (Borken, Dülmen) in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, examined at baseline between 1985 and 1994 and followed up from 2006 onwards; initiated by the State Government of North Rhine-Westphalia to study the health effects of air pollution in women, and run by the IUF – Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine, Düsseldorf.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24645673") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4000047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study population consists of women from the industrialized Ruhr Area in Germany (Dortmund, Duisburg, Herne, Gelsenkirchen, Essen) and two non-industrialized rural areas north of the Ruhr area (Borken, Dülmen).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002618> "A population-based longitudinal cohort of women aged 55 years at recruitment from the industrialised Ruhr Area and rural areas north of it (Borken, Dülmen) in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, examined at baseline between 1985 and 1994 and followed up from 2006 onwards; initiated by the State Government of North Rhine-Westphalia to study the health effects of air pollution in women, and run by the IUF – Leibniz Research Institute for Environmental Medicine, Düsseldorf.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6499508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants were healthy adults aged 25–70 y with LDL cholesterol ≥3.5 mmol/L, total cholesterol was within the normal range for each age group, and triglycerides (TGs) were ≤2.6 mmol/L.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6499508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted an 8-wk, double-blind, randomized controlled dietary intervention study at the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences and the University of Oslo, Norway, from July 2012 until April 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6499508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recently conducted an 8-wk, double-blind, randomized controlled trial replacing SFAs with PUFAs in healthy subjects with moderate hypercholesterolemia (n = 99).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6499508/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recently performed a double-blind, randomized controlled dietary intervention study exchanging similar food items with improved fat quality (replacing SFAs with PUFAs), which led to an 11% reduction in LDL cholesterol and a 9% reduction in total cholesterol in the experimental (Ex-diet) group compared with the control-diet (C-diet) group (10).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Moreover, we wanted to gain insight into the molecular mechanisms of the cholesterol-lowering effect of replacing SFA with PUFA in humans by analyzing gene expression in immune cells and blood metabolomics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31051508") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.med.uio.no/imb/english/research/projects/noma/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall aim of the NoMa study was to study the effect of intake of commercially available food products, in which SFA had been replaced by PUFA, on lipid profile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002619> "The participants of an 8-week double-blind randomised controlled dietary intervention trial run from 2012 to 2014 by the University of Oslo and the Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences, Norway, in which adults with moderately elevated cholesterol ate commercial food items in which saturated fat had been replaced by polyunsaturated fat, or control items, to study effects on blood lipids, immune-cell gene expression and blood metabolites.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A two-stage stratified random sampling scheme was applied, with the primary sampling unit being the municipality/local community (first stage) and the final unit being the individual (second stage) for to select the HYDRIA representative survey sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible individuals were men and women aged 18 years and over residing permanently in Greece based on the latest Greek general census (2011).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HYDRIA study is the first national health and nutrition survey conducted on a large representative sample of the adult population in Greece, providing evidence for the dietary and health status of the population [3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HYDRIA survey sampling frame covered all the 51 prefectures of the 13 regions of the country [3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The data collection started in June 2013 and was completed in December 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35334847") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8949101/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study design for the HYDRIA survey followed the recommendations of the European Health Examination Survey (EHES) [18] and the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) [19] for the collection of health and dietary data at a national level, allowing for intercountry comparisons.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002620> "A cross-sectional national health examination and nutrition survey of a representative sample of adults aged 18 years and over in Greece, drawn by two-stage stratified random sampling across all prefectures and examined between June 2013 and December 2014 by the Hellenic Health Foundation, following European Health Examination Survey and EFSA methodology, to describe the population's dietary intake, nutritional status and health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4230797/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A four-week run-in period with low grain fibre intake preceded two consecutive four-week test periods with high grain fibre intake in randomized, cross-over manner (Figure 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4230797/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Healthy men and women were recruited based on one or several of the following self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after ingestion of grain products, especially rye bread: flatulence, bloating, discomfort, constipation, and diarrhea.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4230797/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim was to investigate whether the white wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran (BRB + WW) promotes similar effects to WGR on glucose metabolism and plasma levels of SCFAs in healthy subjects with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4230797/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was carried out as a part of the FIBREFECTS (Grain fiber modification for gut mediated health effects) funded mainly by TEKES – The Finnish Funding Agency for Technology and Innovation – and to a smaller extent by Oy Karl Fazer Ab, Vaasan Oy, and Ravintoraisio Oy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4230797/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "White wheat bread (WW; 3% fibre) was consumed during the run-in, and WGR and BRB + WW (10% fibre) during the test periods.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25370913") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03550365") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/FEF") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start/End data collection 2011 until 2011") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002621> "The participants of a randomised crossover dietary intervention trial started in 2011 by the University of Eastern Finland with VTT Technical Research Centre of Finland, within the FIBREFECTS project, in which adults with self-reported gastrointestinal symptoms after eating grain products ate white wheat bread during a run-in and then wholegrain rye bread and wheat bread enriched with bioprocessed rye bran, to study the effects of modified cereal fibre on glucose metabolism, gut fermentation and gut-mediated health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3926689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biological material is collected, processed and temporarily cryopreserved in the maternity centers and periodically transferred to the Piccolipiù biobank, located at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità (ISS, Italian National Institute of Health), for final storage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3926689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Blood samples (4 ml in EDTA and 5 ml in serum separator tubes) are drawn from mother’s cubital vein just before or after delivery, and from the child’s umbilical cord soon after birth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3926689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Piccolipiù is an Italian birth cohort recently set up to investigate the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors acting during pre-natal and early post-natal life on infant and child health and development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3926689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Postnatal follow-up currently occurs at 6, 12, and 24 months of age using on-line or postal self administered questionnaire; further questionnaires and medical examinations are envisaged.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3926689/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Piccolipiù birth cohort is a relatively large cohort combining detailed information from questionnaires and repeated follow-up contacts, with a biobank that stores samples from participating mother-newborn pairs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24506846") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36191030") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9529104/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Piccolipiù is the name of a birth cohort of 3,358 children enrolled in six maternity wards located in five Italian cities (Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin, and Viareggio) between October 2011 and March 2015 [26].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002622> "An Italian multicentre prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from October 2011 to March 2015 in six maternity units in Florence, Rome, Trieste, Turin and Viareggio, with maternal blood, cord blood and other samples stored in a biobank at the Istituto Superiore di Sanità and follow-up by questionnaires through childhood, set up to study the effects of environmental exposures, parental conditions and social factors in pre- and early post-natal life on child health and development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3389694/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "After the weight-loss period, the subjects were randomized, stratified by age and sex, into two diet groups: higher-satiety food group (HSF) and lower-satiety food group (LSF) (Table 4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3389694/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Originally 99 (28 males, 71 females) obese (inclusion criteria being body mass index (BMI) 30–40 kg/m2, age 30–65 years) subjects were recruited into the intervention study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3389694/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The weight-loss period was performed by using very-low-calorie-diet (VLCD) products (Nutrifast, Leiras Finland Ltd) providing 600 kcal/day.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3389694/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They were recruited by an announcement in a local newspaper and among the eligible subjects who had participated previously in the studies performed at the University of Kuopio, Kuopio, Finland (currently University of Eastern Finland).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3389694/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study aimed to investigate factors associated with weight management, especially whether satiety value of food as a part of a weight-maintenance diet would affect self-regulation of food intake and weight management.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22792447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN67529475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ELIPA") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start/End data collection 2008 until 2009") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002623> "The participants of a randomised controlled weight-management trial run from 2008 to 2010 by the Institute of Public Health and Clinical Nutrition, University of Kuopio (now University of Eastern Finland), Finland, in which adults aged 30–65 with obesity followed a very-low-energy diet and were then randomised to weight-maintenance diets containing foods of higher or lower predetermined satiety value, to study whether food satiety value affects self-regulation of food intake and weight management.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CONSTANCES is designed as a randomly selected representative sample of French adults aged 18–69 years at inception; 200,000 subjects will be included over a five-year period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inception started at the end of 2012, and the final cohort will be constituted by the end of 2017.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The CONSTANCES general-purpose cohort is intended to serve as an epidemiological research infrastructure accessible to the epidemiologic research community with a focus on occupational and social factors, and on chronic diseases and aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The follow-up includes a yearly self-administered questionnaire, and a periodic visit to an HSC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects included in CONSTANCES are also followed up “passively” (so-called because this follow-up does not require the subjects’ participation) by annual linkage with three national social and health data databases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4690834/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "due to our partnership with the National Health Insurance Fund administered by the “Caisse Nationale d’Assurance Maladie des travailleurs salaries” (CNAMTS), we had to restrict the source population of CONSTANCES to salaried workers, professionally active or retired and their family") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26520638") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.constances.fr/la-cohorte/le-projet/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Une biobanque regroupe 1,4 million d’échantillons de sang et d’urine recueillis lors de la visite médicale.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002624> "A French general-purpose population-based cohort of adults aged 18–69 years at inclusion, randomly sampled from people covered by the national health insurance fund (CNAMTS) and included from the end of 2012 through health examinations at selected Health Screening Centres across France, with yearly questionnaires, periodic examinations, a biobank and linkage to national social and health databases; run by Inserm as a research infrastructure with a focus on occupational and social factors, chronic diseases and ageing.")

