AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2672398/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "On their first visit to a general practitioner, all pregnant women living in Kaunas between 2007 and 2008 were invited to join the cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2672398/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a prospective cohort study of pregnant women as a part of the European Commission FP6 HiWATE project [27].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2672398/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited these women for the prospective cohort study, enrolling them at first trimester of gestation at the four prenatal care clinics affiliated to the hospitals of the Kaunas University of Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2672398/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women whose medical records indicated that they had pregnancy-induced hypertension, a history of diabetes mellitus or living outside the Kaunas municipality, were excluded from the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27067890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4838715/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2012–2013, we invited the KANC cohort of 3294 mothers and their 4−6-year-old children to participate in this study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19440446") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30206078") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6144482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Concentrations of drinking water disinfection by-products (DBPs) during pregnancy were estimated from water company concentration and distribution data as part of the water contaminants and stillbirth, congenital anomalies, birth weight, preterm delivery (HiWate) project in four of the cohorts (BiB, KANC, INMA, RHEA).38") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002626> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women living in Kaunas municipality, Lithuania, recruited in the first trimester at four prenatal care clinics of the Kaunas University of Medicine hospitals from 2007, first as the Kaunas cohort of the EU HiWATE project on drinking-water contaminants and pregnancy outcomes, and their children, later followed up in childhood and within the HELIX exposome project.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11142448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Young Adults cohort is an on-going follow-up study of the Czech part of the ELSPAC birth cohort (European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood) that was initiated in 1991–1992 in the Czech Republic, in Brno and Znojmo region.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Obracíme se na Vás, původní účastníky studie ELSPAC, dnes již mladé dospělé, abyste s námi pokračovali v navazující studii, a spolu s Vámi také Vaši sourozenci a partneři a partnerky nehledě na věk, místo narození a státní příslušnost.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sledujte s námi vliv faktorů životního stylu a sociálních faktorů na rozvoj civilizačních onemocnění, výskyt deprese nebo kvalitu spánku.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Stejně tak se do studie mohou přihlásit vrstevníci původních účastníků ELSPAC, tedy kdokoli narozen v letech 1991 a 1992, a to bez ohledu na místo narození.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Studie Young Adults, spuštěna v březnu 2019, je pokračováním dlouholetého výzkumu ELSPAC, který sledoval děti narozené v roce 1991 a 1992 v Brně a Znojmě a jejich rodiče.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38820320") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/youngadults") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Z biologických vzorků se kromě žilní krve odebírá také ranní moč a provádí se bukální stěr.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002627> "A follow-up study, begun in 2019 at Masaryk University in Brno, Czech Republic, of the young adults born in 1991 and 1992 who took part in the Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood, joined by their siblings and partners and by others born in those years, who are examined clinically, give blood, urine and buccal samples and answer questionnaires, to study how lifestyle, social and environmental factors relate to early signs of chronic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A comprehensive electronic database was completed in 2012 when the ELSPAC study became a part of the RECETOX open-access research infrastructure at Masaryk University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ELSPAC was designed as a population-based prospective longitudinal birth cohort study to investigate the effects of biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental factors on pregnancy, delivery and subsequent child´s development and health.1") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participating women also invited their partners to join the study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Self-reported questionnaires for mothers and fathers were administered at 6th and 18th months after birth, and subsequently during the 3rd, 5th, 7th, 11th, 15th and 19th years of the child.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The birth cohort consists of children born in the Brno and Znojmo regions (South Moravia, Czech Republic) in 1991 and 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27380795") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5837270/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was initiated by the World Health Organization (WHO) Regional Office for Europe in 1985, with the aim to enrol 40 000 children across Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002628> "The Czech arm of the European Longitudinal Study of Pregnancy and Childhood initiated by the WHO Regional Office for Europe: a population-based prospective birth cohort of children born in 1991 and 1992 in the Brno and Znojmo regions of South Moravia, Czech Republic, and their parents, followed from pregnancy into early adulthood by questionnaires, medical records and examinations to study biological, psychosocial, economic and environmental influences on pregnancy, delivery, child development and health, and now held by RECETOX at Masaryk University.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3222984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Gynecologists, obstetricians, and ultrasonographers recruited women during consultations in early pregnancy, informing them about the nature of the study and asking them to participate (after providing written consent).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3222984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study used a case-cohort design nested in a prospective birth cohort conducted in the Brittany region of France from 2002 through 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3222984/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were enrolled before the 19th week of gestation after providing written informed consent and completing a questionnaire at home concerning family social and demographic characteristics, diet, and lifestyle.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24295221") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3893486/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PELAGIE mother-child cohort study, fully described elsewhere [14,15] enrolled 3421 pregnant women before 19 weeks of gestation in three districts of Brittany (France), from 2002 through 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28250046") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28250046+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated the associations between prenatal and childhood exposure to pyrethroid insecticides and behavioural skills in 6-year-olds.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21367690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.pelagie-inserm.fr/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PELAGIE") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PELAGIE mother-child cohort was set up with the aim to study the effect of prenatal exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals on reproduction and child development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002629> "A mother-child cohort set up by INSERM in Rennes of pregnant women enrolled before the 19th week of gestation by gynaecologists, obstetricians and ultrasonographers in three départements of Brittany, France, between 2002 and 2006, whose children are followed from birth through childhood into young adulthood, to study the effects of prenatal and childhood exposure to environmental and occupational chemicals such as pesticides on pregnancy, fertility and child development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13013234/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between April 2005 and August 2006, 8647 liveborn infants were enrolled in all the public maternity wards in the Porto Metropolitan Area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13013234/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were drawn from Generation XXI, a prospective population-based birth cohort study assembled in Porto, Portugal [21, 22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2005, it was possible to meet the logistic conditions needed to start this work and thus it was born the Geração 21 project at the Departmento de Epidemiologia Clinica, Medicina preditiva e Saúde pública da Universidade do Porto.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 13-year evaluation took place between August 2018 and March 2020, at the Department of Clinical Epidemiology, Predictive Medicine and Public Health of the Faculty of Medicine of the University of Porto.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 18-year follow-up assessment was conducted between May 2023 and July 2025 at the Department of Clinical Epidemiology, Predictive Medicine and Public Health, Faculty of Medicine, University of Porto.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41874644") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.geracao21.com/en/project") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We intend to follow the evolution of several health parameters (social, behavioral, organizational, biological) in order to explore new hypothesis, new problems, that may allow us to understand the influence of prenatal and early life years in the development and health during adolescence and adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002630> "A prospective population-based birth cohort of infants born between April 2005 and August 2006 in all the public maternity units of the Porto Metropolitan Area, Portugal, and their families, set up at the University of Porto and followed through childhood and adolescence to study how pregnancy and early-life characteristics relate to later growth, health and risk of chronic disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11247150/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A randomly selected subset of the entire Moli-sani cohort was recalled for an active follow-up 12 years (median value; range 10–14 years) after the baseline assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11247150/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We utilized data from the Moli-sani Study, a population-based cohort established between 2005 and 2010, comprising 24,325 men and women aged ≥35 years residing in the Southern Italian region of Molise.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A follow-up based on linkage with hospital discharge records, clinical records and mortality regional registry was performed at December 2011 (FUP1) with a median of 4.3 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Citrated plasma, EDTA plasma, serum, cellular pellet and urinary spots are stored in liquid nitrogen in a specific Biobank.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First, townships were sampled in major areas by cluster sampling; then, within each township, participants aged ≥35 years were selected by simple random sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39010980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.moli-sani.org/?page_id=423") Annotation(rdfs:comment "“Moli-sani” (www.moli-sani.org) is a cohort study aiming at evaluating the risk factors (environmental, genetics, biomolecular) linked to chronic-degenerative disease with particular regard to cancer, cardiovascular disease and their intermediate phenotypes hypertension, diabetes, dyslipidemia, obesity and metabolic syndrome.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002631> "A population-based cohort of men and women aged 35 years or more living in the Molise region of southern Italy, randomly sampled with their family members from the city registries of Molise towns and recruited between 2005 and 2010, examined at baseline with a biobank of their samples and followed by linkage to regional health and mortality registries and a recall examination, to study genetic and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular, cancer and neurodegenerative diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11303690/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Central European Longitudinal Studies of Parents and Children: The Next Generation (CELSPAC: TNG) study is designed as a new prospective birth cohort which will follow up on 2,000 children from their prenatal period to adolescence with the aim of assessing exposome factors affecting children’s health32.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11303690/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The mothers (age ≥18 years) were recruited in their 38th week of pregnancy at University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, in 2015 and 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pro získání celkového pohledu na průběh těhotenství, porod, zdraví a vývoj dítěte nejen odebíráme biologický materiál, který dále analyzujeme, ale také získáváme data ze zdravotní dokumentace a vyplněných online dotazníků.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Studie The Next Generation (TNG), neboli Další generace, je unikátní projekt Masarykovy univerzity a Fakultní nemocnice Brno, který pomocí dlouhodobého zkoumání studie příčiny chronických onemocnění a poruch vývoje dítěte.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TNG sleduje matku před porodem a poté společně s dítětem od jeho narození až do věku 5 let.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39107353") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.celspac.cz/tng") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TNG započala v roce 2017 a nabírala těhotné ženy až do roku 2026.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002632> "A prospective birth cohort run by RECETOX at Masaryk University with University Hospital Brno, Czech Republic, which enrolled pregnant women from 2017 (after a 2015-2016 pilot) and follows them and their children from pregnancy through early childhood, collecting biological samples and questionnaires, to study exposome factors such as environment, lifestyle, nutrition, genetics and the gut microbiome behind chronic diseases and developmental disorders in children.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "During the annual assessments, children’s exposome parameters from the three main exposome domains will be evaluated using different assessment types, i.e., molecular biomarkers of exposure/effect, sensors, and questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Cyprus, participant recruitment took place between October 2023 and January 2024 and data collection for the baseline assessment was conducted from January 2024 to June 2024.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Randomly selected public primary schools will be the study’s main recruitment setting.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort will consist of children enrolled in the first grade of primary school, who will undergo annual follow-up assessments until completion of primary education.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "evaluate the effect of single and multiple environmental exposures on early-life biological programming linked to chronic disease risk, by applying validated biomarkers of exposure and effect, related to cardio-metabolic, neurodevelopmental, and respiratory outcomes and their early precursors") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://web.cut.ac.cy/childrenfirstcy/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42044183") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13119864/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the main biospecimens that will be collected in annual assessments will be urine and saliva samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002633> "The Cypriot site of the CHILDREN_FIRST multi-country prospective exposome cohort: children in the first grade of randomly selected public primary schools in Cyprus, recruited from October 2023 by the Cyprus University of Technology with the biobank of the University of Cyprus and assessed every year until the end of primary school with questionnaires, urine and saliva samples and home and school environmental measurements, to study how the exposome shapes early risk of cardiometabolic, neurodevelopmental and respiratory disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6360765/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Similar to the ORISCAV-LUX baseline study [2], the participation to the second wave included 3 main steps: filling in a self-reported questionnaire; clinical and anthropometric measurements according to standardised operating procedures; and blood, urine and hair samples collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6360765/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall sample (1558 participants) was mainly composed of randomly selected subjects, including 660 from the baseline sample and 455 from other health examination survey sample and 269 from civil registry sample (constituting in total 88.8%), against only 174 volunteers (11.2%), with significantly different characteristics and health status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6360765/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The “Observation of Cardiovascular Risk Factors in Luxembourg” (ORISCAV-LUX) survey, conducted between November 2007 and January 2009, was the first nationwide cross-sectional survey of cardiovascular health monitoring in Luxembourg [2].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34959934") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8706514/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the original ORISCAV-LUX survey (2007–2008) [8], N = 1432 participants were included by a systematic random sampling procedure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ORISCAV-LUX study was carried out by the Luxembourg Institute of Health (LIH) within the Department of Precision Health in 2007–2009 (Wave 1, 1432 participants) and in 2016-2018 (Wave 2, 1558 participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30717671") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.lih.lu/en/oriscav-lux/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study made it possible to conduct epidemiologic research and describe major traditional and emerging cardiovascular risk factors and associated conditions, such as diabetes, hypertension, lipid disorders and their evolution between 2008 and 2018.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002634> "A nationwide population-based study of adults living in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, run by the Luxembourg Institute of Health, whose first wave (2007-2009) examined a random sample of residents and whose second wave (2016-2018) re-examined them together with new participants from the civil registry, another national health examination survey and volunteers, with questionnaires, clinical measurements and blood, urine and hair samples, to describe the prevalence and evolution of cardiovascular risk factors.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42051041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13125972/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, it recruited 1080 pregnant women during their first routine hospital visit (weeks 11–14 of gestation), in three tertiary university hospitals (i.e., Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) in Barcelona (Spain) between October 2018 and April 2021 [28].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> "An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42051041") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13125972/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted in the context of the Barcelona Life Study Cohort (BiSC), a population‐based longitudinal birth cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> "An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "BiSC participants were recruited and had their first data collected at the end of the first trimester of pregnancy, with follow-ups in the second and third trimesters of pregnancy, delivery, and months 1, 2, 6, 8, 12, 18, 28, and 48 (ongoing) postnatally.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> "An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Barcelona Life Study Cohort (BiSC) is an exposome birth cohort, aiming to comprehensively evaluate the socio-environmental and genetic determinants (i) of foetal and child health, growth, and development towards adult life and (ii) of maternal mental and physical health and wellbeing during pregnancy and afterwards, while shedding light on the underlying biological mechanisms.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> "An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BiSC") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://projectebisc.org/en/bisc-project/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The enrolment of the BiSC participants (n=1080) was carried out between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain, including Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona, and their corresponding primary healthcare centres.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002635> "An exposome birth cohort of pregnant women enrolled between October 2018 and April 2021 at three tertiary university hospitals in Barcelona, Spain (Hospital Sant Joan de Déu, Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau and Hospital Clínic de Barcelona) and their primary healthcare centres, and of their children, followed from the first trimester of pregnancy through delivery into childhood to study the socio-environmental and genetic determinants of foetal and child health, growth and development and of maternal mental and physical health during and after pregnancy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Moreover, the study was approved by the corresponding ethic committees on each of the participating centers (Code IDs GENOBOX: Córdoba01/2017, Santiago 2011/198, Zaragoza 12/2010 and PUBMEP: Córdoba 260/3408, Santiago 2016/522, Zaragoza 22/2016, Granada 01/2017).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prepubertal boys and girls at the time of the GENOBOX study who have already reached puberty at the time of the PUBMEP study start, were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PUBMEP is a longitudinal study based on the follow-up of a cohort of children who had previously participated in the GENOBOX study (22–29).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9806164/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the PUBMEP study aimed to evaluate the prevalence of MetS and the progression of cardiometabolic risk factors related to it from prepuberty to puberty in a cohort of Spanish children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children were allocated into five experimental groups according to their obesity and insulin resistance (IR) status before and after the onset of puberty.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36601007") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://uceens.ugr.es/en/proyecto/puberty-and-metabolic-risk-in-obese-children-epigenetic-alterations-and-pathophysiological-and-diagnostic-implications/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The objective of the project is to determine biomarkers and epigenetic marks associated with the development of metabolic complications during the development of puberty according to the state of health in the prepuber age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002636> "A multicentre longitudinal follow-up in Spain (Santiago de Compostela, Córdoba, Zaragoza and Granada) of children who had taken part in the GENOBOX study before puberty and were re-examined after reaching puberty, grouped by obesity and insulin resistance status, to study the progression of metabolic syndrome and cardiometabolic risk factors from prepuberty to puberty and to find biomarkers and epigenetic marks of metabolic complications during puberty.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cut flowers are among the leading exports from Ecuador, and Pedro Moncayo is known for its rose and flower cultivation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ESPINA is a prospective cohort established in 2008 that aims to investigate the impacts of pesticide exposure on development from childhood to adulthood in individuals living within the agricultural community of Pedro Moncayo, Pichincha, Ecuador.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present article, we provide pesticide biomonitoring data at two time points of adolescents and young adults in a longitudinal cohort study in the agricultural county of Pedro Moncayo, Ecuador.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Institutions: University of California San Diego, La Jolla, CA, USA; Fundación Cimas del Ecuador, Quito, Pichincha, Ecuador.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12329275/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ESPINA study aimed to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not cohabitate with a floricultural or agricultural worker.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40777557") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://espina.ucsd.edu/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ESPINA is a prospective cohort study established in 2008 aimed at understanding the health effects of agrochemical and pesticide exposures, evaluated from childhood into adulthood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002637> "A prospective cohort set up in 2008 of children living in the agricultural (floricultural) community of Pedro Moncayo County, Pichincha, Ecuador, recruited to include a balanced mix of children who did and did not live with a floricultural or agricultural worker and followed with repeated examinations into adolescence and adulthood, run by the University of California San Diego with Fundación Cimas del Ecuador to study the health effects of pesticide and other agrochemical exposures from childhood to adulthood.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30775931") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6752936/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, information on sex, age, birthplace, marital status, education, and occupation collected from census are linked with the Regional Mortality Register and the Hospital Discharge Register through a personal identifying code, under strict controls to protect individual privacy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31399053") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6689157/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Residential history and vital status were available from the Municipal Register data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9157355/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All data presented in the study are stored by the Department of Epidemiology-Lazio Regional Health Service and only the research team and related Institutions have access to the data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9157355/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We used the Rome Longitudinal Study, the administrative cohort of residents in Rome who filled in the 2001 population census.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Rome Longitudinal Study: administrative cohort of >2 million individuals all ages, enrolled at Census date (Oct. 9 2011) and followed up until 2019 (to be updated).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35641005") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37944432") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROLS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To them, multiple environmental exposures (air pollutants, temperature, greenness, etc.) have been linked.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002638> "An administrative cohort of the residents of Rome, Italy, enrolled from population census returns (the 2001 census and the census of 9 October 2011) linked to the municipal population registry, and followed by record linkage with administrative health databases, with baseline residential addresses linked to environmental exposures such as air pollution, temperature and greenness. It is run by the Department of Epidemiology of the Lazio Regional Health Service (ASL Roma 1) to study social, occupational and environmental determinants of health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26503980+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Occupational health and safety (OHS) services collect a wide range of data during health surveillance.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A26503980+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To build a 'data warehouse' to make OHS data available for research and to investigate sector-specific health problems.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30199412") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30199412+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We investigated work and health's associations in a specific sector: the agricultural sector and for a specific and frequent health complaint: sore throat; using PRECUBE dataset of the Belgian Occupational Health and Safety, containing 381.615 occupational health observations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13487632/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PRECUBE, BelgiumGeneral population: national and regional1993–2025") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13487632/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PRECUBE: established and funded by IDEWE, External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Employees working for an employer who chose IDEWE as official External Service for Protection and Prevention at Work (ESPPW), for the corresponding follow-up period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26503980") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42615545") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Precube") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13487632/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This approval authorizes the secondary use and post hoc analysis of fully anonymized data originally collected in the context of legally mandated occupational health surveillance, in compliance with applicable Belgian legislation and relevant international ethical and data-protection frameworks, including the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002639> "An occupational cohort of the employees of employers in Belgium that chose IDEWE as their External Service for Prevention and Protection at Work, followed from 1993 through the records of their legally required occupational health surveillance. IDEWE pools the records in a data warehouse for research on work-related diseases and sector-specific health problems.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1626086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HAPIEE (Health, Alcohol and Psychosocial factors In Eastern Europe) study consists of three cohorts in Novosibirsk (Russia), Krakow (Poland) and six centres in the Czech Republic (Havirov/Karvina, Hradec Kralove, Jihlava, Kromeriz, Liberec and Usti nad Labem).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1626086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The baseline survey in Russia, Poland and the Czech Republic was conducted in 2002–2005; data were collected by structured questionnaires and examination in clinic including a fasting venous blood sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC1626086/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohorts consist of random samples of men and women aged 45–69 years old at baseline, stratified by gender and 5 year age groups, and selected from population registers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Additionally, geocoding of the Czech participants’ addresses opened the opportunities to link data to numerous external exposome characteristics and census data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data from all four cohorts were linked to national health administrative registers offering a comprehensive view of the participants’ health status over more than 20 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HAPIEE (Health, Alcohol and Psychosocial factors In Eastern Europe) is a population-based longitudinal prospective cohort study established to explore psychosocial, behavioural, and environmental risk factors of chronic conditions and ageing outcomes, including their trajectories, in middle aged and older urban populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17049075") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://europepmc.org/article/PPR/PPR1175525") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/HAPIEE-CZ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12266180/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The follow-up investigation in the Czech Republic was conducted in 2023-2024 and was supported by the NPO „Systemic Risk Institute“ (LX22NPO5101), funded by European Union – Next Generation EU (Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, NPO: EXCELES).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002640> "The Czech Republic cohort of the HAPIEE study: a random sample of men and women aged 45-69 years, stratified by sex and age and selected from population registers in six Czech towns (Havířov/Karviná, Hradec Králové, Jihlava, Kroměříž, Liberec and Ústí nad Labem), examined at baseline in 2002-2005 and followed through re-examinations (most recently in 2023-2024) and linkage to national health registers, with geocoded addresses linked to exposome and census data. The aim is to study psychosocial, behavioural and environmental risk factors for cardiovascular and other chronic diseases and for ageing outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30426668") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://europepmc.org/api/getPdf?pmcid=PMC7198944") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Lipid‐Based Nutrient Supplements Project ‐ DYAD ‐ Malawi (iLiNS‐DYAD‐M) trial was a randomised controlled trial designed to study the impact on child growth and development of providing a lipid‐based nutrient supplement to women during the perinatal period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35909334") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9480947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between February 2011 and August 2012, the iLiNS team enroled 1391 participants at the four study sites in southern Malawi.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35909334") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9480947/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "we compared the incidence of CS and other delivery complications in pregnant women who received small‐quantity (SQ)‐LNSs and two control groups in which pregnant women received capsules containing either IFA or MMN.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37021807") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10262897/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "were partially double‐blind, parallel, individually randomised, controlled trials with three equal‐size groups.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41775864") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13076672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The enrollment took place in one public district hospital (Mangochi), one rural semiprivate hospital (Malindi), and one rural public health center (Lungwena) in Mangochi District") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25646337") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01239693") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/iLiNS%20DOSE%20iLiNS%20DYAD") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women received supplements during pregnancy and lactation, and infants were followed to assess growth and health outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002641> "A randomised, partially double-blind controlled trial cohort in rural Malawi (Mangochi, University of Malawi College of Medicine with Tampere University), part of the International Lipid-Based Nutrient Supplements (iLiNS) Project, of pregnant women enrolled from 2011 and later their infants, in which women received small-quantity lipid-based nutrient supplements, multiple micronutrients or iron-folic acid during pregnancy and lactation and infants were followed to test effects on birth size, child growth and development, with a later follow-up of the children at 9 years.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5101688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In our study area of New Hampshire, USA, approximately 40 % of households rely on unregulated private water systems, of which 10–15 % contain As levels exceeding the US EPA maximum contaminant level of 10 μg/L [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5101688/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The New Hampshire Birth Cohort is an ongoing study and starting in January 2009, we began recruiting 18–45 year old pregnant women receiving prenatal care at study clinics, as previously described [29].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Beginning in 2009, with the help of medical providers in New Hampshire, the study staff at the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, began enrolling pregnant women at clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our research is what is known as a prospective longitudinal cohort study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since 2009, the New Hampshire Birth Cohort Study has been investigating how the impact of environmental contaminants might affect the health of pregnant women and their children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27825389") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.protectkidshealth.com/about") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This basically means that we are actively following our group of study participants over time as they grow and develop - from early pregnancy and into childhood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002642> "A prospective longitudinal cohort of pregnant women enrolled since 2009 at prenatal clinics in the Concord and Lebanon regions of New Hampshire, USA, by the Geisel School of Medicine at Dartmouth, and of their children, followed from early pregnancy into childhood to study how environmental contaminants, such as arsenic from private well water, affect the health of pregnant women and their children.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12910095/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population-based cross-sectional community study, which was carried out in conjunction with the elderly medical examination program, recruited 2287 adults (including males and females, aged 60 years and older) from Dapuqiao Street, Huangpu District, Shanghai, China, from March 2019 to November 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> "A community-based open cohort of older residents of the Dapu (Dapuqiao) neighbourhood of Huangpu District in central Shanghai, China, whose 2019 baseline included adults aged 60 and older, recruited through the Shanghai Municipal Annual Physical Examination Program for older residents and examined in three waves in 2019, 2022 and 2024, mostly as repeated cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset, to study health, lifestyle and cognition in an ageing urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12910095/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "our study focused on AD-related genetic architecture that may contribute to early cognitive decline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> "A community-based open cohort of older residents of the Dapu (Dapuqiao) neighbourhood of Huangpu District in central Shanghai, China, whose 2019 baseline included adults aged 60 and older, recruited through the Shanghai Municipal Annual Physical Examination Program for older residents and examined in three waves in 2019, 2022 and 2024, mostly as repeated cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset, to study health, lifestyle and cognition in an ageing urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As repeated participation across waves was limited (n = 163), the cohort primarily functions as a series of cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> "A community-based open cohort of older residents of the Dapu (Dapuqiao) neighbourhood of Huangpu District in central Shanghai, China, whose 2019 baseline included adults aged 60 and older, recruited through the Shanghai Municipal Annual Physical Examination Program for older residents and examined in three waves in 2019, 2022 and 2024, mostly as repeated cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset, to study health, lifestyle and cognition in an ageing urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data were collected across three examination waves in 2019, 2022, and 2024, with 2287, 1518, and 3554 eligible participants included after exclusions, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> "A community-based open cohort of older residents of the Dapu (Dapuqiao) neighbourhood of Huangpu District in central Shanghai, China, whose 2019 baseline included adults aged 60 and older, recruited through the Shanghai Municipal Annual Physical Examination Program for older residents and examined in three waves in 2019, 2022 and 2024, mostly as repeated cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset, to study health, lifestyle and cognition in an ageing urban population.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41606232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SDACS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were recruited from the Dapu neighborhood in Huangpu District, a central urban area of Shanghai with a high density of older adults, to investigate health and lifestyle characteristics in an aging population.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002643> "A community-based open cohort of older residents of the Dapu (Dapuqiao) neighbourhood of Huangpu District in central Shanghai, China, whose 2019 baseline included adults aged 60 and older, recruited through the Shanghai Municipal Annual Physical Examination Program for older residents and examined in three waves in 2019, 2022 and 2024, mostly as repeated cross-sectional samples with a small longitudinal subset, to study health, lifestyle and cognition in an ageing urban population.")
