# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3780997/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Covering the key areas of life, namely health, socio-economics and social networks, SHARE includes a great variety of information: health variables, physical measures and biomarkers, psychological variables, economic variables and social support variables as well as social network information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23778574+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SHARE's scientific power is based on its panel design that grasps the dynamic character of the ageing process, its multidisciplinary approach that delivers the full picture of individual and societal ageing, and its cross-nationally ex-ante harmonized design that permits international comparisons of health, economic and social outcomes in Europe and the USA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2004 until today, 530,000 in-depth interviews with 140,000 people aged 50 or older from 28 European countries and Israel have been conducted.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2023 onwards, SHARE has found a home in the newly founded SHARE BERLIN Institute, in Berlin, Germany, where it is centrally coordinated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It was selected as one of the projects to be implemented in the European Strategy Forum on Research Infrastructures (ESFRI) in 2006 and given a new legal status as the first ever European Research Infrastructure Consortium (ERIC) in March 2011.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23778574") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-1") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/data/data-documentation/waves-overview/wave-7") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://share-eric.eu/infrastructure") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SHARE, the Survey of Health, Ageing and Retirement in Europe, is a research infrastructure for studying the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life-course of European citizens and beyond.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002644> "A multidisciplinary, cross-nationally harmonised longitudinal panel survey of people aged 50 and older, begun in 2004 in eleven European countries and Israel and extended to all EU member states and Switzerland, run as a European Research Infrastructure Consortium (SHARE-ERIC, coordinated from Munich and later Berlin), that collects data on health, biomarkers, cognition, employment, socio-economic status and social and family networks to study the effects of health, social, economic and environmental policies over the life course.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/about/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A39482079+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Respondents underwent a battery of cognitive tests, geriatric assessments, and venous blood collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> "A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/about/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A two-stage stratified random sampling approach was adopted, oversampling individuals at high risk of cognitive impairment to ensure enough respondents with dementia or mild cognitive impairment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> "A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/about/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The first wave of LASI-DAD drew a sub-sample of respondents from the baseline LASI sample aged 60 and older from 18 states and union territories.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> "A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/about/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample was also expanded from 18 to 22 states and union territories, improving the population representativeness.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> "A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.")
