AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39482079") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/about/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://lasi-dad.org/study-design") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Wave 2 was also fielded in three phases from 2022 – 2024.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002645> "A nationally representative in-depth study of late-life cognition and dementia in India, led from the University of Southern California with Indian partners, that recruited a sub-sample of Longitudinal Aging Study in India (LASI) respondents aged 60 and older, oversampling those at high risk of cognitive impairment, from 18 states and union territories in 2017–2019 and 22 in 2022–2024, and assessed them with the Harmonized Cognitive Assessment Protocol, informant interviews, geriatric assessments, blood biomarkers, neuroimaging, genomics and environmental exposure measures.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(3) identify high-risk groups based on genetic susceptibility to environmental chemicals; and (4) identify the additive effects of various chemicals, including tobacco.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment in the Sapporo cohort was conducted from July 2002 to October 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Our primary objectives are to (1) examine the effects that low-level environmental chemical exposures have on birth outcomes, including birth defects and growth retardation; (2) follow the development of allergies, infectious diseases, and neurobehavioral developmental disorders, as well as perform a longitudinal observation of child development;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hokkaido Study on Environment and Children’s Health is an ongoing study consisting of two birth cohorts of different population sizes: the Sapporo cohort and the Hokkaido cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Hokkaido cohort recruited pregnant women during their first trimester from the entirety of Hokkaido Prefecture, Japan, during 2003-2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Hokkaido%20Study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34022817") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8141139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The subjects included 514 pregnant women who enrolled at 23–35 weeks of gestation and delivered at Toho hospital.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002646> "An ongoing prospective birth cohort study run by the Center for Environmental and Health Sciences of Hokkaido University, Japan, made up of the Sapporo cohort, recruited in pregnancy at one Sapporo hospital in 2002–2005, and the Hokkaido cohort, recruited in the first trimester at clinics and hospitals across Hokkaido Prefecture in 2003–2012, that follows the children to study the effects of prenatal and postnatal exposure to environmental chemicals on birth outcomes, birth defects, growth, allergies, infections and neurodevelopment, and genetic susceptibility to them.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3888562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINIplus (German Infant Nutrition Intervention Study Plus environmental and genetic influences on allergy development) is a population-based prospective birth cohort, with a nutritional intervention, of children born during 1995–1998 in Wesel and Munich, Germany") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3888562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individual estimates are presented by cohort except for the German birth cohorts (LISAplus and GINIplus), which had almost identical study designs and parental questionnaires, and are presented as GINI/LISA North (Wesel) and GINI/LISA South (Munich) because separate air pollution models were developed for each area as part of ESCAPE.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3888562/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LISAplus (Influence of Life-style Factors on the Development of the Immune System and Allergies in Childhood Plus the influence of traffic emissions and genetics) is a population-based prospective birth cohort study of children born during 1997–1999 in Wesel, Munich, Leipzig, and Bad Honnef, Germany") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4112441/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As the GINIplus and LISAplus birth cohorts have nearly identical study designs, data were pooled and are presented per study area (GINI/LISA South and GINI/LISA North).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4112441/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GINI/LISA North covers the rural area near the industrial Ruhr area in Germany (approximately 12 000 km2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24149084") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24862831") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GINI/LISA%20North") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40672052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12266180/supplementaryFiles") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For GINIplus and LISA, which have nearly identical study designs, data were pooled and then analysed separately for the urban area Munich (GINIplus/LISA South) and the rural area Wesel (GINIplus/LISA North).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002647> "The children of the German birth cohorts GINIplus (born 1995–1998) and LISAplus (born 1997–1999) recruited in the rural study area of Wesel, near the industrial Ruhr area in western Germany, whose data are pooled because the two cohorts have nearly identical designs and analysed as one study population, as in the ESCAPE and EXPANSE air pollution and exposome consortia, separately from the urban Munich participants (GINI/LISA South).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8217431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Finally, in the same subsample of 270 participants, we collected extra samples of blood and urine before and after the nutritional intervention to assess potential secondary effects of the intervention") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8217431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The participants eligible were adolescents aged between 11 and 16 years attending regular schools in Barcelona.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8217431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "WALNUTs (WSS) is a multi-school, parallel (two-group), controlled, 6-month superiority randomized clinical trial in a large population-based sample aiming to include 800 healthy teenagers in Barcelona, Spain.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8217431/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a 6-month population-based randomized controlled trial in teenagers (n = 800) and we aimed to determine the effectiveness of the intervention (four walnuts per day, or 30 kernel g, ~1.5g of ALA) in enhancing brain neuropsychological and socio-emotional development compared to a control group with no walnut intervention.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start/End data collection 2016 until 2017") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34169045") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/WALNUTs") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a school-based cohort and walnut intake intervention study, we have environmental and lifestyle data of healthy teenagers from Barcelona.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002648> "A multi-school, population-based, parallel-group randomised controlled trial of healthy adolescents aged 11 to 16 attending schools in Barcelona, Spain, run by researchers of ISGlobal in 2016–2017, that tested whether eating 30 g of walnuts a day for six months improves neuropsychological and socio-emotional development, with cognitive, behavioural, lifestyle and environmental assessments and blood and urine samples from part of the participants.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33171599") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7695147/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENOBOX study was carried out in three hospitals from cities located in different Spanish areas: Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago (Santiago de Compostela), Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa (Zaragoza), and Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía (Córdoba).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35596598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9180328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A sample of 1599 children and adolescents (48.5% males and 70.6% with overweight/obesity) participated in the GENOBOX multicenter case control study, carried out in three Spanish cities: Córdoba, Santiago de Compostela and Zaragoza.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35596598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9180328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Children were classified in two groups: cases with overweight or obesity, and controls with normal weight.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35596598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9180328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The case group was recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm the diagnosis of overweight or obesity or for identification of minor gastrointestinal disorders that were discarded after clinical and laboratory tests.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35596598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9180328/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whereas, the control group were children who came to the emergency departments owing to a common infection, that were not confirmed after laboratory tests.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:35596598 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33171599 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/GENOBOX") Annotation(rdfs:comment "- Hospital cohort - To study the molecular mechanism underlying childhood obesity - To understand better the pathophysiology of childhood obesity helping to the risk stratification - Studying the influence of inflammation biomarkers") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002649> "A multicentre hospital-based case–control study of children and adolescents in Spain, recruited at the university hospitals of Santiago de Compostela (Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago), Zaragoza (Hospital Clínico Universitario Lozano Blesa) and Córdoba (Hospital Universitario Reina Sofía): cases with overweight or obesity, recruited from children who came to the hospitals to confirm that diagnosis or for minor gastrointestinal disorders that were ruled out after clinical and laboratory tests, and controls of normal weight, children who came to the emergency departments with a common infection that was not confirmed by laboratory tests, studied to understand the pathophysiology and cardiometabolic, inflammatory and oxidative-stress risk factors of childhood obesity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32566487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7292139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligibility criteria include pregnant women, 16 years old or older, living in the city of Rio Janeiro, where the Maternity School is the reference hospital for delivery.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32566487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7292139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PIPA Pilot Study was performed for 12 months, from September 2017 to August 2018, at the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro Maternity School, with financial support from Brazil Ministry of Health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32566487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7292139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PIPA project is a birth cohort study in which the study population will comprise all pregnant women and their children, born in the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro (UFRJ), at any gestational age, by either vaginal or cesarean delivery, in a period of 12 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32566487") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7292139/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study protocol includes interviews, physical examinations, and collection of biological samples at the seventh month of pregnancy, at birth, and during the postnatal period until the age of four years old (Table I).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ele é coordenado pelo Instituto de Estudos em Saúde Coletiva da Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro (IESC/UFRJ) e está sendo realizado na Maternidade Escola (ME) da UFRJ, em parceria com a Fundação Oswaldo Cruz (FIOCRUZ), e com o Instituto Evandro Chagas (IEC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32566487 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pipaufrj.me.ufrj.br/sobre/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "O PIPA/UFRJ é um estudo de coorte prospectivo com foco nos efeitos sobre a saúde infantil da exposição a substâncias químicas (especificamente metais, pesticidas e plastificantes), dispersas no ambiente ao qual as crianças estão expostas desde a concepção.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002650> "A hospital-based prospective birth cohort of pregnant women aged 16 or over living in the city of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, and their children born at the Maternity School of the Federal University of Rio de Janeiro, coordinated by the university's Institute for Studies in Collective Health with Fiocruz, in which mothers and children are followed with interviews, examinations and biological samples from pregnancy to age four to study the effects of prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, pesticides and plasticisers on child health and development; a pilot phase ran from September 2017 to August 2018.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42225914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13522492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this analysis, we used 434 full-term children with complete data on air pollution, inhibitory control (Kiddie Continuous Performance Test 2nd Edition™) at 4 years, covariates, and obesity measures from ages 4 to 10.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42225914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13522492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the PROGRESS cohort (n = 434) in Mexico City, we modeled ambient PM2.5 exposure during pregnancy and the first year of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42225914") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13522492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Programming Research in Obesity, Growth, Environment, and Social Stressors (PROGRESS) study recruited pregnant women who received prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security System (Instituto Mexicano del Seguro Social, IMSS) between July 2007 and February 2010.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PROGRESS is a longitudinal birth cohort study conducted in Mexico that investigates prenatal exposure to mixtures of metals, air pollution, and phthalates.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PROGRESS may be the first birth cohort specifically designed to prospectively address the joint impact of chronic stress and toxic metals on child development.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROGRESS") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/ ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42225914 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://mountsinaiexposomics.org/progress/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Programming Research in Obesity, Growth, Environment and Social Stressors (PROGRESS) study is a collaboration between Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and the National Institute of Public Health (INSP) in Mexico and is uniquely poised to conduct this research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002651> "A prospective birth cohort of pregnant women receiving prenatal care through the Mexican Social Security Institute (IMSS) in Mexico City, recruited from July 2007 to February 2010, and their children, run by the Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai, Harvard University and Mexico's National Institute of Public Health, and followed to study how prenatal and early-life exposure to metals, air pollution and phthalates, together with chronic psychosocial stress, affects child neurodevelopment, growth and metabolic health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:29847083 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25198283 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25198283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4256696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "On these plantations, mancozeb is applied weekly by light aircraft.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:29847083 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25198283 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25198283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4256696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Pregnant women were eligible for enrollment if they lived in one of 40 villages in Matina County that were within 5 km of a banana plantation, if they were at least 15 years old, with < 33 weeks of gestation, and if they expected a singleton birth.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:29847083 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25198283 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25198283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4256696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Infants’ Environmental Health Study [Infantes y Salud Ambiental (ISA)] is a prospective community-based birth cohort study in Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, aimed at examining possible effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children’s growth and neurodevelopment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:29847083 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25198283 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25198283") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4256696/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women were identified between March 2010 and June 2011 through meetings in local schools, communal groups, advertisements, and referral.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:29847083 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25198283 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ISA") Annotation(rdfs:comment "aimed at examining possible effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children’s growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory outcomes, as well as several health outcomes outcomes of their mothers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002652> "A prospective community-based birth cohort of pregnant women aged 15 or over living in 40 villages of Matina County, Limón, Costa Rica, within 5 km of large-scale banana plantations where the fungicide mancozeb is sprayed from the air, enrolled from March 2010 to June 2011 by the Central American Institute for Studies on Toxic Substances (IRET) of the Universidad Nacional, and their children, followed to study the effects of prenatal pesticide and manganese exposure on children's growth, neurodevelopment and respiratory health and on the mothers' health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33776890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7992978/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By combining standardized genetic, neuroimaging, and behavioral (cognitive and SDH) measures, we will investigate whether there are unique risk factors for AD and FTD in LAC (e.g., genetic risk factors enriched in LAC populations; underlying cognitive and neural vulnerability due to SDH) compared to US populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33776890") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7992978/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In a regional project based on the ReDLat platform and additionally supported by Takeda, we will extend the protocol to compare multimodal EEG markers.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41586258") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12827047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America (ReDLat) recruited 2162 participants with AD, FTD, or healthy controls from six countries: Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, and Peru.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41586258") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12827047/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To investigate the genetic landscape of neurodegeneration in Latin America, we recruited patients with mild to moderate AD or FTD, along with healthy controls from ten memory clinics across six Latin American countries: Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, and Peru.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42251497") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13242611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ReDLat implements a harmonized data collection framework across multiple centers in Latin America, applying standardized diagnostic protocols and assessments across sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:41586258 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:42251497 ") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://red-lat.com/en-the-project/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33776890 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42251497") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13242611/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The tool was co‐designed by the ReDLat consortium and UCSF‐MAC and harmonized for use across Latin American populations, following the NIA Health Disparities Research Framework, Institute of Medicine recommendations, and best practices for cross‐national comparisons.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002653> "A multicentre cohort of people with Alzheimer's disease or frontotemporal dementia and cognitively unimpaired controls, recruited at memory clinics and other clinical and community sites in Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Mexico and Peru by the Multi-Partner Consortium to Expand Dementia Research in Latin America with the University of California San Francisco Memory and Aging Center, and assessed under a harmonised protocol (clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging and EEG data, and a questionnaire on lifelong social exposures) to study how genetic, social and environmental factors shape dementia and brain health in Latin America compared with the United States.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780516") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8592492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Environmental and biological samples were/are being/will be collected during the 2021 growing season, at 10 case study sites in Europe covering a range of climate zones and crops.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780516") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8592492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Five sample types were, are being or will be collected from each participant: urine, faeces, blood, wristbands, and nasal swabs.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780516") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8592492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The overall design that best serves this aim is a cross-sectional design at different locations in Europe and one in Argentina (Fig 2), covering multiple crops of conventional and organic production.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34780516") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8592492/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To achieve this, we designed a cross-sectional study to compare conventional and organic farm systems across Europe.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37838044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37838044+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the present study, part of the Horizon 2020 funded SPRINT project, the presence of 198 pesticide residues was assessed in 128 indoor dust samples from both conventional and organic farmworker households across Europe, and in Argentina.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34780516 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/SPRINT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cross-sectional study performed in 2021 to assess differences in exposure of farmers (organic and non-organic practises), neighbours (people living close to agricultural fields) and controls ('consumers' living away from agricultural fields) to pesticides.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002654> "A cross-sectional field study of the EU Horizon 2020 SPRINT project in which, during the 2021 growing season, conventional and organic farmers and their families, neighbours living next to or near agricultural fields, and consumers living farther away were recruited at ten case study sites in Europe and one in Argentina, and gave urine, blood, faeces and nasal swabs and wore silicone wristbands (with indoor dust sampled in their homes), to measure their exposure to pesticide mixtures for exposure modelling and health risk assessment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26847446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4743396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Consenting individuals answer an epidemiological survey exploring risk factors (psycho-social, pesticides, diet, alcohol, and physical activity), medical history and physical and cognitive conditions; provide fasting blood, urine, and saliva samples; receive an electrocardiogram, abdominal ultrasound and bio-impedance test; and take a hand-grip strength test.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26847446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4743396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment, including bio-sampling, began in December 2014 and is expected to be completed by December 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26847446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4743396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAUCO is a prospective population-based cohort study of individuals aged 38 to 74 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26847446") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4743396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MAUCO is the core project of the recently established Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS), Universidad de Chile & Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32176288") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7850102/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Beginning in July 2014, we conducted a household census of Molina County to identify potential participants and record household members, geographical coordinates (latitude-longitude format; World Geodetic System 1984) and basic housing conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/MAUCO") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26847446 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32176288") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7850102/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The general objectives of MAUCO are: (i) to analyse the natural history of CVD and cancer, where outcomes of interest include CVD, cancer, mental health, ageing, quality of life and respiratory diseases among others, whereas risk factors of interest include socioeconomic, lifestyle, environmental, genetic and ethnic factors;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002655> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 38 to 74 years living in the agricultural county of Molina, in the Maule Region of central Chile, identified through a household census and enrolled from December 2014 by the Advanced Center for Chronic Diseases (ACCDiS) of the Universidad de Chile and the Pontificia Universidad Católica de Chile, with questionnaires, physical examinations, ultrasound and a biobank of blood, urine and saliva, and followed with repeat visits and surveillance of hospital events to study the natural history and environmental, lifestyle and social determinants of chronic diseases such as cardiometabolic diseases and cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5124445/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, data collection took place between April and September 2015, and response proportion ranged from about 62% in urban areas to 77% in rural sites.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5124445/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SABE Colombia is a population-based cross-sectional study on health, aging, and well-being of elderly individuals aged at least 60 years focusing attention on social determinants of health inequities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5124445/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The methods and procedures were based on those used in the SABE international study to reach comparability [4] but included an analytical approach based on active aging as recommended by WHO to understand factors, processes, or “determinants” that influence individuals, families, and nations over the life course [14].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5124445/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is a cross-sectional study of community-dwelling elderly individuals living in urban and rural areas of Colombia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6774577/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Ministry of Health and Social Protection in the National System of Population Studies and Surveys for Health implemented the first health, well-being and aging survey- SABE-2015 Colombia- to know the living conditions of people 60 years of age or older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:27956896") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31607769") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6774577/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The SABE Colombia 2015 survey is representative of the main indicators of health, well-being and aging in Colombia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002656> "A population-based cross-sectional national survey of community-dwelling adults aged 60 years and over in urban and rural areas of Colombia, carried out in 2015 for the Colombian Ministry of Health and Social Protection by the University of Caldas and the Universidad del Valle with the design of the Latin American and Caribbean Survey on Health, Well-Being, and Aging (SABE), to study health, active ageing and the social determinants of health inequities in older people.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8776471/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In Colombia, South America, the Colombian Institute for Family Wellbeing (ICBF in Spanish) along with the Ministry of Health (MinSalud) conducted the ENSIN-2015, which is representative of 99% of the Colombian population [12].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40221690") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11992871/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "ENSIN is a survey with probabilistic and multistage sampling, which has national coverage with urban and rural representativeness for six regions and, for some of its indicators, for 14 subregions and 32 departments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Este estudio abarca la población colombiana entre 0 y 64 años, y los indicadores de estado nutricional, ingesta dietética, seguridad alimentaria, lactancia materna y alimentación complementaria y actividad física que se presentan por grupos de edad, sexo y nivel socioeconómico.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(rdfs:comment "La Encuesta Nacional de la Situación Nutricional en Colombia - 2005, tiene como marco de referencia el derecho a la alimentación, es la primera versión de esta encuesta, por su integralidad, magnitud y representatividad.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(rdfs:comment "La tercera Encuesta Nacional de Situación Nutricional de Colombia (ENSIN) 2015 es una operación estadística poblacional realizada entre noviembre de 2015 a diciembre de 2016, en la cual, se entrevistaron 151.343 personas de 44.202 hogares en 295 municipios del país.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35070447") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.icbf.gov.co/bienestar/nutricion/encuesta-nacional-situacion-nutricional") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Los resultados de la segunda versión de la Encuesta Nacional de la Situación Nutricional en Colombia 2010 - ENSIN, se presentan como respuesta al compromiso con el País de obtener información periódica que permita tomar decisiones de política pública en el marco del derecho a la alimentación.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002657> "A repeated nationally representative cross-sectional household survey of the nutritional situation of the population of Colombia, conducted by the Colombian Institute for Family Welfare (ICBF) with the Ministry of Health in 2005, 2010 and 2015, covering people aged 0 to 64 years and pregnant women, that measures nutritional status, dietary intake, food security, breastfeeding and physical activity to inform public food and nutrition policy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All pooled individuals have the outcomes of interest, either non-fatal or fatal cardiovascular events (or censored).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "At the time of writing, the daily operations and pooled database are hosted at Imperial College London, though a mid-term goal is to transfer this expertise and operations to LAC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In so doing, we aim to provide regional risk estimates to inform disease burden metrics, as well as other ambitious projects including a cardiovascular risk score to strengthen cardiovascular prevention in LAC.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Initial funding has been provided by a fellowship from the Wellcome Trust Centre for Global Health Research at Imperial College London (Strategic Award, Wellcome Trust–Imperial College Centre for Global Health Research, 100693/Z/12/Z).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The collaboration relies fundamentally on a strong regional network of health researchers and practitioners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39687239") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32888015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7746413/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We have harmonized and pooled approximately population-based cohort data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and outcomes, i.e. participants were not recruited based on disease (e.g. cohort of stroke survivors) or risk factor (e.g. cohort of smokers) history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002658> "A consortium of population-based cohort studies from countries of Latin America and the Caribbean, set up with Wellcome Trust funding and run from Imperial College London with a regional network of researchers, that harmonises and pools individual-level data on cardio-metabolic risk factors and fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular outcomes to produce regional risk estimates and tools for cardiovascular prevention.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4681103/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary study outcomes are atopy, eczema and asthma.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> "A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George's, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4681103/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ECUAVIDA cohort is a prospective cohort study from birth, designed to investigate the effects of pre- and postnatal exposures to STH parasites on the development of atopy and allergic diseases to 8 years of age.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> "A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George's, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4681103/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort also provides the opportunity to investigate the possible effects of other microbial and environmental exposures in early childhood on the development of atopy and allergic diseases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> "A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George's, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24990475+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 2404 newborns were recruited between 2006 and 2009 in a public hospital serving the rural district of Quininde, Esmeraldas Province, in a tropical region of coastal Ecuador.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> "A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George's, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24990475") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A24990475+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ECUAVIDA birth cohort is studying the impact of exposures to soil-transmitted helminth (STH) parasites and early-life microbial exposures on the development of atopy, allergic diseases and immune responses in childhood.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002659> "A prospective birth cohort of newborns recruited from 2006 to 2009 at the hospital serving the rural district of Quinindé, Esmeraldas Province, in tropical coastal Ecuador, run by the Laboratorio de Investigaciones FEPIS with St George's, University of London, that follows the children through childhood to study how soil-transmitted helminth infections and other early-life microbial and environmental exposures affect immune development, atopy, allergic disease and asthma.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11392417/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We included 38 patients diagnosed with BC and treated at the National Cancer Institute between 2007 and 2017, who consented to donate their samples to the Terry Fox National Tumor Bank in Bogota, Colombia (Fig 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12229586/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in this institutional Program consented to donate biological samples to the National Tumor Biobank Terry Fox (BNTTF, in Spanish: Banco Nacional de Tumores Terry Fox), managed by the INC-C, and signed informed consent for DNA biobanking and future research studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12229586/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in this institutional Program consented to donate biological samples to the National Tumor Biobank Terry Fox (BNTTF, in Spanish: Banco Nacional de Tumores Terry Fox), managed by the INC-C, and signed informed consent for DNA biobanking and future research studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(rdfs:comment "De los DC se colectó tejido tumoral (TT) y tejido no tumoral (TNT) adyacente de ~0,5 cm3, preservados así: tejido fresco congelado (TFC) en nitrógeno líquido, congelación rápida en isopentano e inclusión en OCT, almacenado a −80 °C y tejido fi jado en formalina embebido en parafi na-(FFEP), almacenado a −4 °C.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Entre 2011 y 2013 se captaron donantes con cáncer-(DC), donantes sin cáncer-(DCS) y supervivientes, quienes fi rmaron consentimiento informado-(CI) aprobado por el comité de ética institucional") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Se colectó sangre periférica, sin y con anticoagulante (EDTA, heparina, citrato de sodio), que se procesó en menos de 3 h, para obtener hemoderivados (plasma, suero y células blancas (CB)) almacenados a −80 °C.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39264897") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40065011") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BNTTF") Annotation(rdfs:comment "una encuesta epidemiológica-(EE), incluyendo preguntas de identificación, información clínica, socio-demográfi ca, exposición a factores de riesgo, cáncer familiar y hábitos de vida.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002660> "The donors of the Terry Fox National Tumour Bank, the biobank of the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología in Bogotá, Colombia: people with cancer, people without cancer and cancer survivors who gave informed consent, answered an epidemiological questionnaire on clinical, sociodemographic, risk-factor, family cancer and lifestyle information, and donated blood and, at surgery, tumour and adjacent non-tumour tissue, stored for health research with an emphasis on cancer.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937970/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the first stage, 150 county-level units were randomly chosen with a probability-proportional-to-size (PPS) sampling technique from a sampling frame containing all county-level units with the exception of Tibet.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937970/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Samples were chosen through multistage probability sampling.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3937970/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The final sample of 150 counties fell within 28 provinces.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23243115+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A pilot survey for CHARLS was conducted in two provinces of China in 2008, on 2685 individuals, who were resurveyed in 2012.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23243115+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The China Health and Retirement Longitudinal Study (CHARLS) is a nationally representative longitudinal survey of persons in China 45 years of age or older and their spouses, including assessments of social, economic, and health circumstances of community-residents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23243115") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A23243115+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The national baseline survey for the study was conducted between June 2011 and March 2012 and involved 17 708 respondents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002661> "A nationally representative longitudinal survey of community-dwelling people aged 45 years and older in China and their spouses, run from the National School of Development of Peking University, with a 2008 pilot in two provinces and a national baseline in 2011-2012 drawn by multistage probability sampling from 150 counties in 28 provinces, followed up every two years and harmonised with the Health and Retirement Study, to study the health, social and economic consequences of population ageing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33997297") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8095190/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REACT-1 involves cross-sectional surveys of viral detection (virological swab for RT-PCR) tests in repeated samples of 100,000 to 150,000 randomly selected individuals across England.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33997297") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8095190/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The main study (study 5) uses the same design and sampling approach as REACT-1 using a self-administered lateral flow immunoassay (LFIA) test for IgG antibodies in repeated samples of 100,000 to 200,000 adults aged 18 years and above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36893367+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission-1 (REACT-1) Study was funded by the Department of Health and Social Care in England to provide reliable and timely estimates of prevalence of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) infection over time, by person and place.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36893367+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study team (researchers from Imperial College London and its logistics partner Ipsos) wrote to named individuals aged 5 years and older in random cross-sections of the population of England, using the National Health Service list of patients registered with a general practitioner (near-universal coverage) as a sampling frame.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "REACT Cohort is now made up of over 3 million people who have consented to follow-up by providing permission for us to contact them future research and/or to link to their health data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36893367") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37733993") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.imperial.ac.uk/medicine/research-and-impact/groups/react-study/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The REACT Cohort is a major national resource for researchers to study the longer-term impacts of the pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002662> "A national cohort in England of people who took part in the REal-time Assessment of Community Transmission programme of Imperial College London, which from 2020 sent random samples drawn from National Health Service general practice registers SARS-CoV-2 swab tests for people aged 5 years and older (REACT-1) and antibody self-tests for adults aged 18 years and older (REACT-2) for the Department of Health and Social Care, and who consented to recontact and/or linkage to their health records, used to study the longer-term effects of the COVID-19 pandemic and other factors on health and wellbeing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://studie3xg.be/nl") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All pregnant women in the region that fulfilled the inclusion criteria and were expected to give birth between 2010 and 2015 were invited to participate.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> "A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities' disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://studie3xg.be/nl") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3xG study (Health—Municipalities—Birth, translated from Gezondheid, Gemeenten, Geboorten) is a birth cohort study that monitors and promotes health of the inhabitants of three bordering rural communities (Dessel, Mol, and Retie) in Flanders, Belgium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> "A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities' disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://studie3xg.be/nl") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 3xG study is commissioned and co-financed by NIRAS/ONDRAF (Belgian National Agency for Radioactive Waste and enriched Fissile Material), STORA (Study and Consultation Radioactive Waste Dessel) and MONA (Mols Overleg Nucleair Afval).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> "A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities' disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://studie3xg.be/nl") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10058482/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This is performed by researching 301 growing children from the region and by processing the disease and mortality registers of the 3 municipalities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> "A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities' disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36976969") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://studie3xg.be/nl") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/3xG") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose is to monitor environmental and lifestyle exposure and health effects by following up 301 newborns till the age of 18 years old, with human biomonitoring and frequent questionnaires.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002663> "A local birth cohort of children born between 2010 and 2015 to mothers living in the neighbouring rural municipalities of Dessel, Mol and Retie in Flanders, Belgium, run by the Flemish Institute for Technological Research (VITO) and co-financed by the Belgian radioactive waste agency and local consultation bodies, that follows the children with human biomonitoring and questionnaires, alongside the municipalities' disease and mortality registers, to monitor the effects of environmental and lifestyle exposures on health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35816918") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A35816918+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A socio-demographically diverse sample of Hungarian women completed interviews in middle or late pregnancy, as part of the countrywide Cohort '18 Growing Up in Hungary study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10473525/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The survey was launched in 2017 by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute (HDRI) of the HCSO.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37656714+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is based on a nationwide representative sample of pregnant women who gave birth between March 2018 and April 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37656714+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Source of data is the first and second wave of the Cohort '18 -Growing Up in Hungary longitudinal birth cohort study (n = 8185).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Cohort18") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Approximately 8,000 children and their parents participate in the survey.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37656714") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://kohorsz18.hu/en/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/Cohort18") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study aims to understand the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing in Hungary, along with the distinct parental, family and social features that determine the development of children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002664> "A nationally representative longitudinal birth cohort of children born in Hungary between March 2018 and April 2019 and their parents, recruited in pregnancy and run by the Hungarian Demographic Research Institute of the Hungarian Central Statistical Office, to study the circumstances of childbearing and childrearing and the parental, family and social factors that shape children's development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10862406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COMmunity-based Behavior and Attitude survey in Tuvalu (COMBAT) collected data between February and May 2022 from 1030 adults (985 with complete data) from Funafuti, the main island, and the other 8 outlying islands [17].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10862406/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The survey was funded by a collaborative effort between the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government as part of the Fruit and Vegetable Production and Nutrition Enhancement Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38810531+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Two waves of the COMmunity-based Behavior and Attitude (COMBAT) survey were conducted in 2020 and 2022.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40814824") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12355442/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is a secondary data analysis study of the Community-based Behaviour and Attitude Study in Tuvalu (COMBAT), a nationwide administrative survey examining health conditions and related risk factors in Tuvalu under the context of climate change.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It addresses major evidence gaps in climate-vulnerable Pacific Island populations and generates actionable data to inform prevention strategies, health system planning, and climate adaptation through repeated surveys, clinical assessments, and biomonitoring.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Start/End data collection 2025 until 2029") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COMBAT cohort is a longitudinal, community-based study in Tuvalu examining lifestyle behaviors, environmental exposures, and health outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38351973") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38810531") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/all/collections/COMBAT") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The COMBAT cohort sets its framework based on the COMBAT survey since 2020.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002665> "A nationwide community-based survey of adults in Tuvalu, on Funafuti and the eight outer islands, run in waves since 2020 and funded jointly by the Taiwan International Cooperation and Development Fund and the Tuvalu government, studying diet, lifestyle behaviours, climate-related exposures and obesity and other non-communicable diseases; from 2025 it is being continued as a longitudinal cohort with repeated surveys, clinical assessments and biomonitoring.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8097258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "339 (4%) of all crimes in the municipality were located in the Butanta-Jaguaré area (where all children of the cohort reside).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8097258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The São Paulo Western Region Birth Cohort (Região Oeste Coorte – ROC-Cohort) enrolled locally resident babies born at the University Hospital of the School of Medicine of the University of São Paulo between April 1, 2012, and March 31, 2014.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8097258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was conducted in the municipality of São Paulo, Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8097258/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study was designed as a retrospective cross-sectional study linking data collected as part of a prospective cohort study to geocoded administrative data on violent crime.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Secondary objectives are: (i) to identify potential epigenetic changes due to toxic stress exposure and its impact on child development; (ii) to understand the influence of antenatal and post-natal toxic stress exposures on child development;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33952246") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/ROC") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary objective of the ROC study is to assess the impact of social and environmental factors on early childhood development in the modern urban low-income setting of São Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002666> "A prospective birth cohort of babies born at the University Hospital of the University of São Paulo School of Medicine between April 2012 and March 2014 to mothers living in the Butantã-Jaguaré area of São Paulo's Western Region, Brazil, followed to study how social and environmental factors, including toxic stress, affect early childhood development in a low-income urban setting.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2013, the study was transferred to the Centre for Longitudinal Studies (CLS), Institute of Education, University College London, and was funded by the Economic and Social Research Council.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Next Steps (previously known as the Longitudinal Study of Young People in England, LSYPE) is an ongoing, multidisciplinary, longitudinal study following 16 122 people who were in secondary school in England and were born in 1989–90.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since becoming part of the CLS family of longitudinal studies, the focus of Next Steps has broadened, and the study has collected information on many different aspects of life, including physical and educational development, economic circumstances, employment, family life, health behaviour, wellbeing, social participation, and attitudes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The recruited sample was in Year 9 (aged 13–14) of compulsory secondary education and was attending state-funded, private-funded independent schools or pupil referral units in England.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The sample design considered schools the primary sampling unit; among state-funded schools, deprived schools were over-sampled by 50%.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39540417") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11561396/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was initially funded and managed by the Department for Education (formerly the Department for Education and Skills) and began in 2004.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002667> "A national longitudinal cohort of people born in 1989-90 who were in Year 9 of secondary school in England in 2004, sampled through schools with over-sampling of deprived schools and ethnic minorities, begun by the Department for Education and run since 2013 by the Centre for Longitudinal Studies at University College London, following their education, work, economic circumstances, family life, health and wellbeing.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective cohort of 500 children under five are to be followed for 1 year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrolled children will be followed monthly (phone call) and at months 6 and 12 (in person) post-enrolment with upper and lower Acute Respiratory Infections (ARI) examinations, asthma development, asthma control, and genotoxic damage.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PROMESA study will be conducted in Bogotá and Medellín, the two largest cities in Colombia, as both cities report, in their monitoring network records, that PM2.5 is the pollutant that most deteriorates air quality (Fig 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study duration is 2.5 years from July 2021 to January 2024") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9858469/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We will study the children of a single health insurance company in Colombia that has an insurance coverage of 94.3% in Medellín and 6.4% in Bogotá.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/PROMESA") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36662732") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36662732+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study aims to characterize the external exposome (ambient and indoor exposures) and its contribution to clinical respiratory and early biological effects in children.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002668> "A prospective cohort of children under five years old insured by a single health insurance company in Bogotá and Medellín, Colombia, enrolled from 2021 and followed for one year to study how the external exposome, above all particulate matter air pollution, contributes to acute respiratory infections, asthma and early DNA damage.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10464298/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participant recruitment was started in March 2018, and we followed them up to December 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10464298/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participant recruitment was started in March 2018, and we followed them up to December 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10464298/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This study is part of an already ongoing mother–child cohort study established in 2018 by the School of Public Health, Addis Ababa University named Butajira Nutrition, Mental health, and Pregnancy (BUNMAP) Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10464298/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a prospective community-based cohort study among pregnant women in Butajira, Health and Demographic Surveillance System (HDSS) in Meskanena Mareko District of Ethiopia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38605538") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11075105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A cohort consisting of all pregnant women from the HDSS study population was recruited during the study period.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38605538") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11075105/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a prospective cohort study nested within the Butajira Nutrition, Mental Health and Pregnancy (BUNMAP) cohort, established in October 2017 and followed up until November 2020 in rural Ethiopia(34).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37620778") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://molgeniscatalogue.org/Global%20Exposome%20Cohorts/collections/BUNMAP") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Butajira Nutrition, Mental Health, and Pregnancy (BUNMAP) Study, a population-based prospective cohort study aimed at evaluating the role of maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure, and mental health on prenatal and postnatal growth and development") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002669> "A population-based prospective mother-child cohort of pregnant women living in the Butajira Health and Demographic Surveillance Site, Meskan and Mareko district, Ethiopia, enrolled from 2017-2018 by the School of Public Health of Addis Ababa University and followed through pregnancy and after birth to study how maternal nutrition, mycotoxin exposure and mental health affect prenatal and postnatal growth and development.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8277870/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From June to September 2015, eighty low-income pregnant youth were randomized into two groups: intervention (HVP by nurses, n = 40) and control (healthcare as usual, n = 40).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8277870/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were: (a) first pregnancy, (b) pregnant youth aged 14–19 years old, (c) low socioeconomic status (classes C, D, E according to the ABEP scale)45, (d) pregnancy between 8 and 16 weeks, (e) living in the western region of Sao Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8277870/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants were identified in Primary Healthcare Units in the western region of Sao Paulo.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8277870/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Therefore, the objective of the present study is to test the efficacy of Primeiros Laços on child development, maternal and environmental outcomes in the first 2 years of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34257407+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Primeiros Laços is a home visiting intervention delivered by trained nurses that starts during the first 16 weeks of pregnancy and continues to the child's age of 24 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34257407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A34257407+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We conducted a randomized controlled trial to test the efficacy of Primeiros Laços, a nurse HVP for adolescent mothers living in a poor urban area of São Paulo, Brazil.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002670> "The participants of a randomised controlled trial run by the University of São Paulo Medical School from 2015 of Primeiros Laços, a nurse home visiting programme from early pregnancy to the child's age of two years, in low-income first-time pregnant adolescents aged 14-19 recruited through primary healthcare units in the western region of São Paulo, Brazil, and their children, followed to test the programme's effects on child development, maternal and home environment outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781157 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3709199/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Conducting high-quality follow up with negligible loss to follow up and detailed information on cancer occurrence and causes of death.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 75 years enrolled between 2004 and 2008 from rural and urban areas of Golestan province in northeast Iran, set up to study oesophageal cancer and followed for cancers and other outcomes, including those attributable to opium use and smoking.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781157 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3709199/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The primary aims of the GCS are: To identify risk factors for OC by a comprehensive assessment of ethnicity, occupational history, socio-economic status, past medical history, family history of cancers, gastrointestinal symptoms and signs, tobacco, opium and alcohol use, oral health, anthropometric characteristics, physical activity and tea drinking habits, including tea temperature.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 75 years enrolled between 2004 and 2008 from rural and urban areas of Golestan province in northeast Iran, set up to study oesophageal cancer and followed for cancers and other outcomes, including those attributable to opium use and smoking.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781157 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37781157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10541463/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, GCS is a prospective study of 50,045 adults, aged 40–75 years, who were enrolled between 2004 and 2008, from 329 rural and urban areas of the Golestan province in northeast Iran.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 75 years enrolled between 2004 and 2008 from rural and urban areas of Golestan province in northeast Iran, set up to study oesophageal cancer and followed for cancers and other outcomes, including those attributable to opium use and smoking.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781157 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37781157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10541463/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Golestan Cohort Study is the only population-based prospective study that includes a large group of opium users with validated opium use data,13 who have been followed for over a decade with a minimum (around 1%) loss to follow-up.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 75 years enrolled between 2004 and 2008 from rural and urban areas of Golestan province in northeast Iran, set up to study oesophageal cancer and followed for cancers and other outcomes, including those attributable to opium use and smoking.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " PMID:19332502") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37781157 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37781157") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37781157+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We assessed the association between using opium and/or cigarette smoking and various cancers using proportional hazards regression models.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002671> "A population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 40 to 75 years enrolled between 2004 and 2008 from rural and urban areas of Golestan province in northeast Iran, set up to study oesophageal cancer and followed for cancers and other outcomes, including those attributable to opium use and smoking.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00038-012-0379-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In addition to the personal identity number, we used household and family information from the 1960 census to link family members together.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> "A register-based cohort selected from people in Norway who took part in the national censuses from 1960 to 2001 and had personal identity numbers, excluding emigrants who did not take part in the following census, in which family members are linked through personal identity numbers and household and family information from the 1960 census and further linked to health registers and surveys, for multigenerational life-course research in public health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00038-012-0379-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NFLC study is further linked to other health registers and surveys.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> "A register-based cohort selected from people in Norway who took part in the national censuses from 1960 to 2001 and had personal identity numbers, excluding emigrants who did not take part in the following census, in which family members are linked through personal identity numbers and household and family information from the 1960 census and further linked to health registers and surveys, for multigenerational life-course research in public health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00038-012-0379-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The comprehensive multigenerational and family linkage within the database provides large-scale use of family-based designs for investigating life course determinants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> "A register-based cohort selected from people in Norway who took part in the national censuses from 1960 to 2001 and had personal identity numbers, excluding emigrants who did not take part in the following census, in which family members are linked through personal identity numbers and household and family information from the 1960 census and further linked to health registers and surveys, for multigenerational life-course research in public health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00038-012-0379-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population was based on a selection of all Norwegians who participated in the census in 1960, 1970, 1980, 1990 or 2001 and who had received a personal identity number.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> "A register-based cohort selected from people in Norway who took part in the national censuses from 1960 to 2001 and had personal identity numbers, excluding emigrants who did not take part in the following census, in which family members are linked through personal identity numbers and household and family information from the 1960 census and further linked to health registers and surveys, for multigenerational life-course research in public health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22735991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00038-012-0379-4") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those who emigrated between census time points (1960 and later) and who did not participate in the following census were excluded.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002672> "A register-based cohort selected from people in Norway who took part in the national censuses from 1960 to 2001 and had personal identity numbers, excluding emigrants who did not take part in the following census, in which family members are linked through personal identity numbers and household and family information from the 1960 census and further linked to health registers and surveys, for multigenerational life-course research in public health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection provided broad informed consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Before recruitment began, an intensive harmonization phase for the operational installation of the network was carried out for one month under the direction of the BTUCH.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For the long COVID follow-up, we attempted to recontact 2249 participants for a survey with standardized practices in place.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The preparatory harmonization took a month and was followed by a pilot recruitment phase performed at Salvador Hospital in September 2020 for reality-based adjustments.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This paper reports the articulation of a network across Chile and the creation of the Chilean COVID-19 Biorepository, the first nationwide multicenter repository built under biobanking standards to ensure the high quality, reproducibility, and interoperability of samples and data as a resource for collaborative multi-omics research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> " https://biobanco.uchile.cl/proyecto-c19-genonet-2/") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39596552 ") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39596552") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11593408/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, the Chilean COVID-19 Biorepository was finally established through a network of nine nodes across seven of the country’s 16 regions, encompassing all macrozones (Figure 1, left panel).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002673> "A nationwide multicentre cohort of adults with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection, from asymptomatic to fatal, recruited from September 2020 into 2021 through nine recruitment centres in seven regions of Chile by a network of Chilean universities and health centres coordinated by the University of Chile's Biobank of Tissue and Fluids, with blood samples and clinical data banked for multi-omics studies of host genetics and COVID-19 severity, and recontacted for long COVID follow-up; the network behind it became the COVID-19 Genomics Network (C19-GenoNet).")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Completed questionnaires are transferred periodically from the participating screening centres to the study co-ordinating centre at the Imperial Cancer Research Fund Cancer Epidemiology Unit (CEU), Oxford, UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13913/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Million Women Study is a nationwide collaborative research project in the UK, the chief aim of which is to describe the relationship between use of hormone replacement therapy (HRT) and the risk of various conditions, particularly breast cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11056681+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Population-based cohort study of women aged 50-64 in the UK.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A11056681+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Women are asked to join the Million Women Study when they are invited to routine screening for breast cancer at 61 of the screening centres of the UK National Health Service Breast Screening Programme (NHSBSP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 1.3 million UK women were recruited into the study between 1996 and 2001 and have been followed for health outcomes ever since.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11056681") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ceu.ox.ac.uk/research/the-million-women-study") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Million Women Study is one of the largest prospective studies of women’s health in the world.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002674> "A population-based prospective cohort of women aged 50–64 years in the United Kingdom, recruited in 1996–2001 when invited to routine mammography by the National Health Service Breast Screening Programme at centres in England and Scotland and coordinated by the Cancer Epidemiology Unit of the University of Oxford, set up to study the effects of hormone replacement therapy on breast cancer and other outcomes and followed for the effects of many other factors on women's health as they age.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963573/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "MNGHA-affiliated healthcare facilities (described above), which served as the primary sites for enrolling individuals with various medical conditions, and community-based locations such as blood donation centers and the MNGHA-affiliated health sciences university") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963573/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One of the Saudi Biobank’s strengths is its ability to expand the scope of data through linkage to participants’ electronic health records (EHRs) in the MNGHA network.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963573/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One such initiative was the launch of the Saudi Biobank Center at the King Abdullah International Medical Research Center (KAIMRC), which was inaugurated in 2017 [3].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963573/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Saudi Biobank TypePopulation-basedPopulation-based Target PopulationAges 40–69Ages 10+ (no upper limit) Recruitment Period2006–2010 with ongoing follow ups and assessments2017-ongoing Recruitment SourceOpen to public living within travel distance of UK centersSaudi Nationals from MNGHA hospitals, with MRN,Future plan: expand to non-MNGHA individuals") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12963573/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Saudi biobank collected data and samples from participants aged 10 years and above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33194979") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41721974") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.biobanking.org/biobanks/view/462") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This project aims to support a wide range of genetic and epidemiological research studies that are focused on improving the preventive, diagnostic, and treatment of common and rare diseases in KSA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002675> "A population-based biobank of Saudi nationals aged 10 years and over, recruited since 2017 by the Saudi Biobank Center of King Abdullah International Medical Research Center in Riyadh, in person at Ministry of National Guard Health Affairs hospitals and clinics and at community sites such as blood donation centres, with questionnaires, biological samples and linked electronic health records, to support genetic and epidemiological research on common and rare diseases in Saudi Arabia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://persiancohort.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12645788/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Biological specimens—blood, urine, hair, and nails—are systematically collected and processed according to internationally recognised biobanking standards, ensuring sample integrity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> "An ongoing nationwide population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 35–70 years living in 18 regions of Iran chosen to cover its ethnic, environmental and socioeconomic diversity, enrolled since 2014 through a network of Iranian medical universities coordinated by the Digestive Diseases Research Institute of Tehran University of Medical Sciences, with a biobank, to study environmental, lifestyle and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://persiancohort.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12645788/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PERSIAN project is an ongoing, nationwide, population-based prospective cohort that began enrolment in 2014 to characterise environmental, lifestyle, and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases across Iran’s diverse populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> "An ongoing nationwide population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 35–70 years living in 18 regions of Iran chosen to cover its ethnic, environmental and socioeconomic diversity, enrolled since 2014 through a network of Iranian medical universities coordinated by the Digestive Diseases Research Institute of Tehran University of Medical Sciences, with a biobank, to study environmental, lifestyle and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://persiancohort.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12645788/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To achieve this, the Biobank Information Management System (BIMS) was developed by the technical team at the Digestive Diseases Research Institute, Tehran University of Medical Sciences. using Visual Studio 2012 and implemented with the.NET Framework 4.5.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> "An ongoing nationwide population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 35–70 years living in 18 regions of Iran chosen to cover its ethnic, environmental and socioeconomic diversity, enrolled since 2014 through a network of Iranian medical universities coordinated by the Digestive Diseases Research Institute of Tehran University of Medical Sciences, with a biobank, to study environmental, lifestyle and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://persiancohort.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A41286709+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The adult cohort includes Iranian residents aged 35–70 from 18 diverse regions, capturing the country’s ethnic, environmental, and socioeconomic diversity.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> "An ongoing nationwide population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 35–70 years living in 18 regions of Iran chosen to cover its ethnic, environmental and socioeconomic diversity, enrolled since 2014 through a network of Iranian medical universities coordinated by the Digestive Diseases Research Institute of Tehran University of Medical Sciences, with a biobank, to study environmental, lifestyle and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41286709") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://persiancohort.com/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6279089/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "While the Ministry of Health and Medical Education oversees the project, investigators at local universities carry it out.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002676> "An ongoing nationwide population-based prospective cohort of adults aged 35–70 years living in 18 regions of Iran chosen to cover its ethnic, environmental and socioeconomic diversity, enrolled since 2014 through a network of Iranian medical universities coordinated by the Digestive Diseases Research Institute of Tehran University of Medical Sciences, with a biobank, to study environmental, lifestyle and genetic determinants of non-communicable diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11697940/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(1) a smaller Advance Cohort from December 2020; (2) Newborn recruitment, with presence in 58 Victorian maternity services supporting face-to-face approach to parents of babies born 4 October 2021–3 October 2023;") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11697940/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "(3) Intensive remote recruitment to mid-2024 targeting those missed around birth; and (4) Ongoing indefinite enrolment of in-age children and their parents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11697940/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is led from the Melbourne Children’s Campus by the Murdoch Children’s Research Institute (MCRI) with The Royal Children’s Hospital and The University of Melbourne, and in partnership with organisations across Victoria.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13016905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All children living in Victoria, Australia, born between 4 October 2021 and 3 October 2023 and their parents/guardians are eligible for GenV’s ‘Cohort 2020s’.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13016905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Generation Victoria (GenV) is a whole-of-state research platform established to improve child and adult health, development and wellbeing through discovery and interventional research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39754130") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI Codex), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41844214") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13016905/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It comprises participant-provided and service-collected data and biosamples, with planned 5–6 yearly child and parent phenotypic waves.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002677> "A whole-population birth and parent cohort open to all children living in the state of Victoria, Australia, who were born between October 2021 and October 2023, and their parents, recruited from December 2020 (an Advance Cohort, then newborns at Victorian maternity services and later remote and ongoing enrolment) and led from the Murdoch Children's Research Institute, which combines linked administrative and clinical data, biosamples and phenotypic waves as a platform for discovery and intervention research on child and adult health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8271208/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Use the data to identify the genetic and environmental factors underlying non-communicable diseases in South Asians, and translate the findings into new approaches for maintenance of health and well-being.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8271208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In each surveillance site, an environmental mapping exercise was carried out.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8271208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAB is a cross-sectional population-based study that recruited participants from 118 surveillance sites that were centred on local primary community health care units in five study regions: Bangladesh, South India, North India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8271208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAB was launched in 2018 as a partnership between collaborating centres in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan, Sri Lanka and the UK.10 SAB includes rich demographic, lifestyle, clinical, environmental and phenotypic data and biological samples from more than 50 000 South Asian participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8271208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The South Asia Biobank (SAB) is the first comprehensive biobank of South Asian individuals, established to identify the risk factors and their complex interactions underlying the development of type-2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM), cardiovascular disease (CVD) and other chronic diseases in South Asians.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34143882") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8271208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We recruited men and women of self-reported South Asian ethnicity and aged 18 years and above.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002678> "A population-based study of adults aged 18 years and over of South Asian ethnicity, recruited from 2018 at non-communicable disease surveillance sites centred on primary community health care units in Bangladesh, India, Pakistan and Sri Lanka by a partnership of centres in those countries and the United Kingdom led from Imperial College London, with standardised health assessments, environmental mapping and biological samples, to identify the genetic and environmental causes of type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular and other non-communicable diseases in South Asians.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320955/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DPUK collaborates with 42 clinical and population cohorts (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> "A platform established by the UK Medical Research Council to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia, run from the University of Oxford, whose Data Portal, launched in 2017, brings together data from independent population and clinical cohorts, most of them in the United Kingdom, in a shared remote-access environment for collaborative and multi-cohort research on dementia and neurodegeneration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320955/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "DPUK was established by the Medical Research Council (MRC) to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> "A platform established by the UK Medical Research Council to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia, run from the University of Oxford, whose Data Portal, launched in 2017, brings together data from independent population and clinical cohorts, most of them in the United Kingdom, in a shared remote-access environment for collaborative and multi-cohort research on dementia and neurodegeneration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320955/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From launch in November 2017 to end of January 2019, 160 project proposals involving 579 individual cohort data access requests were received.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> "A platform established by the UK Medical Research Council to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia, run from the University of Oxford, whose Data Portal, launched in 2017, brings together data from independent population and clinical cohorts, most of them in the United Kingdom, in a shared remote-access environment for collaborative and multi-cohort research on dementia and neurodegeneration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7320955/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Data Portal provides a secure, fully auditable, remote access environment for the analysis of cohort data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> "A platform established by the UK Medical Research Council to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia, run from the University of Oxford, whose Data Portal, launched in 2017, brings together data from independent population and clinical cohorts, most of them in the United Kingdom, in a shared remote-access environment for collaborative and multi-cohort research on dementia and neurodegeneration.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32328990") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:38506636") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A38506636+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The DPUK collection of independent cohorts can facilitate research in neurodegeneration by combining their genetic and phenotypic data.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002679> "A platform established by the UK Medical Research Council to accelerate the development of new treatments for dementia, run from the University of Oxford, whose Data Portal, launched in 2017, brings together data from independent population and clinical cohorts, most of them in the United Kingdom, in a shared remote-access environment for collaborative and multi-cohort research on dementia and neurodegeneration.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5645672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prospective data about pregnancies and their outcomes was collected in the routine biannual census rounds from 2006 to 2010 in the HDSS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5645672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The HDSS was established in 2004 in collaboration between the two districts of Iganga and Mayuge, Makerere University, Uganda, and Karolinska Instituet, Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9012358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IM-HDSS is in Eastern Uganda and covers the districts of Iganga and Mayuge managed by the Makerere University Centre for health and population research (MUCHAP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9012358/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IM-HDSS was established in 2005 as a platform field research and research training within Makerere University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11816860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The study was conducted within the population cohort of Iganga-Mayuge Health and Demographic Surveillance Sites (IMHDSS) located in eastern Uganda.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28799450") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35427403") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40018598") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11816860/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "This system facilitates the linkage of electronic health records (EHRs) at one community-based health centre (Busowobi HC III) with the households’ and residents’ characteristics.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002680> "A health and demographic surveillance system following the largely rural population of villages in the Iganga and Mayuge districts of eastern Uganda, established in the mid-2000s by Makerere University with the two districts and Karolinska Institutet and run by the Makerere University Centre for Health and Population Research, which records pregnancies, births, deaths and other events in census rounds and links household data with health facility records, as a platform for population health research and research training.")

