AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "HUNT 4 70+: The Trøndelag Health Study, fourth wave, of people aged 70+") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In HUNT4 70+, all inhabitants aged 70+ were invited (N = 19,403), with 9956 (51.3%) participating (Figure 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants from the HUNT4 70+ sub-study were re-evaluated four years later, which offers a unique opportunity to investigate the incidence of dementia and progression from MCI to dementia within this representative cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The fourth wave of the study, referred to as HUNT4, was conducted from 2017 to 2019.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The northern Trøndelag region, where the HUNT Studies were conducted, comprises rural areas and small towns with populations under 25,000 inhabitants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40879407") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12678644/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within this wave, a sub-study, HUNT4 70+, focused on individuals aged 70 and older.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002681> "A sub-study of the fourth wave (HUNT4, 2017–2019) of the Trøndelag Health Study in which all inhabitants aged 70 years and older in the northern Trøndelag region of Norway were invited to detailed assessments of cognition and health, used to study the prevalence and incidence of dementia and mild cognitive impairment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://web.archive.org/web/20241104022517/https://www.ed.ac.uk/coronagenes/about/coronagenes-study") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A research team including scientists from the MRC Human Genetics have launched a new COVID-19 study using data from home genetic-testing kits: June 2020") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682> "A cohort of volunteers recruited online from 2020 by the MRC Human Genetics Unit at the University of Edinburgh who shared genotype data from direct-to-consumer genetic testing services and completed questionnaires on their health, lifestyle and COVID-19 symptoms, to identify genes that influence the risk and severity of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://web.archive.org/web/20241104022517/https://www.ed.ac.uk/coronagenes/about/coronagenes-study") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The team aims to identify genes that influence the risk of developing Covid-19 and those that affect disease severity, by comparing volunteers’ symptoms – or lack of them – with their DNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682> "A cohort of volunteers recruited online from 2020 by the MRC Human Genetics Unit at the University of Edinburgh who shared genotype data from direct-to-consumer genetic testing services and completed questionnaires on their health, lifestyle and COVID-19 symptoms, to identify genes that influence the risk and severity of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://web.archive.org/web/20241104022517/https://www.ed.ac.uk/coronagenes/about/coronagenes-study") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Those taking part in the University of Edinburgh study – called Coronagenes – will complete online questionnaires about their health, lifestyle and any symptoms they have experienced, such as fever or a persistent cough.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682> "A cohort of volunteers recruited online from 2020 by the MRC Human Genetics Unit at the University of Edinburgh who shared genotype data from direct-to-consumer genetic testing services and completed questionnaires on their health, lifestyle and COVID-19 symptoms, to identify genes that influence the risk and severity of COVID-19.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://web.archive.org/web/20241104022517/https://www.ed.ac.uk/coronagenes/about/coronagenes-study") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://institute-genetics-cancer.ed.ac.uk/news-and-events/news-2020/home-dna-test-data-wanted-boost-coronavirus-fight") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-022-04826-7/MediaObjects/41586_2022_4826_MOESM3_ESM.xlsx") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Individuals uploaded raw genotype information from direct-to-consumer DNA genotyping companies, including 23andMe, Ancestry, MyHeritage, and FTDNA.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002682> "A cohort of volunteers recruited online from 2020 by the MRC Human Genetics Unit at the University of Edinburgh who shared genotype data from direct-to-consumer genetic testing services and completed questionnaires on their health, lifestyle and COVID-19 symptoms, to identify genes that influence the risk and severity of COVID-19.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9581448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All study participants are invited for re-examinations at the study centres in 4–5 year intervals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9581448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Basic physical and medical examinations, face-to-face interview, touch-screen-based self-report questionnaires, biomaterial collections (Level 1)2014–2019") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9581448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "NAKO collects follow-up information on incident diseases through a combination of active follow-up using self-report via written questionnaires at 2–3 year intervals and passive follow-up via record linkages.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9581448/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole-body 3T magnetic resonance imaging was performed in 30,861 participants on dedicated scanners.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36260190+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 2014 and 2019, a total of 205,415 men and women aged 19-74 years were recruited and examined in 18 study centres in Germany.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36260190") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A36260190+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The German National Cohort (NAKO) is a multidisciplinary, population-based prospective cohort study that aims to investigate the causes of widespread diseases, identify risk factors and improve early detection and prevention of disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002683> "A multidisciplinary population-based prospective cohort of men and women aged 19 to 74 years drawn at random from the general population and examined between 2014 and 2019 at 18 study centres across Germany, with interviews, questionnaires, biomedical examinations, biosamples and whole-body magnetic resonance imaging in a subsample, followed up by questionnaires, record linkage and re-examination, to investigate the causes, early detection and prevention of common chronic and infectious diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24729425") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4469794/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As part of the government’s increasing efforts to address and investigate the rising trends of non-communicable diseases, the cabinet approved The Malaysian Cohort study in 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6104700/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Ethnicity was defined based on the paternal grandfather’s ethnicity, which was categorized into Malay, Chinese, Indian and other descents.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6104700/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TMC is a nationwide prospective cohort project, which recruited approximately 100 000 Malaysians aged between 35 and 70 y at baseline.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8305012/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For passive surveillance, we received the mortality notification including the cause of death details every six months from the National Registry Department of Malaysia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8305012/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "TMC follow-up methods [23] included a biannual health diary for participants to fill out and return, biannual follow-up calls, and a comprehensive quinquennial follow-up to retain the participants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29462329") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34299667") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8305012/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Malaysian Cohort (TMC) project is a large population-based cohort study that managed to recruit 106,527 participants over a period from the year 2006 until 2012 [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002684> "A nationwide population-based prospective cohort of multi-ethnic Malaysian adults aged 35 to 70 years, recruited from 2006 to 2012 by the UKM Medical Molecular Biology Institute of the National University of Malaysia and followed up by periodic re-surveys, telephone follow-up and registry linkage, to study the causes of non-communicable diseases.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28171707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CPS-3 will be a valuable resource for studies of cancer and other outcomes because of its size; its diversity with respect to age, ethnicity, and geography; and the availability of blood samples and detailed questionnaire information collected over time.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28171707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Enrollment took place primarily at ACS community events and at community enrollment \"drives.\" At enrollment sites, participants completed a brief survey that included an informed consent, identifying information necessary for follow-up, and key exposure information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28171707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants will be followed for incident cancers through linkage with state cancer registries and for cause-specific mortality through linkage with the National Death Index.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28171707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The American Cancer Society (ACS) recruited a new prospective cohort study, Cancer Prevention Study 3 (CPS-3), between 2006 and 2013 from 35 states and Puerto Rico.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28171707+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "They also provided a waist measure and a nonfasting blood sample.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28171707") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39150951") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11329134/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 1,801 participants accepted the invitation and 751 participants who completed the 2015 CPS-3 follow-up survey were enrolled in the AVSS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002685> "A prospective cohort of adults in the United States and Puerto Rico recruited by the American Cancer Society between 2006 and 2013, mainly at community events, who gave a blood sample and survey information and are followed through repeat surveys and linkage with cancer registries and the National Death Index, to study lifestyle, genetic and other causes of cancer and other outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13216552/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants’ ambient environmental exposures were estimated by linking publicly available environmental quality data to their geocoded residential addresses.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13216552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "First administered in 2013, the PEGS Health and Exposure Survey (N = 9,449) collects data on general demographics, family medical history, lifestyle factors such as smoking and alcohol use, and occupational exposures.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13216552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2019, the Broad Institute performed WGS using blood samples from 4,737 PEGS participants with the most complete survey data to interrogate common and rare variants and structural variations, including high-resolution human leukocyte antigen (HLA) variants.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13216552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Originally established in 2002 for ongoing research at the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences (NIEHS), the initial cross-sectional cohort of the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry (EPR) recruited participants by convenience sampling at community events.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13216552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PEGS collects survey-based exposomic, genomic, and geographic information system (GIS) data from a racially and ethnically diverse North Carolina-based cohort of nearly 20,000 individuals.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41927563") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13216552/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of PEGS is to integrate these large-scale, multi-dimensional data to enable researchers to dissect the etiology of disease and identify the collective effects of environment, diet, lifestyle, and genetic factors on human health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002686> "A cohort of demographically diverse adults recruited in North Carolina since 2002 by the National Institute of Environmental Health Sciences, first as the Environmental Polymorphisms Registry, who complete surveys on health, exposures, diet and lifestyle, give biological samples and are genotyped, with geocoded residential data, to study how environment, lifestyle and genes act together on disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10147672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NL Genome Project was based on the random recruitment of participants from General Practice clinics from across the province that were 18 years of age and over, possessed a valid NL health card, and provided written consent.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10147672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NLGP cohort consists of the initial 2,500 participants for whom medical history and saliva samples were obtained with informed consent under a study protocol approved by the Newfoundland and Labrador Health Research Ethics Board (Ethics Reference #: 2018.243).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10147672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Newfoundland and Labrador Genome Project (NLGP) is a general population cohort focused on the characterization of Newfoundland and Labrador’s population (Sequence Bio Inc., 2021).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10147672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To sample the genetic landscape of NL before modern economic migration in the latter 20th century onwards, we applied principal component analysis (PCA) to genotype data from 2446 participants from the Newfoundland and Labrador Genome Project (NLGP—Sequence Bioinformatics, Inc) and world-wide ancestry references from HGDP or KGP3 (see Supplementary Figs. 1–2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:37117635") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://atlas.ihccglobal.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.sequencebio.com/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "100 New Gower Street, St. John’s, NL, Canada") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002687> "A general population cohort of adults in Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada, established by the company Sequence Bioinformatics (Sequence Bio) of St. John's and recruiting from 2019, whose participants, aged 18 and over with a valid provincial health card, were recruited at random from general practice clinics across the province and gave medical history and saliva samples for genotyping, to characterise the genetics of the province's founder population and find genetic causes of disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37183782") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37183782+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1,243,282 women were invited and 205,090 attended for recruitment between April 2001 and September 2005.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37183782") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A37183782+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A bioresource (UKCTOCS Longitudinal Women's Cohort) of longitudinal outcome data and over 0.5 million serum samples including serial annual samples in women in the MMS group was established and to date has been used in many new studies, mainly focused on early detection of cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40067807") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11896025/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Case and control cohorts were identified from samples collected as part of the UKCTOCS trial of post-menopausal women aged 50–74 years, and aligned with UKCTOCS trial exclusion criteria (no history of bilateral oophorectomy or ovarian malignancy, no increased risk of familial ovarian cancer, and no active non-ovarian malignancy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Sample collection stopped at the end of screening in December 2011 (Menon et al, JCO 2015).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established linkage to electronic health records (from 2000-2020):- National Cancer Registries (NHS Digital & Northern Ireland; National Cancer Intelligence Network - NCIN)- Hospital Episode Statistics (HES- In/Out Patient and A&E admissions; England & Wales)- Death Certificates (NHS Digital & Northern Ireland Death Registry)- MINAP (Myocardial Ischaemia National Audit Project; until 2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://uklwc.mrcctu.ucl.ac.uk/overview") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.innovative-ctu.ucl.ac.uk/studies/all-studies/u/uklwc/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "UKLWC is the bioresource created during the course of the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS) as a result of participants (202,280 postmenopausal women from the general population in England, Wales and Northern Ireland) donating their samples and data for use in secondary studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002688> "A cohort of postmenopausal women aged 50–74 from the general population of England, Wales and Northern Ireland, recruited in 2001–2005 to the United Kingdom Collaborative Trial of Ovarian Cancer Screening (UKCTOCS), a randomised trial of ovarian cancer screening, whose donated serum samples (at recruitment and, in the multimodal screening arm, annually until 2011) and linked national health records are kept by the MRC Clinical Trials Unit at University College London as an open bioresource for studies of common diseases and disease markers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A census of all residents was taken between September 2000 and October 2001 defining a population of 198 063.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System (KHDSS) is nested in the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme in Kilifi, on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Kilifi Health and Demographic Surveillance System (KHDSS), located on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, was established in 2000 as a record of births, pregnancies, migration events and deaths and is maintained by 4-monthly household visits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The idea of the KHDSS was conceived in 2000 to create a longitudinal community-based study linked, at inception, to hospital morbidity surveillance by integrating the existing clinical and field-based research infrastructure.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The key strength of the system, and the feature which distinguishes it from most other demographic surveillance studies, is the continuous real-time linkage of morbidity events to our population register; however, this also has significant limitations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22544844") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3396317/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The rationale for the project was (i) to define the incidence and prevalence of significant local diseases of childhood; (ii) to evaluate the impact of new community-based interventions against infectious diseases; and (iii) to provide an epidemiological sampling frame for cross-sectional surveys and case–control studies at the research programme.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002689> "A population cohort of the residents of a defined area around Kilifi on the Indian Ocean coast of Kenya, established in 2000 by the KEMRI-Wellcome Trust Research Programme with a census and followed by regular household visits recording births, pregnancies, migrations and deaths, with residents' admissions to Kilifi District Hospital linked to the population register, to measure the incidence of local diseases, evaluate community interventions against infectious diseases and provide a sampling frame for epidemiological studies.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12015775+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "New questionnaires are sent to surviving cohort members every other year to update exposure information and to ascertain new occurrences of cancer; a 90% response rate was achieved for follow-up questionnaires in 1997 and 1999.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12015775+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Cancer Prevention Study II Nutrition Cohort was established in 1992 and was designed to investigate the relation between diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures and the risk of cancer, mortality, and survival.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12015775+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The cohort includes over 84,000 men and 97,000 women who completed a mailed questionnaire in 1992.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A12015775+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Through a collaborative effort among ACS national and division staff, volunteers, and the American College of Surgeons, blood samples were collected from a subgroup of 40,000 cohort members and are in storage at a central repository for future investigation of dietary, hormonal, genetic, and other factors and cancer risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8000483/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Among those who provided blood samples, 617 CRC cases were identified through 30 June 2015 via self-report which was verified with medical records, state cancer registry linkage, or linkage with the National Death Index") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:12015775") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33803340") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8000483/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men and women in this study were participants in the CPS-II Nutrition Cohort, a subset of 1.2 million participants in the CPS-II Cohort (1982), who resided in 21 U.S. states when they were invited to enroll in the CPS-II Nutrition Cohort of incident cancer follow-up, beginning in 1992–1993 [22].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002690> "A subset of the Cancer Prevention Study II participants, men and women living in 21 US states, enrolled by the American Cancer Society through a mailed questionnaire in 1992–1993 and followed by biennial questionnaires, medical records and registry linkage for incident cancer and death, with blood samples from a subgroup, to study diet and other lifestyle factors and exposures in relation to cancer risk, mortality and survival.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Surveys, interviews, standardized examinations, laboratory analyses, and medical record abstraction are used to obtain information in 5 main outcome areas: pre-, peri-, and postnatal outcomes; neurodevelopment; obesity; airways; and positive health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EWC comprises 69 ongoing and new pregnancy and pediatric cohorts, a Coordinating Center, a Data Analysis Center, and a Person-Reported Outcomes Core.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EWC enrolls pregnant people and children across the United States and Puerto Rico.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The EWC harmonizes extant data and collects new data using a standardized protocol, the ECHO-Wide Cohort Data Collection Protocol (EWCP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Environmental Influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO)-Wide Cohort Study (EWC), a collaborative research design comprising 69 cohorts in 31 consortia, was funded by the National Institutes of Health (NIH) in 2016 to improve children’s health in the United States.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://echochildren.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36963379") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10403303/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The goal of the ECHO Program is to understand how the environment, from preconception through early childhood, influences child health and development to identify opportunities to mitigate the risk of disease and optimize health and thriving (4).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002691> "A collaborative cohort study funded in 2016 by the US National Institutes of Health within the Environmental influences on Child Health Outcomes (ECHO) Program, bringing together existing and new pregnancy and paediatric cohorts across the United States and Puerto Rico under a common data collection protocol to study how early-life environmental exposures affect pre-, peri- and postnatal outcomes, airway health, obesity, neurodevelopment and positive health in children.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6908844/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A central office was established at the National Cancer Center, and regional offices were established in each of the local areas involved.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents aged 40 to 74 years of 16 municipalities in seven prefectural areas of Japan, enrolled from 2011 to 2016 through a central office at the National Cancer Center and regional public health centres and universities as the successor to the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study, with questionnaires and blood and urine samples, to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related diseases and factors that extend healthy life expectancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30713262+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A self-administered questionnaire was distributed to all registered residents aged 40-74, which mainly asked about lifestyle factors, such as socio-demographic situation, personal medical history, smoking, alcohol and dietary habits.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents aged 40 to 74 years of 16 municipalities in seven prefectural areas of Japan, enrolled from 2011 to 2016 through a central office at the National Cancer Center and regional public health centres and universities as the successor to the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study, with questionnaires and blood and urine samples, to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related diseases and factors that extend healthy life expectancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30713262+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As of December 31, 2016, we have established a population-based cohort of 115,385 persons (Response rate 44.1%), among whom 55,278 (47.9% of participants) have provided blood and urine samples.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents aged 40 to 74 years of 16 municipalities in seven prefectural areas of Japan, enrolled from 2011 to 2016 through a central office at the National Cancer Center and regional public health centres and universities as the successor to the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study, with questionnaires and blood and urine samples, to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related diseases and factors that extend healthy life expectancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30713262+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 2011 through 2016, a baseline survey was conducted at 16 municipalities in seven prefectures across the country.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents aged 40 to 74 years of 16 municipalities in seven prefectural areas of Japan, enrolled from 2011 to 2016 through a central office at the National Cancer Center and regional public health centres and universities as the successor to the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study, with questionnaires and blood and urine samples, to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related diseases and factors that extend healthy life expectancy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30713262") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30713262+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study for the Next Generation (JPHC-NEXT) was launched in 2011 to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related disease, elucidate factors that extend healthy life expectancy, and contribute toward personalized healthcare based on our more than 20 years' experience with the JPHC Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002692> "A population-based prospective cohort of residents aged 40 to 74 years of 16 municipalities in seven prefectural areas of Japan, enrolled from 2011 to 2016 through a central office at the National Cancer Center and regional public health centres and universities as the successor to the Japan Public Health Center-based Prospective Study, with questionnaires and blood and urine samples, to identify risk factors for lifestyle-related diseases and factors that extend healthy life expectancy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4716208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "It is designed to screen 0.4 million community-dwelling residents aged 40–75 years with measurements of blood pressure, height and weight, a lipid blood test, and a questionnaire on cardiovascular-related health status.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4716208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Subjects identified as being at high risk of CVD at a screening station are then moved to a designated hospital within each region to receive further assessment, counselling and follow-up care.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4716208/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The pilot phase of China PEACE (Patient-centered Evaluative Assessment of Cardiac Events) Million Persons Project is being conducted during 2014–2015 in four provinces across China to demonstrate the feasibility of a population-based assessment.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7928212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Accordingly, we utilized data of 2.6 million people from the China PEACE (Patient-Centered Evaluative Assessment of Cardiac Events)-Million Persons Project, a government-funded, large-scale population-based screening project in China, to conduct an in-depth analysis of severe hypertension.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7928212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From September 2014 to November 2018, we used a purposive sampling strategy to select 189 sites (114 rural counties, 75 urban districts) from all 31 provinces in mainland China.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26729395") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33038086") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7928212/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We enrolled 2 660 666 participants aged 35–75 years from 31 provinces between 2014 and 2018 in the cross-sectional China Patient-Centered Evaluative Assessment of Cardiac Events Million Persons Project.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002693> "A government-funded, population-based cardiovascular screening cohort run by the National Center for Cardiovascular Diseases (Fuwai Hospital, Beijing) that, after a pilot in four provinces, enrolled community-dwelling residents aged 35 to 75 years at urban districts and rural counties in all 31 provinces of mainland China from 2014, with blood pressure, anthropometric and lipid measurements and a health questionnaire, and gave further assessment, counselling and follow-up to those at high risk, to identify people at high risk of cardiovascular disease and support research on its prevention.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "As such, the PIP cohort provides a powerful resource for HIV, TB and NCD research, and a strong platform to accurately measure population dynamics, disease burden, and use of health and other services, and to implement and evaluate individual- and population-level interventions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2017, the cohort was expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform (PIP).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "PIP is an open cohort consisting of all households within the expanded surveillance area.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Africa Centre Demographic Information System (ACDIS) was established in 2000 by the Africa Health Research Institute (AHRI; formerly the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies), funded by the Wellcome Trust.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The aim of ACDIS was to describe the demographic, social and health impacts of a rapidly progressing HIV epidemic in rural South Africa, and to monitor the impact of intervention strategies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33437994") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7938501/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The original ACDIS surveillance area covered 438 km2 in uMkhanyakude district, KwaZulu-Natal province, South Africa, and included a population of ∼85 000 resident and non-resident individuals in 11 000 households in 2006.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002694> "An open population cohort of all resident and non-resident members of households in a demographic and health surveillance area in the uMkhanyakude district of rural KwaZulu-Natal, South Africa, established in 2000 by the Africa Centre for Health and Population Studies (now the Africa Health Research Institute) and expanded and renamed the Population Intervention Platform in 2017, with repeated household surveillance and population-based HIV surveys, to describe the demographic, social and health impact of the HIV epidemic, and later of tuberculosis and non-communicable diseases, and to evaluate interventions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7087900/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A prospective study combining information on exposures as early as pre-conception and in early life throughout young and mid-adulthood, with the possibility to study a variety of diseases with onset relatively early in life and co-morbidities later in life will open up new research opportunities.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7087900/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Index persons aged 18–45 years old will be recruited and invited to include their household members (partner and any children).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7087900/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LifeGene is designed both as a prospective cohort study and an infrastructure with repeated contacts of study participants approximately every 5 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7087900/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "LifeGene was designed to include collection of data through web-based questionnaires and in person testing to collect biosamples and a range of physical tests, Fig. 1.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7087900/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The household-based design will give the opportunity to involve young couples prior to and during pregnancy, allowing for the first study of children born into cohort with complete pre-and perinatal data from both the mother and father.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21104112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:39934197") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC11814342/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The LifeGene study randomly invited individuals 18 years or older from the general population in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2009 and 201665.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002695> "A population-based prospective cohort study and research infrastructure in Sweden, run from Karolinska Institutet, that from 2009 to 2016 recruited adults from the general population, mainly in the Stockholm region, with index persons aged 18 to 45 years invited to bring their household members, and collected questionnaires, physical assessments and biological samples with planned repeated follow-up, to study diseases with onset early in life, pregnancy and early-life exposures, and later co-morbidity.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Funded by an NMRC OF-LCG grant that brought together four longitudinal cohorts in Singapore, the SG100K cohort is an Investigator-Initiated Study focused on determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> "A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Research phenotype data from four longitudinal population health cohorts (“SG100K Institutions”) supported by the SG100K OF-LCG award:Health for Life in Singapore (HELIOS), NTU Singapore Population Health Studies (SPHS), NUSSingapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases (SEED), SERISingHeart, NHCS") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> "A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PRECISE-SG100K dataset is also linked to electronic health records (EHRs) that includes routinely collected clinical data and other health-related information.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> "A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The PRECISE-SG100K resource is a unique multi-ancestry Asian population cohort dataset of ~100,000 Singaporean residents, jointly created by PRECISE, SG100K Institutions and GIS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> "A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41469377") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.npm.sg/our-data-users/data-access/data-access-to-precise-sg100k/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Whole genome sequencing (short read 30X coverage sequencing) generated in partnership with the Genome Institute of Singapore (GIS, A*STAR) under Phase II of Singapore’s National Precision Medicine Programme.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002696> "A collection of four longitudinal population health cohorts in Singapore (HELIOS, the Singapore Population Health Studies, the Singapore Epidemiology of Eye Diseases and SingHeart), brought together under an NMRC grant and in partnership with Precision Health Research, Singapore (PRECISE) and the Genome Institute of Singapore in phase II of the National Precision Medicine programme, whose multi-ancestry Asian participants were whole-genome sequenced and linked to electronic health records to study the determinants and prediction of cardiovascular disease and diabetes in Asian populations.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2020, the SAPRIN population cohort covered 355 000 individuals for whom data on births and deaths, residency status and migration, household asset ownership status, and measures of well-being including employment, education and social protection are updated three times a year.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "SAPRIN is funded by the Department of Science and Innovation (DSI) as part of the South African Research Infrastructure Road Map (SARIR) and is hosted by the South African Medical Research Council (SAMRC).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The South African Population Research Infrastructure Network (SAPRIN) is a harmonized national network of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes, constituted in 2016 with the aim of establishing a national resource and research platform to strengthen the evidence for informing health and social policy and programming at a time of stringent fiscal constraint.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The population platform will be expanded to include urban nodes in the country’s two main metropolitan areas, Gauteng and the Western Cape.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://saprin.mrc.ac.za/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34966919") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9365637/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The three HDSS founding nodes are hosted by the Medical Research Council/Wits Rural Public Health and Health Transitions Research Unit (Agincourt) in Mpumalanga province, the University of Limpopo (DIMAMO) in Limpopo province and the Africa Health Research Institute (AHRI) in KwaZulu-Natal.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002697> "A national network, established in 2016 by South Africa's Department of Science and Innovation and hosted by the South African Medical Research Council, that harmonises the longitudinal population surveillance of health and demographic surveillance system (HDSS) nodes in South Africa, starting from the rural Agincourt, DIMAMO and Africa Health Research Institute HDSSs and extending to urban nodes, to provide up-to-date longitudinal health, demographic and socioeconomic data for research and national policy.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5448763/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For this purpose, a consortium of cohorts was built, including seven child cohorts and eleven adult cohorts (Fig 2).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC5448763/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "two Swiss cohorts (CoLaus/PsycoLaus [56], random sample of Lausanne inhabitants; Skipogh [57], Swiss volunteer families)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7235337/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Funded by the European Commission Horizon 2020 programme, the Lifepath research consortium aimed to investigate the effects of socioeconomic inequalities on the biology of healthy aging.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7235337/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project adopted a life-course and comparative approach, considering lifetime effects from childhood and adulthood, and pooled data on up to 1.7 million participants of longitudinal cohort studies from Europe, USA, and Australia.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7235337/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The project integrated social science approaches with biology (including molecular epidemiology) using existing population cohorts and omics measurements (particularly epigenomics).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28557991") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "http://www.lifepathproject.eu/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32478023") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7235337/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Using data from the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study (MCCS) including 2,818 participants in whom full resolution DNA methylation data were available") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002698> "A research consortium funded by the European Commission under Horizon 2020 that pooled and harmonised data from existing adult and child cohort studies in Europe, the USA and Australia, including CoLaus, SKIPOGH, Constances and the Melbourne Collaborative Cohort Study, with biomarker and omics sub-studies, to investigate the biological pathways through which socioeconomic position affects healthy ageing over the life course.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2361672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1985 and 2001, 167 371 adult Vorarlberg residents were enrolled in the VHM&PP Study Cohort after signing an informed consent to store and process personal data (height, weight, smoking and other factors).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2361672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Between 1985 and 2002, incident invasive cancers were identified by the Vorarlberg cancer registry, which is accepted for publication by the International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) since 1993 (Parkin et al, 2003).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2361672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cohort data were linked with the Vorarlberg Death Index to identify deaths among cohort members to calculate person-years at risk.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2361672/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The screening examination takes place in the practice of local physicians; it includes a physical examination, a blood test and a consultation with a doctor.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2878454/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The VHM&PP is a population-based risk factor surveillance programme in Vorarlberg, the westernmost province in Austria.12") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:16234822") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19380371") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2878454/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The purpose of the programme was to prevent chronic diseases, foremost cardiovascular diseases and cancer, and it was routinely performed by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002699> "A population-based cohort of adult residents of Vorarlberg, the westernmost province of Austria, enrolled from 1985 through a routine risk-factor surveillance and prevention programme run by the Agency for Social and Preventive Medicine, in which local physicians carried out a physical examination, blood test and consultation, and followed by linkage to the Vorarlberg cancer registry and death index to study metabolic and other risk factors for cancer, cardiovascular disease and mortality.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17881411") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC2557061/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible individuals are mailed an invitation to take part, an information leaflet, the study questionnaire and consent form and a reply paid envelope (available at www.45andUp.org.au).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, between 2005 and 2009, individuals aged ≥45 years and residing in NSW were randomly sampled from the Services Australia (formerly the Health Insurance Commission) Medicare enrolment database (MEDB) if they had received medical care within the previous 2 years.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Over 20 data sets including mortality, hospital and pharmaceutical data are routinely linked to the Study to identify sub-cohorts, risk factors, confounders and outcomes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Residents aged ≥80 years and those living in rural and remote areas were oversampled.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Since the original cohort paper in 2008, an additional 230 712 participants have been recruited and the baseline survey (2005–2009) and two follow-up surveys (2012–2015 and 2018–2020) have been completed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35604374") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9908035/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 45 and Up Study (‘the Study’) recruited 267 357 participants aged ≥45 years from New South Wales, Australia between 2005 and 2009 as a resource for researchers and policy makers to source evidence to support better health and ageing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002700> "A prospective population-based cohort of men and women aged 45 years and over in New South Wales, Australia, randomly sampled from the Medicare enrolment database and recruited by postal questionnaire in 2005–2009 by the Sax Institute, with oversampling of people aged 80 and over and of rural and remote residents, repeated follow-up surveys, biospecimen sub-studies and routine linkage to mortality, hospital, pharmaceutical and other health records, as a resource for research on health and ageing.")

