AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12371067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Established in 2018 to push beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, the IHCC is a community of cohorts advancing global science and health.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701> "An international consortium of large population cohorts, established in 2018 to work beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, whose members are chosen for size, longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection and a commitment to data sharing, and which maintains the IHCC Cohort Atlas, a directory of the data its member cohorts hold.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12371067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IHCC membership criteria prioritize large population cohorts, capability for longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection, and a commitment to data-sharing.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701> "An international consortium of large population cohorts, established in 2018 to work beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, whose members are chosen for size, longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection and a commitment to data sharing, and which maintains the IHCC Cohort Atlas, a directory of the data its member cohorts hold.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12371067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 2020, the Atlas was launched as the first open global directory of large-scale human cohorts, with cohort information gathered from surveys and data dictionaries.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701> "An international consortium of large population cohorts, established in 2018 to work beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, whose members are chosen for size, longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection and a commitment to data sharing, and which maintains the IHCC Cohort Atlas, a directory of the data its member cohorts hold.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40841586") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12371067/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IHCC Global Cohort Atlas serves as a centralized resource for discovering available data across cohorts.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002701> "An international consortium of large population cohorts, established in 2018 to work beyond the constraints of individual health and population cohorts, whose members are chosen for size, longitudinal health follow-up, broad participant selection, biological sample collection and a commitment to data sharing, and which maintains the IHCC Cohort Atlas, a directory of the data its member cohorts hold.")

