# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35281756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41756112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Detailed phenotypic information was collected, including non- invasive vascular function measurements, body surface mapping, and detailed information on presence or progression of AF during 5-years follow up is obtained by use of serial ECGs, 24-hour Holter monitoring and recordings from loop recorders.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704> "A prospective, observational hospital-based cohort of adults with recent-onset paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation for whom a rhythm-control strategy was preferred, conducted at the University Medical Center Groningen and Maastricht University Medical Center in the Netherlands between 2011 and 2016, with detailed cardiovascular phenotyping and serial rhythm monitoring to identify markers of atrial remodelling and atrial fibrillation progression and guide therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35281756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41756112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:29892015") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The AF-Risk study (ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT01510210) is an observational hospital-based cohort (n=500; in GGAF 339) to seek for markers of severity of atrial remodeling and predict outcome of a rhythm control treatment strategy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704> "A prospective, observational hospital-based cohort of adults with recent-onset paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation for whom a rhythm-control strategy was preferred, conducted at the University Medical Center Groningen and Maastricht University Medical Center in the Netherlands between 2011 and 2016, with detailed cardiovascular phenotyping and serial rhythm monitoring to identify markers of atrial remodelling and atrial fibrillation progression and guide therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35281756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41756112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:35281756") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8914333/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "including patients aged ≥ 18 years, with pAF (total AF history < 2 years, or total AF history < 3 years in case of ≤ 2 AF episodes of ≤ 48 h per month terminating spontaneously) or persistent AF (total AF history < 2 years, and total persistent AF duration > 7 days and < 1 year) in whom a rhythm control strategy was preferred.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704> "A prospective, observational hospital-based cohort of adults with recent-onset paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation for whom a rhythm-control strategy was preferred, conducted at the University Medical Center Groningen and Maastricht University Medical Center in the Netherlands between 2011 and 2016, with detailed cardiovascular phenotyping and serial rhythm monitoring to identify markers of atrial remodelling and atrial fibrillation progression and guide therapy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:35281756") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41756112") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41588-018-0133-9/MediaObjects/41588_2018_133_MOESM1_ESM.pdf") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41756112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12933449/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The identification of a risk profile to guide atrial fibrillation therapy (AF-RISK) study was a Dutch prospective, observational multicenter cohort study conducted at the University Medical Centre Groningen and the Maastricht University Medical Centre + between May 2011 and March 2016.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002704> "A prospective, observational hospital-based cohort of adults with recent-onset paroxysmal or persistent atrial fibrillation for whom a rhythm-control strategy was preferred, conducted at the University Medical Center Groningen and Maastricht University Medical Center in the Netherlands between 2011 and 2016, with detailed cardiovascular phenotyping and serial rhythm monitoring to identify markers of atrial remodelling and atrial fibrillation progression and guide therapy.")

