# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By linking the study subjects to the laboratory databases in Stockholm, we retrieved historical PSA values.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "For information on cancer status, we linked the study participants to the Regional Cancer Registry and to the Stockholm part of the National Prostate Cancer Registry (NPCR); information on tumour stage (TNM) and grade (Gleason score) were obtained.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From patient registries in two out of three pathology departments in Stockholm, Sweden, we identified 8088 men who had undergone at least one prostate biopsy between 1 January 2005 and 31 December 2007, representing 75% of all prostate biopsies conducted during this time period in Stockholm.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Men with known PCa before 2005 were also excluded (n = 154), as were men with cancer other than adenocarcinoma detected upon prostate biopsy (n = 10).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We excluded men older than 80 yr at the time of biopsy (n = 468),") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23535732") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21295399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4417350/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We received complete questionnaire data, written consent, and a blood sample from 5241 men (response rate: 75%) (Fig. 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002710> "A cohort of men aged 80 or younger who underwent prostate biopsy in Stockholm, Sweden, between 2005 and 2007, identified through pathology-department registries and excluding men with known prostate cancer before 2005. Participants provided blood samples and questionnaire information, with historical prostate-specific antigen measurements and cancer diagnoses, stage and grade obtained through laboratory and cancer-registry linkage, to investigate inherited susceptibility and improve prostate cancer risk prediction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23403126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "CLIC pools harmonized, individual-level data from case–control and cohort studies, obtained through interviews, record linkage (insurance claims, registries), or geographic information systems, and integrates germline genomic data where available.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> "An international consortium established in 2007 that pools harmonized individual-level epidemiologic and germline genetic data from independent case-control and cohort studies to investigate causes of childhood leukemia and other childhood cancers, with its scope expanded to other cancers in 2019. Its collaborative analyses examine environmental and genetic risk factors, their interactions, exposure timing, and differences among disease subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23403126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Exposure time windows are operationalized using harmonized definitions (e.g., whole gestation or pregnancy by trimester when available; early childhood by developmentally relevant age ranges).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> "An international consortium established in 2007 that pools harmonized individual-level epidemiologic and germline genetic data from independent case-control and cohort studies to investigate causes of childhood leukemia and other childhood cancers, with its scope expanded to other cancers in 2019. Its collaborative analyses examine environmental and genetic risk factors, their interactions, exposure timing, and differences among disease subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23403126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Further, linking germline genomic data with detailed epidemiologic information enables well-powered investigations of gene–environment interactions in childhood cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> "An international consortium established in 2007 that pools harmonized individual-level epidemiologic and germline genetic data from independent case-control and cohort studies to investigate causes of childhood leukemia and other childhood cancers, with its scope expanded to other cancers in 2019. Its collaborative analyses examine environmental and genetic risk factors, their interactions, exposure timing, and differences among disease subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23403126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Harmonized classifications of cancer subtype (including molecular features, where available) and diagnosis age support evaluation of etiologic heterogeneity, critical exposure windows, and plausible etiologic pathways.3.3.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> "An international consortium established in 2007 that pools harmonized individual-level epidemiologic and germline genetic data from independent case-control and cohort studies to investigate causes of childhood leukemia and other childhood cancers, with its scope expanded to other cancers in 2019. Its collaborative analyses examine environmental and genetic risk factors, their interactions, exposure timing, and differences among disease subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23403126") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42628293") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13544941/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Childhood Cancer and Leukemia International Consortium (CLIC) was established in 2007 to study the etiology of childhood leukemia and later expanded in 2019 to include other childhood cancers, principally solid tumors.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002711> "An international consortium established in 2007 that pools harmonized individual-level epidemiologic and germline genetic data from independent case-control and cohort studies to investigate causes of childhood leukemia and other childhood cancers, with its scope expanded to other cancers in 2019. Its collaborative analyses examine environmental and genetic risk factors, their interactions, exposure timing, and differences among disease subtypes.")

