AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17185468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26340796") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:17185468") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1852242/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "InterLymph was established in 2000 as a voluntary consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma (http://epi.grants.cancer.gov/InterLymph).28") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002713> "An international consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma and pools individual-level data from lymphoid malignancy case-control studies to investigate lymphoma etiology and subtype-specific risk factors, including associations with rare exposures and less common lymphoma subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17185468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26340796") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4155460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Formed in 2001, InterLymph’s primary goal was to facilitate pooled analyses of individual-level data from lymphoid malignancy case-control studies with the purpose of increasing statistical power for examining associations with rare exposures and less common NHL subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002713> "An international consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma and pools individual-level data from lymphoid malignancy case-control studies to investigate lymphoma etiology and subtype-specific risk factors, including associations with rare exposures and less common lymphoma subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17185468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26340796") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4155460/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore undertook the “InterLymph NHL Subtypes Project,” a consortium-wide initiative with the aims of 1) evaluating associations for medical history, family history of hematologic malignancy, lifestyle factors, and occupation with specified NHL subtypes, and 2) quantitatively assessing etiologic heterogeneity among NHL subtypes.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002713> "An international consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma and pools individual-level data from lymphoid malignancy case-control studies to investigate lymphoma etiology and subtype-specific risk factors, including associations with rare exposures and less common lymphoma subtypes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17185468") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:25174022") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26340796") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26340796") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC4829988/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The InterLymph consortium of international investigators undertakes research projects to pool data across studies that explore the etiology of lymphoid malignancies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002713> "An international consortium that facilitates collaboration among epidemiologic studies of lymphoma and pools individual-level data from lymphoid malignancy case-control studies to investigate lymphoma etiology and subtype-specific risk factors, including associations with rare exposures and less common lymphoma subtypes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20818855+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We randomly assigned 1370 patients with newly diagnosed early-stage Hodgkin's lymphoma with a favorable prognosis to one of four treatment groups:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–75 years with newly diagnosed, biopsy-proven, early-stage Hodgkin lymphoma without adverse risk factors, assembled by the German Hodgkin Study Group to compare two or four cycles of ABVD chemotherapy followed by involved-field radiotherapy at 20 or 30 Gy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20818855+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We therefore conducted a multicenter, randomized trial comparing four treatment groups consisting of a combination chemotherapy regimen of two different intensities followed by involved-field radiation therapy at two different dose levels.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–75 years with newly diagnosed, biopsy-proven, early-stage Hodgkin lymphoma without adverse risk factors, assembled by the German Hodgkin Study Group to compare two or four cycles of ABVD chemotherapy followed by involved-field radiotherapy at 20 or 30 Gy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3553532/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1998 to 2002, the German Hodgkin Study Group (GHSG) conducted the 4th generation of clinical trials for the treatment of HL (HD10–12) involving a total of 4610 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–75 years with newly diagnosed, biopsy-proven, early-stage Hodgkin lymphoma without adverse risk factors, assembled by the German Hodgkin Study Group to compare two or four cycles of ABVD chemotherapy followed by involved-field radiotherapy at 20 or 30 Gy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3553532/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the HD10 study for early stages (CS I, II without risk factors) patients were randomized to receive 2 or 4 cycles of doxorubicin, bleomycin, vinblastine, and dacarbazine (ABVD) followed by either 30 Gy or 20 Gy involved-field (IF) radiotherapy (Engert et al, 2010).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–75 years with newly diagnosed, biopsy-proven, early-stage Hodgkin lymphoma without adverse risk factors, assembled by the German Hodgkin Study Group to compare two or four cycles of ABVD chemotherapy followed by involved-field radiotherapy at 20 or 30 Gy.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20818855") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3553532/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients between 16 and 75 years (except HD12 trial: not older than 65 years) had to have biopsy-proven HL at diagnosis to be eligible for randomisation.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002714> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–75 years with newly diagnosed, biopsy-proven, early-stage Hodgkin lymphoma without adverse risk factors, assembled by the German Hodgkin Study Group to compare two or four cycles of ABVD chemotherapy followed by involved-field radiotherapy at 20 or 30 Gy.")

