AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21990399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30290903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21990399") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A21990399+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this prospectively randomized multicenter trial, eight cycles of BEACOPP(escalated) was compared with four cycles of BEACOPP(escalated) followed by four cycles of the baseline dose of BEACOPP (BEACOPP(baseline); 4 + 4), and RT with no RT in the case of initial bulk or residual disease.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002716> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–65 years with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed, advanced-stage Hodgkin lymphoma, enrolled by the German Hodgkin Study Group from January 1999 to January 2003 to compare eight cycles of escalated-dose BEACOPP with four escalated-dose followed by four baseline-dose cycles, and to compare consolidation radiotherapy with no radiotherapy for initial bulky or residual disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21990399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30290903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3553532/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "From 1998 to 2002, the German Hodgkin Study Group (GHSG) conducted the 4th generation of clinical trials for the treatment of HL (HD10–12) involving a total of 4610 patients.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002716> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–65 years with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed, advanced-stage Hodgkin lymphoma, enrolled by the German Hodgkin Study Group from January 1999 to January 2003 to compare eight cycles of escalated-dose BEACOPP with four escalated-dose followed by four baseline-dose cycles, and to compare consolidation radiotherapy with no radiotherapy for initial bulky or residual disease.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21990399") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23321510") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30290903") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30290903") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A30290903+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "1670 patients with newly diagnosed, histology-proven, advanced-stage Hodgkin's lymphoma received eight cycles of eBEACOPP or four cycles of eBEACOPP plus four cycles of bBEACOPP (4 + 4), plus consolidation radiotherapy to initial bulk and residual disease or no radiotherapy, to analyse two non-inferiority objectives.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002716> "A randomized multicentre trial cohort of patients aged 16–65 years with newly diagnosed, histologically confirmed, advanced-stage Hodgkin lymphoma, enrolled by the German Hodgkin Study Group from January 1999 to January 2003 to compare eight cycles of escalated-dose BEACOPP with four escalated-dose followed by four baseline-dose cycles, and to compare consolidation radiotherapy with no radiotherapy for initial bulky or residual disease.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this report we present meta- and pooled analyses of published and unpublished data on 10 SNPs corresponding to seven DNA repair genes that play key roles in the NER, BER, HRR, and NHEJ DNA repair pathways.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717> "An international consortium formed in 2005 that pools comparable data from independent bladder cancer studies to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors and their interactions. Its collaborative analyses combine case-control and case-only data, including investigations of DNA repair gene variation and cigarette smoking in bladder cancer susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Specifically, we report findings on the associations between bladder cancer risk and each SNP and their interactions with cigarette smoking.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717> "An international consortium formed in 2005 that pools comparable data from independent bladder cancer studies to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors and their interactions. Its collaborative analyses combine case-control and case-only data, including investigations of DNA repair gene variation and cigarette smoking in bladder cancer susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Consortium of Bladder Cancer (ICBC; http://dceg.cancer.gov/icbc/) was formed in 2005 to facilitate the pooling of comparable data on environmental and genetic risk factors across studies in order to overcome the limited statistical power of individual studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717> "An international consortium formed in 2005 that pools comparable data from independent bladder cancer studies to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors and their interactions. Its collaborative analyses combine case-control and case-only data, including investigations of DNA repair gene variation and cigarette smoking in bladder cancer susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:19706757") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2782435/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Twelve studies contributed case-control data and one study provided case-only data, to the ICBC, for a total of 6,348 cases and 6,752 controls (Table 1).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002717> "An international consortium formed in 2005 that pools comparable data from independent bladder cancer studies to investigate environmental and genetic risk factors and their interactions. Its collaborative analyses combine case-control and case-only data, including investigations of DNA repair gene variation and cigarette smoking in bladder cancer susceptibility.")

