AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Future analyses will include a genome-wide association study and will explore the roles of gene-environment and gene-gene interactions in glioma etiology.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002720> "An international consortium that studies inherited susceptibility to glioma through a familial glioma study and the Glioma International Case-Control Study. It recruits families affected by multiple gliomas and coordinates multisite case-control recruitment, questionnaire data and biospecimen collection to investigate genetic risk and gene-environment interactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we briefly describe the Glioma International Case-Control (GICC) Study (recruitment, 2010–2013), a study being conducted by the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium that integrates data from multiple data collection sites, uses a common protocol and questionnaire, and includes biospecimen collection.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002720> "An international consortium that studies inherited susceptibility to glioma through a familial glioma study and the Glioma International Case-Control Study. It recruits families affected by multiple gliomas and coordinates multisite case-control recruitment, questionnaire data and biospecimen collection to investigate genetic risk and gene-environment interactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Thus, capitalizing upon the infrastructure in place from the GLIOGENE familial study, we have launched a large study of glioma that includes biospecimen collection: the Glioma International Case-Control (GICC) Study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002720> "An international consortium that studies inherited susceptibility to glioma through a familial glioma study and the Glioma International Case-Control Study. It recruits families affected by multiple gliomas and coordinates multisite case-control recruitment, questionnaire data and biospecimen collection to investigate genetic risk and gene-environment interactions.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:17855690") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23290425") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:26656478") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4706682/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To examine the genetic factors underlying familial glioma, the Genetic Epidemiology of Glioma International Consortium (GLIOGENE Consortium) was formed in 2006 to recruit families affected by ≥2 cases of glioma from 14 institutions across 5 countries (12).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002720> "An international consortium that studies inherited susceptibility to glioma through a familial glioma study and the Glioma International Case-Control Study. It recruits families affected by multiple gliomas and coordinates multisite case-control recruitment, questionnaire data and biospecimen collection to investigate genetic risk and gene-environment interactions.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=11150357&retmode=xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The 799 controls were patients admitted to the same hospitals as the patients with brain tumors for a variety of nonmalignant conditions.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=11150357&retmode=xml") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We examined the use of cellular telephones in a case-control study of intracranial tumors of the nervous system conducted between 1994 and 1998.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3850418/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Eligible cases included patients diagnosed with a first primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous neoplasm (codes 9380–9473 and 9490–9506 of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, 2nd edition [ICD-O-2]), meningioma (ICD-O-2 codes 9530–9538), or acoustic neuroma (ICD-O-2 code 9560) within the eight weeks during or preceding hospitalization.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3850418/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Information about occupational history was obtained through a detailed in-person interview that included job-specific modules of questions such that the interview was tailored to each individual’s particular work history.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3850418/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "were frequency-matched to cases (1:1) by sex, age at interview (18–29, 30–39, 40–49, 50–59, 60–69, 70–79, 80–99 years), race/ethnicity (non-Hispanic white, Hispanic white, African-American, other), hospital (Boston, Pittsburgh, Phoenix), and proximity to the hospital (0–4, 5–14, 15–29, 30–49, 50+ miles).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:11150357") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:15494094") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:19234232") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22864249") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22886559") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://media.springernature.com/original/springer-static/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fng.2270/MediaObjects/41588_2012_BFng2270_MOESM14_ESM.pdf") Annotation(rdfs:comment "National Cancer Institute Adult Brain Study 59 NCI-BTS Case-control Hospital- based 332 376 Blood Boston, Massachusetts; Phoenix, Arizona; Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002721> "A hospital-based case-control study of adults aged 18 or older with newly diagnosed primary glioma or other neuroepitheliomatous tumors, meningioma, or acoustic neuroma, and patients admitted for nonmalignant conditions, recruited at referral hospitals in Boston, Phoenix and Pittsburgh, United States, between June 1994 and August 1998. Controls were frequency-matched to the case series on age, sex, race or ethnicity, hospital and residential distance from the hospital. Interviews and biological samples support investigation of brain-tumor risk factors, including cellular-telephone use, occupational exposures and genetic susceptibility.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28632866+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Prospective cohort study of 6036 BRCA1 and 3820 BRCA2 female carriers (5046 unaffected and 4810 with breast or ovarian cancer or both at baseline)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28632866+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "To estimate age-specific risks of breast, ovarian, and contralateral breast cancer for mutation carriers and to evaluate risk modification by family cancer history and mutation location.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A28632866+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "with ascertainment through family clinics (94%) and population-based studies (6%).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7611162/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The combined cohort (“The BRCA1 and BRCA2 Cohort Consortium”) included data from 21 centres in Western countries (supplemental Table 1S).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7611162/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We harmonized risk factor and follow-up data from three prospective cohorts: The International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study (IBCCS) (19), the Kathleen Cuningham Foundation Consortium for Research Into Familial Breast Cancer (kConFab) Follow-Up Study (20,21), and the Breast Cancer Family Registry (BCFR) (22).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:28632866") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31792088") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:32665703") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC7521995/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The prospective cohort included pathogenic variant carriers from the BRCA1 and BRCA2 Cohort Consortium (BBCC)2 and CIMBA13 who were unaffected at recruitment (informed consent and baseline questionnaire).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002722> "An international consortium that harmonizes risk-factor and prospective follow-up data on women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants from the International BRCA1/2 Carrier Cohort Study, Breast Cancer Family Registry and kConFab. Participants are drawn from clinical genetics and population-based family studies to estimate breast, ovarian and contralateral breast cancer risks and investigate their genetic and non-genetic modifiers.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3680948/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Any woman who was known to carry a deleterious mutation in the BRCA1 or BRCA2 gene was eligible, including those diagnosed with cancer and those currently unaffected.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> "A French nationwide prospective cohort initiated in 2000 to estimate breast, ovarian and other cancer risks in women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants and to assess lifestyle, environmental and genetic factors that modify these risks. Participants are recruited through family cancer clinics after genetic counseling and followed for primary or subsequent cancer, including women already diagnosed with cancer and those unaffected at enrollment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3680948/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The GENEPSO study was initiated in 2000 to estimate the risk of breast, ovarian, and other cancers in BRCA1 and BRCA2 mutation carriers and to assess potential risk-modifying factors, either lifestyle or genetic.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> "A French nationwide prospective cohort initiated in 2000 to estimate breast, ovarian and other cancer risks in women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants and to assess lifestyle, environmental and genetic factors that modify these risks. Participants are recruited through family cancer clinics after genetic counseling and followed for primary or subsequent cancer, including women already diagnosed with cancer and those unaffected at enrollment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8320036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "GEMO and GENEPSO are two independent ongoing nation-wide studies involving BRCA1 and BRCA2 carriers, with unconnected databases and whose individuals were not registered by a shared identifier.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> "A French nationwide prospective cohort initiated in 2000 to estimate breast, ovarian and other cancer risks in women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants and to assess lifestyle, environmental and genetic factors that modify these risks. Participants are recruited through family cancer clinics after genetic counseling and followed for primary or subsequent cancer, including women already diagnosed with cancer and those unaffected at enrollment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8320036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In the prospective cohort GENEPSO, which aims at assessing environmental and lifestyle risk factors, BRCA1/2 mutation carriers are followed over time to observe characteristics of subjects who are developing either primary or secondary cancer.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> "A French nationwide prospective cohort initiated in 2000 to estimate breast, ovarian and other cancer risks in women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants and to assess lifestyle, environmental and genetic factors that modify these risks. Participants are recruited through family cancer clinics after genetic counseling and followed for primary or subsequent cancer, including women already diagnosed with cancer and those unaffected at enrollment.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22762150") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31948486") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34325649") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8320036/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Participants in both studies undergo genetic counseling and they are invited to participate in GEMO and/or GENEPSO through the family cancer clinics if tested positive for a mutation in BRCA1 or BRCA2.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002723> "A French nationwide prospective cohort initiated in 2000 to estimate breast, ovarian and other cancer risks in women carrying pathogenic BRCA1 or BRCA2 variants and to assess lifestyle, environmental and genetic factors that modify these risks. Participants are recruited through family cancer clinics after genetic counseling and followed for primary or subsequent cancer, including women already diagnosed with cancer and those unaffected at enrollment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41078339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22561842+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1987, the first Regional Prostate Cancer Register was set up in the South-East health-care region of Sweden.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724> "A nationwide clinical prostate cancer registry in Sweden, originating from a regional register established in 1987 and covering the country since 1998, that records newly diagnosed prostate cancer, diagnostic workup, tumour characteristics and primary treatment to support quality assurance, benchmarking and clinical research on care and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41078339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22561842") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22561842+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Other health-care regions joined and since 1998 virtually all prostate cancer (PCa) cases are registered in the National Prostate Cancer Register (NPCR) of Sweden to provide data for quality assurance, bench marking and clinical research.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724> "A nationwide clinical prostate cancer registry in Sweden, originating from a regional register established in 1987 and covering the country since 1998, that records newly diagnosed prostate cancer, diagnostic workup, tumour characteristics and primary treatment to support quality assurance, benchmarking and clinical research on care and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:22561842") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:41078339") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41078339") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12516312/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The NPCR contains comprehensive data on cancer characteristics at date of diagnosis, diagnostic workup including prostate biopsies and imaging, and primary treatment strategy.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002724> "A nationwide clinical prostate cancer registry in Sweden, originating from a regional register established in 1987 and covering the country since 1998, that records newly diagnosed prostate cancer, diagnostic workup, tumour characteristics and primary treatment to support quality assurance, benchmarking and clinical research on care and outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "By use of the unique 10-digit Swedish person identity number, we linked the NPCR Follow-up Study database to several other national databases.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Inclusion criteria were registration in NPCR from January 1, 1997 (January 1, 1998, in one region), through December 31, 2002; age 70 years or younger at the date of diagnosis; local tumor stage T1–2") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Retrospective study in a nationwide cohort of patients with localized prostate cancer who were 70 years or younger.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Follow-up Study was an observational study in the NPCR, with the aim of assessing outcome among patients with localized prostate cancer who were diagnosed after PSA testing had become prevalent in Sweden and for whom curative treatment may have been indicated.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Verification of eligibility, data on treatment, and the date that surveillance was terminated were extracted from medical records by research nurses in each of six health-care regions in Sweden at a median time of 4 years after the date of diagnosis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:31343436") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "GPT-6 (OpenAI), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20562373") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2897875/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "no signs of lymph node metastases (Nx or N0) or bone metastasis (Mx or M0); and serum PSA levels of less than 20 ng/mL (19).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002725> "A nationwide retrospective observational cohort of men with localized prostate cancer selected from the National Prostate Cancer Register of Sweden, with registration from January 1997 to December 2002, beginning in January 1998 in one healthcare region. Participants were aged 70 years or younger at diagnosis, had clinical local tumour stage T1–T2 and serum prostate-specific antigen below 20 ng/mL, and had no recorded signs of lymph-node or bone metastasis (N0/Nx and M0/Mx). Medical-record review and linkage to national registers were used to assess management and outcomes.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002726> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002726>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30616610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:22777311") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A22777311+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We compared clinical features, hospital management and prognosis of STEMI/NSTEMI in an unselected cohort of 1,496 prospectively enrolled patients (STEMI, 36.9 % and NSTEMI, 63.1 %), admitted in 1 year to one of the six hospitals in Florence health district (Italy).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002726> "A registry of patients with acute myocardial infarction admitted to the coronary units of the six hospitals of the Florence health district, Italy, between April 2008 and April 2009, followed for survival after the infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30616610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30616610") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6323789/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In AMI patients enrolled in the AMI-Florence 2 study, we found a metabolic fingerprint which was able to discriminate patients who died within 2 years from the cardiovascular event from survivors with high accuracy (AUC 0.859), and this result was duplicated in a validation set (AUC 0.801).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002726> "A registry of patients with acute myocardial infarction admitted to the coronary units of the six hospitals of the Florence health district, Italy, between April 2008 and April 2009, followed for survival after the infarction.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:30616610") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30616610") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6323789/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "patients admitted to the coronary units of the six hospitals (five community hospitals and one university hospital, the Careggi Hospital) of the Florence health district between April 2008 and April 2009, and enrolled in the frame of the Florence Acute Myocardial Infarction-2 (AMI-Florence 2) registry [23].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002726> "A registry of patients with acute myocardial infarction admitted to the coronary units of the six hospitals of the Florence health district, Italy, between April 2008 and April 2009, followed for survival after the infarction.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8498921/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "According to the pathological reassessment of independent neuropathologists, all the subjects were consistently diagnosed with glioma and were then further classified according to the 2007/2016 WHO classification system.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8498921/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Glioma tissues and corresponding genomic data and patient follow-up information were obtained from Beijing Tiantan Hospital at Capital Medical University, Tianjin Medical University General Hospital, Sanbo Brain Hospital at Capital Medical University") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8498921/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Here, we developed the Chinese Glioma Genome Atlas (CGGA), a user-friendly data portal for the storage and interactive exploration of cross-omics data, including nearly 2000 primary and recurrent glioma samples from Chinese cohort.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8498921/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "the Second Affiliated Hospital of Harbin Medical University, the First Affiliated Hospital of Nanjing Medical University, and the First Hospital of China Medical University.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34490096") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8416623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Cox proportional hazards regression analysis and survival analysis were used to differentiate the outcome of low- and high-risk patients, and the Chinese Glioma Genome Atlas (CGGA) cohort was used for validation of the data set.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:33662628") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:34490096") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC8416623/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We collected 693 and 512 gliomas with RNA‐seq data and clinical information from TCGA and CGGA databases, respectively.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002727> "A collection of primary and recurrent glioma samples, with genomic data and patient follow-up, from patients treated at Beijing Tiantan Hospital and other hospitals in China, all re-diagnosed by independent neuropathologists and made available through a cross-omics data portal.")

