AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31836702") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6910937/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Patients and their related donors analyzed in this study underwent an allogeneic HSCT in Saint Louis hospital, Paris, France (cohort 1, n = 43) or in one of the 33 French national transplant centers involved in CRYOSTEM Consortium") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002728> "A French national cohort of haematopoietic stem cell transplant recipients, and for some of them their donors, sampled before transplantation, at 100 days, one and two years afterwards and when graft-versus-host disease occurred, to study the complications of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "recipients at post-transplant systematic sampling periods (100 days, one and two years post-transplant), and at the occurence of Graft-versus-Host Disease – acute and chronic -and in the aftermath of the treatments implemented.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002728> "A French national cohort of haematopoietic stem cell transplant recipients, and for some of them their donors, sampled before transplantation, at 100 days, one and two years afterwards and when graft-versus-host disease occurred, to study the complications of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "recipients, and, for some of them, their donors, at pre-transplant sampling periods") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002728> "A French national cohort of haematopoietic stem cell transplant recipients, and for some of them their donors, sampled before transplantation, at 100 days, one and two years afterwards and when graft-versus-host disease occurred, to study the complications of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.cryostem.org/en/about-cryostem/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "to accelerate research in the area of complications of Hematopoietic Stem Cell Transplantation (HSCT)") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002728> "A French national cohort of haematopoietic stem cell transplant recipients, and for some of them their donors, sampled before transplantation, at 100 days, one and two years afterwards and when graft-versus-host disease occurred, to study the complications of haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002729> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002729>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2820141/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In 1981, DFCI and several other institutions in the United States and Canada formed the DFCI ALL Consortium.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002729> "A consortium formed in 1981 by the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute and other institutions in the United States and Canada that has conducted consecutive multi-institutional clinical trial protocols in childhood acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2820141/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this report, we update the results of the four consecutive clinical trials conducted by the DFCI ALL Consortium between 1985–2000.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002729> "A consortium formed in 1981 by the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute and other institutions in the United States and Canada that has conducted consecutive multi-institutional clinical trial protocols in childhood acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:20016537") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A20016537+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Dana-Farber Cancer Institute (DFCI) acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL) Consortium has been conducting multi-institutional clinical trials in childhood ALL since 1981.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002729> "A consortium formed in 1981 by the Dana-Farber Cancer Institute and other institutions in the United States and Canada that has conducted consecutive multi-institutional clinical trial protocols in childhood acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002730> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002730>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29982218") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8478246/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Briefly, ELICIT was a 2 × 2 factorial randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial (RCT) based in the Haydom Global Health Research Centre at Haydom Lutheran Hospital in Haydom, Tanzania [15].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002730> "A randomised, placebo-controlled, factorial trial of antimicrobials (azithromycin and nitazoxanide) and nicotinamide in children recruited within the first 14 days of life in rural Haydom, Tanzania, followed with their mothers through monthly home visits, with the child's length-for-age at 18 months as its primary outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29982218") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8478246/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this double-blind placebo-controlled, randomized controlled trial (RCT), we administered in a 2 × 2 factorial manner scheduled antimicrobials (azithromycin and nitazoxanide) and/or daily nicotinamide to a cohort of 1,188 children 0 to 18 months old, with a primary outcome of length-for-age z-score (LAZ) at 18 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002730> "A randomised, placebo-controlled, factorial trial of antimicrobials (azithromycin and nitazoxanide) and nicotinamide in children recruited within the first 14 days of life in rural Haydom, Tanzania, followed with their mothers through monthly home visits, with the child's length-for-age at 18 months as its primary outcome.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:29982218") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8478246/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Mother–child dyads were enrolled by age 14 days and followed with monthly home visits and every 3-month anthropometry assessments through 18 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002730> "A randomised, placebo-controlled, factorial trial of antimicrobials (azithromycin and nitazoxanide) and nicotinamide in children recruited within the first 14 days of life in rural Haydom, Tanzania, followed with their mothers through monthly home visits, with the child's length-for-age at 18 months as its primary outcome.")

