# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002747> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002747>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40931094") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40931094") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12423329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "A total of 2084 women were prospectively recruited from Preterm Birth Prevention Clinics across five participating sites (Queen Charlottes and Chelsea Hospital, St Mary’s Hospital, Chelsea and Westminster Hospital, and University College Hospital (all in London), and the Royal Infirmary Edinburgh Hospital) between 2014 and 2023 (Fig. 1a–c).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002747> "A cohort of women at risk of preterm birth prospectively recruited from preterm birth prevention clinics at five hospitals in London and Edinburgh, United Kingdom, between 2014 and 2023.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:40931094") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:40931094") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12423329/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Data on women who were defined as being ‘at-risk’ of preterm birth was collected from women participating in the Vaginal Microbiome and Metabonome in Pregnancy (VMET-2) Research study.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002747> "A cohort of women at risk of preterm birth prospectively recruited from preterm birth prevention clinics at five hospitals in London and Edinburgh, United Kingdom, between 2014 and 2023.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15296810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15296810+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "One thousand two hundred HIV-positive pregnant women were recruited in Lusaka, Zambia, and followed with their infants for 24 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:15296810") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=EXT_ID%3A15296810+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core") Annotation(rdfs:comment "We present the rationale and design of the Zambian Exclusive Breast-feeding Study (ZEBS), a randomized trial evaluating the efficacy of short-duration exclusive breast-feeding (EBF) as a strategy to reduce postnatal human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) transmission while preserving the other health benefits of this important mode of infant feeding.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2577610/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All the women planned to breast-feed exclusively to 4 months; 481 were randomly assigned to a counseling program that encouraged abrupt weaning at 4 months, and 477 to a program that encouraged continued breast-feeding for as long as the women chose.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:41152239") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC12568960/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In ZEBS, WLWH were randomized to either breastfeed until usual breastfeeding cessation or to rapidly wean at 4 months.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:42006329") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC13091459/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The ZEBS was conducted between 2001 and 2004 among women living with HIV in Lusaka, Zambia, to evaluate the effects of exclusive breastfeeding for 4 months followed by abrupt weaning on postnatal HIV transmission and mortality through the first 2 years of life.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:18525036") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6905447/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "All women were counseled to breastfeed to at least 4 months, and then half of them were randomized to stop breastfeeding and the other half to continue it.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002748> "A randomised trial in Lusaka, Zambia, in which HIV-infected women who planned to breastfeed exclusively to four months were assigned to counselling that encouraged abrupt weaning at four months or continued breastfeeding, to evaluate the effect of early weaning on the HIV-free survival of their children to 24 months.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31770451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7098874/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Comparing simulated data with real‐world data from the IPDN registries supports the results and the validity of our approach and served as an external validation of the modelling and simulation framework.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> "A global consortium of paediatric nephrology centres dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis, which runs two registries: the IPPN registry for children on chronic peritoneal dialysis and the IPHN registry for children on haemodialysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31770451") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7098874/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Simulation results were challenged by comparing with real‐world data on C.E.R.A. doses and Hb levels obtained from paediatric patients treated with IV (n = 32) and SC (n = 126) C.E.R.A. in the International Pediatric Dialysis Network (IPDN) database (http://www.pedpd.org).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> "A global consortium of paediatric nephrology centres dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis, which runs two registries: the IPPN registry for children on chronic peritoneal dialysis and the IPHN registry for children on haemodialysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37566114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10817843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "IPPN and IPHN collect prospective data (baseline and every 6 months) from pediatric PD and HD centers worldwide.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> "A global consortium of paediatric nephrology centres dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis, which runs two registries: the IPPN registry for children on chronic peritoneal dialysis and the IPHN registry for children on haemodialysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37566114") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC10817843/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The IPDN entertains two registries: the International Pediatric Peritoneal Dialysis Network (IPPN) registry for children on long-term PD, and the International Pediatric Hemodialysis Network (IPHN) registry for children on HD.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> "A global consortium of paediatric nephrology centres dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis, which runs two registries: the IPPN registry for children on chronic peritoneal dialysis and the IPHN registry for children on haemodialysis.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.pedpd.org/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The International Pediatric Dialysis Network is a global consortium of pediatric nephrology centers dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002749> "A global consortium of paediatric nephrology centres dedicated to the care of children on chronic dialysis, which runs two registries: the IPPN registry for children on chronic peritoneal dialysis and the IPHN registry for children on haemodialysis.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9656994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In this population-based prospective cohort, which was established in 2007, three phases covering pregnancy (I), early childhood (II), and early school age (III) periods have already been completed.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> "A population-based multi-centre longitudinal cohort of pregnant women recruited in Poland from 2007 to 2011, with their children followed through infancy, childhood and adolescence, to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle exposures during pregnancy and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9656994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Phase IV gives a uniform opportunity to follow-up children during adolescence in order to evaluate if the consequences of prenatal and early postnatal exposures still persist at the age of 14.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> "A population-based multi-centre longitudinal cohort of pregnant women recruited in Poland from 2007 to 2011, with their children followed through infancy, childhood and adolescence, to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle exposures during pregnancy and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9656994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Polish Mother and Child Cohort (REPRO_PL) is a population-based multi-center longitudinal study established in 2007 in Poland.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> "A population-based multi-centre longitudinal cohort of pregnant women recruited in Poland from 2007 to 2011, with their children followed through infancy, childhood and adolescence, to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle exposures during pregnancy and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9656994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The general aim of the REPRO_PL cohort is to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle-related exposures during the prenatal period and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and/or offspring health during various stages of life (infancy, childhood and adolescence).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> "A population-based multi-centre longitudinal cohort of pregnant women recruited in Poland from 2007 to 2011, with their children followed through infancy, childhood and adolescence, to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle exposures during pregnancy and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and offspring health.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36361044") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC9656994/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The women who agreed to participate in the study were followed-up three times during pregnancy (Phase I of the study, recruitment period: 2007–2011) [11].") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002750> "A population-based multi-centre longitudinal cohort of pregnant women recruited in Poland from 2007 to 2011, with their children followed through infancy, childhood and adolescence, to evaluate the impact of occupational, environmental and lifestyle exposures during pregnancy and after birth on pregnancy outcomes and offspring health.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002751> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002751>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:23269124") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic), 2026-09") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-09") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002751> "A prospective cohort of mother-infant pairs recruited in the coastal Province of Trieste, Italy, in Ljubljana, Slovenia, in Rijeka, Croatia, and on Greek islands, set up within the PHIME project (2006 to 2011) to investigate the effects of prenatal low-level mercury exposure from maternal fish and seafood consumption on child neurodevelopment.")

# Individual: <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> (<http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752>)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3176830/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Population Architecture using Genomics and Epidemiology (PAGE) Study was initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases in several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24068893") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3775722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Assistance with phenotype harmonization, SNP selection and annotation, data cleaning, data management, integration and dissemination, and general study coordination was provided by the PAGE Coordinating Center (U01HG004801-01).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24068893") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3775722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "In brief, a panel of 68 common polymorphisms previously reported to associate with body mass index (BMI) [13], type 2 diabetes (T2D) [14], or lipid levels [15] was genotyped in up to 14,492 self-reported African Americans (AA), 8,202 Hispanic Americans (HA), 5,425 Asian Americans (AS), 6,186 Native Americans (NA), 1,801 Pacific Islanders (PI), and 37,061 EA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24068893") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3775722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Population Architecture Using Genomics and Epidemiology (PAGE) program is funded by the National Human Genome Research Institute (NHGRI).") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:24068893") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC3775722/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Population Architecture Using Genomics and Epidemiology (PAGE) study is a consortium of multi-ancestry, population-based studies formed with the objective of refining our understanding of the genetic architecture of common traits emerging from GWAS.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:28391526") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5485655/") Annotation(rdfs:comment "The Population Architecture using Genomics and Epidemiology (PAGE) Study is comprised of several large study sites/consortia and a coordinating center bringing together samples of diverse populations including those included in this analysis:") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "PMID:21836165") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Anthropic), 2026-10") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/PMC6059436/fullTextXML") Annotation(rdfs:comment "Within each study we conducted a linear regression of SNP associations with self-reported or medical record-derived AAM or ANM (in years), adjusting for birth year, population stratification, and center/region, as appropriate, and meta-analyzed results across studies using multiple meta-analytic techniques.") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/coho/COHO_0002752> "A consortium initiated in 2008 by the National Human Genome Research Institute to investigate the epidemiologic architecture of well-replicated genetic variants associated with complex diseases across several large, ethnically diverse population-based studies of African American, white, Hispanic/Latino, Asian/Pacific Islander and American Indian participants, harmonising phenotypes across the studies and running coordinated cohort-specific analyses and meta-analyses.")

